// Generated by tools/generate-writing-submission-reference-data.mjs. Do not edit by hand.
const referenceData = {"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q1":{"exerciseId":"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q1","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=business-english-standard-response-book-1-q1","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"1. Idea","english":"I would say uncertainty makes business decisions harder, slower, and more delicate, because leaders often have to act without having the full picture.","chinese":"我會說，不確定性會令商業決策變得更困難、更緩慢，也更需要拿捏分寸，因為領導者很多時都要在資訊並不完整的情況下作出決定。"},{"label":"2. Explanation","english":"In business, uncertainty can cloud demand, costs, competition, regulation, and timing. When a company is unsure how the market will move, how customers will respond, or what risks may appear next, every major decision carries more weight. As a result, firms tend to be more cautious with hiring, investment, pricing, and expansion. In that sense, uncertainty does not just create risk; it puts real pressure on judgment.","chinese":"在商業環境裡，不確定性會令需求、成本、競爭、監管以及時機都變得不明朗。當一家公司不確定市場會怎樣走、客戶會如何反應，或者下一個風險會從哪裡冒出來時，每一個重要決策的分量都會變得更重。因此，公司通常會在招聘、投資、定價和擴張方面變得更審慎。從這個角度來看，不確定性不只是帶來風險；它其實是在考驗判斷力。"},{"label":"3. Example","english":"For example, if a company is considering a new product launch but demand is still unclear, it may avoid a full-scale rollout and test the market first. That is often the smarter move, because it limits the downside while keeping the opportunity alive. In uncertain conditions, strong businesses do not bet the farm; they usually stage their decisions.","chinese":"例如，如果一家公司正在考慮推出新產品，但市場需求仍然不明朗，它可能不會一開始就全面推出，而是先做市場測試。這通常是更聰明的做法，因為它一方面能控制下行風險，另一方面又保留住機會。在不確定的環境下，強的企業不會孤注一擲；它們會分階段作決策。"},{"label":"4. Conclusion","english":"So, to me, uncertainty affects business decisions by forcing leaders to balance speed with caution. They still need to move, but they need to move with discipline.","chinese":"所以，在我看來，不確定性對商業決策的影響，在於它迫使領導者在速度和審慎之間取得平衡。他們仍然要行動，只是行動必須更有紀律。"},{"label":"5. Idea 2","english":"That said, uncertainty is not always a purely negative force; sometimes it sharpens decision-making.","chinese":"不過，不確定性也不一定完全是壞事；有時候，它反而會令決策變得更銳利。"},{"label":"6. Explanation 2","english":"When the ground is shifting, weak thinking gets exposed very quickly. Uncertainty forces companies to question assumptions, stress-test plans, protect cash flow, and stay close to customers. It separates businesses that are merely busy from those that are genuinely strategic. In other words, uncertainty can be uncomfortable, but it can also be clarifying.","chinese":"當外部環境不斷變動時，薄弱的思考方式很快就會露出破綻。不確定性會迫使公司重新檢視假設、壓力測試計劃、保護現金流，並且更貼近客戶。它會把那些只是看起來很忙的企業，和那些真正有策略的企業區分開來。換句話說，不確定性也許令人不安，但它有時反而能讓問題變得更清楚。"},{"label":"7. Example","english":"For instance, when market conditions are unstable, a strong management team may break one big decision into smaller moves: they may run a pilot, review the numbers, refine the offer, and scale only when the signal is strong enough. That kind of disciplined flexibility is often what keeps a business resilient.","chinese":"例如，當市場環境不穩定時，一個強的管理團隊可能會把一個大的決策拆成較小的步驟：先做試點、再看數字、再調整方案，然後只在訊號夠明確時才擴大規模。這種有紀律的靈活性，往往正是企業保持韌性的關鍵。"},{"label":"8. Conclusion 2","english":"Overall, I’d say uncertainty does not mean a business should freeze; what it really demands is clearer thinking, better preparation, and smarter decisions. In business, you rarely get perfect clarity, so the real skill is not waiting for the fog to lift, but learning how to lead through it.","chinese":"總結來說，我會說，不確定性並不代表企業應該停住不動；它真正要求的是更清晰的思考、更周全的準備，以及更聰明的決策。在商業世界裡，你很少會得到百分之百的清晰度，所以真正的能力，不是等迷霧散去，而是學會在迷霧中帶路。"}],"vocabulary":[]},"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q2":{"exerciseId":"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q2","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=business-english-standard-response-book-1-q2","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"1. Idea","english":"If I had to choose one, I would say interest rates often put the greatest pressure on businesses overall, because they hit both the cost of money and the pace of demand.","chinese":"如果要我選一項，我會說，整體而言，利率往往對企業造成最大的壓力，因為它同時打擊資金成本，以及市場需求的節奏。"},{"label":"2. Explanation","english":"The reason is that higher interest rates do not just make borrowing more expensive. They also make customers more cautious, slow down investment, tighten cash flow, and raise the bar for every major decision. In that sense, rising rates can squeeze a business from both sides: they push costs up while pulling momentum down. Inflation, rent, and wages are all serious pressures, of course, but interest rates tend to cast the widest shadow.","chinese":"原因在於，較高的利率不只是令借錢變得更昂貴。它同時也會令客戶消費更審慎、投資放慢、現金流收緊，並提高每一個重大決策的門檻。從這個角度來看，利率上升會從兩邊夾擊企業：一邊推高成本，另一邊拖慢動能。當然，通脹、租金和人工上升也都是很嚴重的壓力，但利率的影響範圍通常最廣。"},{"label":"3. Example","english":"For example, if a company has loans, expansion plans, or heavy equipment to finance, a rise in interest rates can bite almost immediately. A firm may delay hiring, cut back investment, or shelve a new project simply because the numbers no longer stack up. It is a bit like driving with both the handbrake on and the road getting steeper.","chinese":"例如，如果一家公司本身有貸款、擴張計劃，或者需要為重型設備融資，利率一上升，壓力往往幾乎立刻就會出現。公司可能會延後招聘、削減投資，甚至把新項目擱置，原因只是那盤數已經不再划算。這有點像一邊拉着手掣開車，一邊前面的路還變得更斜。"},{"label":"4. Conclusion","english":"So, in broad business terms, I would say interest rates are often the heaviest pressure point because they affect financing, confidence, spending, and growth all at once.","chinese":"所以，從整體商業角度來說，我會認為利率往往是最沉重的壓力點，因為它會同時影響融資、信心、消費，以及增長。"},{"label":"5. Idea 2","english":"That said, the real answer still depends on the business model, because pressure lands differently in different industries.","chinese":"不過，真正的答案其實仍然取決於商業模式，因為不同產業承受壓力的方式並不一樣。"},{"label":"6. Explanation 2","english":"For a restaurant, retailer, or labour-intensive service business, rising wages or rent may hurt more directly. For example, if your margins are already thin, even a modest jump in payroll or occupancy costs can eat into profit very quickly. Inflation is also dangerous when a business cannot pass higher costs on to customers. So the bottom line is this: interest rates may be the broadest threat overall, but for some firms, wages or rent are where the pain is felt most sharply.","chinese":"對餐廳、零售商，或者勞動密集型的服務業來說，人工或租金上升可能會帶來更直接的打擊。舉例來說，如果本身利潤空間已經很薄，那麼即使只是薪酬成本或租用成本輕微上升，也可能很快侵蝕利潤。當企業無法把更高的成本轉嫁給客戶時，通脹同樣很危險。所以，最核心的一點是：利率也許是整體上最廣泛的威脅，但對某些公司來說，真正最痛的地方其實是人工或租金。"},{"label":"7. Example","english":"For instance, a software firm with low rent and strong margins may worry far more about interest rates and weaker demand, whereas a small café may feel rising wages and rent far more brutally, because those costs hit the business line by line, month after month.","chinese":"例如，一間租金負擔不高、利潤空間較大的軟件公司，可能更擔心利率上升和需求轉弱；相反，一間小型咖啡店則可能會更直接、更猛烈地感受到人工和租金上升的壓力，因為那些成本是一行一行、每個月都真實地壓在生意上。"},{"label":"8. Conclusion 2","english":"Overall, I’d say interest rates usually create the biggest pressure in the bigger picture, but the sharpest pain depends on where a business is most exposed. In business, pressure rarely arrives in a neat little box; it hits where the model is weakest.","chinese":"總結來說，我會說，從大局來看，利率通常帶來最大的壓力；但最尖銳的痛點，仍然取決於一家企業最脆弱的暴露點在哪裡。在商業世界裡，壓力很少會整整齊齊地裝在一個小盒子裡出現；它往往是朝着商業模式最弱的地方打下去。"}],"vocabulary":[]},"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q3":{"exerciseId":"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q3","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=business-english-standard-response-book-1-q3","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"1. Idea","english":"If I had to boil it down to three, I would choose judgment, communication, and execution.","chinese":"如果要我把它濃縮成三項，我會選判斷力、溝通力，以及執行力。"},{"label":"2. Explanation","english":"To begin with, judgment matters because managers are not paid merely to stay busy; they are paid to make sound calls. They need to separate signals from noise, decide what matters most, and know when to move. Just as importantly, communication is what turns a decision into a shared direction. A vague message creates drift, whereas a clear one creates alignment. Then comes execution, which is where plans either take shape or fall apart. Strategy may win attention, but follow-through wins trust.","chinese":"首先，判斷力之所以重要，是因為管理者的價值不只是忙碌，而是在於能作出穩健決定。他們要分辨甚麼是關鍵訊號、甚麼只是雜音，知道甚麼最重要，也知道何時出手。同樣重要的是，溝通力能把決定轉化為共同方向。訊息一旦含糊，團隊就容易漂移；訊息一旦清楚，方向就能對齊。然後就是執行力，因為計劃究竟能不能落地，往往就在這裡見真章。策略可以吸引注意，但真正贏得信任的，是後續落實。"},{"label":"3. Example","english":"Take a delayed product launch as an example. A strong manager will first identify the real bottleneck, then explain the priority in plain, direct language, and finally get the right people moving in step. That is management in the real world: make the call, bring people with you, and get the work over the line.","chinese":"以產品延期為例，一位強的管理者會先找出真正的卡點，然後用清楚直接的語言講明優先次序，最後推動合適的人同步行動。這就是現實世界裡的管理：作出決定、帶著團隊前進，並把事情真正做完。"},{"label":"4. Conclusion","english":"Seen in that light, the heart of management is not control for its own sake, but the ability to think clearly, align people, and deliver results.","chinese":"從這個角度看，管理的核心並不是為了控制而控制，而是能夠清楚思考、對齊團隊，並交出結果。"},{"label":"5. Idea 2","english":"Even so, those three abilities do not operate in neat little boxes; people leadership runs through all of them.","chinese":"即便如此，這三種能力也不是各自獨立運作的；帶人能力其實貫穿在三者之中。"},{"label":"6. Explanation 2","english":"Put differently, judgment without trust can feel cold, communication without empathy can ring hollow, and execution without buy-in can burn a team out. So, beneath the surface, strong management is also about reading the room, staying steady under pressure, and helping people perform without feeling crushed by the weight of it.","chinese":"換句話說，只有判斷而沒有信任，會顯得冷；只有溝通而沒有同理，會顯得空；只有執行而沒有認同，則很容易把團隊推到耗盡。所以，更深一層來看，強的管理也關乎看懂氣氛、在壓力下保持穩定，以及讓團隊在高表現之下不至於被壓垮。"},{"label":"7. Example","english":"That is why a technically brilliant manager can still fall short. They may spot the issue quickly enough, yet if they cannot build trust or create momentum, the team stalls. By the same token, a manager who is clear, calm, and consistent can often get more done with less friction.","chinese":"這也是為甚麼有些技術上非常出色的管理者，最後仍然帶不好團隊。他們也許很快就能看出問題，但如果無法建立信任，或者無法帶出動能，團隊仍然會卡住。相反，一位清晰、冷靜而且穩定的管理者，往往能以更少的摩擦做成更多事情。"},{"label":"8. Conclusion 2","english":"All told, if you strip management back to its bones, it comes down to three things: sound judgment, clear communication, and disciplined execution. Everything else matters, of course, but those three are the engine room. If they are weak, the whole machine starts to wobble.","chinese":"總結來說，如果把管理拆到最核心的骨架，它其實歸結為三件事：穩健的判斷、清晰的溝通，以及有紀律的執行。其他能力當然也重要，但這三項才是真正的引擎室。一旦它們弱下來，整部機器就會開始搖晃。"}],"vocabulary":[]},"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q4":{"exerciseId":"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q4","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=business-english-standard-response-book-1-q4","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"1. Idea","english":"Micromanagement usually creates three major problems: it weakens trust, slows execution, and reduces ownership.","chinese":"微觀管理通常會帶來三個主要問題：削弱信任、拖慢執行，以及降低責任感。"},{"label":"2. Explanation","english":"When a manager checks every tiny detail, people start to feel second-guessed rather than supported. That quickly drains confidence. Instead of thinking independently, employees wait for approval, play it safe, and stop taking initiative. The manager then becomes a bottleneck, so even simple decisions take longer than they should.","chinese":"當一位管理者連每一個小細節都要盯緊，員工感受到的往往不是支持，而是不被信任、處處被懷疑。這很快就會消磨他們的信心。員工不再主動思考，而是凡事等批准、走最保守的路，也不再主動出擊。到最後，管理者自己反而變成了瓶頸，令本來很簡單的決定都要花更久時間。"},{"label":"3. Example","english":"For example, if a team leader rewrites every email, approves every minor change, and questions every small decision, the team may still look busy, but real progress slows to a crawl. People spend more time managing upwards than solving real problems.","chinese":"例如，如果一位主管連每一封電郵都要改、每一個小改動都要批、每一個小決定都要追問，團隊表面上可能看起來很忙，但真正的進度卻會慢得像爬行一樣。大家花在「向上管理」的時間，可能比真正解決問題的時間還多。"},{"label":"4. Conclusion","english":"So, in practical terms, micromanagement may reduce small short-term risks, but it often creates much bigger long-term costs: lower morale, slower work, and weaker accountability.","chinese":"所以，從實際角度來看，微觀管理也許能減少一些短期的小風險，但它往往會製造更大的長期代價：士氣更低、工作更慢，以及問責更弱。"},{"label":"5. Idea 2","english":"On top of that, micromanagement can quietly damage innovation and retention.","chinese":"除此之外，微觀管理還會在不知不覺間傷害創新能力和人才留任。"},{"label":"6. Explanation 2","english":"When people feel watched at every turn, they usually stop speaking up. They avoid bold ideas, hide small mistakes, and stick to the safest possible option. Over time, capable employees feel boxed in and disengaged, and some eventually walk away. In that sense, micromanagement does not just control work; it shrinks the room people need in order to do their best work.","chinese":"當員工覺得自己每一步都被盯著看時，他們通常就不再願意多說、不再願意主動表達。他們會避開大膽的想法、掩飾小錯誤，並且只選最安全的做法。久而久之，有能力的員工會覺得自己被困住、慢慢失去投入感，有些人最後甚至會選擇離開。從這個角度來看，微觀管理不只是控制工作；它其實是在壓縮員工發揮最佳表現所需要的空間。"},{"label":"7. Example 2","english":"A strong employee in marketing, operations, or product development may have sharp ideas, but if every move is picked apart, that person will soon stop going the extra mile. They will do the job, but they will stop bringing their best judgment to it.","chinese":"一位在市場推廣、營運或產品開發方面本來很有想法的員工，起初也許會提出不少好點子；但如果他做的每一步都被過度挑剔，那麼他很快就不會再願意多走一步。他會把工作做完，但不再把自己最好的判斷力和心力帶進工作裡。"},{"label":"8. Conclusion 2","english":"Overall, micromanagement creates a fragile team: people become dependent, managers become overloaded, and performance loses momentum. That said, close guidance can still be useful when someone is new, when the stakes are unusually high, or when a team is in crisis. The key is to provide direction without choking initiative.","chinese":"總結來說，微觀管理會造成一個脆弱的團隊：員工變得依賴、管理者變得過載，而整體表現也會失去動能。不過，當一個人是新手、事情風險特別高，或者團隊正處於危機時，更密切的指導仍然可能有用。關鍵不在於放任不管，而是在提供方向的同時，不要扼殺主動性。"}],"vocabulary":[]},"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q5":{"exerciseId":"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q5","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=business-english-standard-response-book-1-q5","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"1. Idea","english":"If I had to give one clean answer, I’d say consumers usually come in through function, choose through feeling, and stay through identity.","chinese":"如果要我給一個乾淨俐落的答案，我會說，消費者通常是因功能而走進來，因感受而作出選擇，並因身份認同而留下來。"},{"label":"2. Explanation","english":"At the most basic level, a product has to do the job. If it fails on quality, reliability, or convenience, the rest is just window dressing. That said, once the functional baseline is in place, emotion starts to carry real weight. People are drawn to what feels reassuring, elegant, exciting, safe, or enjoyable. Beyond that, the strongest brands tap into identity: they help customers express who they are, or perhaps who they aspire to be. Put simply, function gets a brand onto the shortlist, but feeling and identity often tip the decision.","chinese":"在最基本的層面，一件產品首先必須把事情做好。如果它在品質、可靠性或便利性上站不住腳，其他包裝其實都只是表面工夫。不過，一旦功能底線已經到位，情感就開始真正發揮分量。人們往往會被那些令人安心、優雅、興奮、安全，或者愉悅的東西吸引。再進一步說，最強的品牌還會觸及身份認同：它們幫助顧客表達自己是怎樣的人，或者想成為怎樣的人。簡單來說，功能讓品牌進入候選名單，但感受和身份認同，往往才是最後推動決定的力量。"},{"label":"3. Example","english":"Take smartphones, for instance. Most major brands are already good enough on the basic functions, so the decision often shifts from “Can it work?” to “How does it feel to use, own, and be seen with it?” That helps explain why a brand like Apple is not selling hardware alone; it is also selling simplicity, taste, and a certain sense of self.","chinese":"以智能手機為例，大多數主要品牌在基本功能上其實都已經「夠用」了，所以決策重心往往會從「它能不能用？」轉向「用起來感覺如何、擁有它感覺如何、被別人看見時又代表甚麼？」這也正好說明了，像 Apple 這樣的品牌賣的並不只是硬件；它同時也在賣簡潔感、品味，以及某種自我形象。"},{"label":"4. Conclusion","english":"Seen in that light, consumers are rarely buying just one thing. On the surface, they may be paying for function, but underneath that, the purchase is often emotional and symbolic as well.","chinese":"從這個角度看，消費者其實很少只是在買單一樣東西。表面上，他們也許是在為功能付款；但更深一層來說，那筆購買往往同時帶有情感和象徵意義。"},{"label":"5. Idea 2","english":"Even so, the balance shifts from category to category, so the real answer depends on what is being sold and what is at stake.","chinese":"即便如此，三者的比重也會因品類而變，所以真正答案仍然取決於賣的是甚麼，以及風險有多高。"},{"label":"6. Explanation 2","english":"In practical, high-stakes, or technical categories, function tends to carry more weight. Nobody wants medicine, financial services, or cybersecurity that sounds impressive but falls apart when it matters. By contrast, in fashion, beauty, hospitality, or premium consumer goods, feeling and identity often move much closer to the centre. In fact, the more interchangeable the function becomes, the more brand meaning starts to matter.","chinese":"在實用型、高風險，或者技術性較強的品類裡，功能通常會佔更重的分量。沒有人會想要那種聽起來很厲害、但關鍵時刻卻掉鏈子的藥物、金融服務或網絡安全方案。相反，在時尚、美妝、酒店服務，或者高端消費品這些領域，感受和身份認同往往就更接近核心位置。事實上，當功能越來越容易被替代時，品牌意義就會變得越來越重要。"},{"label":"7. Example","english":"A bottle of pain relief is bought first for effectiveness. A luxury watch, on the other hand, is bought just as much for what it says. A brand like Nike sits somewhere in the middle: the product still has to perform, of course, but the brand also sells aspiration, confidence, and belonging.","chinese":"一瓶止痛藥，首先是因為有效才會被買下來。相對地，一隻名錶被購買，很大程度上也在於它「說明了甚麼」。像 Nike 這樣的品牌則處於中間位置：產品當然仍然要有表現，但品牌同時也在賣向上追求、自信，以及歸屬感。"},{"label":"8. Conclusion 2","english":"All told, I would not frame it as function or feeling or identity. It is more like a ladder. Function earns credibility, feeling creates preference, and identity builds loyalty. The brands that truly win are the ones that can cover all three, rather than putting all their chips on just one.","chinese":"總結來說，我不會把它理解成「功能、感受、身份認同三選一」。它更像是一道階梯：功能建立可信度，感受創造偏好，而身份認同培養忠誠。真正能贏的品牌，往往是三者都能兼顧，而不是把所有籌碼都押在其中一項上。"}],"vocabulary":[]},"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q6":{"exerciseId":"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q6","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=business-english-standard-response-book-1-q6","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"1. Response Part 1","english":"If I had to choose, I’d say the more important strategic question is usually what not to do.","chinese":"如果一定要我選，我會說更重要的策略問題通常是「不做甚麼」。"},{"label":"2. Response Part 2","english":"The reason is quite simple: strategy is not just about chasing opportunities; it is about making disciplined choices. Every company has limited time, capital, talent, and management attention. If a business tries to do everything, it spreads itself too thin, loses focus, and ends up being busy rather than effective. In that sense, what not to do is where real strategy begins, because it separates priority from distraction.","chinese":"原因其實很簡單：策略不只是追逐機會，更是有紀律地作出取捨。每一家公司都有有限的時間、資金、人才，以及管理層的注意力。如果一間企業甚麼都想做，它就很容易把資源攤得太薄、失去焦點，最後變成看起來很忙，卻未必真的有效。從這個角度來看，「不做甚麼」其實正是策略真正開始的地方，因為它把優先事項和分心因素分開了。"},{"label":"3. Response Part 3","english":"For example, a company may turn down an attractive partnership, drop a weak product line, or stop pursuing a market that looks exciting but does not fit its core strengths. Those decisions can feel uncomfortable in the short term, but they often protect focus and sharpen execution. That is why strong strategy is often less about adding more and more, and more about cutting with precision.","chinese":"例如，一間公司可能會拒絕一個看似吸引的合作機會、砍掉表現疲弱的產品線，或者停止追逐一個雖然很有話題性、卻不符合自己核心優勢的市場。這些決定在短期內也許會讓人覺得可惜，但它們往往能保住焦點，並且令執行更有力。這也就是為甚麼強策略很多時候不是一味加法，而是精準地做減法。"},{"label":"4. Response Part 4","english":"So, from a strategic point of view, knowing what not to do usually protects clarity, speed, and competitive edge.","chinese":"所以，從策略角度來看，知道「不做甚麼」往往更能保護清晰度、速度，以及競爭優勢。"},{"label":"5. Response Part 5","english":"That said, I would not say what to do is unimportant. In fact, without a clear direction, saying no to things becomes empty.","chinese":"不過，我也不會說「做甚麼」不重要。事實上，如果沒有清楚的方向，那麼對很多事情說不，其實也會變得空泛。"},{"label":"6. Response Part 6","english":"A business still needs a strong positive choice: which customers to serve, what value to create, and where it wants to win. In other words, what to do sets the destination, while what not to do protects the route. One gives direction; the other gives focus. The strongest strategies need both, but the harder and more defining discipline is often the ability to say no.","chinese":"一間企業始終還是需要一個明確而正面的選擇：要服務哪些客戶、要創造甚麼價值，以及要在哪裡取勝。換句話說，「做甚麼」決定目的地，而「不做甚麼」保護前進路線。前者提供方向，後者提供焦點。最強的策略其實兩者都需要，但更困難、也更能定義策略功力的，往往是說不的能力。"},{"label":"7. Response Part 7","english":"For instance, an early-stage company may need to explore several options before it knows where its real edge lies. At that stage, deciding what to do may matter more. But once the direction becomes clearer, disciplined restraint becomes critical; otherwise, the company can drift, dilute its brand, and burn energy in too many directions at once.","chinese":"例如，一間早期階段的公司在真正看清自己的優勢之前，可能需要探索幾個不同方向。在那個階段，先決定「做甚麼」也許會更重要。不過，一旦方向開始清晰，有紀律的克制就會變得非常關鍵；否則，公司很容易失焦、稀釋品牌，並且把精力同時耗在太多方向上。"},{"label":"8. Response Part 8","english":"Overall, I’d say strategy is built on both choice and sacrifice, but if a company wants to stay sharp, the more decisive question is often what not to do. After all, strategy is not just about opening doors; it is also about having the judgment to close the wrong ones.","chinese":"總結來說，我會說策略是建立在選擇與取捨之上的；但如果一間公司想保持銳利，那麼更關鍵的問題往往是「不做甚麼」。畢竟，策略不只是打開門，更在於有判斷力去關掉不該走的門。"}],"vocabulary":[]},"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q7":{"exerciseId":"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q7","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=business-english-standard-response-book-1-q7","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"1. Response Part 1","english":"If I had to give one answer, I’d say it is usually a management problem first, even when it looks like a process or talent problem on the surface.","chinese":"如果一定要我只給一個答案，我會說通常首先是管理問題，即使表面上看起來像流程問題或人才問題。"},{"label":"2. Response Part 2","english":"The reason is that management sets direction, priorities, accountability, and operating rhythm. If those things are weak, even strong people and reasonable processes can break down. Teams become unclear about who owns what, decisions move too slowly, and work starts slipping through the cracks. In other words, poor execution is often less about people not working hard, and more about the system around them not giving them a clear path to perform well.","chinese":"原因在於，管理層決定方向、優先次序、問責方式，以及整體運作節奏。如果這些東西本身不夠強，即使有不錯的人才和還算合理的流程，也一樣可能失靈。團隊會開始不清楚誰負責甚麼，決策推進太慢，工作也會一件一件從縫隙中漏掉。換句話說，執行力差很多時候不是因為員工不努力，而是因為他們所處的整個運作系統沒有給他們一條清晰的路去把事情做好。"},{"label":"3. Response Part 3","english":"For example, a company may have smart employees and detailed procedures, but if leaders keep changing priorities, avoid hard decisions, or fail to hold people accountable, execution will still be messy. Meetings multiply, follow-up weakens, and deadlines start to drift. At that point, blaming the team is often missing the main point.","chinese":"例如，一間公司可能擁有聰明的員工，也有很詳細的程序，但如果領導層不斷改變優先事項、迴避困難決定，或者沒有真正做好問責，那麼執行仍然會很混亂。會議愈開愈多，跟進卻愈來愈弱，截止日期也開始一再往後滑。到了這個時候，單純怪罪團隊，往往就是抓錯重點。"},{"label":"4. Response Part 4","english":"So, in many cases, management is the master lever, because it shapes how process and talent actually work in practice.","chinese":"所以，在很多情況下，管理其實是最關鍵的總槓桿，因為它決定了流程和人才在實際上能否真正發揮作用。"},{"label":"5. Response Part 5","english":"That said, I would not say process and talent are secondary in every case. Sometimes they are the immediate cause, even if management is the deeper one.","chinese":"不過，我也不會說流程和人才在每一種情況下都只是次要因素。有時候，它們確實是最直接的問題，即使更深層的原因仍然來自管理。"},{"label":"6. Response Part 6","english":"If the process is bloated, slow, or full of unnecessary approvals, execution can stall even with capable people. Likewise, if the company has the wrong people in key roles, no amount of structure will fully save performance. A weak manager can create confusion, but an outdated process can create friction, and a poor hire can create drag. That is why strong diagnosis matters: the visible symptom and the root cause are not always the same thing.","chinese":"如果流程本身過於肥大、太慢，或者充滿不必要的審批，即使團隊有能力，執行也可能卡住。同樣地，如果公司在關鍵位置放錯了人，再好的架構也未必救得回表現。弱的管理者會製造混亂，過時的流程會製造摩擦，而錯的人選則會拖慢整個團隊。這也就是為甚麼準確診斷很重要：表面症狀和真正根源，不一定是同一件事。"},{"label":"7. Response Part 7","english":"For instance, if sales keeps missing targets, the problem could be poor coaching from managers, but it could also be a broken approval flow, unclear pricing authority, or a team that simply lacks the commercial skills for the role. The smart question is not “Who do we blame?” but “Where is execution losing force?”","chinese":"例如，如果銷售團隊一直達不到目標，問題可能是管理者帶隊和指導做得不好，但也可能是審批流程失靈、定價權限不清，或者團隊本身根本缺乏這個職位所需要的商業能力。真正聰明的問題不是「應該怪誰」，而是「執行力到底在哪一個環節開始流失」。"},{"label":"8. Response Part 8","english":"Overall, I’d say poor execution is usually diagnosed as a process or talent issue, but more often than not, it traces back to management. Good management brings clarity, discipline, and follow-through. Without those, the process becomes paperwork, and talent becomes wasted potential.","chinese":"總結來說，我會說，執行力差表面上常常被診斷成流程問題或人才問題，但很多時候，追根究底還是會回到管理問題。好的管理能帶來清晰度、紀律，以及真正落地的跟進。沒有這些，流程就只會變成文書工作，而人才也只會變成被浪費的潛力。"}],"vocabulary":[]},"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q8":{"exerciseId":"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q8","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=business-english-standard-response-book-1-q8","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"1. Idea","english":"In most cases, I would say no — not unless the value they bring clearly outweighs the disruption they create.","chinese":"在大多數情況下，我會說不應該——除非他帶來的價值，明顯大於他製造的破壞。"},{"label":"2. Explanation","english":"At first glance, raw ability can look irresistible. A brilliant candidate may seem like a shortcut to stronger results. The trouble is that business is rarely a solo sport. Once someone is hard to work with, their talent can come with hidden costs: slower collaboration, weaker trust, lower morale, and constant friction. In other words, a high performer can still be a bad hire if they poison the well around them.","chinese":"乍看之下，純粹的能力確實很吸引。一位非常出色的候選人，看起來好像能成為快速提升表現的捷徑。但問題在於，商業世界很少是單打獨鬥的遊戲。一旦某個人很難合作，他的才能往往就會夾帶隱藏成本：協作變慢、信任削弱、士氣下降，以及持續不斷的摩擦。換句話說，一個高表現者，仍然可能是一個糟糕的聘用決定，因為他會把周圍的環境搞壞。"},{"label":"3. Example","english":"Picture a senior salesperson who brings in big numbers but undermines colleagues, hoards information, and creates tension at every meeting. On paper, that person looks like an asset. In practice, they can burn management time, push good people out, and leave the team walking on eggshells. That is a very expensive kind of brilliance.","chinese":"試想像一位高級業務員，他的業績很亮眼，卻經常拆同事台、把資訊收起來不共享，而且每次開會都搞到氣氛緊張。從紙面上看，這個人像是一項資產；但在現實裡，他可能會消耗管理層大量時間、逼走優秀同事，並讓整個團隊如履薄冰。那其實是一種代價非常高的「聰明」。"},{"label":"4. Conclusion","english":"So, by and large, I would not hire for talent alone. If someone lifts results but drags down the team, the business may still come out behind.","chinese":"所以，整體而言，我不會只因為能力強就聘用一個人。如果一個人提升了表面結果，卻拖垮了整個團隊，那麼企業最後仍然可能是得不償失。"},{"label":"5. Idea 2","english":"That said, I would not rule it out completely, because there are rare situations where the answer could be yes.","chinese":"不過，我也不會完全排除這種可能，因為在少數情況下，答案也可以是「可以」。"},{"label":"6. Explanation 2","english":"A more defensible case would be a highly specialised role, especially when the work is less interdependent, the expectations are crystal clear, and the manager is strong enough to set hard boundaries. Even then, the company should go in with its eyes open. The key question is not “Is this person talented?” but “Can this talent be contained, directed, and made useful without tearing the fabric of the team?” If the answer is no, then the hire is a gamble.","chinese":"比較站得住腳的情況，會是某種高度專業化的角色，尤其當工作本身對跨部門合作依賴較低、要求非常清晰，而且主管也夠強，能夠設下明確界線。即使如此，公司也必須睜大眼睛去看。關鍵問題不在於「這個人有沒有才華」，而在於「這份才華能否被妥善管理、清楚引導，並在不撕裂團隊的前提下發揮價值？」如果答案是否定的，那這個聘用就是一場賭博。"},{"label":"7. Example","english":"Say a company needs a rare technical expert for a short, high-impact project. If the role is tightly scoped, the reporting line is firm, and the behavioural standards are spelled out from day one, the risk may be manageable. Even so, I would treat that as a controlled exception, not a hiring philosophy.","chinese":"假設一家公司因一個短期但影響很大的項目，需要一位極罕有的技術專家。如果那個職位的範圍被清楚界定、匯報線很明確，而且從第一天開始就把行為標準講清楚，那麼風險或許是可控的。即便如此，我也只會把這視為一個受控例外，而不是一種長期招聘理念。"},{"label":"8. Conclusion 2","english":"All things considered, I would say companies should hire not just for horsepower, but for fit, trust, and team effect. A sharp mind is valuable, of course, but if it comes with sharp elbows, the cost can spread fast. Talent may win attention; character decides whether the win lasts.","chinese":"總結來說，我會說，公司招聘時不應只看「馬力」，也應看匹配度、信任感，以及對整個團隊的影響。敏銳的頭腦當然有價值，但如果同時帶著強烈的攻擊性和難合作的個性，代價往往會迅速擴散。才華也許能贏得注意，但真正決定勝負能否持久的，還是品格。"}],"vocabulary":[]},"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q9":{"exerciseId":"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q9","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=business-english-standard-response-book-1-q9","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"1. Idea","english":"Not necessarily. High profit is a strong signal, but it is not a full health check.","chinese":"不一定。高利潤是一個強烈訊號，但它並不是一份完整的健康檢查。"},{"label":"2. Explanation","english":"The trouble is that profit shows one outcome, whereas business health is a much bigger picture. A company can post impressive profits and still have weak cash flow, heavy debt, overreliance on one customer, exhausted staff, or a product line that is quietly losing steam. On top of that, profits can be boosted for a season by raising prices aggressively, cutting too deep, or delaying investment. In other words, the numbers may sparkle, but the foundations may already be cracking.","chinese":"問題在於，利潤反映的只是一個結果，而企業健康其實是一幅更大的全景圖。一家公司即使交出亮眼利潤，仍然可能同時存在現金流薄弱、債務沉重、過度依賴單一客戶、員工過勞，或者產品線正在悄悄失去動能等問題。除此之外，利潤有時也可以靠短期手段被推高，例如激進加價、過度削成本，或者延後必要投資。數字也許很亮，但地基可能早已開始出現裂痕。"},{"label":"3. Example","english":"Take a company that slashes training, freezes hiring, and cuts maintenance to lift earnings this year. On paper, the profit looks superb. In reality, service quality may slip, good people may walk, and future growth may dry up. That is the business version of painting over damp walls: it looks tidy for a while, but the problem is still there.","chinese":"例如，一家公司為了推高今年盈利，大幅削減培訓、凍結招聘，並壓低維修開支。從帳面上看，利潤非常漂亮；但在現實裡，服務質素可能會下滑，優秀員工可能會離開，未來增長也可能慢慢枯萎。這就像把潮濕的牆面重新粉飾一樣：一時之間看起來很整齊，但問題其實還在。"},{"label":"4. Conclusion","english":"Seen that way, high profit can mean strength, but by itself it does not prove health. Profit is a snapshot, not the whole film.","chinese":"從這個角度看，高利潤可以代表實力，但單靠它本身並不能證明企業健康。利潤像一張照片，而不是整部影片。"},{"label":"5. Idea 2","english":"Still, it would be wrong to say profit does not matter. In fact, strong profit becomes very meaningful when it is backed by the right fundamentals.","chinese":"不過，若因此說利潤不重要，那也不對。事實上，當高利潤背後有正確的基本面支撐時，它就非常有意義。"},{"label":"6. Explanation 2","english":"What matters, then, is the quality of the profit. If earnings are recurring, cash-backed, supported by loyal customers, sensible debt levels, and ongoing reinvestment, that is a far healthier picture. In that case, profit is not just a headline number; it is evidence of a business model with real muscle and staying power.","chinese":"因此，真正重要的是利潤的「質素」。如果盈利是可持續、能重複出現的，有現金支持的，而且建立在忠誠客戶、合理債務水平，以及持續再投資之上，那就會是一幅健康得多的圖像。在那種情況下，利潤就不只是一個標題數字，而是商業模式具備真正實力與持久力的證據。"},{"label":"7. Example","english":"Think of a firm with steady repeat business, healthy cash flow, disciplined spending, and enough room to invest in people and products. There, high profit is not smoke and mirrors; it usually reflects a business that is genuinely well run.","chinese":"可以想像一間公司，它擁有穩定的回頭生意、穩健的現金流、紀律良好的開支控制，並且仍有空間投資在人和產品上。在這種情況下，高利潤就不是障眼法，而通常反映這是一門真正被經營得很扎實的生意。"},{"label":"8. Conclusion 2","english":"All told, high profit is a clue, not a verdict. A healthy company is not merely one that makes money today, but one that can keep making money tomorrow without hollowing itself out.","chinese":"總結來說，高利潤是一條線索，但不是最終判決。真正健康的公司，不只是今天賺得到錢的公司，而是明天仍能持續賺錢，同時又不會把自己慢慢掏空的公司。"}],"vocabulary":[]},"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q10":{"exerciseId":"business-english-standard-response-book-1-q10","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=business-english-standard-response-book-1-q10","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"1. Response Part 1","english":"In my view, the biggest reason is that companies like the upside of innovation, but fear the downside of change.","chinese":"在我看來，最大的原因是，企業喜歡創新可能帶來的上升空間，卻害怕改變所附帶的下行風險。"},{"label":"2. Response Part 2","english":"Innovation sounds exciting in principle because it suggests growth, relevance, and competitive edge. However, in practice, real innovation is disruptive. It costs money, creates uncertainty, slows people down in the short term, and sometimes threatens the very systems that currently make the business profitable. That is why many firms praise innovation in meetings and slide decks, but become cautious the moment it starts touching budgets, power structures, or quarterly targets. Put simply, they want the fruit, but not always the shake of the tree.","chinese":"創新在原則上聽起來很吸引，因為它代表增長、競爭力，以及不被時代拋下。不過，真正的創新在實際上往往帶有破壞性。它要花錢、會帶來不確定性、短期內會拖慢節奏，有時甚至會威脅到目前正為公司賺錢的那套系統。這就是為甚麼很多企業在會議和簡報裡都大談創新，但一旦創新真的碰到預算、權力結構，或者季度業績目標時，就立刻變得保守。說白一點，他們想要果實，卻未必真的想承受搖樹的震動。"},{"label":"3. Response Part 3","english":"For example, a company may say it wants fresh ideas, but when a team proposes a new product, a different pricing model, or a faster digital process, the response is often, “Let’s study it further,” “This is not the right time,” or “What if it affects the core business?” On the surface, that sounds prudent. In reality, it can be a polished way of saying no.","chinese":"例如，一間公司可能口頭上說自己歡迎新想法，但當團隊真的提出新產品、不同的定價模式，或者更快的數碼流程時，常見回應往往是：「我們再研究一下」、「現在不是最合適的時機」，或者「如果影響到核心業務怎麼辦？」表面上，這些說法聽起來很審慎；但實際上，它有時只是比較包裝得體的拒絕。"},{"label":"4. Response Part 4","english":"So, very often, the gap between talk and action comes down to incentives: people are rewarded for protecting results, not for disturbing them.","chinese":"所以，很多時候，企業嘴上說創新、行動上卻保守，關鍵就在於激勵機制：人們得到獎勵，往往是因為守住業績，而不是因為打破現狀。"},{"label":"5. Response Part 5","english":"On top of that, large organisations tend to become conservative because size brings layers, and layers bring friction.","chinese":"除此之外，大型組織之所以容易變保守，還有一個原因：規模一大，層級就會變多；層級一多，摩擦也會跟著增加。"},{"label":"6. Response Part 6","english":"The more approvals, stakeholders, and reporting lines a company has, the harder it becomes to move with speed and conviction. New ideas are often watered down, delayed, or pushed into endless review. At the same time, middle managers may be especially cautious, because they are expected to deliver results without making visible mistakes. In that environment, safe choices look sensible, while bold choices start to feel career-limiting. In other words, the organisation may speak the language of innovation, but emotionally it is still wired for control.","chinese":"一間公司愈多審批、愈多持份者、愈多匯報線，想要快速而果斷地推動新想法就愈困難。很多新點子最後不是被稀釋，就是被拖延，或者被送進沒完沒了的檢討程序裡。與此同時，中層管理者往往特別謹慎，因為他們被要求交出成果，卻又不能犯下太明顯的錯誤。在這種環境下，安全選擇看起來就很合理，而大膽選擇反而開始像是在拿自己的職涯冒險。換句話說，整個組織嘴巴上講的是創新，但情感和本能上仍然是為了控制而設計的。"},{"label":"7. Response Part 7","english":"A good example would be a company that sets up an “innovation task force” but gives it little budget, little authority, and no real protection from short-term performance pressure. That team may produce ideas, but without backing, those ideas rarely leave the whiteboard. Innovation then becomes theatre rather than transformation.","chinese":"一個很好的例子，就是公司成立了一個所謂的「創新小組」，但給它的預算很少、權限很弱，也沒有真正替它擋住短期業績壓力。那個團隊也許能想出不少點子，但如果沒有真正支持，這些點子通常很難走出白板。到了最後，創新就變成一場表演，而不是真正的轉變。"},{"label":"8. Response Part 8","english":"Overall, I’d say companies often sound innovative because the market rewards that language, but they behave conservatively because their incentives, structures, and fears pull in the opposite direction. Real innovation only happens when a business is willing not just to praise new ideas, but to fund them, protect them, and live with the discomfort that comes with them.","chinese":"總結來說，我會說，企業之所以常常在口頭上很創新，是因為市場喜歡聽這種語言；但它們在行動上卻很保守，是因為激勵機制、組織結構，以及對風險的恐懼，把它們拉向了相反方向。真正的創新，只有在一間企業不只是稱讚新想法，而是願意為它們投資、保護它們，並且承受創新本身帶來的不舒服時，才真正會發生。"}],"vocabulary":[]},"dse-writing-2012-part-a":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2012-part-a","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2012-part-a","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-a/2012","paragraphs":[{"label":"Title","english":"Chasing Truth, Not Headlines","chinese":"追求真相，而不是追逐標題"},{"label":"The best part of my job","english":"The best part of my job","chinese":"我工作中最美好的部分"},{"label":"The best part of my job","english":"Reporting has taken me from subdivided flats to international summits. Yet the greatest privilege is not interviewing celebrities; it is earning ordinary people’s trust. When someone shares a story others have ignored, I can carry that voice beyond one room and, occasionally, prompt real change. A reporter has a front-row seat to history—and a duty to record it honestly.","chinese":"新聞報道工作曾帶我從劏房走到國際峰會。 然而，最大的榮幸並不是訪問名人，而是贏得普通人的信任。 當有人分享一個被其他人忽略的故事時，我能夠把那把聲音帶出一個房間之外，並偶爾促成真正的改變。 記者能夠坐在歷史前排見證時代，也有責任誠實地記錄它。"},{"label":"The biggest challenge I have ever faced in my job","english":"The biggest challenge I have ever faced in my job","chinese":"我工作中曾面對過的最大挑戰"},{"label":"The biggest challenge I have ever faced in my job","english":"While I was covering a devastating earthquake in Sichuan, aftershocks shook the ground beneath us. The danger was frightening; interviewing grieving families was harder. One mother held a dusty schoolbag and asked me to tell Hong Kong about her son. I checked every fact and let her speak in her own words, without asking intrusive questions. Only then did I understand that accuracy without humanity is not enough.","chinese":"當我報道四川一場嚴重地震時，餘震搖晃着我們腳下的土地。 危險令人恐懼；但訪問悲痛的家庭更加艱難。 一位母親拿着一個滿是塵土的書包，請我把她兒子的故事告訴香港。 我核實每一項事實，並讓她用自己的說話表達，而沒有提出冒犯性的問題。 直到那一刻，我才明白，只有準確而缺乏人情味是不足夠的。"},{"label":"My school days","english":"My school days","chinese":"我的求學時光"},{"label":"My school days","english":"My career began here, with the school magazine. My first article came back covered in red ink, but my English teacher wrote, “Keep asking why.” I did. Those words still guide every investigation.","chinese":"我的事業就是從這裏、從校刊開始的。 我第一篇文章被改得滿是紅筆痕跡，但我的英文老師寫下了：「Keep asking why.」 我照做了。 那些說話至今仍然指引着我的每一次調查。"},{"label":"A word to future reporters","english":"A word to future reporters","chinese":"給未來記者的一句話"},{"label":"A word to future reporters","english":"Stay curious, but verify before publishing. Above all, never turn another person’s pain into entertainment. A microphone can amplify a voice, but it is integrity that gives it value.","chinese":"保持好奇，但在發布之前必須核實。 最重要的是，永遠不要把別人的痛苦變成娛樂。 咪高峰可以放大一把聲音，但真正賦予它價值的，是誠信。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"chase truth, not headlines","chinese":"追求真相，而不是追逐標題"},{"english":"the best part of my job","chinese":"我工作中最美好的部分"},{"english":"reporting","chinese":"新聞報道工作"},{"english":"take someone from ... to ...","chinese":"帶某人由……走到……"},{"english":"subdivided flats","chinese":"劏房"},{"english":"international summits","chinese":"國際峰會"},{"english":"the greatest privilege","chinese":"最大的榮幸"},{"english":"interview celebrities","chinese":"訪問名人"},{"english":"earn someone's trust","chinese":"贏得某人的信任"},{"english":"ordinary people","chinese":"普通人"},{"english":"share a story","chinese":"分享一個故事"},{"english":"others have ignored","chinese":"其他人忽略了的"},{"english":"carry that voice beyond one room","chinese":"將那把聲音帶出一個房間之外"},{"english":"beyond one room","chinese":"超越一個房間的範圍"},{"english":"occasionally","chinese":"偶爾"},{"english":"prompt real change","chinese":"促成真正改變"},{"english":"have a front-row seat to history","chinese":"近距離見證歷史"},{"english":"a duty to","chinese":"有責任去……"},{"english":"record it honestly","chinese":"誠實地記錄它"},{"english":"the biggest challenge I have ever faced","chinese":"我曾面對過的最大挑戰"},{"english":"cover an earthquake","chinese":"採訪地震"},{"english":"devastating earthquake","chinese":"災情嚴重的地震"},{"english":"aftershocks","chinese":"餘震"},{"english":"shake the ground beneath us","chinese":"震動我們腳下的地面"},{"english":"beneath us","chinese":"在我們腳下"},{"english":"the danger was frightening","chinese":"危險令人恐懼"},{"english":"grieving families","chinese":"悲痛的家庭"},{"english":"hold a dusty schoolbag","chinese":"拿着一個滿是灰塵的書包"},{"english":"tell Hong Kong about","chinese":"向香港講述……"},{"english":"check every fact","chinese":"核實每一項事實"},{"english":"let someone speak","chinese":"讓某人發聲"},{"english":"in her own words","chinese":"用她自己的說話"},{"english":"intrusive questions","chinese":"冒犯私隱的問題"},{"english":"only then","chinese":"直到那時才"},{"english":"accuracy without humanity","chinese":"沒有人性的準確並不足夠"},{"english":"not enough","chinese":"並不足夠"},{"english":"school days","chinese":"學生時代"},{"english":"career began here","chinese":"事業從這裏開始"},{"english":"school magazine","chinese":"校刊"},{"english":"come back covered in red ink","chinese":"被紅筆改得滿篇都是"},{"english":"covered in red ink","chinese":"滿是紅筆批改"},{"english":"keep asking why","chinese":"不斷追問原因"},{"english":"guide every investigation","chinese":"指引每一次調查"},{"english":"investigation","chinese":"調查"},{"english":"a word to future reporters","chinese":"給未來記者的一句話"},{"english":"stay curious","chinese":"保持好奇心"},{"english":"verify before publishing","chinese":"發表前先核實"},{"english":"above all","chinese":"最重要的是"},{"english":"turn someone's pain into entertainment","chinese":"將他人的痛苦變成娛樂"},{"english":"microphone","chinese":"麥克風"},{"english":"amplify a voice","chinese":"放大一把聲音"},{"english":"integrity","chinese":"誠信；操守"},{"english":"give something value","chinese":"賦予……價值"}]},"dse-writing-2013-part-a":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2013-part-a","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2013-part-a","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-a/2013","paragraphs":[{"label":"Photo 1: “Chalkboard Dreams”","english":"Photo 1: “Chalkboard Dreams”","chinese":"照片一：「黑板上的夢想」"},{"label":"Photo 1: “Chalkboard Dreams”","english":"This photo features a concentrated young schoolgirl standing at a large blackboard, intently writing with a piece of chalk. It immediately transports me back to my primary school days, where every blank space on the board felt like an invitation to explore new ideas. The girl’s focused posture reminds me of the pure excitement I once felt whenever I was given the precious opportunity to stand in front of the class, sharing my original thoughts and practicing my handwriting. For me, this image symbolizes not only the innocence of childhood but also the boundless potential we as teenagers possess at a young age. It serves as a vivid reminder that every journey of learning, in fact, begins with a simple spark of curiosity, with an incentive as simple as a little chalk. Even now, I look at this photo to rekindle that sense of wonder and remind myself never to lose my love for discovering something new, and never cease thinking.","chinese":"這張照片呈現了一名專心致志的年輕女學生站在一塊大黑板前，正專注地用粉筆書寫。 它立刻把我帶回小學時光，那時黑板上的每一處空白位置，都像是在邀請我探索新的想法。 那女孩專注的姿態，令我想起昔日每當我獲得寶貴機會站在全班面前，分享自己的原創想法並練習書寫時，心中那份純粹的興奮。 對我而言，這張照片不但象徵童年的純真，也象徵我們作為青少年在年輕時所擁有的無限潛能。 它生動地提醒我，每一段學習旅程，其實都始於一點簡單的好奇心，也可以由一支小小的粉筆這樣簡單的推動力開始。 即使到了現在，我仍會看着這張照片，重新燃起那份驚奇感，並提醒自己永遠不要失去探索新事物的熱愛，也不要停止思考。"},{"label":"Photo 2: “Circle of Friendship”","english":"Photo 2: “Circle of Friendship”","chinese":"照片二：「友誼之圈」"},{"label":"Photo 2: “Circle of Friendship”","english":"In contrast, my second photo shows a tight circle of friends standing in a huddle with their hands joined at the focal point. It captures a heartwarming sense of unity and mutual support between the companions. Whenever I gaze at this snapshot, I recall how friendship empowers us to overcome obstacles we cannot tackle alone. These interlocked arms remind me of a project we once completed as a close-knit team, celebrating every small but significant victory, and encouraging one another through setbacks from life. That experience taught me the true value of trust, empathy, and collaboration. Today, this photo continues to inspire me to appreciate the people in my life, and to remain grateful for the unwavering support that friendship offers.","chinese":"相比之下，我的第二張照片展示了一群朋友緊密地圍成一圈站在一起，他們的手在畫面焦點處交疊。 它捕捉了朋友之間令人感到溫暖的團結感和互相支持。 每當我凝望這張照片時，我都會想起友誼如何賦予我們力量，去克服那些我們無法獨自應付的障礙。 這些交纏在一起的手臂，令我想起我們曾經作為一個緊密團隊完成的一項計劃；我們慶祝每一個細小卻重要的勝利，也在人生的挫折中互相鼓勵。 那次經歷教會了我信任、同理心和合作的真正價值。 直到今天，這張照片仍然激勵我珍惜生命中的人，並繼續感激友誼所帶來的堅定支持。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"Chalkboard Dreams","chinese":"黑板上的夢想"},{"english":"feature","chinese":"以……為主要內容；呈現"},{"english":"a concentrated young schoolgirl","chinese":"一名專心致志的年輕女學生"},{"english":"stand at a large blackboard","chinese":"站在一塊大黑板前"},{"english":"intently","chinese":"專注地"},{"english":"write with a piece of chalk","chinese":"用粉筆書寫"},{"english":"immediately transport someone back to","chinese":"立即把某人帶回……"},{"english":"primary school days","chinese":"小學時光"},{"english":"blank space","chinese":"空白位置"},{"english":"an invitation to","chinese":"一種……的邀請"},{"english":"explore new ideas","chinese":"探索新想法"},{"english":"focused posture","chinese":"專注的姿勢"},{"english":"remind someone of","chinese":"令某人想起……"},{"english":"pure excitement","chinese":"純粹的興奮"},{"english":"be given the precious opportunity to","chinese":"獲得寶貴機會去……"},{"english":"stand in front of the class","chinese":"站在全班面前"},{"english":"share my original thoughts","chinese":"分享自己的原創想法"},{"english":"practise my handwriting","chinese":"練習書法；練習書寫"},{"english":"symbolise not only…but also…","chinese":"不但象徵……亦象徵……"},{"english":"the innocence of childhood","chinese":"童年的純真"},{"english":"boundless potential","chinese":"無限潛能"},{"english":"possess at a young age","chinese":"年紀輕輕便擁有"},{"english":"serve as a vivid reminder that","chinese":"生動地提醒我們……"},{"english":"a journey of learning","chinese":"學習旅程"},{"english":"begin with","chinese":"由……開始"},{"english":"a simple spark of curiosity","chinese":"一點簡單的好奇心"},{"english":"something as simple as","chinese":"像……般簡單的東西"},{"english":"rekindle that sense of wonder","chinese":"重新燃起那份驚奇感"},{"english":"a sense of wonder","chinese":"驚奇感；對世界的好奇"},{"english":"never lose my love for","chinese":"永遠不要失去對……的熱愛"},{"english":"discover something new","chinese":"發現新事物"},{"english":"never stop thinking","chinese":"永遠不要停止思考"},{"english":"Circle of Friendship","chinese":"友誼之圈"},{"english":"in contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"a tight circle of friends","chinese":"一群緊密圍成一圈的朋友"},{"english":"stand in a huddle","chinese":"圍在一起站立"},{"english":"with their hands joined","chinese":"雙手合在一起"},{"english":"at the focal point","chinese":"在焦點位置"},{"english":"capture a heartwarming sense of","chinese":"捕捉到一種溫暖的……感覺"},{"english":"unity and mutual support","chinese":"團結與互相支持"},{"english":"between the companions","chinese":"同伴之間"},{"english":"gaze at this snapshot","chinese":"凝望這張照片"},{"english":"recall how","chinese":"想起……如何"},{"english":"empower someone to","chinese":"使某人有力量去……"},{"english":"overcome obstacles","chinese":"克服困難"},{"english":"tackle something alone","chinese":"獨自處理……"},{"english":"interlocked arms","chinese":"交疊相扣的手臂"},{"english":"close-knit team","chinese":"緊密合作的團隊"},{"english":"celebrate every small but significant victory","chinese":"慶祝每一個細小但重要的勝利"},{"english":"small but significant","chinese":"細小但重要的"},{"english":"encourage one another through","chinese":"在……中互相鼓勵"},{"english":"setbacks in life","chinese":"人生中的挫折"},{"english":"teach someone the true value of","chinese":"使某人明白……的真正價值"},{"english":"trust, empathy, and collaboration","chinese":"信任、同理心與合作"},{"english":"continue to inspire someone to","chinese":"繼續啟發某人去……"},{"english":"appreciate the people in my life","chinese":"珍惜生命中的人"},{"english":"remain grateful for","chinese":"對……一直心存感激"},{"english":"unwavering support","chinese":"堅定不移的支持"},{"english":"friendship offers","chinese":"友誼所帶來的……"}]},"dse-writing-2014-part-a":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2014-part-a","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2014-part-a","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-a/2014","paragraphs":[{"label":"Title","english":"Lucky Village: Where Tradition Meets Transformation","chinese":"幸運村：傳統與蛻變交匯之地"},{"label":"Background","english":"Located on the outskirts of Hong Kong, Lucky Village was once a peaceful farming community with just a handful of wooden huts and lush rice fields. Forty years ago, residents rose at sunrise to tend their crops and shared simple meals cooked over charcoal stoves. Electricity was scarce, so families often gathered by candlelight and passed down stories that united the community.","chinese":"Lucky Village 位於香港市郊，曾經是一個寧靜的農村社區，只有寥寥幾間木屋和一片片茂盛的稻田。 四十年前，居民日出而作，照料農作物，並分享用炭爐煮成的簡樸飯菜。 當時電力稀少，因此一家人經常在燭光下聚在一起，傳承凝聚社區的故事。"},{"label":"Transformation","english":"Everything changed in 1974, when a massive redevelopment project introduced modern roads, electricity, and piped water. Although many locals initially worried about losing their traditional lifestyle, better infrastructure brought exciting new opportunities. The village school expanded, and small businesses sprang up, allowing families to improve their quality of life and attract visitors from neighboring towns.","chinese":"1974 年，一項大型重建計劃引入了現代化道路、電力和自來水，一切從此改變 雖然許多本地居民最初擔心會失去傳統的生活方式，但更完善的基礎設施帶來了令人振奮的新機遇。 村內學校得以擴建，小型商店也紛紛興起，讓家庭能夠改善生活質素，並吸引來自鄰近城鎮的遊客。"},{"label":"Present Day","english":"Today, Lucky Village is famous for its vibrant Spring Festival, held every April to honor the village’s rich heritage. Thousands of tourists flock here to watch colorful parades, sample homemade pastries, and admire the centuries‐old banyan trees lining the main street. This unique blend of old and new has turned Lucky Village into a captivating destination for anyone seeking a glimpse of Hong Kong’s rural past—while still enjoying modern conveniences. Locals proudly carry on their cherished traditions, ensuring Lucky Village remains true to its name.","chinese":"如今，Lucky Village 以每年四月舉行、充滿活力的春季節慶聞名，藉此紀念村莊豐富的文化傳承。 成千上萬的遊客蜂擁而至，觀看色彩繽紛的巡遊、品嘗自家製糕點，並欣賞排列在大街兩旁、已有數百年歷史的榕樹。 這種新舊交融的獨特特色，令 Lucky Village 成為一個迷人的目的地，適合任何想一窺香港昔日鄉村面貌，同時又享受現代便利的人。 本地居民自豪地延續他們珍視的傳統，確保 Lucky Village 名副其實，繼續成為一個充滿福氣與魅力的地方。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"Where Tradition Meets Transformation","chinese":"傳統與蛻變交匯之地"},{"english":"located on the outskirts of","chinese":"位於……市郊"},{"english":"the outskirts of Hong Kong","chinese":"香港市郊"},{"english":"was once","chinese":"曾經是"},{"english":"a peaceful farming community","chinese":"寧靜的農村社區"},{"english":"a handful of","chinese":"少數；寥寥幾個"},{"english":"wooden huts","chinese":"木屋"},{"english":"lush rice fields","chinese":"茂盛的稻田"},{"english":"forty years ago","chinese":"四十年前"},{"english":"rise at sunrise","chinese":"日出時起床"},{"english":"tend their crops","chinese":"照料農作物"},{"english":"simple meals","chinese":"簡樸的飯菜"},{"english":"cooked over charcoal stoves","chinese":"用炭爐煮成"},{"english":"charcoal stoves","chinese":"炭爐"},{"english":"electricity was scarce","chinese":"電力供應不足"},{"english":"gather by candlelight","chinese":"在燭光下聚集"},{"english":"pass down stories","chinese":"傳承故事"},{"english":"unite the community","chinese":"凝聚社區"},{"english":"Everything changed in","chinese":"一切在……改變"},{"english":"a massive redevelopment project","chinese":"大型重建計劃"},{"english":"introduce modern roads","chinese":"引入現代道路"},{"english":"piped water","chinese":"自來水"},{"english":"many locals","chinese":"很多本地居民"},{"english":"initially worried about","chinese":"起初擔心"},{"english":"lose their traditional lifestyle","chinese":"失去傳統生活方式"},{"english":"better infrastructure","chinese":"更完善的基建"},{"english":"exciting new opportunities","chinese":"令人振奮的新機會"},{"english":"the village school expanded","chinese":"村校擴展"},{"english":"small businesses sprang up","chinese":"小商戶湧現"},{"english":"allow families to","chinese":"讓家庭能夠……"},{"english":"improve their quality of life","chinese":"改善生活質素"},{"english":"attract visitors from","chinese":"吸引來自……的遊客"},{"english":"neighboring towns","chinese":"鄰近城鎮"},{"english":"be famous for","chinese":"以……聞名"},{"english":"vibrant Spring Festival","chinese":"充滿活力的春季節慶"},{"english":"held every April","chinese":"每年四月舉行"},{"english":"honor the village's rich heritage","chinese":"表揚村莊豐富的文化傳承"},{"english":"rich heritage","chinese":"豐富的文化傳承"},{"english":"thousands of tourists","chinese":"數以千計的遊客"},{"english":"flock here","chinese":"蜂擁而至"},{"english":"colorful parades","chinese":"色彩繽紛的巡遊"},{"english":"sample homemade pastries","chinese":"品嘗自家製糕點"},{"english":"homemade pastries","chinese":"自家製糕點"},{"english":"admire the centuries-old banyan trees","chinese":"欣賞百年榕樹"},{"english":"centuries-old banyan trees","chinese":"百年榕樹"},{"english":"lining the main street","chinese":"沿着大街排列"},{"english":"a unique blend of old and new","chinese":"新舊交融的獨特結合"},{"english":"turn something into","chinese":"把……變成"},{"english":"a captivating destination","chinese":"迷人的旅遊目的地"},{"english":"anyone seeking","chinese":"任何尋找……的人"},{"english":"a glimpse of","chinese":"一瞥；短暫感受"},{"english":"Hong Kong's rural past","chinese":"香港昔日鄉郊面貌"},{"english":"while still enjoying","chinese":"同時仍然享受"},{"english":"modern conveniences","chinese":"現代化便利設施"},{"english":"proudly carry on","chinese":"自豪地延續"},{"english":"cherished traditions","chinese":"珍而重之的傳統"},{"english":"ensure something remains","chinese":"確保……保持"},{"english":"remain true to its name","chinese":"名副其實"}]},"dse-writing-2015-part-a-argument-against":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2015-part-a-argument-against","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2015-part-a-argument-against","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-a/2015","paragraphs":[{"label":"Salutation","english":"Dear Editor,","chinese":"編輯先生／女士："},{"label":"Introduction","english":"I am writing in response to the recent article in the Young Post suggesting that an 8:00 am start makes students tired and sleepy. As a secondary student, I agree that the early bell is part of the problem, but it is far from the whole story.","chinese":"本人寫信是為了回應《Young Post》最近一篇文章，該文章指出早上 8 時上課會令學生疲倦和昏昏欲睡。 作為一名中學生，我同意清晨的上課鐘聲是問題的一部分，但這遠遠不是全部原因。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Many students are exhausted not because they are lazy, but because their day does not end when school ends. After lessons, they rush to tutorials, activities and revision. By the time their homework is finished, it may already be late. Long commutes make matters worse, as some classmates leave home before sunrise, so breakfast is rushed and sleep is cut short. Screen time is another quiet culprit. A phone beside the pillow can turn “five minutes” into an hour, leaving the brain awake when the body should be resting.","chinese":"許多學生感到疲憊，並不是因為他們懶惰，而是因為他們的一天並不會在放學時結束。 下課後，他們趕去補習、參與活動和溫習。 當他們完成家課時，時間可能已經很晚。 漫長的通勤令情況更加嚴重，因為有些同學在日出前已經離家，所以早餐吃得匆忙，睡眠時間也被縮短。 螢幕時間是另一個不易察覺的元兇。 放在枕頭旁的手機，可以把「五分鐘」變成一小時，令身體本應休息時，大腦卻仍然清醒。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"A 9:00 am start would certainly help. It would give students a more humane morning and allow many to gain precious extra sleep. However, it would not solve the problem by itself. If schools simply push lessons later but keep the same workload, students may only go home later and sleep no earlier.","chinese":"上午 9 時上課當然會有幫助。 這會給學生一個更人性化的早晨，並讓許多人獲得寶貴的額外睡眠。 然而，它本身並不能解決問題。 如果學校只是把課堂推遲，卻維持相同的功課量，學生可能只會更晚回家，而不會更早入睡。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"Therefore, schools should consider a later start together with lighter homework, better timetable planning and education on healthy digital habits. Sleep is not a luxury, but the foundation of learning.","chinese":"因此，學校應該在考慮較遲上課的同時，也減少功課量、改善時間表規劃，並教育學生建立健康的數碼習慣。 睡眠不是奢侈品，而是學習的基礎。"},{"label":"Sign-off","english":"Yours faithfully,","chinese":"此致"},{"label":"Signature","english":"Chris Wong","chinese":"Chris Wong"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"Dear Editor","chinese":"編輯先生／女士"},{"english":"write in response to","chinese":"寫信回應……"},{"english":"recent article","chinese":"最近的文章"},{"english":"suggest that","chinese":"指出；認為"},{"english":"starting school at 8:00 a.m.","chinese":"早上八時上課"},{"english":"leave students drained and unfocused","chinese":"令學生精疲力竭、難以集中精神"},{"english":"while it is true that","chinese":"雖然……是真的"},{"english":"half-asleep","chinese":"半睡半醒；未完全清醒"},{"english":"the roots of","chinese":"……的根源"},{"english":"exhaustion","chinese":"疲憊；精疲力竭"},{"english":"go far deeper than","chinese":"遠比……深層"},{"english":"early morning routine","chinese":"早晨作息；早上上學安排"},{"english":"face overwhelming schedules","chinese":"面對繁重得令人吃不消的日程"},{"english":"overwhelming","chinese":"壓倒性的；令人吃不消的"},{"english":"juggle","chinese":"同時應付"},{"english":"after-school activities","chinese":"課後活動"},{"english":"heavy homework loads","chinese":"繁重的功課量"},{"english":"part-time jobs","chinese":"兼職工作"},{"english":"force someone to","chinese":"迫使某人……"},{"english":"stay up late","chinese":"熬夜"},{"english":"reduce essential sleeping hours","chinese":"減少必要睡眠時間"},{"english":"essential sleeping hours","chinese":"必要睡眠時間"},{"english":"moreover","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"modern teenagers","chinese":"現代青少年"},{"english":"electronic devices","chinese":"電子裝置"},{"english":"disrupt natural circadian rhythms","chinese":"擾亂自然生理時鐘"},{"english":"circadian rhythms","chinese":"生理時鐘；晝夜節律"},{"english":"make it harder to","chinese":"令……更加困難"},{"english":"fall asleep","chinese":"入睡"},{"english":"at a reasonable time","chinese":"在合理時間"},{"english":"moving the start time to","chinese":"把開始時間改至……"},{"english":"provide valuable extra rest","chinese":"提供寶貴的額外休息"},{"english":"valuable extra rest","chinese":"寶貴的額外休息"},{"english":"by no means","chinese":"絕不是"},{"english":"cure-all solution","chinese":"萬靈丹式的解決方法"},{"english":"clash with","chinese":"與……衝突"},{"english":"parents' work schedules","chinese":"父母的工作時間表"},{"english":"push extracurriculars further into the evening","chinese":"把課外活動推遲至更晚時間"},{"english":"extracurriculars","chinese":"課外活動"},{"english":"potentially","chinese":"有可能"},{"english":"perpetuate","chinese":"使……持續下去"},{"english":"the cycle of sleep deprivation","chinese":"睡眠不足的惡性循環"},{"english":"sleep deprivation","chinese":"睡眠不足"},{"english":"what truly matters is","chinese":"真正重要的是"},{"english":"time-management skills","chinese":"時間管理技巧"},{"english":"promote a healthier lifestyle","chinese":"推廣更健康的生活方式"},{"english":"healthier lifestyle","chinese":"更健康的生活方式"},{"english":"such as","chinese":"例如"},{"english":"limit late-night screen time","chinese":"限制深夜使用電子屏幕的時間"},{"english":"late-night screen time","chinese":"深夜使用電子屏幕的時間"},{"english":"ultimately","chinese":"最終；歸根究底"},{"english":"address the issue of","chinese":"處理……問題"},{"english":"student tiredness","chinese":"學生疲倦問題"},{"english":"real progress demands","chinese":"真正進展需要……"},{"english":"holistic approach","chinese":"全面的方法"},{"english":"involve parents, schools, and students alike","chinese":"涉及家長、學校和學生各方"},{"english":"alike","chinese":"同樣地；都"},{"english":"Yours faithfully","chinese":"謹啟（正式信件結尾）"},{"english":"tired and sleepy","chinese":"疲倦和眼睏"},{"english":"as a secondary student","chinese":"作為一名中學生"},{"english":"the early bell","chinese":"早響的上課鐘"},{"english":"be part of the problem","chinese":"是問題的一部分"},{"english":"far from the whole story","chinese":"遠非問題的全部"},{"english":"be exhausted","chinese":"筋疲力盡"},{"english":"not because…, but because…","chinese":"不是因為……，而是因為……"},{"english":"their day does not end","chinese":"他們的一天並未結束"},{"english":"when school ends","chinese":"放學時"},{"english":"rush to","chinese":"匆忙趕去……"},{"english":"tutorials, activities and revision","chinese":"補習、活動和溫習"},{"english":"by the time","chinese":"到……的時候"},{"english":"homework is finished","chinese":"功課完成"},{"english":"it may already be late","chinese":"可能已經很晚"},{"english":"long commutes","chinese":"長途通勤"},{"english":"make matters worse","chinese":"令情況更糟"},{"english":"leave home before sunrise","chinese":"日出前離家"},{"english":"breakfast is rushed","chinese":"匆忙吃早餐"},{"english":"sleep is cut short","chinese":"睡眠時間被縮短"},{"english":"screen time","chinese":"使用電子屏幕的時間"},{"english":"a quiet culprit","chinese":"隱形元兇"},{"english":"beside the pillow","chinese":"放在枕邊"},{"english":"turn “five minutes” into an hour","chinese":"把「五分鐘」變成一小時"},{"english":"leave the brain awake","chinese":"令大腦保持清醒"},{"english":"when the body should be resting","chinese":"當身體本應休息時"},{"english":"would certainly help","chinese":"一定會有幫助"},{"english":"a more humane morning","chinese":"較人性化的早上安排"},{"english":"allow someone to","chinese":"讓某人能夠"},{"english":"gain precious extra sleep","chinese":"獲得寶貴的額外睡眠"},{"english":"solve the problem by itself","chinese":"單靠本身解決問題"},{"english":"push lessons later","chinese":"把課堂推遲"},{"english":"keep the same workload","chinese":"維持相同功課量"},{"english":"go home later","chinese":"更遲回家"},{"english":"sleep no earlier","chinese":"不會更早睡"},{"english":"therefore","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"consider a later start","chinese":"考慮較遲上課"},{"english":"together with","chinese":"連同；與……一起"},{"english":"lighter homework","chinese":"較少功課"},{"english":"better timetable planning","chinese":"更好的時間表規劃"},{"english":"education on healthy digital habits","chinese":"健康數碼習慣教育"},{"english":"healthy digital habits","chinese":"健康數碼習慣"},{"english":"not a luxury, but…","chinese":"不是奢侈品，而是……"},{"english":"the foundation of learning","chinese":"學習的基礎"}]},"dse-writing-2015-part-a-argument-for":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2015-part-a-argument-for","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2015-part-a-argument-for","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-a/2015","paragraphs":[{"label":"Salutation","english":"Dear Editor,","chinese":"編輯先生／女士："},{"label":"Introduction","english":"I am writing in response to the recent article suggesting that starting school at 8:00 a.m. leaves students drained and unfocused. While it is true that many teenagers arrive half-asleep, the roots of their exhaustion go far deeper than just an early morning routine.","chinese":"本人寫信是為了回應最近一篇文章，該文章指出早上 8 時上課會令學生精疲力竭、難以集中精神。 雖然許多青少年半睡半醒地到校確實是事實，但他們疲倦的根源遠不只是早上的作息安排。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Firstly, most students face overwhelming schedules, juggling after-school activities, heavy homework loads, and even part-time jobs. This often forces them to stay up late, reducing essential sleeping hours. Moreover, modern teenagers frequently use electronic devices at night, which disrupts their natural circadian rhythms and makes it harder to fall asleep at a reasonable time.","chinese":"首先，大多數學生都面對令人吃不消的時間表，要同時應付課後活動、沉重的功課量，甚至兼職工作。 這往往迫使他們熬夜，從而減少必要的睡眠時間。 此外，現代青少年經常在晚上使用電子裝置，這會擾亂他們自然的生理時鐘，令他們更難在合理時間入睡。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Although moving the start time to 9:00 a.m. may provide valuable extra rest, it is by no means a cure-all solution. A later start could clash with parents’ work schedules and push extracurriculars further into the evening, potentially perpetuating the cycle of sleep deprivation. What truly matters is teaching time-management skills and promoting a healthier lifestyle, such as limiting late-night screen time.","chinese":"雖然把上課時間延遲至上午 9 時，可能會提供寶貴的額外休息時間，但它絕不是萬能的解決方法。 較遲上課可能會與家長的工作時間表產生衝突，並把課外活動進一步推遲至晚上，從而可能延續睡眠不足的循環。 真正重要的是教授時間管理技巧，並推廣更健康的生活方式，例如限制深夜使用螢幕的時間。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"Ultimately, while a later school start can help address the issue of student tiredness, real progress demands a holistic approach, involving parents, schools, and students alike.","chinese":"最終，雖然較遲開始上課能夠幫助處理學生疲倦的問題，但真正的進展需要一個全面的方法，並讓家長、學校和學生共同參與。"},{"label":"Sign-off","english":"Yours faithfully,","chinese":"此致"},{"label":"Signature","english":"Chris Wong","chinese":"Chris Wong"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"Dear Editor","chinese":"編輯先生／女士"},{"english":"write in response to","chinese":"寫信回應……"},{"english":"recent article","chinese":"最近的文章"},{"english":"suggest that","chinese":"指出；認為"},{"english":"starting school at 8:00 a.m.","chinese":"早上八時上課"},{"english":"leave students drained and unfocused","chinese":"令學生精疲力竭、難以集中精神"},{"english":"while it is true that","chinese":"雖然……是真的"},{"english":"half-asleep","chinese":"半睡半醒；未完全清醒"},{"english":"the roots of","chinese":"……的根源"},{"english":"exhaustion","chinese":"疲憊；精疲力竭"},{"english":"go far deeper than","chinese":"遠比……深層"},{"english":"early morning routine","chinese":"早晨作息；早上上學安排"},{"english":"face overwhelming schedules","chinese":"面對繁重得令人吃不消的日程"},{"english":"overwhelming","chinese":"壓倒性的；令人吃不消的"},{"english":"juggle","chinese":"同時應付"},{"english":"after-school activities","chinese":"課後活動"},{"english":"heavy homework loads","chinese":"繁重的功課量"},{"english":"part-time jobs","chinese":"兼職工作"},{"english":"force someone to","chinese":"迫使某人……"},{"english":"stay up late","chinese":"熬夜"},{"english":"reduce essential sleeping hours","chinese":"減少必要睡眠時間"},{"english":"essential sleeping hours","chinese":"必要睡眠時間"},{"english":"moreover","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"modern teenagers","chinese":"現代青少年"},{"english":"electronic devices","chinese":"電子裝置"},{"english":"disrupt natural circadian rhythms","chinese":"擾亂自然生理時鐘"},{"english":"circadian rhythms","chinese":"生理時鐘；晝夜節律"},{"english":"make it harder to","chinese":"令……更加困難"},{"english":"fall asleep","chinese":"入睡"},{"english":"at a reasonable time","chinese":"在合理時間"},{"english":"moving the start time to","chinese":"把開始時間改至……"},{"english":"provide valuable extra rest","chinese":"提供寶貴的額外休息"},{"english":"valuable extra rest","chinese":"寶貴的額外休息"},{"english":"by no means","chinese":"絕不是"},{"english":"cure-all solution","chinese":"萬靈丹式的解決方法"},{"english":"clash with","chinese":"與……衝突"},{"english":"parents' work schedules","chinese":"父母的工作時間表"},{"english":"push extracurriculars further into the evening","chinese":"把課外活動推遲至更晚時間"},{"english":"extracurriculars","chinese":"課外活動"},{"english":"potentially","chinese":"有可能"},{"english":"perpetuate","chinese":"使……持續下去"},{"english":"the cycle of sleep deprivation","chinese":"睡眠不足的惡性循環"},{"english":"sleep deprivation","chinese":"睡眠不足"},{"english":"what truly matters is","chinese":"真正重要的是"},{"english":"time-management skills","chinese":"時間管理技巧"},{"english":"promote a healthier lifestyle","chinese":"推廣更健康的生活方式"},{"english":"healthier lifestyle","chinese":"更健康的生活方式"},{"english":"such as","chinese":"例如"},{"english":"limit late-night screen time","chinese":"限制深夜使用電子屏幕的時間"},{"english":"late-night screen time","chinese":"深夜使用電子屏幕的時間"},{"english":"ultimately","chinese":"最終；歸根究底"},{"english":"address the issue of","chinese":"處理……問題"},{"english":"student tiredness","chinese":"學生疲倦問題"},{"english":"real progress demands","chinese":"真正進展需要……"},{"english":"holistic approach","chinese":"全面的方法"},{"english":"involve parents, schools, and students alike","chinese":"涉及家長、學校和學生各方"},{"english":"alike","chinese":"同樣地；都"},{"english":"Yours faithfully","chinese":"謹啟（正式信件結尾）"},{"english":"tired and sleepy","chinese":"疲倦和眼睏"},{"english":"as a secondary student","chinese":"作為一名中學生"},{"english":"the early bell","chinese":"早響的上課鐘"},{"english":"be part of the problem","chinese":"是問題的一部分"},{"english":"far from the whole story","chinese":"遠非問題的全部"},{"english":"be exhausted","chinese":"筋疲力盡"},{"english":"not because…, but because…","chinese":"不是因為……，而是因為……"},{"english":"their day does not end","chinese":"他們的一天並未結束"},{"english":"when school ends","chinese":"放學時"},{"english":"rush to","chinese":"匆忙趕去……"},{"english":"tutorials, activities and revision","chinese":"補習、活動和溫習"},{"english":"by the time","chinese":"到……的時候"},{"english":"homework is finished","chinese":"功課完成"},{"english":"it may already be late","chinese":"可能已經很晚"},{"english":"long commutes","chinese":"長途通勤"},{"english":"make matters worse","chinese":"令情況更糟"},{"english":"leave home before sunrise","chinese":"日出前離家"},{"english":"breakfast is rushed","chinese":"匆忙吃早餐"},{"english":"sleep is cut short","chinese":"睡眠時間被縮短"},{"english":"screen time","chinese":"使用電子屏幕的時間"},{"english":"a quiet culprit","chinese":"隱形元兇"},{"english":"beside the pillow","chinese":"放在枕邊"},{"english":"turn “five minutes” into an hour","chinese":"把「五分鐘」變成一小時"},{"english":"leave the brain awake","chinese":"令大腦保持清醒"},{"english":"when the body should be resting","chinese":"當身體本應休息時"},{"english":"would certainly help","chinese":"一定會有幫助"},{"english":"a more humane morning","chinese":"較人性化的早上安排"},{"english":"allow someone to","chinese":"讓某人能夠"},{"english":"gain precious extra sleep","chinese":"獲得寶貴的額外睡眠"},{"english":"solve the problem by itself","chinese":"單靠本身解決問題"},{"english":"push lessons later","chinese":"把課堂推遲"},{"english":"keep the same workload","chinese":"維持相同功課量"},{"english":"go home later","chinese":"更遲回家"},{"english":"sleep no earlier","chinese":"不會更早睡"},{"english":"therefore","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"consider a later start","chinese":"考慮較遲上課"},{"english":"together with","chinese":"連同；與……一起"},{"english":"lighter homework","chinese":"較少功課"},{"english":"better timetable planning","chinese":"更好的時間表規劃"},{"english":"education on healthy digital habits","chinese":"健康數碼習慣教育"},{"english":"healthy digital habits","chinese":"健康數碼習慣"},{"english":"not a luxury, but…","chinese":"不是奢侈品，而是……"},{"english":"the foundation of learning","chinese":"學習的基礎"}]},"dse-writing-2016-part-a":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2016-part-a","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2016-part-a","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-a/2016","paragraphs":[{"label":"Advice on School Rules","english":"First, please take school rules seriously. Rules are not there to make your school life dull or restrictive. Rather, they are there to make sure everyone can learn in a safe and respectful environment. When you arrive on time, wear your uniform properly, keep the campus clean and use your phone responsibly, you are showing respect not only for the school, but also for the people around you. These habits may seem small at first, but over time, they assist you to become more disciplined and dependable. After all, students who can manage themselves well are more likely to make the most of every opportunity here.","chinese":"首先，請認真看待校規。 校規的存在，並不是為了令你的校園生活變得沉悶或受到束縛。 相反，校規是為了確保每個人都能在安全而互相尊重的環境中學習。 當你準時到校、正確穿著校服、保持校園清潔，並負責任地使用手機時，你所展現的尊重不只是對學校的尊重，也是對身邊人的尊重。 這些習慣一開始或許看似微小，但長遠而言，它們會幫助你變得更自律，也更值得信賴。 畢竟，能夠好好管理自己的學生，更有可能充分把握這裏遇到的每一個機會"},{"label":"Advice on Relationships","english":"At the same time, school life is never just about grades. The friends you make, the teachers you learn from and the people you meet in different activities will shape your experience in important ways. Be willing to listen, even when others see things differently. If you make a mistake, apologise sincerely; If someone looks lost or nervous, offer a hand, because a friendly word at the right moment may mean more than you realise.","chinese":"同時，校園生活從來不只是關於成績。 你結交的朋友、向其學習的老師，以及在不同活動中遇到的人，都會以重要的方式塑造你的校園經歷。 即使別人的看法與你不同，也要願意聆聽。 如果你犯了錯，請真誠道歉；如果有人看起來迷惘或緊張，請伸出援手，因為在適當時候一句友善的說話，可能比你想像中更有意義。"},{"label":"Closing","english":"As you begin this new chapter, I sincerely hope you will see our school not only as a place to study, but as a community where you can grow with confidence. I wish you all a happy and meaningful school year. Thank you.","chinese":"當你開始這個新篇章時，我衷心希望你不只把我們的學校視為一個學習的地方，也把它看作一個能讓你自信成長的社群。 我祝願大家度過一個愉快而有意義的學年。 謝謝大家。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"take school rules seriously","chinese":"認真看待校規"},{"english":"school rules","chinese":"校規"},{"english":"be not there to","chinese":"並不是為了……而存在"},{"english":"make your school life dull","chinese":"令你的校園生活沉悶"},{"english":"restrictive","chinese":"限制多的；束縛人的"},{"english":"rather","chinese":"相反；反而"},{"english":"make sure","chinese":"確保"},{"english":"safe and respectful environment","chinese":"安全而互相尊重的環境"},{"english":"arrive on time","chinese":"準時到達"},{"english":"wear your uniform properly","chinese":"整齊穿着校服"},{"english":"keep the campus clean","chinese":"保持校園清潔"},{"english":"use your phone responsibly","chinese":"負責任地使用電話"},{"english":"show respect for","chinese":"表示對……的尊重"},{"english":"not only for..., but also for...","chinese":"不但對……，也對……"},{"english":"the people around you","chinese":"你身邊的人"},{"english":"seem small at first","chinese":"起初看似微不足道"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨着時間過去"},{"english":"help you become","chinese":"幫助你變得……"},{"english":"more disciplined","chinese":"更自律"},{"english":"dependable","chinese":"可靠的"},{"english":"after all","chinese":"畢竟"},{"english":"manage themselves well","chinese":"好好管理自己"},{"english":"be more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"make the most of","chinese":"充分利用"},{"english":"every opportunity","chinese":"每一個機會"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"與此同時"},{"english":"school life","chinese":"校園生活"},{"english":"be never just about","chinese":"從來不只是關於……"},{"english":"grades","chinese":"成績"},{"english":"the friends you make","chinese":"你結交的朋友"},{"english":"the teachers you learn from","chinese":"你向其學習的老師"},{"english":"people you meet","chinese":"你遇到的人"},{"english":"in different activities","chinese":"在不同活動中"},{"english":"shape your experience","chinese":"塑你的經歷"},{"english":"in important ways","chinese":"以重要的方式"},{"english":"be willing to","chinese":"願意去……"},{"english":"listen","chinese":"聆聽"},{"english":"see things differently","chinese":"有不同看法"},{"english":"make a mistake","chinese":"犯錯"},{"english":"apologise sincerely","chinese":"真誠道歉"},{"english":"look lost or nervous","chinese":"看起來迷惘或緊張"},{"english":"offer a hand","chinese":"伸出援手"},{"english":"a friendly word","chinese":"一句友善的說話"},{"english":"at the right moment","chinese":"在適當時候"},{"english":"mean more than you realise","chinese":"比你想像中更有意義"},{"english":"begin this new chapter","chinese":"開始這個新篇章"},{"english":"sincerely hope","chinese":"衷心希望"},{"english":"not only as..., but as...","chinese":"不只視為……，而是視為……"},{"english":"a place to study","chinese":"學習的地方"},{"english":"a community where","chinese":"一個讓你……的群體"},{"english":"grow with confidence","chinese":"自信地成長"},{"english":"a happy and meaningful school year","chinese":"快樂而有意義的學年"},{"english":"thank you","chinese":"謝謝"}]},"dse-writing-2017-part-a":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2017-part-a","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2017-part-a","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-a/2017","paragraphs":[{"label":"Salutation","english":"Dear Ms Lee,","chinese":"李女士鈞鑒："},{"label":"Salutation","english":"I hope this letter finds you well. As Chairperson of the Social Service Club, I would like to propose a novel project to strengthen our school’s relationship with the community, particularly with Evergreen Elderly Home. Instead of reading sessions or technology workshops, we wish to implement a weekly “Taste of Traditions” cooking program.","chinese":"祝安。 作為社會服務學會主席，我希望提出一個新穎的項目，以加強本校與社區的關係，尤其是與 Evergreen Elderly Home 的聯繫。 我們希望推行一個每週舉行的「Taste of Traditions」烹飪活動，而不是舉辦閱讀活動或科技工作坊。"},{"label":"Project Details","english":"During each session, our student volunteers and the elderly residents will come together to cook simple, culturally significant dishes such as handmade dumplings or traditional desserts. By pairing each student with a senior “cooking mentor,” we can provide ample one-on-one interaction, enabling both parties to share skills and family recipes while exchanging stories behind each dish. These sessions will culminate in a mini-tasting event, where participants can appreciate one another’s creations and celebrate cultural diversity.","chinese":"在每一節活動中，我們的學生義工和長者院友將會聚在一起，烹調一些簡單而具有文化意義的菜式，例如手製餃子或傳統甜品。 透過把每位學生與一位長者「烹飪導師」配對，我們可以提供充足的一對一互動機會，讓雙方分享技巧和家傳食譜，同時交流每道菜背後的故事。 這些活動將以一個小型試食活動作結，讓參加者欣賞彼此的作品，並慶祝文化多樣性。"},{"label":"Benefits","english":"I firmly believe that “Taste of Traditions” will benefit Evergreen Elderly Home by enhancing its residents’ sense of purpose and belonging, as they pass on cherished knowledge. At the same time, our students will broaden their culinary horizons and gain deeper respect for older generations. Through this collaborative and creative atmosphere, we can forge meaningful bonds and enrich everyone’s overall well-being.","chinese":"我堅信，「Taste of Traditions」將會令 Evergreen Elderly Home 受益，因為長者院友在傳承珍貴知識的過程中，能夠提升自己的目標感和歸屬感。 與此同時，我們的學生將能擴闊自己的烹飪視野，並對年長一輩產生更深的尊重。 透過這種協作而富創意的氛圍，我們可以建立有意義的聯繫，並提升每個人的整體福祉。"},{"label":"Closing","english":"Thank you for considering my proposal, and please feel free to contact me should you have any questions.","chinese":"感謝您考慮我的建議；如有任何問題，請隨時與我聯絡。"},{"label":"Closing","english":"Yours sincerely,","chinese":"謹啟"},{"label":"Closing","english":"Chris Wong","chinese":"Chris Wong"},{"label":"Closing","english":"Chairperson, Social Service Club","chinese":"社會服務學會主席"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"Dear Ms Lee","chinese":"李女士鈞鑒"},{"english":"I hope this letter finds you well","chinese":"祝安；希望你一切安好"},{"english":"Chairperson of","chinese":"……主席"},{"english":"Social Service Club","chinese":"社會服務學會"},{"english":"would like to propose","chinese":"希望提出"},{"english":"novel project","chinese":"新穎的項目"},{"english":"strengthen our school's relationship with","chinese":"加強我們學校與……的關係"},{"english":"the community","chinese":"社區"},{"english":"particularly with","chinese":"尤其是與……"},{"english":"Evergreen Elderly Home","chinese":"Evergreen Elderly Home"},{"english":"instead of","chinese":"而不是"},{"english":"reading sessions","chinese":"閱讀活動"},{"english":"technology workshops","chinese":"科技工作坊"},{"english":"wish to implement","chinese":"希望推行"},{"english":"weekly cooking programme","chinese":"每週烹飪活動"},{"english":"Taste of Traditions","chinese":"Taste of Traditions（傳統滋味）"},{"english":"during each session","chinese":"在每節活動中"},{"english":"student volunteers","chinese":"學生義工"},{"english":"elderly residents","chinese":"長者院友"},{"english":"come together to","chinese":"聚在一起去……"},{"english":"culturally significant dishes","chinese":"具有文化意義的菜式"},{"english":"handmade dumplings","chinese":"手製餃子"},{"english":"traditional desserts","chinese":"傳統甜品"},{"english":"pair each student with","chinese":"將每名學生與……配對"},{"english":"senior cooking mentor","chinese":"長者烹飪導師"},{"english":"provide ample interaction","chinese":"提供充足互動"},{"english":"one-on-one interaction","chinese":"一對一互動"},{"english":"enabling both parties to","chinese":"讓雙方能夠……"},{"english":"both parties","chinese":"雙方"},{"english":"share skills","chinese":"分享技能"},{"english":"family recipes","chinese":"家傳食譜"},{"english":"exchange stories behind each dish","chinese":"交流每道菜背後的故事"},{"english":"culminate in","chinese":"以……作結"},{"english":"mini-tasting event","chinese":"小型試食活動"},{"english":"appreciate one another's creations","chinese":"欣賞彼此的作品"},{"english":"celebrate cultural diversity","chinese":"慶祝文化多元"},{"english":"firmly believe that","chinese":"堅信"},{"english":"benefit","chinese":"使……受益"},{"english":"enhance someone's sense of purpose","chinese":"提升某人的人生目標感"},{"english":"sense of belonging","chinese":"歸屬感"},{"english":"pass on cherished knowledge","chinese":"傳承珍貴知識"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"與此同時"},{"english":"broaden their culinary horizons","chinese":"擴闊烹飪視野"},{"english":"gain deeper respect for","chinese":"對……有更深尊重"},{"english":"older generations","chinese":"老一輩"},{"english":"collaborative and creative atmosphere","chinese":"協作而富創意的氣氛"},{"english":"forge meaningful bonds","chinese":"建立有意義的連繫"},{"english":"enrich everyone's overall well-being","chinese":"提升每個人的整體身心健康"},{"english":"thank you for considering","chinese":"感謝你考慮……"},{"english":"please feel free to","chinese":"歡迎隨時……"},{"english":"should you have any questions","chinese":"如有任何問題"},{"english":"Yours sincerely","chinese":"謹啟"},{"english":"Chairperson, Social Service Club","chinese":"社會服務學會主席"}]},"dse-writing-2018-part-a":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2018-part-a","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2018-part-a","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-a/2018","paragraphs":[{"label":"Salutation","english":"Dear Parents/Carers,","chinese":"各位家長／照顧者："},{"label":"Salutation","english":"I hope this letter finds you well.","chinese":"展信安好。"},{"label":"Introduction","english":"I am writing to inform you about an exciting school trip for Class 6A, which will be held next month. We will be visiting sky100 Hong Kong Observation Deck, located on the 100th floor of the International Commerce Centre (ICC) in West Kowloon. This is the highest indoor observation deck in the city, and our main goal of the school outing is to broaden students’ horizons by showing them Hong Kong’s spectacular skyline from an entirely new perspective.","chinese":"本人寫信是為了通知各位有關 6A 班下月舉行的一次精彩學校旅行。 我們將參觀位於西九龍環球貿易廣場（ICC）100 樓的 sky100 香港觀景台。 這是全城最高的室內觀景台，而是次學校外出的主要目標，是透過讓學生從一個全新的角度欣賞香港壯麗的天際線，從而擴闊他們的視野。"},{"label":"Trip Details","english":"With respect to the details of the school trip, we will first depart from the school by coach at 9:00 a.m. and shall be dismissed at 4:00 p.m. The entrance fee is HKD 150, and the transportation cost will be HKD 20 per student. Students are advised to wear comfortable and casual outfits and bring a small backpack for personal belongings. We will have lunch together at a nearby restaurant; however, those with special dietary requirements are welcome to pack their own meals. After lunch, there will be a short debriefing session, during which students will work in groups to discuss their observations and gain insights into Hong Kong’s architecture.","chinese":"關於是次學校旅行的詳情，我們將首先於上午 9 時乘坐旅遊巴從學校出發，並於下午 4 時解散。 入場費為 HKD 150，而每位學生的交通費為 HKD 20。 學生宜穿著舒適的便服，並攜帶一個小背包放置個人物品。 我們將在附近一間餐廳一同用膳；然而，如學生有特殊飲食需要，亦歡迎自行攜帶午餐。 午膳後，學生將參與一個簡短的匯報環節，期間他們會分組討論自己的觀察，並加深對香港建築的理解。"},{"label":"Action Required","english":"To proceed, please complete and return the permission slip attached in the letter. Should you have any questions or concerns, please do not hesitate to contact me at the school office. Thank you for your cooperation, and I look forward to an enriching and memorable trip.","chinese":"為便安排，請填妥並交回本信所附的同意書。 如各位有任何問題或疑慮，請隨時透過學校辦公室與本人聯絡。 感謝各位的合作，本人期待這次旅程能夠充實而難忘。"},{"label":"Sign-off","english":"Yours sincerely,","chinese":"此致"},{"label":"Sign-off","english":"Chris Wong","chinese":"Chris Wong"},{"label":"Sign-off","english":"Class Teacher of 6A","chinese":"6A 班班主任"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"Dear Parents/Carers","chinese":"親愛的家長／照顧者"},{"english":"I hope this letter finds you well","chinese":"希望你們一切安好"},{"english":"I am writing to inform you about","chinese":"現寫信通知你們有關……"},{"english":"an exciting school trip","chinese":"一次令人期待的學校旅行"},{"english":"be held next month","chinese":"將於下月舉行"},{"english":"be visiting","chinese":"將會參觀"},{"english":"sky100 Hong Kong Observation Deck","chinese":"香港天際100觀景台"},{"english":"be located on","chinese":"位於……"},{"english":"the 100th floor of","chinese":"……的一百樓"},{"english":"International Commerce Centre","chinese":"環球貿易廣場"},{"english":"West Kowloon","chinese":"西九龍"},{"english":"indoor observation deck","chinese":"室內觀景台"},{"english":"the highest indoor observation deck","chinese":"最高的室內觀景台"},{"english":"main goal","chinese":"主要目的"},{"english":"school outing","chinese":"學校郊遊；學校旅行"},{"english":"broaden students' horizons","chinese":"擴闊學生的視野"},{"english":"Hong Kong's spectacular skyline","chinese":"香港壯麗的天際線"},{"english":"from an entirely new perspective","chinese":"從全新的角度"},{"english":"with respect to","chinese":"關於……"},{"english":"details of the school trip","chinese":"學校旅行詳情"},{"english":"depart from the school","chinese":"從學校出發"},{"english":"by coach","chinese":"乘旅遊巴"},{"english":"at 9:00 a.m.","chinese":"上午九時"},{"english":"be dismissed at","chinese":"於……解散"},{"english":"entrance fee","chinese":"入場費"},{"english":"transportation cost","chinese":"交通費"},{"english":"per student","chinese":"每名學生"},{"english":"be advised to","chinese":"建議……"},{"english":"wear comfortable and casual clothes","chinese":"穿着舒適便服"},{"english":"comfortable and casual clothes","chinese":"舒適便服"},{"english":"bring a small backpack","chinese":"帶備小背囊"},{"english":"personal belongings","chinese":"個人物品"},{"english":"have lunch together","chinese":"一起用膳"},{"english":"nearby restaurant","chinese":"附近餐廳"},{"english":"special dietary requirements","chinese":"特別飲食需要"},{"english":"be welcome to","chinese":"歡迎……"},{"english":"pack their own meals","chinese":"自備飯餐"},{"english":"after lunch","chinese":"午膳後"},{"english":"debriefing session","chinese":"總結環節；匯報環節"},{"english":"during which","chinese":"在此期間"},{"english":"work in groups","chinese":"分組合作"},{"english":"discuss their observations","chinese":"討論他們的觀察"},{"english":"gain insights into","chinese":"深入了解……"},{"english":"Hong Kong's architecture","chinese":"香港建築"},{"english":"to proceed","chinese":"如要參加；為了辦理相關安排"},{"english":"complete and return","chinese":"填妥並交回"},{"english":"permission slip","chinese":"回條；同意書"},{"english":"attached to the letter","chinese":"附於信件內"},{"english":"Should you have any questions or concerns","chinese":"如有任何疑問或關注"},{"english":"questions or concerns","chinese":"疑問或關注"},{"english":"please do not hesitate to","chinese":"請隨時……"},{"english":"contact me at the school office","chinese":"透過學校辦公室聯絡我"},{"english":"Thank you for your cooperation","chinese":"感謝你們的合作"},{"english":"look forward to","chinese":"期待"},{"english":"an enriching and memorable trip","chinese":"一次充實而難忘的旅程"},{"english":"Yours sincerely","chinese":"此致"},{"english":"Class Teacher of 6A","chinese":"6A班主任"}]},"dse-writing-2019-part-a":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2019-part-a","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2019-part-a","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-a/2019","paragraphs":[{"label":"Title","english":"Yearbook Entry: Class 6C – Reflections","chinese":"年刊文章：6C 班回顧"},{"label":"1.1: ACADEMIC LIFE","english":"Looking back on my years at Kowloon Secondary School, one subject that truly captivated me was Biology. Delving into microscopic worlds and conducting hands‐on experiments in the lab never ceased to amaze me. Although memorizing complicated processes and Latin names could be daunting, that sense of challenge spurred me to push my limits and achieve more than I ever thought possible. To this day, I still recall how exhilarating it felt to unravel the mysteries of life—from cells dividing under the microscope to analyzing blood samples during practical sessions.","chinese":"回顧我在九龍中學的歲月，其中一科真正令我著迷的是生物。 探索微觀世界，以及在實驗室親手進行實驗，總是令我驚嘆不已。 雖然記憶複雜的過程和拉丁名稱有時令人卻步，但那份挑戰感推動我突破自己的極限，成就比我原本想像中更多的事。 直到今天，我仍然記得揭開生命奧秘時那種令人振奮的感覺——從在顯微鏡下觀察細胞分裂，到在實習課中分析血液樣本，都是難忘的經歷。"},{"label":"1.2: STUDENT LIFE","english":"Beyond academics, what I will miss most about Class 6C is our unbreakable bond. Whether we were working together on group projects, sharing jokes in the corridor, or encouraging one another before crucial exams, our camaraderie made every moment truly special. I especially cherish how we supported each other, turning stressful deadlines into opportunities for collaboration. These small acts of kindness and mutual respect transformed our classroom into a second home. As we embark on new journeys, I feel grateful for the friendships forged in Class 6C and I truly believe these precious memories will forever light up our paths ahead.","chinese":"除了學業之外，最令我懷念 6C 班的，是我們之間牢不可破的情誼。 無論我們是在小組專題中一起合作、在走廊上分享笑話，還是在重要考試前互相鼓勵，這份同窗情誼都令每一刻變得格外珍貴。 我尤其珍惜我們彼此支持的方式，因為我們把充滿壓力的截止日期，轉化成互相合作的機會 這些細小的善意和彼此尊重，讓我們的課室變成了第二個家。 當我們踏上新的旅程時，我很感激在 6C 班建立起來的友誼，也真心相信這些珍貴回憶將永遠照亮我們前方的道路。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"Yearbook Entry","chinese":"畢業紀念冊文章"},{"english":"reflections","chinese":"感想；回顧"},{"english":"looking back on","chinese":"回顧……"},{"english":"my years at","chinese":"我在……的歲月"},{"english":"one subject that truly captivated me","chinese":"一科真正吸引我的科目"},{"english":"truly captivated me","chinese":"深深吸引我"},{"english":"delve into","chinese":"深入探索"},{"english":"microscopic worlds","chinese":"微觀世界"},{"english":"conduct hands-on experiments","chinese":"進行親身實驗"},{"english":"hands-on experiments","chinese":"親身實驗；實作實驗"},{"english":"in the lab","chinese":"在實驗室"},{"english":"never ceased to amaze me","chinese":"一直令我驚嘆"},{"english":"memorising complicated processes","chinese":"記憶複雜過程"},{"english":"complicated processes","chinese":"複雜過程"},{"english":"Latin names","chinese":"拉丁名稱"},{"english":"could be daunting","chinese":"可能令人卻步"},{"english":"that sense of challenge","chinese":"那種挑戰感"},{"english":"spur someone to","chinese":"激勵某人去……"},{"english":"push my limits","chinese":"挑戰自己的極限"},{"english":"achieve more than","chinese":"成就比……更多"},{"english":"ever thought possible","chinese":"曾經以為可能的"},{"english":"To this day","chinese":"直到今天"},{"english":"still recall","chinese":"仍然記得"},{"english":"how exhilarating it felt to","chinese":"……是多麼令人振奮"},{"english":"unravel the mysteries of life","chinese":"解開生命的奧秘"},{"english":"cells dividing under the microscope","chinese":"顯微鏡下正在分裂的細胞"},{"english":"under the microscope","chinese":"在顯微鏡下"},{"english":"analyse blood samples","chinese":"分析血液樣本"},{"english":"blood samples","chinese":"血液樣本"},{"english":"practical sessions","chinese":"實習課；實驗課"},{"english":"beyond academics","chinese":"除了學業之外"},{"english":"what I will miss most","chinese":"我最會懷念的"},{"english":"unbreakable bond","chinese":"牢不可破的情誼"},{"english":"whether we were","chinese":"無論我們是……"},{"english":"work together on","chinese":"一起做……"},{"english":"group projects","chinese":"小組專題"},{"english":"sharing jokes in the corridor","chinese":"在走廊說笑"},{"english":"encourage one another","chinese":"互相鼓勵"},{"english":"before crucial exams","chinese":"在重要考試之前"},{"english":"camaraderie","chinese":"同窗情誼；友愛"},{"english":"make every moment truly special","chinese":"令每一刻都格外珍貴"},{"english":"especially cherish","chinese":"特別珍惜"},{"english":"support each other","chinese":"互相支持"},{"english":"stressful deadlines","chinese":"令人有壓力的截止日期"},{"english":"turn something into opportunities for","chinese":"把……轉化成……的機會"},{"english":"opportunities for collaboration","chinese":"合作的機會"},{"english":"small acts of kindness","chinese":"細微的善意"},{"english":"mutual respect","chinese":"互相尊重"},{"english":"transform something into","chinese":"把……轉化成"},{"english":"a second home","chinese":"第二個家"},{"english":"embark on new journeys","chinese":"展開新的旅程"},{"english":"feel grateful for","chinese":"感激……"},{"english":"friendships forged in","chinese":"在……建立的友誼"},{"english":"precious memories","chinese":"珍貴回憶"},{"english":"forever light up our paths ahead","chinese":"永遠照亮我們前方的路"}]},"dse-writing-2020-part-a":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2020-part-a","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2020-part-a","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-a/2020","paragraphs":[{"label":"Title","english":"Restaurant Review: Dim Sum One","chinese":"餐廳評論：Dim Sum One"},{"label":"Introduction","english":"I recently visited Dim Sum One, Hong Kong’s hottest new dim sum restaurant, and was eager to find out if it lived up to its impressive reputation. From the moment I walked in, I was greeted by a friendly hostess and ushered to a sleek, modern dining area that still managed to feel remarkably cozy.","chinese":"我最近到訪了 Dim Sum One，這間香港最炙手可熱的新點心餐廳，並十分期待看看它是否名副其實，配得上那令人印象深刻的聲譽。 從我走進餐廳的一刻起，一位友善的女接待員便向我打招呼，並帶我前往一個設計時尚現代、卻仍然令人感到格外舒適的用餐區。"},{"label":"Food and Service","english":"The food was simply outstanding, with delicate shrimp dumplings and perfectly steamed barbecue pork buns stealing the spotlight. Each dish was artfully presented and bursting with authentic Cantonese flavors. Furthermore, the service was top-notch; staff members politely explained each item on the menu and kept our teapots filled without delay.","chinese":"食物實在非常出色，其中精緻的蝦餃和蒸得恰到好處的叉燒包尤其搶眼。 每一道菜都擺盤講究，並充滿正宗的廣東風味。 此外，服務也是一流的；職員有禮貌地講解餐牌上每一款食品，並且總是及時為我們添茶"},{"label":"Drawbacks","english":"Nevertheless, I found the prices slightly steep compared to other dim sum spots in the city. Additionally, the seating felt a bit cramped during peak hours, which might diminish the otherwise relaxed ambiance. Despite these drawbacks, the overall dining environment remained inviting and well-lit.","chinese":"不過，與城中其他點心店相比，我覺得這裏的價格略為偏高。 此外，在繁忙時段，座位感覺有點擠迫，這可能會削弱原本輕鬆的氣氛。 儘管有這些不足之處，整體用餐環境仍然舒適宜人，而且光線充足。"},{"label":"Recommendation","english":"In my opinion, Dim Sum One is an excellent choice for small gatherings and special occasions, thanks to its premium food quality and warm hospitality. I wholeheartedly recommend it if you are willing to pay a little extra for a memorable feast.","chinese":"在我看來，Dim Sum One 是小型聚會和特別場合的絕佳選擇，因為它擁有高質素的食物和親切周到的款待。 如果你願意多花一點錢，享受一頓難忘的盛宴，我會衷心推薦這間餐廳。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"restaurant review","chinese":"餐廳評論"},{"english":"recently visited","chinese":"最近到訪"},{"english":"Hong Kong's hottest new","chinese":"香港最熱門的新……"},{"english":"dim sum restaurant","chinese":"點心餐廳"},{"english":"be eager to","chinese":"急切想"},{"english":"find out if","chinese":"弄清楚是否"},{"english":"live up to","chinese":"不負……；符合……期望"},{"english":"impressive reputation","chinese":"令人印象深刻的名聲"},{"english":"from the moment","chinese":"從……一刻起"},{"english":"walk in","chinese":"走進去"},{"english":"be greeted by","chinese":"受到……迎接"},{"english":"friendly hostess","chinese":"友善的女接待員"},{"english":"be ushered to","chinese":"被帶到"},{"english":"sleek, modern dining area","chinese":"時尚現代的用餐區"},{"english":"still managed to feel","chinese":"仍然令人感到"},{"english":"remarkably cosy","chinese":"格外舒適"},{"english":"simply outstanding","chinese":"非常出色"},{"english":"delicate shrimp dumplings","chinese":"精緻蝦餃"},{"english":"perfectly steamed","chinese":"蒸得恰到好處"},{"english":"barbecue pork buns","chinese":"叉燒包"},{"english":"steal the spotlight","chinese":"成為焦點；最搶眼"},{"english":"artfully presented","chinese":"擺盤精美"},{"english":"burst with","chinese":"充滿……"},{"english":"authentic Cantonese flavours","chinese":"正宗廣東風味"},{"english":"furthermore","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"top-notch","chinese":"一流的；非常出色的"},{"english":"staff members","chinese":"職員"},{"english":"politely explained","chinese":"有禮貌地解釋"},{"english":"each item on the menu","chinese":"餐牌上的每一款食品"},{"english":"keep our teapots filled","chinese":"不斷為我們添茶"},{"english":"without delay","chinese":"毫不耽誤；很快"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"slightly steep","chinese":"稍為偏貴"},{"english":"compared to","chinese":"與……相比"},{"english":"dim sum spots","chinese":"點心店；點心餐廳"},{"english":"in the city","chinese":"在市內"},{"english":"additionally","chinese":"另外"},{"english":"seating","chinese":"座位安排"},{"english":"a bit cramped","chinese":"有點擠迫"},{"english":"during peak hours","chinese":"在繁忙時間"},{"english":"diminish","chinese":"減弱；削弱"},{"english":"otherwise relaxed ambiance","chinese":"原本輕鬆的氣氛"},{"english":"despite these drawbacks","chinese":"儘管有這些缺點"},{"english":"overall dining environment","chinese":"整體用餐環境"},{"english":"remain inviting","chinese":"仍然吸引；仍令人感到親切"},{"english":"well-lit","chinese":"光線充足"},{"english":"in my opinion","chinese":"依我看"},{"english":"an excellent choice for","chinese":"……的絕佳選擇"},{"english":"small gatherings","chinese":"小型聚會"},{"english":"special occasions","chinese":"特別場合"},{"english":"thanks to","chinese":"由於；多虧"},{"english":"premium food quality","chinese":"高級食物質素"},{"english":"warm hospitality","chinese":"熱情款待"},{"english":"wholeheartedly recommend","chinese":"真心推薦"},{"english":"be willing to","chinese":"願意"},{"english":"pay a little extra","chinese":"額外多付一點"},{"english":"memorable feast","chinese":"難忘盛宴"}]},"dse-writing-2021-part-a":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2021-part-a","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2021-part-a","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-a/2021","paragraphs":[{"label":"Greeting","english":"Good morning, everyone!","chinese":"各位早上好！"},{"label":"Introduction","english":"I am thrilled to announce that our annual School Fair will take place on Saturday, 29 May 2021, from 12 p.m. to 4 p.m. With tickets at only $10, this unmissable event promises an afternoon filled with excitement, creativity, and camaraderie.","chinese":"我很高興宣布，我們一年一度的學校園遊會將於 2021 年 5 月 29 日星期六中午 12 時至下午 4 時舉行。 門票只需 $10，這場不容錯過的活動將為大家帶來一個充滿興奮、創意和同伴情誼的下午。"},{"label":"Event Activities","english":"There will be lively food stalls showcasing both local and international treats, alongside fun-filled games and arts & crafts stations that will challenge your imagination. For those who love the spotlight, we have student performances and a special alumni football match where our former players return to face our current school team. Don’t forget to check out the displays of student work, which highlight the diverse talents here at Hong Kong Banyan School. Best of all, prizes await lucky winners in various competitions!","chinese":"屆時將設有熱鬧的美食攤位，展示本地及國際特色小食，旁邊亦會有充滿樂趣的遊戲和美術工藝攤位，挑戰大家的想像力。 對於喜歡站在舞台焦點之中的同學，我們將安排學生表演，以及一場特別的校友足球賽，屆時昔日球員將重返校園，與現任校隊對壘。 不要忘記參觀學生作品展覽，這些展品將展現香港榕樹學校學生多方面的才華。 最令人期待的是，各項比賽的幸運得獎者將有機會獲得獎品！"},{"label":"Invitation","english":"We warmly invite all past and present pupils, teachers, friends, and family to come along. If you would like to help make this fair even more successful, we need volunteers for setting up booths and managing visitor flow. Simply email Mr. Chris Wong at chriswong@hkbs.edu.hk to sign up.","chinese":"我們誠意邀請所有舊生、在校學生、老師、朋友和家人一同參與。 如果你希望協助我們令這次園遊會更加成功，我們現正招募義工，協助設置攤位及管理訪客人流。 如欲報名，只需電郵至 chriswong@hkbs.edu.hk 聯絡 Chris Wong 先生。"},{"label":"Closing","english":"Mark your calendars and spread the word. We look forward to seeing you all there!","chinese":"請大家記下日期，並把這個消息告訴身邊的人。 我們期待在當天見到大家！"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"be thrilled to announce","chinese":"很高興宣布"},{"english":"annual School Fair","chinese":"一年一度的學校嘉年華"},{"english":"take place on","chinese":"於……舉行"},{"english":"from 12 p.m. to 4 p.m.","chinese":"中午十二時至下午四時"},{"english":"with tickets at only","chinese":"門票只需……"},{"english":"unmissable event","chinese":"不容錯過的活動"},{"english":"promise an afternoon filled with","chinese":"承諾帶來一個充滿……的下午"},{"english":"filled with excitement","chinese":"充滿刺激和興奮"},{"english":"creativity","chinese":"創意"},{"english":"camaraderie","chinese":"友誼；團結情誼"},{"english":"lively food stalls","chinese":"熱鬧的食物攤位"},{"english":"showcase","chinese":"展示；呈現"},{"english":"local and international treats","chinese":"本地及國際美食"},{"english":"alongside","chinese":"與……一同"},{"english":"fun-filled games","chinese":"充滿樂趣的遊戲"},{"english":"arts and crafts stations","chinese":"手工藝攤位"},{"english":"challenge your imagination","chinese":"激發你的想像力"},{"english":"for those who love the spotlight","chinese":"對於喜歡成為焦點的人來說"},{"english":"love the spotlight","chinese":"喜歡成為眾人焦點"},{"english":"student performances","chinese":"學生表演"},{"english":"special alumni football match","chinese":"特別校友足球賽"},{"english":"alumni","chinese":"校友"},{"english":"former players","chinese":"前球員；舊生球員"},{"english":"return to face","chinese":"回來對戰……"},{"english":"current school team","chinese":"現屆校隊"},{"english":"Don't forget to","chinese":"不要忘記……"},{"english":"check out","chinese":"看看；參觀"},{"english":"displays of student work","chinese":"學生作品展覽"},{"english":"highlight","chinese":"突顯"},{"english":"diverse talents","chinese":"多元才華"},{"english":"best of all","chinese":"最好的是"},{"english":"prizes await","chinese":"獎品等待着……"},{"english":"lucky winners","chinese":"幸運得獎者"},{"english":"various competitions","chinese":"各項比賽"},{"english":"warmly invite","chinese":"熱誠邀請"},{"english":"past and present pupils","chinese":"舊生和現屆學生"},{"english":"friends and family","chinese":"朋友和家人"},{"english":"come along","chinese":"一同前來參加"},{"english":"help make this fair even more successful","chinese":"幫助令嘉年華更加成功"},{"english":"need volunteers for","chinese":"需要義工協助……"},{"english":"set up booths","chinese":"設置攤位"},{"english":"manage visitor flow","chinese":"管理人流"},{"english":"simply email","chinese":"只需電郵……"},{"english":"sign up","chinese":"報名"},{"english":"Mark your calendars","chinese":"記下這個日子"},{"english":"spread the word","chinese":"廣傳消息"},{"english":"look forward to seeing you all there","chinese":"期待在那裏見到大家"}]},"dse-writing-2022-part-a":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2022-part-a","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2022-part-a","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-a/2022","paragraphs":[{"label":"Title","english":"A First-Time Visitor’s Guide to Hong Kong Adventure Farm","chinese":"首次遊覽香港冒險農場指南"},{"label":"About Hong Kong Adventure Farm","english":"About Hong Kong Adventure Farm","chinese":"關於香港冒險農場"},{"label":"About Hong Kong Adventure Farm","english":"Established in 2010 and nestled in the green hills of Sai Kung, Hong Kong Adventure Farm is a refreshing escape from city life. Our scenic railway links four stations, placing spectacular views, outdoor adventures and farm-fresh food within easy reach of visitors of all ages seeking an unforgettable day out.","chinese":"香港冒險農場成立於 2010 年，坐落於西貢青翠的山丘之中，是一個讓人暫時遠離城市生活、煥然一新的好去處。 我們的觀景鐵路連接四個車站，讓各個年齡層的遊客都能輕鬆欣賞壯麗景色、體驗戶外歷險，並品嘗農場新鮮美食，度過難忘的一天。"},{"label":"Top three things to see and do","english":"Top three things to see and do","chinese":"三大必看必玩活動"},{"label":"Activity 1: Waterfall Station","english":"Board the railway at Entrance Main Station and make Waterfall Station your first stop. A short walk leads to the farm’s natural showpiece: a magnificent waterfall. Stop at the marked photo point to frame the cascading water against the surrounding greenery—an unforgettable snapshot of your visit.","chinese":"在入口主站登上鐵路，並把瀑布站作為你的第一站。 步行一小段路後，便會到達農場最具代表性的自然景觀：一座壯麗的瀑布。 你可以在標示清楚的拍照點停下來，把飛瀉而下的水流與四周綠意一同收進鏡頭，為這次旅程留下難忘的一幕。"},{"label":"Activity 2: Lake Side Station","english":"Next, continue to Lake Side Station and try kayaking. As you paddle across the water, the wooded landscape unfolds around you, making the experience peaceful yet exhilarating. Those wishing to slow down can also pause nearby for a warm drink before continuing their journey.","chinese":"接着，繼續前往湖畔站，體驗划獨木舟。 當你划槳穿過水面時，林木環繞的景色會在你身邊徐徐展開，令整個體驗既寧靜又令人振奮。 想放慢腳步的遊客，也可以在附近稍作停留，喝一杯暖飲後再繼續旅程。"},{"label":"Activity 3: Riding Area and Farmers’ Market","english":"Finally, make your way to the riding area on the eastern side of the farm. Exploring the countryside on horseback offers a change of pace and a closer connection with nature. Before leaving, travel to Farmers’ Market Station, where you can enjoy a hearty meal and browse fresh farm produce—the perfect way to round off an action-packed day.","chinese":"最後，你可以前往農場東面的騎乘區。 騎馬探索鄉郊景色，能讓旅程節奏有所轉變，也讓你與大自然建立更親近的連繫。 離開之前，你可以前往農夫市集站，在那裏享用一頓豐富的餐點，並選購新鮮農產品，為充滿活動的一天畫上完美句號。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"first-time visitor","chinese":"首次到訪的遊客"},{"english":"visitor's guide","chinese":"遊客指南"},{"english":"Hong Kong Adventure Farm","chinese":"香港冒險農場"},{"english":"established in","chinese":"於……成立"},{"english":"nestled in","chinese":"坐落於；隱於"},{"english":"green hills","chinese":"翠綠山丘"},{"english":"Sai Kung","chinese":"西貢"},{"english":"refreshing escape from","chinese":"令人放鬆的逃離……之地"},{"english":"city life","chinese":"城市生活"},{"english":"scenic railway","chinese":"景觀鐵路"},{"english":"link four stations","chinese":"連接四個車站"},{"english":"spectacular views","chinese":"壯麗景色"},{"english":"outdoor adventures","chinese":"戶外冒險活動"},{"english":"farm-fresh food","chinese":"農場新鮮食物"},{"english":"within easy reach of","chinese":"讓……輕易到達"},{"english":"visitors of all ages","chinese":"各個年齡層的遊客"},{"english":"seek an unforgettable day out","chinese":"尋找難忘的一日遊"},{"english":"unforgettable day out","chinese":"難忘的一日遊"},{"english":"top three things to see and do","chinese":"三大必看必玩活動"},{"english":"board the railway","chinese":"登上鐵路"},{"english":"Entrance Main Station","chinese":"Entrance Main Station（正門站）"},{"english":"make something your first stop","chinese":"將……作為第一站"},{"english":"Waterfall Station","chinese":"Waterfall Station（瀑布站）"},{"english":"a short walk leads to","chinese":"步行一小段路便到達"},{"english":"natural showpiece","chinese":"自然景觀亮點"},{"english":"magnificent waterfall","chinese":"壯觀的瀑布"},{"english":"marked photo point","chinese":"指定拍照點"},{"english":"frame something against","chinese":"以……作背景拍攝……"},{"english":"cascading water","chinese":"傾瀉而下的流水"},{"english":"surrounding greenery","chinese":"周圍的綠意"},{"english":"unforgettable snapshot","chinese":"難忘的照片"},{"english":"continue to","chinese":"繼續前往"},{"english":"Lake Side Station","chinese":"Lake Side Station（湖畔站）"},{"english":"try kayaking","chinese":"嘗試划獨木舟"},{"english":"paddle across the water","chinese":"划過水面"},{"english":"wooded landscape","chinese":"樹林景觀"},{"english":"unfold around you","chinese":"在你身邊展開"},{"english":"peaceful yet exhilarating","chinese":"寧靜卻令人振奮"},{"english":"slow down","chinese":"放慢節奏"},{"english":"pause nearby","chinese":"在附近稍作停留"},{"english":"warm drink","chinese":"熱飲"},{"english":"continue their journey","chinese":"繼續旅程"},{"english":"make your way to","chinese":"前往"},{"english":"riding area","chinese":"騎馬區"},{"english":"eastern side of","chinese":"……的東面"},{"english":"explore the countryside","chinese":"探索郊野"},{"english":"on horseback","chinese":"騎馬"},{"english":"offer a change of pace","chinese":"帶來不同節奏"},{"english":"closer connection with nature","chinese":"與大自然更親近"},{"english":"before leaving","chinese":"離開前"},{"english":"Farmers' Market Station","chinese":"Farmers' Market Station（農墟站）"},{"english":"hearty meal","chinese":"豐富的一餐"},{"english":"browse fresh farm produce","chinese":"瀏覽新鮮農產品"},{"english":"fresh farm produce","chinese":"新鮮農產品"},{"english":"the perfect way to","chinese":"……的完美方式"},{"english":"round off","chinese":"圓滿結束"},{"english":"action-packed day","chinese":"充滿活動的一天"}]},"dse-writing-2022-part-b-q3":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2022-part-b-q3","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2022-part-b-q3","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"Title","english":"A Dream Needs More Than a Dream","chinese":"夢想需要的不只是夢想"},{"label":"Salutation","english":"Dear Kam Chai,","chinese":"親愛的 Kam Chai："},{"label":"Introduction","english":"Your letter has the smell of roasted coffee, but also the weight of a real decision. At 25, you are standing between two doors: one opens to a better-paid promotion in work that does not excite you; the other opens to a café dream shared with friends, full of freedom, risk and possibility. The stakeholder who matters most here is not your company, your friends, or even your future customers. It is you. On balance, my advice is clear: do not resign immediately. Accept the promotion for now, but treat it not as a surrender of your dream, but as a strategic bridge towards it.","chinese":"你的來信帶有烘焙咖啡的香氣，但同時也承載着一個真正重大決定的重量。 在 25 歲的年紀，你正站在兩扇門之間：一扇門通往一份薪酬更高的晉升機會，但那份工作並不能令你感到興奮；另一扇門則通往你與朋友共同擁有的咖啡店夢想，當中充滿自由、風險與可能性。 在這件事上，最重要的持份者不是你的公司、你的朋友，甚至也不是你未來的顧客。 而是你自己。 整體衡量之下，我的建議很清楚：不要立即辭職。 暫時接受這次晉升，但不要把它視為對夢想的放棄，而要把它看成通往夢想的一座策略性橋樑。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"First, a café is a business before it is a romance. Many people imagine warm lighting, the handwritten menu and the smell of fresh pastries; fewer imagine rent, renovation costs, staff wages, food waste, licensing rules, supplier problems and quiet Tuesdays when only three customers walk in. The trouble with passion is that it can make danger look decorative. If you leave now without a financial cushion, one bad month may force you to borrow money, quarrel with your friends, or close before your idea has had time to breathe. Instead, use the promotion to build a runway. For example, set a target: save twelve months of personal expenses and six months of basic business costs; research three possible districts; compare rents; calculate how many cups of coffee and meals you must sell each day to break even. Better still, test the concept through weekend pop-ups, an Instagram pre-order dessert menu, or a booth at a community market. Only when customers pay for your idea, not merely praise it, will you know whether your dream has commercial legs. In practical terms, staying now protects your future freedom.","chinese":"首先，咖啡店在成為一種浪漫之前，先是一門生意。 很多人會想像溫暖的燈光、手寫的餐牌，以及新鮮糕點的香氣；但較少人會想像租金、裝修費、員工薪金、食物浪費、牌照規定、供應商問題，以及只有三位顧客走進來的冷清星期二。 熱情的問題在於，它有時會把危險裝飾得像美好的東西一樣。 如果你現在在沒有財務緩衝的情況下離職，一個差劣的月份就可能迫使你借錢、與朋友爭吵，甚至在你的構思還未有時間發展之前便結業。 相反，你應該利用這次晉升去建立一條起飛跑道。 例如，設定一個目標：儲起十二個月的個人生活開支和六個月的基本營運成本；研究三個可能的地區；比較租金；計算你每天必須賣出多少杯咖啡和多少份餐點才能收支平衡。 更理想的是，透過週末快閃店、Instagram 預訂甜品餐牌，或社區市集攤位來測試這個概念。 只有當顧客願意為你的構思付錢，而不只是口頭稱讚它時，你才會知道你的夢想是否具有商業可行性。 從實際角度來說，現在留下來是在保護你未來的自由。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Second, the promotion may give you skills that a young café owner badly needs. You say you are “not that interested” in the work. That matters, but boredom does not always mean uselessness. If the new role involves supervising people, handling clients, meeting targets, preparing budgets or solving complaints, it can become a training ground in disguise. A café owner must negotiate with landlords, manage staff, control costs, respond to bad reviews, design promotions and stay calm when the espresso machine breaks down during the lunch rush. These are not dreamy tasks; they are daily survival. Your company, dull as it may seem, might teach you how to listen, decide and act under pressure. Meanwhile, the higher salary can fund your café instead of replacing it. Ask yourself: can I turn this job into a paid apprenticeship for entrepreneurship? If the answer is yes, the promotion is not a cage. It is capital, training and time.","chinese":"第二，這次晉升可能會給你一位年輕咖啡店老闆非常需要的技能。 你說你對這份工作「並不是那麼感興趣」。 這一點很重要，但沉悶並不總是等於無用。 如果新的職位涉及管理員工、處理客戶、達成目標、準備預算或解決投訴，它就可以成為一個偽裝起來的訓練場。 一位咖啡店老闆必須與業主談判、管理員工、控制成本、回應負評、設計推廣活動，並在午餐繁忙時段意式咖啡機壞掉時保持冷靜。 這些不是夢幻的任務；它們是日常生存。 你的公司雖然看起來沉悶，卻可能教會你如何在壓力下聆聽、決定和行動。 與此同時，更高的薪金可以資助你的咖啡店夢想，而不是取代它。 問問自己：我能否把這份工作變成一個有薪的創業學徒訓練？ 如果答案是肯定的，那麼這次晉升就不是一個牢籠。 它是資本、訓練和時間。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 3","english":"Granted, your friends may say, “Why wait? You are young only once.” They have a point. Dreams can become dusty if they are postponed forever. Comfort has a quiet way of becoming a chain, and a good salary can make an unhappy person stay “just one more year” until the dream becomes a dinner story. Be that as it may, the solution is not reckless resignation; it is a deadline with conditions. Do not say vaguely, “I’ll wait a few years.” Say, “I will prepare for eighteen to twenty-four months, and I will leave only if these milestones are met.” Those milestones should include a written partnership agreement with your friends, a tested menu, a realistic budget, a clear division of duties, savings, and evidence of real customer demand. If, after that period, the job is still draining your spirit and the café plan has become solid, leave with courage. If the evidence is weak, revise the plan instead of gambling your future on wishful thinking.","chinese":"誠然，你的朋友可能會說：「為甚麼要等？青春只有一次。」 他們有一定道理。 如果夢想被永遠推遲，它們也會蒙上灰塵。 安逸會悄悄變成鎖鏈，而一份不錯的薪水也可能令一個不快樂的人一年又一年地說「再多做一年」，直到夢想變成飯桌上的故事。 即便如此，解決方法也不是魯莽辭職；而是一個附帶條件的期限。 不要含糊地說：「我會等幾年。」 你應該說：「我會準備十八至二十四個月，而且只有在這些里程碑達成後，我才會離開。」 這些里程碑應包括一份與朋友簽訂的書面合夥協議、一份經過測試的餐牌、一個現實可行的預算、清晰的職責分工、儲蓄，以及真實顧客需求的證據。 如果在那段時間之後，這份工作仍然在耗盡你的精神，而咖啡店計劃已經變得穩固，那就勇敢離開。 如果證據薄弱，就應該修改計劃，而不是把自己的未來押在一廂情願的想法上"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"So, Kam Chai, choose neither fear nor fantasy. Accept the promotion, build your financial base, test your café idea, and set a firm departure date tied to measurable progress. At the end of the day, the best entrepreneurs are not those who leap blindly, but those who prepare so well that the leap becomes smaller. Your dream deserves bravery, yes — but it also deserves discipline. Brew it slowly, and when the time comes, serve it well.","chinese":"所以，Kam Chai，不要選擇恐懼，也不要選擇幻想。 接受這次晉升，建立你的財務基礎，測試你的咖啡店構思，並設定一個與可衡量進展掛鉤的明確離職日期。 說到底，最好的創業者不是那些盲目跳躍的人，而是那些準備得非常充分，以至於跳躍本身變得更小的人。 你的夢想確實值得勇氣——但它同樣值得紀律。 慢慢沖泡它；到了時機成熟之時，就把它好好端上桌。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"a real decision","chinese":"一個真正重要的決定"},{"english":"standing between two doors","chinese":"站在兩扇門之間；面對兩個選擇"},{"english":"one opens to...; the other opens to...","chinese":"一扇門通向……；另一扇門通向……"},{"english":"on balance","chinese":"權衡之後；總體而言"},{"english":"my advice is clear","chinese":"我的建議很清楚"},{"english":"do not resign immediately","chinese":"不要立即辭職"},{"english":"accept the promotion for now","chinese":"目前接受晉升"},{"english":"not as a surrender, but as a strategic bridge","chinese":"不是投降，而是策略性的橋樑"},{"english":"choose neither fear nor fantasy","chinese":"既不要選擇恐懼，也不要選擇幻想"},{"english":"leave with courage","chinese":"勇敢地離開"},{"english":"a better-paid promotion","chinese":"薪酬更高的晉升"},{"english":"work that does not excite you","chinese":"不能令你興奮的工作"},{"english":"not that interested in the work","chinese":"對工作不是很感興趣"},{"english":"boredom does not always mean uselessness","chinese":"沉悶不一定等於無用"},{"english":"the new role","chinese":"新職位；新角色"},{"english":"supervising people","chinese":"管理 / 監督員工"},{"english":"handling clients","chinese":"處理客戶"},{"english":"meeting targets","chinese":"達成目標"},{"english":"preparing budgets","chinese":"準備預算"},{"english":"solving complaints","chinese":"處理投訴"},{"english":"a training ground in disguise","chinese":"偽裝成普通工作的訓練場"},{"english":"a paid apprenticeship for entrepreneurship","chinese":"一個有薪的創業學徒期"},{"english":"the higher salary can fund your café","chinese":"較高薪水可以資助你的咖啡店"},{"english":"dull as it may seem","chinese":"雖然它看起來沉悶"},{"english":"act under pressure","chinese":"在壓力下行動"},{"english":"job is draining your spirit","chinese":"工作正在耗盡你的精神"},{"english":"a café dream","chinese":"咖啡店夢想"},{"english":"shared with friends","chinese":"與朋友共同擁有 / 分享"},{"english":"freedom, risk and possibility","chinese":"自由、風險和可能性"},{"english":"a business before it is a romance","chinese":"它首先是生意，其次才是浪漫"},{"english":"warm lighting","chinese":"溫暖燈光"},{"english":"the handwritten menu","chinese":"手寫餐牌"},{"english":"the smell of fresh pastries","chinese":"新鮮糕點的香氣"},{"english":"rent","chinese":"租金"},{"english":"renovation costs","chinese":"裝修成本"},{"english":"staff wages","chinese":"員工工資"},{"english":"food waste","chinese":"食物浪費"},{"english":"licensing rules","chinese":"牌照規定"},{"english":"supplier problems","chinese":"供應商問題"},{"english":"quiet Tuesdays","chinese":"冷清的星期二"},{"english":"only three customers walk in","chinese":"只有三個客人進門"},{"english":"a financial cushion","chinese":"財政緩衝 / 儲備"},{"english":"one bad month","chinese":"一個糟糕的月份"},{"english":"build a runway","chinese":"建立跑道 / 預備起飛空間"},{"english":"personal expenses","chinese":"個人開支"},{"english":"basic business costs","chinese":"基本營運成本"},{"english":"possible districts","chinese":"可能的地區 / 選址區域"},{"english":"compare rents","chinese":"比較租金"},{"english":"break even","chinese":"收支平衡"},{"english":"test the concept","chinese":"測試概念"},{"english":"weekend pop-ups","chinese":"週末快閃店"},{"english":"an Instagram pre-order dessert menu","chinese":"Instagram 預訂甜品餐牌"},{"english":"a booth at a community market","chinese":"社區市集攤位"},{"english":"customers pay for your idea, not merely praise it","chinese":"顧客為你的想法付錢，而不只是稱讚它"},{"english":"commercial legs","chinese":"商業上的可行性 / 持久能力"},{"english":"evidence of real customer demand","chinese":"真實顧客需求的證據"},{"english":"risk and possibility","chinese":"風險和可能性"},{"english":"danger look decorative","chinese":"令危險看起來像裝飾一樣美好"},{"english":"borrow money","chinese":"借錢"},{"english":"quarrel with your friends","chinese":"與朋友爭吵"},{"english":"close before your idea has had time to breathe","chinese":"在想法有時間成長前就結業"},{"english":"set a target","chinese":"設定目標"},{"english":"save twelve months of personal expenses","chinese":"儲起十二個月個人開支"},{"english":"six months of basic business costs","chinese":"六個月基本營運成本"},{"english":"a deadline with conditions","chinese":"帶有條件的期限"},{"english":"eighteen to twenty-four months","chinese":"十八至二十四個月"},{"english":"milestones are met","chinese":"達成里程碑"},{"english":"a realistic budget","chinese":"現實的預算"},{"english":"measurable progress","chinese":"可衡量的進展"},{"english":"wishful thinking","chinese":"一廂情願的想法"},{"english":"your friends may say","chinese":"你的朋友可能會說"},{"english":"written partnership agreement","chinese":"書面合夥協議"},{"english":"clear division of duties","chinese":"清晰分工"},{"english":"shared dream","chinese":"共同夢想"},{"english":"negotiate with landlords","chinese":"與業主談判"},{"english":"manage staff","chinese":"管理員工"},{"english":"control costs","chinese":"控制成本"},{"english":"respond to bad reviews","chinese":"回應差評"},{"english":"design promotions","chinese":"設計促銷活動"},{"english":"stay calm","chinese":"保持冷靜"},{"english":"during the lunch rush","chinese":"午餐繁忙時段"},{"english":"daily survival","chinese":"每日生存；日常營運求存"},{"english":"listen, decide and act under pressure","chinese":"在壓力下聆聽、決定和行動"},{"english":"your dream","chinese":"你的夢想"},{"english":"surrender of your dream","chinese":"放棄夢想"},{"english":"towards it","chinese":"朝著它前進"},{"english":"dreams can become dusty","chinese":"夢想會蒙塵"},{"english":"the dream becomes a dinner story","chinese":"夢想變成飯桌故事"},{"english":"bravery","chinese":"勇氣"},{"english":"discipline","chinese":"紀律；自律"},{"english":"brew it slowly","chinese":"慢慢沖泡它"},{"english":"serve it well","chinese":"好好端上它；好好實現它"},{"english":"First","chinese":"首先"},{"english":"Second","chinese":"第二"},{"english":"For example","chinese":"例如"},{"english":"Better still","chinese":"更好的是"},{"english":"In practical terms","chinese":"實際而言"},{"english":"Meanwhile","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"Granted","chinese":"誠然；固然"},{"english":"They have a point","chinese":"他們有道理"},{"english":"Be that as it may","chinese":"即便如此；話雖如此"},{"english":"Do not say vaguely","chinese":"不要含糊地說"},{"english":"If the evidence is weak","chinese":"如果證據不足"},{"english":"instead of","chinese":"而不是"},{"english":"At the end of the day","chinese":"歸根究底；到頭來"}]},"dse-writing-2023-part-a":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2023-part-a","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2023-part-a","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-a/2023","paragraphs":[{"label":"Title","english":"Pop-up Shop Application Form","chinese":"快閃店申請表"},{"label":"Section A: Company Profile","english":"Section A: Company Profile","chinese":"A 部分：公司簡介"},{"label":"Section A: Company Profile","english":"Planet Smart is a Hong Kong-based enterprise dedicated to designing and distributing eco-friendly household and lifestyle products. Established five years ago, we have steadily built a reputation for championing sustainability through ethically sourced materials, carbon-neutral shipping, and active community outreach programs. Our vision is to reduce plastic waste and promote greener consumption habits across the city.","chinese":"Planet Smart 是一家以香港為基地的企業，致力於設計及分銷環保家居和生活產品。 成立於五年前，我們透過符合道德標準採購的材料、碳中和運輸，以及積極的社區外展計劃，逐步建立起倡導可持續發展的聲譽。 我們的願景是在全城減少塑膠廢物，並推廣更環保的消費習慣。"},{"label":"Section B: Best-selling Product","english":"Section B: Best-selling Product","chinese":"B 部分：最暢銷產品"},{"label":"Section B: Best-selling Product","english":"Among our wide range of items, our reusable BambooSip Water Bottle has emerged as a customer favorite. Crafted from responsibly harvested bamboo, it offers outstanding insulation while remaining lightweight and durable. By switching to BambooSip, users can decrease single-use plastic bottle usage and enjoy a stylish, minimalist design perfect for daily commutes or weekend hikes.","chinese":"在我們種類繁多的產品之中，可重用的 BambooSip Water Bottle 已成為顧客最喜愛的產品。 它由負責任採伐的竹材製成，既具備出色的保溫效能，同時又保持輕巧耐用。 透過轉用 BambooSip，使用者可以減少一次性塑膠瓶的使用，並享受時尚而簡約的設計，非常適合日常通勤或週末遠足。"},{"label":"Section C: In-store Event","english":"Section C: In-store Event","chinese":"C 部分：店內活動"},{"label":"Section C: In-store Event","english":"To spark interest and educate new customers, we plan to host a “Zero-Waste Living Workshop” at our pop-up shop. Participants will learn practical tips to reduce waste at home, including food storage hacks and DIY cleaning solutions. By sharing hands-on demonstrations and offering exclusive product discounts, we aim to inspire our visitors to adopt more sustainable lifestyles and boost our brand’s visibility.","chinese":"為了引起興趣並教育新顧客，我們計劃在快閃店舉辦一個「零廢生活工作坊」。 參加者將學習在家中減少廢物的實用貼士，包括食物儲存技巧和自製清潔方案。 透過分享親身示範並提供專屬產品折扣，我們旨在啟發訪客採納更可持續的生活方式，並提升我們品牌的知名度。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"Pop-up Shop Application Form","chinese":"快閃店申請表"},{"english":"company profile","chinese":"公司簡介"},{"english":"Hong Kong-based enterprise","chinese":"以香港為基地的企業"},{"english":"dedicated to","chinese":"致力於"},{"english":"designing and distributing","chinese":"設計和分銷"},{"english":"eco-friendly household and lifestyle products","chinese":"環保家居及生活用品"},{"english":"established five years ago","chinese":"五年前成立"},{"english":"steadily built a reputation for","chinese":"逐步建立……的名聲"},{"english":"championing sustainability","chinese":"倡導可持續發展"},{"english":"ethically sourced materials","chinese":"符合道德採購原則的材料"},{"english":"carbon-neutral shipping","chinese":"碳中和運送"},{"english":"active community outreach programs","chinese":"積極的社區外展計劃"},{"english":"our vision is to","chinese":"我們的願景是"},{"english":"reduce plastic waste","chinese":"減少塑膠廢物"},{"english":"promote greener consumption habits","chinese":"推廣更環保的消費習慣"},{"english":"across the city","chinese":"在全城；遍及全市"},{"english":"best-selling product","chinese":"最暢銷產品"},{"english":"among our wide range of items","chinese":"在我們眾多產品之中"},{"english":"wide range of","chinese":"種類繁多的"},{"english":"has emerged as","chinese":"已成為"},{"english":"customer favorite","chinese":"深受顧客喜愛的產品"},{"english":"crafted from","chinese":"由……製成"},{"english":"responsibly harvested bamboo","chinese":"負責任採收的竹材"},{"english":"offers outstanding insulation","chinese":"具備出色保溫效能"},{"english":"remaining lightweight and durable","chinese":"同時保持輕巧耐用"},{"english":"lightweight and durable","chinese":"輕巧耐用"},{"english":"by switching to","chinese":"透過轉用"},{"english":"decrease single-use plastic bottle usage","chinese":"減少即棄膠樽使用量"},{"english":"single-use plastic bottle","chinese":"即棄膠樽"},{"english":"stylish, minimalist design","chinese":"時尚簡約的設計"},{"english":"perfect for","chinese":"非常適合"},{"english":"daily commutes","chinese":"日常通勤"},{"english":"weekend hikes","chinese":"週末遠足"},{"english":"in-store event","chinese":"店內活動"},{"english":"spark interest","chinese":"激發興趣"},{"english":"educate new customers","chinese":"教育新顧客"},{"english":"plan to host","chinese":"計劃舉辦"},{"english":"Zero-Waste Living Workshop","chinese":"零廢生活工作坊"},{"english":"participants will learn","chinese":"參加者將會學習"},{"english":"practical tips","chinese":"實用貼士"},{"english":"reduce waste at home","chinese":"減少家居廢物"},{"english":"food storage hacks","chinese":"食物儲存小技巧"},{"english":"DIY cleaning solutions","chinese":"自製清潔用品方法"},{"english":"hands-on demonstrations","chinese":"實際示範"},{"english":"exclusive product discounts","chinese":"獨家產品折扣"},{"english":"aim to inspire","chinese":"旨在啟發"},{"english":"adopt more sustainable lifestyles","chinese":"採納更可持續的生活方式"},{"english":"boost our brand's visibility","chinese":"提升品牌曝光度"}]},"dse-writing-2024-part-a":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2024-part-a","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2024-part-a","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-a/2024","paragraphs":[{"label":"Salutation","english":"Dear Hotel Manager,","chinese":"尊敬的酒店經理："},{"label":"Introduction","english":"I am writing to lodge a formal complaint about my recent one-night stay at the Seaside Hotel, booked through your website for HK$1,580. I made the reservation in good faith because the advertisement clearly promised a non-smoking room with a balcony, an ocean view, Wi-Fi, room service, air conditioning, and all taxes and fees included.","chinese":"本人寫信是為了就最近透過貴酒店網站預訂、價值港幣 1,580 元的 Seaside Hotel 一晚住宿，正式提出投訴。 本人是基於信任而作出預訂，因為該廣告清楚承諾房間為非吸煙客房，並設有露台、海景、Wi-Fi、客房送餐服務、空調，而且所有稅項及費用均已包括在內。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Unfortunately, the room allocated to me fell far below this description. Far from enjoying an ocean view, I was given a room facing a noisy main road, and there was no balcony at all. In addition, the Wi-Fi connection was so weak that it was practically unusable, while the air conditioner was both loud and ineffective. When I attempted to order room service, I was informed that it was unavailable. Most disturbingly, the room smelled strongly of cigarette smoke despite being advertised as non-smoking. To make matters worse, I was charged an additional service fee at check-out, even though your website explicitly stated that taxes and fees were included.","chinese":"可惜，分配給本人的房間遠遠低於上述描述。 本人不但沒有享受到海景，反而被安排入住一間面向嘈雜大馬路的房間，而且完全沒有露台。 此外，Wi-Fi 連線非常微弱，實際上幾乎無法使用，而空調既嘈吵又沒有實際效用。 當本人嘗試要求客房送餐服務時，卻被告知該服務並不提供。 最令人不安的是，儘管該房間被宣傳為非吸煙客房，房內卻有濃烈的香煙氣味。 更糟糕的是，本人在退房時被額外收取服務費，儘管貴酒店網站明確列明稅項及費用均已包括在內。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"As I relied on the accuracy of your advertisement when making my booking, I find this discrepancy both misleading and unacceptable. I would therefore expect a partial refund, a written apology, and a clear explanation of how this matter will be addressed. I also strongly urge your hotel to amend the online advertisement immediately so that future guests will not be similarly misled.","chinese":"由於本人在預訂時依賴貴酒店廣告內容的準確性，因此本人認為這種差異既具誤導性，也令人無法接受。 因此，本人期望獲得部分退款、書面道歉，以及一個清楚說明貴酒店將如何處理此事的解釋。 本人強烈敦促貴酒店立即修改網上廣告，以免日後的住客同樣受到類似誤導。"},{"label":"Sign-off","english":"Yours faithfully,","chinese":"此致"},{"label":"Name","english":"Chris Wong","chinese":"Chris Wong"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"lodge a formal complaint","chinese":"正式投訴"},{"english":"recent one-night stay","chinese":"最近一晚的住宿"},{"english":"booked through","chinese":"透過……預訂"},{"english":"made the reservation","chinese":"作出預訂"},{"english":"in good faith","chinese":"出於信任；真誠地"},{"english":"the advertisement clearly promised","chinese":"廣告清楚承諾"},{"english":"non-smoking room","chinese":"非吸煙房"},{"english":"with a balcony","chinese":"設有露台"},{"english":"an ocean view","chinese":"海景"},{"english":"room service","chinese":"客房送餐服務"},{"english":"air conditioning","chinese":"空調"},{"english":"all taxes and fees included","chinese":"已包括所有稅項及費用"},{"english":"the room allocated to me","chinese":"分配給我的房間"},{"english":"fell far below","chinese":"遠遠低於；與……相差甚遠"},{"english":"this description","chinese":"這個描述"},{"english":"far from enjoying","chinese":"不但沒有……反而"},{"english":"facing a noisy main road","chinese":"面向嘈雜的大路"},{"english":"no balcony at all","chinese":"完全沒有露台"},{"english":"in addition","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"Wi-Fi connection","chinese":"Wi-Fi 連接"},{"english":"so weak that","chinese":"弱到……以致"},{"english":"practically unusable","chinese":"幾乎無法使用"},{"english":"both loud and ineffective","chinese":"既嘈吵又無效"},{"english":"attempted to order","chinese":"嘗試點叫"},{"english":"was informed that","chinese":"被告知"},{"english":"most disturbingly","chinese":"最令人不安的是"},{"english":"smelled strongly of","chinese":"有強烈的……氣味"},{"english":"cigarette smoke","chinese":"香煙煙味"},{"english":"despite being advertised as","chinese":"儘管被宣傳為"},{"english":"to make matters worse","chinese":"更糟的是"},{"english":"was charged","chinese":"被收取"},{"english":"an additional service fee","chinese":"額外服務費"},{"english":"at check-out","chinese":"退房時"},{"english":"even though","chinese":"即使"},{"english":"explicitly stated that","chinese":"明確說明"},{"english":"taxes and fees","chinese":"稅項及費用"},{"english":"relied on the accuracy of","chinese":"依賴……的準確性"},{"english":"when making my booking","chinese":"預訂時"},{"english":"this discrepancy","chinese":"這種不符之處"},{"english":"both misleading and unacceptable","chinese":"既具誤導性又不可接受"},{"english":"would therefore expect","chinese":"因此期望"},{"english":"a partial refund","chinese":"部分退款"},{"english":"a written apology","chinese":"書面道歉"},{"english":"a clear explanation of","chinese":"清楚解釋"},{"english":"how this matter will be addressed","chinese":"這件事將如何處理"},{"english":"strongly urge","chinese":"強烈敦促"},{"english":"amend the online advertisement","chinese":"修改網上廣告"},{"english":"future guests","chinese":"日後住客"},{"english":"similarly misled","chinese":"同樣被誤導"}]},"dse-writing-2024-part-b-q5":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2024-part-b-q5","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2024-part-b-q5","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"Title","english":"One Night, 100,000 Likes, and a Lesson I Never Expected","chinese":"一夜之間，十萬個讚，以及一個我從未預料到的教訓"},{"label":"Intro","english":"At 10:58 p.m. on a perfectly ordinary Tuesday, I posted a 45-second video and put my phone aside, expecting nothing more than a few amused comments from friends. By the time I woke up the next morning, however, that same video had gathered over 100,000 likes. For a few stunned seconds, I simply stared at the screen, wondering whether I was still half asleep. In an age when social media can turn an ordinary student into a minor celebrity overnight, many young people dream of going viral. After experiencing it myself, though, I have realised that sudden online fame is not only exciting but also unexpectedly exhausting, unsettling and deeply instructive.","chinese":"在一個再普通不過的星期二晚上 10 點 58 分，我發佈了一段 45 秒的影片，然後把手機放到一旁，原本只預期朋友們會留下幾則覺得好笑的留言而已。 然而，等我隔天早上醒來時，那段影片竟然已經累積超過十萬個讚。 有好幾秒鐘，我只是愣愣地盯著螢幕，懷疑自己是不是還沒完全睡醒。 在這個社群媒體可以一夜之間把普通學生變成小小網紅的時代，許多年輕人都夢想著自己能爆紅。 但親身經歷之後，我明白到，突如其來的網路名氣不僅令人興奮，也會出乎意料地讓人疲憊、不安，並帶來深刻的啟發。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The video itself was hardly a masterpiece. It was a short, light-hearted clip showing “a day in the life of a Hong Kong student before exams”. I had filmed myself rushing to school, balancing a sandwich and revision notes in one hand, falling asleep briefly on the bus, and then pretending to be full of energy in class. I added some humorous captions, a trending sound effect and posted it without much thought. Apparently, however, thousands of students found it painfully relatable. Within hours, the notifications on my phone were exploding so rapidly that I could barely read them. Likes were rising by the second. Comments came from people I had never met, from different schools, cities and even countries. At first, the experience felt almost magical. It was flattering to know that something I had created in my bedroom could make so many strangers laugh.","chinese":"那段影片本身其實根本算不上什麼傑作。 那只是一段簡短而輕鬆的影片，內容是「香港學生考試前一天的生活」。 我拍下自己匆忙趕去上學、一手拿著三明治和複習筆記、在巴士上短暫睡著，然後到了課堂上又假裝精神飽滿的樣子。 我加上了一些幽默字幕和一個流行音效，沒有多想就把它發出去了。 然而，顯然有成千上萬的學生都覺得那內容真是太有共鳴了。 短短幾個小時內，我手機上的通知爆炸式地增加，快到我幾乎來不及看清楚。 按讚數每一秒都在上升，留言則來自我從未見過的人，他們來自不同的學校、城市，甚至不同國家。 一開始，這種經歷幾乎讓人覺得像魔法一樣。 知道自己在房間裡做出來的東西，竟然能讓那麼多陌生人發笑，的確令人感到受寵若驚。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Yet the thrill did not last in its pure form for very long. The first change was practical: my phone became impossible to ignore. Every few seconds, it lit up again. Every buzz seemed to demand my attention. Instead of doing homework, I kept checking the latest numbers, wondering whether the video had reached 120,000 or 130,000 views. In other words, I was no longer using social media; social media was using me. What surprised me most was how quickly enjoyment turned into dependence. The more attention I received, the more I wanted. A single successful post, rather than making me satisfied, made me anxious about whether I could repeat that success. What had begun as a joke was slowly turning into pressure.","chinese":"然而，這份興奮並沒有長久維持最初那種單純的樣子。 第一個改變是很實際的：我的手機變得讓人無法忽視。 每隔幾秒，它就又亮起來一次；每一次震動都像是在要求我立刻注意它。 我沒有好好做功課，反而一直在查看最新數字，想知道影片是不是已經到了十二萬或十三萬觀看次數。 換句話說，不再是我在使用社群媒體，而是社群媒體在使用我。 最讓我驚訝的是，快樂竟然那麼迅速地轉變成依賴。 我得到的關注越多，就越想要更多。 一則成功的貼文，不但沒有讓我感到滿足，反而讓我開始焦慮自己是否還能再複製同樣的成功。 原本只是個玩笑的事情，慢慢地卻變成了一種壓力。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 3","english":"A second lesson came from reading the comments. Many were kind, generous and genuinely funny. Some people wrote that they had never felt so “seen” before, while others tagged their friends and said, “This is literally us.” Those responses reminded me that social media can create connections in a powerful and immediate way. A simple video can reassure people that they are not alone in their stress, awkwardness or daily struggles. However, not all comments were encouraging. A few criticised my appearance, my voice or even the way I walked. One accused me of “trying too hard to be relatable”, while another claimed the video was “cringe”. I knew, logically, that strangers on the internet do not know me well enough to define me. Even so, harsh words have a peculiar way of lingering longer than praise. That was when I understood a difficult truth: online popularity brings not only visibility, but also vulnerability.","chinese":"第二個教訓來自閱讀留言。 其中很多留言都很友善、很大方，也真的很有趣。 有些人寫道，他們從來沒有像這次一樣感到自己「被看見」；也有人標記朋友並說：「這根本就是我們。」 這些回應提醒了我，社群媒體確實能夠以強而有力又直接的方式創造連結。 一段簡單的影片，就能讓人明白自己在壓力、尷尬或日常掙扎中並不孤單。 然而，並不是所有留言都令人鼓舞。 有些人批評我的外表、聲音，甚至連我走路的樣子也不放過。 有人指責我「太刻意想讓人產生共鳴」，還有人說那支影片「很尷尬」。 從理性上來說，我知道網路上的陌生人其實並不了解我，沒有資格定義我是誰。 即使如此，刺耳的話總有一種特別的力量，會比稱讚停留得更久。 就在那一刻，我明白了一個不容易接受的事實：網路上的受歡迎，不只帶來曝光，也帶來脆弱。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 4","english":"Most importantly, the whole experience changed the way I think about success. Before this happened, I might have assumed that getting 100,000 likes would feel like reaching a finish line. In reality, it felt more like stepping onto a moving treadmill. Numbers rise, people react, trends shift, and attention moves on. By the following week, the excitement had already begun to fade. The internet, after all, has a very short memory. What remains, however, is not the number itself but the lesson behind it. I learned that recognition is enjoyable, but it is unreliable if it becomes the main source of one’s confidence. I also learned that creativity matters far more than chasing approval. The happiest moment in the entire experience was not seeing the number 100,000; it was creating something honest that others connected with.","chinese":"最重要的是，整個經歷改變了我對成功的看法。 在這件事發生之前，我也許會以為得到十萬個讚，就像抵達終點線一樣。 但實際上，那感覺更像是踏上了一台不停移動的跑步機。 數字會上升，人們會反應，潮流會改變，而注意力也會很快轉移。 到了下一個星期，那份興奮感其實已經開始消退。 畢竟，網路的記憶是非常短暫的。 然而，真正留下來的，並不是那個數字本身，而是它背後帶來的教訓。 我明白了，被認可固然令人開心，但如果它變成一個人自信的主要來源，那就是不可靠的。 我也學會了，創意遠比追逐認同更加重要。 整個經歷中最快樂的時刻，不是看見十萬這個數字，而是創造出一樣真誠的東西，並讓別人與之產生共鳴。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"Looking back, I am grateful that the video went viral, not because it made me “famous” for a day, but because it taught me to view social media more critically and more calmly. It can be a platform for humour, creativity and shared experience, but it can also be addictive and emotionally unpredictable. If there is one message I would like to leave with fellow students, it is this: enjoy the excitement of online attention if it comes, but do not build your self-worth on it. A viral post may last for a night, but self-knowledge lasts much longer.","chinese":"回頭看，我很感激那支影片爆紅，不是因為它讓我「紅了一天」，而是因為它教會我用更冷靜、更有批判性的眼光去看待社群媒體。 它可以是一個承載幽默、創意與共同經驗的平台，但同時也可能令人上癮，並在情緒上難以預測。 如果我想留給同學們一個訊息，那就是：如果網路上的關注真的來了，就享受那份興奮吧，但不要把自己的自我價值建立在它上面。 一則爆紅的貼文也許只會持續一晚，但對自我的了解卻會長久得多。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"go viral","chinese":"在網上爆紅；病毒式傳播"},{"english":"sudden online fame","chinese":"突如其來的網上名氣"},{"english":"a viral post","chinese":"爆紅的帖文 / 爆紅的貼文"},{"english":"a minor celebrity overnight","chinese":"一夜之間成為小有名氣的人"},{"english":"online attention","chinese":"網上關注"},{"english":"online popularity","chinese":"網上人氣"},{"english":"recognition","chinese":"認可；被看見；被肯定"},{"english":"visibility","chinese":"能見度；被看見的程度"},{"english":"famous for a day","chinese":"出名一天；短暫成名"},{"english":"the internet has a very short memory","chinese":"網絡的記憶很短暫"},{"english":"post a video","chinese":"發佈影片"},{"english":"put my phone aside","chinese":"把手機放在一旁"},{"english":"gather likes","chinese":"獲得讚好"},{"english":"notifications","chinese":"通知"},{"english":"notifications were exploding","chinese":"通知爆炸式湧現"},{"english":"likes were rising by the second","chinese":"讚好數每秒上升"},{"english":"comments came from strangers","chinese":"留言來自陌生人"},{"english":"tag their friends","chinese":"標記朋友"},{"english":"a trending sound effect","chinese":"熱門音效"},{"english":"check the latest numbers","chinese":"查看最新數字"},{"english":"reach 120,000 or 130,000 views","chinese":"達到十二萬或十三萬觀看次數"},{"english":"social media was using me","chinese":"社交媒體在使用我"},{"english":"a Hong Kong student before exams","chinese":"考試前的香港學生"},{"english":"revision notes","chinese":"溫習筆記"},{"english":"rushing to school","chinese":"匆忙趕回學校"},{"english":"falling asleep on the bus","chinese":"在巴士上睡著"},{"english":"pretending to be full of energy","chinese":"假裝充滿精力"},{"english":"exam stress","chinese":"考試壓力"},{"english":"daily struggles","chinese":"日常掙扎"},{"english":"awkwardness","chinese":"尷尬；笨拙感"},{"english":"relatable student life","chinese":"有共鳴的學生生活"},{"english":"stunned","chinese":"震驚的"},{"english":"half asleep","chinese":"半睡半醒的"},{"english":"exciting","chinese":"令人興奮的"},{"english":"exhausting","chinese":"令人疲憊的"},{"english":"unsettling","chinese":"令人不安的"},{"english":"deeply instructive","chinese":"深具啟發性的"},{"english":"almost magical","chinese":"幾乎像魔法般的"},{"english":"flattering","chinese":"令人受寵若驚的"},{"english":"dependence","chinese":"依賴"},{"english":"anxious","chinese":"焦慮的"},{"english":"pressure","chinese":"壓力"},{"english":"emotionally unpredictable","chinese":"情緒上難以預測的"},{"english":"painfully relatable","chinese":"令人痛苦地有共鳴；太真實而有共鳴"},{"english":"feel seen","chinese":"感到被看見；感到被理解"},{"english":"create connection","chinese":"建立連結"},{"english":"shared experience","chinese":"共同經歷"},{"english":"reassure people","chinese":"讓人安心；安慰人"},{"english":"strangers laugh","chinese":"令陌生人發笑"},{"english":"kind responses","chinese":"友善的回應"},{"english":"tagged their friends","chinese":"標記朋友"},{"english":"harsh words","chinese":"尖刻的說話"},{"english":"criticise my appearance","chinese":"批評我的外貌"},{"english":"criticise my voice","chinese":"批評我的聲音"},{"english":"trying too hard to be relatable","chinese":"太刻意想令人有共鳴"},{"english":"cringe","chinese":"尷尬得令人不舒服；肉麻；尷尬"},{"english":"strangers on the internet","chinese":"網絡上的陌生人"},{"english":"define me","chinese":"定義我"},{"english":"vulnerability","chinese":"脆弱感；容易受傷害的狀態"},{"english":"linger longer than praise","chinese":"比讚美停留得更久"},{"english":"think about success","chinese":"思考成功"},{"english":"reaching a finish line","chinese":"到達終點線"},{"english":"stepping onto a moving treadmill","chinese":"踏上一部移動中的跑步機"},{"english":"attention moves on","chinese":"注意力轉移"},{"english":"recognition is unreliable","chinese":"認可是靠不住的"},{"english":"main source of confidence","chinese":"自信的主要來源"},{"english":"self-worth","chinese":"自我價值"},{"english":"self-knowledge","chinese":"自我認識"},{"english":"chasing approval","chinese":"追逐認可"},{"english":"creativity","chinese":"創意"},{"english":"create something honest","chinese":"創作真誠的東西"},{"english":"connected with others","chinese":"與他人產生連結"},{"english":"humour","chinese":"幽默"},{"english":"view social media critically","chinese":"批判地看待社交媒體"},{"english":"view social media calmly","chinese":"冷靜地看待社交媒體"},{"english":"deeply instructive experience","chinese":"深具啟發性的經歷"},{"english":"After experiencing it myself","chinese":"在親身經歷之後"},{"english":"At first","chinese":"起初"},{"english":"Yet","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"In other words","chinese":"換句話說"},{"english":"What surprised me most was","chinese":"最令我驚訝的是"},{"english":"A second lesson came from","chinese":"第二個教訓來自"},{"english":"Most importantly","chinese":"最重要的是"},{"english":"In reality","chinese":"實際上"},{"english":"After all","chinese":"畢竟"},{"english":"Looking back","chinese":"回望過去"},{"english":"If there is one message I would like to leave with...","chinese":"如果有一個訊息我想留給……"}]},"dse-writing-2025-part-a":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2025-part-a","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2025-part-a","flashDeckId":"dse/writing/part-a/2025","paragraphs":[{"label":"Our background","english":"Our background","chinese":"我們的背景"},{"label":"Our background","english":"Founded by local artists and dedicated teachers, 852 Teen Art Club believes every teenager deserves a chance to express themselves through art. Over the years, we have welcomed students from different schools and backgrounds to explore painting, photography, ceramics and calligraphy in a friendly, inspiring environment. More than a place to learn techniques, the club helps young people exchange ideas, gain confidence, build friendships and discover their creative identity.","chinese":"852 Teen Art Club 由本地藝術家和敬業的老師創立，深信每一位青少年都應該有機會透過藝術表達自己。 多年來，我們歡迎來自不同學校和背景的學生，在一個友善而富啟發性的環境中探索繪畫、攝影、陶藝和書法。 本會不只是一個學習技巧的地方，更幫助年輕人交流想法、建立信心、建立友誼，並發掘自己的創意身份。"},{"label":"A club member’s most memorable experience","english":"A club member’s most memorable experience","chinese":"一位會員最難忘的經歷"},{"label":"A club member’s most memorable experience","english":"For Jason, a Secondary Four member, his most memorable experience was last summer’s community mural project. Although he had never painted on such a large wall before, encouragement from other members helped him step out of his comfort zone. His sketch of old Hong Kong streets became part of a colourful public mural. Seeing passers-by stop, smile and take photos gave him a deep sense of pride. As he said, art can speak to people and bring a community closer together.","chinese":"對中四會員 Jason 來說，他最難忘的經歷是去年夏天的社區壁畫計劃。 雖然他以前從未在這麼大的牆上作畫，但其他會員的鼓勵幫助他走出舒適圈。 他筆下舊香港街道的草圖，最終成為一幅色彩繽紛的公共壁畫的一部分。 看見途人停下腳步、露出笑容並拍照，令他產生了深深的自豪感。 正如他所說，藝術能夠與人溝通，並令社區更加團結。"},{"label":"Our future activities","english":"Our future activities","chinese":"我們未來的活動"},{"label":"Our future activities","english":"This term, members can join a street photography walk, a pottery workshop, an inter-school exhibition, museum visits and a charity art sale. Whether experienced or new to art, teenagers are welcome to explore their potential and let their creativity flourish.","chinese":"本學期，會員可以參加街頭攝影步行活動、陶藝工作坊、校際展覽、博物館參觀活動，以及慈善藝術義賣。 無論是有經驗，還是剛接觸藝術的青少年，我們都歡迎他們發掘自己的潛能，讓創意盡情綻放。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"founded by","chinese":"由……創立"},{"english":"local artists","chinese":"本地藝術家"},{"english":"dedicated teachers","chinese":"盡心盡力的老師"},{"english":"believe every teenager deserves","chinese":"相信每位青少年都值得……"},{"english":"deserve a chance to","chinese":"值得有機會去……"},{"english":"express themselves through art","chinese":"透過藝術表達自己"},{"english":"over the years","chinese":"多年來"},{"english":"welcome students from","chinese":"歡迎來自……的學生"},{"english":"different schools and backgrounds","chinese":"不同學校及背景"},{"english":"explore painting, photography, ceramics and calligraphy","chinese":"探索繪畫、攝影、陶藝及書法"},{"english":"painting","chinese":"繪畫"},{"english":"photography","chinese":"攝影"},{"english":"ceramics","chinese":"陶藝"},{"english":"calligraphy","chinese":"書法"},{"english":"friendly, inspiring environment","chinese":"友善而啟發人的環境"},{"english":"more than a place to","chinese":"不只是一個……的地方"},{"english":"learn techniques","chinese":"學習技巧"},{"english":"exchange ideas","chinese":"交流想法"},{"english":"gain confidence","chinese":"建立自信"},{"english":"build friendships","chinese":"建立友誼"},{"english":"discover their creative identity","chinese":"發掘自己的創意身份"},{"english":"a club member's most memorable experience","chinese":"一名會員最難忘的經歷"},{"english":"Secondary Four member","chinese":"中四會員"},{"english":"community mural project","chinese":"社區壁畫計劃"},{"english":"last summer's","chinese":"去年夏天的"},{"english":"although","chinese":"雖然"},{"english":"paint on such a large wall","chinese":"在如此大的牆上作畫"},{"english":"encouragement from","chinese":"來自……的鼓勵"},{"english":"step out of his comfort zone","chinese":"走出舒適圈"},{"english":"sketch of","chinese":"……的素描"},{"english":"old Hong Kong streets","chinese":"舊香港街道"},{"english":"become part of","chinese":"成為……的一部分"},{"english":"colourful public mural","chinese":"色彩繽紛的公共壁畫"},{"english":"passers-by","chinese":"路人"},{"english":"take photos","chinese":"拍照"},{"english":"give someone a deep sense of pride","chinese":"令某人深感自豪"},{"english":"a deep sense of pride","chinese":"深深的自豪感"},{"english":"art can speak to people","chinese":"藝術能打動人心"},{"english":"bring a community closer together","chinese":"拉近社區之間的距離"},{"english":"future activities","chinese":"未來活動"},{"english":"this term","chinese":"本學期"},{"english":"street photography walk","chinese":"街頭攝影漫步"},{"english":"pottery workshop","chinese":"陶藝工作坊"},{"english":"inter-school exhibition","chinese":"聯校展覽"},{"english":"museum visits","chinese":"博物館參觀活動"},{"english":"charity art sale","chinese":"慈善藝術義賣"},{"english":"whether experienced or new to art","chinese":"不論有經驗還是初學藝術"},{"english":"be welcome to","chinese":"歡迎……"},{"english":"explore their potential","chinese":"發掘自己的潛能"},{"english":"let their creativity flourish","chinese":"讓創意蓬勃發展"}]},"dse-writing-2025-part-b-q3":{"exerciseId":"dse-writing-2025-part-b-q3","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=dse-writing-2025-part-b-q3","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"Title","english":"When Eateries Become Classrooms","chinese":"當食肆變成課室"},{"label":"Salutation","english":"Dear Editor,","chinese":"尊敬的編輯："},{"label":"Intro","english":"In recent years, coffee shops and fast-food restaurants in Hong Kong have quietly taken on a new role. Besides serving meals, they are increasingly being used for lengthy activities such as tutorial lessons, mock interviews and worksheet drilling. In a city defined by cramped flats, soaring rents and limited public space, this trend may appear understandable at first glance. Yet it has also led restaurant owners, frontline staff and ordinary customers to ask whether private educational activities should be allowed to occupy commercial dining space for hours at a time. In my view, this practice should not be accepted as normal, because it places an unfair burden on businesses, inconveniences the public and conceals a deeper problem that Hong Kong should address properly. If we continue treating eateries as makeshift classrooms, we will not solve the city’s space problem; we will merely shift its cost onto others.","chinese":"近年來，香港的咖啡店和快餐店悄悄地承擔起了一種新的角色。 除了供應餐飲之外，它們也越來越常被用來進行長時間的活動，例如補習課、模擬面試以及反覆操練作業。 在一個以居住空間狹小、租金高昂以及公共空間有限為特徵的城市裡，這種趨勢乍看之下似乎可以理解。 然而，這也讓餐廳東主、前線員工以及一般顧客開始質疑，私人教育活動是否應該被允許一連數小時佔用商業餐飲空間。 在我看來，這種做法不應該被視為正常，因為它對商家造成不公平的負擔、為公眾帶來不便，並掩蓋了一個香港應該妥善處理的更深層問題。 如果我們繼續把食肆當成臨時教室，我們並不會解決這座城市的空間問題；我們只是把其代價轉嫁到別人身上而已。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"First, using restaurants as tutorial venues is fundamentally unfair to the businesses involved. A café or fast-food shop exists to serve diners efficiently, not to function as a low-cost classroom rented out through a single cup of coffee. When a tutor and several students occupy a four-person table for two or three hours after ordering the bare minimum, the shop loses far more than one seat. It loses turnover during peak hours, staff must manage lingering customers tactfully, and new diners may leave after seeing a lack of available tables. In Hong Kong, where rent and labour costs are notoriously high, such lost business is not a minor inconvenience but a real financial penalty. The problem becomes even worse once a venue develops a reputation as a “good place for tutoring”, because one lesson quickly attracts another. What begins as an individual choice can therefore become a systematic misuse of space. Put simply, tutors earn private income while restaurants absorb the hidden overhead. That is neither fair nor sustainable.","chinese":"首先，把餐廳當作補習場所，從根本上來說對相關商家並不公平。 咖啡店或快餐店存在的目的，是要有效率地服務用餐顧客，而不是透過一杯咖啡就被當成低成本教室來出租。 當一位補習老師和幾名學生只點最基本的餐飲，卻佔據一張四人桌兩三個小時時，店家失去的遠遠不只是一個座位。 店家在繁忙時段失去翻桌率，員工必須小心地處理久坐不走的顧客，而新來的食客看到沒有空位，也可能直接離開。 在香港這個租金與勞工成本都出名高昂的地方，這種生意損失不是小小的不便，而是真正的經濟懲罰。 一旦某個地點形成了「適合補習的好地方」這種名聲，問題就會變得更嚴重，因為一堂課很快就會吸引另一堂課。 因此，原本只是個人的選擇，最後可能演變成一種制度化的空間濫用。 簡單來說，補習老師賺取的是私人收入，而餐廳卻承擔了隱藏的營運成本。這既不公平，也無法長久持續。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Moreover, this habit damages the wider social environment and promotes the wrong values. Education should cultivate discipline, respect and social awareness. However, holding tutorial lessons in eateries often teaches the opposite lesson: that as long as one can pay for a drink, one may effectively privatise shared space. Other patrons then bear the consequences. Office workers on a short lunch break may struggle to find seats. Elderly customers who simply want a place to rest are squeezed out. Families with children may have to carry trays around crowded dining areas because several tables have already been turned into mini-classrooms covered in notes, pens and past papers. At the same time, the learning environment itself is far from ideal. The constant clatter of trays, background chatter and frequent interruptions are hardly conducive to serious concentration. Students may complete exercises, but they are also absorbing an unhealthy message: convenience matters more than consideration. A city already under pressure should not normalize behaviour that erodes everyday courtesy.","chinese":"此外，這種習慣會破壞更廣泛的社會環境，並傳遞錯誤的價值觀。 教育本應培養紀律、尊重以及社會意識。 然而，在食肆裡進行補習，往往教會人的卻是相反的一課：只要付得起一杯飲料的錢，就可以實際上把共享空間私有化。 接著，其他顧客便必須承受後果。 在短暫午休中的上班族，可能會很難找到座位。 只想找個地方稍作休息的長者，也會被擠出去。 帶著孩子的家庭，可能得端著餐盤在擁擠的用餐區四處尋找座位，因為好幾張桌子早已被變成堆滿筆記、筆和歷屆試題的小型教室。 同時，這種學習環境本身也遠遠稱不上理想。 餐盤碰撞的聲音、背景雜談，以及頻繁的干擾，幾乎不利於真正專心學習。 學生也許完成了練習，但他們同時也在吸收一個不健康的訊息：方便比體諒他人更重要。 一座本來就壓力沉重的城市，不應該把侵蝕日常禮貌的行為視為正常。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 3","english":"Admittedly, some people defend this practice by arguing that many Hong Kong students do not have quiet homes, while libraries and study rooms are often full. That concern is real and should not be dismissed. Nevertheless, sympathy should not become justification. The fact that proper study space is insufficient does not mean restaurants should be expected to fill the gap for free. That is the wrong solution to the right problem. If tutorial activities are genuinely necessary, then tutorial centres should rent appropriate premises, schools should open more classrooms after hours, and community centres or public libraries should expand accessible study areas during examination seasons. Allowing commercial eateries to become unofficial classrooms simply lets the private tutoring industry externalise its operating costs while avoiding responsibility. In other words, it relieves pressure for a few individuals but entrenches the larger structural problem for everyone else.","chinese":"誠然，有些人為這種做法辯護，理由是許多香港學生家中並沒有安靜的學習環境，而圖書館和自修室也常常爆滿。 這種憂慮是真實存在的，不應被忽視。 然而，同情不應該變成合理化的藉口。 適當的學習空間不足，並不代表餐廳就應該被期待免費填補這個缺口。 這是用錯誤的方法去處理正確的問題。 如果補習活動真的是必要的，那麼補習社就應該租用合適的場地，學校應該在課後開放更多課室，而社區中心或公共圖書館也應該在考試季擴充可供使用的溫習空間。 讓商業食肆變成非正式教室，實際上只是讓私人補習產業把營運成本外部化，同時逃避本應承擔的責任。 換句話說，這樣做或許減輕了少數人的壓力，卻讓更大的結構性問題對所有其他人更加根深蒂固。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I firmly believe that coffee shops and fast-food restaurants should not be treated as long-stay tutorial venues. Such a practice is unfair to businesses, inconsiderate to other customers and educationally misguided. Hong Kong needs proper answers, not improvised ones. Restaurant chains can introduce clearer seating policies, tutors should act more responsibly, and schools as well as the government should expand affordable study spaces so that students have somewhere suitable to learn without inconveniencing the public. If we truly care about both education and civic responsibility, we must stop pretending that a corner table and a cheap drink are an acceptable substitute for a real classroom.","chinese":"總而言之，我堅定相信咖啡店和快餐店不應該被當作可長時間逗留的補習場所。 這種做法對商家不公平、對其他顧客缺乏體諒，而且在教育上也有誤導之嫌。 香港需要的是妥善的解決方法，而不是臨時拼湊的權宜之計。 連鎖餐廳可以制定更清楚的座位使用政策，補習老師應該更負責任地行事，而學校與政府也應擴充可負擔的學習空間，讓學生能有適合學習的地方，同時不會打擾公眾。 如果我們真的同時重視教育與公民責任，我們就必須停止假裝角落裡的一張桌子和一杯便宜飲料，可以成為真正教室的合理替代品。"},{"label":"Closing","english":"Yours faithfully, Chris Wong","chinese":"此致敬禮， Chris Wong"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"eateries","chinese":"食肆；餐飲場所"},{"english":"coffee shops and fast-food restaurants","chinese":"咖啡店和快餐店"},{"english":"commercial dining space","chinese":"商業用餐空間"},{"english":"restaurant owners","chinese":"餐廳東主；食肆經營者"},{"english":"frontline staff","chinese":"前線員工"},{"english":"ordinary customers / other patrons","chinese":"普通顧客 / 其他顧客"},{"english":"diners","chinese":"食客；用餐人士"},{"english":"shared space","chinese":"共享空間"},{"english":"available tables","chinese":"可用餐桌；空桌"},{"english":"crowded dining areas","chinese":"擁擠的用餐區"},{"english":"corner table","chinese":"角落餐桌"},{"english":"a cheap drink","chinese":"一杯便宜飲品"},{"english":"private educational activities","chinese":"私人教育活動"},{"english":"tutorial lessons","chinese":"補習課"},{"english":"mock interviews","chinese":"模擬面試"},{"english":"worksheet drilling","chinese":"操練工作紙"},{"english":"tutorial venues","chinese":"補習場所"},{"english":"tutorial centres","chinese":"補習中心"},{"english":"the private tutoring industry","chinese":"私人補習行業"},{"english":"learning environment","chinese":"學習環境"},{"english":"serious concentration","chinese":"認真專注；深度集中"},{"english":"students may complete exercises","chinese":"學生可能完成練習"},{"english":"real classroom","chinese":"真正的課室"},{"english":"schools should open more classrooms after hours","chinese":"學校應在課後開放更多課室"},{"english":"community centres or public libraries","chinese":"社區中心或公共圖書館"},{"english":"cramped flats","chinese":"狹小單位；擠迫住所"},{"english":"soaring rents","chinese":"急升的租金；高昂租金"},{"english":"limited public space","chinese":"有限的公共空間"},{"english":"the city's space problem","chinese":"城市的空間問題"},{"english":"makeshift classrooms","chinese":"臨時課室；權宜課室"},{"english":"improvised answers","chinese":"臨時湊合的答案；權宜方法"},{"english":"proper study space","chinese":"合適學習空間"},{"english":"accessible study areas","chinese":"可使用的學習區域"},{"english":"suitable to learn","chinese":"適合學習"},{"english":"an unfair burden on businesses","chinese":"對商戶造成不公平負擔"},{"english":"low-cost classroom","chinese":"低成本課室"},{"english":"ordering the bare minimum","chinese":"只點最低限度的消費"},{"english":"the shop loses turnover","chinese":"店舖失去翻枱率 / 營業流轉"},{"english":"peak hours","chinese":"繁忙時段；高峰時段"},{"english":"lost business","chinese":"損失的生意"},{"english":"a real financial penalty","chinese":"真正的財務懲罰"},{"english":"hidden overhead","chinese":"隱藏營運成本"},{"english":"externalise operating costs","chinese":"將營運成本外部化 / 轉嫁給他人"},{"english":"neither fair nor sustainable","chinese":"既不公平，也不可持續"},{"english":"inconveniences the public","chinese":"妨礙公眾；令公眾不便"},{"english":"other patrons bear the consequences","chinese":"其他顧客承受後果"},{"english":"office workers on a short lunch break","chinese":"午飯時間短暫的上班族"},{"english":"elderly customers","chinese":"長者顧客"},{"english":"families with children","chinese":"帶著孩子的家庭"},{"english":"everyday courtesy","chinese":"日常禮貌；日常公德"},{"english":"civic responsibility","chinese":"公民責任"},{"english":"consideration","chinese":"為他人著想；體諒"},{"english":"social awareness","chinese":"社會意識"},{"english":"inconsiderate to other customers","chinese":"對其他顧客不體貼"},{"english":"promotes the wrong values","chinese":"宣揚錯誤價值觀"},{"english":"privatise shared space","chinese":"私有化共享空間"},{"english":"convenience matters more than consideration","chinese":"方便比體諒更重要"},{"english":"educationally misguided","chinese":"教育上方向錯誤的"},{"english":"normalize behaviour","chinese":"將行為正常化"},{"english":"the wrong solution to the right problem","chinese":"對正確問題作出錯誤解法"},{"english":"sympathy should not become justification","chinese":"同情不應變成合理化理由"},{"english":"in recent years","chinese":"近年"},{"english":"quietly taken on a new role","chinese":"悄悄承擔新角色"},{"english":"this trend may appear understandable at first glance","chinese":"這趨勢乍看可以理解"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"should not be accepted as normal","chinese":"不應被接受為正常做法"},{"english":"first","chinese":"首先"},{"english":"moreover","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"admittedly","chinese":"誠然；無可否認"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而；儘管如此"},{"english":"in other words","chinese":"換言之"},{"english":"in conclusion","chinese":"總而言之"},{"english":"if we truly care about","chinese":"如果我們真正關心……"}]},"hkpf-civic-composition-4":{"exerciseId":"hkpf-civic-composition-4","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=hkpf-civic-composition-4","flashDeckId":"government/hkpf/writing-composition/composition-4","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The proposal to raise the non-local student ceiling should be supported in principle, but not as a race for numbers. Hong Kong benefits when its universities attract bright students from the mainland, Asia and beyond: a more international campus can sharpen ideas, deepen cultural understanding and strengthen the city’s role as an education hub. However, the final arrangement must be built on one firm principle: local students must not lose opportunities in practice, even if their funded places remain unchanged on paper.","chinese":"提高非本地學生比例上限的建議，原則上值得支持，但它不應變成一場追逐數字的競賽。 當香港的大學能夠吸引來自內地、亞洲以至其他地區的優秀學生時，香港可以從中受益：一個更國際化的校園能夠激發思想、深化文化理解，並加強香港作為教育樞紐的角色。 然而，最終安排必須建立在一項堅定原則之上：即使本地學生的資助學額在紙面上維持不變，他們在實際上也不應失去機會。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main risk is that university life is more than admission quotas. Hostel rooms, laboratory space, tutorial attention, counselling services, exchange places and internships are all limited resources. If enrolment grows faster than capacity, the policy may look like a golden bridge but feel like a crowded corridor. Local students could then face stronger competition for campus opportunities, while non-local students may also receive weaker support after arrival. Therefore, the Government should require each university to conduct a capacity audit before further expansion is approved. Non-local tuition income should be partly ring-fenced for new hostel places, upgraded teaching facilities, mental health services, language support and career guidance. Clear indicators, such as hostel supply, staff-student ratios and internship availability, should be published annually.","chinese":"主要風險在於，大學生活並不只是取錄名額的問題。 宿舍房間、實驗室空間、小組教學關注、輔導服務、交換生名額和實習機會，全部都是有限資源。 如果收生增長快於大學承載能力，這項政策表面上可能像一座黃金橋樑，但實際感受卻可能像一條擠迫的走廊。 到時本地學生可能會在校園機會上面對更強競爭，而非本地學生抵港後也可能得不到足夠支援。 因此，政府應要求每所大學在批准進一步擴收之前，先進行承載能力審核。 非本地學生的學費收入應部分指定用於新增宿舍宿位、改善教學設施、加強心理健康服務、語言支援及就業輔導。 政府和大學亦應每年公布清晰指標，例如宿舍供應、師生比例及實習機會數量"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Universities should also manage the change through phased implementation rather than a sudden leap. They should set transparent rules for hostel allocation, exchange nominations and scholarship distribution, so that fairness is seen as well as claimed. At the same time, universities can work with employers, alumni and professional bodies to create more internships, mentoring schemes and community projects for both local and non-local students. In this way, internationalisation will not become a zero-sum game. With careful planning, honest communication and measurable safeguards, Hong Kong can open its doors wider without squeezing its own students out of the room.","chinese":"大學亦應透過分階段推行來管理這項轉變，而不是突然大幅擴展。 大學應就宿舍分配、交換生提名及獎學金分配訂立透明規則，讓公平不只是口頭承諾，而是清楚可見。 同時，大學可以與僱主、校友及專業團體合作，為本地和非本地學生創造更多實習、師友計劃和社區項目。 這樣一來，國際化便不會變成一場零和遊戲。 只要有周詳規劃、坦誠溝通和可量度的保障措施，香港便可以把大門開得更闊，而不會把本地學生擠出房間之外。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the proposal to raise","chinese":"提高……的建議"},{"english":"raise the non-local student ceiling","chinese":"提高非本地學生上限"},{"english":"non-local student ceiling","chinese":"非本地學生上限"},{"english":"be supported in principle","chinese":"原則上應支持"},{"english":"in principle","chinese":"原則上"},{"english":"not as a race for numbers","chinese":"不應變成追逐數字的競賽"},{"english":"a race for numbers","chinese":"追逐數字的競賽"},{"english":"Hong Kong benefits when","chinese":"當……時，香港會受惠"},{"english":"attract bright students","chinese":"吸引優秀學生"},{"english":"bright students","chinese":"優秀學生"},{"english":"from the mainland, Asia and beyond","chinese":"來自內地、亞洲及其他地區"},{"english":"the mainland","chinese":"內地"},{"english":"Asia and beyond","chinese":"亞洲及其他地區"},{"english":"a more international campus","chinese":"更國際化的校園"},{"english":"sharpen ideas","chinese":"激發思維；磨礪想法"},{"english":"deepen cultural understanding","chinese":"加深文化理解"},{"english":"strengthen the city's role as","chinese":"加強城市作為……的角色"},{"english":"the city's role as","chinese":"城市作為……的角色"},{"english":"an education hub","chinese":"教育樞紐"},{"english":"the final arrangement","chinese":"最終安排"},{"english":"be built on","chinese":"建基於……"},{"english":"one firm principle","chinese":"一個堅定原則"},{"english":"local students","chinese":"本地學生"},{"english":"lose opportunities in practice","chinese":"實際上失去機會"},{"english":"in practice","chinese":"實際上"},{"english":"funded places","chinese":"資助學額"},{"english":"remain unchanged on paper","chinese":"紙面上維持不變"},{"english":"on paper","chinese":"紙面上"},{"english":"the main risk","chinese":"主要風險"},{"english":"university life","chinese":"大學生活"},{"english":"more than admission quotas","chinese":"不只是收生限額"},{"english":"admission quotas","chinese":"收生限額"},{"english":"hostel rooms","chinese":"宿位"},{"english":"laboratory space","chinese":"實驗室空間"},{"english":"tutorial attention","chinese":"導修支援；導修課上的關注"},{"english":"counselling services","chinese":"輔導服務"},{"english":"exchange places","chinese":"交流名額"},{"english":"internships","chinese":"實習機會"},{"english":"limited resources","chinese":"有限資源"},{"english":"enrollment grows faster than capacity","chinese":"收生增長快於承載能力"},{"english":"capacity","chinese":"承載能力"},{"english":"look like a golden bridge","chinese":"看似一座黃金橋樑"},{"english":"feel like a crowded corridor","chinese":"感覺像一條擠迫走廊"},{"english":"a golden bridge","chinese":"黃金橋樑"},{"english":"a crowded corridor","chinese":"擠迫走廊"},{"english":"face stronger competition for","chinese":"面對更激烈的……競爭"},{"english":"stronger competition","chinese":"更激烈的競爭"},{"english":"campus opportunities","chinese":"校園機會"},{"english":"receive weaker support","chinese":"得到較弱支援"},{"english":"after arrival","chinese":"抵港後；到埗後"},{"english":"require each university to","chinese":"要求每間大學……"},{"english":"conduct a capacity audit","chinese":"進行承載能力審核"},{"english":"a capacity audit","chinese":"承載能力審核"},{"english":"before further expansion is approved","chinese":"在進一步擴展獲批之前"},{"english":"further expansion","chinese":"進一步擴展"},{"english":"be approved","chinese":"獲得批准"},{"english":"non-local tuition income","chinese":"非本地學生學費收入"},{"english":"be partly ring-fenced for","chinese":"部分撥作指定用途"},{"english":"ring-fenced","chinese":"指定用途的；專款專用的"},{"english":"new hostel places","chinese":"新宿位"},{"english":"upgraded teaching facilities","chinese":"升級後的教學設施"},{"english":"teaching facilities","chinese":"教學設施"},{"english":"mental health services","chinese":"精神健康服務"},{"english":"language support","chinese":"語言支援"},{"english":"career guidance","chinese":"就業輔導；職涯指導"},{"english":"clear indicators","chinese":"清晰指標"},{"english":"hostel supply","chinese":"宿位供應"},{"english":"staff-student ratios","chinese":"師生比例"},{"english":"internship availability","chinese":"實習機會供應情況"},{"english":"be published annually","chinese":"每年公布"},{"english":"manage the change","chinese":"管理這項轉變"},{"english":"phased implementation","chinese":"分階段實施"},{"english":"rather than a sudden leap","chinese":"而不是突然大幅躍進"},{"english":"a sudden leap","chinese":"突然大幅躍進"},{"english":"set transparent rules for","chinese":"為……訂立透明規則"},{"english":"transparent rules","chinese":"透明規則"},{"english":"hostel allocation","chinese":"宿位分配"},{"english":"exchange nominations","chinese":"交流提名"},{"english":"scholarship distribution","chinese":"獎學金分配"},{"english":"fairness is seen as well as claimed","chinese":"不但聲稱公平，也要讓人看見公平"},{"english":"as well as claimed","chinese":"不只是口頭聲稱"},{"english":"work with employers","chinese":"與僱主合作"},{"english":"employers","chinese":"僱主"},{"english":"alumni","chinese":"校友"},{"english":"professional bodies","chinese":"專業團體"},{"english":"create more internships","chinese":"創造更多實習機會"},{"english":"mentoring schemes","chinese":"導師計劃"},{"english":"community projects","chinese":"社區項目"},{"english":"for both local and non-local students","chinese":"為本地及非本地學生"},{"english":"internationalisation","chinese":"國際化"},{"english":"a zero-sum game","chinese":"零和遊戲"},{"english":"with careful planning","chinese":"透過周詳規劃"},{"english":"honest communication","chinese":"坦誠溝通"},{"english":"measurable safeguards","chinese":"可量度的保障措施"},{"english":"open its doors wider","chinese":"進一步開放大門"},{"english":"squeeze someone out of","chinese":"把某人擠出……"},{"english":"without squeezing its own students out of the room","chinese":"在不擠走本地學生的情況下"},{"english":"its own students","chinese":"本地學生；自己的學生"},{"english":"student numbers","chinese":"學生人數"},{"english":"put pressure on","chinese":"對……造成壓力"},{"english":"campus resources","chinese":"校園資源"},{"english":"keep up with","chinese":"跟上……"},{"english":"student growth","chinese":"學生人數增長"},{"english":"adapt to university life","chinese":"適應大學生活"},{"english":"invest more in","chinese":"加大投放於……"},{"english":"be used as a measure of","chinese":"被用作衡量……的指標"},{"english":"allocated","chinese":"被分配"},{"english":"career opportunities","chinese":"就業機會；職業發展機會"},{"english":"benefit the whole university community","chinese":"令整個大學社群受惠"},{"english":"reduce misunderstanding","chinese":"減少誤解"},{"english":"attract talent from elsewhere","chinese":"從其他地方吸引人才"}]},"hkpf-civic-composition-5":{"exerciseId":"hkpf-civic-composition-5","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=hkpf-civic-composition-5","flashDeckId":"government/hkpf/writing-composition/composition-5","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Hong Kong is competing with Singapore, Dubai and other financial centres for global capital, family offices and investment talent. In this context, expanding tax concessions for asset and wealth managers is understandable. The proposal should be supported in principle, but not as a blank cheque for the wealthy. The final scheme must attract genuine economic activity while protecting revenue, fairness and public confidence.","chinese":"香港正與新加坡、杜拜及其他金融中心競爭，以吸引全球資本、家族辦公室及投資人才 在這個背景下，擴大資產及財富管理行業的稅務優惠，是可以理解的。 原則上，這項建議值得支持，但它不應成為給富裕人士的「空白支票」。最終方案必須吸引真正的經濟活動，同時保障公共收入、稅制公平及公眾信心"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest argument for the proposal is that it could deepen Hong Kong’s asset-management ecosystem. Funds bring more than money; they create legal, accounting, compliance and banking work, and they help anchor skilled professionals in the city. Clearer carried-interest relief may encourage managers to place real decision-making teams in Hong Kong instead of using the city as a convenient label. However, the benefit should be earned, not simply handed out. The Government should require economic substance, such as local staff, local investment committees, audited operations and a minimum amount of assets managed from Hong Kong. Paper companies should not receive golden treatment.","chinese":"支持這項建議最有力的理由是，它可以深化香港的資產管理生態系統。 基金帶來的不只是資金；它們還會創造法律、會計、合規及銀行相關工作，並有助於吸引專業人才留在香港。 更清晰的附帶權益稅務寬免，可能會鼓勵基金經理把真正的決策團隊設在香港，而不是只把香港當作一個方便使用的名義標籤。 然而，這種優惠應該是憑實質貢獻而獲得，而不是簡單派發。 政府應要求受惠者具備實質經濟活動，例如本地員工、本地投資委員會、經審計的營運紀錄，以及一定規模由香港管理的資產。 空殼公司不應享有黃金待遇。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"At the same time, fairness concerns cannot be brushed aside. A tax break for wealthy investors can look like a private lift for those already on the top floor, especially when ordinary residents face heavy living costs. Therefore, the Financial Services and the Treasury Bureau, the Inland Revenue Department and regulators should shape the scheme through consultation, clear eligibility rules, anti-abuse tests and annual reporting. There should also be a sunset review, so ineffective concessions can be revised or withdrawn. Part of the extra economic gain should support financial-talent training, financial-crime compliance and public services. With firm safeguards, Hong Kong can open the door to quality capital without selling the house.","chinese":"與此同時，公平方面的憂慮不應被輕輕帶過。 在普通市民面對沉重生活成本的情況下，為富裕投資者提供稅務優惠，很容易看起來像是為本來已在頂層的人提供私人升降機。 因此，財經事務及庫務局、稅務局及相關監管機構應透過諮詢、清晰的資格要求、防濫用審查及年度匯報來制定最終方案。 方案亦應設有日落檢討機制，以便修改或撤回成效不佳的優惠安排。 部分額外經濟收益應用於支持金融人才培訓、金融罪案合規工作及公共服務。 只要設有穩固的保障，香港便可以向優質資本打開大門，而不必犧牲自身根基"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"compete with","chinese":"與……競爭"},{"english":"financial centres","chinese":"金融中心"},{"english":"global capital","chinese":"全球資本"},{"english":"family offices","chinese":"家族辦公室"},{"english":"investment talent","chinese":"投資人才"},{"english":"in this context","chinese":"在這個背景下"},{"english":"tax concessions","chinese":"稅務優惠"},{"english":"asset and wealth managers","chinese":"資產及財富管理人"},{"english":"understandable","chinese":"可以理解的"},{"english":"be supported in principle","chinese":"原則上應予支持"},{"english":"in principle","chinese":"原則上"},{"english":"a blank cheque for","chinese":"給予……的空白支票；無限制好處"},{"english":"the wealthy","chinese":"富裕人士"},{"english":"the final scheme","chinese":"最終方案"},{"english":"attract genuine economic activity","chinese":"吸引真正經濟活動"},{"english":"genuine economic activity","chinese":"真正經濟活動"},{"english":"protect revenue","chinese":"保障收入"},{"english":"fairness","chinese":"公平"},{"english":"public confidence","chinese":"公眾信心"},{"english":"the strongest argument for","chinese":"支持……的最有力論點"},{"english":"deepen Hong Kong's asset-management ecosystem","chinese":"深化香港資產管理生態系統"},{"english":"asset-management ecosystem","chinese":"資產管理生態系統"},{"english":"funds bring more than money","chinese":"基金帶來的不只是資金"},{"english":"legal, accounting, compliance and banking work","chinese":"法律、會計、合規及銀行工作"},{"english":"compliance","chinese":"合規"},{"english":"anchor skilled professionals in","chinese":"吸引並留住熟練專業人士於……"},{"english":"skilled professionals","chinese":"熟練專業人士"},{"english":"clearer carried-interest relief","chinese":"更清晰的附帶權益稅務寬免"},{"english":"carried-interest relief","chinese":"附帶權益稅務寬免"},{"english":"place real decision-making teams in","chinese":"將真正決策團隊設於……"},{"english":"real decision-making teams","chinese":"真正決策團隊"},{"english":"instead of using the city as","chinese":"而不是將該城市用作……"},{"english":"a convenient label","chinese":"方便的標籤"},{"english":"the benefit should be earned","chinese":"好處應靠實質貢獻換取"},{"english":"not simply handed out","chinese":"不是簡單派發"},{"english":"simply handed out","chinese":"直接派發；隨便給予"},{"english":"require economic substance","chinese":"要求經濟實質"},{"english":"economic substance","chinese":"經濟實質"},{"english":"local staff","chinese":"本地員工"},{"english":"local investment committees","chinese":"本地投資委員會"},{"english":"audited operations","chinese":"經審計的營運"},{"english":"a minimum amount of assets managed from Hong Kong","chinese":"從香港管理的最低資產規模"},{"english":"assets managed from Hong Kong","chinese":"從香港管理的資產"},{"english":"paper companies","chinese":"空殼公司"},{"english":"receive golden treatment","chinese":"獲得優厚待遇"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"與此同時"},{"english":"fairness concerns","chinese":"公平方面的關注"},{"english":"cannot be brushed aside","chinese":"不能被輕輕帶過；不能被忽視"},{"english":"a tax break for","chinese":"給予……的稅務減免"},{"english":"wealthy investors","chinese":"富裕投資者"},{"english":"look like a private lift for","chinese":"看起來像給……的私人升降機"},{"english":"already on the top floor","chinese":"已經位於最上層"},{"english":"ordinary residents","chinese":"普通市民"},{"english":"face heavy living costs","chinese":"面對沉重生活成本"},{"english":"the Financial Services and the Treasury Bureau","chinese":"財經事務及庫務局"},{"english":"the Inland Revenue Department","chinese":"稅務局"},{"english":"regulators","chinese":"監管機構"},{"english":"shape the scheme through consultation","chinese":"透過諮詢制定方案"},{"english":"consultation","chinese":"諮詢"},{"english":"clear eligibility rules","chinese":"清晰資格準則"},{"english":"eligibility rules","chinese":"資格準則"},{"english":"anti-abuse tests","chinese":"防濫用測試"},{"english":"annual reporting","chinese":"年度匯報"},{"english":"a sunset review","chinese":"日落檢討；定期屆滿檢討"},{"english":"ineffective concessions","chinese":"無效的稅務優惠"},{"english":"be revised or withdrawn","chinese":"被修訂或撤回"},{"english":"withdrawn","chinese":"撤回"},{"english":"extra economic gain","chinese":"額外經濟收益"},{"english":"support financial-talent training","chinese":"支持金融人才培訓"},{"english":"financial-talent training","chinese":"金融人才培訓"},{"english":"financial-crime compliance","chinese":"金融罪行合規工作"},{"english":"public services","chinese":"公共服務"},{"english":"with firm safeguards","chinese":"在有堅實保障措施下"},{"english":"firm safeguards","chinese":"堅實保障措施"},{"english":"open the door to","chinese":"向……打開大門"},{"english":"quality capital","chinese":"優質資本"},{"english":"without selling the house","chinese":"不犧牲自身根基；不賤賣家當"},{"english":"short-term money","chinese":"短期資金"},{"english":"protect fairness and public confidence","chinese":"保障公平和公眾信心"}]},"hkpf-civic-composition-6":{"exerciseId":"hkpf-civic-composition-6","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=hkpf-civic-composition-6","flashDeckId":"government/hkpf/writing-composition/composition-6","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Encouraging primary school mergers is a reasonable response to Hong Kong’s shrinking student population, but the final scheme must be handled with care, transparency and compassion. With some schools unable to admit even 16 Primary One pupils, maintaining every campus unchanged may stretch public resources and weaken students’ learning environment. Still, a school is not just bricks and walls; it is a small community built on trust.","chinese":"鼓勵小學合併，是應對香港學齡人口下降的一個合理方向；然而，最終方案必須以謹慎、透明和具同理心的方式處理。 由於部分學校甚至未能取錄十六名小一學生，若所有校舍都維持不變，可能會令公共資源承受壓力，亦會削弱學生的學習環境。 然而，學校並不只是磚牆與校舍；它是一個建立在信任之上的小社群。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One major concern is that a one-year grace period may be too short for schools to merge properly. Mergers involve far more than combining two nameplates. Principals must redesign classes, teachers may need redeployment, parents need reassurance, and young pupils require emotional support. Therefore, the Education Bureau should offer a three-year transition framework instead of a sudden countdown. Each merging school should submit a clear roadmap covering staffing, curriculum integration, student counselling, transport arrangements and parent communication. The Government should also provide targeted merger grants so that schools can upgrade facilities and support affected students. This would give schools breathing space rather than pushing them to jump before the ground is ready.","chinese":"一個主要憂慮是，一年的寬限期可能太短，未必足以讓學校妥善完成合併。 合併所涉及的，遠不只是把兩間學校的名字合在一起。 校長必須重新設計班級安排，教師可能需要重新調配，家長需要得到安心解釋，而年幼學生亦需要情緒支援。 因此，教育局應提供一個三年過渡框架，而不是只給學校一個突然開始倒數的期限。 每間準備合併的學校都應提交清晰路線圖，涵蓋人手安排、課程整合、學生輔導、交通安排及家長溝通。 政府亦應提供具針對性的合併津貼，讓學校能夠改善設施，並支援受影響的學生。 這樣做能給予學校喘息空間，而不是在基礎尚未準備好之前，迫使它們倉促跳下去。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The final scheme should also be district-based and child-centred. Clear criteria should be published to explain when merger, closure or special support will apply, so that parents do not feel decisions are made behind a closed door. Extra help should be given to pupils with special educational needs, low-income families and children in remote districts, because distance can become a silent barrier. Unused campuses should be converted into special education centres, after-school care hubs or community learning spaces. With careful planning, Hong Kong can reduce empty classrooms without abandoning children, teachers or neighbourhood trust.","chinese":"最終方案亦應以地區為本，並以兒童福祉為中心。 政府應公布清晰準則，說明在甚麼情況下會推動合併、停辦或提供特別支援，讓家長不會覺得決定是在閉門之後作出的。 政府應為有特殊教育需要的學生、低收入家庭及偏遠地區兒童提供額外支援，因為距離往往會成為一種無聲的障礙。 空置校舍應改作特殊教育中心、課後照顧中心或社區學習空間。 只要規劃周詳，香港既可以減少空置課室，也不必放棄學生、教師或社區信任"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"encouraging primary school mergers","chinese":"鼓勵小學合併"},{"english":"primary school mergers","chinese":"小學合併"},{"english":"a reasonable response to","chinese":"對……的合理回應"},{"english":"Hong Kong's shrinking student population","chinese":"香港學生人口萎縮"},{"english":"shrinking student population","chinese":"學生人口萎縮"},{"english":"the final scheme","chinese":"最終方案"},{"english":"be handled with care","chinese":"需要謹慎處理"},{"english":"transparency and compassion","chinese":"透明度與同理心"},{"english":"unable to admit","chinese":"未能取錄"},{"english":"Primary One pupils","chinese":"小一學生"},{"english":"maintaining every campus unchanged","chinese":"維持每個校舍不變"},{"english":"stretch public resources","chinese":"令公共資源吃緊"},{"english":"public resources","chinese":"公共資源"},{"english":"weaken students' learning environment","chinese":"削弱學生的學習環境"},{"english":"learning environment","chinese":"學習環境"},{"english":"bricks and walls","chinese":"磚牆；硬件建築"},{"english":"a small community","chinese":"一個小社群"},{"english":"built on trust","chinese":"建基於信任"},{"english":"one major concern","chinese":"一個主要憂慮"},{"english":"a one-year grace period","chinese":"一年寬限期"},{"english":"merge properly","chinese":"妥善合併"},{"english":"involve far more than","chinese":"遠不止於……"},{"english":"combining two nameplates","chinese":"合併兩塊校名牌"},{"english":"redesign classes","chinese":"重新設計班級安排"},{"english":"need redeployment","chinese":"需要重新調配"},{"english":"redeployment","chinese":"重新調配；調職安排"},{"english":"need reassurance","chinese":"需要安心；需要得到安撫"},{"english":"require emotional support","chinese":"需要情緒支援"},{"english":"emotional support","chinese":"情緒支援"},{"english":"the Education Bureau","chinese":"教育局"},{"english":"offer a three-year transition framework","chinese":"提供三年過渡框架"},{"english":"a three-year transition framework","chinese":"三年過渡框架"},{"english":"instead of a sudden countdown","chinese":"而不是突然倒數"},{"english":"a sudden countdown","chinese":"突然倒數；突然限期"},{"english":"each merging school","chinese":"每間合併中的學校"},{"english":"submit a clear roadmap","chinese":"提交清晰路線圖"},{"english":"a clear roadmap","chinese":"清晰路線圖"},{"english":"staffing","chinese":"人手安排"},{"english":"curriculum integration","chinese":"課程整合"},{"english":"student counselling","chinese":"學生輔導"},{"english":"transport arrangements","chinese":"交通安排"},{"english":"parent communication","chinese":"家長溝通"},{"english":"provide targeted merger grants","chinese":"提供具針對性的合併資助"},{"english":"targeted merger grants","chinese":"具針對性的合併資助"},{"english":"upgrade facilities","chinese":"改善設施；提升設施"},{"english":"support affected students","chinese":"支援受影響學生"},{"english":"affected students","chinese":"受影響學生"},{"english":"give schools breathing space","chinese":"給學校喘息空間"},{"english":"breathing space","chinese":"喘息空間"},{"english":"push someone to jump before the ground is ready","chinese":"在準備不足時迫使某人倉促行動"},{"english":"the ground is ready","chinese":"條件成熟"},{"english":"district-based","chinese":"以地區為本"},{"english":"child-centred","chinese":"以兒童為本"},{"english":"clear criteria","chinese":"清晰準則"},{"english":"be published","chinese":"被公布"},{"english":"merger, closure or special support","chinese":"合併、停辦或特別支援"},{"english":"special support","chinese":"特別支援"},{"english":"will apply","chinese":"適用"},{"english":"behind a closed door","chinese":"閉門作決定；暗中決定"},{"english":"extra help","chinese":"額外幫助"},{"english":"pupils with special educational needs","chinese":"有特殊教育需要的學生"},{"english":"special educational needs","chinese":"特殊教育需要"},{"english":"low-income families","chinese":"低收入家庭"},{"english":"remote districts","chinese":"偏遠地區"},{"english":"distance can become a silent barrier","chinese":"距離可以成為無聲障礙"},{"english":"a silent barrier","chinese":"無聲障礙；隱形障礙"},{"english":"unused campuses","chinese":"空置校舍"},{"english":"be converted into","chinese":"被改建成"},{"english":"special education centres","chinese":"特殊教育中心"},{"english":"after-school care hubs","chinese":"課後照顧中心"},{"english":"community learning spaces","chinese":"社區學習空間"},{"english":"with careful planning","chinese":"透過周詳規劃"},{"english":"reduce empty classrooms","chinese":"減少空置課室"},{"english":"without abandoning","chinese":"而不放棄……"},{"english":"neighbourhood trust","chinese":"社區信任"}]},"hkpf-civic-composition-7":{"exerciseId":"hkpf-civic-composition-7","essayKey":"","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=hkpf-civic-composition-7","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Hong Kong’s taxi trade has long been a vital part of public transport, but its payment practice has not always kept pace with a cashless city and a tourism-driven economy. The new requirement for taxi drivers to provide at least two electronic payment methods is therefore a reasonable step towards modernisation. It can make journeys smoother for tourists, office workers and younger passengers, while still preserving cash as a safety net. However, e-payment should be treated as a bridge to better service, not a magic wand.","chinese":"香港的的士行業一直是公共交通的重要一環，但其付款方式並不總是能夠跟上無現金城市和旅遊經濟的步伐。 因此，要求的士司機提供最少兩種電子支付方式，是邁向現代化的合理一步。 這可以令遊客、上班族和年輕乘客的乘車過程更加順暢，同時仍然保留現金作為安全網。然而，電子支付應被視為改善服務的橋樑，而不是一支能解決所有問題的魔法棒。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main benefit is convenience. When passengers can pay by QR code or card, they avoid the small but familiar frustration of having no cash, no change or no suitable banknotes. This is especially important for visitors, who may see taxis as the city’s moving front door. If the first ride feels slow, awkward or outdated, Hong Kong’s image suffers. To implement the policy effectively, the Government, payment operators and taxi associations should provide hands-on training, simple operating manuals, a driver hotline and short video demonstrations. Older drivers should not be left to wrestle with new machines like swimmers thrown into deep water.","chinese":"主要好處是便利。 當乘客可以透過二維碼或卡付款時，他們便可以避免沒有現金、沒有零錢或沒有合適紙幣這種雖小卻常見的煩惱。 這對旅客尤其重要，因為他們可能會把的士視為這座城市「流動的門面」。 如果他們第一次乘車時感到緩慢、尷尬或落後，香港的形象便會受損。 為了有效推行這項政策，政府、支付平台營辦商和的士業界組織應提供實務培訓、簡明操作手冊、司機支援熱線和簡短教學影片。 年長司機不應被迫獨自應付新設備，就像被扔進深水中的泳客一樣手足無措"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"At the same time, the policy must be practical and enforceable. Payment devices can fail, signals can be weak, and some drivers may fear transaction fees or technical disputes. Therefore, the Government should offer time-limited subsidies for approved devices, require clear stickers showing accepted payment methods, and set a grace period before strict penalties begin. Transport officers should focus first on education and repeated non-compliance, rather than heavy-handed punishment. More importantly, e-payment alone will not rescue poor service. Fare transparency, polite conduct, clean vehicles and an efficient complaint channel must develop hand in hand. With training, fair enforcement and wider service standards, this reform can modernise taxis without leaving drivers behind.","chinese":"同時，這項政策必須具備實際可行性和執法可操作性。 付款設備可能會故障，網絡訊號可能較弱，而部分司機亦可能擔心交易費用或技術爭議。 因此，政府應為認可設備提供有時限的資助，要求車廂內張貼清晰標示以顯示可接受的付款方式，並在嚴格罰則實施前設立寬限期。 運輸部門人員應先著重教育和處理屢次違規個案，而不是一開始便採取高壓式懲罰。 更重要的是，單靠電子支付並不能拯救差劣服務。 收費透明度、禮貌態度、車廂整潔和高效投訴渠道必須同步發展。 只要有培訓、公平執法和更全面的服務標準，這項改革便能令的士服務現代化，同時不會把司機拋在後面。"}],"vocabulary":[]},"model-essay-1-ielts-task1-bar-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-1-ielts-task1-bar-charts","essayKey":"bar-charts:1","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-1-ielts-task1-bar-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/bar-charts/bar-chart-1","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The bar chart compares the number of US households, measured in millions, across five annual income bands in 2007, 2011 and 2015.","chinese":"這張柱狀圖比較了 2007 年、 2011 年和 2015 年美國家庭在五個年收入組別中的數量，單位為百萬戶。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the distribution was dominated by households earning below $50,000 and by those earning $100,000 or more, while the two middle-income groups were consistently smaller. The highest-income category became clearly the largest by 2015, whereas the $75,000–$99,999 group remained the least common throughout.","chinese":"整體而言，年收入低於 50,000 美元的家庭以及年收入 100,000 美元或以上的家庭佔比較大，而兩個中等收入組別的家庭數量一直較少。 到 2015 年，最高收入組別明顯成為最大的類別；相反， 75,000 至 99,999 美元收入組在整段期間都是最少見的組別。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 2007, about 25 million households earned under $25,000, compared with roughly 27 million in the $25,000–$49,999 bracket. Both groups increased by 2011, reaching just under 29 million and around 30 million, respectively. By 2015, they had edged down slightly, to approximately 28 million and 29 million, although they were still among the largest categories.","chinese":"在 2007 年，約有 2,500 萬戶家庭年收入低於 25,000 美元，而 25,000 至 49,999 美元收入組則約有 2,700 萬戶。 到 2011 年，這兩個組別均有所上升，分別達到接近 2,900 萬戶和約 3,000 萬戶。 到 2015 年，兩者都輕微回落，分別降至約 2,800 萬戶和 2,900 萬戶，但它們仍然屬於最大的組別之一。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The remaining three bands showed less uniform movement. The number of households earning $50,000–$74,999 stayed almost unchanged at about 21 million in all three years. Those in the $75,000–$99,999 range were consistently the smallest group, at around 14–15 million. By contrast, households with incomes of at least $100,000 dipped from about 29 million to 28 million in 2011, before rising sharply to approximately 33 million in 2015.","chinese":"其餘三個收入組別的變化則沒有那麼一致。 年收入 50,000 至 74,999 美元的家庭數量在三個年份中幾乎沒有變化，均約為2,100 萬戶。 年收入 75,000 至 99,999 美元的家庭一直是最小的組別，數量約為 1,400 萬至1,500 萬戶。 相比之下，年收入至少 100,000 美元的家庭數量先從約 2,900 萬戶下降至 2011年的 2,800 萬戶，之後在 2015 年大幅上升至約 3,300 萬戶。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the bar chart compares","chinese":"柱形圖比較"},{"english":"the number of US households","chinese":"美國住戶數目"},{"english":"measured in millions","chinese":"以百萬計"},{"english":"across five annual income bands","chinese":"涵蓋五個全年收入組別"},{"english":"annual income bands","chinese":"全年收入組別"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"the distribution was dominated by","chinese":"分佈主要由……佔主導"},{"english":"households earning below $50,000","chinese":"年收入低於50,000美元的住戶"},{"english":"earning $100,000 or more","chinese":"年收入達100,000美元或以上"},{"english":"middle-income groups","chinese":"中等收入組別"},{"english":"were consistently smaller","chinese":"一直較少"},{"english":"the highest-income category","chinese":"最高收入類別"},{"english":"became clearly the largest","chinese":"明顯成為最大類別"},{"english":"by 2015","chinese":"到2015年"},{"english":"the $75,000–$99,999 group","chinese":"75,000至99,999美元組別"},{"english":"remained the least common throughout","chinese":"全期一直最少見"},{"english":"In 2007","chinese":"在2007年"},{"english":"about 25 million households","chinese":"約2,500萬戶"},{"english":"earned under $25,000","chinese":"年收入低於25,000美元"},{"english":"compared with","chinese":"與……相比"},{"english":"roughly 27 million","chinese":"約2,700萬"},{"english":"the $25,000–$49,999 bracket","chinese":"25,000至49,999美元組別"},{"english":"both groups increased","chinese":"兩個組別均有所增加"},{"english":"by 2011","chinese":"到2011年"},{"english":"reaching just under 29 million","chinese":"達到略低於2,900萬"},{"english":"around 30 million","chinese":"約3,000萬"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"edged down slightly","chinese":"輕微下降"},{"english":"to approximately 28 million","chinese":"至約2,800萬"},{"english":"although","chinese":"雖然；儘管"},{"english":"still among the largest categories","chinese":"仍屬最大類別之一"},{"english":"the remaining three bands","chinese":"其餘三個組別"},{"english":"showed less uniform movement","chinese":"走勢較不一致"},{"english":"households earning $50,000–$74,999","chinese":"年收入50,000至74,999美元的住戶"},{"english":"stayed almost unchanged","chinese":"幾乎維持不變"},{"english":"at about 21 million","chinese":"約2,100萬"},{"english":"in all three years","chinese":"在三個年份中"},{"english":"those in the $75,000–$99,999 range","chinese":"75,000至99,999美元範圍內的住戶"},{"english":"consistently the smallest group","chinese":"一直是最小組別"},{"english":"at around 14–15 million","chinese":"約1,400萬至1,500萬"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"households with incomes of at least $100,000","chinese":"收入最少100,000美元的住戶"},{"english":"dipped from about 29 million to 28 million","chinese":"由約2,900萬跌至2,800萬"},{"english":"before rising sharply to","chinese":"隨後急升至"},{"english":"approximately 33 million","chinese":"約3,300萬"}]},"model-essay-1-ielts-task1-line-graph":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-1-ielts-task1-line-graph","essayKey":"line-graph:1","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-1-ielts-task1-line-graph","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/line-graphs/line-graph-1","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The line graph illustrates the number of participants in five activities at a social centre in Melbourne, Australia, from 2000 to 2020.","chinese":"這張折線圖說明了澳洲墨爾本一所社交中心在 2000 年至 2020 年間五項活動的參加人數。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the film club remained the leading activity throughout, despite minor fluctuations. Table tennis recorded by far the most dramatic growth and became second by 2020, whereas amateur dramatics declined after a brief rise and finished as the least popular option.","chinese":"整體而言，電影俱樂部雖然有輕微波動，但在整個期間一直是參加人數最多的活動。 乒乓球的增長幅度明顯最大，並在 2020 年成為第二受歡迎的活動；相反，業餘戲劇在短暫上升後下跌，最後成為最不受歡迎的選項。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 2000, around 65 people attended the film club, compared with 36 for martial arts and 26 for amateur dramatics. The film club then dipped slightly to 60 in 2010 before recovering to about 66 at the end of the period. Martial arts showed no clear long-term change: after falling to 32 in 2005, it rose to 38 in 2010 and ended close to its starting point, at roughly 36.","chinese":"在 2000 年，約有 65 人參加電影俱樂部，相比之下，武術約有 36 人，而業餘戲劇約有 26 人。 之後，電影俱樂部的人數在 2010 年小幅下降至 60 人，然後在期末回升至約 66人。 武術沒有明顯的長期變化：它在 2005 年跌至 32 人後，於 2010 年升至 38 人，最後以約 36 人結束，接近起點水平。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The remaining activities changed more noticeably. Table tennis increased only modestly from 16 to 20 participants between 2000 and 2010, but then climbed sharply to 35 in 2015 and approximately 54 in 2020. Musical performances, which had no participants in the first two years shown, rose gradually to 18. By contrast, amateur dramatics fell from a peak of 28 in 2005 to just 6 by 2020.","chinese":"其餘活動的變化則更加明顯。 乒乓球在 2000 年至 2010 年間只從 16 人小幅增加至 20 人，但之後迅速上升，在2015 年達到 35 人，並在 2020 年達到約 54 人。 音樂表演在圖中最初兩個年份沒有參加者，但之後逐漸上升至 18 人。 相比之下，業餘戲劇從 2005 年的峰值 28 人下降至 2020 年的僅 6 人。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"The line graph illustrates","chinese":"折線圖顯示"},{"english":"the number of participants","chinese":"參加者人數"},{"english":"participants in five activities","chinese":"五項活動的參加者"},{"english":"at a social centre","chinese":"在一間社交中心"},{"english":"from 2000 to 2020","chinese":"從2000年至2020年"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"the film club","chinese":"電影俱樂部"},{"english":"remained the leading activity","chinese":"仍然是最受歡迎的活動"},{"english":"throughout","chinese":"整個期間"},{"english":"despite minor fluctuations","chinese":"儘管有輕微波動"},{"english":"minor fluctuations","chinese":"輕微波動"},{"english":"table tennis","chinese":"乒乓球"},{"english":"recorded by far the most dramatic growth","chinese":"錄得遠遠最顯著的增長"},{"english":"the most dramatic growth","chinese":"最顯著的增長"},{"english":"became second by 2020","chinese":"到2020年成為第二位"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；然而"},{"english":"amateur dramatics","chinese":"業餘戲劇"},{"english":"declined after a brief rise","chinese":"在短暫上升後下降"},{"english":"a brief rise","chinese":"短暫上升"},{"english":"finished as the least popular option","chinese":"最後成為最不受歡迎的選項"},{"english":"the least popular option","chinese":"最不受歡迎的選項"},{"english":"around 65 people attended","chinese":"約65人參加"},{"english":"attended the film club","chinese":"參加電影俱樂部"},{"english":"compared with","chinese":"與……相比"},{"english":"martial arts","chinese":"武術"},{"english":"amateur dramatics","chinese":"業餘戲劇"},{"english":"dipped slightly to 60","chinese":"輕微下降至60"},{"english":"before recovering to","chinese":"隨後回升至"},{"english":"recovering to about 66","chinese":"回升至約66"},{"english":"at the end of the period","chinese":"在期末"},{"english":"showed no clear long-term change","chinese":"沒有明顯長期變化"},{"english":"long-term change","chinese":"長期變化"},{"english":"after falling to 32","chinese":"在跌至32後"},{"english":"rose to 38","chinese":"上升至38"},{"english":"ended close to its starting point","chinese":"最終接近起點水平"},{"english":"its starting point","chinese":"其起點水平"},{"english":"at roughly 36","chinese":"約為36"},{"english":"the remaining activities","chinese":"其餘活動"},{"english":"changed more noticeably","chinese":"變化更明顯"},{"english":"increased only modestly","chinese":"只輕微增加"},{"english":"from 16 to 20 participants","chinese":"由16名增至20名參加者"},{"english":"between 2000 and 2010","chinese":"在2000年至2010年間"},{"english":"climbed sharply to 35","chinese":"急升至35"},{"english":"approximately 54","chinese":"約54"},{"english":"musical performances","chinese":"音樂表演"},{"english":"had no participants","chinese":"沒有參加者"},{"english":"the first two years shown","chinese":"圖中顯示的首兩年"},{"english":"rose gradually to 18","chinese":"逐步上升至18"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"fell from a peak of 28","chinese":"從28的高峰下跌"},{"english":"a peak of 28","chinese":"28的高峰"},{"english":"to just 6 by 2020","chinese":"到2020年跌至僅6"}]},"model-essay-1-ielts-task1-maps":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-1-ielts-task1-maps","essayKey":"maps:1","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-1-ielts-task1-maps","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/maps/maps-1","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The two plans illustrate the layout of Beechwood Farm in 1950 and the arrangement of the same site today.","chinese":"這兩張平面圖展示了比奇伍德農場在 1950 年的佈局，以及同一地點現今的安排。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the farm has been transformed from a mainly agricultural site into a more diversified complex. The river, main road, farmhouse, chicken enclosure and three crop areas have been retained, whereas the sheep field and basic tracks have given way to roads, visitor facilities and solar panels.","chinese":"整體而言，該農場已由一個主要用於農業的地點，轉變成一個功能更多元化的綜合場地。 河流、主要道路、農舍、雞舍和三個種植區都被保留下來；相反，原本的羊群牧場和簡單小徑則已被道路、遊客設施和太陽能板取代。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 1950, the western half was used for crops: fruit trees lay in the northwest, with soft fruits and vegetables in adjacent plots to the south. A large sheep field occupied most of the north-eastern area. Access was provided only by tracks, one running from the main road towards the barn and another leading to the farmhouse. The farmhouse stood in the southeast, just above the chickens and inside the bend of the river.","chinese":"在 1950 年，西半部主要用作種植農作物：果樹位於西北部，而漿果類作物和蔬菜則分別位於其南面的相鄰地塊。 一大片羊群牧場佔據了東北部的大部分地方。 當時的通道只由小徑提供，其中一條由主要道路通往穀倉，另一條則通向農舍。 農舍位於東南部，正好在雞舍上方，並坐落於河流彎曲處的內側。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Today, the crop plots remain in similar positions, but a farm shop and car park have been added near the entrance. The former sheep pasture is now divided between a camping field and a solar-panel area, with another car park nearby. In the east, holiday cottages have been built above the farmhouse, while the barn has been moved south-west.","chinese":"現今，農作物地塊仍大致保留在相似的位置，但入口附近新增了一間農場商店和一個停車場。 昔日的羊群牧場現在被分成露營地和太陽能板區，附近還設有另一個停車場。 在東部，度假小屋已建於農舍上方，而穀倉則被移至西南方向。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the plans below","chinese":"以下平面圖"},{"english":"the site of a farm","chinese":"一個農場的所在地"},{"english":"the same site today","chinese":"現今同一地點"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"by selecting and reporting","chinese":"透過選取並報告……"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"illustrate the layout of","chinese":"展示……的佈局"},{"english":"the arrangement of","chinese":"……的安排；佈局"},{"english":"has been transformed from","chinese":"已由……轉變"},{"english":"a mainly agricultural site","chinese":"以農業為主的場地"},{"english":"a more diversified complex","chinese":"更多元化的綜合場地"},{"english":"have been retained","chinese":"得以保留"},{"english":"chicken enclosure","chinese":"雞隻圍欄區"},{"english":"crop areas","chinese":"作物種植區"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相反"},{"english":"have given way to","chinese":"已讓位予……；被……取代"},{"english":"basic tracks","chinese":"簡單小路；基本路徑"},{"english":"visitor facilities","chinese":"遊客設施"},{"english":"solar panels","chinese":"太陽能板"},{"english":"the western half","chinese":"西半部"},{"english":"was used for crops","chinese":"被用作種植作物"},{"english":"fruit trees","chinese":"果樹"},{"english":"lay in the north-west","chinese":"位於西北面"},{"english":"soft fruits","chinese":"軟果類水果"},{"english":"adjacent plots","chinese":"相鄰地塊"},{"english":"to the south","chinese":"在南面"},{"english":"a large sheep field","chinese":"大型羊群牧場"},{"english":"occupied most of","chinese":"佔據……的大部分"},{"english":"the north-eastern area","chinese":"東北部地區"},{"english":"access was provided by","chinese":"通道由……提供"},{"english":"running from…towards…","chinese":"由……伸延至……"},{"english":"the main road","chinese":"主要道路"},{"english":"leading to","chinese":"通往……"},{"english":"the farmhouse","chinese":"農舍"},{"english":"stood in the south-east","chinese":"位於東南面"},{"english":"just above","chinese":"就在……上方"},{"english":"inside the bend of the river","chinese":"位於河道彎位之內"},{"english":"crop plots","chinese":"作物地塊"},{"english":"remain in similar positions","chinese":"保持在相若位置"},{"english":"have been added near","chinese":"已在……附近增設"},{"english":"near the entrance","chinese":"在入口附近"},{"english":"farm shop","chinese":"農場商店"},{"english":"car park","chinese":"停車場"},{"english":"the former sheep pasture","chinese":"昔日的牧羊草地"},{"english":"is now divided between","chinese":"現時分為……"},{"english":"camping field","chinese":"露營場地"},{"english":"solar-panel area","chinese":"太陽能板區"},{"english":"with another car park nearby","chinese":"附近另有一個停車場"},{"english":"in the east","chinese":"在東面"},{"english":"holiday cottages","chinese":"度假小屋"},{"english":"have been built above","chinese":"已建於……上方"},{"english":"the barn","chinese":"穀倉"},{"english":"has been moved south-west","chinese":"已遷往西南面"},{"english":"a more developed road system","chinese":"更完善的道路系統"},{"english":"replaced by","chinese":"被……取代"},{"english":"tourist and energy-related facilities","chinese":"旅遊及能源相關設施"}]},"model-essay-1-ielts-task1-mixed-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-1-ielts-task1-mixed-charts","essayKey":"mixed-charts:1","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-1-ielts-task1-mixed-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/mixed-charts/mixed-charts-1","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The graphics summarise Little Chalfont Library’s age profile, loan categories in 2016, and annual loan totals from 2007 to 2016.","chinese":"這些圖表概述了 Little Chalfont Library 的會員年齡分布、2016年的借閱類別，以及2007年至2016年間每年的總借閱量。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, adults aged 18–64 made up the majority of members, while fiction was by far the dominant type of borrowing. Total lending rose across the period, despite a brief dip around 2013.","chinese":"整體而言，18至64歲的成年人佔會員的大多數，而小說明顯是最主要的借閱類型。 儘管在2013年前後曾短暫下降，整體借閱量在整段期間仍然上升。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 2016, adults aged 18–64 accounted for 51% of members, more than twice the share of children, at 22%. Young adults and people aged 65 or over were smaller groups, at 15% and 12% respectively. Loans were concentrated in two categories: children’s fiction and adult fiction each represented 38%, together making up just over three quarters of all borrowing. Adult non-fiction was next, at 13%, whereas children’s non-fiction accounted for only 6%. Young adults and adult audio books stood at 2% each, and children’s DVDs were negligible, at 1%.","chinese":"在2016年，18至64歲的成年人佔會員的51%，是兒童比例22%的兩倍多。 青年成人和65歲或以上人士則是較小的群體，分別佔15%和12%。 借閱主要集中在兩個類別：兒童小說和成人小說各佔38%，兩者合計佔全部借閱量的四分之三多一點。 成人非小說類排在其後，佔13%；相比之下，兒童非小說類只佔6%。 青年成人類和成人有聲書各佔2%，而兒童 DVDs 幾乎可以忽略，只佔1%。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Annual loans increased from just under 16,000 in 2007 to about 19,000 in 2008 and 2009. The figure then stayed mostly above 20,000 until 2012, fell slightly below this level in 2013, and recovered steadily to a peak of roughly 21,500 in 2016.","chinese":"每年借閱量由2007年的略低於16,000次，上升至2008年和2009年的約19,000次。 此後，該數字到2012年大多維持在20,000次以上，2013年略跌至此水平以下，然後穩步回升，並在2016年達到約21,500次的高峰。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"give information about","chinese":"提供關於……的資料"},{"english":"a public library","chinese":"公共圖書館"},{"english":"a town called","chinese":"一個名為……的小鎮"},{"english":"Little Chalfont","chinese":"Little Chalfont"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"selecting and reporting","chinese":"選取並報告"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"the charts summarise","chinese":"圖表概述"},{"english":"age profile","chinese":"年齡分佈"},{"english":"loan categories","chinese":"借閱類別"},{"english":"annual loan totals","chinese":"每年借出總數"},{"english":"from 2007 to 2016","chinese":"由2007年至2016年"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"adults aged 18–64","chinese":"18至64歲的成年人"},{"english":"made up the majority of","chinese":"佔……的大多數"},{"english":"library members","chinese":"圖書館會員"},{"english":"while","chinese":"而"},{"english":"fiction","chinese":"小說"},{"english":"by far the dominant type of","chinese":"遠遠是最主要的……類型"},{"english":"type of borrowing","chinese":"借閱類型"},{"english":"total lending","chinese":"總借出量"},{"english":"rose across the period","chinese":"在整個時期內上升"},{"english":"despite a brief dip","chinese":"儘管短暫下跌"},{"english":"a brief dip around","chinese":"在……左右短暫下跌"},{"english":"In 2016","chinese":"在2016年"},{"english":"accounted for 51% of","chinese":"佔……的51%"},{"english":"more than twice the share of","chinese":"超過……比例的兩倍"},{"english":"the share of children","chinese":"兒童所佔比例"},{"english":"at 22%","chinese":"為22%"},{"english":"young adults","chinese":"青年成年人"},{"english":"people aged 65 or over","chinese":"65歲或以上人士"},{"english":"smaller groups","chinese":"較小的群組"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"were concentrated in","chinese":"集中於"},{"english":"children's fiction","chinese":"兒童小說"},{"english":"adult fiction","chinese":"成人小說"},{"english":"each represented 38%","chinese":"各佔38%"},{"english":"represented","chinese":"佔"},{"english":"together making up","chinese":"合共佔"},{"english":"just over three quarters of","chinese":"略高於四分之三"},{"english":"all borrowing","chinese":"所有借閱量"},{"english":"adult non-fiction","chinese":"成人非小說類書籍"},{"english":"was next","chinese":"其次是"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相比之下"},{"english":"children's non-fiction","chinese":"兒童非小說類書籍"},{"english":"accounted for only","chinese":"僅佔"},{"english":"young adult books","chinese":"青年讀物"},{"english":"adult audio books","chinese":"成人有聲書"},{"english":"stood at 2% each","chinese":"各為2%"},{"english":"children's DVDs","chinese":"兒童DVD"},{"english":"were negligible","chinese":"微不足道"},{"english":"at 1%","chinese":"為1%"},{"english":"annual loans","chinese":"每年借出量"},{"english":"increased from … to …","chinese":"由……增加至……"},{"english":"just under 16,000","chinese":"略低於16,000"},{"english":"about 19,000","chinese":"約19,000"},{"english":"the figure then","chinese":"其後該數字"},{"english":"stayed mostly above","chinese":"大多保持在……以上"},{"english":"above 20,000","chinese":"高於20,000"},{"english":"until 2012","chinese":"直到2012年"},{"english":"fell slightly below","chinese":"略跌至……以下"},{"english":"this level","chinese":"這一水平"},{"english":"recovered steadily","chinese":"穩步回升"},{"english":"to a peak of","chinese":"達到……的高峰"},{"english":"roughly 21,500","chinese":"約21,500"}]},"model-essay-1-ielts-task1-pie-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-1-ielts-task1-pie-charts","essayKey":"pie-charts:1","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-1-ielts-task1-pie-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/pie-charts/pie-chart-1","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The three pie charts compare the average shares of sodium, saturated fat and added sugar consumed at breakfast, lunch, dinner and snack times in the USA.","chinese":"這三個圓餅圖比較了美國人在早餐、午餐、晚餐和零食時間中攝入的鈉、飽和脂肪和添加糖的平均比例。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, dinner is the main contributor to sodium and saturated fat intake, whereas snacks account for the greatest proportion of added sugar. Breakfast consistently makes the smallest, or joint-smallest, contribution, while lunch occupies an intermediate position across all three nutrients.","chinese":"整體而言，晚餐是鈉和飽和脂肪攝入的主要來源，而零食則佔添加糖的最大比例。 早餐在各項中一直佔最小或並列最小比例，而午餐在三種營養素中大致處於中間位置。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Breakfast is comparatively light in all categories, representing 14% of sodium and 16% of both saturated fat and added sugar. Lunch contributes noticeably more sodium and saturated fat, at 29% and 26% respectively, but its share of added sugar is lower, at 19%. Thus, these two earlier meals are generally less dominant than the later ones, although lunch is still a substantial source of sodium.","chinese":"早餐在所有類別中所佔比例都相對較低，分別佔鈉的 14% ，以及飽和脂肪和添加糖的 16% 。 午餐所佔的鈉和飽和脂肪比例明顯較高，分別為 29% 和 26% ，但其添加糖比例較低，為 19% 。 因此，這兩個較早的餐次整體上不及較晚的餐次突出，不過午餐仍然是鈉的一個重要來源。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Dinner is the most sodium-heavy meal, with its share reaching 43%, and it also leads saturated fat consumption at 37%. Its contribution to added sugar, however, is much lower, at 23%. Snacks show the reverse pattern: they account for only 14% of sodium and 21% of saturated fat, but dominate added sugar at 42%, almost double the dinner figure.","chinese":"晚餐是含鈉比例最高的一餐，佔 43% ，同時也以 37% 成為飽和脂肪比例最高的一餐。 然而，它在添加糖方面的比例低得多，只有 23% 。 零食則呈現相反模式：它們只佔鈉的 14% 和飽和脂肪的 21% ，但在添加糖方面佔主導地位，達到 42% ，幾乎是晚餐比例的兩倍。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the three pie charts compare","chinese":"三個圓形圖比較"},{"english":"the average shares of","chinese":"平均所佔比例"},{"english":"sodium","chinese":"鈉"},{"english":"saturated fat","chinese":"飽和脂肪"},{"english":"added sugar","chinese":"添加糖"},{"english":"consumed at breakfast","chinese":"在早餐時攝取"},{"english":"snack times","chinese":"小食時間"},{"english":"in the USA","chinese":"在美國"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"the main contributor to","chinese":"……的主要來源"},{"english":"sodium and saturated fat intake","chinese":"鈉和飽和脂肪攝取量"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"然而；而"},{"english":"account for the greatest proportion of","chinese":"佔……的最大比例"},{"english":"the greatest proportion of added sugar","chinese":"添加糖的最大比例"},{"english":"consistently makes the smallest contribution","chinese":"一直作出最小貢獻"},{"english":"joint-smallest contribution","chinese":"並列最小貢獻"},{"english":"while","chinese":"而；同時"},{"english":"occupies an intermediate position","chinese":"處於中間位置"},{"english":"across all three nutrients","chinese":"在三種營養成分中"},{"english":"comparatively light","chinese":"相對較少"},{"english":"in all categories","chinese":"在所有類別中"},{"english":"representing 14% of sodium","chinese":"佔鈉攝取量的14%"},{"english":"16% of both saturated fat and added sugar","chinese":"飽和脂肪和添加糖均佔16%"},{"english":"contributes noticeably more","chinese":"貢獻明顯較多"},{"english":"at 29% and 26% respectively","chinese":"分別為29%和26%"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"its share of added sugar","chinese":"其添加糖所佔比例"},{"english":"is lower, at 19%","chinese":"較低，為19%"},{"english":"Thus","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"these two earlier meals","chinese":"這兩個較早進食的餐次"},{"english":"generally less dominant than","chinese":"一般不及……佔主導"},{"english":"the later ones","chinese":"較後的餐次"},{"english":"although","chinese":"雖然；儘管"},{"english":"a substantial source of sodium","chinese":"鈉的重要來源"},{"english":"Dinner is the most sodium-heavy meal","chinese":"晚餐是含鈉比例最高的一餐"},{"english":"sodium-heavy meal","chinese":"含鈉比例高的一餐"},{"english":"with its share reaching 43%","chinese":"其比例達43%"},{"english":"leads saturated fat consumption","chinese":"在飽和脂肪攝取方面居首"},{"english":"at 37%","chinese":"為37%"},{"english":"its contribution to added sugar","chinese":"其對添加糖的貢獻"},{"english":"much lower","chinese":"低得多"},{"english":"show the reverse pattern","chinese":"呈現相反模式"},{"english":"the reverse pattern","chinese":"相反模式"},{"english":"account for only 14% of sodium","chinese":"僅佔鈉的14%"},{"english":"21% of saturated fat","chinese":"佔飽和脂肪的21%"},{"english":"dominate added sugar","chinese":"在添加糖方面佔主導"},{"english":"at 42%","chinese":"為42%"},{"english":"almost double the dinner figure","chinese":"幾乎是晚餐數字的兩倍"},{"english":"the dinner figure","chinese":"晚餐的數字"}]},"model-essay-1-ielts-task1-process-diagram":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-1-ielts-task1-process-diagram","essayKey":"process-diagram:1","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-1-ielts-task1-process-diagram","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/process-diagrams/process-diagram-1","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The diagram illustrates the process by which bamboo is converted into fabric and, ultimately, clothing items.","chinese":"該圖說明竹子如何被轉化成布料，並最終製成衣物。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, this is a linear, nine-stage manufacturing process, beginning with the cultivation of bamboo plants in spring and ending with finished garments. The early stages are concerned with growing and mechanically preparing the bamboo, while the later stages turn the extracted fibres into yarn and woven cloth.","chinese":"整體而言，這是一個線性的九階段製造流程，從春季種植竹子開始，以製成成衣結束。 前期階段主要涉及竹子的生長和機械處理，而後期階段則把提取出的纖維轉化為紗線和織布。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"At the outset, bamboo plants are planted in spring and left to mature until autumn, when they are harvested. Once the crop has been collected, the stems are cut into narrow strips. These strips are then crushed so that they are reduced to a liquid pulp. Following this, the pulp is filtered in order to separate the long fibres from the remaining liquid.","chinese":"一開始，竹子在春季被種下，並被留待生長至秋季，然後被收割。 當作物被收集後，竹莖會被切成細條。 然後，這些竹條會被壓碎，使其變成液態漿料。 接著，漿料會被過濾，以便把長纖維從剩餘液體中分離出來。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"In the next stage, the extracted fibres are softened through the addition of water and amine oxide. After they have been treated in this way, they are spun into yarn. The yarn is subsequently woven to produce bamboo fabric. Finally, this fabric is made into everyday clothing products, such as socks and T-shirts.","chinese":"在下一階段，提取出的纖維會透過加入水和胺氧化物而被軟化。 當它們以這種方式處理後，便會被紡成紗線。 隨後，紗線會被編織成竹纖維布料。 最後，這些布料會被製成日常衣物產品，例如襪子和 T 恤。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"The diagram illustrates","chinese":"圖解顯示"},{"english":"the process by which","chinese":"……的過程"},{"english":"is converted into","chinese":"被轉化成"},{"english":"fabric","chinese":"布料"},{"english":"ultimately","chinese":"最終"},{"english":"clothing items","chinese":"衣物"},{"english":"a linear, nine-stage manufacturing process","chinese":"線性的九階段製造過程"},{"english":"linear process","chinese":"線性過程"},{"english":"nine-stage manufacturing process","chinese":"九階段製造過程"},{"english":"beginning with","chinese":"以……開始"},{"english":"ending with","chinese":"以……結束"},{"english":"the cultivation of bamboo plants","chinese":"種植竹子"},{"english":"finished garments","chinese":"製成衣物"},{"english":"the early stages","chinese":"早期階段"},{"english":"are concerned with","chinese":"涉及；關乎"},{"english":"mechanically preparing","chinese":"以機械方式處理"},{"english":"the later stages","chinese":"後期階段"},{"english":"turn the extracted fibres into","chinese":"將提取出的纖維變成"},{"english":"extracted fibres","chinese":"提取出的纖維"},{"english":"yarn","chinese":"紗線"},{"english":"woven cloth","chinese":"梭織布料"},{"english":"At the outset","chinese":"一開始"},{"english":"are planted in spring","chinese":"在春天種植"},{"english":"left to mature","chinese":"被留待成熟"},{"english":"until autumn","chinese":"直到秋天"},{"english":"are harvested","chinese":"被收割"},{"english":"Once the crop has been collected","chinese":"當農作物被收集後"},{"english":"the crop","chinese":"農作物"},{"english":"has been collected","chinese":"已被收集"},{"english":"stems","chinese":"莖"},{"english":"are cut into narrow strips","chinese":"被切成幼長條"},{"english":"narrow strips","chinese":"幼長條"},{"english":"are then crushed","chinese":"然後被壓碎"},{"english":"are reduced to","chinese":"被變成；被分解成"},{"english":"liquid pulp","chinese":"液態漿"},{"english":"Following this","chinese":"隨後"},{"english":"is filtered","chinese":"被過濾"},{"english":"in order to separate","chinese":"以便分離"},{"english":"long fibres","chinese":"長纖維"},{"english":"remaining liquid","chinese":"餘下液體"},{"english":"In the next stage","chinese":"在下一階段"},{"english":"are softened through","chinese":"透過……被軟化"},{"english":"the addition of","chinese":"加入……"},{"english":"water and amine oxide","chinese":"水和氧化胺"},{"english":"amine oxide","chinese":"氧化胺"},{"english":"treated in this way","chinese":"以這種方式處理"},{"english":"are spun into yarn","chinese":"被紡成紗線"},{"english":"subsequently woven","chinese":"隨後被編織"},{"english":"produce bamboo fabric","chinese":"製成竹纖維布料"},{"english":"bamboo fabric","chinese":"竹纖維布料"},{"english":"Finally","chinese":"最後"},{"english":"is made into","chinese":"被製成"},{"english":"everyday clothing products","chinese":"日常衣物產品"},{"english":"such as socks and T-shirts","chinese":"例如襪和T恤"}]},"model-essay-1-ielts-task1-tables":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-1-ielts-task1-tables","essayKey":"tables:1","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-1-ielts-task1-tables","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/tables/table-1","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The tables present changes in the population of New York City as a whole and compare Manhattan with the other four districts between 1800 and 2000.","chinese":"這些表格呈現了 1800 年至 2000 年間整個紐約市人口的變化，並將曼哈頓與其他四個區作比較。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the city’s population rose dramatically across the two centuries, but the balance shifted sharply away from Manhattan. While Manhattan made up more than three quarters of New York’s residents in 1800, the other districts accounted for over four fifths by 2000.","chinese":"整體而言，在這兩個世紀中，該市人口大幅上升，但人口分布的重心明顯從曼哈頓轉移開來。 雖然曼哈頓在 1800 年佔紐約居民的四分之三以上，但到 2000 年，其他區已佔超過五分之四。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 1800, New York City had only 79,216 inhabitants. By 1900 this figure had increased to 3,437,202, before reaching 8,009,185 in 2000. The first century therefore saw the more explosive expansion, with the population multiplying more than fortyfold; over the following hundred years it still grew substantially, though by a little over twice.","chinese":"1800 年，紐約市只有 79,216 名居民。 到 1900 年，這一數字已增至 3,437,202 ，之後在 2000 年達到 8,009,185 。 因此，第一個世紀出現了更爆炸性的增長，人口增加了四十多倍；在接下來的一百年中，人口仍然大幅增長，儘管只是略多於兩倍。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Manhattan followed a different path from the rest of the city. Its population climbed from 60,515 in 1800 to 1,850,093 in 1900, but then declined to 1,538,096 by 2000. Its share consequently fell from 76% to 54%, and finally to just 19%. By contrast, the other districts grew continuously, from 18,701 to 1,587,109 and then to 6,471,089, raising their combined share from 24% to 81%.","chinese":"曼哈頓的發展路徑與城市其他地區不同。 其人口從 1800 年的 60,515 上升至 1900 年的 1,850,093 ，但到 2000 年又下降至。 因此，其所佔比例從 76% 下降至 54% ，最後降至僅 19% 。 相比之下，其他區的人口持續增長，從 18,701 上升至 1,587,109 ，然後再增至6,471,089 ，使它們的合計比例從 24% 上升至 81% 。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the first table below shows","chinese":"下方第一個表格顯示"},{"english":"changes in the total population","chinese":"總人口的變化"},{"english":"the total population of","chinese":"……的總人口"},{"english":"New York City","chinese":"紐約市"},{"english":"from 1800 to 2000","chinese":"由1800年至2000年"},{"english":"the second and third tables show","chinese":"第二和第三個表格顯示"},{"english":"the population of the five boroughs","chinese":"五個行政區的人口"},{"english":"five boroughs of the city","chinese":"該市五個行政區"},{"english":"Manhattan","chinese":"曼哈頓"},{"english":"Brooklyn","chinese":"布魯克林"},{"english":"the Bronx","chinese":"布朗克斯"},{"english":"Queens","chinese":"皇后區"},{"english":"Staten Island","chinese":"史泰登島"},{"english":"over the same period","chinese":"在同一時期內"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"selecting and reporting","chinese":"選取並報告"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"the tables present changes in","chinese":"表格呈現……的變化"},{"english":"as a whole","chinese":"作為一個整體"},{"english":"compare Manhattan with","chinese":"將曼哈頓與……作比較"},{"english":"the other four boroughs","chinese":"其他四個行政區"},{"english":"between 1800 and 2000","chinese":"在1800年至2000年間"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"the city's population","chinese":"該市人口"},{"english":"rose dramatically","chinese":"大幅上升"},{"english":"across the two centuries","chinese":"在這兩個世紀中"},{"english":"the balance shifted sharply away from","chinese":"重心大幅從……轉移"},{"english":"shifted sharply away from","chinese":"大幅從……轉移"},{"english":"made up more than three quarters of","chinese":"佔……超過四分之三"},{"english":"more than three quarters of","chinese":"超過四分之三"},{"english":"New York's residents","chinese":"紐約居民"},{"english":"accounted for over four fifths","chinese":"佔超過五分之四"},{"english":"over four fifths","chinese":"超過五分之四"},{"english":"by 2000","chinese":"到2000年"},{"english":"had only 79,216 inhabitants","chinese":"只有79,216名居民"},{"english":"inhabitants","chinese":"居民"},{"english":"by 1900","chinese":"到1900年"},{"english":"this figure had increased to","chinese":"這一數字已增加至"},{"english":"3,437,202","chinese":"3,437,202"},{"english":"before reaching","chinese":"之後達到"},{"english":"reached 8,009,185","chinese":"達到8,009,185"},{"english":"the first century","chinese":"第一個世紀"},{"english":"saw the more explosive expansion","chinese":"出現更爆炸性的擴張"},{"english":"explosive expansion","chinese":"爆炸性擴張"},{"english":"multiplying more than fortyfold","chinese":"增加超過四十倍"},{"english":"more than fortyfold","chinese":"超過四十倍"},{"english":"over the following hundred years","chinese":"在接下來的一百年間"},{"english":"grew substantially","chinese":"大幅增長"},{"english":"though by a little over twice","chinese":"但只是略多於兩倍"},{"english":"a little over twice","chinese":"略多於兩倍"},{"english":"followed a different path from","chinese":"走勢與……不同"},{"english":"the rest of the city","chinese":"該市其餘地區"},{"english":"climbed from … to …","chinese":"由……上升至……"},{"english":"from 60,515 to 1,850,093","chinese":"由60,515升至1,850,093"},{"english":"then declined to","chinese":"其後下降至"},{"english":"declined to 1,538,096","chinese":"下降至1,538,096"},{"english":"its share consequently fell","chinese":"其比例因此下降"},{"english":"consequently","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"fell from 76% to 54%","chinese":"由76%跌至54%"},{"english":"finally to just 19%","chinese":"最終只剩19%"},{"english":"just 19%","chinese":"只有19%"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"grew continuously","chinese":"持續增長"},{"english":"from 18,701 to 1,587,109","chinese":"由18,701升至1,587,109"},{"english":"then to 6,471,089","chinese":"其後升至6,471,089"},{"english":"raising their combined share","chinese":"使其合計比例上升"},{"english":"combined share","chinese":"合計比例"},{"english":"from 24% to 81%","chinese":"由24%升至81%"}]},"model-essay-2-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-2-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:2","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-2-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q2","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many countries, purchasing goods through digital platforms has become part of everyday life. This development brings clear benefits to both consumers and businesses, particularly in terms of convenience and efficiency, although it also creates several notable drawbacks. Overall, I believe that online shopping is a positive trend because its advantages are more significant than its disadvantages for both individuals and companies.","chinese":"在許多國家，透過數位平台購買商品已成為日常生活的一部分。 這種發展為消費者和企業都帶來了明顯好處，尤其是在便利性和效率方面，儘管它也造成了一些值得注意的缺點。 總的來說，我認為網上購物是一項正面的趨勢，因為對個人和企業而言，它的優點比缺點更為顯著。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The principal advantage of online shopping is the efficiency it creates. For individuals, online marketplaces allow people to compare prices, read reviews, and complete purchases within minutes, which saves both time and effort. Instead of travelling from one shop to another, a busy parent, for example, can order groceries or school supplies during a lunch break and have them delivered directly home. This convenience is especially valuable for those with demanding schedules or limited access to physical stores. Companies also benefit substantially. By selling online, businesses can reduce costs related to rent, shop maintenance, and in-store staff, while at the same time reaching a much wider customer base. A small independent bookshop, for instance, can move beyond relying on local foot traffic and sell to buyers across the country through a website or online marketplace. As a result, online retailing increases accessibility for consumers and improves commercial efficiency for firms.","chinese":"網上購物最主要的優點是它所帶來的效率。 對個人而言，網上市場讓人們可以在幾分鐘內比價、閱讀評論並完成購買，這樣能同時節省時間與精力。 例如，一位忙碌的家長不必一家店接一家店地奔波，只需在午休時間訂購雜貨或學用品，並直接送到家中。 這種便利對於行程繁忙或不容易前往實體商店的人尤其有價值。 企業同樣能獲得相當大的好處。 透過線上銷售，企業可以降低與租金、店面維護及店內員工相關的成本，同時接觸到更廣大的顧客群。 例如，一家小型獨立書店可以不再只依賴在地客流，而是透過網站或網上市場把書賣給全國各地的買家。 因此，線上零售提升了消費者的可及性，也改善了企業的商業效率。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, online shopping also has clear disadvantages. For individuals, the inability to inspect products physically means that purchases are often based only on pictures and descriptions, which can be misleading. This can lead to disappointment when an item arrives in the wrong size, poor quality, or a different appearance from what was advertised. Someone who buys clothing or furniture online, for example, may have to go through an inconvenient returns process after discovering that the product does not meet expectations. For companies, the digital marketplace is highly competitive and fragile. Because customers can compare dozens of sellers instantly, businesses are forced into price competition that can reduce profit margins. In addition, one delivery failure, data breach, or widely shared negative review can rapidly damage a company’s reputation. Therefore, while e-commerce offers speed and reach, it also exposes both shoppers and firms to significant risks.","chinese":"然而，網上購物也有明顯的缺點。 對個人而言，無法親自檢查商品意味著購買往往只能根據圖片與描述作出，而這些資訊可能具有誤導性。 這可能導致失望，因為商品送達時可能尺寸不對、品質不佳，或外觀與廣告宣傳不符。 例如，某人若在網上購買衣服或家具，發現商品不符合預期後，可能必須經歷一個麻煩的退貨流程。 對企業而言，數位市場競爭非常激烈，而且相當脆弱。 由於顧客能夠立即比較數十家賣家，企業被迫陷入價格競爭，而這可能壓縮利潤空間。 此外，一次配送失誤、資料外洩，或一則被廣泛傳播的負評，都可能迅速損害一家公司的聲譽。 因此，雖然電子商務提供了速度與廣泛觸及的優勢，但它也使消費者與企業同時面臨重大的風險。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, online shopping does present disadvantages, particularly product uncertainty for consumers and competitive pressure for businesses. Nevertheless, because it provides greater convenience for individuals and lower costs together with broader market access for companies, the advantages of shopping online clearly outweigh the disadvantages.","chinese":"總結來說，網上購物確實帶來缺點，尤其是消費者面臨商品不確定性，以及企業承受競爭壓力。 然而，由於它為個人帶來更大的便利，也為企業帶來更低的成本與更廣的市場接觸，因此網上購物的優點明顯大於缺點。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"purchasing goods","chinese":"購買商品"},{"english":"digital platforms","chinese":"數碼平台"},{"english":"everyday life","chinese":"日常生活"},{"english":"this development","chinese":"這項發展"},{"english":"clear benefits","chinese":"明顯好處"},{"english":"consumers and businesses","chinese":"消費者和企業"},{"english":"particularly in terms of","chinese":"尤其在……方面"},{"english":"convenience and efficiency","chinese":"方便和效率"},{"english":"notable drawbacks","chinese":"明顯缺點"},{"english":"a positive trend","chinese":"正面的趨勢"},{"english":"more significant than","chinese":"比……更重要"},{"english":"individuals and companies","chinese":"個人和公司"},{"english":"the principal advantage of","chinese":"……的主要好處"},{"english":"online marketplaces","chinese":"網上平台；網上市場"},{"english":"compare prices","chinese":"比較價格"},{"english":"read reviews","chinese":"閱讀評價"},{"english":"complete purchases","chinese":"完成購物"},{"english":"within minutes","chinese":"在數分鐘內"},{"english":"saves both time and effort","chinese":"節省時間和精力"},{"english":"instead of travelling from one shop to another","chinese":"而不是從一間店走到另一間店"},{"english":"a busy parent","chinese":"忙碌的家長"},{"english":"order groceries","chinese":"訂購日用品；訂購雜貨"},{"english":"school supplies","chinese":"學校用品"},{"english":"during a lunch break","chinese":"午膳休息期間"},{"english":"delivered directly home","chinese":"直接送到家中"},{"english":"especially valuable for","chinese":"對……尤其有價值"},{"english":"demanding schedules","chinese":"繁忙的日程"},{"english":"limited access to","chinese":"接觸……的機會有限"},{"english":"physical stores","chinese":"實體店"},{"english":"benefit substantially","chinese":"大大受惠"},{"english":"by selling online","chinese":"透過網上銷售"},{"english":"reduce costs related to","chinese":"減少與……有關的成本"},{"english":"shop maintenance","chinese":"店舖維修保養"},{"english":"in-store staff","chinese":"店內職員"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"reach a much wider customer base","chinese":"接觸更廣泛的顧客群"},{"english":"customer base","chinese":"顧客群"},{"english":"a small independent bookshop","chinese":"小型獨立書店"},{"english":"move beyond relying on","chinese":"不再只依賴"},{"english":"local foot traffic","chinese":"本地店舖人流"},{"english":"across the country","chinese":"全國各地"},{"english":"online retailing","chinese":"網上零售"},{"english":"increases accessibility for","chinese":"增加……的可接觸性"},{"english":"commercial efficiency","chinese":"商業效率"},{"english":"clear disadvantages","chinese":"明顯缺點"},{"english":"the inability to inspect products physically","chinese":"無法親身檢查產品"},{"english":"inspect products physically","chinese":"親身檢查產品"},{"english":"be based only on","chinese":"只基於"},{"english":"pictures and descriptions","chinese":"圖片和描述"},{"english":"be misleading","chinese":"具誤導性"},{"english":"lead to disappointment","chinese":"導致失望"},{"english":"the wrong size","chinese":"尺碼錯誤"},{"english":"poor quality","chinese":"質素差"},{"english":"a different appearance from","chinese":"外觀與……不同"},{"english":"what was advertised","chinese":"廣告所展示的內容"},{"english":"clothing or furniture","chinese":"衣服或家具"},{"english":"go through","chinese":"經歷"},{"english":"an inconvenient returns process","chinese":"麻煩的退貨程序"},{"english":"does not meet expectations","chinese":"不符合期望"},{"english":"the digital marketplace","chinese":"數碼市場"},{"english":"highly competitive","chinese":"競爭激烈"},{"english":"fragile","chinese":"脆弱"},{"english":"dozens of sellers","chinese":"數十個賣家"},{"english":"instantly","chinese":"即時"},{"english":"be forced into","chinese":"被迫陷入"},{"english":"price competition","chinese":"價格競爭"},{"english":"reduce profit margins","chinese":"降低利潤率"},{"english":"profit margins","chinese":"利潤率"},{"english":"in addition","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"delivery failure","chinese":"送貨失誤"},{"english":"data breach","chinese":"資料外洩"},{"english":"widely shared negative review","chinese":"被廣泛分享的負面評價"},{"english":"rapidly damage","chinese":"迅速損害"},{"english":"a company's reputation","chinese":"公司的聲譽"},{"english":"e-commerce","chinese":"電子商貿"},{"english":"speed and reach","chinese":"速度和接觸範圍"},{"english":"exposes both shoppers and firms to","chinese":"令購物者和企業面對"},{"english":"significant risks","chinese":"重大風險"},{"english":"does present disadvantages","chinese":"確實存在缺點"},{"english":"product uncertainty","chinese":"產品不確定性"},{"english":"competitive pressure","chinese":"競爭壓力"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"greater convenience","chinese":"更大的便利"},{"english":"lower costs","chinese":"較低成本"},{"english":"broader market access","chinese":"更廣泛的市場接觸機會"},{"english":"clearly outweigh","chinese":"明顯大於"}]},"model-essay-2-ielts-cause-solution":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-2-ielts-cause-solution","essayKey":"cause-solution:2","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-2-ielts-cause-solution","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Large companies are often able to spend heavily on advertising, sponsorship and online promotion, so their products become more visible than those made by smaller local producers. This trend can damage local economies and weaken choice, but measures can make local goods easier to buy.","chinese":"大型企業通常有能力在廣告、贊助和網上推廣方面投入大量資金，因此它們的產品會比小型本地生產商所製造的產品更加顯眼。 這種趨勢可能損害本地經濟並削弱消費者選擇，但一些措施可以令本地產品更容易被購買。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first problem is that smaller firms are pushed into the shadows. When shoppers repeatedly see the same brands on television, social media and supermarket shelves, they tend to trust those names almost automatically, even when a local alternative is just as good. As sales move towards large corporations, independent shops and small manufacturers lose revenue, cut jobs and, in the worst cases, close altogether. This drains money from the community and leaves high streets less varied and less alive. A second problem is that consumer decisions become shaped by image rather than real value. A heavily advertised snack, for instance, may seem superior simply because its packaging, slogan and celebrity endorsement are everywhere. As a result, people may pay more for familiarity, while healthier or fresher local products are overlooked.","chinese":"第一個問題是，小型企業會被推到陰影之中。 當消費者不斷在電視、社交媒體和超市貨架上看到相同品牌時，他們往往會幾乎自動地信任這些品牌名稱，即使本地替代產品同樣出色。 隨著銷售額流向大型企業，獨立商店和小型製造商會失去收入、削減職位，最嚴重時甚至完全結業。 這會使金錢從社區中流走，並令商業街變得較缺乏多樣性，也較沒有生氣。 第二個問題是，消費者的決定會被形象塑造，而不是由真正價值決定。 例如，一款被大量宣傳的零食，可能只是因為它的包裝、標語和名人代言隨處可見，便顯得更優越。 結果，人們可能會為熟悉感支付更高價格，而更健康或更新鮮的本地產品卻被忽略。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"To encourage local purchasing, governments and councils should first make local products more visible. They could fund farmers’ markets, local-product sections in supermarkets, and digital platforms where nearby producers can sell directly to residents. If a family can find local vegetables, bread or handmade goods as easily as a global brand, buying locally becomes a convenient habit rather than a moral chore. Retailers can also help by using clear labelling and fair shelf space. A simple “made locally” label, paired with brief information about the producer, can turn an ordinary purchase into a small act of community support. Public campaigns can also remind consumers that local spending sustains jobs, skills and neighbourhood identity.","chinese":"為了鼓勵人們購買本地產品，政府和地方議會首先應該讓本地產品更加顯眼。 它們可以資助農夫市集、超市中的本地產品專區，以及讓附近生產商能夠直接向居民銷售的數碼平台。 如果一個家庭能夠像找到全球品牌一樣容易地找到本地蔬菜、麵包或手工製品，那麼購買本地產品就會變成一種方便的習慣，而不是一項道德上的苦差。 零售商也可以透過清晰標籤和公平的貨架空間提供幫助。 一個簡單的「本地製造」標籤，再配上關於生產者的簡短資料，可以把一次普通的購物轉化為一個支持社區的小小行動。 公共宣傳活動也可以提醒消費者，本地消費能夠維持就業、技術和社區身份。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, the marketing power of large businesses can undermine local firms and encourage more brand-led consumption. However, if local goods are made visible, convenient and meaningful to consumers, communities can tilt demand back towards their own producers.","chinese":"總結來說，大型企業的行銷力量可能削弱本地企業，並鼓勵更多由品牌主導的消費。 然而，如果本地商品能夠變得顯眼、方便，並且對消費者具有意義，社區便能夠把需求重新引導回自己的生產者身上。"}],"vocabulary":[]},"model-essay-2-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-2-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:2","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-2-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q2","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The success of a company often depends less on ambitious strategy than on how consistently its employees perform in daily work. To increase staff productivity, firms should focus on two practical areas: making work easier to do well and creating conditions in which people want to do their best.","chinese":"一家公司的成功往往與其說取決於雄心勃勃的策略，不如說取決於員工在日常工作中能否持續穩定地表現。 為了提高員工生產力，企業應該專注於兩個實際範疇：讓工作更容易被做好，以及創造一種讓人願意盡力而為的環境。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first step is to make work clearer, better supported, and less wasteful. Many employees are not unproductive because they are lazy; rather, they lose time because instructions are vague, systems are slow, or priorities change too often. Companies should therefore set clear targets, divide large projects into manageable tasks, and ensure that workers know exactly what is expected of them. Regular but concise feedback is also important, as it allows staff to correct mistakes before small problems become expensive ones. Training should also be treated as a core investment rather than an occasional extra. When employees are taught how to use new software, communicate with clients, or manage their workload, they can work with greater confidence and fewer errors. A well-trained team is rarely a luxury; it is the engine of a productive company.","chinese":"第一步是讓工作變得更清晰、得到更好的支援，並減少浪費。 許多員工缺乏生產力並不是因為他們懶惰；相反，他們浪費時間，是因為指示含糊、系統緩慢，或者優先事項變動太頻繁。 因此，公司應該設定清晰目標，將大型項目分拆成可管理的任務，並確保員工準確知道自己被期望完成甚麼。 定期但簡潔的回饋同樣重要，因為它能讓員工在小問題變成昂貴錯誤之前及時修正。 培訓也應該被視為一項核心投資，而不是偶爾才提供的額外安排。 當員工被教導如何使用新軟件、與客戶溝通，或管理自己的工作量時，他們便能更有信心地工作，並減少錯誤。 一支訓練有素的團隊很少只是奢侈品；它是一間高生產力公司的引擎。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another effective way to improve productivity is to protect employees’ motivation and well-being. If staff are constantly exhausted, underpaid, or ignored, their performance will eventually decline, even if they are talented. Companies can prevent this by offering fair salaries, recognising good work, and giving employees realistic workloads. Flexible working arrangements can also help, especially when they reduce unnecessary commuting and allow workers to concentrate during their most productive hours. Managers should also create a culture in which employees feel trusted rather than watched. People usually work harder when they feel respected, because they see their job not merely as a duty, but as a contribution.","chinese":"另一個提高生產力的有效方法，是保護員工的動力和身心健康。 如果員工長期感到疲憊、薪酬不足，或被忽視，即使他們很有才華，表現最終也會下降 公司可以透過提供公平薪酬、認可優秀工作，以及給予員工合理的工作量來防止這種情況 彈性工作安排也能有所幫助，尤其是當它們能減少不必要的通勤，並讓員工在自己最有效率的時間集中工作時。 管理者也應該創造一種讓員工感到被信任，而不是被監視的文化。 當人們感到被尊重時，通常會更努力工作，因為他們不只是把工作看作一項職責，而是把它看作一種貢獻。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, companies can raise staff productivity by improving work systems, providing useful training, and maintaining a healthy, motivating workplace. Productivity grows best when efficiency and morale move together.","chinese":"總結來說，公司可以透過改善工作制度、提供有用的培訓，以及維持一個健康而具激勵性的工作環境來提升員工生產力。 當效率與士氣同步提升時，生產力最能自然增長。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the success of a company","chinese":"一間公司的成功"},{"english":"depends less on...than on...","chinese":"與其取決於……不如取決於……"},{"english":"ambitious strategy","chinese":"具雄心的策略"},{"english":"consistently perform","chinese":"持續表現良好"},{"english":"daily work","chinese":"日常工作"},{"english":"increase staff productivity","chinese":"提高員工生產力"},{"english":"focus on","chinese":"專注於"},{"english":"practical areas","chinese":"實際範疇"},{"english":"making work easier to do well","chinese":"令工作更容易做好"},{"english":"creating conditions in which","chinese":"創造讓……的條件"},{"english":"do their best","chinese":"盡力做到最好"},{"english":"the first step","chinese":"第一步"},{"english":"better supported","chinese":"得到更好支援"},{"english":"less wasteful","chinese":"減少浪費"},{"english":"unproductive","chinese":"生產力低"},{"english":"lose time because","chinese":"因為……而浪費時間"},{"english":"instructions are vague","chinese":"指示含糊"},{"english":"systems are slow","chinese":"系統緩慢"},{"english":"priorities change too often","chinese":"優先事項變動太頻繁"},{"english":"set clear targets","chinese":"訂立清晰目標"},{"english":"divide large projects into","chinese":"將大型項目分成……"},{"english":"manageable tasks","chinese":"可處理的任務"},{"english":"ensure that","chinese":"確保"},{"english":"what is expected of them","chinese":"對他們的期望"},{"english":"regular but concise feedback","chinese":"定期但簡潔的回饋"},{"english":"correct mistakes","chinese":"改正錯誤"},{"english":"small problems become expensive ones","chinese":"小問題變成代價高昂的問題"},{"english":"be treated as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"a core investment","chinese":"核心投資"},{"english":"rather than an occasional extra","chinese":"而不是偶爾才有的額外安排"},{"english":"an occasional extra","chinese":"偶爾才有的額外安排"},{"english":"be taught how to","chinese":"被教導如何……"},{"english":"use new software","chinese":"使用新軟件"},{"english":"communicate with clients","chinese":"與客戶溝通"},{"english":"manage their workload","chinese":"管理工作量"},{"english":"work with greater confidence","chinese":"更有信心地工作"},{"english":"fewer errors","chinese":"較少錯誤"},{"english":"a well-trained team","chinese":"受過良好培訓的團隊"},{"english":"rarely a luxury","chinese":"很少是奢侈品"},{"english":"the engine of","chinese":"……的引擎；推動力"},{"english":"a productive company","chinese":"高生產力的公司"},{"english":"another effective way to","chinese":"另一個有效方法去……"},{"english":"protect employees' motivation and well-being","chinese":"保護員工的動力和身心健康"},{"english":"well-being","chinese":"身心健康"},{"english":"constantly exhausted","chinese":"長期疲憊"},{"english":"underpaid","chinese":"薪酬過低"},{"english":"ignored","chinese":"被忽視"},{"english":"eventually decline","chinese":"最終下降"},{"english":"talented","chinese":"有才能的"},{"english":"offering fair salaries","chinese":"提供公平薪酬"},{"english":"recognising good work","chinese":"認可出色工作"},{"english":"realistic workloads","chinese":"合理工作量"},{"english":"flexible working arrangements","chinese":"彈性工作安排"},{"english":"reduce unnecessary commuting","chinese":"減少不必要的通勤"},{"english":"concentrate during","chinese":"在……期間專心"},{"english":"most productive hours","chinese":"生產力最高的時段"},{"english":"create a culture in which","chinese":"建立一種讓……的文化"},{"english":"feel trusted rather than watched","chinese":"感到被信任，而不是被監視"},{"english":"feel respected","chinese":"感到被尊重"},{"english":"not merely as a duty","chinese":"不只是作為責任"},{"english":"as a contribution","chinese":"作為一種貢獻"},{"english":"raise staff productivity","chinese":"提高員工生產力"},{"english":"improving work systems","chinese":"改善工作系統"},{"english":"providing useful training","chinese":"提供有用培訓"},{"english":"maintaining a healthy, motivating workplace","chinese":"維持健康而有激勵性的工作場所"},{"english":"efficiency and morale","chinese":"效率和士氣"},{"english":"move together","chinese":"一起提升；並行發展"}]},"model-essay-2-ielts-task1-bar-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-2-ielts-task1-bar-charts","essayKey":"bar-charts:2","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-2-ielts-task1-bar-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/bar-charts/bar-chart-2","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The bar chart compares the proportions of weekly income that families in one country spent on eight categories in 1968 and 2018.","chinese":"這張柱狀圖比較了一個國家的家庭在 1968 年和 2018 年把每週收入花在八個類別上的比例。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, household spending shifted noticeably over the 50-year period. Food was by far the dominant item in 1968, but its share fell sharply by 2018, when leisure, housing and transport had become much more significant. Several smaller categories declined, while household goods remained broadly stable.","chinese":"整體而言，在這 50 年間，家庭支出結構出現了明顯轉變。 食物在 1968 年是遠遠最主要的支出項目，但到 2018 年其比例大幅下降；同時，休閒、住房和交通變得重要得多。 幾個較小的類別有所下降，而家居用品則大致保持穩定。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 1968, families allocated about 35% of their income to food, more than three times the proportion spent on housing or clothing and footwear, each at around 10%. Leisure and transport were also relatively modest, at just under 10% and about 8% respectively. Household goods and personal goods accounted for similar shares, at roughly 7–8%, while fuel and power was slightly lower, at around 6%.","chinese":"在 1968 年，家庭把大約 35% 的收入花在食物上，這是住房或服裝及鞋類支出比例的三倍多；後兩者各約佔 10% 。 休閒和交通的比例也相對較低，分別為略低於 10% 和約 8% 。 家居用品和個人用品所佔比例相近，約為 7% 至 8% ；而燃料和能源則稍低，約為 6% 。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"By 2018, leisure had become the largest category, rising to just over a fifth of income. Housing almost doubled to approximately 19%, and transport increased to about 14%. In contrast, food dropped to around 17%, clothing and footwear halved to 5%, and personal goods and fuel and power both fell to about 4%. Household goods changed very little, remaining near 7%.","chinese":"到 2018 年，休閒已成為最大的類別，上升至略高於收入的五分之一。 住房幾乎翻倍，升至約 19% ；交通則增加至約 14% 。 相比之下，食物下降至約 17% ，服裝及鞋類減半至 5% ，而個人用品以及燃料和能源都下降至約 4% 。 家居用品變化很小，仍維持在約 7% 。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"bar chart","chinese":"棒形圖"},{"english":"compares the proportions of","chinese":"比較……的比例"},{"english":"proportions of weekly income","chinese":"每週收入的比例"},{"english":"spent on eight categories","chinese":"用於八個類別"},{"english":"household spending","chinese":"家庭開支"},{"english":"shifted noticeably","chinese":"明顯轉變"},{"english":"over the 50-year period","chinese":"在50年間"},{"english":"by far the dominant item","chinese":"遠遠是最主要的項目"},{"english":"dominant item","chinese":"主要項目"},{"english":"its share fell sharply","chinese":"其比例大幅下降"},{"english":"by 2018","chinese":"到2018年時"},{"english":"had become much more significant","chinese":"已變得重要得多"},{"english":"leisure","chinese":"消閒"},{"english":"housing","chinese":"住屋"},{"english":"transport","chinese":"交通"},{"english":"several smaller categories","chinese":"數個較小類別"},{"english":"declined","chinese":"下降"},{"english":"household goods","chinese":"家庭用品"},{"english":"remained broadly stable","chinese":"大致保持穩定"},{"english":"allocated about 35% of their income to","chinese":"將約35%的收入分配予……"},{"english":"allocated income to","chinese":"將收入分配予……"},{"english":"more than three times the proportion","chinese":"超過三倍比例"},{"english":"proportion spent on","chinese":"用於……的比例"},{"english":"clothing and footwear","chinese":"衣履"},{"english":"each at around 10%","chinese":"各約10%"},{"english":"relatively modest","chinese":"相對較少；相對不高"},{"english":"just under 10%","chinese":"略低於10%"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"accounted for similar shares","chinese":"佔相近比例"},{"english":"similar shares","chinese":"相近比例"},{"english":"at roughly 7–8%","chinese":"約7至8%"},{"english":"fuel and power","chinese":"燃料及電力"},{"english":"slightly lower","chinese":"略低"},{"english":"had become the largest category","chinese":"已成為最大類別"},{"english":"the largest category","chinese":"最大類別"},{"english":"rising to","chinese":"上升至"},{"english":"just over a fifth of income","chinese":"收入的略多於五分之一"},{"english":"almost doubled to","chinese":"幾乎翻倍至"},{"english":"approximately 19%","chinese":"約19%"},{"english":"increased to","chinese":"增至"},{"english":"in contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"dropped to around 17%","chinese":"下降至約17%"},{"english":"halved to 5%","chinese":"減半至5%"},{"english":"personal goods","chinese":"個人用品"},{"english":"both fell to about 4%","chinese":"兩者均下降至約4%"},{"english":"changed very little","chinese":"變化很小"},{"english":"remaining near 7%","chinese":"維持在接近7%"}]},"model-essay-2-ielts-task1-line-graph":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-2-ielts-task1-line-graph","essayKey":"line-graph:2","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-2-ielts-task1-line-graph","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/line-graphs/line-graph-2","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The line graph compares the percentage of people living in cities in the Philippines, Malaysia, Thailand and Indonesia from 1970 to 2020, with forecasts to 2040.","chinese":"這張折線圖比較了 1970 年至 2020 年間菲律賓、馬來西亞、泰國和印尼城市人口所佔百分比，並附有到 2040 年的預測。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, all four countries became more urbanised. Malaysia rose to and is expected to remain the clear leader, while Indonesia records the fastest long-term growth, moving from the lowest position to second place. By contrast, the Philippines fluctuated, and Thailand grew more slowly, becoming the least urbanised country from 2010 onwards.","chinese":"整體而言，四個國家的城市化程度都提高了。 馬來西亞上升後成為、並預計會繼續保持明顯領先的位置；與此同時，印尼錄得最顯著的長期增長，從最低位置升至第二位。 相比之下，菲律賓的數據有所波動，而泰國增長較慢，從 2010 年起成為城市化比例最低的國家。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 1970, the Philippines led slightly, at just over 30%, compared with about 30% in Malaysia. The Philippine figure reached nearly 50% in 1990, then declined to just above 40% in 2010, before recovering to roughly 46% in 2020; it is projected to rise to about 56% by 2040. Malaysia, however, climbed steadily from around 30% to 60% between 1970 and 2000, and is forecast to exceed 80% by the end.","chinese":"在 1970 年，菲律賓以略高於 30% 的城市人口比例小幅領先，而馬來西亞約為。 菲律賓的數據在 1990 年達到接近 50% ，之後在 2010 年下降至略高於 40% ，再於2020 年回升至約 46% ；預計到 2040 年將升至約 56% 。 然而，馬來西亞從 1970 年的約 30% 穩步上升至 2000 年的 60% ，並預計在最後一年超過 80% 。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Indonesia began at only about 13%, but rose continuously, equalling the Philippines at around 43% in 2010 and reaching just over 50% in 2020. It should climb further to the mid-60s, whereas Thailand is expected to grow from just above 30% in 2020 to 50% in 2040.","chinese":"印尼的起點只有約 13% ，但其比例持續上升，在 2010 年以約 43% 追平菲律賓，並於 2020 年達到略高於 50% 。 預計印尼會進一步升至 60 多 % 的中段，而泰國則預計會從 2020 年的略高於30% 升至 2040 年的 50% 。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"line graph","chinese":"折線圖"},{"english":"compares the percentage of","chinese":"比較……的百分比"},{"english":"people living in cities","chinese":"居於城市的人口"},{"english":"from 1970 to 2020","chinese":"由1970年至2020年"},{"english":"with forecasts to 2040","chinese":"並預測至2040年"},{"english":"forecasts","chinese":"預測"},{"english":"became more urbanised","chinese":"變得更城市化"},{"english":"more urbanised","chinese":"城市化程度較高"},{"english":"rose to","chinese":"上升至"},{"english":"is expected to remain","chinese":"預料會維持"},{"english":"the clear leader","chinese":"明顯領先者"},{"english":"records the fastest long-term growth","chinese":"錄得最快長期增長"},{"english":"fastest long-term growth","chinese":"最快長期增長"},{"english":"moving from the lowest position to second place","chinese":"由最低位置升至第二位"},{"english":"the lowest position","chinese":"最低位置"},{"english":"second place","chinese":"第二位"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"fluctuated","chinese":"波動"},{"english":"grew more slowly","chinese":"增長較慢"},{"english":"the least urbanised country","chinese":"城市化程度最低的國家"},{"english":"from 2010 onwards","chinese":"從2010年起"},{"english":"led slightly","chinese":"略為領先"},{"english":"at just over 30%","chinese":"略高於30%"},{"english":"compared with","chinese":"與……相比"},{"english":"reached nearly 50%","chinese":"達接近50%"},{"english":"the Philippine figure","chinese":"菲律賓的數字"},{"english":"then declined to","chinese":"然後下降至"},{"english":"just above 40%","chinese":"略高於40%"},{"english":"before recovering to","chinese":"之後回升至"},{"english":"roughly 46%","chinese":"約46%"},{"english":"is projected to rise to","chinese":"預計上升至"},{"english":"by 2040","chinese":"到2040年時"},{"english":"however","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"climbed steadily","chinese":"穩步上升"},{"english":"from around 30% to 60%","chinese":"由約30%升至60%"},{"english":"between 1970 and 2000","chinese":"在1970年至2000年間"},{"english":"is forecast to exceed","chinese":"預測會超過"},{"english":"exceed 80%","chinese":"超過80%"},{"english":"by the end","chinese":"到期末時"},{"english":"began at only about 13%","chinese":"起初只有約13%"},{"english":"rose continuously","chinese":"持續上升"},{"english":"equalling the Philippines","chinese":"與菲律賓持平"},{"english":"at around 43%","chinese":"約43%"},{"english":"reaching just over 50%","chinese":"達略高於50%"},{"english":"should climb further to","chinese":"應會進一步上升至"},{"english":"the mid-60s","chinese":"60多個百分點的中段"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相比之下"},{"english":"is expected to grow from…to…","chinese":"預計由……增至……"},{"english":"just above 30%","chinese":"略高於30%"},{"english":"to 50% in 2040","chinese":"到2040年增至50%"},{"english":"urbanisation rate","chinese":"城市化率"},{"english":"long-term trend","chinese":"長期趨勢"},{"english":"upward trend","chinese":"上升趨勢"},{"english":"projected figure","chinese":"預測數字"},{"english":"urban population","chinese":"城市人口比例"},{"english":"over the period","chinese":"在整段期間"}]},"model-essay-2-ielts-task1-maps":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-2-ielts-task1-maps","essayKey":"maps:2","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-2-ielts-task1-maps","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/maps/maps-2","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The two plans illustrate how Porth Harbour has changed since 2000.","chinese":"這兩幅平面圖展示了 Porth Harbour 自 2000 年以來的變化。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the harbour has become more developed and visitor-oriented. The main changes are the addition of hotel and commercial facilities, the creation of a private beach, the expansion of the dock area, and the relocation of the marina and fishing boats.","chinese":"整體而言，這個港口變得更加發達，也更以遊客為導向。 主要變化包括新增酒店和商業設施、設立私人海灘、擴建碼頭區，以及搬遷私人遊艇碼頭和漁船停泊區。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"On the western side, the two car parks and the main road are still in place, and the original showers and toilets have been retained beside the northern car park. However, the marina for private yachts, formerly in the north-west basin, has been moved southwards to the area once used by fishing boats. These boats now occupy the former marina site. A second block of showers and toilets has been built near the lower car park, while cafés and shops have been added west of the lifeboat station.","chinese":"在西面，兩個停車場和主路仍然保留，而原有的淋浴間和洗手間也保留在北面停車場旁邊。 然而，原本位於西北面水域的私人遊艇碼頭，已經向南遷移到原本停泊漁船的區域。 這些漁船現在則停泊在原本私人遊艇碼頭所在的位置。 另一座淋浴間和洗手間已在較南面的停車場附近建成，而咖啡店和商店則新增在救生艇站的西面。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Further east, the dock has been enlarged with extra mooring space, although the passenger ferries remain nearby. The disused castle on the small peninsula has been replaced by a hotel, accessed by an extended road. The southern beach is now reserved for hotel guests, whereas the northern public beach and lifeboat station remain largely unchanged.","chinese":"再往東面，碼頭已經擴建，並增加了停泊空間，不過客運渡輪仍停留在附近。 小半島上原本廢棄的城堡已被一間酒店取代，而該酒店可通過延伸道路到達。 南面的海灘現在只供酒店住客使用；相反，北面的公共海灘和救生艇站則大致保持不變。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the plans below show","chinese":"下列平面圖顯示"},{"english":"a harbour","chinese":"港口"},{"english":"how it looks today","chinese":"它現時的樣貌"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"selecting and reporting the main features","chinese":"選取並報告主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"The two plans illustrate how","chinese":"兩幅平面圖顯示……如何"},{"english":"Porth Harbour","chinese":"Porth Harbour"},{"english":"has changed since","chinese":"自……以來已有變化"},{"english":"since 2000","chinese":"自2000年以來"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"has become more developed","chinese":"變得發展程度更高"},{"english":"visitor-oriented","chinese":"以遊客為導向"},{"english":"the main changes are","chinese":"主要變化是"},{"english":"the addition of","chinese":"增設……"},{"english":"hotel and commercial facilities","chinese":"酒店及商業設施"},{"english":"the creation of","chinese":"設立……"},{"english":"a private beach","chinese":"私人海灘"},{"english":"the expansion of","chinese":"……的擴建"},{"english":"the dock area","chinese":"碼頭區"},{"english":"the relocation of","chinese":"……的搬遷"},{"english":"the marina","chinese":"遊艇碼頭"},{"english":"fishing boats","chinese":"漁船"},{"english":"On the western side","chinese":"在西面"},{"english":"car parks","chinese":"停車場"},{"english":"the main road","chinese":"主要道路"},{"english":"still in place","chinese":"仍然保留原位"},{"english":"the original showers and toilets","chinese":"原有的淋浴及洗手間設施"},{"english":"have been retained","chinese":"已被保留"},{"english":"retained beside","chinese":"保留在……旁邊"},{"english":"the northern car park","chinese":"北面的停車場"},{"english":"However","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"private yachts","chinese":"私人遊艇"},{"english":"formerly in","chinese":"以前位於"},{"english":"the north-west basin","chinese":"西北面的港池"},{"english":"has been moved southwards","chinese":"已向南搬遷"},{"english":"the area once used by","chinese":"以往由……使用的地方"},{"english":"once used by fishing boats","chinese":"以往由漁船使用"},{"english":"now occupy","chinese":"現時佔用"},{"english":"the former marina site","chinese":"原來的遊艇碼頭位置"},{"english":"a second block of","chinese":"第二座；第二組"},{"english":"has been built near","chinese":"已在……附近興建"},{"english":"the lower car park","chinese":"下方的停車場"},{"english":"cafés and shops","chinese":"咖啡店及商店"},{"english":"have been added west of","chinese":"已在……以西增設"},{"english":"the lifeboat station","chinese":"救生艇站"},{"english":"Further east","chinese":"再往東面"},{"english":"has been enlarged with","chinese":"已擴建並加入……"},{"english":"extra mooring space","chinese":"額外停泊空間"},{"english":"although","chinese":"雖然"},{"english":"passenger ferries","chinese":"客運渡輪"},{"english":"remain nearby","chinese":"仍然在附近"},{"english":"the disused castle","chinese":"荒廢城堡"},{"english":"the small peninsula","chinese":"小半島"},{"english":"has been replaced by","chinese":"已被……取代"},{"english":"accessed by","chinese":"經由……到達"},{"english":"an extended road","chinese":"延伸道路"},{"english":"the southern beach","chinese":"南面的海灘"},{"english":"is now reserved for","chinese":"現時專供……使用"},{"english":"hotel guests","chinese":"酒店住客"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相比之下"},{"english":"the northern public beach","chinese":"北面的公眾海灘"},{"english":"remain largely unchanged","chinese":"大致維持不變"}]},"model-essay-2-ielts-task1-mixed-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-2-ielts-task1-mixed-charts","essayKey":"mixed-charts:2","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-2-ielts-task1-mixed-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/mixed-charts/mixed-charts-2","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The pie chart shows where young people in an Australian town attend dance classes, while the bar chart compares the numbers of under-11s and 11- to 16-year-olds taking ballet, tap and modern dance.","chinese":"圓餅圖顯示澳洲某城鎮的年輕人在哪些地點上舞蹈課，而柱狀圖則比較了 11歲以下以及 11 至 16 歲學生參加芭蕾舞、踢踏舞和現代舞課程的人數。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, private studios are by far the most common venue, accounting for nearly half of all classes, whereas college-based studios represent the smallest share. In terms of dance style, ballet is clearly the leading choice among younger children, while modern dance is more popular with the older group; tap attracts broadly similar numbers in both age bands.","chinese":"整體而言，私人舞蹈室是目前最常見的上課地點，佔所有課程的接近一半；相反，設於學院的舞蹈室所佔比例最小。 就舞蹈類型而言，芭蕾舞明顯是較年幼兒童的首選，而現代舞則更受年齡較大的學生歡迎；踢踏舞在兩個年齡組中的人數大致相近。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Looking first at locations, 48% of classes are held in private studios, exactly twice the proportion taking place in after-school sessions in school halls, at 24%. Community halls and other venues make up a further 18%, leaving college-based studios with only 10%, or around one tenth of the total.","chinese":"先看上課地點， 48% 的課程在私人舞蹈室舉行，這正好是學校禮堂課後課程比例的兩倍，後者為 24% 。 社區禮堂和其他場地另佔 18% ，而學院舞蹈室只佔 10% ，即大約佔整體的十分之一。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Regarding class types, about 600 children under 11 attend ballet, compared with roughly 300 students aged 11–16. Modern dance shows the opposite pattern, with just under 300 younger participants but approximately 520 older ones. Tap is more evenly balanced, at around 450 under-11s and slightly over 400 students in the older age group.","chinese":"就課程類型而言，大約 600 名 11 歲以下兒童參加芭蕾舞課，相比之下， 11 至16 歲的學生約為 300 人。 現代舞則呈現相反模式，較年幼組別的人數略低於 300 ，而較年長組別約有520 人。 踢踏舞的人數分布較平均， 11 歲以下學生約為 450 人，而較年長組別則略高於 400 人。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the charts below","chinese":"以下圖表"},{"english":"give information on","chinese":"提供關於……的資料"},{"english":"the location and types of","chinese":"……的地點及類型"},{"english":"dance classes","chinese":"舞蹈班"},{"english":"young people in a town","chinese":"一個城鎮的年輕人"},{"english":"a town in Australia","chinese":"澳洲一個城鎮"},{"english":"are currently attending","chinese":"現時正在參加"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"by selecting and reporting","chinese":"透過選取並報告……"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"the pie chart shows where","chinese":"圓形圖顯示……在哪裏"},{"english":"attend dance classes","chinese":"參加舞蹈班"},{"english":"the bar chart compares","chinese":"柱形圖比較……"},{"english":"the numbers of","chinese":"……的人數"},{"english":"under-11s","chinese":"11歲以下兒童"},{"english":"11- to 16-year-olds","chinese":"11至16歲學生"},{"english":"taking ballet","chinese":"學習芭蕾舞"},{"english":"ballet","chinese":"芭蕾舞"},{"english":"tap","chinese":"踢踏舞"},{"english":"modern dance","chinese":"現代舞"},{"english":"private studios","chinese":"私人舞蹈室"},{"english":"by far the most common","chinese":"遠遠是最常見的"},{"english":"the most common venue","chinese":"最常見場地"},{"english":"accounting for","chinese":"佔……"},{"english":"nearly half of","chinese":"接近一半"},{"english":"all classes","chinese":"所有課堂"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相反"},{"english":"college-based studios","chinese":"設於學院的舞蹈室"},{"english":"represent the smallest share","chinese":"佔最小比例"},{"english":"the smallest share","chinese":"最小比例"},{"english":"in terms of","chinese":"就……而言"},{"english":"dance style","chinese":"舞蹈類型"},{"english":"the leading choice","chinese":"最主要選擇"},{"english":"among younger children","chinese":"在較年幼兒童之中"},{"english":"more popular with","chinese":"較受……歡迎"},{"english":"the older group","chinese":"較年長組別"},{"english":"attracts broadly similar numbers","chinese":"吸引大致相若的人數"},{"english":"broadly similar numbers","chinese":"大致相若的人數"},{"english":"in both age bands","chinese":"在兩個年齡組別中"},{"english":"looking first at","chinese":"首先看……"},{"english":"are held in","chinese":"在……舉行"},{"english":"exactly twice the proportion","chinese":"比例剛好是……的兩倍"},{"english":"taking place in","chinese":"在……舉行"},{"english":"after-school sessions","chinese":"課後課程"},{"english":"school halls","chinese":"學校禮堂"},{"english":"at 24%","chinese":"為24%"},{"english":"community halls","chinese":"社區會堂"},{"english":"other venues","chinese":"其他場地"},{"english":"make up a further","chinese":"另佔……"},{"english":"leaving X with Y","chinese":"令 X 只佔 Y"},{"english":"only 10%","chinese":"只有10%"},{"english":"around one tenth of","chinese":"約十分之一"},{"english":"the total","chinese":"總數"},{"english":"regarding class types","chinese":"關於課堂類型"},{"english":"about 600 children","chinese":"約600名兒童"},{"english":"children under 11","chinese":"11歲以下兒童"},{"english":"compared with","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"roughly 300 students","chinese":"約300名學生"},{"english":"aged 11–16","chinese":"年齡介乎11至16歲"},{"english":"shows the opposite pattern","chinese":"呈現相反模式"},{"english":"the opposite pattern","chinese":"相反模式"},{"english":"just under 300","chinese":"不足300"},{"english":"younger participants","chinese":"較年幼參加者"},{"english":"approximately 520","chinese":"約520"},{"english":"older ones","chinese":"較年長的一批"},{"english":"more evenly balanced","chinese":"分佈較平均"},{"english":"at around 450","chinese":"約為450"},{"english":"slightly over 400","chinese":"略多於400"},{"english":"the older age group","chinese":"較年長年齡組別"},{"english":"class locations","chinese":"課堂地點"},{"english":"class types","chinese":"課堂類型"},{"english":"venue distribution","chinese":"場地分佈"},{"english":"age-group comparison","chinese":"年齡組別比較"},{"english":"dance-class preferences","chinese":"舞蹈班偏好"},{"english":"a clear preference for","chinese":"明顯偏好……"},{"english":"be dominated by","chinese":"由……主導"},{"english":"remain relatively close","chinese":"保持相對接近"},{"english":"the gap between","chinese":"……之間的差距"},{"english":"twice as high as","chinese":"約為……的兩倍"},{"english":"a noticeable contrast","chinese":"明顯對比"}]},"model-essay-2-ielts-task1-pie-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-2-ielts-task1-pie-charts","essayKey":"pie-charts:2","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-2-ielts-task1-pie-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/pie-charts/pie-chart-2","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The six pie charts compare how water is allocated to agriculture, industry and domestic purposes in six regions of the world.","chinese":"六個餅圖比較了世界六個地區的用水如何分配於農業、工業和家庭用途。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, agriculture dominates water consumption in four of the six regions, particularly Central Asia, Africa and South East Asia. By contrast, industrial use takes the largest share in Europe and North America, while household use remains comparatively small everywhere and never represents the leading category.","chinese":"整體而言，農業在六個地區中的四個地區佔據用水主導地位，尤其是在中亞、非洲和東南亞。 相比之下，工業用途在歐洲和北美佔最大比例，而家庭用水在所有地區都相對較小，並且從未成為主導類別。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In the two regions where industry is the main user, Europe records the highest industrial proportion, at 53%, slightly above North America’s 48%. Agricultural use is lower in both places, accounting for 32% in Europe and 39% in North America, whereas domestic consumption is modest, at 15% and 13% respectively.","chinese":"在工業是主要用水者的兩個地區中，歐洲的工業用水比例最高，為 53% ，略高於北美的 48% 。 在這兩個地區，農業用水比例都較低，歐洲為 32% ，北美為 39% ；而家庭用水比例則較溫和，分別為 15% 和 13% 。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The remaining four regions are clearly agriculture-centred. Central Asia has the most pronounced reliance on farming, with 88% of water used for this purpose, followed closely by Africa at 84% and South East Asia at 81%. South America also devotes a large majority to agriculture, at 71%, although its domestic share, 19%, is noticeably higher than in the other agriculture-dominated regions. Industrial use is minimal in these areas, ranging from only 5% in Central Asia to 12% in South East Asia.","chinese":"其餘四個地區明顯以農業用水為中心。 中亞對農業用水的依賴最明顯，有 88% 的水用於此目的，其次是非洲的 84% 和東南亞的 81% 。 南美洲也將絕大部分水用於農業，比例為 71% ；不過其家庭用水比例為 19% ，明顯高於其他以農業為主的地區。 在這些地區，工業用水比例很低，從中亞的僅 5% 到東南亞的 12% 不等。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"six pie charts","chinese":"六個圓形圖"},{"english":"compare how water is allocated to","chinese":"比較水資源如何分配予……"},{"english":"be allocated to","chinese":"被分配予……"},{"english":"agriculture","chinese":"農業"},{"english":"industry","chinese":"工業"},{"english":"domestic purposes","chinese":"家居用途"},{"english":"six regions of the world","chinese":"世界六個地區"},{"english":"dominates water consumption","chinese":"主導用水量"},{"english":"water consumption","chinese":"用水量"},{"english":"in four of the six regions","chinese":"在六個地區中的四個"},{"english":"particularly","chinese":"尤其是"},{"english":"Central Asia","chinese":"中亞"},{"english":"South East Asia","chinese":"東南亞"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"industrial use","chinese":"工業用水"},{"english":"takes the largest share","chinese":"佔最大比例"},{"english":"household use","chinese":"家居用水"},{"english":"remains comparatively small","chinese":"仍然相對較小"},{"english":"comparatively small","chinese":"相對較小"},{"english":"never represents the leading category","chinese":"從未成為主要類別"},{"english":"leading category","chinese":"主要類別"},{"english":"the main user","chinese":"主要使用者"},{"english":"records the highest industrial proportion","chinese":"錄得最高工業比例"},{"english":"industrial proportion","chinese":"工業比例"},{"english":"at 53%","chinese":"達53%"},{"english":"slightly above","chinese":"略高於"},{"english":"agricultural use","chinese":"農業用水"},{"english":"lower in both places","chinese":"在兩地均較低"},{"english":"in both places","chinese":"在兩地"},{"english":"accounting for","chinese":"佔"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相比之下"},{"english":"domestic consumption","chinese":"家居用水量"},{"english":"modest","chinese":"不高；有限"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"the remaining four regions","chinese":"其餘四個地區"},{"english":"agriculture-centred","chinese":"以農業為中心的"},{"english":"the most pronounced reliance on","chinese":"對……最明顯依賴"},{"english":"reliance on farming","chinese":"對農業的依賴"},{"english":"with 88% of water used for this purpose","chinese":"有88%的水用於此用途"},{"english":"used for this purpose","chinese":"用於此用途"},{"english":"followed closely by","chinese":"緊隨其後的是"},{"english":"at 84%","chinese":"達84%"},{"english":"devotes a large majority to","chinese":"將大部分……用於"},{"english":"a large majority","chinese":"大部分"},{"english":"although","chinese":"雖然"},{"english":"domestic share","chinese":"家居用水比例"},{"english":"noticeably higher than","chinese":"明顯高於"},{"english":"agriculture-dominated regions","chinese":"以農業為主的地區"},{"english":"industrial use is minimal","chinese":"工業用水極少"},{"english":"minimal","chinese":"極少的"},{"english":"ranging from…to…","chinese":"介乎……至……"},{"english":"ranging from only 5%","chinese":"由僅5%起"},{"english":"to 12%","chinese":"至12%"},{"english":"these areas","chinese":"這些地區"}]},"model-essay-2-ielts-task1-process-diagram":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-2-ielts-task1-process-diagram","essayKey":"process-diagram:2","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-2-ielts-task1-process-diagram","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/process-diagrams/process-diagram-2","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The diagram illustrates the cyclical process by which the biofuel ethanol is produced from plant material and then used as an energy source.","chinese":"該圖說明生物燃料乙醇如何由植物材料製成，然後被用作能源的循環過程。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, ethanol production begins with the growth of plants and trees, which use sunlight and carbon dioxide, and ends with ethanol being consumed by vehicles. A key feature is that the carbon dioxide released during use is returned to the atmosphere and can be absorbed by new vegetation, allowing the cycle to continue.","chinese":"整體而言，乙醇的生產始於植物和樹木的生長，它們利用陽光和二氧化碳；最後則以乙醇被交通工具消耗作結。 一個關鍵特徵是，使用過程中釋放出的二氧化碳會回到大氣中，並可被新的植被吸收，使整個循環得以持續。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In the first stage, plants and trees grow through exposure to sunlight and carbon dioxide. Once mature, they are harvested by machinery and sent for pre-processing, where the raw biomass is prepared. The material is then reduced to cellulose, which is transferred to a processing plant.","chinese":"在第一階段，植物和樹木透過接觸陽光和二氧化碳而生長。 當它們成熟後，會由機械收割，並送往預處理階段，在那裡原始生物質會被準備好。 接著，這些材料會被轉化為纖維素，並被送往加工廠。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Inside the plant, cellulose is broken down into sugars. Microbes are subsequently added to these sugars, and this biological stage converts them into ethanol. The finished fuel is then distributed for use in transport, including cars, lorries and aircraft. As these vehicles consume ethanol, carbon dioxide is emitted; this gas then becomes part of the next growing stage when it is taken up again by plants and trees.","chinese":"在加工廠內，纖維素會被分解成糖。 隨後，微生物會被加入這些糖中，而這一生物階段會把它們轉化為乙醇。 完成後的燃料接著會被分配到交通運輸中使用，包括汽車、貨車和飛機。 當這些交通工具消耗乙醇時，二氧化碳會被排放出來；之後，這種氣體會在再次被植物和樹木吸收時，成為下一個生長階段的一部分。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"diagram illustrates","chinese":"圖示說明"},{"english":"cyclical process","chinese":"循環過程"},{"english":"by which","chinese":"藉此；通過這個方式"},{"english":"biofuel ethanol","chinese":"生物燃料乙醇"},{"english":"is produced from","chinese":"由……生產"},{"english":"plant material","chinese":"植物材料"},{"english":"used as an energy source","chinese":"用作能源"},{"english":"energy source","chinese":"能源"},{"english":"ethanol production","chinese":"乙醇生產"},{"english":"begins with","chinese":"以……開始"},{"english":"the growth of plants and trees","chinese":"植物及樹木的生長"},{"english":"carbon dioxide","chinese":"二氧化碳"},{"english":"ends with","chinese":"以……結束"},{"english":"being consumed by vehicles","chinese":"被車輛消耗"},{"english":"a key feature is that","chinese":"一個主要特點是"},{"english":"released during use","chinese":"在使用期間釋放"},{"english":"returned to the atmosphere","chinese":"返回大氣層"},{"english":"atmosphere","chinese":"大氣層"},{"english":"absorbed by new vegetation","chinese":"被新植被吸收"},{"english":"new vegetation","chinese":"新植被"},{"english":"allowing the cycle to continue","chinese":"使循環得以延續"},{"english":"the cycle to continue","chinese":"循環延續"},{"english":"in the first stage","chinese":"在第一階段"},{"english":"grow through exposure to","chinese":"通過接觸……而生長"},{"english":"exposure to sunlight","chinese":"接觸陽光"},{"english":"once mature","chinese":"成熟後"},{"english":"are harvested by machinery","chinese":"由機器收割"},{"english":"machinery","chinese":"機器；機械"},{"english":"sent for pre-processing","chinese":"被送往預處理"},{"english":"pre-processing","chinese":"預處理"},{"english":"raw biomass","chinese":"原始生物質"},{"english":"is prepared","chinese":"被準備；被處理"},{"english":"is reduced to cellulose","chinese":"被分解成纖維素"},{"english":"cellulose","chinese":"纖維素"},{"english":"transferred to","chinese":"被轉移至"},{"english":"processing plant","chinese":"加工廠"},{"english":"inside the plant","chinese":"在工廠內"},{"english":"broken down into","chinese":"被分解成"},{"english":"sugars","chinese":"糖分"},{"english":"microbes","chinese":"微生物"},{"english":"are subsequently added to","chinese":"隨後被加入……"},{"english":"subsequently","chinese":"隨後"},{"english":"biological stage","chinese":"生物階段"},{"english":"converts them into","chinese":"將它們轉化成"},{"english":"finished fuel","chinese":"製成的燃料"},{"english":"distributed for use in transport","chinese":"被分發作交通用途"},{"english":"transport","chinese":"交通運輸"},{"english":"including cars, lorries and aircraft","chinese":"包括汽車、貨車及飛機"},{"english":"lorries","chinese":"貨車"},{"english":"aircraft","chinese":"飛機"},{"english":"consume ethanol","chinese":"消耗乙醇"},{"english":"is emitted","chinese":"被排放"},{"english":"becomes part of","chinese":"成為……的一部分"},{"english":"the next growing stage","chinese":"下一個生長階段"},{"english":"taken up again by","chinese":"再次被……吸收"},{"english":"process diagram","chinese":"流程圖"},{"english":"production cycle","chinese":"生產循環"},{"english":"renewable fuel","chinese":"可再生燃料"},{"english":"carbon cycle","chinese":"碳循環"}]},"model-essay-2-ielts-task1-tables":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-2-ielts-task1-tables","essayKey":"tables:2","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-2-ielts-task1-tables","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/tables/table-2","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The tables compare sales of Fairtrade-labelled coffee and bananas, measured in millions of euros, in five European countries in 1999 and 2004.","chinese":"這些表格比較了 1999 年和 2004 年五個歐洲國家的公平貿易標籤咖啡和香蕉銷售額，單位為百萬歐元。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, coffee sales increased in every market, with the UK recording by far the most striking rise and becoming the leading purchaser by 2004. Banana sales showed a less even pattern: Switzerland remained dominant and grew sharply, whereas Sweden and Denmark experienced declines.","chinese":"整體而言，咖啡銷售額在每個市場都有上升，其中英國的升幅最為顯著，並在 2004 年成為最大的購買國。 香蕉銷售額的變化則沒有那麼一致：瑞士仍然佔主導地位並大幅增長，而瑞典和丹麥則出現下降。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Regarding coffee, Switzerland had the highest figure in 1999, at 3 million euros, followed by Denmark at 1.8 million and the UK at 1.5 million. By 2004, however, the UK had surged to 20 million euros, more than three times Switzerland’s figure of 6 million. The remaining countries saw only modest growth, with Denmark edging up to 2 million, Belgium to 1.7 million and Sweden to 1 million.","chinese":"就咖啡而言，瑞士在 1999 年的銷售額最高，為 300 萬歐元，其次是丹麥的 180 萬歐元和英國的 150 萬歐元。 然而，到 2004 年，英國銷售額激增至 2,000 萬歐元，是瑞士 600 萬歐元的三倍多。 其餘國家只錄得溫和增長，其中丹麥微升至 200 萬歐元，比利時升至 170 萬歐元，瑞典則升至 100 萬歐元。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Banana sales were led by Switzerland in both years, rising from 15 to 47 million euros, which was far ahead of all other markets. The UK and Belgium also increased substantially, reaching 5.5 million and 4 million respectively in 2004. By contrast, Sweden fell from 1.8 to 1 million, while Denmark dropped from 2 to 0.9 million, becoming the smallest market.","chinese":"香蕉銷售額在兩個年份都由瑞士領先，從 1,500 萬歐元上升至 4,700 萬歐元，遠高於所有其他市場。 英國和比利時也大幅增長，在 2004 年分別達到 550 萬歐元和 400 萬歐元。 相比之下，瑞典從 180 萬歐元下降至 100 萬歐元，而丹麥則從 200 萬歐元跌至 90萬歐元，成為最小的市場。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"give information about","chinese":"提供關於……的資料"},{"english":"sales of","chinese":"……的銷售額"},{"english":"Fairtrade-labelled coffee","chinese":"貼有公平貿易標籤的咖啡"},{"english":"Fairtrade-labelled bananas","chinese":"貼有公平貿易標籤的香蕉"},{"english":"in 1999 and 2004","chinese":"在1999年和2004年"},{"english":"five European countries","chinese":"五個歐洲國家"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"selecting and reporting","chinese":"選取並報告"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"the tables compare","chinese":"表格比較"},{"english":"measured in millions of euros","chinese":"以百萬歐元計算"},{"english":"millions of euros","chinese":"百萬歐元"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"coffee sales","chinese":"咖啡銷售額"},{"english":"increased in every market","chinese":"在每個市場均上升"},{"english":"every market","chinese":"每個市場"},{"english":"with the UK recording","chinese":"其中英國錄得"},{"english":"by far the most striking rise","chinese":"遠遠最顯著的升幅"},{"english":"the most striking rise","chinese":"最顯著的升幅"},{"english":"becoming the leading purchaser","chinese":"成為最大購買國"},{"english":"the leading purchaser","chinese":"最大購買國"},{"english":"by 2004","chinese":"到2004年"},{"english":"banana sales","chinese":"香蕉銷售額"},{"english":"showed a less even pattern","chinese":"呈現較不平均的模式"},{"english":"a less even pattern","chinese":"較不平均的模式"},{"english":"remained dominant","chinese":"仍然佔主導地位"},{"english":"grew sharply","chinese":"大幅增長"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相比之下"},{"english":"experienced declines","chinese":"經歷下跌"},{"english":"Regarding coffee","chinese":"至於咖啡方面"},{"english":"had the highest figure","chinese":"數字最高"},{"english":"the highest figure","chinese":"最高數字"},{"english":"at 3 million euros","chinese":"為300萬歐元"},{"english":"followed by","chinese":"其次是"},{"english":"at 1.8 million","chinese":"為180萬"},{"english":"at 1.5 million","chinese":"為150萬"},{"english":"however","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"had surged to","chinese":"已急升至"},{"english":"20 million euros","chinese":"2,000萬歐元"},{"english":"more than three times","chinese":"超過三倍"},{"english":"Switzerland's figure","chinese":"瑞士的數字"},{"english":"the remaining countries","chinese":"其餘國家"},{"english":"saw only modest growth","chinese":"只錄得溫和增長"},{"english":"modest growth","chinese":"溫和增長"},{"english":"edging up to","chinese":"輕微上升至"},{"english":"Belgium","chinese":"比利時"},{"english":"Sweden","chinese":"瑞典"},{"english":"Banana sales were led by","chinese":"香蕉銷售由……領先"},{"english":"in both years","chinese":"在兩年中"},{"english":"rising from … to …","chinese":"由……上升至……"},{"english":"from 15 to 47 million euros","chinese":"由1,500萬歐元升至4,700萬歐元"},{"english":"far ahead of","chinese":"遠遠領先於"},{"english":"all other markets","chinese":"所有其他市場"},{"english":"also increased substantially","chinese":"亦大幅增加"},{"english":"increased substantially","chinese":"大幅增加"},{"english":"reaching 5.5 million","chinese":"達到550萬"},{"english":"reaching 4 million respectively","chinese":"分別達到400萬"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"fell from … to …","chinese":"由……跌至……"},{"english":"from 1.8 to 1 million","chinese":"由180萬跌至100萬"},{"english":"while","chinese":"而"},{"english":"dropped from … to …","chinese":"由……下降至……"},{"english":"from 2 to 0.9 million","chinese":"由200萬跌至90萬"},{"english":"becoming the smallest market","chinese":"成為最小的市場"},{"english":"the smallest market","chinese":"最小的市場"}]},"model-essay-3-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-3-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:3","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-3-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q3","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"It has become increasingly common for school-leavers to spend a gap year doing charitable work in less developed countries before entering university. Although this choice can create emotional and academic difficulties, it is ultimately a highly positive experience for young people because it develops maturity and gives them a far deeper understanding of society than a conventional year at home would.","chinese":"在進入大學前先花一年到海外從事慈善工作，已愈來愈成為離校生常見的選擇。 雖然這個決定可能帶來情緒壓力，並打亂原有的學習習慣， 本文將論證，這樣的經歷對年輕人而言最終是有益的，因為它能加速個人成長，並加深他們對社會的理解。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The primary advantage is accelerated personal growth. When young volunteers live abroad, they must budget, solve practical problems and communicate in unfamiliar settings without the daily support of parents or teachers. This pushes them to become more self-reliant, adaptable and resilient, which are precisely the qualities needed for university life and later employment. A student helping to organise food distribution, for example, may need to cope with transport failures, limited resources and language barriers on a daily basis. A second benefit is the way such work broadens moral and intellectual perspective. Seeing inadequate schooling, poor sanitation or limited medical care at first hand turns abstract global issues into concrete human realities. As a result, many young people become more socially aware and more purposeful about their future. Someone who assists in a rural clinic, for instance, may return home determined to study medicine, public health or international development.","chinese":"到海外從事義工工作的第一個優點，是它能促進快速的個人成長。 生活在一個陌生的國家，會迫使年輕人自己管理金錢、處理日常問題，並在沒有父母或老師持續支援的情況下獨立與人溝通。 因此，他們會變得更獨立、更有適應力，也更堅韌，而這些正是大學生活及未來就業所必需的特質。 例如，一名協助安排糧食分發的學生，可能每天都要處理交通失誤、資源不足以及語言障礙。 義工工作也能擴闊年輕人的道德與思想視野。 親眼看到教育體系薄弱、衛生條件惡劣或醫療資源不足，會把抽象的全球問題轉化為具體的人類現實。 這往往會使義工變得更有社會意識，也更清楚自己未來的人生方向。 例如，一位在鄉村診所幫忙的人，回國後可能會下定決心修讀醫學、公共衛生或國際發展。 基於以上原因，義工工作能在個人層面與思想層面同時令年輕人受益。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, there are undeniable disadvantages. One is the emotional strain of working in communities affected by poverty, illness or trauma. Many teenagers are still psychologically inexperienced, so constant exposure to suffering can leave them distressed, guilty or overwhelmed rather than inspired. A volunteer in an orphanage, for example, may form strong attachments and then find the eventual separation deeply upsetting. Another drawback is that a gap year can weaken academic momentum. After spending many months outside formal education, some students struggle to readjust to lectures, deadlines and examinations, especially when university courses demand intense concentration from the outset. For example, a school-leaver who has spent a year on construction or community projects may find essay writing and exam preparation unexpectedly difficult on returning to study.","chinese":"然而，主要的缺點在於情緒壓力與學業中斷。 在受貧窮、疾病或創傷影響的社區工作，對於心理上仍未成熟的青少年而言，可能會造成沉重的心理負擔。 長期接觸苦難，可能不會令他們受到鼓舞，反而會使他們感到痛苦、內疚或不堪負荷。 例如，一名在孤兒院服務的義工，可能會與孩子建立深厚感情，而最終的分離則會令他十分難受。 空檔年也可能削弱原有的學習節奏。 在離開正規教育數月之後，有些學生在大學開始時，會難以重新適應講課、截止日期和考試。 尤其當學位課程一開始就要求高度專注與嚴格的學習習慣時，這種情況更為明顯。 例如，一名把一年時間投入建設或社區項目的畢業生，在回到校園後，可能會發現寫論文與準備考試比預期更困難。 即便如此，這些缺點仍不足以蓋過這段經歷的長遠價值。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, volunteering abroad is not an easy option for young people, as it can be emotionally demanding and can interrupt study habits. Even so, it remains a profoundly worthwhile experience, since few alternatives cultivate independence, perspective and long-term purpose so effectively.","chinese":"總而言之，我認為在空檔年到海外從事義工工作，對年輕人而言最終是利大於弊的。 雖然它可能帶來情緒壓力並打斷學習習慣，但它能培養獨立性、韌性與社會意識，而這些往往是一般經歷難以帶來的。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"increasingly common for","chinese":"對……來說越來越常見"},{"english":"school-leavers","chinese":"中學畢業生"},{"english":"spend a gap year","chinese":"度過空檔年"},{"english":"charitable work","chinese":"慈善工作"},{"english":"less developed countries","chinese":"發展程度較低的國家"},{"english":"before entering university","chinese":"入讀大學之前"},{"english":"this choice","chinese":"這個選擇"},{"english":"emotional and academic difficulties","chinese":"情緒和學業上的困難"},{"english":"ultimately","chinese":"最終"},{"english":"a highly positive experience","chinese":"非常正面的經歷"},{"english":"develops maturity","chinese":"培養成熟度"},{"english":"gives them a far deeper understanding of","chinese":"令他們對……有深入得多的理解"},{"english":"a conventional year at home","chinese":"傳統留在本地的一年"},{"english":"the primary advantage","chinese":"主要好處"},{"english":"accelerated personal growth","chinese":"加速的個人成長"},{"english":"live abroad","chinese":"在海外生活"},{"english":"budget","chinese":"管理預算"},{"english":"solve practical problems","chinese":"解決實際問題"},{"english":"unfamiliar settings","chinese":"陌生環境"},{"english":"without the daily support of","chinese":"沒有……的日常支援"},{"english":"pushes them to become","chinese":"推動他們變得"},{"english":"self-reliant","chinese":"自力更生"},{"english":"adaptable","chinese":"適應力強的"},{"english":"resilient","chinese":"有抗逆力的"},{"english":"precisely the qualities needed for","chinese":"正正是……所需要的素質"},{"english":"university life","chinese":"大學生活"},{"english":"later employment","chinese":"日後就業"},{"english":"helping to organise","chinese":"協助組織"},{"english":"food distribution","chinese":"食物派發"},{"english":"cope with","chinese":"應付"},{"english":"transport failures","chinese":"交通失誤；交通安排出問題"},{"english":"limited resources","chinese":"有限資源"},{"english":"language barriers","chinese":"語言障礙"},{"english":"on a daily basis","chinese":"每日；日常地"},{"english":"a second benefit","chinese":"第二個好處"},{"english":"broadens moral and intellectual perspective","chinese":"擴闊道德和思想視野"},{"english":"inadequate schooling","chinese":"不足的學校教育"},{"english":"poor sanitation","chinese":"惡劣衞生環境"},{"english":"limited medical care","chinese":"有限醫療服務"},{"english":"at first hand","chinese":"親身"},{"english":"abstract global issues","chinese":"抽象的全球議題"},{"english":"concrete human realities","chinese":"具體的人類現實"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"socially aware","chinese":"有社會意識的"},{"english":"more purposeful about","chinese":"對……更有目標"},{"english":"assists in","chinese":"在……協助"},{"english":"a rural clinic","chinese":"鄉村診所"},{"english":"return home determined to","chinese":"回家後決心去……"},{"english":"public health","chinese":"公共衞生"},{"english":"international development","chinese":"國際發展"},{"english":"undeniable disadvantages","chinese":"無可否認的缺點"},{"english":"emotional strain","chinese":"情緒壓力"},{"english":"communities affected by","chinese":"受……影響的社區"},{"english":"poverty, illness or trauma","chinese":"貧窮、疾病或創傷"},{"english":"psychologically inexperienced","chinese":"心理上仍缺乏經驗"},{"english":"constant exposure to","chinese":"持續接觸……"},{"english":"suffering","chinese":"苦難"},{"english":"leave them distressed","chinese":"令他們感到痛苦"},{"english":"guilty or overwhelmed","chinese":"愧疚或不知所措"},{"english":"rather than inspired","chinese":"而不是受到啟發"},{"english":"form strong attachments","chinese":"建立深厚感情"},{"english":"an orphanage","chinese":"孤兒院"},{"english":"eventual separation","chinese":"最終分離"},{"english":"deeply upsetting","chinese":"令人非常難過"},{"english":"another drawback","chinese":"另一個缺點"},{"english":"weaken academic momentum","chinese":"削弱學習動力和節奏"},{"english":"outside formal education","chinese":"在正規教育之外"},{"english":"struggle to readjust to","chinese":"難以重新適應"},{"english":"lectures, deadlines and examinations","chinese":"講課、限期和考試"},{"english":"demand intense concentration","chinese":"要求高度專注"},{"english":"from the outset","chinese":"從一開始"},{"english":"construction or community projects","chinese":"建築或社區項目"},{"english":"essay writing","chinese":"文章寫作"},{"english":"exam preparation","chinese":"考試準備"},{"english":"unexpectedly difficult","chinese":"出乎意料地困難"},{"english":"returning to study","chinese":"重返學習"},{"english":"not an easy option","chinese":"不是輕鬆的選擇"},{"english":"emotionally demanding","chinese":"情緒上要求很高的"},{"english":"interrupt study habits","chinese":"打斷學習習慣"},{"english":"even so","chinese":"即使如此"},{"english":"profoundly worthwhile","chinese":"非常值得的"},{"english":"few alternatives","chinese":"很少其他選擇"},{"english":"cultivate independence","chinese":"培養獨立性"},{"english":"long-term purpose","chinese":"長遠目標感"},{"english":"so effectively","chinese":"如此有效地"}]},"model-essay-3-ielts-cause-solution":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-3-ielts-cause-solution","essayKey":"cause-solution:3","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-3-ielts-cause-solution","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/problem-and-cause/EdmundBd9CnS-Q3","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The gap between wealthy and impoverished nations has widened in many parts of the world, creating a cycle in which prosperity attracts more prosperity while poverty becomes harder to escape. The main cause of this problem is the unequal access countries have to the systems that create long-term wealth. This essay will explain this cause and suggest practical ways to address it.","chinese":"在世界許多地方，富裕國家與貧困國家之間的差距已經擴大，形成了一種富裕吸引更多富裕、而貧困變得更難擺脫的循環。 這個問題的主要原因是，各國在取得能夠創造長期財富的系統方面存在不平等。 本文將解釋這個原因，並提出實際可行的方法來處理這個問題。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The central reason is that rich countries usually possess better education systems, stronger institutions, advanced technology and easier access to investment. These advantages allow them to produce high-value goods and services, such as medicines, software and financial products, which generate large profits. Poor countries, by contrast, often depend on exporting raw materials or low-paid labour. As a result, they earn less, collect less tax and struggle to build the roads, schools and hospitals that would help them compete. This becomes a vicious circle: the less a country can invest in its people and infrastructure, the harder it is for that country to move beyond survival and into genuine development.","chinese":"核心原因是，富裕國家通常擁有更好的教育制度、更強大的制度、先進科技，以及更容易取得投資的渠道。 這些優勢使它們能夠生產高價值的商品和服務，例如藥物、軟件和金融產品，而這些都能創造龐大利潤。 相比之下，貧困國家往往依賴出口原材料或低薪勞動力。 結果是，它們賺得更少、徵收的稅收更少，也難以建設能幫助它們競爭的道路、學校和醫院。 這便形成了一個惡性循環：一個國家越無法投資於人民和基礎建設，它就越難從僅僅維持生存，走向真正的發展。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"To reduce this gap, both international reform and domestic improvement are needed. Wealthier countries and global institutions should make trade rules fairer, reduce unfair debt burdens and support poorer nations with targeted investment in education, healthcare and clean infrastructure. This would give developing economies the tools to grow rather than leaving them permanently dependent on aid. At the same time, governments in poorer countries must strengthen transparency, reduce corruption and invest public money in industries that can create skilled employment. For example, supporting vocational training and small local businesses can help workers move from unstable informal jobs into more productive work. In this way, aid becomes a stepping stone, not a crutch.","chinese":"要縮小這個差距，國際層面的改革和國內層面的改善都是必要的。 較富裕的國家和全球機構應該使貿易規則更加公平、減少不公平的債務負擔，並透過針對教育、醫療和清潔基礎建設的投資來支持較貧困的國家。 這將給予發展中經濟體成長所需的工具，而不是讓它們永久依賴援助。 與此同時，貧困國家的政府必須加強透明度、減少貪污，並把公共資金投放於能夠創造技術型就業的產業。 例如，支持職業培訓和本地小型企業，可以幫助工人從不穩定的非正式工作轉向更具生產力的工作。 這樣一來，援助便會成為踏腳石，而不是拐杖。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, the widening wealth gap is mainly caused by unequal access to education, technology, capital and stable institutions. It can be reduced through fairer global rules, responsible investment and stronger domestic governance.","chinese":"總結來說，財富差距擴大的主要原因，是各國在取得教育、科技、資本和穩定制度方面存在不平等。 這個問題可以透過更公平的全球規則、負責任的投資，以及更強大的國內治理來減輕。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the gap between","chinese":"……之間的差距"},{"english":"wealthy and impoverished nations","chinese":"富裕國家和貧困國家"},{"english":"has widened","chinese":"已經擴大"},{"english":"creating a cycle","chinese":"形成一個循環"},{"english":"prosperity attracts more prosperity","chinese":"繁榮吸引更多繁榮"},{"english":"harder to escape","chinese":"更難擺脫"},{"english":"the main cause of","chinese":"……的主要原因"},{"english":"unequal access to","chinese":"不平等地獲得……的機會"},{"english":"the systems that create long-term wealth","chinese":"創造長遠財富的系統"},{"english":"practical ways to address it","chinese":"處理它的實際方法"},{"english":"the central reason","chinese":"核心原因"},{"english":"possess better education systems","chinese":"擁有較好的教育制度"},{"english":"stronger institutions","chinese":"更健全的制度"},{"english":"advanced technology","chinese":"先進科技"},{"english":"easier access to investment","chinese":"較容易獲得投資"},{"english":"these advantages","chinese":"這些優勢"},{"english":"allow them to","chinese":"讓他們能夠"},{"english":"high-value goods and services","chinese":"高價值商品和服務"},{"english":"financial products","chinese":"金融產品"},{"english":"generate large profits","chinese":"產生巨額利潤"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"depend on exporting","chinese":"依賴出口"},{"english":"raw materials","chinese":"原材料"},{"english":"low-paid labour","chinese":"低薪勞工"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此；結果"},{"english":"collect less tax","chinese":"收取較少稅款"},{"english":"struggle to build","chinese":"難以建設"},{"english":"help them compete","chinese":"幫助他們競爭"},{"english":"a vicious circle","chinese":"惡性循環"},{"english":"invest in its people and infrastructure","chinese":"投資於人民和基礎設施"},{"english":"move beyond survival","chinese":"超越僅僅維持生存的階段"},{"english":"genuine development","chinese":"真正發展"},{"english":"reduce this gap","chinese":"縮小這個差距"},{"english":"international reform","chinese":"國際改革"},{"english":"domestic improvement","chinese":"國內改善"},{"english":"global institutions","chinese":"全球機構"},{"english":"make trade rules fairer","chinese":"令貿易規則更公平"},{"english":"reduce unfair debt burdens","chinese":"減輕不公平的債務負擔"},{"english":"targeted investment in","chinese":"對……的針對性投資"},{"english":"clean infrastructure","chinese":"清潔基礎設施"},{"english":"developing economies","chinese":"發展中經濟體"},{"english":"the tools to grow","chinese":"增長所需的工具"},{"english":"rather than leaving them","chinese":"而不是令它們……"},{"english":"permanently dependent on aid","chinese":"長期依賴援助"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"與此同時"},{"english":"strengthen transparency","chinese":"加強透明度"},{"english":"reduce corruption","chinese":"減少貪污"},{"english":"invest public money in","chinese":"將公帑投資於……"},{"english":"skilled employment","chinese":"技術型就業"},{"english":"vocational training","chinese":"職業培訓"},{"english":"small local businesses","chinese":"小型本地企業"},{"english":"unstable informal jobs","chinese":"不穩定的非正式工作"},{"english":"more productive work","chinese":"生產力更高的工作"},{"english":"in this way","chinese":"這樣一來"},{"english":"a stepping stone, not a crutch","chinese":"踏腳石，而不是拐杖"},{"english":"the widening wealth gap","chinese":"不斷擴大的財富差距"},{"english":"capital","chinese":"資本"},{"english":"stable institutions","chinese":"穩定制度"},{"english":"fairer global rules","chinese":"更公平的全球規則"},{"english":"responsible investment","chinese":"負責任的投資"},{"english":"stronger domestic governance","chinese":"更強的國內治理"}]},"model-essay-3-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-3-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:3","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-3-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q3","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Many organisations require employees to wear a standard uniform whenever they are on duty. Although this may seem like a simple rule about clothing, it can serve several important business purposes and can also make daily working life easier for employees.","chinese":"許多機構要求員工在值班時必須穿著標準制服。 儘管這看起來可能只是一項關於服裝的簡單規定，但它可以服務於幾個重要的商業目的，也可以讓員工的日常工作生活變得更容易。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"For companies, the clearest advantage is that uniforms create a consistent and professional public image. When customers see staff dressed in the same recognisable way, the business appears more organised, reliable and trustworthy. This is especially important in service industries such as hotels, airlines and restaurants, where first impressions can shape the customer’s view of the whole company. A uniform also makes employees easy to identify. As a result, customers can ask for help more quickly, managers can supervise the workplace more efficiently, and outsiders are less likely to enter restricted areas unnoticed. In jobs involving food, healthcare or machinery, a uniform can also support hygiene and safety because workers are dressed in clothing designed for that particular environment.","chinese":"對公司而言，最明顯的優點是制服能夠塑造一致而專業的公眾形象。 當顧客看到員工以同樣容易識別的方式穿著時，該企業會顯得更有組織、更可靠，也更值得信任。 這在酒店、航空公司和餐廳等服務行業中尤其重要，因為第一印象可以塑造顧客對整間公司的看法。 制服也讓員工容易被識別。 因此，顧客可以更快尋求幫助，管理人員可以更有效率地監督工作場所，而外來人士也較不可能在未被察覺的情況下進入限制區域。 在涉及食品、醫療或機械的工作中，制服也可以支持衛生和安全，因為員工穿著的是為該特定環境而設計的服裝。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"There are clear benefits for staff as well. First, uniforms remove the daily pressure of deciding what to wear and reduce the need to spend money on fashionable or work-appropriate clothes. This is a practical advantage, particularly for lower-paid employees who might otherwise feel judged by their appearance. Secondly, uniforms can create a stronger sense of equality and belonging. When everyone wears similar clothing, differences in wealth, taste or social background become less visible, and staff may feel that they are part of the same team. In addition, well-designed uniforms can be comfortable and protective, allowing employees to focus on their tasks rather than on their clothing.","chinese":"對員工而言，也有明顯的好處。 首先，制服消除了每天決定穿甚麼的壓力，也減少了在時尚服裝或適合工作的服裝上花錢的需要。 這是一個實際的優點，尤其是對收入較低的員工而言，否則他們可能會因自己的外表而感到被評價。 其次，制服可以創造更強的平等感和歸屬感。 當每個人穿著相似的服裝時，財富、品味或社會背景上的差異會變得較不明顯，而員工也可能會覺得自己是同一個團隊的一部分。 此外，設計良好的制服可以既舒適又具保護性，讓員工能夠專注於自己的工作任務，而不是自己的衣著。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, uniforms benefit companies by strengthening brand image, improving identification and supporting workplace control. They can also benefit employees by saving time and money, reducing social pressure and encouraging a shared sense of professionalism.","chinese":"總結來說，制服透過強化品牌形象、改善識別度和支持工作場所管理，為公司帶來好處 它們也可以透過節省時間和金錢、減少社交壓力，以及鼓勵共同的專業意識，為員工帶來好處。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"require employees to","chinese":"要求員工去"},{"english":"a standard uniform","chinese":"標準制服"},{"english":"on duty","chinese":"當值；值勤"},{"english":"may seem like","chinese":"可能看似"},{"english":"a simple rule about clothing","chinese":"關於衣着的簡單規則"},{"english":"serve several important business purposes","chinese":"發揮幾個重要商業作用"},{"english":"daily working life","chinese":"日常工作生活"},{"english":"the clearest advantage","chinese":"最明顯的好處"},{"english":"create a consistent and professional public image","chinese":"建立一致而專業的公眾形象"},{"english":"dressed in the same recognisable way","chinese":"以相同而容易辨認的方式穿着"},{"english":"appears more organised","chinese":"顯得更有組織"},{"english":"reliable and trustworthy","chinese":"可靠而值得信任"},{"english":"service industries","chinese":"服務行業"},{"english":"first impressions","chinese":"第一印象"},{"english":"shape the customer's view of","chinese":"塑造顧客對……的看法"},{"english":"the whole company","chinese":"整間公司"},{"english":"easy to identify","chinese":"容易辨認"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"ask for help more quickly","chinese":"更快尋求協助"},{"english":"supervise the workplace more efficiently","chinese":"更有效率地監督工作場所"},{"english":"outsiders","chinese":"外來人士"},{"english":"restricted areas","chinese":"限制進入區域"},{"english":"enter restricted areas unnoticed","chinese":"未被察覺地進入限制區域"},{"english":"jobs involving food, healthcare or machinery","chinese":"涉及食物、醫療或機械的工作"},{"english":"support hygiene and safety","chinese":"支持衞生和安全"},{"english":"designed for","chinese":"為……而設計"},{"english":"that particular environment","chinese":"該特定環境"},{"english":"benefits for staff","chinese":"對員工的好處"},{"english":"remove the daily pressure of","chinese":"消除每日……的壓力"},{"english":"deciding what to wear","chinese":"決定穿甚麼"},{"english":"reduce the need to","chinese":"減少……的需要"},{"english":"spend money on","chinese":"花錢在……上"},{"english":"fashionable clothes","chinese":"時尚衣服"},{"english":"work-appropriate clothes","chinese":"適合工作的衣服"},{"english":"a practical advantage","chinese":"實際好處"},{"english":"lower-paid employees","chinese":"薪酬較低的員工"},{"english":"might otherwise feel judged by","chinese":"否則可能因……而覺得被評頭品足"},{"english":"their appearance","chinese":"他們的外表"},{"english":"create a stronger sense of equality","chinese":"建立更強的平等感"},{"english":"belonging","chinese":"歸屬感"},{"english":"similar clothing","chinese":"相似的衣着"},{"english":"differences in wealth","chinese":"財富差異"},{"english":"taste or social background","chinese":"品味或社會背景"},{"english":"become less visible","chinese":"變得較不明顯"},{"english":"part of the same team","chinese":"同一團隊的一分子"},{"english":"well-designed uniforms","chinese":"設計良好的制服"},{"english":"comfortable and protective","chinese":"舒適並具保護作用"},{"english":"allowing employees to","chinese":"讓員工能夠"},{"english":"focus on their tasks","chinese":"專注於工作任務"},{"english":"rather than on their clothing","chinese":"而不是放在衣着上"},{"english":"strengthening brand image","chinese":"加強品牌形象"},{"english":"improving identification","chinese":"改善識別度"},{"english":"supporting workplace control","chinese":"支持工作場所管理"},{"english":"saving time and money","chinese":"節省時間和金錢"},{"english":"reducing social pressure","chinese":"減少社交壓力"},{"english":"encouraging a shared sense of professionalism","chinese":"鼓勵共同的專業感"}]},"model-essay-3-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-3-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:3","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-3-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q3","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Museums and galleries help shape how the public understands art, history and cultural identity. Some people therefore argue that these institutions should display only local artists instead of showing work from other countries. This essay strongly disagrees with that view because international collections broaden public understanding and also strengthen the long-term development of local art.","chinese":"博物館和美術館有助塑造公眾如何理解藝術、歷史和文化身分認同。 因此，有些人主張這些機構應只展示本地藝術家，而不應展出其他國家的作品。 本文強烈不同意這種看法。 因為國際館藏既能擴闊公眾理解，也能加強本地藝術的長遠發展。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Showing foreign work makes museums far more educational. First, if visitors see only domestic traditions, their understanding of art becomes narrow because they have no meaningful basis for comparison. When a gallery places local painting beside Japanese prints or African sculpture, for example, students can immediately see how different cultures use colour, symbolism and form to express similar human concerns. Second, exposure to international art can deepen social understanding. Works produced in other societies often reflect war, migration, religion or inequality, so encountering them helps viewers appreciate experiences beyond their own environment. For that reason, excluding foreign art would reduce both the intellectual and the cultural value of museums.","chinese":"展示外國作品會使博物館變得更具教育意義。 第一，如果參觀者只看到本國傳統，他們對藝術的理解便會變得狹窄，因為他們沒有有意義的比較基礎。 當美術館把本地繪畫與日本版畫或非洲雕塑並列展示時，例如，學生便能立即看見不同文化如何運用色彩、象徵和形式來表達相似的人類關懷。 第二，接觸國際藝術能加深社會理解。 其他社會所創作的作品往往反映戰爭、遷徙、宗教或不平等，因此接觸這些作品能幫助觀眾理解自己環境以外的經驗。 正因如此，排除外國藝術會削弱博物館在知識和文化上的價值。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Displaying international art also benefits local artists and the institutions that support them. First, artists improve when they are challenged by unfamiliar techniques and artistic philosophies. If museums show only local work, the creative environment can become repetitive; by contrast, exposure to outside influences encourages painters, sculptors and photographers to refine their methods and produce more original work. A young artist who studies European modernism, for instance, may return to local subjects with fresher ways of representing light, space or emotion. Second, varied exhibitions attract broader audiences and keep galleries vibrant. When institutions alternate local shows with international ones, they draw more students, critics and repeat visitors, who then become more likely to discover local talent as well.","chinese":"展出國際藝術也能使本地藝術家及支持他們的機構受益。 第一，當藝術家受到陌生技法和藝術理念的挑戰時，他們便會進步。 如果博物館只展示本地作品，創作環境可能會變得重複乏味；相反，接觸外來影響會鼓勵畫家、雕塑家和攝影師精煉自己的方法，並創作出更原創的作品。 例如，一位研究歐洲現代主義的年輕藝術家，可能會以更新鮮的方式回到本地題材，去表現光線、空間或情感。 第二，多元展覽會吸引更廣泛的觀眾，並使美術館保持活力。 當機構把本地展覽與國際展覽交替安排時，它們會吸引更多學生、評論家和回流觀眾，而這些人之後也更可能發掘本地人才。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, museums and galleries should not restrict themselves to local artists. I strongly disagree with this view because international art both enriches public understanding and creates a healthier environment for local artistic growth.","chinese":"總而言之，博物館和美術館不應把自己限制於本地藝術家。 我強烈不同意這種看法。 因為國際藝術既能豐富公眾理解，也能為本地藝術成長創造更健康的環境。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"museums and galleries","chinese":"博物館和美術館"},{"english":"shape how the public understands","chinese":"塑造公眾如何理解"},{"english":"cultural identity","chinese":"文化身份"},{"english":"these institutions","chinese":"這些機構"},{"english":"display only local artists","chinese":"只展出本地藝術家"},{"english":"instead of showing","chinese":"而不是展示"},{"english":"work from other countries","chinese":"來自其他國家的作品"},{"english":"strongly disagrees with","chinese":"強烈不同意"},{"english":"international collections","chinese":"國際館藏"},{"english":"broaden public understanding","chinese":"擴闊公眾理解"},{"english":"strengthen the long-term development of","chinese":"加強……的長遠發展"},{"english":"local art","chinese":"本地藝術"},{"english":"foreign work","chinese":"外國作品"},{"english":"far more educational","chinese":"教育價值高得多"},{"english":"domestic traditions","chinese":"本土傳統"},{"english":"become narrow","chinese":"變得狹窄"},{"english":"meaningful basis for comparison","chinese":"有意義的比較基礎"},{"english":"place local painting beside","chinese":"將本地繪畫放在……旁邊"},{"english":"Japanese prints","chinese":"日本版畫"},{"english":"African sculpture","chinese":"非洲雕塑"},{"english":"immediately see how","chinese":"立刻看出如何"},{"english":"different cultures","chinese":"不同文化"},{"english":"symbolism and form","chinese":"象徵手法和形式"},{"english":"express similar human concerns","chinese":"表達相似的人類關注"},{"english":"exposure to international art","chinese":"接觸國際藝術"},{"english":"deepen social understanding","chinese":"加深社會理解"},{"english":"works produced in other societies","chinese":"其他社會創作的作品"},{"english":"reflect war, migration, religion or inequality","chinese":"反映戰爭、移民、宗教或不平等"},{"english":"encountering them","chinese":"接觸它們"},{"english":"appreciate experiences beyond","chinese":"理解……以外的經歷"},{"english":"their own environment","chinese":"他們自身的環境"},{"english":"for that reason","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"excluding foreign art","chinese":"排除外國藝術"},{"english":"reduce both the intellectual and the cultural value of","chinese":"同時降低……的知識和文化價值"},{"english":"displaying international art","chinese":"展出國際藝術"},{"english":"benefit local artists","chinese":"令本地藝術家受惠"},{"english":"the institutions that support them","chinese":"支持他們的機構"},{"english":"be challenged by","chinese":"受到……挑戰"},{"english":"unfamiliar techniques","chinese":"不熟悉的技巧"},{"english":"artistic philosophies","chinese":"藝術理念"},{"english":"creative environment","chinese":"創作環境"},{"english":"become repetitive","chinese":"變得重複乏味"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相反"},{"english":"outside influences","chinese":"外來影響"},{"english":"encourage painters, sculptors and photographers to","chinese":"鼓勵畫家、雕塑家和攝影師去"},{"english":"refine their methods","chinese":"改進自己的方法"},{"english":"produce more original work","chinese":"創作更具原創性的作品"},{"english":"European modernism","chinese":"歐洲現代主義"},{"english":"return to local subjects","chinese":"回到本地題材"},{"english":"fresher ways of representing","chinese":"更新鮮的表現方式"},{"english":"light, space or emotion","chinese":"光線、空間或情感"},{"english":"varied exhibitions","chinese":"多元化展覽"},{"english":"attract broader audiences","chinese":"吸引更廣泛觀眾"},{"english":"keep galleries vibrant","chinese":"令美術館保持活力"},{"english":"alternate local shows with international ones","chinese":"本地展覽和國際展覽輪流舉行"},{"english":"draw more students, critics and repeat visitors","chinese":"吸引更多學生、評論家和回頭訪客"},{"english":"become more likely to","chinese":"變得更有可能"},{"english":"discover local talent","chinese":"發掘本地人才"},{"english":"restrict themselves to","chinese":"將自己限制於"},{"english":"enrich public understanding","chinese":"豐富公眾理解"},{"english":"create a healthier environment for","chinese":"為……創造更健康的環境"},{"english":"local artistic growth","chinese":"本地藝術發展"}]},"model-essay-3-ielts-task1-bar-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-3-ielts-task1-bar-charts","essayKey":"bar-charts:3","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-3-ielts-task1-bar-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/bar-charts/bar-chart-3","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The bar chart compares the proportions of residents in Sydney, Melbourne, Brisbane, Adelaide and Hobart who bought fresh or instant coffee, or visited a café for coffee or tea, over the previous four weeks.","chinese":"這張柱狀圖比較了悉尼、墨爾本、布里斯本、阿德萊德和霍巴特居民在過去四星期內購買新鮮咖啡、即溶咖啡，或到咖啡店喝咖啡或茶的比例。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, going to a café was the most common habit in most cities, while buying fresh coffee was consistently the least popular option. Instant coffee was more widely purchased than fresh coffee in every city, and Adelaide was the only place where café visits did not occupy first position.","chinese":"整體而言，在大多數城市中，到咖啡店是最常見的習慣，而購買新鮮咖啡則一直是最不受歡迎的選項。 在每個城市中，即溶咖啡的購買比例都高於新鮮咖啡；而阿德萊德是唯一一個咖啡店到訪率沒有排在第一位的城市。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Café-going was especially popular in Melbourne and Hobart, at about 64% and 63% respectively, followed by Sydney, where just over three fifths of residents reported doing so. The figures were lower in Brisbane, at around 56%, and Adelaide, at just under 50%, making it the weakest city for café visits.","chinese":"到咖啡店在墨爾本和霍巴特尤其普遍，比例分別約為 64% 和 63% ；其次是悉尼，當地略多於五分之三的居民表示曾這樣做。 布里斯本的比例較低，約為 56% ；而阿德萊德則略低於 50% ，因此成為咖啡店到訪率最低的城市。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"In terms of coffee purchases, instant coffee recorded relatively high figures in Hobart and Brisbane, at roughly 54% and 53%. Adelaide stood at about 50%, while Melbourne and Sydney were slightly lower, at approximately 48% and 45% respectively. By contrast, fresh coffee attracted smaller shares everywhere: around 44% in Sydney, 43% in Melbourne, 39% in Hobart, and only about 34% in Brisbane and 35% in Adelaide.","chinese":"就咖啡購買而言，即溶咖啡在霍巴特和布里斯本錄得相對較高的比例，分別約為 54% 和 53% 。 阿德萊德約為 50% ；而墨爾本和悉尼則稍低，分別約為 48% 和 45% 。 相比之下，新鮮咖啡在所有城市中的比例都較低：悉尼約為 44% ，墨爾本約為43% ，霍巴特約為 39% ，而布里斯本和阿德萊德分別只有約 34% 和 35% 。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"compares the proportions of residents","chinese":"比較居民比例"},{"english":"the proportions of residents","chinese":"居民比例"},{"english":"bought fresh or instant coffee","chinese":"購買新鮮咖啡或即溶咖啡"},{"english":"visited a café for coffee or tea","chinese":"到咖啡店飲咖啡或茶"},{"english":"over the previous four weeks","chinese":"在過去四星期內"},{"english":"going to a café","chinese":"到咖啡店"},{"english":"the most common habit","chinese":"最普遍的習慣"},{"english":"in most cities","chinese":"在大部分城市"},{"english":"buying fresh coffee","chinese":"購買新鮮咖啡"},{"english":"consistently the least popular option","chinese":"一直是最不受歡迎的選項"},{"english":"instant coffee","chinese":"即溶咖啡"},{"english":"more widely purchased than","chinese":"較……更多人購買"},{"english":"in every city","chinese":"在每個城市"},{"english":"the only place where","chinese":"唯一一個……的地方"},{"english":"café visits","chinese":"到咖啡店"},{"english":"occupy first position","chinese":"佔據第一位"},{"english":"café-going","chinese":"到咖啡店的習慣"},{"english":"especially popular in","chinese":"在……尤其受歡迎"},{"english":"at about 64% and 63% respectively","chinese":"分別約為64%和63%"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"followed by Sydney","chinese":"其次是悉尼"},{"english":"just over three fifths of residents","chinese":"略高於五分之三的居民"},{"english":"reported doing so","chinese":"表示有這樣做"},{"english":"the figures were lower","chinese":"數字較低"},{"english":"at around 56%","chinese":"約為56%"},{"english":"at just under 50%","chinese":"略低於50%"},{"english":"making it the weakest city for","chinese":"使其成為……方面最弱的城市"},{"english":"the weakest city for café visits","chinese":"到咖啡店比例最低的城市"},{"english":"in terms of coffee purchases","chinese":"就咖啡購買而言"},{"english":"coffee purchases","chinese":"咖啡購買情況"},{"english":"recorded relatively high figures","chinese":"錄得相對較高的數字"},{"english":"relatively high figures","chinese":"相對較高的數字"},{"english":"at roughly 54% and 53%","chinese":"約為54%和53%"},{"english":"stood at about 50%","chinese":"處於約50%"},{"english":"slightly lower","chinese":"稍低"},{"english":"at approximately 48% and 45% respectively","chinese":"分別約為48%和45%"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"fresh coffee","chinese":"新鮮咖啡"},{"english":"attracted smaller shares","chinese":"吸引較小比例"},{"english":"smaller shares everywhere","chinese":"各地比例均較小"},{"english":"around 44% in Sydney","chinese":"悉尼約為44%"},{"english":"43% in Melbourne","chinese":"墨爾本為43%"},{"english":"39% in Hobart","chinese":"荷伯特為39%"},{"english":"only about 34% in Brisbane","chinese":"布里斯本僅約34%"},{"english":"35% in Adelaide","chinese":"阿德萊德為35%"}]},"model-essay-3-ielts-task1-line-graph":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-3-ielts-task1-line-graph","essayKey":"line-graph:3","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-3-ielts-task1-line-graph","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/line-graphs/line-graph-3","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The line graph illustrates month-on-month percentage changes in the prices of copper, nickel and zinc in 2014.","chinese":"這張折線圖說明了 2014 年銅、鎳和鋅價格相對上個月的百分比變化。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, nickel was the most volatile metal, starting with the strongest rise but later recording the steepest fall. Copper changed more modestly, whereas zinc ended the year with the highest monthly change. All three metals weakened around mid-year before recovering in November and December.","chinese":"整體而言，鎳是波動最大的金屬，年初錄得最強升幅，但之後又出現最大跌幅。 銅的變化較為溫和；相反，鋅在年底錄得最高的月度變化。 三種金屬都在年中附近走弱，然後在 11 月和 12 月回升。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"At the beginning of the year, nickel rose by about 6%, compared with 2% for copper and 1% for zinc. In February, nickel remained high at roughly 4%, while zinc peaked at 3%. After this, the figures for all three metals fell steadily: by May, nickel and zinc had dropped to around 0.5% and 1% respectively, while copper had slipped to about -0.5%.","chinese":"年初，鎳上升約 6% ，相比之下，銅和鋅分別上升約 2% 和 1% 。 2 月，鎳仍維持在約 4% 的高位，而鋅則達到 3% 的高峰。 此後，三種金屬的數字都穩步下降：到 5 月，鎳和鋅分別跌至約 0.5% 和 1% ，而銅則下滑至約 -0.5% 。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"June was the clear low point. Nickel plunged to approximately -3%, far below zinc at -1% and copper at about -0.5%. From July to September, copper recovered to around 1%, whereas nickel stayed at -1% and zinc hovered near -0.5%. In October, nickel slipped again to -2%, but by December all three were positive, with zinc at 2%, copper at around 1.5% and nickel at 1%.","chinese":"6 月是明顯的低點。 鎳急跌至約 -3% ，遠低於鋅的 -1% 和銅的約 -0.5% 。 從 7 月到 9 月，銅回升至約 1% ；相反，鎳維持在 -1% ，而鋅則徘徊在約 -0.5% 。 10 月，鎳再次下滑至 -2% ；但到 12 月，三種金屬都回到正值，其中鋅為 2% ，銅約為 1.5% ，鎳為 1% 。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"The line graph illustrates","chinese":"折線圖顯示"},{"english":"month-on-month percentage changes","chinese":"按月百分比變化"},{"english":"the prices of copper, nickel and zinc","chinese":"銅、鎳和鋅的價格"},{"english":"copper","chinese":"銅"},{"english":"nickel","chinese":"鎳"},{"english":"zinc","chinese":"鋅"},{"english":"in 2014","chinese":"在2014年"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"the most volatile metal","chinese":"波動最大的金屬"},{"english":"starting with the strongest rise","chinese":"一開始錄得最大升幅"},{"english":"the strongest rise","chinese":"最大升幅"},{"english":"later recording the steepest fall","chinese":"其後錄得最急跌幅"},{"english":"the steepest fall","chinese":"最急跌幅"},{"english":"changed more modestly","chinese":"變化較溫和"},{"english":"ended the year with","chinese":"以……結束全年"},{"english":"the highest monthly change","chinese":"最高的按月變化"},{"english":"all three metals","chinese":"三種金屬全部"},{"english":"weakened around mid-year","chinese":"在年中左右走弱"},{"english":"mid-year","chinese":"年中"},{"english":"before recovering in November and December","chinese":"隨後在11月和12月回升"},{"english":"recovering in November and December","chinese":"在11月和12月回升"},{"english":"at the beginning of the year","chinese":"在年初"},{"english":"rose by about 6%","chinese":"上升約6%"},{"english":"compared with","chinese":"與……相比"},{"english":"2% for copper","chinese":"銅為2%"},{"english":"1% for zinc","chinese":"鋅為1%"},{"english":"remained high at roughly 4%","chinese":"維持在約4%的高位"},{"english":"peaked at 3%","chinese":"在3%見頂"},{"english":"After this","chinese":"此後"},{"english":"the figures for all three metals","chinese":"三種金屬的數字"},{"english":"fell steadily","chinese":"穩步下跌"},{"english":"by May","chinese":"到5月"},{"english":"had dropped to around 0.5%","chinese":"已跌至約0.5%"},{"english":"1% respectively","chinese":"分別為0.5%和1%"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"had slipped to about −0.5%","chinese":"已跌至約負0.5%"},{"english":"slipped to","chinese":"下滑至"},{"english":"June was the clear low point","chinese":"6月是明顯低位"},{"english":"the clear low point","chinese":"明顯低位"},{"english":"plunged to approximately −3%","chinese":"急跌至約負3%"},{"english":"far below","chinese":"遠低於"},{"english":"zinc at −1%","chinese":"鋅為負1%"},{"english":"copper at about −0.5%","chinese":"銅約為負0.5%"},{"english":"from July to September","chinese":"從7月至9月"},{"english":"recovered to around 1%","chinese":"回升至約1%"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；然而"},{"english":"stayed at −1%","chinese":"維持在負1%"},{"english":"hovered near −0.5%","chinese":"徘徊在約負0.5%附近"},{"english":"slipped again to −2%","chinese":"再次下滑至負2%"},{"english":"by December","chinese":"到12月"},{"english":"all three were positive","chinese":"三者均錄得正數"},{"english":"with zinc at 2%","chinese":"其中鋅為2%"},{"english":"copper at around 1.5%","chinese":"銅約為1.5%"},{"english":"nickel at 1%","chinese":"鎳為1%"}]},"model-essay-3-ielts-task1-maps":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-3-ielts-task1-maps","essayKey":"maps:3","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-3-ielts-task1-maps","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/maps/maps-3","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The two plans illustrate how the Central Library has been reorganised over the last two decades.","chinese":"這兩張平面圖說明中央圖書館在過去二十年間如何被重新規劃。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the library has changed from a mainly book- and reading-based space into a more varied facility, with new areas for technology, events, lectures and refreshments. Although the entrance remains in the same position, the central seating has disappeared and several services have been relocated or modernised.","chinese":"整體而言，該圖書館已經從一個主要以藏書和閱讀為主的空間，轉變成一個功能更為多元的設施，新增了科技、活動、講座和餐飲相關區域。 雖然入口仍在相同位置，但中央座位區已經消失，而多項服務已被重新安置或現代化。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Twenty years ago, the middle of the library was occupied by tables and chairs, with rooms arranged around it. On the left, there was a media room for CDs, videos and computer games in the north-west corner, adult fiction books in the centre, and a reading room for newspapers and magazines near the entrance. Today, this side has been fully reorganised: the former media and fiction sections contain children’s fiction books, storytelling space and sofas, while the old reading room has become a computer room. A section for all reference books has also been introduced.","chinese":"二十年前，圖書館中央設有桌椅，周圍則分布著不同房間。 在左側，西北角有一個供放置 CDs 、錄像和電腦遊戲的媒體室，中部是成人小說書籍區，靠近入口處則是供閱讀報紙和雜誌的閱覽室。 如今，這一側已被完全重新規劃：原來的媒體室和成人小說區變成兒童小說書籍區、講故事活動空間和沙發區，而舊閱覽室則變成電腦室。 此外，圖書館亦新增了一個全部參考書區。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"On the right, the old children’s books area has been replaced by a lecture room. The former adult non-fiction section now houses adult fiction, an information desk and self-service machines, whereas the old enquiry desk has been converted into a café.","chinese":"在右側，舊兒童書籍區已被講座室取代。 原本的成人非小說書籍區現在設有成人小說、資訊服務台和自助服務機，而舊詢問處則已被改建成咖啡館。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the floor plan of","chinese":"……的平面圖"},{"english":"a public library","chinese":"公共圖書館"},{"english":"20 years ago","chinese":"20年前"},{"english":"how it looks now","chinese":"它現時的樣貌"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"selecting and reporting","chinese":"選取並報告"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"The two plans illustrate how","chinese":"兩幅平面圖顯示……如何"},{"english":"the Central Library","chinese":"Central Library"},{"english":"has been reorganised","chinese":"已被重新規劃"},{"english":"over the last two decades","chinese":"在過去二十年間"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"has changed from … into …","chinese":"由……變成……"},{"english":"a mainly book- and reading-based space","chinese":"以藏書及閱讀為主的空間"},{"english":"a more varied facility","chinese":"功能更多元化的設施"},{"english":"new areas for","chinese":"……的新區域"},{"english":"technology, events, lectures and refreshments","chinese":"科技、活動、講座及茶點飲品"},{"english":"although","chinese":"雖然"},{"english":"the entrance remains in the same position","chinese":"入口仍在同一位置"},{"english":"remains in the same position","chinese":"仍在同一位置"},{"english":"the central seating","chinese":"中央座位區"},{"english":"has disappeared","chinese":"已消失；已不復存在"},{"english":"services have been relocated","chinese":"服務已被遷移"},{"english":"have been relocated or modernised","chinese":"已被遷移或現代化"},{"english":"Twenty years ago","chinese":"20年前"},{"english":"the middle of the library","chinese":"圖書館中央"},{"english":"was occupied by","chinese":"被……佔據"},{"english":"tables and chairs","chinese":"桌椅"},{"english":"with rooms arranged around it","chinese":"房間圍繞它排列"},{"english":"arranged around","chinese":"圍繞……排列"},{"english":"On the left","chinese":"在左邊"},{"english":"a media room","chinese":"媒體室"},{"english":"CDs, videos and computer games","chinese":"CD、影片及電腦遊戲"},{"english":"in the north-west corner","chinese":"在西北角"},{"english":"adult fiction books","chinese":"成人小說"},{"english":"in the centre","chinese":"在中央"},{"english":"a reading room for","chinese":"供……使用的閱覽室"},{"english":"newspapers and magazines","chinese":"報紙及雜誌"},{"english":"near the entrance","chinese":"在入口附近"},{"english":"Today","chinese":"現時"},{"english":"this side","chinese":"這一邊"},{"english":"has been fully reorganised","chinese":"已被全面重新規劃"},{"english":"the former media section","chinese":"原來的媒體區"},{"english":"the former fiction section","chinese":"原來的小說區"},{"english":"children's fiction books","chinese":"兒童小說"},{"english":"storytelling space","chinese":"講故事空間"},{"english":"sofas","chinese":"梳化"},{"english":"while","chinese":"而"},{"english":"the old reading room","chinese":"原來的閱覽室"},{"english":"has become","chinese":"已變成"},{"english":"a computer room","chinese":"電腦室"},{"english":"a section for","chinese":"……專區"},{"english":"reference books","chinese":"參考書"},{"english":"has also been introduced","chinese":"亦已增設"},{"english":"On the right","chinese":"在右邊"},{"english":"the old children's books area","chinese":"原來的兒童圖書區"},{"english":"has been replaced by","chinese":"已被……取代"},{"english":"a lecture room","chinese":"講座室"},{"english":"the former adult non-fiction section","chinese":"原來的成人非小說區"},{"english":"adult non-fiction","chinese":"成人非小說書籍"},{"english":"now houses","chinese":"現時設有"},{"english":"adult fiction","chinese":"成人小說"},{"english":"an information desk","chinese":"查詢處；服務台"},{"english":"self-service machines","chinese":"自助服務機"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相比之下"},{"english":"the old enquiry desk","chinese":"原來的查詢處"},{"english":"has been converted into","chinese":"已被改建成"},{"english":"a café","chinese":"咖啡店"}]},"model-essay-3-ielts-task1-mixed-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-3-ielts-task1-mixed-charts","essayKey":"mixed-charts:3","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-3-ielts-task1-mixed-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/mixed-charts/mixed-charts-3","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The table compares the police budget in one area of Britain in 2017 and 2018 by funding source, while the pie charts show how the money was spent.","chinese":"該表格按照資金來源比較了英國某地區在2017年和2018年的警察預算，而餅圖則顯示了這筆錢的支出方式。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the budget rose modestly over the two years. The national government remained the main source of funding, although the increase came chiefly from local taxes. In terms of expenditure, salaries continued to dominate the budget, but their share fell as technology took a larger proportion.","chinese":"整體而言，這兩年間警察預算有小幅上升。 中央政府仍然是主要資金來源，儘管預算增幅主要來自地方稅收。 在支出方面，薪金仍然佔據預算的最大部分，但其比例有所下降，而科技支出所佔比例則增加了。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 2017, the total police budget stood at £304.7 million. Of this, £175.5 million came from the national government, far more than the £91.2 million raised through local taxes and the £38 million from other sources, such as grants. By 2018, the total had climbed to £318.6 million. Government funding increased only slightly, to £177.8 million, while local-tax revenue rose more sharply to £102.3 million. Other sources changed very little, reaching £38.5 million.","chinese":"2017年，警察總預算為3.047億英鎊。 其中，1.755億英鎊來自中央政府，遠高於地方稅收籌得的9,120萬英鎊，以及來自其他來源如補助金的3,800萬英鎊。 到2018年，總預算上升至3.186億英鎊。 政府撥款只小幅增加至1.778億英鎊，而地方稅收則更明顯地上升至1.023億英鎊。 其他來源變化很小，達到3,850萬英鎊。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Regarding spending, salaries accounted for three quarters of the budget in 2017, before declining to 69% in 2018. By contrast, technology almost doubled its share, rising from 8% to 14%, whereas buildings and transport remained unchanged at 17%.","chinese":"在支出方面，薪金在2017年佔預算的四分之三，之後在2018年下降至69%。 相比之下，科技支出所佔比例幾乎翻倍，從8%上升至14%；而建築物和交通支出則保持不變，均為17%。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"give information on","chinese":"提供關於……的資料"},{"english":"the police budget","chinese":"警察預算"},{"english":"for 2017 and 2018","chinese":"2017年和2018年的"},{"english":"in one area of Britain","chinese":"在英國某一地區"},{"english":"where the money came from","chinese":"資金來自哪裏"},{"english":"how it was distributed","chinese":"它如何分配"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"selecting and reporting","chinese":"選取並報告"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"the table compares","chinese":"表格比較"},{"english":"by funding source","chinese":"按資金來源"},{"english":"funding source","chinese":"資金來源"},{"english":"while","chinese":"而"},{"english":"pie charts","chinese":"餅圖"},{"english":"how the money was spent","chinese":"資金如何使用"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"rose modestly","chinese":"小幅上升"},{"english":"over the two years","chinese":"在這兩年間"},{"english":"the national government","chinese":"中央政府"},{"english":"remained the main source of funding","chinese":"仍然是主要資金來源"},{"english":"the main source of funding","chinese":"主要資金來源"},{"english":"although","chinese":"雖然；儘管"},{"english":"the increase came chiefly from","chinese":"增幅主要來自"},{"english":"came chiefly from","chinese":"主要來自"},{"english":"local taxes","chinese":"地方稅收"},{"english":"In terms of expenditure","chinese":"在支出方面"},{"english":"expenditure","chinese":"支出"},{"english":"salaries","chinese":"薪金"},{"english":"continued to dominate","chinese":"繼續佔主導地位"},{"english":"dominate the budget","chinese":"佔預算最大部分"},{"english":"their share fell","chinese":"其所佔比例下降"},{"english":"as technology took a larger proportion","chinese":"隨着科技佔比增加"},{"english":"technology","chinese":"科技"},{"english":"took a larger proportion","chinese":"佔較大比例"},{"english":"the total police budget","chinese":"警察總預算"},{"english":"stood at £304.7 million","chinese":"為3.047億英鎊"},{"english":"Of this","chinese":"其中"},{"english":"came from the national government","chinese":"來自中央政府"},{"english":"£175.5 million","chinese":"1.755億英鎊"},{"english":"far more than","chinese":"遠多於"},{"english":"raised through local taxes","chinese":"透過地方稅收籌得"},{"english":"£91.2 million","chinese":"9,120萬英鎊"},{"english":"other sources","chinese":"其他來源"},{"english":"such as grants","chinese":"例如補助金"},{"english":"grants","chinese":"補助金"},{"english":"By 2018","chinese":"到2018年"},{"english":"the total had climbed to","chinese":"總額已上升至"},{"english":"climbed to £318.6 million","chinese":"上升至3.186億英鎊"},{"english":"government funding","chinese":"政府撥款"},{"english":"increased only slightly","chinese":"只小幅增加"},{"english":"to £177.8 million","chinese":"至1.778億英鎊"},{"english":"local tax revenue","chinese":"地方稅收收入"},{"english":"rose more sharply","chinese":"上升得更明顯"},{"english":"to £102.3 million","chinese":"至1.023億英鎊"},{"english":"changed very little","chinese":"變化很小"},{"english":"reaching £38.5 million","chinese":"達到3,850萬英鎊"},{"english":"Regarding spending","chinese":"在支出方面"},{"english":"accounted for three quarters of","chinese":"佔……的四分之三"},{"english":"three quarters of the budget","chinese":"預算的四分之三"},{"english":"before declining to","chinese":"之後下降至"},{"english":"declining to 69%","chinese":"下降至69%"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"almost doubled its share","chinese":"所佔比例幾乎翻倍"},{"english":"doubled its share","chinese":"所佔比例翻倍"},{"english":"rising from 8% to 14%","chinese":"由8%上升至14%"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相比之下"},{"english":"buildings and transport","chinese":"建築物及交通"},{"english":"remained unchanged at 17%","chinese":"維持在17%不變"}]},"model-essay-3-ielts-task1-pie-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-3-ielts-task1-pie-charts","essayKey":"pie-charts:3","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-3-ielts-task1-pie-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/pie-charts/pie-chart-3","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The two pie charts compare British students at a university in England according to the additional language or languages they could speak besides English in 2000 and 2010.","chinese":"這兩個圓餅圖比較了英格蘭一所大學的英國學生在 2000 年和 2010 年除英語以外能說的額外語言情況。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, students became more likely to speak at least one language besides English: the share reporting no additional language fell markedly, while Spanish, another language and two other languages all increased. Spanish remained the dominant category in both years.","chinese":"整體而言，學生變得更有可能會說至少一種英語以外的語言：表示不會任何額外語言的比例明顯下降，而除英語外只會西班牙語、另一種語言以及另外兩種語言的比例均有所上升。 除英語外只會西班牙語在兩個年份中都保持為最大類別。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 2000, Spanish only accounted for the largest segment, at 30% of students. This was followed by those with no other language, who made up one fifth of the total. French only and another language were equal at 15% each, whereas German only and two other languages were the smallest categories, both standing at 10%.","chinese":"在 2000 年，除英語外只會西班牙語佔最大部分，為學生總數的 30% 。 其次是不會任何其他語言的學生，他們佔總數的五分之一。 除英語外只會法語和會另一種語言的比例相同，均為 15% ；相反，只會德語和會另外兩種語言是最小的類別，兩者都為 10% 。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"By 2010, Spanish had strengthened its lead, rising to 35%. The proportion speaking another language also increased, from 15% to 20%, while the figure for students able to speak two other languages grew by five percentage points to 15%. By contrast, the percentage with no additional language halved to 10%, and French only fell to the same level. German remained unchanged at 10%.","chinese":"到 2010 年，除英語外只會西班牙語進一步擴大領先優勢，上升至 35% 。 會另一種語言的比例也從 15% 上升至 20% ，而能說另外兩種語言的學生比例則增加了五個百分點，達到 15% 。 相比之下，不會任何額外語言的比例減半至 10% ，而除英語外只會法語的比例也下降至同一水平。 除英語外只會德語的比例則保持不變，仍為 10% 。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the two pie charts compare","chinese":"兩個圓形圖比較"},{"english":"British students","chinese":"英國學生"},{"english":"at a university in England","chinese":"在英格蘭一所大學"},{"english":"according to","chinese":"根據"},{"english":"additional language or languages","chinese":"額外一種或多種語言"},{"english":"could speak","chinese":"能夠說"},{"english":"besides English","chinese":"除英語以外"},{"english":"in 2000 and 2010","chinese":"在2000年和2010年"},{"english":"became more likely to","chinese":"變得更有可能"},{"english":"speak at least one language","chinese":"說至少一種語言"},{"english":"at least one language besides English","chinese":"除英語外至少一種語言"},{"english":"the share reporting no additional language","chinese":"表示沒有額外語言的比例"},{"english":"no additional language","chinese":"沒有額外語言"},{"english":"fell markedly","chinese":"明顯下降"},{"english":"another language","chinese":"另一種語言"},{"english":"two other languages","chinese":"另外兩種語言"},{"english":"remained the dominant category","chinese":"仍然是主導類別"},{"english":"the dominant category","chinese":"主導類別"},{"english":"in both years","chinese":"在兩個年份中"},{"english":"accounted for the largest segment","chinese":"佔最大部分"},{"english":"the largest segment","chinese":"最大部分"},{"english":"at 30% of students","chinese":"佔學生的30%"},{"english":"This was followed by","chinese":"其次是"},{"english":"those with no other language","chinese":"沒有其他語言的人"},{"english":"made up one fifth of the total","chinese":"佔總數五分之一"},{"english":"one fifth of the total","chinese":"總數的五分之一"},{"english":"French only","chinese":"只懂法語"},{"english":"were equal at 15% each","chinese":"各佔15%，比例相同"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；然而"},{"english":"German only","chinese":"只懂德語"},{"english":"the smallest categories","chinese":"最小的類別"},{"english":"both standing at 10%","chinese":"兩者均為10%"},{"english":"By 2010","chinese":"到2010年"},{"english":"strengthened its lead","chinese":"擴大其領先優勢"},{"english":"rising to 35%","chinese":"上升至35%"},{"english":"the proportion speaking another language","chinese":"說另一種語言的比例"},{"english":"increased from 15% to 20%","chinese":"由15%增至20%"},{"english":"the figure for students able to speak","chinese":"能夠說……的學生數字"},{"english":"able to speak two other languages","chinese":"能夠說另外兩種語言"},{"english":"grew by five percentage points","chinese":"增加了五個百分點"},{"english":"percentage points","chinese":"百分點"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"the percentage with no additional language","chinese":"沒有額外語言的百分比"},{"english":"halved to 10%","chinese":"減半至10%"},{"english":"fell to the same level","chinese":"下降至相同水平"},{"english":"the same level","chinese":"相同水平"},{"english":"remained unchanged at 10%","chinese":"維持10%不變"}]},"model-essay-3-ielts-task1-process-diagram":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-3-ielts-task1-process-diagram","essayKey":"process-diagram:3","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-3-ielts-task1-process-diagram","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/process-diagrams/process-diagram-3","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The diagram illustrates the process by which sugar is produced from sugar cane.","chinese":"該圖說明糖是如何由甘蔗製成的。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the production of sugar is a linear, seven-stage process that begins with growing cane and ends with drying and cooling the finished crystals. Broadly, it moves from an agricultural phase, involving cultivation and harvesting, to an industrial phase in which juice is extracted, purified, thickened and separated.","chinese":"整體而言，糖的生產是一個線性的七階段流程，從種植甘蔗開始，最後以乾燥和冷卻成品糖晶體結束。 大致來說，這個流程由涉及栽培和收割的農業階段，轉向工業階段；在工業階段中，汁液會被提取、淨化、濃縮並分離。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"First, sugar cane is grown for 12 to 18 months until it reaches maturity. It is then harvested in one of two ways: mechanically, with a vehicle cutting and loading the crop, or manually, with workers cutting the stalks by hand. After harvesting, the cane is crushed in a machine, and this step squeezes out the juice required for the later stages.","chinese":"首先，甘蔗會被種植十二至十八個月，直到成熟。 然後，甘蔗會以兩種方式之一被收割：一種是機械收割，由車輛切割並裝載作物；另一種是人工收割，由工人用手切割甘蔗莖。 收割後，甘蔗會在機器中被壓碎，而這一步會擠出後續階段所需的汁液。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The extracted juice is next purified by passing through a limestone filter. Once it has been cleaned, it is heated in an evaporator, where excess water is removed and the liquid becomes syrup. This syrup is then spun in a centrifuge, which separates sugar crystals from the remaining syrup. In the final stage, the crystals are dried and cooled, leaving the finished sugar.","chinese":"提取出的汁液接著會通過石灰石過濾器被淨化。 當汁液被清潔後，它會在蒸發器中被加熱；在這一步中，多餘的水分會被去除，而液體會變成糖漿。 然後，糖漿會在離心機中旋轉，離心機會把糖晶體從剩餘糖漿中分離出來。 在最後階段，糖晶體會被乾燥和冷卻，最終留下成品糖。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"The diagram illustrates","chinese":"圖解顯示"},{"english":"the process by which","chinese":"……的過程"},{"english":"sugar is produced from sugar cane","chinese":"糖由甘蔗製成"},{"english":"sugar cane","chinese":"甘蔗"},{"english":"the production of sugar","chinese":"糖的生產"},{"english":"a linear, seven-stage process","chinese":"線性的七階段過程"},{"english":"begins with growing cane","chinese":"以種植甘蔗開始"},{"english":"ends with drying and cooling","chinese":"以烘乾和冷卻結束"},{"english":"finished crystals","chinese":"製成的晶體"},{"english":"Broadly","chinese":"廣義而言；概括來說"},{"english":"moves from an agricultural phase to","chinese":"由農業階段轉向"},{"english":"an agricultural phase","chinese":"農業階段"},{"english":"involving cultivation and harvesting","chinese":"涉及種植和收割"},{"english":"cultivation","chinese":"種植"},{"english":"harvesting","chinese":"收割"},{"english":"an industrial phase","chinese":"工業階段"},{"english":"juice is extracted","chinese":"汁液被提取"},{"english":"purified, thickened and separated","chinese":"被淨化、濃縮和分離"},{"english":"reaches maturity","chinese":"達到成熟"},{"english":"is grown for 12 to 18 months","chinese":"種植12至18個月"},{"english":"is then harvested","chinese":"然後被收割"},{"english":"in one of two ways","chinese":"以兩種方式之一"},{"english":"mechanically","chinese":"以機械方式"},{"english":"cutting and loading the crop","chinese":"切割並裝載農作物"},{"english":"the crop","chinese":"農作物"},{"english":"manually","chinese":"以人手方式"},{"english":"workers cutting the stalks by hand","chinese":"工人用手切割莖幹"},{"english":"stalks","chinese":"莖幹"},{"english":"by hand","chinese":"用手；人手"},{"english":"After harvesting","chinese":"收割後"},{"english":"is crushed in a machine","chinese":"在機器中被壓榨"},{"english":"squeezes out the juice","chinese":"擠出汁液"},{"english":"required for the later stages","chinese":"後續階段所需"},{"english":"the extracted juice","chinese":"提取出的汁液"},{"english":"is next purified","chinese":"接着被淨化"},{"english":"by passing through","chinese":"透過經過……"},{"english":"a limestone filter","chinese":"石灰石過濾器"},{"english":"Once it has been cleaned","chinese":"當它被清潔後"},{"english":"is heated in an evaporator","chinese":"在蒸發器中被加熱"},{"english":"evaporator","chinese":"蒸發器"},{"english":"excess water is removed","chinese":"多餘水分被去除"},{"english":"the liquid becomes syrup","chinese":"液體變成糖漿"},{"english":"syrup","chinese":"糖漿"},{"english":"is then spun in a centrifuge","chinese":"然後在離心機中旋轉"},{"english":"centrifuge","chinese":"離心機"},{"english":"separates sugar crystals from","chinese":"將糖晶體與……分離"},{"english":"sugar crystals","chinese":"糖晶體"},{"english":"the remaining syrup","chinese":"餘下糖漿"},{"english":"In the final stage","chinese":"在最後階段"},{"english":"are dried and cooled","chinese":"被烘乾和冷卻"},{"english":"leaving the finished sugar","chinese":"最後形成製成糖"},{"english":"the finished sugar","chinese":"製成糖"}]},"model-essay-3-ielts-task1-tables":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-3-ielts-task1-tables","essayKey":"tables:3","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-3-ielts-task1-tables","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/tables/table-3","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The table compares six major MRT systems by year of completion, network length and annual carrying capacity.","chinese":"這個表格比較了六個主要地鐵系統的完工年份、網絡長度和年度載客容量。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, London and Paris are the earliest and most extensive systems, with London’s network standing well ahead of all the others in length. In contrast, Tokyo has by far the greatest yearly capacity despite being much shorter, while Kyoto is the smallest system on both measures.","chinese":"整體而言，倫敦和巴黎是最早完工且網絡規模最大的系統，其中倫敦的路線長度明顯遠超所有其他城市。 相比之下，東京雖然路線短得多，卻擁有遠遠最高的年度載客容量；而京都在路線長度和載客容量兩方面都是最小的系統。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"London was completed first, in 1863, and covers 1,100 kilometres, almost twice Paris’s 594 kilometres. Paris, which opened in 1890, nevertheless carries more passengers annually than London, at 850 million compared with 548 million. Tokyo was completed in 1904 and is only 149 kilometres long, yet it dominates in capacity, handling 1,434 million passengers per year.","chinese":"倫敦最早完工，時間是 1863 年，總長度為 1,100 公里，幾乎是巴黎 594 公里的兩倍。 巴黎於 1890 年開通，但其年度載客容量仍高於倫敦，分別為 8.5 億和 5.48 億。 東京於 1904 年完工，長度只有 149 公里，但它在載客容量方面居於首位，每年可承載 14.34 億乘客。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The other three systems are on a much smaller scale. Washington DC, completed in 1921, has 114 kilometres of track, but its annual capacity is just 70 million. Kyoto and Los Angeles are the newest networks, finished in 1980 and 2001 respectively, and both are extremely short, at 11 and 14 kilometres. However, Los Angeles can carry 90 million passengers annually, far more than Kyoto’s 11 million.","chinese":"另外三個系統的規模則小得多。 華盛頓特區於 1921 年完工，擁有 114 公里路線，但其年度載客容量只有 7,000 萬。 京都和洛杉磯是最新的兩個網絡，分別於 1980 年和 2001 年完工，而且兩者都非常短，分別只有 11 公里和 14 公里。 然而，洛杉磯每年可承載 9,000 萬乘客，遠高於京都的 1,100 萬。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"compares six major MRT systems","chinese":"比較六個主要地鐵系統"},{"english":"six major MRT systems","chinese":"六個主要地鐵系統"},{"english":"year of completion","chinese":"完工年份；落成年份"},{"english":"network length","chinese":"路網長度"},{"english":"annual carrying capacity","chinese":"每年載客能力"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"the earliest and most extensive systems","chinese":"最早及規模最大的系統"},{"english":"most extensive","chinese":"規模最大的；覆蓋最廣的"},{"english":"standing well ahead of","chinese":"遠遠領先於"},{"english":"all the others","chinese":"其他所有"},{"english":"in length","chinese":"在長度方面"},{"english":"In contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"by far the greatest yearly capacity","chinese":"遠遠最高的每年載客能力"},{"english":"yearly capacity","chinese":"每年載客能力"},{"english":"despite being much shorter","chinese":"儘管短得多"},{"english":"much shorter","chinese":"短得多"},{"english":"the smallest system on both measures","chinese":"在兩項指標上都是最小的系統"},{"english":"on both measures","chinese":"在兩項指標上"},{"english":"was completed first","chinese":"最早完工"},{"english":"in 1863","chinese":"在1863年"},{"english":"covers 1,100 kilometres","chinese":"覆蓋1,100公里"},{"english":"covers","chinese":"覆蓋；全長為"},{"english":"almost twice","chinese":"幾乎是兩倍"},{"english":"Paris's 594 kilometres","chinese":"巴黎的594公里"},{"english":"opened in 1890","chinese":"於1890年開通"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而；儘管如此"},{"english":"carries more passengers annually","chinese":"每年運載更多乘客"},{"english":"annually","chinese":"每年"},{"english":"at 850 million","chinese":"為8.5億"},{"english":"compared with","chinese":"與……相比"},{"english":"548 million","chinese":"5.48億"},{"english":"was completed in 1904","chinese":"於1904年完工"},{"english":"only 149 kilometres long","chinese":"全長只有149公里"},{"english":"yet","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"dominates in capacity","chinese":"在載客能力方面佔主導地位"},{"english":"handling 1,434 million passengers per year","chinese":"每年運載14.34億乘客"},{"english":"passengers per year","chinese":"每年乘客量"},{"english":"the other three systems","chinese":"其餘三個系統"},{"english":"on a much smaller scale","chinese":"規模小得多"},{"english":"much smaller scale","chinese":"小得多的規模"},{"english":"completed in 1921","chinese":"於1921年完工"},{"english":"has 114 kilometres of track","chinese":"擁有114公里路軌"},{"english":"kilometres of track","chinese":"公里路軌"},{"english":"annual capacity","chinese":"每年載客能力"},{"english":"just 70 million","chinese":"只有7,000萬"},{"english":"the newest networks","chinese":"最新的路網"},{"english":"finished in 1980 and 2001 respectively","chinese":"分別於1980年和2001年完成"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"extremely short","chinese":"極短"},{"english":"at 11 and 14 kilometres","chinese":"分別為11和14公里"},{"english":"However","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"can carry","chinese":"可運載"},{"english":"90 million passengers annually","chinese":"每年9,000萬乘客"},{"english":"far more than","chinese":"遠多於"},{"english":"Kyoto's 11 million","chinese":"京都的1,100萬"}]},"model-essay-4-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-4-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:4","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-4-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q4","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Change is an inevitable part of modern life, yet people respond to it in very different ways. While some actively welcome new experiences, others prefer to protect their routines and avoid disruption whenever possible. Although both approaches bring certain benefits and drawbacks, embracing change is ultimately the more advantageous mindset because it fosters adaptability and growth, whereas avoiding change mainly provides short-term security.","chinese":"[改變是現代生活中不可避免的一部分，然而人們對它的反應卻非常不同。] [有些人會主動迎接新的經驗，另一些人則傾向維持原有的生活規律，並在可能的情況下避免干擾。] [雖然這兩種做法都有一些優點和缺點，但擁抱改變最終是更有利的心態，因為它能培養適應力與成長，而避免改變主要只是提供短期的安全感。]"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"People who enjoy change usually gain stronger long-term benefits, even though this way of life is not without cost. When individuals enter unfamiliar situations, they are forced to learn new skills, solve unexpected problems and interact with different kinds of people, which gradually makes them more resilient and capable. For example, a graduate who moves abroad for work must adjust to a new culture, new colleagues and new expectations, and this process often leaves them more confident and employable. However, constant change can also create instability. If someone changes jobs, cities or relationships too frequently, they may struggle to build lasting support networks or any real sense of security. A worker who continually moves from one short-term role to another, for instance, may enjoy variety, but may also feel financially and emotionally unsettled.","chinese":"[喜歡改變的人通常能獲得更強的長遠好處，儘管這種生活方式並非毫無代價。] [當人們進入陌生情境時，他們會被迫學習新技能、解決意料之外的問題，並與不同類型的人互動，而這些過程會逐漸令他們變得更有韌性、更有能力。] [例如，一位到國外工作的畢業生必須適應新的文化、新的同事以及新的期待，而這個過程往往會讓他變得更有自信，也更具就業競爭力。] [然而，不斷的改變也可能造成不穩定。] [如果一個人過於頻繁地更換工作、城市或人際關係，他們可能難以建立持久的支持網絡，或任何真正的安全感。] [例如，一位不斷在不同短期工作之間轉換的員工，也許會享受多樣性，但同時也可能在經濟和情緒上感到不安定。] [即便如此，改變所帶來的個人成長，往往仍然大於它暫時造成的不穩定。]"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"By contrast, people who try to avoid change benefit from stability, but this preference can easily become a serious limitation. Remaining in a familiar environment reduces stress because routines are predictable, responsibilities are clear and long-term relationships can deepen over time. Someone who stays in one community for many years, for example, may enjoy close friendships, a reliable support system and a steady career path. The disadvantage, however, is that excessive caution often leads to stagnation. When people reject new technology, training or opportunities simply because these feel uncomfortable, they may fall behind both personally and professionally. An employee who refuses to learn new digital systems may preserve the comfort of old habits for a while, but may eventually become less useful in a changing workplace.","chinese":"[相比之下，試圖避免改變的人可以從穩定中獲益，但這種偏好也很容易成為一種嚴重的限制。] [留在熟悉的環境中能減少壓力，因為生活規律是可預測的、責任是清晰的，而且長期關係也能隨時間加深。] [例如，一個在同一個社區生活多年的人，可能會擁有親密的友誼、可靠的支持系統，以及穩定的職涯道路。] [然而，這種做法的缺點在於，過度謹慎往往會導致停滯。] [當人們只是因為新科技、培訓或機會讓人感到不舒服，就拒絕接受它們時，他們可能會在個人和職業層面上同時落後。] [一名拒絕學習新數位系統的員工，也許能暫時保住舊習慣帶來的舒適感，但最終可能會在不斷改變的職場中變得不那麼有用。] [基於這一點，避免改變所獲得的穩定，往往會被這種謹慎所扼殺的機會抵消。]"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, both attitudes have understandable advantages: enjoying change encourages development, while avoiding it offers stability. Nevertheless, welcoming change is clearly the better approach, because a flexible person can still create stability, whereas an inflexible one may lose valuable opportunities that never return.","chinese":"[總而言之，雖然這兩種態度都提供了一些好處，但擁抱改變顯然是更好的做法。] [這是因為它能促進韌性、成長與適應力；相反地，避免改變主要只是提供暫時的舒適，卻同時增加停滯與錯失機會的風險。]"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"an inevitable part of","chinese":"……中不可避免的一部分"},{"english":"modern life","chinese":"現代生活"},{"english":"respond to it in very different ways","chinese":"以很不同的方式回應它"},{"english":"actively welcome","chinese":"積極歡迎"},{"english":"new experiences","chinese":"新體驗"},{"english":"protect their routines","chinese":"保護自己的日常規律"},{"english":"avoid disruption","chinese":"避免干擾；避免被打亂"},{"english":"whenever possible","chinese":"只要可能"},{"english":"both approaches","chinese":"兩種做法"},{"english":"bring certain benefits and drawbacks","chinese":"帶來某些好處和缺點"},{"english":"embracing change","chinese":"擁抱改變"},{"english":"the more advantageous mindset","chinese":"較有利的心態"},{"english":"fosters adaptability and growth","chinese":"培養適應力和成長"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相比之下"},{"english":"short-term security","chinese":"短期安全感"},{"english":"gain stronger long-term benefits","chinese":"獲得更大的長遠好處"},{"english":"not without cost","chinese":"並非沒有代價"},{"english":"enter unfamiliar situations","chinese":"進入陌生情況"},{"english":"be forced to","chinese":"被迫去"},{"english":"learn new skills","chinese":"學習新技能"},{"english":"solve unexpected problems","chinese":"解決意想不到的問題"},{"english":"interact with different kinds of people","chinese":"與不同類型的人互動"},{"english":"gradually makes them","chinese":"逐漸令他們"},{"english":"more resilient and capable","chinese":"更有抗逆力和能力"},{"english":"moves abroad for work","chinese":"移居海外工作"},{"english":"adjust to","chinese":"適應"},{"english":"a new culture","chinese":"新文化"},{"english":"new colleagues","chinese":"新同事"},{"english":"new expectations","chinese":"新期望"},{"english":"leaves them more confident and employable","chinese":"令他們變得更有信心和更具就業能力"},{"english":"constant change","chinese":"持續不斷的改變"},{"english":"create instability","chinese":"造成不穩定"},{"english":"too frequently","chinese":"過於頻繁地"},{"english":"struggle to build","chinese":"難以建立"},{"english":"lasting support networks","chinese":"持久的支援網絡"},{"english":"a real sense of security","chinese":"真正的安全感"},{"english":"continually moves from...to...","chinese":"不斷從……轉到……"},{"english":"one short-term role to another","chinese":"一份短期職位到另一份短期職位"},{"english":"enjoy variety","chinese":"享受變化"},{"english":"financially and emotionally unsettled","chinese":"在財務和情感上感到不安定"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"try to avoid change","chinese":"嘗試避免改變"},{"english":"benefit from stability","chinese":"從穩定中受惠"},{"english":"become a serious limitation","chinese":"成為嚴重限制"},{"english":"remaining in a familiar environment","chinese":"留在熟悉的環境"},{"english":"reduces stress","chinese":"減少壓力"},{"english":"routines are predictable","chinese":"日常規律是可預期的"},{"english":"responsibilities are clear","chinese":"責任清晰"},{"english":"long-term relationships","chinese":"長遠關係"},{"english":"deepen over time","chinese":"隨時間加深"},{"english":"stays in one community","chinese":"留在同一個社區"},{"english":"close friendships","chinese":"親密友誼"},{"english":"a reliable support system","chinese":"可靠的支援系統"},{"english":"a steady career path","chinese":"穩定的事業發展路徑"},{"english":"excessive caution","chinese":"過度謹慎"},{"english":"leads to stagnation","chinese":"導致停滯不前"},{"english":"reject new technology","chinese":"拒絕新科技"},{"english":"simply because","chinese":"只是因為"},{"english":"feel uncomfortable","chinese":"感到不舒服；不自在"},{"english":"fall behind","chinese":"落後"},{"english":"both personally and professionally","chinese":"在個人和專業方面"},{"english":"refuses to learn","chinese":"拒絕學習"},{"english":"digital systems","chinese":"數碼系統"},{"english":"preserve the comfort of old habits","chinese":"保持舊習慣帶來的舒適感"},{"english":"for a while","chinese":"一段時間"},{"english":"eventually become less useful","chinese":"最終變得較沒用處"},{"english":"a changing workplace","chinese":"不斷變化的工作場所"},{"english":"both attitudes","chinese":"兩種態度"},{"english":"understandable advantages","chinese":"可以理解的好處"},{"english":"encourages development","chinese":"鼓勵發展"},{"english":"offers stability","chinese":"提供穩定"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"welcoming change","chinese":"歡迎改變"},{"english":"a flexible person","chinese":"靈活的人"},{"english":"an inflexible one","chinese":"不靈活的人"},{"english":"lose valuable opportunities","chinese":"失去寶貴機會"},{"english":"never return","chinese":"永不再來"}]},"model-essay-4-ielts-cause-solution":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-4-ielts-cause-solution","essayKey":"cause-solution:4","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-4-ielts-cause-solution","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/problem-and-cause/EdmundBd9CnS-Q4","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Internet access has become a normal part of childhood, especially as many children now use online platforms to chat, play games and build friendships. However, when this happens without adult supervision, children may be exposed to risks which they are not mature enough to recognise. The main problems are contact with dangerous strangers and cyberbullying, and these can be addressed through stronger parental guidance, school education and platform responsibility.","chinese":"互聯網使用已成為童年生活中很正常的一部分，尤其是現在許多兒童都會使用網上平台聊天、玩遊戲和建立友誼。 然而，當這種情況在沒有成年人監督下發生時，兒童可能會接觸到一些他們尚未成熟到能夠辨認的風險。 主要問題是接觸危險的陌生人以及網絡欺凌，而這些問題可以透過更強的家長引導、學校教育和平台責任來解決。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first major problem is that children can come into contact with people who hide their real identity. In gaming platforms, messaging apps or social media groups, an adult may pretend to be another child in order to gain trust, ask for private information, or persuade the child to keep secrets from their family. Since young children are often trusting and eager to be accepted, this can lead to grooming, blackmail or exploitation. A second problem is cyberbullying. Unlike ordinary playground conflict, online abuse can follow a child home, spread quickly, and feel impossible to escape. Repeated insults, rumours or humiliating images can seriously damage a child’s confidence and mental well-being.","chinese":"第一個主要問題是，兒童可能會接觸到隱藏自己真實身份的人。 在遊戲平台、即時通訊應用程式或社交媒體群組中，成年人可能會假裝成另一名兒童，以取得信任、索取私人資料，或說服孩子向家人保守秘密。 由於年幼兒童通常容易信任別人，而且渴望被接納，這可能會導致誘導、勒索或剝削。 第二個問題是網絡欺凌。 與普通的操場衝突不同，網上辱罵可以跟隨孩子回到家中，迅速擴散，並讓人感到無法逃避。 反覆的侮辱、謠言或令人羞辱的圖片，可能會嚴重損害孩子的自信心和心理健康。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"These problems can be reduced if parents take an active but sensible role in children’s internet use. Rather than simply banning the internet, parents should set clear rules, use age-appropriate safety settings, and regularly talk to their children about what they see online. This makes supervision feel like protection rather than punishment. Schools also have an important role to play. Digital safety lessons should teach children how to identify suspicious behaviour, protect personal information, block abusive users and report threatening messages. At the same time, technology companies should design safer spaces for young users, with stronger age checks, easier reporting tools and faster removal of harmful content.","chinese":"如果父母在孩子使用互聯網時扮演積極而理性的角色，這些問題是可以被減少的。 父母不應只是簡單地禁止孩子使用互聯網，而應該設定清晰的規則，使用適合年齡的安全設定，並定期與孩子談論他們在網上看到的內容。 這會令監督感覺像是一種保護，而不是懲罰。 學校也有重要的角色要發揮。 數碼安全課程應該教導兒童如何辨認可疑行為、保護個人資料、封鎖辱罵性的使用者，以及舉報具威脅性的訊息。 與此同時，科技公司應該為年幼使用者設計更安全的空間，包括更嚴格的年齡檢查、更容易使用的舉報工具，以及更快速移除有害內容的機制。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, unsupervised internet use can expose children to manipulation by strangers and damaging forms of cyberbullying. These dangers are best tackled through responsible parenting, practical digital education and safer online platforms.","chinese":"總結來說，沒有監督的互聯網使用可能會令兒童暴露於陌生人的操控，以及具傷害性的網絡欺凌之中。 這些危險最好透過負責任的家長教育、實用的數碼教育，以及更安全的網上平台來處理。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"internet access","chinese":"互聯網使用；上網渠道"},{"english":"a normal part of childhood","chinese":"童年生活的正常一部分"},{"english":"online platforms","chinese":"網上平台"},{"english":"build friendships","chinese":"建立友誼"},{"english":"without adult supervision","chinese":"沒有成人監督"},{"english":"be exposed to risks","chinese":"暴露於風險之中"},{"english":"mature enough to recognise","chinese":"成熟到足以辨認"},{"english":"dangerous strangers","chinese":"危險的陌生人"},{"english":"cyberbullying","chinese":"網絡欺凌"},{"english":"be addressed through","chinese":"可透過……處理"},{"english":"parental guidance","chinese":"家長指導"},{"english":"school education","chinese":"學校教育"},{"english":"platform responsibility","chinese":"平台責任"},{"english":"come into contact with","chinese":"接觸到；遇上"},{"english":"hide their real identity","chinese":"隱藏真實身份"},{"english":"gaming platforms","chinese":"遊戲平台"},{"english":"messaging apps","chinese":"即時通訊應用程式"},{"english":"social media groups","chinese":"社交媒體群組"},{"english":"pretend to be","chinese":"假扮成"},{"english":"gain trust","chinese":"取得信任"},{"english":"private information","chinese":"私人資料"},{"english":"persuade the child to keep secrets from","chinese":"說服孩子向……隱瞞秘密"},{"english":"trusting and eager to be accepted","chinese":"容易信任別人並渴望被接納"},{"english":"lead to grooming","chinese":"導致兒童誘騙"},{"english":"blackmail","chinese":"勒索"},{"english":"exploitation","chinese":"剝削；利用"},{"english":"ordinary playground conflict","chinese":"一般校園衝突"},{"english":"online abuse","chinese":"網上辱罵；網上傷害"},{"english":"follow a child home","chinese":"追到孩子家中；延伸到家中"},{"english":"spread quickly","chinese":"迅速傳開"},{"english":"impossible to escape","chinese":"令人覺得無法逃避"},{"english":"repeated insults","chinese":"反覆侮辱"},{"english":"rumours","chinese":"謠言"},{"english":"humiliating images","chinese":"令人羞辱的圖片"},{"english":"damage a child's confidence","chinese":"打擊孩子的自信"},{"english":"mental well-being","chinese":"精神健康"},{"english":"take an active but sensible role in","chinese":"在……中採取積極但理性的角色"},{"english":"children's internet use","chinese":"兒童使用互聯網"},{"english":"rather than simply banning","chinese":"而不是單純禁止"},{"english":"set clear rules","chinese":"訂立清晰規則"},{"english":"age-appropriate safety settings","chinese":"適合年齡的安全設定"},{"english":"regularly talk to","chinese":"定期與……交談"},{"english":"what they see online","chinese":"他們在網上看到的內容"},{"english":"supervision feel like protection rather than punishment","chinese":"令監督感覺像保護而不是懲罰"},{"english":"have an important role to play","chinese":"有重要角色"},{"english":"digital safety lessons","chinese":"數碼安全課程"},{"english":"identify suspicious behaviour","chinese":"辨認可疑行為"},{"english":"protect personal information","chinese":"保護個人資料"},{"english":"block abusive users","chinese":"封鎖辱罵性用戶"},{"english":"report threatening messages","chinese":"舉報威脅訊息"},{"english":"technology companies","chinese":"科技公司"},{"english":"safer spaces for young users","chinese":"給年輕用戶的更安全空間"},{"english":"stronger age checks","chinese":"更嚴格的年齡核查"},{"english":"easier reporting tools","chinese":"更易用的舉報工具"},{"english":"faster removal of harmful content","chinese":"更快移除有害內容"},{"english":"harmful content","chinese":"有害內容"},{"english":"unsupervised internet use","chinese":"無人監督下使用互聯網"},{"english":"expose children to manipulation by strangers","chinese":"令兒童暴露於陌生人的操控之中"},{"english":"manipulation by strangers","chinese":"被陌生人操控"},{"english":"damaging forms of cyberbullying","chinese":"具傷害性的網絡欺凌形式"},{"english":"be best tackled through","chinese":"最好透過……處理"},{"english":"responsible parenting","chinese":"負責任的家長管教"},{"english":"practical digital education","chinese":"實用的數碼教育"},{"english":"safer online platforms","chinese":"更安全的網上平台"}]},"model-essay-4-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-4-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:4","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-4-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q4","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In sales, it is tempting to assume that the best employees are those who chase money most aggressively, because commission rewards output directly. I disagree with this view: money is not the true driving force behind sustained hard work, and recruitment should focus on character and customer-facing ability rather than financial hunger alone.","chinese":"在銷售行業中，人們很容易假設最好的員工就是那些最積極追求金錢的人，因為佣金會直接獎勵工作成果。 我不同意這種觀點：金錢並不是持續努力工作的真正推動力，而招聘應該著重於品格和面對客戶的能力，而不是單靠對金錢的渴望。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Money may push people to make an extra call or close one more deal, but it rarely produces lasting dedication by itself. If a salesperson is motivated only by income, their effort depends on whether a reward is immediately visible. When targets become harder, customers become cautious, or rejection piles up, that motivation can burn out quickly. More importantly, a money-first employee may treat clients as transactions rather than people, which can damage trust and weaken long-term business relationships. Genuine hard work is more likely to come from professional pride, resilience, and a belief in the product being sold. These qualities keep a person steady when the easy rewards disappear.","chinese":"金錢也許能推動人們多打一通電話，或多完成一筆交易，但它本身很少能產生持久的投入感。 如果一名銷售人員只受到收入驅動，他們的努力便取決於回報是否能夠即時看見。 當目標變得更困難、客戶變得更謹慎，或者拒絕不斷累積時，這種動力便可能很快耗盡。 更重要的是，一個金錢至上的員工可能會把客戶視為交易，而不是有真實需要的人，這可能會損害信任，並削弱長期商業關係。 真正的努力工作更有可能來自專業自豪感、抗壓能力，以及對所銷售產品的信念。 當容易得到的回報消失時，這些特質能讓一個人保持穩定。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"When recruiting sales staff, companies should therefore consider several practical qualities. The first is communication skill: a good salesperson must listen carefully, explain benefits clearly, and adjust their tone to different customers. Sales is not merely talking; it is reading people. The second factor is resilience, because rejection is part of the job. A candidate who can stay calm after losing a deal is far more valuable than one who is energetic only when everything goes well. Finally, integrity should be treated as essential. Sales staff represent the company’s face, and one dishonest promise can poison a brand’s reputation for years.","chinese":"因此，在招聘銷售員工時，公司應該考慮幾項實際的特質。 第一項是溝通能力：一名優秀的銷售人員必須細心聆聽、清楚解釋產品好處，並根據不同客戶調整語氣。 銷售不只是說話；它是理解人。 第二個因素是抗壓能力，因為被拒絕是這份工作的一部分。 一個在失去交易後仍能保持冷靜的求職者，遠比一個只有在一切順利時才充滿幹勁的人更有價值。 最後，誠信應該被視為不可或缺的特質。 銷售員工代表公司的形象，而一個不誠實的承諾可能會多年來損害一個品牌的聲譽。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, money may be a useful incentive, but it should not be seen as the main engine of hard work. For sales positions, firms should recruit people who are persuasive, resilient, ethical, and genuinely capable of building trust with customers.","chinese":"總結來說，金錢也許是一種有用的激勵，但不應被視為努力工作的主要引擎。 對於銷售職位，公司應該招聘那些具說服力、有抗壓能力、有道德操守，並真正能夠與客戶建立信任的人。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"in sales","chinese":"在銷售行業"},{"english":"it is tempting to assume that","chinese":"很容易假設"},{"english":"chase money aggressively","chinese":"積極追求金錢"},{"english":"commission rewards output directly","chinese":"佣金直接獎勵業績"},{"english":"disagree with this view","chinese":"不同意這個看法"},{"english":"the true driving force behind","chinese":"……背後真正的推動力"},{"english":"sustained hard work","chinese":"持續努力工作"},{"english":"recruitment should focus on","chinese":"招聘應集中於"},{"english":"character","chinese":"品格"},{"english":"customer-facing ability","chinese":"面對顧客的能力"},{"english":"rather than financial hunger alone","chinese":"而不是單靠對金錢的渴求"},{"english":"financial hunger","chinese":"對金錢的渴求"},{"english":"make an extra call","chinese":"多打一個電話"},{"english":"close one more deal","chinese":"多完成一宗交易"},{"english":"lasting dedication","chinese":"持久的投入"},{"english":"by itself","chinese":"單靠本身"},{"english":"motivated only by income","chinese":"只受收入推動"},{"english":"depend on whether","chinese":"取決於是否"},{"english":"immediately visible","chinese":"即時可見"},{"english":"targets become harder","chinese":"目標變得更難"},{"english":"customers become cautious","chinese":"顧客變得謹慎"},{"english":"rejection piles up","chinese":"被拒絕的次數累積"},{"english":"burn out quickly","chinese":"很快耗盡"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"a money-first employee","chinese":"金錢至上的員工"},{"english":"treat clients as transactions","chinese":"將客戶視為交易"},{"english":"rather than people","chinese":"而不是視為人"},{"english":"damage trust","chinese":"損害信任"},{"english":"weaken long-term business relationships","chinese":"削弱長遠商業關係"},{"english":"genuine hard work","chinese":"真正的努力工作"},{"english":"be more likely to come from","chinese":"更可能來自"},{"english":"professional pride","chinese":"專業自豪感"},{"english":"a belief in the product","chinese":"對產品的信念"},{"english":"keep a person steady","chinese":"令一個人保持穩定"},{"english":"the easy rewards disappear","chinese":"容易得到的回報消失"},{"english":"sales staff","chinese":"銷售職員"},{"english":"practical qualities","chinese":"實際特質"},{"english":"communication skill","chinese":"溝通能力"},{"english":"listen carefully","chinese":"細心聆聽"},{"english":"explain benefits clearly","chinese":"清楚解釋好處"},{"english":"adjust their tone to","chinese":"按……調整語氣"},{"english":"different customers","chinese":"不同顧客"},{"english":"not merely talking","chinese":"不只是說話"},{"english":"reading people","chinese":"讀懂別人"},{"english":"part of the job","chinese":"工作的一部分"},{"english":"stay calm after losing a deal","chinese":"失去交易後保持冷靜"},{"english":"far more valuable than","chinese":"比……有價值得多"},{"english":"energetic only when","chinese":"只有在……時才有幹勁"},{"english":"everything goes well","chinese":"一切順利"},{"english":"integrity","chinese":"誠信"},{"english":"be treated as essential","chinese":"應被視為必要"},{"english":"represent the company's face","chinese":"代表公司的形象"},{"english":"a dishonest promise","chinese":"不誠實的承諾"},{"english":"poison a brand's reputation","chinese":"破壞品牌聲譽"},{"english":"for years","chinese":"多年來"},{"english":"a useful incentive","chinese":"有用的誘因"},{"english":"the main engine of hard work","chinese":"努力工作的主要動力"},{"english":"sales positions","chinese":"銷售職位"},{"english":"persuasive","chinese":"有說服力的"},{"english":"ethical","chinese":"有道德的"},{"english":"genuinely capable of","chinese":"真正有能力"},{"english":"building trust with customers","chinese":"與顧客建立信任"}]},"model-essay-4-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-4-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:4","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-4-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q4","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many countries, small and medium-sized firms are built around family ownership, and this arrangement is often seen as a strong foundation for commercial success. I disagree. In my view, running a business mainly through family ties is not the best model, because it can weaken professional judgement and turn private conflict into commercial risk.","chinese":"在許多國家，中小型企業都是圍繞家族所有權建立起來的，而這種安排常被視為商業成功的穩固基礎。 我不同意。 在我看來，主要依靠家族關係來經營企業並不是最佳模式，因為這可能削弱專業判斷，並把私人衝突轉化為商業風險。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first problem is that family-run firms often blur the line between affection and competence. A successful company needs employees who are selected, promoted, and corrected according to performance. When relatives are given senior roles because of blood rather than ability, poor management may be protected by loyalty. This creates a serious chain of damage: capable non-family workers feel undervalued, standards become inconsistent, and difficult decisions are delayed. For example, if an owner’s son repeatedly loses important clients, other managers may hesitate to challenge him because criticism could be treated as a family insult. Over time, such favouritism reduces trust within the workplace and makes the firm less competitive.","chinese":"第一個問題是，家族經營的企業往往會模糊親情與能力之間的界線。 一間成功的公司需要根據表現來選拔、晉升和糾正員工。 當親屬因血緣而不是能力獲得高層職位時，糟糕的管理可能會受到忠誠感的保護。這會造成一連串嚴重損害：有能力的非家族員工會覺得自己不受重視，標準會變得不一致，而艱難的決定也會被拖延。 例如，如果老闆的兒子不斷失去重要客戶，其他經理可能會猶豫是否要質疑他，因為批評可能會被視為對家族的侮辱。 長遠而言，這種偏袒會削弱工作場所內的信任，並使企業的競爭力下降。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another major issue is that family disputes can easily spill into the business. In a professionally managed company, disagreements can be handled through contracts, clear job descriptions, and formal procedures. In a family firm, however, arguments over inheritance, leadership, or money may become deeply personal. A disagreement between siblings over who should take control of the company, for instance, can paralyse hiring, investment, and expansion plans. Ordinary staff may also feel forced to take sides, creating an unhealthy atmosphere in which business priorities are pushed behind personal loyalties. This is especially dangerous during succession, when the firm needs stability rather than rivalry. A company cannot grow steadily if its steering wheel is constantly pulled by family tension.","chinese":"另一個主要問題是，家族糾紛很容易蔓延到企業之中。 在一間由專業方式管理的公司中，分歧可透過合約、清晰的職責說明和正式程序來處理 然而，在家族企業中，圍繞繼承權、領導權或金錢的爭執可能會變得非常私人化。 例如，兄弟姊妹之間若因誰應該掌管公司而產生分歧，便可能令招聘、投資和擴展計劃陷入停頓。 普通員工也可能覺得自己被迫選邊站，從而造成一種不健康的氣氛，使商業優先事項被個人忠誠壓到後面。 這在接班期間尤其危險，因為企業在這個時候需要的是穩定，而不是競爭。 如果一間公司的方向盤不斷被家族矛盾拉扯，它就不可能穩定成長。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"Overall, I believe family-run businesses are more likely to create problems than provide the ideal business structure. Businesses need fairness, expertise, and clear governance, and these qualities are often compromised when family relationships dominate commercial decisions.","chinese":"總結來說，我認為家族經營的企業更可能製造問題，而不是提供理想的企業結構。 企業需要公平、專業知識和清晰的治理，而當家族關係主導商業決策時，這些特質往往會受到損害。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"small and medium-sized firms","chinese":"中小型企業"},{"english":"be built around","chinese":"以……為核心建立"},{"english":"family ownership","chinese":"家族擁有權"},{"english":"this arrangement","chinese":"這種安排"},{"english":"be seen as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"a strong foundation for","chinese":"……的穩固基礎"},{"english":"commercial success","chinese":"商業成功"},{"english":"In my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"family ties","chinese":"家族關係"},{"english":"the best model","chinese":"最佳模式"},{"english":"weaken professional judgement","chinese":"削弱專業判斷"},{"english":"private conflict","chinese":"私人衝突"},{"english":"commercial risk","chinese":"商業風險"},{"english":"The first problem is that","chinese":"第一個問題是"},{"english":"family-run firms","chinese":"家族經營企業"},{"english":"blur the line between","chinese":"模糊……之間的界線"},{"english":"affection and competence","chinese":"感情和能力"},{"english":"selected, promoted, and corrected","chinese":"被挑選、晉升和糾正"},{"english":"according to performance","chinese":"根據表現"},{"english":"given senior roles","chinese":"被給予高級職位"},{"english":"because of blood rather than ability","chinese":"因血緣而不是能力"},{"english":"poor management","chinese":"糟糕的管理"},{"english":"protected by loyalty","chinese":"受到忠誠保護"},{"english":"a serious chain of damage","chinese":"一連串嚴重損害"},{"english":"capable non-family workers","chinese":"有能力的非家族員工"},{"english":"feel undervalued","chinese":"感到不受重視"},{"english":"standards become inconsistent","chinese":"標準變得不一致"},{"english":"difficult decisions are delayed","chinese":"困難決定被拖延"},{"english":"repeatedly loses important clients","chinese":"反覆失去重要客戶"},{"english":"hesitate to challenge","chinese":"猶豫是否挑戰；不敢質疑"},{"english":"be treated as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"a family insult","chinese":"對家族的冒犯"},{"english":"Over time","chinese":"隨時間"},{"english":"favouritism","chinese":"偏私；偏袒"},{"english":"reduces trust within","chinese":"降低……內部的信任"},{"english":"less competitive","chinese":"競爭力較弱"},{"english":"Another major issue is that","chinese":"另一個主要問題是"},{"english":"family disputes","chinese":"家族糾紛"},{"english":"spill into","chinese":"蔓延到"},{"english":"professionally managed company","chinese":"專業管理的公司"},{"english":"be handled through","chinese":"透過……處理"},{"english":"clear job descriptions","chinese":"清晰的職位說明"},{"english":"formal procedures","chinese":"正式程序"},{"english":"arguments over","chinese":"關於……的爭執"},{"english":"inheritance","chinese":"繼承權；遺產"},{"english":"deeply personal","chinese":"非常私人化"},{"english":"a disagreement between siblings","chinese":"兄弟姊妹之間的分歧"},{"english":"take control of","chinese":"掌控"},{"english":"paralyse hiring","chinese":"令招聘停頓"},{"english":"investment and expansion plans","chinese":"投資和擴展計劃"},{"english":"ordinary staff","chinese":"普通員工"},{"english":"feel forced to","chinese":"感到被迫"},{"english":"take sides","chinese":"選邊站"},{"english":"an unhealthy atmosphere","chinese":"不健康的氣氛"},{"english":"business priorities","chinese":"商業優先事項"},{"english":"pushed behind","chinese":"被放在……之後"},{"english":"personal loyalties","chinese":"私人忠誠"},{"english":"especially dangerous during","chinese":"在……期間特別危險"},{"english":"succession","chinese":"接班；繼承"},{"english":"stability rather than rivalry","chinese":"穩定而不是競爭"},{"english":"grow steadily","chinese":"穩定成長"},{"english":"steering wheel","chinese":"方向盤"},{"english":"family tension","chinese":"家族緊張關係"},{"english":"more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"create problems than provide","chinese":"造成問題而不是提供"},{"english":"the ideal business structure","chinese":"理想的企業結構"},{"english":"fairness, expertise, and clear governance","chinese":"公平、專業知識和清晰管治"},{"english":"clear governance","chinese":"清晰管治"},{"english":"be compromised","chinese":"被削弱；受到損害"},{"english":"family relationships dominate","chinese":"家族關係佔主導"},{"english":"commercial decisions","chinese":"商業決策"}]},"model-essay-4-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-4-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:4","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-4-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q4","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Artists are often expected to challenge convention, so some degree of creative freedom is clearly necessary. Some people therefore argue that they should have total freedom to express any thoughts they choose. This essay will argue that this view is wrong because unlimited artistic expression can damage society and because no one who speaks to the public should escape responsibility.","chinese":"人們通常期待藝術家挑戰傳統，因此某種程度的創作自由顯然是必要的。 因此，有些人主張，藝術家應該擁有完全的自由，去表達任何他們想表達的想法。 本文將論證，這種觀點是錯誤的，因為毫無限制的藝術表達可能會傷害社會，而且任何向公眾發聲的人都不應逃避責任。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason total freedom should not be allowed is that art can shape attitudes, not merely reflect them. When films, lyrics or exhibitions glorify racial hatred, violence or extremism, repeated exposure can make such ideas seem less shocking and more defensible. Once this happens, discrimination and aggression become easier to excuse in daily life. For example, propaganda art has often been used to dehumanise minorities before broader hostility followed. Unrestricted expression can also harm people directly. Work that humiliates vulnerable groups for attention may create fear, distress and exclusion, especially when it spreads rapidly online. Artistic freedom, therefore, cannot be unlimited.","chinese":"第一個不應允許完全自由的原因是，藝術不只是反映態度，它也能塑造態度。 當電影、歌詞或展覽美化種族仇恨、暴力或極端思想時，反覆接觸這些內容會讓這些想法看起來不再那麼令人震驚，甚至更容易被辯護。 一旦出現這種情況，歧視與攻擊行為在日常生活中就會變得更容易被合理化。 例如，宣傳藝術經常被用來先剝奪少數群體的人性，而更廣泛的敵意往往隨後而來。 不受限制的表達也可能直接傷害他人。 那些為了吸引關注而羞辱弱勢群體的作品，可能會造成恐懼、痛苦與排斥，尤其當它們在網路上快速傳播時更是如此。 因此，藝術自由不可能是毫無限制的。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"A second reason is that public expression always carries public responsibility. Once a work is published or performed, it is no longer a private thought; it becomes an act that can affect other people's dignity, safety and reputation. If artists received absolute protection, they could evade accountability for defamation or incitement simply by calling such acts art. No fair society should place any group above the law. Moreover, creativity itself does not require total freedom. Boundaries often force artists to rely on symbolism, irony and craft, which can make criticism more powerful rather than less. Many great novels, films and satirical works challenge authority strongly without crossing basic legal or moral lines.","chinese":"第二個原因是，公開表達永遠伴隨著公開責任。 一旦作品被出版或表演，它就不再只是私人想法；它會變成一種可能影響他人尊嚴、安全與名譽的行為。 如果藝術家獲得絕對保護，他們就可能只靠把某些行為稱為藝術，來逃避對誹謗或煽動行為的責任。 任何公平的社會都不應把任何群體置於法律之上。 此外，創造力本身並不需要完全的自由。 界線往往會迫使藝術家依靠象徵、反諷與技巧，而這反而可能使批評更有力量，而不是削弱它。 許多偉大的小說、電影和諷刺作品，都能強烈挑戰權威，同時又不越過基本的法律或道德界線。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely disagree that artists should have total freedom to express any idea whatsoever. Creativity needs room to develop, but once expression seriously harms others or violates their rights, society is justified in imposing limits.","chinese":"總而言之，我完全不同意藝術家應該擁有表達任何想法的絕對自由。 創造力的確需要發展空間，但一旦某種表達嚴重傷害他人，或侵犯他人的權利，社會就有正當理由加以限制。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"be expected to","chinese":"被期望去"},{"english":"challenge convention","chinese":"挑戰傳統；挑戰常規"},{"english":"some degree of creative freedom","chinese":"某程度的創作自由"},{"english":"clearly necessary","chinese":"明顯必要"},{"english":"total freedom to","chinese":"完全自由去"},{"english":"express any thoughts they choose","chinese":"表達任何自己選擇的想法"},{"english":"this view is wrong","chinese":"這個觀點是錯誤的"},{"english":"unlimited artistic expression","chinese":"無限制的藝術表達"},{"english":"damage society","chinese":"損害社會"},{"english":"speak to the public","chinese":"向公眾發聲"},{"english":"escape responsibility","chinese":"逃避責任"},{"english":"should not be allowed","chinese":"不應被容許"},{"english":"shape attitudes","chinese":"塑造態度"},{"english":"not merely reflect them","chinese":"不只是反映它們"},{"english":"films, lyrics or exhibitions","chinese":"電影、歌詞或展覽"},{"english":"glorify racial hatred","chinese":"美化種族仇恨"},{"english":"violence or extremism","chinese":"暴力或極端主義"},{"english":"repeated exposure","chinese":"反覆接觸"},{"english":"make such ideas seem less shocking","chinese":"令這些想法顯得不那麼令人震驚"},{"english":"more defensible","chinese":"更像是可以辯護的"},{"english":"once this happens","chinese":"一旦這種情況發生"},{"english":"discrimination and aggression","chinese":"歧視和攻擊行為"},{"english":"become easier to excuse","chinese":"變得更容易被合理化"},{"english":"in daily life","chinese":"在日常生活中"},{"english":"propaganda art","chinese":"宣傳藝術"},{"english":"be used to","chinese":"被用作"},{"english":"dehumanise minorities","chinese":"將少數群體非人化"},{"english":"broader hostility","chinese":"更廣泛的敵意"},{"english":"unrestricted expression","chinese":"不受限制的表達"},{"english":"harm people directly","chinese":"直接傷害他人"},{"english":"work that humiliates vulnerable groups","chinese":"羞辱弱勢群體的作品"},{"english":"vulnerable groups","chinese":"弱勢群體"},{"english":"for attention","chinese":"為了吸引注意"},{"english":"create fear, distress and exclusion","chinese":"製造恐懼、困擾和排斥"},{"english":"especially when","chinese":"尤其當"},{"english":"spread rapidly online","chinese":"在網上迅速傳播"},{"english":"cannot be unlimited","chinese":"不能是無限制的"},{"english":"public expression","chinese":"公開表達"},{"english":"carry public responsibility","chinese":"承擔公共責任"},{"english":"be published or performed","chinese":"被出版或演出"},{"english":"no longer a private thought","chinese":"不再是私人想法"},{"english":"become an act that","chinese":"成為一種會……的行為"},{"english":"affect other people's dignity","chinese":"影響他人的尊嚴"},{"english":"safety and reputation","chinese":"安全和名譽"},{"english":"receive absolute protection","chinese":"獲得絕對保護"},{"english":"evade accountability for","chinese":"逃避對……的問責"},{"english":"defamation","chinese":"誹謗"},{"english":"incitement","chinese":"煽動"},{"english":"simply by calling such acts art","chinese":"只靠把這些行為稱為藝術"},{"english":"no fair society should","chinese":"沒有公平社會應該"},{"english":"place any group above the law","chinese":"令任何群體凌駕於法律之上"},{"english":"moreover","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"creativity itself","chinese":"創意本身"},{"english":"require total freedom","chinese":"需要完全自由"},{"english":"boundaries","chinese":"界限；限制"},{"english":"force artists to rely on","chinese":"迫使藝術家依靠"},{"english":"symbolism","chinese":"象徵手法"},{"english":"irony","chinese":"反諷"},{"english":"craft","chinese":"技巧；藝術手法"},{"english":"make criticism more powerful","chinese":"令批判更有力量"},{"english":"rather than less","chinese":"而不是更少"},{"english":"satirical works","chinese":"諷刺作品"},{"english":"challenge authority","chinese":"挑戰權威"},{"english":"without crossing","chinese":"在不越過……的情況下"},{"english":"basic legal or moral lines","chinese":"基本法律或道德界線"},{"english":"any idea whatsoever","chinese":"任何想法"},{"english":"room to develop","chinese":"發展空間"},{"english":"seriously harms others","chinese":"嚴重傷害他人"},{"english":"violates their rights","chinese":"侵犯他人的權利"},{"english":"be justified in","chinese":"有合理理由去"},{"english":"imposing limits","chinese":"施加限制"}]},"model-essay-4-ielts-task1-bar-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-4-ielts-task1-bar-charts","essayKey":"bar-charts:4","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-4-ielts-task1-bar-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/bar-charts/bar-chart-4","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The bar chart compares the percentages of households living in owner-occupied and rented accommodation in England and Wales between 1918 and 2011.","chinese":"這張柱狀圖比較了 1918 年至 2011 年間，英格蘭和威爾斯居住在自有住房和租住住房中的家庭比例。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, home ownership followed a clear upward trajectory for most of the period, whereas renting moved in the opposite direction. The two categories were equal in 1971, after which ownership became dominant, although it slipped slightly in the final year.","chinese":"整體而言，在大部分期間，自有住房比例呈現明顯上升趨勢；相反，租住住房比例則朝相反方向變化。 這兩個類別在 1971 年持平；其後，自有住房成為主導類別，儘管它在最後一年略有回落。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 1918, renting accounted for by far the larger share, at just under four fifths of households, while ownership stood at only about 22%. By 1939 and 1953, the rental figure had fallen to around 68%, with owner-occupation rising to roughly 31–32%. The gap narrowed further in 1961, when about 42% of households owned their homes, compared with just under 60% that rented.","chinese":"在 1918 年，租住住房佔明顯較大的比例，略低於五分之四；而自有住房比例僅約為 22% 。 到 1939 年和 1953 年，租住住房比例已下降至約 68% ，而自有住房比例則上升至約 31% 至 32% 。 到 1961 年，兩者之間的差距進一步收窄，當時約 42% 的家庭擁有自己的住房，而租住住房的比例則略低於 60% 。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The turning point came in 1971, when both categories stood at exactly 50%. Thereafter, ownership climbed to approximately 60% in 1981 and almost 70% in 2001, reaching its peak. By contrast, renting declined to just over 30% by 2001. In 2011, however, the pattern changed modestly: ownership decreased to about 64%, while renting recovered to around 36%.","chinese":"轉折點出現在 1971 年，當時兩個類別的比例均為 50% 。 此後，自有住房比例在 1981 年上升至約 60% ，並在 2001 年接近 70% ，達最高點。 相比之下，租住住房比例到 2001 年下降至略高於 30% 。 然而，到 2011 年，這一模式出現了輕微變化：自有住房比例下降至約 64% ，而租住住房比例則回升至約 36% 。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"compares the percentages of households","chinese":"比較住戶百分比"},{"english":"households living in","chinese":"居於……的住戶"},{"english":"owner-occupied accommodation","chinese":"自置物業"},{"english":"rented accommodation","chinese":"租住物業"},{"english":"between 1918 and 2011","chinese":"在1918年至2011年之間"},{"english":"home ownership","chinese":"置業；自置居所"},{"english":"followed a clear upward trajectory","chinese":"呈現明顯上升趨勢"},{"english":"for most of the period","chinese":"在大部分時期"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"然而；而"},{"english":"moved in the opposite direction","chinese":"朝相反方向變化"},{"english":"the two categories were equal","chinese":"兩個類別相同"},{"english":"after which","chinese":"此後；之後"},{"english":"ownership became dominant","chinese":"自置居所成為主導"},{"english":"slipped slightly","chinese":"輕微下跌"},{"english":"in the final year","chinese":"在最後一年"},{"english":"renting accounted for","chinese":"租住佔"},{"english":"by far the larger share","chinese":"遙遙領先的較大比例"},{"english":"at just under four fifths","chinese":"略低於五分之四"},{"english":"while ownership stood at","chinese":"而自置居所處於"},{"english":"stood at only about 22%","chinese":"僅約為22%"},{"english":"by 1939 and 1953","chinese":"到1939年和1953年"},{"english":"the rental figure","chinese":"租住比例"},{"english":"had fallen to around 68%","chinese":"已跌至約68%"},{"english":"owner-occupation","chinese":"自置居所"},{"english":"rising to roughly 31–32%","chinese":"上升至約31%至32%"},{"english":"the gap narrowed further","chinese":"差距進一步收窄"},{"english":"in 1961","chinese":"在1961年"},{"english":"owned their homes","chinese":"擁有自己的住所"},{"english":"compared with","chinese":"與……相比"},{"english":"just under 60%","chinese":"略低於60%"},{"english":"the turning point came in","chinese":"轉捩點出現在"},{"english":"stood at exactly 50%","chinese":"正好處於50%"},{"english":"Thereafter","chinese":"此後"},{"english":"climbed to approximately 60%","chinese":"攀升至約60%"},{"english":"almost 70%","chinese":"接近70%"},{"english":"reaching its peak","chinese":"達到高峰"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"declined to just over 30%","chinese":"下降至略高於30%"},{"english":"by 2001","chinese":"到2001年"},{"english":"the pattern changed modestly","chinese":"模式出現輕微變化"},{"english":"ownership decreased to about 64%","chinese":"自置居所下降至約64%"},{"english":"while renting recovered to","chinese":"而租住回升至"},{"english":"recovered to around 36%","chinese":"回升至約36%"}]},"model-essay-4-ielts-task1-line-graph":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-4-ielts-task1-line-graph","essayKey":"line-graph:4","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-4-ielts-task1-line-graph","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/line-graphs/line-graph-4","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The line graph compares the numbers of shop closures and openings in one country from 2011 to 2018.","chinese":"這張折線圖比較了某一國家在 2011 年至 2018 年間商店關閉和新開商店的數量。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, shop openings showed a clear downward trend, ending at their lowest point, while closures fluctuated markedly. Apart from the initial year and the exceptional trough in closures in 2015, more shops closed than opened.","chinese":"整體而言，新開商店數量呈現明顯下降趨勢，並在最後達到最低點；相反，關店數量則大幅波動。 除第一年以及 2015 年關店數出現異常低谷之外，關閉的商店數量多於新開商店數量。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 2011, openings were far higher, at about 8,500, compared with roughly 6,400 closures. The number of new shops then almost halved to around 4,000 in 2012, before recovering to about 5,000 in 2013 and just over 6,000 in 2014. After this brief rebound, openings fell back to 4,000 in 2015 and 2016, edged up slightly to around 4,200 in 2017, and then declined to approximately 3,000 in 2018.","chinese":"2011 年，新開商店數量遠高於關店數，約為 8,500 間，而關店數約為 6,400 間。 之後，新開商店數量在 2012 年幾乎減半至約 4,000 間，然後在 2013 年回升至約5,000 間，並在 2014 年升至略高於 6,000 間。 在這次短暫回升之後，新開商店數量在 2015 年和 2016 年回落至 4,000 間， 2017年小幅上升至約 4,200 間，然後在 2018 年下降至約 3,000 間。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Closures followed a less steady pattern. The figure slipped from around 6,400 to just under 6,000 in 2012, then rose to a peak of about 7,200 in 2013. It remained high in 2014, at roughly 6,500, before plunging to only about 500 in 2015. However, closures rebounded sharply to just over 5,000 in 2016 and then stayed close to this level in the final two years.","chinese":"關店數量的走勢則較不穩定。 該數字從約 6,400 間下降至 2012 年的略低於 6,000 間，之後在 2013 年上升至約7,200 間的高峰。 2014 年，關店數仍然維持在較高水平，約為 6,500 間，然後在 2015 年急跌至只有約 500 間。 然而，關店數在 2016 年大幅反彈至略高於 5,000 間，之後在最後兩年保持在接近這一水平。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"line graph","chinese":"折線圖"},{"english":"shop closures and openings","chinese":"商店結業及開業"},{"english":"shop closures","chinese":"商店結業"},{"english":"shop openings","chinese":"商店開業"},{"english":"from 2011 to 2018","chinese":"由2011年至2018年"},{"english":"showed a clear downward trend","chinese":"呈現明顯下降趨勢"},{"english":"downward trend","chinese":"下降趨勢"},{"english":"ending at their lowest point","chinese":"最後跌至最低點"},{"english":"lowest point","chinese":"最低點"},{"english":"fluctuated markedly","chinese":"明顯波動"},{"english":"apart from","chinese":"除了……之外"},{"english":"the initial year","chinese":"最初一年"},{"english":"exceptional trough","chinese":"異常低谷"},{"english":"trough in closures","chinese":"結業數字的低谷"},{"english":"more shops closed than opened","chinese":"結業商店多於開業商店"},{"english":"far higher","chinese":"高得多"},{"english":"at about 8,500","chinese":"約為8,500"},{"english":"compared with roughly","chinese":"與約……相比"},{"english":"roughly 6,400 closures","chinese":"約6,400宗結業"},{"english":"the number of new shops","chinese":"新開商店數目"},{"english":"almost halved to","chinese":"幾乎減半至"},{"english":"around 4,000","chinese":"約4,000"},{"english":"before recovering to","chinese":"之後回升至"},{"english":"recovering to","chinese":"回升至"},{"english":"just over 6,000","chinese":"略高於6,000"},{"english":"brief rebound","chinese":"短暫反彈"},{"english":"fell back to","chinese":"回落至"},{"english":"edged up slightly","chinese":"輕微上升"},{"english":"declined to approximately","chinese":"下降至約"},{"english":"approximately 3,000","chinese":"約3,000"},{"english":"followed a less steady pattern","chinese":"呈現較不穩定的模式"},{"english":"less steady pattern","chinese":"較不穩定的模式"},{"english":"the figure slipped from…to…","chinese":"數字由……微跌至……"},{"english":"slipped from","chinese":"由……微跌"},{"english":"just under 6,000","chinese":"略低於6,000"},{"english":"rose to a peak of","chinese":"上升至峰值"},{"english":"peak of about 7,200","chinese":"約7,200的峰值"},{"english":"remained high","chinese":"維持高水平"},{"english":"at roughly 6,500","chinese":"約為6,500"},{"english":"before plunging to","chinese":"之後急跌至"},{"english":"plunged to only about","chinese":"急跌至只有約"},{"english":"only about 500","chinese":"只有約500"},{"english":"however","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"rebounded sharply","chinese":"大幅反彈"},{"english":"just over 5,000","chinese":"略高於5,000"},{"english":"stayed close to this level","chinese":"維持接近這一水平"},{"english":"this level","chinese":"這一水平"},{"english":"in the final two years","chinese":"在最後兩年"},{"english":"clear downward movement","chinese":"明顯下跌走勢"},{"english":"marked fluctuation","chinese":"明顯波動"},{"english":"initial gap","chinese":"初期差距"},{"english":"final figure","chinese":"最終數字"}]},"model-essay-4-ielts-task1-maps":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-4-ielts-task1-maps","essayKey":"maps:4","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-4-ielts-task1-maps","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/maps/maps-4","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The two maps compare the present industrial area in Norbiton with the proposed redevelopment of the site.","chinese":"這兩幅地圖比較了諾比頓目前的工業區與該地點擬議的未來重建規劃。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the area is set to be transformed from a factory complex into a residential district with public amenities. The road network will also be expanded, especially northwards across the river and southwards to the main road, while the river and the main east–west road will largely remain in place.","chinese":"整體而言，該區域將由一個工廠群轉變為設有公共設施的住宅區。 道路網也將會擴展，尤其會向北跨過河流，並向南連接主要道路；同時，河流和主要東西向道路大致會保留在原位。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Currently, the site is centred on a roundabout south of the river. From this junction, one road runs east, with several factories on both sides and another at its far end. Other factories stand immediately north and west of the roundabout, and a short road links the junction to the main east–west road. The town lies to the west.","chinese":"目前，該地點以河流以南的一個迴旋處為中心。 從這個交匯處，一條道路向東延伸，道路兩側有數間工廠，最東端還有另一間工廠。 其他工廠位於迴旋處正北方和西側，而一條短路把這個交匯處連接到主要的東西向道路。 城鎮位於西側。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"In the future plan, all factories will be removed and replaced mainly by housing. Homes will be added west of the roundabout, along the eastern road and, after a bridge is built, north of the river. A second roundabout will be constructed on the southern access road. Shops, a medical centre, a playground and a school will also be introduced in the southern, eastern and northeastern parts of the site.","chinese":"在未來規劃中，所有工廠都將被移除，並主要由住宅取代。 住宅將會被增設在迴旋處西側、東面道路沿線，及在橋樑建成後的河流北側。 第二個迴旋處將會建在南面的通道上。 商店、醫療中心、遊樂場和學校也將分別被引入該地點南部、東部和東北部。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the maps below","chinese":"以下地圖"},{"english":"an industrial area","chinese":"工業區"},{"english":"the town of Norbiton","chinese":"Norbiton 鎮"},{"english":"planned future development","chinese":"計劃中的未來發展"},{"english":"future development of the site","chinese":"該地點的未來發展"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"by selecting and reporting","chinese":"透過選取並報告……"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"compare X with Y","chinese":"比較 X 和 Y"},{"english":"the present industrial area","chinese":"現時的工業區"},{"english":"the proposed redevelopment","chinese":"擬議的重建計劃"},{"english":"redevelopment of the site","chinese":"該地點的重建"},{"english":"is set to be transformed","chinese":"將會被改造成"},{"english":"be transformed from X into Y","chinese":"由 X 改造成 Y"},{"english":"a factory complex","chinese":"工廠群；工廠綜合區"},{"english":"a residential district","chinese":"住宅區"},{"english":"public amenities","chinese":"公共設施"},{"english":"the road network","chinese":"道路網絡"},{"english":"will be expanded","chinese":"將會擴展"},{"english":"northwards across the river","chinese":"向北跨過河流"},{"english":"southwards to the main road","chinese":"向南伸延至主要道路"},{"english":"the main road","chinese":"主要道路"},{"english":"the main east–west road","chinese":"主要東西向道路"},{"english":"will largely remain in place","chinese":"大致保留原位"},{"english":"be centred on","chinese":"以……為中心"},{"english":"a roundabout","chinese":"迴旋處"},{"english":"south of the river","chinese":"在河流以南"},{"english":"from this junction","chinese":"從這個交匯處"},{"english":"run east","chinese":"向東伸延"},{"english":"on both sides","chinese":"在兩旁"},{"english":"at its far end","chinese":"在其盡頭"},{"english":"stand immediately north and west of","chinese":"緊接位於……的北面和西面"},{"english":"immediately north of","chinese":"緊接在……北面"},{"english":"west of the roundabout","chinese":"在迴旋處西面"},{"english":"a short road","chinese":"一條短路"},{"english":"link X to Y","chinese":"連接 X 和 Y"},{"english":"the junction","chinese":"交匯處"},{"english":"lie to the west","chinese":"位於西面"},{"english":"in the future plan","chinese":"在未來規劃中"},{"english":"will be removed","chinese":"將會被拆除"},{"english":"be replaced mainly by","chinese":"主要被……取代"},{"english":"housing","chinese":"住宅"},{"english":"homes will be added","chinese":"將會增建住宅"},{"english":"to the west of the roundabout","chinese":"在迴旋處以西"},{"english":"along the eastern road","chinese":"沿着東面道路"},{"english":"after a bridge is built","chinese":"在橋建成後"},{"english":"a bridge is built","chinese":"建成一條橋"},{"english":"north of the river","chinese":"在河流以北"},{"english":"a second roundabout","chinese":"第二個迴旋處"},{"english":"will be constructed","chinese":"將會建成"},{"english":"the southern access road","chinese":"南面的出入通道"},{"english":"will also be introduced","chinese":"亦會增設"},{"english":"shops","chinese":"商店"},{"english":"a medical centre","chinese":"醫療中心"},{"english":"a playground","chinese":"遊樂場"},{"english":"in the southern part of the site","chinese":"在該地點南部"},{"english":"in the eastern part of the site","chinese":"在該地點東部"},{"english":"in the north-eastern part of the site","chinese":"在該地點東北部"},{"english":"residential and community facilities","chinese":"住宅及社區設施"},{"english":"replace industrial land with housing","chinese":"以住宅取代工業用地"}]},"model-essay-4-ielts-task1-mixed-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-4-ielts-task1-mixed-charts","essayKey":"mixed-charts:4","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-4-ielts-task1-mixed-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/mixed-charts/mixed-charts-4","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The bar chart compares the export earnings of a country in five product categories in 2015 and 2016, while the table indicates the percentage change in each category over the same period.","chinese":"這張柱狀圖比較了一個國家在 2015 年和 2016 年五個產品類別的出口收入，而表格則顯示了同一期間每個類別出口價值的百分比變化。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, export revenue rose in four of the five categories, with gems and jewellery being the only sector to decline. Petroleum products remained the largest earner in both years, whereas textiles, despite starting from the lowest base, recorded the fastest growth.","chinese":"整體而言，五個類別中有四個的出口收入上升，只有寶石與珠寶這一類出現下降。 石油產品在兩年中都是出口收入最高的類別；相反，紡織品雖然起點最低，卻錄得最快的增長。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 2015, petroleum products generated about $61 billion, slightly more than engineered goods, at roughly $58 billion. Both categories increased in 2016: the former rose modestly by 3% to around $63 billion, while the latter climbed more sharply, by 8.5%, to approximately $62 billion. Gems and jewellery followed a different path, falling from about $43 billion to roughly $41 billion, a decrease of 5.18%.","chinese":"2015 年，石油產品創造了約 610 億美元的出口收入，略高於工程產品的約 580億美元。 這兩個類別在 2016 年均有所上升：前者溫和增長 3% ，達到約 630 億美元；後者則上升更明顯，增幅為 8.5% ，達到約 620 億美元。 寶石與珠寶則呈現不同走勢，從約 430 億美元下降至約 410 億美元，跌幅為。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Among the lower-earning categories, agricultural products changed very little, remaining at around $31 billion in both years after a marginal rise of 0.81%. Textiles, by contrast, grew markedly from about $26 billion to roughly $31 billion, representing a 15.24% increase and making it nearly equal to agricultural products by 2016.","chinese":"在收入較低的類別中，農產品變化非常小，在輕微上升 0.81% 後，兩年都維持在約 310 億美元左右。 相比之下，紡織品從約 260 億美元顯著增長至約 310 億美元，增幅為 15.24% ，到2016 年幾乎與農產品持平。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the chart below","chinese":"以下圖表"},{"english":"give information on","chinese":"提供關於……的資料"},{"english":"Anthropology graduates","chinese":"人類學畢業生"},{"english":"from one university","chinese":"來自某一所大學"},{"english":"after finishing","chinese":"完成……後"},{"english":"undergraduate degree course","chinese":"本科學位課程"},{"english":"the table shows","chinese":"表格顯示"},{"english":"salaries of","chinese":"……的薪酬"},{"english":"anthropologists in work","chinese":"在職人類學家"},{"english":"after five years","chinese":"五年後"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"by selecting and reporting","chinese":"透過選取並報告……"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"the bar chart compares","chinese":"柱形圖比較"},{"english":"export earnings","chinese":"出口收益"},{"english":"product categories","chinese":"產品類別"},{"english":"in 2015 and 2016","chinese":"在2015年和2016年"},{"english":"while the table indicates","chinese":"而表格顯示"},{"english":"percentage change","chinese":"百分比變化"},{"english":"in each category","chinese":"在每個類別中"},{"english":"over the same period","chinese":"在同一期間"},{"english":"export revenue","chinese":"出口收入"},{"english":"rose in four of the five categories","chinese":"在五個類別中的四個上升"},{"english":"with X being the only Y","chinese":"其中 X 是唯一的 Y"},{"english":"gems and jewellery","chinese":"寶石及珠寶"},{"english":"the only sector to decline","chinese":"唯一下跌的行業"},{"english":"petroleum products","chinese":"石油產品"},{"english":"remained the largest earner","chinese":"仍然是最大收益來源"},{"english":"in both years","chinese":"在兩年中"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相反"},{"english":"textiles","chinese":"紡織品"},{"english":"despite starting from","chinese":"儘管由……開始"},{"english":"the lowest base","chinese":"最低基數；最低起點"},{"english":"recorded the fastest growth","chinese":"錄得最快增長"},{"english":"generated about","chinese":"創造約……收益"},{"english":"slightly more than","chinese":"略多於"},{"english":"engineered goods","chinese":"工程產品"},{"english":"at roughly","chinese":"約為"},{"english":"both categories increased","chinese":"兩個類別均上升"},{"english":"the former","chinese":"前者"},{"english":"rose modestly by","chinese":"溫和上升……"},{"english":"to around","chinese":"至約……"},{"english":"while the latter","chinese":"而後者"},{"english":"climbed more sharply","chinese":"更大幅上升"},{"english":"followed a different path","chinese":"走勢不同"},{"english":"falling from X to Y","chinese":"由 X 下跌至 Y"},{"english":"a decrease of","chinese":"……的跌幅"},{"english":"lower-earning categories","chinese":"收益較低的類別"},{"english":"agricultural products","chinese":"農產品"},{"english":"changed very little","chinese":"變化很小"},{"english":"remaining at around","chinese":"維持在約……"},{"english":"a marginal rise","chinese":"輕微升幅"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"grew markedly","chinese":"顯著增長"},{"english":"representing a 15.24% increase","chinese":"代表15.24%的升幅"},{"english":"making it nearly equal to","chinese":"使其幾乎等同於……"},{"english":"nearly equal to","chinese":"幾乎等同於"},{"english":"by 2016","chinese":"到2016年時"},{"english":"the highest-earning export","chinese":"最高收益出口產品"},{"english":"the fastest-growing category","chinese":"增長最快的類別"},{"english":"the only declining category","chinese":"唯一下跌的類別"},{"english":"narrow the gap","chinese":"收窄差距"},{"english":"a more modest increase","chinese":"較溫和的升幅"},{"english":"a sharper increase","chinese":"較大幅的升幅"},{"english":"remained broadly stable","chinese":"大致保持穩定"},{"english":"experienced a decline","chinese":"經歷下跌"},{"english":"showed little movement","chinese":"變動不大"},{"english":"almost caught up with","chinese":"幾乎追上"},{"english":"compared with","chinese":"與……相比"},{"english":"over the two-year period","chinese":"在兩年間"},{"english":"the overall trend","chinese":"整體趨勢"},{"english":"the strongest percentage growth","chinese":"最強百分比增長"},{"english":"the weakest performance","chinese":"最弱表現"}]},"model-essay-4-ielts-task1-pie-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-4-ielts-task1-pie-charts","essayKey":"pie-charts:4","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-4-ielts-task1-pie-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/pie-charts/pie-chart-4","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The two pie charts compare energy consumption in an average Australian household with the proportions of greenhouse gas emissions produced by each use.","chinese":"這兩個圓餅圖比較澳洲一般家庭的能源消耗，以及每種能源用途所產生的溫室氣體排放比例。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, heating and water heating account for most household energy use, whereas emissions are more evenly distributed. Although heating is by far the largest consumer of energy, it produces a much smaller share of emissions; by contrast, other appliances, refrigeration and lighting generate proportionally more greenhouse gas than the energy they use.","chinese":"整體而言，供暖和熱水加熱佔家庭能源使用的大部分；相反，溫室氣體排放的分布則更加平均。 雖然供暖是迄今最大的能源消耗項目，但它產生的排放比例卻小得多；相反，其他電器、冷藏和照明所產生的溫室氣體比例高於它們所使用的能源比例。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In the first chart, heating makes up 42% of total energy consumption, making it the dominant category. Water heating is second at 30%, so these two uses together represent almost three quarters of household energy demand. The remaining categories are much smaller: other appliances account for 15%, refrigeration for 7%, lighting for 4%, and cooling for just 2%.","chinese":"在第一個圖中，供暖佔總能源消耗的 42% ，使其成為主導類別。 熱水加熱位居第二，佔 30% ，因此這兩種用途合計幾乎佔家庭能源需求的四分之三。 其餘類別則小得多：其他電器佔 15% ，冷藏佔 7% ，照明佔 4% ，而冷氣只佔 2%。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"In the emissions chart, water heating is the leading source, at 32%, while other appliances almost double their energy share, producing 28% of emissions. Heating, however, is responsible for only 15%. Refrigeration and lighting also have higher emission figures, at 14% and 8% respectively, while cooling remains the smallest contributor, at 3%.","chinese":"在排放圖中，熱水加熱是最大的來源，佔 32% ；同時，其他電器的排放比例幾乎是其能源使用比例的兩倍，產生 28% 的排放。 然而，供暖只佔 15% 的排放。 冷藏和照明的排放數字也較高，分別為 14% 和 8% ；而冷氣仍然是最小的排放來源，佔 3% 。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"two pie charts","chinese":"兩個圓形圖"},{"english":"energy consumption","chinese":"能源消耗"},{"english":"an average Australian household","chinese":"一個澳洲普通家庭"},{"english":"proportions of greenhouse gas emissions","chinese":"溫室氣體排放比例"},{"english":"greenhouse gas emissions","chinese":"溫室氣體排放"},{"english":"produced by each use","chinese":"由每種用途產生"},{"english":"account for most","chinese":"佔大部分"},{"english":"household energy use","chinese":"家庭能源使用量"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相比之下"},{"english":"more evenly distributed","chinese":"分佈較平均"},{"english":"by far the largest consumer of energy","chinese":"明顯是最大的能源消耗項目"},{"english":"consumer of energy","chinese":"能源消耗項目"},{"english":"a much smaller share of emissions","chinese":"小得多的排放比例"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"other appliances","chinese":"其他電器"},{"english":"refrigeration","chinese":"冷藏設備；雪櫃冷藏"},{"english":"lighting","chinese":"照明"},{"english":"generate proportionally more","chinese":"按比例產生更多"},{"english":"greenhouse gas","chinese":"溫室氣體"},{"english":"the energy they use","chinese":"它們所使用的能源"},{"english":"makes up 42% of","chinese":"佔……的42%"},{"english":"total energy consumption","chinese":"總能源消耗量"},{"english":"making it the dominant category","chinese":"使其成為主要類別"},{"english":"dominant category","chinese":"主要類別"},{"english":"water heating","chinese":"熱水加熱"},{"english":"is second at","chinese":"以……位居第二"},{"english":"these two uses together","chinese":"這兩種用途合共"},{"english":"represent almost three quarters of","chinese":"佔接近四分之三"},{"english":"household energy demand","chinese":"家庭能源需求"},{"english":"the remaining categories","chinese":"其餘類別"},{"english":"much smaller","chinese":"小得多"},{"english":"account for 15%","chinese":"佔15%"},{"english":"for just 2%","chinese":"僅佔2%"},{"english":"cooling","chinese":"製冷；冷氣"},{"english":"emissions chart","chinese":"排放圖"},{"english":"the leading source","chinese":"主要來源"},{"english":"while","chinese":"而；同時"},{"english":"almost double their energy share","chinese":"幾乎是其能源使用比例的兩倍"},{"english":"energy share","chinese":"能源使用比例"},{"english":"producing 28% of emissions","chinese":"產生28%的排放"},{"english":"is responsible for only","chinese":"只佔……的責任；只產生"},{"english":"only 15%","chinese":"僅15%"},{"english":"higher emission figures","chinese":"較高的排放數字"},{"english":"emission figures","chinese":"排放數字"},{"english":"at 14% and 8% respectively","chinese":"分別為14%及8%"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"remains the smallest contributor","chinese":"仍然是最小的來源"},{"english":"smallest contributor","chinese":"最小的來源"},{"english":"contributor","chinese":"來源；促成因素"}]},"model-essay-4-ielts-task1-process-diagram":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-4-ielts-task1-process-diagram","essayKey":"process-diagram:4","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-4-ielts-task1-process-diagram","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/process-diagrams/process-diagram-4","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The diagram illustrates the process by which plastic bottles are recycled and converted into new goods.","chinese":"該圖說明塑膠瓶如何被回收，並轉化為新的商品。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the procedure contains nine main stages, beginning with the disposal of used bottles and ending with the manufacture of various end products. It is largely linear, although the production of new bottles means that some items can re-enter the same recycling loop.","chinese":"整體而言，這個流程包含九個主要階段，從丟棄使用過的塑膠瓶開始，到製造各種最終產品結束。 它大致上是一個線性流程；不過，由於最終產品中包括新的塑膠瓶，一些物品可以重新進入同一個回收循環。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"At the initial stage, consumers place discarded plastic bottles in dedicated recycling bins. These containers are then emptied by a collection truck, which transports the waste to a recycling centre. Once there, the bottles are sorted on a conveyor belt, with suitable items separated from rejected materials. The accepted bottles are subsequently compressed into dense blocks, making them easier to handle before further processing.","chinese":"在最初階段，消費者把丟棄的塑膠瓶放入專門的回收箱中。 這些回收箱隨後由收集卡車清空，而卡車會把廢棄物運送到回收中心。 到達回收中心後，塑膠瓶會在輸送帶上被分類，合適的物品會與被拒收的材料分開。 合格的塑膠瓶隨後被壓縮成密集的方塊，以便在進一步加工前更容易處理。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"In the next phase, the compacted blocks are crushed into small fragments, which are washed to remove impurities. The cleaned pieces are fed into a machine and turned into plastic pellets. After this, the pellets are heated and transformed into raw material, which is stored in large bundles. Finally, this material is used to manufacture a range of products, including new bottles, food containers, T-shirts, shopping bags and pencils.","chinese":"在下一階段，被壓縮的方塊會被粉碎成小碎片，然後被清洗以去除雜質。 清洗後的碎片會被送入機器，並轉化成塑膠顆粒。 之後，這些塑膠粒會被加熱並轉化為原材料，而原材料會被存放成大型捆包。 最後，這些材料會被用來製造一系列產品，包括新的塑膠瓶、食物容器、 T 恤、購物袋和鉛筆。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"diagram illustrates","chinese":"圖示說明"},{"english":"the process by which","chinese":"……的過程"},{"english":"plastic bottles are recycled","chinese":"膠樽被回收"},{"english":"converted into new goods","chinese":"被轉化成新產品"},{"english":"new goods","chinese":"新產品"},{"english":"the procedure contains","chinese":"這個程序包含"},{"english":"nine main stages","chinese":"九個主要階段"},{"english":"beginning with","chinese":"以……開始"},{"english":"disposal of used bottles","chinese":"棄置用過的膠樽"},{"english":"ending with","chinese":"以……結束"},{"english":"manufacture of various end products","chinese":"製造各種最終產品"},{"english":"end products","chinese":"最終產品"},{"english":"largely linear","chinese":"大致是線性的"},{"english":"the production of new bottles","chinese":"生產新膠樽"},{"english":"re-enter the same recycling loop","chinese":"重新進入同一個回收循環"},{"english":"recycling loop","chinese":"回收循環"},{"english":"at the initial stage","chinese":"在最初階段"},{"english":"discarded plastic bottles","chinese":"被棄置的膠樽"},{"english":"dedicated recycling bins","chinese":"指定回收箱"},{"english":"these containers are then emptied","chinese":"這些容器隨後被清空"},{"english":"emptied by a collection truck","chinese":"由收集車清空"},{"english":"collection truck","chinese":"收集車"},{"english":"transports the waste to","chinese":"將廢物運送到……"},{"english":"recycling centre","chinese":"回收中心"},{"english":"once there","chinese":"到達那裏後"},{"english":"sorted on a conveyor belt","chinese":"在輸送帶上分類"},{"english":"conveyor belt","chinese":"輸送帶"},{"english":"suitable items","chinese":"合適物品"},{"english":"separated from rejected materials","chinese":"與被拒收的物料分開"},{"english":"rejected materials","chinese":"被拒收的物料"},{"english":"accepted bottles","chinese":"合格膠樽"},{"english":"are subsequently compressed into","chinese":"隨後被壓縮成"},{"english":"subsequently","chinese":"隨後"},{"english":"dense blocks","chinese":"緊密塊狀物"},{"english":"easier to handle","chinese":"較容易處理"},{"english":"before further processing","chinese":"在進一步加工之前"},{"english":"further processing","chinese":"進一步加工"},{"english":"in the next phase","chinese":"在下一階段"},{"english":"compacted blocks","chinese":"壓實塊"},{"english":"crushed into small fragments","chinese":"被壓碎成小碎片"},{"english":"small fragments","chinese":"小碎片"},{"english":"washed to remove impurities","chinese":"被清洗以去除雜質"},{"english":"remove impurities","chinese":"去除雜質"},{"english":"cleaned pieces","chinese":"清潔後的碎片"},{"english":"fed into a machine","chinese":"被送入機器"},{"english":"turned into plastic pellets","chinese":"被製成塑膠粒"},{"english":"plastic pellets","chinese":"塑膠粒"},{"english":"after this","chinese":"之後"},{"english":"heated and transformed into","chinese":"被加熱並轉化成"},{"english":"raw material","chinese":"原材料"},{"english":"stored in large bundles","chinese":"以大捆形式儲存"},{"english":"large bundles","chinese":"大捆"},{"english":"used to manufacture","chinese":"用於製造"},{"english":"a range of products","chinese":"一系列產品"},{"english":"including new bottles","chinese":"包括新膠樽"},{"english":"food containers","chinese":"食物容器"},{"english":"shopping bags","chinese":"購物袋"},{"english":"recycling process","chinese":"回收過程"},{"english":"manufacturing stage","chinese":"製造階段"},{"english":"linear process","chinese":"線性流程"}]},"model-essay-4-ielts-task1-tables":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-4-ielts-task1-tables","essayKey":"tables:4","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-4-ielts-task1-tables","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/tables/table-4","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The table presents data on the number of nights spent in Germany by domestic and international tourists between 2016 and 2022, measured in millions.","chinese":"這個表格呈現了 2016 年至 2022 年間，本地及國際遊客在德國逗留晚數的數據，單位為百萬晚。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, domestic tourism accounted for far more overnight stays than international tourism throughout the period. Both categories rose steadily until 2019, before falling sharply in 2020; although they recovered strongly by 2022, neither returned fully to its pre-decline peak.","chinese":"整體而言，在整個時期內，本地旅遊所佔的過夜住宿晚數遠遠高於國際旅遊。 兩個類別都穩步上升至 2019 年，之後在 2020 年急劇下跌；雖然到 2022 年兩者均明顯回升，但都未完全恢復至下跌前的高峰。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"From 2016 to 2019, domestic-tourist nights increased consistently, rising from 366.4 million to 405.7 million. The international figure followed a similar but much smaller upward trend, climbing from 80.8 million to 89.9 million over the same years. As a result, domestic stays were roughly four and a half times as high as overseas stays during this initial period.","chinese":"從 2016 年至 2019 年，本地遊客住宿晚數持續上升，從 3.664 億晚增至 4.057 億晚。 國際遊客的數字也呈現相似但規模小得多的上升趨勢，同期從 8,080 萬晚增至 8,990 萬晚。 因此，在這一初期階段，本地住宿晚數大約是海外遊客住宿晚數的四倍半。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The pattern changed markedly after 2019. Domestic nights dropped to 270.3 million in 2020, a fall of more than 130 million, before edging up to 279.23 million in 2021. International nights fell even more steeply in proportional terms, plunging from 89.9 million in 2019 to 32 million in 2020 and then slipping to 31.01 million in 2021. By 2022, domestic and international figures had rebounded to 382.62 million and 68.09 million respectively, but both remained below their 2019 levels.","chinese":"2019 年之後，這一模式出現了明顯變化。 本地遊客住宿晚數在 2020 年跌至 2.703 億晚，下降超過 1.3 億晚，之後在 2021 年小幅回升至 2.7923 億晚。 按比例來看，國際遊客住宿晚數跌幅更為陡峭，從 2019 年的 8,990 萬晚急跌至2020 年的 3,200 萬晚，之後在 2021 年再微跌至 3,101 萬晚。 到 2022 年，本地及國際遊客住宿晚數分別反彈至 3.8262 億晚和 6,809 萬晚，但兩者仍低於 2019 年的水平。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the table below shows","chinese":"下列表格顯示"},{"english":"the number of nights spent","chinese":"留宿晚數"},{"english":"domestic and international tourists","chinese":"本地及國際旅客"},{"english":"in Germany","chinese":"在德國"},{"english":"from 2016 to 2022","chinese":"由2016年至2022年"},{"english":"measured in millions","chinese":"以百萬計算"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"selecting and reporting","chinese":"選取並報告"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"presents data on","chinese":"呈現關於……的數據"},{"english":"nights spent in Germany","chinese":"在德國留宿的晚數"},{"english":"by domestic and international tourists","chinese":"由本地及國際旅客"},{"english":"between 2016 and 2022","chinese":"在2016年至2022年間"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"domestic tourism","chinese":"本地旅遊"},{"english":"international tourism","chinese":"國際旅遊"},{"english":"accounted for far more","chinese":"佔遠多於"},{"english":"overnight stays","chinese":"過夜住宿晚數"},{"english":"throughout the period","chinese":"在整個時期內"},{"english":"both categories","chinese":"兩個類別"},{"english":"rose steadily until","chinese":"穩步上升至"},{"english":"before falling sharply","chinese":"之後急跌"},{"english":"falling sharply","chinese":"急劇下跌"},{"english":"although","chinese":"雖然"},{"english":"recovered strongly","chinese":"強勁回升"},{"english":"by 2022","chinese":"到2022年"},{"english":"neither returned fully to","chinese":"兩者均未完全回到"},{"english":"its pre-decline peak","chinese":"下跌前高峰"},{"english":"From 2016 to 2019","chinese":"由2016年至2019年"},{"english":"domestic-tourist nights","chinese":"本地旅客留宿晚數"},{"english":"increased consistently","chinese":"持續上升"},{"english":"rising from … to …","chinese":"由……上升至……"},{"english":"from 366.4 million to 405.7 million","chinese":"由3.664億升至4.057億"},{"english":"the international figure","chinese":"國際旅客的數字"},{"english":"followed a similar but much smaller upward trend","chinese":"呈現相似但規模小得多的上升趨勢"},{"english":"a similar upward trend","chinese":"相似的上升趨勢"},{"english":"much smaller","chinese":"小得多"},{"english":"climbing from … to …","chinese":"由……攀升至……"},{"english":"from 80.8 million to 89.9 million","chinese":"由8,080萬升至8,990萬"},{"english":"over the same years","chinese":"在同一幾年間"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"domestic stays","chinese":"本地旅客住宿晚數"},{"english":"overseas stays","chinese":"海外旅客住宿晚數"},{"english":"roughly four and a half times as high as","chinese":"大約是……的四倍半"},{"english":"during this initial period","chinese":"在最初這段時期"},{"english":"the pattern changed markedly","chinese":"模式明顯改變"},{"english":"after 2019","chinese":"2019年之後"},{"english":"domestic nights","chinese":"本地旅客留宿晚數"},{"english":"dropped to","chinese":"下降至"},{"english":"270.3 million","chinese":"2.703億"},{"english":"a fall of more than","chinese":"超過……的跌幅"},{"english":"more than 130 million","chinese":"超過1.3億"},{"english":"before edging up to","chinese":"之後輕微回升至"},{"english":"edging up to","chinese":"輕微上升至"},{"english":"279.23 million","chinese":"2.7923億"},{"english":"international nights","chinese":"國際旅客留宿晚數"},{"english":"fell even more steeply","chinese":"下跌得更加急劇"},{"english":"in proportional terms","chinese":"按比例計算"},{"english":"plunging from … to …","chinese":"由……暴跌至……"},{"english":"plunged from 89.9 million to 32 million","chinese":"由8,990萬暴跌至3,200萬"},{"english":"then slipping to","chinese":"其後再下滑至"},{"english":"slipped to 31.01 million","chinese":"下滑至3,101萬"},{"english":"had rebounded to","chinese":"已反彈至"},{"english":"domestic and international figures","chinese":"本地及國際旅客數字"},{"english":"382.62 million and 68.09 million respectively","chinese":"分別為3.8262億及6,809萬"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"remained below","chinese":"仍低於"},{"english":"their 2019 levels","chinese":"它們2019年的水平"}]},"model-essay-5-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-5-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:5","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-5-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q5","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In both working life and private life, a growing proportion of communication is now conducted through digital technology instead of face-to-face interaction. Although this development can weaken the quality of human relationships and increase the risk of misunderstanding, I believe its advantages are greater overall because it makes communication far more efficient and keeps people connected despite geographical separation.","chinese":"無論在工作還是私人生活中，越來越多的溝通如今都是透過數位科技進行，而不是面對面交流。 儘管這種發展可能削弱人際關係的品質，並增加誤解的風險， 我認為整體而言，它的優點更大，因為它使溝通更有效率，並能讓人們即使相隔遙遠也保持聯繫。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main benefit of technology-based communication is speed and convenience. In professional settings, email, messaging platforms and video conferencing remove the need for travel and allow decisions to be made almost immediately. This shortens response times, reduces operating costs and enables companies to coordinate teams across different cities or even continents with remarkable ease. For instance, a manager can resolve a production issue with overseas colleagues in a single online meeting rather than waiting days for an in-person discussion. The same principle applies socially: parents, children and friends who live far apart can speak daily through calls and messages, thereby maintaining close relationships that might otherwise weaken over time.","chinese":"科技化溝通最主要的優點是速度和便利性。 在專業環境中，電子郵件、即時通訊平台和視像會議免除了人們出行的需要，並使決策幾乎可以即時作出。 這不但縮短了回應時間、降低了營運成本，還使公司能夠非常輕鬆地協調分布在不同城市甚至不同大洲的團隊。 例如，一位經理可以透過一次線上會議便與海外同事解決生產問題，而不是等待數天才進行一次面對面的討論。 同樣的情況也適用於社交層面：住得很遠的父母、子女和朋友仍然可以透過通話和訊息每天聯絡。 結果是，人際關係更容易維持，也較不會隨時間而逐漸淡化。 例如，一個家庭即使成員分散在不同國家，仍然可以透過視像通話分享日常近況並提供情感支持。 因此，數位溝通大大提升了工作和個人生活中的效率與可及性。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Nevertheless, digital communication has important drawbacks, the most serious of which is its lack of emotional richness. Face-to-face conversation conveys tone, facial expression and body language, which help people interpret meaning accurately, show empathy and build trust. When these cues disappear, messages are more easily misread; a brief email or text, for example, may sound cold or hostile even when no offence was intended. This is especially problematic in workplaces, where trust and nuance are essential for leadership, negotiation and teamwork. Over time, heavy reliance on screens may also encourage shallow social habits. People can remain constantly in contact online yet still feel isolated, because frequent messaging is not the same as receiving genuine attention and human presence.","chinese":"然而，數位溝通也有重要的缺點，其中最嚴重的是它缺乏情感上的豐富性。 面對面的交談能傳達語氣、面部表情和肢體語言，這些都有助於人們準確理解意思、表達同理心並建立信任。 當這些線索消失時，訊息便更容易被誤解，從而導致困惑甚至衝突。 例如，一封簡短的電郵或文字訊息即使本無惡意，也可能顯得冷淡甚至帶有敵意。 這在職場中尤其成問題，因為信任和細膩的理解對領導、協商和團隊合作都至關重要。 長遠而言，過度依賴螢幕也可能助長膚淺的社交習慣，因此人們即使在線上一直保持聯絡，仍可能感到孤立。 例如，一個人即使經常透過社交媒體聊天，仍可能感到孤單，因為數位接觸始終無法完全取代真正的關注和人的陪伴。 因此，儘管科技讓溝通成為可能，它同時也可能削弱清晰度、信任感和情感深度。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, communicating through technology offers clear advantages in terms of efficiency and accessibility, even though it may reduce the depth and clarity of human interaction. Overall, I believe the benefits outweigh the disadvantages because digital tools allow both professional and personal communication to function effectively across time and distance.","chinese":"總結來說，透過科技進行溝通在效率和可及性方面具有明顯優勢，儘管它可能削弱人際互動的深度與清晰度。 整體而言，我認為其優點大於缺點，因為數位工具使工作和個人生活中的溝通都能跨越時間與距離而有效運作。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"working life and private life","chinese":"工作生活和私人生活"},{"english":"a growing proportion of","chinese":"越來越大比例的……"},{"english":"be conducted through","chinese":"透過……進行"},{"english":"digital technology","chinese":"數碼科技"},{"english":"instead of face-to-face interaction","chinese":"而不是面對面互動"},{"english":"face-to-face interaction","chinese":"面對面互動"},{"english":"weaken the quality of","chinese":"削弱……的質素"},{"english":"human relationships","chinese":"人際關係"},{"english":"increase the risk of misunderstanding","chinese":"增加誤解風險"},{"english":"greater overall","chinese":"整體上較大"},{"english":"far more efficient","chinese":"效率高得多"},{"english":"keep people connected","chinese":"讓人保持聯繫"},{"english":"despite geographical separation","chinese":"儘管地理上分隔"},{"english":"technology-based communication","chinese":"以科技為基礎的溝通"},{"english":"speed and convenience","chinese":"速度和便利"},{"english":"professional settings","chinese":"專業工作環境"},{"english":"messaging platforms","chinese":"訊息平台"},{"english":"video conferencing","chinese":"視像會議"},{"english":"remove the need for travel","chinese":"免卻出行需要"},{"english":"allow decisions to be made","chinese":"讓決定得以作出"},{"english":"almost immediately","chinese":"幾乎即時"},{"english":"shorten response times","chinese":"縮短回應時間"},{"english":"reduce operating costs","chinese":"降低營運成本"},{"english":"coordinate teams across","chinese":"協調分佈於……的團隊"},{"english":"different cities or even continents","chinese":"不同城市甚至不同洲份"},{"english":"with remarkable ease","chinese":"非常輕易地"},{"english":"resolve a production issue","chinese":"解決生產問題"},{"english":"overseas colleagues","chinese":"海外同事"},{"english":"in a single online meeting","chinese":"在一次網上會議中"},{"english":"rather than waiting days for","chinese":"而不是等數天才……"},{"english":"an in-person discussion","chinese":"面對面討論"},{"english":"the same principle applies socially","chinese":"同一道理也適用於社交方面"},{"english":"live far apart","chinese":"相隔很遠居住"},{"english":"speak daily through calls and messages","chinese":"透過電話和訊息每日交談"},{"english":"maintaining close relationships","chinese":"維持親密關係"},{"english":"might otherwise weaken over time","chinese":"否則可能隨時間逐漸減弱"},{"english":"digital communication has important drawbacks","chinese":"數碼溝通有重要缺點"},{"english":"the most serious of which","chinese":"其中最嚴重的是"},{"english":"lack of emotional richness","chinese":"缺乏情感層次"},{"english":"conveys tone","chinese":"傳達語氣"},{"english":"facial expression and body language","chinese":"面部表情和身體語言"},{"english":"interpret meaning accurately","chinese":"準確理解意思"},{"english":"show empathy","chinese":"表達同理心"},{"english":"build trust","chinese":"建立信任"},{"english":"these cues disappear","chinese":"這些提示消失"},{"english":"more easily misread","chinese":"更容易被誤解"},{"english":"a brief email or text","chinese":"簡短的電郵或短訊"},{"english":"sound cold or hostile","chinese":"聽起來冷淡或帶敵意"},{"english":"no offence was intended","chinese":"本無冒犯之意"},{"english":"especially problematic in workplaces","chinese":"在工作場尤其成問題"},{"english":"trust and nuance","chinese":"信任和細微語意"},{"english":"essential for leadership","chinese":"對領導力不可或缺"},{"english":"negotiation and teamwork","chinese":"談判和團隊合作"},{"english":"heavy reliance on screens","chinese":"對屏幕的高度依賴"},{"english":"encourage shallow social habits","chinese":"助長膚淺的社交習慣"},{"english":"remain constantly in contact online","chinese":"在網上持續保持聯絡"},{"english":"yet still feel isolated","chinese":"但仍然感到孤立"},{"english":"frequent messaging","chinese":"頻繁傳訊息"},{"english":"genuine attention","chinese":"真誠的關注"},{"english":"human presence","chinese":"人與人真實相處的存在感"},{"english":"in terms of efficiency and accessibility","chinese":"在效率和可取得性方面"},{"english":"reduce the depth and clarity of","chinese":"降低……的深度和清晰度"},{"english":"outweigh the disadvantages","chinese":"利多於弊"},{"english":"function effectively across time and distance","chinese":"跨越時間和距離有效運作"},{"english":"across time and distance","chinese":"跨越時間和距離"}]},"model-essay-5-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-5-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:5","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-5-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q5","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In consumer markets, price is more than a number on a label; it often functions as a signal. I would argue that price strongly influences potential buyers, especially when it suggests status or quality, but the final decision is also shaped by practical factors such as need, trust and personal experience.","chinese":"在消費市場中，價格不僅僅是標籤上的一個數字；它往往也具有信號作用。 我會主張，價格會強烈影響潛在買家，尤其當它暗示地位或品質時；但最終決定也會受到實際因素影響，例如需要、信任和個人經驗。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"A high price can attract consumers because many people associate cost with quality. When buyers do not have specialist knowledge, they may use price as a shortcut: an expensive phone, watch or handbag is assumed to be better designed, more durable or more prestigious. This is particularly true in luxury markets, where the price itself becomes part of the appeal. A cheap diamond necklace, for instance, may make buyers suspicious rather than excited, because its low price weakens the image of rarity. In this sense, price can create desire by giving a product an aura of value. It tells buyers not only what the item costs, but also what owning it might say about them.","chinese":"高價格可以吸引消費者，因為很多人會把成本與品質聯繫起來。 當買家沒有專業知識時，他們可能會把價格當作一種捷徑：一部昂貴的手機、一隻手錶或一個手袋，往往會被認為設計更好、更耐用或更有聲望。 這在奢侈品市場中尤其真實，因為價格本身已成為吸引力的一部分。 例如，一條便宜的鑽石項鏈可能會令買家感到懷疑，而不是興奮，因為它的低價削弱了稀有性的形象。 從這個意義上說，價格可以透過賦予產品一種價值光環來創造購買慾望。它告訴買家的不只是這件物品的成本，也包括擁有它可能代表著他們是怎樣的人。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, price alone rarely carries a purchase decision from beginning to end. Buyers are also influenced by the usefulness of the product, the reputation of the brand, reviews from other customers and the emotional experience attached to ownership. A parent choosing a child’s laptop, for example, may care less about whether it looks fashionable and more about battery life, reliability and after-sales support. Similarly, a product with strong advertising may initially catch the eye, but poor reviews can quickly pour cold water on that interest. Convenience also matters: people often choose items that are easy to obtain, simple to use and compatible with their daily routines.","chinese":"然而，單靠價格很少能從頭到尾支撐一個購買決定。 買家也會受到產品實用性、品牌聲譽、其他顧客評價，以及擁有該產品所帶來的情感體驗所影響。 例如，一位家長為孩子選擇手提電腦時，可能不太在意它看起來是否時尚，而更重視電池壽命、可靠性和售後支援。 同樣地，一件擁有強力廣告宣傳的產品一開始可能會吸引目光，但差劣的評價很快就會為這份興趣潑冷水。 便利性同樣重要：人們往往會選擇容易取得、使用簡單，並且能配合他們日常生活習慣的物品。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, price has a powerful influence because it can suggest quality, prestige and social meaning. Nevertheless, people ultimately buy products when price works together with trust, usefulness, reputation and convenience. A high price may open the door, but other factors usually decide whether buyers walk through it.","chinese":"總結來說，價格具有強大的影響力，因為它可以暗示品質、聲望和社會意義。 然而，人們最終會在價格與信任、實用性、聲譽和便利性共同發揮作用時購買產品。 高價格也許能打開那扇門，但其他因素通常才決定買家是否真的會走進去。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"consumer markets","chinese":"消費市場"},{"english":"more than a number on a label","chinese":"不只是標籤上的數字"},{"english":"functions as a signal","chinese":"發揮信號作用"},{"english":"strongly influences potential buyers","chinese":"強烈影響潛在買家"},{"english":"potential buyers","chinese":"潛在買家"},{"english":"suggests status or quality","chinese":"暗示地位或質素"},{"english":"the final decision","chinese":"最終決定"},{"english":"be shaped by","chinese":"受到……塑造；受……影響"},{"english":"practical factors","chinese":"實際因素"},{"english":"personal experience","chinese":"個人經驗"},{"english":"associate cost with quality","chinese":"將價格與質素聯繫起來"},{"english":"specialist knowledge","chinese":"專門知識"},{"english":"use price as a shortcut","chinese":"將價格當作捷徑"},{"english":"be assumed to be","chinese":"被假定為"},{"english":"better designed","chinese":"設計得更好"},{"english":"more durable","chinese":"更耐用"},{"english":"more prestigious","chinese":"更有地位；更高檔"},{"english":"luxury markets","chinese":"奢侈品市場"},{"english":"part of the appeal","chinese":"吸引力的一部分"},{"english":"make buyers suspicious","chinese":"令買家起疑"},{"english":"rather than excited","chinese":"而不是興奮"},{"english":"weakens the image of","chinese":"削弱……的形象"},{"english":"the image of rarity","chinese":"稀有性的形象"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"create desire","chinese":"製造渴望"},{"english":"an aura of value","chinese":"價值感；價值光環"},{"english":"what owning it might say about them","chinese":"擁有它可能反映出的身份"},{"english":"price alone","chinese":"單靠價格"},{"english":"carries a purchase decision","chinese":"支撐一個購買決定"},{"english":"from beginning to end","chinese":"由始至終"},{"english":"be influenced by","chinese":"受到……影響"},{"english":"the usefulness of the product","chinese":"產品的實用性"},{"english":"the reputation of the brand","chinese":"品牌聲譽"},{"english":"reviews from other customers","chinese":"其他顧客的評價"},{"english":"emotional experience","chinese":"情感體驗"},{"english":"attached to ownership","chinese":"與擁有某物相關的"},{"english":"care less about whether","chinese":"較不在意是否……"},{"english":"looks fashionable","chinese":"看起來時尚"},{"english":"battery life","chinese":"電池續航力"},{"english":"reliability","chinese":"可靠性"},{"english":"after-sales support","chinese":"售後支援"},{"english":"strong advertising","chinese":"強力廣告宣傳"},{"english":"initially catch the eye","chinese":"起初吸引注意"},{"english":"poor reviews","chinese":"差評"},{"english":"pour cold water on","chinese":"對……潑冷水；打擊……"},{"english":"that interest","chinese":"那份興趣"},{"english":"convenience also matters","chinese":"便利性也很重要"},{"english":"easy to obtain","chinese":"容易取得"},{"english":"simple to use","chinese":"使用簡單"},{"english":"compatible with","chinese":"與……配合"},{"english":"daily routines","chinese":"日常生活習慣"},{"english":"a powerful influence","chinese":"強大的影響力"},{"english":"social meaning","chinese":"社會意義"},{"english":"ultimately buy products","chinese":"最終購買產品"},{"english":"works together with","chinese":"與……共同發揮作用"},{"english":"open the door","chinese":"打開機會之門"},{"english":"walk through it","chinese":"真的走進去；採取下一步"}]},"model-essay-5-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-5-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:5","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-5-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q5","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Recruitment is one of the most important decisions a company makes because employees shape not only its output but also its culture. Some argue that firms should hire people who are imaginative and capable of working without close supervision, whereas others believe that cooperative candidates who can follow directions are more valuable. Although independent thinkers can help a business grow, I believe companies should mainly prioritise people who can work well in teams and respect instructions.","chinese":"招聘是公司所作出的最重要決定之一，因為員工不但塑造公司的產出，也塑造公司文化 有些人認為公司應該聘請富有想像力、並且能夠在沒有密切監督下工作的人；然而，另一些人則認為能夠合作並遵從指示的求職者更有價值。 儘管獨立思考者能幫助企業成長，我認為公司應主要優先考慮那些能夠良好團隊合作並尊重指示的人。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"There are clear reasons why innovative and self-reliant employees are attractive to employers. In competitive markets, companies cannot survive by repeating the same methods year after year. Workers who question old practices, suggest fresh solutions and take ownership of tasks can help an organisation move faster than its rivals. For example, a software developer who notices an inefficient internal system may design a better tool without waiting for a manager to point out the problem. In this sense, independent employees can act as engines of progress, especially in industries where creativity and rapid problem-solving are essential.","chinese":"創新而自立的員工對僱主具有吸引力，這背後有明顯原因。 在競爭激烈的市場中，公司不能年復一年只靠重複相同的方法生存。 那些會質疑舊做法、提出新解決方法並主動承擔工作的員工，能夠幫助一個機構比競爭對手行動得更快。 例如，一位注意到內部系統效率低下的軟件開發人員，可能會在不等待經理指出問題的情況下，設計出一個更好的工具。 從這個意義上說，獨立的員工可以成為推動進步的引擎，尤其是在創意和快速解決問題至關重要的行業中。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, the stronger argument is that most companies depend more heavily on teamwork and disciplined execution. A business is rarely a collection of isolated individuals; it is a network of departments, deadlines and shared responsibilities. If employees are unable to communicate, accept feedback or follow established procedures, even brilliant ideas can become disruptive rather than useful. For instance, in healthcare, construction or finance, ignoring instructions can lead to serious mistakes, legal problems or safety risks. Team-oriented workers, by contrast, help create a stable workplace where tasks are completed consistently and colleagues can trust one another.","chinese":"然而，更有力的論點是，大多數公司更加依賴團隊合作和有紀律的執行。 一間企業很少只是一群孤立個體的集合；它是一個由部門、期限和共同責任組成的網絡 如果員工不能溝通、接受回饋或遵從既定程序，即使是出色的想法也可能變得具有破壞性，而不是有用。 例如，在醫療、建築或金融行業中，忽視指示可能導致嚴重錯誤、法律問題或安全風險 相比之下，以團隊為本的員工能夠幫助建立一個穩定的工作場所，讓任務能夠穩定完成，同事之間也能互相信任。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In my view, therefore, while innovation and independence are valuable qualities, they should not be the main priority in recruitment. A company can train creative thinking over time, but it is much harder to function when employees resist cooperation or basic rules. Overall, businesses should first recruit people who can contribute reliably to a team, because shared discipline is the foundation on which real innovation can later be built.","chinese":"因此，在我看來，雖然創新能力和獨立性是有價值的特質，但它們不應該是招聘中的主要優先考慮。 公司可以隨著時間訓練員工的創意思維，但當員工抗拒合作或基本規則時，公司要正常運作就困難得多。 整體而言，企業應該首先招聘那些能夠可靠地為團隊作出貢獻的人，因為共同的紀律正是真正創新日後得以建立的基礎。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"recruitment","chinese":"招聘"},{"english":"one of the most important decisions","chinese":"最重要的決定之一"},{"english":"shape not only...but also...","chinese":"不但塑造……，也塑造……"},{"english":"output","chinese":"產出"},{"english":"company culture","chinese":"公司文化"},{"english":"hire people who","chinese":"聘請……的人"},{"english":"imaginative","chinese":"有想像力的"},{"english":"capable of working without","chinese":"有能力在沒有……下工作"},{"english":"close supervision","chinese":"緊密監督"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"然而；而"},{"english":"cooperative candidates","chinese":"合作型求職者"},{"english":"follow directions","chinese":"遵從指示"},{"english":"more valuable","chinese":"更有價值"},{"english":"independent thinkers","chinese":"獨立思考者"},{"english":"help a business grow","chinese":"幫助企業成長"},{"english":"mainly prioritise","chinese":"主要優先考慮"},{"english":"work well in teams","chinese":"在團隊中合作良好"},{"english":"respect instructions","chinese":"尊重指示"},{"english":"clear reasons why","chinese":"明確原因解釋為何"},{"english":"innovative","chinese":"有創新能力的"},{"english":"self-reliant employees","chinese":"自力更生的員工"},{"english":"attractive to employers","chinese":"對僱主有吸引力"},{"english":"competitive markets","chinese":"競爭激烈的市場"},{"english":"cannot survive by","chinese":"不能靠……生存"},{"english":"repeating the same methods","chinese":"重複相同方法"},{"english":"year after year","chinese":"年復一年"},{"english":"question old practices","chinese":"質疑舊做法"},{"english":"suggest fresh solutions","chinese":"提出新穎解決方案"},{"english":"take ownership of tasks","chinese":"主動承擔工作責任"},{"english":"move faster than its rivals","chinese":"比競爭對手行動更快"},{"english":"software developer","chinese":"軟件開發人員"},{"english":"inefficient internal system","chinese":"低效的內部系統"},{"english":"design a better tool","chinese":"設計更好的工具"},{"english":"without waiting for","chinese":"不用等待"},{"english":"point out the problem","chinese":"指出問題"},{"english":"In this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"act as engines of progress","chinese":"成為進步的推動力"},{"english":"especially in industries where","chinese":"尤其在……的行業中"},{"english":"rapid problem-solving","chinese":"快速解難"},{"english":"are essential","chinese":"是不可或缺的"},{"english":"the stronger argument","chinese":"更有力的論點"},{"english":"depend more heavily on","chinese":"更大程度上依賴"},{"english":"teamwork","chinese":"團隊合作"},{"english":"disciplined execution","chinese":"有紀律的執行"},{"english":"a collection of isolated individuals","chinese":"一群互不相干的個體"},{"english":"a network of","chinese":"由……組成的網絡"},{"english":"departments","chinese":"部門"},{"english":"deadlines","chinese":"截止期限"},{"english":"shared responsibilities","chinese":"共同責任"},{"english":"unable to communicate","chinese":"無法溝通"},{"english":"accept feedback","chinese":"接受意見"},{"english":"follow established procedures","chinese":"遵循既定程序"},{"english":"brilliant ideas","chinese":"出色想法"},{"english":"disruptive rather than useful","chinese":"造成干擾而不是有用"},{"english":"ignoring instructions","chinese":"忽視指示"},{"english":"lead to serious mistakes","chinese":"導致嚴重錯誤"},{"english":"legal problems","chinese":"法律問題"},{"english":"safety risks","chinese":"安全風險"},{"english":"team-oriented workers","chinese":"以團隊為本的員工"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"a stable workplace","chinese":"穩定的工作環境"},{"english":"completed consistently","chinese":"穩定一致地完成"},{"english":"trust one another","chinese":"互相信任"},{"english":"valuable qualities","chinese":"有價值的特質"},{"english":"the main priority in recruitment","chinese":"招聘中的首要考慮"},{"english":"train creative thinking","chinese":"培養創意思維"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨時間"},{"english":"much harder to function","chinese":"更難運作"},{"english":"resist cooperation","chinese":"抗拒合作"},{"english":"basic rules","chinese":"基本規則"},{"english":"recruit people who","chinese":"招聘……的人"},{"english":"contribute reliably to","chinese":"可靠地為……作出貢獻"},{"english":"shared discipline","chinese":"共同紀律"},{"english":"the foundation on which","chinese":"……得以建立的基礎"},{"english":"real innovation","chinese":"真正創新"}]},"model-essay-5-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-5-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:5","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-5-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q5","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Because market demand does not always reward socially valuable work, some professions remain poorly paid despite making an important contribution to society. For this reason, some people argue that artists, who often earn low salaries, should receive government funding so that they can continue producing their work. I completely agree because artistic labour strengthens cultural life and also supports significant economic activity.","chinese":"由於市場需求並不總是會回報那些具有社會價值的工作，因此有些職業雖然對社會作出重要貢獻，薪酬卻依然偏低。 基於這個原因，有些人主張，藝術家因為收入往往偏低，應該獲得政府資助，讓他們能夠繼續創作。 我完全同意。 因為藝術勞動不但能強化文化生活，也能支持重要的經濟活動。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason public funding is justified is that art creates public benefits which private income alone does not reflect. When artists cannot earn enough to remain in the profession, many are forced to leave for more stable jobs. As a result, fewer plays, exhibitions, concerts and community projects are produced, which reduces the public’s access to culture. Over time, this weakens social cohesion because shared stories, traditions and forms of expression become less visible in everyday life. For example, if a local theatre or music programme must survive only through ticket sales, it may disappear from poorer communities altogether, whereas public support allows children and families to engage with the arts regularly. This exposure also develops imagination, empathy and communication skills, so funding artists benefits society in educational as well as cultural terms.","chinese":"第一個支持公共資助的理由是，藝術能創造公共利益，而這些利益單靠私人收入是無法充分反映的。 當藝術家無法靠這個職業獲得足夠收入時，許多人就會被迫離開，轉而從事更穩定的工作。 結果就是，戲劇、展覽、音樂會和社區計畫都會減少，從而削弱公眾接觸文化的機會。 久而久之，這會削弱社會凝聚力，因為共同的故事、傳統與表達方式在日常生活中會變得愈來愈不明顯。 例如，如果一個地方劇院或音樂計畫只能依靠售票維持生存，那麼它可能會完全從較貧困的社區中消失；相反，有了公共資助，孩子和家庭就能定期接觸藝術。 這種接觸同時也能培養想像力、同理心與溝通能力，因此資助藝術家不但有文化上的好處，也有教育上的價值。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Government support for artists is also economically sensible rather than merely charitable. Stable grants or commissions allow creators to keep producing work, purchasing materials and collaborating with venues, technicians and small businesses, so the initial investment quickly circulates through the wider economy. More importantly, many profitable industries depend on artistic talent at an earlier stage of development. Film, design, advertising, fashion and digital media all rely on writers, musicians and visual artists whose skills are often developed in publicly supported spaces. If these people are pushed out of the profession by persistently low pay, a country eventually loses both creative capacity and future revenue. Cities that invest in artists, by contrast, often attract visitors, revive cultural districts and create employment beyond the arts themselves.","chinese":"政府支持藝術家在經濟上也是合理的，而不只是出於慈善考慮。 穩定的補助或委託能讓創作者持續創作、購買材料，並與場地、技術人員和小型企業合作，因此最初的投資很快便會在更廣泛的經濟體系中流動。 更重要的是，許多有利潤的產業在發展初期都依賴藝術人才。 電影、設計、廣告、時尚以及數位媒體都依賴作家、音樂家和視覺藝術家，而這些人的能力往往是在受到公共資助的空間中培養出來的。 如果這些人因長期低薪而被迫退出這個行業，一個國家最終失去的將不只是創造力，也包括未來的收入來源。 相反，那些投資藝術家的城市，往往能吸引遊客、帶動文化區復興，並創造出藝術本身以外的就業機會。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely agree that artists should receive government funding. Their work preserves public access to culture, develops valuable human qualities and sustains wider economic growth, so supporting them is a necessary and well-judged public policy.","chinese":"總而言之，我完全同意藝術家應該獲得政府資助。 他們的工作能維持公眾接觸文化的機會，培養有價值的人文素質，並支撐更廣泛的經濟成長， 因此，支持藝術家是一項必要而且明智的公共政策。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"market demand","chinese":"市場需求"},{"english":"reward socially valuable work","chinese":"回報具社會價值的工作"},{"english":"socially valuable work","chinese":"具社會價值的工作"},{"english":"remain poorly paid","chinese":"仍然薪酬偏低"},{"english":"despite making an important contribution to","chinese":"儘管對……作出重要貢獻"},{"english":"an important contribution to society","chinese":"對社會的重要貢獻"},{"english":"for this reason","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"earn low salaries","chinese":"薪酬偏低"},{"english":"receive government funding","chinese":"獲得政府資助"},{"english":"continue producing their work","chinese":"繼續創作"},{"english":"artistic labour","chinese":"藝術勞動；藝術工作"},{"english":"strengthen cultural life","chinese":"豐富文化生活"},{"english":"support significant economic activity","chinese":"支持重要經濟活動"},{"english":"public funding is justified","chinese":"公帑資助是合理的"},{"english":"create public benefits","chinese":"創造公共利益"},{"english":"private income alone","chinese":"單靠私人收入"},{"english":"does not reflect","chinese":"未能反映"},{"english":"earn enough to remain in","chinese":"賺到足以留在……的收入"},{"english":"remain in the profession","chinese":"留在這個行業"},{"english":"be forced to leave","chinese":"被迫離開"},{"english":"more stable jobs","chinese":"更穩定的工作"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"plays, exhibitions, concerts and community projects","chinese":"戲劇、展覽、音樂會和社區項目"},{"english":"reduce the public's access to","chinese":"減少公眾接觸……的機會"},{"english":"access to culture","chinese":"接觸文化的機會"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨時間"},{"english":"weaken social cohesion","chinese":"削弱社會凝聚力"},{"english":"shared stories","chinese":"共同故事"},{"english":"traditions and forms of expression","chinese":"傳統和表達形式"},{"english":"become less visible","chinese":"變得較不明顯"},{"english":"everyday life","chinese":"日常生活"},{"english":"local theatre","chinese":"本地劇院"},{"english":"music programme","chinese":"音樂節目；音樂計劃"},{"english":"survive only through ticket sales","chinese":"只靠門票收入生存"},{"english":"ticket sales","chinese":"門票收入"},{"english":"disappear from poorer communities altogether","chinese":"從較貧困社區完全消失"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"public support","chinese":"公共支持；政府支持"},{"english":"engage with the arts","chinese":"接觸藝術；參與藝術活動"},{"english":"regularly","chinese":"定期地"},{"english":"this exposure","chinese":"這種接觸"},{"english":"develop imagination","chinese":"培養想像力"},{"english":"empathy","chinese":"同理心"},{"english":"communication skills","chinese":"溝通技巧"},{"english":"in educational as well as cultural terms","chinese":"從教育和文化角度來看"},{"english":"economically sensible","chinese":"在經濟上合理"},{"english":"rather than merely charitable","chinese":"而不只是慈善"},{"english":"stable grants","chinese":"穩定撥款"},{"english":"commissions","chinese":"委約創作；委託項目"},{"english":"creators","chinese":"創作者"},{"english":"keep producing work","chinese":"持續創作"},{"english":"purchasing materials","chinese":"購買材料"},{"english":"collaborating with","chinese":"與……合作"},{"english":"venues","chinese":"場地"},{"english":"technicians","chinese":"技術人員"},{"english":"initial investment","chinese":"初始投資"},{"english":"circulate through","chinese":"在……中流動"},{"english":"the wider economy","chinese":"更廣泛的經濟"},{"english":"profitable industries","chinese":"有盈利的行業"},{"english":"depend on artistic talent","chinese":"依賴藝術人才"},{"english":"at an earlier stage of development","chinese":"在較早發展階段"},{"english":"digital media","chinese":"數碼媒體"},{"english":"rely on","chinese":"依賴"},{"english":"visual artists","chinese":"視覺藝術家"},{"english":"publicly supported spaces","chinese":"由公帑支持的空間"},{"english":"be pushed out of","chinese":"被迫離開"},{"english":"persistently low pay","chinese":"長期偏低薪酬"},{"english":"eventually loses","chinese":"最終失去"},{"english":"creative capacity","chinese":"創意能力"},{"english":"future revenue","chinese":"未來收入"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相反"},{"english":"invest in artists","chinese":"投資於藝術家"},{"english":"attract visitors","chinese":"吸引遊客"},{"english":"revive cultural districts","chinese":"重振文化區"},{"english":"create employment beyond","chinese":"在……以外創造就業"},{"english":"the arts themselves","chinese":"藝術本身"},{"english":"preserves public access to culture","chinese":"保留公眾接觸文化的機會"},{"english":"valuable human qualities","chinese":"寶貴的人文素質"},{"english":"sustain wider economic growth","chinese":"維持更廣泛的經濟增長"},{"english":"well-judged public policy","chinese":"明智的公共政策"}]},"model-essay-5-ielts-task1-bar-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-5-ielts-task1-bar-charts","essayKey":"bar-charts:5","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-5-ielts-task1-bar-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/bar-charts/bar-chart-5","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The bar chart compares electricity production and consumption in the ten leading countries in 2014, in billions of kilowatt-hours.","chinese":"這張柱狀圖比較了 2014 年十大主要國家的電力生產量和耗電量，單位為十億千瓦時。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, China and the United States were by far the largest producers and users, whereas the other eight countries recorded much lower figures. It is also clear that output exceeded consumption in every country except Germany.","chinese":"整體而言，中國和美國是明顯最大的電力生產國和消耗國，而其餘八個國家的數字則低得多。 另一個明顯特徵是，除了德國之外，每個國家的電力產量都高於耗電量。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"China led the ranking, producing 5,398 billion kWh and consuming a marginally lower 5,322 billion kWh. The United States was second, at 4,099 billion kWh for production and 3,866 billion kWh for consumption; despite being well behind China, it remained far ahead of all other nations. Russia ranked third, generating 1,057 billion kWh and using 1,038 billion kWh, while Japan followed with 936.2 and 856.7 billion kWh, respectively.","chinese":"中國位居第一，電力產量為 5,398 十億千瓦時，耗電量則略低，為 5,322 十億千瓦時。 美國排名第二，電力產量為 4,099 十億千瓦時，耗電量為 3,866 十億千瓦時；雖然明顯落後於中國，但仍遠遠高於其他所有國家。 俄羅斯排名第三，發電量為 1,057 十億千瓦時，用電量為 1,038 十億千瓦時；日本緊隨其後，生產和消耗分別為 936.2 和 856.7 十億千瓦時。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"In the remaining countries, the figures were much smaller. India produced 871 billion kWh but consumed only 698.8 billion kWh. Canada, France and Brazil showed broadly similar patterns, each generating more electricity than it used, with production between 530.7 and 618.9 billion kWh. Germany was the only exception, consuming 582.5 billion kWh compared with output of 526.6 billion kWh. South Korea had the lowest totals, at 485.1 and 449.5 billion kWh.","chinese":"在其餘國家中，相關數字要小得多。 印度生產了 871 十億千瓦時的電力，但只消耗了 698.8 十億千瓦時。 加拿大、法國和巴西呈現大致相似的模式，三國的發電量都高於耗電量，而產量介乎 530.7 至 618.9 十億千瓦時之間。 德國是唯一例外，其耗電量為 582.5 十億千瓦時，高於 526.6 十億千瓦時的產量。 南韓的總量最低，產量和耗電量分別為 485.1 和 449.5 十億千瓦時。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"electricity production and consumption","chinese":"電力生產及消耗"},{"english":"the ten leading countries","chinese":"十個領先國家"},{"english":"in billions of kilowatt-hours","chinese":"以十億千瓦時為單位"},{"english":"kilowatt-hours","chinese":"千瓦時"},{"english":"by far the largest","chinese":"明顯是最大的"},{"english":"producers and users","chinese":"生產及使用電力的國家"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相比之下"},{"english":"recorded much lower figures","chinese":"錄得低得多的數字"},{"english":"It is also clear that","chinese":"亦可清楚看出"},{"english":"output exceeded consumption","chinese":"產量超過消耗量"},{"english":"in every country except","chinese":"除了……以外的每個國家"},{"english":"led the ranking","chinese":"位居榜首"},{"english":"producing…and consuming…","chinese":"生產……並消耗……"},{"english":"a marginally lower","chinese":"略低的"},{"english":"was second","chinese":"位居第二"},{"english":"at…for production","chinese":"生產量為……"},{"english":"for consumption","chinese":"消耗量為……"},{"english":"despite being well behind","chinese":"儘管遠遠落後於……"},{"english":"remained far ahead of","chinese":"仍然遠遠領先於……"},{"english":"all other nations","chinese":"所有其他國家"},{"english":"ranked third","chinese":"排名第三"},{"english":"generating…and using…","chinese":"發電……並使用……"},{"english":"followed with","chinese":"隨後錄得"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"the remaining countries","chinese":"其餘國家"},{"english":"the figures were much smaller","chinese":"數字小得多"},{"english":"produced…but consumed only…","chinese":"生產……但只消耗……"},{"english":"consumed only","chinese":"只消耗"},{"english":"showed broadly similar patterns","chinese":"呈現大致相似的模式"},{"english":"broadly similar patterns","chinese":"大致相似的模式"},{"english":"each generating more electricity than it used","chinese":"各自發電量高於用電量"},{"english":"with production between…and…","chinese":"產量介乎……與……之間"},{"english":"between 530.7 and 618.9 billion kWh","chinese":"介乎530.7至618.9十億千瓦時"},{"english":"the only exception","chinese":"唯一例外"},{"english":"compared with output of","chinese":"相比之下產量為……"},{"english":"had the lowest totals","chinese":"總數最低"},{"english":"lowest totals","chinese":"最低總數"},{"english":"among the ten countries","chinese":"在十個國家之中"},{"english":"electricity figures","chinese":"電力數據"},{"english":"production and consumption figures","chinese":"生產及消耗數據"},{"english":"much lower figures","chinese":"低得多的數字"},{"english":"well behind China","chinese":"遠遠落後於中國"},{"english":"far ahead of all other nations","chinese":"遠遠領先於所有其他國家"},{"english":"general pattern","chinese":"整體模式"},{"english":"compared with","chinese":"與……相比"},{"english":"output","chinese":"產量；發電量"}]},"model-essay-5-ielts-task1-line-graph":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-5-ielts-task1-line-graph","essayKey":"line-graph:5","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-5-ielts-task1-line-graph","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/line-graphs/line-graph-5","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The two line charts illustrate changes in the proportion of households owning three electrical appliances and the average time spent on housework each week in one country from 1920 to 2019.","chinese":"這兩張折線圖說明了 1920 年至 2019 年間，某一國家家庭擁有三種電器的比例變化，以及每週平均花在家務上的時間變化。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, ownership of all three appliances increased, with refrigerators and vacuum cleaners becoming almost universal by the end of the period. Meanwhile, weekly housework fell markedly, from 50 hours to only 10.","chinese":"整體而言，三種電器的擁有率均有所上升，其中雪櫃和吸塵機到期末時幾乎已普及到所有家庭。 與此同時，每週家務時間大幅下降，從 50 小時減少至僅 10 小時。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 1920, washing machines were the most common appliance, at around 40%, compared with 30% for vacuum cleaners and almost no refrigerator ownership. The refrigerator then recorded the sharpest growth, rising to about 55% in 1940 and 90% in 1960, before reaching full ownership in 1980. Vacuum cleaners increased more steadily, climbing from 30% to 70% between 1920 and 1960 and reaching 100% by 2000. By contrast, washing machines grew more modestly, from 40% to 70% in 1960, dipped to roughly 65% in 1980, and then recovered to about 75% in 2019.","chinese":"在 1920 年，洗衣機是最常見的電器，約有 40% 的家庭擁有；相比之下，吸塵機的擁有率為 30% ，而幾乎沒有家庭擁有雪櫃。 之後，雪櫃的增長最為顯著，擁有率在 1940 年升至約 55% ， 1960 年升至 90% ，並在 1980 年達到完全普及。 吸塵機的擁有率則以較穩定的方式上升，從 1920 年的 30% 增至 1960 年的 70% ，並在 2000 年達到 100% 。 相比之下，洗衣機的增長較為溫和，從 1920 年的 40% 升至 1960 年的 70% ，其後在 1980 年下降至約 65% ，最後在 2019 年回升至約 75% 。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The second chart shows an opposite pattern. Housework declined from 50 hours per week in 1920 to 35 in 1940, then fell further to 20 by 1960. Thereafter, the decrease was slower, reaching 15 hours in 1980 and 2000, before dropping to 10 in 2019.","chinese":"第二張圖顯示出相反的趨勢。 每週家務時間從 1920 年的 50 小時下降至 1940 年的 35 小時，然後到 1960 年進一步下降至 20 小時。 此後，下降速度放緩，在 1980 年和 2000 年達到 15 小時，最後在 2019 年降至 10 小時。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the two line charts illustrate","chinese":"兩個折線圖顯示"},{"english":"changes in the proportion of households","chinese":"住戶比例的變化"},{"english":"the proportion of households owning","chinese":"擁有……的住戶比例"},{"english":"electrical appliances","chinese":"電器"},{"english":"average time spent on housework","chinese":"平均花在家務上的時間"},{"english":"housework","chinese":"家務"},{"english":"each week","chinese":"每星期"},{"english":"in one country","chinese":"在某一個國家"},{"english":"from 1920 to 2019","chinese":"從1920年至2019年"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"ownership of all three appliances","chinese":"三種電器的擁有率"},{"english":"increased","chinese":"上升"},{"english":"with refrigerators and vacuum cleaners becoming","chinese":"其中雪櫃和吸塵機變得……"},{"english":"refrigerators","chinese":"雪櫃"},{"english":"vacuum cleaners","chinese":"吸塵機"},{"english":"almost universal","chinese":"幾乎普及"},{"english":"by the end of the period","chinese":"到期末"},{"english":"Meanwhile","chinese":"與此同時"},{"english":"weekly housework","chinese":"每星期家務時間"},{"english":"fell markedly","chinese":"明顯下降"},{"english":"from 50 hours to only 10","chinese":"由50小時降至僅10小時"},{"english":"washing machines","chinese":"洗衣機"},{"english":"the most common appliance","chinese":"最常見的電器"},{"english":"at around 40%","chinese":"約為40%"},{"english":"compared with","chinese":"與……相比"},{"english":"almost no refrigerator ownership","chinese":"幾乎沒有人擁有雪櫃"},{"english":"recorded the sharpest growth","chinese":"錄得最急劇增長"},{"english":"the sharpest growth","chinese":"最急劇增長"},{"english":"rising to about 55%","chinese":"上升至約55%"},{"english":"before reaching full ownership","chinese":"隨後達至全面擁有"},{"english":"full ownership","chinese":"全面擁有；百分百擁有率"},{"english":"increased more steadily","chinese":"更穩定地上升"},{"english":"climbing from 30% to 70%","chinese":"由30%攀升至70%"},{"english":"between 1920 and 1960","chinese":"在1920年至1960年間"},{"english":"reaching 100% by 2000","chinese":"到2000年達到100%"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"grew more modestly","chinese":"增長較溫和"},{"english":"dipped to roughly 65%","chinese":"下跌至約65%"},{"english":"then recovered to about 75%","chinese":"隨後回升至約75%"},{"english":"the second chart shows","chinese":"第二個圖表顯示"},{"english":"an opposite pattern","chinese":"相反模式"},{"english":"declined from 50 hours per week","chinese":"由每星期50小時下降"},{"english":"hours per week","chinese":"每星期小時數"},{"english":"then fell further to","chinese":"然後進一步下降至"},{"english":"by 1960","chinese":"到1960年"},{"english":"Thereafter","chinese":"此後"},{"english":"the decrease was slower","chinese":"下降速度較慢"},{"english":"reaching 15 hours","chinese":"達到15小時"},{"english":"before dropping to 10","chinese":"隨後下降至10"},{"english":"dropping to 10 in 2019","chinese":"在2019年下降至10小時"}]},"model-essay-5-ielts-task1-maps":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-5-ielts-task1-maps","essayKey":"maps:5","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-5-ielts-task1-maps","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/maps/maps-5","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The two plans illustrate the current layout of Southwest Airport and the way it is expected to look after redevelopment next year.","chinese":"這兩張平面圖展示了 Southwest Airport 現時的布局，以及它預計在明年重新發展後的樣貌。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the airport will be substantially enlarged, especially airside, where the existing pier with eight gates will be replaced by a Y-shaped concourse containing eighteen gates and a sky train. The terminal will also offer more passenger facilities, although its basic division into departures and arrivals will remain.","chinese":"整體而言，該機場將會大幅擴建，尤其是在空側區域；現有設有八個登機閘口的登機廊將被一個 Y 形候機大廳取代，當中會有十八個登機閘口和一條空中列車。Main Feature 2 （主要特徵二）。 航站樓亦會提供更多乘客服務設施，不過其基本的離境和入境分區將會保留。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"At present, the airport has a small terminal, with departures on the left and arrivals on the right. Departing passengers pass through security and passport control before using a walkway to reach eight gates arranged around a rectangular pier. The departures area contains only check-in facilities and a café, while arrivals are limited to passport control and customs.","chinese":"目前，該機場有一個較小的航站樓，離境區位於左邊，入境區位於右邊。 離境乘客會先通過安檢和護照檢查，然後經由一條步行通道前往圍繞矩形登機廊排列的八個登機閘口。 離境區只設有辦理登機手續的設施和一間咖啡店，而入境區則只包括護照檢查和海關。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"After redevelopment, the departures hall will include a bag drop, check-in area and café. Shops will be added beyond security, leading to the enlarged concourse. Instead of a simple walkway, passengers will use a sky train along the main pier, which will branch into two arms and increase the number of gates to eighteen. The arrivals side will also gain a café, an ATM and car-hire facilities near the exit.","chinese":"重新發展後，離境大堂將會包括行李托運處、辦理登機手續區和咖啡店。 商店將會增設在安檢之後的位置，並通往擴大的候機大廳。 乘客將不再只使用簡單的步行通道，而是會沿著主登機廊乘坐空中列車；該登機廊會分成兩條支線，並把登機閘口數量增加至十八個。 入境區一側亦會在出口附近增設咖啡店、自動櫃員機和租車設施。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the plans below show","chinese":"下列平面圖顯示"},{"english":"the site of an airport","chinese":"機場所在地；機場範圍"},{"english":"how it will look","chinese":"它將來的樣貌"},{"english":"after redevelopment","chinese":"重建後"},{"english":"next year","chinese":"明年"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"selecting and reporting","chinese":"選取並報告"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"The two plans illustrate","chinese":"兩幅平面圖顯示"},{"english":"the current layout of","chinese":"……目前的佈局"},{"english":"Southwest Airport","chinese":"Southwest Airport"},{"english":"the way it is expected to look","chinese":"預計將會呈現的樣貌"},{"english":"is expected to look","chinese":"預計會呈現……的樣貌"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"will be substantially enlarged","chinese":"將會大幅擴建"},{"english":"substantially enlarged","chinese":"大幅擴大"},{"english":"especially airside","chinese":"尤其是機場禁區範圍"},{"english":"airside","chinese":"機場禁區範圍；空側"},{"english":"the existing pier","chinese":"現有客運廊"},{"english":"with eight gates","chinese":"設有八個閘口"},{"english":"will be replaced by","chinese":"將被……取代"},{"english":"a Y-shaped concourse","chinese":"Y形客運廊"},{"english":"containing eighteen gates","chinese":"設有十八個閘口"},{"english":"a sky train","chinese":"機場列車"},{"english":"the terminal","chinese":"客運大樓"},{"english":"will also offer","chinese":"亦會提供"},{"english":"passenger facilities","chinese":"旅客服務設施"},{"english":"its basic division into","chinese":"其分為……的基本劃分"},{"english":"departures and arrivals","chinese":"離境及抵達區"},{"english":"will remain","chinese":"將會保留"},{"english":"At present","chinese":"目前"},{"english":"a small terminal","chinese":"小型客運大樓"},{"english":"departures on the left","chinese":"離境區在左邊"},{"english":"arrivals on the right","chinese":"抵達區在右邊"},{"english":"departing passengers","chinese":"離境旅客"},{"english":"pass through security","chinese":"通過保安檢查"},{"english":"passport control","chinese":"護照檢查；出入境檢查"},{"english":"before using","chinese":"在使用……之前"},{"english":"a walkway","chinese":"行人通道"},{"english":"to reach eight gates","chinese":"前往八個閘口"},{"english":"arranged around","chinese":"圍繞……排列"},{"english":"a rectangular pier","chinese":"長方形客運廊"},{"english":"the departures area","chinese":"離境區"},{"english":"contains only","chinese":"只設有"},{"english":"check-in facilities","chinese":"辦理登機手續設施"},{"english":"while arrivals are limited to","chinese":"而抵達區只限於"},{"english":"are limited to","chinese":"僅限於；只有"},{"english":"customs","chinese":"海關"},{"english":"After redevelopment","chinese":"重建後"},{"english":"the departures hall","chinese":"離境大堂"},{"english":"will include","chinese":"將包括"},{"english":"a bag drop","chinese":"行李托運處"},{"english":"check-in area","chinese":"辦理登機手續區"},{"english":"shops will be added","chinese":"將增設商店"},{"english":"beyond security","chinese":"過了保安檢查後"},{"english":"leading to","chinese":"通往；連接至"},{"english":"the enlarged concourse","chinese":"擴建後的客運廊"},{"english":"Instead of","chinese":"而不是"},{"english":"a simple walkway","chinese":"簡單的行人通道"},{"english":"along the main pier","chinese":"沿着主客運廊"},{"english":"the main pier","chinese":"主客運廊"},{"english":"will branch into two arms","chinese":"將分成兩條分支"},{"english":"two arms","chinese":"兩條分支"},{"english":"increase the number of gates","chinese":"增加閘口數目"},{"english":"to eighteen","chinese":"增至十八個"},{"english":"the arrivals side","chinese":"抵達區一邊"},{"english":"will also gain","chinese":"亦會增設"},{"english":"an ATM","chinese":"自動櫃員機"},{"english":"car-hire facilities","chinese":"租車設施"},{"english":"near the exit","chinese":"在出口附近"}]},"model-essay-5-ielts-task1-mixed-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-5-ielts-task1-mixed-charts","essayKey":"mixed-charts:5","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-5-ielts-task1-mixed-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/mixed-charts/mixed-charts-5","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The bar chart compares the export earnings of five product categories in one country in 2015 and 2016, while the table indicates the percentage change in each category over the same period.","chinese":"這張柱狀圖比較了一個國家在 2015 年和 2016 年五個產品類別的出口收入，而表格則顯示同一期間每個類別的百分比變化。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, export revenues increased in four of the five categories, with gems and jewellery being the only sector to decline. Petroleum products remained the highest-earning export in both years, while textiles recorded the strongest percentage growth despite starting from the lowest base.","chinese":"整體而言，五個出口類別中有四個的收入上升，而寶石和珠寶是唯一下降的類別。 石油產品在兩年中都是收入最高的出口類別；相反，紡織品雖然起點最低，但錄得最強的百分比增長。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 2015, petroleum products generated about $61 billion, slightly more than engineered goods, which stood at roughly $58 billion. By 2016, both categories had risen, to approximately $63 billion and $62 billion respectively. Although petroleum products still led the chart, engineered goods narrowed the gap after an 8.5% increase, compared with a more modest 3% rise in petroleum exports.","chinese":"2015 年，石油產品創造了約 610 億美元的收入，略高於工程產品約 580 億美元。 到 2016 年，這兩個類別均有所上升，分別達到約 630 億美元和 620 億美元。 雖然石油產品仍然位居首位，但工程產品在增長 8.5% 後縮小了差距；相比之下，石油產品的增幅較溫和，只有 3% 。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The remaining categories earned less. Gems and jewellery fell from around $43 billion to about $41 billion, representing a decline of 5.18%. Agricultural products changed very little, edging up by only 0.81% from just over $30 billion. By contrast, textiles climbed markedly from approximately $26 billion to $31 billion, making it the fastest-growing category at 15.24%.","chinese":"其餘類別的收入較低。 寶石和珠寶的收入從約 430 億美元下降至約 410 億美元，代表下降了 5.18% 。 農產品變化非常小，從略高於 300 億美元的水平只微升了 0.81% 。 相比之下，紡織品從約 260 億美元顯著上升至 310 億美元，使其成為增長最快的類別，增幅達 15.24% 。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the chart below shows","chinese":"下列圖表顯示"},{"english":"the value of exports","chinese":"出口價值"},{"english":"one country's exports","chinese":"某國的出口"},{"english":"in various categories","chinese":"在不同類別中"},{"english":"during 2015 and 2016","chinese":"在2015年和2016年間"},{"english":"the table shows","chinese":"表格顯示"},{"english":"the percentage change in","chinese":"……的百分比變化"},{"english":"each category of exports","chinese":"每個出口類別"},{"english":"compared with 2015","chinese":"與2015年相比"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"selecting and reporting","chinese":"選取並報告"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"the bar chart compares","chinese":"柱狀圖比較"},{"english":"export earnings","chinese":"出口收入"},{"english":"five product categories","chinese":"五個產品類別"},{"english":"while","chinese":"而"},{"english":"indicates the percentage change","chinese":"顯示百分比變化"},{"english":"over the same period","chinese":"在同一時期內"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"export revenues","chinese":"出口收入"},{"english":"increased in four of the five categories","chinese":"在五個類別中的四個上升"},{"english":"with … being the only sector to decline","chinese":"其中……是唯一下降的行業"},{"english":"gems and jewellery","chinese":"寶石及首飾"},{"english":"the only sector to decline","chinese":"唯一下跌的行業"},{"english":"petroleum products","chinese":"石油產品"},{"english":"remained the highest-earning export","chinese":"仍然是收入最高的出口"},{"english":"in both years","chinese":"在兩年中"},{"english":"textiles","chinese":"紡織品"},{"english":"recorded the strongest percentage growth","chinese":"錄得最大百分比升幅"},{"english":"percentage growth","chinese":"百分比增長"},{"english":"despite starting from","chinese":"儘管起點是……"},{"english":"the lowest base","chinese":"最低基數；最低起點"},{"english":"generated about $61 billion","chinese":"創造約610億美元"},{"english":"slightly more than","chinese":"略多於"},{"english":"engineered goods","chinese":"工程產品"},{"english":"stood at roughly","chinese":"約為"},{"english":"roughly $58 billion","chinese":"約580億美元"},{"english":"By 2016","chinese":"到2016年"},{"english":"both categories had risen","chinese":"兩個類別均已上升"},{"english":"approximately $63 billion","chinese":"約630億美元"},{"english":"$62 billion respectively","chinese":"分別為620億美元"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"Although","chinese":"雖然"},{"english":"still led the chart","chinese":"仍然在圖表中居首"},{"english":"narrowed the gap","chinese":"收窄差距"},{"english":"after an 8.5% increase","chinese":"在上升8.5%後"},{"english":"compared with","chinese":"與……相比"},{"english":"a more modest 3% rise","chinese":"較溫和的3%升幅"},{"english":"petroleum exports","chinese":"石油出口"},{"english":"the remaining categories","chinese":"其餘類別"},{"english":"earned less","chinese":"收入較低"},{"english":"fell from … to …","chinese":"由……跌至……"},{"english":"around $43 billion","chinese":"約430億美元"},{"english":"about $41 billion","chinese":"約410億美元"},{"english":"representing a decline of","chinese":"代表下降……"},{"english":"a decline of 5.18%","chinese":"5.18%的跌幅"},{"english":"agricultural products","chinese":"農產品"},{"english":"changed very little","chinese":"變化很小"},{"english":"edging up by only","chinese":"只輕微上升"},{"english":"by only 0.81%","chinese":"只增加0.81%"},{"english":"from just over $30 billion","chinese":"由剛高於300億美元"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"climbed markedly","chinese":"大幅上升"},{"english":"from approximately $26 billion to $31 billion","chinese":"由約260億美元升至310億美元"},{"english":"making it the fastest-growing category","chinese":"使其成為增長最快的類別"},{"english":"the fastest-growing category","chinese":"增長最快的類別"},{"english":"at 15.24%","chinese":"達15.24%"}]},"model-essay-5-ielts-task1-pie-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-5-ielts-task1-pie-charts","essayKey":"pie-charts:5","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-5-ielts-task1-pie-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/pie-charts/pie-chart-5","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The pie charts compare the age profiles of the populations of Yemen and Italy in 2000 and show projections for 2050.","chinese":"這些圓餅圖比較了葉門和意大利在 2000 年的人口年齡結構，並展示了 2050 年的預測。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, Yemen had a markedly younger population than Italy in 2000, and this is expected to remain the case in 2050. However, both countries are projected to age: the share of children will decline, while older groups, especially those aged 60 and above in Italy, will become more prominent.","chinese":"整體而言，葉門在 2000 年的人口明顯比意大利年輕，而這種情況預計在 2050年仍會維持。 然而，兩國人口都預計會老化：兒童所佔比例將會下降，而較年長的群體會變得更突出，尤其是意大利 60 歲及以上的人口。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In Yemen, children aged 0–14 made up just over half of the population in 2000, at 50.1%, slightly exceeding the 46.3% recorded for people aged 15–59. By 2050, this pattern is forecast to reverse, with the working-age group rising to 57.3% and children falling to 37.0%. The elderly population will remain comparatively small, though it is expected to increase from 3.6% to 5.7%.","chinese":"在葉門， 0 至 14 歲兒童在 2000 年佔人口略多於一半，為 50.1% ，稍高於 15 至 59 歲人口的 46.3% 。 到 2050 年，這種模式預計會逆轉，工作年齡人口將上升至 57.3% ，而兒童比例則下降至 37.0% 。 老年人口仍會相對較少，儘管預計會從 3.6% 上升至 5.7% 。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Italy showed a far older structure. In 2000, people aged 15–59 accounted for the largest proportion, at 61.6%, while those over 60 represented 24.1%; children made up only 14.3%. By 2050, the 60-plus group is projected to surge to 42.3%, close to the working-age share of 46.2%, whereas the youngest group will shrink slightly to 11.5%.","chinese":"意大利則呈現出明顯更老化的人口結構。 在 2000 年， 15 至 59 歲人口佔最大比例，為 61.6% ； 60 歲以上人口佔 24.1% ；兒童則只佔 14.3% 。 到 2050 年， 60 歲以上人口預計會大幅上升至 42.3% ，接近工作年齡人口的46.2% ；相反，最年輕組別將小幅下降至 11.5% 。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the pie charts compare","chinese":"圓形圖比較"},{"english":"age profiles","chinese":"年齡結構"},{"english":"the populations of Yemen and Italy","chinese":"也門和意大利的人口"},{"english":"show projections for 2050","chinese":"顯示2050年的預測"},{"english":"projections for 2050","chinese":"2050年的預測"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"a markedly younger population","chinese":"明顯較年輕的人口"},{"english":"than Italy","chinese":"比意大利"},{"english":"is expected to remain the case","chinese":"預計情況仍會如此"},{"english":"remain the case","chinese":"情況仍然如此"},{"english":"However","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"are projected to age","chinese":"預計會人口老化"},{"english":"the share of children","chinese":"兒童所佔比例"},{"english":"will decline","chinese":"將會下降"},{"english":"older groups","chinese":"較年長組別"},{"english":"especially those aged 60 and above","chinese":"尤其是60歲或以上人士"},{"english":"aged 60 and above","chinese":"60歲或以上"},{"english":"become more prominent","chinese":"變得更突出"},{"english":"children aged 0–14","chinese":"0至14歲兒童"},{"english":"made up just over half of","chinese":"佔略多於一半"},{"english":"just over half of the population","chinese":"人口的略多於一半"},{"english":"at 50.1%","chinese":"為50.1%"},{"english":"slightly exceeding","chinese":"略高於"},{"english":"recorded for people aged 15–59","chinese":"15至59歲人士錄得的數字"},{"english":"people aged 15–59","chinese":"15至59歲人士"},{"english":"By 2050","chinese":"到2050年"},{"english":"this pattern is forecast to reverse","chinese":"預測這一模式會逆轉"},{"english":"is forecast to reverse","chinese":"預測會逆轉"},{"english":"the working-age group","chinese":"工作年齡組別"},{"english":"rising to 57.3%","chinese":"上升至57.3%"},{"english":"falling to 37.0%","chinese":"下降至37.0%"},{"english":"the elderly population","chinese":"老年人口"},{"english":"remain comparatively small","chinese":"仍然相對較小"},{"english":"though","chinese":"雖然；不過"},{"english":"is expected to increase from","chinese":"預計由……增加"},{"english":"from 3.6% to 5.7%","chinese":"由3.6%增至5.7%"},{"english":"showed a far older structure","chinese":"呈現年老得多的人口結構"},{"english":"a far older structure","chinese":"年老得多的結構"},{"english":"accounted for the largest proportion","chinese":"佔最大比例"},{"english":"the largest proportion","chinese":"最大比例"},{"english":"while those over 60","chinese":"而60歲以上人士"},{"english":"those over 60","chinese":"60歲以上人士"},{"english":"represented 24.1%","chinese":"佔24.1%"},{"english":"made up only 14.3%","chinese":"僅佔14.3%"},{"english":"the 60-plus group","chinese":"60歲以上組別"},{"english":"is projected to surge to","chinese":"預計會急升至"},{"english":"surge to 42.3%","chinese":"急升至42.3%"},{"english":"close to the working-age share","chinese":"接近工作年齡人口比例"},{"english":"the working-age share","chinese":"工作年齡人口比例"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；然而"},{"english":"the youngest group","chinese":"最年輕組別"},{"english":"shrink slightly to 11.5%","chinese":"輕微縮減至11.5%"}]},"model-essay-5-ielts-task1-process-diagram":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-5-ielts-task1-process-diagram","essayKey":"process-diagram:5","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-5-ielts-task1-process-diagram","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/process-diagrams/process-diagram-5","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The diagram illustrates the industrial process by which instant noodles are manufactured.","chinese":"該圖說明即食麵是如何透過工業流程被製造出來的。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, this is a linear, eight-stage procedure that starts with flour being stored in silos and ends with finished noodle cups being sealed and labelled. Broadly, the process can be divided into two phases: preparing and shaping the dough, followed by cooking, flavouring and packaging the product.","chinese":"整體而言，這是一個線性的八階段流程，從麵粉被存放在筒倉開始，以完成的麵杯被密封並貼上標籤結束。 大致上，該流程可分為兩個階段：先準備並塑造麵團，然後烹煮、調味並包裝產品。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"At the beginning, flour is delivered by truck and kept in storage silos. It is then transferred to a mixer, where water and oil are added to form dough. After this mixture has been prepared, it passes through a series of rollers, which flatten it into thin dough sheets. These sheets are subsequently cut into narrow strips, and the strips are shaped into round noodle discs.","chinese":"一開始，麵粉由貨車運送，並被存放在儲存筒倉中。 然後，麵粉被轉移到攪拌機中，在那裡加入水和油以形成麵團。 當這種混合物準備完成後，它會通過一系列滾軸，被壓平成薄薄的麵團片。 隨後，這些麵團片被切成狹長條狀，而這些條狀物再被塑造成圓形麵餅。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"In the second half of the process, the noodle discs are cooked in oil and then dried. Once this heating stage has been completed, the dried discs are placed into individual cups. Vegetables and spices are added at this point, turning the plain noodles into a complete convenience product. Finally, the cups are sealed and labelled before leaving the production line.","chinese":"在流程的後半部分，麵餅會在油中被烹煮，然後被烘乾。 當這個加熱階段完成後，乾燥的麵餅會被放入各自的杯子中。 在這個階段，蔬菜和香料會被加入，使原本普通的麵條變成完整的便利食品。 最後，杯子在離開生產線前會被密封並貼上標籤。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"The diagram illustrates","chinese":"圖解顯示"},{"english":"industrial process","chinese":"工業流程"},{"english":"the process by which","chinese":"……的過程"},{"english":"instant noodles","chinese":"即食麵"},{"english":"are manufactured","chinese":"被製造"},{"english":"a linear, eight-stage procedure","chinese":"線性的八階段程序"},{"english":"starts with","chinese":"以……開始"},{"english":"flour being stored in silos","chinese":"麵粉被儲存在筒倉內"},{"english":"ends with","chinese":"以……結束"},{"english":"finished noodle cups","chinese":"完成的杯麵"},{"english":"being sealed and labelled","chinese":"被密封和貼上標籤"},{"english":"Broadly","chinese":"概括來說"},{"english":"can be divided into","chinese":"可分為"},{"english":"two phases","chinese":"兩個階段"},{"english":"preparing and shaping the dough","chinese":"準備和塑造麵團"},{"english":"followed by","chinese":"隨後是"},{"english":"cooking, flavouring and packaging","chinese":"烹煮、調味和包裝"},{"english":"the product","chinese":"產品"},{"english":"At the beginning","chinese":"一開始"},{"english":"is delivered by truck","chinese":"由貨車運送"},{"english":"kept in storage silos","chinese":"儲存在筒倉內"},{"english":"storage silos","chinese":"儲存筒倉"},{"english":"transferred to a mixer","chinese":"被轉移到攪拌機"},{"english":"a mixer","chinese":"攪拌機"},{"english":"water and oil are added","chinese":"加入水和油"},{"english":"to form dough","chinese":"以形成麵團"},{"english":"dough","chinese":"麵團"},{"english":"this mixture has been prepared","chinese":"這混合物被準備好後"},{"english":"passes through","chinese":"經過"},{"english":"a series of rollers","chinese":"一系列滾軸"},{"english":"flatten it into","chinese":"將它壓平成"},{"english":"thin dough sheets","chinese":"薄麵皮"},{"english":"are subsequently cut into","chinese":"隨後被切成"},{"english":"narrow strips","chinese":"幼長條"},{"english":"are shaped into","chinese":"被塑造成"},{"english":"round noodle discs","chinese":"圓形麵餅"},{"english":"in the second half of the process","chinese":"在流程的後半部分"},{"english":"are cooked in oil","chinese":"在油中烹煮"},{"english":"then dried","chinese":"然後被烘乾"},{"english":"this heating stage","chinese":"這個加熱階段"},{"english":"has been completed","chinese":"已經完成"},{"english":"the dried discs","chinese":"烘乾後的麵餅"},{"english":"are placed into individual cups","chinese":"被放入獨立杯中"},{"english":"individual cups","chinese":"獨立杯"},{"english":"vegetables and spices","chinese":"蔬菜和香料"},{"english":"are added at this point","chinese":"在這一點加入"},{"english":"turning the plain noodles into","chinese":"將普通麵條變成"},{"english":"plain noodles","chinese":"普通麵條"},{"english":"a complete convenience product","chinese":"完整的便利食品"},{"english":"Finally","chinese":"最後"},{"english":"are sealed and labelled","chinese":"被密封和貼上標籤"},{"english":"before leaving the production line","chinese":"在離開生產線之前"},{"english":"the production line","chinese":"生產線"}]},"model-essay-5-ielts-task1-tables":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-5-ielts-task1-tables","essayKey":"tables:5","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-5-ielts-task1-tables","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/tables/table-5","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The table compares the global market shares of mobile phone sales held by several manufacturers in 2005 and 2006.","chinese":"這張表比較了數間手機製造商在 2005 年和 2006 年所佔的全球手機銷售市場份額。Overview （總覽）Main Feature 1 （主要特徵一）。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, Nokia remained the clear market leader and slightly strengthened its position, while Motorola recorded the most notable gain among the named companies. By contrast, Samsung, LG, BenQ Mobile and the collective “Others” category all lost market share; Sony Ericsson was the only smaller named brand to grow.","chinese":"整體而言， Nokia 仍然是明顯的市場領導者，並略微鞏固了其地位；而在所有列名公司之中， Motorola 錄得最顯著的增長。Main Feature 2 （主要特徵二）。 相比之下， Samsung 、 LG 、 BenQ Mobile 以及合併計算的「其他」類別均失去市場份額； Sony Ericsson 則是較小型列名品牌中唯一錄得增長的一間。Body Paragraph 1 （正文第一段）Leading Companies Details （主要公司細節）。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 2005, Nokia accounted for 32.5% of worldwide sales, almost twice Motorola’s share of 17.7% and well ahead of Samsung, at 12.7%. One year later, Nokia had risen to 35%, widening its lead despite Motorola’s increase to 21.1%. Motorola’s rise, at 3.4 percentage points, was the largest improvement in the table, whereas Samsung slipped slightly to 11.8%.","chinese":"2005 年， Nokia 佔全球銷售的 32.5% ，幾乎是 Motorola 17.7% 的兩倍，並遠高於Samsung 的 12.7% 。 一年後， Nokia 上升至 35% ；儘管 Motorola 也增至 21.1% ， Nokia 仍進一步擴大其領先優勢。 Motorola 上升了 3.4 個百分點，是表中最大增幅；相反， Samsung 則輕微下跌至 11.8% 。Body Paragraph 2 （正文第二段）Smaller Companies and Others （較小公司及其他類別）。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The remaining named manufacturers held much smaller shares. Sony Ericsson rose from 6.3% to 7.4%, overtaking LG, whose figure declined marginally from 6.7% to 6.3%. The steepest fall was seen in BenQ Mobile, which more than halved from 4.9% to 2.4%. Other manufacturers also became less significant collectively, dropping from 19.2% to 16.2%.","chinese":"其餘列名製造商所佔的市場份額明顯較小。 Sony Ericsson 從 6.3% 上升至 7.4% ，並超越了 LG ；後者的數字則由 6.7% 輕微下降至 6.3% 。 最大跌幅出現在 BenQ Mobile ，其市場份額由 4.9% 跌至 2.4% ，縮減了一半以上。 其他製造商合計所佔的重要性亦有所下降，從 19.2% 跌至 16.2% 。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the table shows","chinese":"表格顯示"},{"english":"worldwide market share","chinese":"全球市場佔有率"},{"english":"the mobile phone market","chinese":"手提電話市場"},{"english":"manufacturers","chinese":"製造商"},{"english":"in the years 2005 and 2006","chinese":"在2005年和2006年"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"by selecting and reporting","chinese":"透過選取並報告……"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"the table compares","chinese":"表格比較"},{"english":"global market shares","chinese":"全球市場佔有率"},{"english":"mobile phone sales","chinese":"手提電話銷售"},{"english":"held by","chinese":"由……持有"},{"english":"several manufacturers","chinese":"幾間製造商"},{"english":"remained the clear market leader","chinese":"仍然是明顯的市場領導者"},{"english":"the clear market leader","chinese":"明顯的市場領導者"},{"english":"slightly strengthened its position","chinese":"稍為鞏固其地位"},{"english":"recorded the most notable gain","chinese":"錄得最明顯增長"},{"english":"the most notable gain","chinese":"最明顯增幅"},{"english":"among the named companies","chinese":"在列明名稱的公司之中"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"collective “Others” category","chinese":"「其他」合計類別"},{"english":"lost market share","chinese":"失去市場佔有率"},{"english":"the only smaller named brand to grow","chinese":"唯一增長的較小型具名品牌"},{"english":"smaller named brand","chinese":"較小型具名品牌"},{"english":"in 2005","chinese":"在2005年"},{"english":"accounted for","chinese":"佔……"},{"english":"worldwide sales","chinese":"全球銷售"},{"english":"almost twice","chinese":"幾乎是……的兩倍"},{"english":"Motorola's share","chinese":"Motorola 的佔有率"},{"english":"well ahead of","chinese":"遠高於；大幅領先"},{"english":"at 12.7%","chinese":"為12.7%"},{"english":"one year later","chinese":"一年後"},{"english":"had risen to","chinese":"已上升至"},{"english":"widening its lead","chinese":"擴大其領先優勢"},{"english":"despite","chinese":"儘管"},{"english":"Motorola's increase","chinese":"Motorola 的升幅"},{"english":"increase to","chinese":"增加至"},{"english":"percentage points","chinese":"百分點"},{"english":"the largest improvement","chinese":"最大改善；最大升幅"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相反"},{"english":"slipped slightly to","chinese":"輕微下跌至"},{"english":"the remaining named manufacturers","chinese":"其餘具名製造商"},{"english":"held much smaller shares","chinese":"佔有率低得多"},{"english":"rose from X to Y","chinese":"由 X 上升至 Y"},{"english":"overtaking","chinese":"超越"},{"english":"whose figure declined marginally","chinese":"其數字輕微下降"},{"english":"declined marginally","chinese":"輕微下降"},{"english":"the steepest fall","chinese":"最大跌幅"},{"english":"was seen in","chinese":"出現在……"},{"english":"more than halved","chinese":"跌幅超過一半"},{"english":"from 4.9% to 2.4%","chinese":"由4.9%跌至2.4%"},{"english":"other manufacturers","chinese":"其他製造商"},{"english":"became less significant collectively","chinese":"整體重要性下降"},{"english":"collectively","chinese":"整體而言；合計"},{"english":"dropping from X to Y","chinese":"由 X 下降至 Y"},{"english":"market share increased","chinese":"市場佔有率上升"},{"english":"market share declined","chinese":"市場佔有率下降"},{"english":"strengthen its lead","chinese":"鞏固其領先地位"},{"english":"maintain first place","chinese":"保持第一位"},{"english":"narrow the gap","chinese":"收窄差距"},{"english":"gain ground","chinese":"取得進展；擴大佔有率"},{"english":"lose ground","chinese":"失去優勢；佔有率下降"},{"english":"a slight increase","chinese":"輕微增幅"},{"english":"a noticeable increase","chinese":"明顯增幅"},{"english":"a marginal decline","chinese":"輕微跌幅"},{"english":"a sharp decline","chinese":"大幅下跌"},{"english":"the dominant company","chinese":"佔主導地位的公司"},{"english":"the second-largest manufacturer","chinese":"第二大製造商"},{"english":"smaller competitors","chinese":"較小型競爭者"},{"english":"the gap between X and Y","chinese":"X 和 Y 之間的差距"},{"english":"widened in 2006","chinese":"在2006年擴大"},{"english":"the overall pattern","chinese":"整體模式"},{"english":"the strongest performer","chinese":"表現最強者"},{"english":"the weakest performer","chinese":"表現最弱者"},{"english":"in terms of percentage-point growth","chinese":"就百分點增長而言"}]},"model-essay-6-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-6-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:6","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-6-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q6","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In today’s highly connected world, digital communication has made it possible for people from different countries to interact instantly and regularly. Through social media, messaging apps and video calls, individuals who would otherwise never meet are now able to exchange ideas, build relationships and work together. This is an overwhelmingly positive development because it expands access to valuable opportunities and promotes greater understanding between societies, although a few disadvantages do exist.","chinese":"在當今高度互聯的世界裡，數位溝通已使來自不同國家的人能夠即時而持續地互動。 透過社交媒體、即時通訊應用程式和視像通話，那些原本根本沒有機會相遇的人，如今也能交流想法、建立關係並彼此合作。 這無疑是一項整體上非常正面的發展，因為它擴大了人們接觸寶貴機會的途徑，並促進了不同社會之間更深入的理解，儘管它確實也存在一些缺點。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The most significant advantage is that online international communication gives people access to relationships and opportunities that geography would normally prevent. A student in Hong Kong, for instance, can seek advice from a university mentor in Britain, join an online discussion group with members from several countries, and later develop academic or professional connections that would have been impossible in the past. This matters because such interaction is not merely casual conversation; it can lead to practical outcomes such as improved education, better employment prospects and broader career networks. Another major benefit is that regular contact with people from other cultures can reduce ignorance and prejudice. When individuals communicate directly with foreigners, they are exposed to different customs, viewpoints and lifestyles, which makes them more open-minded and better prepared for life in a globalised society. Therefore, online international communication is highly beneficial because it creates both practical opportunities and deeper intercultural understanding.","chinese":"最重要的優點是，跨國網上溝通讓人們得以接觸那些原本會因地理限制而無法建立的人際關係與機會。 例如，一名身在香港的學生可以向英國的大學導師請教，加入由多個國家成員組成的網上討論群組，並進一步發展出過去根本不可能建立的學術或專業聯繫。 這一點之所以重要，是因為這種互動並不只是隨意閒聊；它可以帶來實際成果，例如提升教育機會、改善就業前景，以及擴闊職業人脈網絡。 另一項主要好處是，與不同文化背景的人保持經常接觸，可以減少無知與偏見。 當人們直接與外國人交流時，他們會接觸到不同的習俗、觀點和生活方式，這會使他們變得更開放，也更能為全球化社會中的生活作好準備。 因此，跨國網上溝通極具價值，因為它同時創造了實際機會，並促進了更深層次的跨文化理解。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"There are, however, some disadvantages. The most serious is that online platforms can spread false or harmful information across borders with alarming speed. Misleading claims about politics, health or social issues can reach large audiences before they are corrected, which may create confusion or mistrust. In addition, digital interaction can sometimes be less genuine than face-to-face communication. Because people can hide behind anonymous accounts or present edited versions of themselves, online relationships may occasionally be superficial or even deceptive. Nevertheless, these problems are relatively limited and are usually caused by irresponsible use of technology rather than by international communication itself.","chinese":"然而，這種溝通方式也的確存在一些缺點。 其中最嚴重的一點是，網上平台能夠以驚人的速度跨越國界傳播錯誤或有害的信息。 有關政治、健康或社會議題的誤導性言論，往往在被更正之前便已傳播給大量受眾，從而造成混亂或不信任。 此外，數位互動有時不如面對面交流那樣真誠。 由於人們可以躲在匿名帳戶背後，或只展示經過修飾的自己，網上關係有時可能流於表面，甚至帶有欺騙性。 儘管如此，這些問題相對有限，而且通常是由不負責任地使用科技所造成的，而非跨國網上溝通本身所必然導致的結果。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, the ability to communicate online with people from other countries brings substantial benefits, especially by creating opportunities and encouraging intercultural understanding. Although it may also enable misinformation and insincere interaction, these drawbacks are minor in comparison, so the overall effect is clearly positive.","chinese":"總結來說，能夠在網上與來自其他國家的人交流，帶來了重大的好處，尤其體現在創造機會以及促進跨文化理解方面。 雖然它也可能助長錯誤資訊的傳播，以及不夠真誠的互動，但與其優點相比，這些缺點只是次要的。 因此，整體影響顯然是正面的。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"introduction","chinese":"引言"},{"english":"background","chinese":"背景"},{"english":"in today's highly connected world","chinese":"在當今高度互聯的世界"},{"english":"digital communication","chinese":"數碼溝通"},{"english":"make it possible for","chinese":"令……成為可能"},{"english":"interact instantly and regularly","chinese":"即時而定期互動"},{"english":"paraphrasing","chinese":"改寫"},{"english":"social media","chinese":"社交媒體"},{"english":"messaging apps","chinese":"即時通訊應用程式"},{"english":"video calls","chinese":"視像通話"},{"english":"would otherwise never meet","chinese":"否則永遠不會相遇"},{"english":"exchange ideas","chinese":"交流想法"},{"english":"build relationships","chinese":"建立關係"},{"english":"thesis statement","chinese":"中心論點"},{"english":"an overwhelmingly positive development","chinese":"極為正面的發展"},{"english":"expands access to","chinese":"擴大接觸……的機會"},{"english":"valuable opportunities","chinese":"寶貴機會"},{"english":"promotes greater understanding between","chinese":"促進……之間更深入的理解"},{"english":"a few disadvantages do exist","chinese":"確實存在一些缺點"},{"english":"body paragraph","chinese":"正文段落"},{"english":"topic sentence","chinese":"主題句"},{"english":"the most significant advantage","chinese":"最重要的優點"},{"english":"online international communication","chinese":"跨國網上溝通"},{"english":"gives people access to","chinese":"讓人們接觸到"},{"english":"geography would normally prevent","chinese":"地理因素通常會阻礙"},{"english":"supporting detail","chinese":"支持細節"},{"english":"seek advice from","chinese":"向……請教"},{"english":"a university mentor","chinese":"大學導師"},{"english":"join an online discussion group","chinese":"加入網上討論群組"},{"english":"develop academic or professional connections","chinese":"建立學術或專業聯繫"},{"english":"would have been impossible in the past","chinese":"在過去本來不可能"},{"english":"logic chain","chinese":"邏輯鏈"},{"english":"this matters because","chinese":"這一點重要，因為"},{"english":"not merely casual conversation","chinese":"不只是隨意閒聊"},{"english":"lead to practical outcomes","chinese":"帶來實際成果"},{"english":"improved education","chinese":"改善了的教育"},{"english":"better employment prospects","chinese":"更好的就業前景"},{"english":"broader career networks","chinese":"更廣闊的職業人脈網絡"},{"english":"another major benefit","chinese":"另一個主要好處"},{"english":"regular contact with","chinese":"與……定期接觸"},{"english":"other cultures","chinese":"其他文化"},{"english":"reduce ignorance and prejudice","chinese":"減少無知和偏見"},{"english":"communicate directly with","chinese":"直接與……溝通"},{"english":"be exposed to","chinese":"接觸到"},{"english":"different customs","chinese":"不同習俗"},{"english":"viewpoints and lifestyles","chinese":"觀點和生活方式"},{"english":"open-minded","chinese":"思想開放的"},{"english":"better prepared for","chinese":"更能為……作好準備"},{"english":"a globalised society","chinese":"全球化社會"},{"english":"highly beneficial","chinese":"極有益"},{"english":"practical opportunities","chinese":"實際機會"},{"english":"intercultural understanding","chinese":"跨文化理解"},{"english":"there are, however","chinese":"然而，也有"},{"english":"online platforms","chinese":"網上平台"},{"english":"false or harmful information","chinese":"錯誤或有害資料"},{"english":"across borders","chinese":"跨越國界"},{"english":"with alarming speed","chinese":"以驚人的速度"},{"english":"misleading claims","chinese":"誤導性說法"},{"english":"social issues","chinese":"社會議題"},{"english":"reach large audiences","chinese":"傳到大量受眾"},{"english":"before they are corrected","chinese":"在被更正之前"},{"english":"create confusion or mistrust","chinese":"造成混亂或不信任"},{"english":"in addition","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"digital interaction","chinese":"數碼互動"},{"english":"less genuine than","chinese":"不如……真誠"},{"english":"face-to-face communication","chinese":"面對面溝通"},{"english":"hide behind anonymous accounts","chinese":"躲在匿名帳戶背後"},{"english":"anonymous accounts","chinese":"匿名帳戶"},{"english":"present edited versions of themselves","chinese":"展示經修飾的自己"},{"english":"superficial","chinese":"表面的；膚淺的"},{"english":"deceptive","chinese":"具欺騙性的"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"儘管如此"},{"english":"relatively limited","chinese":"相對有限"},{"english":"irresponsible use of technology","chinese":"不負責任地使用科技"},{"english":"rather than by","chinese":"而不是由……造成"},{"english":"international communication itself","chinese":"跨國溝通本身"},{"english":"reiterating stance","chinese":"重申立場"},{"english":"substantial benefits","chinese":"重大好處"},{"english":"encouraging intercultural understanding","chinese":"促進跨文化理解"},{"english":"misinformation","chinese":"錯誤資訊"},{"english":"insincere interaction","chinese":"不真誠的互動"},{"english":"minor in comparison","chinese":"相比之下是次要的"},{"english":"final judgment","chinese":"最終判斷"},{"english":"the overall effect","chinese":"整體影響"},{"english":"clearly positive","chinese":"明顯正面"}]},"model-essay-6-ielts-cause-solution":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-6-ielts-cause-solution","essayKey":"cause-solution:6","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-6-ielts-cause-solution","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/problem-and-cause/EdmundBd9CnS-Q6","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many parts of the world, cities record more crime than villages and small towns. This is not simply because urban residents are less law-abiding; rather, city life creates conditions in which crime is easier to commit and harder to prevent. The most effective response is therefore to reduce both the opportunities for crime and the pressures that push people towards it.","chinese":"在世界許多地方，城市錄得的犯罪比鄉村和小鎮更多。 這並不只是因為城市居民較不守法；相反，城市生活創造了一些條件，使犯罪更容易發生，也更難預防。 因此，最有效的應對方法，是同時減少犯罪機會，以及減輕那些把人推向犯罪的壓力。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One major reason is the anonymity of urban life. In a small rural community, people tend to know one another, so suspicious behaviour is more visible and social pressure acts as a quiet form of control. In a large city, by contrast, offenders can disappear into the crowd. For example, pickpocketing is easier in a packed train station than in a village market, because victims, witnesses and police officers may struggle to identify the offender. Another reason is inequality. Cities often bring wealth and poverty face to face: luxury apartments may stand only a few streets away from overcrowded housing. When people feel excluded from the prosperity around them, some may turn to theft, drug dealing or gang activity, especially if legal routes to success seem blocked.","chinese":"其中一個主要原因，是城市生活的匿名性。 在一個細小的鄉村社區中，人們往往彼此認識，因此可疑行為更容易被看見，而社會壓力也會成為一種安靜但有效的控制力量。 相比之下，在大城市裡，犯罪者可以消失在人群之中。 例如，在擠迫的火車站裡扒竊，會比在鄉村市場中更容易，因為受害者、目擊者和警察都可能難以辨認犯罪者。 另一個原因是不平等。 城市往往使富裕與貧窮正面相遇：豪華住宅可能只與擁擠的住房相隔幾條街。 當人們覺得自己被排除在周圍的繁榮之外時，有些人可能會轉向盜竊、販毒或幫派活動，尤其是在合法取得成功的途徑似乎被堵塞時。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"To reduce urban crime, governments should first design cities in ways that make offending more difficult. Better lighting, reliable public transport, visible community policing and well-maintained public spaces can all reduce the sense that certain areas are unsafe or uncontrolled. For instance, a park that is clean, busy and properly lit is far less likely to become a place for drug dealing or violence. At the same time, prevention must go deeper than surveillance. Cities need stronger youth services, affordable education, job training and support for families under pressure. If young people can see a realistic path into work and belonging, crime becomes less attractive and less necessary.","chinese":"為了減少城市犯罪，政府首先應該以令犯罪更困難的方式來設計城市。 更好的照明、可靠的公共交通、可見的社區警務，以及保養良好的公共空間，都能減少某些地區不安全或失控的感覺。 例如，一個乾淨、熱鬧而且照明充足的公園，遠不容易變成販毒或暴力活動的場所。 與此同時，預防工作必須比監控走得更深入。 城市需要更完善的青少年服務、可負擔的教育、職業培訓，以及對承受壓力的家庭的支援。 如果年輕人能看見一條通向工作和歸屬感的現實道路，犯罪便會變得較不吸引，也較不必要。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, crime is often higher in urban areas because cities combine anonymity with sharper social inequality. Reducing it requires both practical safety measures and long-term social investment.","chinese":"總結來說，城市地區的犯罪率往往較高，是因為城市結合了匿名性和更尖銳的社會不平等。 要減少犯罪，既需要實際的安全措施，也需要長遠的社會投資。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"in many parts of the world","chinese":"在世界很多地方"},{"english":"record more crime than","chinese":"錄得比……更多罪案"},{"english":"villages and small towns","chinese":"鄉村和小鎮"},{"english":"not simply because","chinese":"不只是因為"},{"english":"urban residents","chinese":"城市居民"},{"english":"law-abiding","chinese":"守法的"},{"english":"creates conditions in which","chinese":"創造出……的條件"},{"english":"easier to commit","chinese":"較容易犯下"},{"english":"harder to prevent","chinese":"較難預防"},{"english":"the most effective response","chinese":"最有效的應對方法"},{"english":"opportunities for crime","chinese":"犯罪機會"},{"english":"pressures that push people towards","chinese":"將人推向……的壓力"},{"english":"one major reason","chinese":"一個主要原因"},{"english":"the anonymity of urban life","chinese":"城市生活的匿名性"},{"english":"a small rural community","chinese":"小型鄉郊社區"},{"english":"tend to know one another","chinese":"往往彼此認識"},{"english":"suspicious behaviour","chinese":"可疑行為"},{"english":"more visible","chinese":"更容易被看見"},{"english":"social pressure","chinese":"社會壓力"},{"english":"acts as","chinese":"發揮……作用"},{"english":"a quiet form of control","chinese":"一種無形的控制"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"offenders","chinese":"犯罪者"},{"english":"disappear into the crowd","chinese":"消失在人群中"},{"english":"pickpocketing","chinese":"扒竊"},{"english":"a packed train station","chinese":"擠迫的火車站"},{"english":"village market","chinese":"鄉村市場"},{"english":"victims, witnesses and police officers","chinese":"受害人、目擊者和警員"},{"english":"struggle to identify","chinese":"難以辨認"},{"english":"the offender","chinese":"犯罪者"},{"english":"another reason is","chinese":"另一個原因是"},{"english":"inequality","chinese":"不平等"},{"english":"bring wealth and poverty face to face","chinese":"令富裕與貧窮正面並存"},{"english":"luxury apartments","chinese":"豪華住宅"},{"english":"stand only a few streets away from","chinese":"只相隔幾條街"},{"english":"overcrowded housing","chinese":"過度擠迫的住房"},{"english":"feel excluded from","chinese":"感到被排除於……之外"},{"english":"prosperity around them","chinese":"身邊的繁榮"},{"english":"turn to theft","chinese":"轉向盜竊"},{"english":"drug dealing","chinese":"販毒"},{"english":"gang activity","chinese":"幫派活動"},{"english":"legal routes to success","chinese":"通往成功的合法途徑"},{"english":"seem blocked","chinese":"似乎受阻"},{"english":"reduce urban crime","chinese":"減少城市罪案"},{"english":"design cities in ways that","chinese":"以……的方式設計城市"},{"english":"make offending more difficult","chinese":"令犯罪更困難"},{"english":"better lighting","chinese":"更好的照明"},{"english":"reliable public transport","chinese":"可靠的公共交通"},{"english":"visible community policing","chinese":"明顯可見的社區警政"},{"english":"well-maintained public spaces","chinese":"保養良好的公共空間"},{"english":"reduce the sense that","chinese":"減少……的感覺"},{"english":"unsafe or uncontrolled","chinese":"不安全或無人管理"},{"english":"properly lit","chinese":"照明充足"},{"english":"far less likely to","chinese":"可能性低得多"},{"english":"become a place for","chinese":"成為……的地方"},{"english":"violence","chinese":"暴力"},{"english":"go deeper than","chinese":"必須比……更深入"},{"english":"surveillance","chinese":"監察"},{"english":"youth services","chinese":"青少年服務"},{"english":"affordable education","chinese":"負擔得起的教育"},{"english":"job training","chinese":"職業培訓"},{"english":"support for families under pressure","chinese":"對受壓家庭的支援"},{"english":"a realistic path into work","chinese":"進入職場的現實途徑"},{"english":"belonging","chinese":"歸屬感"},{"english":"less attractive and less necessary","chinese":"較不吸引，也較不必要"},{"english":"higher in urban areas","chinese":"在城市地區較高"},{"english":"combine anonymity with","chinese":"將匿名性與……結合"},{"english":"sharper social inequality","chinese":"更明顯的社會不平等"},{"english":"practical safety measures","chinese":"實際安全措施"},{"english":"long-term social investment","chinese":"長期社會投資"}]},"model-essay-6-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-6-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:6","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-6-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q6","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Many people equate business success with the amount of money a company or entrepreneur earns. However, money is not a true indicator of success, because it can hide weak foundations, poor ethics and unstable growth. A business should instead be judged by whether it creates lasting value for customers, workers and society.","chinese":"許多人把商業成功等同於一間公司或一位企業家所賺取的金錢數量。 然而，金錢並不是成功的真正指標，因為它可能掩蓋薄弱的基礎、不良的道德操守，以及不穩定的增長。 相反，一門生意應該根據它是否為顧客、員工和社會創造持久價值來評判。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main problem with using money as the only measure is that financial results can be misleading. A company may make large profits by cutting corners, underpaying staff or selling low-quality products aggressively. On paper, such a business may look successful; in reality, it is building a house on sand. If customers eventually lose trust, employees leave and the brand becomes associated with dishonesty, its short-term income means very little. In this sense, money shows that a business is earning, but it does not prove that the business is healthy, respected or likely to survive.","chinese":"把金錢作為唯一衡量標準的主要問題在於，財務結果可能具有誤導性。 一間公司可能透過偷工減料、低薪對待員工，或積極銷售低質素產品來獲取龐大利潤。 從表面上看，這樣的生意可能顯得成功；但實際上，它是在沙上建屋，根基並不穩固。 如果顧客最終失去信任、員工離職，而品牌也變得與不誠實聯繫在一起，那麼它的短期收入其實意義不大。 從這個角度來看，金錢只能顯示一門生意正在賺錢，但不能證明這門生意是健康的、受人尊重的，或有可能長久生存。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"There are several better ways to measure business success. One key measure is customer loyalty, because repeated purchases and positive word of mouth show that people genuinely value what the company provides. Another important measure is employee retention. A business whose staff feel fairly treated is more likely to maintain quality, innovation and strong internal culture. Success can also be judged by long-term sustainability, such as whether the company adapts to changing markets without damaging the environment or exploiting vulnerable people. For example, a modest local company that pays fair wages, keeps loyal customers and operates responsibly may be more successful than a larger firm that earns more money but burns trust as quickly as it generates revenue.","chinese":"衡量商業成功有幾種更好的方法。 其中一個關鍵衡量標準是顧客忠誠度，因為重複購買和正面的口碑顯示，人們真正重視這間公司所提供的東西。 另一個重要的衡量標準是員工留任率。 如果一間公司的員工覺得自己受到公平對待，這間公司便更有可能維持品質、創新能力和強大的內部文化。 成功也可以根據長期可持續性來評判，例如公司是否能夠適應不斷變化的市場，同時不破壞環境或剝削弱勢群體。 例如，一間規模不大的本地公司，如果能支付公平薪酬、留住忠實顧客，並以負責任的方式經營，可能比一間賺更多錢、但在創造收入的同時迅速消耗信任的大公司更成功。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, money is not a true indicator of business success. It is only a surface-level sign of financial performance. Real success should be measured by trust, stability, ethical conduct and the ability to create value that lasts.","chinese":"總結來說，金錢並不是商業成功的真正指標。 它只是一種表層的財務表現標誌。 真正的成功應該由信任、穩定性、道德操守，以及創造持久價值的能力來衡量。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"equate business success with","chinese":"將商業成功等同於"},{"english":"the amount of money","chinese":"金錢數額"},{"english":"a company or entrepreneur","chinese":"公司或企業家"},{"english":"earns","chinese":"賺取"},{"english":"a true indicator of","chinese":"……的真正指標"},{"english":"hide weak foundations","chinese":"掩蓋薄弱基礎"},{"english":"poor ethics","chinese":"不良道德操守"},{"english":"unstable growth","chinese":"不穩定的增長"},{"english":"be judged by","chinese":"根據……來判斷"},{"english":"creates lasting value for","chinese":"為……創造持久價值"},{"english":"customers, workers and society","chinese":"顧客、員工和社會"},{"english":"the only measure","chinese":"唯一衡量標準"},{"english":"financial results","chinese":"財務表現"},{"english":"be misleading","chinese":"具誤導性"},{"english":"make large profits","chinese":"賺取巨額利潤"},{"english":"cutting corners","chinese":"走捷徑；偷工減料"},{"english":"underpaying staff","chinese":"給員工過低薪酬"},{"english":"low-quality products","chinese":"低質素產品"},{"english":"selling low-quality products aggressively","chinese":"大力銷售低質素產品"},{"english":"on paper","chinese":"表面上；從數字上看"},{"english":"in reality","chinese":"實際上"},{"english":"building a house on sand","chinese":"建在沙上的房子；基礎不穩"},{"english":"eventually lose trust","chinese":"最終失去信任"},{"english":"employees leave","chinese":"員工離職"},{"english":"become associated with","chinese":"與……聯繫起來"},{"english":"dishonesty","chinese":"不誠實"},{"english":"short-term income","chinese":"短期收入"},{"english":"means very little","chinese":"意義不大"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"prove that","chinese":"證明"},{"english":"healthy, respected or likely to survive","chinese":"健康、受尊重或有可能生存下去"},{"english":"several better ways to","chinese":"幾種更好的方法去"},{"english":"measure business success","chinese":"衡量商業成功"},{"english":"one key measure","chinese":"一個關鍵衡量標準"},{"english":"customer loyalty","chinese":"顧客忠誠度"},{"english":"repeated purchases","chinese":"重複購買"},{"english":"positive word of mouth","chinese":"正面口碑"},{"english":"genuinely value","chinese":"真正重視"},{"english":"what the company provides","chinese":"公司所提供的東西"},{"english":"employee retention","chinese":"員工留任率"},{"english":"feel fairly treated","chinese":"感到受到公平對待"},{"english":"maintain quality","chinese":"維持質素"},{"english":"innovation","chinese":"創新"},{"english":"strong internal culture","chinese":"強大的內部文化"},{"english":"long-term sustainability","chinese":"長遠可持續性"},{"english":"adapts to changing markets","chinese":"適應不斷變化的市場"},{"english":"damaging the environment","chinese":"破壞環境"},{"english":"exploiting vulnerable people","chinese":"剝削弱勢人士"},{"english":"a modest local company","chinese":"規模不大的本地公司"},{"english":"pays fair wages","chinese":"支付公平工資"},{"english":"loyal customers","chinese":"忠實顧客"},{"english":"operates responsibly","chinese":"負責任地營運"},{"english":"a larger firm","chinese":"較大型公司"},{"english":"burns trust","chinese":"消耗信任"},{"english":"generates revenue","chinese":"產生收入"},{"english":"a surface-level sign of","chinese":"……的表面跡象"},{"english":"financial performance","chinese":"財務表現"},{"english":"real success","chinese":"真正的成功"},{"english":"be measured by","chinese":"以……來衡量"},{"english":"trust","chinese":"信任"},{"english":"stability","chinese":"穩定性"},{"english":"ethical conduct","chinese":"道德行為"},{"english":"the ability to create value that lasts","chinese":"創造持久價值的能力"}]},"model-essay-6-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-6-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:6","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-6-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q6","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Some people argue that a business can only become successful if it offers a unique product. While originality can certainly help a company stand out, I do not believe it is the only factor behind commercial success. In my view, a company succeeds mainly because it understands its customers, manages its operations well, and builds long-term trust.","chinese":"有些人認為，一間企業只有在提供獨特產品的情況下，才能取得成功。 雖然原創性確實能幫助一間公司脫穎而出，但我不認為它是商業成功背後的唯一因素。 在我看來，一間公司之所以成功，主要是因為它了解顧客、良好管理營運，並建立長期信任。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first major factor is whether a company can meet real customer needs. A product does not have to be completely original if it solves a problem better, faster, or more conveniently than its competitors. In fact, many successful businesses sell ordinary products, such as food, clothing, or household goods, but they do so in a way that customers find reliable and accessible. For example, a small café may not offer anything revolutionary, yet it can become profitable if it provides good coffee, fair prices, and a comfortable atmosphere. This shows that success often depends less on being unique and more on being useful, consistent, and relevant to the market.","chinese":"第一個主要因素是，一間公司能否滿足真正的顧客需求。 如果一件產品能比競爭對手更好、更快或更方便地解決問題，它並不一定需要完全原創 事實上，許多成功的企業出售的都是普通產品，例如食物、衣服或家居用品，但它們以一種讓顧客覺得可靠且容易接觸的方式去經營。 例如，一間小咖啡店未必提供任何革命性的東西，但如果它能提供好咖啡、公道價格和舒適環境，它仍然可以獲利。 這表明，成功往往較少取決於是否獨特，而更多取決於是否實用、穩定，並且符合市場需要。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important factor is the quality of management. Even an excellent product can fail if a company has poor leadership, weak financial control, or careless customer service. Good managers make sensible decisions about pricing, staff training, marketing, and cost control. They also adapt when the market changes, instead of clinging to old methods. For instance, a business that responds quickly to online shopping trends or changing consumer habits is more likely to survive than one that refuses to modernise. In addition, companies that treat customers well can develop a strong reputation, and this reputation becomes a powerful asset over time.","chinese":"另一個重要因素是管理質素。 即使產品十分出色，如果公司領導不善、財務控制薄弱，或顧客服務粗心大意，它仍然可能失敗。 優秀的管理者會在定價、員工培訓、市場推廣和成本控制方面作出明智決定。 當市場發生變化時，他們也會作出調整，而不是死守舊方法。 例如，一間能夠快速回應網上購物趨勢或消費者習慣變化的企業，比一間拒絕現代化的企業更有可能生存下來。 此外，善待顧客的公司能夠建立良好聲譽，而這種聲譽隨著時間會成為一項強大的資"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, having a unique product can give a business an initial advantage, but it is not the only route to success. The most successful companies are those that understand their market, operate efficiently, adapt intelligently, and earn the trust of their customers.","chinese":"總結來說，擁有獨特產品可以給企業帶來初步優勢，但這並不是通往成功的唯一途徑。 最成功的公司，是那些了解市場、高效營運、明智適應變化，並贏得顧客信任的公司。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"can only become successful if","chinese":"只有在……情況下才能成功"},{"english":"offers a unique product","chinese":"提供獨特產品"},{"english":"originality","chinese":"原創性"},{"english":"stand out","chinese":"突圍而出；突出"},{"english":"the only factor behind","chinese":"……背後的唯一因素"},{"english":"commercial success","chinese":"商業成功"},{"english":"In my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"succeeds mainly because","chinese":"成功主要是因為"},{"english":"understands its customers","chinese":"了解顧客"},{"english":"manages its operations well","chinese":"妥善管理營運"},{"english":"builds long-term trust","chinese":"建立長遠信任"},{"english":"the first major factor","chinese":"第一個主要因素"},{"english":"meet real customer needs","chinese":"滿足真正的顧客需要"},{"english":"does not have to be","chinese":"不一定要"},{"english":"completely original","chinese":"完全原創"},{"english":"solves a problem","chinese":"解決問題"},{"english":"better, faster, or more conveniently","chinese":"更好、更快或更方便地"},{"english":"than its competitors","chinese":"比競爭對手"},{"english":"In fact","chinese":"事實上"},{"english":"successful businesses","chinese":"成功企業"},{"english":"ordinary products","chinese":"普通產品"},{"english":"household goods","chinese":"家居用品"},{"english":"do so in a way that","chinese":"以一種……的方式這樣做"},{"english":"find reliable and accessible","chinese":"覺得可靠而容易接觸"},{"english":"a small café","chinese":"小型咖啡店"},{"english":"anything revolutionary","chinese":"任何革命性的東西"},{"english":"become profitable","chinese":"變得有盈利"},{"english":"fair prices","chinese":"公道價格"},{"english":"a comfortable atmosphere","chinese":"舒適的氣氛"},{"english":"This shows that","chinese":"這顯示"},{"english":"depends less on","chinese":"較少取決於"},{"english":"being unique","chinese":"獨特性"},{"english":"more on being useful","chinese":"更多取決於有用"},{"english":"consistent","chinese":"穩定一致"},{"english":"relevant to the market","chinese":"符合市場需要"},{"english":"another important factor","chinese":"另一個重要因素"},{"english":"the quality of management","chinese":"管理質素"},{"english":"an excellent product","chinese":"出色產品"},{"english":"poor leadership","chinese":"糟糕的領導"},{"english":"weak financial control","chinese":"薄弱的財務控制"},{"english":"careless customer service","chinese":"粗心大意的客戶服務"},{"english":"make sensible decisions about","chinese":"就……作出明智決定"},{"english":"pricing","chinese":"定價"},{"english":"staff training","chinese":"員工培訓"},{"english":"cost control","chinese":"成本控制"},{"english":"adapt when the market changes","chinese":"在市場變化時適應"},{"english":"instead of clinging to","chinese":"而不是死守"},{"english":"old methods","chinese":"舊方法"},{"english":"responds quickly to","chinese":"迅速回應"},{"english":"online shopping trends","chinese":"網上購物趨勢"},{"english":"changing consumer habits","chinese":"不斷改變的消費者習慣"},{"english":"more likely to survive","chinese":"更有可能生存下去"},{"english":"refuses to modernise","chinese":"拒絕現代化"},{"english":"In addition","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"treat customers well","chinese":"善待顧客"},{"english":"develop a strong reputation","chinese":"建立良好聲譽"},{"english":"a powerful asset","chinese":"強大的資產"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨時間"},{"english":"give a business an initial advantage","chinese":"給企業初期優勢"},{"english":"an initial advantage","chinese":"初期優勢"},{"english":"the only route to success","chinese":"成功的唯一途徑"},{"english":"understand their market","chinese":"了解市場"},{"english":"operate efficiently","chinese":"高效營運"},{"english":"adapt intelligently","chinese":"明智地適應"},{"english":"earn the trust of","chinese":"贏得……的信任"}]},"model-essay-6-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-6-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:6","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-6-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q6","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Because retail markets are increasingly dominated by supermarket chains, independent shops in many towns now struggle to survive. I completely agree that the disappearance of small local businesses can lead to the death of local communities, because these businesses sustain both social relationships and the economic life on which community identity depends.","chinese":"由於零售市場愈來愈被連鎖超級市場主導，許多城鎮中的獨立商店如今都在艱難求存。 我完全同意，小型本地企業的消失可能會導致地方社區走向衰亡，因為這些企業維繫着社區賴以建立自身認同的人際關係，以及其所依存的經濟生活。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"First, small businesses function as social anchors rather than mere places of transaction. When residents regularly visit the same bakery, grocer or café, they develop familiarity with the people who work there. Over time, these repeated exchanges create trust, local knowledge and a sense of belonging. This matters especially for older residents and people who live alone, for whom such encounters may form an important part of daily life. Once these shops close, shopping becomes more impersonal, as people simply visit a supermarket, pay and leave. For example, an elderly customer who once spoke to a local shopkeeper every morning may lose one of his few social contacts. As a result, the informal ties that hold a neighbourhood together begin to weaken.","chinese":"首先，小型企業的作用不只是交易場所，更是社交關係的支點。 當居民經常光顧同一家麵包店、雜貨店或咖啡館時，他們便會逐漸熟悉在那裏工作的人。 隨着時間過去，這些一再出現的互動會建立起信任、對地方的了解，以及歸屬感。 這一點對年長居民和獨居人士尤其重要，因為這類相遇很可能構成了他們日常生活中重要的一部分。 一旦這些商店倒閉，購物便會變得更加缺乏人情味，因為人們只是走進超市、付款，然後離開。 例如，一位原本每早都會和本地店主交談的長者，可能會失去他少數的社交接觸之一 結果，維繫整個社區的非正式聯繫便開始削弱。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Local businesses also keep money and character within the area. Because they are often owned by local families, their earnings are more likely to be reinvested nearby through local hiring, nearby suppliers and support for neighbourhood events. This creates a cycle in which local spending helps other local services survive. Independent shops also give a town centre its distinctive identity; a street filled with family-run bookstores, cafés and food stalls reflects the people who live there. By contrast, when chain supermarkets dominate, profits and decision-making are centralised, and high streets gradually become uniform. A place may still contain shops and consumers, but it no longer functions as a genuine community in the fuller social sense.","chinese":"本地企業也能把資金和地方特色留在社區之內。 由於它們往往由本地家庭擁有，因此其收益更有可能透過聘用本地員工、採用附近供應商，以及支持社區活動等方式，再投放回當地。 這便形成了一個循環：本地消費幫助其他本地服務持續生存。 獨立商店也賦予城鎮中心鮮明而獨特的身分；一條街若佈滿家庭經營的書店、咖啡館和小吃攤，便能反映出居住於此的人們的面貌。 相反，當連鎖超級市場佔據主導地位時，利潤和決策權都會被集中起來，而商業街也會逐漸變得千篇一律。 一個地方也許仍然有商店和消費者，但從更完整的社會意義來看，它已不再作為一個真正的社區而存在。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I strongly agree that the closure of small local businesses can bring about the death of local communities. Without them, neighbourhoods lose both the human relationships and the locally rooted economic networks that make communal life possible.","chinese":"總而言之，我強烈同意，小型本地企業的倒閉可能會導致地方社區的消亡。 沒有了它們，社區失去的將不只是人與人之間的聯繫，還有那些扎根於本地、使共同生活成為可能的經濟網絡。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"retail markets","chinese":"零售市場"},{"english":"be increasingly dominated by","chinese":"越來越受……主導"},{"english":"supermarket chains","chinese":"連鎖超級市場"},{"english":"independent shops","chinese":"獨立店舖"},{"english":"struggle to survive","chinese":"難以生存"},{"english":"the disappearance of","chinese":"……的消失"},{"english":"small local businesses","chinese":"本地小商戶"},{"english":"lead to","chinese":"導致"},{"english":"the death of local communities","chinese":"本地社區的消亡"},{"english":"sustain both","chinese":"同時維持"},{"english":"social relationships","chinese":"社交關係"},{"english":"the economic life","chinese":"經濟生活；經濟活力"},{"english":"community identity","chinese":"社區身份"},{"english":"depend on","chinese":"取決於；依賴"},{"english":"function as","chinese":"發揮……作用"},{"english":"social anchors","chinese":"社交支柱；社區連繫的支點"},{"english":"rather than mere places of transaction","chinese":"而不只是交易場所"},{"english":"places of transaction","chinese":"交易場所"},{"english":"regularly visit","chinese":"定期到訪"},{"english":"develop familiarity with","chinese":"對……產生熟悉感"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨時間"},{"english":"repeated exchanges","chinese":"重複的交流"},{"english":"create trust","chinese":"建立信任"},{"english":"local knowledge","chinese":"本地資訊；對本地的了解"},{"english":"a sense of belonging","chinese":"歸屬感"},{"english":"this matters especially for","chinese":"這對……尤其重要"},{"english":"older residents","chinese":"年長居民"},{"english":"live alone","chinese":"獨居"},{"english":"for whom","chinese":"對……來說"},{"english":"such encounters","chinese":"這類相遇；這類接觸"},{"english":"form an important part of","chinese":"構成……的重要部分"},{"english":"daily life","chinese":"日常生活"},{"english":"once these shops close","chinese":"一旦這些店舖結業"},{"english":"become more impersonal","chinese":"變得更沒有人情味"},{"english":"simply visit a supermarket, pay and leave","chinese":"只是去超級市場付款後離開"},{"english":"a local shopkeeper","chinese":"本地店主"},{"english":"one of his few social contacts","chinese":"他為數不多的社交接觸之一"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"informal ties","chinese":"非正式聯繫"},{"english":"hold a neighbourhood together","chinese":"凝聚社區"},{"english":"begin to weaken","chinese":"開始減弱"},{"english":"keep money and character within the area","chinese":"將金錢和特色留在區內"},{"english":"be owned by local families","chinese":"由本地家庭擁有"},{"english":"earnings","chinese":"收入；收益"},{"english":"be reinvested nearby","chinese":"在附近再投資"},{"english":"local hiring","chinese":"本地招聘"},{"english":"nearby suppliers","chinese":"附近供應商"},{"english":"support for neighbourhood events","chinese":"對社區活動的支持"},{"english":"create a cycle in which","chinese":"形成一個……的循環"},{"english":"local spending","chinese":"本地消費"},{"english":"local services","chinese":"本地服務"},{"english":"give a town centre its distinctive identity","chinese":"賦予市中心獨特身份"},{"english":"distinctive identity","chinese":"獨特身份；獨有特色"},{"english":"family-run bookstores","chinese":"家庭經營的書店"},{"english":"food stalls","chinese":"小食檔；食物攤檔"},{"english":"reflect the people who live there","chinese":"反映當地居民的特色"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相反"},{"english":"chain supermarkets","chinese":"連鎖超級市場"},{"english":"dominate","chinese":"主導"},{"english":"profits and decision-making","chinese":"利潤和決策"},{"english":"be centralised","chinese":"被集中"},{"english":"high streets","chinese":"主要商業街"},{"english":"gradually become uniform","chinese":"逐漸變得千篇一律"},{"english":"contain shops and consumers","chinese":"有店舖和消費者"},{"english":"no longer functions as","chinese":"不再發揮……作用"},{"english":"a genuine community","chinese":"真正的社區"},{"english":"in the fuller social sense","chinese":"從更完整的社會意義上"},{"english":"the closure of","chinese":"……的結業"},{"english":"bring about","chinese":"帶來；導致"},{"english":"without them","chinese":"沒有它們"},{"english":"human relationships","chinese":"人與人之間的關係"},{"english":"locally rooted economic networks","chinese":"扎根本地的經濟網絡"},{"english":"communal life","chinese":"社群生活；社區生活"},{"english":"make communal life possible","chinese":"令社區生活成為可能"}]},"model-essay-6-ielts-task1-bar-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-6-ielts-task1-bar-charts","essayKey":"bar-charts:6","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-6-ielts-task1-bar-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/bar-charts/bar-chart-6","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The bar chart compares the percentages of Australian men and women in six age groups who did regular physical activity in 2010.","chinese":"這張柱狀圖比較了 2010 年澳洲男性和女性在六個年齡組中定期進行體育活動的百分比。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, women were more active than men in all age groups except 15–24. Male participation was highest among the youngest adults, then fell to a low in middle age before rising gradually, while the female figures remained relatively steady at around 48% to 53%.","chinese":"整體而言，除了 15 至 24 歲組之外，女性在所有年齡組中都比男性更活躍。 男性參與率在最年輕的成年人中最高，之後下降至中年低點，然後逐漸回升；相比之下，女性數據則相對穩定，大約維持在 48% 至 53% 之間。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In the 15–24 group, 52.8% of men exercised regularly, compared with 47.7% of women. The pattern then reversed: male participation dropped to 42.2% among 25- to 34-year-olds and reached its lowest point, 39.5%, in the 35–44 category. By contrast, the corresponding female rates rose from 48.9% to 52.5%, creating the largest gender gap, at 13 percentage points.","chinese":"在 15 至 24 歲組中， 52.8% 的男性定期運動，而女性則為 47.7% 。 之後，這一模式出現逆轉： 25 至 34 歲男性的參與率下降至 42.2% ，並在 35 至 44 歲組達到最低點，為 39.5% 。 相比之下，相應的女性比率從 48.9% 上升至 52.5% ，形成了最大的性別差距，達13 個百分點。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"In the older age groups, the male figure recovered from 43.1% for those aged 45–54 to 45.1% among 55–64s and 46.7% among people aged 65 and over. Women reached their peak in the 45–54 group, at 53.3%, and remained almost as high for 55–64s, at 53.0%. In the oldest cohort, however, female participation fell to 47.1%, almost matching the male rate.","chinese":"在較年長的年齡組中，男性數據有所回升： 45 至 54 歲組為 43.1% ， 55 至 64 歲組升至 45.1% ， 65 歲及以上組則達到 46.7% 。 女性在 45 至 54 歲組達到最高點，為 53.3% ；在 55 至 64 歲組中仍幾乎同樣高，為。 然而，在最年長的群體中，女性參與率下降至 47.1% ，幾乎與男性比率相同。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"compares the percentages of","chinese":"比較……的百分比"},{"english":"Australian men and women","chinese":"澳洲男性及女性"},{"english":"in six age groups","chinese":"在六個年齡組別中"},{"english":"did regular physical activity","chinese":"定期做體能活動"},{"english":"regular physical activity","chinese":"定期體能活動"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"more active than","chinese":"比……更活躍"},{"english":"in all age groups except","chinese":"除……外所有年齡組別"},{"english":"male participation","chinese":"男性參與率"},{"english":"was highest among","chinese":"在……之中最高"},{"english":"the youngest adults","chinese":"最年輕的成年人"},{"english":"fell to a low","chinese":"跌至低位"},{"english":"in middle age","chinese":"在中年時期"},{"english":"before rising gradually","chinese":"隨後逐漸上升"},{"english":"female figures","chinese":"女性數字"},{"english":"remained relatively steady","chinese":"保持相對穩定"},{"english":"at around 48% to 53%","chinese":"約在48%至53%之間"},{"english":"in the 15–24 group","chinese":"在15至24歲組別中"},{"english":"exercised regularly","chinese":"定期運動"},{"english":"compared with","chinese":"與……相比"},{"english":"the pattern then reversed","chinese":"之後模式逆轉"},{"english":"dropped to","chinese":"下降至"},{"english":"among 25- to 34-year-olds","chinese":"在25至34歲人士之中"},{"english":"reached its lowest point","chinese":"達到最低點"},{"english":"the 35–44 category","chinese":"35至44歲類別"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"the corresponding female rates","chinese":"相應的女性比率"},{"english":"rose from 48.9% to 52.5%","chinese":"由48.9%上升至52.5%"},{"english":"creating the largest gender gap","chinese":"形成最大的性別差距"},{"english":"the largest gender gap","chinese":"最大的性別差距"},{"english":"at 13 percentage points","chinese":"達13個百分點"},{"english":"percentage points","chinese":"百分點"},{"english":"in the older age groups","chinese":"在較年長組別中"},{"english":"the male figure","chinese":"男性數字"},{"english":"recovered from","chinese":"從……回升"},{"english":"those aged 45–54","chinese":"45至54歲人士"},{"english":"among 55–64s","chinese":"在55至64歲人士之中"},{"english":"people aged 65 and over","chinese":"65歲或以上人士"},{"english":"reached their peak","chinese":"達到高峰"},{"english":"in the 45–54 group","chinese":"在45至54歲組別中"},{"english":"remained almost as high","chinese":"仍然幾乎一樣高"},{"english":"for 55–64s","chinese":"對55至64歲人士而言"},{"english":"in the oldest cohort","chinese":"在最年長群組中"},{"english":"female participation","chinese":"女性參與率"},{"english":"fell to 47.1%","chinese":"下降至47.1%"},{"english":"almost matching the male rate","chinese":"幾乎與男性比率相同"},{"english":"the male rate","chinese":"男性比率"}]},"model-essay-6-ielts-task1-line-graph":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-6-ielts-task1-line-graph","essayKey":"line-graph:6","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-6-ielts-task1-line-graph","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/line-graphs/line-graph-6","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The line graph illustrates tourist numbers on a Caribbean island between 2010 and 2017, separating visitors who stayed on cruise ships from those accommodated on the island.","chinese":"這張折線圖說明了 2010 年至 2017 年間前往某個加勒比海島嶼的遊客人數，並區分了住在遊輪上的遊客和住在島上的遊客。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, total arrivals rose substantially, more than tripling across the period. Island-based tourists were the larger group at first, but cruise passengers grew much faster and had become the leading category by 2017.","chinese":"整體而言，總到訪人數在整段期間大幅上升，增加了超過三倍。 起初，住在島上的遊客是較大的群體，但遊輪遊客增長得更快，並在 2017 年成為主要類別。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 2010, the island attracted 1 million visitors, about three quarters of whom stayed on the island. This total rose steadily to 2 million in 2013, when island-based tourists reached 1.5 million. Over the same early period, the cruise-ship figure moved unevenly, increasing from 250,000 to 500,000 in 2011 before falling back to 250,000 in 2012.","chinese":"2010 年，該島吸引了 100 萬名遊客，其中約四分之三住在島上。 到 2013 年，總遊客人數穩步上升至 200 萬，而當時住在島上的遊客達到 150 萬。 在同一前期階段，遊輪遊客人數變化不太穩定，先從 25 萬上升至 2011 年的 50萬，然後在 2012 年回落至 25 萬。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"From 2014 onwards, cruise passengers became the main driver of growth. Their number climbed from 1 million in 2014 to 1.5 million in 2016, overtaking the island-based group, before reaching 2 million in 2017. By contrast, tourists staying on the island remained close to 1.5 million after 2013, except for a slight fall in 2016. Consequently, total arrivals plateaued at around 2.75 million in 2015 and 2016, then rose sharply to 3.5 million.","chinese":"從 2014 年起，遊輪遊客成為推動增長的主要因素。 其人數從 2014 年的 100 萬上升至 2016 年的 150 萬，超過了住在島上的遊客，並在 2017 年達到 200 萬。 相比之下， 2013 年之後，住在島上的遊客人數大致維持在接近 150 萬的水平，只是在 2016 年略有下降。 因此，總到訪人數在 2015 年和 2016 年停留在約 275 萬，隨後急升至 350 萬。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"line graph","chinese":"折線圖"},{"english":"illustrates tourist numbers","chinese":"顯示遊客人數"},{"english":"tourist numbers","chinese":"遊客人數"},{"english":"a Caribbean island","chinese":"一個加勒比海島嶼"},{"english":"between 2010 and 2017","chinese":"在2010年至2017年間"},{"english":"separating visitors who stayed on cruise ships from","chinese":"將住在郵輪上的遊客與……分開"},{"english":"stayed on cruise ships","chinese":"住在郵輪上"},{"english":"accommodated on the island","chinese":"在島上住宿"},{"english":"total arrivals","chinese":"總到訪人數"},{"english":"rose substantially","chinese":"大幅上升"},{"english":"more than tripling","chinese":"增加至三倍以上"},{"english":"across the period","chinese":"在整段期間"},{"english":"island-based tourists","chinese":"住在島上的遊客"},{"english":"the larger group at first","chinese":"起初是較大組別"},{"english":"cruise passengers","chinese":"郵輪乘客"},{"english":"grew much faster","chinese":"增長快得多"},{"english":"had become the leading category","chinese":"已成為主要類別"},{"english":"leading category","chinese":"主要類別"},{"english":"by 2017","chinese":"到2017年時"},{"english":"attracted 1 million visitors","chinese":"吸引100萬名遊客"},{"english":"about three quarters of whom","chinese":"其中約四分之三"},{"english":"stayed on the island","chinese":"住在島上"},{"english":"this total rose steadily to","chinese":"這個總數穩步上升至"},{"english":"rose steadily to","chinese":"穩步上升至"},{"english":"when island-based tourists reached","chinese":"當時住在島上的遊客達到"},{"english":"reached 1.5 million","chinese":"達到150萬"},{"english":"over the same early period","chinese":"在同一早期時段"},{"english":"cruise-ship figure","chinese":"郵輪遊客數字"},{"english":"moved unevenly","chinese":"走勢不平均"},{"english":"increasing from…to…","chinese":"由……增加至……"},{"english":"before falling back to","chinese":"之後回落至"},{"english":"falling back to","chinese":"回落至"},{"english":"from 2014 onwards","chinese":"從2014年起"},{"english":"the main driver of growth","chinese":"增長的主要推動因素"},{"english":"driver of growth","chinese":"增長推動因素"},{"english":"their number climbed from…to…","chinese":"其數字由……上升至……"},{"english":"climbed from 1 million to 1.5 million","chinese":"由100萬上升至150萬"},{"english":"overtaking","chinese":"超越"},{"english":"the island-based group","chinese":"住在島上的組別"},{"english":"before reaching 2 million","chinese":"之後達到200萬"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"tourists staying on the island","chinese":"住在島上的遊客"},{"english":"remained close to","chinese":"維持接近"},{"english":"after 2013","chinese":"2013年之後"},{"english":"except for","chinese":"除了……之外"},{"english":"a slight fall","chinese":"輕微下降"},{"english":"consequently","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"plateaued at around","chinese":"穩定在約……"},{"english":"around 2.75 million","chinese":"約275萬"},{"english":"in the final two years","chinese":"在最後兩年"},{"english":"then rose sharply to","chinese":"然後急升至"},{"english":"rose sharply to","chinese":"急升至"},{"english":"3.5 million","chinese":"350萬"},{"english":"visitor arrivals","chinese":"遊客到訪人數"},{"english":"cruise-ship visitors","chinese":"郵輪遊客"},{"english":"island accommodation","chinese":"島上住宿"},{"english":"long-term increase","chinese":"長期增長"},{"english":"overall growth","chinese":"整體增長"}]},"model-essay-6-ielts-task1-maps":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-6-ielts-task1-maps","essayKey":"maps:6","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-6-ielts-task1-maps","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/maps/maps-6","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The two plans illustrate the layout of Grange Park when it opened in 1920 and its arrangement today.","chinese":"這兩張平面圖展示了格蘭奇公園在 1920 年首次開放時的布局，以及它今天的安排。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the park has been substantially modernised, with recreational facilities such as an amphitheatre, café, children’s play area and underground parking added. However, the two main entrances on Arnold Avenue and Eldon Street have been retained, and rose gardens remain important, although they have been reduced and reorganised.","chinese":"整體而言，該公園已大幅現代化，新增了露天劇場、咖啡館、兒童遊樂區和地下停車場等休閒設施。 然而，位於阿諾德大道和埃爾登街的兩個主要入口被保留下來，而玫瑰園仍然是重要元素，儘管它們的數量已減少並被重新安排。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 1920, the park had a formal layout. A fountain stood at its centre, while a stage for musicians occupied the western side. Three rose gardens were located in the northwest, northeast and southwest corners, and seating was distributed around the edges. The eastern half contained a pond for water plants in the northeast and a glasshouse in the southeast.","chinese":"在 1920 年，該公園具有較正式的布局。 一座噴泉位於公園中央，而音樂家表演台則佔據西側位置。 三個玫瑰園分別位於西北角、東北角和西南角，座位則分布在公園邊緣一帶。 公園東半部包含位於東北方的水生植物池，以及位於東南方的玻璃溫室。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Today, the central fountain has been replaced by a square rose garden, surrounded by seats on all four sides. The former musicians’ stage has given way to a larger amphitheatre for concerts. On the eastern side, the old pond and glasshouse have disappeared; in their place are a café, a children’s play area and a water feature. A new entrance to an underground car park has also been introduced from the southeast.","chinese":"如今，中央噴泉已被一個方形玫瑰園取代，而其四周均設有座位。 原本的音樂家表演台已被一個更大的露天音樂會劇場取代。 在東側，舊有的池塘和玻璃溫室已經消失；取而代之的是咖啡館、兒童遊樂區和水景設施。 此外，東南方也新增了一個通往地下停車場的入口。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the plans below","chinese":"以下平面圖"},{"english":"a public park","chinese":"公園"},{"english":"when it first opened","chinese":"初次開放時"},{"english":"the same park today","chinese":"現今同一個公園"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"by selecting and reporting","chinese":"透過選取並報告……"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"illustrate the layout of","chinese":"展示……的佈局"},{"english":"Grange Park","chinese":"Grange Park 公園"},{"english":"its arrangement today","chinese":"其現今佈局"},{"english":"has been substantially modernised","chinese":"已大幅現代化"},{"english":"recreational facilities","chinese":"康樂設施"},{"english":"such as","chinese":"例如"},{"english":"an amphitheatre","chinese":"露天劇場"},{"english":"children's play area","chinese":"兒童遊樂區"},{"english":"underground parking","chinese":"地下停車場"},{"english":"have been retained","chinese":"得以保留"},{"english":"main entrances","chinese":"主要入口"},{"english":"rose gardens remain important","chinese":"玫瑰園仍然重要"},{"english":"have been reduced and reorganised","chinese":"已縮減並重新規劃"},{"english":"had a formal layout","chinese":"採用正式對稱的佈局"},{"english":"stood at its centre","chinese":"位於其中央"},{"english":"a fountain","chinese":"噴水池"},{"english":"a stage for musicians","chinese":"音樂家表演台"},{"english":"occupied the western side","chinese":"佔據西面"},{"english":"three rose gardens","chinese":"三個玫瑰園"},{"english":"were located in","chinese":"位於……"},{"english":"the north-west corner","chinese":"西北角"},{"english":"the north-east corner","chinese":"東北角"},{"english":"the south-west corner","chinese":"西南角"},{"english":"seating was distributed around","chinese":"座位分佈於……周圍"},{"english":"around the edges","chinese":"沿邊緣"},{"english":"the eastern half","chinese":"東半部"},{"english":"contained","chinese":"設有；包含"},{"english":"a pond for water plants","chinese":"水生植物池"},{"english":"water plants","chinese":"水生植物"},{"english":"a glasshouse","chinese":"溫室"},{"english":"the south-east","chinese":"東南面"},{"english":"the central fountain","chinese":"中央噴水池"},{"english":"has been replaced by","chinese":"已被……取代"},{"english":"a square rose garden","chinese":"正方形玫瑰園"},{"english":"surrounded by","chinese":"被……包圍"},{"english":"on all four sides","chinese":"在四邊"},{"english":"the former musicians' stage","chinese":"昔日的音樂家表演台"},{"english":"has given way to","chinese":"已讓位予……；被……取代"},{"english":"a larger amphitheatre","chinese":"較大型露天劇場"},{"english":"for concerts","chinese":"用作舉行音樂會"},{"english":"on the eastern side","chinese":"在東面"},{"english":"have disappeared","chinese":"已消失"},{"english":"in their place","chinese":"取而代之的是"},{"english":"a water feature","chinese":"水景設施"},{"english":"a new entrance to","chinese":"通往……的新入口"},{"english":"underground car park","chinese":"地下停車場"},{"english":"has also been introduced","chinese":"亦已增設"},{"english":"from the south-east","chinese":"從東南面"},{"english":"remain in place","chinese":"保持原位"},{"english":"be reorganised around","chinese":"圍繞……重新規劃"},{"english":"modern visitor facilities","chinese":"現代化遊客設施"},{"english":"leisure-oriented space","chinese":"以休閒為主的空間"},{"english":"formal garden features","chinese":"正式園林特色"},{"english":"be converted into","chinese":"被改造成"},{"english":"the overall structure","chinese":"整體結構"},{"english":"the original layout","chinese":"原本佈局"},{"english":"the present layout","chinese":"現時佈局"}]},"model-essay-6-ielts-task1-mixed-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-6-ielts-task1-mixed-charts","essayKey":"mixed-charts:6","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-6-ielts-task1-mixed-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/mixed-charts/mixed-charts-6","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The table and pie charts compare attendance at Ashdown Museum and visitors’ satisfaction levels in the years before and after its refurbishment.","chinese":"該表格和圓餅圖比較了阿什當博物館翻新前後兩年中的參觀人數，以及訪客對參觀體驗的滿意程度。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the museum became both more popular and more highly rated after the work was completed. The total number of visitors rose markedly, while positive responses replaced dissatisfaction as the dominant pattern.","chinese":"整體而言，翻新工程完成後，該博物館不但更受歡迎，也獲得了更高的評價。 總訪客人數明顯上升，而正面回應也取代不滿意，成為主要的滿意度模式。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In terms of attendance, the museum received 74,000 visitors before the refurbishment, but this figure increased to 92,000 in the following year, a rise of 18,000. The improvement in satisfaction was even more striking. Before the changes, only 15% of respondents said they were very satisfied and a further 30% were satisfied, meaning that positive feedback accounted for less than half of all responses. After refurbishment, however, these two categories climbed to 35% and 40%, respectively, so three quarters of visitors expressed satisfaction.","chinese":"就參觀人數而言，該博物館在翻新前一年接待了 74,000 名訪客，但在翻新後一年，這一數字上升至 92,000 ，增加了 18,000 人。 滿意度方面的改善甚至更加明顯。 在翻新前，只有 15% 的受訪者表示非常滿意，另有 30% 表示滿意，這意味著正面回饋佔所有回應不到一半。 然而，翻新後，這兩個類別分別上升至 35% 和 40% ，因此有四分之三的訪客表達了滿意。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"By contrast, the proportion of dissatisfied visitors fell sharply. In the year before refurbishment, 40% reported being dissatisfied, making this the largest single group, while 10% were very dissatisfied. In the year after refurbishment, these figures dropped to 15% and 5%, respectively. The share giving no response remained unchanged at 5% in both years.","chinese":"相比之下，不滿意訪客的比例大幅下降。 在翻新前一年， 40% 的訪客表示不滿意，使其成為最大的單一組別，而另有10% 表示非常不滿意。 在翻新後一年，這兩項數字分別下降至 15% 和 5% 。 沒有回應的比例在兩年中都保持在 5% ，沒有變化。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the table below","chinese":"以下表格"},{"english":"the number of visitors","chinese":"參觀人數"},{"english":"Ashdown Museum","chinese":"Ashdown博物館"},{"english":"during the year before","chinese":"在……前一年期間"},{"english":"during the year after","chinese":"在……後一年期間"},{"english":"was refurbished","chinese":"經過翻新"},{"english":"the results of surveys","chinese":"調查結果"},{"english":"asking visitors how satisfied they were","chinese":"詢問遊客滿意程度"},{"english":"how satisfied they were with","chinese":"對……有多滿意"},{"english":"during the same two periods","chinese":"在同樣兩個時期"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"by selecting and reporting","chinese":"透過選取並報告……"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"the table and pie charts","chinese":"表格及圓形圖"},{"english":"compare attendance at","chinese":"比較……的入場人數"},{"english":"visitors' satisfaction levels","chinese":"遊客滿意程度"},{"english":"in the years before and after","chinese":"在……前後兩年"},{"english":"its refurbishment","chinese":"其翻新工程"},{"english":"became both more popular and more highly rated","chinese":"變得更受歡迎且評價更高"},{"english":"more popular","chinese":"更受歡迎"},{"english":"more highly rated","chinese":"評價更高"},{"english":"after the work was completed","chinese":"工程完成後"},{"english":"the total number of visitors","chinese":"總參觀人數"},{"english":"rose markedly","chinese":"顯著上升"},{"english":"positive responses","chinese":"正面回應"},{"english":"replaced dissatisfaction as","chinese":"取代不滿成為……"},{"english":"dissatisfaction","chinese":"不滿"},{"english":"the dominant pattern","chinese":"主要模式"},{"english":"in terms of attendance","chinese":"就參觀人數而言"},{"english":"received 74,000 visitors","chinese":"接待了74,000名遊客"},{"english":"before the refurbishment","chinese":"翻新前"},{"english":"this figure increased to","chinese":"這個數字增加至"},{"english":"in the following year","chinese":"在隨後一年"},{"english":"a rise of 18,000","chinese":"增加18,000"},{"english":"the improvement in satisfaction","chinese":"滿意度的改善"},{"english":"even more striking","chinese":"更加明顯；更為突出"},{"english":"before the changes","chinese":"改動前"},{"english":"respondents","chinese":"受訪者"},{"english":"very satisfied","chinese":"非常滿意"},{"english":"a further 30%","chinese":"另外30%"},{"english":"were satisfied","chinese":"感到滿意"},{"english":"meaning that","chinese":"這意味著"},{"english":"positive feedback","chinese":"正面評價"},{"english":"accounted for","chinese":"佔……"},{"english":"less than half of","chinese":"少於一半"},{"english":"all responses","chinese":"所有回應"},{"english":"after refurbishment","chinese":"翻新後"},{"english":"these two categories","chinese":"這兩個類別"},{"english":"climbed to","chinese":"上升至"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"three quarters of","chinese":"四分之三"},{"english":"expressed satisfaction","chinese":"表示滿意"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"the proportion of dissatisfied visitors","chinese":"不滿遊客的比例"},{"english":"fell sharply","chinese":"大幅下跌"},{"english":"reported being dissatisfied","chinese":"表示不滿"},{"english":"dissatisfied","chinese":"不滿意"},{"english":"the largest single group","chinese":"最大單一組別"},{"english":"very dissatisfied","chinese":"非常不滿意"},{"english":"in the year after refurbishment","chinese":"翻新後一年"},{"english":"these figures dropped to","chinese":"這些數字下降至"},{"english":"dropped to","chinese":"下降至"},{"english":"the share giving no response","chinese":"沒有回應者的比例"},{"english":"no response","chinese":"沒有回應"},{"english":"remained unchanged","chinese":"維持不變"},{"english":"at 5%","chinese":"為5%"},{"english":"in both years","chinese":"在兩年中"},{"english":"attendance figures","chinese":"入場人數數據"},{"english":"satisfaction survey results","chinese":"滿意度調查結果"},{"english":"visitor numbers","chinese":"遊客人數"},{"english":"an increase from X to Y","chinese":"由X增加至Y"},{"english":"a marked increase","chinese":"顯著增加"},{"english":"a sharp fall","chinese":"大幅下跌"},{"english":"negative responses","chinese":"負面回應"},{"english":"a clear shift from X to Y","chinese":"由X明顯轉向Y"},{"english":"from dissatisfaction to satisfaction","chinese":"由不滿轉為滿意"},{"english":"the most notable change","chinese":"最明顯的變化"},{"english":"the least changed category","chinese":"變化最少的類別"},{"english":"the combined share of","chinese":"……的合計比例"},{"english":"satisfied visitors","chinese":"滿意的遊客"},{"english":"dissatisfied visitors","chinese":"不滿的遊客"},{"english":"reached 75%","chinese":"達到75%"},{"english":"fell to 20%","chinese":"下降至20%"},{"english":"showed a major improvement","chinese":"顯示重大改善"},{"english":"became the clear majority","chinese":"成為明顯多數"},{"english":"the refurbishment appears to have","chinese":"翻新工程似乎已經……"},{"english":"improved both X and Y","chinese":"同時改善X和Y"}]},"model-essay-6-ielts-task1-pie-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-6-ielts-task1-pie-charts","essayKey":"pie-charts:6","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-6-ielts-task1-pie-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/pie-charts/pie-chart-6","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The three pie charts compare how a UK school allocated its annual budget across five categories in 1981, 1991 and 2001.","chinese":"這三個圓餅圖比較了一所英國學校在 1981 年、 1991 年和 2001 年如何將年度預算分配到五個項目中。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, teachers’ salaries consistently took the largest share of spending, although this figure peaked in 1991 before declining slightly. Insurance remained the smallest item throughout, while spending on other workers fell steadily and the two material-related categories moved in opposite directions.","chinese":"整體而言，教師薪資一直佔學校開支中最大的比例，不過這一數字在 1991 年達到最高點後略有下降。 保險在整段期間一直是最小的支出項目，而其他員工薪資持續下降；同時，兩個與物資和設備相關的項目呈現相反走勢。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 1981, staff pay was the dominant expense, with teachers’ salaries at 40% and other workers’ pay at 28%. A decade later, teachers’ salaries rose to half of total expenditure, while spending on other employees fell to 22%, so staff costs together accounted for 72%. By 2001, the former had eased to 45% and the latter had dropped more sharply to 15%, reducing the combined salary share to 60%.","chinese":"在 1981 年，員工薪資是主要支出，其中教師薪資佔 40% ，其他員工薪資佔 28%。 十年後，教師薪資上升至總開支的一半，而其他員工薪資則下降至 22% ，因此兩項員工薪資合計佔 72% 。 到 2001 年，前者回落至 45% ，後者則更明顯地下降至 15% ，使整體薪資開支比例降至 60% 。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The remaining items changed unevenly. Resources such as books increased from 15% in 1981 to 20% in 1991, before falling to 9% in 2001. In contrast, furniture and equipment followed the opposite path: it fell from 15% to 5%, then climbed to 23%, becoming the second-largest item in 2001. Insurance, although always the smallest category, rose steadily from 2% to 3% and finally to 8%.","chinese":"其餘項目的變化並不一致。 書本等資源開支由 1981 年的 15% 上升至 1991 年的 20% ，之後在 2001 年下降至 9%。 相反，家具和設備開支呈現相反走勢：它先由 15% 下降至 5% ，然後上升至 23%，並在 2001 年成為第二大支出項目。 保險雖然一直是最小的類別，但仍由 2% 持續上升至 3% ，最後達到 8% 。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"three pie charts","chinese":"三個圓形圖"},{"english":"allocated its annual budget","chinese":"分配其年度預算"},{"english":"annual budget","chinese":"年度預算"},{"english":"across five categories","chinese":"分配至五個類別"},{"english":"teachers' salaries","chinese":"教師薪金"},{"english":"consistently took the largest share","chinese":"一直佔最大比例"},{"english":"largest share of spending","chinese":"開支中最大比例"},{"english":"peaked in 1991","chinese":"在1991年達到最高點"},{"english":"before declining slightly","chinese":"之後輕微下降"},{"english":"declining slightly","chinese":"輕微下降"},{"english":"insurance","chinese":"保險"},{"english":"remained the smallest item throughout","chinese":"全期一直是最小項目"},{"english":"the smallest item","chinese":"最小項目"},{"english":"throughout","chinese":"在整段期間"},{"english":"spending on other workers","chinese":"其他員工開支"},{"english":"fell steadily","chinese":"穩步下降"},{"english":"material-related categories","chinese":"與物資相關的類別"},{"english":"moved in opposite directions","chinese":"走勢相反"},{"english":"staff pay","chinese":"員工薪酬"},{"english":"dominant expense","chinese":"主要開支"},{"english":"other workers' pay","chinese":"其他員工薪金"},{"english":"at 40%","chinese":"為40%"},{"english":"a decade later","chinese":"十年後"},{"english":"rose to half of","chinese":"上升至……的一半"},{"english":"half of total expenditure","chinese":"總開支的一半"},{"english":"total expenditure","chinese":"總開支"},{"english":"spending on other employees","chinese":"其他員工開支"},{"english":"fell to 22%","chinese":"下降至22%"},{"english":"staff costs together","chinese":"員工成本合共"},{"english":"accounted for 72%","chinese":"佔72%"},{"english":"by 2001","chinese":"到2001年時"},{"english":"the former","chinese":"前者"},{"english":"had eased to","chinese":"回落至"},{"english":"the latter","chinese":"後者"},{"english":"dropped more sharply to","chinese":"更大幅下降至"},{"english":"reducing the combined salary share","chinese":"令合計薪金比例下降"},{"english":"combined salary share","chinese":"合計薪金比例"},{"english":"the remaining items","chinese":"其餘項目"},{"english":"changed unevenly","chinese":"變化不平均"},{"english":"resources such as books","chinese":"書本等資源"},{"english":"increased from…to…","chinese":"由……增加至……"},{"english":"before falling to","chinese":"之後下降至"},{"english":"in contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"furniture and equipment","chinese":"傢俬及設備"},{"english":"followed the opposite path","chinese":"走勢相反"},{"english":"fell from…to…","chinese":"由……下降至……"},{"english":"then climbed to","chinese":"然後上升至"},{"english":"becoming the second-largest item","chinese":"成為第二大項目"},{"english":"second-largest item","chinese":"第二大項目"},{"english":"although always the smallest category","chinese":"雖然一直是最小類別"},{"english":"rose steadily","chinese":"穩步上升"},{"english":"from 2% to 3% and finally to 8%","chinese":"由2%升至3%，最後升至8%"},{"english":"salary share","chinese":"薪金比例"},{"english":"school budget","chinese":"學校預算"},{"english":"spending category","chinese":"開支類別"}]},"model-essay-6-ielts-task1-process-diagram":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-6-ielts-task1-process-diagram","essayKey":"process-diagram:6","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-6-ielts-task1-process-diagram","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/process-diagrams/process-diagram-6","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The diagram illustrates how a hydroelectric power station produces electricity by using water stored at different heights.","chinese":"該圖說明一座水力發電站如何利用儲存在不同高度的水來產生電力。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the system works as a daily cycle: during the day, water flows downwards from an upper reservoir to generate electricity, while at night the same water is pumped back uphill for reuse. A dam and reversible turbines are the central features, and the electricity produced is sent to the national grid.","chinese":"整體而言，該系統以每日循環的方式運作：白天，水從上方水庫向下流動以產生電力；夜晚，同一批水會被抽回高處，以便再次使用。 水壩和可逆式渦輪機是該系統的核心部件，而產生的電力會被輸送到國家電網。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In the daytime, river water is held in the high-level reservoir behind the dam. When the intake is opened, the stored water is released through a sloping pipe towards the power station. As it passes through the reversible turbines, these operate a generator, which converts the energy from the moving water into electricity. The power is then transmitted by power lines to the national grid, while the used water is discharged into the low-level reservoir.","chinese":"白天，河水被儲存在水壩後方的高位水庫中。 當進水口打開時，儲存的水會通過一條傾斜的管道流向發電站。 當水流經可逆式渦輪機時，渦輪機會帶動發電機，而發電機會把水流的能量轉化為電力。 隨後，電力會通過電力線輸送到國家電網，而使用過的水則被排入低位水。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"At night, the direction of movement is reversed. The intake at the dam is closed, and water from the lower reservoir is pumped back through the same turbine system and conduit to the upper reservoir. This restores the supply of water, allowing the process to begin again the following day.","chinese":"到了夜晚，水流方向會反過來。 水壩處的進水口會關閉，而低位水庫中的水會通過同一套渦輪系統和導管被抽回高位水庫。 這樣可以恢復高位水庫中的水量，使整個過程能夠在第二天再次開始。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"diagram illustrates","chinese":"圖示說明"},{"english":"hydroelectric power station","chinese":"水力發電站"},{"english":"produces electricity by using","chinese":"透過使用……來發電"},{"english":"water stored at different heights","chinese":"儲存在不同高度的水"},{"english":"different heights","chinese":"不同高度"},{"english":"the system works as","chinese":"這個系統以……方式運作"},{"english":"daily cycle","chinese":"每日循環"},{"english":"during the day","chinese":"在日間"},{"english":"flows downwards from","chinese":"從……向下流"},{"english":"upper reservoir","chinese":"上水庫"},{"english":"generate electricity","chinese":"發電"},{"english":"while at night","chinese":"而在夜間"},{"english":"pumped back uphill","chinese":"被泵回高處"},{"english":"for reuse","chinese":"供再次使用"},{"english":"dam","chinese":"水壩"},{"english":"reversible turbines","chinese":"可逆式渦輪機"},{"english":"central features","chinese":"主要特徵；核心部分"},{"english":"electricity produced","chinese":"所產生的電力"},{"english":"sent to the national grid","chinese":"被送往全國電網"},{"english":"national grid","chinese":"全國電網"},{"english":"in the daytime","chinese":"在日間"},{"english":"river water","chinese":"河水"},{"english":"held in the high-level reservoir","chinese":"被儲存在高位水庫"},{"english":"high-level reservoir","chinese":"高位水庫"},{"english":"behind the dam","chinese":"在水壩後方"},{"english":"when the intake is opened","chinese":"當進水口打開時"},{"english":"intake","chinese":"進水口"},{"english":"stored water","chinese":"儲存的水"},{"english":"released through","chinese":"經由……釋放"},{"english":"sloping pipe","chinese":"傾斜管道"},{"english":"towards the power station","chinese":"朝向發電站"},{"english":"as it passes through","chinese":"當它流經……時"},{"english":"passes through","chinese":"流經"},{"english":"operate a generator","chinese":"驅動發電機"},{"english":"generator","chinese":"發電機"},{"english":"converts the energy from…into…","chinese":"將來自……的能量轉化成……"},{"english":"moving water","chinese":"流動的水"},{"english":"power is then transmitted","chinese":"電力隨後被輸送"},{"english":"transmitted by power lines","chinese":"透過電纜輸送"},{"english":"power lines","chinese":"電纜；輸電線"},{"english":"used water","chinese":"使用後的水"},{"english":"discharged into","chinese":"被排入"},{"english":"low-level reservoir","chinese":"低位水庫"},{"english":"direction of movement","chinese":"移動方向"},{"english":"is reversed","chinese":"被反轉"},{"english":"intake at the dam","chinese":"水壩的進水口"},{"english":"is closed","chinese":"被關閉"},{"english":"lower reservoir","chinese":"下水庫"},{"english":"pumped back through","chinese":"被泵回並通過……"},{"english":"turbine system","chinese":"渦輪系統"},{"english":"conduit","chinese":"導管；水道"},{"english":"restores the supply of water","chinese":"恢復供水"},{"english":"supply of water","chinese":"供水量；水源"},{"english":"allowing the process to begin again","chinese":"使過程可以重新開始"},{"english":"begin again","chinese":"重新開始"},{"english":"the following day","chinese":"翌日；第二天"},{"english":"daytime operation","chinese":"日間運作"},{"english":"night-time operation","chinese":"夜間運作"},{"english":"pumped-storage system","chinese":"抽水蓄能系統"},{"english":"water flow","chinese":"水流"},{"english":"energy conversion","chinese":"能量轉換"}]},"model-essay-6-ielts-task1-tables":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-6-ielts-task1-tables","essayKey":"tables:6","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-6-ielts-task1-tables","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/tables/table-6","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The table compares the percentages of first-year students in Economics, Law and Commerce who rated five aspects of their course as “very good”.","chinese":"該表格比較了經濟學、法律和商科三個課程中，一年級學生把其課程五個方面評為「非常好」的比例。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, Commerce received the strongest evaluations, leading or sharing first place in every aspect. Economics was rated highly for teaching and tutor support but much less favourably for pre-course information and resources, whereas Law showed a more balanced pattern, with teaching quality its weakest area.","chinese":"整體而言，商科獲得最強的評價，在每一個方面都位列第一或並列第一。 經濟學在教學質素和導師支援方面評價很高，但在課前資訊和資源方面明顯較不理想；相比之下，法律的表現較為均衡，而教學質素是其最弱的一項。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In terms of teaching-related measures, Economics and Commerce both recorded 95% for teaching quality, far above Law at 67%. Tutor support followed a similar pattern: Commerce was marginally ahead at 93%, with Economics close behind at 92%, while Law was lower, though still fairly positive, at 79%. These figures made Economics and Commerce the clear leaders in these two areas.","chinese":"在教學相關指標方面，經濟學和商科的教學質素同樣錄得 95% ，遠高於法律的 67% 。 導師支援呈現相似模式：商科以 93% 略微領先，經濟學以 92% 緊隨其後，而法律則較低，儘管 79% 仍算相當正面。 這些數字使經濟學和商科在這兩個方面明顯領先。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"For the remaining aspects, Commerce again stood out. It achieved 95% for pre-course information, compared with 72% for Law and just 55% for Economics. The same hierarchy appeared for printed resources, at 81%, 70% and 59%, respectively. Other resources were also rated most highly in Commerce, at 85%, followed by Law at 80%, leaving Economics clearly behind at 62%.","chinese":"至於其餘方面，商科再次突出。 它在課前資訊方面達到 95% ，相比之下，法律為 72% ，經濟學只有 55% 。 印刷資源方面也出現相同排序，商科、法律和經濟學分別為 81% 、 70% 和 59%。 其他資源方面，商科亦獲最高評價，達 85% ；法律以 80% 居次，而經濟學則以62% 明顯落後。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the results of a survey","chinese":"調查結果"},{"english":"first-year students","chinese":"一年級學生"},{"english":"taking various courses","chinese":"修讀不同課程"},{"english":"a particular university","chinese":"某一所大學"},{"english":"various aspects of their course","chinese":"課程的不同方面"},{"english":"considered X to be Y","chinese":"認為 X 是 Y"},{"english":"rated X as “very good”","chinese":"將 X 評為「非常好」"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"by selecting and reporting","chinese":"透過選取並報告……"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"the table compares","chinese":"表格比較"},{"english":"the percentages of","chinese":"……的百分比"},{"english":"Economics, Law and Commerce","chinese":"經濟學、法律及商科"},{"english":"five aspects of their course","chinese":"課程的五個方面"},{"english":"received the strongest evaluations","chinese":"獲得最高評價"},{"english":"the strongest evaluations","chinese":"最高評價"},{"english":"leading or sharing first place","chinese":"領先或並列第一"},{"english":"in every aspect","chinese":"在每一方面"},{"english":"rated highly for","chinese":"在……方面獲得高評價"},{"english":"teaching","chinese":"教學"},{"english":"tutor support","chinese":"導師支援"},{"english":"much less favourably","chinese":"評價低得多"},{"english":"pre-course information","chinese":"課程前資料"},{"english":"resources","chinese":"資源"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相反"},{"english":"showed a more balanced pattern","chinese":"呈現較平均的模式"},{"english":"teaching quality","chinese":"教學質素"},{"english":"its weakest area","chinese":"其最弱的一方面"},{"english":"in terms of","chinese":"就……而言"},{"english":"teaching-related measures","chinese":"與教學相關的指標"},{"english":"both recorded 95%","chinese":"兩者均錄得95%"},{"english":"far above","chinese":"遠高於"},{"english":"at 67%","chinese":"為67%"},{"english":"followed a similar pattern","chinese":"呈現相似模式"},{"english":"marginally ahead","chinese":"略為領先"},{"english":"close behind","chinese":"緊隨其後"},{"english":"while Law was lower","chinese":"而法律較低"},{"english":"though still fairly positive","chinese":"雖然仍算正面"},{"english":"fairly positive","chinese":"相當正面"},{"english":"the clear leaders","chinese":"明顯領先者"},{"english":"in these two areas","chinese":"在這兩個方面"},{"english":"the remaining aspects","chinese":"其餘方面"},{"english":"stood out","chinese":"表現突出"},{"english":"achieved 95% for","chinese":"在……取得95%"},{"english":"compared with","chinese":"與……相比"},{"english":"just 55%","chinese":"只有55%"},{"english":"the same hierarchy","chinese":"相同排名"},{"english":"printed resources","chinese":"印刷資料"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"other resources","chinese":"其他資源"},{"english":"rated most highly","chinese":"評價最高"},{"english":"followed by","chinese":"其次是"},{"english":"leaving Economics clearly behind","chinese":"令經濟學明顯落後"},{"english":"clearly behind","chinese":"明顯落後"},{"english":"course evaluation","chinese":"課程評價"},{"english":"student satisfaction","chinese":"學生滿意度"},{"english":"survey respondents","chinese":"調查受訪者"},{"english":"percentage of respondents","chinese":"受訪者百分比"},{"english":"give very good ratings","chinese":"給予「非常好」評價"},{"english":"score highly","chinese":"取得高分"},{"english":"score poorly","chinese":"得分較低"},{"english":"perform best overall","chinese":"整體表現最佳"},{"english":"perform weakest overall","chinese":"整體表現最弱"},{"english":"lead the table","chinese":"在表格中領先"},{"english":"share the top position","chinese":"並列第一"},{"english":"rank second","chinese":"排名第二"},{"english":"rank last","chinese":"排名最後"},{"english":"across the five categories","chinese":"在五個類別中"},{"english":"a consistent pattern","chinese":"一貫模式"},{"english":"a mixed picture","chinese":"好壞參半的情況"},{"english":"a clear contrast","chinese":"明顯對比"},{"english":"resource-related categories","chinese":"與資源相關的類別"},{"english":"teaching-related categories","chinese":"與教學相關的類別"},{"english":"the highest figure","chinese":"最高數字"},{"english":"the lowest figure","chinese":"最低數字"},{"english":"the largest gap","chinese":"最大差距"},{"english":"a gap of 40 percentage points","chinese":"40個百分點的差距"},{"english":"percentage-point gap","chinese":"百分點差距"},{"english":"considerably higher than","chinese":"明顯高於"},{"english":"slightly higher than","chinese":"略高於"},{"english":"broadly similar to","chinese":"與……大致相若"},{"english":"remain above","chinese":"維持在……以上"},{"english":"fall below","chinese":"低於……"},{"english":"above 90%","chinese":"超過90%"},{"english":"below 60%","chinese":"低於60%"},{"english":"the most favourable ratings","chinese":"最有利評價"},{"english":"the least favourable ratings","chinese":"最不理想評價"},{"english":"course aspects","chinese":"課程方面"},{"english":"quality of support","chinese":"支援質素"},{"english":"information provided before the course","chinese":"課程開始前提供的資料"},{"english":"availability of resources","chinese":"資源供應情況"},{"english":"relatively strong performance","chinese":"相對強勁表現"},{"english":"relatively weak performance","chinese":"相對較弱表現"},{"english":"the overall leader","chinese":"整體領先者"},{"english":"the lowest-ranked course","chinese":"排名最低的課程"},{"english":"strongest in teaching quality","chinese":"在教學質素方面最強"},{"english":"weakest in pre-course information","chinese":"在課程前資料方面最弱"}]},"model-essay-7-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-7-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:7","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-7-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q7","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many legal systems, judges are expected to decide punishments after considering both the crime itself and the circumstances surrounding it. Some people, however, argue that a system of fixed punishments would be more efficient. While this approach does offer certain practical benefits, I believe its disadvantages are considerably greater because it would undermine justice and could even worsen crime in the long term.","chinese":"無論在工作還是私人生活中，越來越多的溝通如今都是透過數位科技進行，而不是面對面交流。 儘管這種發展可能削弱人際關係的品質，並增加誤解的風險， 我認為整體而言，它的優點更大，因為它使溝通更有效率，並能讓人們即使相隔遙遠也保持聯繫。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main advantage of fixed sentencing is that it would make the legal process faster and more straightforward. If the penalty for each offence were predetermined, courts would spend less time debating the appropriate sentence, which would reduce delays and lower administrative costs. As a result, cases could be resolved more quickly, and victims would not have to wait as long for closure. Another benefit is greater consistency. When punishments are standardised, similar offences are more likely to receive similar penalties, which may strengthen public confidence in the justice system. For example, fixed fines and licence suspensions for traffic offences are often accepted because they are transparent and easy for the public to understand.","chinese":"科技化溝通最主要的優點是速度和便利性。 在專業環境中，電子郵件、即時通訊平台和視像會議免除了人們出行的需要，並使決策幾乎可以即時作出。 這不但縮短了回應時間、降低了營運成本，還使公司能夠非常輕鬆地協調分布在不同城市甚至不同大洲的團隊。 例如，一位經理可以透過一次線上會議便與海外同事解決生產問題，而不是等待數天才進行一次面對面的討論。 同樣的情況也適用於社交層面：住得很遠的父母、子女和朋友仍然可以透過通話和訊息每天聯絡。 結果是，人際關係更容易維持，也較不會隨時間而逐漸淡化。 例如，一個家庭即使成員分散在不同國家，仍然可以透過視像通話分享日常近況並提供情感支持。 因此，數位溝通大大提升了工作和個人生活中的效率與可及性。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Nevertheless, the disadvantages of such a system are far more serious. Most importantly, fixed punishments ignore the fact that crimes differ enormously in motive, severity and context. A person who steals food out of desperation should not automatically receive the same sentence as a repeat offender who commits theft for profit. If the law fails to recognise such differences, justice becomes mechanical rather than fair. In addition, rigid sentencing can damage rehabilitation and ultimately make society less safe. When first-time or low-risk offenders are given the same punishment as hardened criminals, they may leave prison more alienated, less employable and more likely to reoffend. For instance, a teenager involved in a minor drug offence may be pushed further into criminal behaviour if treated identically to an experienced trafficker.","chinese":"然而，數位溝通也有重要的缺點，其中最嚴重的是它缺乏情感上的豐富性。 面對面的交談能傳達語氣、面部表情和肢體語言，這些都有助於人們準確理解意思、表達同理心並建立信任。 當這些線索消失時，訊息便更容易被誤解，從而導致困惑甚至衝突。 例如，一封簡短的電郵或文字訊息即使本無惡意，也可能顯得冷淡甚至帶有敵意。 這在職場中尤其成問題，因為信任和細膩的理解對領導、協商和團隊合作都至關重要。 長遠而言，過度依賴螢幕也可能助長膚淺的社交習慣，因此人們即使在線上一直保持聯絡，仍可能感到孤立。 例如，一個人即使經常透過社交媒體聊天，仍可能感到孤單，因為數位接觸始終無法完全取代真正的關注和人的陪伴。 因此，儘管科技讓溝通成為可能，它同時也可能削弱清晰度、信任感和情感深度。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, fixed punishments may improve efficiency and consistency, but these benefits are outweighed by their profound weaknesses. Because crime must be judged in relation to both the act and the offender, a flexible sentencing system is clearly the more just and effective approach.","chinese":"總結來說，透過科技進行溝通在效率和可及性方面具有明顯優勢，儘管它可能削弱人際互動的深度與清晰度。 整體而言，我認為其優點大於缺點，因為數位工具使工作和個人生活中的溝通都能跨越時間與距離而有效運作。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"legal systems","chinese":"法律制度"},{"english":"be expected to","chinese":"被期望要……"},{"english":"decide punishments","chinese":"決定刑罰"},{"english":"after considering both...and...","chinese":"在同時考慮……和……之後"},{"english":"the crime itself","chinese":"罪行本身"},{"english":"the circumstances surrounding it","chinese":"圍繞該事件的情況"},{"english":"a system of fixed punishments","chinese":"固定刑罰制度"},{"english":"more efficient","chinese":"更有效率"},{"english":"this approach","chinese":"這種做法"},{"english":"certain practical benefits","chinese":"某些實際好處"},{"english":"considerably greater","chinese":"大得多"},{"english":"undermine justice","chinese":"損害公義"},{"english":"worsen crime in the long term","chinese":"長遠而言令罪案惡化"},{"english":"fixed sentencing","chinese":"固定判刑"},{"english":"the legal process","chinese":"法律程序"},{"english":"faster and more straightforward","chinese":"更快捷和更簡單直接"},{"english":"the penalty for","chinese":"……的刑罰"},{"english":"each offence","chinese":"每項罪行"},{"english":"predetermined","chinese":"預先決定的"},{"english":"spend less time debating","chinese":"花較少時間爭論"},{"english":"the appropriate sentence","chinese":"合適刑期；合適判刑"},{"english":"reduce delays","chinese":"減少延誤"},{"english":"lower administrative costs","chinese":"降低行政成本"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此；結果"},{"english":"be resolved more quickly","chinese":"更快得到解決"},{"english":"victims","chinese":"受害人"},{"english":"wait as long for closure","chinese":"等那麼久才得到了結"},{"english":"greater consistency","chinese":"更高一致性"},{"english":"be standardised","chinese":"被標準化"},{"english":"similar offences","chinese":"類似罪行"},{"english":"receive similar penalties","chinese":"得到類似刑罰"},{"english":"strengthen public confidence in","chinese":"增強公眾對……的信心"},{"english":"the justice system","chinese":"司法制度"},{"english":"fixed fines","chinese":"固定罰款"},{"english":"licence suspensions","chinese":"暫停駕駛執照"},{"english":"traffic offences","chinese":"交通違例"},{"english":"transparent and easy to understand","chinese":"透明而容易理解"},{"english":"such a system","chinese":"這樣的制度"},{"english":"far more serious","chinese":"嚴重得多"},{"english":"most importantly","chinese":"最重要的是"},{"english":"ignore the fact that","chinese":"忽視……這個事實"},{"english":"differ enormously in","chinese":"在……方面有極大差異"},{"english":"motive, severity and context","chinese":"動機、嚴重程度和背景"},{"english":"steals food out of desperation","chinese":"因絕望而偷食物"},{"english":"automatically receive","chinese":"自動得到"},{"english":"the same sentence as","chinese":"與……相同的判刑"},{"english":"a repeat offender","chinese":"重犯者"},{"english":"commits theft for profit","chinese":"為牟利而盜竊"},{"english":"fails to recognise","chinese":"未能承認"},{"english":"such differences","chinese":"這些差異"},{"english":"mechanical rather than fair","chinese":"機械化而非公平"},{"english":"rigid sentencing","chinese":"僵化判刑"},{"english":"damage rehabilitation","chinese":"損害更生"},{"english":"ultimately make society less safe","chinese":"最終令社會更不安全"},{"english":"first-time offenders","chinese":"初犯者"},{"english":"low-risk offenders","chinese":"低風險罪犯"},{"english":"hardened criminals","chinese":"慣犯；老練罪犯"},{"english":"leave prison more alienated","chinese":"離開監獄時更加疏離"},{"english":"less employable","chinese":"就業能力較低"},{"english":"more likely to reoffend","chinese":"更有可能再犯"},{"english":"a minor drug offence","chinese":"輕微毒品罪行"},{"english":"be pushed further into","chinese":"被進一步推向……"},{"english":"criminal behaviour","chinese":"犯罪行為"},{"english":"treated identically to","chinese":"被以完全相同方式對待"},{"english":"an experienced trafficker","chinese":"有經驗的販毒者"},{"english":"efficiency and consistency","chinese":"效率和一致性"},{"english":"be outweighed by","chinese":"被……超過；不及……重要"},{"english":"profound weaknesses","chinese":"深層弱點"},{"english":"be judged in relation to","chinese":"必須按……來判斷"},{"english":"the act and the offender","chinese":"行為和犯罪者"},{"english":"a flexible sentencing system","chinese":"靈活判刑制度"},{"english":"the more just and effective approach","chinese":"更公正和有效的做法"}]},"model-essay-7-ielts-cause-solution":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-7-ielts-cause-solution","essayKey":"cause-solution:7","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-7-ielts-cause-solution","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/problem-and-cause/EdmundBd9CnS-Q7","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"At university level, science courses remain unevenly populated, with male students greatly outnumbering female students. This imbalance is not mainly a question of ability. It is more often caused by social expectations that shape girls’ confidence and subject choices long before they apply to university. To balance the numbers, schools and universities need to change both the image of science and the support available to female students.","chinese":"在大學階段，科學課程中的學生比例仍然不均衡，男學生的人數遠遠多於女學生。 這種不平衡主要並不是能力問題。 它更多是由社會期望所造成，而這些期望早在女生申請大學之前，已經塑造了她們的自信和科目選擇。 為了平衡人數，學校和大學需要同時改變科學的形象，以及提供給女學生的支援。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main reason is that science is still widely presented, directly or indirectly, as a male domain. From childhood, boys are more often encouraged to build, experiment and solve technical problems, while girls may be guided towards subjects seen as more caring, verbal or socially suitable. As a result, many capable female students begin to doubt whether they belong in physics, engineering or computer science. This doubt can become self-fulfilling: if a girl rarely sees female scientists, teachers or classmates around her, science starts to look less like an open door and more like a room built for someone else.","chinese":"主要原因是，科學在很大程度上仍然被直接或間接地呈現為男性領域。 從童年開始，男孩往往更常被鼓勵去建造、實驗和解決技術問題，而女孩則可能被引導到一些被認為更具照顧性、更偏語言性，或更符合社會期待的科目。 結果是，許多有能力的女學生開始懷疑自己是否屬於物理、工程或電腦科學這些領域。 這種懷疑可能會變成自我實現的結果：如果一個女孩很少在身邊看見女性科學家、教師或同學，科學便開始不像一扇向她敞開的門，而更像是一個為別人而建的房間。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"One effective solution is to intervene earlier, before university choices are fixed. Schools should expose girls to practical science projects, female role models and career talks that show the real range of scientific work, from medical research to environmental technology. At the same time, teachers should actively challenge the quiet stereotypes that influence subject selection, so that girls are not simply allowed to study science but genuinely expected to succeed in it.","chinese":"一個有效的解決方法是在大學選擇確定之前，更早作出干預。 學校應該讓女生接觸實用的科學項目、女性榜樣，以及能展示科學工作真正範圍的職業講座，從醫學研究到環境科技都應包括在內。 同時，教師應該積極挑戰那些悄悄影響科目選擇的刻板印象，讓女生不只是被允許修讀科學，而是真正被期待能在科學中取得成功。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 3","english":"Universities can also help by making science courses feel less isolating. Mentoring schemes, scholarships, outreach programmes and visible female academic staff can reassure applicants that they will not be walking into hostile territory alone. Admission campaigns should also show science as collaborative, creative and socially valuable, rather than only technical and competitive.","chinese":"大學也可以透過讓科學課程感覺不那麼孤立來提供幫助。 導師計劃、獎學金、外展項目，以及可見的女性學術人員，都可以讓申請者放心，知道自己並不是獨自走進一片充滿敵意的領地。 招生宣傳也應該把科學呈現為合作性強、富有創意並具有社會價值的領域，而不只是技術性強和競爭激烈的領域。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, the gender gap in university science is largely rooted in early stereotypes and a lack of visible belonging. It can be narrowed through earlier encouragement, stronger role models and more supportive university environments.","chinese":"總結來說，大學科學領域中的性別差距，很大程度上源於早期形成的刻板印象，以及缺乏可見的歸屬感。 這種差距可以透過更早的鼓勵、更有力的榜樣，以及更具支援性的university環境來縮小"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"at university level","chinese":"在大學層面"},{"english":"science courses","chinese":"科學課程"},{"english":"remain unevenly populated","chinese":"人數分佈仍然不平均"},{"english":"male students greatly outnumbering female students","chinese":"男學生人數大大多於女學生"},{"english":"this imbalance","chinese":"這種不平衡"},{"english":"a question of ability","chinese":"能力問題"},{"english":"social expectations","chinese":"社會期望"},{"english":"shape girls' confidence","chinese":"塑造女生的信心"},{"english":"subject choices","chinese":"科目選擇"},{"english":"long before they apply to university","chinese":"早在她們申請大學之前"},{"english":"balance the numbers","chinese":"平衡人數"},{"english":"the image of science","chinese":"科學的形象"},{"english":"support available to","chinese":"可供……使用的支援"},{"english":"the main reason","chinese":"主要原因"},{"english":"widely presented","chinese":"被廣泛呈現"},{"english":"directly or indirectly","chinese":"直接或間接地"},{"english":"a male domain","chinese":"男性的領域"},{"english":"from childhood","chinese":"從童年開始"},{"english":"be encouraged to","chinese":"被鼓勵去"},{"english":"build, experiment and solve technical problems","chinese":"建造、實驗和解決技術問題"},{"english":"technical problems","chinese":"技術問題"},{"english":"be guided towards","chinese":"被引導去選擇"},{"english":"subjects seen as","chinese":"被視為……的科目"},{"english":"more caring, verbal or socially suitable","chinese":"較照顧性、語文性或社會上較合適的"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"capable female students","chinese":"有能力的女學生"},{"english":"begin to doubt whether","chinese":"開始懷疑是否"},{"english":"belong in","chinese":"屬於；適合留在"},{"english":"physics, engineering or computer science","chinese":"物理、工程或電腦科學"},{"english":"self-fulfilling","chinese":"自我實現的"},{"english":"rarely sees","chinese":"很少看見"},{"english":"female scientists","chinese":"女性科學家"},{"english":"starts to look less like","chinese":"開始看起來不像"},{"english":"an open door","chinese":"敞開的大門；開放的機會"},{"english":"a room built for someone else","chinese":"為別人而設的房間"},{"english":"one effective solution","chinese":"一個有效的解決方法"},{"english":"intervene earlier","chinese":"更早介入"},{"english":"university choices are fixed","chinese":"大學選擇已定下來"},{"english":"expose girls to","chinese":"讓女生接觸"},{"english":"practical science projects","chinese":"實用科學項目"},{"english":"female role models","chinese":"女性榜樣"},{"english":"career talks","chinese":"職業講座"},{"english":"the real range of","chinese":"……的真正範圍"},{"english":"scientific work","chinese":"科學工作"},{"english":"medical research","chinese":"醫學研究"},{"english":"environmental technology","chinese":"環境科技"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"與此同時"},{"english":"actively challenge","chinese":"積極挑戰"},{"english":"quiet stereotypes","chinese":"隱性的刻板印象"},{"english":"influence subject selection","chinese":"影響科目選擇"},{"english":"not simply allowed to","chinese":"不只是被容許去"},{"english":"genuinely expected to succeed","chinese":"真正被期望成功"},{"english":"making science courses feel less isolating","chinese":"令科學課程感覺較不孤立"},{"english":"mentoring schemes","chinese":"導師計劃"},{"english":"scholarships","chinese":"獎學金"},{"english":"outreach programmes","chinese":"外展計劃"},{"english":"visible female academic staff","chinese":"可見的女性學術人員"},{"english":"reassure applicants","chinese":"讓申請者安心"},{"english":"walking into hostile territory alone","chinese":"獨自走進充滿敵意的地方"},{"english":"admission campaigns","chinese":"招生活動"},{"english":"collaborative, creative and socially valuable","chinese":"需要合作、有創意並對社會有價值的"},{"english":"rather than only technical and competitive","chinese":"而不只是技術性和競爭性的"},{"english":"the gender gap","chinese":"性別差距"},{"english":"be largely rooted in","chinese":"主要根源於"},{"english":"early stereotypes","chinese":"早期形成的刻板印象"},{"english":"a lack of visible belonging","chinese":"缺乏可見的歸屬感"},{"english":"be narrowed through","chinese":"透過……收窄"},{"english":"earlier encouragement","chinese":"更早的鼓勵"},{"english":"stronger role models","chinese":"更有力的榜樣"},{"english":"supportive university environments","chinese":"支援性的大學環境"}]},"model-essay-7-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-7-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:7","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-7-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q7","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Success at school and success in life do not always depend on the same abilities. While education is valuable, it measures only a limited range of skills. Some people therefore succeed after academic failure because life rewards broader strengths, and the most important of these is resilience.","chinese":"學校中的成功與人生中的成功並不總是取決於相同的能力。雖然教育很有價值，但它只衡量有限範圍的技能。 因此，有些人在學業失敗後仍然取得成功，是因為人生獎賞的是更廣泛的能力，而其中最重要的是韌性。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One reason is that schools often reward discipline, memory, examination technique and the ability to follow a fixed system. These qualities are useful, but they are not the whole story. Outside the classroom, people may succeed because they are practical, socially intelligent, creative or willing to take calculated risks. A student who struggles with written exams, for example, may still have a sharp instinct for business, an ability to understand customers, or the courage to start again after failure. In this sense, poor school results are not always a final judgement on a person’s ability; they may simply show that one particular system did not suit them. Once such people find work that feels purposeful, they can develop the focus and confidence that they never showed in school.","chinese":"其中一個原因是，學校往往獎賞紀律、記憶力、考試技巧，以及遵從固定制度的能力。 這些素質是有用的，但它們並不是全部。 在課室之外，人們可能會成功，是因為他們務實、具備社交智慧、有創意，或者願意承擔經過計算的風險。 例如，一個在筆試中表現吃力的學生，仍然可能擁有敏銳的商業直覺、理解顧客的能力，或者在失敗後重新開始的勇氣。 從這個意義上說，糟糕的學校成績並不總是對一個人能力的最終判斷；它們可能只是顯示某一個特定制度並不適合他們。 一旦這些人找到讓他們感到有目標的工作，他們便能培養出在學校裡從未展現過的專注力和自信。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The most important thing for success in life is resilience. Talent, education and luck all matter, but they are fragile advantages if a person gives up too easily. Life rarely moves in a straight line: people lose jobs, make poor decisions, face rejection and meet problems that no textbook has prepared them for. Resilience allows them to absorb these setbacks without being defined by them. More importantly, it turns failure into feedback. For instance, a young entrepreneur whose first idea collapses may learn how to manage money, listen to customers and build a stronger plan. Without resilience, that first failure becomes an ending; with resilience, it becomes a rough but useful apprenticeship.","chinese":"人生成功最重要的東西是韌性。 天賦、教育和運氣都很重要，但如果一個人太容易放棄，這些優勢都是脆弱的。 人生很少會沿著一條直線前進：人們會失去工作、作出錯誤決定、面對拒絕，並遇上沒有任何教科書曾經讓他們準備好的問題。 韌性使他們能夠承受這些挫折，而不被這些挫折所定義。 更重要的是，它把失敗轉化為回饋。 例如，一位年輕創業者的第一個想法失敗後，可能會學會如何管理金錢、聆聽顧客，以及建立一個更強的計劃。 沒有韌性，那第一次失敗便會成為終點；有了韌性，它便會成為一段艱難但有用的學徒期。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, some people succeed after failing at school because life rewards far more than academic performance. Resilience is the most essential quality because it helps people keep learning, adapting and moving forward when things go wrong.","chinese":"總結來說，有些人在學校失敗後仍然成功，是因為人生獎賞的遠遠不只是學業表現。 韌性是最重要的素質，因為它能幫助人們在事情出錯時繼續學習、適應，並向前走。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"success at school","chinese":"學業上的成功"},{"english":"success in life","chinese":"人生中的成功"},{"english":"depend on","chinese":"取決於"},{"english":"the same abilities","chinese":"相同的能力"},{"english":"education is valuable","chinese":"教育是有價值的"},{"english":"a limited range of skills","chinese":"有限範圍的技能"},{"english":"academic failure","chinese":"學業失敗"},{"english":"life rewards broader strengths","chinese":"人生會回報更廣泛的長處"},{"english":"broader strengths","chinese":"更廣泛的長處"},{"english":"the most important of these","chinese":"其中最重要的是"},{"english":"resilience","chinese":"抗逆力"},{"english":"reward discipline","chinese":"重視自律"},{"english":"examination technique","chinese":"考試技巧"},{"english":"follow a fixed system","chinese":"跟從固定制度"},{"english":"these qualities","chinese":"這些特質"},{"english":"not the whole story","chinese":"不是全部"},{"english":"outside the classroom","chinese":"在課室以外"},{"english":"socially intelligent","chinese":"有社交智慧"},{"english":"willing to take calculated risks","chinese":"願意承擔經過衡量的風險"},{"english":"calculated risks","chinese":"經過衡量的風險"},{"english":"struggles with written exams","chinese":"應付筆試有困難"},{"english":"a sharp instinct for business","chinese":"敏銳的商業直覺"},{"english":"understand customers","chinese":"了解顧客"},{"english":"the courage to start again","chinese":"重新開始的勇氣"},{"english":"after failure","chinese":"失敗之後"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"poor school results","chinese":"差的學業成績"},{"english":"a final judgement on","chinese":"對……的最終判斷"},{"english":"one particular system","chinese":"某一套特定制度"},{"english":"did not suit them","chinese":"不適合他們"},{"english":"find work that feels purposeful","chinese":"找到有意義的工作"},{"english":"feels purposeful","chinese":"感覺有意義"},{"english":"develop the focus and confidence","chinese":"培養專注力和信心"},{"english":"the most important thing for","chinese":"對……最重要的事情"},{"english":"fragile advantages","chinese":"脆弱的優勢"},{"english":"give up too easily","chinese":"太容易放棄"},{"english":"rarely moves in a straight line","chinese":"很少一帆風順"},{"english":"make poor decisions","chinese":"作出錯誤決定"},{"english":"face rejection","chinese":"面對拒絕"},{"english":"no textbook has prepared them for","chinese":"沒有課本能讓他們預先準備"},{"english":"absorb these setbacks","chinese":"承受這些挫折"},{"english":"be defined by","chinese":"被……界定"},{"english":"turn failure into feedback","chinese":"將失敗變成回饋"},{"english":"a young entrepreneur","chinese":"年輕創業者"},{"english":"first idea collapses","chinese":"第一個想法失敗"},{"english":"manage money","chinese":"管理金錢"},{"english":"listen to customers","chinese":"聆聽顧客意見"},{"english":"build a stronger plan","chinese":"制定更完善的計劃"},{"english":"becomes an ending","chinese":"變成終點"},{"english":"a rough but useful apprenticeship","chinese":"艱辛但有用的學習過程"},{"english":"far more than academic performance","chinese":"遠不止學業表現"},{"english":"academic performance","chinese":"學業表現"},{"english":"the most essential quality","chinese":"最必要的特質"},{"english":"keep learning, adapting and moving forward","chinese":"繼續學習、適應和向前走"},{"english":"when things go wrong","chinese":"當事情出錯時"}]},"model-essay-7-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-7-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:7","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-7-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q7","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"How citizens use their income has a major influence on a country’s economy. While some argue that consumer spending keeps businesses alive and creates employment, others believe that saving is more beneficial because it strengthens financial stability and supports long-term investment. In my view, although spending is useful in the short term, a culture of saving is ultimately better for the economy.","chinese":"公民如何使用自己的收入，對一個國家的經濟有重大影響。 雖然有些人認為，消費支出能讓企業維持運作並創造就業，但另一些人則認為，儲蓄更有利，因為它能加強財務穩定並支持長期投資。 在我看來，雖然消費在短期內是有用的，但儲蓄文化最終對經濟更好。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Those who support spending have a reasonable argument. When people buy goods and services, money circulates rather than sitting idle. Restaurants, shops, transport companies and online businesses all depend on customers who are ready to pay for what they want or need. If consumers suddenly stopped spending, many firms would lose revenue, reduce production, or lay off staff. For example, a family that regularly eats out, buys clothes and travels is not only satisfying its own needs; it is also helping waiters, shop assistants and drivers earn a living. In this sense, spending acts as the bloodstream of an economy because it keeps trade moving and confidence alive.","chinese":"支持消費的人有其合理的論點。 當人們購買商品和服務時，金錢會流通，而不是閒置不動。 餐廳、商店、運輸公司和網上企業都依賴那些願意為自己想要或需要的東西付款的顧客。 如果消費者突然停止消費，許多公司便會失去收入、減少生產，或裁減員工。 例如，一個經常外出用餐、購買衣服和旅遊的家庭，不只是滿足自己的需要；它同時也在幫助侍應、店員和司機維持生計。 從這個意義上說，消費就像經濟的血液，因為它讓貿易保持流動，也讓信心保持活力。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, I believe saving offers a deeper and more sustainable economic benefit. People who save are less vulnerable to sudden unemployment, illness or price rises, so they are less likely to depend heavily on government support during difficult periods. More importantly, savings can become investment. Banks can lend deposited money to businesses, families can fund education, and individuals can start small enterprises without falling into dangerous debt. A society that spends every dollar may look prosperous on the surface, but it can become fragile, like a house built on sand. By contrast, widespread saving creates a financial cushion and provides the capital needed for future growth. This makes the economy more resilient, not merely more active.","chinese":"然而，我認為儲蓄能帶來更深層、更可持續的經濟好處。 有儲蓄的人較不容易受到突然失業、疾病或物價上升的嚴重影響，因此在困難時期，他們也較不可能嚴重依賴政府支援。 更重要的是，儲蓄可以轉化為投資。 銀行可以把存款借給企業，家庭可以資助教育，而個人也可以在不陷入危險債務的情況下創辦小型企業。 一個把每一元都花掉的社會，表面上可能看似繁榮，但它可能變得脆弱，就像建在沙上的房子一樣。 相比之下，廣泛的儲蓄能創造財務緩衝，並提供未來增長所需的資本。 這會使經濟更有韌性，而不只是更活躍。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, consumer spending is important because it supports demand, jobs and business income. Nevertheless, I firmly believe that saving is more valuable for a nation’s economy, as it promotes stability, reduces financial risk and lays a stronger foundation for long-term development.","chinese":"總結來說，消費支出是重要的，因為它支持需求、就業和企業收入。 然而，我堅定認為，儲蓄對一個國家的經濟更有價值，因為它能促進穩定、降低財務風險，並為長期發展奠定更強大的基礎。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"use their income","chinese":"運用收入"},{"english":"has a major influence on","chinese":"對……有重大影響"},{"english":"a country's economy","chinese":"一個國家的經濟"},{"english":"consumer spending","chinese":"消費開支"},{"english":"keeps businesses alive","chinese":"令企業得以生存"},{"english":"creates employment","chinese":"創造就業"},{"english":"more beneficial","chinese":"更有益"},{"english":"strengthens financial stability","chinese":"加強財務穩定"},{"english":"supports long-term investment","chinese":"支持長遠投資"},{"english":"in the short term","chinese":"短期內"},{"english":"a culture of saving","chinese":"儲蓄文化"},{"english":"ultimately better for","chinese":"最終對……更好"},{"english":"support spending","chinese":"支持消費"},{"english":"a reasonable argument","chinese":"合理的論點"},{"english":"buy goods and services","chinese":"購買商品和服務"},{"english":"money circulates","chinese":"金錢流通"},{"english":"rather than sitting idle","chinese":"而不是閒置"},{"english":"depend on customers","chinese":"依賴顧客"},{"english":"ready to pay for","chinese":"願意為……付款"},{"english":"stopped spending","chinese":"停止消費"},{"english":"lose revenue","chinese":"失去收入"},{"english":"reduce production","chinese":"減少生產"},{"english":"lay off staff","chinese":"裁員"},{"english":"regularly eats out","chinese":"經常外出用餐"},{"english":"satisfying its own needs","chinese":"滿足自己的需要"},{"english":"earn a living","chinese":"謀生"},{"english":"In this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"acts as the bloodstream of","chinese":"像……的血液一樣發揮作用"},{"english":"keeps trade moving","chinese":"令貿易持續運作"},{"english":"keeps confidence alive","chinese":"維持信心"},{"english":"offers a deeper and more sustainable benefit","chinese":"提供更深層、更可持續的好處"},{"english":"economic benefit","chinese":"經濟好處"},{"english":"less vulnerable to","chinese":"較不容易受……影響"},{"english":"sudden unemployment","chinese":"突然失業"},{"english":"price rises","chinese":"物價上升"},{"english":"less likely to","chinese":"較不可能"},{"english":"depend heavily on","chinese":"嚴重依賴"},{"english":"government support","chinese":"政府支援"},{"english":"during difficult periods","chinese":"在困難時期"},{"english":"become investment","chinese":"變成投資"},{"english":"lend deposited money to","chinese":"把存款借給"},{"english":"deposited money","chinese":"存款"},{"english":"fund education","chinese":"資助教育"},{"english":"start small enterprises","chinese":"創辦小型企業"},{"english":"fall into dangerous debt","chinese":"陷入危險債務"},{"english":"spends every dollar","chinese":"花光每一元"},{"english":"look prosperous on the surface","chinese":"表面上看起來繁榮"},{"english":"become fragile","chinese":"變得脆弱"},{"english":"built on sand","chinese":"建在沙上的"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"widespread saving","chinese":"普遍儲蓄"},{"english":"creates a financial cushion","chinese":"建立財務緩衝"},{"english":"provides the capital needed for","chinese":"提供……所需的資本"},{"english":"future growth","chinese":"未來增長"},{"english":"more resilient","chinese":"更有韌性"},{"english":"not merely more active","chinese":"不只是更活躍"},{"english":"supports demand","chinese":"支持需求"},{"english":"business income","chinese":"企業收入"},{"english":"Nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"more valuable for","chinese":"對……更有價值"},{"english":"a nation's economy","chinese":"國家經濟"},{"english":"promotes stability","chinese":"促進穩定"},{"english":"reduces financial risk","chinese":"降低財務風險"},{"english":"lays a stronger foundation for","chinese":"為……奠定更穩固基礎"},{"english":"long-term development","chinese":"長遠發展"}]},"model-essay-7-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-7-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:7","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-7-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q7","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Modern businesses derive substantial benefits from the communities in which they operate, so it is reasonable to expect something in return. I completely agree that companies should provide sports and social facilities for local residents, because these amenities improve public well-being and because profitable firms have a clear responsibility to reinvest locally.","chinese":"現代企業從營運所在的社區中獲得了大量利益，因此合理地可以期待它們作出某種回饋 我完全同意。 企業應該為當地居民提供體育及社交設施，因為這些設施能提升公眾福祉，而獲利企業也明確有責任把資源重新投放到本地社區。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that such facilities generate direct social gains. When a company funds a sports ground, gym or community hall, residents gain affordable access to exercise and organised interaction. This can improve physical health, since people who have safe and convenient places to be active are more likely to form regular habits rather than drift into sedentary lifestyles. The effects are psychological as well. Team sports, clubs and neighbourhood events reduce isolation, especially among teenagers and older people, which in turn can strengthen confidence, lower stress and create a stronger sense of belonging. For example, if a factory sponsors an evening football league and opens a social centre at weekends, it gives young people structure and helps families mix more regularly.","chinese":"第一個原因是，這類設施能帶來直接的社會效益。 當企業資助興建運動場、健身房或社區會堂時，居民便能以可負擔的方式接觸運動與有組織的社交活動。 這能改善身體健康，因為當人們擁有安全而方便的活動空間時，他們更有可能養成規律習慣，而不是逐漸陷入久坐不動的生活方式。 這種影響也同樣體現在心理層面上。 團隊運動、興趣社團與社區活動能減少孤立感，尤其對青少年和長者而言更是如此，而這進一步能增強自信、減低壓力，並建立更強的歸屬感。 例如，如果一間工廠資助夜間足球聯賽，並在週末開放社交中心，這就能為年輕人提供有規律的活動，也能幫助家庭之間更經常地互動交流。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"There is also a strong moral and practical case for expecting companies to make this contribution. Large firms profit from local labour, use public infrastructure and sometimes place pressure on the surrounding environment. In return, they should help raise the quality of life in the same area. More importantly, this is not merely charitable, because businesses benefit when communities are healthier and more cohesive. Areas with better facilities are likely to experience less social tension, stronger goodwill towards employers and a more stable workforce. For instance, a company that builds a shared sports complex near its offices may find it easier to recruit staff, maintain a positive public image and secure long-term public support for its operations.","chinese":"此外，從道德和實際層面來看，要求企業作出這種貢獻也同樣有充分理由。 大型企業從本地勞動力中獲利，使用公共基礎建設，並且有時也會對周邊環境造成壓力。 因此，作為回報，它們應該幫助提升同一地區居民的生活質素。 更重要的是，這不僅僅是慈善行為，因為當社區更健康、更有凝聚力時，企業本身也會受益。 擁有更完善設施的地區，往往較少出現社會緊張關係，居民對僱主也會有更強的善意，而勞動力也會更穩定。 例如，一間在辦公地點附近興建共享體育設施的公司，可能會發現自己更容易招聘員工、維持正面的公眾形象，並獲得社會對其長期營運的支持。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely agree that companies should provide sports and social facilities for local communities. Such investment improves health, strengthens social cohesion and represents a fair return to the communities that help businesses prosper.","chinese":"總而言之，我完全同意企業應該為本地社區提供體育和社交設施。 這類投資能改善健康、加強社會凝聚力，並且是企業對那些幫助其繁榮發展的社區所作出的公平回饋。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"derive substantial benefits from","chinese":"從……獲得重大好處"},{"english":"the communities in which they operate","chinese":"它們營運所在的社區"},{"english":"it is reasonable to expect","chinese":"期望……是合理的"},{"english":"something in return","chinese":"回報；作為回饋"},{"english":"provide sports and social facilities","chinese":"提供運動及社交設施"},{"english":"local residents","chinese":"本地居民"},{"english":"these amenities","chinese":"這些設施"},{"english":"improve public well-being","chinese":"改善公眾福祉"},{"english":"profitable firms","chinese":"有盈利的公司"},{"english":"have a clear responsibility to","chinese":"明確有責任去"},{"english":"reinvest locally","chinese":"在本地再投資"},{"english":"such facilities","chinese":"這類設施"},{"english":"generate direct social gains","chinese":"帶來直接社會效益"},{"english":"fund a sports ground","chinese":"資助運動場"},{"english":"community hall","chinese":"社區會堂"},{"english":"gain affordable access to","chinese":"以可負擔價錢使用"},{"english":"organised interaction","chinese":"有組織的互動"},{"english":"improve physical health","chinese":"改善身體健康"},{"english":"safe and convenient places","chinese":"安全方便的地方"},{"english":"be active","chinese":"活動身體；保持活躍"},{"english":"form regular habits","chinese":"養成規律習慣"},{"english":"rather than drift into","chinese":"而不是漸漸陷入"},{"english":"sedentary lifestyles","chinese":"久坐少動的生活方式"},{"english":"the effects are psychological as well","chinese":"影響亦包括心理層面"},{"english":"team sports","chinese":"團隊運動"},{"english":"neighbourhood events","chinese":"社區活動"},{"english":"reduce isolation","chinese":"減少孤立感"},{"english":"especially among","chinese":"尤其在……之中"},{"english":"which in turn","chinese":"這反過來"},{"english":"strengthen confidence","chinese":"增強信心"},{"english":"lower stress","chinese":"減低壓力"},{"english":"create a stronger sense of belonging","chinese":"建立更強的歸屬感"},{"english":"sponsor an evening football league","chinese":"贊助夜間足球聯賽"},{"english":"open a social centre","chinese":"開放社交中心"},{"english":"at weekends","chinese":"在週末"},{"english":"give young people structure","chinese":"令年輕人生活更有規律"},{"english":"help families mix more regularly","chinese":"幫助家庭更經常交流"},{"english":"a strong moral and practical case for","chinese":"有強烈的道德及實際理由支持"},{"english":"make this contribution","chinese":"作出這份貢獻"},{"english":"profit from local labour","chinese":"從本地勞動力獲利"},{"english":"use public infrastructure","chinese":"使用公共基建"},{"english":"place pressure on","chinese":"對……造成壓力"},{"english":"the surrounding environment","chinese":"周邊環境"},{"english":"in return","chinese":"作為回報"},{"english":"raise the quality of life","chinese":"提高生活質素"},{"english":"in the same area","chinese":"在同一地區"},{"english":"not merely charitable","chinese":"不只是慈善"},{"english":"benefit when","chinese":"在……時受惠"},{"english":"healthier and more cohesive","chinese":"更健康、更有凝聚力"},{"english":"better facilities","chinese":"更好的設施"},{"english":"be likely to experience","chinese":"有可能經歷"},{"english":"less social tension","chinese":"較少社會緊張"},{"english":"stronger goodwill towards","chinese":"對……有更強善意"},{"english":"employers","chinese":"僱主"},{"english":"a more stable workforce","chinese":"更穩定的勞動力"},{"english":"build a shared sports complex","chinese":"興建共用運動綜合設施"},{"english":"near its offices","chinese":"在辦公室附近"},{"english":"find it easier to","chinese":"發現更容易"},{"english":"recruit staff","chinese":"招聘員工"},{"english":"maintain a positive public image","chinese":"維持正面的公眾形象"},{"english":"secure long-term public support","chinese":"獲得長期公眾支持"},{"english":"its operations","chinese":"其營運"},{"english":"local communities","chinese":"本地社區"},{"english":"such investment","chinese":"這類投資"},{"english":"strengthen social cohesion","chinese":"加強社會凝聚力"},{"english":"represent a fair return to","chinese":"代表對……的合理回報"},{"english":"help businesses prosper","chinese":"幫助企業興旺發展"}]},"model-essay-7-ielts-task1-bar-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-7-ielts-task1-bar-charts","essayKey":"bar-charts:7","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-7-ielts-task1-bar-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/bar-charts/bar-chart-7","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The two bar charts compare the destinations of UK graduates and postgraduates who left college in 2008 but did not enter full-time employment.","chinese":"這兩張柱狀圖比較了 2008 年英國大學畢業生和研究生離開學院後，在沒有進入全職工作的情況下所選擇的去向。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, further study was the most common route for both groups, whereas voluntary work attracted the fewest students. Although the graduate figures were much higher in every category, the overall pattern was broadly similar.","chinese":"整體而言，繼續深造是兩組學生最常見的去向，而從事志願工作的人數最少。 雖然大學畢業生在每一個類別中人數都遠高於研究生，但整體模式大致相似。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Among graduates, almost 30,000 continued their education, making further study the clear leading destination. Part-time work came next, at 17,735, only slightly ahead of unemployment, which stood at 16,235. By contrast, just 3,500 graduates chose voluntary work, less than a quarter of the number without a job and far below the total in further study.","chinese":"在大學畢業生中，接近 30,000 人繼續學業，使繼續深造成為明顯最多人選擇的去向。 兼職工作位居第二，有 17,735 人，只比失業人數 16,235 略高。 相比之下，只有 3,500 名畢業生選擇志願工作，這還不到失業人數的四分之一，也遠低於繼續深造的人數。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The same order was evident among postgraduates, though the numbers were smaller. Further study again ranked first, with 2,725 students, but it was only narrowly higher than part-time work, at 2,535. Unemployment involved 1,625 postgraduates, while voluntary work remained the least common option, at 345. Across all four destinations, graduates outnumbered postgraduates substantially, especially in further study, where the difference exceeded 26,000.","chinese":"研究生中也呈現相同的排序，不過人數較少。 繼續深造再次排名第一，有 2,725 人，但它只略高於兼職工作的 2,535 人。 失業的研究生人數為 1,625 ，而志願工作仍然是最不常見的選項，只有 345 人。 在四個去向中，大學畢業生的人數都明顯多於研究生，尤其是在繼續深造方面，兩者差距超過 26,000 人。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"two bar charts","chinese":"兩個棒形圖"},{"english":"compare the destinations of","chinese":"比較……的去向"},{"english":"UK graduates and postgraduates","chinese":"英國大學畢業生及研究院畢業生"},{"english":"left college","chinese":"離開大學；畢業"},{"english":"enter full-time employment","chinese":"進入全職就業"},{"english":"full-time employment","chinese":"全職就業"},{"english":"further study","chinese":"繼續升學"},{"english":"the most common route","chinese":"最常見的去向"},{"english":"for both groups","chinese":"對兩個組別而言"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相比之下"},{"english":"voluntary work","chinese":"義務工作"},{"english":"attracted the fewest students","chinese":"吸引最少學生"},{"english":"graduate figures","chinese":"大學畢業生的數字"},{"english":"much higher in every category","chinese":"在每個類別都高得多"},{"english":"overall pattern","chinese":"整體模式"},{"english":"broadly similar","chinese":"大致相似"},{"english":"among graduates","chinese":"在大學畢業生當中"},{"english":"almost 30,000","chinese":"接近30,000人"},{"english":"continued their education","chinese":"繼續接受教育；繼續升學"},{"english":"making further study the clear leading destination","chinese":"使繼續升學成為明顯最主要去向"},{"english":"the clear leading destination","chinese":"明顯最主要的去向"},{"english":"part-time work","chinese":"兼職工作"},{"english":"came next","chinese":"位居其次"},{"english":"at 17,735","chinese":"數字為17,735"},{"english":"only slightly ahead of","chinese":"只略高於……"},{"english":"unemployment","chinese":"失業"},{"english":"stood at","chinese":"處於；數字為"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"chose voluntary work","chinese":"選擇義務工作"},{"english":"less than a quarter of","chinese":"少於……的四分之一"},{"english":"the number without a job","chinese":"沒有工作的人的數目"},{"english":"far below","chinese":"遠低於"},{"english":"the total in further study","chinese":"繼續升學的總數"},{"english":"the same order was evident","chinese":"呈現相同排序"},{"english":"among postgraduates","chinese":"在研究院畢業生當中"},{"english":"though the numbers were smaller","chinese":"雖然數字較小"},{"english":"ranked first","chinese":"排名第一"},{"english":"with 2,725 students","chinese":"有2,725名學生"},{"english":"narrowly higher than","chinese":"僅略高於"},{"english":"involved 1,625 postgraduates","chinese":"涉及1,625名研究院畢業生"},{"english":"remained the least common option","chinese":"仍然是最少見的選項"},{"english":"the least common option","chinese":"最少見的選項"},{"english":"across all four destinations","chinese":"在全部四個去向中"},{"english":"outnumbered postgraduates substantially","chinese":"數量大幅多於研究院畢業生"},{"english":"substantially","chinese":"大幅地；顯著地"},{"english":"especially in further study","chinese":"尤其是在繼續升學方面"},{"english":"the difference exceeded","chinese":"差距超過"},{"english":"exceeded 26,000","chinese":"超過26,000"},{"english":"destinations","chinese":"去向"},{"english":"category","chinese":"類別"},{"english":"route","chinese":"路徑；去向"}]},"model-essay-7-ielts-task1-line-graph":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-7-ielts-task1-line-graph","essayKey":"line-graph:7","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-7-ielts-task1-line-graph","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/line-graphs/line-graph-7","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The line graph compares average carbon dioxide emissions per person in the United Kingdom, Sweden, Italy and Portugal from 1967 to 2007, measured in metric tonnes.","chinese":"該折線圖比較了 1967 年至 2007 年間英國、瑞典、義大利和葡萄牙的人均二氧化碳排放量，單位為公噸。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the United Kingdom remained the highest emitter throughout, although its figure declined gradually. Sweden also ended lower than it began after reaching a peak in the late 1970s, whereas Italy and Portugal recorded steady growth, with Italy ranking second by 2007.","chinese":"整體而言，英國在整段期間一直是人均排放量最高的國家，儘管其數字逐漸下降。 瑞典在 1970 年代末達到高峰後，最終排放量低於起點；相反，義大利和葡萄牙均穩定上升，其中義大利到 2007 年排名第二。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 1967, the UK produced just under 11 tonnes per person, compared with about 8.7 tonnes in Sweden. Sweden then rose to just over 10 tonnes in 1977, almost matching the UK, before falling markedly to around 7 tonnes in 1987 and then to approximately 5.5 tonnes by the final year. The UK followed a gentler downward path, slipping from nearly 11 tonnes to about 8.7 tonnes over the same period.","chinese":"1967 年，英國人均二氧化碳排放量略低於 11 公噸，而瑞典約為 8.7 公噸。 瑞典隨後在 1977 年升至略高於 10 公噸，幾乎追平英國，之後在 1987 年大幅下降至約 7 公噸，並在最後一年降至約 5.5 公噸。 英國則呈現較溫和的下降趨勢，在同一期間由接近 11 公噸降至約 8.7 公噸。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"By contrast, Italy climbed from roughly 4.2 tonnes in 1967 to about 6.3 tonnes in 1977, and then increased further to around 7.7 tonnes in 1997, where it levelled off. Portugal, initially the lowest at just over 1 tonne, rose steadily to about 5.5 tonnes in 2007, almost converging with Sweden.","chinese":"相比之下，義大利的人均排放量從 1967 年的約 4.2 公噸上升至 1977 年的約 6.3 公噸，之後進一步升至 1997 年的約 7.7 公噸，並在此後趨於平穩。 葡萄牙起初最低，略高於 1 公噸，但到 2007 年穩定上升至約 5.5 公噸，幾乎與瑞典匯合。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"The line graph compares","chinese":"折線圖比較"},{"english":"average carbon dioxide emissions","chinese":"平均二氧化碳排放量"},{"english":"carbon dioxide emissions","chinese":"二氧化碳排放量"},{"english":"per person","chinese":"每人"},{"english":"the United Kingdom","chinese":"英國"},{"english":"Sweden","chinese":"瑞典"},{"english":"Italy","chinese":"意大利"},{"english":"Portugal","chinese":"葡萄牙"},{"english":"from 1967 to 2007","chinese":"從1967年至2007年"},{"english":"measured in metric tonnes","chinese":"以公噸計"},{"english":"metric tonnes","chinese":"公噸"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"remained the highest emitter throughout","chinese":"全期一直是最高排放國"},{"english":"the highest emitter","chinese":"最高排放國"},{"english":"throughout","chinese":"整個期間"},{"english":"although","chinese":"雖然；儘管"},{"english":"its figure declined gradually","chinese":"其數字逐漸下降"},{"english":"declined gradually","chinese":"逐漸下降"},{"english":"ended lower than it began","chinese":"結束時低於起點"},{"english":"after reaching a peak","chinese":"在達到高峰後"},{"english":"reaching a peak","chinese":"達到高峰"},{"english":"in the late 1970s","chinese":"在1970年代後期"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；然而"},{"english":"recorded steady growth","chinese":"錄得穩定增長"},{"english":"steady growth","chinese":"穩定增長"},{"english":"with Italy ranking second by 2007","chinese":"其中意大利到2007年排名第二"},{"english":"ranking second","chinese":"排名第二"},{"english":"produced just under 11 tonnes","chinese":"排放略低於11公噸"},{"english":"just under 11 tonnes","chinese":"略低於11公噸"},{"english":"compared with","chinese":"與……相比"},{"english":"about 8.7 tonnes","chinese":"約8.7公噸"},{"english":"rose to just over 10 tonnes","chinese":"上升至略高於10公噸"},{"english":"just over 10 tonnes","chinese":"略高於10公噸"},{"english":"almost matching the UK","chinese":"幾乎追平英國"},{"english":"before falling markedly to","chinese":"隨後明顯下降至"},{"english":"falling markedly","chinese":"明顯下降"},{"english":"around 7 tonnes","chinese":"約7公噸"},{"english":"approximately 5.5 tonnes","chinese":"約5.5公噸"},{"english":"by the final year","chinese":"到最後一年"},{"english":"followed a gentler downward path","chinese":"呈現較溫和的下降走勢"},{"english":"a gentler downward path","chinese":"較溫和的下降走勢"},{"english":"slipping from nearly 11 tonnes to about 8.7 tonnes","chinese":"由接近11公噸下滑至約8.7公噸"},{"english":"over the same period","chinese":"在同一期間"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"climbed from roughly 4.2 tonnes","chinese":"由約4.2公噸攀升"},{"english":"roughly 4.2 tonnes","chinese":"約4.2公噸"},{"english":"increased further to around 7.7 tonnes","chinese":"進一步上升至約7.7公噸"},{"english":"where it levelled off","chinese":"隨後在該水平持平"},{"english":"levelled off","chinese":"趨於平穩"},{"english":"initially the lowest","chinese":"最初最低"},{"english":"at just over 1 tonne","chinese":"略高於1公噸"},{"english":"rose steadily to about 5.5 tonnes","chinese":"穩步上升至約5.5公噸"},{"english":"almost converging with Sweden","chinese":"幾乎與瑞典匯合"},{"english":"converging with","chinese":"與……趨於一致"}]},"model-essay-7-ielts-task1-maps":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-7-ielts-task1-maps","essayKey":"maps:7","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-7-ielts-task1-maps","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/maps/maps-7","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The maps compare road access to a city hospital in 2007 and 2010.","chinese":"這兩幅地圖比較了 2007 年和 2010 年通往一所城市醫院的道路通達情況。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the layout was substantially reorganised: two roundabouts and a bus station were introduced, and the original combined car park was replaced by separate staff and public parking facilities. The three main roads, however, remained in the same positions.","chinese":"整體而言，該區佈局被大幅重新規劃：新增了兩個迴旋處和一個巴士總站，而原本供員工和公眾共同使用的停車場則被分成員工停車場和公眾停車場。 然而，三條主要道路的位置保持不變。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 2007, Hospital Road ran northwards from City Road to the Ring Road, which surrounded the hospital. Six small bus stops were placed along Hospital Road, three on each side. A single car park for both staff and the public stood to the east of this road, just below the Ring Road.","chinese":"2007 年，醫院路從城市路向北延伸至環路，而環路圍繞著醫院。 六個小型巴士站沿醫院路設置，左右兩側各三個。 一個供員工和公眾共同使用的停車場位於這條路以東、環路正下方。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"By 2010, traffic flow had been redesigned more systematically. A roundabout had been built at each end of Hospital Road, one at its junction with City Road and the other where it joined the Ring Road. The bus stops had been removed and replaced by a bus station on the western side, with access links to both roundabouts. Parking was also separated: the staff car park occupied the area east of Hospital Road, while a new public car park was constructed east of the hospital, reached directly from the Ring Road.","chinese":"到 2010 年，交通流線已被更有系統地重新設計。 醫院路兩端各建了一個迴旋處，一個位於它與城市路的交界處，另一個位於它與環路相接的位置。 原有巴士站被移除，並由西側的一個巴士總站取代，而該巴士總站有道路連接至兩個迴旋處。 停車安排也被分開：員工停車場佔據醫院路以東的區域，而一個新的公眾停車場則建於醫院東側，可直接從環路進入。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the two maps below show","chinese":"下列兩幅地圖顯示"},{"english":"road access to","chinese":"前往……的道路通達情況"},{"english":"a city hospital","chinese":"城市醫院"},{"english":"in 2007 and in 2010","chinese":"在2007年及2010年"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"selecting and reporting","chinese":"選取並報告"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"The maps compare","chinese":"兩幅地圖比較"},{"english":"compare road access","chinese":"比較道路通達情況"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"the layout","chinese":"佈局"},{"english":"was substantially reorganised","chinese":"已被大幅重新規劃"},{"english":"substantially reorganised","chinese":"大幅重新規劃"},{"english":"two roundabouts","chinese":"兩個迴旋處"},{"english":"a bus station","chinese":"巴士站；巴士總站"},{"english":"were introduced","chinese":"已被增設"},{"english":"the original combined car park","chinese":"原來共用的停車場"},{"english":"combined car park","chinese":"共用停車場"},{"english":"was replaced by","chinese":"已被……取代"},{"english":"separate staff and public parking facilities","chinese":"分開的職員及公眾泊車設施"},{"english":"parking facilities","chinese":"泊車設施"},{"english":"the three main roads","chinese":"三條主要道路"},{"english":"however","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"remained in the same positions","chinese":"仍在相同位置"},{"english":"In 2007","chinese":"在2007年"},{"english":"Hospital Road","chinese":"Hospital Road"},{"english":"ran northwards from","chinese":"由……向北延伸"},{"english":"City Road","chinese":"City Road"},{"english":"the Ring Road","chinese":"Ring Road；環形道路"},{"english":"surrounded the hospital","chinese":"圍繞醫院"},{"english":"six small bus stops","chinese":"六個小型巴士站"},{"english":"were placed along","chinese":"沿着……設置"},{"english":"along Hospital Road","chinese":"沿着 Hospital Road"},{"english":"three on each side","chinese":"每邊三個"},{"english":"a single car park","chinese":"單一停車場"},{"english":"for both staff and the public","chinese":"供職員及公眾使用"},{"english":"stood to the east of","chinese":"位於……以東"},{"english":"to the east of this road","chinese":"在這條路以東"},{"english":"just below","chinese":"就在……下方"},{"english":"By 2010","chinese":"到2010年"},{"english":"traffic flow","chinese":"交通流向"},{"english":"had been redesigned","chinese":"已被重新設計"},{"english":"more systematically","chinese":"更有系統地"},{"english":"a roundabout had been built","chinese":"已建成一個迴旋處"},{"english":"at each end of","chinese":"在……兩端各處"},{"english":"its junction with","chinese":"與……的交匯處"},{"english":"where it joined","chinese":"在它連接……的位置"},{"english":"the bus stops had been removed","chinese":"巴士站已被移除"},{"english":"removed and replaced by","chinese":"被移除並由……取代"},{"english":"on the western side","chinese":"在西面"},{"english":"with access links to","chinese":"設有通往……的連接路"},{"english":"both roundabouts","chinese":"兩個迴旋處"},{"english":"parking was also separated","chinese":"泊車區亦被分開"},{"english":"the staff car park","chinese":"職員停車場"},{"english":"occupied the area east of","chinese":"佔據……以東的區域"},{"english":"while","chinese":"而"},{"english":"a new public car park","chinese":"新的公眾停車場"},{"english":"was constructed east of","chinese":"已在……以東興建"},{"english":"east of the hospital","chinese":"在醫院以東"},{"english":"reached directly from","chinese":"可由……直接到達"},{"english":"directly from the Ring Road","chinese":"直接由 Ring Road 到達"}]},"model-essay-7-ielts-task1-mixed-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-7-ielts-task1-mixed-charts","essayKey":"mixed-charts:7","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-7-ielts-task1-mixed-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/mixed-charts/mixed-charts-7","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The table and pie charts compare attendance at Ashdown Museum and visitors’ satisfaction levels in the years before and after its refurbishment.","chinese":"該表格和圓餅圖比較了阿什當博物館翻新前後兩年中的參觀人數，以及訪客對參觀體驗的滿意程度。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the museum became both more popular and more highly rated after the work was completed. The total number of visitors rose markedly, while positive responses replaced dissatisfaction as the dominant pattern.","chinese":"整體而言，翻新工程完成後，該博物館不但更受歡迎，也獲得了更高的評價。 總訪客人數明顯上升，而正面回應也取代不滿意，成為主要的滿意度模式。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In terms of attendance, the museum received 74,000 visitors before the refurbishment, but this figure increased to 92,000 in the following year, a rise of 18,000. The improvement in satisfaction was even more striking. Before the changes, only 15% of respondents said they were very satisfied and a further 30% were satisfied, meaning that positive feedback accounted for less than half of all responses. After refurbishment, however, these two categories climbed to 35% and 40%, respectively, so three quarters of visitors expressed satisfaction.","chinese":"就參觀人數而言，該博物館在翻新前一年接待了 74,000 名訪客，但在翻新後一年，這一數字上升至 92,000 ，增加了 18,000 人。 滿意度方面的改善甚至更加明顯。 在翻新前，只有 15% 的受訪者表示非常滿意，另有 30% 表示滿意，這意味著正面回饋佔所有回應不到一半。 然而，翻新後，這兩個類別分別上升至 35% 和 40% ，因此有四分之三的訪客表達了滿意。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"By contrast, the proportion of dissatisfied visitors fell sharply. In the year before refurbishment, 40% reported being dissatisfied, making this the largest single group, while 10% were very dissatisfied. In the year after refurbishment, these figures dropped to 15% and 5%, respectively. The share giving no response remained unchanged at 5% in both years.","chinese":"相比之下，不滿意訪客的比例大幅下降。 在翻新前一年， 40% 的訪客表示不滿意，使其成為最大的單一組別，而另有10% 表示非常不滿意。 在翻新後一年，這兩項數字分別下降至 15% 和 5% 。 沒有回應的比例在兩年中都保持在 5% ，沒有變化。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the table below","chinese":"以下表格"},{"english":"the number of visitors","chinese":"參觀人數"},{"english":"Ashdown Museum","chinese":"Ashdown博物館"},{"english":"during the year before","chinese":"在……前一年期間"},{"english":"during the year after","chinese":"在……後一年期間"},{"english":"was refurbished","chinese":"經過翻新"},{"english":"the results of surveys","chinese":"調查結果"},{"english":"asking visitors how satisfied they were","chinese":"詢問遊客滿意程度"},{"english":"how satisfied they were with","chinese":"對……有多滿意"},{"english":"during the same two periods","chinese":"在同樣兩個時期"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"by selecting and reporting","chinese":"透過選取並報告……"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"the table and pie charts","chinese":"表格及圓形圖"},{"english":"compare attendance at","chinese":"比較……的入場人數"},{"english":"visitors' satisfaction levels","chinese":"遊客滿意程度"},{"english":"in the years before and after","chinese":"在……前後兩年"},{"english":"its refurbishment","chinese":"其翻新工程"},{"english":"became both more popular and more highly rated","chinese":"變得更受歡迎且評價更高"},{"english":"more popular","chinese":"更受歡迎"},{"english":"more highly rated","chinese":"評價更高"},{"english":"after the work was completed","chinese":"工程完成後"},{"english":"the total number of visitors","chinese":"總參觀人數"},{"english":"rose markedly","chinese":"顯著上升"},{"english":"positive responses","chinese":"正面回應"},{"english":"replaced dissatisfaction as","chinese":"取代不滿成為……"},{"english":"dissatisfaction","chinese":"不滿"},{"english":"the dominant pattern","chinese":"主要模式"},{"english":"in terms of attendance","chinese":"就參觀人數而言"},{"english":"received 74,000 visitors","chinese":"接待了74,000名遊客"},{"english":"before the refurbishment","chinese":"翻新前"},{"english":"this figure increased to","chinese":"這個數字增加至"},{"english":"in the following year","chinese":"在隨後一年"},{"english":"a rise of 18,000","chinese":"增加18,000"},{"english":"the improvement in satisfaction","chinese":"滿意度的改善"},{"english":"even more striking","chinese":"更加明顯；更為突出"},{"english":"before the changes","chinese":"改動前"},{"english":"respondents","chinese":"受訪者"},{"english":"very satisfied","chinese":"非常滿意"},{"english":"a further 30%","chinese":"另外30%"},{"english":"were satisfied","chinese":"感到滿意"},{"english":"meaning that","chinese":"這意味著"},{"english":"positive feedback","chinese":"正面評價"},{"english":"accounted for","chinese":"佔……"},{"english":"less than half of","chinese":"少於一半"},{"english":"all responses","chinese":"所有回應"},{"english":"after refurbishment","chinese":"翻新後"},{"english":"these two categories","chinese":"這兩個類別"},{"english":"climbed to","chinese":"上升至"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"three quarters of","chinese":"四分之三"},{"english":"expressed satisfaction","chinese":"表示滿意"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"the proportion of dissatisfied visitors","chinese":"不滿遊客的比例"},{"english":"fell sharply","chinese":"大幅下跌"},{"english":"reported being dissatisfied","chinese":"表示不滿"},{"english":"dissatisfied","chinese":"不滿意"},{"english":"the largest single group","chinese":"最大單一組別"},{"english":"very dissatisfied","chinese":"非常不滿意"},{"english":"in the year after refurbishment","chinese":"翻新後一年"},{"english":"these figures dropped to","chinese":"這些數字下降至"},{"english":"dropped to","chinese":"下降至"},{"english":"the share giving no response","chinese":"沒有回應者的比例"},{"english":"no response","chinese":"沒有回應"},{"english":"remained unchanged","chinese":"維持不變"},{"english":"at 5%","chinese":"為5%"},{"english":"in both years","chinese":"在兩年中"},{"english":"attendance figures","chinese":"入場人數數據"},{"english":"satisfaction survey results","chinese":"滿意度調查結果"},{"english":"visitor numbers","chinese":"遊客人數"},{"english":"an increase from X to Y","chinese":"由X增加至Y"},{"english":"a marked increase","chinese":"顯著增加"},{"english":"a sharp fall","chinese":"大幅下跌"},{"english":"negative responses","chinese":"負面回應"},{"english":"a clear shift from X to Y","chinese":"由X明顯轉向Y"},{"english":"from dissatisfaction to satisfaction","chinese":"由不滿轉為滿意"},{"english":"the most notable change","chinese":"最明顯的變化"},{"english":"the least changed category","chinese":"變化最少的類別"},{"english":"the combined share of","chinese":"……的合計比例"},{"english":"satisfied visitors","chinese":"滿意的遊客"},{"english":"dissatisfied visitors","chinese":"不滿的遊客"},{"english":"reached 75%","chinese":"達到75%"},{"english":"fell to 20%","chinese":"下降至20%"},{"english":"showed a major improvement","chinese":"顯示重大改善"},{"english":"became the clear majority","chinese":"成為明顯多數"},{"english":"the refurbishment appears to have","chinese":"翻新工程似乎已經……"},{"english":"improved both X and Y","chinese":"同時改善X和Y"}]},"model-essay-7-ielts-task1-process-diagram":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-7-ielts-task1-process-diagram","essayKey":"process-diagram:7","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-7-ielts-task1-process-diagram","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/process-diagrams/process-diagram-7","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The diagram illustrates the operation of a geothermal power plant and the stages through which underground heat is converted into electricity.","chinese":"該圖說明地熱發電廠的運作方式，以及地下熱能如何經過多個階段被轉化為電力。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, this is a five-stage, linear process. It begins with cold water being pumped deep below the surface and ends with electricity being generated, with the key transformation occurring when water is heated by hot rocks and then used to produce steam.","chinese":"整體而言，這是一個五階段的線性流程。 它從冷水被泵入地表深處開始，以電力的產生結束；其中關鍵轉化發生在水被熱岩加熱後，再被用來產生蒸汽。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"At the first stage, cold water stored at ground level is forced down through an injection well to a depth of about 4.5 kilometres. Once it reaches the geothermal zone, the water passes horizontally through an area of hot rocks, where it absorbs heat. It then travels back towards the surface through a separate production well, in contrast to the initial downward movement through the injection well.","chinese":"第一階段，儲存在地面上的冷水被迫通過注入井下送至約 4.5 公里深處。 當水到達地熱區後，它會水平流經一片熱岩區，並在此吸收熱量。 然後，它會通過一口獨立的生產井返回地表；這與最初通過注入井向下流動形成對比。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"After the heated water has been pumped up, it enters a condenser, from which steam is released. This steam is directed into a turbine, causing the turbine blades to rotate. In the final stage, the rotating turbine powers a generator, which produces electricity that is then transmitted through power lines.","chinese":"加熱後的水被泵上來後，會進入冷凝器，並由此釋放出蒸汽。 這些蒸汽被引導進入渦輪機，使渦輪葉片旋轉。 在最後階段，旋轉的渦輪機帶動發電機，而發電機產生的電力隨後通過電線輸送出去。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"The diagram illustrates","chinese":"圖解顯示"},{"english":"the operation of","chinese":"……的運作"},{"english":"a geothermal power plant","chinese":"地熱發電廠"},{"english":"the stages through which","chinese":"……所經過的階段"},{"english":"underground heat","chinese":"地底熱能"},{"english":"is converted into electricity","chinese":"被轉化成電力"},{"english":"a five-stage, linear process","chinese":"線性的五階段過程"},{"english":"begins with","chinese":"以……開始"},{"english":"cold water being pumped","chinese":"冷水被泵送"},{"english":"deep below the surface","chinese":"地面深處"},{"english":"ends with","chinese":"以……結束"},{"english":"electricity being generated","chinese":"電力被產生"},{"english":"the key transformation","chinese":"關鍵轉化"},{"english":"occurring when","chinese":"發生於……時"},{"english":"is heated by hot rocks","chinese":"被熱岩石加熱"},{"english":"hot rocks","chinese":"熱岩石"},{"english":"used to produce steam","chinese":"用作產生蒸汽"},{"english":"At the first stage","chinese":"在第一階段"},{"english":"stored at ground level","chinese":"儲存在地面水平"},{"english":"ground level","chinese":"地面水平"},{"english":"is forced down through","chinese":"被迫向下通過"},{"english":"an injection well","chinese":"注入井"},{"english":"to a depth of about 4.5 kilometres","chinese":"到約4.5公里深處"},{"english":"Once it reaches","chinese":"一旦到達"},{"english":"the geothermal zone","chinese":"地熱區"},{"english":"passes horizontally through","chinese":"水平流經"},{"english":"an area of hot rocks","chinese":"一片熱岩石區"},{"english":"absorbs heat","chinese":"吸收熱力"},{"english":"travels back towards the surface","chinese":"回流至地面方向"},{"english":"a separate production well","chinese":"另一條生產井"},{"english":"in contrast to","chinese":"與……相反"},{"english":"the initial downward movement","chinese":"最初的向下流動"},{"english":"through the injection well","chinese":"經由注入井"},{"english":"After the heated water has been pumped up","chinese":"當熱水被泵回上來後"},{"english":"the heated water","chinese":"加熱後的水"},{"english":"has been pumped up","chinese":"已被泵回上來"},{"english":"enters a condenser","chinese":"進入冷凝器"},{"english":"a condenser","chinese":"冷凝器"},{"english":"from which steam is released","chinese":"蒸汽從中被釋放"},{"english":"steam is released","chinese":"蒸汽被釋放"},{"english":"is directed into a turbine","chinese":"被引導進入渦輪機"},{"english":"a turbine","chinese":"渦輪機"},{"english":"causing the turbine blades to rotate","chinese":"令渦輪葉片旋轉"},{"english":"turbine blades","chinese":"渦輪葉片"},{"english":"to rotate","chinese":"旋轉"},{"english":"In the final stage","chinese":"在最後階段"},{"english":"the rotating turbine","chinese":"旋轉中的渦輪機"},{"english":"powers a generator","chinese":"驅動發電機"},{"english":"a generator","chinese":"發電機"},{"english":"produces electricity","chinese":"產生電力"},{"english":"is then transmitted through","chinese":"然後經由……輸送"},{"english":"power lines","chinese":"輸電線"}]},"model-essay-7-ielts-task1-tables":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-7-ielts-task1-tables","essayKey":"tables:7","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-7-ielts-task1-tables","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/tables/table-7","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The table compares international tourist arrivals, measured in millions, in the listed destinations in 2009 and 2010, together with the percentage change over the period.","chinese":"該表格比較了所列目的地在 2009 年和 2010 年的國際遊客到訪人數，以百萬為單位，並展示了期間的百分比變化。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, France remained the most visited destination, despite recording no growth. Most places attracted more tourists in the second year, but the increases were generally modest among the larger markets and far stronger among Germany, China and Turkey. Hong Kong was the only destination to decline.","chinese":"整體而言，法國雖然沒有錄得增長，但仍然是最多遊客到訪的目的地。 大部分地區在第二年吸引了更多遊客，但較大型市場的升幅普遍溫和，而德國、中國和土耳其的增長則強勁得多。 香港是唯一出現下跌的目的地。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Among the leading destinations, France received 76 million tourists in both years, staying well ahead of the US, whose figure edged up from 66 to 67 million. Spain and the UK were level at 55 million in 2009, but the UK grew more quickly, reaching 57 million and narrowly overtaking Spain, which rose to 56 million. Italy also increased slightly, from 44 to 45 million.","chinese":"在主要目的地之中，法國兩年均接待了 7,600 萬名遊客，仍然大幅領先美國；而美國的數字則由 6,600 萬微升至 6,700 萬。 西班牙和英國在 2009 年同為 5,500 萬，但英國增長較快，達到 5,700 萬，並以輕微差距超越西班牙；西班牙則上升至 5,600 萬。 意大利亦輕微上升，由 4,400 萬增至 4,500 萬。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The remaining destinations showed much sharper relative changes. Turkey, China and Germany each gained 12 million arrivals, climbing from 33 to 45 million, 22 to 34 million and 11 to 23 million respectively. Because Germany started from the lowest base, this represented the largest percentage rise, at 109%. By contrast, Hong Kong fell from 10 to 9 million, a decrease of 11%.","chinese":"其餘目的地則呈現出更明顯的相對變化。 土耳其、中國和德國的到訪人數均增加了 1,200 萬，分別由 3,300 萬升至 4,500萬、由 2,200 萬升至 3,400 萬，以及由 1,100 萬升至 2,300 萬。 由於德國的起點最低，因此這代表了最大的百分比升幅，達 109% 。 相比之下，香港由 1,000 萬下降至 900 萬，跌幅為 11% 。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the table compares","chinese":"表格比較"},{"english":"international tourist arrivals","chinese":"國際旅客到訪人次"},{"english":"measured in millions","chinese":"以百萬計"},{"english":"listed destinations","chinese":"列出的目的地"},{"english":"in 2009 and 2010","chinese":"在2009年和2010年"},{"english":"together with","chinese":"連同；以及"},{"english":"percentage change","chinese":"百分比變化"},{"english":"over the period","chinese":"在該期間"},{"english":"remained the most visited destination","chinese":"仍然是最多人到訪的目的地"},{"english":"the most visited destination","chinese":"最多人到訪的目的地"},{"english":"despite recording no growth","chinese":"儘管沒有錄得增長"},{"english":"recording no growth","chinese":"沒有錄得增長"},{"english":"most places attracted more tourists","chinese":"大部分地方吸引更多旅客"},{"english":"in the second year","chinese":"在第二年"},{"english":"generally modest","chinese":"普遍溫和"},{"english":"larger markets","chinese":"較大型市場"},{"english":"far stronger among","chinese":"在……之中強勁得多"},{"english":"the only destination to decline","chinese":"唯一下跌的目的地"},{"english":"leading destinations","chinese":"主要目的地"},{"english":"received 76 million tourists","chinese":"接待了7,600萬名旅客"},{"english":"in both years","chinese":"在兩年中"},{"english":"staying well ahead of","chinese":"保持大幅領先"},{"english":"well ahead of","chinese":"遠高於；大幅領先"},{"english":"the US","chinese":"美國"},{"english":"whose figure edged up","chinese":"其數字輕微上升"},{"english":"edged up from X to Y","chinese":"由 X 輕微上升至 Y"},{"english":"Spain and the UK","chinese":"西班牙和英國"},{"english":"were level at","chinese":"同為；持平於"},{"english":"but the UK grew more quickly","chinese":"但英國增長較快"},{"english":"reaching 57 million","chinese":"達到5,700萬"},{"english":"narrowly overtaking","chinese":"僅僅超越"},{"english":"which rose to","chinese":"而……上升至"},{"english":"increased slightly","chinese":"輕微增加"},{"english":"the remaining destinations","chinese":"其餘目的地"},{"english":"much sharper relative changes","chinese":"相對變化大得多"},{"english":"relative changes","chinese":"相對變化"},{"english":"each gained","chinese":"各增加"},{"english":"gained 12 million arrivals","chinese":"增加1,200萬到訪人次"},{"english":"climbing from X to Y","chinese":"由 X 攀升至 Y"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"started from the lowest base","chinese":"從最低基數開始"},{"english":"the lowest base","chinese":"最低基數；最低起點"},{"english":"this represented","chinese":"這代表"},{"english":"the largest percentage rise","chinese":"最大百分比升幅"},{"english":"at 109%","chinese":"為109%"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"fell from X to Y","chinese":"由 X 下跌至 Y"},{"english":"a decrease of 11%","chinese":"11%的跌幅"},{"english":"tourist numbers","chinese":"旅客人數"},{"english":"visitor arrivals","chinese":"旅客到訪人次"},{"english":"tourist destinations","chinese":"旅遊目的地"},{"english":"attract tourists","chinese":"吸引旅客"},{"english":"no change","chinese":"沒有變化"},{"english":"modest growth","chinese":"溫和增長"},{"english":"strong growth","chinese":"強勁增長"},{"english":"a sharp increase","chinese":"大幅增加"},{"english":"a slight increase","chinese":"輕微增加"},{"english":"a small rise","chinese":"小幅上升"},{"english":"a fall in arrivals","chinese":"到訪人次下跌"},{"english":"unchanged at","chinese":"維持在"},{"english":"rose by 12 million","chinese":"增加1,200萬"},{"english":"more than doubled","chinese":"增加超過一倍"},{"english":"overtook Spain","chinese":"超越西班牙"},{"english":"remained ahead of","chinese":"仍然領先於"},{"english":"ranked first","chinese":"排名第一"},{"english":"ranked second","chinese":"排名第二"},{"english":"among the top destinations","chinese":"在主要目的地之中"},{"english":"smaller markets","chinese":"較小型市場"},{"english":"a higher growth rate","chinese":"較高增長率"},{"english":"the greatest absolute increase","chinese":"最大實際增幅"},{"english":"absolute increase","chinese":"實際增幅"},{"english":"percentage increase","chinese":"百分比升幅"},{"english":"percentage decline","chinese":"百分比跌幅"},{"english":"the overall pattern","chinese":"整體模式"},{"english":"remained dominant","chinese":"仍然佔主導地位"},{"english":"widened the gap","chinese":"擴大差距"},{"english":"narrowed the gap","chinese":"收窄差距"},{"english":"caught up with","chinese":"追上"},{"english":"broadly stable","chinese":"大致穩定"},{"english":"stronger relative performance","chinese":"最強相對表現"},{"english":"weaker performance","chinese":"較弱表現"},{"english":"the only negative figure","chinese":"唯一負數"},{"english":"positive growth","chinese":"正增長"},{"english":"the highest figure","chinese":"最高數字"},{"english":"the lowest figure","chinese":"最低數字"},{"english":"compared with","chinese":"與……相比"},{"english":"by the end of the period","chinese":"到該期間結束時"},{"english":"from a lower starting point","chinese":"從較低起點開始"},{"english":"in absolute terms","chinese":"以實際數字計"},{"english":"in percentage terms","chinese":"以百分比計"},{"english":"tourist arrivals rose","chinese":"旅客到訪人次上升"},{"english":"tourist arrivals declined","chinese":"旅客到訪人次下跌"}]},"model-essay-8-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-8-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:8","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-8-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q8","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Schools are increasingly expected to prepare young people not only for academic success but also for life in an interconnected world. In this context, some educators argue that international exchange visits are beneficial for teenagers. I strongly believe that the advantages of these programmes far outweigh the disadvantages, because they develop maturity and intercultural competence in ways that ordinary classroom learning rarely can, whereas the drawbacks are generally short-lived and manageable.","chinese":"無論在工作還是私人生活中，越來越多的溝通如今都是透過數位科技進行，而不是面對面交流。 儘管這種發展可能削弱人際關係的品質，並增加誤解的風險， 我認為整體而言，它的優點更大，因為它使溝通變得更有效率，並讓人們即使相隔遙遠也能保持聯繫。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The greatest advantage of international exchange visits is that they accelerate teenagers’ personal growth. When students spend time in a different country, they are forced to deal with unfamiliar routines, different school expectations and everyday practical challenges without depending entirely on their parents. This process makes them more independent, adaptable and responsible. For example, a student staying with a host family may initially struggle to follow a new timetable or communicate minor needs, but very quickly that student learns to ask questions confidently, manage time more effectively and solve problems calmly. A second major benefit is that these visits deepen cultural and linguistic understanding. Instead of learning about another society in an abstract way, teenagers experience it directly through conversation, school life and daily interaction. As a result, they often become more open-minded and more capable of communicating with people from different backgrounds.","chinese":"科技化溝通最主要的優點是速度和便利性。 在專業環境中，電子郵件、即時通訊平台和視像會議免除了人們出行的需要，並使決策幾乎可以即時作出。 這不但縮短了回應時間、降低了營運成本，還使公司能夠非常輕鬆地協調分布在不同城市甚至不同大洲的團隊。 例如，一位經理可以透過一次線上會議便與海外同事解決生產問題，而不是等待數天才進行一次面對面的討論。 同樣的情況也適用於社交層面：住得很遠的父母、子女和朋友仍然可以透過通話和訊息每天聯絡。 結果是，人際關係更容易維持，也較不會隨時間而逐漸淡化。 例如，一個家庭即使成員分散在不同國家，仍然可以透過視像通話分享日常近況並提供情感支持。 因此，數位溝通大大提升了工作和個人生活中的效率與可及性。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Admittedly, there are some disadvantages, but they are not significant enough to challenge the overall value of such visits. One concern is cost, since travel, accommodation and insurance can be expensive. However, many exchange programmes are short, subsidised or organised through school partnerships, so the financial burden is often reduced considerably. Another possible drawback is that some teenagers may feel homesick or anxious in an unfamiliar environment. Nevertheless, this discomfort is usually temporary and can even be beneficial, because overcoming it helps young people build emotional resilience. For instance, a student who feels lonely during the first few days of an exchange often returns home noticeably more confident after forming friendships and adapting successfully.","chinese":"然而，數位溝通也有重要的缺點，其中最嚴重的是它缺乏情感上的豐富性。 面對面的交談能傳達語氣、面部表情和肢體語言，這些都有助於人們準確理解意思、表達同理心並建立信任。 當這些線索消失時，訊息便更容易被誤解，從而導致困惑甚至衝突。 例如，一封簡短的電郵或文字訊息即使本無惡意，也可能顯得冷淡甚至帶有敵意。 這在職場中尤其成問題，因為信任和細膩的理解對領導、協商和團隊合作都至關重要。 長遠而言，過度依賴螢幕也可能助長膚淺的社交習慣，因此人們即使在線上一直保持聯絡，仍可能感到孤立。 例如，一個人即使經常透過社交媒體聊天，仍可能感到孤單，因為數位接觸無法完全取代真正的關注和人的陪伴。 因此，儘管科技讓溝通成為可能，它同時也可能削弱清晰度、信任感和情感深度。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, international exchange visits offer teenagers far more than a simple change of scenery. Because they foster independence, cultural awareness and real-world communication skills, and because their disadvantages are limited and manageable, their advantages decisively outweigh their disadvantages.","chinese":"總結來說，透過科技進行溝通在效率和可及性方面具有明顯優勢，儘管它可能削弱人際互動的深度與清晰度。 整體而言，我認為其優點大於缺點，因為數位工具使工作和個人生活中的溝通都能跨越時間與距離而有效運作。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"increasingly expected to","chinese":"越來越被期望／要求去……"},{"english":"prepare young people for","chinese":"為年輕人準備好面對……"},{"english":"not only for...but also for...","chinese":"不只為了……也為了……"},{"english":"academic success","chinese":"學業成功"},{"english":"an interconnected world","chinese":"互相聯繫的世界"},{"english":"in this context","chinese":"在這個背景下"},{"english":"educators argue that","chinese":"教育工作者認為"},{"english":"international exchange visits","chinese":"國際交流訪問"},{"english":"beneficial for teenagers","chinese":"對青少年有益"},{"english":"strongly believe that","chinese":"強烈相信"},{"english":"the advantages of these programmes","chinese":"這些計劃的好處"},{"english":"far outweigh the disadvantages","chinese":"遠遠大於缺點"},{"english":"develop maturity","chinese":"培養成熟"},{"english":"intercultural competence","chinese":"跨文化能力"},{"english":"ordinary classroom learning","chinese":"普通課堂學習"},{"english":"rarely can","chinese":"很少能夠"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相比之下"},{"english":"drawbacks","chinese":"缺點"},{"english":"short-lived and manageable","chinese":"短暫且可處理的"},{"english":"the greatest advantage","chinese":"最大的好處"},{"english":"accelerate teenagers' personal growth","chinese":"加快青少年的個人成長"},{"english":"personal growth","chinese":"個人成長"},{"english":"spend time in a different country","chinese":"在不同國家逗留"},{"english":"be forced to deal with","chinese":"被迫處理"},{"english":"unfamiliar routines","chinese":"不熟悉的日常規律"},{"english":"different school expectations","chinese":"不同的學校期望"},{"english":"everyday practical challenges","chinese":"日常實際挑戰"},{"english":"without depending entirely on","chinese":"不完全依賴"},{"english":"this process","chinese":"這個過程"},{"english":"independent, adaptable and responsible","chinese":"獨立、有適應力和負責任"},{"english":"staying with a host family","chinese":"與寄宿家庭同住"},{"english":"initially struggle to","chinese":"起初難以"},{"english":"follow a new timetable","chinese":"遵循新的時間表"},{"english":"communicate minor needs","chinese":"表達小需要"},{"english":"very quickly","chinese":"很快"},{"english":"ask questions confidently","chinese":"有信心地提問"},{"english":"manage time more effectively","chinese":"更有效地管理時間"},{"english":"solve problems calmly","chinese":"冷靜地解決問題"},{"english":"a second major benefit","chinese":"第二個主要好處"},{"english":"deepen cultural and linguistic understanding","chinese":"加深文化和語言理解"},{"english":"instead of","chinese":"而不是"},{"english":"in an abstract way","chinese":"以抽象方式"},{"english":"experience it directly","chinese":"直接體驗它"},{"english":"daily interaction","chinese":"日常互動"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"open-minded","chinese":"思想開明的"},{"english":"capable of communicating with","chinese":"有能力與……溝通"},{"english":"different backgrounds","chinese":"不同背景"},{"english":"admittedly","chinese":"誠然"},{"english":"significant enough to","chinese":"重要到足以……"},{"english":"challenge the overall value of","chinese":"質疑……的整體價值"},{"english":"such visits","chinese":"這類訪問"},{"english":"one concern is cost","chinese":"其中一個憂慮是費用"},{"english":"travel, accommodation and insurance","chinese":"交通、住宿和保險"},{"english":"exchange programmes","chinese":"交流計劃"},{"english":"subsidised","chinese":"受資助的"},{"english":"organised through school partnerships","chinese":"透過學校合作安排"},{"english":"financial burden","chinese":"財政負擔"},{"english":"reduced considerably","chinese":"大幅減輕／降低"},{"english":"possible drawback","chinese":"可能的缺點"},{"english":"homesick","chinese":"思鄉的"},{"english":"anxious","chinese":"焦慮的"},{"english":"an unfamiliar environment","chinese":"陌生環境"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"temporary","chinese":"暫時的"},{"english":"can even be beneficial","chinese":"甚至可以是有益的"},{"english":"overcoming it","chinese":"克服它"},{"english":"build emotional resilience","chinese":"建立情緒抗逆力"},{"english":"during the first few days of","chinese":"在……最初幾天"},{"english":"returns home","chinese":"回家；回到本地"},{"english":"noticeably more confident","chinese":"明顯更有信心"},{"english":"forming friendships","chinese":"建立友誼"},{"english":"adapting successfully","chinese":"成功適應"},{"english":"offer teenagers far more than","chinese":"給青少年的遠不止……"},{"english":"a simple change of scenery","chinese":"簡單換個環境"},{"english":"foster independence","chinese":"培養獨立性"},{"english":"cultural awareness","chinese":"文化意識"},{"english":"real-world communication skills","chinese":"現實世界中的溝通技巧"},{"english":"limited and manageable","chinese":"有限且可處理的"},{"english":"decisively outweigh","chinese":"明顯大於"}]},"model-essay-8-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-8-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:8","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-8-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q8","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Management interviews often examine far more than a candidate’s technical competence, because managers are expected to influence people, make decisions and represent the values of an organisation. In my view, leadership is not an innate skill; rather, it is a practical ability developed through training, experience and self-awareness. Companies also tend to look for emotional intelligence, sound judgement and reliability when selecting managers.","chinese":"管理層面試通常考察的遠遠不只是候選人的專業能力，因為經理被期望能影響他人、作出決策，並代表一個機構的價值觀。 在我看來，領導力並不是一種天生技能；相反，它是一種透過訓練、經驗和自我覺察而發展出來的實用能力。 公司在挑選經理時，通常也會尋找情緒智商、良好判斷力和可靠性。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Leadership should not be seen as something people are simply born with. Although some individuals may naturally appear more confident or charismatic, these qualities alone do not make them effective leaders. Real leadership involves listening carefully, resolving conflict, setting clear expectations and helping others perform well under pressure. These abilities are usually built through repeated exposure to difficult situations. For example, a junior employee who gradually learns how to handle dissatisfied clients, support weaker colleagues and organise team projects may become a far stronger leader than someone who merely has a naturally dominant personality. In this sense, leadership is less like a gift and more like a muscle: it becomes stronger when it is trained, tested and corrected.","chinese":"領導力不應被視為人們只是天生便擁有的東西。 儘管有些人可能天生看起來更有自信或更有魅力，但單靠這些特質並不能使他們成為有效的領導者。 真正的領導力包括仔細聆聽、解決衝突、設定清晰期望，以及幫助他人在壓力下有良好表現。 這些能力通常是透過反覆面對困難情況而建立起來的。 例如，一位初級員工如果逐漸學會如何處理不滿的客戶、支援能力較弱的同事，以及組織團隊項目，可能會比一個只是天生性格強勢的人，成為更出色的領導者。 從這個意義上說，領導力與其說像一份天賦，不如說更像一塊肌肉：當它被訓練、考驗和修正時，它就會變得更強。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Apart from leadership, companies usually want managers who can understand people and make balanced decisions. Emotional intelligence is essential because a manager who cannot read the mood of a team may create unnecessary tension, even if their technical knowledge is excellent. A good manager must know when to encourage, when to challenge and when to step back. In addition, firms look for integrity and accountability. Managers often control budgets, evaluate staff and communicate sensitive information, so they must be trusted to act fairly rather than protect their own interests. Without these qualities, a manager may become efficient on paper but harmful in practice.","chinese":"除了領導力之外，公司通常希望經理能夠理解他人，並作出平衡的決定。 情緒智商是必不可少的，因為一位無法察覺團隊氣氛的經理，即使技術知識很出色，也可能製造不必要的緊張。 一位好的經理必須知道何時應該鼓勵、何時應該提出挑戰，以及何時應該退一步。 此外，企業也會尋找誠信和問責能力。 經理經常掌管預算、評估員工，並傳達敏感資訊，因此他們必須被信任會公平行事，而不是保護自己的利益。 如果沒有這些品質，一位經理可能在表面上顯得有效率，但在實際工作中卻會造成傷害"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, leadership is not an inborn talent but a skill shaped by experience and deliberate improvement. For this reason, companies rightly assess personality as well as knowledge, especially qualities such as empathy, judgement, integrity and responsibility.","chinese":"總結來說，領導力並不是一種天生才能，而是一種由經驗和有意識的改進所塑造的技能 基於這個原因，公司不只評估知識，也評估性格是合理的，尤其是同理心、判斷力、誠信和責任感等品質。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"management interviews","chinese":"管理層面試"},{"english":"examine far more than","chinese":"考核的遠不止……"},{"english":"technical competence","chinese":"技術能力"},{"english":"be expected to","chinese":"被期望要……"},{"english":"influence people","chinese":"影響他人"},{"english":"make decisions","chinese":"作出決定"},{"english":"represent the values of","chinese":"代表……的價值觀"},{"english":"an organisation","chinese":"一個機構"},{"english":"an innate skill","chinese":"天生技能"},{"english":"a practical ability","chinese":"實際能力"},{"english":"developed through","chinese":"透過……培養出來"},{"english":"self-awareness","chinese":"自我覺察"},{"english":"tend to look for","chinese":"傾向尋找"},{"english":"emotional intelligence","chinese":"情緒智商"},{"english":"sound judgement","chinese":"良好的判斷力"},{"english":"reliability","chinese":"可靠性"},{"english":"be seen as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"be born with","chinese":"與生俱來"},{"english":"appear more confident","chinese":"顯得更有信心"},{"english":"charismatic","chinese":"有魅力的"},{"english":"these qualities alone","chinese":"單靠這些特質"},{"english":"effective leaders","chinese":"有效的領袖"},{"english":"real leadership involves","chinese":"真正的領導力包括"},{"english":"listening carefully","chinese":"細心聆聽"},{"english":"resolving conflict","chinese":"解決衝突"},{"english":"setting clear expectations","chinese":"訂立清晰期望"},{"english":"perform well under pressure","chinese":"在壓力下表現良好"},{"english":"repeated exposure to","chinese":"反覆接觸……"},{"english":"difficult situations","chinese":"困難情況"},{"english":"a junior employee","chinese":"初級員工"},{"english":"gradually learns how to","chinese":"逐漸學會如何……"},{"english":"handle dissatisfied clients","chinese":"處理不滿的客戶"},{"english":"support weaker colleagues","chinese":"支援能力較弱的同事"},{"english":"organise team projects","chinese":"組織團隊項目"},{"english":"a far stronger leader","chinese":"強得多的領袖"},{"english":"naturally dominant personality","chinese":"天生強勢的性格"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"less like a gift and more like","chinese":"與其說像……，不如說像……"},{"english":"trained, tested and corrected","chinese":"經過訓練、考驗和修正"},{"english":"apart from leadership","chinese":"除了領導力之外"},{"english":"understand people","chinese":"理解人"},{"english":"make balanced decisions","chinese":"作出平衡的決定"},{"english":"is essential because","chinese":"……是必要的，因為"},{"english":"read the mood of","chinese":"察覺……的氣氛"},{"english":"create unnecessary tension","chinese":"製造不必要的緊張氣氛"},{"english":"technical knowledge","chinese":"專業知識"},{"english":"know when to","chinese":"知道何時應該……"},{"english":"step back","chinese":"退一步；放手"},{"english":"in addition","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"look for integrity and accountability","chinese":"尋找誠信和問責精神"},{"english":"control budgets","chinese":"管理預算"},{"english":"evaluate staff","chinese":"評核職員"},{"english":"communicate sensitive information","chinese":"傳達敏感資料"},{"english":"be trusted to act fairly","chinese":"被信任會公平行事"},{"english":"protect their own interests","chinese":"保護自己的利益"},{"english":"efficient on paper","chinese":"表面上有效率"},{"english":"harmful in practice","chinese":"實際上有害"},{"english":"an inborn talent","chinese":"天生才能"},{"english":"shaped by experience","chinese":"由經驗塑造"},{"english":"deliberate improvement","chinese":"有意識的改進"},{"english":"rightly assess","chinese":"正確地評估"},{"english":"personality as well as knowledge","chinese":"性格以及知識"},{"english":"qualities such as","chinese":"例如……的素質"},{"english":"empathy","chinese":"同理心"},{"english":"judgement, integrity and responsibility","chinese":"判斷力、誠信和責任感"}]},"model-essay-8-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-8-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:8","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-8-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q8","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Happiness at different stages of life is often debated. Some people believe that teenagers enjoy a happier life than adults, while others argue that adulthood offers a deeper and more stable form of happiness. In my view, adults are generally happier because they have greater independence and a clearer sense of direction.","chinese":"人生不同階段的幸福感經常受到討論。有些人認為青少年的生活比成年人更快樂，而另一些人則認為成年生活能帶來更深層、更穩定的幸福感。 在我看來，成年人通常更快樂，因為他們擁有更大的獨立性和更清晰的人生方向。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"On the one hand, teenagers may appear happier because their lives are usually less burdened by serious responsibilities. Many of them do not have to pay bills, support a family, or make major financial decisions, so they can spend more time on friendships, hobbies, entertainment, and personal interests. For example, a secondary school student may finish classes and then play sports, chat with friends, or watch films without worrying about rent or job security. This freedom can make teenage life feel light and enjoyable. In this sense, adolescence can seem like a carefree period, especially when compared with the pressure-filled world of work and family duties.","chinese":"一方面，青少年可能看起來更快樂，因為他們的生活通常較少受到重大責任的負擔 他們當中許多人不需要支付帳單、養家，或作出重大的財務決定，因此可以把更多時間花在友誼、興趣、娛樂和個人喜好上。 例如，一名中學生放學後可以去做運動、和朋友聊天，或看電影，而不必擔心租金或工作穩定性。 這種自由能使青少年生活感覺輕鬆而愉快。 從這個意義上說，青春期可能看起來像是一段無憂無慮的時期，尤其是與充滿工作和家庭責任壓力的成人世界相比。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"On the other hand, I believe adults are happier overall because their happiness is often built on independence, achievement, and emotional maturity. Adults can choose where to live, what career to pursue, how to spend their money, and who to build relationships with. These choices give them control over their lives, which is a powerful source of satisfaction. Moreover, adults are usually better at understanding themselves and dealing with problems. For instance, an adult who has worked hard to develop a career or support a family may feel a strong sense of purpose that teenagers rarely experience. Although adult life can be stressful, that stress is often balanced by meaningful rewards.","chinese":"另一方面，我認為成年人整體上更快樂，因為他們的幸福感往往建立在獨立、成就和情感成熟之上。 成年人可以選擇住在哪裡、追求甚麼職業、如何使用金錢，以及與誰建立關係。 這些選擇讓他們能掌控自己的生活，而這是一種強大的滿足感來源。 此外，成年人通常更擅長了解自己和處理問題。 例如，一名努力發展事業或支撐家庭的成年人，可能會感受到一種青少年很少經歷到的強烈人生目標感。 雖然成年生活可能充滿壓力，但這種壓力往往會被有意義的回報所平衡。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, teenagers may have more free time and fewer responsibilities, which can make them seem happier on the surface. However, I believe adults are generally happier because their lives contain more independence, purpose, and lasting fulfillment. Happiness is not just the absence of pressure; it is also the feeling that one’s life has direction and meaning.","chinese":"總結來說，青少年可能有更多自由時間和較少責任，這使他們表面上看起來更快樂。 然而，我認為成年人通常更快樂，因為他們的生活包含更多獨立性、目標感和持久的滿足。 幸福不只是沒有壓力；它也是一種感覺，即一個人的人生具有方向和意義。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"different stages of life","chinese":"人生不同階段"},{"english":"is often debated","chinese":"經常受到討論"},{"english":"teenagers enjoy a happier life","chinese":"青少年享有更快樂的生活"},{"english":"adulthood offers","chinese":"成年階段提供"},{"english":"a deeper and more stable form of","chinese":"更深層、更穩定的……形式"},{"english":"In my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"generally happier","chinese":"整體上更快樂"},{"english":"greater independence","chinese":"更大的獨立性"},{"english":"a clearer sense of direction","chinese":"更清晰的方向感"},{"english":"On the one hand","chinese":"一方面"},{"english":"may appear happier","chinese":"可能看起來更快樂"},{"english":"less burdened by","chinese":"較少受……負擔"},{"english":"serious responsibilities","chinese":"重大責任"},{"english":"pay bills","chinese":"交帳單"},{"english":"support a family","chinese":"養家"},{"english":"make major financial decisions","chinese":"作出重大財務決定"},{"english":"spend more time on","chinese":"花更多時間在……上"},{"english":"personal interests","chinese":"個人興趣"},{"english":"a secondary school student","chinese":"中學生"},{"english":"finish classes","chinese":"完成課堂"},{"english":"chat with friends","chinese":"和朋友聊天"},{"english":"without worrying about","chinese":"不用擔心"},{"english":"rent","chinese":"租金"},{"english":"job security","chinese":"工作保障"},{"english":"feel light and enjoyable","chinese":"感覺輕鬆愉快"},{"english":"In this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"adolescence","chinese":"青春期；青少年階段"},{"english":"a carefree period","chinese":"無憂無慮的時期"},{"english":"especially when compared with","chinese":"特別是與……相比時"},{"english":"pressure-filled","chinese":"充滿壓力的"},{"english":"the world of work","chinese":"職場世界"},{"english":"family duties","chinese":"家庭責任"},{"english":"On the other hand","chinese":"另一方面"},{"english":"happier overall","chinese":"整體上更快樂"},{"english":"built on independence","chinese":"建基於獨立"},{"english":"achievement","chinese":"成就"},{"english":"emotional maturity","chinese":"情緒成熟"},{"english":"choose where to live","chinese":"選擇住在哪裏"},{"english":"what career to pursue","chinese":"追求甚麼事業"},{"english":"how to spend their money","chinese":"如何花錢"},{"english":"build relationships with","chinese":"與……建立關係"},{"english":"give them control over","chinese":"讓他們掌控"},{"english":"control over their lives","chinese":"對自己生活的掌控"},{"english":"a powerful source of satisfaction","chinese":"強大的滿足感來源"},{"english":"Moreover","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"better at understanding themselves","chinese":"更擅長了解自己"},{"english":"dealing with problems","chinese":"處理問題"},{"english":"For instance","chinese":"例如"},{"english":"worked hard to","chinese":"努力去"},{"english":"develop a career","chinese":"發展事業"},{"english":"support a family","chinese":"養家"},{"english":"a strong sense of purpose","chinese":"強烈的目標感"},{"english":"rarely experience","chinese":"很少經歷"},{"english":"adult life","chinese":"成年生活"},{"english":"be stressful","chinese":"有壓力"},{"english":"balanced by","chinese":"由……平衡"},{"english":"meaningful rewards","chinese":"有意義的回報"},{"english":"free time","chinese":"空閒時間"},{"english":"fewer responsibilities","chinese":"較少責任"},{"english":"on the surface","chinese":"表面上"},{"english":"However","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"contain more independence","chinese":"包含更多獨立性"},{"english":"lasting fulfilment","chinese":"持久的滿足感"},{"english":"the absence of pressure","chinese":"沒有壓力"},{"english":"one's life has direction and meaning","chinese":"自己的人生有方向和意義"}]},"model-essay-8-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-8-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:8","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-8-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q8","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In competitive markets, even products that genuinely solve consumers’ problems do not automatically sell themselves. Some people therefore argue that advertising is unnecessary if a product is already high-quality and useful. This essay completely disagrees, because advertising is still essential both for informing consumers and for helping good products gain credibility in crowded markets.","chinese":"在競爭激烈的市場中，即使產品確實能解決消費者的問題，也不會自然而然地自行暢銷 因此，有些人認為，如果一項產品本身已經品質優良而且實用，廣告便沒有必要。 本文完全不同意這種看法，因為廣告在向消費者提供資訊，以及幫助優質產品在選擇繁多、競爭激烈的市場中建立可信度這兩方面，仍然至關重要。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason advertising remains necessary is that consumers cannot choose a product they have never encountered. In most industries, buyers face countless similar options and do not have time to research each one independently. Advertising therefore performs an informative function: it tells people what a product does, who it is for, how it differs from rival goods and where it can be bought. Without this information, even an excellent product may remain invisible, meaning consumer needs are not met in practice. For example, a small company may produce an energy-efficient washing machine that cuts electricity bills and lasts longer than competing models, yet many households will still buy familiar brands if they never hear about this better alternative.","chinese":"廣告之所以仍然有其必要，第一個原因在於：消費者不可能選擇一項自己從未接觸過的產品。 在大多數行業中，買家面對的是無數相似的選擇，並沒有時間逐一獨立研究每一項產品。 因此，廣告發揮了資訊傳遞的功能：它告訴人們產品有甚麼用途、適合哪些人、與競爭商品有何不同，以及可以在哪裡購買。 若缺乏這些資訊，即使是一項優秀的產品，也可能一直不被看見，這意味着消費者的需要在實際上無法得到滿足。 例如，一家小公司也許生產出一款節能洗衣機，不但能降低電費開支，而且比競爭對手的型號更耐用；然而，如果許多家庭從未聽說過這個更好的替代選項，他們仍然會購買自己熟悉的品牌。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Advertising is also necessary because quality alone does not remove perceived risk. When a brand is unfamiliar, consumers may still worry about reliability, safety or after-sales service, even if the product itself is highly effective. Advertising reduces this hesitation by showing demonstrations, guarantees, certifications and consistent brand messages, all of which make a company appear more credible. For instance, a start-up producing safer baby bottles may be overlooked until its advertising explains the materials used, the testing standards met and the refund policy offered.","chinese":"廣告之所以同樣必要，是因為單憑品質本身，並不能消除消費者主觀感受到的風險。 當一個品牌並不為人熟悉時，即使產品本身十分有效，消費者仍可能擔心它的可靠性、安全性或售後服務。 廣告透過展示產品示範、保證、認證，以及一致的品牌訊息，來減少這種猶豫；而這一切都能使一家公司顯得更具可信性。 例如，一家生產更安全奶瓶的新創公司，可能一直被人忽視，直到它的廣告清楚說明所採用的材料、符合的測試標準，以及所提供的退款政策為止。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely disagree that advertising becomes unnecessary when a product is good. However useful a product may be, consumers still need information and reassurance, and without advertising many excellent goods would remain unnoticed and untrusted.","chinese":"總而言之，我完全不同意「只要產品優良，廣告便變得沒有必要」這種說法。 無論一項產品多麼實用，消費者仍然需要資訊與安心感；若沒有廣告，許多優秀的商品都會繼續無人注意，也難以獲得信任。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"in competitive markets","chinese":"在競爭激烈的市場中"},{"english":"genuinely solve consumers' problems","chinese":"真正解決消費者的問題"},{"english":"automatically sell themselves","chinese":"自動賣出；自然有人買"},{"english":"some people therefore argue that","chinese":"因此有些人認為"},{"english":"advertising is unnecessary","chinese":"廣告是不必要的"},{"english":"high-quality and useful","chinese":"高質素而實用"},{"english":"completely disagrees","chinese":"完全不同意"},{"english":"be still essential","chinese":"仍然必要"},{"english":"informing consumers","chinese":"向消費者提供資料"},{"english":"helping good products gain credibility","chinese":"幫助好產品建立可信度"},{"english":"gain credibility","chinese":"建立可信度"},{"english":"crowded markets","chinese":"擁擠的市場；競爭激烈的市場"},{"english":"the first reason","chinese":"第一個原因"},{"english":"remains necessary","chinese":"仍然必要"},{"english":"choose a product","chinese":"選擇產品"},{"english":"have never encountered","chinese":"從未接觸過"},{"english":"in most industries","chinese":"在大多數行業中"},{"english":"face countless similar options","chinese":"面對無數相似選擇"},{"english":"research each one independently","chinese":"獨立研究每一個"},{"english":"perform an informative function","chinese":"發揮提供資訊的功能"},{"english":"what a product does","chinese":"產品的用途"},{"english":"who it is for","chinese":"適合哪些人"},{"english":"differs from rival goods","chinese":"與競爭產品不同"},{"english":"rival goods","chinese":"競爭產品"},{"english":"where it can be bought","chinese":"可以在哪裏購買"},{"english":"without this information","chinese":"沒有這些資料"},{"english":"remain invisible","chinese":"仍然不被看見"},{"english":"consumer needs are not met","chinese":"消費者需要未被滿足"},{"english":"in practice","chinese":"在實際情況中"},{"english":"a small company","chinese":"小型公司"},{"english":"energy-efficient","chinese":"節能的"},{"english":"washing machine","chinese":"洗衣機"},{"english":"cut electricity bills","chinese":"減少電費"},{"english":"last longer than","chinese":"比……更耐用"},{"english":"competing models","chinese":"競爭型號"},{"english":"familiar brands","chinese":"熟悉的品牌"},{"english":"hear about","chinese":"聽說；得知"},{"english":"a better alternative","chinese":"更好的替代選擇"},{"english":"quality alone","chinese":"單靠質素"},{"english":"remove perceived risk","chinese":"消除感知風險"},{"english":"perceived risk","chinese":"感知風險"},{"english":"an unfamiliar brand","chinese":"不熟悉的品牌"},{"english":"worry about reliability","chinese":"擔心可靠性"},{"english":"after-sales service","chinese":"售後服務"},{"english":"the product itself","chinese":"產品本身"},{"english":"highly effective","chinese":"非常有效"},{"english":"reduce this hesitation","chinese":"減少這種猶豫"},{"english":"showing demonstrations","chinese":"展示示範"},{"english":"guarantees","chinese":"保證"},{"english":"certifications","chinese":"認證"},{"english":"consistent brand messages","chinese":"一致的品牌訊息"},{"english":"appear more credible","chinese":"顯得更可信"},{"english":"a start-up","chinese":"初創公司"},{"english":"safer baby bottles","chinese":"更安全的奶瓶"},{"english":"be overlooked","chinese":"被忽視"},{"english":"the materials used","chinese":"所使用的材料"},{"english":"the testing standards met","chinese":"符合的測試標準"},{"english":"the refund policy offered","chinese":"所提供的退款政策"},{"english":"become unnecessary","chinese":"變得不必要"},{"english":"however useful a product may be","chinese":"無論產品多有用"},{"english":"need information and reassurance","chinese":"需要資料和安心感"},{"english":"remain unnoticed and untrusted","chinese":"仍然無人注意和不被信任"}]},"model-essay-8-ielts-task1-bar-charts":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-8-ielts-task1-bar-charts","essayKey":"bar-charts:8","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-8-ielts-task1-bar-charts","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/bar-charts/bar-chart-8","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The bar chart compares the total duration of telephone calls made in the UK, measured in billions of minutes, across three categories between 1995 and 2002.","chinese":"這張柱狀圖比較了 1995 年至 2002 年間英國三類電話通話的總時長，單位為十億分鐘。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, local fixed-line calls remained the largest category throughout, despite rising to a peak in the late 1990s and then returning to their initial level. By contrast, national and international fixed-line calls increased steadily, while mobile calls, though starting from a very low base, recorded by far the sharpest growth.","chinese":"整體而言，本地固定電話通話在整段期間一直是最大類別，雖然其通話時長在 1990 年代末升至高點，之後又回到起初水平。 相比之下，國內及國際固定電話通話穩定上升；而流動電話通話雖然起點非常低，卻錄得遠遠最顯著的增長。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 1995, local fixed-line calls accounted for about 72 billion minutes, almost twice the figure for national and international calls, at roughly 37 billion. The local category then climbed each year to around 90 billion minutes in 1998 and 1999, before falling back gradually to about 72 billion by 2002.","chinese":"在 1995 年，本地固定電話通話約佔 720 億分鐘，幾乎是國內及國際固定電話通話的兩倍，後者約為 370 億分鐘。 之後，本地通話類別逐年上升，在 1998 年和 1999 年達到約 900 億分鐘，然後逐步回落，到 2002 年降至約 720 億分鐘。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The other two categories both followed upward trends. National and international fixed-line calls rose consistently from approximately 37 billion minutes in 1995 to just over 60 billion in 2002. Mobile calls showed a much more dramatic pattern: after increasing only modestly from about 3 to 12 billion minutes between 1995 and 1999, they surged to roughly 25 billion in 2000 and reached around 45 billion by the final year.","chinese":"其餘兩個類別都呈現上升趨勢。 國內及國際固定電話通話由 1995 年的約 370 億分鐘穩定上升至 2002 年的略高於 600 億分鐘。 流動電話通話則呈現更加顯著的變化：在 1995 年至 1999 年間，它只由約 30 億分鐘溫和上升至 120 億分鐘，但在 2000 年急升至約 250 億分鐘，並在最後一年達到約 450 億分鐘。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the total duration of telephone calls","chinese":"電話通話總時長"},{"english":"telephone calls made in the UK","chinese":"在英國撥打的電話"},{"english":"measured in billions of minutes","chinese":"以十億分鐘計"},{"english":"across three categories","chinese":"涵蓋三個類別"},{"english":"between 1995 and 2002","chinese":"在1995年至2002年間"},{"english":"local fixed-line calls","chinese":"本地固網電話"},{"english":"remained the largest category throughout","chinese":"全期一直是最大類別"},{"english":"despite rising to a peak","chinese":"儘管升至高峰"},{"english":"rising to a peak","chinese":"上升至高峰"},{"english":"in the late 1990s","chinese":"在1990年代後期"},{"english":"returning to their initial level","chinese":"回到最初水平"},{"english":"their initial level","chinese":"最初水平"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"national and international fixed-line calls","chinese":"國內及國際固網電話"},{"english":"increased steadily","chinese":"穩步上升"},{"english":"mobile calls","chinese":"流動電話通話"},{"english":"starting from a very low base","chinese":"從很低的基數開始"},{"english":"a very low base","chinese":"很低的基數"},{"english":"recorded by far the sharpest growth","chinese":"錄得遠遠最急劇的增長"},{"english":"by far the sharpest growth","chinese":"遠遠最急劇的增長"},{"english":"accounted for about 72 billion minutes","chinese":"佔約720億分鐘"},{"english":"almost twice the figure for","chinese":"幾乎是……數字的兩倍"},{"english":"the figure for national and international calls","chinese":"國內及國際電話的數字"},{"english":"at roughly 37 billion","chinese":"約為370億"},{"english":"the local category","chinese":"本地類別"},{"english":"climbed each year","chinese":"每年上升"},{"english":"around 90 billion minutes","chinese":"約900億分鐘"},{"english":"before falling back gradually","chinese":"隨後逐步回落"},{"english":"falling back gradually","chinese":"逐步回落"},{"english":"to about 72 billion by 2002","chinese":"到2002年回落至約720億"},{"english":"the other two categories","chinese":"其餘兩個類別"},{"english":"followed upward trends","chinese":"呈上升趨勢"},{"english":"rose consistently from","chinese":"由……持續上升"},{"english":"approximately 37 billion minutes","chinese":"約370億分鐘"},{"english":"to just over 60 billion","chinese":"至略高於600億"},{"english":"just over 60 billion","chinese":"略高於600億"},{"english":"showed a much more dramatic pattern","chinese":"呈現更急劇的走勢"},{"english":"a much more dramatic pattern","chinese":"急劇得多的走勢"},{"english":"after increasing only modestly","chinese":"在起初只輕微上升後"},{"english":"increasing only modestly","chinese":"只輕微上升"},{"english":"from about 3 to 12 billion minutes","chinese":"由約30億增至120億分鐘"},{"english":"between 1995 and 1999","chinese":"在1995年至1999年間"},{"english":"surged to roughly 25 billion","chinese":"急升至約250億"},{"english":"reached around 45 billion","chinese":"達到約450億"},{"english":"by the final year","chinese":"到最後一年"}]},"model-essay-8-ielts-task1-line-graph":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-8-ielts-task1-line-graph","essayKey":"line-graph:8","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-8-ielts-task1-line-graph","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/line-graphs/line-graph-8","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The line graph illustrates the amount of energy consumed in the United States from six fuel sources between 1980 and 2030, measured in quadrillion units, with later figures projected.","chinese":"該折線圖說明了 1980 年至 2030 年間美國六種燃料來源的能源消耗量，單位為千萬億單位，後期數據為預測值。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, petrol and oil remained, and are expected to remain, the dominant fuel source. Coal and natural gas formed a second tier, though coal is projected to overtake gas after about 2015, while nuclear, solar/wind and hydropower accounted for only small amounts throughout.","chinese":"整體而言，汽油和石油一直是、並預計仍將是最主要的燃料來源。 煤和天然氣構成第二梯隊，不過煤預計在約 2015 年後超越天然氣；相反，核能、太陽能／風能和水電在整段期間的消耗量都很小。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 1980, petrol and oil consumption stood at around 35 quadrillion units, compared with about 20 for natural gas and 16 for coal. After dipping to just over 30 in the mid-1980s, petrol and oil rose steadily, reaching roughly 40 by 2005 and a projected 49 by 2030. Coal followed a gentler upward path, increasing to about 22 in the mid-1990s, remaining close to that level for several years, and then rising to approximately 32 by the end. Natural gas fluctuated around the low twenties before leveling off at about 25 from 2015 onwards.","chinese":"1980 年，汽油和石油的消耗量約為 35 千萬億單位，相比之下，天然氣約為 20 ，煤約為 16 。 在 1980 年代中期下降至略高於 30 後，汽油和石油的消耗量穩步上升，到 2005年達到約 40 ，並預計到 2030 年達到 49 。 煤的上升趨勢較為溫和，在 1990 年代中期增至約 22 ，之後數年保持在接近該水平，最後升至約 32 。 天然氣在二十出頭的水平附近波動，之後從 2015 年起穩定在約 25 。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The remaining fuels were much less significant. Nuclear power climbed gradually from around 4 to about 8–9 units. Solar/wind also rose modestly to around 6, whereas hydropower fluctuated slightly and finished at roughly 4.","chinese":"其餘燃料的消耗量明顯小得多。 核能由約 4 逐漸上升至約 8 至 9 個單位。 太陽能／風能也溫和上升至約 6 ；相反，水電只是輕微波動，最後約為 4 。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"line graph","chinese":"折線圖"},{"english":"illustrates the amount of","chinese":"顯示……的數量"},{"english":"energy consumed","chinese":"所消耗的能源"},{"english":"fuel sources","chinese":"燃料來源"},{"english":"between 1980 and 2030","chinese":"在1980年至2030年間"},{"english":"measured in quadrillion units","chinese":"以千萬億單位計算"},{"english":"quadrillion units","chinese":"千萬億單位"},{"english":"with later figures projected","chinese":"後期數字為預測"},{"english":"projected","chinese":"預測的"},{"english":"petrol and oil","chinese":"汽油及石油"},{"english":"remained, and are expected to remain","chinese":"一直是，並預料仍會是"},{"english":"the dominant fuel source","chinese":"主要燃料來源"},{"english":"coal","chinese":"煤"},{"english":"natural gas","chinese":"天然氣"},{"english":"formed a second tier","chinese":"構成第二梯隊"},{"english":"second tier","chinese":"第二梯隊"},{"english":"is projected to overtake","chinese":"預計會超越"},{"english":"overtake gas","chinese":"超越天然氣"},{"english":"after about 2015","chinese":"約2015年後"},{"english":"nuclear","chinese":"核能"},{"english":"solar/wind","chinese":"太陽能／風能"},{"english":"hydropower","chinese":"水力發電"},{"english":"accounted for only small amounts","chinese":"只佔少量"},{"english":"small amounts","chinese":"少量"},{"english":"throughout","chinese":"在整段期間"},{"english":"consumption stood at around","chinese":"消耗量約為"},{"english":"stood at around","chinese":"約為"},{"english":"compared with about","chinese":"與約……相比"},{"english":"after dipping to","chinese":"在跌至……後"},{"english":"dipping to","chinese":"下跌至"},{"english":"just over 30","chinese":"略高於30"},{"english":"in the mid-1980s","chinese":"在1980年代中期"},{"english":"rose steadily","chinese":"穩步上升"},{"english":"reaching roughly 40","chinese":"達到約40"},{"english":"by 2005","chinese":"到2005年時"},{"english":"a projected 49","chinese":"預測為49"},{"english":"by 2030","chinese":"到2030年時"},{"english":"followed a gentler upward path","chinese":"呈現較溫和的上升走勢"},{"english":"gentler upward path","chinese":"較溫和的上升走勢"},{"english":"increasing to about","chinese":"增至約"},{"english":"in the mid-1990s","chinese":"在1990年代中期"},{"english":"remaining close to that level","chinese":"維持接近該水平"},{"english":"that level","chinese":"該水平"},{"english":"for several years","chinese":"數年間"},{"english":"rising to approximately","chinese":"上升至約"},{"english":"by the end","chinese":"到期末時"},{"english":"fluctuated around","chinese":"在……附近波動"},{"english":"the low twenties","chinese":"二十出頭"},{"english":"before leveling off at","chinese":"之後在……趨於平穩"},{"english":"leveling off","chinese":"趨於平穩"},{"english":"from 2015 onwards","chinese":"從2015年起"},{"english":"the remaining fuels","chinese":"其餘燃料"},{"english":"much less significant","chinese":"重要性低得多"},{"english":"nuclear power","chinese":"核能"},{"english":"climbed gradually","chinese":"逐步上升"},{"english":"from around 4 to about 8–9 units","chinese":"由約4升至約8至9單位"},{"english":"rose modestly","chinese":"溫和上升"},{"english":"to around 6","chinese":"至約6"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相比之下"},{"english":"fluctuated slightly","chinese":"輕微波動"},{"english":"finished at roughly","chinese":"最後約為"},{"english":"roughly 4","chinese":"約4"},{"english":"energy consumption","chinese":"能源消耗"},{"english":"long-term projection","chinese":"長期預測"},{"english":"upward trend","chinese":"上升趨勢"},{"english":"steady increase","chinese":"穩定增長"}]},"model-essay-8-ielts-task1-maps":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-8-ielts-task1-maps","essayKey":"maps:8","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-8-ielts-task1-maps","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/maps/maps-8","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The two plans illustrate the current layout of a university sports centre and its proposed redevelopment.","chinese":"這兩張平面圖說明一所大學體育中心目前的布局，以及其擬議重建後的樣。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the centre is expected to expand westwards and eastwards, replacing both outdoor court areas with indoor facilities. The existing central core, including the 25-metre pool, reception, original changing room and seating area, will remain largely unchanged, while the gym will be enlarged and new leisure and commercial amenities will be added.","chinese":"整體而言，該中心預計會向西和向東擴展，並用室內設施取代兩側的戶外球場區。 現有的中央核心區，包括 25 米泳池、接待處、原有更衣室和座位區，將大致保持不變；同時，健身房會擴大，並會增設新的休閒和商業設施。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"At present, the sports centre consists of a compact rectangular building. A 25-metre pool occupies the middle, with a gym directly to its north. On the western side of the pool there is a changing room, whereas seating is located to the east. The reception area stands at the southern entrance, and the building is flanked by outdoor courts on both sides.","chinese":"目前，該體育中心由一座緊湊的矩形建築組成。 一個 25 米泳池位於中間，其正北方是健身房。 泳池西側設有更衣室，而座位區位於東側。 接待處位於南面的入口處，而建築兩側各有一片戶外球場。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"After redevelopment, the western courts will be replaced by a large leisure pool, with an additional changing room and a sports shop to its south. On the eastern side, the courts will give way to a sports hall, two dance studios, a café and another changing room. The gym will also be extended across the northern part of the complex.","chinese":"重建後，西側球場將被一個大型休閒泳池取代，其南面會新增一間更衣室和一間體育用品商店。 在東側，球場將讓位給一個體育館、兩間舞蹈室、一間咖啡廳和另一間更衣室。 健身房也將沿著建築群北部擴建。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"illustrate the current layout of","chinese":"展示……的現時佈局"},{"english":"the current layout","chinese":"現時佈局"},{"english":"a university sports centre","chinese":"大學體育中心"},{"english":"its proposed redevelopment","chinese":"其擬議重建"},{"english":"proposed redevelopment","chinese":"擬議重建"},{"english":"is expected to","chinese":"預計會"},{"english":"expand westwards and eastwards","chinese":"向西及向東擴展"},{"english":"replacing X with Y","chinese":"以Y取代X"},{"english":"outdoor court areas","chinese":"戶外球場區"},{"english":"indoor facilities","chinese":"室內設施"},{"english":"the existing central core","chinese":"現有中央核心區"},{"english":"including","chinese":"包括"},{"english":"25-metre pool","chinese":"25米泳池"},{"english":"reception","chinese":"接待處"},{"english":"original changing room","chinese":"原有更衣室"},{"english":"seating area","chinese":"座位區"},{"english":"remain largely unchanged","chinese":"大致保持不變"},{"english":"while","chinese":"而；同時"},{"english":"the gym will be enlarged","chinese":"健身室將會擴大"},{"english":"leisure and commercial amenities","chinese":"休閒及商業設施"},{"english":"will be added","chinese":"將會增設"},{"english":"at present","chinese":"目前"},{"english":"consists of","chinese":"由……組成"},{"english":"a compact rectangular building","chinese":"緊湊的長方形建築"},{"english":"occupies the middle","chinese":"佔據中央位置"},{"english":"directly to its north","chinese":"就在其北面"},{"english":"on the western side of","chinese":"在……西面"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相反"},{"english":"be located to the east","chinese":"位於東面"},{"english":"the reception area","chinese":"接待區"},{"english":"stands at the southern entrance","chinese":"位於南面入口"},{"english":"the southern entrance","chinese":"南面入口"},{"english":"be flanked by","chinese":"兩側有……"},{"english":"on both sides","chinese":"在兩邊"},{"english":"after redevelopment","chinese":"重建後"},{"english":"the western courts","chinese":"西面的球場"},{"english":"will be replaced by","chinese":"將會被……取代"},{"english":"a large leisure pool","chinese":"大型休閒泳池"},{"english":"an additional changing room","chinese":"額外更衣室"},{"english":"a sports shop","chinese":"體育用品店"},{"english":"to its south","chinese":"在其南面"},{"english":"on the eastern side","chinese":"在東面"},{"english":"give way to","chinese":"讓位予……；被……取代"},{"english":"a sports hall","chinese":"體育館"},{"english":"dance studios","chinese":"舞蹈室"},{"english":"a café","chinese":"咖啡店"},{"english":"another changing room","chinese":"另一個更衣室"},{"english":"will also be extended","chinese":"亦會擴建"},{"english":"across the northern part","chinese":"橫跨北部"},{"english":"the northern part of the complex","chinese":"綜合建築的北部"},{"english":"the complex","chinese":"綜合建築；綜合設施"},{"english":"both outdoor courts","chinese":"兩邊戶外球場"},{"english":"be converted into indoor space","chinese":"被改造成室內空間"},{"english":"new facilities will be introduced","chinese":"將會引入新設施"},{"english":"the central section","chinese":"中央部分"},{"english":"the western extension","chinese":"西面擴建部分"},{"english":"the eastern extension","chinese":"東面擴建部分"},{"english":"the redeveloped centre","chinese":"重建後的體育中心"}]},"model-essay-8-ielts-task1-process-diagram":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-8-ielts-task1-process-diagram","essayKey":"process-diagram:8","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-8-ielts-task1-process-diagram","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/process-diagrams/process-diagram-8","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The diagrams illustrate the life cycle of the salmon, showing the habitats, durations and sizes associated with its main developmental stages.","chinese":"這些圖表說明鮭魚的生命週期，展示其主要發育階段所對應的棲息地、所需時間和體型大小。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, salmon pass through three named growth stages—fry, smolt and adult salmon—and move from freshwater rivers to the open sea before returning upstream to reproduce. The cycle lasts roughly nine and a half years, with the longest period spent in the sea and most growth occurring during the marine phase.","chinese":"整體而言，鮭魚會經歷三個有名稱的成長階段 —— 幼魚、銀鮭幼魚和成年鮭魚，並從淡水河流移往開闊海域，之後再逆流返回繁殖。 整個週期大約持續九年半，其中最長的階段是在海中度過，而大部分體型增長也發生在海洋階段。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"At the beginning, salmon eggs are laid in the upper river, where slow-moving water, reeds and small stones provide the spawning environment. After approximately five to six months, they hatch into fry, measuring only 3–8 cm. These young fish then move downstream to the lower river, a faster-flowing area. They remain there for about four years, growing into smolt of around 12–15 cm.","chinese":"一開始，鮭魚卵被產在上游河段；那裡水流緩慢，並有蘆葦和小石頭，為產卵提供合適環境。 大約五至六個月後，魚卵孵化成幼魚，體長只有三至八厘米。 這些幼魚接著向下游移動，到達水流較快的下游河段。 牠們會在那裡停留大約四年，並成長為體長約十二至十五厘米的銀鮭幼魚。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Following this freshwater stage, the smolt migrate to the open sea. This is the longest single phase, lasting about five years, during which they develop into adult salmon. By this point, their length has increased markedly to 70–76 cm. Finally, the mature fish swim back to the upper river, where they lay eggs and restart the cycle.","chinese":"在完成這個淡水階段後，銀鮭幼魚會遷徙到開闊海域。 這是最長的單一階段，持續約五年；在此期間，牠們發育成成年鮭魚。 到這個階段，牠們的體長已明顯增加到七十至七十六厘米。 最後，成熟的鮭魚會游回上游河段，在那裡產卵並重新開始整個週期。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"diagrams illustrate","chinese":"圖示說明"},{"english":"life cycle","chinese":"生命週期"},{"english":"the salmon","chinese":"三文魚；鮭魚"},{"english":"habitats","chinese":"棲息地"},{"english":"durations","chinese":"持續時間"},{"english":"sizes associated with","chinese":"與……相關的大小"},{"english":"main developmental stages","chinese":"主要發育階段"},{"english":"pass through","chinese":"經歷"},{"english":"named growth stages","chinese":"具名成長階段"},{"english":"fry","chinese":"幼魚"},{"english":"smolt","chinese":"銀化幼魚"},{"english":"adult salmon","chinese":"成年三文魚；成年鮭魚"},{"english":"freshwater rivers","chinese":"淡水河流"},{"english":"the open sea","chinese":"外海"},{"english":"returning upstream","chinese":"逆流而上返回"},{"english":"reproduce","chinese":"繁殖"},{"english":"lasts roughly","chinese":"大約持續"},{"english":"nine and a half years","chinese":"九年半"},{"english":"the longest period","chinese":"最長時期"},{"english":"spent in the sea","chinese":"在海中度過"},{"english":"most growth occurring during","chinese":"大部分成長發生於……期間"},{"english":"marine phase","chinese":"海洋階段"},{"english":"at the beginning","chinese":"在開始時"},{"english":"salmon eggs","chinese":"三文魚卵；鮭魚卵"},{"english":"are laid in","chinese":"被產於"},{"english":"upper river","chinese":"河流上游"},{"english":"slow-moving water","chinese":"流速緩慢的水"},{"english":"reeds","chinese":"蘆葦"},{"english":"small stones","chinese":"小石"},{"english":"provide the spawning environment","chinese":"提供產卵環境"},{"english":"spawning environment","chinese":"產卵環境"},{"english":"after approximately","chinese":"約……之後"},{"english":"five to six months","chinese":"五至六個月"},{"english":"hatch into fry","chinese":"孵化成幼魚"},{"english":"measuring only","chinese":"只有……長"},{"english":"3–8 cm","chinese":"3至8厘米"},{"english":"young fish","chinese":"幼魚"},{"english":"move downstream","chinese":"順流而下"},{"english":"lower river","chinese":"河流下游"},{"english":"faster-flowing area","chinese":"水流較快的區域"},{"english":"remain there for","chinese":"在那裏停留……"},{"english":"about four years","chinese":"約四年"},{"english":"growing into smolt","chinese":"成長為銀化幼魚"},{"english":"around 12–15 cm","chinese":"約12至15厘米"},{"english":"following this freshwater stage","chinese":"在這個淡水階段之後"},{"english":"freshwater stage","chinese":"淡水階段"},{"english":"migrate to","chinese":"遷移至"},{"english":"longest single phase","chinese":"最長的單一階段"},{"english":"lasting about five years","chinese":"持續約五年"},{"english":"during which","chinese":"在此期間"},{"english":"develop into","chinese":"發育成"},{"english":"by this point","chinese":"到這時"},{"english":"length has increased markedly","chinese":"長度大幅增加"},{"english":"markedly","chinese":"大幅地；明顯地"},{"english":"70–76 cm","chinese":"70至76厘米"},{"english":"mature fish","chinese":"成熟魚類"},{"english":"swim back to","chinese":"游回"},{"english":"lay eggs","chinese":"產卵"},{"english":"restart the cycle","chinese":"重新開始循環"},{"english":"developmental process","chinese":"發育過程"},{"english":"growth phase","chinese":"成長階段"},{"english":"river habitat","chinese":"河流棲息地"},{"english":"sea stage","chinese":"海洋階段"}]},"model-essay-8-ielts-task1-tables":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-8-ielts-task1-tables","essayKey":"tables:8","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-8-ielts-task1-tables","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/tables/table-8","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The table compares the percentage of management posts occupied by women in finance, manufacturing, IT and hospitality in a European country in 2006.","chinese":"該表格比較了 2006 年某歐洲國家中，女性在金融、製造業、資訊科技和酒店款待業所佔管理職位的百分比。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, women were most strongly represented in hospitality and least represented in manufacturing across the three levels. In addition, their share generally decreased as seniority rose, although hospitality was an exception at the top level, where the proportion of female CEOs slightly exceeded that of female executives.","chinese":"整體而言，在三個職級中，女性在酒店款待業的代表性最高，而在製造業的代表性最低。 此外，女性所佔比例通常隨職級上升而下降；不過，酒店款待業在最高層級是一個例外，女性行政總裁的比例略高於女性行政人員。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Among managers, hospitality had by far the highest figure, at 33.14%, roughly twice the shares recorded in finance and IT, which were almost identical at 16.39% and 16.04% respectively. Manufacturing was noticeably lower, with women making up only 9% of managers.","chinese":"在經理職位中，酒店款待業的數字遠高於其他行業，達 33.14% ，大約是金融和資訊科技業的兩倍；後兩者的比例幾乎相同，分別為 16.39% 和 16.04% 。 製造業則明顯較低，女性只佔經理職位的 9% 。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"A similar ranking can be seen among executives and CEOs, though the percentages were smaller. In hospitality, women accounted for 19.9% of executives and 20.6% of CEOs, far ahead of IT, where the equivalent figures were 12.82% and 6.58%. Female representation was much weaker in finance, at 4.58% for executives and just 1.98% for CEOs. Manufacturing had the lowest levels overall, with only 1.98% of executives and 1.21% of CEOs being women.","chinese":"在行政人員和行政總裁層面，也可以看到相似的排名，不過比例整體較低。 在酒店款待業中，女性佔行政人員的 19.9% ，並佔行政總裁的 20.6% ，遠高於資訊科技業；後者相應數字為 12.82% 和 6.58% 。 金融業的女性代表性則弱得多，女性行政人員佔 4.58% ，而女性行政總裁僅佔。 製造業整體水平最低，女性只佔行政人員的 1.98% ，並只佔行政總裁的 1.21%。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the table compares","chinese":"表格比較"},{"english":"the percentage of","chinese":"……的百分比"},{"english":"management posts","chinese":"管理職位"},{"english":"occupied by women","chinese":"由女性擔任"},{"english":"held by women","chinese":"由女性擔任"},{"english":"in finance","chinese":"在金融業"},{"english":"manufacturing","chinese":"製造業"},{"english":"IT","chinese":"資訊科技業"},{"english":"hospitality","chinese":"酒店及款待業"},{"english":"in a European country","chinese":"在一個歐洲國家"},{"english":"in 2006","chinese":"在2006年"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"women were most strongly represented","chinese":"女性代表性最高"},{"english":"strongly represented","chinese":"代表性高"},{"english":"least represented","chinese":"代表性最低"},{"english":"across the three levels","chinese":"在三個級別中"},{"english":"their share","chinese":"她們所佔比例"},{"english":"generally decreased","chinese":"整體下降"},{"english":"as seniority rose","chinese":"隨着職級上升"},{"english":"seniority","chinese":"職級高低；資歷級別"},{"english":"although","chinese":"雖然"},{"english":"an exception at the top level","chinese":"高層級別的例外"},{"english":"at the top level","chinese":"在最高級別"},{"english":"the proportion of female CEOs","chinese":"女性行政總裁比例"},{"english":"female CEOs","chinese":"女性行政總裁"},{"english":"slightly exceeded","chinese":"略高於"},{"english":"that of female executives","chinese":"女性行政人員的比例"},{"english":"female executives","chinese":"女性行政人員"},{"english":"Among managers","chinese":"在經理級別中"},{"english":"by far the highest figure","chinese":"遠遠最高的數字"},{"english":"at 33.14%","chinese":"為33.14%"},{"english":"roughly twice","chinese":"大約兩倍"},{"english":"the shares recorded in","chinese":"在……錄得的比例"},{"english":"finance and IT","chinese":"金融業及資訊科技業"},{"english":"almost identical","chinese":"幾乎相同"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"noticeably lower","chinese":"明顯較低"},{"english":"with women making up","chinese":"其中女性佔"},{"english":"making up only 9%","chinese":"只佔9%"},{"english":"a similar ranking","chinese":"相似的排名"},{"english":"can be seen among","chinese":"可見於……之中"},{"english":"executives and CEOs","chinese":"行政人員及行政總裁"},{"english":"though","chinese":"不過；雖然"},{"english":"the percentages were smaller","chinese":"百分比較低"},{"english":"accounted for 19.9% of","chinese":"佔……的19.9%"},{"english":"far ahead of","chinese":"遠高於"},{"english":"the equivalent figures","chinese":"對應數字"},{"english":"12.82% and 6.58%","chinese":"12.82%及6.58%"},{"english":"female representation","chinese":"女性代表性"},{"english":"much weaker","chinese":"弱得多；低得多"},{"english":"at 4.58% for executives","chinese":"行政人員為4.58%"},{"english":"just 1.98% for CEOs","chinese":"行政總裁只有1.98%"},{"english":"had the lowest levels overall","chinese":"整體水平最低"},{"english":"the lowest levels overall","chinese":"整體最低水平"},{"english":"with only","chinese":"只有"},{"english":"1.98% of executives","chinese":"1.98%的行政人員"},{"english":"1.21% of CEOs","chinese":"1.21%的行政總裁"},{"english":"being women","chinese":"是女性"}]},"model-essay-9-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-9-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:9","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-9-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q9","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many schools, uniforms are treated as a basic part of discipline, while others allow children to dress with far more freedom. Requiring pupils to wear a uniform has several clear benefits, especially in relation to equality and school identity, but it can also create problems for self-expression and family finances.","chinese":"在許多學校中，校服被視為紀律的基本部分，而另一些學校則容許學生在衣著上有更多自由。 要求學生穿校服有幾個明顯好處，尤其是在平等和學校身份認同方面；但它也可能在自我表達和家庭財政方面帶來問題。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One major advantage is that a uniform reduces visible social differences among children. If everyone wears similar clothes, pupils from poorer families are less likely to feel embarrassed by cheap or unfashionable outfits, and wealthier pupils have fewer chances to display expensive brands. This can make the classroom feel like a more equal place, where children are judged more by their behaviour and effort than by what they wear. Uniforms can also strengthen a sense of belonging. A child who puts on the same colours and badge as their classmates may feel that they are part of a shared community, much like a sports team whose kit quietly reminds its members that they represent something larger than themselves.","chinese":"其中一個主要優點是，校服可以減少孩子之間外在可見的社會差異。 如果每個人都穿著相似的衣服，來自較貧困家庭的學生便較不容易因為衣服便宜或不時尚而感到尷尬，而較富裕的學生也較少機會展示昂貴品牌。 這可以令課室感覺上更平等，孩子受到評價時，更多是基於他們的行為和努力，而不是他們穿甚麼。 校服也可以加強學生的歸屬感。 一個孩子穿上與同學相同顏色和校徽的校服時，可能會感到自己是共同群體的一部分，就像一支運動隊伍的隊服，會默默提醒隊員他們代表著比個人更大的整體。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, school uniforms also have disadvantages. The most obvious one is that they limit individuality. Children, especially teenagers, often use clothing to explore their personality, confidence, and taste. If every detail is tightly controlled, school may start to feel unnecessarily rigid, and minor choices such as hairstyles, shoes, or accessories can become sources of conflict rather than learning. Another drawback is cost. Although uniforms are meant to simplify clothing, they can be surprisingly expensive when schools require specific jackets, shoes, sportswear, or seasonal items from selected suppliers. For families with several children, these costs can place a real strain on the household budget.","chinese":"然而，校服也有缺點。 最明顯的一點是，校服限制了個人特色。 孩子，尤其是青少年，往往會透過衣著探索自己的個性、自信和品味。 如果每一個細節都受到嚴格控制，學校便可能開始令人覺得不必要地僵化，而髮型、鞋子或飾物這些小選擇，也可能變成衝突來源，而不是學習的一部分。 另一個缺點是成本。 雖然校服本意是簡化學生的衣著安排，但當學校要求學生購買特定外套、鞋子、運動服或指定供應商提供的季節性服裝時，校服的費用可能會出乎意料地高。 對於有幾個孩子的家庭來說，這些開支可能會對家庭預算造成實際壓力。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, school uniforms can promote equality, discipline, and a stronger school identity, but they may also restrict personal expression and create financial pressure. Overall, they bring clear social benefits, while also creating practical and personal drawbacks.","chinese":"總結來說，校服可以促進平等、紀律和更強的學校身份認同，但它們也可能限制個人表達，並造成財政壓力。 整體而言，校服帶來明顯的社會好處，但同時也會造成實際和個人層面的缺點。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"school uniforms","chinese":"校服"},{"english":"be treated as","chinese":"被視為……"},{"english":"a basic part of discipline","chinese":"紀律的基本部分"},{"english":"allow children to dress with far more freedom","chinese":"讓孩子穿着上有大得多的自由"},{"english":"dress with far more freedom","chinese":"穿着上有大得多的自由"},{"english":"requiring pupils to wear a uniform","chinese":"要求學生穿校服"},{"english":"several clear benefits","chinese":"幾個明顯好處"},{"english":"in relation to","chinese":"在……方面"},{"english":"equality and school identity","chinese":"平等和學校身份認同"},{"english":"create problems for","chinese":"為……帶來問題"},{"english":"self-expression","chinese":"自我表達"},{"english":"family finances","chinese":"家庭財政"},{"english":"one major advantage","chinese":"一個主要優點"},{"english":"reduces visible social differences","chinese":"減少可見的社會差異"},{"english":"visible social differences","chinese":"可見的社會差異"},{"english":"among children","chinese":"在孩子之間"},{"english":"pupils from poorer families","chinese":"來自較貧困家庭的學生"},{"english":"less likely to feel embarrassed by","chinese":"較不容易因……而感到尷尬"},{"english":"cheap or unfashionable outfits","chinese":"便宜或不時髦的衣着"},{"english":"wealthier pupils","chinese":"較富裕的學生"},{"english":"have fewer chances to","chinese":"較少機會去……"},{"english":"display expensive brands","chinese":"展示昂貴品牌"},{"english":"make the classroom feel like","chinese":"令課室感覺像……"},{"english":"a more equal place","chinese":"更平等的地方"},{"english":"be judged more by","chinese":"更多按……被評價"},{"english":"behaviour and effort","chinese":"行為和努力"},{"english":"than by what they wear","chinese":"而不是按他們的穿着"},{"english":"strengthen a sense of belonging","chinese":"加強歸屬感"},{"english":"a sense of belonging","chinese":"歸屬感"},{"english":"puts on the same colours and badge","chinese":"穿上相同顏色和校徽"},{"english":"classmates","chinese":"同班同學"},{"english":"part of a shared community","chinese":"共同群體的一分子"},{"english":"much like","chinese":"很像……"},{"english":"a sports team","chinese":"運動隊伍"},{"english":"quietly reminds its members that","chinese":"默默提醒其成員……"},{"english":"represent something larger than themselves","chinese":"代表比自己更大的整體"},{"english":"the most obvious one","chinese":"最明顯的一點"},{"english":"limit individuality","chinese":"限制個性"},{"english":"especially teenagers","chinese":"尤其是青少年"},{"english":"use clothing to explore","chinese":"用衣着去探索……"},{"english":"personality, confidence, and taste","chinese":"個性、自信和品味"},{"english":"every detail is tightly controlled","chinese":"每個細節都被嚴格控制"},{"english":"start to feel unnecessarily rigid","chinese":"開始令人覺得不必要地僵化"},{"english":"minor choices","chinese":"細微選擇"},{"english":"hairstyles, shoes, or accessories","chinese":"髮型、鞋履或配飾"},{"english":"sources of conflict","chinese":"衝突來源"},{"english":"rather than learning","chinese":"而不是學習"},{"english":"another drawback is cost","chinese":"另一個缺點是成本"},{"english":"are meant to simplify","chinese":"原意是簡化……"},{"english":"surprisingly expensive","chinese":"貴得令人意外"},{"english":"specific jackets","chinese":"指定外套"},{"english":"sportswear","chinese":"運動服"},{"english":"seasonal items","chinese":"季節性用品"},{"english":"selected suppliers","chinese":"指定供應商"},{"english":"families with several children","chinese":"有幾個孩子的家庭"},{"english":"place a real strain on","chinese":"對……造成實際壓力"},{"english":"household budget","chinese":"家庭預算"},{"english":"promote equality","chinese":"促進平等"},{"english":"a stronger school identity","chinese":"更強的學校身份認同"},{"english":"restrict personal expression","chinese":"限制個人表達"},{"english":"create financial pressure","chinese":"造成財政壓力"},{"english":"overall","chinese":"總括而言"},{"english":"clear social benefits","chinese":"明顯的社會好處"},{"english":"practical and personal drawbacks","chinese":"實際及個人方面的缺點"}]},"model-essay-9-ielts-cause-solution":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-9-ielts-cause-solution","essayKey":"cause-solution:9","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-9-ielts-cause-solution","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/problem-and-cause/EdmundBd9CnS-Q9","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"An increasing number of people now face serious health risks because they are overweight. This problem is best understood not as a simple failure of personal discipline, but as the result of a modern environment that quietly encourages inactivity and unhealthy eating. The most effective solution, therefore, is to make healthier routines easier to follow in ordinary life.","chinese":"越來越多人如今因為超重而面臨嚴重的健康風險。 這個問題最應被理解為現代環境所造成的結果，而不是單純的個人自律失敗；這種環境正悄悄鼓勵人們缺乏活動並養成不健康的飲食習慣。 因此，最有效的解決方法是讓較健康的日常習慣在普通生活中更容易實行。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main reason for the growth in overweight people is that many daily routines now involve too little movement and too much convenient, calorie-dense food. In many cities, people sit for long hours at school, at work and during travel, so their bodies use far less energy than before. At the same time, fast food, sugary drinks and processed snacks are cheap, widely available and heavily promoted. When these two forces work together, weight gain can become almost automatic. For example, a student who spends the day in class, travels home by car and then relaxes with online games may gradually build a lifestyle in which eating is easy but physical activity is rare.","chinese":"超重人數增加的主要原因是，現今許多日常生活模式都包含太少活動，以及太多方便而高熱量密度的食物。 在許多城市中，人們在學校、工作和通勤期間都長時間坐著，因此身體消耗的能量比以前少得多。 與此同時，快餐、含糖飲品和加工零食價格便宜、隨處可得，而且被大量推廣。 當這兩種力量同時發揮作用時，體重增加幾乎會變成一種自然而然的結果。 例如，一名學生整天在課室上課，放學後坐車回家，然後用網上遊戲放鬆，便可能逐漸形成一種飲食很容易、但體能活動很少的生活方式。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"To solve this problem, governments, schools and employers need to change the conditions that shape everyday behaviour. Governments could limit junk-food advertising aimed at children, require clearer nutrition labels and make fresh food more affordable. Schools should provide regular physical education and healthier meals, while workplaces could encourage active breaks, flexible lunch hours and safe facilities for walking or cycling. These measures are useful because they do not depend only on willpower. If healthy food is reasonably priced and exercise is built into the day, people are more likely to maintain a healthy weight without feeling that they are fighting their own routine.","chinese":"為了解決這個問題，政府、學校和僱主需要改變那些塑造日常行為的條件。 政府可以限制針對兒童的垃圾食品廣告，要求更清晰的營養標籤，並令新鮮食物更容易負擔。 學校應該提供定期的體育教育和更健康的膳食，而工作場所則可以鼓勵活動休息、彈性午餐時間，以及安全的步行或單車設施。 這些措施是有用的，因為它們並不只是依賴個人意志力。 如果健康食物價格合理，而運動又被融入日常生活之中，人們便更有可能維持健康體重，而不會覺得自己正在對抗自己的生活規律。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, the rise in overweight people is mainly caused by sedentary lifestyles combined with easy access to unhealthy food. It can be reduced by creating environments in which eating well and moving regularly become normal, practical and affordable choices.","chinese":"總結來說，超重人數上升主要是由久坐的生活方式，加上不健康食物容易取得所造成的。 這個問題可以透過創造一種環境來減少；在這種環境中，健康飲食和定期活動會成為正常、實際而且負擔得起的選擇。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"an increasing number of","chinese":"越來越多"},{"english":"face serious health risks","chinese":"面對嚴重健康風險"},{"english":"overweight","chinese":"超重"},{"english":"be best understood as","chinese":"最好理解為"},{"english":"a simple failure of personal discipline","chinese":"個人自律失敗這麼簡單"},{"english":"personal discipline","chinese":"個人自律"},{"english":"the result of","chinese":"……的結果"},{"english":"a modern environment","chinese":"現代環境"},{"english":"quietly encourages inactivity","chinese":"悄悄鼓勵缺乏活動"},{"english":"unhealthy eating","chinese":"不健康飲食"},{"english":"the most effective solution","chinese":"最有效的解決方法"},{"english":"healthier routines","chinese":"更健康的日常習慣"},{"english":"easier to follow","chinese":"更容易跟從"},{"english":"ordinary life","chinese":"日常生活"},{"english":"the growth in overweight people","chinese":"超重人口增加"},{"english":"daily routines","chinese":"日常習慣"},{"english":"involve too little movement","chinese":"涉及太少活動"},{"english":"convenient, calorie-dense food","chinese":"方便而高熱量的食物"},{"english":"calorie-dense food","chinese":"高熱量食物"},{"english":"sit for long hours","chinese":"長時間坐着"},{"english":"during travel","chinese":"在通勤途中"},{"english":"use far less energy","chinese":"消耗少得多能量"},{"english":"than before","chinese":"比以前"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"fast food","chinese":"快餐"},{"english":"sugary drinks","chinese":"含糖飲品"},{"english":"processed snacks","chinese":"加工零食"},{"english":"widely available","chinese":"隨處可得"},{"english":"heavily promoted","chinese":"被大力宣傳"},{"english":"work together","chinese":"共同作用"},{"english":"weight gain","chinese":"體重增加"},{"english":"almost automatic","chinese":"幾乎自然而然"},{"english":"spend the day in class","chinese":"整天上課"},{"english":"travel home by car","chinese":"坐車回家"},{"english":"relax with online games","chinese":"玩網上遊戲放鬆"},{"english":"gradually build a lifestyle","chinese":"逐漸建立一種生活方式"},{"english":"physical activity","chinese":"體能活動"},{"english":"be rare","chinese":"很少見"},{"english":"solve this problem","chinese":"解決這個問題"},{"english":"change the conditions","chinese":"改變條件"},{"english":"shape everyday behaviour","chinese":"塑造日常行為"},{"english":"limit junk-food advertising","chinese":"限制垃圾食物廣告"},{"english":"aimed at children","chinese":"針對兒童"},{"english":"nutrition labels","chinese":"營養標籤"},{"english":"make fresh food more affordable","chinese":"令新鮮食物更可負擔"},{"english":"regular physical education","chinese":"定期體育課"},{"english":"healthier meals","chinese":"更健康的膳食"},{"english":"active breaks","chinese":"活動小休"},{"english":"flexible lunch hours","chinese":"彈性午膳時間"},{"english":"safe facilities for walking or cycling","chinese":"安全的步行或踩單車設施"},{"english":"do not depend only on","chinese":"不只依賴"},{"english":"willpower","chinese":"意志力"},{"english":"reasonably priced","chinese":"價格合理"},{"english":"be built into the day","chinese":"融入日常"},{"english":"maintain a healthy weight","chinese":"維持健康體重"},{"english":"fight their own routine","chinese":"與自己的日常習慣對抗"},{"english":"the rise in overweight people","chinese":"超重人口上升"},{"english":"sedentary lifestyles","chinese":"久坐少動的生活方式"},{"english":"be combined with","chinese":"與……結合"},{"english":"easy access to","chinese":"容易接觸到"},{"english":"unhealthy food","chinese":"不健康食物"},{"english":"be reduced by","chinese":"可以透過……減少"},{"english":"creating environments in which","chinese":"創造一種……的環境"},{"english":"eating well","chinese":"飲食健康"},{"english":"moving regularly","chinese":"定期活動"},{"english":"normal, practical and affordable choices","chinese":"正常、實際而可負擔的選擇"}]},"model-essay-9-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-9-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:9","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-9-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q9","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Juvenile crime is often blamed on violent films, video games and online content, because these influences are visible and easy to criticise. However, I do not agree that media violence is the main cause. In my view, young people are far more likely to offend when they lack stable guidance, meaningful supervision and constructive outlets for their energy. The best response is therefore early intervention through families, schools and local communities.","chinese":"青少年犯罪常常被歸咎於暴力電影、電子遊戲和網上內容，因為這些影響因素十分顯眼，也很容易被批評。 然而，我不同意媒體暴力是主要原因。 在我看來，當年輕人缺乏穩定的引導、有意義的監督，以及能夠正面釋放精力的途徑時，他們犯罪的可能性要大得多。 因此，最好的應對方法是透過家庭、學校和本地社區進行早期介入。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The central cause of youth crime is not what teenagers watch, but the environment in which they learn how to behave. If parents are absent, overwhelmed or unable to set boundaries, children may never develop a clear sense of consequence. A violent scene on a screen may shock them briefly, but daily neglect can quietly teach them that aggression, theft or defiance bring no serious cost. This problem becomes even worse in areas where teenagers have few positive role models and little to do after school. For instance, a boy who spends every evening with older peers involved in petty crime is not merely copying television; he is being pulled into a real social script.","chinese":"青少年犯罪的核心原因並不是他們觀看了甚麼，而是他們學習如何行為處事的環境。 如果父母缺席、不堪重負，或者無法設立界線，孩子可能永遠無法建立清晰的後果意識。 螢幕上的一個暴力場面可能會短暫地震撼他們，但日常的忽視卻可能悄悄地教會他們：攻擊、偷竊或反抗並不會帶來嚴重代價。 在一些青少年缺乏正面榜樣、放學後也沒有甚麼事情可做的地區，這個問題會變得更加嚴重。 例如，一個每天晚上都和參與輕微犯罪的年長同伴混在一起的男孩，並不只是單純地模仿電視；他其實是被拉進了一套真實的社會劇本之中。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"To deal with this situation, governments and communities should focus on support before punishment. Schools should identify pupils who show repeated aggression, truancy or isolation and connect them with counsellors, mentors and family-support services before their behaviour hardens into a pattern. At the same time, local authorities should fund affordable sports, arts and vocational programmes, especially in deprived neighbourhoods. These activities give teenagers structure, belonging and a legitimate sense of achievement. A young person who has a coach, a team and a reason to be proud is less likely to seek status through crime.","chinese":"為了處理這種情況，政府和社區應該先著重支援，而不是先著重懲罰。 學校應該識別那些反覆表現出攻擊行為、逃學或孤立情況的學生，並在他們的行為固化成一種模式之前，把他們與輔導員、導師和家庭支援服務連接起來。 同時，地方政府應該資助價格可負擔的體育、藝術和職業培訓項目，尤其是在資源匱乏的社區。 這些活動能給予青少年規律、歸屬感，以及一種正當的成就感。 一個擁有教練、團隊，以及值得自豪理由的年輕人，較不容易透過犯罪來尋求地位。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, media violence may seem like a convenient explanation, but it is not the main cause of juvenile crime. The deeper roots are weak supervision, poor support and under-resourced communities, and the best solutions are early intervention, stronger family support and purposeful activities for young people.","chinese":"總結來說，媒體暴力看似是一個方便的解釋，但它並不是青少年犯罪的主要原因。 更深層的根源在於薄弱的監督、不足的支援，以及資源不足的社區，而最好的解決方法是早期介入、更強的家庭支援，以及為年輕人提供有目的的活動。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"juvenile crime","chinese":"青少年犯罪"},{"english":"be blamed on","chinese":"被歸咎於"},{"english":"violent films","chinese":"暴力電影"},{"english":"online content","chinese":"網上內容"},{"english":"these influences","chinese":"這些影響因素"},{"english":"visible and easy to criticise","chinese":"明顯而容易批評"},{"english":"media violence","chinese":"媒體暴力"},{"english":"the main cause","chinese":"主要原因"},{"english":"far more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"offend","chinese":"犯法；犯罪"},{"english":"lack stable guidance","chinese":"缺乏穩定指導"},{"english":"meaningful supervision","chinese":"有實質意義的監督"},{"english":"constructive outlets for","chinese":"……的建設性出口"},{"english":"early intervention","chinese":"早期介入"},{"english":"local communities","chinese":"本地社區"},{"english":"the central cause of","chinese":"……的核心原因"},{"english":"youth crime","chinese":"青少年犯罪"},{"english":"learn how to behave","chinese":"學習如何行事"},{"english":"parents are absent","chinese":"父母缺席"},{"english":"overwhelmed","chinese":"不勝負荷的"},{"english":"set boundaries","chinese":"設立界線"},{"english":"develop a clear sense of consequence","chinese":"建立清晰的後果意識"},{"english":"a violent scene on a screen","chinese":"螢幕上的暴力場面"},{"english":"shock them briefly","chinese":"短暫震撼他們"},{"english":"daily neglect","chinese":"日常忽視"},{"english":"quietly teach them that","chinese":"悄悄教會他們"},{"english":"aggression, theft or defiance","chinese":"攻擊行為、偷竊或反抗"},{"english":"bring no serious cost","chinese":"不會帶來嚴重代價"},{"english":"positive role models","chinese":"正面的榜樣"},{"english":"little to do after school","chinese":"放學後無所事事"},{"english":"spends every evening with","chinese":"每晚都與……一起"},{"english":"older peers","chinese":"年紀較大的朋輩"},{"english":"involved in petty crime","chinese":"參與輕微犯罪"},{"english":"not merely copying","chinese":"不只是模仿"},{"english":"be pulled into","chinese":"被拉入；被捲入"},{"english":"a real social script","chinese":"真實的社會劇本"},{"english":"deal with this situation","chinese":"處理這種情況"},{"english":"focus on support before punishment","chinese":"先支援，後懲罰"},{"english":"repeated aggression","chinese":"反覆攻擊行為"},{"english":"truancy","chinese":"逃學"},{"english":"isolation","chinese":"孤立；孤僻"},{"english":"connect them with","chinese":"將他們與……連繫起來"},{"english":"counsellors","chinese":"輔導員"},{"english":"mentors","chinese":"導師；良師"},{"english":"family-support services","chinese":"家庭支援服務"},{"english":"hardens into a pattern","chinese":"固化成一種模式"},{"english":"local authorities","chinese":"地方政府；地方當局"},{"english":"affordable sports, arts and vocational programmes","chinese":"負擔得起的體育、藝術及職業培訓課程"},{"english":"vocational programmes","chinese":"職業培訓課程"},{"english":"deprived neighbourhoods","chinese":"貧困社區"},{"english":"give teenagers structure","chinese":"給青少年規律"},{"english":"belonging","chinese":"歸屬感"},{"english":"a legitimate sense of achievement","chinese":"正當的成就感"},{"english":"a reason to be proud","chinese":"值得自豪的理由"},{"english":"seek status through crime","chinese":"透過犯罪尋求地位"},{"english":"a convenient explanation","chinese":"方便的解釋"},{"english":"the deeper roots","chinese":"更深層的根源"},{"english":"weak supervision","chinese":"監督不足"},{"english":"poor support","chinese":"支援不足"},{"english":"under-resourced communities","chinese":"資源不足的社區"},{"english":"stronger family support","chinese":"更強的家庭支援"},{"english":"purposeful activities","chinese":"有目標的活動"},{"english":"young people","chinese":"年輕人"}]},"model-essay-9-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-9-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:9","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-9-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q9","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Human intelligence has long been debated, partly because some people appear naturally quick-minded while others develop their abilities gradually. Although innate ability can give individuals an early advantage, I believe intelligence is far more strongly shaped by education, practice and sustained learning.","chinese":"人類智力長久以來一直備受爭議，部分原因是有些人似乎天生反應敏捷，而另一些人則逐漸發展自己的能力。 儘管天生能力可以給予個人早期優勢，但我認為智力在更大程度上是由教育、練習和持續學習塑造的。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Those who see intelligence as inborn often argue that people differ naturally in memory, reasoning and problem-solving speed. This view is understandable because children in the same classroom may receive the same instruction yet perform very differently. For instance, one student may grasp mathematical patterns almost instantly, while another needs repeated explanation before the idea becomes clear. Such differences suggest that certain mental capacities, like musical talent or athletic potential, may be partly inherited. If a person is born with a sharper ability to process information, learning may feel easier and faster from the beginning. In this sense, natural intelligence can act as a head start.","chinese":"那些認為智力是天生的人，往往主張人們在記憶力、推理能力和解決問題的速度方面天生就存在差異。 這種觀點是可以理解的，因為同一個課室裡的孩子可能接受相同的教學，但表現卻非常不同。 例如，一個學生可能幾乎立即掌握數學規律，而另一個學生則需要反覆解釋，才會明白這個概念。 這些差異顯示，某些心智能力，例如音樂天賦或運動潛能，可能有部分是遺傳而來的。 如果一個人天生具備較敏銳的資訊處理能力，那麼學習從一開始就可能感覺更容易、更快速。 從這個意義上說，天生智力可以起到領先起步的作用。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, I firmly believe that intelligence is not fixed, because learning can change how people think, analyse and solve problems. When students read widely, practise difficult skills and receive proper feedback, they gradually build stronger habits of reasoning. A child who struggles with science, for example, may become highly capable after years of guided practice, experiments and patient correction. This does not mean that everyone will reach exactly the same level, but it shows that intellectual ability can be stretched far beyond its starting point. More importantly, many forms of intelligence, such as judgement, creativity and emotional understanding, depend heavily on experience rather than birth. A naturally clever person who never studies may hit a ceiling, whereas a disciplined learner can continue to grow.","chinese":"然而，我堅定地認為智力並不是固定不變的，因為學習能夠改變人們思考、分析和解決問題的方式。 當學生廣泛閱讀、練習困難技能並獲得適當回饋時，他們會逐漸建立更強的推理習慣。 例如，一個在科學方面感到吃力的孩子，在多年有指導的練習、實驗和耐心糾正之後，可能會變得非常有能力。 這並不意味著每個人都會達到完全相同的水平，但它說明智力能力可以被延展到遠遠超出其起點的位置。 更重要的是，許多形式的智力，例如判斷力、創造力和情感理解，都高度依賴經驗，而不是出生時已經決定。 一個天生聰明但從不學習的人，可能會碰到上限；相反，一個自律的學習者則可以持續成長。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, innate ability may influence how quickly people learn at first, and it would be unrealistic to deny that some individuals have natural advantages. Nevertheless, intelligence is best understood as something that can be developed through learning, because education, effort and experience determine how far a person’s mind can truly go.","chinese":"總結來說，天生能力可能會影響人們最初學習的速度，而否認某些人具有天生優勢是不現實的。 然而，智力最好被理解為一種可以透過學習發展的東西，因為教育、努力和經驗決定了一個人的思維真正能走多遠。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"human intelligence","chinese":"人類智力"},{"english":"has long been debated","chinese":"長久以來備受爭議"},{"english":"partly because","chinese":"部分原因是"},{"english":"appear naturally quick-minded","chinese":"看起來天生反應快"},{"english":"develop their abilities gradually","chinese":"逐漸發展能力"},{"english":"innate ability","chinese":"天生能力"},{"english":"give individuals an early advantage","chinese":"給予個人早期優勢"},{"english":"far more strongly shaped by","chinese":"更大程度上受……塑造"},{"english":"sustained learning","chinese":"持續學習"},{"english":"see intelligence as inborn","chinese":"視智力為天生"},{"english":"differ naturally in","chinese":"在……方面天生有差異"},{"english":"reasoning","chinese":"推理能力"},{"english":"problem-solving speed","chinese":"解難速度"},{"english":"This view is understandable","chinese":"這種看法可以理解"},{"english":"receive the same instruction","chinese":"接受相同教學"},{"english":"perform very differently","chinese":"表現很不同"},{"english":"For instance","chinese":"例如"},{"english":"grasp mathematical patterns","chinese":"掌握數學規律"},{"english":"almost instantly","chinese":"幾乎立即"},{"english":"needs repeated explanation","chinese":"需要反覆解釋"},{"english":"the idea becomes clear","chinese":"概念變得清晰"},{"english":"Such differences suggest that","chinese":"這些差異顯示"},{"english":"mental capacities","chinese":"心智能力"},{"english":"musical talent","chinese":"音樂天賦"},{"english":"athletic potential","chinese":"運動潛能"},{"english":"partly inherited","chinese":"部分遺傳"},{"english":"be born with","chinese":"天生具有"},{"english":"a sharper ability to","chinese":"更敏銳的……能力"},{"english":"process information","chinese":"處理資料"},{"english":"feel easier and faster","chinese":"感覺更容易、更快"},{"english":"from the beginning","chinese":"從一開始"},{"english":"In this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"act as a head start","chinese":"成為起步優勢"},{"english":"firmly believe","chinese":"堅信"},{"english":"is not fixed","chinese":"並非固定不變"},{"english":"change how people think","chinese":"改變人們的思考方式"},{"english":"analyse and solve problems","chinese":"分析和解決問題"},{"english":"read widely","chinese":"廣泛閱讀"},{"english":"practise difficult skills","chinese":"練習困難技能"},{"english":"receive proper feedback","chinese":"獲得適當回饋"},{"english":"gradually build stronger habits of","chinese":"逐漸建立更強的……習慣"},{"english":"habits of reasoning","chinese":"推理習慣"},{"english":"struggles with science","chinese":"在科學方面感到吃力"},{"english":"highly capable","chinese":"能力很強"},{"english":"guided practice","chinese":"有指導的練習"},{"english":"patient correction","chinese":"耐心糾正"},{"english":"reach exactly the same level","chinese":"達到完全相同的水平"},{"english":"intellectual ability","chinese":"智力能力"},{"english":"be stretched far beyond","chinese":"被大大延伸至超越"},{"english":"its starting point","chinese":"它的起點"},{"english":"More importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"forms of intelligence","chinese":"智力形式"},{"english":"judgement","chinese":"判斷力"},{"english":"creativity","chinese":"創意"},{"english":"emotional understanding","chinese":"情感理解能力"},{"english":"depend heavily on","chinese":"很大程度上取決於"},{"english":"rather than birth","chinese":"而不是出生條件"},{"english":"naturally clever","chinese":"天生聰明"},{"english":"hit a ceiling","chinese":"遇到上限"},{"english":"a disciplined learner","chinese":"自律的學習者"},{"english":"continue to grow","chinese":"繼續成長"},{"english":"influence how quickly","chinese":"影響……有多快"},{"english":"at first","chinese":"起初"},{"english":"it would be unrealistic to deny that","chinese":"否認……並不現實"},{"english":"natural advantages","chinese":"天然優勢"},{"english":"Nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"best understood as","chinese":"最好理解為"},{"english":"developed through learning","chinese":"透過學習發展"},{"english":"education, effort and experience","chinese":"教育、努力和經驗"},{"english":"determine how far","chinese":"決定……能走多遠"},{"english":"a person's mind","chinese":"一個人的頭腦；心智能力"}]},"model-essay-9-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-9-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:9","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-9-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q9","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Because public policy shapes the long-term direction of a national economy, governments must decide where their support will produce the greatest benefit. Although many countries try to attract overseas corporations, I completely agree that governments should focus primarily on encouraging local businesses because domestic firms keep economic value within the country and provide a more stable basis for future growth.","chinese":"由於公共政策會塑造一國經濟的長期發展方向，政府必須決定應把支持投向何處，才能產生最大的效益。 雖然許多國家都試圖吸引海外企業，但我完全同意政府應優先把重點放在扶持本地企業，因為本國企業能把經濟價值留在國內，並為未來成長提供更穩定的基礎。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason local enterprises deserve greater support is that they circulate wealth through the domestic economy far more effectively. When a home-grown company expands, its profits are more likely to be reinvested locally, its taxes are paid to the same government that assisted it, and its operations usually depend on other national firms. This creates a powerful multiplier effect. A growing local business buys materials from domestic suppliers, pays wages to local employees, and purchases services such as transport, marketing and accounting from nearby companies. As a result, income spreads across several sectors rather than being transferred abroad, which strengthens employment and increases tax revenue. For example, if a locally owned food manufacturer receives government assistance, its growth may also benefit farmers, delivery companies and packaging providers within the same country.","chinese":"本地企業之所以更值得獲得支持，第一個原因在於它們能更有效地讓財富在國內經濟中流動。 當一家本土企業擴張時，它的利潤更有可能重新投資於本地；它所繳納的稅款也會回到曾經扶持它的同一個政府；而且它的營運通常也依賴其他本國企業。 這就會產生強大的乘數效應。 一家正在成長的本地企業會向國內供應商購買原料，支付薪資給本地員工，並向附近公司購買運輸、行銷及會計等服務。 因此，收入會擴散到多個產業，而不是被轉移到國外，這不但能強化就業，也能增加稅收。 例如，若一家由本地人擁有的食品製造商獲得政府援助，它的成長也可能同時讓同一國家的農民、配送公司及包裝供應商受惠。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Governments should also prioritise local firms because excessive reliance on foreign companies can weaken national competitiveness over time. Large multinational corporations often enter new markets with vast financial resources, established global brands and the ability to undercut smaller rivals. If they are also offered tax breaks or special incentives, domestic businesses can struggle to survive, even when they have long-term potential. Once local competitors disappear, key industries may become dependent on foreign-owned firms whose decisions are made overseas. This creates a serious risk: if labour costs rise or profits fall, those companies can relocate, leaving job losses and economic disruption behind. A clear example can be seen when foreign retail chains dominate a market, forcing smaller local shops to close before later reducing investment when conditions become less favourable.","chinese":"政府也應該優先扶持本地企業，因為過度依賴外國公司，長遠而言可能削弱國家的競爭力。 大型跨國企業進入新市場時，往往挾帶雄厚的財力、成熟的全球品牌，以及以低價壓過較小競爭對手的能力。 如果這些企業還獲得減稅或特殊優惠，那麼本國企業即使具有長期發展潛力，也可能難以生存。 一旦本地競爭者消失，關鍵產業就可能轉而依賴外資擁有的企業，而這些企業的決策卻是在海外作出的。 這會造成嚴重風險：一旦勞工成本上升或利潤下跌，這些公司便可能遷走，留下失業問題與經濟動盪。 一個明顯的例子是，當外國零售連鎖企業主導市場時，它們會迫使規模較小的本地商店倒閉；而當市場條件變得不再那麼有利時，它們之後又可能減少投資。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I wholly agree that governments should prioritise local businesses over foreign ones. Supporting domestic enterprise keeps wealth at home, strengthens related industries and builds a more self-reliant economy, whereas overdependence on overseas corporations can undermine long-term national resilience.","chinese":"總而言之，我完全同意政府應該優先支持本地企業，而不是外國企業。 支持本國企業能把財富留在國內、強化相關產業，並建立更具自立性的經濟體；相反地，過度依賴海外企業則可能削弱國家長期的韌性。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"public policy","chinese":"公共政策"},{"english":"shape the long-term direction of","chinese":"塑造……的長遠方向"},{"english":"a national economy","chinese":"國家經濟"},{"english":"decide where","chinese":"決定在哪裏"},{"english":"produce the greatest benefit","chinese":"產生最大效益"},{"english":"attract overseas corporations","chinese":"吸引海外企業"},{"english":"focus primarily on","chinese":"主要集中於"},{"english":"encouraging local businesses","chinese":"鼓勵本地企業"},{"english":"domestic firms","chinese":"本地企業"},{"english":"keep economic value within the country","chinese":"將經濟價值留在國內"},{"english":"provide a more stable basis for","chinese":"為……提供更穩定的基礎"},{"english":"future growth","chinese":"未來增長"},{"english":"local enterprises","chinese":"本地企業"},{"english":"deserve greater support","chinese":"值得得到更多支持"},{"english":"circulate wealth through","chinese":"令財富在……內流動"},{"english":"the domestic economy","chinese":"本地經濟"},{"english":"far more effectively","chinese":"有效得多"},{"english":"a home-grown company","chinese":"本土公司"},{"english":"profits are more likely to","chinese":"利潤更有可能"},{"english":"be reinvested locally","chinese":"在本地再投資"},{"english":"taxes are paid to","chinese":"稅款繳交給"},{"english":"assist","chinese":"協助"},{"english":"depend on","chinese":"依賴"},{"english":"national firms","chinese":"國內企業"},{"english":"a powerful multiplier effect","chinese":"強大的乘數效應"},{"english":"a growing local business","chinese":"正在增長的本地企業"},{"english":"domestic suppliers","chinese":"本地供應商"},{"english":"pay wages to","chinese":"向……支付工資"},{"english":"local employees","chinese":"本地僱員"},{"english":"purchase services such as","chinese":"購買例如……的服務"},{"english":"nearby companies","chinese":"附近公司"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"income spreads across","chinese":"收入擴散至"},{"english":"several sectors","chinese":"多個行業"},{"english":"rather than being transferred abroad","chinese":"而不是被轉移到海外"},{"english":"strengthen employment","chinese":"加強就業"},{"english":"increase tax revenue","chinese":"增加稅收"},{"english":"a locally owned food manufacturer","chinese":"本地擁有的食品製造商"},{"english":"receive government assistance","chinese":"獲得政府援助"},{"english":"benefit farmers","chinese":"令農民受惠"},{"english":"delivery companies","chinese":"送貨公司"},{"english":"packaging providers","chinese":"包裝供應商"},{"english":"within the same country","chinese":"在同一國家內"},{"english":"prioritise local firms","chinese":"優先支持本地企業"},{"english":"excessive reliance on","chinese":"過度依賴"},{"english":"foreign companies","chinese":"外國公司"},{"english":"weaken national competitiveness","chinese":"削弱國家競爭力"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨時間"},{"english":"large multinational corporations","chinese":"大型跨國企業"},{"english":"enter new markets","chinese":"進入新市場"},{"english":"vast financial resources","chinese":"龐大財政資源"},{"english":"established global brands","chinese":"已建立的全球品牌"},{"english":"undercut smaller rivals","chinese":"以低價擊敗較小競爭對手"},{"english":"tax breaks","chinese":"稅務寬減"},{"english":"special incentives","chinese":"特別優惠措施"},{"english":"struggle to survive","chinese":"難以生存"},{"english":"long-term potential","chinese":"長遠潛力"},{"english":"local competitors","chinese":"本地競爭者"},{"english":"key industries","chinese":"關鍵行業"},{"english":"become dependent on","chinese":"變得依賴"},{"english":"foreign-owned firms","chinese":"外資企業"},{"english":"be made overseas","chinese":"在海外作出"},{"english":"a serious risk","chinese":"嚴重風險"},{"english":"labour costs rise","chinese":"勞工成本上升"},{"english":"profits fall","chinese":"利潤下降"},{"english":"relocate","chinese":"遷走；遷移業務"},{"english":"leaving job losses behind","chinese":"留下失業問題"},{"english":"economic disruption","chinese":"經濟混亂"},{"english":"a clear example can be seen when","chinese":"一個明顯例子是"},{"english":"foreign retail chains","chinese":"外國零售連鎖店"},{"english":"dominate a market","chinese":"主導市場"},{"english":"force smaller local shops to close","chinese":"迫使較小本地店舖結業"},{"english":"reducing investment","chinese":"減少投資"},{"english":"conditions become less favourable","chinese":"情況變得較不利"},{"english":"wholly agree","chinese":"完全同意"},{"english":"prioritise local businesses over foreign ones","chinese":"優先支持本地企業而非外國企業"},{"english":"supporting domestic enterprise","chinese":"支持本地企業"},{"english":"keep wealth at home","chinese":"將財富留在本地"},{"english":"strengthen related industries","chinese":"加強相關行業"},{"english":"build a more self-reliant economy","chinese":"建立更自力更生的經濟"},{"english":"overdependence on","chinese":"過度依賴"},{"english":"overseas corporations","chinese":"海外企業"},{"english":"undermine long-term national resilience","chinese":"削弱國家的長遠韌性"}]},"model-essay-9-ielts-task1-line-graph":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-9-ielts-task1-line-graph","essayKey":"line-graph:9","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-9-ielts-task1-line-graph","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/line-graphs/line-graph-9","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The line graph illustrates the volume of goods transported in the UK by road, water, rail and pipeline between 1974 and 2002.","chinese":"該折線圖說明了 1974 年至 2002 年間，英國透過公路、水路、鐵路和管道運輸的貨物量。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, road was consistently the dominant mode and recorded the largest increase. Water transport also rose considerably, whereas rail fluctuated and finished only slightly above its initial level. Pipeline remained the least-used method, despite steady growth.","chinese":"整體而言，公路運輸一直是最主要的運輸方式，並錄得最大的絕對增幅。 水路運輸也有明顯上升；相反，鐵路運輸有所波動，最後只略高於最初水平。 儘管管道運輸穩定增長，但它始終是使用量最低的運輸方式。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 1974, road haulage stood at about 70 million tonnes, compared with roughly 38 million by water and 40 million by rail. After a slight rise in 1978 and a dip in 1982, the road figure climbed to just over 80 million tonnes in 1990. It then fell marginally in 1994 before rising sharply to almost 100 million tonnes by 2002.","chinese":"在 1974 年，公路貨運量約為 7,000 萬噸，相比之下，水路約為 3,800 萬噸，鐵路約為 4,000 萬噸。 在 1978 年小幅上升、 1982 年回落之後，公路運輸量在 1990 年升至略高於 8,000萬噸。 隨後，它在 1994 年略微下降，之後大幅上升，到 2002 年接近 1 億噸。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Water followed a gentler upward trend. Its volume increased from just under 40 million tonnes to around 55 million in 1982, stayed near this level until 1994, dipped in 1998, and then recovered to approximately 65 million tonnes. By contrast, rail dropped to around 30 million tonnes in 1986 and, despite another dip in 1994, recovered to just over 40 by the end. Pipeline transport rose steadily from about 5 to slightly above 20 million tonnes.","chinese":"水路運輸呈現較溫和的上升趨勢。 其運輸量從略低於 4,000 萬噸上升至 1982 年的約 5,500 萬噸，並一直維持在接近這一水平直到 1994 年，之後在 1998 年下降，最後回升至約 6,500 萬噸。 相比之下，鐵路運輸量在 1986 年下降至約 3,000 萬噸；儘管它在 1994 年再次下跌，但到最後回升至略高於 4,000 萬噸。 管道運輸量則從約 500 萬噸穩定上升至略高於 2,000 萬噸。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"line graph","chinese":"折線圖"},{"english":"illustrates the volume of","chinese":"顯示……的數量"},{"english":"the volume of goods transported","chinese":"貨物運輸量"},{"english":"goods transported by","chinese":"以……運送的貨物"},{"english":"by road, water, rail and pipeline","chinese":"以公路、水路、鐵路及管道方式"},{"english":"between 1974 and 2002","chinese":"在1974年至2002年間"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"consistently the dominant mode","chinese":"一直是佔主導地位的方式"},{"english":"the dominant mode of transport","chinese":"主要運輸方式"},{"english":"recorded the largest increase","chinese":"錄得最大升幅"},{"english":"the largest increase","chinese":"最大升幅"},{"english":"water transport","chinese":"水路運輸"},{"english":"rose considerably","chinese":"大幅上升"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相比之下"},{"english":"rail transport","chinese":"鐵路運輸"},{"english":"fluctuated","chinese":"波動"},{"english":"finished only slightly above its initial level","chinese":"最終只略高於起初水平"},{"english":"its initial level","chinese":"起初水平"},{"english":"pipeline transport","chinese":"管道運輸"},{"english":"remained the least-used method","chinese":"仍然是使用量最低的方式"},{"english":"the least-used method","chinese":"使用量最低的方式"},{"english":"despite steady growth","chinese":"儘管穩定增長"},{"english":"steady growth","chinese":"穩定增長"},{"english":"road haulage","chinese":"公路貨運"},{"english":"stood at about","chinese":"約為"},{"english":"about 70 million tonnes","chinese":"約7,000萬噸"},{"english":"million tonnes","chinese":"百萬噸"},{"english":"compared with roughly","chinese":"相比之下，約為"},{"english":"roughly 38 million","chinese":"約3,800萬"},{"english":"by water","chinese":"以水路方式"},{"english":"by rail","chinese":"以鐵路方式"},{"english":"a slight rise","chinese":"輕微上升"},{"english":"a dip in","chinese":"在……出現下跌"},{"english":"the figure for road transport","chinese":"公路運輸的數字"},{"english":"climbed to just over","chinese":"升至剛高於"},{"english":"just over 80 million tonnes","chinese":"剛高於8,000萬噸"},{"english":"fell marginally","chinese":"輕微下跌"},{"english":"before rising sharply","chinese":"之後急升"},{"english":"rose sharply to","chinese":"急升至"},{"english":"almost 100 million tonnes","chinese":"接近1億噸"},{"english":"followed a gentler upward trend","chinese":"呈現較溫和的上升趨勢"},{"english":"a gentler upward trend","chinese":"較溫和的上升趨勢"},{"english":"increased from","chinese":"由……增加"},{"english":"increased from … to …","chinese":"由……增加至……"},{"english":"just under 40 million tonnes","chinese":"剛低於4,000萬噸"},{"english":"around 55 million tonnes","chinese":"約5,500萬噸"},{"english":"stayed near this level","chinese":"保持接近這水平"},{"english":"near this level","chinese":"接近這水平"},{"english":"dipped in","chinese":"在……下跌"},{"english":"recovered to approximately","chinese":"回升至大約"},{"english":"approximately 65 million tonnes","chinese":"約6,500萬噸"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下；相反"},{"english":"dropped to around","chinese":"跌至約"},{"english":"around 30 million tonnes","chinese":"約3,000萬噸"},{"english":"despite another dip","chinese":"儘管再度下跌"},{"english":"another dip in","chinese":"在……再度下跌"},{"english":"recovered to just over","chinese":"回升至剛高於"},{"english":"just over 40 million tonnes","chinese":"剛高於4,000萬噸"},{"english":"by the end of the period","chinese":"到該時期結束時"},{"english":"rose steadily from","chinese":"由……穩步上升"},{"english":"from about … to slightly above …","chinese":"由約……升至略高於……"},{"english":"slightly above 20 million tonnes","chinese":"略高於2,000萬噸"}]},"model-essay-9-ielts-task1-maps":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-9-ielts-task1-maps","essayKey":"maps:9","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-9-ielts-task1-maps","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The two plans illustrate the layout of Grange Park when it opened in 1920 and its arrangement today.","chinese":"這兩張平面圖展示了格蘭奇公園在 1920 年首次開放時的布局，以及它今天的安排。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the park has been substantially modernised, with recreational facilities such as an amphitheatre, café, children’s play area and underground parking added. However, the two main entrances on Arnold Avenue and Eldon Street have been retained, and rose gardens remain important, although they have been reduced and reorganised.","chinese":"整體而言，該公園已大幅現代化，新增了露天劇場、咖啡館、兒童遊樂區和地下停車場等休閒設施。 然而，位於阿諾德大道和埃爾登街的兩個主要入口被保留下來，而玫瑰園仍然是重要元素，儘管它們的數量已減少並被重新安排。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 1920, the park had a formal layout. A fountain stood at its centre, while a stage for musicians occupied the western side. Three rose gardens were located in the northwest, northeast and southwest corners, and seating was distributed around the edges. The eastern half contained a pond for water plants in the northeast and a glasshouse in the southeast.","chinese":"在 1920 年，該公園具有較正式的布局。 一座噴泉位於公園中央，而音樂家表演台則佔據西側位置。 三個玫瑰園分別位於西北角、東北角和西南角，座位則分布在公園邊緣一帶。 公園東半部包含位於東北方的水生植物池，以及位於東南方的玻璃溫室。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Today, the central fountain has been replaced by a square rose garden, surrounded by seats on all four sides. The former musicians’ stage has given way to a larger amphitheatre for concerts. On the eastern side, the old pond and glasshouse have disappeared; in their place are a café, a children’s play area and a water feature. A new entrance to an underground car park has also been introduced from the southeast.","chinese":"如今，中央噴泉已被一個方形玫瑰園取代，而其四周均設有座位。 原本的音樂家表演台已被一個更大的露天音樂會劇場取代。 在東側，舊有的池塘和玻璃溫室已經消失；取而代之的是咖啡館、兒童遊樂區和水景設施。 此外，東南方也新增了一個通往地下停車場的入口。"}],"vocabulary":[]},"model-essay-9-ielts-task1-process-diagram":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-9-ielts-task1-process-diagram","essayKey":"process-diagram:9","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-9-ielts-task1-process-diagram","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/process-diagrams/process-diagram-9","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The diagrams illustrate the stages and equipment used to make cement, and how this cement is then used to produce concrete for construction.","chinese":"這些圖表說明了製造水泥所使用的階段和設備，以及這種水泥如何進一步用於生產建築用混凝土。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, cement manufacture is a multi-stage linear process involving crushing, mixing, heating and grinding, whereas concrete production is much simpler, requiring only the blending of four measured ingredients. Gravel accounts for by far the largest share of concrete, while water is the smallest component.","chinese":"整體而言，水泥製造是一個多階段的線性流程，涉及壓碎、混合、加熱和研磨；相比之下，混凝土生產簡單得多，只需要把四種按比例計量的原料混合起來。 碎石在混凝土中佔遠遠最大的比例，而水則是最小的組成部分。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"At the beginning of the cement-making process, limestone and clay are fed into a crusher, where they are reduced to powder. This powder is transferred to a mixer and then passes into a rotating heater. As the mixture moves through this cylinder, heat is applied from one end, after which the heated material is processed in a grinder. The resulting cement is finally packed into bags.","chinese":"在水泥製造過程的開始，石灰石和黏土被送入破碎機，在那裡被壓碎成粉末。 這些粉末接著被轉移到混合器，然後進入旋轉加熱器。 當混合物通過這個圓筒時，熱量從一端施加；之後，加熱後的材料會在研磨機中進一步處理。 最後，製成的水泥被裝入袋中。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Concrete production involves fewer stages. Cement, sand, gravel and water are all poured into a concrete mixer, which rotates to combine them. Gravel, labelled as small stones, makes up half of the mixture, while sand accounts for a further quarter. Cement and water constitute 15% and 10%, respectively, before the finished concrete is ready for building work.","chinese":"混凝土生產涉及的階段較少。 水泥、沙、碎石和水全部被倒入混凝土攪拌機中，該機器會旋轉將它們混合。 碎石，也就是圖中標註的小石子，佔整個混合物的一半，而沙則佔另外四分之一。 水泥和水分別佔 15% 和 10% ，然後製成的混凝土便可用於建築工程。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"diagrams illustrate","chinese":"圖示說明"},{"english":"stages and equipment","chinese":"階段及設備"},{"english":"used to make cement","chinese":"用於製造水泥"},{"english":"cement","chinese":"水泥"},{"english":"used to produce concrete","chinese":"用於生產混凝土"},{"english":"concrete","chinese":"混凝土"},{"english":"for construction","chinese":"用於建築"},{"english":"cement manufacture","chinese":"水泥製造"},{"english":"multi-stage linear process","chinese":"多階段線性流程"},{"english":"involving crushing, mixing, heating and grinding","chinese":"涉及壓碎、混合、加熱及研磨"},{"english":"crushing","chinese":"壓碎"},{"english":"mixing","chinese":"混合"},{"english":"heating","chinese":"加熱"},{"english":"grinding","chinese":"研磨"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相比之下"},{"english":"concrete production","chinese":"混凝土生產"},{"english":"much simpler","chinese":"簡單得多"},{"english":"requiring only","chinese":"只需要"},{"english":"blending of four measured ingredients","chinese":"混合四種已量度的材料"},{"english":"measured ingredients","chinese":"已量度的材料"},{"english":"gravel","chinese":"碎石"},{"english":"accounts for by far the largest share","chinese":"明顯佔最大比例"},{"english":"largest share of concrete","chinese":"混凝土中最大比例"},{"english":"smallest component","chinese":"最小成分"},{"english":"at the beginning of","chinese":"在……開始時"},{"english":"cement-making process","chinese":"水泥製造過程"},{"english":"limestone and clay","chinese":"石灰石及黏土"},{"english":"fed into a crusher","chinese":"被送入壓碎機"},{"english":"crusher","chinese":"壓碎機"},{"english":"reduced to powder","chinese":"被壓碎成粉末"},{"english":"powder","chinese":"粉末"},{"english":"transferred to a mixer","chinese":"被轉移到攪拌機"},{"english":"mixer","chinese":"攪拌機"},{"english":"passes into","chinese":"進入；通過進入"},{"english":"rotating heater","chinese":"旋轉加熱器"},{"english":"as the mixture moves through","chinese":"當混合物通過……時"},{"english":"cylinder","chinese":"圓筒"},{"english":"heat is applied from one end","chinese":"從一端加熱"},{"english":"heated material","chinese":"經加熱的物料"},{"english":"processed in a grinder","chinese":"在研磨機中處理"},{"english":"grinder","chinese":"研磨機"},{"english":"resulting cement","chinese":"形成的水泥"},{"english":"finally packed into bags","chinese":"最後被裝入袋中"},{"english":"concrete production involves fewer stages","chinese":"混凝土生產涉及較少階段"},{"english":"fewer stages","chinese":"較少階段"},{"english":"poured into a concrete mixer","chinese":"被倒入混凝土攪拌機"},{"english":"concrete mixer","chinese":"混凝土攪拌機"},{"english":"rotates to combine them","chinese":"旋轉以混合它們"},{"english":"labelled as small stones","chinese":"標示為小石"},{"english":"small stones","chinese":"小石"},{"english":"makes up half of the mixture","chinese":"佔混合物的一半"},{"english":"half of the mixture","chinese":"混合物的一半"},{"english":"accounts for a further quarter","chinese":"另佔四分之一"},{"english":"a further quarter","chinese":"另外四分之一"},{"english":"constitute 15% and 10%","chinese":"分別構成15%及10%"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"finished concrete","chinese":"製成的混凝土"},{"english":"ready for building work","chinese":"可用於建築工程"},{"english":"building work","chinese":"建築工程"},{"english":"production process","chinese":"生產過程"},{"english":"raw materials","chinese":"原材料"},{"english":"final product","chinese":"最終產品"},{"english":"construction material","chinese":"建築材料"}]},"model-essay-9-ielts-task1-tables":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-9-ielts-task1-tables","essayKey":"tables:9","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-9-ielts-task1-tables","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/tables/table-9","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The table compares the daily per-person calorie intake from rice, wheat and maize in Cambodia, Poland, Egypt and Mexico.","chinese":"該表比較了柬埔寨、波蘭、埃及和墨西哥四國人民每日每人從米、小麥和玉米中攝取的卡路里。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, each country shows a clear dependence on a different staple: rice in Cambodia, wheat in Poland and Egypt, and maize in Mexico. Egypt records the broadest consumption across all three foods, while Poland has the narrowest pattern, with no calories from maize.","chinese":"整體而言，每個國家都明顯依賴不同的主食：柬埔寨主要依賴米，波蘭和埃及主要依賴小麥，而墨西哥則主要依賴玉米。 埃及在三種食物中都有較廣泛的攝取，而波蘭的飲食模式最狹窄，完全沒有來自玉米的卡路里。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Rice is overwhelmingly dominant in Cambodia, at 1,445 calories per person per day, which is nearly three times Egypt's figure of 501. The two remaining countries consume little rice: Mexico stands at 57 calories, while Poland records only 19. Wheat, by contrast, is barely eaten in Cambodia, at just 18 calories. It is the main source in Egypt and Poland, at 1,095 and 865 calories respectively, whereas Mexico's figure is much lower, at 275.","chinese":"米在柬埔寨佔絕對主導地位，達到每日每人 1,445 卡路里，幾乎是埃及 501 卡路里的三倍。 其餘兩國的米攝取量很低：墨西哥為 57 卡路里，而波蘭只有 19 卡路里。 相比之下，小麥在柬埔寨幾乎不被食用，只有 18 卡路里。 小麥是埃及和波蘭的主要來源，分別為 1,095 和 865 卡路里，而墨西哥的數字則低得多，為 275 卡路里。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Maize consumption follows a different pattern. Mexico records the highest intake, at 1,083 calories, far ahead of Egypt's 578 and over ten times Cambodia's 103. Poland, however, reports no maize consumption at all.","chinese":"玉米的攝取情況則呈現不同模式。 墨西哥的玉米攝取量最高，達 1,083 卡路里，遠高於埃及的 578 卡路里，也超過柬埔寨 103 卡路里的十倍。 然而，波蘭完全沒有玉米攝取量。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the table compares","chinese":"表格比較"},{"english":"daily per-person calorie intake","chinese":"每人每日卡路里攝取量"},{"english":"calorie intake","chinese":"卡路里攝取量"},{"english":"from rice, wheat and maize","chinese":"來自米飯、小麥和粟米"},{"english":"Cambodia, Poland, Egypt and Mexico","chinese":"柬埔寨、波蘭、埃及和墨西哥"},{"english":"each country shows","chinese":"每個國家都顯示"},{"english":"a clear dependence on","chinese":"明顯依賴……"},{"english":"a different staple","chinese":"不同主糧"},{"english":"staple","chinese":"主糧"},{"english":"rice in Cambodia","chinese":"柬埔寨的米飯"},{"english":"wheat in Poland and Egypt","chinese":"波蘭和埃及的小麥"},{"english":"maize in Mexico","chinese":"墨西哥的粟米"},{"english":"shows the broadest pattern of consumption","chinese":"顯示最廣泛的消費模式"},{"english":"across all three foods","chinese":"在三種食物之中"},{"english":"the narrowest pattern","chinese":"最狹窄的模式"},{"english":"with no calories from","chinese":"沒有來自……的卡路里"},{"english":"overwhelmingly dominant","chinese":"佔絕對主導地位"},{"english":"dominant in","chinese":"在……佔主導地位"},{"english":"at 1,445 calories","chinese":"為1,445卡路里"},{"english":"calories per person per day","chinese":"每人每日卡路里"},{"english":"nearly three times","chinese":"接近……的三倍"},{"english":"Egypt's figure","chinese":"埃及的數字"},{"english":"the two remaining countries","chinese":"其餘兩個國家"},{"english":"consume little rice","chinese":"米飯攝取量很少"},{"english":"stands at","chinese":"為；達到"},{"english":"records only","chinese":"只錄得"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"barely eaten","chinese":"幾乎不被食用"},{"english":"at just 18 calories","chinese":"只有18卡路里"},{"english":"the main source","chinese":"主要來源"},{"english":"in Egypt and Poland","chinese":"在埃及和波蘭"},{"english":"at 1,095 and 865 calories respectively","chinese":"分別為1,095和865卡路里"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相反"},{"english":"much lower","chinese":"低得多"},{"english":"maize consumption","chinese":"粟米消費量"},{"english":"follows a different pattern","chinese":"呈現不同模式"},{"english":"records the highest intake","chinese":"錄得最高攝取量"},{"english":"the highest intake","chinese":"最高攝取量"},{"english":"far ahead of","chinese":"遠高於；大幅領先"},{"english":"over ten times","chinese":"超過……的十倍"},{"english":"reports no maize consumption","chinese":"沒有粟米攝取量"},{"english":"no maize consumption at all","chinese":"完全沒有粟米攝取"},{"english":"different pattern of consumption","chinese":"不同消費模式"},{"english":"main calorie source","chinese":"主要卡路里來源"},{"english":"dietary pattern","chinese":"飲食模式"},{"english":"staple-food consumption","chinese":"主糧消費"},{"english":"food intake","chinese":"食物攝取量"},{"english":"vary greatly","chinese":"差異很大"},{"english":"the highest figure","chinese":"最高數字"},{"english":"the lowest figure","chinese":"最低數字"},{"english":"a non-zero figure","chinese":"非零數字"},{"english":"remain heavily dependent on","chinese":"仍然高度依賴……"},{"english":"rely mainly on","chinese":"主要依靠……"},{"english":"account for most calories","chinese":"佔大部分卡路里"},{"english":"contribute no calories","chinese":"沒有提供卡路里"},{"english":"a sharp contrast","chinese":"明顯對比"},{"english":"an uneven distribution","chinese":"分佈不平均"},{"english":"a balanced intake","chinese":"較平均的攝取量"},{"english":"the broadest spread","chinese":"最廣泛的分佈"},{"english":"the narrowest spread","chinese":"最狹窄的分佈"},{"english":"compared with","chinese":"與……相比"},{"english":"contrast strongly with","chinese":"與……形成強烈對比"},{"english":"be concentrated in","chinese":"集中於……"},{"english":"spread across","chinese":"分佈於……"},{"english":"substantial intake","chinese":"大量攝取"},{"english":"minimal intake","chinese":"極少攝取"},{"english":"no intake from","chinese":"沒有來自……的攝取量"},{"english":"the overall pattern","chinese":"整體模式"},{"english":"the dominant food","chinese":"主要食物"},{"english":"the least consumed food","chinese":"消耗最少的食物"},{"english":"the most heavily consumed food","chinese":"消耗最多的食物"},{"english":"the figure for X","chinese":"X 的數字"},{"english":"X's figure is much lower","chinese":"X 的數字低得多"},{"english":"in relative terms","chinese":"以相對數字而言"},{"english":"in absolute terms","chinese":"以實際數字而言"},{"english":"a clear reliance on","chinese":"明顯依賴……"},{"english":"the calorie contribution from","chinese":"來自……的卡路里貢獻"},{"english":"a country-specific pattern","chinese":"因國家而異的模式"},{"english":"unlike","chinese":"不像……"},{"english":"while","chinese":"而"},{"english":"however","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"overall dependence","chinese":"整體依賴"},{"english":"consumption profile","chinese":"消費概況"},{"english":"calorie source","chinese":"卡路里來源"}]},"model-essay-10-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-10-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:10","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-10-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q10","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In some education systems, girls and boys are educated separately rather than together. Although this arrangement can produce a few short-term academic benefits, I believe its chief disadvantage is more significant: it leaves young people less prepared for the mixed world beyond school.","chinese":"在某些教育制度中，男女生並不是一起接受教育，而是分別在不同的學校就讀。 儘管這種安排可能帶來一些短期的學業好處，但我認為它更大的缺點更為嚴重：它會令年輕人較難為學校以外那個男女共處的真實世界作好準備。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One advantage of single-sex schooling is that it can reduce distraction during adolescence. In mixed schools, some teenagers become overly concerned with appearance, popularity, or attracting the opposite sex. For example, part of a lesson can be lost to students trying to impress one another or becoming excessively self-conscious. When that pressure is removed, classrooms often become calmer and more focused. A second benefit is that students may participate more confidently in subjects that are often shaped by gender stereotypes. For instance, girls in an all-girls environment may speak up more readily in physics, while boys in a boys’ school may feel less embarrassed about contributing in literature or languages.","chinese":"單一性別學校的一個優點，是它能在青少年時期減少分心的情況。 在男女混合學校中，一些青少年可能會過分在意自己的外表、受歡迎程度，或是否能吸引異性。 例如，課堂上的一部分時間可能會被學生彼此取悅、刻意表現，或過度在意自己形象所浪費掉。 當這種壓力被移除後，課堂氣氛往往會變得更平靜，學生也更能集中注意力。 第二個好處是，學生在一些經常受性別刻板印象影響的科目中，可能會更有自信地參與。 例如，在全女校環境中，女生在物理課上可能會更願意發言；而在男校中，男生在文學或語言課堂上發表意見時，也可能較少感到尷尬。 因此，單一性別教育有時確實能營造出一個更專注、也更能建立自信的學習環境。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Even so, the main disadvantage is that such schools can create an artificial social bubble. If students spend most of their formative years apart, they may enter adulthood with unnecessary awkwardness or shallow assumptions about the opposite sex. This is a serious problem because real life is not divided in that way: universities, workplaces, and public institutions all require men and women to communicate and cooperate naturally. A student who performs well in a sheltered setting may therefore struggle in mixed-group presentations at university or in workplace teams, where maturity, ease of interaction, and mutual respect matter just as much as academic knowledge.","chinese":"即便如此，這類學校最主要的缺點在於，它們可能會形成一種不自然的社交溫室。 如果學生在成長中最關鍵的那些年大多與異性分隔開來，他們長大後便可能帶著不必要的尷尬感，或對異性抱有流於表面的假設與誤解。 這是一個嚴重的問題，因為現實生活並不是這樣被劃分開來的：大學、職場以及各種公共機構，都要求男女能自然地溝通與合作。 因此，一個在受保護環境中表現優秀的學生，到了大學需要進行男女混合的小組報告時，或進入職場團隊合作時，便可能顯得不知所措；因為在那些情境中，成熟度、互動的自然程度，以及彼此尊重，和學術能力同樣重要。 因此，單一性別教育或許能在短期內保護學生，但同時也可能令他們較難應對成年後真實世界的要求。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"Overall, separate schooling may improve concentration and classroom confidence for some students, but those gains are outweighed by its larger social cost. Schools should not merely help children achieve good grades; they should also prepare them for life as it is actually lived.","chinese":"總結來說，單一性別教育或許能提升某些學生的專注力與課堂自信，但這些好處仍然被它更大的社會代價所蓋過。 學校不應只幫助孩子取得好成績；它們也應該讓學生為現實生活中真正的社會互動作好準備。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"education systems","chinese":"教育制度"},{"english":"be educated separately","chinese":"分開接受教育"},{"english":"rather than together","chinese":"而不是一起"},{"english":"this arrangement","chinese":"這種安排"},{"english":"short-term academic benefits","chinese":"短期學業好處"},{"english":"chief disadvantage","chinese":"主要缺點"},{"english":"more significant","chinese":"更重要"},{"english":"leave young people less prepared for","chinese":"令年輕人較沒有準備面對"},{"english":"the mixed world beyond school","chinese":"學校以外男女混合的世界"},{"english":"single-sex schooling","chinese":"單性別教育"},{"english":"reduce distraction","chinese":"減少分心"},{"english":"during adolescence","chinese":"青春期期間"},{"english":"mixed schools","chinese":"男女混合學校"},{"english":"overly concerned with","chinese":"過分關注"},{"english":"appearance and popularity","chinese":"外表和受歡迎程度"},{"english":"the opposite sex","chinese":"異性"},{"english":"part of a lesson can be lost to","chinese":"一堂課部分時間可能耗於"},{"english":"impress one another","chinese":"令彼此留下深刻印象"},{"english":"excessively self-conscious","chinese":"過分在意自己形象"},{"english":"when that pressure is removed","chinese":"當這種壓力被移除時"},{"english":"calmer and more focused","chinese":"更平靜和更專注"},{"english":"a second benefit","chinese":"第二個好處"},{"english":"participate more confidently","chinese":"更有信心地參與"},{"english":"be shaped by","chinese":"受……影響"},{"english":"gender stereotypes","chinese":"性別定型觀念"},{"english":"an all-girls environment","chinese":"全女校環境"},{"english":"speak up more readily","chinese":"更願意發言"},{"english":"physics","chinese":"物理"},{"english":"a boys' school","chinese":"男校"},{"english":"feel less embarrassed about","chinese":"對……較不感到尷尬"},{"english":"contributing in","chinese":"在……中發表意見"},{"english":"literature or languages","chinese":"文學或語言科"},{"english":"even so","chinese":"即使如此"},{"english":"the main disadvantage","chinese":"主要缺點"},{"english":"an artificial social bubble","chinese":"人為的社交泡沫"},{"english":"formative years","chinese":"成長形成期"},{"english":"enter adulthood with","chinese":"帶着……進入成年"},{"english":"unnecessary awkwardness","chinese":"不必要的尷尬"},{"english":"shallow assumptions about","chinese":"對……的膚淺假設"},{"english":"a serious problem","chinese":"嚴重問題"},{"english":"real life","chinese":"現實生活"},{"english":"be divided in that way","chinese":"以那種方式被分隔"},{"english":"public institutions","chinese":"公共機構"},{"english":"communicate and cooperate naturally","chinese":"自然地溝通和合作"},{"english":"performs well in","chinese":"在……表現良好"},{"english":"a sheltered setting","chinese":"受保護的環境"},{"english":"struggle in","chinese":"在……中感到困難"},{"english":"mixed-group presentations","chinese":"男女混合小組匯報"},{"english":"workplace teams","chinese":"職場團隊"},{"english":"maturity","chinese":"成熟程度"},{"english":"ease of interaction","chinese":"互動時的自然程度"},{"english":"mutual respect","chinese":"互相尊重"},{"english":"just as much as","chinese":"與……同樣重要"},{"english":"academic knowledge","chinese":"學術知識"},{"english":"overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"separate schooling","chinese":"分開教育"},{"english":"improve concentration","chinese":"提高專注力"},{"english":"classroom confidence","chinese":"課堂信心"},{"english":"those gains","chinese":"那些得益"},{"english":"be outweighed by","chinese":"被……蓋過"},{"english":"larger social cost","chinese":"更大的社會代價"},{"english":"not merely help children achieve good grades","chinese":"不只是幫助孩子取得好成績"},{"english":"achieve good grades","chinese":"取得好成績"},{"english":"prepare them for life","chinese":"讓他們為生活作好準備"},{"english":"as it is actually lived","chinese":"真實生活的樣子"}]},"model-essay-10-ielts-cause-solution":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-10-ielts-cause-solution","essayKey":"cause-solution:10","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-10-ielts-cause-solution","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/problem-and-cause/EdmundBd9CnS-Q10","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Although walking is one of the simplest and cheapest ways to stay healthy, it has quietly disappeared from many people’s daily routines. This decline stems mainly from car-centred urban design and increasingly sedentary lifestyles. It can be addressed by improving public spaces and making walking a normal part of work, school and transport habits.","chinese":"儘管步行是保持健康最簡單、最便宜的方法之一，它卻已悄然從許多人的日常生活中消失。 這種下降主要源於以汽車為中心的城市設計，以及越來越久坐不動的生活方式。 這個問題可以透過改善公共空間，以及使步行成為工作、學校和交通習慣中的正常部分來解決。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One major reason is that many modern cities are built around speed rather than movement. When homes, offices, shops and schools are far apart, walking becomes inconvenient or unsafe, especially in areas with wide roads, poor pavements and little shade. As a result, people choose cars, buses or ride-hailing services, not because walking has no value, but because the environment pushes them away from it. Another reason is the rise of desk-based routines. Many people spend long hours in front of screens, and after a tiring day they often choose the easiest option: lifts instead of stairs, online shopping instead of local errands, and entertainment at home instead of a short walk outside. Over time, these small choices harden into a sedentary lifestyle.","chinese":"其中一個主要原因是，許多現代城市是圍繞速度而非身體活動來建造的。 當住宅、辦公室、商店和學校相距甚遠時，步行就會變得不方便或不安全，尤其是在道路寬闊、行人路質素差、遮蔭不足的地區。 結果，人們選擇私家車、巴士或叫車服務，並不是因為步行沒有價值，而是因為環境把他們推離了步行。 另一個原因是以辦公桌為中心的日常模式越來越普遍。 許多人長時間坐在螢幕前，而在疲憊的一天過後，他們往往會選擇最輕鬆的選項：乘搭升降機而不是走樓梯、網上購物而不是到附近辦事、在家娛樂而不是到戶外短暫散步。 久而久之，這些小選擇便會固化成一種久坐不動的生活方式。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"To tackle this problem, governments should make walking safer, easier and more attractive. Wider pavements, shaded streets, better lighting, pedestrian zones and crossings can turn walking from a chore into a daily option. For example, if a neighbourhood has pleasant routes to schools, parks and shops, families are more likely to walk without feeling that they are sacrificing time or safety. At the same time, employers and schools should build movement into ordinary routines. Workplaces can encourage walking meetings and active commuting, while schools can promote walking buses or step-based challenges. These measures matter because they make walking feel like part of daily life, not an extra task squeezed into a crowded schedule.","chinese":"為了解決這個問題，政府應該使步行變得更安全、更容易，也更具吸引力。 更寬闊的行人路、有遮蔭的街道、更好的照明、行人專區和過路設施，可以把步行由一件麻煩事變成一個日常選項。 例如，如果一個社區有舒適的路線通往學校、公園和商店，家庭便更有可能步行，而不會覺得自己正在犧牲時間或安全。 同時，僱主和學校應該把身體活動融入日常安排之中。 工作場所可以鼓勵步行會議和主動通勤，而學校則可以推廣步行巴士或以步數為基礎的挑戰活動。 這些措施之所以重要，是因為它們能讓步行感覺像日常生活的一部分，而不是一項被硬塞進繁忙日程中的額外任務。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, fewer people are walking because their surroundings and routines often make inactivity easier than movement. The most effective response is to design walkable communities and create daily habits that make walking convenient, safe and normal again.","chinese":"總結來說，越來越少人步行，是因為他們所處的環境和日常習慣，往往令不活動比活動更容易。 最有效的應對方法，是設計適合步行的社區，並建立日常習慣，使步行重新變得方便、安全和正常。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"one of the simplest and cheapest ways to","chinese":"……最簡單又最便宜的方法之一"},{"english":"stay healthy","chinese":"保持健康"},{"english":"quietly disappeared from","chinese":"悄悄從……中消失"},{"english":"daily routines","chinese":"日常習慣"},{"english":"this decline stems mainly from","chinese":"這種下降主要源於"},{"english":"car-centred urban design","chinese":"以汽車為中心的城市設計"},{"english":"increasingly sedentary lifestyles","chinese":"越來越久坐的生活方式"},{"english":"be addressed by","chinese":"透過……處理"},{"english":"improving public spaces","chinese":"改善公共空間"},{"english":"a normal part of","chinese":"……的正常一部分"},{"english":"transport habits","chinese":"交通習慣"},{"english":"built around speed rather than movement","chinese":"圍繞速度而非活動來建設"},{"english":"far apart","chinese":"相距很遠"},{"english":"walking becomes inconvenient or unsafe","chinese":"步行變得不方便或不安全"},{"english":"wide roads","chinese":"寬闊馬路"},{"english":"poor pavements","chinese":"欠佳的行人路"},{"english":"little shade","chinese":"缺少遮蔭"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"ride-hailing services","chinese":"網約車服務"},{"english":"pushes them away from","chinese":"令……遠離"},{"english":"the rise of","chinese":"……的興起"},{"english":"desk-based routines","chinese":"以坐着辦公為主的日常模式"},{"english":"spend long hours in front of screens","chinese":"長時間坐在螢幕前"},{"english":"after a tiring day","chinese":"在疲累的一天後"},{"english":"the easiest option","chinese":"最容易的選擇"},{"english":"lifts instead of stairs","chinese":"升降機而不是樓梯"},{"english":"online shopping instead of local errands","chinese":"網上購物而不是到附近辦事"},{"english":"entertainment at home","chinese":"家中娛樂"},{"english":"harden into","chinese":"逐漸固定成"},{"english":"a sedentary lifestyle","chinese":"久坐的生活方式"},{"english":"tackle this problem","chinese":"處理這個問題"},{"english":"safer, easier and more attractive","chinese":"更安全、更方便、更吸引"},{"english":"wider pavements","chinese":"更寬闊的行人路"},{"english":"shaded streets","chinese":"有遮蔭的街道"},{"english":"better lighting","chinese":"更好的照明"},{"english":"pedestrian zones","chinese":"行人專區"},{"english":"crossings","chinese":"行人過路處"},{"english":"turn walking from a chore into","chinese":"將步行由苦差變成……"},{"english":"a daily option","chinese":"日常選擇"},{"english":"pleasant routes to","chinese":"通往……的舒適路線"},{"english":"are more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"sacrificing time or safety","chinese":"犧牲時間或安全"},{"english":"build movement into","chinese":"將活動融入……"},{"english":"ordinary routines","chinese":"日常安排"},{"english":"walking meetings","chinese":"步行會議"},{"english":"active commuting","chinese":"主動通勤；以步行或踩單車通勤"},{"english":"promote walking buses","chinese":"推廣步行校巴"},{"english":"step-based challenges","chinese":"以步數為目標的挑戰"},{"english":"these measures matter because","chinese":"這些措施重要，因為"},{"english":"part of daily life","chinese":"日常生活的一部分"},{"english":"an extra task","chinese":"額外任務"},{"english":"squeezed into","chinese":"被勉強擠進"},{"english":"a crowded schedule","chinese":"排得很滿的日程"},{"english":"surroundings and routines","chinese":"周邊環境和日常習慣"},{"english":"make inactivity easier than movement","chinese":"令不活動比活動更容易"},{"english":"the most effective response","chinese":"最有效的回應"},{"english":"walkable communities","chinese":"適合步行的社區"},{"english":"create daily habits","chinese":"建立日常習慣"},{"english":"convenient, safe and normal again","chinese":"再次變得方便、安全和正常"}]},"model-essay-10-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-10-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:10","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-10-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q10","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Alcohol-related crime is a serious social problem because alcohol can weaken self-control, intensify aggression and turn minor disputes into violence. However, I do not think a total ban on alcohol would be an effective way to reduce crime. It would attack the surface of the problem rather than the behaviour that leads to crime.","chinese":"與酒精相關的犯罪是一個嚴重的社會問題，因為酒精會削弱自制力、加劇攻擊性，並把小爭執變成暴力事件。 然而，我不認為全面禁止酒精會是一種有效減少犯罪的方法。 這只會處理問題的表面，而不是處理導致犯罪的行為本身。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main weakness of prohibition is that it would be difficult to enforce and could create new criminal activity. If demand for alcohol remains high, people are likely to look for illegal suppliers, and a black market can quickly develop. Criminal groups could then sell unsafe products, exploit vulnerable customers and avoid regulation altogether. In this situation, the police would waste time chasing ordinary drinkers and underground sellers instead of focusing on violent offenders. Therefore, banning alcohol may simply move the problem into the shadows rather than remove it.","chinese":"禁酒的主要弱點在於它難以執行，而且可能製造新的犯罪活動。 如果人們對酒精的需求仍然很高，他們很可能會尋找非法供應者，而黑市也可能迅速形成。 犯罪集團便可能出售不安全的產品、剝削脆弱的顧客，並完全逃避監管。 在這種情況下，警方會把時間浪費在追查普通飲酒者和地下賣家身上，而不是集中處理暴力罪犯。 因此，禁止酒精可能只是把問題推入陰影之中，而不是把問題真正消除。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"A more effective solution is targeted control. Governments should restrict late-night alcohol sales, impose heavy penalties for drunk driving and alcohol-related violence, and require bars to refuse service to clearly intoxicated customers. These measures focus on the moments when drinking is most likely to trigger crime. For example, if a nightclub knows it may lose its licence for serving drunk customers, staff will have a strong reason to intervene before an argument turns into a fight. Prevention at this stage is far more practical than a blanket ban.","chinese":"一個更有效的解決方法是針對性的管制。 政府應該限制深夜售酒、對醉酒駕駛和與酒精相關的暴力行為施加嚴厲懲罰，並要求酒吧拒絕服務明顯醉酒的顧客。 這些措施集中處理飲酒最有可能引發犯罪的時刻。 例如，如果一間夜店知道自己可能因為服務醉酒顧客而失去牌照，員工便會有很強的理由在爭執變成打鬥之前介入。 在這個階段進行預防，遠比一刀切的禁令實際得多。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 3","english":"Another useful measure is treatment and education for people who repeatedly misuse alcohol. Some offenders do not simply need punishment; they need counselling, addiction support and a clearer understanding of the harm they cause. If schools and communities teach young people how alcohol affects judgment and self-control, future crime can be reduced at its roots.","chinese":"另一個有用的措施，是為反覆濫用酒精的人提供治療和教育。 有些犯罪者並不只是需要懲罰；他們需要輔導、戒癮支援，以及更清楚地理解自己所造成的傷害。 如果學校和社區能教導年輕人酒精如何影響判斷力和自制力，未來的犯罪便可以從根源上減少。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, banning alcohol is not an effective anti-crime policy. Stricter regulation, stronger enforcement and proper support for alcohol misuse would reduce alcohol-related crime more realistically and sustainably.","chinese":"總結來說，禁止酒精並不是一項有效的反犯罪政策。 更嚴格的規管、更有力的執法，以及對酒精濫用提供適當支援，才能以更現實和更可持續的方式減少與酒精相關的犯罪。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"alcohol-related crime","chinese":"與酒精有關的罪案"},{"english":"a serious social problem","chinese":"嚴重的社會問題"},{"english":"weaken self-control","chinese":"削弱自制能力"},{"english":"intensify aggression","chinese":"加劇攻擊性"},{"english":"minor disputes","chinese":"小爭執"},{"english":"turn minor disputes into violence","chinese":"將小爭執演變成暴力"},{"english":"a total ban on alcohol","chinese":"全面禁酒"},{"english":"an effective way to reduce crime","chinese":"減少罪案的有效方法"},{"english":"attack the surface of the problem","chinese":"只處理問題表面"},{"english":"rather than the behaviour that leads to crime","chinese":"而不是處理導致罪案的行為"},{"english":"the main weakness of","chinese":"……的主要弱點"},{"english":"prohibition","chinese":"禁令；禁酒令"},{"english":"difficult to enforce","chinese":"難以執行"},{"english":"create new criminal activity","chinese":"製造新的犯罪活動"},{"english":"demand for alcohol remains high","chinese":"對酒精的需求仍然高"},{"english":"look for illegal suppliers","chinese":"尋找非法供應者"},{"english":"a black market","chinese":"黑市"},{"english":"quickly develop","chinese":"迅速形成；迅速發展"},{"english":"criminal groups","chinese":"犯罪集團"},{"english":"unsafe products","chinese":"不安全產品"},{"english":"exploit vulnerable customers","chinese":"剝削弱勢顧客"},{"english":"avoid regulation altogether","chinese":"完全避開規管"},{"english":"waste time chasing","chinese":"浪費時間追查"},{"english":"ordinary drinkers","chinese":"普通飲酒人士"},{"english":"underground sellers","chinese":"地下賣家"},{"english":"violent offenders","chinese":"暴力罪犯"},{"english":"move the problem into the shadows","chinese":"將問題推入暗處"},{"english":"rather than remove it","chinese":"而不是將其消除"},{"english":"targeted control","chinese":"針對性管制"},{"english":"restrict late-night alcohol sales","chinese":"限制深夜酒精銷售"},{"english":"impose heavy penalties for","chinese":"對……施加重罰"},{"english":"drunk driving","chinese":"酒後駕駛"},{"english":"alcohol-related violence","chinese":"與酒精有關的暴力"},{"english":"refuse service to","chinese":"拒絕向……提供服務"},{"english":"clearly intoxicated customers","chinese":"明顯醉酒的顧客"},{"english":"focus on the moments when","chinese":"集中處理……的時刻"},{"english":"trigger crime","chinese":"引發罪案"},{"english":"lose its licence","chinese":"失去牌照"},{"english":"serve drunk customers","chinese":"向醉酒顧客提供服務"},{"english":"have a strong reason to intervene","chinese":"有充分理由介入"},{"english":"before an argument turns into a fight","chinese":"在爭執演變成打鬥之前"},{"english":"prevention at this stage","chinese":"在這個階段作出預防"},{"english":"far more practical than","chinese":"比……實際得多"},{"english":"a blanket ban","chinese":"一刀切禁令"},{"english":"treatment and education","chinese":"治療和教育"},{"english":"repeatedly misuse alcohol","chinese":"反覆濫用酒精"},{"english":"not simply need punishment","chinese":"不只是需要懲罰"},{"english":"counselling","chinese":"輔導"},{"english":"addiction support","chinese":"戒癮支援"},{"english":"a clearer understanding of","chinese":"對……有更清楚的理解"},{"english":"the harm they cause","chinese":"他們造成的傷害"},{"english":"affects judgment and self-control","chinese":"影響判斷力和自制力"},{"english":"be reduced at its roots","chinese":"從根源減少"},{"english":"anti-crime policy","chinese":"打擊罪案政策"},{"english":"stricter regulation","chinese":"更嚴格的規管"},{"english":"stronger enforcement","chinese":"更強力的執法"},{"english":"proper support for alcohol misuse","chinese":"對酒精濫用的適當支援"},{"english":"realistically and sustainably","chinese":"更實際和可持續地"}]},"model-essay-10-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-10-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:10","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-10-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q10","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"People often make quick judgments when they meet someone for the first time. While some argue that these early impressions are important because they help us respond quickly in social and professional situations, I believe that it is much wiser not to judge people too soon.","chinese":"人們第一次見到某個人時，往往會很快作出判斷。 雖然有些人認為這些早期印象很重要，因為它們能幫助我們在社交和專業場合中迅速作出反應，但我認為，不要太快評斷別人會明智得多。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"On the one hand, first impressions can be useful because they give us immediate clues about a person’s attitude and behaviour. In many situations, people do not have the luxury of spending a long time getting to know one another. For example, during a job interview, an employer may notice whether a candidate arrives on time, speaks politely and listens carefully. These small details can suggest reliability, confidence and respect. In this sense, a first impression acts like a doorway: it does not show the whole house, but it tells us whether we may want to step inside.","chinese":"一方面，第一印象可能是有用的，因為它們能讓我們即時看出一個人的態度和行為。 在很多情況下，人們並沒有充裕的時間去慢慢了解彼此。 例如，在求職面試中，僱主可能會留意一位應徵者是否準時到達、說話是否有禮貌，以及是否用心聆聽。 這些細節可以反映出可靠、自信和尊重。 從這個角度來看，第一印象就像一道門口：它不能展示整間屋子的全貌，但它能告訴我們是否想走進去看看。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"On the other hand, judging someone too quickly can be deeply unfair, because a first meeting often captures only a temporary version of a person. Someone may seem quiet because they are nervous, distant because they are under pressure, or awkward because they are in an unfamiliar environment. If others label them immediately, that label may stick even when it is inaccurate. For instance, a new student who says very little on the first day may later become kind, loyal and helpful once they feel comfortable. Real character is shown through repeated actions, not through one brief encounter.","chinese":"另一方面，太快評斷一個人可能非常不公平，因為第一次見面往往只捕捉到一個人暫時的狀態。 一個人可能看起來安靜，是因為他們緊張；看起來疏離，是因為他們承受壓力；看起來笨拙，是因為他們身處陌生環境。 如果別人立刻給他們貼上標籤，即使那個標籤並不準確，也可能會一直留在他們身上。 例如，一位新學生第一天可能很少說話，但當他感到自在之後，日後可能會變得善良、忠誠，而且樂於助人。 真正的性格是透過反覆的行動展現出來的，而不是透過一次短暫的相遇。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In my opinion, although first impressions can provide useful signals, they should never become the final basis for judging another person. People are complex, and their true qualities usually appear only over time. Therefore, it is better to treat first impressions as a starting point, not a verdict.","chinese":"在我看來，雖然第一印象能提供有用的訊號，但它們絕不應該成為評斷另一個人的最終依據。 人是複雜的，而他們真正的品質通常只有經過時間才會顯現。 因此，我們最好把第一印象視為一個起點，而不是一項判決。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"crime prevention","chinese":"預防罪案"},{"english":"a central part of","chinese":"……的核心部分"},{"english":"safe and civilised society","chinese":"安全而文明的社會"},{"english":"take responsibility for","chinese":"為……承擔責任"},{"english":"their own safety","chinese":"自身安全"},{"english":"preventing crime","chinese":"預防犯罪"},{"english":"the duty of the state","chinese":"國家的責任"},{"english":"in my opinion","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"act sensibly","chinese":"行事謹慎；明智行事"},{"english":"carry the primary responsibility","chinese":"承擔首要責任"},{"english":"authority and resources","chinese":"權力和資源"},{"english":"reduce crime on a large scale","chinese":"大規模減少罪案"},{"english":"individual responsibility","chinese":"個人責任"},{"english":"lower their own risk","chinese":"降低自身風險"},{"english":"making careful choices","chinese":"作出謹慎選擇"},{"english":"install security cameras","chinese":"安裝保安攝錄機"},{"english":"avoid leaving valuables in visible places","chinese":"避免將貴重物品放在顯眼地方"},{"english":"valuables","chinese":"貴重物品"},{"english":"be cautious when","chinese":"在……時保持謹慎"},{"english":"sharing personal information online","chinese":"在網上分享個人資料"},{"english":"many crimes are opportunistic","chinese":"很多罪案是伺機而作的"},{"english":"make themselves an easy target","chinese":"令自己成為容易下手的目標"},{"english":"be more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"take advantage of","chinese":"利用；乘機傷害"},{"english":"from this perspective","chinese":"從這個角度來看"},{"english":"personal awareness","chinese":"個人警覺性"},{"english":"act as the first line of defence","chinese":"作為第一道防線"},{"english":"daily situations","chinese":"日常情況"},{"english":"physically present","chinese":"親身在場"},{"english":"cannot depend mainly on","chinese":"不能主要依賴"},{"english":"be responsible for creating and maintaining","chinese":"負責建立和維持"},{"english":"make society safe","chinese":"令社會安全"},{"english":"effective policing","chinese":"有效警務"},{"english":"fair laws","chinese":"公平法律"},{"english":"street lighting","chinese":"街燈照明"},{"english":"public education","chinese":"公眾教育"},{"english":"social support","chinese":"社會支援"},{"english":"a neighbourhood","chinese":"社區；街區"},{"english":"poor law enforcement","chinese":"執法不力"},{"english":"weak surveillance","chinese":"監察薄弱"},{"english":"few opportunities for young people","chinese":"年輕人機會不足"},{"english":"to a limited extent","chinese":"在有限程度上"},{"english":"lock its doors","chinese":"鎖門"},{"english":"organised crime","chinese":"有組織犯罪"},{"english":"unsafe public spaces","chinese":"不安全的公共空間"},{"english":"wider social problems","chinese":"更廣泛的社會問題"},{"english":"push people towards illegal behaviour","chinese":"推使人走向非法行為"},{"english":"illegal behaviour","chinese":"非法行為"},{"english":"coordinated public action","chinese":"協調一致的公共行動"},{"english":"private caution","chinese":"個人謹慎"},{"english":"take reasonable steps to","chinese":"採取合理措施去"},{"english":"protect themselves","chinese":"保護自己"},{"english":"replace the role of government","chinese":"取代政府的角色"},{"english":"a social problem rather than","chinese":"是社會問題，而不是"},{"english":"merely a personal inconvenience","chinese":"只屬個人不便"},{"english":"the state","chinese":"國家；政府"},{"english":"chiefly responsible for","chinese":"對……負主要責任"}]},"model-essay-10-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-10-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:10","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-10-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q10","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In modern markets, businesses are under constant pressure to attract attention, so advertising is often treated as the decisive ingredient of commercial success. It is therefore unsurprising that some people believe marketing and promotion are the key to a successful business. This essay completely disagrees, because firms prosper above all when they offer genuine value and operate efficiently.","chinese":"在現代市場中，企業不斷承受吸引注意力的壓力，因此廣告常常被視為商業成功的決定性因素。 因此，有些人認為市場推廣和宣傳是企業成功的關鍵，這其實並不令人意外。 本文完全不同意這個看法， 因為企業真正能夠繁榮發展，最重要的是它們能提供真實價值並且有效率地運作。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The primary reason promotion is not the key is that customers remain loyal only when a business delivers something worthwhile. A persuasive campaign may generate initial sales, but continued success comes from satisfaction: when goods are dependable or services are consistently professional, buyers return, spend more over time and recommend the company to others. This creates repeat custom and organic growth, both of which are far more stable than attention purchased through advertising. For example, a new restaurant may fill its tables through online discounts and social-media campaigns, yet those customers will not return if the food is mediocre or the staff are inattentive. In addition, strong products develop reputations of their own. Once trust is established, word of mouth becomes a powerful source of demand, showing that quality, rather than promotion, is the real engine of long-term success.","chinese":"宣傳之所以不是關鍵，最主要的原因是：只有當企業真正提供有價值的東西時，顧客才會保持忠誠。 一場有說服力的宣傳活動也許能帶來最初的銷售，但持續的成功來自滿意度：當產品可靠、服務穩定而專業時，顧客才會再度光顧、長期花費更多，並向他人推薦這家公司。 這樣便能帶來回頭客和自然成長，而這兩者都比透過廣告買來的關注穩定得多。 例如，一間新餐廳也許能透過網上折扣和社交媒體宣傳坐滿顧客，但如果食物品質普通，或員工服務不夠周到，那些顧客就不會再回來。 此外，優秀的產品本身也會建立起自己的聲譽。 一旦信任建立起來，口碑就會成為強大的需求來源，這說明真正推動長期成功的引擎是品質，而不是宣傳。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Equally important is the way a business is managed. Even the most visible brand will struggle if it cannot control costs, train employees properly or deliver what it has promised. In such cases, marketing may actually accelerate failure: the more customers a weak company attracts, the more delayed orders, complaints and refund requests it creates, and these quickly damage public confidence. This pattern is common in e-commerce, where an aggressively advertised firm can still lose market share if deliveries are unreliable or customer support is ineffective. Sound management also enables a company to adapt, whether by improving products, responding to competition or investing wisely. These decisions determine whether a business survives beyond the short term, whereas promotion merely amplifies whatever underlying strengths or weaknesses already exist.","chinese":"同樣重要的，還有企業本身的管理方式。 即使是一個曝光率再高的品牌，如果無法控制成本、妥善培訓員工，或履行自己作出的承諾，最終也會陷入困境。 在這種情況下，市場推廣甚至可能加速失敗：一家本來就薄弱的公司吸引越多顧客，就會製造出越多延誤訂單、投訴和退款要求，而這些問題很快就會損害公眾信心。 這種情況在電子商務中十分常見：一家大力宣傳的公司，如果送貨不可靠或客服支援無效，仍然可能失去市場佔有率。 良好的管理也能讓企業具備適應能力，不論是改良產品、回應競爭，還是作出明智投資。 這些決定才真正左右一家企業能否超越短期生存，而宣傳本身不過只是放大原本已存在的優勢或弱點而已。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely disagree that marketing and promotion are the key to a successful business. They may attract initial attention, but durable success is built on genuine value, customer trust and competent management.","chinese":"總而言之，我完全不同意市場推廣和宣傳是企業成功的關鍵。 它們也許能帶來最初的注意力，但持久的成功是建立在真實價值、顧客信任以及有能力的管理之上的。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"in modern markets","chinese":"在現代市場中"},{"english":"be under constant pressure to","chinese":"持續面對……的壓力"},{"english":"attract attention","chinese":"吸引注意"},{"english":"be treated as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"the decisive ingredient of","chinese":"……的決定性因素"},{"english":"commercial success","chinese":"商業成功"},{"english":"it is therefore unsurprising that","chinese":"因此難怪"},{"english":"marketing and promotion","chinese":"市場推廣和宣傳"},{"english":"the key to","chinese":"……的關鍵"},{"english":"firms prosper","chinese":"企業興旺發展"},{"english":"above all","chinese":"最重要的是"},{"english":"offer genuine value","chinese":"提供真正價值"},{"english":"operate efficiently","chinese":"高效營運"},{"english":"the primary reason","chinese":"主要原因"},{"english":"remain loyal","chinese":"保持忠誠"},{"english":"deliver something worthwhile","chinese":"提供有價值的東西"},{"english":"a persuasive campaign","chinese":"有說服力的宣傳活動"},{"english":"generate initial sales","chinese":"帶來初期銷售"},{"english":"continued success","chinese":"持續成功"},{"english":"come from satisfaction","chinese":"來自滿意度"},{"english":"goods are dependable","chinese":"商品可靠"},{"english":"services are consistently professional","chinese":"服務一貫專業"},{"english":"spend more over time","chinese":"隨時間花費更多"},{"english":"recommend the company to others","chinese":"向其他人推薦公司"},{"english":"repeat custom","chinese":"回頭客生意"},{"english":"organic growth","chinese":"自然增長"},{"english":"far more stable than","chinese":"比……穩定得多"},{"english":"attention purchased through advertising","chinese":"透過廣告買回來的關注"},{"english":"fill its tables","chinese":"坐滿餐桌；客滿"},{"english":"online discounts","chinese":"網上折扣"},{"english":"social-media campaigns","chinese":"社交媒體宣傳活動"},{"english":"mediocre","chinese":"平平無奇；質素一般"},{"english":"inattentive","chinese":"不夠細心；服務不周"},{"english":"in addition","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"develop reputations of their own","chinese":"建立本身的名聲"},{"english":"trust is established","chinese":"信任建立後"},{"english":"word of mouth","chinese":"口碑"},{"english":"a powerful source of demand","chinese":"強大的需求來源"},{"english":"rather than promotion","chinese":"而不是宣傳"},{"english":"the real engine of","chinese":"……的真正推動力"},{"english":"long-term success","chinese":"長遠成功"},{"english":"equally important","chinese":"同樣重要的是"},{"english":"the way a business is managed","chinese":"企業的管理方式"},{"english":"the most visible brand","chinese":"最受注目的品牌"},{"english":"will struggle if","chinese":"如果……便會陷入困難"},{"english":"control costs","chinese":"控制成本"},{"english":"train employees properly","chinese":"適當培訓員工"},{"english":"deliver what it has promised","chinese":"履行承諾"},{"english":"in such cases","chinese":"在這些情況下"},{"english":"accelerate failure","chinese":"加速失敗"},{"english":"the more customers a company attracts","chinese":"公司吸引越多顧客"},{"english":"delayed orders","chinese":"延誤訂單"},{"english":"complaints","chinese":"投訴"},{"english":"refund requests","chinese":"退款要求"},{"english":"damage public confidence","chinese":"損害公眾信心"},{"english":"this pattern is common in","chinese":"這種情況在……很常見"},{"english":"e-commerce","chinese":"電子商務"},{"english":"an aggressively advertised firm","chinese":"大力賣廣告的公司"},{"english":"lose market share","chinese":"失去市場佔有率"},{"english":"deliveries are unreliable","chinese":"送貨不可靠"},{"english":"customer support is ineffective","chinese":"客戶支援成效不彰"},{"english":"sound management","chinese":"穩健管理"},{"english":"enable a company to adapt","chinese":"使公司能夠適應"},{"english":"whether by","chinese":"不論是透過"},{"english":"improving products","chinese":"改善產品"},{"english":"responding to competition","chinese":"回應競爭"},{"english":"investing wisely","chinese":"明智地投資"},{"english":"determine whether","chinese":"決定是否"},{"english":"survive beyond the short term","chinese":"短期過後仍能生存"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"merely amplifies","chinese":"只是放大"},{"english":"underlying strengths or weaknesses","chinese":"潛在優勢或弱點"},{"english":"attract initial attention","chinese":"吸引初期注意"},{"english":"durable success","chinese":"持久成功"},{"english":"be built on","chinese":"建基於"},{"english":"customer trust","chinese":"顧客信任"},{"english":"competent management","chinese":"有能力的管理"}]},"model-essay-10-ielts-task1-maps":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-10-ielts-task1-maps","essayKey":"maps:10","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-10-ielts-task1-maps","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/maps/maps-10","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The two maps compare an island before and after the construction of tourist facilities.","chinese":"這兩張地圖比較了一個島嶼在旅遊設施建設前後的情況。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, the island has been transformed from a largely undeveloped natural area into a compact resort, with accommodation, catering facilities and transport links added mainly in the western and central sections. However, the beach and most palm-tree areas have been retained, while the eastern end remains largely untouched.","chinese":"整體而言，這座島已經由一個基本未開發的自然區域轉變成一個小型度假區，住宿、餐飲設施和交通連接主要集中在西部和中部地區。 然而，海灘和大部分棕櫚樹區域被保留下來，而島的東端基本上仍未受到改動。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Before development, the island contained only natural features. A beach lay on the western shore, and groups of palm trees were scattered across the middle and, more densely, towards the east. There were no buildings, roads, paths or landing facilities, so access to and movement around the island were not formally provided.","chinese":"在開發前，這座島只包含自然特徵。 一片海灘位於西岸，而棕櫚樹群分布在島的中部，並且在東部一帶更加密集。 圖中沒有建築物、道路、小徑或登岸設施，因此島上的進出和內部移動並沒有正式的安排。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Following construction, two clusters of accommodation huts have been built: one close to the beach in the west and another around an open central area. These are linked by footpaths, one of which also runs to the beach, now marked for swimming. A reception building stands near the centre, with a restaurant just to its north. To the south, a pier has been added for boats, and vehicle tracks now connect it with both main service buildings.","chinese":"建設完成後，兩組住宿小屋被建成：一組靠近西部的海灘，另一組則圍繞中部的一片開放區域。 這些住宿小屋由步行小徑連接，其中一條小徑也通向海灘，而海灘現在被標示為游泳區。 一座接待處位於島的中部附近，其北面緊鄰一間餐廳。 在南部，一座供船隻使用的碼頭已被增設，而車道現在把碼頭與兩座主要服務建築連接起來。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the two maps below","chinese":"以下兩幅地圖"},{"english":"before and after","chinese":"……之前和之後"},{"english":"the construction of","chinese":"……的興建"},{"english":"tourist facilities","chinese":"旅遊設施"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"by selecting and reporting","chinese":"透過選取並報告……"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"compare X before and after Y","chinese":"比較 X 在 Y 前後的情況"},{"english":"has been transformed from","chinese":"已由……轉變"},{"english":"a largely undeveloped natural area","chinese":"大致未發展的自然地區"},{"english":"a compact resort","chinese":"小型集中式度假區"},{"english":"accommodation","chinese":"住宿設施"},{"english":"catering facilities","chinese":"餐飲設施"},{"english":"transport links","chinese":"交通連接"},{"english":"have been added mainly in","chinese":"主要增設於……"},{"english":"the western and central sections","chinese":"西部及中央部分"},{"english":"have been retained","chinese":"得以保留"},{"english":"palm-tree areas","chinese":"棕櫚樹區"},{"english":"the eastern end","chinese":"東端"},{"english":"remains largely untouched","chinese":"大致未受影響；大致保持原貌"},{"english":"before development","chinese":"發展前"},{"english":"natural features","chinese":"自然特徵"},{"english":"lay on the western shore","chinese":"位於西岸"},{"english":"the western shore","chinese":"西岸"},{"english":"groups of palm trees","chinese":"一簇簇棕櫚樹"},{"english":"were scattered across","chinese":"散佈於……各處"},{"english":"across the middle","chinese":"橫跨中部"},{"english":"more densely","chinese":"更密集地"},{"english":"towards the east","chinese":"朝東面；在東面一帶"},{"english":"no buildings, roads or paths","chinese":"沒有建築物、道路或小徑"},{"english":"landing facilities","chinese":"登岸設施"},{"english":"access to","chinese":"前往……的通道"},{"english":"movement around","chinese":"在……內四處移動"},{"english":"access to and movement around","chinese":"前往及在……內移動"},{"english":"were not formally provided","chinese":"並無正式提供"},{"english":"following construction","chinese":"建成後"},{"english":"two clusters of","chinese":"兩組；兩簇"},{"english":"accommodation huts","chinese":"住宿小屋"},{"english":"have been built","chinese":"已建成"},{"english":"close to the beach","chinese":"靠近海灘"},{"english":"around an open central area","chinese":"圍繞中央空地"},{"english":"an open central area","chinese":"中央空地"},{"english":"are linked by","chinese":"由……連接"},{"english":"footpaths","chinese":"行人小徑"},{"english":"one of which","chinese":"其中一條"},{"english":"runs to the beach","chinese":"通往海灘"},{"english":"marked for swimming","chinese":"標示為游泳區"},{"english":"a reception building","chinese":"接待處大樓"},{"english":"stands near the centre","chinese":"位於中心附近"},{"english":"a restaurant","chinese":"餐廳"},{"english":"just to its north","chinese":"就在其北面"},{"english":"to the south","chinese":"在南面"},{"english":"a pier","chinese":"碼頭"},{"english":"has been added for","chinese":"已增設作……用途"},{"english":"for boats","chinese":"供船隻使用"},{"english":"vehicle tracks","chinese":"車道；車輛通道"},{"english":"now connect X with Y","chinese":"現時連接 X 和 Y"},{"english":"both main service buildings","chinese":"兩座主要服務建築"},{"english":"service buildings","chinese":"服務建築"},{"english":"the developed area","chinese":"已發展區域"},{"english":"be concentrated in","chinese":"集中於……"},{"english":"remain natural","chinese":"保持自然狀態"},{"english":"new tourist infrastructure","chinese":"新旅遊基建"},{"english":"a small-scale development","chinese":"小規模發展"},{"english":"retain its natural character","chinese":"保留其自然特色"}]},"model-essay-10-ielts-task1-tables":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-10-ielts-task1-tables","essayKey":"tables:10","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-10-ielts-task1-tables","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/tables/table-10","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The table compares the proportions of pupils enrolled in four types of secondary school in 2000, 2005 and 2009.","chinese":"該表格比較了 2000 年、 2005 年和 2009 年四類中學的學生就讀比例。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, attendance shifted markedly away from voluntary-controlled and grammar schools towards community schools. While voluntary-controlled schools had by far the largest share at the beginning, community schools became the dominant type by 2009, and specialist schools remained the smallest or joint-smallest category throughout.","chinese":"整體而言，學生就讀比例明顯由志願控制學校和文法學校轉向社區學校。 雖然志願控制學校在最初佔比遠遠最高，但到 2009 年，社區學校已成為最主要的類別，而專科學校在整段期間一直是最小或並列最小的類別。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In 2000, just over half of pupils attended voluntary-controlled schools, at 52%, making this sector more than twice as large as grammar schools, which accounted for 24%. Specialist and community schools each had 12%, so their combined share was equal to that of grammar schools alone. By 2005, however, voluntary-controlled schools had fallen to 38%, while community schools had climbed sharply to 32%, narrowing the gap between the two leading categories to only six percentage points.","chinese":"在 2000 年，剛過半數學生就讀於志願控制學校，比例為 52% ，使這一類別的佔比超過文法學校的兩倍；文法學校則佔 24% 。 專科學校和社區學校各佔 12% ，因此兩者合計比例正好等同於文法學校單獨的比例。 然而，到 2005 年，志願控制學校已下降至 38% ，而社區學校則大幅上升至 32%，使兩個主要類別之間的差距收窄至僅 6 個百分點。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The change became more pronounced by 2009. Community schools rose further to 58%, almost five times their initial proportion. By contrast, voluntary-controlled schools dropped to 20%, less than half their 2000 figure. Grammar schools also declined steadily, from 24% to 12%, while specialist schools slipped only slightly, from 12% to 10%.","chinese":"到 2009 年，這一變化變得更加明顯。 社區學校進一步上升至 58% ，幾乎是其最初比例的五倍。 相比之下，志願控制學校下降至 20% ，不到其 2000 年數字的一半。 文法學校也持續下降，從 24% 跌至 12% ；而專科學校則只輕微下滑，從 12% 降至。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the table shows","chinese":"表格顯示"},{"english":"the proportions of pupils","chinese":"學生比例"},{"english":"attending four secondary school types","chinese":"就讀四類中學"},{"english":"secondary school types","chinese":"中學類型"},{"english":"between 2000 and 2009","chinese":"在2000年至2009年間"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"selecting and reporting","chinese":"選取並報告"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"the table compares","chinese":"表格比較"},{"english":"enrolled in","chinese":"就讀於"},{"english":"four types of secondary school","chinese":"四類中學"},{"english":"in 2000, 2005 and 2009","chinese":"在2000年、2005年及2009年"},{"english":"Overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"attendance shifted markedly","chinese":"就讀比例明顯轉移"},{"english":"shifted markedly away from","chinese":"明顯從……轉移"},{"english":"towards community schools","chinese":"轉向社區學校"},{"english":"voluntary-controlled schools","chinese":"自願受控學校"},{"english":"grammar schools","chinese":"文法學校"},{"english":"community schools","chinese":"社區學校"},{"english":"specialist schools","chinese":"專科學校"},{"english":"had by far the largest share","chinese":"遠遠佔最大比例"},{"english":"the largest share","chinese":"最大比例"},{"english":"at the beginning","chinese":"在初期"},{"english":"became the dominant type","chinese":"成為主導類型"},{"english":"the dominant type","chinese":"主導類型"},{"english":"by 2009","chinese":"到2009年"},{"english":"remained the smallest category","chinese":"仍然是最小類別"},{"english":"joint-smallest category","chinese":"並列最小類別"},{"english":"throughout","chinese":"在整個時期內"},{"english":"In 2000","chinese":"在2000年"},{"english":"just over half of pupils","chinese":"略多於一半學生"},{"english":"attended voluntary-controlled schools","chinese":"就讀自願受控學校"},{"english":"at 52%","chinese":"為52%"},{"english":"making this sector","chinese":"使這一類別"},{"english":"this sector","chinese":"這一類別"},{"english":"more than twice as large as","chinese":"是……的兩倍多"},{"english":"accounted for 24%","chinese":"佔24%"},{"english":"each had 12%","chinese":"各佔12%"},{"english":"their combined share","chinese":"它們的合計比例"},{"english":"was equal to","chinese":"等於"},{"english":"grammar schools alone","chinese":"單是文法學校"},{"english":"By 2005","chinese":"到2005年"},{"english":"had fallen to","chinese":"已下降至"},{"english":"while","chinese":"而"},{"english":"had climbed sharply to","chinese":"已急升至"},{"english":"climbed sharply","chinese":"急升"},{"english":"narrowing the gap between","chinese":"收窄……之間的差距"},{"english":"the gap between","chinese":"……之間的差距"},{"english":"the two leading categories","chinese":"兩個領先類別"},{"english":"only six percentage points","chinese":"只有六個百分點"},{"english":"percentage points","chinese":"百分點"},{"english":"became more pronounced","chinese":"變得更加明顯"},{"english":"more pronounced","chinese":"更加明顯"},{"english":"rose further to","chinese":"進一步上升至"},{"english":"almost five times","chinese":"幾乎是五倍"},{"english":"their initial proportion","chinese":"其最初比例"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"dropped to 20%","chinese":"下降至20%"},{"english":"less than half","chinese":"不足一半"},{"english":"their 2000 figure","chinese":"它們2000年的數字"},{"english":"declined steadily","chinese":"穩步下降"},{"english":"from 24% to 12%","chinese":"由24%下降至12%"},{"english":"slipped only slightly","chinese":"只輕微下跌"},{"english":"from 12% to 10%","chinese":"由12%跌至10%"}]},"model-essay-11-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-11-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:11","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-11-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q11","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"As classrooms become more digital, a growing number of schools no longer insist that children spend significant time improving their handwriting. This shift may free up lessons for computer-based skills and reduce pressure on pupils whose script is untidy. Nevertheless, I believe the disadvantages far outweigh the advantages, because handwriting still plays a crucial role in both learning and everyday independence.","chinese":"無論在職場還是私人生活中，愈來愈多的溝通如今都是透過數碼科技進行，而非面對面交流。 儘管這種發展可能削弱人際關係的質素，並增加誤解的風險， 我認為整體而言，它的優點更為顯著，因為它大幅提升了溝通效率，並使人們即使相隔遙遠，仍能維持聯繫。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main drawback is education. Writing by hand is a slower and more deliberate process than typing, so children must select key ideas, process language carefully and form each word consciously. This extra mental effort improves concentration, reinforces spelling and helps information stay in long-term memory. For example, a pupil who writes a short summary of a science lesson in a notebook is more likely to remember the key concepts than one who copies full sentences onto a screen with little thought. A second problem is that regular handwriting practice develops fine motor control and written fluency. If schools neglect it, children may become less confident in situations where handwriting is still required, such as handwritten tests, annotating printed texts or completing forms.","chinese":"科技化溝通最主要的優勢在於速度與便利性。 在專業環境中，電子郵件、即時通訊平台及視像會議免除了人們出行的需要，並使決策幾乎可以即時作出。 這不但縮短了回應時間、降低了營運成本，亦令企業能夠相當輕鬆地協調分布於不同城市，甚至不同大洲的團隊。 例如，一位經理可以透過一次網上會議便與海外同事解決生產問題，而不必等待數天後才進行面對面討論。 同樣的原理也適用於社交層面：居於不同地方的父母、子女及朋友，仍可透過通話和訊息每天保持聯絡。 因此，人際關係更容易維繫，也較不容易隨時間而逐漸疏遠。 例如，即使一家人的成員分散在不同國家，他們仍可透過視像通話分享日常近況，並彼此提供情感支持。 因此，數碼溝通在工作與個人生活兩方面都大大提升了效率與可及性。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Admittedly, there are some benefits to reducing the emphasis on handwriting. First, schools can devote more time to typing, online research and digital communication, which are undeniably useful in higher education and many modern jobs. For instance, teaching children how to use collaborative software may prepare them more directly for office-based work. Second, weaker writers may feel less frustrated if neat penmanship is no longer treated as a sign of intelligence. However, these advantages are relatively limited. Digital literacy can be taught alongside handwriting rather than instead of it, and pupils with poor handwriting can be supported through targeted help without lowering expectations for everyone.","chinese":"然而，數碼溝通亦存在重要缺點，其中最嚴重的一點，是它缺乏情感層次。 面對面交流能傳遞語氣、面部表情及肢體語言，而這些元素有助人們更準確地理解意思、表達同理心，並建立信任。 當這些線索消失後，訊息便更容易被誤解，從而引發困惑，甚至衝突。 例如，一封簡短的電郵或文字訊息，即使本無冒犯之意，也可能給人冷淡甚至帶有敵意的感覺。 這在職場中尤其成問題，因為信任與細膩的理解對領導、協商及團隊合作都至關重要。 長遠而言，過度依賴螢幕亦可能助長表面的社交習慣，令人在網上看似時刻保持聯繫，卻依然感到孤立。 例如，一個人即使經常透過社交媒體與他人交談，仍可能感到孤單，因為數碼接觸始終無法完全取代真實的關注與人的陪伴。 因此，儘管科技讓溝通變得更容易，它同時亦可能削弱清晰度、信任感與情感深度。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, although this trend may appear practical in a technological age, its disadvantages are clearly more significant. Schools should modernise their curricula without treating handwriting as an obsolete skill, since it remains essential for deeper learning, functional competence and children’s overall development.","chinese":"總括而言，透過科技進行溝通在效率與可及性方面具有明顯優勢，儘管它可能削弱人際互動的深度與清晰度。 整體而言，我認為其優點大於缺點，因為數碼工具使工作與個人生活中的溝通都能跨越時間與距離而有效運作。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"classrooms become more digital","chinese":"課室變得更加數碼化"},{"english":"a growing number of","chinese":"越來越多的"},{"english":"no longer insist that","chinese":"不再堅持"},{"english":"spend significant time","chinese":"花大量時間"},{"english":"improving their handwriting","chinese":"改善書寫"},{"english":"this shift","chinese":"這種轉變"},{"english":"free up lessons for","chinese":"騰出課堂時間給……"},{"english":"computer-based skills","chinese":"電腦相關技能"},{"english":"reduce pressure on","chinese":"減輕……的壓力"},{"english":"pupils whose script is untidy","chinese":"字跡潦草的學生"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"far outweigh the advantages","chinese":"遠遠超過好處"},{"english":"plays a crucial role in","chinese":"在……中發揮關鍵作用"},{"english":"everyday independence","chinese":"日常生活上的獨立能力"},{"english":"the main drawback","chinese":"主要缺點"},{"english":"writing by hand","chinese":"用手書寫"},{"english":"a slower and more deliberate process","chinese":"較慢而更需要思考的過程"},{"english":"select key ideas","chinese":"篩選重點概念"},{"english":"process language carefully","chinese":"仔細處理語言"},{"english":"form each word consciously","chinese":"有意識地寫出每個字"},{"english":"extra mental effort","chinese":"額外的腦力付出"},{"english":"improves concentration","chinese":"提升專注力"},{"english":"reinforces spelling","chinese":"鞏固串字能力"},{"english":"stay in long-term memory","chinese":"留在長期記憶中"},{"english":"a short summary of","chinese":"……的簡短摘要"},{"english":"key concepts","chinese":"核心概念"},{"english":"copies full sentences onto a screen","chinese":"將完整句子複製到螢幕上"},{"english":"with little thought","chinese":"幾乎沒有思考"},{"english":"regular handwriting practice","chinese":"定期手寫練習"},{"english":"develops fine motor control","chinese":"發展精細動作控制能力"},{"english":"written fluency","chinese":"書寫流暢度"},{"english":"neglect it","chinese":"忽視它"},{"english":"less confident in situations where","chinese":"在……情況下較缺乏信心"},{"english":"handwriting is still required","chinese":"仍然需要手寫"},{"english":"handwritten tests","chinese":"手寫測驗"},{"english":"annotating printed texts","chinese":"在印刷文本上作註解"},{"english":"completing forms","chinese":"填寫表格"},{"english":"admittedly","chinese":"誠然"},{"english":"reducing the emphasis on","chinese":"減少對……的重視"},{"english":"devote more time to","chinese":"投放更多時間於……"},{"english":"typing","chinese":"打字"},{"english":"online research","chinese":"網上資料搜集"},{"english":"digital communication","chinese":"數碼溝通"},{"english":"undeniably useful in","chinese":"在……中無可否認地有用"},{"english":"higher education","chinese":"高等教育"},{"english":"modern jobs","chinese":"現代工作"},{"english":"collaborative software","chinese":"協作軟件"},{"english":"prepare them more directly for","chinese":"令他們更直接為……作準備"},{"english":"office-based work","chinese":"辦公室工作"},{"english":"weaker writers","chinese":"書寫能力較弱的學生"},{"english":"feel less frustrated","chinese":"感到較少挫敗"},{"english":"neat penmanship","chinese":"工整字體"},{"english":"be treated as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"a sign of intelligence","chinese":"智力的標誌"},{"english":"relatively limited","chinese":"相對有限"},{"english":"digital literacy","chinese":"數碼素養"},{"english":"alongside handwriting rather than instead of it","chinese":"與手寫並行，而不是取代手寫"},{"english":"targeted help","chinese":"針對性幫助"},{"english":"without lowering expectations for everyone","chinese":"不降低對所有人的期望"},{"english":"appear practical in a technological age","chinese":"在科技時代看似實際"},{"english":"clearly more significant","chinese":"明顯更重要"},{"english":"modernise their curricula","chinese":"更新課程"},{"english":"obsolete skill","chinese":"過時技能"},{"english":"remains essential for","chinese":"對……仍然必要"},{"english":"deeper learning","chinese":"更深入的學習"},{"english":"functional competence","chinese":"實用能力"},{"english":"overall development","chinese":"全面發展"}]},"model-essay-11-ielts-cause-solution":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-11-ielts-cause-solution","essayKey":"cause-solution:11","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-11-ielts-cause-solution","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/problem-and-cause/EdmundBd9CnS-Q11","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many parts of the world, rural-to-urban migration has become increasingly common. This movement is mainly driven by the belief that cities offer better life chances than villages or small towns. However, it can place serious pressure on urban systems and leave rural communities increasingly fragile.","chinese":"在世界許多地方，從農村遷往城市的現象已變得越來越普遍。 這種流動主要是由一種信念所推動：城市比村莊或小城鎮能提供更好的人生機會。 然而，這可能會對城市系統造成嚴重壓力，並使農村社區變得越來越脆弱。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One major reason for this trend is economic opportunity. In many rural areas, work is still closely connected to farming, local trade, or small family businesses, all of which may provide unstable income. By contrast, cities usually offer a wider range of jobs in factories, offices, retail, hospitality, and technology. A young person who moves to a city, for example, may start with an entry-level position but still see a path towards promotion, training, and higher earnings. This sense of upward mobility makes urban life extremely attractive.","chinese":"造成這一趨勢的一個主要原因是經濟機會。 在許多農村地區，工作仍然與農業、本地貿易或小型家庭生意密切相關，而這些工作都可能帶來不穩定的收入。 相比之下，城市通常在工廠、辦公室、零售、酒店服務業和科技行業中提供更廣泛的工作選擇。 例如，一個搬到城市的年輕人可能一開始只是從事入門級職位，但仍然能看到晉升、培訓和獲得更高收入的路徑。 這種向上流動的感覺使城市生活極具吸引力。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important reason is access to essential services. Cities tend to have better schools, universities, hospitals, transport networks, and digital infrastructure. For families, this can be decisive because education and healthcare are not luxuries; they are the foundations of long-term security. If a rural parent believes that a city school will give their child stronger qualifications and wider social exposure, relocation may seem not only sensible but necessary.","chinese":"另一個重要原因是能夠獲得基本服務。 城市往往擁有更好的學校、大學、醫院、交通網絡和數位基礎設施。 對家庭而言，這可能是決定性的因素，因為教育和醫療並不是奢侈品；它們是長遠保障的基礎。 如果一位農村家長相信城市學校能給孩子更強的資歷和更廣闊的社會接觸，那麼搬遷可能看起來不只是明智的選擇，而是必要的選擇。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 3","english":"This movement, however, can cause several problems. The most immediate one is urban overcrowding. When population growth is faster than planning, housing becomes expensive, roads become congested, and public services are stretched thin. As a result, some migrants may end up living in poor-quality accommodation while competing for limited jobs. At the same time, rural areas may decline. As younger and more capable residents leave, villages can lose workers, customers, and future community leaders. Schools may close, local businesses may struggle, and elderly residents may become increasingly isolated.","chinese":"然而，這種人口流動可能造成幾個問題。 最直接的一個問題是城市過度擁擠。 當人口增長快於城市規劃時，住房會變得昂貴，道路會變得擁堵，而公共服務也會被拉得非常緊張。 結果是，一些移民最終可能住在質素較差的住所，同時還要競爭有限的工作機會。 與此同時，農村地區可能會衰落。 隨著較年輕和較有能力的居民離開，村莊可能會失去工人、顧客，以及未來的社區領袖。 學校可能會關閉，本地商業可能會陷入困境，而年長居民也可能變得越來越孤立。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, people move to cities mainly for better employment prospects and access to services. Nevertheless, this trend can overload urban areas and weaken the social and economic life of the countryside.","chinese":"總結來說，人們搬到城市主要是為了更好的就業前景和獲得服務的機會。 然而，這一趨勢可能會使城市地區負荷過重，並削弱農村的社會和經濟生活。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"rural-to-urban migration","chinese":"由農村遷往城市"},{"english":"become increasingly common","chinese":"變得越來越普遍"},{"english":"this movement","chinese":"這種人口流動"},{"english":"be mainly driven by","chinese":"主要由……推動"},{"english":"life chances","chinese":"人生機會"},{"english":"villages or small towns","chinese":"村落或小城鎮"},{"english":"place serious pressure on","chinese":"對……造成嚴重壓力"},{"english":"urban systems","chinese":"城市系統"},{"english":"rural communities","chinese":"農村社區"},{"english":"increasingly fragile","chinese":"越來越脆弱"},{"english":"one major reason for","chinese":"……的一個主要原因"},{"english":"this trend","chinese":"這個趨勢"},{"english":"economic opportunity","chinese":"經濟機會"},{"english":"closely connected to","chinese":"與……密切相關"},{"english":"farming","chinese":"農耕"},{"english":"local trade","chinese":"本地商貿"},{"english":"small family businesses","chinese":"小型家族生意"},{"english":"unstable income","chinese":"不穩定收入"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"a wider range of","chinese":"更廣泛的"},{"english":"retail","chinese":"零售業"},{"english":"hospitality","chinese":"酒店及餐飲服務業"},{"english":"entry-level position","chinese":"入門級職位"},{"english":"a path towards","chinese":"通往……的路徑"},{"english":"promotion","chinese":"晉升"},{"english":"higher earnings","chinese":"更高收入"},{"english":"upward mobility","chinese":"向上流動"},{"english":"urban life","chinese":"城市生活"},{"english":"extremely attractive","chinese":"極具吸引力"},{"english":"access to essential services","chinese":"獲得基本服務的機會"},{"english":"tend to have","chinese":"往往有"},{"english":"transport networks","chinese":"交通網絡"},{"english":"digital infrastructure","chinese":"數碼基礎設施"},{"english":"this can be decisive","chinese":"這可以成為決定性因素"},{"english":"not luxuries","chinese":"不是奢侈品"},{"english":"the foundations of","chinese":"……的基礎"},{"english":"long-term security","chinese":"長遠保障"},{"english":"stronger qualifications","chinese":"更有競爭力的學歷"},{"english":"wider social exposure","chinese":"更廣闊的社會接觸"},{"english":"relocation","chinese":"遷居"},{"english":"not only sensible but necessary","chinese":"不但合理，而且必要"},{"english":"cause several problems","chinese":"造成幾個問題"},{"english":"the most immediate one","chinese":"最即時的一個"},{"english":"urban overcrowding","chinese":"城市過度擠迫"},{"english":"population growth","chinese":"人口增長"},{"english":"faster than planning","chinese":"比規劃更快"},{"english":"housing becomes expensive","chinese":"住房變得昂貴"},{"english":"roads become congested","chinese":"道路變得擠塞"},{"english":"public services are stretched thin","chinese":"公共服務不勝負荷"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"end up living in","chinese":"最終住在"},{"english":"poor-quality accommodation","chinese":"低質素住所"},{"english":"competing for limited jobs","chinese":"競爭有限的工作機會"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"與此同時"},{"english":"rural areas may decline","chinese":"農村地區可能衰落"},{"english":"younger and more capable residents","chinese":"較年輕和較有能力的居民"},{"english":"future community leaders","chinese":"未來的社區領袖"},{"english":"local businesses may struggle","chinese":"本地生意可能經營困難"},{"english":"elderly residents","chinese":"年長居民"},{"english":"increasingly isolated","chinese":"越來越孤立"},{"english":"employment prospects","chinese":"就業前景"},{"english":"access to services","chinese":"獲得服務的機會"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"overload urban areas","chinese":"令城市地區不勝負荷"},{"english":"weaken the social and economic life of","chinese":"削弱……的社會和經濟生活"},{"english":"the countryside","chinese":"農村地區"}]},"model-essay-11-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-11-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:11","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-11-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q11","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many families, academic achievement is treated not merely as a personal goal for children, but as a measure of future security. This is why some parents place excessive pressure on their children to perform well at school. In my view, parents should be supportive guides in education: they should create discipline and confidence without turning learning into a source of fear.","chinese":"在許多家庭中，學業成就不僅被視為孩子的個人目標，也被看作未來保障的一種衡量標準。這就是為甚麼一些父母會給孩子施加過度壓力，要求他們在學校表現優異。 在我看來，父母在教育中應該成為支持性的引導者：他們應該建立紀律和信心，而不是把學習變成恐懼的來源。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One reason parents become over-demanding is that they see education as the safest route to social mobility. In competitive societies, a strong academic record is often linked to better universities, higher-status jobs, and a more stable life. As a result, some parents believe that every grade and ranking may affect their child’s future. This fear can easily become pressure, especially when parents compare their children with classmates or relatives. Another reason is that some adults project their own ambitions or regrets onto their children. If they once missed educational opportunities themselves, they may push their sons or daughters too hard, hoping to rewrite their own story through the next generation.","chinese":"父母變得要求過高的一個原因是，他們把教育視為實現社會流動最安全的途徑。 在競爭激烈的社會中，優秀的學業成績往往與更好的大學、更高地位的工作，以及更穩定的生活相連。 因此，一些父母相信，每一個分數和排名都可能影響孩子的未來。 這種恐懼很容易變成壓力，尤其當父母把自己的孩子與同學或親戚作比較時。 另一個原因是，一些成年人會把自己的抱負或遺憾投射到孩子身上。 如果他們自己曾經錯過教育機會，他們可能會過分催迫自己的子女，希望透過下一代改寫自己的人生故事。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, the proper role of a parent is not to act as a second examiner at home. Parents should provide a calm structure: regular study habits, a suitable learning environment, and reasonable expectations. They should also notice when a child is genuinely struggling and respond with patience rather than blame. For example, if a child performs poorly in mathematics, a helpful parent would try to understand whether the problem is weak foundations, anxiety, or poor study methods, instead of simply demanding higher marks. Most importantly, parents should protect their child’s long-term attitude towards learning. Encouragement, honest feedback, and emotional security can help children become resilient and self-motivated, whereas constant pressure may make them associate education with shame and exhaustion.","chinese":"然而，父母的恰當角色並不是在家中扮演第二個考官。 父母應該提供一種平穩的結構：規律的學習習慣、合適的學習環境，以及合理的期望。 他們也應該留意孩子真正感到吃力的時候，並以耐心而不是責備作出回應。 例如，如果一個孩子數學表現不佳，一位有幫助的父母會嘗試了解問題是否來自基礎薄弱、焦慮，或學習方法不當，而不是單純要求更高分數。 最重要的是，父母應該保護孩子對學習的長遠態度。 鼓勵、誠實的回饋和情感上的安全感，可以幫助孩子變得有韌性並具備自我動力；相反，持續的壓力可能令他們把教育與羞愧和疲憊聯繫起來。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, excessive parental pressure often comes from fear, competition, and personal ambition. A parent’s true responsibility is to support learning firmly but kindly, so that education becomes a path to growth rather than a burden to survive.","chinese":"總結來說，過度的父母壓力往往來自恐懼、競爭，以及個人抱負。 父母真正的責任，是堅定但溫和地支持學習，使教育成為一條通向成長的道路，而不是一個需要硬撐過去的負擔。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"academic achievement","chinese":"學業成就"},{"english":"be treated not merely as","chinese":"不只是被視為"},{"english":"a personal goal","chinese":"個人目標"},{"english":"a measure of future security","chinese":"未來保障的衡量標準"},{"english":"place excessive pressure on","chinese":"對……施加過大壓力"},{"english":"perform well at school","chinese":"在學校表現良好"},{"english":"supportive guides in education","chinese":"教育上的支持者和引導者"},{"english":"create discipline and confidence","chinese":"培養自律和信心"},{"english":"turn learning into","chinese":"將學習變成……"},{"english":"a source of fear","chinese":"恐懼的來源"},{"english":"become over-demanding","chinese":"變得要求過高"},{"english":"the safest route to","chinese":"通往……最安全的途徑"},{"english":"social mobility","chinese":"社會流動"},{"english":"competitive societies","chinese":"競爭激烈的社會"},{"english":"a strong academic record","chinese":"優秀的學業成績"},{"english":"be linked to","chinese":"與……有關"},{"english":"higher-status jobs","chinese":"社會地位較高的工作"},{"english":"a more stable life","chinese":"更穩定的生活"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"every grade and ranking","chinese":"每個分數和排名"},{"english":"affect their child's future","chinese":"影響孩子的將來"},{"english":"compare their children with","chinese":"將自己的孩子與……比較"},{"english":"classmates or relatives","chinese":"同學或親戚"},{"english":"project their own ambitions onto","chinese":"將自己的抱負投射到……身上"},{"english":"project their regrets onto","chinese":"將自己的遺憾投射到……身上"},{"english":"missed educational opportunities","chinese":"錯過教育機會"},{"english":"push their children too hard","chinese":"對孩子逼得太緊"},{"english":"rewrite their own story","chinese":"改寫自己的人生故事"},{"english":"the next generation","chinese":"下一代"},{"english":"the proper role of","chinese":"……的恰當角色"},{"english":"act as a second examiner","chinese":"扮演第二個考官"},{"english":"provide a calm structure","chinese":"提供平和而有條理的安排"},{"english":"regular study habits","chinese":"定期學習習慣"},{"english":"a suitable learning environment","chinese":"合適的學習環境"},{"english":"reasonable expectations","chinese":"合理期望"},{"english":"genuinely struggling","chinese":"真的遇到困難"},{"english":"respond with patience rather than blame","chinese":"以耐性而非責備回應"},{"english":"performs poorly in","chinese":"在……表現欠佳"},{"english":"weak foundations","chinese":"基礎薄弱"},{"english":"poor study methods","chinese":"不良學習方法"},{"english":"demanding higher marks","chinese":"要求更高分數"},{"english":"long-term attitude towards learning","chinese":"對學習的長遠態度"},{"english":"honest feedback","chinese":"坦誠回饋"},{"english":"emotional security","chinese":"情感安全感"},{"english":"become resilient and self-motivated","chinese":"變得有抗逆力和自我推動"},{"english":"constant pressure","chinese":"持續不斷的壓力"},{"english":"associate education with","chinese":"將教育與……聯繫起來"},{"english":"shame and exhaustion","chinese":"羞愧和疲憊"},{"english":"excessive parental pressure","chinese":"過度的父母壓力"},{"english":"personal ambition","chinese":"個人抱負"},{"english":"true responsibility","chinese":"真正責任"},{"english":"support learning firmly but kindly","chinese":"堅定而仁慈地支持學習"},{"english":"a path to growth","chinese":"成長之路"},{"english":"a burden to survive","chinese":"必須捱過的負擔"}]},"model-essay-11-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-11-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:11","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-11-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q11","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Crime prevention is a central part of any safe and civilised society. While some people argue that individuals should take responsibility for their own safety, others believe that preventing crime is mainly the duty of the state. In my opinion, although citizens should act sensibly, the government must carry the primary responsibility because only it has the authority and resources to reduce crime on a large scale.","chinese":"預防犯罪是任何安全而文明的社會中的核心部分。 雖然有人認為個人應該為自身安全負責，但另一些人則相信預防犯罪主要是國家的責任 我認為，儘管市民應該理智地行事，但政府必須承擔主要責任，因為只有政府才擁有大規模減少犯罪所需的權力和資源。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Those who support individual responsibility argue that people can lower their own risk by making careful choices. For example, homeowners can install security cameras, avoid leaving valuables in visible places, and be cautious when sharing personal information online. These habits are useful because many crimes are opportunistic; if a person makes themselves an easy target, criminals may be more likely to take advantage of them. From this perspective, personal awareness acts as the first line of defence, especially in daily situations where the police cannot be physically present.","chinese":"支持個人責任的人認為，人們可以透過作出謹慎的選擇來降低自身風險。 例如，屋主可以安裝保安攝像頭，避免把貴重物品放在顯眼的位置，並在網上分享個人資料時保持謹慎。 這些習慣是有用的，因為許多犯罪都是機會主義式的；如果一個人使自己成為容易下手的目標，罪犯便可能更容易利用他們。 從這個角度來看，個人警覺性就是第一道防線，尤其是警察無法親身在場的日常情況中"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, I believe that crime prevention cannot depend mainly on individuals. The government is responsible for creating and maintaining the systems that make society safe, such as effective policing, fair laws, street lighting, public education, and social support. If a neighbourhood has poor law enforcement, weak surveillance, and few opportunities for young people, individuals can only protect themselves to a limited extent. A family may lock its doors every night, but it cannot control organised crime, unsafe public spaces, or wider social problems that push people towards illegal behaviour. These issues require coordinated public action, not just private caution.","chinese":"然而，我認為預防犯罪不能主要依賴個人。 政府有責任建立並維持使社會安全的系統，例如有效的警務、公平的法律、街道照明、公共教育和社會支援。 如果一個社區執法不足、監察薄弱，而且年輕人的機會很少，個人就只能在有限程度上保護自己。 一個家庭或許可以每晚鎖好門，但它無法控制有組織犯罪、不安全的公共空間，或那些把人推向違法行為的更廣泛社會問題。 這些問題需要有組織的公共行動，而不只是個人的小心謹慎。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, individuals should certainly take reasonable steps to protect themselves, but this cannot replace the role of government. Since crime is a social problem rather than merely a personal inconvenience, the state should be chiefly responsible for preventing it.","chinese":"總結來說，個人當然應該採取合理措施保護自己，但這不能取代政府的角色。 由於犯罪是一個社會問題，而不僅僅是個人的不便，因此國家應該主要負責預防犯罪。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"crime prevention","chinese":"預防罪案"},{"english":"a central part of","chinese":"……的核心部分"},{"english":"safe and civilised society","chinese":"安全而文明的社會"},{"english":"take responsibility for","chinese":"為……承擔責任"},{"english":"their own safety","chinese":"自身安全"},{"english":"preventing crime","chinese":"預防犯罪"},{"english":"the duty of the state","chinese":"國家的責任"},{"english":"in my opinion","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"act sensibly","chinese":"行事謹慎；明智行事"},{"english":"carry the primary responsibility","chinese":"承擔首要責任"},{"english":"authority and resources","chinese":"權力和資源"},{"english":"reduce crime on a large scale","chinese":"大規模減少罪案"},{"english":"individual responsibility","chinese":"個人責任"},{"english":"lower their own risk","chinese":"降低自身風險"},{"english":"making careful choices","chinese":"作出謹慎選擇"},{"english":"install security cameras","chinese":"安裝保安攝錄機"},{"english":"avoid leaving valuables in visible places","chinese":"避免將貴重物品放在顯眼地方"},{"english":"valuables","chinese":"貴重物品"},{"english":"be cautious when","chinese":"在……時保持謹慎"},{"english":"sharing personal information online","chinese":"在網上分享個人資料"},{"english":"many crimes are opportunistic","chinese":"很多罪案是伺機而作的"},{"english":"make themselves an easy target","chinese":"令自己成為容易下手的目標"},{"english":"be more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"take advantage of","chinese":"利用；乘機傷害"},{"english":"from this perspective","chinese":"從這個角度來看"},{"english":"personal awareness","chinese":"個人警覺性"},{"english":"act as the first line of defence","chinese":"作為第一道防線"},{"english":"daily situations","chinese":"日常情況"},{"english":"physically present","chinese":"親身在場"},{"english":"cannot depend mainly on","chinese":"不能主要依賴"},{"english":"be responsible for creating and maintaining","chinese":"負責建立和維持"},{"english":"make society safe","chinese":"令社會安全"},{"english":"effective policing","chinese":"有效警務"},{"english":"fair laws","chinese":"公平法律"},{"english":"street lighting","chinese":"街燈照明"},{"english":"public education","chinese":"公眾教育"},{"english":"social support","chinese":"社會支援"},{"english":"a neighbourhood","chinese":"社區；街區"},{"english":"poor law enforcement","chinese":"執法不力"},{"english":"weak surveillance","chinese":"監察薄弱"},{"english":"few opportunities for young people","chinese":"年輕人機會不足"},{"english":"to a limited extent","chinese":"在有限程度上"},{"english":"lock its doors","chinese":"鎖門"},{"english":"organised crime","chinese":"有組織犯罪"},{"english":"unsafe public spaces","chinese":"不安全的公共空間"},{"english":"wider social problems","chinese":"更廣泛的社會問題"},{"english":"push people towards illegal behaviour","chinese":"推使人走向非法行為"},{"english":"illegal behaviour","chinese":"非法行為"},{"english":"coordinated public action","chinese":"協調一致的公共行動"},{"english":"private caution","chinese":"個人謹慎"},{"english":"take reasonable steps to","chinese":"採取合理措施去"},{"english":"protect themselves","chinese":"保護自己"},{"english":"replace the role of government","chinese":"取代政府的角色"},{"english":"a social problem rather than","chinese":"是社會問題，而不是"},{"english":"merely a personal inconvenience","chinese":"只屬個人不便"},{"english":"the state","chinese":"國家；政府"},{"english":"chiefly responsible for","chinese":"對……負主要責任"}]},"model-essay-11-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-11-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:11","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-11-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q11","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Employment decisions should be based on competence and business need rather than assumptions about an applicant’s private life. Some people nevertheless argue that small businesses should avoid hiring young women who have not yet started families so that maternity leave will not become a future expense. This essay will argue that this view is entirely wrong because it replaces merit with discrimination and because it is financially short-sighted.","chinese":"聘用決策應該根據能力與業務需要，而不是建立在對求職者私人生活的假設之上。 然而，有些人仍然主張，小企業應避免聘用尚未開始組織家庭的年輕女性，以免未來需要承擔產假的成本。 本文將論證，這種看法完全錯誤，因為它以歧視取代了能力與才幹的評估，而且在財務上也十分目光短淺。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason I completely disagree is that recruitment based on possible motherhood is unfair and prevents businesses from selecting the strongest candidates. Once an employer excludes qualified women for a factor unrelated to job performance, the talent pool immediately becomes smaller, which makes poor hiring decisions more likely. A small design firm, for example, might reject an excellent applicant and appoint a less capable worker instead, leading to weaker ideas, lower client satisfaction and reduced revenue. This policy can also damage the workplace more broadly. When employees realise that hiring is shaped by prejudice rather than ability, confidence in management declines and morale suffers. In a small business, where every member of staff has a visible impact, this loss of trust can quickly undermine teamwork and productivity.","chinese":"我第一個完全不同意的理由是：根據女性未來可能成為母親來作招聘判斷，不但不公平，也會妨礙企業選出最優秀的人才。 一旦僱主因為與工作表現無關的因素而排除合資格女性，可供挑選的人才庫便會立刻縮小，也使錯誤的聘用決定更容易出現。 例如，一家小型設計公司可能拒絕一位非常優秀的申請者，反而聘用能力較弱的人，結果導致創意較差、客戶滿意度下降，以及收入減少。 這種政策也會對整體工作環境造成更廣泛的損害。 當員工意識到聘用決定是由偏見而不是能力所主導時，他們對管理層的信心便會下降，士氣也會受到打擊。 在小型企業裡，每一位員工的影響都清晰可見，因此這種信任的流失很快便會削弱團隊合作與工作效率。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The second reason is that the financial logic behind this argument is deeply flawed. Maternity leave is a temporary and predictable cost, whereas bad recruitment and repeated staff turnover create much more serious long-term expense. If a company hires from a restricted group, it is more likely to spend money retraining unsuitable employees, correcting mistakes and replacing people who do not perform well. By contrast, fair and supportive employment practices often improve retention. Workers who feel respected are more likely to remain with the company and repay that support with loyalty and conscientious work. For instance, a small retailer that arranges temporary cover during parental leave may face a short-term cost, but it is far more likely to keep an experienced employee for years.","chinese":"第二個理由是，這種主張背後的財務邏輯本身就有很大的缺陷。 產假是一種暫時而且可預見的成本；相反地，錯誤的招聘以及反覆的人員流動，卻會造成更嚴重的長期開支。 如果公司只從受限制的群體中招聘，就更有可能把金錢花在重新培訓不合適的員工、修正錯誤，以及替換表現不佳的人身上。 相比之下，公平而具支持性的聘用做法往往能提高員工留任率。 感到被尊重的員工更有可能留在公司，並以忠誠和盡責的工作回報這份支持。 例如，一家在育兒假期間安排臨時替補的小型零售商，也許要承擔短期成本，但卻更有可能把一名經驗豐富的員工留住多年。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely disagree that small businesses should avoid hiring young women in order to avoid maternity leave. This approach is unjust, wastes talent and rests on a false understanding of cost, so recruitment should always be based on merit rather than anticipated family choices.","chinese":"總而言之，我完全不同意小企業為了避免產假成本而不聘用年輕女性。 這種做法既不公正，也浪費人才，並且建立在對成本的錯誤理解之上，因此招聘應永遠以能力為依據，而不是以對未來家庭選擇的預測作判斷。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"employment decisions","chinese":"招聘決定；僱傭決定"},{"english":"be based on","chinese":"建基於"},{"english":"competence and business need","chinese":"能力和業務需要"},{"english":"rather than assumptions about","chinese":"而不是基於對……的假設"},{"english":"an applicant's private life","chinese":"申請人的私人生活"},{"english":"nevertheless argue that","chinese":"然而仍然認為"},{"english":"small businesses","chinese":"小型企業"},{"english":"avoid hiring","chinese":"避免聘請"},{"english":"have not yet started families","chinese":"尚未成家的"},{"english":"maternity leave","chinese":"產假"},{"english":"become a future expense","chinese":"成為日後開支"},{"english":"this view is entirely wrong","chinese":"這個觀點完全錯誤"},{"english":"replace merit with discrimination","chinese":"以歧視取代才幹"},{"english":"financially short-sighted","chinese":"財政上短視"},{"english":"recruitment based on","chinese":"基於……的招聘"},{"english":"possible motherhood","chinese":"可能成為母親"},{"english":"prevent businesses from","chinese":"阻止企業去"},{"english":"selecting the strongest candidates","chinese":"選出最強的候選人"},{"english":"once an employer excludes","chinese":"一旦僱主排除"},{"english":"qualified women","chinese":"合資格女性"},{"english":"a factor unrelated to","chinese":"與……無關的因素"},{"english":"job performance","chinese":"工作表現"},{"english":"the talent pool","chinese":"人才庫"},{"english":"become smaller","chinese":"變得更小"},{"english":"poor hiring decisions","chinese":"差劣的招聘決定"},{"english":"be more likely","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"a small design firm","chinese":"小型設計公司"},{"english":"reject an excellent applicant","chinese":"拒絕一位出色的申請人"},{"english":"appoint a less capable worker instead","chinese":"轉而任命能力較低的員工"},{"english":"leading to","chinese":"導致"},{"english":"weaker ideas","chinese":"較弱的想法；較差的創意"},{"english":"lower client satisfaction","chinese":"較低的客戶滿意度"},{"english":"reduced revenue","chinese":"收入減少"},{"english":"damage the workplace more broadly","chinese":"更廣泛地損害工作環境"},{"english":"realise that","chinese":"意識到"},{"english":"be shaped by prejudice","chinese":"受偏見影響"},{"english":"rather than ability","chinese":"而不是能力"},{"english":"confidence in management declines","chinese":"對管理層的信心下降"},{"english":"morale suffers","chinese":"士氣受損"},{"english":"every member of staff","chinese":"每位員工"},{"english":"have a visible impact","chinese":"有明顯影響"},{"english":"loss of trust","chinese":"信任流失"},{"english":"quickly undermine","chinese":"迅速削弱"},{"english":"teamwork and productivity","chinese":"團隊合作和生產力"},{"english":"the financial logic behind","chinese":"……背後的財務邏輯"},{"english":"deeply flawed","chinese":"有嚴重缺陷"},{"english":"a temporary and predictable cost","chinese":"暫時而可預計的成本"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"bad recruitment","chinese":"差劣招聘"},{"english":"repeated staff turnover","chinese":"反覆的員工流失"},{"english":"create much more serious long-term expense","chinese":"造成嚴重得多的長期開支"},{"english":"hire from a restricted group","chinese":"從受限制的群體中招聘"},{"english":"retraining unsuitable employees","chinese":"重新培訓不合適員工"},{"english":"correcting mistakes","chinese":"糾正錯誤"},{"english":"replacing people who do not perform well","chinese":"替換表現不佳的人"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相反"},{"english":"fair and supportive employment practices","chinese":"公平而有支援的僱傭做法"},{"english":"improve retention","chinese":"提高留任率"},{"english":"feel respected","chinese":"感到受尊重"},{"english":"remain with the company","chinese":"留在公司"},{"english":"repay that support with","chinese":"以……回報那份支持"},{"english":"loyalty and conscientious work","chinese":"忠誠和盡責工作"},{"english":"arrange temporary cover","chinese":"安排臨時人手"},{"english":"parental leave","chinese":"育兒假"},{"english":"face a short-term cost","chinese":"面對短期成本"},{"english":"keep an experienced employee","chinese":"留住有經驗員工"},{"english":"in order to avoid","chinese":"為了避免"},{"english":"this approach is unjust","chinese":"這種做法不公義"},{"english":"waste talent","chinese":"浪費人才"},{"english":"rest on","chinese":"建基於"},{"english":"a false understanding of cost","chinese":"對成本的錯誤理解"},{"english":"based on merit","chinese":"基於才幹"},{"english":"anticipated family choices","chinese":"預期的家庭選擇"}]},"model-essay-11-ielts-task1-tables":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-11-ielts-task1-tables","essayKey":"tables:11","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-11-ielts-task1-tables","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-1/tables/table-11","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The table compares the cost of meeting the minimum daily water requirement per person in five countries, expressed both in US cents and as a share of the average daily wage.","chinese":"該表比較了五個國家中，每人每日達到最低用水需求所需的成本，並同時以美仙及平均日薪比例呈現。"},{"label":"Overview","english":"Overall, Tanzania records the highest cost and the greatest wage burden, while the US has the lowest figures on both measures. More broadly, Tanzania, Uganda and Pakistan spend far larger proportions of daily earnings on this basic requirement than the UK and the US, even though the cash differences are only a few cents.","chinese":"整體而言，坦桑尼亞的用水成本最高，對工資造成的負擔也最大；而美國在兩項指標上都是最低。 更廣泛而言，坦桑尼亞、烏干達和巴基斯坦在這項基本需求上所花費的日薪比例，遠高於英國和美國，即使它們在實際金額上的差距只有數美仙。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"In monetary terms, Tanzania leads the table, at 6.4 cents per person per day. Uganda is next, at 4.1 cents, while Pakistan’s figure is considerably lower, at 1.76 cents. The two remaining countries are cheaper still: the UK stands at 1.3 cents, and the US records the lowest daily cost, at 0.85 cents.","chinese":"以金額來看，坦桑尼亞位居首位，每人每日成本為 6.4 美仙。 烏干達緊隨其後，為 4.1 美仙；而巴基斯坦的數字則低得多，為 1.76 美仙。 其餘兩個國家的成本更低：英國為 1.3 美仙，而美國錄得最低的每日成本，只有 0.85 美仙。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The percentage figures show a much sharper contrast. In Tanzania, the minimum requirement takes up 5.7% of the average daily wage, compared with 3.2% in Uganda and 1.1% in Pakistan. By contrast, the equivalent shares in the UK and the US are tiny, at only 0.013% and 0.006% respectively; indeed, Tanzania’s percentage is almost 1,000 times the US figure.","chinese":"百分比數據呈現出更鮮明的對比。 在坦桑尼亞，最低用水需求佔平均日薪的 5.7% ；相比之下，烏干達為 3.2% ，巴基斯坦則為 1.1% 。 相比之下，英國和美國的相應比例極小，分別只有 0.013% 和 0.006% ；事實上，坦桑尼亞的比例幾乎是美國的 1,000 倍。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the table below","chinese":"以下表格"},{"english":"gives information about","chinese":"提供關於……的資料"},{"english":"the daily cost of water","chinese":"每日用水成本"},{"english":"per person","chinese":"每人"},{"english":"five different countries","chinese":"五個不同國家"},{"english":"summarise the information","chinese":"概述資料"},{"english":"by selecting and reporting","chinese":"透過選取並報告……"},{"english":"the main features","chinese":"主要特徵"},{"english":"make comparisons where relevant","chinese":"在相關之處作出比較"},{"english":"the table compares","chinese":"表格比較"},{"english":"the cost of meeting","chinese":"滿足……所需的成本"},{"english":"minimum daily water requirement","chinese":"每日最低用水需求"},{"english":"expressed both in","chinese":"同時以……表示"},{"english":"US cents","chinese":"美仙"},{"english":"as a share of","chinese":"佔……的比例"},{"english":"average daily wage","chinese":"平均每日工資"},{"english":"records the highest cost","chinese":"錄得最高成本"},{"english":"the greatest wage burden","chinese":"最大工資負擔"},{"english":"the lowest figures","chinese":"最低數字"},{"english":"on both measures","chinese":"在兩項指標上"},{"english":"more broadly","chinese":"更廣泛而言"},{"english":"spend far larger proportions of","chinese":"花費大得多的比例於……"},{"english":"daily earnings","chinese":"每日收入"},{"english":"this basic requirement","chinese":"這項基本需求"},{"english":"even though","chinese":"即使"},{"english":"cash differences","chinese":"現金差距"},{"english":"only a few cents","chinese":"只有幾美仙"},{"english":"in monetary terms","chinese":"以金額計"},{"english":"leads the table","chinese":"在表格中居首"},{"english":"at 6.4 cents","chinese":"為6.4美仙"},{"english":"cents per person per day","chinese":"每人每日美仙"},{"english":"is next","chinese":"其次是"},{"english":"considerably lower","chinese":"低得多"},{"english":"the two remaining countries","chinese":"其餘兩個國家"},{"english":"cheaper still","chinese":"更便宜"},{"english":"stands at","chinese":"為；達到"},{"english":"records the lowest daily cost","chinese":"錄得最低每日成本"},{"english":"daily cost","chinese":"每日成本"},{"english":"percentage figures","chinese":"百分比數字"},{"english":"a much sharper contrast","chinese":"更鮮明的對比"},{"english":"takes up","chinese":"佔用；佔去"},{"english":"compared with","chinese":"與……相比"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"equivalent shares","chinese":"相應比例"},{"english":"are tiny","chinese":"非常小"},{"english":"at only","chinese":"只有"},{"english":"respectively","chinese":"分別"},{"english":"indeed","chinese":"事實上"},{"english":"almost 1,000 times","chinese":"接近1,000倍"},{"english":"the US figure","chinese":"美國的數字"},{"english":"wage burden","chinese":"工資負擔"},{"english":"water requirement","chinese":"用水需求"},{"english":"basic water needs","chinese":"基本用水需要"},{"english":"affordability of water","chinese":"用水負擔能力"},{"english":"water affordability","chinese":"用水負擔能力"},{"english":"varies greatly","chinese":"差異很大"},{"english":"from country to country","chinese":"因國家而異"},{"english":"in absolute terms","chinese":"以實際金額計"},{"english":"in percentage terms","chinese":"以百分比計"},{"english":"a share of income","chinese":"收入比例"},{"english":"relative to wages","chinese":"相對於工資"},{"english":"the highest cash cost","chinese":"最高現金成本"},{"english":"the lowest cash cost","chinese":"最低現金成本"},{"english":"a small cash gap","chinese":"小額現金差距"},{"english":"a large percentage gap","chinese":"大幅百分比差距"},{"english":"the largest gap","chinese":"最大差距"},{"english":"a striking difference","chinese":"顯著差異"},{"english":"a clear divide","chinese":"明顯分野"},{"english":"the richer countries","chinese":"較富裕國家"},{"english":"the poorer countries","chinese":"較貧窮國家"},{"english":"far larger than","chinese":"遠大於"},{"english":"much smaller than","chinese":"遠小於"},{"english":"only slightly higher than","chinese":"只略高於"},{"english":"considerably higher than","chinese":"明顯高於"},{"english":"rank first","chinese":"排名第一"},{"english":"rank last","chinese":"排名最後"},{"english":"the overall pattern","chinese":"整體模式"},{"english":"the main contrast","chinese":"主要對比"},{"english":"the most expensive country","chinese":"成本最高的國家"},{"english":"the least expensive country","chinese":"成本最低的國家"},{"english":"a heavier burden","chinese":"較沉重負擔"},{"english":"a negligible burden","chinese":"微不足道的負擔"},{"english":"account for a small share","chinese":"佔小比例"},{"english":"account for a large share","chinese":"佔大比例"},{"english":"the minimum requirement","chinese":"最低需求"},{"english":"meeting basic needs","chinese":"滿足基本需要"},{"english":"expressed as a percentage","chinese":"以百分比表示"},{"english":"monetary cost","chinese":"金錢成本"},{"english":"relative cost","chinese":"相對成本"},{"english":"purchasing power","chinese":"購買力"},{"english":"financial burden","chinese":"財政負擔"},{"english":"the burden is minimal","chinese":"負擔極低"},{"english":"despite small cash differences","chinese":"儘管現金差距很小"},{"english":"widen dramatically","chinese":"大幅擴大"},{"english":"when expressed as","chinese":"當以……表示時"}]},"model-essay-12-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-12-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:12","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-12-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q12","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"It is often argued that the place where a child grows up can shape nearly every aspect of his or her development. While cities are widely associated with opportunity and convenience, the countryside is often regarded as a healthier and more peaceful environment. This essay will examine the advantages and disadvantages of both settings.","chinese":"[無論在職場還是私人生活中，越來越多的溝通如今都是透過數位科技進行，而不是以面對面互動的方式完成。] [儘管這種發展可能削弱人際關係的質素，並增加誤解的風險，] [我認為整體而言，它的優點更大，因為它使溝通變得高效得多，並讓人們即使相隔遙遠也能保持聯繫。]"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Growing up in a city offers several important benefits. To begin with, urban areas usually provide better access to high-quality schools, specialised healthcare and a wide range of extracurricular activities. This means that children are more likely to receive strong academic support and to discover talents in fields such as music, sport or technology. In addition, city life exposes them to cultural diversity, which can broaden their horizons and help them become more adaptable. However, these advantages often come with serious drawbacks. Cities are frequently crowded, noisy and polluted, and many children have limited access to safe outdoor space. Moreover, heavy traffic, higher crime rates and the fast pace of urban life can create stress for both children and their parents.","chinese":"[科技化溝通最主要的優點在於速度與便利。] [在專業環境中，電子郵件、即時通訊平台以及視像會議免除了人們出行的需要，並使決策幾乎能夠即時作出。] [這不但縮短了回應時間、降低了營運成本，還使公司能夠極為輕鬆地協調分布於不同城市甚至不同大洲的團隊。] [例如，一位經理可以透過一次線上會議便與海外同事解決生產問題，而不必等待數天後才進行一次面對面的討論。] [同樣的道理也適用於社交層面：住得很遠的父母、子女和朋友，仍然可以透過通話和訊息每天聯絡。] [結果是，人際關係更容易維持，也較不容易隨時間流逝而逐漸淡化。] [例如，一個家庭即使成員分散於不同國家，仍然可以透過視像通話分享日常近況，並彼此提供情感支持。] [因此，數位溝通大大提升了工作與個人生活中的效率與可及性。]"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"By contrast, the countryside can provide a calmer and more grounded childhood. Cleaner air, open spaces and closer contact with nature are all conducive to physical health and emotional well-being. Rural communities are also often more close-knit, so children may grow up with a stronger sense of belonging and security. Nevertheless, life in the countryside is not without disadvantages. Educational and medical facilities may be fewer in number and less advanced, which can restrict children’s development in the long run. Furthermore, rural areas may offer fewer social, cultural and recreational opportunities, and this relative isolation can sometimes limit a child’s exposure to different people and ideas.","chinese":"[然而，數位溝通也有重要的缺點，其中最嚴重的一點在於它缺乏情感上的豐富性。] [面對面的交談能傳達語氣、面部表情和肢體語言，而這些都有助於人們更準確地理解意思、表達同理心，並建立信任。] [當這些線索消失時，訊息便更容易被誤讀，從而導致困惑，甚至引發衝突。] [例如，一封簡短的電郵或文字訊息，即使本來並無冒犯之意，也可能顯得冷淡，甚至帶有敵意。] [這在職場中尤其成問題，因為信任與細膩的理解對領導、協商及團隊合作都至關重要。] [長遠而言，過度依賴螢幕也可能助長膚淺的社交習慣，因此人們即使在線上一直保持聯絡，仍然可能感到孤立。] [例如，一個人即使經常透過社交媒體聊天，仍可能感到孤單，因為數位接觸始終無法完全取代真正的關注與人的陪伴。] [因此，儘管科技使溝通成為可能，它同時也可能削弱清晰度、信任感與情感深度。]"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, both the city and the countryside offer distinct advantages and disadvantages for children. Urban life provides opportunity and variety, whereas rural life offers space, tranquillity and a stronger connection to nature.","chinese":"[總結來說，透過科技進行溝通在效率與可及性方面具有明顯優勢，儘管它可能削弱人際互動的深度與清晰度。] [整體而言，我認為其優點大於缺點，因為數位工具使工作與個人生活中的溝通都能跨越時間與距離而有效運作。]"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the place where a child grows up","chinese":"孩子成長的地方"},{"english":"shape nearly every aspect of","chinese":"塑造……幾乎每一方面"},{"english":"development","chinese":"發展"},{"english":"be widely associated with","chinese":"被廣泛聯想到"},{"english":"opportunity and convenience","chinese":"機會和便利"},{"english":"be regarded as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"a healthier and more peaceful environment","chinese":"更健康、更平靜的環境"},{"english":"examine the advantages and disadvantages of","chinese":"探討……的優點和缺點"},{"english":"both settings","chinese":"兩種環境"},{"english":"growing up in","chinese":"在……成長"},{"english":"urban areas","chinese":"城市地區"},{"english":"provide better access to","chinese":"提供更好的……機會"},{"english":"high-quality schools","chinese":"優質學校"},{"english":"specialised healthcare","chinese":"專門醫療服務"},{"english":"a wide range of","chinese":"廣泛的"},{"english":"extracurricular activities","chinese":"課外活動"},{"english":"be more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"receive strong academic support","chinese":"獲得強大的學業支援"},{"english":"discover talents in","chinese":"發掘在……方面的才能"},{"english":"fields such as","chinese":"例如……的領域"},{"english":"exposes them to","chinese":"讓他們接觸到"},{"english":"cultural diversity","chinese":"文化多樣性"},{"english":"broaden their horizons","chinese":"擴闊他們的眼界"},{"english":"become more adaptable","chinese":"變得更有適應力"},{"english":"come with serious drawbacks","chinese":"伴隨嚴重缺點"},{"english":"crowded, noisy and polluted","chinese":"擠迫、嘈吵和受污染"},{"english":"limited access to","chinese":"有限地接觸；缺乏……機會"},{"english":"safe outdoor space","chinese":"安全的戶外空間"},{"english":"moreover","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"heavy traffic","chinese":"繁忙交通"},{"english":"higher crime rates","chinese":"較高罪案率"},{"english":"the fast pace of urban life","chinese":"城市生活的急速節奏"},{"english":"create stress for","chinese":"為……造成壓力"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"a calmer and more grounded childhood","chinese":"更平靜、更踏實的童年"},{"english":"cleaner air","chinese":"更清新的空氣"},{"english":"open spaces","chinese":"開闊空間"},{"english":"closer contact with nature","chinese":"與大自然更親近"},{"english":"be conducive to","chinese":"有助於"},{"english":"physical health","chinese":"身體健康"},{"english":"emotional well-being","chinese":"情緒健康"},{"english":"rural communities","chinese":"鄉郊社區"},{"english":"close-knit","chinese":"關係緊密的"},{"english":"grow up with","chinese":"帶着……成長"},{"english":"a stronger sense of belonging and security","chinese":"更強的歸屬感和安全感"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"not without disadvantages","chinese":"並非沒有缺點"},{"english":"educational and medical facilities","chinese":"教育和醫療設施"},{"english":"fewer in number","chinese":"數量較少"},{"english":"less advanced","chinese":"較不先進"},{"english":"restrict children's development","chinese":"限制兒童發展"},{"english":"in the long run","chinese":"長遠而言"},{"english":"furthermore","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"recreational opportunities","chinese":"康樂機會"},{"english":"relative isolation","chinese":"相對孤立"},{"english":"limit a child's exposure to","chinese":"限制孩子接觸……"},{"english":"different people and ideas","chinese":"不同的人和想法"},{"english":"distinct advantages and disadvantages","chinese":"明顯不同的優點和缺點"},{"english":"provides opportunity and variety","chinese":"提供機會和多樣性"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；相比之下"},{"english":"tranquillity","chinese":"寧靜"},{"english":"a stronger connection to nature","chinese":"與大自然更強的聯繫"}]},"model-essay-12-ielts-cause-solution":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-12-ielts-cause-solution","essayKey":"cause-solution:12","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-12-ielts-cause-solution","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/problem-and-cause/EdmundBd9CnS-Q12","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"As cities attract more people in search of employment and better prospects, urban overpopulation has become a serious challenge. This essay will discuss two major problems caused by this trend, namely pressure on housing and public services, and the decline of everyday living conditions, before suggesting practical ways to address them.","chinese":"隨著城市吸引越來越多人前來尋找工作和更好的發展前景，城市人口過多已成為一個嚴重的挑戰。 本文將討論這一趨勢所造成的兩個主要問題，即住房和公共服務所承受的壓力，以及日常生活條件的下降，然後提出實際的方法來解決這些問題。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first problem is that housing becomes increasingly unaffordable and inadequate. When too many people compete for a limited number of homes, rents rise sharply, and poorer residents may be forced into cramped apartments or informal settlements. This also places heavy pressure on schools, hospitals and sanitation systems, because public services have to serve more people than they were designed for. As a result, city life may promise opportunity, but for many residents it becomes expensive, stressful and unhealthy.","chinese":"第一個問題是，住房變得越來越負擔不起，而且越來越不足。 當太多人爭奪數量有限的住房時，租金會急劇上升，而較貧困的居民可能被迫住進狹小的公寓或非正式聚居區。 這也會對學校、醫院和衛生系統造成沉重壓力，因為公共服務需要服務的人數超出了原本設計時所能承受的範圍。 結果是，城市生活也許象徵著機會，但對許多居民而言，它卻變得昂貴、充滿壓力，而且不健康。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another serious problem is the deterioration of daily life in crowded urban areas. Large populations usually lead to traffic congestion, longer commuting times and higher levels of air pollution. For example, if thousands of workers travel into the same business districts every morning, roads and public transport systems quickly become overloaded. This wastes time, reduces productivity and gradually turns the city into a place where people spend more time surviving the routine than enjoying its opportunities.","chinese":"另一個嚴重問題是，擁擠城市地區的日常生活質素下降。 龐大的人口通常會導致交通擠塞、通勤時間延長，以及空氣污染水平上升。 例如，如果每天早上有數以千計的上班族前往相同的商業區，道路和公共交通系統很快便會不勝負荷。 這會浪費時間、降低生產力，並逐漸把城市變成一個讓人花更多時間應付日常壓力，而不是享受城市機會的地方。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 3","english":"These problems can be solved through a combination of regional development and better urban planning. Governments should create jobs, universities and reliable public services in smaller towns so that moving to a major city is not the only path to a better life. At the same time, cities need more affordable housing, stronger public transport networks and stricter planning rules to prevent overcrowded neighbourhoods from expanding without proper infrastructure.","chinese":"這些問題可以透過區域發展和更好的城市規劃相結合來解決。 政府應該在較小的城鎮創造就業機會、建立大學，並提供可靠的公共服務，使搬到大城市不再是通往更好生活的唯一途徑。 與此同時，城市需要更多可負擔的住房、更完善的公共交通網絡，以及更嚴格的規劃規則，以防止過度擁擠的社區在缺乏適當基礎設施的情況下繼續擴張。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, overpopulation in cities can cause housing shortages, pressure on public services, congestion and pollution. However, these problems can be reduced if governments make smaller regions more attractive and manage urban growth more carefully.","chinese":"總結來說，城市人口過多可能會造成住房短缺、公共服務壓力、交通擠塞和污染。 然而，如果政府能使較小地區更具吸引力，並更謹慎地管理城市增長，這些問題便可以得到減輕。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"attract more people","chinese":"吸引更多人"},{"english":"in search of employment","chinese":"為了尋找工作"},{"english":"better prospects","chinese":"更好的前景"},{"english":"urban overpopulation","chinese":"城市人口過多"},{"english":"a serious challenge","chinese":"嚴重挑戰"},{"english":"two major problems caused by this trend","chinese":"由這個趨勢造成的兩個主要問題"},{"english":"pressure on housing and public services","chinese":"對房屋及公共服務的壓力"},{"english":"the decline of everyday living conditions","chinese":"日常生活條件下降"},{"english":"practical ways to address them","chinese":"處理這些問題的實際方法"},{"english":"increasingly unaffordable and inadequate","chinese":"越來越負擔不起及不足"},{"english":"compete for a limited number of homes","chinese":"爭奪數量有限的住所"},{"english":"a limited number of homes","chinese":"數量有限的住所"},{"english":"rents rise sharply","chinese":"租金急升"},{"english":"poorer residents","chinese":"較貧困的居民"},{"english":"be forced into","chinese":"被迫進入；被迫入住"},{"english":"cramped apartments","chinese":"狹窄的單位"},{"english":"informal settlements","chinese":"非正式聚居區；臨時聚居區"},{"english":"place heavy pressure on","chinese":"對……造成沉重壓力"},{"english":"sanitation systems","chinese":"衛生系統；環境衞生設施"},{"english":"serve more people than they were designed for","chinese":"服務超出原本設計承載的人數"},{"english":"city life may promise opportunity","chinese":"城市生活可能承諾機會"},{"english":"expensive, stressful and unhealthy","chinese":"昂貴、壓力大及不健康"},{"english":"the deterioration of daily life","chinese":"日常生活質素惡化"},{"english":"crowded urban areas","chinese":"擠迫的市區"},{"english":"lead to traffic congestion","chinese":"導致交通擠塞"},{"english":"longer commuting times","chinese":"更長的通勤時間"},{"english":"higher levels of air pollution","chinese":"更高程度的空氣污染"},{"english":"travel into the same business districts","chinese":"前往同一批商業區"},{"english":"business districts","chinese":"商業區"},{"english":"quickly become overloaded","chinese":"很快變得超出負荷"},{"english":"public transport systems","chinese":"公共交通系統"},{"english":"wastes time","chinese":"浪費時間"},{"english":"reduces productivity","chinese":"降低生產力"},{"english":"gradually turns the city into","chinese":"逐漸把城市變成"},{"english":"surviving the routine","chinese":"勉強應付日常生活"},{"english":"enjoying its opportunities","chinese":"享受其機會"},{"english":"through a combination of","chinese":"透過結合……"},{"english":"regional development","chinese":"區域發展"},{"english":"better urban planning","chinese":"更好的城市規劃"},{"english":"reliable public services","chinese":"可靠的公共服務"},{"english":"smaller towns","chinese":"較小的城鎮"},{"english":"the only path to a better life","chinese":"通往更好生活的唯一途徑"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"affordable housing","chinese":"可負擔房屋"},{"english":"stronger public transport networks","chinese":"更完善的公共交通網絡"},{"english":"stricter planning rules","chinese":"更嚴格的規劃規則"},{"english":"prevent overcrowded neighbourhoods from expanding","chinese":"防止過度擠迫的社區擴張"},{"english":"proper infrastructure","chinese":"適當的基礎設施"},{"english":"housing shortages","chinese":"房屋短缺"},{"english":"congestion and pollution","chinese":"交通擠塞及污染"},{"english":"make smaller regions more attractive","chinese":"令較小地區更具吸引力"},{"english":"manage urban growth more carefully","chinese":"更審慎地管理城市增長"}]},"model-essay-12-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-12-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:12","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-12-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q12","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Discipline is one of the most difficult responsibilities teachers face, especially when one child repeatedly prevents others from learning. However, I do not think asking a disruptive child to leave the classroom is the best way to handle the problem. It may create immediate silence, but it rarely addresses the reasons behind the behaviour. A better approach is to combine firm classroom management with support from the school and parents.","chinese":"紀律管理是教師面對的其中一項最困難的責任，尤其是當一名孩子反覆阻礙其他人學習時。 然而，我不認為要求一名擾亂課堂的孩子離開課室，是處理這個問題的最佳方法。 這樣做可能會立即帶來安靜，但它很少能處理該行為背後的原因。 更好的做法是把堅定的課堂管理，與學校和家長的支援結合起來。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first solution is to establish clear rules and predictable consequences before serious disruption occurs. Many children behave badly not because they are deliberately malicious, but because they do not understand boundaries or have never been made to face consistent outcomes. If a teacher explains what behaviour is acceptable, gives a warning when rules are broken, and then applies a fair consequence, students are more likely to take responsibility for their actions. For example, a pupil who keeps interrupting others could be moved to another seat, asked to complete a reflection task after class, or given a short meeting with the teacher. This keeps the child within the learning environment while making it clear that poor behaviour has a cost.","chinese":"第一個解決方法是在嚴重擾亂發生之前，建立清晰的規則和可預期的後果。 許多孩子表現不佳，並不是因為他們故意懷有惡意，而是因為他們不明白界線，或者從未被要求面對一致的後果。 如果老師解釋甚麼行為是可以接受的，在規則被打破時給予警告，然後施加公平的後果，學生便更有可能為自己的行為負責。 例如，一名不斷打斷別人的學生，可以被安排坐到另一個座位、被要求在課後完成一項反思任務，或者與老師進行一次簡短會面。 這樣既能讓孩子留在學習環境之中，同時也清楚表明不良行為是有代價的。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important solution is to involve parents, counsellors, or senior teachers when the problem becomes repeated. Disruption is often a symptom of deeper issues, such as stress at home, low academic confidence, attention difficulties, or a desire for peer approval. Simply sending the child out may turn the corridor into an escape route rather than a real consequence. By contrast, a coordinated plan can identify the cause and respond more effectively. A school might set behavioural targets, offer counselling, or arrange regular communication with parents so that the child receives the same message from every direction.","chinese":"另一個重要的解決方法是，當問題反覆出現時，讓家長、輔導員或資深教師介入。 擾亂行為往往是更深層問題的症狀，例如家庭壓力、學業信心不足、注意力困難，或者渴望得到同輩認可。 單純把孩子送出去，可能會把走廊變成一條逃避路線，而不是真正的後果。 相比之下，一個協調一致的計劃能夠找出原因，並作出更有效的回應。 學校可以設定行為目標、提供輔導，或者安排與家長定期溝通，從而讓孩子從各方面都收到一致的訊息。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, removing a disruptive child from class is not the best response because it solves the appearance of disorder rather than the source of it. Clear rules, consistent consequences, and cooperation between teachers, families, and school specialists are more effective solutions.","chinese":"總結來說，把一名擾亂課堂的孩子移離課室並不是最佳回應，因為它解決的是混亂的表象，而不是混亂的根源。 清晰的規則、一致的後果，以及教師、家庭和學校專業人員之間的合作，才是更有效的解決方法。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"one of the most difficult responsibilities","chinese":"最困難的責任之一"},{"english":"teachers face","chinese":"教師面對的"},{"english":"repeatedly prevents others from","chinese":"反覆阻礙其他人"},{"english":"a disruptive child","chinese":"擾亂課堂的孩子"},{"english":"leave the classroom","chinese":"離開課室"},{"english":"the best way to handle the problem","chinese":"處理問題的最佳方法"},{"english":"create immediate silence","chinese":"立即帶來安靜"},{"english":"addresses the reasons behind","chinese":"處理……背後的原因"},{"english":"the behaviour","chinese":"行為"},{"english":"a better approach","chinese":"更好的做法"},{"english":"combine...with...","chinese":"將……與……結合"},{"english":"firm classroom management","chinese":"堅定的課堂管理"},{"english":"support from the school and parents","chinese":"來自學校和家長的支援"},{"english":"establish clear rules","chinese":"建立清晰規則"},{"english":"predictable consequences","chinese":"可預期的後果"},{"english":"before serious disruption occurs","chinese":"在嚴重擾亂發生之前"},{"english":"behave badly","chinese":"表現差；行為不當"},{"english":"deliberately malicious","chinese":"故意惡意的"},{"english":"understand boundaries","chinese":"明白界線"},{"english":"be made to face","chinese":"被要求面對"},{"english":"consistent outcomes","chinese":"一致的後果"},{"english":"acceptable behaviour","chinese":"可接受的行為"},{"english":"gives a warning","chinese":"給予警告"},{"english":"rules are broken","chinese":"規則被違反"},{"english":"applies a fair consequence","chinese":"執行公平的後果"},{"english":"take responsibility for","chinese":"對……負責"},{"english":"their actions","chinese":"他們的行為"},{"english":"keeps interrupting others","chinese":"不斷打斷別人"},{"english":"be moved to another seat","chinese":"被調到另一個座位"},{"english":"complete a reflection task","chinese":"完成反思任務"},{"english":"after class","chinese":"下課後"},{"english":"a short meeting with the teacher","chinese":"與老師短暫面談"},{"english":"within the learning environment","chinese":"在學習環境之內"},{"english":"poor behaviour has a cost","chinese":"不良行為是有代價的"},{"english":"involve parents","chinese":"讓家長參與"},{"english":"counsellors","chinese":"輔導員"},{"english":"senior teachers","chinese":"資深教師"},{"english":"the problem becomes repeated","chinese":"問題變得反覆出現"},{"english":"a symptom of deeper issues","chinese":"更深層問題的徵兆"},{"english":"stress at home","chinese":"家庭壓力"},{"english":"low academic confidence","chinese":"學業信心低"},{"english":"attention difficulties","chinese":"專注困難"},{"english":"a desire for peer approval","chinese":"渴望得到朋輩認同"},{"english":"sending the child out","chinese":"將孩子趕出課室"},{"english":"turn the corridor into","chinese":"將走廊變成"},{"english":"an escape route","chinese":"逃避途徑"},{"english":"rather than a real consequence","chinese":"而不是真正的後果"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"a coordinated plan","chinese":"協調一致的計劃"},{"english":"identify the cause","chinese":"找出原因"},{"english":"respond more effectively","chinese":"更有效地回應"},{"english":"set behavioural targets","chinese":"設定行為目標"},{"english":"offer counselling","chinese":"提供輔導"},{"english":"arrange regular communication with","chinese":"安排與……定期溝通"},{"english":"receives the same message from every direction","chinese":"從各方面收到一致訊息"},{"english":"removing a disruptive child from class","chinese":"將擾亂課堂的孩子帶離課室"},{"english":"solves the appearance of disorder","chinese":"解決表面的混亂"},{"english":"the source of it","chinese":"問題的根源"},{"english":"consistent consequences","chinese":"一致的後果"},{"english":"cooperation between","chinese":"……之間的合作"},{"english":"school specialists","chinese":"學校專業人員"},{"english":"more effective solutions","chinese":"更有效的解決方法"}]},"model-essay-12-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-12-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:12","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-12-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q12","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Discipline has become a growing concern in many schools, as teachers increasingly have to deal with disruptive behaviour alongside their academic duties. While some people argue that teachers should be mainly responsible for maintaining discipline, others believe that parents must take the lead. In my view, although teachers play an important role in enforcing rules at school, parents should bear the primary responsibility for shaping children’s behaviour.","chinese":"在許多學校中，紀律已成為一個日益令人關注的問題，因為教師除了履行教學職責之外，也越來越需要處理擾亂課堂的行為。 有些人認為教師應主要負責維持紀律，而另一些人則認為父母必須擔當主導角色。 在我看來，雖然教師在學校執行規則方面扮演重要角色，但父母應該承擔塑造孩子行為的主要責任。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"On the one hand, teachers are clearly responsible for creating an orderly learning environment. Since students spend many hours in classrooms, schools must have rules that prevent lessons from being constantly interrupted. For example, if a student repeatedly talks over others, refuses to follow instructions, or distracts classmates, the teacher has to respond immediately; otherwise, the whole class may suffer. In this sense, discipline is not separate from education. Without basic classroom control, even the most skilled teacher may struggle to teach effectively. Schools can also provide consistent consequences, such as detentions or behavioural reports, so that students understand that actions have limits.","chinese":"一方面，教師顯然有責任創造一個有秩序的學習環境。 由於學生每天在課室中度過許多時間，學校必須制定規則，以防止課堂不斷被打斷。 例如，如果一名學生反覆打斷別人說話、拒絕遵從指示，或者分散同學的注意力，教師就必須立即作出回應；否則，整個班級都可能受到影響。 從這個意義上說，紀律並不是與教育分開的事情。 如果沒有基本的課堂管理，即使是最有能力的教師也可能難以有效教學。 學校也可以提供一致的後果，例如留堂或行為報告，讓學生明白行為是有界線的。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"On the other hand, good discipline usually begins long before a child enters the classroom. Parents are the first people who teach children respect, self-control, and responsibility. If a child has never been taught at home to listen to adults, control anger, or accept consequences, teachers are forced to repair habits that have already become deeply rooted. For instance, a child who is allowed to shout, ignore rules, or blame others at home is likely to bring the same behaviour into school. Teachers can manage such behaviour temporarily, but parents shape the character behind it. This is why parental guidance is more fundamental than school punishment.","chinese":"另一方面，良好的紀律通常早在孩子進入課室之前就已經開始形成。 父母是最早教導孩子尊重、自制力和責任感的人。 如果一個孩子在家中從未被教導要聆聽成年人、控制憤怒或接受後果，教師就會被迫修正一些已經根深蒂固的習慣。 例如，一個在家中被允許大叫、無視規則或責怪他人的孩子，很可能會把同樣的行為帶到學校。 教師可以暫時管理這類行為，但父母才是在塑造其背後的品格。 這就是為甚麼父母的引導比學校的懲罰更根本。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, teachers must maintain discipline within school because learning cannot happen in chaos. However, I believe parents have the greater responsibility, as children’s attitudes towards authority, respect, and self-control are mainly formed at home. A school can enforce rules, but a family builds the habits that make those rules work.","chinese":"總結來說，教師必須在學校內維持紀律，因為學習不可能在混亂中發生。 然而，我認為父母負有更大的責任，因為孩子對權威、尊重和自制力的態度主要是在家中形成的。 學校可以執行規則，但家庭建立的習慣，才是讓這些規則真正發揮作用的關鍵。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"discipline","chinese":"紀律；管教"},{"english":"a growing concern","chinese":"日益受關注的問題"},{"english":"deal with disruptive behaviour","chinese":"處理擾亂秩序的行為"},{"english":"disruptive behaviour","chinese":"擾亂秩序的行為"},{"english":"alongside their academic duties","chinese":"在履行學業職責的同時"},{"english":"academic duties","chinese":"學業職責"},{"english":"be mainly responsible for","chinese":"主要負責"},{"english":"maintaining discipline","chinese":"維持紀律"},{"english":"take the lead","chinese":"帶頭；主導"},{"english":"enforcing rules at school","chinese":"在學校執行規則"},{"english":"bear the primary responsibility for","chinese":"承擔首要責任"},{"english":"shaping children's behaviour","chinese":"塑造兒童行為"},{"english":"on the one hand","chinese":"一方面"},{"english":"create an orderly learning environment","chinese":"建立有秩序的學習環境"},{"english":"since","chinese":"由於"},{"english":"spend many hours in classrooms","chinese":"在課室度過很多時間"},{"english":"prevent lessons from being constantly interrupted","chinese":"防止課堂不斷被打斷"},{"english":"be constantly interrupted","chinese":"不斷被打斷"},{"english":"repeatedly talks over others","chinese":"不斷打斷別人說話"},{"english":"refuse to follow instructions","chinese":"拒絕遵從指示"},{"english":"distract classmates","chinese":"分散同學注意力"},{"english":"respond immediately","chinese":"立即回應"},{"english":"otherwise","chinese":"否則"},{"english":"the whole class may suffer","chinese":"全班都可能受影響"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"not separate from","chinese":"與……並非分開"},{"english":"basic classroom control","chinese":"基本課堂管理"},{"english":"struggle to teach effectively","chinese":"難以有效教學"},{"english":"skilled teacher","chinese":"熟練的老師"},{"english":"provide consistent consequences","chinese":"提供一致的後果；作出一致處分"},{"english":"detentions","chinese":"留堂"},{"english":"behavioural reports","chinese":"行為報告"},{"english":"actions have limits","chinese":"行為有界限"},{"english":"on the other hand","chinese":"另一方面"},{"english":"begin long before","chinese":"早在……之前開始"},{"english":"enter the classroom","chinese":"進入課室"},{"english":"teach children respect","chinese":"教導孩子尊重"},{"english":"self-control","chinese":"自制能力"},{"english":"responsibility","chinese":"責任感"},{"english":"be taught at home to","chinese":"在家中被教導去"},{"english":"listen to adults","chinese":"聆聽成年人說話"},{"english":"control anger","chinese":"控制怒氣"},{"english":"accept consequences","chinese":"承擔後果"},{"english":"be forced to repair","chinese":"被迫修補；被迫糾正"},{"english":"deeply rooted","chinese":"根深蒂固"},{"english":"be allowed to","chinese":"被容許去"},{"english":"ignore rules","chinese":"無視規則"},{"english":"blame others","chinese":"責怪他人"},{"english":"be likely to","chinese":"很可能會"},{"english":"bring the same behaviour into school","chinese":"將同樣行為帶到學校"},{"english":"manage such behaviour temporarily","chinese":"暫時管理這類行為"},{"english":"shape the character behind it","chinese":"塑造行為背後的品格"},{"english":"parental guidance","chinese":"父母指導"},{"english":"more fundamental than","chinese":"比……更根本"},{"english":"school punishment","chinese":"學校懲罰"},{"english":"maintain discipline within school","chinese":"在校內維持紀律"},{"english":"learning cannot happen in chaos","chinese":"學習不能在混亂中發生"},{"english":"the greater responsibility","chinese":"更大的責任"},{"english":"attitudes towards authority","chinese":"對權威的態度"},{"english":"respect and self-control","chinese":"尊重和自制"},{"english":"be mainly formed at home","chinese":"主要在家中形成"},{"english":"enforce rules","chinese":"執行規則"},{"english":"build the habits that","chinese":"建立令……奏效的習慣"},{"english":"make those rules work","chinese":"令那些規則奏效"}]},"model-essay-12-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-12-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:12","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-12-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q12","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In an age of increasingly frictionless spending, borrowing has become so easy that many people barely notice when ordinary purchases turn into long-term financial liabilities. It is often argued that this problem is mainly caused by the excessive and irresponsible use of credit cards, and that banks should not provide such cards unless an applicant can clearly afford to repay what is borrowed. This essay completely agrees, because credit cards encourage spending without immediate financial pain, while banks have a clear duty to prevent unaffordable lending.","chinese":"在一個消費愈來愈毫不費力的時代，借貸已變得如此容易，以致許多人幾乎察覺不到，日常購物何時已變成長期的債務負擔。 人們常主張，這個問題主要是由過度且不負責任地使用信用卡所造成，而銀行不應發出這類卡片，除非申請人明確有能力償還所借款項。 本文完全同意這個觀點，因為信用卡會鼓勵人們在沒有即時財務痛感的情況下消費，而銀行也有明確責任防止人們承擔無力償還的借貸。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason for agreeing with this view is that credit cards weaken the natural restraint that other forms of payment impose. Because no money visibly leaves a person’s account at the moment of purchase, unnecessary spending feels harmless, so small discretionary expenses are repeated until they become difficult to control. For example, an office worker who routinely uses a credit card for takeaway meals, taxis and online shopping may not realise how much has been spent until the monthly statement arrives. The problem is then intensified by the repayment structure itself. Minimum payments create the illusion that the debt is manageable, whereas interest charges quietly increase the total balance. Someone who pays only a small portion of a holiday bill, for instance, may still be repaying it many months later.","chinese":"我之所以最同意這個觀點，最有力的理由是：信用卡削弱了其他付款方式原本會帶來的自然節制作用。 因為在購買當下，金錢並不會明顯地從個人帳戶中流出，因此不必要的消費會讓人覺得無傷大雅，而小額的非必要支出也就一再重複，直到變得難以控制。 例如，一名經常用信用卡支付外賣餐點、計程車和網上購物費用的上班族，可能要等到每月帳單寄來時，才意識到自己究竟花了多少錢。 而且，還款機制本身又會進一步加劇這個問題。 最低還款額會製造一種債務仍然可控的假象，然而利息費用卻會在不知不覺間推高總欠款額。 例如，一個人若在假期消費後只償還帳單中的一小部分，那麼幾個月之後，他可能仍然還在償還這筆債務。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Banks should therefore issue credit cards only after carrying out strict affordability checks. In the first place, financial institutions possess the income data, credit history and risk-assessment tools needed to judge whether borrowing is realistic. A bank can see, for example, if an applicant already has multiple loans, unstable earnings or a record of overdraft use. More importantly, irresponsible lending can trap households in a cycle in which interest payments begin to consume money needed for essentials. A family living on one income, for instance, may start struggling with rent or utility bills once a poorly screened credit-card balance begins to grow. Requiring convincing proof of repayment ability is therefore not excessive caution but responsible lending.","chinese":"因此，銀行只有在進行嚴格的負擔能力審查之後，才應發出信用卡。 首先，金融機構掌握了判斷借貸是否實際可行所需的收入資料、信用紀錄以及風險評估工具。 例如，銀行可以看出申請人是否已經背負多筆貸款、收入不穩定，或有使用透支的紀錄。 更重要的是，不負責任的放貸會使家庭陷入一種惡性循環：利息支出開始吞噬原本應該用於基本生活所需的金錢。 例如，一個只靠單一收入維生的家庭，一旦經審查不周而產生的信用卡欠款開始增加，就可能開始難以負擔房租或水電費。 因此，要求申請人提出具說服力的還款能力證明，並不是過度謹慎，而是負責任的放貸。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely agree that irresponsible credit-card use is a major cause of personal debt and that banks should not issue credit cards unless repayment is clearly affordable. Because such borrowing encourages detached spending and because lenders are uniquely placed to prevent debt spirals, stricter controls are both justified and necessary.","chinese":"總而言之，我完全同意，不負責任地使用信用卡是造成個人債務的主要原因之一，而除非申請人明確有能力負擔還款，否則銀行不應發出信用卡。 因為這種借貸會助長與實際支出脫節的消費方式，而放貸者又處於獨特的位置，能夠防止債務惡性循環的形成，所以更嚴格的管制既合理，也有其必要。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"in an age of","chinese":"在……的時代"},{"english":"increasingly frictionless spending","chinese":"越來越方便、幾乎無阻力的消費"},{"english":"borrowing has become so easy that","chinese":"借貸變得如此容易，以致"},{"english":"barely notice","chinese":"幾乎沒有察覺"},{"english":"ordinary purchases","chinese":"日常購物"},{"english":"turn into","chinese":"變成"},{"english":"long-term financial liabilities","chinese":"長期財務負擔"},{"english":"it is often argued that","chinese":"人們經常認為"},{"english":"be mainly caused by","chinese":"主要由……造成"},{"english":"excessive and irresponsible use of","chinese":"過度及不負責任地使用"},{"english":"credit cards","chinese":"信用卡"},{"english":"provide such cards","chinese":"提供這類卡"},{"english":"unless an applicant can clearly afford to","chinese":"除非申請人明顯有能力"},{"english":"repay what is borrowed","chinese":"償還所借款項"},{"english":"encourage spending","chinese":"鼓勵消費"},{"english":"immediate financial pain","chinese":"即時的財務痛楚"},{"english":"have a clear duty to","chinese":"明確有責任去"},{"english":"prevent unaffordable lending","chinese":"防止負擔不起的借貸"},{"english":"the strongest reason for agreeing with","chinese":"同意……的最有力原因"},{"english":"weaken the natural restraint","chinese":"削弱自然的節制"},{"english":"forms of payment","chinese":"付款方式"},{"english":"impose restraint","chinese":"施加約束"},{"english":"no money visibly leaves","chinese":"沒有金錢明顯離開"},{"english":"at the moment of purchase","chinese":"在購買的一刻"},{"english":"unnecessary spending","chinese":"不必要的消費"},{"english":"feel harmless","chinese":"感覺無害"},{"english":"discretionary expenses","chinese":"非必要開支；可自由決定的開支"},{"english":"be repeated until","chinese":"不斷重複，直到"},{"english":"difficult to control","chinese":"難以控制"},{"english":"routinely uses","chinese":"經常使用"},{"english":"takeaway meals","chinese":"外賣餐"},{"english":"online shopping","chinese":"網上購物"},{"english":"realise how much has been spent","chinese":"意識到已花了多少錢"},{"english":"the monthly statement arrives","chinese":"月結單到達"},{"english":"be intensified by","chinese":"因……而加劇"},{"english":"repayment structure","chinese":"還款結構"},{"english":"minimum payments","chinese":"最低還款額"},{"english":"create the illusion that","chinese":"製造……的錯覺"},{"english":"the debt is manageable","chinese":"債務可應付"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"interest charges","chinese":"利息費用"},{"english":"quietly increase","chinese":"悄悄增加"},{"english":"the total balance","chinese":"總結欠"},{"english":"pay only a small portion of","chinese":"只支付……的一小部分"},{"english":"a holiday bill","chinese":"假期開支賬單"},{"english":"still be repaying it","chinese":"仍在償還"},{"english":"many months later","chinese":"多個月後"},{"english":"issue credit cards","chinese":"發出信用卡"},{"english":"only after carrying out","chinese":"只有在進行……之後"},{"english":"strict affordability checks","chinese":"嚴格的負擔能力審查"},{"english":"in the first place","chinese":"首先"},{"english":"financial institutions","chinese":"金融機構"},{"english":"possess","chinese":"擁有"},{"english":"income data","chinese":"收入資料"},{"english":"credit history","chinese":"信貸紀錄"},{"english":"risk-assessment tools","chinese":"風險評估工具"},{"english":"judge whether borrowing is realistic","chinese":"判斷借貸是否實際可行"},{"english":"multiple loans","chinese":"多筆貸款"},{"english":"unstable earnings","chinese":"不穩定收入"},{"english":"a record of overdraft use","chinese":"使用透支的紀錄"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"irresponsible lending","chinese":"不負責任的放貸"},{"english":"trap households in a cycle","chinese":"令家庭陷入循環"},{"english":"interest payments","chinese":"利息付款"},{"english":"begin to consume","chinese":"開始消耗"},{"english":"money needed for essentials","chinese":"生活必需開支所需的金錢"},{"english":"living on one income","chinese":"靠一份收入生活"},{"english":"struggle with rent or utility bills","chinese":"難以應付租金或水電煤費"},{"english":"poorly screened","chinese":"審批不嚴的"},{"english":"credit-card balance","chinese":"信用卡結欠"},{"english":"begin to grow","chinese":"開始增加"},{"english":"convincing proof of repayment ability","chinese":"具說服力的還款能力證明"},{"english":"not excessive caution but responsible lending","chinese":"不是過分謹慎，而是負責任放貸"},{"english":"personal debt","chinese":"個人債務"},{"english":"a major cause of","chinese":"……的主要原因"},{"english":"repayment is clearly affordable","chinese":"還款明顯負擔得起"},{"english":"detached spending","chinese":"與實際金錢感脫節的消費"},{"english":"lenders are uniquely placed to","chinese":"貸款人特別有條件去"},{"english":"prevent debt spirals","chinese":"防止債務惡性循環"},{"english":"stricter controls","chinese":"更嚴格的管制"},{"english":"both justified and necessary","chinese":"既合理亦有必要"}]},"model-essay-13-ielts-cause-solution":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-13-ielts-cause-solution","essayKey":"cause-solution:13","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-13-ielts-cause-solution","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/problem-and-cause/EdmundBd9CnS-Q13","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Children are going online with less adult supervision and from early ages, which can expose them to risks they are not mature enough to recognise. Parents therefore face two main difficulties: keeping children safe from harmful digital material and helping them develop self-control online. This essay will discuss these problems and suggest solutions.","chinese":"兒童在較少成人監督的情況下上網，而且從較小的年齡便開始接觸網絡，這可能使他們面對一些他們尚未成熟到足以辨識的風險。 因此，父母面對兩個主要困難：保護孩子遠離有害的數位內容，以及幫助他們在網上培養自我控制能力。 本文將討論這些問題並提出解決方法。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One major problem is that parents cannot easily monitor what children see or whom they communicate with. The internet is not a single controlled space: a child may start by watching cartoons, but one click can lead to violent videos, misleading information, or conversations with strangers. Since children often lack the judgement to separate entertainment from manipulation, they may reveal private information, copy unsuitable behaviour, or become frightened by disturbing content. Another difficulty is the battle over screen time. Digital devices are designed to hold attention, so children may resist limits, rush homework, sleep late, or prefer online stimulation to face-to-face play. Parents are therefore managing not only a device, but also a powerful habit.","chinese":"其中一個主要問題是，父母難以輕易監察孩子在網上看到甚麼，或與誰交流。 互聯網並不是一個單一而受控制的空間：一個孩子可能只是從觀看卡通開始，但一次點擊便可能通向暴力影片、誤導性資訊，或與陌生人的對話。 由於孩子往往缺乏判斷力，難以分辨娛樂與操控之間的界線，他們可能會透露私人資料、模仿不合適的行為，或因令人不安的內容而感到害怕。 另一個困難是圍繞螢幕時間的拉鋸。 數位設備本身就是為了吸引注意力而設計的，因此孩子可能會抗拒限制、匆忙完成作業、晚睡，或更偏好網上刺激而不是面對面的玩耍。 因此，父母所管理的不只是一部設備，更是一種強大的習慣。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"These problems can be reduced through clear rules, technical safeguards and education. First, parents should create consistent household routines: devices can be used in shared areas, screen time can be limited after homework, and phones should be kept out of bedrooms at night. Second, parents should use age-appropriate controls, privacy settings and safe-search tools, not as a substitute for parenting, but as a safety net. Finally, children need to be taught digital judgement. Schools and parents can explain why personal details should not be shared, why online strangers may be dangerous, and why upsetting content should be reported immediately. This turns internet safety from a hidden battle into an open conversation.","chinese":"這些問題可以透過清晰規則、技術保障和教育來減少。 首先，父母應建立一致的家庭規律：設備可以只在公共空間使用，螢幕時間可以限制在完成功課之後，而手機在晚上應該放在睡房之外。 其次，父母應使用適合孩子年齡的管控功能、私隱設定和安全搜尋工具；這些不是用來取代父母管教，而是作為一張安全網。 最後，孩子需要被教導數位判斷力。 學校和父母可以解釋為甚麼不應分享個人資料、為甚麼網上陌生人可能很危險，以及為甚麼令人不安的內容應立即舉報。 這能把網絡安全從一場隱藏的角力，轉化為一場公開的對話。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, unsupervised internet use creates problems because parents struggle to monitor online risks and control digital habits. The most effective response is not a total ban, but a steady combination of boundaries, protection and education, so that children can use the internet safely as they grow.","chinese":"總結來說，缺乏監督的互聯網使用會造成問題，因為父母難以監察網上風險，也難以控制孩子的數位習慣。 最有效的應對方法並不是全面禁止，而是穩定地結合界線、保護和教育，使孩子在成長過程中能夠安全地使用互聯網。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"go online","chinese":"上網"},{"english":"less adult supervision","chinese":"較少成人監管"},{"english":"from an early age","chinese":"從小；年紀很小時"},{"english":"expose them to risks","chinese":"使他們接觸風險"},{"english":"mature enough to recognise","chinese":"成熟到足以識別"},{"english":"face two main difficulties","chinese":"面對兩個主要困難"},{"english":"harmful digital material","chinese":"有害的數碼內容"},{"english":"develop self-control online","chinese":"培養網上自制能力"},{"english":"monitor what children see","chinese":"監察兒童看到的內容"},{"english":"communicate with","chinese":"與……溝通"},{"english":"a single controlled space","chinese":"單一受控制的空間"},{"english":"one click can lead to","chinese":"一按就可能導致"},{"english":"violent videos","chinese":"暴力影片"},{"english":"misleading information","chinese":"誤導性資料"},{"english":"conversations with strangers","chinese":"與陌生人交談"},{"english":"lack the judgement to","chinese":"缺乏判斷力去……"},{"english":"separate entertainment from manipulation","chinese":"分辨娛樂和操控"},{"english":"reveal private information","chinese":"透露私人資料"},{"english":"unsuitable behaviour","chinese":"不合適的行為"},{"english":"disturbing content","chinese":"令人不安的內容"},{"english":"the battle over screen time","chinese":"圍繞屏幕時間的爭拗"},{"english":"screen time","chinese":"屏幕時間"},{"english":"be designed to hold attention","chinese":"被設計成吸引注意力"},{"english":"resist limits","chinese":"抗拒限制"},{"english":"rush homework","chinese":"匆忙完成家課"},{"english":"sleep late","chinese":"晚睡"},{"english":"online stimulation","chinese":"網上刺激"},{"english":"face-to-face play","chinese":"面對面的玩樂"},{"english":"managing not only","chinese":"不只是管理"},{"english":"a powerful habit","chinese":"強大的習慣"},{"english":"be reduced through","chinese":"透過……減少"},{"english":"clear rules","chinese":"清晰規則"},{"english":"technical safeguards","chinese":"技術保障措施"},{"english":"consistent household routines","chinese":"一致的家庭常規"},{"english":"shared areas","chinese":"共用空間"},{"english":"be limited after homework","chinese":"在完成家課後受限制"},{"english":"kept out of bedrooms","chinese":"不應放在睡房內"},{"english":"age-appropriate controls","chinese":"適合年齡的管制設定"},{"english":"privacy settings","chinese":"私隱設定"},{"english":"safe-search tools","chinese":"安全搜尋工具"},{"english":"a substitute for parenting","chinese":"育兒的替代品"},{"english":"a safety net","chinese":"安全網"},{"english":"digital judgement","chinese":"數碼判斷力"},{"english":"personal details","chinese":"個人資料"},{"english":"online strangers","chinese":"網上陌生人"},{"english":"upsetting content","chinese":"令人不安的內容"},{"english":"be reported immediately","chinese":"應立即舉報"},{"english":"internet safety","chinese":"網絡安全"},{"english":"a hidden battle","chinese":"隱藏的鬥爭"},{"english":"an open conversation","chinese":"開放的對話"},{"english":"unsupervised internet use","chinese":"無人監管的互聯網使用"},{"english":"struggle to monitor","chinese":"難以監察"},{"english":"online risks","chinese":"網上風險"},{"english":"control digital habits","chinese":"控制數碼習慣"},{"english":"the most effective response","chinese":"最有效的回應"},{"english":"a total ban","chinese":"全面禁止"},{"english":"a steady combination of","chinese":"……的穩定結合"},{"english":"boundaries","chinese":"界線"},{"english":"protection and education","chinese":"保護和教育"},{"english":"as they grow","chinese":"隨着他們成長"}]},"model-essay-13-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-13-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:13","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-13-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q13","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Formal education is often treated as the clearest route to social value, especially because doctors, engineers and researchers rely on advanced knowledge. However, I do not think educated people are the most valuable members of society. Society is best served when academic expertise is combined with practical competence, and many essential skills are learned by doing rather than by studying alone.","chinese":"正規教育常被視為創造社會價值最清晰的途徑，尤其是因為醫生、工程師和研究人員都依賴高深知識。 然而，我並不認為受過教育的人就是社會中最有價值的成員。 當學術專業知識與實際能力結合時，社會才能得到最好的服務，而許多重要技能是透過實踐學會的，而不是單靠學習得來。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main reason is that value should be measured by contribution, not by credentials. An educated person may understand theories, systems and principles, but this knowledge only becomes socially useful when it is applied with judgment. A qualified manager, for instance, may know how an organisation should operate, yet an experienced shop owner, builder or community volunteer may understand people, timing and risk far better because they have solved real problems repeatedly. In this sense, education is a powerful tool, but it is not a crown that automatically makes one person more valuable than another. A society that respects only degrees can become blind to the quiet competence that keeps daily life running.","chinese":"主要原因是，價值應該以貢獻來衡量，而不是以學歷或資歷來衡量。 一個受過教育的人也許明白理論、系統和原則，但這些知識只有在被有判斷力地應用時，才會對社會真正有用。 例如，一位合資格的經理也許知道一個機構應該如何運作，但一位有經驗的店主、建築工人或社區義工，可能更了解人、時機和風險，因為他們已經反覆解決過真實問題。 從這個意義上說，教育是一種強大的工具，但它不是一頂能自動使一個人比另一個人更有價值的皇冠。 一個只尊重學位的社會，可能會看不見那些默默維持日常生活運作的實際能力。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"People can also learn several socially valuable skills through experience. One is practical problem-solving: workers who repair machines, care for children or manage busy kitchens often learn to notice small warning signs before they become serious failures. This benefits society because it prevents waste, accidents and disorder. Another is human judgment. Through years of dealing with customers, patients, neighbours or colleagues, people learn patience, negotiation and empathy, which help reduce conflict and build trust. For example, an experienced nurse, mechanic or elderly caregiver may calm a tense situation not because they have memorised a rule, but because they can read the room and respond wisely.","chinese":"人們也可以透過經驗學會幾種對社會有價值的技能。 其中一種是實際解決問題的能力：修理機器、照顧兒童或管理繁忙廚房的工人，往往會學懂在小小的警號變成嚴重失誤之前就先注意到它們。 這對社會有益，因為它能防止浪費、意外和混亂。 另一種是人的判斷力。 透過多年與顧客、病人、鄰居或同事打交道，人們會學會耐性、協商和同理心，而這些都有助於減少衝突並建立信任。 例如，一位有經驗的護士、機械師或長者照顧者，可能能夠安撫一個緊張的局面，不是因為他們背熟了一條規則，而是因為他們能夠看懂現場氣氛，並作出明智回應。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I do not believe that educated people are the most valuable for society. Education is important, but social value also comes from experience-based skills such as practical judgment, communication, emotional intelligence and hands-on problem-solving.","chinese":"總結來說，我不相信受過教育的人就是對社會最有價值的人。 教育很重要，但社會價值也來自以經驗為基礎的技能，例如實際判斷力、溝通能力、情緒智慧和親手解決問題的能力。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"formal education","chinese":"正規教育"},{"english":"be treated as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"the clearest route to","chinese":"通往……最明確的途徑"},{"english":"social value","chinese":"社會價值"},{"english":"rely on advanced knowledge","chinese":"依賴高深知識"},{"english":"advanced knowledge","chinese":"高深知識"},{"english":"valuable members of society","chinese":"社會中有價值的成員"},{"english":"be best served when","chinese":"當……時最能受惠"},{"english":"academic expertise","chinese":"學術專業知識"},{"english":"be combined with","chinese":"與……結合"},{"english":"practical competence","chinese":"實務能力"},{"english":"essential skills","chinese":"必要技能"},{"english":"learned by doing","chinese":"從實踐中學習"},{"english":"rather than by studying alone","chinese":"而不是單靠讀書"},{"english":"be measured by","chinese":"應以……衡量"},{"english":"contribution, not credentials","chinese":"貢獻，而不是資歷"},{"english":"understand theories, systems and principles","chinese":"理解理論、系統和原則"},{"english":"socially useful","chinese":"對社會有用"},{"english":"be applied with judgment","chinese":"以判斷力加以運用"},{"english":"a qualified manager","chinese":"合資格的管理者"},{"english":"how an organisation should operate","chinese":"一個組織應如何運作"},{"english":"an experienced shop owner","chinese":"有經驗的店主"},{"english":"community volunteer","chinese":"社區義工"},{"english":"understand people, timing and risk","chinese":"理解人情、時機和風險"},{"english":"solve real problems repeatedly","chinese":"反覆解決真實問題"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"a powerful tool","chinese":"強大的工具"},{"english":"not a crown","chinese":"不是一頂冠冕"},{"english":"automatically makes one person more valuable","chinese":"自動令一個人更有價值"},{"english":"respects only degrees","chinese":"只尊重學位"},{"english":"become blind to","chinese":"對……視而不見"},{"english":"quiet competence","chinese":"默默的能力"},{"english":"keep daily life running","chinese":"維持日常生活運作"},{"english":"socially valuable skills","chinese":"對社會有價值的技能"},{"english":"through experience","chinese":"透過經驗"},{"english":"practical problem-solving","chinese":"實際解難能力"},{"english":"repair machines","chinese":"維修機器"},{"english":"care for children","chinese":"照顧兒童"},{"english":"manage busy kitchens","chinese":"管理繁忙的廚房"},{"english":"notice small warning signs","chinese":"察覺細微警號"},{"english":"serious failures","chinese":"嚴重故障；嚴重失誤"},{"english":"prevent waste, accidents and disorder","chinese":"防止浪費、意外和混亂"},{"english":"human judgment","chinese":"人情判斷；人的判斷力"},{"english":"years of dealing with","chinese":"多年處理……的經驗"},{"english":"patience, negotiation and empathy","chinese":"耐性、協商和同理心"},{"english":"reduce conflict","chinese":"減少衝突"},{"english":"build trust","chinese":"建立信任"},{"english":"an elderly caregiver","chinese":"長者照顧者"},{"english":"calm a tense situation","chinese":"平息緊張局面"},{"english":"memorise a rule","chinese":"背熟一條規則"},{"english":"read the room","chinese":"觀察現場氣氛；看懂場合"},{"english":"respond wisely","chinese":"明智地回應"},{"english":"experience-based skills","chinese":"以經驗為基礎的技能"},{"english":"practical judgment","chinese":"實際判斷力"},{"english":"emotional intelligence","chinese":"情緒智商"},{"english":"hands-on problem-solving","chinese":"親身實踐的解難能力"}]},"model-essay-13-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-13-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:13","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-13-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q13","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Homework is a long-standing part of schooling, but there is disagreement about whether children should receive it every day. Some argue that daily homework is essential for academic success, whereas others believe that children need regular breaks from schoolwork. In my view, children should not be given homework every day, because learning is stronger when practice is purposeful rather than constant.","chinese":"功課一直是學校教育中存在已久的一部分，但人們對於孩子是否應該每天都有功課存在分歧。 有些人認為每天做功課對學業成功是必要的，而另一些人則認為孩子需要定期從課業中休息。 在我看來，孩子不應該每天都有功課，因為當練習是有目的的，而不是不斷重複時，學習效果會更好。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Those who support daily homework usually believe that it builds discipline and reinforces classroom learning. When pupils review a topic shortly after a lesson, they are more likely to remember key ideas and identify gaps in their understanding. For example, a child who practises a few mathematics problems after studying fractions may notice mistakes before the next lesson, rather than allowing confusion to grow quietly. Daily assignments can also create a steady routine, which may help less organised students develop responsibility. From this perspective, homework is not merely extra work; it is a structure that keeps children engaged with their studies.","chinese":"支持每天有功課的人通常認為，功課能培養紀律，並鞏固課堂學習。 當學生在課後不久複習一個課題時，他們更有可能記住重點概念，並發現自己理解上的漏洞。 例如，一個孩子在學習分數後做幾道數學題，可能會在下一課之前發現錯誤，而不是讓困惑在不知不覺中加深。 每天的功課也能建立穩定的日常習慣，這可能有助於較缺乏組織能力的學生培養責任感 從這個角度來看，功課不只是額外的工作；它是一種讓孩子持續投入學習的結構。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, I believe that giving homework every day can be counterproductive, especially for younger students. Children need time to rest, play, exercise, read for pleasure and interact with their families. If every school day ends with more academic tasks, education can begin to feel like an endless conveyor belt, and this may weaken motivation rather than strengthen it. A tired child who completes a worksheet mechanically is not necessarily learning deeply. Moreover, excessive homework can crowd out activities that also support success at school, such as sleep, sport and social development. These are not luxuries; they help children return to class with better concentration and emotional balance.","chinese":"然而，我認為每天給功課可能會適得其反，尤其是對年紀較小的學生而言。 孩子需要時間休息、玩耍、運動、為興趣而閱讀，以及與家人互動。 如果每個上學日都以更多學業任務作結，教育便可能開始像一條無止境的輸送帶，而這可能會削弱學習動機，而不是增強它。 一個疲倦的孩子即使機械式地完成工作紙，也不一定是在深入學習。 此外，過量功課可能擠走一些同樣有助於學業成功的活動，例如睡眠、運動和社交發展 這些並不是奢侈的東西；它們能幫助孩子以更好的專注力和情緒平衡回到課堂。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, daily homework may help students revise lessons and build study habits, but it should not be treated as a requirement for success. Schools should assign homework when it genuinely consolidates learning, not simply because another day has passed. A balanced approach is more educationally sound than a rigid daily routine.","chinese":"總結來說，每天做功課或許能幫助學生複習課堂內容並建立學習習慣，但它不應被視為成功的必要條件。 學校應該在功課真正能鞏固學習時才佈置功課，而不是單純因為又過了一天就安排功課。 相比僵化的每日功課安排，一種平衡的做法在教育上更加合理。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"a long-standing part of","chinese":"長久以來是……的一部分"},{"english":"schooling","chinese":"學校教育"},{"english":"there is disagreement about whether","chinese":"對於是否……有分歧"},{"english":"receive it every day","chinese":"每日收到它"},{"english":"daily homework","chinese":"每日家課"},{"english":"be essential for academic success","chinese":"對學業成功不可或缺"},{"english":"regular breaks from","chinese":"定期從……中休息"},{"english":"schoolwork","chinese":"學校功課"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"should not be given","chinese":"不應被給予"},{"english":"learning is stronger when","chinese":"當……時學習更有效"},{"english":"purposeful rather than constant","chinese":"有目的，而不是不停重複"},{"english":"support daily homework","chinese":"支持每日家課"},{"english":"build discipline","chinese":"培養自律"},{"english":"reinforce classroom learning","chinese":"鞏固課堂學習"},{"english":"review a topic","chinese":"重溫一個課題"},{"english":"shortly after a lesson","chinese":"上課後不久"},{"english":"remember key ideas","chinese":"記住重點概念"},{"english":"identify gaps in their understanding","chinese":"找出理解上的空隙"},{"english":"practise a few mathematics problems","chinese":"練習幾條數學題"},{"english":"studying fractions","chinese":"學習分數"},{"english":"notice mistakes","chinese":"發現錯誤"},{"english":"before the next lesson","chinese":"下一課之前"},{"english":"rather than allowing","chinese":"而不是任由"},{"english":"confusion to grow quietly","chinese":"困惑悄悄加深"},{"english":"daily assignments","chinese":"每日作業"},{"english":"create a steady routine","chinese":"建立穩定常規"},{"english":"less organised students","chinese":"組織能力較弱的學生"},{"english":"develop responsibility","chinese":"培養責任感"},{"english":"from this perspective","chinese":"從這個角度來看"},{"english":"not merely extra work","chinese":"不只是額外工作"},{"english":"a structure that keeps children engaged with","chinese":"讓孩子持續投入……的結構"},{"english":"engaged with their studies","chinese":"投入學習"},{"english":"giving homework every day","chinese":"每日給家課"},{"english":"counterproductive","chinese":"適得其反"},{"english":"younger students","chinese":"年幼學生"},{"english":"read for pleasure","chinese":"為興趣而閱讀"},{"english":"interact with their families","chinese":"與家人互動"},{"english":"every school day ends with","chinese":"每個上學日都以……結束"},{"english":"academic tasks","chinese":"學業任務"},{"english":"begin to feel like","chinese":"開始感覺像"},{"english":"an endless conveyor belt","chinese":"永無止境的輸送帶"},{"english":"weaken motivation rather than strengthen it","chinese":"削弱而不是增強動力"},{"english":"a tired child","chinese":"疲累的孩子"},{"english":"complete a worksheet mechanically","chinese":"機械式完成工作紙"},{"english":"not necessarily learning deeply","chinese":"不一定在深入學習"},{"english":"excessive homework","chinese":"過量家課"},{"english":"crowd out","chinese":"擠走；排擠掉"},{"english":"support success at school","chinese":"支持學校成功"},{"english":"social development","chinese":"社交發展"},{"english":"these are not luxuries","chinese":"這些不是奢侈品"},{"english":"return to class with","chinese":"帶着……回到課堂"},{"english":"better concentration","chinese":"更佳專注力"},{"english":"emotional balance","chinese":"情緒平衡"},{"english":"revise lessons","chinese":"複習課堂內容"},{"english":"build study habits","chinese":"建立學習習慣"},{"english":"be treated as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"a requirement for success","chinese":"成功的必要條件"},{"english":"assign homework","chinese":"分配家課"},{"english":"genuinely consolidates learning","chinese":"真正鞏固學習"},{"english":"not simply because","chinese":"不只是因為"},{"english":"another day has passed","chinese":"又過了一天"},{"english":"a balanced approach","chinese":"平衡做法"},{"english":"educationally sound","chinese":"在教育上更合理"},{"english":"a rigid daily routine","chinese":"僵化的每日常規"}]},"model-essay-13-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-13-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:13","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-13-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q13","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In most areas of life, meaningful success does not happen by accident. Many people therefore believe that ambition is indispensable to achievement. I completely agree, because ambition gives people both the endurance to continue through difficulty and the drive to improve until opportunities become tangible results.","chinese":"在生活的大多數範疇中，有意義的成功並不是偶然發生的。 因此，許多人相信，抱負對成就而言是不可或缺的。 我完全同意， 因為抱負既給予人們在困難中堅持下去的耐力，也給予人們不斷進步的動力，直到機會轉化為具體成果。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason ambition is essential is that it sustains effort over long periods of time. Real success normally demands discipline, and ambitious people are far more willing to tolerate inconvenience in order to reach a goal. A student aiming for a highly competitive scholarship, for example, may spend evenings revising, reduce social activities and practise under constant pressure for months. Just as importantly, ambition helps people recover from setbacks instead of abandoning their plans at the first disappointment. When such a student performs badly in an early mock exam, ambition encourages them to analyse weaknesses and try again rather than conclude that success is impossible. Because achievement usually comes after sacrifice and failure, this kind of persistence is not optional; it is fundamental.","chinese":"抱負之所以重要，第一個原因是它能讓人長時間維持努力。 真正的成功通常需要紀律，而有抱負的人為了達成目標，往往更願意忍受種種不便。 例如，一名以競爭激烈的獎學金為目標的學生，可能會在晚上持續溫習、減少社交活動，並在持續壓力下練習數月。 同樣重要的是，抱負能幫助人們在遭遇挫折後重新站起來，而不是在第一次失望時就放棄原本的計劃。 當這樣的學生在早期模擬考中表現欠佳時，抱負會促使他們分析自己的弱點，並再次嘗試，而不是直接認定成功是不可能的。 因為成就通常是在犧牲與失敗之後才出現，這種堅持並不是可有可無的，而是根本性的條件。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Ambition is equally important because it pushes people beyond mere competence. Those who genuinely want to succeed do not simply repeat familiar routines; they actively seek better methods, higher standards and more demanding responsibilities. An ambitious employee, for instance, is more likely to learn new software, request feedback and strengthen communication skills in order to prepare for promotion. Ambition also makes people alert to opportunities that less driven individuals often ignore. The same worker may volunteer for a difficult project or propose an innovative idea to senior managers, thereby gaining both experience and visibility. As a result, ambition does not just improve a person’s ability; it places that ability in situations where it can be recognised and rewarded.","chinese":"抱負同樣重要，因為它能推動人們超越僅僅「勝任」的層次。 真正想成功的人不會只是重複熟悉的做法；他們會主動尋求更好的方法、更高的標準，以及更具挑戰性的責任。 例如，一位有抱負的員工更有可能主動學習新軟件、要求回饋，並加強溝通能力，為晉升作準備。 抱負也會讓人更敏銳地留意那些較缺乏動力的人往往忽略的機會。 同一位員工可能會主動請纓參與艱難的項目，或向高層管理人員提出創新構想，從而同時獲得經驗與曝光機會。 因此，抱負不僅能提升一個人的能力，還能把這種能力放進能夠被看見和獲得回報的情境之中。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely agree that ambition is essential for success. It enables people to endure sacrifice, recover from failure, pursue improvement and seize opportunities, and these are precisely the conditions in which meaningful achievement becomes possible.","chinese":"總而言之，我完全同意抱負對成功而言是不可或缺的。 它使人能夠承受犧牲、從失敗中恢復、追求進步並把握機會，而這些正是有意義的成就得以實現的條件。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"in most areas of life","chinese":"在生活大部分範疇中"},{"english":"meaningful success","chinese":"有意義的成功"},{"english":"happen by accident","chinese":"偶然發生"},{"english":"many people therefore believe that","chinese":"因此很多人相信"},{"english":"ambition","chinese":"雄心；抱負"},{"english":"be indispensable to","chinese":"對……不可或缺"},{"english":"achievement","chinese":"成就"},{"english":"I completely agree","chinese":"我完全同意"},{"english":"give people both","chinese":"同時給予人……和……"},{"english":"the endurance to continue through difficulty","chinese":"面對困難時堅持下去的耐力"},{"english":"the drive to improve","chinese":"進步的動力"},{"english":"tangible results","chinese":"實質成果"},{"english":"the first reason","chinese":"第一個原因"},{"english":"be essential","chinese":"是必要的"},{"english":"sustain effort","chinese":"維持努力"},{"english":"over long periods of time","chinese":"長時間地"},{"english":"real success","chinese":"真正的成功"},{"english":"demand discipline","chinese":"需要自律"},{"english":"be far more willing to","chinese":"更加願意"},{"english":"tolerate inconvenience","chinese":"忍受不便"},{"english":"in order to reach a goal","chinese":"為了達成目標"},{"english":"aim for","chinese":"以……為目標"},{"english":"a highly competitive scholarship","chinese":"競爭非常激烈的獎學金"},{"english":"spend evenings revising","chinese":"晚上花時間溫習"},{"english":"reduce social activities","chinese":"減少社交活動"},{"english":"practise under constant pressure","chinese":"在持續壓力下練習"},{"english":"just as importantly","chinese":"同樣重要的是"},{"english":"recover from setbacks","chinese":"從挫折中恢復過來"},{"english":"instead of","chinese":"而不是"},{"english":"abandon their plans","chinese":"放棄計劃"},{"english":"at the first disappointment","chinese":"一遇到失望便"},{"english":"perform badly","chinese":"表現欠佳"},{"english":"an early mock exam","chinese":"早期的模擬考試"},{"english":"analyse weaknesses","chinese":"分析弱點"},{"english":"try again rather than conclude that","chinese":"再嘗試，而不是斷定"},{"english":"success is impossible","chinese":"成功是不可能的"},{"english":"come after sacrifice and failure","chinese":"在犧牲和失敗之後出現"},{"english":"this kind of persistence","chinese":"這種堅持"},{"english":"not optional","chinese":"並非可有可無"},{"english":"be fundamental","chinese":"是根本的"},{"english":"be equally important","chinese":"同樣重要"},{"english":"push people beyond","chinese":"推動人超越……"},{"english":"mere competence","chinese":"單純稱職；基本能力"},{"english":"genuinely want to succeed","chinese":"真心想成功"},{"english":"simply repeat familiar routines","chinese":"只是重複熟悉的例行工作"},{"english":"familiar routines","chinese":"熟悉的例行工作"},{"english":"actively seek","chinese":"積極尋求"},{"english":"better methods","chinese":"更好的方法"},{"english":"higher standards","chinese":"更高標準"},{"english":"more demanding responsibilities","chinese":"要求更高的責任"},{"english":"for instance","chinese":"例如"},{"english":"be more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"learn new software","chinese":"學習新軟件"},{"english":"request feedback","chinese":"要求回饋"},{"english":"strengthen communication skills","chinese":"加強溝通技巧"},{"english":"prepare for promotion","chinese":"為晉升作準備"},{"english":"make people alert to","chinese":"令某人對……保持敏銳"},{"english":"alert to opportunities","chinese":"對機會保持敏銳"},{"english":"less driven individuals","chinese":"動力較低的人"},{"english":"volunteer for","chinese":"自願參與"},{"english":"a difficult project","chinese":"困難的項目"},{"english":"propose an innovative idea","chinese":"提出創新想法"},{"english":"senior managers","chinese":"高層經理"},{"english":"thereby gaining","chinese":"從而獲得"},{"english":"experience and visibility","chinese":"經驗和曝光機會"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"does not just improve","chinese":"不只是改善"},{"english":"place that ability in situations where","chinese":"將這種能力放在……的情境中"},{"english":"be recognised and rewarded","chinese":"得到認可和獎勵"},{"english":"in conclusion","chinese":"總括而言"},{"english":"enable people to","chinese":"使人能夠"},{"english":"endure sacrifice","chinese":"承受犧牲"},{"english":"recover from failure","chinese":"從失敗中恢復過來"},{"english":"pursue improvement","chinese":"追求進步"},{"english":"seize opportunities","chinese":"把握機會"},{"english":"precisely the conditions in which","chinese":"正正是……的條件"},{"english":"become possible","chinese":"變得可能"}]},"model-essay-14-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-14-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:14","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-14-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q14","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many countries, renting has become a common housing choice, especially in large cities where property prices are extremely high. This arrangement offers several clear advantages, including financial flexibility and greater mobility, although it also brings notable disadvantages, such as insecurity and the absence of long-term ownership benefits.","chinese":"在許多國家，租屋已成為一種常見的居住選擇，尤其是在房價極高的大城市裡更是如此。 雖然這種安排在靈活性和較低的初期成本方面具有明顯優勢， 但它同時也存在一些重要缺點，例如居住上的不穩定性，以及缺乏長遠的財務回報。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One major advantage of renting is that it requires far less money at the outset. Buying a property usually demands a substantial deposit, legal fees and long-term mortgage repayments, whereas renting is far more accessible for young adults, newly married couples and people with modest incomes. As a result, tenants can direct their savings towards other priorities, such as education, childcare or emergency funds. Renting also gives people the freedom to move more easily. If a worker receives a job offer in another city, for instance, it is usually much easier to move at the end of a lease than to sell a home. Moreover, tenants are often spared major repair costs, which would otherwise place a heavy burden on homeowners.","chinese":"租住房屋的一大優點，是它在經濟上比買房容易負擔得多。 購買房產通常需要支付一大筆首期、法律費用以及長期按揭；相比之下，租屋在一開始所需的資金要少得多。 這降低了居住的財務門檻，並使人們——特別是年輕成年人或低收入家庭——可以把儲蓄用於其他重要需要。 例如，一對年輕夫婦可能會選擇租住一個單位，並把金錢用於育兒或進修，而不是讓自己被沉重的按揭負擔綁住。 租屋的另一個好處是，它提供了更高的流動性。 當工作、經濟狀況或家庭情況出現變化時，租客通常能更容易搬遷，而這對業主來說往往困難得多。 例如，一個人在另一個城市獲得工作機會時，可以在租約結束後直接搬走，而不必經歷出售物業那漫長又繁瑣的過程。 因此，租屋之所以具有很大吸引力，是因為它既減少了前期支出，也在充滿不確定性的世界中提供了更大的靈活性。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, renting is not without drawbacks. Perhaps the most serious one is the lack of security it creates. Tenants may face rising rents, restrictive contracts or sudden eviction if the landlord decides to sell the property. This uncertainty can be especially difficult for families with children, whose schooling and social lives may be disrupted by frequent moves. Another disadvantage is that rent payments do not build equity. After years of paying monthly rent, a tenant may have little to show for it financially, while homeowners gradually acquire an asset that may increase in value over time. Renters also have limited control over their living space, since even minor alterations often require the landlord’s approval.","chinese":"然而，租屋也有顯著的缺點，其中最嚴重的便是它所帶來的不穩定感。 如果業主決定出售物業，租客便可能面對租金上升、租約限制，甚至被迫遷出。 這種不確定性會令人難以安頓下來、規劃未來，或建立穩定的家庭生活。 例如，一個有學齡兒童的家庭可能被迫一再搬遷，從而干擾孩子的教育和社交關係。 租屋的另一個缺點是，租金支出最終不會轉化為房產擁有權。 即使多年來持續支付租金，租客也無法累積資產；相反，業主則會逐步擁有一項可能隨時間升值的財產。 例如，一個人若租屋二十年，可能已花費一大筆金錢，但到了最後仍然一無所有。 因此，雖然租屋在短期內可能相當實際，但從長遠來看，它可能使人們在財務和心理上都處於較脆弱的狀態。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In summary, renting can be attractive because it lowers the initial financial barrier, offers flexibility and reduces responsibility for major maintenance. Nevertheless, these benefits are balanced by weaker residential security, limited personal control and the fact that tenants do not accumulate property wealth.","chinese":"總結來說，租住房屋有明顯的優點，尤其是較低的初期成本，以及更大的搬遷自由。 與此同時，它也涉及嚴重的缺點，包括較低的居住穩定性，以及缺乏長遠的財務收益。 正因如此，租屋對某些人來說可以是一種務實的解決方式，但對另一些人而言，則未必是理想的安排。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"renting","chinese":"租樓"},{"english":"a common housing choice","chinese":"常見住屋選擇"},{"english":"large cities","chinese":"大城市"},{"english":"property prices","chinese":"樓價；物業價格"},{"english":"extremely high","chinese":"極高"},{"english":"this arrangement","chinese":"這種安排"},{"english":"clear advantages","chinese":"明顯好處"},{"english":"financial flexibility","chinese":"財政彈性"},{"english":"greater mobility","chinese":"更大的流動性"},{"english":"notable disadvantages","chinese":"明顯缺點"},{"english":"insecurity","chinese":"缺乏保障；不穩定"},{"english":"the absence of","chinese":"缺乏"},{"english":"long-term ownership benefits","chinese":"長期擁有業權的好處"},{"english":"one major advantage of","chinese":"……的一個主要好處"},{"english":"require far less money","chinese":"需要少得多金錢"},{"english":"at the outset","chinese":"一開始"},{"english":"demands a substantial deposit","chinese":"需要大額首期"},{"english":"legal fees","chinese":"律師費；法律費用"},{"english":"long-term mortgage repayments","chinese":"長期按揭還款"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"然而；相比之下"},{"english":"far more accessible for","chinese":"對……容易負擔得多"},{"english":"young adults","chinese":"年輕成年人"},{"english":"newly married couples","chinese":"新婚夫婦"},{"english":"modest incomes","chinese":"中低收入"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"tenants","chinese":"租客"},{"english":"direct their savings towards","chinese":"將積蓄用於"},{"english":"other priorities","chinese":"其他優先事項"},{"english":"childcare","chinese":"照顧子女"},{"english":"emergency funds","chinese":"應急儲備"},{"english":"the freedom to move","chinese":"搬遷的自由"},{"english":"receive a job offer","chinese":"收到工作機會"},{"english":"in another city","chinese":"在另一個城市"},{"english":"at the end of a lease","chinese":"在租約期滿時"},{"english":"sell a home","chinese":"出售住宅"},{"english":"be spared","chinese":"免於承擔"},{"english":"major repair costs","chinese":"大型維修費用"},{"english":"would otherwise place a heavy burden on","chinese":"否則會對……造成沉重負擔"},{"english":"a heavy burden","chinese":"沉重負擔"},{"english":"homeowners","chinese":"自置物業人士；業主"},{"english":"not without drawbacks","chinese":"並非沒有缺點"},{"english":"perhaps the most serious one","chinese":"也許最嚴重的一點"},{"english":"the lack of security","chinese":"缺乏保障"},{"english":"rising rents","chinese":"租金上升"},{"english":"restrictive contracts","chinese":"限制多的合約"},{"english":"sudden eviction","chinese":"突然被迫遷"},{"english":"the landlord","chinese":"業主"},{"english":"sell the property","chinese":"出售物業"},{"english":"this uncertainty","chinese":"這種不確定性"},{"english":"especially difficult for","chinese":"對……尤其困難"},{"english":"schooling and social lives","chinese":"學業和社交生活"},{"english":"be disrupted by","chinese":"受……打亂"},{"english":"frequent moves","chinese":"頻繁搬遷"},{"english":"rent payments","chinese":"租金付款"},{"english":"build equity","chinese":"累積物業權益"},{"english":"monthly rent","chinese":"每月租金"},{"english":"have little to show for it","chinese":"沒有多少實質成果"},{"english":"financially","chinese":"在財政上"},{"english":"acquire an asset","chinese":"獲得一項資產"},{"english":"increase in value over time","chinese":"隨時間升值"},{"english":"limited control over","chinese":"對……控制有限"},{"english":"living space","chinese":"居住空間"},{"english":"minor alterations","chinese":"小型改動"},{"english":"require the landlord's approval","chinese":"需要業主批准"},{"english":"in summary","chinese":"總括而言"},{"english":"be attractive because","chinese":"因為……而具吸引力"},{"english":"lower the initial financial barrier","chinese":"降低最初的財政門檻"},{"english":"initial financial barrier","chinese":"最初的財政門檻"},{"english":"reduce responsibility for","chinese":"減少對……的責任"},{"english":"major maintenance","chinese":"大型維修保養"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"be balanced by","chinese":"被……抵消"},{"english":"residential security","chinese":"居住保障"},{"english":"personal control","chinese":"個人控制權"},{"english":"accumulate property wealth","chinese":"累積物業財富"}]},"model-essay-14-ielts-cause-solution":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-14-ielts-cause-solution","essayKey":"cause-solution:14","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-14-ielts-cause-solution","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/problem-and-cause/EdmundBd9CnS-Q14","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Tourism has made air travel a normal part of modern life, and the rising number of travellers has naturally created greater demand for flights. This essay will discuss the environmental problems caused by this trend, especially carbon emissions and damage around airports, before suggesting practical measures to reduce these effects.","chinese":"旅遊業已經使航空旅行成為現代生活中正常的一部分，而旅客人數的上升自然也創造了對更多航班的更大需求。 本文將討論這一趨勢所造成的環境問題，尤其是碳排放和機場周邊的破壞，然後提出可行的措施來減少這些影響。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The most serious problem is that more flights lead to higher fuel consumption and, therefore, greater greenhouse gas emissions. Aircraft burn large amounts of aviation fuel, so when airlines operate extra routes or increase flight frequency, more carbon dioxide is released into the atmosphere. Over time, this contributes to global warming, which can intensify heatwaves, rising sea levels and extreme weather. A second problem is the environmental pressure created on the ground. Busier airports often require larger terminals, longer runways and heavier road traffic, all of which can disturb nearby habitats and worsen local air and noise pollution. For communities and wildlife living close to airports, the constant movement of planes can become a heavy environmental burden.","chinese":"最嚴重的問題是，更多航班會導致更高的燃料消耗，因此也會帶來更多的溫室氣體排放。 飛機會燃燒大量航空燃料，所以當航空公司營運額外航線或增加航班頻率時，更多二氧化碳便會被釋放到大氣中。 長遠而言，這會加劇全球暖化，而全球暖化可能使熱浪、海平面上升和極端天氣變得更加嚴重。 第二個問題是在地面上造成的環境壓力。 更繁忙的機場通常需要更大的客運大樓、更長的跑道和更密集的道路交通，而這些都可能干擾附近的棲息地，並惡化當地的空氣和噪音污染。 對於居住在機場附近的社區和野生動物而言，飛機不斷升降移動可能會成為沉重的環境負擔"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"There are several measures that could limit these problems. First, governments should encourage cleaner aviation by setting stricter emissions standards and supporting investment in more efficient aircraft, sustainable aviation fuels and better air-traffic management. If planes use less fuel and spend less time circling or waiting on runways, each journey will leave a smaller environmental footprint. Second, countries should reduce unnecessary demand for short flights. For example, high-speed rail, better coach networks and convenient domestic transport can give travellers a realistic alternative when the destination is not far away. Airlines could also be required to include environmental costs in ticket prices, so that extremely cheap flights no longer encourage people to travel casually without considering the impact.","chinese":"有幾項措施可以限制這些問題。 首先，政府應該透過制定更嚴格的排放標準，並支持對更高效飛機、可持續航空燃料和更完善空中交通管理的投資，來鼓勵更清潔的航空業。 如果飛機使用較少燃料，並減少在空中盤旋或在跑道上等待的時間，每一次旅程所留下的環境足跡便會更小。 第二，各國應該減少對短途航班的不必要需求。 例如，當目的地並不遙遠時，高速鐵路、更完善的長途巴士網絡和便利的本地交通可以為旅客提供一個現實可行的替代選擇。 航空公司也可以被要求把環境成本納入機票價格之中，這樣極其便宜的航班便不再鼓勵人們在不考慮影響的情況下隨意出行。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, the rising demand for flights damages the environment mainly through increased emissions and greater pressure around airports. Cleaner technology, stricter regulation and attractive alternatives to flying are therefore necessary to reduce these problems.","chinese":"總結來說，對航班需求的上升主要透過增加排放和加大機場周邊壓力來破壞環境。 因此，更清潔的技術、更嚴格的監管，以及具吸引力的飛行替代方案，都是減少這些問題所必需的。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"air travel","chinese":"航空旅遊；乘搭飛機出行"},{"english":"a normal part of modern life","chinese":"現代生活的正常一部分"},{"english":"the rising number of travellers","chinese":"旅客人數上升"},{"english":"greater demand for flights","chinese":"對航班更大的需求"},{"english":"environmental problems caused by","chinese":"由……造成的環境問題"},{"english":"this trend","chinese":"這個趨勢"},{"english":"carbon emissions","chinese":"碳排放"},{"english":"damage around airports","chinese":"機場周邊的破壞"},{"english":"practical measures","chinese":"實際可行的措施"},{"english":"reduce these effects","chinese":"減少這些影響"},{"english":"the most serious problem","chinese":"最嚴重的問題"},{"english":"lead to","chinese":"導致"},{"english":"higher fuel consumption","chinese":"更高燃料消耗"},{"english":"greenhouse gas emissions","chinese":"溫室氣體排放"},{"english":"burn large amounts of","chinese":"燃燒大量……"},{"english":"aviation fuel","chinese":"航空燃料"},{"english":"operate extra routes","chinese":"營運額外航線"},{"english":"increase flight frequency","chinese":"增加航班班次"},{"english":"be released into the atmosphere","chinese":"被釋放到大氣中"},{"english":"carbon dioxide","chinese":"二氧化碳"},{"english":"contributes to global warming","chinese":"導致；促成全球暖化"},{"english":"intensify heatwaves","chinese":"加劇熱浪"},{"english":"rising sea levels","chinese":"海平面上升"},{"english":"extreme weather","chinese":"極端天氣"},{"english":"environmental pressure","chinese":"環境壓力"},{"english":"created on the ground","chinese":"在地面造成的"},{"english":"busier airports","chinese":"更繁忙的機場"},{"english":"larger terminals","chinese":"更大型客運大樓"},{"english":"longer runways","chinese":"更長跑道"},{"english":"heavier road traffic","chinese":"更繁忙的道路交通"},{"english":"disturb nearby habitats","chinese":"干擾附近棲息地"},{"english":"worsen local air and noise pollution","chinese":"令本地空氣和噪音污染惡化"},{"english":"local air pollution","chinese":"本地空氣污染"},{"english":"noise pollution","chinese":"噪音污染"},{"english":"communities and wildlife","chinese":"社區和野生動物"},{"english":"living close to airports","chinese":"住在／生活在機場附近"},{"english":"the constant movement of planes","chinese":"飛機不停升降和移動"},{"english":"a heavy environmental burden","chinese":"沉重的環境負擔"},{"english":"several measures","chinese":"幾項措施"},{"english":"limit these problems","chinese":"限制；減少這些問題"},{"english":"encourage cleaner aviation","chinese":"推動更清潔的航空業"},{"english":"stricter emissions standards","chinese":"更嚴格的排放標準"},{"english":"supporting investment in","chinese":"支持對……的投資"},{"english":"more efficient aircraft","chinese":"更高效的飛機"},{"english":"sustainable aviation fuels","chinese":"可持續航空燃料"},{"english":"better air-traffic management","chinese":"更好的空中交通管理"},{"english":"use less fuel","chinese":"使用較少燃料"},{"english":"spend less time circling","chinese":"花較少時間盤旋"},{"english":"waiting on runways","chinese":"在跑道上等候"},{"english":"each journey","chinese":"每趟旅程"},{"english":"leave a smaller environmental footprint","chinese":"留下較小的環境足跡"},{"english":"unnecessary demand for","chinese":"對……的不必要需求"},{"english":"short flights","chinese":"短途航班"},{"english":"high-speed rail","chinese":"高速鐵路"},{"english":"better coach networks","chinese":"更完善的長途巴士網絡"},{"english":"convenient domestic transport","chinese":"便利的本地交通"},{"english":"a realistic alternative","chinese":"現實可行的替代選擇"},{"english":"the destination is not far away","chinese":"目的地不遠"},{"english":"be required to","chinese":"被要求去……"},{"english":"include environmental costs in","chinese":"將環境成本包括在……內"},{"english":"ticket prices","chinese":"機票價格"},{"english":"extremely cheap flights","chinese":"極低價航班"},{"english":"travel casually","chinese":"隨意出行"},{"english":"considering the impact","chinese":"考慮影響"},{"english":"rising demand for flights","chinese":"對航班日益上升的需求"},{"english":"increased emissions","chinese":"增加的排放"},{"english":"greater pressure around airports","chinese":"機場周邊更大的壓力"},{"english":"cleaner technology","chinese":"更清潔的技術"},{"english":"stricter regulation","chinese":"更嚴格的規管"},{"english":"attractive alternatives to flying","chinese":"具吸引力的飛行替代方案"}]},"model-essay-14-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-14-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:14","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-14-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q14","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The widening gap between education in wealthy and poor nations is a serious problem because it limits social mobility and traps many young people in cycles of disadvantage. Several practical solutions can reduce this divide, especially if governments, international organisations, and private institutions work together rather than treating education as a local issue alone.","chinese":"富裕國家與貧困國家之間的教育差距不斷擴大，是一個嚴重問題，因為它限制了社會流動，並使許多年輕人陷入劣勢循環之中。 有幾個實際可行的解決方法可以縮小這種差距，尤其是當政府、國際組織和私人機構共同合作，而不是只把教育視為單一地區問題時。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One important solution is to increase long-term investment in basic educational infrastructure. In many poorer countries, students are not failing because they lack ability; they are held back by overcrowded classrooms, poorly equipped schools, and a shortage of trained teachers. International aid should therefore be directed not only towards building schools, but also towards maintaining them, supplying learning materials, and paying teachers properly. For example, a rural school with reliable electricity, internet access, textbooks, and qualified staff would immediately give its students a fairer chance to compete with those in richer countries. Without these foundations, even the most ambitious education reforms will remain paper promises.","chinese":"其中一個重要的解決方法，是增加對基礎教育設施的長期投資。 在許多較貧困的國家，學生失敗並不是因為他們缺乏能力；他們是被過度擁擠的課室、設備不足的學校，以及受過訓練教師的短缺所拖累。 因此，國際援助不應只投向興建學校，也應投向維修保養學校、提供學習材料，以及合理支付教師薪酬。 例如，一所擁有穩定電力、網絡連接、課本和合資格教職員的鄉村學校，會立即給予學生更公平的機會，去與富裕國家的學生競爭。 沒有這些基礎，即使是最有抱負的教育改革，也只會停留在紙上承諾。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another effective approach is to expand teacher training and digital learning. Teachers in poorer regions often have limited access to modern teaching methods, so regular professional development could help them deliver lessons more effectively. At the same time, technology can narrow the educational gap if it is introduced carefully. Online courses, recorded lectures, and low-cost learning platforms can bring high-quality instruction to students who would otherwise have no access to specialist teachers. However, this should not mean simply handing out devices. Governments and charities must also provide affordable internet, technical support, and locally relevant content, so that technology becomes a bridge rather than another barrier.","chinese":"另一個有效方法，是擴大教師培訓和數位學習。 較貧困地區的教師往往較少接觸現代教學方法，因此定期的專業發展可以幫助他們更有效地授課。 同時，如果科技被謹慎地引入，它也可以縮小教育差距。 網上課程、錄影講座和低成本學習平台，可以把高質素教學帶給那些原本無法接觸專科教師的學生。 然而，這不應該只是簡單地派發電子設備。 政府和慈善機構也必須提供可負擔的網絡、技術支援，以及符合本地需要的內容，使科技成為橋樑，而不是另一道障礙。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, the education gap between rich and poor countries cannot be solved by one quick policy. It requires sustained investment in schools, better teacher training, and well-managed digital access. If these measures are combined, poorer countries can give their young people not just classrooms, but genuine opportunities.","chinese":"總結來說，富裕國家與貧困國家之間的教育差距，不能靠一項快速政策解決。 它需要對學校的持續投資、更好的教師培訓，以及管理得宜的數位使用途徑。 如果這些措施能夠結合起來，較貧困的國家便能給予年輕人不只是課室，而是真正的機會"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the widening gap between","chinese":"……之間不斷擴大的差距"},{"english":"wealthy and poor nations","chinese":"富裕和貧窮國家"},{"english":"a serious problem","chinese":"嚴重問題"},{"english":"limits social mobility","chinese":"限制社會流動"},{"english":"traps many young people in","chinese":"令很多年輕人陷入……"},{"english":"cycles of disadvantage","chinese":"惡性劣勢循環"},{"english":"practical solutions","chinese":"實際可行的解決方法"},{"english":"reduce this divide","chinese":"縮小這種差距"},{"english":"international organisations","chinese":"國際組織"},{"english":"private institutions","chinese":"私營機構"},{"english":"work together","chinese":"合作"},{"english":"rather than treating","chinese":"而不是把……視為"},{"english":"a local issue alone","chinese":"單純的本地問題"},{"english":"long-term investment in","chinese":"對……的長期投資"},{"english":"basic educational infrastructure","chinese":"基本教育基礎設施"},{"english":"lack ability","chinese":"缺乏能力"},{"english":"held back by","chinese":"被……拖慢發展；受到……阻礙"},{"english":"overcrowded classrooms","chinese":"過度擠迫的課室"},{"english":"poorly equipped schools","chinese":"設備不足的學校"},{"english":"a shortage of trained teachers","chinese":"受訓教師短缺"},{"english":"international aid","chinese":"國際援助"},{"english":"be directed towards","chinese":"被投放於……"},{"english":"building schools","chinese":"興建學校"},{"english":"maintaining them","chinese":"維修和保養它們"},{"english":"supplying learning materials","chinese":"提供學習材料"},{"english":"paying teachers properly","chinese":"合理支付教師薪酬"},{"english":"a rural school","chinese":"鄉村學校"},{"english":"reliable electricity","chinese":"穩定供電"},{"english":"internet access","chinese":"互聯網接入"},{"english":"qualified staff","chinese":"合資格職員；合資格教師"},{"english":"give its students a fairer chance","chinese":"給學生更公平的機會"},{"english":"compete with","chinese":"與……競爭"},{"english":"those in richer countries","chinese":"較富裕國家的學生"},{"english":"without these foundations","chinese":"沒有這些基礎"},{"english":"ambitious education reforms","chinese":"具雄心的教育改革"},{"english":"remain paper promises","chinese":"只停留在空頭承諾"},{"english":"another effective approach","chinese":"另一個有效方法"},{"english":"expand teacher training","chinese":"擴大教師培訓"},{"english":"digital learning","chinese":"數碼學習"},{"english":"poorer regions","chinese":"較貧窮地區"},{"english":"limited access to","chinese":"有限機會接觸……"},{"english":"modern teaching methods","chinese":"現代教學方法"},{"english":"regular professional development","chinese":"定期專業發展"},{"english":"deliver lessons more effectively","chinese":"更有效地授課"},{"english":"narrow the educational gap","chinese":"縮小教育差距"},{"english":"introduced carefully","chinese":"被謹慎引入"},{"english":"online courses","chinese":"網上課程"},{"english":"recorded lectures","chinese":"錄製講課"},{"english":"low-cost learning platforms","chinese":"低成本學習平台"},{"english":"high-quality instruction","chinese":"高質素教學"},{"english":"would otherwise have no access to","chinese":"否則無法接觸到……"},{"english":"specialist teachers","chinese":"專科教師"},{"english":"handing out devices","chinese":"派發裝置"},{"english":"affordable internet","chinese":"負擔得起的互聯網"},{"english":"technical support","chinese":"技術支援"},{"english":"locally relevant content","chinese":"切合本地需要的內容"},{"english":"becomes a bridge rather than another barrier","chinese":"成為橋樑，而不是另一道障礙"},{"english":"cannot be solved by","chinese":"不能靠……解決"},{"english":"one quick policy","chinese":"一項速成政策"},{"english":"sustained investment in schools","chinese":"對學校的持續投資"},{"english":"better teacher training","chinese":"更好的教師培訓"},{"english":"well-managed digital access","chinese":"管理得宜的數碼接入"},{"english":"if these measures are combined","chinese":"如果這些措施結合起來"},{"english":"genuine opportunities","chinese":"真正的機會"}]},"model-essay-14-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-14-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:14","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-14-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q14","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"It is sometimes argued that children should spend their spare time on educational pursuits, while others believe that this creates unnecessary pressure. I agree with the latter view, because childhood free time should mainly serve recovery, play, and social development rather than become an extension of the classroom.","chinese":"有人有時主張，孩子應該把空閒時間用於教育活動，而另一些人則認為，這樣做會造成不必要的壓力。 我同意後者的觀點，因為童年的空閒時間應該主要用於恢復精力、玩樂和社交發展，而不是成為課堂的延伸。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Those who support educational activities make a reasonable point. Many parents worry that unstructured leisure will be wasted on screens, games, or passive entertainment. If children use part of their free time to read, practise a language, learn music, or solve puzzles, they may strengthen useful skills in a less formal setting. Such activities can also build discipline: a child who gets used to reading after school, for example, may develop concentration and curiosity that support later academic success. From this perspective, educational leisure is not a punishment but a way of planting seeds for the future.","chinese":"支持教育活動的人提出了一個合理的觀點。 許多父母擔心，沒有安排的休閒時間會被浪費在螢幕、遊戲或被動娛樂上。 如果孩子利用部分空閒時間閱讀、練習語言、學習音樂或解謎，他們便可能在較非正式的環境中強化有用的技能。 這些活動也能培養自律：例如，一個習慣放學後閱讀的孩子，可能會培養出有助於日後學業成功的專注力和好奇心。 從這個角度來看，教育性休閒並不是一種懲罰，而是一種為未來播種的方式。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, I believe that turning free time into another learning session places children under harmful pressure. After school, many children are already mentally tired from lessons, homework, tests, and constant evaluation. If their evenings and weekends are filled with extra academic tasks, rest disappears, and learning begins to feel like a cage rather than a source of growth. A child who moves from school to tuition to online exercises may appear productive, but in reality they may become anxious, resentful, and less motivated. This is especially damaging because play is not an empty time. Through games, sport, imagination, and casual conversation, children learn cooperation, emotional control, independence, and problem-solving in ways that worksheets cannot easily provide.","chinese":"然而，我認為，把空閒時間變成另一段學習時間，會使孩子承受有害的壓力。 放學後，許多孩子已經因為課堂、功課、測驗和持續評估而在精神上感到疲累。 如果他們的晚上和週末都被額外的學業任務填滿，休息便會消失，而學習也會開始像一個牢籠，而不是成長的來源。 一個從學校到補習、再到網上練習的孩子，表面上可能看起來很有成效，但實際上他們可能會變得焦慮、反感，並且更缺乏動力。 這尤其有害，因為玩樂並不是空白的時間。 透過遊戲、運動、想像和日常交談，孩子能以工作紙難以輕易提供的方式，學習合作、情緒控制、獨立性和解決問題的能力。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, although this parental approach may have good intentions, I firmly believe that children should not be expected to spend their free time studying. Childhood should not be scheduled so tightly that every spare hour has an academic purpose. Free time is not wasted time; it is where children breathe, grow, and become whole people.","chinese":"總結來說，儘管這種父母的做法可能出於好意，但我堅定地認為，孩子不應被期望把空閒時間用於學習。 童年不應被安排得如此緊密，以至於每一個空閒小時都有學業目的。 空閒時間並不是被浪費的時間；它是孩子得以喘息、成長，並成為完整的人的地方。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"it is sometimes argued that","chinese":"有時有人認為"},{"english":"spare time","chinese":"空餘時間"},{"english":"educational pursuits","chinese":"教育性活動；學習追求"},{"english":"unnecessary pressure","chinese":"不必要壓力"},{"english":"the latter view","chinese":"後者觀點"},{"english":"childhood free time","chinese":"童年空餘時間"},{"english":"serve recovery, play, and social development","chinese":"用於恢復、玩樂和社交發展"},{"english":"rather than become","chinese":"而不是變成"},{"english":"an extension of the classroom","chinese":"課室的延伸"},{"english":"support educational activities","chinese":"支持教育性活動"},{"english":"make a reasonable point","chinese":"提出合理觀點"},{"english":"unstructured leisure","chinese":"沒有安排的休閒時間"},{"english":"be wasted on","chinese":"被浪費在"},{"english":"screens, games, or passive entertainment","chinese":"螢幕、遊戲或被動娛樂"},{"english":"use part of their free time to","chinese":"用部分空餘時間去"},{"english":"practise a language","chinese":"練習一種語言"},{"english":"learn music","chinese":"學音樂"},{"english":"solve puzzles","chinese":"解謎題"},{"english":"strengthen useful skills","chinese":"加強有用技能"},{"english":"in a less formal setting","chinese":"在較非正式的環境中"},{"english":"build discipline","chinese":"培養自律"},{"english":"get used to","chinese":"習慣於"},{"english":"reading after school","chinese":"放學後閱讀"},{"english":"develop concentration and curiosity","chinese":"培養專注力和好奇心"},{"english":"later academic success","chinese":"日後學業成功"},{"english":"from this perspective","chinese":"從這個角度來看"},{"english":"educational leisure","chinese":"教育性休閒活動"},{"english":"not a punishment but","chinese":"不是懲罰，而是"},{"english":"plant seeds for the future","chinese":"為將來播下種子"},{"english":"turning free time into","chinese":"將空餘時間變成"},{"english":"another learning session","chinese":"另一節學習時間"},{"english":"place children under harmful pressure","chinese":"令兒童承受有害壓力"},{"english":"mentally tired from","chinese":"因……而精神疲累"},{"english":"constant evaluation","chinese":"持續評核"},{"english":"be filled with","chinese":"充滿"},{"english":"extra academic tasks","chinese":"額外學業任務"},{"english":"rest disappears","chinese":"休息消失"},{"english":"feel like a cage rather than","chinese":"感覺像牢籠，而不是"},{"english":"a source of growth","chinese":"成長的來源"},{"english":"move from school to tuition to","chinese":"從學校轉到補習再到"},{"english":"tuition","chinese":"補習"},{"english":"online exercises","chinese":"網上練習"},{"english":"appear productive","chinese":"看似有成效"},{"english":"in reality","chinese":"實際上"},{"english":"anxious, resentful, and less motivated","chinese":"焦慮、憤恨和較缺乏動力"},{"english":"especially damaging","chinese":"尤其有害"},{"english":"not an empty time","chinese":"不是空白無用的時間"},{"english":"through games, sport, imagination, and casual conversation","chinese":"透過遊戲、運動、想像和輕鬆交談"},{"english":"cooperation","chinese":"合作"},{"english":"emotional control","chinese":"情緒控制"},{"english":"independence and problem-solving","chinese":"獨立性和解難能力"},{"english":"worksheets","chinese":"工作紙"},{"english":"cannot easily provide","chinese":"不能輕易提供"},{"english":"parental approach","chinese":"家長做法"},{"english":"good intentions","chinese":"良好原意"},{"english":"be expected to","chinese":"被期望去"},{"english":"spend their free time studying","chinese":"用空餘時間學習"},{"english":"be scheduled so tightly","chinese":"被安排得如此緊密"},{"english":"every spare hour","chinese":"每一個空餘小時"},{"english":"an academic purpose","chinese":"學業目的"},{"english":"wasted time","chinese":"浪費了的時間"},{"english":"breathe, grow, and become whole people","chinese":"喘息、成長並成為完整的人"}]},"model-essay-14-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-14-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:14","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-14-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q14","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many societies, successful people are often imagined as confident, magnetic, and naturally charming. As a result, some argue that charisma is a necessary ingredient for achievement. I completely disagree with this view, because long-term success depends far more on competence, discipline, and trustworthiness than on personal charm.","chinese":"在許多社會中，成功人士常常被想像成自信、有吸引力，而且天生具有人格魅力的人。因此，有些人認為個人魅力是取得成就的必要條件。 我完全不同意這個觀點，因為長期的成功更多取決於能力、自律和可靠性，而不是個人魅力。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main reason charisma is not essential is that many forms of success are built on skill rather than social appeal. In most professions, people are ultimately judged by whether they can solve problems, make sound decisions, and deliver consistent results. A doctor, for example, does not become successful simply by speaking warmly to patients; he or she must diagnose illnesses accurately and provide effective treatment. Similarly, an engineer whose work prevents a bridge from collapsing may be quiet and socially reserved, but that does not make the achievement any less valuable. In these cases, charisma may make communication smoother, but it cannot replace expertise. Success is therefore more like a foundation than a spotlight: what matters most is not how brightly a person shines in public, but how solidly they perform when real responsibility is placed on them.","chinese":"個人魅力並非必不可少的主要原因是，許多形式的成功是建立在技能之上，而不是建立在社交吸引力之上。 在大多數職業中，人們最終會根據他們是否能解決問題、作出明智決定，並持續交出穩定成果來受到評價。 例如，一名醫生並不會單純因為能親切地和病人說話而成功；他或她必須準確診斷疾病，並提供有效的治療。 同樣地，一名工程師的工作如果能防止一座橋倒塌，即使他可能安靜且不擅社交，這也不會令他的成就變得較不重要。 在這些情況下，個人魅力也許能讓溝通更順暢，但它不能取代專業能力。 因此，成功更像是一個基礎，而不是一道聚光燈：最重要的並不是一個人在公眾面前閃耀得多麼耀眼，而是當真正的責任落在他身上時，他能表現得多麼穩健。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that charisma without substance can be fragile, and sometimes even dangerous. Charismatic people may attract attention quickly, but attention is not the same as achievement. If a leader is charming but unreliable, employees may initially feel inspired, yet they will soon lose confidence when promises are broken or decisions are poorly made. By contrast, a less charismatic person who is honest, prepared, and dependable can gradually earn deep respect. This kind of respect is quieter, but it lasts longer. In business, education, and public life, people eventually trust results more than attractive words.","chinese":"另一個原因是，沒有實質能力支撐的個人魅力可能很脆弱，有時甚至會很危險。 有魅力的人也許能很快吸引注意力，但注意力並不等同於成就。 如果一位領導者很有魅力但不可靠，員工起初可能會受到鼓舞，但當承諾被打破或決策做得很差時，他們很快就會失去信心。 相比之下，一個魅力較少但誠實、有準備且可靠的人，能夠逐漸贏得深厚的尊重。 這種尊重較為安靜，但卻更持久。 在商業、教育和公共生活中，人們最終會信任成果多於動聽的言辭。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, charisma can be useful, but it is not essential for success. Real success is built on ability, consistency, and integrity, not merely on the power to impress others.","chinese":"總結來說，個人魅力可以是有用的，但它並不是成功所必需的。 真正的成功是建立在能力、穩定性和誠信之上，而不僅僅是建立在打動他人的能力之上"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"in many societies","chinese":"在很多社會中"},{"english":"be imagined as","chinese":"被想像成"},{"english":"confident, magnetic, and naturally charming","chinese":"自信、有吸引力而且天生有魅力"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"argue that","chinese":"主張；認為"},{"english":"charisma","chinese":"個人魅力"},{"english":"a necessary ingredient for achievement","chinese":"成就的必要因素"},{"english":"completely disagree with this view","chinese":"完全不同意這個看法"},{"english":"long-term success","chinese":"長遠的成功"},{"english":"depend far more on","chinese":"更大程度上取決於"},{"english":"competence, discipline, and trustworthiness","chinese":"能力、自律和可靠"},{"english":"personal charm","chinese":"個人魅力"},{"english":"the main reason","chinese":"主要原因"},{"english":"not essential","chinese":"並非必要"},{"english":"many forms of success","chinese":"很多形式的成功"},{"english":"be built on","chinese":"建基於"},{"english":"rather than","chinese":"而不是"},{"english":"social appeal","chinese":"社交吸引力"},{"english":"in most professions","chinese":"在大多數職業中"},{"english":"be ultimately judged by","chinese":"最終根據……被評價"},{"english":"solve problems","chinese":"解決問題"},{"english":"make sound decisions","chinese":"作出明智決定"},{"english":"deliver consistent results","chinese":"持續取得穩定成果"},{"english":"become successful simply by","chinese":"單靠……而成功"},{"english":"speak warmly to","chinese":"溫和親切地對……說話"},{"english":"diagnose illnesses accurately","chinese":"準確診斷疾病"},{"english":"provide effective treatment","chinese":"提供有效治療"},{"english":"similarly","chinese":"同樣地"},{"english":"prevent a bridge from collapsing","chinese":"防止橋樑倒塌"},{"english":"socially reserved","chinese":"不太擅長社交；性格較內斂"},{"english":"make the achievement any less valuable","chinese":"令成就變得較不值錢"},{"english":"in these cases","chinese":"在這些情況下"},{"english":"make communication smoother","chinese":"令溝通更順暢"},{"english":"cannot replace expertise","chinese":"不能取代專業知識"},{"english":"be more like a foundation than a spotlight","chinese":"更像基礎，而不是聚光燈"},{"english":"what matters most is not","chinese":"最重要的不是"},{"english":"shine in public","chinese":"在公眾面前發光發亮"},{"english":"perform solidly","chinese":"表現穩健"},{"english":"real responsibility","chinese":"真正的責任"},{"english":"be placed on","chinese":"落在……身上"},{"english":"another reason is that","chinese":"另一個原因是"},{"english":"without substance","chinese":"缺乏實質內容"},{"english":"can be fragile","chinese":"可能很脆弱"},{"english":"attract attention quickly","chinese":"很快吸引注意"},{"english":"attention is not the same as achievement","chinese":"受關注不等於有成就"},{"english":"charming but unreliable","chinese":"有魅力但不可靠"},{"english":"initially feel inspired","chinese":"起初感到受鼓舞"},{"english":"lose confidence","chinese":"失去信心"},{"english":"promises are broken","chinese":"承諾被打破"},{"english":"decisions are poorly made","chinese":"決策做得差"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相反"},{"english":"a less charismatic person","chinese":"魅力較少的人"},{"english":"honest, prepared, and dependable","chinese":"誠實、有準備而可靠"},{"english":"gradually earn deep respect","chinese":"逐漸贏得深厚尊重"},{"english":"this kind of respect","chinese":"這種尊重"},{"english":"last longer","chinese":"維持更久"},{"english":"in business, education, and public life","chinese":"在商業、教育和公共生活中"},{"english":"eventually trust results more than attractive words","chinese":"最終更相信成果，而不是動聽說話"},{"english":"in conclusion","chinese":"總括而言"},{"english":"can be useful, but not essential","chinese":"可以有用，但並非必要"},{"english":"real success is built on","chinese":"真正的成功建基於"},{"english":"ability, consistency, and integrity","chinese":"能力、穩定性和誠信"},{"english":"not merely on","chinese":"不只是建基於"},{"english":"the power to impress others","chinese":"令人留下深刻印象的能力"}]},"model-essay-15-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-15-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:15","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-15-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q15","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many education systems, children are encouraged to begin learning a foreign language in primary school rather than in their teenage years. While this policy can create practical problems, I believe it is beneficial because younger learners acquire languages more easily and early instruction gives all pupils opportunities later in life.","chinese":"在許多教育制度中，兒童被鼓勵在小學階段而非青少年時期才開始學習外語。 雖然這項政策可能帶來一些實際問題， 我認為這樣做是有益的，因為年紀較小的學習者更容易掌握語言，而及早接受外語教育也能為所有學生在日後提供更多機會。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The chief advantage is that young children absorb pronunciation and sentence patterns with unusual ease. Because they are less self-conscious than adolescents, they are usually more willing to repeat unfamiliar sounds, make mistakes and try again. This creates a chain effect: frequent practice improves memory, stronger memory builds fluency, and growing fluency makes later study far less intimidating. For example, a six-year-old who learns songs, greetings and simple classroom expressions often becomes a more confident speaker in secondary school than a student who starts with grammar at thirteen. Early language education also promotes fairness. If schools provide it to all children, the benefits of speaking another language, such as cultural awareness and better study or work options, are not limited to those whose parents can afford private lessons.","chinese":"在年幼時學習外語的主要優點，在於孩子能夠更自然、更有自信地吸收這門語言。 年紀較小的學習者通常比年長學生更容易模仿發音和基本句型。 由於他們較少感到難為情，也較不害怕犯錯，因此往往更願意反覆練習；持續練習會加強記憶，更好的記憶會培養流暢度，而更高的流暢度則使日後的學習不那麼令人畏懼。 例如，一個六歲時便學習歌曲、問候語及簡單課堂用語的孩子，到了中學階段往往會比十三歲才開始正式學習文法的學生更有口語自信。 及早進行外語教育也能促進公平，因為它讓所有孩子都有機會接觸有價值的語言能力。 如果學校為所有學生提供外語教學，那麼更廣闊的文化視野以及更好的升學或就業機會，便不會只屬於那些負擔得起私人補習的家庭的孩子。 例如，來自低收入家庭的孩子即使無力負擔私人補習，仍然可以透過學校教育培養實用的語言能力。 因此，及早學習外語既能提升長遠的語言能力，也能促進機會平等。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The disadvantages are real but less significant. One problem is that badly designed lessons can create pressure. If young pupils are forced to memorise long vocabulary lists and are corrected too harshly, enjoyment can turn into anxiety, which reduces participation and weakens motivation. Another drawback is that, in poorly resourced schools, adding a compulsory subject may take time away from essential literacy work. For instance, a school with too few trained staff may squeeze basic language drills into a crowded timetable while weaker readers still need support in their first language. However, these are problems of implementation rather than proof that early language learning is misguided.","chinese":"然而，及早推行外語教育確實也有缺點，尤其是在實施方式欠佳的情況下。 其中一個問題是，設計不良的課程可能帶來壓力，而不是激發好奇心。 如果年幼學生被迫背誦冗長的單字表，並且在犯錯時受到過於嚴厲的糾正，原本的樂趣便可能轉化為焦慮；一旦焦慮取代了好奇心，學生的參與度便會下降，自信心會減弱，持續學習的動機也會隨之降低。 例如，一個孩子若因發音錯誤而一再受到批評，最終可能會在課堂上完全不願開口。 另一個缺點是，在資源不足的學校中，加入一門必修外語課程可能會擠壓基礎讀寫教育的時間。 當課程表本已十分緊湊，而受過專業訓練的教師又不足時，學校可能會把過多時間投入外語基本操練，然而閱讀能力較弱的學生其實仍需要母語方面的支援。 例如，一所合資格教師不足的小學，可能會為了把外語課塞進本已擁擠的課程安排中，而減少閱讀支援課節。 然而，這些問題反映的其實是實施不當，而非及早學習外語本身有何缺陷。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, teaching a foreign language at an early age has some disadvantages, especially when schools lack time or expertise, but the advantages are clearly greater. It helps children develop stronger long-term language ability and ensures that these benefits are available to all, not just the most privileged.","chinese":"總結而言，幼年開始學習外語確實存在一些缺點，尤其是在學校缺乏時間或專業能力的情況下，但其優點顯然更大。 它不但有助於孩子培養更強的長遠語言能力，也確保這些好處能夠惠及所有學生，而不只是最有優勢的一群。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"education systems","chinese":"教育制度"},{"english":"be encouraged to","chinese":"被鼓勵去……"},{"english":"begin learning a foreign language","chinese":"開始學習外語"},{"english":"primary school","chinese":"小學"},{"english":"rather than in","chinese":"而不是在……"},{"english":"teenage years","chinese":"青少年時期"},{"english":"this policy","chinese":"這項政策"},{"english":"create practical problems","chinese":"造成實際問題"},{"english":"beneficial because","chinese":"有益，因為……"},{"english":"younger learners","chinese":"較年幼的學習者"},{"english":"acquire languages","chinese":"學會語言"},{"english":"early instruction","chinese":"早期教學"},{"english":"opportunities later in life","chinese":"人生較後階段的機會"},{"english":"the chief advantage","chinese":"主要好處"},{"english":"absorb pronunciation and sentence patterns","chinese":"吸收發音和句式"},{"english":"with unusual ease","chinese":"異常容易地"},{"english":"less self-conscious than","chinese":"比……較少自我拘束"},{"english":"adolescents","chinese":"青少年"},{"english":"willing to repeat","chinese":"願意重複"},{"english":"unfamiliar sounds","chinese":"陌生的聲音"},{"english":"make mistakes and try again","chinese":"犯錯並再試"},{"english":"creates a chain effect","chinese":"產生連鎖效應"},{"english":"frequent practice","chinese":"頻繁練習"},{"english":"improves memory","chinese":"改善記憶"},{"english":"builds fluency","chinese":"建立流暢度"},{"english":"growing fluency","chinese":"不斷提升的流暢度"},{"english":"far less intimidating","chinese":"沒那麼令人畏懼"},{"english":"a six-year-old","chinese":"六歲小朋友"},{"english":"simple classroom expressions","chinese":"簡單課堂用語"},{"english":"a more confident speaker","chinese":"更有信心的說話者"},{"english":"secondary school","chinese":"中學"},{"english":"starts with grammar","chinese":"從文法開始"},{"english":"early language education","chinese":"早期語言教育"},{"english":"promotes fairness","chinese":"促進公平"},{"english":"provide it to all children","chinese":"向所有兒童提供"},{"english":"the benefits of speaking another language","chinese":"學會另一種語言的好處"},{"english":"cultural awareness","chinese":"文化意識"},{"english":"better study or work options","chinese":"更好的升學或工作選擇"},{"english":"be limited to","chinese":"只限於……"},{"english":"afford private lessons","chinese":"負擔得起私人補習"},{"english":"less significant","chinese":"較不重要"},{"english":"badly designed lessons","chinese":"設計欠佳的課堂"},{"english":"create pressure","chinese":"造成壓力"},{"english":"young pupils","chinese":"年幼學生"},{"english":"be forced to memorise","chinese":"被迫死記"},{"english":"long vocabulary lists","chinese":"長長的生字表"},{"english":"corrected too harshly","chinese":"被過分嚴厲地糾正"},{"english":"turn into anxiety","chinese":"變成焦慮"},{"english":"reduces participation","chinese":"減少參與"},{"english":"weakens motivation","chinese":"削弱動力"},{"english":"another drawback","chinese":"另一個缺點"},{"english":"poorly resourced schools","chinese":"資源不足的學校"},{"english":"adding a compulsory subject","chinese":"增加一科必修科"},{"english":"take time away from","chinese":"佔用……的時間"},{"english":"essential literacy work","chinese":"基本讀寫訓練"},{"english":"too few trained staff","chinese":"受訓教師太少；受訓人手太少"},{"english":"squeeze basic language drills into","chinese":"將基本語言操練硬擠進……"},{"english":"basic language drills","chinese":"基本語言操練"},{"english":"a crowded timetable","chinese":"排得很滿的時間表"},{"english":"weaker readers","chinese":"閱讀能力較弱的學生"},{"english":"their first language","chinese":"他們的第一語言"},{"english":"problems of implementation","chinese":"執行上的問題"},{"english":"proof that","chinese":"……的證據"},{"english":"early language learning","chinese":"早期語言學習"},{"english":"misguided","chinese":"方向錯誤的"},{"english":"at an early age","chinese":"在年幼時"},{"english":"lack time or expertise","chinese":"缺乏時間或專業知識"},{"english":"clearly greater","chinese":"明顯更大"},{"english":"long-term language ability","chinese":"長遠語言能力"},{"english":"not just the most privileged","chinese":"不只是最有優勢的人"}]},"model-essay-15-ielts-cause-solution":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-15-ielts-cause-solution","essayKey":"cause-solution:15","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-15-ielts-cause-solution","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/problem-and-cause/EdmundBd9CnS-Q15","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Eco-tourism is often promoted as a responsible way to travel, but when visitors enter remote areas, they can place serious pressure on local cultures and communities. This essay will discuss the cultural and social problems that may result from eco-tourism, before suggesting practical measures to protect local people and their traditions.","chinese":"生態旅遊通常被宣傳為一種負責任的旅行方式，但當遊客進入偏遠地區時，他們可能會對當地文化和社區造成嚴重壓力。 本文將討論生態旅遊可能帶來的文化和社會問題，然後提出保護當地居民及其傳統的實際措施。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One major problem is that local culture may be commercialised. When tourists are willing to pay for “authentic” experiences, traditional ceremonies, clothing, music, and religious practices may gradually be turned into performances. As a result, customs that once had deep spiritual or social meaning can become little more than tourist attractions. This can weaken local identity, especially among younger people, who may start to see their own culture as something to sell rather than something to preserve. Another problem is that remote communities may be disrupted by sudden outside influence. Tourists can bring different values, spending habits, and expectations, which may change local behaviour and increase tension between residents and visitors. In some cases, prices for food, land, and services may rise, making everyday life harder for local families.","chinese":"其中一個主要問題是，當地文化可能會被商業化。 當遊客願意為「地道」體驗付費時，傳統儀式、服飾、音樂和宗教習俗可能會逐漸被變成表演。 結果是，原本具有深厚精神或社會意義的習俗，可能會變得只不過是旅遊景點而已。 這可能會削弱當地身份認同，尤其是在年輕人當中，因為他們可能會開始把自己的文化看成可以出售的東西，而不是應該保存的東西。 另一個問題是，偏遠社區可能會受到突然出現的外來影響所干擾。 遊客可能會帶來不同的價值觀、消費習慣和期望，而這些可能會改變當地人的行為，並增加居民與遊客之間的緊張關係。 在某些情況下，食物、土地和服務的價格可能會上升，使當地家庭的日常生活變得更加困難"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Several measures can be taken to reduce these problems. First, eco-tourism should be controlled by local communities rather than outside companies. Local leaders should decide how many tourists may visit, which areas are open to outsiders, and which cultural practices should remain private. This would allow communities to benefit from tourism without losing control of their way of life. Second, governments and tourism operators should introduce clear rules for visitors. For example, tourists should be educated about local customs, dress codes, sacred sites, and acceptable behaviour before entering remote areas. Visitor numbers should also be limited, and part of the income from eco-tourism should be used to support local schools, cultural centres, healthcare, and environmental protection.","chinese":"可以採取幾項措施來減少這些問題。 首先，生態旅遊應該由當地社區控制，而不是由外來公司控制。 當地領袖應該決定可以接待多少遊客、哪些地區可以向外來者開放，以及哪些文化習俗應該保持私密。 這能讓社區從旅遊中受益，同時不會失去對自身生活方式的控制。 第二，政府和旅遊營運者應該為遊客制定清晰的規則。 例如，在進入偏遠地區之前，遊客應該接受有關當地習俗、服裝規範、神聖場所和可接受行為的教育。 遊客人數也應該受到限制，而生態旅遊收入的一部分應該用來支持當地學校、文化中心、醫療服務和環境保護。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, eco-tourism can damage remote communities by commercialising culture and disturbing local life. However, community control, visitor education, and careful regulation can help protect local traditions while still allowing tourism to bring economic benefits.","chinese":"總結來說，生態旅遊可能會透過將文化商業化和干擾當地生活，對偏遠社區造成傷害。 然而，社區控制、遊客教育和審慎規管可以幫助保護當地傳統，同時仍然讓旅遊帶來經濟利益。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"eco-tourism","chinese":"生態旅遊"},{"english":"be promoted as","chinese":"被宣傳為"},{"english":"a responsible way to travel","chinese":"負責任的旅遊方式"},{"english":"enter remote areas","chinese":"進入偏遠地區"},{"english":"place serious pressure on","chinese":"對……造成嚴重壓力"},{"english":"local cultures and communities","chinese":"本地文化和社區"},{"english":"cultural and social problems","chinese":"文化和社會問題"},{"english":"may result from","chinese":"可能由……引起"},{"english":"practical measures","chinese":"實際措施"},{"english":"local people and their traditions","chinese":"本地居民及其傳統"},{"english":"one major problem","chinese":"一個主要問題"},{"english":"local culture","chinese":"本地文化"},{"english":"be commercialised","chinese":"被商業化"},{"english":"be willing to pay for","chinese":"願意付錢購買"},{"english":"authentic experiences","chinese":"原汁原味的體驗"},{"english":"traditional ceremonies","chinese":"傳統儀式"},{"english":"religious practices","chinese":"宗教習俗"},{"english":"gradually be turned into","chinese":"逐漸被變成"},{"english":"performances","chinese":"表演"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"customs","chinese":"習俗"},{"english":"deep spiritual or social meaning","chinese":"深層的精神或社會意義"},{"english":"become little more than","chinese":"變得只不過是"},{"english":"tourist attractions","chinese":"旅遊景點；遊客賣點"},{"english":"weaken local identity","chinese":"削弱本地身份認同"},{"english":"especially among younger people","chinese":"尤其在年輕人之中"},{"english":"start to see","chinese":"開始視為"},{"english":"their own culture","chinese":"他們自己的文化"},{"english":"something to sell rather than something to preserve","chinese":"可出售的東西，而不是要保育的東西"},{"english":"remote communities","chinese":"偏遠社區"},{"english":"be disrupted by","chinese":"被……擾亂"},{"english":"sudden outside influence","chinese":"突然的外來影響"},{"english":"bring different values","chinese":"帶來不同價值觀"},{"english":"spending habits","chinese":"消費習慣"},{"english":"expectations","chinese":"期望"},{"english":"change local behaviour","chinese":"改變本地人的行為"},{"english":"increase tension between","chinese":"增加……之間的緊張關係"},{"english":"residents and visitors","chinese":"居民和遊客"},{"english":"in some cases","chinese":"在某些情況下"},{"english":"prices for food, land, and services","chinese":"食物、土地和服務的價格"},{"english":"making everyday life harder for","chinese":"令……的日常生活更困難"},{"english":"local families","chinese":"本地家庭"},{"english":"several measures can be taken","chinese":"可以採取幾項措施"},{"english":"reduce these problems","chinese":"減少這些問題"},{"english":"be controlled by","chinese":"由……控制"},{"english":"rather than outside companies","chinese":"而不是由外來公司"},{"english":"local leaders","chinese":"本地領袖"},{"english":"decide how many tourists may visit","chinese":"決定可以有多少遊客到訪"},{"english":"open to outsiders","chinese":"向外來人士開放"},{"english":"cultural practices","chinese":"文化習俗"},{"english":"remain private","chinese":"保持私人；不對外公開"},{"english":"allow communities to benefit from","chinese":"讓社區從……受惠"},{"english":"without losing control of","chinese":"而不會失去對……的控制"},{"english":"their way of life","chinese":"他們的生活方式"},{"english":"tourism operators","chinese":"旅遊營辦商"},{"english":"introduce clear rules for","chinese":"為……引入清晰規則"},{"english":"be educated about","chinese":"接受有關……的教育"},{"english":"local customs","chinese":"本地習俗"},{"english":"dress codes","chinese":"衣着規定"},{"english":"sacred sites","chinese":"神聖地點"},{"english":"acceptable behaviour","chinese":"可接受的行為"},{"english":"visitor numbers","chinese":"遊客人數"},{"english":"be limited","chinese":"被限制"},{"english":"part of the income from","chinese":"來自……的部分收入"},{"english":"support local schools","chinese":"支援本地學校"},{"english":"cultural centres","chinese":"文化中心"},{"english":"healthcare","chinese":"醫療服務"},{"english":"environmental protection","chinese":"環境保護"},{"english":"damage remote communities","chinese":"損害偏遠社區"},{"english":"commercialising culture","chinese":"將文化商業化"},{"english":"disturbing local life","chinese":"擾亂本地生活"},{"english":"community control","chinese":"社區主導"},{"english":"visitor education","chinese":"遊客教育"},{"english":"careful regulation","chinese":"審慎規管"},{"english":"while still allowing","chinese":"同時仍然容許"},{"english":"bring economic benefits","chinese":"帶來經濟利益"}]},"model-essay-15-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-15-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:15","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-15-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q15","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In several secondary schools, students are expected to take part in community service, including supporting elderly people or those with disabilities. I believe this benefits young people by developing empathy and practical maturity, and it should definitely be included in the school curriculum.","chinese":"在一些中學裡，學生被要求參與社區服務，包括支援長者或殘疾人士。 我認為這能透過培養同理心和實際成熟度來令年輕人受益，而且它絕對應該被納入學校課程之中。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The clearest benefit is that community work helps students become more compassionate and socially aware. Many teenagers spend most of their time with people of a similar age, so their understanding of hardship can remain quite limited. When they assist an elderly person with daily tasks or spend time with someone who has a disability, they begin to see that vulnerability is not an abstract idea but a real part of human life. This experience can teach patience, respect, and responsibility far more effectively than a lecture in a classroom. For example, a student who helps an elderly resident use a phone or carry groceries may realise how small acts of kindness can make another person’s day easier. In this way, community service can turn moral values from empty words into lived experience.","chinese":"最明顯的好處是，社區服務能幫助學生變得更有同情心，也更具社會意識。 許多青少年大部分時間都和年齡相近的人相處，因此他們對困難處境的理解可能仍然相當有限。 當他們協助長者處理日常事務，或與殘疾人士共度時間時，他們便開始明白，脆弱並不是一個抽象概念，而是人類生活中真實存在的一部分。 這種經歷比課堂上的講授更能有效地教會學生耐性、尊重和責任感。 例如，一名學生如果幫助一位年長居民使用電話或提購物袋，可能會意識到小小的善意行為如何能令另一個人的一天變得更容易。 透過這種方式，社區服務可以把道德價值從空洞的說話轉化為真實的生活經驗。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"I also think this should be a formal part of the curriculum because schools should educate character as well as academic ability. If community work is left entirely to personal choice, only students who are already motivated may participate, while others may miss an important opportunity to grow. Making it part of school life ensures that every student is exposed to people beyond their usual social circle. It can also make education more balanced, since young people learn not only how to pass exams but also how to contribute to society. As long as the work is age-appropriate and properly supervised, it can become a meaningful stepping stone towards responsible adulthood.","chinese":"我也認為這應該成為正式課程的一部分，因為學校不僅應該培養學術能力，也應該培養品格。 如果社區服務完全由個人選擇決定，可能只有本身已有動力的學生會參與，而其他學生則可能錯過一個重要的成長機會。 把它納入學校生活之中，能確保每一位學生都接觸到自己平常社交圈以外的人。 它也能使教育更加平衡，因為年輕人學到的不只是如何通過考試，也包括如何為社會作出貢獻。 只要這些工作適合學生年齡，並且受到適當監督，它便可以成為邁向負責任成年階段的一塊有意義的踏腳石。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, community work benefits students by building empathy, maturity, and social responsibility. For this reason, I strongly believe it should be a required part of the high school curriculum.","chinese":"總結來說，社區服務透過建立同理心、成熟度和社會責任感來令學生受益。 基於這個原因，我強烈認為它應該成為高中課程中的必修部分。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"secondary schools","chinese":"中學"},{"english":"be expected to","chinese":"被期望；應該"},{"english":"take part in","chinese":"參與"},{"english":"community service","chinese":"社區服務"},{"english":"supporting elderly people","chinese":"支援長者"},{"english":"those with disabilities","chinese":"殘疾人士"},{"english":"benefit young people by","chinese":"透過……令年輕人受惠"},{"english":"developing empathy","chinese":"培養同理心"},{"english":"practical maturity","chinese":"實際處事上的成熟"},{"english":"be included in","chinese":"被納入……"},{"english":"the school curriculum","chinese":"學校課程"},{"english":"the clearest benefit","chinese":"最明顯的好處"},{"english":"community work","chinese":"社區工作"},{"english":"helps students become","chinese":"幫助學生成為；幫助學生變得"},{"english":"compassionate","chinese":"有同情心的"},{"english":"socially aware","chinese":"有社會意識的"},{"english":"people of a similar age","chinese":"年齡相近的人"},{"english":"understanding of hardship","chinese":"對困難處境的理解"},{"english":"remain quite limited","chinese":"仍然相當有限"},{"english":"assist an elderly person with","chinese":"協助長者處理……"},{"english":"daily tasks","chinese":"日常事務"},{"english":"spend time with","chinese":"花時間陪伴"},{"english":"someone who has a disability","chinese":"有殘疾的人"},{"english":"begin to see that","chinese":"開始明白"},{"english":"vulnerability","chinese":"脆弱；弱勢處境"},{"english":"an abstract idea","chinese":"抽象概念"},{"english":"a real part of human life","chinese":"人類生活中真實的一部分"},{"english":"teach patience, respect, and responsibility","chinese":"教會耐性、尊重和責任感"},{"english":"far more effectively than","chinese":"比……有效得多"},{"english":"a lecture in a classroom","chinese":"課室裏的一堂講課"},{"english":"an elderly resident","chinese":"年長居民"},{"english":"carry groceries","chinese":"拿雜貨；拿日用品"},{"english":"small acts of kindness","chinese":"小小的善舉"},{"english":"make another person's day easier","chinese":"令別人的一天輕鬆一點"},{"english":"in this way","chinese":"這樣一來"},{"english":"turn moral values from empty words into lived experience","chinese":"將道德價值由空話變成親身體驗"},{"english":"empty words","chinese":"空話"},{"english":"lived experience","chinese":"親身經歷；生活體驗"},{"english":"a formal part of","chinese":"……的正式部分"},{"english":"educate character","chinese":"培養品格"},{"english":"as well as academic ability","chinese":"以及學業能力"},{"english":"be left entirely to","chinese":"完全交由……決定；完全交給……負責"},{"english":"personal choice","chinese":"個人選擇"},{"english":"already motivated","chinese":"本身已有動力的"},{"english":"miss an important opportunity to grow","chinese":"錯過重要的成長機會"},{"english":"making it part of school life","chinese":"將它變成學校生活的一部分"},{"english":"ensures that","chinese":"確保"},{"english":"be exposed to","chinese":"接觸到"},{"english":"beyond their usual social circle","chinese":"在平常社交圈子以外"},{"english":"make education more balanced","chinese":"令教育更均衡"},{"english":"pass exams","chinese":"通過考試"},{"english":"contribute to society","chinese":"貢獻社會"},{"english":"as long as","chinese":"只要"},{"english":"age-appropriate","chinese":"適合年齡的"},{"english":"properly supervised","chinese":"得到適當監督"},{"english":"a meaningful stepping stone towards","chinese":"邁向……的有意義踏腳石"},{"english":"responsible adulthood","chinese":"負責任的成年階段"},{"english":"social responsibility","chinese":"社會責任感"},{"english":"a required part of","chinese":"……的必修部分"},{"english":"the high school curriculum","chinese":"高中課程"}]},"model-essay-15-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-15-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:15","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-15-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q15","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In an increasingly connected world, the ability to speak a foreign language has become a valuable educational asset. While some people believe that pupils should first study another language in secondary school, I firmly believe that language learning should begin at primary school.","chinese":"在一個日益互聯的世界中，能夠說一門外語已成為一項有價值的教育資產。 雖然有些人認為學生應該在中學才開始學習另一種語言， 我堅定地認為，語言學習應該從小學開始。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Those who support a later start often argue that secondary school students are more mature. At that age, learners can understand grammar rules, sentence patterns and abstract vocabulary more consciously, so teachers may be able to explain the language in a systematic way. Older students may also have clearer academic goals, such as preparing for examinations or future employment. For example, a teenager who knows that English, French or Mandarin could improve career prospects may study with stronger discipline. From this perspective, secondary school can seem like a more efficient stage for serious language instruction.","chinese":"支持較遲開始的人通常認為，中學生更加成熟。 在那個年齡，學習者能夠更有意識地理解文法規則、句子結構和抽象詞彙，因此老師也許能夠以更有系統的方式解釋語言。 年紀較大的學生也可能有更清晰的學業目標，例如準備考試或未來就業。 例如，一個知道英語、法語或普通話能改善職業前景的青少年，可能會以更強的自律性去學習。 從這個角度來看，中學似乎可以是一個更有效率地進行認真語言教學的階段。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, the stronger argument is that primary school children are usually in a better position to build natural language habits. Young learners tend to absorb pronunciation, rhythm and basic expressions more easily because they are less self-conscious and more willing to imitate sounds. If a child regularly sings songs, plays language games and hears simple classroom instructions in another language, that language gradually becomes familiar rather than frightening. This early confidence matters because language learning is not mastered overnight; it grows through repeated exposure, mistakes and correction. A student who has met a foreign language from the age of six is therefore far less likely to see it as a wall to climb when it becomes more demanding in secondary school.","chinese":"然而，更有力的論點是，小學生通常處於更有利的位置去建立自然的語言習慣。 年幼的學習者往往更容易吸收發音、節奏和基本表達，因為他們較少感到自我意識過強，也更願意模仿聲音。 如果一個孩子經常唱歌、玩語言遊戲，並聽到另一種語言的簡單課堂指示，那種語言便會逐漸變得熟悉，而不是令人害怕。 這種早期信心十分重要，因為語言學習並不是一夜之間就能掌握的；它是透過反覆接觸、犯錯和改正慢慢成長的。 因此，一個從六歲起便接觸外語的學生，在中學階段語言學習變得更具要求時，便遠較不可能把它視為一道難以攀越的高牆。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, although secondary school students may study languages more deliberately, primary school is the better starting point. Early exposure builds confidence, natural habits and steady progress, making foreign-language learning far more effective.","chinese":"總結來說，儘管中學生可能會更有意識地學習語言，小學仍然是更好的起點。 早期接觸能建立信心、自然習慣和穩定進步，從而使外語學習有效得多。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"in an increasingly connected world","chinese":"在一個聯繫日益緊密的世界"},{"english":"the ability to speak","chinese":"說……的能力"},{"english":"a foreign language","chinese":"外語"},{"english":"a valuable educational asset","chinese":"寶貴的教育資產"},{"english":"pupils","chinese":"小學生；學生"},{"english":"first study another language","chinese":"首先學習另一種語言"},{"english":"firmly believe that","chinese":"堅信"},{"english":"language learning","chinese":"語言學習"},{"english":"begin at primary school","chinese":"在小學開始"},{"english":"those who support","chinese":"支持……的人"},{"english":"a later start","chinese":"較遲開始"},{"english":"secondary school students","chinese":"中學生"},{"english":"more mature","chinese":"較成熟"},{"english":"at that age","chinese":"在那個年紀"},{"english":"grammar rules","chinese":"文法規則"},{"english":"sentence patterns","chinese":"句式"},{"english":"abstract vocabulary","chinese":"抽象詞彙"},{"english":"more consciously","chinese":"更有意識地"},{"english":"in a systematic way","chinese":"以有系統的方式"},{"english":"clearer academic goals","chinese":"更清晰的學業目標"},{"english":"preparing for examinations","chinese":"準備考試"},{"english":"future employment","chinese":"未來就業"},{"english":"improve career prospects","chinese":"改善事業前景"},{"english":"study with stronger discipline","chinese":"以更強自律學習"},{"english":"from this perspective","chinese":"從這個角度來看"},{"english":"a more efficient stage","chinese":"更有效率的階段"},{"english":"serious language instruction","chinese":"認真的語言教學"},{"english":"the stronger argument","chinese":"更有力的論點"},{"english":"be in a better position to","chinese":"更有條件去"},{"english":"build natural language habits","chinese":"建立自然的語言習慣"},{"english":"young learners","chinese":"年幼學習者"},{"english":"tend to","chinese":"往往會"},{"english":"absorb pronunciation","chinese":"吸收發音"},{"english":"rhythm and basic expressions","chinese":"節奏和基本表達"},{"english":"less self-conscious","chinese":"較少自我意識；較不怕尷尬"},{"english":"more willing to imitate","chinese":"更願意模仿"},{"english":"imitate sounds","chinese":"模仿聲音"},{"english":"regularly sings songs","chinese":"定期唱歌"},{"english":"language games","chinese":"語言遊戲"},{"english":"classroom instructions","chinese":"課堂指示"},{"english":"gradually becomes familiar","chinese":"逐漸變得熟悉"},{"english":"rather than frightening","chinese":"而不是令人害怕"},{"english":"early confidence","chinese":"早期信心"},{"english":"is not mastered overnight","chinese":"不是一夜之間掌握"},{"english":"repeated exposure","chinese":"反覆接觸"},{"english":"mistakes and correction","chinese":"錯誤和糾正"},{"english":"from the age of six","chinese":"從六歲起"},{"english":"far less likely to","chinese":"遠遠較不可能"},{"english":"see it as a wall to climb","chinese":"將它視為一道要攀過的牆"},{"english":"becomes more demanding","chinese":"變得要求更高"},{"english":"in secondary school","chinese":"在中學"},{"english":"study languages more deliberately","chinese":"更有意識地學習語言"},{"english":"the better starting point","chinese":"更好的起點"},{"english":"early exposure","chinese":"早期接觸"},{"english":"build confidence","chinese":"建立信心"},{"english":"natural habits","chinese":"自然習慣"},{"english":"steady progress","chinese":"穩定進步"},{"english":"making foreign-language learning far more effective","chinese":"令外語學習有效得多"}]},"model-essay-15-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-15-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:15","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-15-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q15","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The ability to speak persuasively in public is often regarded as a key ingredient of success. I completely agree that oratory skills are essential, because success rarely depends only on what people know; it also depends on how convincingly they can express, defend, and share that knowledge.","chinese":"在公共場合具說服力地表達的能力，通常被視為成功的一個關鍵要素。 我完全同意演說能力是必不可少的，因為成功很少只取決於人們知道甚麼；它也取決於他們能多有說服力地表達、捍衛和分享那些知識。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"First, strong speaking skills allow people to make their ideas visible. In the workplace, many capable employees remain overlooked not because their work lacks value, but because they cannot explain it clearly to colleagues, clients, or managers. By contrast, a person who can present an argument in an organised and engaging way is more likely to win trust, secure promotion, and lead others. For example, an engineer may design an excellent product, but if she cannot explain its benefits to investors or customers, the idea may never leave the meeting room. In this sense, public speaking turns private ability into public influence, which is central to professional success.","chinese":"首先，強大的表達能力使人們能夠讓自己的想法被看見。 在職場中，許多有能力的員工仍然被忽視，並不是因為他們的工作缺乏價值，而是因為他們無法向同事、客戶或管理層清楚解釋自己的工作。 相比之下，一個能夠以有條理且吸引人的方式提出論點的人，更有可能贏得信任、獲得晉升，並領導他人。 例如，一位工程師可能設計出一件出色的產品，但如果她無法向投資者或客戶解釋其好處，這個想法可能永遠無法離開會議室。 從這個意義上說，公開演說把個人的能力轉化為公共影響力，而這正是職業成功的核心"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Moreover, oratory skills are essential because success often requires cooperation. Leaders, teachers, entrepreneurs, and community organisers all need to encourage, negotiate, calm, and inspire others. When people speak with confidence and sensitivity, they can reduce misunderstandings and bring others onto the same page. A manager who gives clear instructions and motivates a team during a crisis will achieve more than one who has technical expertise but communicates poorly. Similarly, students who can ask questions, defend opinions, and participate in discussions develop a confidence that later opens doors in both study and work. Effective speech, therefore, does not merely decorate ability; it releases it.","chinese":"此外，演說能力之所以重要，是因為成功往往需要合作。 領袖、教師、企業家和社區組織者都需要鼓勵、協商、安撫和激勵他人。 當人們能夠自信而敏銳地說話時，他們便能減少誤解，並讓其他人達成共識。 一位在危機中能給出清晰指示並激勵團隊的管理者，會比一位擁有技術專長但溝通能力差的管理者取得更多成就。 同樣地，能夠提出問題、捍衛觀點並參與討論的學生，會培養出一種自信，而這種自信日後會在學習和工作中為他們打開機會之門。 因此，有效的表達並不只是為能力作裝飾；它能真正釋放能力。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely agree that oratory skills are essential for success. They help people present their abilities clearly, persuade others effectively, and build the relationships through which achievement usually happens.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意演說能力對成功是必不可少的。 它們幫助人們清楚展示自己的能力、有效說服他人，並建立那些通常使成就得以發生的人際關係。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the ability to","chinese":"……的能力"},{"english":"speak persuasively in public","chinese":"在公開場合有說服力地發言"},{"english":"be regarded as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"a key ingredient of success","chinese":"成功的關鍵因素"},{"english":"I completely agree that","chinese":"我完全同意"},{"english":"oratory skills","chinese":"演說技巧"},{"english":"depend only on","chinese":"只取決於"},{"english":"express, defend, and share","chinese":"表達、捍衛和分享"},{"english":"make their ideas visible","chinese":"令自己的想法被看見"},{"english":"in the workplace","chinese":"在職場上"},{"english":"capable employees","chinese":"有能力的員工"},{"english":"remain overlooked","chinese":"仍然被忽視"},{"english":"lack value","chinese":"缺乏價值"},{"english":"explain it clearly to","chinese":"向……清楚解釋"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相反"},{"english":"present an argument","chinese":"提出論點"},{"english":"in an organised and engaging way","chinese":"以有條理而吸引人的方式"},{"english":"win trust","chinese":"贏得信任"},{"english":"secure promotion","chinese":"獲得晉升"},{"english":"lead others","chinese":"領導他人"},{"english":"design an excellent product","chinese":"設計一件出色產品"},{"english":"explain its benefits to","chinese":"向……解釋其好處"},{"english":"investors or customers","chinese":"投資者或顧客"},{"english":"leave the meeting room","chinese":"走出會議室；得到實行"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"turn private ability into public influence","chinese":"將個人能力轉化為公眾影響力"},{"english":"be central to","chinese":"對……至關重要"},{"english":"professional success","chinese":"事業上的成功"},{"english":"moreover","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"require cooperation","chinese":"需要合作"},{"english":"community organisers","chinese":"社區組織者"},{"english":"encourage, negotiate, calm, and inspire","chinese":"鼓勵、協商、安撫和激勵"},{"english":"speak with confidence and sensitivity","chinese":"自信而體貼地說話"},{"english":"reduce misunderstandings","chinese":"減少誤解"},{"english":"bring others onto the same page","chinese":"令其他人達成共識"},{"english":"give clear instructions","chinese":"給予清晰指示"},{"english":"motivate a team","chinese":"激勵團隊"},{"english":"during a crisis","chinese":"在危機期間"},{"english":"technical expertise","chinese":"專業技術知識"},{"english":"communicate poorly","chinese":"溝通不善"},{"english":"ask questions","chinese":"提問"},{"english":"defend opinions","chinese":"捍衛意見"},{"english":"participate in discussions","chinese":"參與討論"},{"english":"open doors","chinese":"帶來機會"},{"english":"in both study and work","chinese":"在學業和工作兩方面"},{"english":"effective speech","chinese":"有效表達"},{"english":"does not merely decorate ability","chinese":"不只是為能力加上裝飾"},{"english":"release ability","chinese":"釋放能力；發揮能力"},{"english":"in conclusion","chinese":"總括而言"},{"english":"present their abilities clearly","chinese":"清楚展示自己的能力"},{"english":"persuade others effectively","chinese":"有效說服他人"},{"english":"build the relationships through which","chinese":"建立令……得以實現的人際關係"},{"english":"achievement usually happens","chinese":"成就通常得以實現"}]},"model-essay-16-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-16-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:16","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-16-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q16","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In contemporary society, people are exposed to commercial messages almost constantly, whether on their phones, in print, or across city streets. This advertising-driven culture of consumerism can stimulate economic activity and encourage product improvement; however, I believe its overall impact is negative because it promotes wasteful spending and accelerates environmental damage.","chinese":"在當代社會中，人們幾乎時刻都暴露在商業訊息之下，無論是在手機上、印刷媒體中，還是在城市街道上。 這種由廣告推動的消費主義文化，的確能刺激經濟活動，並促使產品改善；然而， 我認為它的整體影響是負面的，因為它助長浪費性的消費，並加速環境破壞。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Admittedly, consumerism can produce genuine benefits for the economy. To begin with, strong demand for goods keeps companies profitable and allows them to employ people across manufacturing, retail, logistics, and marketing. When a heavily advertised product sells well, the resulting income supports an entire chain of jobs rather than a single business. In turn, governments may collect more tax revenue, which can be used to fund public services. In addition, the need to attract customers often forces companies to improve what they sell. Since businesses must persuade consumers that a new item is worth buying, they tend to enhance quality, convenience, and efficiency. The smartphone industry illustrates this clearly, as intense competition has led to better batteries, stronger security systems, and more reliable cameras.","chinese":"誠然，消費主義的確能為經濟帶來真實的好處。 首先，對商品的強勁需求能使企業維持盈利，並讓它們在製造、零售、物流和市場推廣等領域提供就業機會。 當一項被大力宣傳的產品銷售表現良好時，由此產生的收入所支撐的並不只是單一企業，而是整條就業鏈。進一步來說，政府亦可因此獲得更多稅收，並將這些資金用於公共服務。 例如，一項被廣泛宣傳的消費產品若大賣，不但能為店舖員工帶來工作，也能同時帶動工廠工人、運輸司機以及廣告公司的就業。 此外，為了吸引顧客，企業往往不得不改良自己所出售的產品。 由於企業必須說服消費者某項新產品值得購買，它們通常會提升產品的品質、便利性和效率。 智能手機產業便清楚說明了這一點，因為激烈的競爭已促使電池更耐用、保安系統更強，以及相機功能更可靠。 因此，消費主義確實能促進經濟增長，並推動產品創新。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Even so, the negative effects are more serious. The first is financial harm at the individual level. By repeatedly presenting non-essential items as symbols of success or happiness, advertising can blur the distinction between wants and needs. As a result, many people buy impulsively, reduce their savings, or rely on credit to purchase goods that add little real value to their lives. A young worker who frequently upgrades perfectly functional devices simply to follow trends, for example, may create unnecessary financial pressure. The second drawback is environmental. Consumerism depends on continual production, packaging, transport, and replacement, all of which consume energy and raw materials. Moreover, many cheap clothes and electronic products are discarded long before the end of their useful life, increasing landfill waste and pollution. For this reason, a culture of constant purchasing places a heavy burden on the planet.","chinese":"即便如此，消費主義所帶來的負面影響更加嚴重。 第一個問題，是它會在個人層面造成財務上的損害。 廣告一再把非必要物品包裝成成功或幸福的象徵，便會模糊「想要」與「需要」之間的界線。結果，很多人會衝動購物、減少儲蓄，甚至依賴借貸去購買一些對生活其實沒有太大實際價值的商品。 例如，一名年輕上班族若只是為了追趕潮流，便頻繁更換仍然運作良好的電子產品，便可能為自己帶來不必要的財務壓力。 第二個缺點則與環境有關。 消費主義依賴持續不斷的生產、包裝、運輸和替換，而這些過程全都會消耗能源和原材料。此外，許多廉價衣物和電子產品在尚未真正用盡之前便被丟棄，從而增加堆填區廢物及污染。 因此，這種不斷購買的文化，對地球造成了沉重的負擔。 因此，消費主義不但鼓勵不必要的消費，亦加劇了環境惡化。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, although consumerism can create employment and drive innovation, its disadvantages are ultimately more significant. Because it encourages needless expenditure and deepens environmental degradation, it is, on balance, a harmful social trend.","chinese":"總括而言，雖然消費主義能創造就業並推動創新，但它的缺點始終更為重大。 因為它助長不必要的開支，並加深環境破壞，所以整體來說，它是一種有害的社會趨勢"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"contemporary society","chinese":"當代社會"},{"english":"be exposed to","chinese":"接觸到"},{"english":"commercial messages","chinese":"商業訊息"},{"english":"almost constantly","chinese":"幾乎不斷地"},{"english":"whether on their phones, in print, or across city streets","chinese":"無論在手機上、印刷品中，還是在城市街道各處"},{"english":"advertising-driven culture","chinese":"由廣告推動的文化"},{"english":"consumerism","chinese":"消費主義"},{"english":"stimulate economic activity","chinese":"刺激經濟活動"},{"english":"encourage product improvement","chinese":"鼓勵產品改良"},{"english":"overall impact","chinese":"整體影響"},{"english":"promote wasteful spending","chinese":"鼓吹浪費性消費"},{"english":"accelerate environmental damage","chinese":"加速環境破壞"},{"english":"admittedly","chinese":"誠然"},{"english":"genuine benefits","chinese":"真正的好處"},{"english":"to begin with","chinese":"首先"},{"english":"strong demand for goods","chinese":"對商品的強勁需求"},{"english":"keeps companies profitable","chinese":"令公司保持盈利"},{"english":"employ people across","chinese":"在……各範疇聘用人手"},{"english":"manufacturing","chinese":"製造業"},{"english":"retail","chinese":"零售業"},{"english":"logistics","chinese":"物流業"},{"english":"a heavily advertised product","chinese":"大量宣傳的產品"},{"english":"sells well","chinese":"銷量好"},{"english":"the resulting income","chinese":"隨之而來的收入"},{"english":"an entire chain of jobs","chinese":"整條就業鏈"},{"english":"rather than a single business","chinese":"而不是單一企業"},{"english":"in turn","chinese":"繼而"},{"english":"collect more tax revenue","chinese":"收取更多稅收"},{"english":"fund public services","chinese":"資助公共服務"},{"english":"in addition","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"attract customers","chinese":"吸引顧客"},{"english":"forces companies to","chinese":"迫使公司去"},{"english":"persuade consumers that","chinese":"說服消費者"},{"english":"worth buying","chinese":"值得購買"},{"english":"tend to enhance","chinese":"往往會提升"},{"english":"quality, convenience, and efficiency","chinese":"質素、便利性和效率"},{"english":"illustrates this clearly","chinese":"清楚說明這一點"},{"english":"intense competition","chinese":"激烈競爭"},{"english":"has led to","chinese":"導致；帶來"},{"english":"stronger security systems","chinese":"更強的保安系統"},{"english":"more reliable cameras","chinese":"更可靠的相機"},{"english":"even so","chinese":"即使如此"},{"english":"negative effects","chinese":"負面影響"},{"english":"financial harm","chinese":"財務損害"},{"english":"at the individual level","chinese":"在個人層面"},{"english":"repeatedly presenting","chinese":"反覆呈現"},{"english":"non-essential items","chinese":"非必需品"},{"english":"symbols of success or happiness","chinese":"成功或快樂的象徵"},{"english":"blur the distinction between","chinese":"模糊……之間的區別"},{"english":"wants and needs","chinese":"想要的東西和需要的東西"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"buy impulsively","chinese":"衝動購物"},{"english":"reduce their savings","chinese":"減少儲蓄"},{"english":"rely on credit","chinese":"依賴信用貸款"},{"english":"add little real value to","chinese":"對……幾乎沒有真正價值"},{"english":"frequently upgrades","chinese":"經常升級"},{"english":"perfectly functional devices","chinese":"完全能正常使用的裝置"},{"english":"follow trends","chinese":"跟隨潮流"},{"english":"create unnecessary financial pressure","chinese":"造成不必要的財務壓力"},{"english":"the second drawback","chinese":"第二個缺點"},{"english":"continual production","chinese":"持續生產"},{"english":"packaging","chinese":"包裝"},{"english":"replacement","chinese":"替換"},{"english":"consume energy and raw materials","chinese":"消耗能源和原材料"},{"english":"moreover","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"cheap clothes and electronic products","chinese":"廉價衣服和電子產品"},{"english":"be discarded","chinese":"被棄置"},{"english":"long before the end of their useful life","chinese":"遠在其使用壽命結束之前"},{"english":"increasing landfill waste","chinese":"增加堆填區廢物"},{"english":"pollution","chinese":"污染"},{"english":"a culture of constant purchasing","chinese":"不斷購買的文化"},{"english":"places a heavy burden on","chinese":"對……造成沉重負擔"},{"english":"the planet","chinese":"地球"},{"english":"create employment","chinese":"創造就業"},{"english":"drive innovation","chinese":"推動創新"},{"english":"ultimately more significant","chinese":"最終更重要"},{"english":"needless expenditure","chinese":"不必要開支"},{"english":"deepens environmental degradation","chinese":"加劇環境惡化"},{"english":"on balance","chinese":"總體而言"},{"english":"a harmful social trend","chinese":"有害的社會趨勢"}]},"model-essay-16-ielts-cause-solution":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-16-ielts-cause-solution","essayKey":"cause-solution:16","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-16-ielts-cause-solution","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/problem-and-cause/EdmundBd9CnS-Q16","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many cities and towns, roads are carrying more vehicles than they can reasonably absorb. This problem is mainly caused by car-centred planning and weak alternatives to private transport. It can be addressed by improving public transport, managing road use more carefully and making short local journeys easier without a car.","chinese":"在許多城市和城鎮中，道路正承載著超出其合理容納範圍的車輛數量。 這個問題主要是由以汽車為中心的城市規劃，以及私人交通工具以外的替代選擇不足所造成的。 這個問題可以透過改善公共交通、更審慎地管理道路使用，以及讓人們在不使用汽車的情況下更容易完成短途本地出行來解決。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One important cause is that many urban areas have been built around driving. When homes, workplaces, schools and shops are spread across wide distances, ordinary routines almost force people onto the road. A parent, for example, may need to drive to a school, an office and a supermarket in one morning, turning one household into several car trips. A second cause is the poor quality of public transport. If buses are slow, trains are overcrowded, or services do not connect well with residential areas, people will naturally see driving as the only practical choice. In that situation, each driver tries to save time, but everyone ends up losing time in congestion.","chinese":"其中一個重要原因是，許多城市地區都是圍繞駕車而建設的。 當住宅、工作場所、學校和商店分散在很遠的距離之間時，日常生活的安排幾乎會迫使人們上路開車。 例如，一位家長可能需要在一個早上開車前往學校、辦公室和超級市場，結果一個家庭便產生了數次汽車出行。 第二個原因是公共交通的質素欠佳。 如果巴士速度緩慢、火車過度擁擠，或者交通服務與住宅區連接不佳，人們自然會把駕車視為唯一實際可行的選擇。 在這種情況下，每位司機都試圖節省時間，但最後所有人都在交通擠塞中浪費了時間。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The first solution is to make public transport genuinely convenient. Governments should invest in frequent buses, reliable rail services and simple ticketing systems, so that using a bus or train feels less like a sacrifice and more like common sense. For instance, a worker who can cross a city quickly with one affordable ticket is far less likely to drive. In addition, local authorities should manage car use through congestion charges, limited parking and bus lanes. Cities should also build safe walking and cycling routes, especially for short trips. These measures reduce unnecessary traffic without banning cars completely, leaving road space for essential journeys, deliveries and emergency vehicles.","chinese":"第一個解決方法是讓公共交通真正變得方便。 政府應投資於班次頻密的巴士、可靠的鐵路服務和簡單的票務系統，使乘搭巴士或火車感覺上不再像是一種犧牲，而更像是理所當然的選擇。 例如，如果一名上班族能夠用一張價格合理的車票快速穿越城市，他開車的可能性便會大大降低。 此外，地方政府應透過擁堵收費、限制泊車位和設置巴士專線來管理汽車使用。 城市亦應建設安全的步行和單車路線，尤其是為短途出行而設。 這些措施能在不完全禁止汽車的情況下減少不必要的交通流量，從而為必要出行、送貨車輛和緊急車輛騰出道路空間。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, heavy traffic is largely the result of car-dependent planning and unattractive transport alternatives. It can be reduced if cities improve public transport while encouraging people to make shorter and less essential journeys in other ways.","chinese":"總結來說，交通繁忙很大程度上是依賴汽車的城市規劃，以及缺乏吸引力的交通替代方案所造成的。 如果城市改善公共交通，同時鼓勵人們以其他方式完成較短和較不必要的出行，交通擠塞便可以得到減少。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"roads are carrying more vehicles than they can reasonably absorb","chinese":"道路承載的車輛超出可合理容納的程度"},{"english":"car-centred planning","chinese":"以汽車為中心的規劃"},{"english":"weak alternatives to private transport","chinese":"私人交通工具以外選擇不足"},{"english":"be addressed by","chinese":"可透過……處理；解決"},{"english":"improving public transport","chinese":"改善公共交通"},{"english":"managing road use more carefully","chinese":"更審慎地管理道路使用"},{"english":"short local journeys","chinese":"區內短途出行"},{"english":"without a car","chinese":"不用汽車"},{"english":"urban areas","chinese":"市區"},{"english":"built around driving","chinese":"圍繞駕駛而規劃"},{"english":"be spread across wide distances","chinese":"分散在很大範圍內"},{"english":"ordinary routines","chinese":"日常例行活動"},{"english":"force people onto the road","chinese":"迫使人們駕車上路"},{"english":"in one morning","chinese":"在一個早上內"},{"english":"turning one household into several car trips","chinese":"令一個家庭產生多次駕車行程"},{"english":"car trips","chinese":"駕車行程；汽車出行次數"},{"english":"the poor quality of public transport","chinese":"公共交通質素差"},{"english":"trains are overcrowded","chinese":"鐵路過於擠迫"},{"english":"connect well with residential areas","chinese":"與住宅區銜接良好"},{"english":"residential areas","chinese":"住宅區"},{"english":"see driving as the only practical choice","chinese":"視駕車為唯一實際可行的選擇"},{"english":"the only practical choice","chinese":"唯一實際可行的選擇"},{"english":"save time","chinese":"節省時間"},{"english":"end up losing time","chinese":"最終浪費時間"},{"english":"in congestion","chinese":"在交通擠塞中"},{"english":"make public transport genuinely convenient","chinese":"令公共交通真正方便"},{"english":"invest in","chinese":"投資於"},{"english":"frequent buses","chinese":"班次頻密的巴士"},{"english":"reliable rail services","chinese":"可靠的鐵路服務"},{"english":"simple ticketing systems","chinese":"簡單的票務系統"},{"english":"less like a sacrifice and more like common sense","chinese":"不像犧牲，而更像明智自然的選擇"},{"english":"cross a city quickly","chinese":"快速橫越一個城市"},{"english":"one affordable ticket","chinese":"一張負擔得起的車票"},{"english":"far less likely to drive","chinese":"駕車的機會大大降低"},{"english":"local authorities","chinese":"地方當局"},{"english":"manage car use through","chinese":"透過……管理汽車使用"},{"english":"congestion charges","chinese":"交通擠塞收費"},{"english":"limited parking","chinese":"限制泊車；有限泊車位"},{"english":"bus lanes","chinese":"巴士專線"},{"english":"safe walking and cycling routes","chinese":"安全的步行及單車路線"},{"english":"especially for short trips","chinese":"特別是短途出行"},{"english":"reduce unnecessary traffic","chinese":"減少不必要的交通流量"},{"english":"without banning cars completely","chinese":"無須完全禁止汽車"},{"english":"leaving road space for","chinese":"為……騰出道路空間"},{"english":"essential journeys","chinese":"必要行程"},{"english":"deliveries","chinese":"送貨"},{"english":"emergency vehicles","chinese":"緊急車輛"},{"english":"heavy traffic","chinese":"交通繁忙；嚴重交通擠塞"},{"english":"largely the result of","chinese":"很大程度上是……的結果"},{"english":"car-dependent planning","chinese":"依賴汽車的規劃"},{"english":"unattractive transport alternatives","chinese":"缺乏吸引力的交通替代選擇"},{"english":"encouraging people to","chinese":"鼓勵人們去"},{"english":"shorter and less essential journeys","chinese":"較短及非必要的行程"},{"english":"in other ways","chinese":"以其他方式"}]},"model-essay-16-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-16-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:16","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-16-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q16","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Some people see teaching as the simple transfer of facts from an expert to a learner. I strongly disagree with this limited view. In my opinion, a teacher’s central role is to motivate and inspire students, because knowledge only becomes valuable when students are willing to engage with it, question it and use it beyond the classroom.","chinese":"有些人認為，教學只是把知識從專家傳遞給學習者。 我強烈不同意這種狹隘的看法。 在我看來，教師的核心角色是激勵和啟發學生，因為知識只有在學生願意投入其中、質疑它，並在課堂以外運用它時，才會真正變得有價值。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that motivation turns information into real learning. A teacher can deliver a perfectly accurate lesson, but if students are bored, passive or afraid of making mistakes, most of that knowledge will evaporate after the examination. By contrast, an inspiring teacher creates curiosity. Such a teacher does not merely tell students what happened in history or how a formula works; they help students see why it matters. For instance, a history teacher who connects past conflicts with modern ideas of justice may lead students to debate, challenge assumptions and remember the lesson more deeply. In this sense, inspiration is not decorative; it is the engine that keeps learning alive.","chinese":"第一個原因是，動機能把資訊轉化為真正的學習。 一位教師可以講授一堂完全準確的課，但如果學生感到沉悶、被動，或者害怕犯錯，那麼大部分知識在考試後都會逐漸消散。 相比之下，一位能啟發學生的教師會激發好奇心。 這樣的教師不只是告訴學生歷史上發生了甚麼，或者一條公式如何運作；他們會幫助學生明白為甚麼這些知識重要。 例如，一位把過去的衝突與現代正義觀念連繫起來的歷史老師，可能會引導學生辯論、挑戰既有假設，並更深刻地記住那堂課。 從這個意義上說，啟發並不是裝飾性的東西；它是讓學習持續運轉的引擎。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that teachers shape attitudes, confidence and habits that students carry into adulthood. Facts can now be found in books, videos and digital platforms, but a young person still needs guidance to develop discipline, resilience and intellectual courage. A teacher who motivates students can change how they see themselves as learners. For example, when a science teacher encourages a weak student after a failed experiment, the student may stop seeing failure as humiliation and start seeing it as part of discovery. That lesson is far more durable than a single chapter in a textbook.","chinese":"另一個原因是，教師會塑造學生帶入成年階段的態度、自信和習慣。 事實性知識現在可以在書本、影片和數碼平台上找到，但年輕人仍然需要引導，才能培養自律、韌性和intellectualcourage。 一位能激勵學生的教師，可以改變學生如何看待自己作為學習者的身份。 例如，當一位科學老師在一次實驗失敗後鼓勵一名能力較弱的學生時，這名學生可能會停止把失敗視為羞辱，並開始把它看成探索的一部分。 這一課比教科書中的單一章節更加持久。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, although teachers must explain knowledge clearly, their deeper role is to inspire students to care about learning. Information can be handed over, but confidence, curiosity and purpose have to be awakened.","chinese":"總結來說，雖然教師必須清楚解釋知識，但他們更深層的角色是啟發學生去重視學習。 資訊可以被傳遞，但自信、好奇心和目標感必須被喚醒"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"see teaching as","chinese":"將教學視為……"},{"english":"the simple transfer of facts","chinese":"簡單傳授知識"},{"english":"from an expert to a learner","chinese":"從專家到學習者"},{"english":"strongly disagree with","chinese":"強烈不同意……"},{"english":"this limited view","chinese":"這種狹隘看法"},{"english":"in my opinion","chinese":"在我看來；依我之見"},{"english":"a teacher's central role","chinese":"教師的核心角色"},{"english":"motivate and inspire","chinese":"激勵和啟發"},{"english":"becomes valuable when","chinese":"當……時才變得有價值"},{"english":"be willing to","chinese":"願意……"},{"english":"engage with","chinese":"投入；接觸並思考"},{"english":"question it","chinese":"質疑它"},{"english":"beyond the classroom","chinese":"在課室以外"},{"english":"turns information into real learning","chinese":"將資訊轉化為真正學習"},{"english":"deliver a lesson","chinese":"講授一堂課"},{"english":"a perfectly accurate lesson","chinese":"完全準確的一堂課"},{"english":"passive","chinese":"被動的"},{"english":"afraid of making mistakes","chinese":"害怕犯錯"},{"english":"most of that knowledge","chinese":"大部分知識"},{"english":"evaporate after the examination","chinese":"考試後消失"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"an inspiring teacher","chinese":"有啟發性的教師"},{"english":"creates curiosity","chinese":"引發好奇心"},{"english":"does not merely","chinese":"不只是……"},{"english":"how a formula works","chinese":"公式如何運作"},{"english":"see why it matters","chinese":"明白它為何重要"},{"english":"past conflicts","chinese":"過去的衝突"},{"english":"modern ideas of justice","chinese":"現代的公義觀念"},{"english":"lead students to","chinese":"引導學生去……"},{"english":"challenge assumptions","chinese":"挑戰假設"},{"english":"remember the lesson more deeply","chinese":"更深刻地記住課堂內容"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"decorative","chinese":"裝飾性的；可有可無的"},{"english":"the engine that keeps learning alive","chinese":"令學習保持活力的引擎"},{"english":"shape attitudes","chinese":"塑造態度"},{"english":"carry into adulthood","chinese":"帶到成年階段"},{"english":"can now be found in","chinese":"現在可以在……找到"},{"english":"digital platforms","chinese":"數碼平台"},{"english":"guidance","chinese":"指導"},{"english":"develop discipline","chinese":"培養自律"},{"english":"resilience","chinese":"抗逆力"},{"english":"intellectual courage","chinese":"思想上的勇氣"},{"english":"change how they see themselves","chinese":"改變他們如何看待自己"},{"english":"see themselves as learners","chinese":"視自己為學習者"},{"english":"a weak student","chinese":"成績較弱的學生"},{"english":"a failed experiment","chinese":"失敗的實驗"},{"english":"stop seeing failure as","chinese":"不再將失敗視為……"},{"english":"humiliation","chinese":"羞辱"},{"english":"start seeing it as","chinese":"開始將它視為……"},{"english":"part of discovery","chinese":"探索過程的一部分"},{"english":"far more durable than","chinese":"比……持久得多"},{"english":"a single chapter in a textbook","chinese":"教科書中的單一章節"},{"english":"explain knowledge clearly","chinese":"清楚解釋知識"},{"english":"their deeper role","chinese":"他們更深層的角色"},{"english":"care about learning","chinese":"重視學習"},{"english":"be handed over","chinese":"被交付；被傳遞"},{"english":"confidence, curiosity and purpose","chinese":"信心、好奇心和目標感"},{"english":"have to be awakened","chinese":"必須被喚醒"}]},"model-essay-16-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-16-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:16","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-16-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q16","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Education budgets are often debated because schools must decide whether limited funds should be directed towards modern equipment or human instruction. Some argue that greater investment in technology, such as computers and digital platforms, is essential, while others believe that teachers deserve more financial support. In my view, although technology is useful, schools should prioritise spending on teachers because they remain the central force behind effective learning.","chinese":"教育預算經常引起討論，因為學校必須決定有限的資金應該投放於現代設備，還是投放於人的教學。 有些人認為，增加對科技的投資，例如電腦和數碼平台，是必不可少的；而另一些人則認為，教師更值得得到更多財政支持。 在我看來，儘管科技是有用的，學校仍應優先把資金用於教師身上，因為教師仍然是有效學習背後的核心力量。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Those who support greater investment in technology argue that digital tools can make education more efficient and accessible. Computers allow students to research information quickly, practise independently, and develop digital skills that are now required in most workplaces. For example, a student who has access to online learning software can review difficult topics at home and learn at a pace that suits them. In this sense, technology can widen learning opportunities and prepare students for a world in which digital literacy is no longer optional.","chinese":"支持增加科技投資的人認為，數碼工具可以令教育更有效率，也更容易獲得。 電腦讓學生能夠快速搜尋資料、獨立練習，並培養現今大多數職場都需要的數碼技能。 例如，一名能夠使用網上學習軟件的學生，可以在家中重溫困難的課題，並按照適合自己的速度學習。 從這個角度來看，科技能夠擴大學習機會，並幫助學生為一個數碼素養已不再是可有可無的世界做好準備。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, spending more money on teachers is far more important because even the best technology cannot replace professional guidance, emotional support, and classroom judgment. A skilled teacher does not merely deliver information; they explain difficult ideas, notice when students are confused, adjust lessons, and motivate learners who may otherwise give up. For instance, a computer programme can mark an answer as wrong, but a teacher can identify why the mistake was made and show the student how to improve. Without well-trained and well-paid teachers, expensive devices may become little more than shiny distractions.","chinese":"然而，把更多金錢投放於教師身上重要得多，因為即使是最好的科技，也無法取代專業指導、情感支持和課堂判斷。 一位有能力的教師不只是傳遞資訊；他們會解釋困難的概念、察覺學生何時感到困惑、調整課堂，並鼓勵那些否則可能會放棄的學習者。 例如，一個電腦程式可以把答案標示為錯誤，但教師能夠指出錯誤產生的原因，並向學生展示如何改進。 如果沒有受過良好訓練並獲得合理薪酬的教師，昂貴的設備可能只會變成華而不實的干擾物。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 3","english":"I therefore believe that schools should invest more heavily in teachers. Better salaries can attract talented graduates into the profession, while regular training can help existing teachers use both traditional and digital methods more effectively. If teachers are supported properly, they can also make technology more meaningful in the classroom.","chinese":"因此，我認為學校應該更大力投資於教師。 更好的薪酬可以吸引有才華的畢業生加入這個行業，而定期培訓則可以幫助現有教師更有效地使用傳統和數碼教學方法。 如果教師得到適當支持，他們也能夠讓科技在課堂中變得更有意義。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, technology has a valuable role in modern education, but teachers should receive the larger share of school funding. Computers can assist learning, but teachers shape understanding, confidence, and long-term academic growth.","chinese":"總結來說，科技在現代教育中具有重要作用，但教師應該獲得學校資金中較大的部分。 電腦可以輔助學習，但教師塑造的是理解力、信心，以及長遠的學術成長。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"education budgets","chinese":"教育預算"},{"english":"be often debated","chinese":"經常被討論"},{"english":"limited funds","chinese":"有限資金"},{"english":"be directed towards","chinese":"被投放於"},{"english":"modern equipment","chinese":"現代設備"},{"english":"human instruction","chinese":"人的教學；教師指導"},{"english":"greater investment in","chinese":"對……更多投資"},{"english":"digital platforms","chinese":"數碼平台"},{"english":"be essential","chinese":"是必要的"},{"english":"deserve more financial support","chinese":"值得更多財政支持"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"prioritise spending on","chinese":"優先將資金投放於"},{"english":"the central force behind","chinese":"……背後的核心力量"},{"english":"effective learning","chinese":"有效學習"},{"english":"those who support","chinese":"支持……的人"},{"english":"digital tools","chinese":"數碼工具"},{"english":"make education more efficient and accessible","chinese":"令教育更高效和更容易取得"},{"english":"research information quickly","chinese":"快速查找資料"},{"english":"practise independently","chinese":"獨立練習"},{"english":"develop digital skills","chinese":"培養數碼技能"},{"english":"be required in","chinese":"在……中被要求"},{"english":"most workplaces","chinese":"大多數工作場所"},{"english":"have access to","chinese":"可以使用；可以取得"},{"english":"online learning software","chinese":"網上學習軟件"},{"english":"review difficult topics","chinese":"重溫困難課題"},{"english":"learn at a pace that suits them","chinese":"按適合自己的進度學習"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"widen learning opportunities","chinese":"擴闊學習機會"},{"english":"prepare students for","chinese":"讓學生為……作準備"},{"english":"digital literacy","chinese":"數碼素養"},{"english":"no longer optional","chinese":"不再是可有可無"},{"english":"spending more money on","chinese":"在……上花更多錢"},{"english":"far more important","chinese":"重要得多"},{"english":"even the best technology","chinese":"即使是最好的科技"},{"english":"cannot replace","chinese":"不能取代"},{"english":"professional guidance","chinese":"專業指導"},{"english":"emotional support","chinese":"情感支援"},{"english":"classroom judgment","chinese":"課堂判斷力"},{"english":"a skilled teacher","chinese":"熟練的老師"},{"english":"not merely deliver information","chinese":"不只是傳遞資訊"},{"english":"explain difficult ideas","chinese":"解釋困難概念"},{"english":"notice when students are confused","chinese":"留意到學生何時感到困惑"},{"english":"adjust lessons","chinese":"調整課堂"},{"english":"motivate learners","chinese":"激勵學習者"},{"english":"may otherwise give up","chinese":"否則可能會放棄"},{"english":"a computer programme","chinese":"電腦程式"},{"english":"mark an answer as wrong","chinese":"將答案標示為錯誤"},{"english":"identify why","chinese":"找出為何"},{"english":"the mistake was made","chinese":"錯誤是怎樣造成的"},{"english":"show the student how to improve","chinese":"向學生展示如何改進"},{"english":"well-trained and well-paid teachers","chinese":"受良好培訓且薪酬合理的老師"},{"english":"expensive devices","chinese":"昂貴裝置"},{"english":"little more than","chinese":"只不過是"},{"english":"shiny distractions","chinese":"外表吸引但分散注意力的東西"},{"english":"invest more heavily in","chinese":"加大對……的投資"},{"english":"better salaries","chinese":"更好的薪酬"},{"english":"attract talented graduates","chinese":"吸引有才華的畢業生"},{"english":"into the profession","chinese":"進入這個行業"},{"english":"regular training","chinese":"定期培訓"},{"english":"existing teachers","chinese":"現職教師"},{"english":"traditional and digital methods","chinese":"傳統和數碼方法"},{"english":"more effectively","chinese":"更有效地"},{"english":"be supported properly","chinese":"得到適當支持"},{"english":"make technology more meaningful","chinese":"令科技更有意義"},{"english":"in the classroom","chinese":"在課堂中"},{"english":"a valuable role in","chinese":"在……中有寶貴作用"},{"english":"modern education","chinese":"現代教育"},{"english":"the larger share of","chinese":"較大份額的"},{"english":"school funding","chinese":"學校資金"},{"english":"assist learning","chinese":"輔助學習"},{"english":"shape understanding","chinese":"塑造理解"},{"english":"confidence","chinese":"信心"},{"english":"long-term academic growth","chinese":"長遠學業成長"}]},"model-essay-16-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-16-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:16","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-16-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q16","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Success is rarely achieved in isolation. In almost every field, from education to business, people have to work with others, persuade them, and respond to their expectations. For this reason, I completely agree that people skills are essential for success, because they turn individual ability into useful social and professional outcomes.","chinese":"成功很少是獨自一人便能取得的。在幾乎每一個領域中，從教育到商業，人們都必須與他人合作、說服他人，並回應他人的期望。 因此，我完全同意人際交往能力對成功至關重要，因為它們能把個人的能力轉化為有用的社交和專業成果。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"First, interpersonal skills determine how effectively a person can cooperate in a group. A capable worker who communicates poorly may produce good ideas, but those ideas can be misunderstood, ignored, or resisted. By contrast, someone who listens carefully, explains clearly, and handles disagreement calmly can keep a team moving in the same direction. For example, in a workplace project, the employee who can divide responsibilities tactfully and discuss problems before they become personal conflicts is more likely to deliver results than a brilliant colleague who alienates everyone. In this sense, people skills act as the bridge between competence and performance.","chinese":"首先，人際交往能力決定了一個人能多有效地在群體中合作。 一位有能力但溝通欠佳的員工或許能提出好主意，但那些想法可能會被誤解、忽視，甚至遭到抗拒。 相比之下，一個能夠仔細聆聽、清楚解釋，並冷靜處理分歧的人，能夠讓團隊朝著同一方向前進。 例如，在一個職場項目中，能夠得體地分配責任，並在問題變成人際衝突之前加以討論的員工，比起一位才華出眾卻疏遠所有人的同事，更有可能取得成果。 從這個意義上說，人際交往能力就像能力與表現之間的橋樑。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Second, success often depends on trust and long-term relationships. Employers, clients, teachers, and colleagues are more likely to support people who appear reliable, respectful, and emotionally mature. Opportunities are rarely offered to qualifications on paper alone; they are offered to people whose character others can read and trust. A small business owner, for instance, may sell an excellent product, but if he dismisses customers’ concerns or treats staff harshly, his reputation will quickly suffer. On the other hand, an owner who listens to complaints, encourages employees, and builds loyalty can turn ordinary transactions into lasting relationships. These relationships often become the foundation of future growth.","chinese":"第二，成功往往取決於信任和長遠關係。 僱主、客戶、老師和同事更有可能支持那些看起來可靠、尊重他人，並且情緒成熟的人。 機會很少只會因紙面上的資歷而被提供；它們會被提供給那些其品格能被他人理解並信任的人。 例如，一位小企業老闆可能售賣非常出色的產品，但如果他忽視顧客的憂慮，或嚴苛對待員工，他的聲譽很快便會受損。 另一方面，一位願意聆聽投訴、鼓勵員工並建立忠誠度的老闆，能夠把普通的交易轉化為長久的關係。 這些關係往往會成為未來發展的基礎。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully agree that people skills are essential for success. Knowledge, talent, and hard work matter greatly, but without the ability to communicate, cooperate, and earn trust, those strengths are far less likely to produce meaningful achievement.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意人際交往能力對成功至關重要。 知識、天分和努力都非常重要，但如果缺乏溝通、合作和贏得信任的能力，這些優勢便遠不那麼可能產生有意義的成就。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"success","chinese":"成功"},{"english":"rarely achieved in isolation","chinese":"很少能孤立地取得"},{"english":"in almost every field","chinese":"在幾乎每個領域"},{"english":"from education to business","chinese":"從教育到商業"},{"english":"work with others","chinese":"與他人合作"},{"english":"persuade them","chinese":"說服他們"},{"english":"respond to their expectations","chinese":"回應他們的期望"},{"english":"for this reason","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"people skills","chinese":"人際技巧"},{"english":"essential for success","chinese":"對成功必不可少"},{"english":"turn individual ability into","chinese":"將個人能力轉化為……"},{"english":"useful social and professional outcomes","chinese":"有用的社交和專業成果"},{"english":"interpersonal skills","chinese":"人際交往技巧"},{"english":"determine how effectively","chinese":"決定……有多有效"},{"english":"cooperate in a group","chinese":"在小組中合作"},{"english":"capable worker","chinese":"有能力的員工"},{"english":"communicates poorly","chinese":"溝通欠佳"},{"english":"produce good ideas","chinese":"提出好想法"},{"english":"be misunderstood, ignored, or resisted","chinese":"被誤解、忽視或抗拒"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"listens carefully","chinese":"細心聆聽"},{"english":"explains clearly","chinese":"清楚解釋"},{"english":"handles disagreement calmly","chinese":"冷靜處理分歧"},{"english":"keep a team moving in the same direction","chinese":"令團隊朝同一方向前進"},{"english":"workplace project","chinese":"工作項目"},{"english":"divide responsibilities tactfully","chinese":"圓滑地分配責任"},{"english":"discuss problems before","chinese":"在……之前討論問題"},{"english":"personal conflicts","chinese":"個人衝突"},{"english":"be more likely to deliver results","chinese":"更有可能取得成果"},{"english":"brilliant colleague","chinese":"才華出眾的同事"},{"english":"alienates everyone","chinese":"疏離所有人"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"act as the bridge between","chinese":"成為……之間的橋樑"},{"english":"competence and performance","chinese":"能力和表現"},{"english":"depends on trust","chinese":"取決於信任"},{"english":"long-term relationships","chinese":"長遠關係"},{"english":"employers, clients, teachers, and colleagues","chinese":"僱主、客戶、老師和同事"},{"english":"be more likely to support","chinese":"更有可能支持"},{"english":"appear reliable","chinese":"顯得可靠"},{"english":"respectful","chinese":"尊重他人的"},{"english":"emotionally mature","chinese":"情緒成熟"},{"english":"qualifications on paper alone","chinese":"單靠紙面資歷"},{"english":"whose character others can read and trust","chinese":"其品格能被他人理解和信任的人"},{"english":"small business owner","chinese":"小企業東主"},{"english":"sell an excellent product","chinese":"銷售出色產品"},{"english":"dismisses customers' concerns","chinese":"漠視顧客的憂慮"},{"english":"treats staff harshly","chinese":"嚴厲對待員工"},{"english":"reputation will suffer","chinese":"聲譽會受損"},{"english":"on the other hand","chinese":"另一方面"},{"english":"listens to complaints","chinese":"聆聽投訴"},{"english":"encourages employees","chinese":"鼓勵員工"},{"english":"builds loyalty","chinese":"建立忠誠"},{"english":"ordinary transactions","chinese":"普通交易"},{"english":"lasting relationships","chinese":"持久關係"},{"english":"foundation of future growth","chinese":"未來發展的基礎"},{"english":"knowledge, talent, and hard work","chinese":"知識、才能和努力"},{"english":"matter greatly","chinese":"非常重要"},{"english":"the ability to communicate","chinese":"溝通能力"},{"english":"cooperate","chinese":"合作"},{"english":"earn trust","chinese":"贏得信任"},{"english":"far less likely to","chinese":"可能性低得多"},{"english":"meaningful achievement","chinese":"有意義的成就"}]},"model-essay-17-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-17-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:17","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-17-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q17","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Public libraries have long been physical spaces where people borrow books, study quietly, and seek reliable information. However, some believe that these institutions will soon exist only online, with all books and services becoming digitally accessible. This development would bring several clear benefits, although it would also create notable drawbacks.","chinese":"[長久以來，公共圖書館一直是人們借閱書籍、安靜學習，以及尋找可靠資訊的實體場所。] [然而，有些人認為，這些機構很快將只以線上形式存在，所有書籍和服務都會以數碼方式供大眾使用。] [這種發展會帶來幾個明顯的好處，但同時也會產生不容忽視的缺點。]"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One major advantage of online-only libraries is accessibility. Digital platforms allow users to obtain books, journals, and reference materials instantly, regardless of location or opening hours. This is especially beneficial for people living in remote areas, those with mobility issues, and full-time workers who may find it difficult to visit a library building in person. Another benefit is efficiency. Online collections can be updated more quickly, and searching for a specific title or topic becomes far easier when readers can use keywords rather than walk through shelves. In addition, digital services may reduce certain operational costs, such as maintaining large buildings or printing multiple physical copies of the same text.","chinese":"[線上圖書館的一大優點是可及性。] [數碼平台讓使用者無論身在何處，也不受開放時間限制，都能即時取得書籍、期刊和參考資料。] [這對居住在偏遠地區的人、行動不便者，以及難以親身前往圖書館的全職工作者尤其有利。] [另一個優點是效率。] [線上館藏可以更快更新，而當讀者能以關鍵字搜尋，而不是在書架間來回尋找時，要找到特定書名或主題也會容易得多。] [此外，數碼服務還可能降低某些營運成本，例如維持大型館舍的開支，或印刷同一文本的多本實體副本。] [因此，線上圖書館能同時提升資訊取得的便利性，以及圖書館服務的效率。]"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, the disappearance of library buildings would also have serious disadvantages. The most obvious is digital inequality. Not everyone has a stable internet connection, suitable devices, or the technical skills needed to use online resources comfortably. For such individuals, a fully digital system would not broaden access but narrow it. Furthermore, public libraries are more than book-lending services; they are community spaces. Many people rely on them as quiet places to study, attend workshops, use computers, or ask librarians for face-to-face guidance. Once a library exists only on a screen, that human element may be lost. Knowledge may remain available, yet the sense of welcome, support, and public belonging could quietly disappear.","chinese":"[然而，圖書館建築的消失也會帶來嚴重的缺點。] [其中最明顯的一點就是數碼不平等。] [並不是每個人都擁有穩定的網絡連線、合適的設備，或足以熟練使用網上資源的技術能力。] [對這些人而言，全面數碼化的系統不但不會擴大使用機會，反而會收窄它。] [此外，公共圖書館不只是借書服務；它們同時也是社區空間。] [很多人依賴圖書館作為安靜的學習場所、參加工作坊的地點、使用電腦的空間，或向館員尋求面對面的指導。] [一旦圖書館只存在於螢幕之上，那種人性化的元素便可能消失。知識也許仍然可以被取得，但那份被歡迎、被支持，以及對公共空間的歸屬感，卻可能悄然消散。] [因此，純線上圖書館在理論上看似提升可及性，但在實際上卻可能排除弱勢群體，並削弱社區生活。]"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, turning public libraries into entirely online services would improve convenience, reach, and efficiency. At the same time, it could deepen social inequality and weaken the wider community role that physical libraries still play.","chinese":"[總結來說，把公共圖書館完全轉為線上服務，將會提升便利性、覆蓋範圍和整體效率。] [與此同時，這也可能加劇社會不平等，並削弱實體圖書館至今仍然承擔的更廣泛社區功能。]"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"public libraries","chinese":"公共圖書館"},{"english":"have long been","chinese":"長久以來一直是"},{"english":"physical spaces","chinese":"實體空間"},{"english":"borrow books","chinese":"借閱圖書"},{"english":"study quietly","chinese":"安靜地溫習；安靜地學習"},{"english":"seek reliable information","chinese":"尋求可靠資料"},{"english":"these institutions","chinese":"這些機構"},{"english":"exist only online","chinese":"只以網上形式存在"},{"english":"digitally accessible","chinese":"可透過數碼方式取得"},{"english":"several clear benefits","chinese":"幾個明顯好處"},{"english":"notable drawbacks","chinese":"顯著缺點"},{"english":"online-only libraries","chinese":"純網上圖書館"},{"english":"accessibility","chinese":"可取得性；便利程度"},{"english":"digital platforms","chinese":"數碼平台"},{"english":"obtain books, journals, and reference materials","chinese":"取得圖書、期刊及參考資料"},{"english":"reference materials","chinese":"參考資料"},{"english":"regardless of location or opening hours","chinese":"不受地點或開放時間限制"},{"english":"opening hours","chinese":"開放時間"},{"english":"especially beneficial for","chinese":"對……尤其有益"},{"english":"remote areas","chinese":"偏遠地區"},{"english":"mobility issues","chinese":"行動不便"},{"english":"full-time workers","chinese":"全職工作人士"},{"english":"visit a library building in person","chinese":"親身到訪圖書館大樓"},{"english":"another benefit is efficiency","chinese":"另一個好處是效率"},{"english":"online collections","chinese":"網上館藏"},{"english":"be updated more quickly","chinese":"更快更新"},{"english":"searching for a specific title or topic","chinese":"搜尋特定書名或主題"},{"english":"far easier","chinese":"容易得多"},{"english":"use keywords","chinese":"使用關鍵字"},{"english":"walk through shelves","chinese":"在書架之間逐一尋找"},{"english":"digital services","chinese":"數碼服務"},{"english":"operational costs","chinese":"營運成本"},{"english":"maintaining large buildings","chinese":"維護大型建築物"},{"english":"printing multiple physical copies","chinese":"印製多本實體副本"},{"english":"physical copies","chinese":"實體副本"},{"english":"the disappearance of library buildings","chinese":"圖書館大樓的消失"},{"english":"serious disadvantages","chinese":"嚴重缺點"},{"english":"digital inequality","chinese":"數碼不平等"},{"english":"a stable internet connection","chinese":"穩定的互聯網連接"},{"english":"suitable devices","chinese":"合適的裝置"},{"english":"technical skills","chinese":"技術技能"},{"english":"online resources","chinese":"網上資源"},{"english":"broaden access","chinese":"擴大使用機會"},{"english":"narrow it","chinese":"收窄使用機會"},{"english":"book-lending services","chinese":"借書服務"},{"english":"community spaces","chinese":"社區空間"},{"english":"rely on them as","chinese":"依賴它們作為……"},{"english":"attend workshops","chinese":"參加工作坊"},{"english":"face-to-face guidance","chinese":"面對面指導"},{"english":"exists only on a screen","chinese":"只存在於屏幕上"},{"english":"the human element","chinese":"人情味；人與人之間的元素"},{"english":"may be lost","chinese":"可能會失去"},{"english":"knowledge may remain available","chinese":"知識可能仍然可取得"},{"english":"the sense of welcome","chinese":"受歡迎和被接納的感覺"},{"english":"public belonging","chinese":"公共歸屬感"},{"english":"quietly disappear","chinese":"悄然消失"},{"english":"turning public libraries into","chinese":"將公共圖書館變成……"},{"english":"entirely online services","chinese":"完全網上化的服務"},{"english":"improve convenience, reach, and efficiency","chinese":"提升便利性、覆蓋範圍和效率"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"deepen social inequality","chinese":"加深社會不平等"},{"english":"weaken the wider community role","chinese":"削弱更廣泛的社區角色"},{"english":"physical libraries","chinese":"實體圖書館"},{"english":"still play","chinese":"仍然發揮"}]},"model-essay-17-ielts-cause-solution":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-17-ielts-cause-solution","essayKey":"cause-solution:17","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-17-ielts-cause-solution","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/problem-and-cause/EdmundBd9CnS-Q17","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many countries, a growing number of people from farming communities are leaving the countryside and moving to cities in search of paid employment. This trend can create serious pressure both in urban centres and in rural areas, but it can be addressed through stronger rural investment and better-managed urban planning.","chinese":"在許多國家，越來越多來自農業社群的人正離開鄉村，搬到城市尋找有薪工作。 這種趨勢可能同時為城市中心和農村地區帶來嚴重壓力，但它可以透過更強的農村投資和更妥善管理的城市規劃來應對。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One major consequence is that cities may become overcrowded before they are ready to absorb the new population. When large numbers of rural workers arrive within a short period, housing, transport and public services can be stretched beyond their normal capacity. As a result, many newcomers may end up living in poor-quality accommodation, working in unstable jobs, or competing intensely for low-paid work. For example, a young farmer who moves to a major city without recognised qualifications may find that the city offers more opportunities in theory than in practice. At the same time, this movement can weaken rural communities. If too many working-age people leave agriculture, farms may lose labour, villages may become dominated by the elderly, and local food production may gradually decline.","chinese":"一個主要後果是，城市可能在尚未準備好吸收新增人口之前便變得過度擁擠。 當大量農村勞工在短時間內湧入城市時，住房、交通和公共服務可能會被拉扯到超出其正常承載能力的程度。 結果是，許多新來者最終可能住在質素低劣的住所中，從事不穩定的工作，或為低薪工作進行激烈競爭。 例如，一位沒有受認可資歷的年輕農民搬到大城市後，可能會發現這座城市在理論上提供更多機會，但在實際上並非如此。 與此同時，這種人口流動也可能削弱農村社群。 如果太多處於工作年齡的人離開農業，農場可能會失去勞動力，村莊可能會變成以長者為主，而本地糧食生產也可能逐漸下降。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"One practical response is to make rural life economically viable rather than treating cities as the only path to progress. Governments could invest in irrigation, storage facilities, rural roads and digital access so that farmers can sell their products more efficiently and earn a steadier income. They should also support modern agricultural training, small businesses and food-processing industries, which would create employment near people’s homes. In cities, authorities need to plan for migration instead of simply reacting to it. Affordable housing, vocational training and reliable public transport would help new arrivals enter the formal economy and avoid being pushed to the margins.","chinese":"一個實際的應對方法，是令農村生活在經濟上變得可行，而不是把城市視為唯一的進步道路。 政府可以投資灌溉系統、儲存設施、農村道路和數位連接，使農民能夠更有效率地出售產品，並賺取更穩定的收入。 他們也應該支持現代農業培訓、小型企業和食品加工產業，這些都能在人們居住地附近創造就業機會。 在城市中，當局需要為人口遷移作出規劃，而不是單純在問題出現後才作出反應。 可負擔住房、職業培訓和可靠的公共交通，將有助於新來者進入正規經濟體系，並避免被推向社會邊緣。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, rural-to-urban migration can lead to overcrowded cities, insecure employment and a decline in agricultural communities. However, if governments improve rural opportunities while managing urban growth carefully, this movement can become far less damaging and more sustainable.","chinese":"總結來說，農村到城市的人口遷移可能導致城市過度擁擠、就業不穩定，以及農業社群衰落。 然而，如果政府在謹慎管理城市增長的同時改善農村機會，這種人口流動便可以變得危害少得多，也更加可持續。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"a growing number of","chinese":"越來越多"},{"english":"farming communities","chinese":"農業社區"},{"english":"leave the countryside","chinese":"離開鄉郊"},{"english":"move to cities","chinese":"搬到城市"},{"english":"in search of paid employment","chinese":"尋找受薪工作"},{"english":"create serious pressure","chinese":"造成嚴重壓力"},{"english":"urban centres","chinese":"城市中心"},{"english":"rural areas","chinese":"鄉郊地區"},{"english":"be addressed through","chinese":"透過……處理"},{"english":"rural investment","chinese":"鄉郊投資"},{"english":"better-managed urban planning","chinese":"管理更完善的城市規劃"},{"english":"one major consequence","chinese":"一個主要後果"},{"english":"become overcrowded","chinese":"變得過度擠迫"},{"english":"be ready to absorb","chinese":"準備好吸收"},{"english":"the new population","chinese":"新增人口"},{"english":"rural workers","chinese":"鄉郊工人"},{"english":"within a short period","chinese":"在短時間內"},{"english":"public services","chinese":"公共服務"},{"english":"be stretched beyond","chinese":"超出……負荷"},{"english":"normal capacity","chinese":"正常承載能力"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"newcomers","chinese":"新來者"},{"english":"end up living in","chinese":"最終住在"},{"english":"poor-quality accommodation","chinese":"質素差的住所"},{"english":"unstable jobs","chinese":"不穩定的工作"},{"english":"compete intensely for","chinese":"激烈競爭"},{"english":"low-paid work","chinese":"低薪工作"},{"english":"recognised qualifications","chinese":"受承認的資歷"},{"english":"in theory than in practice","chinese":"理論上多於實際上"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"weaken rural communities","chinese":"削弱鄉郊社區"},{"english":"working-age people","chinese":"適齡工作人口"},{"english":"leave agriculture","chinese":"離開農業"},{"english":"lose labour","chinese":"失去勞動力"},{"english":"be dominated by the elderly","chinese":"以長者為主"},{"english":"local food production","chinese":"本地糧食生產"},{"english":"gradually decline","chinese":"逐漸下降"},{"english":"one practical response","chinese":"一個實際對策"},{"english":"economically viable","chinese":"經濟上可行"},{"english":"the only path to progress","chinese":"進步的唯一途徑"},{"english":"invest in irrigation","chinese":"投資灌溉"},{"english":"storage facilities","chinese":"儲存設施"},{"english":"rural roads","chinese":"鄉郊道路"},{"english":"digital access","chinese":"數碼連接"},{"english":"sell their products more efficiently","chinese":"更有效率地銷售產品"},{"english":"earn a steadier income","chinese":"賺取較穩定的收入"},{"english":"modern agricultural training","chinese":"現代農業培訓"},{"english":"small businesses","chinese":"小型企業"},{"english":"food-processing industries","chinese":"食品加工業"},{"english":"create employment near","chinese":"在……附近創造就業"},{"english":"plan for migration","chinese":"為人口遷移作規劃"},{"english":"instead of simply reacting to it","chinese":"而不是只作被動回應"},{"english":"affordable housing","chinese":"可負擔住房"},{"english":"vocational training","chinese":"職業培訓"},{"english":"reliable public transport","chinese":"可靠的公共交通"},{"english":"new arrivals","chinese":"新到埗人士"},{"english":"enter the formal economy","chinese":"進入正規經濟"},{"english":"be pushed to the margins","chinese":"被推到邊緣"},{"english":"rural-to-urban migration","chinese":"鄉郊至城市的人口遷移"},{"english":"overcrowded cities","chinese":"過度擠迫的城市"},{"english":"insecure employment","chinese":"不穩定就業"},{"english":"a decline in agricultural communities","chinese":"農業社區的衰落"},{"english":"improve rural opportunities","chinese":"改善鄉郊機會"},{"english":"manage urban growth carefully","chinese":"謹慎管理城市增長"},{"english":"far less damaging","chinese":"破壞性大大降低"},{"english":"more sustainable","chinese":"更可持續"}]},"model-essay-17-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-17-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:17","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-17-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q17","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Population growth and rapid urban expansion are placing intense pressure on forests, coastlines, rivers and other scenic areas. Protecting these places is not simply an environmental preference; it brings clear public, economic and cultural benefits. This essay will discuss those benefits and suggest how governments can prevent further loss.","chinese":"人口增長和快速城市擴張，正對森林、海岸線、河流以及其他風景優美的地區造成巨大壓力。 保護這些地方並不只是環境方面的偏好；它能帶來明顯的公共、經濟和文化利益。 本文將討論這些好處，並提出政府可以如何防止這些地方進一步流失。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"First, preserving natural beauty spots improves public health and quality of life. Parks, beaches and woodlands give people a place to breathe, walk and recover from the mental strain of city life. Without such spaces, urban living can become a concrete cage, especially for children and elderly residents who have few affordable ways to relax. These places also support tourism and local employment. A well-protected mountain trail or coastal reserve can attract visitors, create jobs for guides and small businesses, and give communities a reason to value their landscape rather than sell it off piece by piece. In addition, natural sites preserve a country’s identity, as many landscapes are tied to local history, traditions and collective memory.","chinese":"首先，保護自然美景地點能改善公共健康和生活質素。 公園、海灘和林地為人們提供了一個可以呼吸、散步，並從城市生活的精神壓力中恢復過來的地方。 如果沒有這些空間，城市生活可能會變成一個混凝土牢籠，尤其是對於兒童和長者而言，因為他們可負擔的放鬆方式並不多。 這些地方也能支持旅遊業和本地就業。 一條受到良好保護的山徑或海岸保護區，可以吸引遊客、為導遊和小型企業創造職位，並讓社區有理由珍惜自己的景觀，而不是把它一點一點地出售。 此外，自然地點也能保存一個國家的身份認同，因為許多景觀都與本地歷史、傳統和集體記憶緊密相連。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"This problem can be tackled through stronger planning laws and practical conservation funding. Governments should set legal boundaries around important natural sites, limit construction in sensitive zones, and require developers to restore or replace green space when building is unavoidable. This ensures that expansion does not spread like an unchecked tide across every open area. At the same time, protection must be made financially realistic. Entrance fees, eco-tourism revenue and public-private partnerships can fund maintenance, waste control and park staff, while schools and media campaigns can teach citizens why these places matter. When people see natural beauty as shared public wealth rather than empty land waiting to be developed, they are more likely to defend it.","chinese":"這個問題可以透過更強有力的規劃法律和實際的保育資金來處理。 政府應該在重要自然地點周圍設立法律邊界，限制在敏感地區進行建設，並在建築工程無法避免時，要求發展商修復或補回綠化空間。 這能確保城市擴張不會像失控的潮水一樣蔓延到每一片開放空間。 同時，保護工作必須在財政上變得切實可行。 入場費、生態旅遊收入和公私營合作，可以為維修保養、廢物管理和公園員工提供資金，而學校和媒體宣傳活動則可以教導市民為何這些地方重要。 當人們把自然美景視為共享的公共財富，而不是等待發展的空地時，他們更有可能保護它"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, protecting natural beauty spots benefits public health, local economies and cultural identity. The loss of these places can be reduced through firm urban planning, reliable funding and public education, so that development and environmental protection can move forward together.","chinese":"總結來說，保護自然美景地點有利於公共健康、本地經濟和文化身份。 這些地方的流失可以透過堅定的城市規劃、可靠的資金和公共教育來減少，從而讓發展與環境保護能夠共同向前推進。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"population growth","chinese":"人口增長"},{"english":"rapid urban expansion","chinese":"急速城市擴張"},{"english":"placing intense pressure on","chinese":"對……造成巨大壓力"},{"english":"forests, coastlines and rivers","chinese":"森林、海岸線和河流"},{"english":"scenic areas","chinese":"風景區"},{"english":"protecting these places","chinese":"保護這些地方"},{"english":"not simply an environmental preference","chinese":"不只是環保取向"},{"english":"clear public, economic and cultural benefits","chinese":"明顯的公眾、經濟和文化好處"},{"english":"prevent further loss","chinese":"防止進一步流失"},{"english":"preserving natural beauty spots","chinese":"保育自然景點"},{"english":"public health and quality of life","chinese":"公眾健康和生活質素"},{"english":"give people a place to","chinese":"給人們一個地方去……"},{"english":"recover from","chinese":"從……中恢復過來"},{"english":"the mental strain of","chinese":"……帶來的精神壓力"},{"english":"city life","chinese":"城市生活"},{"english":"urban living","chinese":"城市生活"},{"english":"a concrete cage","chinese":"混凝土牢籠"},{"english":"affordable ways to relax","chinese":"負擔得起的放鬆方式"},{"english":"elderly residents","chinese":"年長居民"},{"english":"support tourism and local employment","chinese":"支持旅遊業和本地就業"},{"english":"a well-protected mountain trail","chinese":"保護良好的山徑"},{"english":"coastal reserve","chinese":"海岸保護區"},{"english":"attract visitors","chinese":"吸引遊客"},{"english":"create jobs for","chinese":"為……創造職位"},{"english":"small businesses","chinese":"小型企業"},{"english":"give communities a reason to","chinese":"給社區理由去……"},{"english":"value their landscape","chinese":"珍惜自己的景觀"},{"english":"sell it off piece by piece","chinese":"逐步賣掉"},{"english":"preserve a country's identity","chinese":"保留一個國家的身份特色"},{"english":"be tied to","chinese":"與……有關連"},{"english":"local history and traditions","chinese":"本地歷史和傳統"},{"english":"collective memory","chinese":"集體記憶"},{"english":"be tackled through","chinese":"透過……處理"},{"english":"stronger planning laws","chinese":"更嚴格的規劃法例"},{"english":"practical conservation funding","chinese":"實際可行的保育資金"},{"english":"set legal boundaries around","chinese":"為……劃定法律界線"},{"english":"important natural sites","chinese":"重要自然地點"},{"english":"limit construction in","chinese":"限制在……興建"},{"english":"sensitive zones","chinese":"敏感地帶"},{"english":"require developers to","chinese":"要求發展商去……"},{"english":"restore or replace green space","chinese":"修復或替代綠化空間"},{"english":"when building is unavoidable","chinese":"當建設無可避免時"},{"english":"does not spread like","chinese":"不會像……般蔓延"},{"english":"an unchecked tide","chinese":"失控的潮水"},{"english":"every open area","chinese":"每一片開放空間"},{"english":"financially realistic","chinese":"財政上可行"},{"english":"entrance fees","chinese":"入場費"},{"english":"eco-tourism revenue","chinese":"生態旅遊收入"},{"english":"public-private partnerships","chinese":"公私營合作"},{"english":"fund maintenance","chinese":"資助維護工作"},{"english":"waste control","chinese":"廢物管理"},{"english":"park staff","chinese":"公園職員"},{"english":"media campaigns","chinese":"媒體宣傳活動"},{"english":"shared public wealth","chinese":"共享公共財富"},{"english":"empty land waiting to be developed","chinese":"等待開發的空地"},{"english":"more likely to defend","chinese":"更有可能捍衛"},{"english":"firm urban planning","chinese":"嚴格的城市規劃"},{"english":"reliable funding","chinese":"可靠資金"},{"english":"public education","chinese":"公眾教育"},{"english":"move forward together","chinese":"一起向前發展；並行發展"}]},"model-essay-17-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-17-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:17","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-17-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q17","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"It is widely believed that a child’s academic progress is shaped either mainly by parents or mainly by teachers. While parents are undeniably important because they create the home environment in which learning habits begin, I believe teachers have the greater influence on academic development, as they directly control the quality, structure and direction of a child’s formal education.","chinese":"人們普遍認為，孩子的學業進步主要是由父母或老師所塑造的。 雖然父母無疑十分重要，因為他們創造了孩子學習習慣開始形成的家庭環境， 但我認為老師對學業發展有更大的影響，因為他們直接掌控孩子正規教育的質素、結構和方向。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"On the one hand, parents play a powerful role in shaping a child’s attitude towards study. Children who grow up in homes where reading, discipline and curiosity are encouraged are more likely to see education as a normal part of daily life rather than a burden. For example, a parent who sets regular study times, limits distractions and praises effort can help a child build persistence long before exam pressure appears. In this sense, parents are like the soil in which academic confidence first takes root: without their support, even a capable student may lose motivation.","chinese":"一方面，父母在塑造孩子對學習的態度方面扮演著重要角色。 在鼓勵閱讀、自律和好奇心的家庭中成長的孩子，更有可能把教育視為日常生活中正常的一部分，而不是一種負擔。 例如，一位會設定固定學習時間、限制干擾並讚賞努力的父母，能夠在考試壓力出現之前很早便幫助孩子建立堅持的能力。 從這個意義上說，父母就像學業信心最初扎根的土壤：如果沒有他們的支持，即使是有能力的學生也可能失去動力。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"On the other hand, teachers usually have a more direct and professional impact on a child’s academic growth. Their influence is not limited to encouragement; they design lessons, explain complex ideas, assess progress and correct misunderstandings before they become permanent weaknesses. A skilled mathematics teacher, for instance, can identify why a student keeps making the same algebra mistake and then adjust the explanation until the concept becomes clear. This kind of targeted academic guidance is difficult for most parents to provide, especially as subjects become more specialised. Moreover, teachers can compare a child’s performance with that of many peers, which allows them to judge strengths and weaknesses more accurately.","chinese":"另一方面，老師通常對孩子的學業成長有更直接且更專業的影響。 他們的影響並不局限於鼓勵；他們會設計課程、解釋複雜概念、評估進度，並在誤解變成長期弱點之前加以糾正。 例如，一位熟練的數學老師可以判斷為甚麼某個學生不斷犯同一個代數錯誤，然後調整解釋方式，直到概念變得清晰為止。 這種具針對性的學業指導，是大多數父母難以提供的，尤其當學科變得更加專門化時更是如此。 此外，老師可以將一個孩子的表現與許多同齡人作比較，這使他們能夠更準確地判斷孩子的優點和弱點。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, parents build the foundations of a child’s learning habits and emotional attitude towards education. However, because teachers possess subject expertise, teaching methods and regular access to academic performance, I believe they exert a greater influence on a child’s academic development.","chinese":"總結來說，父母建立了孩子學習習慣和對教育情感態度的基礎。 然而，由於老師擁有學科專業知識、教學方法，並能定期了解學生的學業表現，我認為他們對孩子的學業發展發揮更大的影響。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"it is widely believed that","chinese":"人們普遍相信"},{"english":"academic progress","chinese":"學業進展"},{"english":"be shaped by","chinese":"受……塑造"},{"english":"either mainly by ... or mainly by","chinese":"主要由……或主要由……"},{"english":"undeniably important","chinese":"無可否認地重要"},{"english":"create the home environment","chinese":"營造家庭環境"},{"english":"learning habits","chinese":"學習習慣"},{"english":"the greater influence on","chinese":"對……有更大影響"},{"english":"academic development","chinese":"學業發展"},{"english":"directly control","chinese":"直接控制"},{"english":"the quality, structure and direction of","chinese":"……的質素、結構和方向"},{"english":"formal education","chinese":"正規教育"},{"english":"on the one hand","chinese":"一方面"},{"english":"play a powerful role in","chinese":"在……中扮演重要角色"},{"english":"shape a child's attitude towards study","chinese":"塑造孩子對學習的態度"},{"english":"grow up in homes where","chinese":"在……的家庭中長大"},{"english":"reading, discipline and curiosity","chinese":"閱讀、自律和好奇心"},{"english":"be encouraged","chinese":"被鼓勵"},{"english":"be more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"see education as","chinese":"將教育視為"},{"english":"a normal part of daily life","chinese":"日常生活的正常一部分"},{"english":"rather than a burden","chinese":"而不是負擔"},{"english":"set regular study times","chinese":"設定固定溫習時間"},{"english":"limit distractions","chinese":"減少干擾"},{"english":"praise effort","chinese":"讚賞努力"},{"english":"build persistence","chinese":"建立毅力"},{"english":"long before","chinese":"早在……之前"},{"english":"exam pressure","chinese":"考試壓力"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"be like the soil in which","chinese":"像……扎根的土壤"},{"english":"academic confidence","chinese":"學業信心"},{"english":"take root","chinese":"扎根"},{"english":"without their support","chinese":"沒有他們的支持"},{"english":"a capable student","chinese":"有能力的學生"},{"english":"lose motivation","chinese":"失去動力"},{"english":"on the other hand","chinese":"另一方面"},{"english":"a more direct and professional impact on","chinese":"對……有更直接和專業的影響"},{"english":"academic growth","chinese":"學業成長"},{"english":"not limited to","chinese":"不限於"},{"english":"design lessons","chinese":"設計課堂"},{"english":"explain complex ideas","chinese":"解釋複雜概念"},{"english":"assess progress","chinese":"評估進展"},{"english":"correct misunderstandings","chinese":"糾正誤解"},{"english":"permanent weaknesses","chinese":"長期弱點"},{"english":"a skilled mathematics teacher","chinese":"熟練的數學老師"},{"english":"identify why","chinese":"找出為何"},{"english":"keep making the same mistake","chinese":"不斷犯同一個錯誤"},{"english":"algebra mistake","chinese":"代數錯誤"},{"english":"adjust the explanation","chinese":"調整解釋方式"},{"english":"the concept becomes clear","chinese":"概念變得清晰"},{"english":"targeted academic guidance","chinese":"針對性的學業指導"},{"english":"be difficult for most parents to provide","chinese":"對大多數家長來說難以提供"},{"english":"become more specialised","chinese":"變得更專門"},{"english":"compare a child's performance with","chinese":"將孩子的表現與……比較"},{"english":"peers","chinese":"同齡人；同學"},{"english":"judge strengths and weaknesses","chinese":"判斷強項和弱點"},{"english":"more accurately","chinese":"更準確地"},{"english":"build the foundations of","chinese":"建立……的基礎"},{"english":"emotional attitude towards","chinese":"對……的情感態度"},{"english":"possess subject expertise","chinese":"具備學科專業知識"},{"english":"teaching methods","chinese":"教學方法"},{"english":"regular access to","chinese":"定期接觸；定期掌握"},{"english":"academic performance","chinese":"學業表現"},{"english":"exert a greater influence on","chinese":"對……施加更大影響"}]},"model-essay-17-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-17-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:17","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-17-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q17","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"It is sometimes claimed that people in earlier generations were happier than people are today. I completely disagree with this view because modern life, despite its pressures, gives people better protection, wider choices, and more control over their lives.","chinese":"有時有人聲稱，以往世代的人比今天的人更加快樂。 我完全不同意這個觀點，因為現代生活雖然有壓力，但它給予人們更好的保障、更廣泛的選擇，以及對自己人生更大的掌控權。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that people today are less exposed to many of the basic fears that shaped life in the past. Earlier generations may be remembered through the warm light of nostalgia, but daily life was often physically harsher and more uncertain. Illness, unsafe work, limited public services, and financial insecurity could turn one setback into a family crisis. By contrast, modern healthcare, labour protection, sanitation, and social support reduce the amount of suffering that people have to accept as normal. For example, a worker who becomes seriously ill today is more likely to receive medical treatment, sick leave, or community support, whereas a similar problem in the past could easily destroy a household’s income. Happiness is not only about having a simple life; it also depends on being safe from preventable misery.","chinese":"第一個原因是，今天的人較少暴露於許多曾經塑造過去生活的基本恐懼之中。 以往世代也許會在懷舊的溫暖光影中被記起，但當時的日常生活往往在物質上更加艱苦，也更加不穩定。 疾病、不安全的工作、有限的公共服務，以及經濟上的不穩定，都可能把一次挫折變成一場家庭危機。 相比之下，現代醫療、勞工保障、衛生設施和社會支援，減少了人們必須視為正常的痛苦。 例如，今天一名嚴重患病的工人更有可能獲得醫療治療、病假或社區支援；然而，在過去，類似的問題很容易摧毀一個家庭的收入。 快樂不只是關於擁有簡單的生活；它也取決於人們是否能遠離可以避免的痛苦。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important point is that modern society allows more personal freedom. In previous generations, many people were trapped by rigid expectations about gender, class, marriage, religion, and work. They might have appeared content, but appearance is not the same as inner happiness. Today, people are more able to choose their education, career, partner, lifestyle, and beliefs. This freedom can create pressure, but it also gives individuals room to build a life that actually fits them. For instance, a young woman who wants to study abroad, start a business, or delay marriage has far more freedom now than her grandmother probably had. That kind of choice is not a small luxury; it is one of the foundations of genuine fulfilment.","chinese":"另一個重要觀點是，現代社會容許更多個人自由。 在以往世代，許多人都被關於性別、階級、婚姻、宗教和工作的僵化期望所束縛。 他們或許看起來滿足，但外表上的滿足並不等同於內心真正的快樂。 今天，人們更能夠選擇自己的教育、職業、伴侶、生活方式和信念。 這種自由可能會帶來壓力，但它也給予個人空間去建立真正適合自己的生活。 例如，一位想出國讀書、創業或推遲婚姻的年輕女性，今天所擁有的自由很可能遠遠多於她祖母當年所擁有的自由。 這種選擇並不是一種微不足道的奢侈；它是真正滿足感的其中一個基礎。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely reject the idea that earlier generations were happier. The past may look peaceful from a distance, but modern life offers greater security, freedom, and human dignity, which make true happiness more attainable today.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全否定以往世代的人更快樂這個想法。 從遠處看，過去也許顯得平靜，但現代生活提供了更大的安全感、自由和人的尊嚴，而這些都使真正的快樂在今天更加容易達到。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"it is sometimes claimed that","chinese":"有時有人聲稱……"},{"english":"earlier generations","chinese":"較早幾代人"},{"english":"completely disagree with","chinese":"完全不同意……"},{"english":"modern life","chinese":"現代生活"},{"english":"despite its pressures","chinese":"儘管有壓力"},{"english":"better protection","chinese":"更好的保障"},{"english":"wider choices","chinese":"更廣泛的選擇"},{"english":"more control over their lives","chinese":"對自己生活有更多掌控"},{"english":"be less exposed to","chinese":"較少面對……"},{"english":"basic fears","chinese":"基本恐懼"},{"english":"shaped life","chinese":"塑造生活"},{"english":"in the past","chinese":"在過去"},{"english":"be remembered through","chinese":"透過……被記住"},{"english":"warm light of nostalgia","chinese":"懷舊的溫暖光芒"},{"english":"daily life","chinese":"日常生活"},{"english":"physically harsher","chinese":"體力上更艱苦"},{"english":"more uncertain","chinese":"更不穩定；更難預測"},{"english":"unsafe work","chinese":"不安全的工作"},{"english":"limited public services","chinese":"有限的公共服務"},{"english":"financial insecurity","chinese":"經濟不穩"},{"english":"one setback","chinese":"一次挫折；一次打擊"},{"english":"family crisis","chinese":"家庭危機"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"modern healthcare","chinese":"現代醫療"},{"english":"labour protection","chinese":"勞工保障"},{"english":"sanitation","chinese":"衞生設施；公共衞生"},{"english":"social support","chinese":"社會支援"},{"english":"reduce the amount of suffering","chinese":"減少痛苦的程度"},{"english":"accept as normal","chinese":"視為正常而接受"},{"english":"seriously ill","chinese":"病重"},{"english":"be more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"medical treatment","chinese":"醫療治療"},{"english":"sick leave","chinese":"病假"},{"english":"community support","chinese":"社區支援"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；然而"},{"english":"destroy a household's income","chinese":"摧毀一個家庭的收入"},{"english":"household income","chinese":"家庭收入"},{"english":"simple life","chinese":"簡單生活"},{"english":"depends on","chinese":"取決於"},{"english":"preventable misery","chinese":"可避免的苦難"},{"english":"personal freedom","chinese":"個人自由"},{"english":"previous generations","chinese":"以往幾代人"},{"english":"be trapped by","chinese":"被……困住"},{"english":"rigid expectations","chinese":"僵化的期望"},{"english":"gender, class, marriage, religion, and work","chinese":"性別、階級、婚姻、宗教和工作"},{"english":"appeared content","chinese":"看似滿足"},{"english":"inner happiness","chinese":"內心幸福"},{"english":"be more able to","chinese":"更有能力去……"},{"english":"career, partner, lifestyle, and beliefs","chinese":"事業、伴侶、生活方式和信念"},{"english":"create pressure","chinese":"造成壓力"},{"english":"gives individuals room to","chinese":"給予個人空間去……"},{"english":"build a life","chinese":"建立一種生活"},{"english":"actually fits them","chinese":"真正適合他們"},{"english":"study abroad","chinese":"到外國留學"},{"english":"start a business","chinese":"創業"},{"english":"delay marriage","chinese":"延遲結婚"},{"english":"far more freedom","chinese":"多得多的自由"},{"english":"small luxury","chinese":"小小的奢侈品"},{"english":"one of the foundations of","chinese":"……的基礎之一"},{"english":"genuine fulfilment","chinese":"真正的滿足感"},{"english":"completely reject the idea that","chinese":"完全否定……的想法"},{"english":"look peaceful from a distance","chinese":"從遠處看似平靜"},{"english":"greater security","chinese":"更大的安全保障"},{"english":"human dignity","chinese":"人性尊嚴"},{"english":"true happiness","chinese":"真正幸福"},{"english":"more attainable","chinese":"更容易達到"}]},"model-essay-18-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-18-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:18","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-18-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q18","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Economic development is widely seen as one of the most effective ways to raise living standards. Although rapid growth can weaken values such as community spirit and family cohesion, I firmly believe that its advantages clearly outweigh its disadvantages because it reduces material hardship and gives governments the means to improve essential public services.","chinese":"經濟發展普遍被視為提升生活水準最有效的方法之一。 儘管快速增長可能削弱社區精神和家庭凝聚力等價值， 我仍然堅信其優點明顯大於缺點，因為它不但能減輕物質匱乏，還能讓政府有能力改善關鍵的公共服務。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The principal advantage of economic development is that it improves people’s lives in immediate, practical ways. As industries expand and businesses invest, more jobs are created, which allows families to earn stable incomes rather than merely get by. With higher earnings, people can afford better housing, more nutritious food and adequate medical care. At the same time, stronger economic activity generates more tax revenue, enabling governments to build schools, hospitals and transport systems. In many developing regions, for example, growth has brought clean water, reliable electricity and wider access to education, transforming daily life from the ground up.","chinese":"經濟發展最主要的優點，是它能以直接而實際的方式改善人們的生活。 當產業擴張、企業增加投資時，就會創造更多就業機會，讓家庭能夠獲得穩定收入，而不只是勉強維生。 有了更高的收入，人們便能負擔更好的住房、更有營養的食物，以及足夠的醫療照顧。 例如，當父母從收入不穩定的低薪工作轉為穩定就業時，他們的孩子通常更有可能享有更健康的飲食和更可靠的醫療照顧。 同時，更活躍的經濟活動也會帶來更多稅收，使政府能夠興建學校、醫院和交通系統。 這意味著，經濟增長不僅能在家庭層面提升生活水準，也能在整體社會層面帶來改善。 例如，在許多發展中地區，經濟增長帶來了潔淨的供水、穩定的電力，以及更廣泛的教育機會，從根本上改變了人們的日常生活。 因此，經濟發展以廣泛而明確的方式，為個人和整個社會帶來了實質的物質利益。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Admittedly, economic progress can come at a social cost. In fast-paced, competitive societies, people often work longer hours, relocate for employment and become more preoccupied with personal success. As a result, values such as neighbourliness, family duty and collective responsibility may gradually fade into the background. For instance, in rapidly expanding cities, adult children may move away for work, leaving elderly parents with less day-to-day support. Consumerism can also encourage the belief that a person’s worth is measured mainly by income. Even so, these losses, serious as they are, do not outweigh the gains. Social values are not gone beyond repair; they can be strengthened through education, family upbringing and public policy, whereas poverty and poor public services cause deeper and more lasting harm.","chinese":"誠然，經濟進步也可能伴隨社會代價。 在節奏快速、競爭激烈的社會中，人們往往工時更長、因工作而搬遷，並且更加執著於個人成就。 結果，鄰里情誼、家庭責任和集體責任等價值，便可能逐漸退居次要位置。 例如，在快速擴張的城市中，成年子女可能因工作而搬離家鄉，令年長父母在日常生活中得到更少照顧與支持。 消費主義也可能助長一種觀念：一個人的價值主要是以收入來衡量的。 當金錢成就成為主要衡量標準時，善良、忠誠和公共精神等品質便可能不再受到同等重視。 這一點可見於某些人會自然而然地崇拜財富，即使那些財富是以犧牲家庭生活或社區責任為代價換來的。 即便如此，這些社會損失雖然嚴重，仍不足以超過經濟發展所帶來的好處，特別是因為這些價值仍可透過教育、家庭培養和公共政策重新加以強化。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, while economic development may erode some important social values, its overall impact is far more positive. By reducing poverty and funding better public services, it improves quality of life on a scale that the disadvantages do not surpass.","chinese":"總結來說，雖然經濟發展可能侵蝕一些重要的社會價值，但它的整體影響仍然遠較正面 透過減少貧窮並為更完善的公共服務提供資金，它在大規模上提升了生活品質，而這是其缺點所無法超越的。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"economic development","chinese":"經濟發展"},{"english":"be widely seen as","chinese":"被廣泛視為"},{"english":"one of the most effective ways to","chinese":"……最有效的方法之一"},{"english":"raise living standards","chinese":"提高生活水平"},{"english":"rapid growth","chinese":"快速增長"},{"english":"weaken values","chinese":"削弱價值觀"},{"english":"community spirit","chinese":"社區精神"},{"english":"family cohesion","chinese":"家庭凝聚力"},{"english":"clearly outweigh","chinese":"明顯大於"},{"english":"material hardship","chinese":"物質困難"},{"english":"gives governments the means to","chinese":"令政府有能力去"},{"english":"essential public services","chinese":"必要公共服務"},{"english":"the principal advantage of","chinese":"……的主要好處"},{"english":"immediate, practical ways","chinese":"即時而實際的方式"},{"english":"industries expand","chinese":"產業擴展"},{"english":"businesses invest","chinese":"企業投資"},{"english":"stable incomes","chinese":"穩定收入"},{"english":"rather than merely get by","chinese":"而不是僅僅勉強過活"},{"english":"get by","chinese":"勉強過活"},{"english":"higher earnings","chinese":"更高收入"},{"english":"afford better housing","chinese":"負擔得起更好的住屋"},{"english":"more nutritious food","chinese":"更有營養的食物"},{"english":"adequate medical care","chinese":"足夠的醫療護理"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"stronger economic activity","chinese":"更強的經濟活動"},{"english":"tax revenue","chinese":"稅務收入"},{"english":"enabling governments to","chinese":"使政府能夠"},{"english":"transport systems","chinese":"交通系統"},{"english":"developing regions","chinese":"發展中地區"},{"english":"clean water","chinese":"清潔食水"},{"english":"reliable electricity","chinese":"可靠電力供應"},{"english":"wider access to education","chinese":"更廣泛的教育機會"},{"english":"transform daily life","chinese":"改變日常生活"},{"english":"from the ground up","chinese":"從根本上"},{"english":"admittedly","chinese":"無可否認"},{"english":"economic progress","chinese":"經濟進步"},{"english":"come at a social cost","chinese":"付出社會代價"},{"english":"fast-paced, competitive societies","chinese":"節奏急速、競爭激烈的社會"},{"english":"work longer hours","chinese":"工作時間更長"},{"english":"relocate for employment","chinese":"為工作而搬遷"},{"english":"become more preoccupied with","chinese":"變得更專注於"},{"english":"personal success","chinese":"個人成就"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"neighbourliness","chinese":"鄰里情誼"},{"english":"family duty","chinese":"家庭責任"},{"english":"collective responsibility","chinese":"集體責任"},{"english":"gradually fade into the background","chinese":"逐漸被淡化"},{"english":"rapidly expanding cities","chinese":"急速擴張的城市"},{"english":"move away for work","chinese":"因工作而搬離"},{"english":"elderly parents","chinese":"年老父母"},{"english":"day-to-day support","chinese":"日常支援"},{"english":"consumerism","chinese":"消費主義"},{"english":"encourage the belief that","chinese":"鼓勵一種……的信念"},{"english":"a person's worth","chinese":"一個人的價值"},{"english":"be measured mainly by","chinese":"主要以……衡量"},{"english":"even so","chinese":"即使如此"},{"english":"serious as they are","chinese":"儘管它們很嚴重"},{"english":"the gains","chinese":"得益；好處"},{"english":"beyond repair","chinese":"無法修復"},{"english":"be strengthened through","chinese":"透過……加強"},{"english":"family upbringing","chinese":"家庭教養"},{"english":"public policy","chinese":"公共政策"},{"english":"poverty","chinese":"貧窮"},{"english":"poor public services","chinese":"差劣的公共服務"},{"english":"deeper and more lasting harm","chinese":"更深遠和更持久的傷害"},{"english":"erode important social values","chinese":"侵蝕重要社會價值"},{"english":"overall impact","chinese":"整體影響"},{"english":"far more positive","chinese":"正面得多"},{"english":"reducing poverty","chinese":"減少貧窮"},{"english":"funding better public services","chinese":"資助更好的公共服務"},{"english":"quality of life","chinese":"生活質素"},{"english":"on a scale that","chinese":"以……的規模"},{"english":"do not surpass","chinese":"不會超過"}]},"model-essay-18-ielts-cause-solution":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-18-ielts-cause-solution","essayKey":"cause-solution:18","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-18-ielts-cause-solution","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/problem-and-cause/EdmundBd9CnS-Q18","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many modern societies, work has expanded beyond the office and begun to crowd out family, rest and personal growth. This problem is usually caused by unrealistic workplace expectations and weakened boundaries between professional and private life. It can be reduced if employers design healthier systems and individuals learn to protect their time deliberately.","chinese":"在許多現代社會中，工作已經延伸到辦公室之外，並開始擠壓家庭、休息和個人成長的空間。 這個問題通常是由不切實際的職場期望，以及工作生活與私人生活之間界線變得薄弱所造成的。 如果僱主能設計更健康的工作制度，而個人也學會有意識地保護自己的時間，這個問題便可以得到減輕。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One major reason is that many employees are expected to be constantly available. Emails, messaging apps and online meetings allow work to follow people home, so the end of the working day no longer feels like a real end. As a result, a person may be physically with their family but mentally still at their desk. Another cause is financial pressure. When housing, childcare and daily expenses are high, people often accept overtime, second jobs or heavier workloads, even when these choices damage their health. Over time, this creates a cycle in which tired workers perform less efficiently, need more time to finish tasks, and lose even more of their personal lives.","chinese":"其中一個主要原因是，許多員工被期望隨時都能回應工作。 電子郵件、即時通訊應用程式和線上會議讓工作可以跟著人們回到家中，因此工作日的結束不再感覺像真正的結束。 結果是，一個人身體上可能和家人在一起，但精神上仍然停留在辦公桌前。 另一個原因是經濟壓力。 當住房、育兒和日常開支高昂時，人們即使知道這些選擇會損害健康，也往往會接受加班、第二份工作或更沉重的工作量。 長遠而言，這會形成一個循環：疲憊的員工工作效率下降，需要更多時間完成任務，並失去更多私人生活。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The most effective solution is for employers to set clearer limits on work. For instance, companies can discourage non-urgent messages after office hours, monitor excessive overtime and give staff more control over when and where they work. These measures do not simply make employees happier; they also help them return to work with sharper concentration and better judgement. At the same time, individuals need to manage their own routines more firmly. This may mean setting fixed times for exercise, family meals or sleep, and treating these commitments as seriously as meetings with clients. Without such boundaries, personal life becomes the first thing to be sacrificed.","chinese":"最有效的解決方法是讓僱主為工作設立更清晰的界線。 例如，公司可以不鼓勵員工在辦公時間後發送非緊急訊息、監察過度加班的情況，並讓員工對自己的工作時間和工作地點有更多掌控權。 這些措施不只是讓員工更快樂；它們也能幫助員工以更敏銳的專注力和更好的判斷力重新投入工作。 同時，個人也需要更堅定地管理自己的日常安排。 這可能意味著為運動、家庭用餐或睡眠設定固定時間，並像對待與客戶的會議一樣認真看待這些承諾。 如果沒有這些界線，私人生活就會成為最先被犧牲的東西。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, poor work-life balance is mainly the result of constant connectivity, high workplace demands and financial pressure. However, it can be overcome when organisations create more humane working conditions and individuals draw a clearer line between their jobs and the rest of their lives.","chinese":"總結來說，糟糕的工作與生活平衡主要是由持續連線、高度職場要求和經濟壓力所造成的。 然而，當機構創造更人性化的工作條件，而個人也在工作和生活其他部分之間劃出更清晰的界線時，這個問題便可以被克服。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"modern societies","chinese":"現代社會"},{"english":"expanded beyond","chinese":"擴展至……之外"},{"english":"crowd out","chinese":"擠走；排擠掉"},{"english":"personal growth","chinese":"個人成長"},{"english":"unrealistic workplace expectations","chinese":"不切實際的職場期望"},{"english":"weakened boundaries between","chinese":"……之間變得薄弱的界線"},{"english":"professional and private life","chinese":"工作與私人生活"},{"english":"design healthier systems","chinese":"設計更健康的制度"},{"english":"protect their time deliberately","chinese":"有意識地保護自己的時間"},{"english":"one major reason","chinese":"一個主要原因"},{"english":"constantly available","chinese":"隨時候命"},{"english":"messaging apps","chinese":"通訊應用程式"},{"english":"online meetings","chinese":"網上會議"},{"english":"allow work to follow people home","chinese":"令工作跟着人回家"},{"english":"the working day","chinese":"工作日；工作時間"},{"english":"no longer feels like","chinese":"不再感覺像……"},{"english":"a real end","chinese":"真正的結束"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此；結果"},{"english":"physically with their family","chinese":"身體上與家人在一起"},{"english":"mentally still at their desk","chinese":"精神上仍在工作"},{"english":"financial pressure","chinese":"經濟壓力"},{"english":"daily expenses","chinese":"日常開支"},{"english":"accept overtime","chinese":"接受加班"},{"english":"second jobs","chinese":"第二份工作"},{"english":"heavier workloads","chinese":"更沉重的工作量"},{"english":"damage their health","chinese":"損害健康"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨時間；久而久之"},{"english":"creates a cycle in which","chinese":"形成一個……的循環"},{"english":"tired workers","chinese":"疲累的員工"},{"english":"perform less efficiently","chinese":"工作效率較低"},{"english":"finish tasks","chinese":"完成任務"},{"english":"lose even more of","chinese":"失去更多……"},{"english":"the most effective solution","chinese":"最有效的解決方法"},{"english":"set clearer limits on","chinese":"為……設定更清晰的限制"},{"english":"discourage non-urgent messages","chinese":"不鼓勵非緊急訊息"},{"english":"after office hours","chinese":"辦公時間後"},{"english":"monitor excessive overtime","chinese":"監察過度加班"},{"english":"give staff more control over","chinese":"讓員工對……有更多控制權"},{"english":"when and where they work","chinese":"工作時間和地點"},{"english":"these measures","chinese":"這些措施"},{"english":"sharper concentration","chinese":"更敏銳的專注力"},{"english":"better judgement","chinese":"更好的判斷力"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"manage their own routines","chinese":"管理自己的日常安排"},{"english":"more firmly","chinese":"更堅定地"},{"english":"setting fixed times for","chinese":"為……設定固定時間"},{"english":"family meals","chinese":"家庭用餐時間"},{"english":"treating these commitments as seriously as","chinese":"像對待……一樣認真對待這些承諾"},{"english":"meetings with clients","chinese":"與客戶的會議"},{"english":"such boundaries","chinese":"這樣的界線"},{"english":"personal life","chinese":"私人生活"},{"english":"the first thing to be sacrificed","chinese":"第一個被犧牲的東西"},{"english":"poor work-life balance","chinese":"差劣的工作與生活平衡"},{"english":"constant connectivity","chinese":"持續連線狀態"},{"english":"high workplace demands","chinese":"高職場要求"},{"english":"be overcome","chinese":"被克服"},{"english":"humane working conditions","chinese":"更人性化的工作條件"},{"english":"draw a clearer line between","chinese":"在……之間劃出更清晰的界線"},{"english":"the rest of their lives","chinese":"生活的其他部分"}]},"model-essay-18-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-18-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:18","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-18-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q18","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"As forests are cleared, cities expand, and wildlife is hunted for profit, many species are being pushed out of the ecosystems that once sustained them. I believe protecting animals is essential, not merely for sentimental reasons but because their survival is tied to ecological stability and, ultimately, human welfare.","chinese":"隨著森林被砍伐、城市不斷擴張，以及野生動物因牟利而被獵殺，許多物種正被迫離開曾經支撐它們生存的生態系統。 我認為保護動物是必要的，這並不只是出於情感上的原因，而是因為牠們的生存與生態穩定息息相關，並最終關乎人類福祉。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason animals must be protected is that they form part of a delicate natural balance. When one species disappears, the effect rarely stops there; it can ripple through the food chain and weaken an entire habitat. For instance, if predators are removed from a forest, smaller animals may multiply too quickly, damage vegetation, and reduce the food available for other species. In this sense, extinction is not just the loss of one creature; it is a crack in a much larger living system. Protecting animals therefore helps preserve the environmental conditions on which human beings also depend.","chinese":"動物必須受到保護的第一個原因是，牠們構成了脆弱自然平衡的一部分。 當一個物種消失時，其影響很少會就此停止；它可能會沿著食物鏈擴散，並削弱整個棲息地。 例如，如果捕食者從森林中消失，較小型的動物可能會繁殖得過快、破壞植被，並減少其他物種可獲得的食物。 從這個意義上說，滅絕並不只是失去一種生物；它是一個更龐大的生命系統中出現的一道裂縫。 因此，保護動物有助於維持人類同樣依賴的環境條件。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Several practical measures can be taken to address this problem. Governments should first create and enforce stronger protected areas, where logging, construction, and hunting are strictly controlled. Such laws, however, must be more than words on paper: rangers need proper funding, illegal hunters must face serious penalties, and companies that destroy habitats should be held financially responsible. At the same time, conservation will be more effective if local communities are given a real stake in it. When people can earn income through eco-tourism, sustainable farming, or conservation-related jobs, they are less likely to see wildlife as an obstacle to survival.","chinese":"可以採取幾項實際措施來處理這個問題。 政府首先應該建立並執行更強力的保護區制度，在這些區域內，伐木、建設和狩獵都受到嚴格管制。 然而，這些法律不能只是紙上文字：護林員需要充足資金，非法獵人必須面對嚴厲懲罰，而破壞棲息地的公司亦應承擔財務責任。 同時，如果當地社區能夠在保育工作中擁有真正的利益，保育便會更加有效。 當人們能夠透過生態旅遊、可持續農業，或與保育相關的工作獲得收入時，他們便較不會把野生動物視為生存的障礙。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, animal protection is highly important because endangered species are part of the natural foundation that supports life itself. The most effective response is not a single dramatic solution, but a combination of strict legal protection, responsible land use, and community involvement.","chinese":"總結來說，動物保護非常重要，因為瀕危物種是支撐生命本身的自然基礎的一部分。 最有效的應對方法並不是某一個戲劇性的單一方案，而是結合嚴格的法律保護、負責任的土地使用，以及社區參與。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"As forests are cleared","chinese":"隨着森林被砍伐"},{"english":"cities expand","chinese":"城市擴張"},{"english":"wildlife is hunted for profit","chinese":"野生動物被獵殺牟利"},{"english":"many species","chinese":"許多物種"},{"english":"be pushed out of","chinese":"被迫離開……"},{"english":"ecosystems that once sustained them","chinese":"曾經維持牠們生存的生態系統"},{"english":"protecting animals","chinese":"保護動物"},{"english":"not merely for sentimental reasons","chinese":"不只是出於感情原因"},{"english":"be tied to","chinese":"與……息息相關"},{"english":"ecological stability","chinese":"生態穩定"},{"english":"ultimately","chinese":"最終"},{"english":"human welfare","chinese":"人類福祉"},{"english":"form part of","chinese":"是……的一部分"},{"english":"a delicate natural balance","chinese":"脆弱的自然平衡"},{"english":"one species disappears","chinese":"一個物種消失"},{"english":"the effect rarely stops there","chinese":"影響很少就此停止"},{"english":"ripple through","chinese":"波及；連鎖影響"},{"english":"the food chain","chinese":"食物鏈"},{"english":"weaken an entire habitat","chinese":"削弱整個棲息地"},{"english":"predators are removed from","chinese":"掠食者被從……移除"},{"english":"multiply too quickly","chinese":"繁殖得太快"},{"english":"damage vegetation","chinese":"破壞植被"},{"english":"reduce the food available for","chinese":"減少可供……的食物"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"extinction","chinese":"物種滅絕"},{"english":"the loss of one creature","chinese":"失去一種生物"},{"english":"a crack in","chinese":"……中的裂痕"},{"english":"a much larger living system","chinese":"更大的生命系統"},{"english":"helps preserve","chinese":"有助保護"},{"english":"environmental conditions","chinese":"環境條件"},{"english":"depend on","chinese":"依賴"},{"english":"practical measures","chinese":"實際措施"},{"english":"address this problem","chinese":"處理這個問題"},{"english":"create and enforce","chinese":"建立並執行"},{"english":"protected areas","chinese":"保護區"},{"english":"logging, construction, and hunting","chinese":"伐木、建築工程和狩獵"},{"english":"strictly controlled","chinese":"受到嚴格管制"},{"english":"laws must be more than words on paper","chinese":"法律不能只是紙上談兵"},{"english":"rangers","chinese":"護林員；巡護員"},{"english":"proper funding","chinese":"充足資金"},{"english":"illegal hunters","chinese":"非法獵人"},{"english":"face serious penalties","chinese":"面對嚴厲懲罰"},{"english":"destroy habitats","chinese":"破壞棲息地"},{"english":"be held financially responsible","chinese":"被追究經濟責任"},{"english":"conservation","chinese":"保育"},{"english":"local communities","chinese":"本地社區"},{"english":"be given a real stake in","chinese":"在……中有實質利益"},{"english":"earn income through","chinese":"透過……賺取收入"},{"english":"eco-tourism","chinese":"生態旅遊"},{"english":"sustainable farming","chinese":"可持續農業"},{"english":"conservation-related jobs","chinese":"與保育相關的工作"},{"english":"be less likely to","chinese":"較不可能"},{"english":"see wildlife as an obstacle to survival","chinese":"視野生動物為生存障礙"},{"english":"endangered species","chinese":"瀕危物種"},{"english":"the natural foundation that supports life","chinese":"支撐生命的自然基礎"},{"english":"the most effective response","chinese":"最有效的回應"},{"english":"a single dramatic solution","chinese":"單一而轟動的解決方法"},{"english":"a combination of","chinese":"……的結合"},{"english":"strict legal protection","chinese":"嚴格的法律保護"},{"english":"responsible land use","chinese":"負責任的土地使用"},{"english":"community involvement","chinese":"社區參與"}]},"model-essay-18-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-18-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:18","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-18-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q18","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Learning does not stop at any fixed age; it remains valuable even in later life. While some people argue that people over 65 are too old to acquire new knowledge or skills, I completely disagree. In my view, older people benefit greatly from learning because it keeps their minds active and allows them to live more independent, meaningful lives.","chinese":"學習不會在任何固定年齡停止；即使在人生後期，它仍然具有價值。 雖然有人認為65歲以上的人年紀太大，已經無法獲得新知識或新技能，但我完全不同意 在我看來，較年長的人能從學習中獲得很大益處，因為學習能使他們的思維保持活躍，並讓他們過上更獨立、更有意義的生活。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that learning something new gives elderly people a strong mental and emotional lift. Many retirees suddenly lose the daily structure that work once provided, so their days can become repetitive and empty. When they learn a language, musical instrument, digital skill or craft, they are not merely filling time; they are giving their minds a fresh challenge. This kind of challenge encourages concentration, patience and problem-solving, which can help them feel capable rather than forgotten. For example, an older person who joins a painting class may begin with shaky confidence, but over time the process of improving can become a quiet source of pride. In this sense, learning acts like a light being switched on in a room that had been growing dim.","chinese":"第一個原因是，學習新事物能給長者帶來強大的精神和情感提升。 許多退休人士會突然失去過去由工作所提供的日常結構，因此他們的日子可能變得重複而空洞。 當他們學習一種語言、一種樂器、一項數碼技能或一門手藝時，他們不只是填補時間；他們是在給自己的頭腦一個新的挑戰。這種挑戰能促進專注力、耐性和解難能力，從而幫助他們感到自己仍然有能力，而不是被遺忘。 例如，一位參加繪畫班的長者起初可能信心不足，但隨著時間過去，不斷進步的過程可以成為一種安靜而穩定的自豪感來源。 從這個意義上說，學習就像在一個逐漸變暗的房間裡打開了一盞燈。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important benefit is that new skills help older people stay connected with modern society. The world changes quickly, especially through technology, and those who refuse to learn may become increasingly dependent on others. If senior citizens learn how to use smartphones, online banking or video calls, they can communicate with family, manage daily tasks and participate more fully in community life. This is not a small advantage; it protects their dignity. For instance, a grandmother who learns to use video chat can speak to her grandchildren abroad instead of feeling cut off from them. Such learning builds a bridge between generations.","chinese":"另一個重要好處是，新技能能幫助較年長的人與現代社會保持聯繫。 世界變化很快，尤其是在科技方面，而那些拒絕學習的人可能會越來越依賴他人。 如果長者學會使用智能手機、網上銀行或視像通話，他們便能與家人溝通、處理日常事務，並更充分地參與社區生活。 這並不是一個小小的優勢；它保護了他們的尊嚴。 例如，一位學會使用視像聊天的祖母，可以和身在海外的孫兒女說話，而不是感到與他們隔絕。 這樣的學習在不同世代之間建立了一座橋樑。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, it is never too late for older people to learn. After 65, learning is not a luxury; it is one of the best ways to preserve confidence, independence and a sense of purpose.","chinese":"總結來說，對較年長的人而言，學習永遠不會太遲。 65歲以後，學習並不是一種奢侈；它是維持自信、獨立和人生目標感的最佳方法之一。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"learning does not stop at","chinese":"學習不會在……停止"},{"english":"any fixed age","chinese":"任何固定年齡"},{"english":"remain valuable","chinese":"仍然有價值"},{"english":"in later life","chinese":"晚年；人生較後階段"},{"english":"people over 65","chinese":"65歲以上人士"},{"english":"too old to acquire","chinese":"年紀太大而不能學習"},{"english":"acquire new knowledge or skills","chinese":"學習新知識或技能"},{"english":"completely disagree","chinese":"完全不同意"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"benefit greatly from","chinese":"從……大大受惠"},{"english":"keep their minds active","chinese":"保持頭腦活躍"},{"english":"live more independent, meaningful lives","chinese":"過更獨立、更有意義的生活"},{"english":"the first reason","chinese":"第一個原因"},{"english":"elderly people","chinese":"長者"},{"english":"a strong mental and emotional lift","chinese":"精神和情緒上的強大提升"},{"english":"retirees","chinese":"退休人士"},{"english":"daily structure","chinese":"日常規律"},{"english":"work once provided","chinese":"工作曾經提供"},{"english":"repetitive and empty","chinese":"重複而空虛"},{"english":"learn a language","chinese":"學習一種語言"},{"english":"musical instrument","chinese":"樂器"},{"english":"digital skill","chinese":"數碼技能"},{"english":"craft","chinese":"手工藝"},{"english":"not merely filling time","chinese":"不只是消磨時間"},{"english":"a fresh challenge","chinese":"新鮮挑戰"},{"english":"this kind of challenge","chinese":"這種挑戰"},{"english":"encourage concentration","chinese":"促進專注"},{"english":"patience and problem-solving","chinese":"耐性和解難能力"},{"english":"feel capable rather than forgotten","chinese":"感到有能力，而不是被遺忘"},{"english":"joins a painting class","chinese":"參加繪畫班"},{"english":"begin with shaky confidence","chinese":"起初信心不足"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨時間"},{"english":"the process of improving","chinese":"進步的過程"},{"english":"a quiet source of pride","chinese":"默默的自豪感來源"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"acts like","chinese":"像……一樣發揮作用"},{"english":"a light being switched on","chinese":"一盞被打開的燈"},{"english":"growing dim","chinese":"逐漸變暗"},{"english":"another important benefit","chinese":"另一個重要好處"},{"english":"stay connected with","chinese":"與……保持聯繫"},{"english":"modern society","chinese":"現代社會"},{"english":"the world changes quickly","chinese":"世界變化迅速"},{"english":"especially through technology","chinese":"尤其透過科技"},{"english":"refuse to learn","chinese":"拒絕學習"},{"english":"become increasingly dependent on","chinese":"變得越來越依賴"},{"english":"senior citizens","chinese":"長者"},{"english":"smartphones","chinese":"智能手機"},{"english":"online banking","chinese":"網上銀行"},{"english":"video calls","chinese":"視像通話"},{"english":"communicate with family","chinese":"與家人溝通"},{"english":"manage daily tasks","chinese":"處理日常事務"},{"english":"participate more fully in","chinese":"更全面地參與"},{"english":"community life","chinese":"社區生活"},{"english":"not a small advantage","chinese":"這不是小小的好處"},{"english":"protect their dignity","chinese":"保護他們的尊嚴"},{"english":"use video chat","chinese":"使用視像聊天"},{"english":"grandchildren abroad","chinese":"海外的孫兒女"},{"english":"instead of feeling cut off from","chinese":"而不是感到與……隔絕"},{"english":"such learning","chinese":"這種學習"},{"english":"build a bridge between generations","chinese":"在世代之間建立橋樑"},{"english":"it is never too late for","chinese":"對……來說永遠不會太遲"},{"english":"after 65","chinese":"65歲之後"},{"english":"not a luxury","chinese":"不是奢侈品"},{"english":"one of the best ways to","chinese":"……的最佳方法之一"},{"english":"preserve confidence","chinese":"保持信心"},{"english":"independence","chinese":"獨立性"},{"english":"a sense of purpose","chinese":"目標感"}]},"model-essay-18-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-18-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:18","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-18-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q18","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Stress has always been part of human life, and each generation has carried its own burdens. However, I completely disagree that people in previous generations were more stressed than people are today. Modern life, in my view, creates a more constant form of pressure because work is harder to escape and personal success is now judged against endless social comparison.","chinese":"壓力一直都是人類生活的一部分，而每一代人也都承受著各自的負擔。 然而，我完全不同意過去幾代人比今天的人承受更大壓力這一說法。 在我看來，現代生活製造了一種更持續的壓力，因為工作變得更難擺脫，而個人成就如今也會被放在無止境的社會比較之中衡量。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that modern work follows people far beyond the workplace. In the past, many jobs were physically exhausting, but once the working day ended, responsibilities were more likely to stop at the factory gate, the shop door, or the family farm. By contrast, many employees today are expected to answer messages, check emails and remain reachable even at home. This turns rest into another extension of work. For example, an office worker may leave the office at six, yet still feel anxious whenever a phone notification appears at night. Over time, this constant alertness can damage sleep, weaken concentration and make people feel that they are never truly off duty.","chinese":"第一個原因是，現代工作會跟隨人們遠遠超出工作場所本身。 在過去，許多工作在體力上令人疲憊，但一旦工作日結束，責任往往更有可能停留在工廠大門、店鋪門口或家庭農場之內。 相比之下，今天許多員工即使在家中，也被期望回覆訊息、查看電郵，並保持隨時可聯絡的狀態。 這使休息變成了工作的另一種延伸。 例如，一位辦公室員工可能六點已經離開公司，但每當晚上手機通知出現時，仍然會感到焦慮。 長遠而言，這種持續的警覺狀態會損害睡眠、削弱專注力，並令人覺得自己從未真正下班。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another major cause of stress today is the pressure to compare one’s life with others. Previous generations usually judged success against people in their immediate community, whereas people today are exposed to carefully polished versions of other people’s achievements, relationships and lifestyles. Social media can make an ordinary person feel inadequate even when nothing is seriously wrong with their own life. For instance, a student may feel unsuccessful simply because classmates appear to be winning prizes, travelling abroad or building impressive careers online. This quiet psychological pressure is easy to dismiss, but it can weigh heavily on self-esteem and mental health.","chinese":"今天另一個主要的壓力來源，是人們將自己的生活與他人比較的壓力。 過去幾代人通常是與自己身邊社區的人比較成功，而今天的人卻會接觸到別人被精心美化過的成就、關係和生活方式。 社交媒體可以使一個普通人在自己的生活並沒有嚴重問題的情況下，仍然感到自己不夠好。 例如，一名學生可能只是因為同學在網上看起來正在獲獎、到海外旅行，或建立令人印象深刻的事業，便覺得自己不成功。 這種安靜的心理壓力很容易被忽視，但可能會沉重地壓在一個人的自尊和心理健康之上"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully disagree with the view that earlier generations were more stressed. They faced real hardship, but modern people live under pressure that is more continuous, more visible and far harder to switch off.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全不同意較早幾代人壓力更大的觀點。 他們確實面對真實的艱難處境，但現代人生活在一種更持續、更明顯，而且更難關掉的壓力之下。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"stress","chinese":"壓力"},{"english":"part of human life","chinese":"人類生活的一部分"},{"english":"each generation","chinese":"每一代人"},{"english":"carried its own burdens","chinese":"承受自己的負擔"},{"english":"previous generations","chinese":"以往幾代人"},{"english":"more stressed than","chinese":"比……壓力更大"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"constant form of pressure","chinese":"更持續的壓力形式"},{"english":"harder to escape","chinese":"更難逃離"},{"english":"personal success","chinese":"個人成功"},{"english":"be judged against","chinese":"以……作標準評價"},{"english":"endless social comparison","chinese":"無休止的社會比較"},{"english":"modern work","chinese":"現代工作"},{"english":"follows people far beyond","chinese":"遠遠跟隨人們超出……"},{"english":"the workplace","chinese":"工作場所"},{"english":"in the past","chinese":"在過去"},{"english":"physically exhausting","chinese":"體力上令人筋疲力盡"},{"english":"working day ended","chinese":"工作日結束"},{"english":"be more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"factory gate","chinese":"工廠大門"},{"english":"shop door","chinese":"店舖門口"},{"english":"family farm","chinese":"家庭農場"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"be expected to","chinese":"被期望去……"},{"english":"answer messages","chinese":"回覆訊息"},{"english":"check emails","chinese":"查看電郵"},{"english":"remain reachable","chinese":"隨時可聯絡"},{"english":"even at home","chinese":"即使在家中"},{"english":"turns rest into","chinese":"將休息變成……"},{"english":"extension of work","chinese":"工作的延伸"},{"english":"office worker","chinese":"辦公室員工"},{"english":"feel anxious","chinese":"感到焦慮"},{"english":"phone notification","chinese":"手機通知"},{"english":"appears at night","chinese":"在晚上出現"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨着時間過去"},{"english":"constant alertness","chinese":"持續警覺"},{"english":"damage sleep","chinese":"損害睡眠"},{"english":"weaken concentration","chinese":"削弱專注力"},{"english":"truly off duty","chinese":"真正下班；真正不用當值"},{"english":"major cause of stress","chinese":"壓力的主要成因"},{"english":"compare one's life with others","chinese":"將自己的生活與別人比較"},{"english":"judged success against","chinese":"以……衡量成功"},{"english":"immediate community","chinese":"身邊社群"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；然而"},{"english":"be exposed to","chinese":"接觸到……"},{"english":"carefully polished versions of","chinese":"經精心修飾的……版本"},{"english":"achievements, relationships and lifestyles","chinese":"成就、關係和生活方式"},{"english":"social media","chinese":"社交媒體"},{"english":"ordinary person","chinese":"普通人"},{"english":"feel inadequate","chinese":"覺得自己不足"},{"english":"even when","chinese":"即使在……時"},{"english":"nothing is seriously wrong with","chinese":"……沒有甚麼嚴重問題"},{"english":"feel unsuccessful","chinese":"感到不成功"},{"english":"simply because","chinese":"只是因為"},{"english":"appear to be","chinese":"看似正在……"},{"english":"winning prizes","chinese":"得獎"},{"english":"travelling abroad","chinese":"到外國旅行"},{"english":"building impressive careers","chinese":"建立令人羨慕的事業"},{"english":"quiet psychological pressure","chinese":"無聲的心理壓力"},{"english":"easy to dismiss","chinese":"容易被輕視"},{"english":"weigh heavily on","chinese":"對……造成沉重負擔"},{"english":"self-esteem","chinese":"自尊感"},{"english":"mental health","chinese":"精神健康"},{"english":"earlier generations","chinese":"較早幾代人"},{"english":"real hardship","chinese":"真正困難"},{"english":"live under pressure","chinese":"生活在壓力之下"},{"english":"more continuous","chinese":"更持續"},{"english":"more visible","chinese":"更明顯"},{"english":"far harder to switch off","chinese":"難得多去關掉"}]},"model-essay-19-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-19-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:19","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-19-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q19","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Globalisation has become a defining feature of modern life, influencing how people trade, work, travel and consume culture. Although it can place pressure on local businesses and traditions, I believe its advantages are greater overall because it creates wider opportunities and brings societies into closer cooperation.","chinese":"全球化已成為現代生活的一個重要特徵，影響著人們如何貿易、工作、旅行，以及消費文化。 儘管它可能對本地企業和傳統造成壓力， 我認為整體而言，它的優點更大，因為全球化能創造更廣闊的機會，並使不同社會之間有更緊密的合作。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One major disadvantage is that globalisation can weaken local economies. When international companies enter a country, small businesses may struggle to survive because they cannot match the prices, advertising power or supply networks of global brands. For example, a family-owned clothes shop may lose customers when a large foreign retailer opens nearby and sells similar products at lower prices. This can reduce local employment and make communities dependent on outside corporations. Another drawback is cultural dilution. If young people everywhere watch the same films, eat the same fast food and follow the same fashion trends, local customs may slowly fade into the background. In this sense, globalisation can sometimes make the world feel less like a garden of different flowers and more like one repeated pattern.","chinese":"全球化其中一個主要缺點是，它可能削弱本地經濟。 當國際企業進入一個國家時，小型企業可能難以生存，因為它們無法與全球品牌的價格、廣告能力或供應網絡競爭。 例如，當一間大型外國零售商在附近開業，並以更低價格出售類似產品時，一間家庭經營的服裝店可能會流失顧客。 這可能會減少本地就業機會，並使社區依賴外來企業。 另一個缺點是文化被淡化。 如果世界各地的年輕人都觀看相同的電影、吃相同的快餐，並追隨相同的時尚潮流，本地習俗便可能慢慢退到背景之中。 從這個意義上說，全球化有時會使世界不再像一個開滿不同花朵的花園，而更像是一個不斷重複的單一圖案。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, the benefits are more significant. Globalisation allows goods, knowledge and services to move across borders, which can improve people’s living standards. For instance, a hospital in a developing country may gain access to imported medical equipment, while students in poorer regions can use online courses created by overseas universities. These exchanges are not merely commercial; they can open doors that would otherwise remain closed. Globalisation also creates opportunities for workers and businesses. A small software company, for example, can sell its services to clients abroad instead of depending only on its local market. At the same time, contact between cultures can make people more open-minded, especially when they work, study or communicate with those from different backgrounds.","chinese":"然而，全球化的好處更加重要。 全球化使商品、知識和服務能夠跨越國界流動，這可以提升人們的生活水平。 例如，一間發展中國家的醫院可能可以獲得進口醫療設備，而較貧困地區的學生也可以使用海外大學製作的網上課程。 這些交流並不只是商業活動；它們能打開一些原本可能一直關上的大門。 全球化也為工人和企業創造機會。 例如，一間小型軟件公司可以把服務賣給海外客戶，而不是只依賴本地市場。 同時，文化之間的接觸也能使人變得更開明，尤其當他們與來自不同背景的人一起工作、學習或交流時。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, globalisation does have disadvantages, particularly for local businesses and cultural traditions. Nevertheless, I firmly believe it is positive overall because it spreads opportunity, knowledge and cooperation far more widely than a closed world ever could.","chinese":"總結來說，全球化確實有缺點，尤其是對本地企業和文化傳統而言。 然而，我堅定地認為，整體而言全球化是正面的，因為它比一個封閉的世界更能廣泛地傳播機會、知識和合作。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"globalisation","chinese":"全球化"},{"english":"a defining feature of","chinese":"……的標誌性特徵"},{"english":"modern life","chinese":"現代生活"},{"english":"influencing how people","chinese":"影響人們如何……"},{"english":"consume culture","chinese":"消費文化"},{"english":"place pressure on","chinese":"對……造成壓力"},{"english":"local businesses and traditions","chinese":"本地企業和傳統"},{"english":"greater overall","chinese":"整體而言更大"},{"english":"creates wider opportunities","chinese":"創造更廣泛的機會"},{"english":"brings societies into closer cooperation","chinese":"令社會之間更緊密合作"},{"english":"one major disadvantage","chinese":"一個主要缺點"},{"english":"weaken local economies","chinese":"削弱本地經濟"},{"english":"international companies","chinese":"跨國公司"},{"english":"enter a country","chinese":"進入一個國家"},{"english":"struggle to survive","chinese":"掙扎求存"},{"english":"match the prices","chinese":"與……的價格競爭"},{"english":"advertising power","chinese":"廣告力量"},{"english":"supply networks","chinese":"供應網絡"},{"english":"global brands","chinese":"全球品牌"},{"english":"a family-owned clothes shop","chinese":"家庭經營的服裝店"},{"english":"lose customers","chinese":"失去顧客"},{"english":"a large foreign retailer","chinese":"大型外國零售商"},{"english":"opens nearby","chinese":"在附近開業"},{"english":"similar products","chinese":"類似產品"},{"english":"at lower prices","chinese":"以較低價格"},{"english":"reduce local employment","chinese":"減少本地就業"},{"english":"make communities dependent on","chinese":"令社區依賴……"},{"english":"outside corporations","chinese":"外來企業"},{"english":"another drawback","chinese":"另一個缺點"},{"english":"cultural dilution","chinese":"文化淡化"},{"english":"follow the same fashion trends","chinese":"追隨相同的時尚潮流"},{"english":"local customs","chinese":"本地習俗"},{"english":"fade into the background","chinese":"逐漸退到背景；逐漸被淡忘"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"less like...and more like...","chinese":"與其說像……，不如說像……"},{"english":"a garden of different flowers","chinese":"百花齊放的花園"},{"english":"one repeated pattern","chinese":"單一重複的模式"},{"english":"the benefits are more significant","chinese":"好處更為重要"},{"english":"goods, knowledge and services","chinese":"商品、知識和服務"},{"english":"move across borders","chinese":"跨越國界流動"},{"english":"improve people's living standards","chinese":"改善人們的生活水平"},{"english":"a developing country","chinese":"發展中國家"},{"english":"gain access to","chinese":"獲得使用／接觸……的機會"},{"english":"imported medical equipment","chinese":"進口醫療設備"},{"english":"poorer regions","chinese":"較貧窮地區"},{"english":"online courses","chinese":"網上課程"},{"english":"overseas universities","chinese":"海外大學"},{"english":"these exchanges","chinese":"這些交流"},{"english":"not merely commercial","chinese":"不只是商業上的"},{"english":"open doors","chinese":"打開機會之門"},{"english":"would otherwise remain closed","chinese":"否則仍會關閉"},{"english":"creates opportunities for","chinese":"為……創造機會"},{"english":"a small software company","chinese":"小型軟件公司"},{"english":"sell its services to","chinese":"向……出售服務"},{"english":"clients abroad","chinese":"海外客戶"},{"english":"instead of depending only on","chinese":"而不是只依賴……"},{"english":"local market","chinese":"本地市場"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"contact between cultures","chinese":"文化之間的接觸"},{"english":"open-minded","chinese":"思想開明的"},{"english":"different backgrounds","chinese":"不同背景"},{"english":"particularly for","chinese":"尤其對於……"},{"english":"cultural traditions","chinese":"文化傳統"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"firmly believe","chinese":"堅信"},{"english":"positive overall","chinese":"整體而言是正面的"},{"english":"spreads opportunity, knowledge and cooperation","chinese":"傳播機會、知識和合作"},{"english":"far more widely than","chinese":"遠比……更廣泛"},{"english":"a closed world","chinese":"封閉的世界"}]},"model-essay-19-ielts-cause-solution":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-19-ielts-cause-solution","essayKey":"cause-solution:19","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-19-ielts-cause-solution","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/problem-and-cause/EdmundBd9CnS-Q19","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many developing countries, children in rural communities are held back not by a lack of ability, but by a shortage of high-quality teachers. This problem is largely caused by poor working conditions and limited career prospects, and it can be addressed through targeted incentives and stronger professional support.","chinese":"在許多發展中國家，農村社區的兒童受到限制，並不是因為能力不足，而是因為缺乏高質素的教師。 這個問題主要是由惡劣的工作條件和有限的職業前景造成的，而它可以透過有針對性的激勵措施和更強的專業支援來解決。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One major reason skilled teachers avoid rural areas is that these posts often come with serious personal and professional disadvantages. Many rural schools lack basic facilities, reliable transport, proper accommodation, and teaching materials, so even committed teachers may feel that they are being asked to do an important job with one hand tied behind their back. For example, a science teacher who has no laboratory, no stable internet connection, and overcrowded classes may struggle to deliver lessons effectively, which can quickly lead to frustration and burnout. Another reason is that rural appointments may appear to damage a teacher’s long-term career. In cities, teachers usually have better access to training, senior colleagues, promotion opportunities, and professional networks. By contrast, a rural teacher may feel invisible, no matter how hard he or she works.","chinese":"優秀教師避免到農村地區工作的其中一個主要原因，是這些職位往往伴隨嚴重的個人和職業劣勢。 許多農村學校缺乏基本設施、可靠交通、合適住宿和教學材料，因此即使是有熱誠的教師，也可能會覺得自己像是被綁住一隻手去完成一份重要工作。 例如，一位沒有實驗室、沒有穩定網絡連接，還要面對過度擠迫班級的科學老師，可能很難有效地授課，而這很快便會導致挫敗感和職業倦怠。 另一個原因是，農村任職安排可能看起來會損害教師的長遠職業發展。 在城市，教師通常更容易獲得培訓機會、接觸資深同事、得到晉升機會，並建立專業人脈網絡。 相比之下，一位農村教師無論多努力工作，都可能會覺得自己被忽視。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"To solve this problem, governments should first make rural teaching financially and practically attractive. This could include higher salaries, free housing, transport allowances, and priority access to future promotions. Such measures would not merely reward teachers; they would also signal that rural education is a national priority rather than a professional dead end. In addition, rural teachers need regular support, not just a contract and a classroom. Governments and schools could provide online mentoring, mobile training teams, and partnerships between urban and rural schools, so that teachers in remote areas can continue to improve their skills. Over time, developing local teacher-training programmes would also help, because teachers who come from rural communities are more likely to understand local needs and remain there.","chinese":"為了解決這個問題，政府首先應該使農村教學在經濟和實際層面上都更具吸引力。 這可以包括更高薪酬、免費住房、交通津貼，以及未來晉升的優先機會。 這些措施不只是獎勵教師；它們也會傳達一個訊息：農村教育是國家優先事項，而不是一條職業死路。 此外，農村教師需要定期支援，而不只是一份合約和一間課室。 政府和學校可以提供網上指導、流動培訓團隊，以及城鄉學校之間的合作關係，讓偏遠地區的教師能夠持續提升自己的技能。 長遠而言，發展本地教師培訓課程也會有幫助，因為來自農村社區的教師更有可能理解當地需要，並留在那裡工作。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, good teachers often avoid rural schools because the conditions are difficult and the career rewards are limited. Better incentives, stronger training, and clearer career pathways would make rural teaching more sustainable and improve children’s access to quality education.","chinese":"總結來說，優秀教師往往避免到農村學校工作，因為那裡的條件艱難，而且職業回報有限。 更好的激勵措施、更強的培訓，以及更清晰的職業發展路徑，將會使農村教學更可持續，並改善兒童接受優質教育的機會。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"developing countries","chinese":"發展中國家"},{"english":"rural communities","chinese":"農村社區"},{"english":"be held back not by..., but by...","chinese":"不是因為……而受阻，而是因為……"},{"english":"a lack of ability","chinese":"能力不足"},{"english":"a shortage of","chinese":"……短缺"},{"english":"high-quality teachers","chinese":"優質教師"},{"english":"largely caused by","chinese":"主要由……造成"},{"english":"poor working conditions","chinese":"惡劣工作條件"},{"english":"limited career prospects","chinese":"有限的事業前景"},{"english":"be addressed through","chinese":"透過……處理"},{"english":"targeted incentives","chinese":"針對性誘因"},{"english":"stronger professional support","chinese":"更強的專業支援"},{"english":"one major reason","chinese":"一個主要原因"},{"english":"skilled teachers","chinese":"有能力的教師"},{"english":"avoid rural areas","chinese":"避開農村地區"},{"english":"posts often come with","chinese":"職位往往伴隨"},{"english":"serious personal and professional disadvantages","chinese":"嚴重的個人及專業劣勢"},{"english":"lack basic facilities","chinese":"缺乏基本設施"},{"english":"reliable transport","chinese":"可靠交通"},{"english":"proper accommodation","chinese":"合適住宿"},{"english":"teaching materials","chinese":"教學材料"},{"english":"committed teachers","chinese":"敬業的教師"},{"english":"be asked to do","chinese":"被要求去做"},{"english":"with one hand tied behind their back","chinese":"束手束腳；在條件受限下做事"},{"english":"stable internet connection","chinese":"穩定的互聯網連接"},{"english":"overcrowded classes","chinese":"過度擠迫的班級"},{"english":"struggle to","chinese":"努力但困難地"},{"english":"deliver lessons effectively","chinese":"有效授課"},{"english":"lead to frustration and burnout","chinese":"導致挫敗感和倦怠"},{"english":"frustration and burnout","chinese":"挫敗感和倦怠"},{"english":"rural appointments","chinese":"農村任教崗位"},{"english":"appear to damage","chinese":"看似會損害"},{"english":"long-term career","chinese":"長遠事業發展"},{"english":"have better access to","chinese":"較容易獲得"},{"english":"senior colleagues","chinese":"資深同事"},{"english":"promotion opportunities","chinese":"晉升機會"},{"english":"professional networks","chinese":"專業人脈網絡"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"feel invisible","chinese":"感到被忽視"},{"english":"no matter how hard","chinese":"無論多努力"},{"english":"to solve this problem","chinese":"為了解決這個問題"},{"english":"financially and practically attractive","chinese":"在經濟和實際層面具吸引力"},{"english":"higher salaries","chinese":"更高薪酬"},{"english":"free housing","chinese":"免費住房"},{"english":"transport allowances","chinese":"交通津貼"},{"english":"priority access to future promotions","chinese":"優先獲得日後晉升機會"},{"english":"such measures","chinese":"這些措施"},{"english":"not merely reward","chinese":"不只是獎勵"},{"english":"signal that","chinese":"顯示"},{"english":"a national priority","chinese":"國家優先事項"},{"english":"rather than","chinese":"而不是"},{"english":"a professional dead end","chinese":"事業上的死胡同"},{"english":"regular support","chinese":"定期支援"},{"english":"not just a contract and a classroom","chinese":"不只是一份合約和一間課室"},{"english":"online mentoring","chinese":"網上指導"},{"english":"mobile training teams","chinese":"流動培訓團隊"},{"english":"partnerships between urban and rural schools","chinese":"城市與農村學校之間的合作"},{"english":"remote areas","chinese":"偏遠地區"},{"english":"continue to improve their skills","chinese":"持續提升技能"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨着時間"},{"english":"developing local teacher-training programmes","chinese":"發展本地教師培訓課程"},{"english":"come from rural communities","chinese":"來自農村社區"},{"english":"understand local needs","chinese":"了解本地需要"},{"english":"remain there","chinese":"留在當地"},{"english":"career rewards","chinese":"事業回報"},{"english":"clearer career pathways","chinese":"更清晰的事業發展路徑"},{"english":"more sustainable","chinese":"更可持續"},{"english":"children's access to quality education","chinese":"兒童接受優質教育的機會"}]},"model-essay-19-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-19-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:19","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-19-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q19","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Human beings have altered the natural world on an unprecedented scale. Because forests have been cleared, oceans polluted and many species pushed towards extinction, some people argue that the damage done to plants and animals is now beyond repair. While I understand this pessimistic view, I believe that practical action can still reduce environmental harm and allow nature to recover.","chinese":"人類以前所未有的規模改變了自然世界。 由於森林被砍伐、海洋受到污染，許多物種也被推向滅絕邊緣，有些人認為人類對動植物造成的傷害如今已經無法修復。 雖然我理解這種悲觀觀點， 但我相信實際行動仍然可以減少環境傷害，並讓自然恢復。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Those who think change is impossible usually point to the permanent nature of some environmental damage. Once a species disappears, for instance, no law or campaign can bring it back. In addition, modern life depends heavily on activities that harm ecosystems, such as mass farming, road building, air travel and industrial production. These activities are not small habits that can be removed overnight; they are woven into the way economies operate. As a result, even when governments promise greener policies, businesses and consumers often continue to prioritise convenience, profit and short-term growth. From this perspective, human impact seems like a tide that is too powerful to turn back.","chinese":"那些認為改變是不可能的人，通常會指出某些環境破壞具有永久性。 例如，一旦一個物種消失，就沒有任何法律或運動能夠把它帶回來。 此外，現代生活高度依賴會破壞生態系統的活動，例如大規模農業、道路建設、航空旅行和工業生產。 這些活動並不是可以一夜之間改掉的小習慣；它們已經編織進經濟運作的方式之中。 結果是，即使政府承諾推行更環保的政策，企業和消費者仍然經常優先考慮便利、利潤和短期增長。 從這個角度來看，人類的影響就像一股過於強大的潮水，似乎已經無法逆轉。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, I would argue that this view is too defeatist. Although some losses are irreversible, many forms of environmental damage can be limited, slowed or even partly reversed. Governments can protect forests, restrict illegal hunting, restore wetlands and punish companies that pollute rivers or destroy habitats. At the same time, individuals can change demand by eating less wastefully, choosing sustainable products and supporting conservation projects. For example, when a city creates protected green spaces and controls development, birds, insects and native plants can return over time. Nature is often remarkably resilient if people stop putting constant pressure on it.","chinese":"然而，我會認為這種觀點過於失敗主義。 雖然有些損失是不可逆轉的，但許多形式的環境破壞仍然可以被限制、減緩，甚至部分逆轉。 政府可以保護森林、限制非法狩獵、修復濕地，並懲罰污染河流或破壞棲息地的公司。 同時，個人也可以透過減少飲食浪費、選擇可持續產品，以及支持保育項目來改變需求 例如，當一座城市建立受保護的綠化空間並控制發展時，鳥類、昆蟲和本地植物可以隨著時間逐漸回歸。 如果人們停止不斷向自然施加壓力，自然往往具有驚人的復原力。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, human activity has undoubtedly caused deep damage to the natural world, and some of that damage cannot be undone. Nevertheless, I strongly believe that change is still possible. With firm laws, responsible businesses and more thoughtful daily choices, humans can stop making the problem worse and give plants and animals a real chance to survive.","chinese":"總結來說，人類活動無疑已對自然世界造成了深重傷害，而且其中一些傷害無法被復原 然而，我強烈相信改變仍然是可能的。 透過堅定的法律、負責任的企業，以及更審慎的日常選擇，人類可以停止讓問題惡化，並給予動植物真正的生存機會。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"alter the natural world","chinese":"改變自然世界"},{"english":"on an unprecedented scale","chinese":"以前所未有的規模"},{"english":"forests have been cleared","chinese":"森林被清除"},{"english":"oceans polluted","chinese":"海洋受到污染"},{"english":"be pushed towards extinction","chinese":"被推向滅絕"},{"english":"the damage done to","chinese":"對……造成的破壞"},{"english":"plants and animals","chinese":"動植物"},{"english":"beyond repair","chinese":"無法修復"},{"english":"this pessimistic view","chinese":"這種悲觀看法"},{"english":"practical action","chinese":"實際行動"},{"english":"reduce environmental harm","chinese":"減少環境傷害"},{"english":"allow nature to recover","chinese":"讓大自然恢復"},{"english":"point to","chinese":"指出；以……作為理由"},{"english":"the permanent nature of","chinese":"……的永久性"},{"english":"environmental damage","chinese":"環境破壞"},{"english":"once a species disappears","chinese":"一旦一個物種消失"},{"english":"bring it back","chinese":"使其回復；帶回來"},{"english":"in addition","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"depend heavily on","chinese":"非常依賴"},{"english":"harm ecosystems","chinese":"破壞生態系統"},{"english":"mass farming","chinese":"大規模農業"},{"english":"road building","chinese":"道路建設"},{"english":"air travel","chinese":"航空旅行"},{"english":"industrial production","chinese":"工業生產"},{"english":"be removed overnight","chinese":"一夜之間被移除"},{"english":"be woven into","chinese":"融入……之中"},{"english":"the way economies operate","chinese":"經濟運作方式"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"greener policies","chinese":"更環保的政策"},{"english":"continue to prioritise","chinese":"繼續優先考慮"},{"english":"convenience, profit and short-term growth","chinese":"方便、利潤和短期增長"},{"english":"from this perspective","chinese":"從這個角度來看"},{"english":"human impact","chinese":"人類影響"},{"english":"too powerful to turn back","chinese":"強大到無法扭轉"},{"english":"this view is too defeatist","chinese":"這個看法過於消極"},{"english":"irreversible","chinese":"不可逆轉的"},{"english":"many forms of","chinese":"很多形式的"},{"english":"be limited, slowed or even partly reversed","chinese":"被限制、減慢，甚至局部逆轉"},{"english":"protect forests","chinese":"保護森林"},{"english":"restrict illegal hunting","chinese":"限制非法狩獵"},{"english":"restore wetlands","chinese":"修復濕地"},{"english":"punish companies that","chinese":"懲罰……的公司"},{"english":"pollute rivers","chinese":"污染河流"},{"english":"destroy habitats","chinese":"破壞棲息地"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"change demand","chinese":"改變需求"},{"english":"eating less wastefully","chinese":"減少飲食浪費"},{"english":"sustainable products","chinese":"可持續產品"},{"english":"supporting conservation projects","chinese":"支持保育項目"},{"english":"protected green spaces","chinese":"受保護綠化空間"},{"english":"control development","chinese":"控制發展"},{"english":"native plants","chinese":"本土植物"},{"english":"return over time","chinese":"隨時間回歸"},{"english":"remarkably resilient","chinese":"具有驚人的復原力"},{"english":"put constant pressure on","chinese":"對……施加持續壓力"},{"english":"undoubtedly caused deep damage to","chinese":"毫無疑問對……造成深遠破壞"},{"english":"the natural world","chinese":"自然世界"},{"english":"cannot be undone","chinese":"不能被逆轉"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"firm laws","chinese":"強硬法律"},{"english":"responsible businesses","chinese":"負責任的企業"},{"english":"thoughtful daily choices","chinese":"經深思熟慮的日常選擇"},{"english":"stop making the problem worse","chinese":"停止令問題惡化"},{"english":"give plants and animals a real chance to survive","chinese":"給動植物真正的生存機會"}]},"model-essay-19-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-19-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:19","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-19-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q19","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In the modern media landscape, many celebrities are admired less for what they have done than for how luxurious their lives appear. I completely agree that this shift is harmful, because it teaches young people to value image, consumption and instant attention more than genuine achievement.","chinese":"在現代媒體環境中，許多名人受到仰慕，並不是因為他們做過甚麼，而是因為他們的生活看起來多麼奢華。 我完全同意這種轉變是有害的，因為它教導年輕人重視形象、消費和即時關注，而不是重視真正的成就。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first problem is that celebrity culture often presents success as something visual rather than earned. When young people constantly see famous figures praised for designer clothes, expensive cars and perfectly staged photos, they may begin to believe that public admiration matters more than effort, discipline or contribution. This is dangerous because achievement usually grows slowly, through practice, failure and patience, whereas glamour offers the illusion of overnight success. For example, a teenager who spends hours following influencers may become more interested in looking wealthy than in building real skills. Over time, this can weaken ambition in a quiet but serious way: the goal becomes to be seen, not to be useful.","chinese":"第一個問題是，名人文化常常把成功呈現為一種視覺上的東西，而不是靠努力得來的成果。 當年輕人不斷看到名人因名牌服裝、昂貴汽車和精心擺拍的照片而受到讚賞時，他們可能會開始相信，公眾的仰慕比努力、自律或貢獻更重要。 這是危險的，因為成就通常是透過練習、失敗和耐心慢慢累積而來的，而魅力和奢華卻製造了一種一夜成功的幻象。 例如，一個花數小時追蹤網紅的青少年，可能會對看起來富有更感興趣，而不是對建立真正技能感興趣。 長遠而言，這會以一種安靜但嚴重的方式削弱抱負：目標變成被看見，而不是變得有用。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason I agree is that this kind of fame can create unhealthy social pressure. Many celebrities display a lifestyle that is polished, selective and often unrealistic, yet young audiences may treat it as normal life. As a result, they may compare their own ordinary homes, bodies and possessions with a carefully manufactured image. This can lead to insecurity, wasteful spending and a belief that personal worth depends on appearance. A student, for instance, might feel embarrassed about using an old phone or wearing simple clothes, not because these things matter, but because the celebrity world has turned luxury into a symbol of status.","chinese":"我同意的另一個原因是，這種名氣可能製造不健康的社會壓力。 許多名人展示的是一種經過修飾、經過篩選，而且往往不現實的生活方式，然而年輕觀眾卻可能把它視為正常生活。 結果是，他們可能會把自己普通的家庭、身體和物品，與一種被精心製造出來的形象作比較。 這可能導致不安全感、浪費性消費，以及一種認為個人價值取決於外表的信念。 例如，一名學生可能會因為使用舊手機或穿著簡單衣服而感到尷尬，並不是因為這些事情本身重要，而是因為名人的世界已經把奢侈變成了地位的象徵。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully agree that celebrities who are celebrated mainly for wealth and glamour set a poor example for young people. Fame should not become a glittering shortcut that replaces character, skill and meaningful achievement.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意，那些主要因財富和魅力而受到推崇的名人，為年輕人樹立了不良榜樣。 名氣不應變成一條閃閃發亮的捷徑，取代品格、技能和有意義的成就。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"modern media landscape","chinese":"現代媒體環境"},{"english":"be admired less for","chinese":"較少因……而受欣賞"},{"english":"what they have done","chinese":"他們所做過的事"},{"english":"luxurious their lives appear","chinese":"他們的生活看起來多奢華"},{"english":"this shift","chinese":"這種轉變"},{"english":"harmful","chinese":"有害的"},{"english":"teaches young people to","chinese":"教導年輕人去……"},{"english":"value image","chinese":"重視形象"},{"english":"consumption","chinese":"消費"},{"english":"instant attention","chinese":"即時關注"},{"english":"genuine achievement","chinese":"真正成就"},{"english":"celebrity culture","chinese":"名人文化"},{"english":"presents success as","chinese":"將成功呈現為……"},{"english":"visual rather than earned","chinese":"視覺上的，而不是努力得來的"},{"english":"famous figures","chinese":"著名人物"},{"english":"be praised for","chinese":"因……而受讚賞"},{"english":"designer clothes","chinese":"名牌衣服"},{"english":"expensive cars","chinese":"昂貴汽車"},{"english":"perfectly staged photos","chinese":"精心擺拍的照片"},{"english":"public admiration","chinese":"公眾仰慕"},{"english":"matters more than","chinese":"比……更重要"},{"english":"effort, discipline or contribution","chinese":"努力、紀律和貢獻"},{"english":"achievement usually grows slowly","chinese":"成就通常慢慢累積"},{"english":"through practice, failure and patience","chinese":"透過練習、失敗和耐性"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；然而"},{"english":"glamour","chinese":"光鮮亮麗"},{"english":"the illusion of","chinese":"……的假象"},{"english":"overnight success","chinese":"一夜成名"},{"english":"following influencers","chinese":"追蹤網紅"},{"english":"looking wealthy","chinese":"看起來富有"},{"english":"building real skills","chinese":"建立真正技能"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨着時間過去"},{"english":"weaken ambition","chinese":"削弱抱負"},{"english":"in a quiet but serious way","chinese":"以不明顯但嚴重的方式"},{"english":"the goal becomes to","chinese":"目標變成……"},{"english":"be seen","chinese":"被看見"},{"english":"be useful","chinese":"有用；有價值"},{"english":"create unhealthy social pressure","chinese":"造成不健康的社會壓力"},{"english":"display a lifestyle","chinese":"展示一種生活方式"},{"english":"polished","chinese":"經修飾的"},{"english":"selective","chinese":"經篩選的"},{"english":"unrealistic","chinese":"不切實際的"},{"english":"young audiences","chinese":"年輕觀眾"},{"english":"treat it as normal life","chinese":"將它視為正常生活"},{"english":"compare their own","chinese":"將自己的……作比較"},{"english":"ordinary homes","chinese":"普通住家"},{"english":"bodies and possessions","chinese":"身體和財物"},{"english":"carefully manufactured image","chinese":"精心製造的形象"},{"english":"lead to insecurity","chinese":"導致不安全感"},{"english":"wasteful spending","chinese":"浪費性的消費"},{"english":"personal worth","chinese":"個人價值"},{"english":"depends on appearance","chinese":"取決於外表"},{"english":"feel embarrassed about","chinese":"因……而感到尷尬"},{"english":"old phone","chinese":"舊電話"},{"english":"wearing simple clothes","chinese":"穿着簡單衣服"},{"english":"these things matter","chinese":"這些東西重要"},{"english":"celebrity world","chinese":"名人世界"},{"english":"turn luxury into","chinese":"將奢華變成……"},{"english":"symbol of status","chinese":"地位象徵"},{"english":"be celebrated mainly for","chinese":"主要因……而受到追捧"},{"english":"wealth and glamour","chinese":"財富和光鮮"},{"english":"set a poor example for","chinese":"為……樹立壞榜樣"},{"english":"glittering shortcut","chinese":"閃亮的捷徑"},{"english":"replaces character","chinese":"取代品格"},{"english":"skill and meaningful achievement","chinese":"技能和有意義的成就"}]},"model-essay-20-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-20-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:20","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-20-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q20","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many land-scarce cities, ageing buildings are torn down to make way for modern development. While replacement can deliver safer and more efficient premises, I believe its drawbacks are greater because it erases heritage and causes avoidable environmental harm; therefore, the advantages do not outweigh the disadvantages.","chinese":"在許多土地短缺的城市中，老舊建築物為了騰出空間進行現代化發展而被拆除。 雖然以新建築取代它們可以提供更安全、更高效的空間， 我認為整體而言，拆除舊建築的弊端更大，因為這樣做會摧毀文化遺產，並造成不必要的環境破壞；因此，其優點並不大於缺點。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The most serious disadvantage is the irreversible loss of historical character and cultural identity. Old buildings are not merely functional structures; they embody a city’s memory and give neighbourhoods a distinct sense of place. When a traditional market, theatre or row of shophouses is replaced by yet another glass tower, a city loses part of the story written into its streets. Over time, urban centres begin to look interchangeable, which can weaken residents’ attachment to their community and even reduce their appeal to visitors. Demolition also carries a heavy environmental cost. It produces vast quantities of rubble, while new construction consumes fresh steel, cement and energy. In short, what is presented as progress often comes with a sizeable ecological bill.","chinese":"拆除舊建築最嚴重的缺點，是歷史風貌與文化身分的不可逆轉流失。 舊建築不只是實體結構；它們承載著一座城市的記憶，並賦予社區鮮明的地方感。 當傳統市場、劇院或成排店屋消失時，城市空間便會逐漸變得千篇一律，這不但會削弱居民對社區的歸屬感，也可能降低城市對遊客的吸引力。 例如，如果一個歷史街區被另一幢玻璃辦公大樓取代，城市或許會增加可用樓面面積，卻同時失去自身故事中一個清晰可見的部分。 此外，拆除工程也會帶來重大的環境代價。 它會產生大量建築廢料，而新建築則需要全新的鋼材、水泥與能源，從而進一步增加資源消耗和碳排放。 例如，一個重建項目在任何一個新住宅單位或辦公空間落成之前，便可能已把大量瓦礫送往堆填區。 因此，拆除舊建築既會損害城市的文化認同，也會破壞其環境可持續性。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The advantages of replacement are clear but ultimately less compelling. New buildings are usually safer, more energy-efficient and better suited to contemporary needs. In densely populated cities, high-rise redevelopment can also create more homes, offices and public facilities on scarce land. Nevertheless, these benefits do not outweigh the disadvantages because most of them are functional gains that can often be achieved through renovation or adaptive reuse. Cities can strengthen an old structure, upgrade its systems and redesign its interior without wiping the slate clean. Heritage, by contrast, is non-renewable: once it is destroyed, it cannot genuinely be recreated.","chinese":"以新建築取代舊建築的確有其好處，但這些優勢最終並不那麼有說服力。 新建築通常更安全、更節能，也更能符合當代需要。 在人口稠密的城市中，重建亦能在有限土地上提供更多住宅、辦公空間及公共設施，從而提升城市運作效率。 例如，以一幢現代高樓取代結構不安全的低層建築，可能既能提升安全標準，也能為更多居民提供空間。 然而，這些功能性的好處很多時候其實可以透過翻新或活化再利用來達成，而不必全面拆卸。 如果城市選擇加固舊建築、升級內部系統並重新設計室內空間，便能在不全部推倒重來的情況下滿足現代需求；相反，文化遺產一旦被破壞，便無法再生。 例如，一座舊倉庫可以改建成辦公室、藝廊或社區設施，同時保留其歷史立面與原有特色。 因此，雖然重建可以帶來實際利益，但這些收益仍不足以抵銷拆除所造成的永久損失。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, demolishing old buildings may produce modern space and more convenient facilities, but it also destroys urban identity and imposes avoidable environmental costs. For this reason, the advantages do not outweigh the disadvantages.","chinese":"總結來說，拆除舊建築或許能創造更安全、更便利的城市空間，但同時也會摧毀文化遺產，並造成本可避免的環境破壞。 整體而言，我認為其缺點更大，因為重建所帶來的實際好處很多時候都可以用較不具破壞性的方式達成；反之，歷史身分一旦失去，便無法真正復原。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"land-scarce cities","chinese":"土地短缺的城市"},{"english":"ageing buildings","chinese":"老化建築物"},{"english":"be torn down","chinese":"被拆卸"},{"english":"make way for","chinese":"為……讓路"},{"english":"modern development","chinese":"現代發展"},{"english":"replacement","chinese":"替換；重建"},{"english":"deliver safer and more efficient premises","chinese":"提供更安全、更高效的場所"},{"english":"drawbacks are greater","chinese":"缺點更大"},{"english":"erase heritage","chinese":"抹去文化遺產"},{"english":"avoidable environmental harm","chinese":"可避免的環境傷害"},{"english":"outweigh the disadvantages","chinese":"好處不大於壞處"},{"english":"the most serious disadvantage","chinese":"最嚴重的缺點"},{"english":"irreversible loss of","chinese":"……的不可逆轉損失"},{"english":"historical character","chinese":"歷史特色"},{"english":"cultural identity","chinese":"文化身份"},{"english":"not merely functional structures","chinese":"不只是實用建築物"},{"english":"embody a city's memory","chinese":"承載一座城市的記憶"},{"english":"give neighbourhoods a distinct sense of place","chinese":"賦予社區獨特的地方感"},{"english":"a traditional market","chinese":"傳統街市"},{"english":"a row of shophouses","chinese":"一排唐樓式商舖"},{"english":"be replaced by","chinese":"被……取代"},{"english":"yet another glass tower","chinese":"又一座玻璃大廈"},{"english":"loses part of the story","chinese":"失去故事的一部分"},{"english":"written into its streets","chinese":"寫進街道之中的"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨着時間"},{"english":"urban centres","chinese":"城市中心"},{"english":"look interchangeable","chinese":"看起來千篇一律"},{"english":"weaken residents' attachment to","chinese":"削弱居民對……的歸屬感"},{"english":"their community","chinese":"他們的社區"},{"english":"reduce their appeal to visitors","chinese":"降低對遊客的吸引力"},{"english":"demolition","chinese":"拆卸"},{"english":"carries a heavy environmental cost","chinese":"帶來沉重的環境代價"},{"english":"vast quantities of rubble","chinese":"大量瓦礫"},{"english":"new construction","chinese":"新建工程"},{"english":"consumes fresh steel, cement and energy","chinese":"消耗新的鋼材、水泥和能源"},{"english":"in short","chinese":"簡而言之"},{"english":"be presented as progress","chinese":"被包裝成進步"},{"english":"comes with","chinese":"伴隨"},{"english":"a sizeable ecological bill","chinese":"相當大的生態代價"},{"english":"ultimately less compelling","chinese":"最終較缺乏說服力"},{"english":"energy-efficient","chinese":"節能的"},{"english":"better suited to","chinese":"更適合"},{"english":"contemporary needs","chinese":"當代需要"},{"english":"densely populated cities","chinese":"人口稠密的城市"},{"english":"high-rise redevelopment","chinese":"高層重建"},{"english":"public facilities","chinese":"公共設施"},{"english":"scarce land","chinese":"稀缺土地"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"functional gains","chinese":"功能上的好處"},{"english":"be achieved through","chinese":"透過……達到"},{"english":"renovation","chinese":"翻新"},{"english":"adaptive reuse","chinese":"活化再利用"},{"english":"strengthen an old structure","chinese":"加固舊建築結構"},{"english":"upgrade its systems","chinese":"升級其系統"},{"english":"redesign its interior","chinese":"重新設計其內部"},{"english":"without wiping the slate clean","chinese":"而不是一切推倒重來"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"non-renewable","chinese":"不可再生的"},{"english":"genuinely be recreated","chinese":"真正被重建出來"},{"english":"demolishing old buildings","chinese":"拆卸舊建築"},{"english":"modern space","chinese":"現代化空間"},{"english":"convenient facilities","chinese":"便利設施"},{"english":"destroys urban identity","chinese":"破壞城市身份"},{"english":"imposes avoidable environmental costs","chinese":"施加可避免的環境成本"}]},"model-essay-20-ielts-cause-solution":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-20-ielts-cause-solution","essayKey":"cause-solution:20","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-20-ielts-cause-solution","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/problem-and-cause/EdmundBd9CnS-Q20","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Highly educated professionals often choose to pursue employment overseas after gaining expertise in their own fields. This is usually driven by stronger career incentives and better professional conditions, and it can create serious difficulties both for their home countries and for the individuals involved.","chinese":"受過良好教育的專業人士在自己的領域累積專門知識後，往往會選擇到海外工作。 這通常是由更強的職業誘因和更好的專業工作條件所推動，而這也可能為他們的原居國以及相關個人帶來嚴重困難。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main reason is that working abroad often offers a level of reward that is difficult to obtain at home. In many countries, even well-qualified workers may face low salaries, limited promotion prospects, or institutions that do not fully recognise their ability. By contrast, foreign employers may provide higher pay, clearer career paths, and more stable working conditions. A doctor, engineer, or researcher, for example, may move not simply for money, but because another country offers modern equipment, stronger professional networks, and a workplace where their skills can genuinely grow. In this sense, migration becomes less an act of escape than a search for room to breathe professionally.","chinese":"主要原因是，在海外工作往往能提供一種在本國難以獲得的回報水平。 在許多國家，即使是資歷優秀的工作者，也可能面對低薪、有限的晉升前景，或未能充分認可他們能力的機構。 相比之下，外國僱主可能提供更高薪酬、更清晰的職業發展道路，以及更穩定的工作條件 例如，一位醫生、工程師或研究人員移居海外，可能不單純是為了金錢，而是因為另一個國家能提供現代化設備、更強大的專業人脈，以及一個能讓他們的技能真正成長的工作環境。 從這個意義上說，移民與其說是一種逃離，不如說是在尋找專業上得以伸展和發展的空間"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, this movement can cause several problems. For the country of origin, the most serious consequence is a loss of human capital. When experienced teachers, medical specialists, scientists, or technical experts leave, the public systems that trained them may be left thinner and weaker. Hospitals may have longer waiting times, universities may lose capable lecturers, and local industries may struggle to innovate. Over time, this “brain drain” can widen the gap between richer and poorer countries, because the places that most need skilled workers are sometimes the least able to keep them. There may also be personal costs: migrants can face loneliness, cultural barriers, and the pressure of starting again in an unfamiliar professional environment.","chinese":"然而，這種流動也可能造成若干問題。 對原居國而言，最嚴重的後果是人力資本的流失。 當有經驗的教師、醫療專家、科學家或技術專家離開時，曾經培訓他們的公共系統可能會變得更薄弱、更缺乏力量。 醫院的輪候時間可能會變得更長，大學可能會失去有能力的講師，而本地產業也可能難以創新。 長遠而言，這種「人才外流」可能擴大富裕國家與較貧窮國家之間的差距，因為最需要技術人才的地方，有時反而最沒有能力留住他們。 此外，也可能存在個人層面的代價：移民者可能面對孤獨、文化障礙，以及在陌生的專業環境中重新開始的壓力。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, educated and experienced people usually move abroad because overseas work can offer better pay, recognition, resources, and long-term career development. Nevertheless, this trend can weaken essential services in their home countries and place emotional and social pressure on the workers themselves.","chinese":"總結來說，受過教育並具備經驗的人通常會移居海外，因為海外工作能提供更好的薪酬、認可、資源，以及長遠的職業發展。 然而，這一趨勢可能削弱他們原居國的重要服務，並為工作者本人帶來情感和社交上的壓力。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"highly educated professionals","chinese":"受過高等教育的專業人士"},{"english":"pursue employment overseas","chinese":"到海外尋求就業"},{"english":"gaining expertise in","chinese":"在……方面累積專業知識"},{"english":"in their own fields","chinese":"在自己的領域"},{"english":"be driven by","chinese":"由……推動"},{"english":"stronger career incentives","chinese":"更強的事業誘因"},{"english":"better professional conditions","chinese":"更好的專業工作條件"},{"english":"create serious difficulties","chinese":"造成嚴重困難"},{"english":"the individuals involved","chinese":"涉及其中的個人"},{"english":"working abroad","chinese":"到海外工作"},{"english":"a level of reward","chinese":"某種程度的回報"},{"english":"difficult to obtain at home","chinese":"在本國難以獲得"},{"english":"well-qualified workers","chinese":"資歷良好的工作者"},{"english":"low salaries","chinese":"低薪"},{"english":"limited promotion prospects","chinese":"有限的晉升前景"},{"english":"recognise their ability","chinese":"承認他們的能力"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"foreign employers","chinese":"外國僱主"},{"english":"higher pay","chinese":"更高薪酬"},{"english":"clearer career paths","chinese":"更清晰的事業發展路徑"},{"english":"stable working conditions","chinese":"穩定的工作條件"},{"english":"modern equipment","chinese":"現代化設備"},{"english":"professional networks","chinese":"專業人脈網絡"},{"english":"genuinely grow","chinese":"真正成長"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"an act of escape","chinese":"逃離的行為"},{"english":"a search for","chinese":"對……的尋求"},{"english":"room to breathe professionally","chinese":"專業上有發展空間"},{"english":"this movement","chinese":"這種流動"},{"english":"the country of origin","chinese":"原籍國"},{"english":"the most serious consequence","chinese":"最嚴重的後果"},{"english":"human capital","chinese":"人力資本"},{"english":"medical specialists","chinese":"醫學專科人員"},{"english":"technical experts","chinese":"技術專家"},{"english":"public systems","chinese":"公共系統"},{"english":"be left thinner and weaker","chinese":"變得人手更薄弱、力量更弱"},{"english":"longer waiting times","chinese":"更長的輪候時間"},{"english":"capable lecturers","chinese":"有能力的講師"},{"english":"local industries","chinese":"本地產業"},{"english":"struggle to innovate","chinese":"難以創新"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨時間"},{"english":"brain drain","chinese":"人才流失"},{"english":"widen the gap between","chinese":"擴大……之間的差距"},{"english":"richer and poorer countries","chinese":"較富裕和較貧窮的國家"},{"english":"skilled workers","chinese":"技術熟練的工作者"},{"english":"the least able to keep them","chinese":"最無能力留住他們"},{"english":"personal costs","chinese":"個人成本；個人代價"},{"english":"cultural barriers","chinese":"文化障礙"},{"english":"the pressure of starting again","chinese":"重新開始的壓力"},{"english":"an unfamiliar professional environment","chinese":"陌生的專業工作環境"},{"english":"educated and experienced people","chinese":"受過教育而有經驗的人"},{"english":"long-term career development","chinese":"長遠事業發展"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"weaken essential services","chinese":"削弱必要服務"},{"english":"emotional and social pressure","chinese":"情緒和社交壓力"},{"english":"place pressure on","chinese":"對……施加壓力"},{"english":"the workers themselves","chinese":"工作者本人"}]},"model-essay-20-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-20-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:20","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-20-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q20","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Air pollution in major cities is often linked to the heavy use of private vehicles. While some people believe that an international car-free day would be a useful way to reduce this problem, others argue that broader measures would be more effective. In my view, although a car-free day can raise public awareness, lasting improvements require stronger and more permanent transport policies.","chinese":"大城市的空氣污染通常與私家車的大量使用有關。 雖然有些人認為，國際無車日會是減少這個問題的有效方法，但另一些人則認為，更廣泛的措施會更加有效。 在我看來，雖然無車日可以提高公眾意識，但持久的改善需要更強而有力、也更具永久性的交通政策。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Supporters of an international car-free day argue that it can produce an immediate, visible reduction in traffic and emissions. If millions of drivers around the world left their cars at home for one day, city streets would become quieter, cleaner, and less congested. This could also encourage people to reflect on their daily travel habits. For example, an office worker who normally drives a short distance to work might realise that public transport, cycling, or walking is not as inconvenient as they had assumed. In this sense, a car-free day can act as a useful wake-up call, showing the public that cleaner urban life is possible.","chinese":"支持國際無車日的人認為，它能夠立即並明顯地減少交通流量和排放。 如果全球數以百萬計的司機有一天把車留在家中，城市街道便會變得更安靜、更清潔，也較不擁擠。 這也可以鼓勵人們反思自己的日常出行習慣。 例如，一位平時開車短途上班的辦公室職員，可能會意識到公共交通、騎單車或步行並不像他們原本以為的那麼不方便。 從這個意義上說，無車日可以成為一個有用的警醒，向公眾展示更清潔的城市生活是可能實現的。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, I believe other solutions are far more effective because air pollution is a daily problem, not a one-day problem. A symbolic event may briefly reduce emissions, but traffic usually returns to normal the next morning. Governments should instead invest in reliable public transport, create safe cycling lanes, and introduce stricter emission standards for vehicles. These policies change people’s behaviour over time because they make cleaner choices practical, affordable, and attractive. For instance, if buses and trains are cheap, punctual, and comfortable, many commuters will naturally choose them instead of driving. Unlike a car-free day, these measures attack the root of the problem.","chinese":"然而，我認為其他解決方法有效得多，因為空氣污染是一個每日存在的問題，而不是一個只存在一天的問題。 一個象徵性的活動也許能短暫地減少排放，但交通通常會在第二天早上恢復正常。 政府反而應該投資於可靠的公共交通、建設安全的單車徑，並為車輛引入更嚴格的排放標準。 這些政策會隨著時間改變人們的行為，因為它們使更清潔的選擇變得實際、負擔得起，並且有吸引力。 例如，如果巴士和火車便宜、準時又舒適，許多通勤者自然會選擇它們，而不是開車。 與無車日不同，這些措施能夠處理問題的根源。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, an international car-free day has some value because it can raise awareness and temporarily reduce pollution. Nevertheless, I firmly believe that long-term transport reform is a much more effective way to improve air quality, as it changes how people travel every day rather than only once a year.","chinese":"總結來說，國際無車日具有一定價值，因為它可以提高意識並暫時減少污染。 然而，我堅定地認為，長遠的交通改革是改善空氣質素更有效的方法，因為它改變的是人們每天的出行方式，而不是一年只有一次的行為。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"air pollution in major cities","chinese":"大城市的空氣污染"},{"english":"be linked to","chinese":"與……有關"},{"english":"the heavy use of","chinese":"大量使用"},{"english":"private vehicles","chinese":"私家車；私人車輛"},{"english":"an international car-free day","chinese":"國際無車日"},{"english":"a useful way to","chinese":"……的有用方法"},{"english":"reduce this problem","chinese":"減少這個問題"},{"english":"broader measures","chinese":"更廣泛的措施"},{"english":"more effective","chinese":"更有效"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"raise public awareness","chinese":"提高公眾意識"},{"english":"lasting improvements","chinese":"持久改善"},{"english":"stronger and more permanent transport policies","chinese":"更強而更永久的交通政策"},{"english":"supporters of","chinese":"……的支持者"},{"english":"produce an immediate, visible reduction in","chinese":"立即而明顯地減少"},{"english":"traffic and emissions","chinese":"交通流量和排放"},{"english":"around the world","chinese":"世界各地"},{"english":"leave their cars at home","chinese":"不駕車出門"},{"english":"for one day","chinese":"一日"},{"english":"city streets","chinese":"城市街道"},{"english":"quieter, cleaner, and less congested","chinese":"更寧靜、更清潔和較不擠塞"},{"english":"encourage people to reflect on","chinese":"鼓勵人反思"},{"english":"daily travel habits","chinese":"日常出行習慣"},{"english":"normally drives a short distance","chinese":"平日駕車走短距離"},{"english":"public transport, cycling, or walking","chinese":"公共交通、踩單車或步行"},{"english":"not as inconvenient as","chinese":"不像……那麼不方便"},{"english":"as they had assumed","chinese":"如他們原本以為般"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"act as a useful wake-up call","chinese":"發揮有用的警醒作用"},{"english":"cleaner urban life","chinese":"更清潔的城市生活"},{"english":"is possible","chinese":"是可能的"},{"english":"other solutions","chinese":"其他解決方法"},{"english":"far more effective","chinese":"有效得多"},{"english":"a daily problem","chinese":"每日都存在的問題"},{"english":"a one-day problem","chinese":"一日的問題"},{"english":"a symbolic event","chinese":"象徵性活動"},{"english":"briefly reduce emissions","chinese":"短暫減少排放"},{"english":"return to normal","chinese":"恢復正常"},{"english":"the next morning","chinese":"第二朝"},{"english":"should instead invest in","chinese":"反而應該投資於"},{"english":"reliable public transport","chinese":"可靠的公共交通"},{"english":"create safe cycling lanes","chinese":"設立安全單車徑"},{"english":"stricter emission standards","chinese":"更嚴格的排放標準"},{"english":"change people's behaviour over time","chinese":"隨時間改變人們的行為"},{"english":"cleaner choices","chinese":"較環保的選擇"},{"english":"practical, affordable, and attractive","chinese":"實際、負擔得起和吸引"},{"english":"cheap, punctual, and comfortable","chinese":"便宜、準時和舒適"},{"english":"commuters","chinese":"通勤人士"},{"english":"naturally choose","chinese":"自然會選擇"},{"english":"instead of driving","chinese":"而不是駕車"},{"english":"unlike","chinese":"不像"},{"english":"attack the root of the problem","chinese":"針對問題根源"},{"english":"have some value","chinese":"有一定價值"},{"english":"temporarily reduce pollution","chinese":"暫時減少污染"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"long-term transport reform","chinese":"長期交通改革"},{"english":"a much more effective way to","chinese":"……有效得多的方法"},{"english":"improve air quality","chinese":"改善空氣質素"},{"english":"changes how people travel every day","chinese":"改變人們每日的出行方式"},{"english":"rather than only once a year","chinese":"而不是一年只有一次"}]},"model-essay-20-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-20-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:20","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-20-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q20","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In the modern entertainment industry, fame often comes with constant attention from newspapers, television programmes, and online platforms. Some people therefore argue that public exposure is simply the price celebrities pay for success. I strongly disagree. In my view, the media should not publish the private lives of famous people unless there is a clear public interest.","chinese":"在現代娛樂產業中，名氣往往伴隨著來自報紙、電視節目和網上平台的持續關注。 因此，有些人認為，公開曝光只是名人為成功所付出的代價。 我強烈不同意這種看法。在我看來，除非涉及明確的公共利益，否則媒體不應公開名人的私人生活。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main reason is that being well known does not remove a person’s basic right to privacy. Celebrities may choose to appear on screen, perform on stage, or promote their work online, but this does not mean they have agreed to have every corner of their personal lives examined. Their family problems, romantic relationships, health issues, and home addresses are usually irrelevant to their professional achievements. If journalists follow them to private places or publish photographs of their children, this is not entertainment; it is intrusion dressed up as news. Over time, such pressure can damage mental health and make normal family life almost impossible.","chinese":"主要原因是，知名並不會剝奪一個人基本的私隱權。 名人也許選擇出現在螢幕上、在舞台上表演，或在網上宣傳自己的作品，但這並不代表他們同意自己私人生活的每一個角落都被審視。 他們的家庭問題、感情關係、健康狀況和住址，通常都與他們的專業成就無關。 如果記者跟蹤他們到私人場所，或公開他們子女的照片，這並不是娛樂；這只是披著新聞外衣的侵犯。 長遠而言，這種壓力可能損害心理健康，並令正常的家庭生活幾乎變得不可能。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that unrestricted media attention encourages a harmful culture of gossip. When audiences are constantly fed stories about scandals and private conflicts, they may start to see celebrities less as human beings and more as public property. This is unfair, especially because many of these stories are exaggerated, misleading, or based on moments taken out of context. For example, a tired actor leaving a hospital or a singer arguing with a family member may be turned into a dramatic headline, even though the situation has nothing to do with the public. Responsible journalism should inform society, not feed curiosity at any cost.","chinese":"另一個原因是，不受限制的媒體關注會助長一種有害的八卦文化。 當觀眾不斷被餵養有關醜聞和私人衝突的故事時，他們可能會開始較少把名人看作人，而更多把他們看成公共財產。 這是不公平的，尤其是因為許多這類故事都被誇大、具有誤導性，或建基於被抽離語境的片刻。 例如，一位疲憊的演員離開醫院，或一位歌手與家人爭執，即使情況與公眾毫無關係，也可能被寫成戲劇性的標題。 負責任的新聞工作應該是告知社會，而不是不惜一切代價滿足人們的好奇心。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, although famous people should expect public discussion of their work and professional behaviour, their private lives should remain protected. Fame may open the door to attention, but it should not give the media a licence to walk through every room.","chinese":"總結來說，儘管名人應該預期自己的工作和專業行為會受到公眾討論，但他們的私人生活仍然應該受到保護。 名氣也許會打開通往關注的大門，但它不應該給予媒體一張可以走進每個房間的通行證"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"modern entertainment industry","chinese":"現代娛樂業"},{"english":"fame","chinese":"名氣；成名"},{"english":"come with","chinese":"伴隨着"},{"english":"constant attention","chinese":"持續關注"},{"english":"online platforms","chinese":"網上平台"},{"english":"public exposure","chinese":"公開曝光"},{"english":"the price celebrities pay for success","chinese":"名人為成功付出的代價"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"the media","chinese":"傳媒"},{"english":"publish the private lives of","chinese":"公開……的私生活"},{"english":"famous people","chinese":"名人"},{"english":"unless there is","chinese":"除非有……"},{"english":"clear public interest","chinese":"明確公眾利益"},{"english":"being well known","chinese":"眾所周知；有名氣"},{"english":"remove a person's basic right to","chinese":"取消一個人的基本……權利"},{"english":"basic right to privacy","chinese":"基本私隱權"},{"english":"choose to appear on screen","chinese":"選擇在螢幕上露面"},{"english":"perform on stage","chinese":"在舞台上表演"},{"english":"promote their work online","chinese":"在網上宣傳作品"},{"english":"agreed to have","chinese":"同意讓……"},{"english":"every corner of their personal lives","chinese":"他們私人生活的每個角落"},{"english":"be examined","chinese":"被檢視；被審視"},{"english":"family problems","chinese":"家庭問題"},{"english":"romantic relationships","chinese":"戀愛關係"},{"english":"health issues","chinese":"健康問題"},{"english":"home addresses","chinese":"住址"},{"english":"be irrelevant to","chinese":"與……無關"},{"english":"professional achievements","chinese":"專業成就"},{"english":"journalists","chinese":"記者"},{"english":"follow them to private places","chinese":"跟蹤他們到私人地方"},{"english":"publish photographs of","chinese":"刊登……的照片"},{"english":"intrusion dressed up as news","chinese":"包裝成新聞的侵擾"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨着時間過去"},{"english":"such pressure","chinese":"這種壓力"},{"english":"damage mental health","chinese":"損害精神健康"},{"english":"normal family life","chinese":"正常家庭生活"},{"english":"almost impossible","chinese":"幾乎不可能"},{"english":"unrestricted media attention","chinese":"不受限制的傳媒關注"},{"english":"harmful culture of gossip","chinese":"有害的八卦文化"},{"english":"audiences are constantly fed","chinese":"觀眾不斷被灌輸"},{"english":"scandals","chinese":"醜聞"},{"english":"private conflicts","chinese":"私人衝突"},{"english":"see celebrities less as","chinese":"較少將名人視為……"},{"english":"human beings","chinese":"有血有肉的人"},{"english":"public property","chinese":"公共財產"},{"english":"exaggerated","chinese":"被誇大的"},{"english":"misleading","chinese":"具誤導性的"},{"english":"based on moments taken out of context","chinese":"基於被抽離脈絡的片刻"},{"english":"taken out of context","chinese":"被抽離脈絡"},{"english":"tired actor","chinese":"疲倦的演員"},{"english":"arguing with a family member","chinese":"與家人爭吵"},{"english":"be turned into","chinese":"被變成"},{"english":"dramatic headline","chinese":"戲劇化標題"},{"english":"have nothing to do with","chinese":"與……無關"},{"english":"responsible journalism","chinese":"負責任的新聞工作"},{"english":"inform society","chinese":"向社會提供資訊"},{"english":"feed curiosity","chinese":"滿足好奇心"},{"english":"at any cost","chinese":"不惜任何代價"},{"english":"expect public discussion of","chinese":"預期會有關於……的公開討論"},{"english":"professional behaviour","chinese":"專業行為"},{"english":"remain protected","chinese":"繼續受到保護"},{"english":"open the door to","chinese":"打開通往……的大門"},{"english":"give the media a licence to","chinese":"給予傳媒……的許可"},{"english":"walk through every room","chinese":"走進人生的每個房間"}]},"model-essay-21-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-21-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:21","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-21-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q21","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Household life has been transformed by technology over the past few decades. Tasks that were once done by hand, from washing clothes to cleaning floors, are now routinely handled by machines. Although this trend has created some new problems, I believe it brings far more advantages than disadvantages because it saves time and reduces the physical burden of domestic work.","chinese":"在過去幾十年間，家庭生活已被科技大大改變。 那些過去需要人手完成的工作，從洗衣服到清潔地板，如今都經常由機器處理。 雖然這種趨勢帶來了一些新的問題，但我認為它整體上是利多於弊，因為它能節省時間，並減輕家務勞動所帶來的體力負擔。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The clearest benefit is efficiency. Machines can perform repetitive chores far more quickly than people can, which allows household members to devote their time to work, childcare or rest instead of routine housework. A washing machine, for example, can clean an entire load of laundry while its user is doing something else. Equally important is the fact that automation has made home life much less physically demanding. Before such appliances became common, many domestic duties involved prolonged standing, scrubbing and lifting, all of which were especially tiring for parents, older people and those in poor health. By taking over much of this domestic drudgery, machines improve comfort as well as overall quality of life.","chinese":"最明顯的好處就是效率提升。 機器執行重複性家務的速度，遠比人手更快。 這使家庭成員能把時間投入工作、照顧孩子或休息，而不是被例行家務佔據。 例如，洗衣機可以在使用者做其他事情的同時，把整桶衣物洗好。 同樣重要的是，自動化也使家庭生活在體力上不再那麼吃力。 在這類家電普及之前，許多家務都涉及長時間站立、刷洗和搬抬，這些工作對父母、長者以及健康欠佳的人尤其辛苦。 透過接手大量繁重而乏味的家務，機器不但提升了生活舒適度，也改善了整體生活質素"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"That said, this development is not entirely harmless. One drawback is overdependence: once people become accustomed to machines, even a simple task may feel difficult when a device breaks down or there is a power cut. Another concern is that some practical household skills may gradually disappear, particularly among younger generations who have never needed to do these jobs manually. However, these disadvantages are relatively limited. Losing the habit of hand-washing clothes is far less serious than spending hours on physically exhausting work every week.","chinese":"話雖如此，這種發展並非完全沒有代價。 其中一個缺點是過度依賴：一旦人們習慣了機器，當電器故障或停電時，即使是簡單的工作也可能變得難以處理。 另一個問題是，一些實用的家務技能可能會逐漸消失，尤其是在從未需要親手做這些工作的年輕一代之中。 不過，這些缺點其實相對有限。 比起每星期花上數小時去做耗費體力的家務，失去手洗衣物的習慣顯然沒有那麼嚴重。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, the mechanisation of household tasks is largely beneficial. Although it can encourage dependence and weaken certain manual skills, its overall effect is to make daily life more efficient, less tiring and more manageable for most families.","chinese":"總結來說，家務機械化整體上是利大於弊的。 雖然它可能助長依賴，並削弱某些手動技能，但它整體上的影響，是讓大多數家庭的日常生活更有效率、更不疲累，也更容易應付。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"household life","chinese":"家庭生活"},{"english":"be transformed by","chinese":"被……改變"},{"english":"over the past few decades","chinese":"在過去幾十年間"},{"english":"done by hand","chinese":"用人手完成"},{"english":"from washing clothes to cleaning floors","chinese":"從洗衣服到清潔地板"},{"english":"routinely handled by machines","chinese":"通常由機器處理"},{"english":"this trend","chinese":"這個趨勢"},{"english":"far more advantages than disadvantages","chinese":"利多於弊"},{"english":"saves time","chinese":"節省時間"},{"english":"reduces the physical burden of","chinese":"減輕……的體力負擔"},{"english":"domestic work","chinese":"家務工作"},{"english":"the clearest benefit","chinese":"最明顯的好處"},{"english":"perform repetitive chores","chinese":"做重複性的家務"},{"english":"far more quickly than","chinese":"比……快得多"},{"english":"household members","chinese":"家庭成員"},{"english":"devote their time to","chinese":"將時間投放於"},{"english":"childcare","chinese":"照顧孩子"},{"english":"routine housework","chinese":"日常家務"},{"english":"an entire load of laundry","chinese":"一整機衣物"},{"english":"while its user is doing something else","chinese":"在使用者做其他事情時"},{"english":"equally important","chinese":"同樣重要的是"},{"english":"automation","chinese":"自動化"},{"english":"made home life much less physically demanding","chinese":"令家居生活體力負擔大大減少"},{"english":"physically demanding","chinese":"體力要求高的"},{"english":"appliances became common","chinese":"電器變得普及"},{"english":"domestic duties","chinese":"家務職責"},{"english":"prolonged standing","chinese":"長時間站立"},{"english":"scrubbing and lifting","chinese":"擦洗和搬抬"},{"english":"especially tiring for","chinese":"對……尤其令人疲累"},{"english":"those in poor health","chinese":"身體狀況欠佳的人"},{"english":"taking over much of","chinese":"接手大部分……"},{"english":"domestic drudgery","chinese":"繁重沉悶的家務"},{"english":"improve comfort","chinese":"提升舒適度"},{"english":"overall quality of life","chinese":"整體生活質素"},{"english":"that said","chinese":"話雖如此"},{"english":"not entirely harmless","chinese":"並非完全無害"},{"english":"one drawback is","chinese":"一個缺點是"},{"english":"overdependence","chinese":"過度依賴"},{"english":"become accustomed to","chinese":"習慣於"},{"english":"a device breaks down","chinese":"裝置壞掉"},{"english":"a power cut","chinese":"停電"},{"english":"another concern is that","chinese":"另一個令人關注的問題是"},{"english":"practical household skills","chinese":"實用家務技能"},{"english":"gradually disappear","chinese":"逐漸消失"},{"english":"younger generations","chinese":"年輕一代"},{"english":"do these jobs manually","chinese":"人手做這些工作"},{"english":"relatively limited","chinese":"相對有限"},{"english":"losing the habit of","chinese":"失去……的習慣"},{"english":"hand-washing clothes","chinese":"人手洗衣服"},{"english":"far less serious than","chinese":"遠沒有……嚴重"},{"english":"physically exhausting work","chinese":"極耗體力的工作"},{"english":"mechanisation of household tasks","chinese":"家務機械化"},{"english":"largely beneficial","chinese":"大致上有益"},{"english":"encourage dependence","chinese":"鼓勵依賴；造成依賴"},{"english":"weaken certain manual skills","chinese":"削弱某些人手技能"},{"english":"its overall effect","chinese":"其整體影響"},{"english":"daily life","chinese":"日常生活"},{"english":"more efficient, less tiring and more manageable","chinese":"更有效率、較不疲累和更易處理"},{"english":"for most families","chinese":"對大多數家庭而言"}]},"model-essay-21-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-21-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:21","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-21-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q21","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Environmental problems are now among the most serious challenges facing humanity. Some argue that global warming should be treated as the greatest threat, while others believe that the destruction of forests does more immediate damage. Although deforestation clearly harms ecosystems and local communities, I believe global warming is the more urgent and far-reaching problem.","chinese":"環境問題如今已成為人類所面對的最嚴重挑戰之一。 有些人認為全球暖化應被視為最大的威脅，而另一些人則認為森林破壞會造成更即時的損害。 儘管砍伐森林明顯會傷害生態系統和本地社群，但我認為全球暖化是更緊迫且影響更深遠的問題。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Those who regard global warming as the main environmental crisis have a strong argument because it affects almost every part of the planet. Rising temperatures can intensify droughts, floods and heatwaves, making ordinary life more difficult for both rich and poor countries. For example, farmers may lose crops after long dry seasons, while coastal cities may face repeated flooding as sea levels rise. This means that global warming is not only an environmental issue, but also a threat to food security, public health and economic stability. Since its effects spread across borders, it is extremely difficult for any single country to escape them.","chinese":"那些把全球暖化視為主要環境危機的人有很有力的理由，因為它幾乎影響地球的每一個部分。 氣溫上升會加劇乾旱、洪水和熱浪，使富裕國家和貧困國家的日常生活都變得更加困難。 例如，農民可能會在漫長的乾旱季節後失去收成，而沿海城市則可能因海平面上升而反覆面對洪水。 這意味著全球暖化不僅是一個環境問題，也對糧食安全、公共健康和經濟穩定構成威脅 由於它的影響會跨越國界，因此任何單一國家都極難逃避這些後果。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"On the other hand, many people see deforestation as even more destructive because forests are the lungs and living shelters of the earth. When large areas of woodland are cleared for farming, housing or commercial profit, countless animals lose their habitats, soil becomes weaker, and indigenous communities may be pushed off land that has supported them for generations. In addition, trees absorb carbon dioxide, so cutting them down can make climate change worse. In this sense, deforestation is not a small local problem; it can tear apart entire ecosystems and accelerate wider environmental damage.","chinese":"另一方面，許多人認為砍伐森林甚至更具破壞性，因為森林是地球的肺，也是生物賴以生存的庇護所。 當大片林地被清除，用於農業、住房或商業利益時，無數動物會失去棲息地，土壤會變得更脆弱，而原住民社群也可能被迫離開世代依靠的土地。 此外，樹木會吸收二氧化碳，因此砍伐樹木會使氣候變化更加嚴重。 從這個意義上說，砍伐森林並不是一個小型的地方問題；它可以摧毀整個生態系統，並加速更廣泛的環境破壞。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In my view, however, global warming remains the greater threat because it magnifies many other environmental problems, including deforestation itself. A destroyed forest is devastating, but an overheating planet can damage forests, oceans, cities and agriculture at the same time. Therefore, while governments must protect forests, tackling global warming should be the top environmental priority.","chinese":"然而，在我看來，全球暖化仍然是更大的威脅，因為它會放大許多其他環境問題，包括砍伐森林本身。 一片被摧毀的森林固然是災難性的，但一個過熱的地球卻可以同時破壞森林、海洋、城市和農業。 因此，儘管政府必須保護森林，應對全球暖化仍應是最優先的環境任務。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"environmental problems","chinese":"環境問題"},{"english":"among the most serious challenges","chinese":"最嚴重的挑戰之一"},{"english":"facing humanity","chinese":"人類面對的"},{"english":"global warming","chinese":"全球暖化"},{"english":"be treated as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"the greatest threat","chinese":"最大威脅"},{"english":"the destruction of forests","chinese":"森林破壞"},{"english":"do more immediate damage","chinese":"造成更即時的破壞"},{"english":"although","chinese":"雖然"},{"english":"deforestation","chinese":"砍伐森林"},{"english":"harm ecosystems","chinese":"破壞生態系統"},{"english":"local communities","chinese":"本地社區"},{"english":"the more urgent and far-reaching problem","chinese":"更迫切且影響深遠的問題"},{"english":"regard ... as","chinese":"將……視為"},{"english":"the main environmental crisis","chinese":"主要環境危機"},{"english":"have a strong argument","chinese":"有有力的論點"},{"english":"affect almost every part of","chinese":"影響……幾乎每個部分"},{"english":"the planet","chinese":"地球"},{"english":"rising temperatures","chinese":"氣溫上升"},{"english":"intensify droughts, floods and heatwaves","chinese":"加劇乾旱、水災和熱浪"},{"english":"ordinary life","chinese":"日常生活"},{"english":"both rich and poor countries","chinese":"富裕國家和貧窮國家"},{"english":"lose crops","chinese":"失去農作物收成"},{"english":"long dry seasons","chinese":"長時間旱季"},{"english":"coastal cities","chinese":"沿海城市"},{"english":"face repeated flooding","chinese":"面對反覆水浸"},{"english":"as sea levels rise","chinese":"隨着海平面上升"},{"english":"sea levels","chinese":"海平面"},{"english":"not only ... but also","chinese":"不但……而且"},{"english":"environmental issue","chinese":"環境問題"},{"english":"a threat to","chinese":"對……的威脅"},{"english":"food security","chinese":"糧食安全"},{"english":"public health","chinese":"公共衞生"},{"english":"economic stability","chinese":"經濟穩定"},{"english":"since","chinese":"由於"},{"english":"spread across borders","chinese":"跨越國界擴散"},{"english":"any single country","chinese":"任何單一國家"},{"english":"escape them","chinese":"逃避它們；避開它們"},{"english":"on the other hand","chinese":"另一方面"},{"english":"even more destructive","chinese":"更具破壞性"},{"english":"the lungs and living shelters of the earth","chinese":"地球的肺和生命庇護所"},{"english":"large areas of woodland","chinese":"大片林地"},{"english":"be cleared for","chinese":"被清除以作"},{"english":"farming, housing or commercial profit","chinese":"農業、房屋或商業利益"},{"english":"countless animals","chinese":"無數動物"},{"english":"lose their habitats","chinese":"失去棲息地"},{"english":"soil becomes weaker","chinese":"土壤變得較脆弱"},{"english":"indigenous communities","chinese":"原住民社群"},{"english":"be pushed off land","chinese":"被迫離開土地"},{"english":"for generations","chinese":"世世代代"},{"english":"in addition","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"absorb carbon dioxide","chinese":"吸收二氧化碳"},{"english":"cutting them down","chinese":"砍伐樹木"},{"english":"make climate change worse","chinese":"令氣候變化惡化"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"not a small local problem","chinese":"不是小型本地問題"},{"english":"tear apart entire ecosystems","chinese":"破壞整個生態系統"},{"english":"accelerate wider environmental damage","chinese":"加速更廣泛的環境破壞"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"remains the greater threat","chinese":"仍然是更大威脅"},{"english":"magnify many other environmental problems","chinese":"放大許多其他環境問題"},{"english":"including deforestation itself","chinese":"包括砍伐森林本身"},{"english":"a destroyed forest","chinese":"被摧毀的森林"},{"english":"devastating","chinese":"破壞性極大；令人震驚"},{"english":"an overheating planet","chinese":"過熱的地球"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"protect forests","chinese":"保護森林"},{"english":"tackling global warming","chinese":"應對全球暖化"},{"english":"the top environmental priority","chinese":"最優先的環境事項"}]},"model-essay-21-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-21-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:21","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-21-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q21","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"It is common for people to form quick impressions from clothing, especially because appearance is often the first thing visible in social interaction. However, I strongly disagree with the view that a person’s dress reveals a great deal about their personality. In my opinion, clothing is more often shaped by circumstance and social expectation than by someone’s inner character.","chinese":"人們常常會從衣著快速形成印象，尤其是因為外表通常是社交互動中最先被看見的東西。 然而，我強烈不同意一個人的衣著能夠大量反映其性格這種看法。 在我看來，衣著更多時候是由處境和社會期望塑造，而不是由一個人的內在性格所決定"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"First, the clothes people wear are frequently determined by external factors. In many workplaces, for instance, employees must follow a dress code, whether they are naturally creative, reserved, confident or unconventional. A lawyer in a dark suit may simply be obeying professional norms, not showing that he is serious in every part of life. Similarly, a student wearing plain or inexpensive clothes may be limited by family income rather than lacking imagination or self-respect. Since clothing is influenced by weather, culture, money, occupation and occasion, it is unsafe to treat it as a clear window into personality. At best, it shows the situation a person is in; it does not reliably reveal who that person is.","chinese":"首先，人們所穿的衣服經常是由外在因素決定的。 例如，在許多工作場所中，員工都必須遵守服裝規定，無論他們本身是有創意、內斂、自信，還是不依常規的人。 一位穿著深色西裝的律師，可能只是遵守專業規範，而不是顯示他在人生每一方面都很嚴肅。 同樣地，一名穿著樸素或廉價衣服的學生，可能只是受家庭收入所限制，而不是缺乏想像力或自尊。 由於衣著會受到天氣、文化、金錢、職業和場合影響，因此把它視為了解性格的清晰窗口並不可靠。 充其量，它只能顯示一個人所處的情境；它並不能可靠地揭示那個人真正是誰。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Second, people often dress to manage impressions rather than to express their true selves. Someone may wear formal clothes to an interview because they want to appear responsible, while a naturally shy person may choose fashionable outfits to seem more confident in public. In these cases, clothing functions almost like a mask: it helps people play a role, but it does not necessarily expose their deeper values, habits or temperament. If society relies too heavily on appearance, thoughtful people may be underestimated and superficial people may be admired too quickly. This can lead to unfair judgement, where the cover is mistaken for the book.","chinese":"第二，人們穿衣往往是為了管理他人印象，而不是表達真正的自我。 有人可能會在面試時穿正式服裝，因為他們希望看起來負責任；而一個天生害羞的人，也可能選擇時尚的服裝，讓自己在公眾場合顯得更有自信。 在這些情況下，衣著幾乎像一個面具：它幫助人們扮演某種角色，但不一定揭示他們更深層的價值觀、習慣或氣質。 如果社會過度依賴外表作判斷，有思想的人可能會被低估，而膚淺的人則可能太快受到欣賞。 這可能導致不公平的判斷，也就是把封面誤認為整本書本身。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I strongly disagree that dress speaks volumes about personality. Although clothes can create first impressions, they are too dependent on context, money and social performance to be a reliable measure of character.","chinese":"總結來說，我強烈不同意衣著能充分反映性格這種說法。 雖然衣服可以製造第一印象，但它們太依賴背景、金錢和社交表現，因此不能成為衡量品格的可靠標準。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"form quick impressions","chinese":"形成快速印象"},{"english":"appearance","chinese":"外表"},{"english":"the first thing visible","chinese":"第一樣看得見的東西"},{"english":"social interaction","chinese":"社交互動"},{"english":"strongly disagree with","chinese":"強烈不同意……"},{"english":"reveals a great deal about","chinese":"透露很多有關……的事情"},{"english":"personality","chinese":"性格"},{"english":"in my opinion","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"be shaped by","chinese":"受……塑造"},{"english":"circumstance","chinese":"處境；情況"},{"english":"social expectation","chinese":"社會期望"},{"english":"inner character","chinese":"內在性格"},{"english":"be determined by","chinese":"由……決定"},{"english":"external factors","chinese":"外在因素"},{"english":"workplaces","chinese":"工作場所"},{"english":"follow a dress code","chinese":"遵守衣着規定"},{"english":"dress code","chinese":"衣着規定"},{"english":"naturally creative","chinese":"天生有創意"},{"english":"reserved","chinese":"內斂的"},{"english":"unconventional","chinese":"不落俗套的"},{"english":"dark suit","chinese":"深色西裝"},{"english":"professional norms","chinese":"專業規範"},{"english":"not showing that","chinese":"並不是顯示……"},{"english":"in every part of life","chinese":"在生活每個方面"},{"english":"similarly","chinese":"同樣地"},{"english":"plain or inexpensive clothes","chinese":"樸素或便宜的衣服"},{"english":"be limited by","chinese":"受……限制"},{"english":"family income","chinese":"家庭收入"},{"english":"lacking imagination","chinese":"缺乏想像力"},{"english":"self-respect","chinese":"自尊"},{"english":"be influenced by","chinese":"受……影響"},{"english":"occupation","chinese":"職業"},{"english":"occasion","chinese":"場合"},{"english":"unsafe to treat it as","chinese":"將它視為……是不可靠的"},{"english":"clear window into","chinese":"清楚看見……的窗口"},{"english":"at best","chinese":"充其量"},{"english":"the situation a person is in","chinese":"一個人所處的情況"},{"english":"reliably reveal","chinese":"可靠地揭示"},{"english":"who that person is","chinese":"那個人真正是怎樣的人"},{"english":"manage impressions","chinese":"管理別人對自己的印象"},{"english":"express their true selves","chinese":"表達真實自我"},{"english":"formal clothes","chinese":"正式衣服"},{"english":"appear responsible","chinese":"顯得負責任"},{"english":"naturally shy person","chinese":"天生害羞的人"},{"english":"fashionable outfits","chinese":"時尚服裝"},{"english":"seem more confident in public","chinese":"在公眾場合顯得更有自信"},{"english":"in these cases","chinese":"在這些情況下"},{"english":"functions almost like","chinese":"幾乎像……一樣發揮作用"},{"english":"a mask","chinese":"面具"},{"english":"play a role","chinese":"扮演角色"},{"english":"not necessarily expose","chinese":"不一定揭示"},{"english":"deeper values","chinese":"更深層的價值觀"},{"english":"habits or temperament","chinese":"習慣或性情"},{"english":"temperament","chinese":"性情；氣質"},{"english":"relies too heavily on","chinese":"過度依賴"},{"english":"thoughtful people","chinese":"有思想的人"},{"english":"be underestimated","chinese":"被低估"},{"english":"superficial people","chinese":"膚淺的人"},{"english":"be admired too quickly","chinese":"太快受到欣賞"},{"english":"lead to","chinese":"導致"},{"english":"unfair judgement","chinese":"不公平判斷"},{"english":"the cover is mistaken for the book","chinese":"將封面誤當成整本書"},{"english":"dress speaks volumes about","chinese":"衣着充分反映……"},{"english":"first impressions","chinese":"第一印象"},{"english":"dependent on","chinese":"取決於"},{"english":"context","chinese":"語境；情境"},{"english":"social performance","chinese":"社交表現"},{"english":"reliable measure of character","chinese":"衡量性格的可靠標準"}]},"model-essay-22-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-22-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:22","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-22-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q22","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Labour-saving household appliances have made it increasingly possible for mothers to take paid employment while still raising dependent children. Although some people argue that this can place extra strain on family life, I believe the disadvantages are clearly outweighed by the advantages, chiefly because a working mother can improve a family’s financial security and create a more balanced home environment.","chinese":"省時省力的家用電器，使母親在照顧仍需依賴父母的子女的同時，也越來越有可能從事有薪工作。 儘管有些人認為這種情況會為家庭生活帶來額外壓力， 我認為其缺點明顯小於優點，主要原因在於，母親工作不但能提升家庭的經濟保障，亦能建立一個更平衡的家庭環境。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first major advantage is economic stability. When both parents earn an income, the household is less vulnerable to inflation, unexpected medical bills, or the loss of one job. This greater financial resilience allows parents to provide better food, safer housing, and stronger educational support, which directly benefits children. For example, a dual-income family may be able to afford reliable childcare, private tutoring, or a home in a better school district, opportunities that might otherwise be out of reach. Just as importantly, reduced financial pressure often leads to fewer arguments over money, so the home becomes calmer and more secure for everyone.","chinese":"第一個主要優點是經濟穩定。 當父母雙方都有收入時，家庭便較不容易受到通貨膨脹、突如其來的醫療開支或其中一方失業的影響。 更強的經濟抗壓能力，能讓父母為孩子提供更好的飲食、更安全的居住環境，以及更充足的教育支援，而這些都會直接令孩子受益。 例如，雙收入家庭可能有能力負擔可靠的托兒服務、私人補習，或搬到校網更佳的地區居住，而這些機會本來可能是他們無法取得的。 同樣重要的是，經濟壓力減輕通常也會減少因金錢而起的爭執，因此整個家庭對每一位成員而言都會變得更平靜、更有安全感。 當父母不再時刻為帳單和開支憂心時，他們更有可能保持耐性、願意合作，並在情感上更能照顧孩子的需要。 例如，一個收入較穩定的家庭，家中衝突往往會較少，這使父母能把時間用來支持孩子，而不是爭論金錢問題。 因此，母親就業所帶來的更大經濟保障，不但能在物質上加強家庭，也能在情感層面令家庭更穩固。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"A second benefit is that maternal employment can improve the overall culture of the family. Children who see their mother contributing professionally are more likely to grow up with a healthier understanding of responsibility, independence, and gender equality. A daughter may learn that motherhood does not require economic dependence, while a son may be less likely to assume that childcare and housework are solely female duties. Admittedly, there are drawbacks, most notably reduced time at home and the risk of fatigue. However, these problems are usually manageable through modern appliances, childcare arrangements, and a fairer division of labour between parents. In other words, a small loss of time is far less damaging than long-term financial insecurity or an unequal family structure.","chinese":"第二個優點是，母親工作可以改善整個家庭的文化與價值觀。 當孩子看見母親在職場上作出貢獻時，他們更有可能在成長過程中建立對責任感、獨立性以及性別平等的更健康理解。 這有助他們明白，男性與女性都可以支撐家庭、作出決策，並對社會作出有意義的貢獻。 例如，女兒可能會明白，成為母親並不代表必須在經濟上依附他人；而兒子則較不會認為照顧孩子和做家務只是女性的責任。 誠然，這樣的安排亦有缺點，其中最明顯的是母親留在家中的時間減少，以及更容易感到疲累。 然而，這些問題通常可以透過現代家電、適當的托兒安排，以及父母之間更公平的家務分工來加以處理。 例如，若父母雙方共同分擔家務，並善用節省時間的家用電器，母親的負擔便可大幅減輕，令這些缺點變得沒有那麼嚴重。 換言之，與長遠的經濟不穩定或不平等的家庭結構相比，少量相處時間的減少所造成的影響其實小得多。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, when a mother works, the family usually gains not only a stronger financial foundation but also a more modern and balanced set of values. While this arrangement can create some practical pressure, the disadvantages are limited and do not outweigh the substantial long-term benefits.","chinese":"總結而言，當母親工作時，家庭通常不但能獲得更穩固的經濟基礎，亦能建立一套更現代、更平衡的價值觀。 雖然這種安排可能帶來一些實際壓力，但其缺點是有限的，並不足以超過那些重大的長遠利益。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"labour-saving household appliances","chinese":"節省勞力的家用電器"},{"english":"increasingly possible for","chinese":"令……越來越有可能"},{"english":"take paid employment","chinese":"從事受薪工作"},{"english":"raise dependent children","chinese":"撫養需要照顧的子女"},{"english":"dependent children","chinese":"需要供養的子女"},{"english":"place extra strain on","chinese":"對……造成額外壓力"},{"english":"family life","chinese":"家庭生活"},{"english":"be clearly outweighed by","chinese":"明顯被……蓋過"},{"english":"chiefly because","chinese":"主要因為"},{"english":"a working mother","chinese":"在職母親"},{"english":"financial security","chinese":"經濟保障"},{"english":"a more balanced home environment","chinese":"更平衡的家庭環境"},{"english":"economic stability","chinese":"經濟穩定"},{"english":"earn an income","chinese":"賺取收入"},{"english":"less vulnerable to","chinese":"較不易受……影響"},{"english":"inflation","chinese":"通脹"},{"english":"unexpected medical bills","chinese":"意料之外的醫療費用"},{"english":"the loss of one job","chinese":"失去其中一份工作"},{"english":"financial resilience","chinese":"財務抗壓能力"},{"english":"educational support","chinese":"教育支援"},{"english":"directly benefits children","chinese":"直接令孩子受惠"},{"english":"a dual-income family","chinese":"雙收入家庭"},{"english":"reliable childcare","chinese":"可靠的托兒服務"},{"english":"private tutoring","chinese":"私人補習"},{"english":"a better school district","chinese":"較好的校區"},{"english":"otherwise be out of reach","chinese":"否則難以負擔；難以得到"},{"english":"just as importantly","chinese":"同樣重要的是"},{"english":"reduced financial pressure","chinese":"減少了的經濟壓力"},{"english":"arguments over money","chinese":"關於金錢的爭拗"},{"english":"calmer and more secure","chinese":"更平靜和更有安全感"},{"english":"maternal employment","chinese":"母親就業"},{"english":"the overall culture of the family","chinese":"家庭的整體文化"},{"english":"contributing professionally","chinese":"在專業上作出貢獻"},{"english":"be more likely to grow up with","chinese":"更有可能在成長中形成"},{"english":"a healthier understanding of","chinese":"對……更健康的理解"},{"english":"responsibility, independence and gender equality","chinese":"責任感、獨立和性別平等"},{"english":"economic dependence","chinese":"經濟依賴"},{"english":"be less likely to assume that","chinese":"較不會假設"},{"english":"childcare and housework","chinese":"照顧子女和家務"},{"english":"solely female duties","chinese":"純粹女性的責任"},{"english":"admittedly","chinese":"無可否認"},{"english":"reduced time at home","chinese":"在家的時間減少"},{"english":"the risk of fatigue","chinese":"疲勞的風險"},{"english":"manageable through","chinese":"可透過……處理"},{"english":"childcare arrangements","chinese":"托兒安排"},{"english":"a fairer division of labour","chinese":"更公平的分工"},{"english":"between parents","chinese":"父母之間"},{"english":"in other words","chinese":"換言之"},{"english":"a small loss of time","chinese":"少量時間上的損失"},{"english":"far less damaging than","chinese":"遠比……破壞性小"},{"english":"long-term financial insecurity","chinese":"長期經濟不穩"},{"english":"an unequal family structure","chinese":"不平等的家庭結構"},{"english":"gains not only","chinese":"不但得到"},{"english":"a stronger financial foundation","chinese":"更穩固的經濟基礎"},{"english":"a more modern and balanced set of values","chinese":"更現代和更平衡的價值觀"},{"english":"this arrangement","chinese":"這種安排"},{"english":"practical pressure","chinese":"實際壓力"},{"english":"do not outweigh","chinese":"不會大於"},{"english":"substantial long-term benefits","chinese":"重大的長遠好處"}]},"model-essay-22-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-22-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:22","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-22-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q22","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Environmental damage has become one of the defining concerns of modern life, affecting air, water, food systems and public health. Some argue that these problems are international in nature and therefore require government intervention, while others believe they can only be solved through individual responsibility. I firmly believe that governments must take the lead, because only they have the authority and resources to create changes on the scale required.","chinese":"環境破壞已成為現代生活中其中一個最具代表性的重大問題，影響著空氣、水資源、食物系統以及公共健康。 有些人認為這些問題本質上是國際性的，因此需要政府介入；而另一些人則相信，這些問題只能透過個人責任來解決。 我堅定地認為，政府必須發揮主導作用，因為只有政府才擁有足夠的權力和資源，去推動所需規模的改變。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Those who support government action point out that many environmental problems are too large for private citizens to control. Climate change, industrial pollution and deforestation are not caused merely by careless household habits, but by national energy systems, transport networks and corporate activity. If a factory releases toxic waste into a river, for instance, ordinary residents may complain or boycott its products, but they cannot legally force it to change its production methods. Governments, by contrast, can impose strict regulations, fine polluters, invest in renewable energy and cooperate with other countries. Without this level of authority, environmental protection becomes a matter of goodwill rather than enforceable responsibility.","chinese":"支持政府行動的人指出，許多環境問題規模太大，並非普通市民能夠控制。 氣候變化、工業污染和森林砍伐，並不只是由粗心大意的家庭習慣造成，而是由國家能源系統、交通網絡和企業活動所造成。 例如，如果一間工廠把有毒廢料排入河流，普通居民可以投訴或抵制它的產品，但他們不能在法律上強制它改變生產方式。 相比之下，政府可以實施嚴格規管、懲罰污染者、投資可再生能源，並與其他國家合作 如果沒有這種層次的權力，環境保護就會變成一種善意行為，而不是可以被強制執行的責任。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"On the other hand, supporters of individual action argue that laws alone will not work if people continue to live wastefully. Everyday choices such as driving less, recycling properly, reducing plastic use and avoiding excessive consumption can collectively reduce pressure on the planet. For example, if millions of households waste less food and electricity, demand for energy and resources will fall. This view is reasonable because environmental damage is not only created in boardrooms and factories; it is also fed by ordinary routines. However, individual effort is like carrying water in a cup when the main pipe is still leaking: useful, but far from sufficient.","chinese":"另一方面，支持個人行動的人認為，如果人們繼續以浪費的方式生活，單靠法律並不能奏效。 日常選擇，例如減少駕車、正確回收、減少使用塑膠以及避免過度消費，都可以共同減輕地球的壓力。 例如，如果數百萬個家庭減少浪費食物和電力，對能源和資源的需求便會下降。 這種觀點是合理的，因為環境破壞不只是在董事會會議室和工廠中產生；它也受到日常生活習慣的推動。 然而，個人努力就像主水管仍在漏水時用杯子盛水一樣：有用，但遠遠不足夠。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, individuals should certainly behave more responsibly, but environmental issues cannot be left mainly to personal choice. Governments are best placed to regulate industries, shape infrastructure and coordinate international action, so they should bear the central responsibility for tackling today’s environmental crisis.","chinese":"總結來說，個人當然應該表現得更負責任，但環境問題不能主要交由個人選擇來處理。 政府最適合去規管產業、塑造基礎建設，並協調國際行動，因此它們應該承擔處理當今環境危機的核心責任。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"environmental damage","chinese":"環境破壞"},{"english":"one of the defining concerns of","chinese":"……中最具代表性的關注之一"},{"english":"modern life","chinese":"現代生活"},{"english":"affecting air, water, food systems and public health","chinese":"影響空氣、水、食物系統和公共衞生"},{"english":"international in nature","chinese":"本質上屬國際性"},{"english":"require government intervention","chinese":"需要政府干預"},{"english":"individual responsibility","chinese":"個人責任"},{"english":"firmly believe that","chinese":"堅信"},{"english":"take the lead","chinese":"帶頭；主導"},{"english":"authority and resources","chinese":"權力和資源"},{"english":"on the scale required","chinese":"達到所需規模"},{"english":"government action","chinese":"政府行動"},{"english":"point out that","chinese":"指出"},{"english":"too large for","chinese":"對……來說太大"},{"english":"private citizens","chinese":"普通公民"},{"english":"climate change","chinese":"氣候變化"},{"english":"industrial pollution","chinese":"工業污染"},{"english":"deforestation","chinese":"砍伐森林"},{"english":"not caused merely by","chinese":"並不只是由……造成"},{"english":"careless household habits","chinese":"不謹慎的家庭習慣"},{"english":"national energy systems","chinese":"國家能源系統"},{"english":"transport networks","chinese":"交通網絡"},{"english":"corporate activity","chinese":"企業活動"},{"english":"releases toxic waste into","chinese":"將有毒廢物排入"},{"english":"toxic waste","chinese":"有毒廢物"},{"english":"ordinary residents","chinese":"普通居民"},{"english":"boycott its products","chinese":"抵制其產品"},{"english":"legally force it to","chinese":"從法律上強制其"},{"english":"change its production methods","chinese":"改變其生產方式"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相反"},{"english":"impose strict regulations","chinese":"實施嚴格規管"},{"english":"fine polluters","chinese":"向污染者罰款"},{"english":"invest in renewable energy","chinese":"投資可再生能源"},{"english":"cooperate with other countries","chinese":"與其他國家合作"},{"english":"without this level of authority","chinese":"沒有這種程度的權力"},{"english":"environmental protection","chinese":"環境保護"},{"english":"a matter of goodwill","chinese":"善意的事情"},{"english":"rather than enforceable responsibility","chinese":"而不是可執行的責任"},{"english":"supporters of individual action","chinese":"個人行動的支持者"},{"english":"laws alone","chinese":"單靠法律"},{"english":"continue to live wastefully","chinese":"繼續浪費地生活"},{"english":"everyday choices","chinese":"日常選擇"},{"english":"driving less","chinese":"少些駕車"},{"english":"recycling properly","chinese":"正確回收"},{"english":"reducing plastic use","chinese":"減少塑膠使用"},{"english":"avoiding excessive consumption","chinese":"避免過度消費"},{"english":"collectively reduce pressure on","chinese":"共同減輕對……的壓力"},{"english":"the planet","chinese":"地球"},{"english":"millions of households","chinese":"數以百萬計的家庭"},{"english":"waste less food and electricity","chinese":"少浪費食物和電力"},{"english":"demand for energy and resources","chinese":"對能源和資源的需求"},{"english":"this view is reasonable","chinese":"這個看法是合理的"},{"english":"boardrooms and factories","chinese":"會議室和工廠"},{"english":"be fed by","chinese":"由……助長"},{"english":"ordinary routines","chinese":"日常習慣"},{"english":"individual effort","chinese":"個人努力"},{"english":"carrying water in a cup","chinese":"用杯裝水"},{"english":"the main pipe is still leaking","chinese":"主水管仍在漏水"},{"english":"far from sufficient","chinese":"遠遠不足夠"},{"english":"behave more responsibly","chinese":"表現得更負責任"},{"english":"cannot be left mainly to","chinese":"不能主要交由……處理"},{"english":"personal choice","chinese":"個人選擇"},{"english":"be best placed to","chinese":"最有條件去"},{"english":"regulate industries","chinese":"規管行業"},{"english":"shape infrastructure","chinese":"塑造基建"},{"english":"coordinate international action","chinese":"協調國際行動"},{"english":"bear the central responsibility for","chinese":"承擔……的核心責任"},{"english":"tackling today's environmental crisis","chinese":"應對當今環境危機"}]},"model-essay-22-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-22-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:22","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-22-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q22","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"With digital technology now embedded in everyday life, many people predict that direct human interaction will eventually disappear. I completely disagree with this view. Although the internet and text messaging have changed the speed and convenience of communication, they cannot replace the emotional depth, trust, and practical value of meeting people in person.","chinese":"隨著數位科技如今已融入日常生活，許多人預測直接的人際互動最終將會消失。 我完全不同意這種觀點。 儘管互聯網和文字訊息改變了溝通的速度與便利性，它們無法取代面對面見面所帶來的情感深度、信任，以及實際價值。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason is that face-to-face communication carries human signals that written messages often flatten or distort. Tone of voice, eye contact, facial expression and body language all help people understand not only what is being said, but also how it is meant. Without these cues, even a simple sentence can be misunderstood, especially in sensitive situations. For example, a manager who needs to comfort an anxious employee, or a doctor who must explain bad news to a patient, cannot rely only on short written messages. In such moments, physical presence acts as a bridge between information and empathy. This is why direct interaction will remain essential wherever trust, reassurance and emotional intelligence are required.","chinese":"最有力的原因是，面對面溝通承載人性的訊號，而文字訊息往往會削弱或扭曲這些訊號 語氣、眼神接觸、面部表情和肢體語言，都能幫助人們理解的不只是說話的內容，還包括說話背後真正的意思。 如果沒有這些線索，即使是一句簡單的話也可能被誤解，尤其是在敏感情況之中。 例如，一位需要安慰焦慮員工的經理，或者一位必須向病人解釋壞消息的醫生，都不能只依賴簡短的文字訊息。 在這些時刻，實際在場就像資訊與同理心之間的一座橋樑。 這就是為甚麼凡是需要信任、安撫和情緒智慧的地方，直接互動都仍然會是不可或缺的"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that many parts of social and professional life still depend on shared physical experience. Families build closeness around meals, friends strengthen relationships through shared activities, and workplaces often solve complex problems more effectively when people are in the same room. Online tools may help people stay in contact, but they do not fully recreate the rhythm of real conversation, where ideas can be exchanged, challenged and refined instantly. A group of colleagues brainstorming around a table, for instance, can read one another’s reactions and adjust their thinking in real time. This makes face-to-face interaction not an outdated habit, but a living part of how societies cooperate.","chinese":"另一個原因是，社交和職業生活中的許多部分仍然依賴共同的實體經驗。 家庭會在一起用餐時建立親近感，朋友會透過共同活動加強關係，而當人們身處同一個房間時，職場也往往能更有效地解決複雜問題。 線上工具或許能幫助人們保持聯繫，但它們無法完全重現真實對話的節奏；在真實對話中，想法可以即時被交換、挑戰和完善。 例如，一群同事圍著桌子腦力激盪時，可以讀懂彼此的反應，並即時調整自己的思路 這使得面對面互動並不是一種過時的習慣，而是社會合作方式中仍然鮮活的一部分。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely reject the idea that face-to-face communication will become obsolete. Digital communication will continue to grow, but direct human contact will remain irreplaceable because it provides emotional clarity, builds trust and supports real social connection.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全反對面對面溝通將會變得過時這一想法。 數位溝通將會繼續發展，但直接的人際接觸仍然無可取代，因為它能提供情感上的清晰度、建立信任，並支持真正的社會連結。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"digital technology","chinese":"數碼科技"},{"english":"be embedded in","chinese":"融入……之中"},{"english":"everyday life","chinese":"日常生活"},{"english":"direct human interaction","chinese":"直接人際互動"},{"english":"eventually disappear","chinese":"最終消失"},{"english":"the internet and text messaging","chinese":"互聯網和文字訊息溝通"},{"english":"changed the speed and convenience of","chinese":"改變了……的速度和便利"},{"english":"communication","chinese":"溝通"},{"english":"cannot replace","chinese":"不能取代"},{"english":"emotional depth","chinese":"情感深度"},{"english":"practical value","chinese":"實際價值"},{"english":"meeting people in person","chinese":"親身見面"},{"english":"the strongest reason","chinese":"最有力的原因"},{"english":"face-to-face communication","chinese":"面對面溝通"},{"english":"human signals","chinese":"人際信號"},{"english":"written messages","chinese":"書面訊息"},{"english":"flatten or distort","chinese":"淡化或扭曲"},{"english":"tone of voice","chinese":"語氣"},{"english":"eye contact","chinese":"眼神接觸"},{"english":"facial expression","chinese":"面部表情"},{"english":"body language","chinese":"肢體語言"},{"english":"not only what is being said","chinese":"不只是所說的內容"},{"english":"how it is meant","chinese":"說話背後的意思"},{"english":"without these cues","chinese":"沒有這些線索"},{"english":"be misunderstood","chinese":"被誤解"},{"english":"sensitive situations","chinese":"敏感情況"},{"english":"comfort an anxious employee","chinese":"安撫焦慮的員工"},{"english":"anxious employee","chinese":"焦慮的員工"},{"english":"explain bad news to","chinese":"向……解釋壞消息"},{"english":"rely only on","chinese":"只依賴"},{"english":"short written messages","chinese":"簡短書面訊息"},{"english":"in such moments","chinese":"在這些時刻"},{"english":"physical presence","chinese":"親身在場"},{"english":"acts as a bridge between","chinese":"成為……之間的橋樑"},{"english":"information and empathy","chinese":"資料和同理心"},{"english":"direct interaction","chinese":"直接互動"},{"english":"remain essential","chinese":"仍然必不可少"},{"english":"wherever","chinese":"在任何……的地方"},{"english":"trust and reassurance","chinese":"信任和安心感"},{"english":"emotional intelligence","chinese":"情緒智能"},{"english":"be required","chinese":"被需要"},{"english":"social and professional life","chinese":"社交和職業生活"},{"english":"depend on","chinese":"依賴"},{"english":"shared physical experience","chinese":"共同的實體經歷"},{"english":"build closeness around meals","chinese":"透過一起吃飯建立親密感"},{"english":"strengthen relationships","chinese":"加強關係"},{"english":"shared activities","chinese":"共同活動"},{"english":"solve complex problems","chinese":"解決複雜問題"},{"english":"more effectively","chinese":"更有效地"},{"english":"in the same room","chinese":"在同一房間"},{"english":"online tools","chinese":"網上工具"},{"english":"stay in contact","chinese":"保持聯絡"},{"english":"fully recreate","chinese":"完全重現"},{"english":"rhythm of real conversation","chinese":"真實對話的節奏"},{"english":"be exchanged, challenged and refined","chinese":"被交流、質疑和完善"},{"english":"instantly","chinese":"即時"},{"english":"group of colleagues","chinese":"一群同事"},{"english":"brainstorming around a table","chinese":"圍坐桌旁腦力激盪"},{"english":"read one another's reactions","chinese":"讀懂彼此的反應"},{"english":"adjust their thinking","chinese":"調整想法"},{"english":"in real time","chinese":"即時"},{"english":"outdated habit","chinese":"過時習慣"},{"english":"living part of","chinese":"……中活生生的一部分"},{"english":"societies cooperate","chinese":"社會如何合作"},{"english":"completely reject the idea that","chinese":"完全否定……的想法"},{"english":"become obsolete","chinese":"變得過時；被淘汰"},{"english":"digital communication","chinese":"數碼溝通"},{"english":"continue to grow","chinese":"繼續發展"},{"english":"direct human contact","chinese":"直接人際接觸"},{"english":"remain irreplaceable","chinese":"仍然無可取代"},{"english":"emotional clarity","chinese":"情感上的清晰度"},{"english":"builds trust","chinese":"建立信任"},{"english":"real social connection","chinese":"真實社交連繫"}]},"model-essay-23-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-23-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:23","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-23-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q23","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In recent decades, the expansion of tourism and other forms of international contact has helped English become the most widely used language in the world. As a result, some people believe that humanity may one day share a single common tongue. Such a development would offer notable practical benefits, but it would also carry profound cultural and social costs.","chinese":"近幾十年來，旅遊業的發展以及其他形式的國際交流，促使英語成為世界上最廣泛使用的語言。 因此，有些人相信，人類有一天可能會共用一種共同語言。 這樣的發展會帶來顯著的實際好處，但同時也會付出深遠的文化與社會代價。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The most obvious advantage of one global language is ease of communication. If people from different countries could speak to one another without interpreters or translation software, travel, trade, diplomacy and academic collaboration would all become more efficient. Misunderstandings could be reduced, and ideas could cross borders far more quickly. A common language could also widen access to education and employment. Students would be able to study abroad more easily, while workers could compete in a broader international labour market. In this sense, a shared language could act as a bridge, bringing people into closer contact with one another.","chinese":"全球只使用一種語言最明顯的優點，就是溝通會變得更容易。 如果來自不同國家的人能夠在沒有口譯員或翻譯軟體的情況下彼此交流，那麼旅遊、貿易、外交以及學術合作都會變得更有效率。 這樣一來，誤解可以減少，而各種想法也能更快速地跨越國界傳播。 例如，如果研究同一項醫療問題的國際研究人員都使用同一種語言，他們便能直接交換研究成果，並更快找到解決方法。 一種共同語言也可以擴大人們接受教育和獲得工作的機會。 學生將更容易到海外升學，而勞工也能在更廣闊的國際就業市場中競爭。 從這個角度來看，共通語言就像一座橋樑，使人與人之間的聯繫更加緊密。 因此，全球共用一種語言可以大大提升效率、流動性以及國際合作。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, serious disadvantages would also arise. Language is not merely a tool for exchanging information; it is also a carrier of memory, identity and tradition. If smaller languages were pushed aside by a global one, communities could lose folk stories, historical knowledge and cultural values that have been passed down for generations. In addition, a one-language world might not be as fair as it appears. Those born into the dominant language would enjoy an immediate advantage in business, media and higher education, whereas others might feel compelled to abandon their mother tongue in order to succeed. What is gained in convenience, therefore, could be paid for in cultural erosion and social imbalance.","chinese":"然而，這樣的情況也會帶來嚴重的缺點，其中最重要的就是語言與文化多樣性可能流失。 語言不僅僅是交換資訊的工具，它同時也是記憶、身份認同與傳統的載體。 如果較小的語言被全球通用語所取代，社群便可能失去那些代代相傳的民間故事、歷史知識以及文化價值。 例如，當一種少數語言消失時，那種獨特的世界觀與表達方式也可能隨之消失。 此外，只有一種語言的世界，未必像表面看起來那麼公平。 以主導語言為母語的人，會在商業、媒體和高等教育方面立刻擁有優勢；相反，其他人則可能被迫放棄母語，以換取成功的機會。 因此，便利所帶來的收穫，可能要以文化侵蝕與社會失衡作為代價。 因此，雖然一種共同語言可能使生活變得更簡單，但它也可能削弱文化認同，並加深不平等。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, having one language worldwide could simplify communication and create wider educational and economic opportunities. Nevertheless, it could also accelerate the loss of linguistic heritage and reinforce inequality between native and non-native speakers.","chinese":"總結來說，全球只使用一種語言可以簡化溝通，並創造更廣泛的教育與經濟機會。 然而，它同時也可能加速語言文化遺產的流失，並強化母語者與非母語者之間的不平等。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"in recent decades","chinese":"近幾十年來"},{"english":"the expansion of tourism","chinese":"旅遊業的擴張"},{"english":"other forms of international contact","chinese":"其他形式的國際接觸"},{"english":"the most widely used language","chinese":"最廣泛使用的語言"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此；結果"},{"english":"humanity","chinese":"人類"},{"english":"one day","chinese":"有一天"},{"english":"share a single common tongue","chinese":"共享一種共同語言"},{"english":"such a development","chinese":"這樣的發展"},{"english":"notable practical benefits","chinese":"顯著的實際好處"},{"english":"carry profound cultural and social costs","chinese":"帶來深遠的文化和社會代價"},{"english":"the most obvious advantage of","chinese":"……最明顯的好處"},{"english":"one global language","chinese":"一種全球語言"},{"english":"ease of communication","chinese":"溝通便利"},{"english":"speak to one another","chinese":"彼此交談"},{"english":"without interpreters or translation software","chinese":"無需傳譯員或翻譯軟件"},{"english":"translation software","chinese":"翻譯軟件"},{"english":"travel, trade, diplomacy and academic collaboration","chinese":"旅遊、貿易、外交和學術合作"},{"english":"academic collaboration","chinese":"學術合作"},{"english":"become more efficient","chinese":"變得更有效率"},{"english":"misunderstandings could be reduced","chinese":"誤解可以減少"},{"english":"cross borders","chinese":"跨越國界"},{"english":"far more quickly","chinese":"快得多"},{"english":"widen access to","chinese":"擴大接觸……的機會"},{"english":"education and employment","chinese":"教育和就業"},{"english":"study abroad","chinese":"到海外升學"},{"english":"compete in","chinese":"在……中競爭"},{"english":"a broader international labour market","chinese":"更廣闊的國際勞動市場"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"a shared language","chinese":"共同語言"},{"english":"act as a bridge","chinese":"發揮橋樑作用"},{"english":"bring people into closer contact with","chinese":"令……更緊密接觸"},{"english":"serious disadvantages would also arise","chinese":"嚴重缺點也會出現"},{"english":"not merely a tool for","chinese":"不只是用來……的工具"},{"english":"exchanging information","chinese":"交換資料"},{"english":"a carrier of memory, identity and tradition","chinese":"記憶、身份和傳統的載體"},{"english":"smaller languages","chinese":"較小語言"},{"english":"pushed aside by","chinese":"被……排擠"},{"english":"communities","chinese":"社群"},{"english":"folk stories","chinese":"民間故事"},{"english":"historical knowledge","chinese":"歷史知識"},{"english":"cultural values","chinese":"文化價值"},{"english":"passed down for generations","chinese":"世代相傳"},{"english":"in addition","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"a one-language world","chinese":"單一語言的世界"},{"english":"as fair as it appears","chinese":"像表面看來那樣公平"},{"english":"born into","chinese":"生於……之中"},{"english":"the dominant language","chinese":"主導語言"},{"english":"enjoy an immediate advantage","chinese":"享有即時優勢"},{"english":"higher education","chinese":"高等教育"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"然而；而"},{"english":"feel compelled to","chinese":"感到被迫去……"},{"english":"abandon their mother tongue","chinese":"放棄母語"},{"english":"in order to succeed","chinese":"為了成功"},{"english":"what is gained in convenience","chinese":"在便利上得到的東西"},{"english":"be paid for in","chinese":"以……為代價"},{"english":"cultural erosion","chinese":"文化侵蝕"},{"english":"social imbalance","chinese":"社會失衡"},{"english":"having one language worldwide","chinese":"全球使用一種語言"},{"english":"simplify communication","chinese":"簡化溝通"},{"english":"create wider educational and economic opportunities","chinese":"創造更廣泛的教育和經濟機會"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而；儘管如此"},{"english":"accelerate the loss of","chinese":"加速……的流失"},{"english":"linguistic heritage","chinese":"語言遺產"},{"english":"reinforce inequality between","chinese":"加深……之間的不平等"},{"english":"native and non-native speakers","chinese":"母語和非母語使用者"}]},"model-essay-23-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-23-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:23","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-23-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q23","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Parents play a decisive role in shaping both the behaviour and the emotional development of their children. While some people believe that parents should mainly correct misbehaviour and teach moral values, others argue that their most important duty is to offer care, security and a stable home. In my view, although discipline is necessary, nurturing children in a safe environment is the more fundamental responsibility.","chinese":"父母在塑造孩子的行為和情感發展方面扮演著決定性的角色。 有些人認為父母主要應該糾正不當行為並教導道德價值，而另一些人則認為父母最重要的責任是提供關愛、安全感和穩定的家庭。 在我看來，雖然紀律是必要的，但在安全的環境中培育孩子才是更根本的責任。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"On the one hand, discipline is clearly an essential part of parenting because children are not born with a complete understanding of acceptable behaviour. Without guidance, they may struggle to respect rules, control their impulses or consider the feelings of others. For example, a child who is never corrected for lying, shouting or behaving selfishly may carry these habits into school and later into adult relationships. In this sense, parents act as a child’s first moral compass: they help children distinguish right from wrong before society has to impose harsher consequences. Good discipline, therefore, does not simply punish children; it teaches them self-control, responsibility and respect for others.","chinese":"一方面，紀律顯然是育兒中不可或缺的一部分，因為孩子並不是天生就完全明白甚麼行為是可以接受的。 如果沒有引導，他們可能會難以尊重規則、控制衝動，或顧及他人的感受。 例如，一個從未因說謊、大叫或自私行為而被糾正的孩子，可能會把這些習慣帶到學校，甚至日後帶進成年後的人際關係之中。 從這個意義上說，父母就像孩子最早的道德指南針：他們在社會不得不施加更嚴厲後果之前，先幫助孩子分辨是非對錯。 因此，良好的紀律並不只是懲罰孩子；它教會孩子自制力、責任感和對他人的尊重。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"On the other hand, I believe that emotional care and safety form the foundation on which all other lessons depend. A child who feels loved, protected and listened to is far more likely to accept guidance from parents, whereas a child raised mainly through fear may obey rules only temporarily. For instance, if parents respond to mistakes with calm explanations rather than constant anger, children can learn from failure without feeling worthless. A secure home also supports mental health, confidence and curiosity, all of which are vital for long-term development. Discipline without nurture is like building walls without a roof: it may create boundaries, but it does not provide true shelter.","chinese":"另一方面，我認為情感上的照顧和安全感構成了所有其他教育所依賴的基礎。 一個感到被愛、被保護和被聆聽的孩子，更有可能接受父母的引導；相反，一個主要在恐懼中長大的孩子，可能只會暫時服從規則。 例如，如果父母在孩子犯錯時以冷靜的解釋回應，而不是持續憤怒，孩子便能從失敗中學習，而不會覺得自己毫無價值。 一個安全的家庭也能支持心理健康、自信心和好奇心，而這些都對長遠發展至關重要。 沒有關愛的紀律就像建造沒有屋頂的牆壁：它或許能建立界線，卻不能提供真正的庇護"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, parents should certainly teach their children right from wrong, as discipline helps them become responsible members of society. However, their primary duty is to nurture them and provide a safe environment, because children can only grow into balanced and moral adults when they first feel secure, valued and emotionally supported.","chinese":"總結來說，父母當然應該教孩子分辨是非，因為紀律能幫助他們成為負責任的社會成員 然而，父母的首要責任是培育孩子並提供安全的環境，因為孩子只有先感到安全、被重視和在情感上受到支持，才能成長為平衡而有道德感的成年人。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"play a decisive role in","chinese":"在……中扮演決定性角色"},{"english":"shape both","chinese":"同時塑造"},{"english":"emotional development","chinese":"情緒發展"},{"english":"mainly correct misbehaviour","chinese":"主要糾正不當行為"},{"english":"teach moral values","chinese":"教導品德價值"},{"english":"their most important duty","chinese":"他們最重要的責任"},{"english":"offer care, security and a stable home","chinese":"提供照顧、安全感和穩定家庭"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"discipline is necessary","chinese":"管教是必要的"},{"english":"nurturing children","chinese":"培育孩子"},{"english":"a safe environment","chinese":"安全環境"},{"english":"the more fundamental responsibility","chinese":"更基本的責任"},{"english":"on the one hand","chinese":"一方面"},{"english":"an essential part of parenting","chinese":"育兒的重要部分"},{"english":"be born with","chinese":"天生具備"},{"english":"a complete understanding of","chinese":"對……的完整理解"},{"english":"acceptable behaviour","chinese":"可接受的行為"},{"english":"without guidance","chinese":"沒有指導"},{"english":"struggle to respect rules","chinese":"難以尊重規則"},{"english":"control their impulses","chinese":"控制衝動"},{"english":"consider the feelings of others","chinese":"顧及他人感受"},{"english":"be corrected for","chinese":"因……而被糾正"},{"english":"lying, shouting or behaving selfishly","chinese":"說謊、大叫或行為自私"},{"english":"carry these habits into","chinese":"將這些習慣帶入"},{"english":"adult relationships","chinese":"成年後的人際關係"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"act as","chinese":"充當；發揮……作用"},{"english":"a child's first moral compass","chinese":"孩子的第一個道德指南針"},{"english":"distinguish right from wrong","chinese":"分辨是非"},{"english":"impose harsher consequences","chinese":"施加更嚴厲後果"},{"english":"good discipline","chinese":"良好管教"},{"english":"does not simply punish","chinese":"不只是懲罰"},{"english":"teach them self-control","chinese":"教導他們自制"},{"english":"responsibility and respect for others","chinese":"責任感和尊重他人"},{"english":"on the other hand","chinese":"另一方面"},{"english":"emotional care and safety","chinese":"情感關懷和安全感"},{"english":"form the foundation","chinese":"構成基礎"},{"english":"all other lessons depend","chinese":"所有其他教導都依賴"},{"english":"feel loved, protected and listened to","chinese":"感到被愛、受保護和被聆聽"},{"english":"be far more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"accept guidance from","chinese":"接受……的引導"},{"english":"be raised mainly through fear","chinese":"主要在恐懼中被養育"},{"english":"obey rules only temporarily","chinese":"只會暫時服從規則"},{"english":"respond to mistakes with","chinese":"以……回應錯誤"},{"english":"calm explanations","chinese":"平靜解釋"},{"english":"rather than constant anger","chinese":"而不是持續憤怒"},{"english":"learn from failure","chinese":"從失敗中學習"},{"english":"without feeling worthless","chinese":"而不會覺得自己毫無價值"},{"english":"a secure home","chinese":"安全穩定的家庭"},{"english":"support mental health","chinese":"支持精神健康"},{"english":"confidence and curiosity","chinese":"信心和好奇心"},{"english":"vital for long-term development","chinese":"對長遠發展至關重要"},{"english":"discipline without nurture","chinese":"沒有關愛的管教"},{"english":"building walls without a roof","chinese":"建牆卻沒有屋頂"},{"english":"create boundaries","chinese":"建立界限"},{"english":"provide true shelter","chinese":"提供真正庇護"},{"english":"teach their children right from wrong","chinese":"教導孩子分辨是非"},{"english":"responsible members of society","chinese":"負責任的社會成員"},{"english":"primary duty","chinese":"首要責任"},{"english":"provide a safe environment","chinese":"提供安全環境"},{"english":"grow into balanced and moral adults","chinese":"成長為平衡而有道德的成年人"},{"english":"feel secure, valued and emotionally supported","chinese":"感到安全、被重視和得到情感支持"}]},"model-essay-23-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-23-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:23","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-23-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q23","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Online communication has become woven into everyday life, allowing people to exchange messages, join communities and maintain relationships across distance. However, I completely disagree that this development means people will never be alone or will always be able to make new friends. Digital contact can widen access to others, but it cannot guarantee genuine companionship.","chinese":"網上溝通已經融入日常生活，使人們能夠交換訊息、加入群體，並跨越距離維持人際關係。 然而，我完全不同意這種發展意味著人們將永遠不會孤單，或永遠能夠結交新朋友。 數位接觸可以擴大人們接觸他人的機會，但它不能保證真正的陪伴。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first problem with the statement is that loneliness is not simply the absence of people around us. It is often caused by a lack of meaningful connection. A person may have hundreds of online contacts and still feel isolated if those exchanges are brief, performative or shallow. Social media, for instance, can encourage users to post polished versions of their lives rather than speak honestly about fear, disappointment or insecurity. When communication becomes a stream of likes, comments and short replies, it may create the impression of a company without providing emotional support. In this sense, online platforms can be a crowded room in which no one truly listens.","chinese":"這個說法的第一個問題是，孤單並不只是身邊沒有人。 它往往是由缺乏有意義的連結所造成的。 一個人即使擁有數百個網上聯絡人，如果那些交流只是短暫、表面化或膚淺的，他仍然可能感到孤立。 例如，社交媒體可能鼓勵用戶發布經過美化的人生版本，而不是誠實地談論恐懼、失望或不安全感。 當溝通變成一連串的讚好、留言和簡短回覆時，它可能營造出有人陪伴的感覺，卻沒有提供真正的情感支持。 從這個意義上說，網上平台可以像一個擠滿人的房間，但其中沒有任何人真正聆聽。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that making friends online still depends on social confidence, trust and shared effort. The internet may open the door, but people must still walk through it. Shy teenagers, elderly users or people who have previously experienced online bullying may find digital interaction stressful rather than liberating. Moreover, online spaces are not always safe or sincere; fake identities, hostile comments and scams can make users cautious about forming new relationships. Even in positive environments, friendships require time, honesty and mutual care, which cannot be produced automatically by technology.","chinese":"另一個原因是，在網上交朋友仍然取決於社交自信、信任和共同努力。 互聯網也許能打開一扇門，但人們仍然必須自己走進去。 害羞的青少年、年長用戶，或曾經遭受網絡欺凌的人，可能會覺得數位互動帶來壓力，而不是帶來解放感。 此外，網上空間並不總是安全或真誠的；虛假身份、敵意留言和騙局都可能令用戶在建立新關係時變得謹慎。 即使在正面環境中，友誼也需要時間、誠實和彼此關心，而這些都不能由科技自動產"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, online communication has made it easier to reach others, but it has not removed loneliness and it cannot promise friendship for everyone. Human connection is built through depth, trust and consistency, not merely through constant access to a screen.","chinese":"總結來說，網上溝通使人們更容易接觸他人，但它並沒有消除孤單，也不能向每個人承諾友誼。 人與人之間的連結是透過深度、信任和持續相處建立的，而不只是透過持續接觸螢幕而形成的。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"online communication","chinese":"網上溝通"},{"english":"become woven into","chinese":"融入……之中"},{"english":"everyday life","chinese":"日常生活"},{"english":"exchange messages","chinese":"交換訊息"},{"english":"join communities","chinese":"加入社群"},{"english":"maintain relationships across distance","chinese":"跨越距離維繫關係"},{"english":"this development means","chinese":"這種發展意味着"},{"english":"never be alone","chinese":"永遠不會孤單"},{"english":"make new friends","chinese":"結交新朋友"},{"english":"digital contact","chinese":"數碼接觸"},{"english":"widen access to","chinese":"擴大接觸……的機會"},{"english":"guarantee genuine companionship","chinese":"保證真正的陪伴"},{"english":"genuine companionship","chinese":"真正的陪伴"},{"english":"the first problem with","chinese":"……的第一個問題"},{"english":"loneliness","chinese":"孤獨；孤獨感"},{"english":"absence of","chinese":"缺乏……"},{"english":"people around us","chinese":"身邊的人"},{"english":"be caused by","chinese":"由……造成"},{"english":"meaningful connection","chinese":"有意義的連繫"},{"english":"online contacts","chinese":"網上聯絡人"},{"english":"feel isolated","chinese":"感到孤立"},{"english":"brief, performative or shallow","chinese":"簡短、表演式或膚淺"},{"english":"social media","chinese":"社交媒體"},{"english":"encourage users to","chinese":"鼓勵用戶去……"},{"english":"polished versions of their lives","chinese":"經修飾的生活版本"},{"english":"rather than speak honestly about","chinese":"而不是坦誠談論……"},{"english":"disappointment","chinese":"失望"},{"english":"insecurity","chinese":"不安全感"},{"english":"a stream of","chinese":"一連串……"},{"english":"likes, comments and short replies","chinese":"讚好、留言和簡短回覆"},{"english":"create the impression of","chinese":"造成……的印象"},{"english":"company","chinese":"陪伴"},{"english":"emotional support","chinese":"情感支援"},{"english":"online platforms","chinese":"網上平台"},{"english":"crowded room","chinese":"擠滿人的房間"},{"english":"truly listens","chinese":"真正聆聽"},{"english":"making friends online","chinese":"在網上交朋友"},{"english":"depends on","chinese":"取決於"},{"english":"social confidence","chinese":"社交自信"},{"english":"shared effort","chinese":"共同努力"},{"english":"open the door","chinese":"打開大門；創造機會"},{"english":"walk through it","chinese":"走進去；把握機會"},{"english":"shy teenagers","chinese":"害羞的青少年"},{"english":"elderly users","chinese":"年長用戶"},{"english":"previously experienced","chinese":"之前經歷過"},{"english":"online bullying","chinese":"網上欺凌"},{"english":"digital interaction","chinese":"數碼互動"},{"english":"stressful rather than liberating","chinese":"有壓力而不是令人解放"},{"english":"online spaces","chinese":"網上空間"},{"english":"safe or sincere","chinese":"安全或真誠"},{"english":"fake identities","chinese":"虛假身份"},{"english":"hostile comments","chinese":"敵意留言"},{"english":"scams","chinese":"騙案"},{"english":"cautious about","chinese":"對……保持謹慎"},{"english":"forming new relationships","chinese":"建立新關係"},{"english":"positive environments","chinese":"正面的環境"},{"english":"mutual care","chinese":"互相關心"},{"english":"be produced automatically by","chinese":"由……自動產生"},{"english":"removed loneliness","chinese":"消除孤獨感"},{"english":"promise friendship for everyone","chinese":"保證每個人都能得到友誼"},{"english":"human connection","chinese":"人與人之間的連繫"},{"english":"be built through","chinese":"透過……建立"},{"english":"depth, trust and consistency","chinese":"深度、信任和持續性"},{"english":"not merely through","chinese":"不只是透過……"},{"english":"constant access to a screen","chinese":"隨時接觸螢幕"}]},"model-essay-24-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-24-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:24","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-24-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q24","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"International air travel, once a luxury enjoyed by a small minority, has become a routine feature of modern life. While this trend has brought undeniable social and economic benefits, I take the firm view that these gains are outweighed by the damage it causes to the natural environment. The advantages are real, but the ecological costs are wider in scale and far more difficult to reverse.","chinese":"國際航空旅行曾經只是少數人才能享受的奢侈活動，如今卻已成為現代生活中的日常現象。 雖然這一趨勢帶來了無可否認的社會與經濟利益， 我堅定認為，這些好處仍然被它對自然環境所造成的破壞所超越。 這些優勢確實存在，但其生態代價影響範圍更廣，而且更難以逆轉。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"On the one hand, the rise in regular international flights has created several important benefits. First, it has stimulated tourism and cross-border business. When people are able to travel quickly and relatively cheaply, more visitors spend money on accommodation, food and local transport, which then supports employment and generates tax revenue. In many island nations and coastal cities, for example, large numbers of jobs depend directly on overseas travellers. Second, frequent flights have made global mobility far easier for students and professionals. This means that people can study abroad, attend international conferences and develop commercial partnerships, all of which promote the exchange of skills, knowledge and investment. A student who trains overseas and later returns home, for instance, may contribute valuable expertise to local industries.","chinese":"一方面，定期國際航班的增加確實帶來了幾項重要的好處。 首先，它促進了旅遊業以及跨境商業活動的發展。 當人們能夠以較快且相對便宜的方式出行時，便會有更多旅客在住宿、餐飲和本地交通方面消費，進而支持就業並帶來稅收收入。 例如，在許多島國和沿海城市，大量職位都直接依賴海外旅客。 其次，頻繁的航班使學生和專業人士的全球流動變得容易得多。 這意味著人們能夠到海外留學、參加國際會議以及建立商業合作關係，而這些都能促進技能、知識與投資的交流。 例如，一名在海外接受培訓後回國的學生，可能會為本地產業帶來寶貴的專業知識。 因此，國際航班的擴張顯然能促進經濟活動、人員流動以及全球交流。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Even so, the environmental disadvantages are more serious. The clearest problem is that air travel is highly carbon-intensive. Every flight burns substantial quantities of aviation fuel, releasing carbon dioxide and other pollutants into the atmosphere; when this is repeated across millions of journeys, it accelerates climate change and worsens environmental instability. A single holiday flight may seem insignificant, but the cumulative effect of countless such trips is enormous. Furthermore, the expansion of air travel creates additional environmental pressure on the ground. More passengers require larger airports, more roads and more tourist infrastructure, which consume land, produce waste and place strain on fragile ecosystems. In popular coastal destinations, for example, rising visitor numbers often lead to habitat loss, litter and resource depletion.","chinese":"即便如此，環境方面的缺點更加嚴重。 最明顯的問題是，航空旅行屬於高度碳密集型活動。 每一趟航班都會燃燒大量航空燃料，向大氣中排放二氧化碳及其他污染物；當這種情況在數以百萬計的旅程中反覆出現時，便會加速氣候變化並惡化環境的不穩定性。 單一次度假航班看似微不足道，但無數類似旅程累積起來的影響卻極其巨大。 此外，航空旅行的擴張還會在地面層面造成額外的環境壓力。 更多旅客意味著需要更大的機場、更多道路以及更多旅遊基礎設施，而這些都會消耗土地、製造廢物，並對脆弱的生態系統造成壓力。 例如，在受歡迎的海岸旅遊地區，遊客數量上升往往會導致棲息地流失、垃圾增加以及資源耗竭。 因此，頻繁飛行所造成的環境危害並不僅限於排放問題，而是進一步擴展至更廣泛的生態破壞。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, regular international flights clearly promote prosperity, mobility and global connection. Nevertheless, because they significantly increase emissions and intensify wider ecological damage, their disadvantages to the environment outweigh their advantages. For this reason, the growth of international air travel should be regarded as a negative development overall.","chinese":"總結而言，定期國際航班的確促進了繁榮、人員流動以及全球連結。 然而，由於它們大幅增加排放，並加劇更廣泛的生態破壞，因此其對環境造成的缺點大於其帶來的好處。 基於這一原因，國際航空旅行的增長整體上應被視為一種負面發展。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"international air travel","chinese":"國際航空旅遊"},{"english":"once a luxury enjoyed by a small minority","chinese":"曾經是少數人享有的奢侈品"},{"english":"a routine feature of","chinese":"……的日常特徵"},{"english":"modern life","chinese":"現代生活"},{"english":"this trend","chinese":"這個趨勢"},{"english":"undeniable social and economic benefits","chinese":"不可否認的社會和經濟好處"},{"english":"take the firm view that","chinese":"堅定認為"},{"english":"these gains are outweighed by","chinese":"這些好處不及……；被……抵消"},{"english":"the natural environment","chinese":"自然環境"},{"english":"ecological costs","chinese":"生態代價"},{"english":"wider in scale","chinese":"規模更廣"},{"english":"difficult to reverse","chinese":"難以逆轉"},{"english":"on the one hand","chinese":"一方面"},{"english":"the rise in","chinese":"……的增加"},{"english":"regular international flights","chinese":"定期國際航班"},{"english":"stimulated tourism","chinese":"刺激旅遊業"},{"english":"cross-border business","chinese":"跨境商業"},{"english":"relatively cheaply","chinese":"相對便宜地"},{"english":"spend money on","chinese":"花錢在……上"},{"english":"accommodation","chinese":"住宿"},{"english":"local transport","chinese":"本地交通"},{"english":"supports employment","chinese":"支持就業"},{"english":"generates tax revenue","chinese":"產生稅收"},{"english":"island nations","chinese":"島國"},{"english":"coastal cities","chinese":"沿海城市"},{"english":"large numbers of jobs","chinese":"大量工作職位"},{"english":"depend directly on","chinese":"直接依賴"},{"english":"overseas travellers","chinese":"海外旅客"},{"english":"frequent flights","chinese":"頻繁航班"},{"english":"global mobility","chinese":"全球流動性"},{"english":"study abroad","chinese":"出國留學"},{"english":"attend international conferences","chinese":"參加國際會議"},{"english":"commercial partnerships","chinese":"商業合作關係"},{"english":"promote the exchange of","chinese":"促進……的交流"},{"english":"skills, knowledge and investment","chinese":"技能、知識和投資"},{"english":"trains overseas","chinese":"在海外接受培訓"},{"english":"returns home","chinese":"回到本地；回國"},{"english":"contribute valuable expertise to","chinese":"為……貢獻寶貴專業知識"},{"english":"local industries","chinese":"本地產業"},{"english":"even so","chinese":"即使如此"},{"english":"environmental disadvantages","chinese":"環境方面的缺點"},{"english":"the clearest problem","chinese":"最明顯的問題"},{"english":"highly carbon-intensive","chinese":"碳排放密集的"},{"english":"burns substantial quantities of","chinese":"消耗大量"},{"english":"aviation fuel","chinese":"航空燃油"},{"english":"releasing carbon dioxide","chinese":"釋放二氧化碳"},{"english":"other pollutants","chinese":"其他污染物"},{"english":"into the atmosphere","chinese":"進入大氣層"},{"english":"repeated across millions of journeys","chinese":"在數以百萬計的旅程中重複出現"},{"english":"accelerates climate change","chinese":"加速氣候變化"},{"english":"worsens environmental instability","chinese":"加劇環境不穩定"},{"english":"a single holiday flight","chinese":"一次假期航班"},{"english":"may seem insignificant","chinese":"可能看似微不足道"},{"english":"the cumulative effect of","chinese":"……的累積影響"},{"english":"countless such trips","chinese":"無數這類旅程"},{"english":"furthermore","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"the expansion of air travel","chinese":"航空旅遊的擴張"},{"english":"additional environmental pressure","chinese":"額外環境壓力"},{"english":"on the ground","chinese":"在地面上"},{"english":"larger airports","chinese":"更大型機場"},{"english":"tourist infrastructure","chinese":"旅遊基礎設施"},{"english":"consume land","chinese":"消耗土地"},{"english":"produce waste","chinese":"製造廢物"},{"english":"place strain on","chinese":"對……造成壓力"},{"english":"fragile ecosystems","chinese":"脆弱的生態系統"},{"english":"popular coastal destinations","chinese":"受歡迎的沿海目的地"},{"english":"rising visitor numbers","chinese":"不斷上升的遊客人數"},{"english":"lead to habitat loss","chinese":"導致棲息地喪失"},{"english":"litter","chinese":"垃圾"},{"english":"resource depletion","chinese":"資源耗盡"},{"english":"promote prosperity","chinese":"促進繁榮"},{"english":"global connection","chinese":"全球聯繫"},{"english":"significantly increase emissions","chinese":"大幅增加排放"},{"english":"intensify wider ecological damage","chinese":"加劇更廣泛的生態破壞"},{"english":"disadvantages to the environment","chinese":"對環境的缺點"},{"english":"outweigh their advantages","chinese":"超過其好處"},{"english":"should be regarded as","chinese":"應被視為"},{"english":"a negative development overall","chinese":"整體而言是負面發展"}]},"model-essay-24-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-24-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:24","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-24-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q24","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Childhood obesity has become a serious public health concern in many countries. While some argue that governments should be blamed for this trend, others believe that parents are mainly responsible. In my view, although parents play an important role in shaping children’s daily habits, the government bears greater responsibility because it controls the wider food and social environment in which families make their choices.","chinese":"兒童肥胖在許多國家已經成為一個嚴重的公共健康問題。 雖然有些人認為政府應該為這種趨勢受到指責，但另一些人則相信父母才是主要責任方 在我看來，儘管父母在塑造兒童日常習慣方面扮演重要角色，但政府承擔更大的責任，因為它掌控著家庭作出選擇時所處的更廣泛飲食和社會環境。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Those who blame parents have a reasonable argument. Children rarely buy groceries, cook meals, or decide their daily routines entirely on their own, so parents strongly influence what they eat and how active they are. If mothers and fathers regularly serve fast food, allow excessive screen time, and fail to encourage exercise, children are likely to develop unhealthy habits from an early age. For example, a child who spends every evening watching videos while eating sugary snacks may gradually see this lifestyle as normal. In this sense, parents are the first line of defence against obesity because they control the home environment.","chinese":"那些責怪父母的人有一個合理的論點。 兒童很少會完全自己購買食材、烹調食物，或決定自己的日常作息，因此父母會強烈影響他們吃甚麼以及有多活躍。 如果父母經常提供快餐、容許過多螢幕時間，並且未能鼓勵運動，兒童很可能從小便養成不健康的習慣。 例如，一個每天晚上邊看影片邊吃含糖零食的孩子，可能會逐漸把這生活方式視為正常 從這個意義上說，父母是對抗肥胖的第一道防線，因為他們掌控著家庭環境。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, I believe governments are more responsible because they shape the conditions that make unhealthy choices so common. Many children are surrounded by aggressive advertising for junk food, cheap processed meals, and neighbourhoods where safe outdoor play is limited. These are not problems that individual parents can easily solve. Governments can restrict unhealthy food marketing, improve school meals, require clearer nutrition labels, and build parks or sports facilities. If public policy makes unhealthy food cheap, visible, and convenient, while healthy options remain expensive or inaccessible, parents are fighting an uphill battle.","chinese":"然而，我認為政府更有責任，因為它們塑造了使不健康選擇變得如此普遍的條件。 許多兒童被垃圾食品的強勢廣告、廉價加工食品，以及安全戶外玩樂空間有限的社區所包圍。 這些並不是個別父母能夠輕易解決的問題。 政府可以限制不健康食品的市場推廣、改善學校膳食、要求更清晰的營養標籤，並興建公園或體育設施。 如果公共政策使不健康食品變得廉價、顯眼和方便，而健康選擇仍然昂貴或難以取得，那麼父母就是在打一場艱難的仗。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, parents certainly influence children’s eating and exercise habits, but the stronger responsibility lies with the government. Families can guide children at home, yet only governments can regulate food companies, improve public spaces, and create a healthier environment for all children. Therefore, childhood obesity should be seen primarily as a failure of public policy rather than simply poor parenting.","chinese":"總結來說，父母固然會影響兒童的飲食和運動習慣，但更大的責任在於政府。 家庭可以在家中引導兒童，但只有政府能夠規管食品公司、改善公共空間，並為所有兒童創造一個更健康的環境。 因此，兒童肥胖應主要被視為公共政策的失敗，而不僅僅是父母教養不善的結果。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"childhood obesity","chinese":"兒童肥胖"},{"english":"a serious public health concern","chinese":"嚴重公共衞生問題"},{"english":"be blamed for","chinese":"因……被責怪"},{"english":"this trend","chinese":"這個趨勢"},{"english":"mainly responsible","chinese":"負主要責任"},{"english":"play an important role in","chinese":"在……中扮演重要角色"},{"english":"shape children's daily habits","chinese":"塑造兒童的日常習慣"},{"english":"bear greater responsibility","chinese":"承擔更大責任"},{"english":"the wider food and social environment","chinese":"更廣泛的食物及社會環境"},{"english":"make their choices","chinese":"作出選擇"},{"english":"blame parents","chinese":"責怪父母"},{"english":"a reasonable argument","chinese":"合理論點"},{"english":"buy groceries","chinese":"買日常食材"},{"english":"cook meals","chinese":"煮飯"},{"english":"decide their daily routines","chinese":"決定自己的日常作息"},{"english":"entirely on their own","chinese":"完全靠自己"},{"english":"strongly influence","chinese":"強烈影響"},{"english":"how active they are","chinese":"他們有多活躍"},{"english":"regularly serve fast food","chinese":"經常提供快餐"},{"english":"excessive screen time","chinese":"過量螢幕時間"},{"english":"fail to encourage exercise","chinese":"未能鼓勵運動"},{"english":"develop unhealthy habits","chinese":"養成不健康習慣"},{"english":"from an early age","chinese":"從小"},{"english":"spend every evening watching videos","chinese":"每晚花時間看影片"},{"english":"sugary snacks","chinese":"高糖零食"},{"english":"gradually see this lifestyle as normal","chinese":"逐漸視這種生活方式為正常"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"the first line of defence against","chinese":"對抗……的第一道防線"},{"english":"control the home environment","chinese":"控制家庭環境"},{"english":"more responsible","chinese":"責任更大"},{"english":"shape the conditions that","chinese":"塑造令……的條件"},{"english":"unhealthy choices","chinese":"不健康選擇"},{"english":"so common","chinese":"如此普遍"},{"english":"be surrounded by","chinese":"被……包圍"},{"english":"aggressive advertising","chinese":"進取的廣告宣傳"},{"english":"junk food","chinese":"垃圾食物"},{"english":"cheap processed meals","chinese":"廉價加工餐食"},{"english":"safe outdoor play","chinese":"安全的戶外玩耍"},{"english":"be limited","chinese":"受到限制"},{"english":"individual parents","chinese":"個別父母"},{"english":"easily solve","chinese":"輕易解決"},{"english":"restrict unhealthy food marketing","chinese":"限制不健康食品推廣"},{"english":"improve school meals","chinese":"改善學校膳食"},{"english":"require clearer nutrition labels","chinese":"要求更清晰的營養標籤"},{"english":"nutrition labels","chinese":"營養標籤"},{"english":"build parks or sports facilities","chinese":"興建公園或運動設施"},{"english":"public policy","chinese":"公共政策"},{"english":"cheap, visible, and convenient","chinese":"便宜、顯眼和方便"},{"english":"healthy options","chinese":"健康選擇"},{"english":"remain expensive or inaccessible","chinese":"仍然昂貴或難以取得"},{"english":"fight an uphill battle","chinese":"打一場艱難仗"},{"english":"eating and exercise habits","chinese":"飲食和運動習慣"},{"english":"the stronger responsibility lies with","chinese":"更大的責任在於"},{"english":"guide children at home","chinese":"在家中引導兒童"},{"english":"regulate food companies","chinese":"規管食品公司"},{"english":"improve public spaces","chinese":"改善公共空間"},{"english":"create a healthier environment for","chinese":"為……創造更健康的環境"},{"english":"be seen primarily as","chinese":"應主要被視為"},{"english":"a failure of public policy","chinese":"公共政策的失敗"},{"english":"rather than simply poor parenting","chinese":"而不只是管教不善"}]},"model-essay-24-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-24-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:24","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-24-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q24","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"It is often argued that the brief and simplified style of text messages and instant online conversations will eventually destroy people’s ability to use grammar and spelling correctly. I disagree with this view because informal digital language is mainly a matter of context, and modern communication can actually strengthen people’s awareness of written language.","chinese":"人們經常認為，文字訊息和即時網上對話那種簡短而簡化的風格，最終會破壞人們正確使用文法和拼字的能力。 我不同意這個觀點，因為非正式的數碼語言主要是語境問題，而現代溝通實際上可以加強人們對書面語言的意識。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that short online messages are not meant to follow the same conventions as academic essays, business letters, or official documents. When people type “u” instead of “you” or leave out punctuation in a quick message to a friend, they are usually choosing speed and convenience, not showing that they have forgotten standard English. This is similar to the way people speak differently at home and in a job interview. A student may write casually in a group chat, but the same student can still use full sentences, correct spelling, and formal vocabulary in an examination. In this sense, texting is not the death of grammar; it is simply another register of communication.","chinese":"第一個原因是，簡短的網上訊息本來就不是為了遵循學術文章、商業信件或正式文件的相同規範。 當人們在給朋友的快速訊息中輸入“u”而不是“you”，或者省略標點符號時，他們通常只是選擇速度和便利，而不是顯示他們已經忘記了標準英語。 這就類似於人們在家中和在工作面試中會用不同方式說話。 一名學生可能會在群組聊天中隨意書寫，但同一名學生仍然可以在考試中使用完整句子、正確拼字和正式詞彙。 從這個意義上說，發短訊並不是文法的死亡；它只不過是另一種溝通語域。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important point is that digital communication has made writing a more regular part of daily life. Many people now compose emails, online comments, captions, messages, and work updates every day, so they are exposed to written language far more often than previous generations were. Admittedly, some online writing is careless, but poor habits are corrected by school, professional expectations, grammar-checking tools, and the need to be taken seriously in public or workplace settings. For example, an employee may use abbreviations with friends, yet still check spelling carefully before sending a proposal to a client. The pressure to communicate clearly has not disappeared; if anything, it has become more visible.","chinese":"另一個重要觀點是，數碼溝通已經使寫作成為日常生活中更常見的一部分。 現在許多人每天都會撰寫電郵、網上評論、圖片說明、訊息和工作更新，因此他們接觸書面語言的頻率遠高於以往世代。 誠然，有些網上寫作是粗心的，但不良習慣會被學校教育、專業期望、文法檢查工具，以及在公共或職場場合中被認真看待的需要所糾正。 例如，一名員工可能會和朋友使用縮寫，但在向客戶發送建議書之前，仍然會仔細檢查拼字。 清楚溝通的壓力並沒有消失；相反，它變得更加明顯。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I do not believe that instant online communication will destroy grammar and spelling. Although texting encourages a shorter and simpler style, people can still adjust their language according to purpose and audience. Grammar is not dying; it is being used more flexibly.","chinese":"總結來說，我不認為即時網上溝通會破壞文法和拼字。 儘管發短訊會鼓勵一種較短和較簡單的風格，人們仍然可以根據目的和受眾調整自己的語言。 文法並沒有死亡；它只是被更靈活地使用。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"it is often argued that","chinese":"人們經常認為……"},{"english":"brief and simplified style","chinese":"簡短和簡化的風格"},{"english":"text messages","chinese":"文字訊息"},{"english":"instant online conversations","chinese":"即時網上對話"},{"english":"eventually destroy","chinese":"最終破壞"},{"english":"ability to use","chinese":"使用……的能力"},{"english":"grammar and spelling","chinese":"文法和串字"},{"english":"correctly","chinese":"正確地"},{"english":"informal digital language","chinese":"非正式數碼語言"},{"english":"a matter of context","chinese":"視乎語境的問題"},{"english":"modern communication","chinese":"現代溝通"},{"english":"strengthen people's awareness of","chinese":"加強人們對……的意識"},{"english":"written language","chinese":"書面語言"},{"english":"short online messages","chinese":"簡短網上訊息"},{"english":"be meant to","chinese":"旨在；本來要"},{"english":"follow the same conventions as","chinese":"遵循與……相同的慣例"},{"english":"academic essays","chinese":"學術文章"},{"english":"business letters","chinese":"商業信件"},{"english":"official documents","chinese":"官方文件"},{"english":"leave out punctuation","chinese":"省略標點符號"},{"english":"choosing speed and convenience","chinese":"選擇速度和方便"},{"english":"standard English","chinese":"標準英語"},{"english":"similar to","chinese":"與……相似"},{"english":"speak differently","chinese":"以不同方式說話"},{"english":"job interview","chinese":"求職面試"},{"english":"write casually","chinese":"隨意地寫"},{"english":"group chat","chinese":"群組聊天"},{"english":"full sentences","chinese":"完整句子"},{"english":"correct spelling","chinese":"正確串字"},{"english":"formal vocabulary","chinese":"正式詞彙"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"the death of grammar","chinese":"文法的死亡"},{"english":"another register of communication","chinese":"另一種溝通語域"},{"english":"digital communication","chinese":"數碼溝通"},{"english":"a more regular part of daily life","chinese":"日常生活中更恆常的一部分"},{"english":"compose emails","chinese":"撰寫電郵"},{"english":"online comments","chinese":"網上留言"},{"english":"captions","chinese":"圖片或影片說明文字"},{"english":"work updates","chinese":"工作進度更新"},{"english":"be exposed to","chinese":"接觸到……"},{"english":"far more often than","chinese":"比……頻密得多"},{"english":"previous generations","chinese":"以往幾代人"},{"english":"admittedly","chinese":"誠然"},{"english":"careless","chinese":"粗心；不嚴謹"},{"english":"poor habits","chinese":"不良習慣"},{"english":"be corrected by","chinese":"被……糾正"},{"english":"professional expectations","chinese":"專業期望"},{"english":"grammar-checking tools","chinese":"文法檢查工具"},{"english":"taken seriously","chinese":"被認真看待"},{"english":"workplace settings","chinese":"職場環境"},{"english":"abbreviations","chinese":"縮寫"},{"english":"proposal","chinese":"建議書"},{"english":"client","chinese":"客戶"},{"english":"pressure to communicate clearly","chinese":"清晰溝通的壓力"},{"english":"has not disappeared","chinese":"並沒有消失"},{"english":"if anything","chinese":"甚至可以說"},{"english":"become more visible","chinese":"變得更明顯"},{"english":"instant online communication","chinese":"即時網上溝通"},{"english":"encourages a shorter and simpler style","chinese":"鼓勵更短和更簡單的風格"},{"english":"adjust their language","chinese":"調整自己的語言"},{"english":"according to","chinese":"根據"},{"english":"purpose and audience","chinese":"目的和受眾"},{"english":"grammar is not dying","chinese":"文法並沒有死亡"},{"english":"being used more flexibly","chinese":"被更靈活地使用"}]},"model-essay-25-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-25-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:25","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-25-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q25","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many countries, once people obtain a driving licence, they can continue driving for years without being formally reassessed. Some therefore argue that motorists should be required to retake their driving test every five years. This policy would bring certain clear benefits, although it would also create practical difficulties.","chinese":"在許多國家，一旦人們取得駕駛執照，他們之後多年都可以繼續駕駛，而無須再接受正式評估。 因此，有些人認為，駕駛者應該被規定每五年重新參加一次駕駛考試。 這項政策會帶來一些明顯的好處，但同時也會造成實際上的困難。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One obvious advantage is that repeated testing could improve road safety by ensuring that drivers still meet an acceptable standard. Over time, people often develop bad habits such as failing to check mirrors properly, signalling too late, or becoming careless at junctions. A compulsory retest would force them to correct these habits before they caused accidents. In addition, such a system would help authorities ensure that drivers remain familiar with current traffic laws. Road rules do not stand still, and many motorists who passed their test decades ago may be unaware of newer regulations on speed limits, mobile phone use, or cyclist protection. A periodic assessment could therefore act as both a safety net and a refresher.","chinese":"一個明顯的優點是，重複測試可以確保駕駛者仍然達到可接受的標準，從而提升道路安全 隨著時間過去，人們往往會養成壞習慣，例如沒有正確查看倒後鏡、打方向燈太遲，或者在路口變得粗心。 強制性的重考會迫使他們在這些習慣引發交通意外之前作出糾正。 此外，這樣的制度也能幫助當局確保駕駛者仍然熟悉現行交通法規。 交通規則並不是一成不變的，而許多在數十年前通過考試的駕駛者，可能並不知道有關車速限制、使用手機或保護單車使用者的新規定。 因此，定期評估既可以成為一道安全保障，也可以起到重新溫習和更新知識的作用。 總體而言，定期重考可以令道路更安全，並讓駕駛者跟上現代法規的更新。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, the drawbacks are equally significant. First, making every driver retake the test every five years would place a heavy burden on testing centres and examiners. In densely populated areas, the number of licence holders is so large that waiting times could become unmanageable, which would frustrate the public and stretch government resources. Second, this policy could unfairly affect competent drivers with long records of safe driving. Someone who has driven responsibly for twenty years may still fail because of nerves on the day rather than genuine incompetence. In that case, the system would punish anxiety instead of improving safety.","chinese":"然而，這項做法的缺點同樣相當明顯。 首先，要求每位駕駛者每五年重考一次，會對考試中心和考官造成沉重負擔。 在人口稠密的地區，持牌駕駛者的人數十分龐大，等候時間可能會變得難以控制，這不但會令公眾感到不滿，也會令政府資源承受壓力。 第二，這項政策可能會對那些長期安全駕駛、實際上很有能力的駕駛者造成不公平影響。 一個已經負責任地駕駛了二十年的人，仍然有可能只是因為當天緊張而未能通過考試，而不是因為真正缺乏駕駛能力。 在那種情況下，這個制度懲罰的其實是緊張情緒，而不是真正提升道路安全。 基於這些原因，強制重考可能會造成嚴重的行政問題，並為某些駕駛者帶來不公平的結果。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In summary, requiring people to retake their driving test every five years could raise driving standards and update drivers’ knowledge, but it could also create serious administrative pressure and unfair outcomes for some motorists.","chinese":"總結來說，要求人們每五年重新參加一次駕駛考試，可以提升駕駛水平，並更新駕駛者的知識。 與此同時，它也可能帶來嚴重的行政壓力，並對某些駕駛者造成不公平的結果。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"obtain a driving licence","chinese":"取得駕駛執照"},{"english":"continue driving for years","chinese":"繼續駕駛多年"},{"english":"without being formally reassessed","chinese":"沒有被正式重新評估"},{"english":"motorists","chinese":"駕駛者"},{"english":"be required to","chinese":"被要求去……"},{"english":"retake their driving test","chinese":"重考駕駛考試"},{"english":"every five years","chinese":"每五年"},{"english":"clear benefits","chinese":"明顯好處"},{"english":"practical difficulties","chinese":"實際困難"},{"english":"one obvious advantage","chinese":"一個明顯優點"},{"english":"repeated testing","chinese":"重複考核"},{"english":"improve road safety","chinese":"改善道路安全"},{"english":"ensuring that","chinese":"確保……"},{"english":"meet an acceptable standard","chinese":"達到可接受水平"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨時間"},{"english":"develop bad habits","chinese":"養成壞習慣"},{"english":"failing to check mirrors properly","chinese":"未有正確查看倒後鏡"},{"english":"signalling too late","chinese":"太遲打燈"},{"english":"becoming careless at junctions","chinese":"在路口變得粗心"},{"english":"compulsory retest","chinese":"強制重考"},{"english":"force them to correct these habits","chinese":"迫使他們改正這些習慣"},{"english":"before they caused accidents","chinese":"在它們造成意外之前"},{"english":"such a system","chinese":"這樣的制度"},{"english":"authorities","chinese":"當局"},{"english":"remain familiar with","chinese":"仍然熟悉……"},{"english":"current traffic laws","chinese":"現行交通法例"},{"english":"do not stand still","chinese":"不會停滯不變"},{"english":"passed their test decades ago","chinese":"數十年前考獲駕駛資格"},{"english":"be unaware of newer regulations","chinese":"不知道較新的規例"},{"english":"newer regulations on","chinese":"關於……的較新規例"},{"english":"speed limits","chinese":"速度限制"},{"english":"mobile phone use","chinese":"使用手機"},{"english":"cyclist protection","chinese":"單車使用者保護"},{"english":"periodic assessment","chinese":"定期評估"},{"english":"act as both","chinese":"同時起……作用"},{"english":"a safety net","chinese":"安全保障"},{"english":"a refresher","chinese":"溫故知新的複習"},{"english":"the drawbacks are equally significant","chinese":"缺點同樣重大"},{"english":"place a heavy burden on","chinese":"對……造成沉重負擔"},{"english":"testing centres","chinese":"考試中心"},{"english":"examiners","chinese":"考牌主任；考官"},{"english":"densely populated areas","chinese":"人口稠密地區"},{"english":"licence holders","chinese":"持牌人"},{"english":"waiting times","chinese":"等候時間"},{"english":"become unmanageable","chinese":"變得難以管理；難以處理"},{"english":"frustrate the public","chinese":"令公眾感到不滿"},{"english":"stretch government resources","chinese":"令政府資源緊張"},{"english":"unfairly affect competent drivers","chinese":"不公平地影響合格稱職的駕駛者"},{"english":"competent drivers","chinese":"合格稱職的駕駛者"},{"english":"long records of safe driving","chinese":"長期安全駕駛紀錄"},{"english":"driven responsibly","chinese":"負責任地駕駛"},{"english":"because of nerves on the day","chinese":"因考試當日緊張"},{"english":"genuine incompetence","chinese":"真正能力不足"},{"english":"punish anxiety instead of","chinese":"懲罰焦慮而不是……"},{"english":"improving safety","chinese":"改善安全"},{"english":"in summary","chinese":"總括而言"},{"english":"requiring people to retake","chinese":"要求人們重考"},{"english":"raise driving standards","chinese":"提高駕駛水平"},{"english":"update drivers' knowledge","chinese":"更新駕駛者的知識"},{"english":"serious administrative pressure","chinese":"嚴重行政壓力"},{"english":"unfair outcomes","chinese":"不公平結果"}]},"model-essay-25-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-25-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:25","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-25-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q25","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Across many modern societies, both mothers and fathers now work full time, so children receive fewer hours of direct parental attention than earlier generations did. The main reason is economic pressure, and this can weaken family bonds and reduce the guidance children receive while they are growing up.","chinese":"在許多現代社會中，母親和父親現在都全職工作，因此與早期世代相比，孩子獲得父母直接關注的時間更少。 主要原因是經濟壓力，而這可能削弱家庭關係，並減少孩子在成長過程中所獲得的引導"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The clearest reason is that one salary is often no longer enough to support a family comfortably. Housing, transport, food, childcare and education are expensive, so many parents feel they must remain in paid employment just to keep the household stable. In this sense, work is not simply a personal ambition; it is a financial lifeline. Because of this, parents often leave home early, return late, and depend on grandparents, nurseries or electronic devices to occupy their children.","chinese":"最明顯的原因是，一份薪金通常已不再足以讓一個家庭舒適地生活。 住房、交通、食物、childcare和教育都十分昂貴，因此許多父母覺得自己必須繼續受薪工作，才能維持家庭穩定。 從這個意義上說，工作不僅僅是個人抱負；它是一條經濟上的生命線。 正因如此，父母往往很早離家、很晚回家，並依靠祖父母、幼兒園或電子設備來讓孩子有事可做。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"One serious problem is emotional distance. Children need more than material comfort: they need small, regular moments of attention, such as family meals, bedtime conversations and help with homework. These routines may look ordinary, but they are the glue that holds relationships together. If they disappear, children may feel less valued or less secure, even when their parents love them deeply. Over time, this can reduce their confidence and make them less willing to discuss fears, mistakes or personal difficulties.","chinese":"其中一個嚴重問題是情感距離。 孩子需要的不只是物質上的舒適：他們需要細小而固定的關注時刻，例如家庭用餐、睡前對話，以及功課上的幫助。 這些日常習慣看起來或許很普通，但它們正是維繫關係的黏合劑。 如果這些習慣消失，即使父母深愛孩子，孩子也可能感到自己較不被重視，或較沒有安全感。 長遠而言，這可能削弱他們的自信，並使他們較不願意討論恐懼、錯誤或個人困難。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 3","english":"Another problem is weaker supervision. When parents are rarely available, children may turn to classmates, social media or online entertainment for advice and approval. For example, a teenager who spends hours online without adult guidance may copy unhealthy habits or absorb harmful values before anyone notices. Even responsible children can struggle to build discipline and self-control if no adult is consistently present to model those qualities.","chinese":"另一個問題是監管較弱。 當父母很少能陪伴在旁時，孩子可能會轉向同學、社交媒體或網上娛樂，以尋求建議和認同。 例如，一個在沒有成年人引導下花數小時上網的青少年，可能會在任何人察覺之前模仿不健康的習慣，或吸收有害的價值觀。 即使是負責任的孩子，如果沒有成年人持續在場示範這些品質，也可能難以建立紀律和自制力。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, children spend less time with their parents mainly because many families now need two incomes to survive. This can create emotional separation and leave children with less support, structure and moral guidance.","chinese":"總結來說，孩子與父母相處的時間減少，主要是因為許多家庭現在需要兩份收入才能維持生活。 這可能造成情感上的疏離，並使孩子得到較少的支持、規律和道德引導。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"across many modern societies","chinese":"在許多現代社會中"},{"english":"work full time","chinese":"全職工作"},{"english":"receive fewer hours of","chinese":"獲得較少時間的……"},{"english":"direct parental attention","chinese":"父母直接關注"},{"english":"earlier generations","chinese":"較早幾代人"},{"english":"the main reason is","chinese":"主要原因是"},{"english":"economic pressure","chinese":"經濟壓力"},{"english":"weaken family bonds","chinese":"削弱家庭聯繫"},{"english":"reduce the guidance children receive","chinese":"減少孩子得到的引導"},{"english":"while they are growing up","chinese":"在他們成長期間"},{"english":"the clearest reason","chinese":"最明顯的原因"},{"english":"one salary","chinese":"一份薪金"},{"english":"no longer enough to","chinese":"不再足以"},{"english":"support a family comfortably","chinese":"讓一家人生活得舒適"},{"english":"housing, transport, food, childcare and education","chinese":"住屋、交通、食物、育兒服務和教育"},{"english":"remain in paid employment","chinese":"繼續受薪工作"},{"english":"keep the household stable","chinese":"維持家庭穩定"},{"english":"In this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"personal ambition","chinese":"個人抱負"},{"english":"a financial lifeline","chinese":"財務生命線"},{"english":"because of this","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"leave home early","chinese":"很早離家"},{"english":"return late","chinese":"很晚回家"},{"english":"depend on","chinese":"依賴"},{"english":"grandparents","chinese":"祖父母；外祖父母"},{"english":"nurseries","chinese":"托兒所"},{"english":"electronic devices","chinese":"電子裝置"},{"english":"occupy their children","chinese":"讓孩子有事做；打發孩子"},{"english":"one serious problem","chinese":"一個嚴重問題"},{"english":"emotional distance","chinese":"情感距離"},{"english":"material comfort","chinese":"物質上的安穩"},{"english":"small, regular moments of attention","chinese":"細小而定期的關注時刻"},{"english":"family meals","chinese":"家庭用餐"},{"english":"bedtime conversations","chinese":"睡前談話"},{"english":"help with homework","chinese":"功課上的幫助"},{"english":"these routines","chinese":"這些日常習慣"},{"english":"look ordinary","chinese":"看起來普通"},{"english":"the glue that holds relationships together","chinese":"維繫關係的黏合劑"},{"english":"feel less valued","chinese":"感到較不受重視"},{"english":"less secure","chinese":"較沒有安全感"},{"english":"even when","chinese":"即使"},{"english":"love them deeply","chinese":"深深愛着他們"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨時間"},{"english":"reduce their confidence","chinese":"降低他們的信心"},{"english":"less willing to discuss","chinese":"較不願意討論"},{"english":"fears, mistakes or personal difficulties","chinese":"恐懼、錯誤或個人困難"},{"english":"another problem","chinese":"另一個問題"},{"english":"weaker supervision","chinese":"較弱的監督"},{"english":"rarely available","chinese":"很少有空"},{"english":"turn to","chinese":"轉向……尋求"},{"english":"classmates","chinese":"同學"},{"english":"social media","chinese":"社交媒體"},{"english":"online entertainment","chinese":"網上娛樂"},{"english":"advice and approval","chinese":"建議和認同"},{"english":"spends hours online","chinese":"花數小時上網"},{"english":"without adult guidance","chinese":"沒有成人引導"},{"english":"copy unhealthy habits","chinese":"模仿不健康習慣"},{"english":"absorb harmful values","chinese":"吸收有害價值觀"},{"english":"before anyone notices","chinese":"在任何人察覺之前"},{"english":"responsible children","chinese":"負責任的孩子"},{"english":"struggle to build","chinese":"難以建立"},{"english":"discipline and self-control","chinese":"紀律和自制力"},{"english":"consistently present","chinese":"持續在場"},{"english":"model those qualities","chinese":"示範那些特質"},{"english":"two incomes","chinese":"兩份收入"},{"english":"to survive","chinese":"為了生存"},{"english":"emotional separation","chinese":"情感分離"},{"english":"leave children with","chinese":"令孩子只有；使孩子缺乏"},{"english":"less support, structure and moral guidance","chinese":"較少支援、規律和道德引導"}]},"model-essay-25-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-25-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:25","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-25-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q25","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Public health has become one of the most important concerns in modern society. Some believe governments should manage it, while others argue individuals must take charge of their own well-being. Although personal habits clearly affect a person’s physical condition, I strongly believe that the government should carry the main responsibility because it controls the systems and rules that shape those habits.","chinese":"公共健康已成為現代社會中最重要的關注之一。 有些人認為政府應該管理公共健康，而另一些人則主張個人必須為自己的健康負責。 儘管個人習慣明顯會影響一個人的身體狀況，我強烈認為政府應該承擔主要責任，因為它掌控著塑造這些習慣的制度和規則。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"On one side, there is a persuasive argument that protecting public health is a duty of the state. Governments are the only bodies with the authority and resources to provide clean water, safe hospitals, vaccination programmes, food-safety inspections, and reliable health education. If these foundations are weak, even disciplined citizens are left exposed to risks they cannot personally control. For example, a family may eat well and exercise regularly, but they cannot inspect every restaurant kitchen, regulate air pollution, or make medical care affordable by themselves. In this sense, public health is not merely a private lifestyle issue; it is part of the social infrastructure that allows whole communities to live safely.","chinese":"一方面，有一個很有說服力的觀點認為，保護公共健康是國家的責任。 政府是唯一擁有權力和資源去提供清潔食水、安全醫院、疫苗接種計劃、食品安全檢查，以及可靠健康教育的機構。 如果這些基礎薄弱，即使是自律的市民，也會暴露在他們個人無法控制的風險之中。 例如，一個家庭可能飲食健康並定期運動，但他們無法親自檢查每一間餐廳的廚房、規管空氣污染，或靠自己令醫療服務變得負擔得起。 從這個意義上說，公共健康並不僅僅是一個私人生活方式問題；它是社會基礎設施的一部分，使整個社區能夠安全地生活。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"By contrast, supporters of individual responsibility argue that no government can force people to make healthy choices every day. A person who smokes heavily, eats mostly fast food, refuses exercise, and ignores medical advice will probably suffer health problems even in a well-funded system. This view is reasonable because daily routines are like the small hinges on which long-term health swings. However, it is less convincing as the main position. People’s choices are often shaped by price, advertising, working hours, local facilities, and education, all of which are strongly influenced by public policy. Therefore, while individuals should cooperate by making sensible decisions, they cannot replace the protective role of the state.","chinese":"相比之下，支持個人責任的人認為，沒有任何政府能夠強迫人們每天作出健康的選擇。 一個大量吸煙、主要吃快餐、拒絕運動，並忽視醫療建議的人，即使身處資金充足的醫療制度中，也很可能會出現健康問題。 這個觀點是合理的，因為日常習慣就像細小的鉸鏈，而長遠健康正是在這些鉸鏈上轉動 然而，把它作為主要立場則較缺乏說服力。 人們的選擇往往受到價格、廣告、工作時間、本地設施和教育所塑造，而這些全部都深受公共政策影響。 因此，雖然個人應該透過作出明智決定來配合，但他們不能取代國家的保護角色。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, people should certainly take care of their own bodies, but public health should remain mainly the responsibility of the government. Individual discipline matters, yet strong public systems are the safety net without which personal effort can easily fall short.","chinese":"總結來說，人們當然應該照顧自己的身體，但公共健康仍應主要由政府負責。 個人自律固然重要，然而強大的公共制度是一張安全網；沒有它，個人的努力很容易不足以應對問題。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"public health","chinese":"公共衞生"},{"english":"one of the most important concerns","chinese":"最重要的關注之一"},{"english":"modern society","chinese":"現代社會"},{"english":"manage it","chinese":"管理它"},{"english":"take charge of","chinese":"掌管；負責"},{"english":"well-being","chinese":"福祉；健康"},{"english":"personal habits","chinese":"個人習慣"},{"english":"physical condition","chinese":"身體狀況"},{"english":"carry the main responsibility","chinese":"承擔主要責任"},{"english":"systems and rules","chinese":"制度和規則"},{"english":"shape those habits","chinese":"塑造那些習慣"},{"english":"on one side","chinese":"一方面"},{"english":"a persuasive argument","chinese":"有說服力的論點"},{"english":"protecting public health","chinese":"保護公共衞生"},{"english":"a duty of the state","chinese":"國家的責任"},{"english":"the only bodies with","chinese":"唯一擁有……的機構"},{"english":"authority and resources","chinese":"權力和資源"},{"english":"provide clean water","chinese":"提供清潔食水"},{"english":"safe hospitals","chinese":"安全醫院"},{"english":"vaccination programmes","chinese":"疫苗接種計劃"},{"english":"food-safety inspections","chinese":"食物安全檢查"},{"english":"reliable health education","chinese":"可靠的健康教育"},{"english":"these foundations","chinese":"這些基礎"},{"english":"be left exposed to","chinese":"被置於……風險之中"},{"english":"disciplined citizens","chinese":"自律的市民"},{"english":"risks they cannot personally control","chinese":"他們個人無法控制的風險"},{"english":"eat well","chinese":"飲食健康"},{"english":"exercise regularly","chinese":"定期運動"},{"english":"inspect every restaurant kitchen","chinese":"檢查每間餐廳廚房"},{"english":"regulate air pollution","chinese":"規管空氣污染"},{"english":"make medical care affordable","chinese":"令醫療服務變得可負擔"},{"english":"by themselves","chinese":"靠自己"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"not merely a private lifestyle issue","chinese":"不只是私人生活方式問題"},{"english":"social infrastructure","chinese":"社會基礎建設"},{"english":"allow whole communities to","chinese":"讓整個社區能夠"},{"english":"live safely","chinese":"安全地生活"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相反"},{"english":"supporters of individual responsibility","chinese":"個人責任的支持者"},{"english":"force people to","chinese":"強迫人們去"},{"english":"make healthy choices","chinese":"作出健康選擇"},{"english":"smokes heavily","chinese":"大量吸煙"},{"english":"eats mostly fast food","chinese":"主要吃快餐"},{"english":"refuses exercise","chinese":"拒絕運動"},{"english":"ignores medical advice","chinese":"忽視醫療建議"},{"english":"suffer health problems","chinese":"出現健康問題"},{"english":"a well-funded system","chinese":"資金充足的制度"},{"english":"this view is reasonable","chinese":"這個看法是合理的"},{"english":"daily routines","chinese":"日常習慣"},{"english":"small hinges on which","chinese":"……所依靠的小鉸鏈"},{"english":"long-term health","chinese":"長遠健康"},{"english":"less convincing as","chinese":"作為……較欠說服力"},{"english":"the main position","chinese":"主要立場"},{"english":"be shaped by","chinese":"受……塑造"},{"english":"price, advertising, working hours, local facilities, and education","chinese":"價格、廣告、工作時間、本地設施和教育"},{"english":"strongly influenced by","chinese":"受到……強烈影響"},{"english":"public policy","chinese":"公共政策"},{"english":"cooperate by","chinese":"透過……合作"},{"english":"making sensible decisions","chinese":"作出明智決定"},{"english":"replace the protective role of","chinese":"取代……的保護作用"},{"english":"the protective role of the state","chinese":"國家的保護作用"},{"english":"take care of their own bodies","chinese":"照顧自己的身體"},{"english":"remain mainly the responsibility of","chinese":"仍應主要由……負責"},{"english":"individual discipline","chinese":"個人自律"},{"english":"matters","chinese":"很重要"},{"english":"strong public systems","chinese":"強大的公共制度"},{"english":"the safety net","chinese":"安全網"},{"english":"without which","chinese":"沒有它便"},{"english":"personal effort","chinese":"個人努力"},{"english":"fall short","chinese":"未能達標；不足以成功"}]},"model-essay-25-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-25-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:25","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-25-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q25","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Personality is often discussed as if it were written into a person before birth, like an invisible script that cannot be revised. I completely disagree with this view. Although genes may create certain tendencies, character is not fixed at birth; it is continually shaped by upbringing, experience and deliberate effort.","chinese":"性格經常被討論得好像人在出生之前就已經被寫好一樣，如同一份無形而無法修改的劇本。 我完全不同意這種看法。 雖然基因可能會造成某些傾向，但人的性格並不是在出生時就固定不變；它會不斷受到成長環境、人生經歷和有意識的努力所塑造。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that a person's environment strongly influences how their traits develop. A child may be naturally quiet, but this does not mean he must remain passive or anxious for life. If he grows up in a supportive family and attends a school where teachers encourage discussion, teamwork and public speaking, he is likely to become more confident over time. By contrast, a harsh environment can make even a cheerful child defensive or withdrawn. This suggests that genes may provide the raw material, but surroundings help mold the final shape of a person's character.","chinese":"第一個原因是，一個人的環境會強烈影響其性格特質如何發展。 一個孩子可能天生安靜，但這並不代表他一生都必然會保持被動或焦慮。 如果他在一個支持性的家庭中成長，並就讀於一所老師鼓勵討論、團隊合作和公開發言的學校，他很可能會隨著時間變得更加自信。 相比之下，一個嚴苛的環境甚至可以令原本開朗的孩子變得防備心重或退縮。 這說明基因或許提供了原材料，但周圍環境會幫助塑造一個人性格的最終形態。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"A second reason is that people can change their behaviour through practice, reflection and repeated experience. Traits such as patience, resilience and self-control are not simply inherited gifts; they can be strengthened like muscles. For example, someone who is easily angered may learn to pause before reacting, listen to feedback and practise calmer ways of handling conflict. Over time, these habits can become part of that person's normal character. Similarly, young adults who enter demanding workplaces often become more disciplined and emotionally mature because daily pressure forces them to adapt. If personality were entirely predetermined, such growth would be impossible, yet ordinary life shows the opposite.","chinese":"第二個原因是，人們可以透過練習、反思和反覆經驗來改變自己的行為。 耐性、韌性和自制力等特質並不只是遺傳而來的天賦；它們可以像肌肉一樣被強化。 例如，一個容易生氣的人可以學會在作出反應之前先停一停、聆聽別人的回饋，並練習以更冷靜的方式處理衝突。 隨著時間過去，這些習慣可以成為那個人正常性格的一部分。 同樣地，進入高要求職場的年輕成年人，往往會變得更有紀律，也在情緒上更加成熟，因為日常壓力會迫使他們適應。 如果性格完全是預先決定的，那麼這種成長便不可能出現；然而，日常生活所顯示的正正相反。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely reject the idea that personality is locked in place before birth. Genes may influence people's starting points, but family, education, relationships and conscious effort can reshape character throughout life. Human personality is not a stone statue; it is more like a living tree, shaped by both its roots and the conditions in which it grows.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全否定性格在出生之前就已經被鎖定不變這種想法。 基因可能會影響人的起點，但家庭、教育、人際關係和有意識的努力，都可以在人生過程中重塑性格。 人的性格並不是一座石像；它更像一棵活著的樹，既受其根部影響，也受它生長環境的條件所塑造。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"personality","chinese":"性格"},{"english":"be discussed as if","chinese":"被討論得好像……"},{"english":"written into","chinese":"寫進……之中"},{"english":"before birth","chinese":"出生之前"},{"english":"invisible script","chinese":"隱形劇本"},{"english":"cannot be revised","chinese":"不能被修改"},{"english":"completely disagree with","chinese":"完全不同意……"},{"english":"genes","chinese":"基因"},{"english":"create certain tendencies","chinese":"形成某些傾向"},{"english":"character","chinese":"品格；性格"},{"english":"fixed at birth","chinese":"出生時已固定"},{"english":"continually shaped by","chinese":"不斷受……塑造"},{"english":"upbringing","chinese":"成長教養"},{"english":"deliberate effort","chinese":"有意識的努力"},{"english":"a person's environment","chinese":"一個人的環境"},{"english":"strongly influences","chinese":"強烈影響"},{"english":"traits","chinese":"特質"},{"english":"naturally quiet","chinese":"天生安靜"},{"english":"remain passive or anxious for life","chinese":"一生都被動或焦慮"},{"english":"supportive family","chinese":"支持性的家庭"},{"english":"attend a school where","chinese":"就讀一間……的學校"},{"english":"encourage discussion","chinese":"鼓勵討論"},{"english":"teamwork and public speaking","chinese":"團隊合作和公開演說"},{"english":"become more confident over time","chinese":"隨着時間變得更自信"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"harsh environment","chinese":"嚴苛環境"},{"english":"cheerful child","chinese":"開朗的孩子"},{"english":"defensive or withdrawn","chinese":"有戒心或退縮"},{"english":"suggests that","chinese":"這顯示……"},{"english":"raw material","chinese":"原材料"},{"english":"surroundings","chinese":"周遭環境"},{"english":"mold the final shape of","chinese":"塑造……的最終形態"},{"english":"change their behaviour","chinese":"改變自己的行為"},{"english":"practice, reflection and repeated experience","chinese":"練習、反思和重複經驗"},{"english":"patience, resilience and self-control","chinese":"耐性、韌性和自制力"},{"english":"inherited gifts","chinese":"遺傳得來的天賦"},{"english":"be strengthened like muscles","chinese":"像肌肉一樣被鍛鍊"},{"english":"easily angered","chinese":"容易發怒"},{"english":"pause before reacting","chinese":"在反應前先停一停"},{"english":"listen to feedback","chinese":"聆聽回饋"},{"english":"handling conflict","chinese":"處理衝突"},{"english":"become part of","chinese":"成為……的一部分"},{"english":"normal character","chinese":"平常性格"},{"english":"young adults","chinese":"年輕成年人"},{"english":"demanding workplaces","chinese":"要求高的工作場所"},{"english":"emotionally mature","chinese":"情緒成熟"},{"english":"daily pressure","chinese":"日常壓力"},{"english":"forces them to adapt","chinese":"迫使他們適應"},{"english":"entirely predetermined","chinese":"完全預先決定"},{"english":"ordinary life","chinese":"日常生活"},{"english":"shows the opposite","chinese":"顯示相反情況"},{"english":"completely reject the idea that","chinese":"完全否定……的想法"},{"english":"locked in place","chinese":"被固定不變"},{"english":"starting points","chinese":"起點"},{"english":"conscious effort","chinese":"有意識的努力"},{"english":"reshape character","chinese":"重塑性格"},{"english":"throughout life","chinese":"終其一生"},{"english":"stone statue","chinese":"石像"},{"english":"living tree","chinese":"活生生的樹"},{"english":"shaped by both","chinese":"同時受兩者塑造"},{"english":"roots","chinese":"根"},{"english":"conditions in which it grows","chinese":"它生長的環境"}]},"model-essay-26-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-26-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:26","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-26-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q26","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Traffic congestion has become a defining problem in many large cities, wasting commuters’ time, harming productivity, and putting pressure on existing transport systems. One proposed solution is to build sky trains, which run on elevated tracks rather than on roads or beneath the ground. This essay will examine the advantages and disadvantages of using this approach to reduce urban congestion.","chinese":"交通擠塞已成為許多大城市的典型問題，不但浪費通勤者的時間、損害生產力，亦對現有交通系統造成壓力。 其中一種被提出的解決方法，是興建空中列車，也就是在高架軌道上運行，而不是在地面道路或地下行駛。 本文將探討利用這種方法來紓緩城市交通擠塞的優點與缺點。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One major advantage of sky trains is that they can transport large numbers of passengers without competing with cars, buses, or delivery vehicles for limited road space. Because the system operates above street level, it is largely unaffected by traffic lights, accidents, and rush-hour bottlenecks, which makes journeys faster and more reliable. For example, a worker travelling from an outer residential district to the city centre could still arrive on time even if the roads below were at a standstill. Another benefit is that elevated lines can, in some cases, be simpler to construct than underground railways, since they do not require extensive tunnelling beneath densely built-up areas. For instance, a city could install pillars and tracks above a wide central avenue more quickly than digging beneath historic buildings and buried utility lines.","chinese":"空中列車其中一個主要優點，是它能夠在不與私家車、巴士或送貨車爭奪有限路面空間的情況下運載大量乘客。 由於這套系統在街道上方運行，它大致不受交通燈、交通意外及繁忙時段樽頸情況影響，因而令行程更快捷，也更可靠。 這意味著通勤人士可以避開路面交通的不確定性，更準時到達目的地，並減輕本已擠塞道路的壓力。 例如，一名由外圍住宅區前往市中心上班的員工，即使下方道路完全陷入停滯，仍然可以準時到達。 另一個好處是，在某些情況下，高架鐵路比地下鐵路更容易興建，因為它不需要在建築密集地區下方進行大規模隧道工程。 結果是，城市可能可以更快擴展公共交通、避免部分工程上的複雜問題，並更早增加運載能力。 例如，一個城市可以在寬闊的中央大道上方興建支柱和軌道，而這往往比在歷史建築及地下公用設施下方開挖地鐵更快完成。 因此，空中列車能透過提供不受路面交通影響的出行方式，以及一種可能更快擴展交通基建的方法，來改善城市流動性。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, this solution also has clear disadvantages. The first is financial cost: although sky trains may be less expensive than subways, they still require substantial investment in land acquisition, engineering, stations, and long-term maintenance. For example, if a city spends most of its transport budget on one elevated line, it may have to postpone improvements to buses or suburban roads that are also badly needed. A second drawback is their impact on the urban environment. Large overhead structures can block sunlight, create noise, and reduce privacy for nearby residents. For instance, people living in apartment blocks beside an elevated track may have trains passing their windows from early morning until late at night, making the area less pleasant to live in.","chinese":"然而，這種解決方案亦有明顯缺點。 第一個缺點是財政成本：雖然空中列車可能比地下鐵路便宜，但它仍然需要在土地取得、工程建設、車站設施及長期維修方面投入大量資金。 當大量公共資金被投放到單一大型項目時，其他交通需求便可能被忽視或延後處理。 例如，如果一個城市把大部分交通預算投放在一條高架鐵路線上，它便可能需要延後改善同樣急需提升的巴士服務或郊區道路。 第二個缺點，是它對城市環境所造成的影響。 大型高架結構可能遮擋陽光、製造噪音，並削弱附近居民的私隱，從而令周邊社區變得較不宜居。 例如，居住在高架軌道旁邊公寓的居民，可能由清晨到深夜都會有列車從窗邊駛過，令日常生活明顯變得較不舒適。 因此，雖然空中列車或許能夠紓緩交通擠塞，但它同時也可能為城市帶來嚴重的財政及環境代價。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In summary, sky trains offer clear benefits because they can bypass road congestion and expand public transport capacity efficiently. At the same time, their high cost and their potential impact on surrounding neighbourhoods mean that they are not a perfect solution to urban traffic problems.","chinese":"總結來說，空中列車具有明顯優點，因為它能避開路面交通擠塞，並更有效地提升運輸能力。 與此同時，其高昂成本以及對周邊社區造成的負面影響，也意味著它並不是解決城市交通問題的完美方案。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"traffic congestion","chinese":"交通擠塞"},{"english":"a defining problem","chinese":"標誌性問題；主要問題"},{"english":"large cities","chinese":"大城市"},{"english":"waste commuters' time","chinese":"浪費通勤人士的時間"},{"english":"commuters","chinese":"通勤人士"},{"english":"harm productivity","chinese":"損害生產力"},{"english":"put pressure on","chinese":"對……造成壓力"},{"english":"existing transport systems","chinese":"現有交通系統"},{"english":"one proposed solution","chinese":"一個被提出的解決方案"},{"english":"sky trains","chinese":"高架列車"},{"english":"elevated tracks","chinese":"高架路軌"},{"english":"rather than on roads","chinese":"而不是在道路上"},{"english":"beneath the ground","chinese":"在地底下"},{"english":"examine the advantages and disadvantages of","chinese":"探討……的優點和缺點"},{"english":"this approach","chinese":"這種方法"},{"english":"reduce urban congestion","chinese":"減少城市交通擠塞"},{"english":"one major advantage","chinese":"一個主要優點"},{"english":"transport large numbers of passengers","chinese":"運載大量乘客"},{"english":"compete with","chinese":"與……競爭"},{"english":"delivery vehicles","chinese":"送貨車輛"},{"english":"limited road space","chinese":"有限道路空間"},{"english":"operate above street level","chinese":"在街道上方運行"},{"english":"largely unaffected by","chinese":"基本不受……影響"},{"english":"traffic lights","chinese":"交通燈"},{"english":"rush-hour bottlenecks","chinese":"繁忙時間的交通瓶頸"},{"english":"faster and more reliable","chinese":"更快和更可靠"},{"english":"an outer residential district","chinese":"外圍住宅區"},{"english":"the city centre","chinese":"市中心"},{"english":"arrive on time","chinese":"準時到達"},{"english":"at a standstill","chinese":"完全停頓"},{"english":"elevated lines","chinese":"高架鐵路線"},{"english":"simpler to construct","chinese":"較易興建"},{"english":"underground railways","chinese":"地下鐵路"},{"english":"extensive tunnelling","chinese":"大規模挖掘隧道"},{"english":"densely built-up areas","chinese":"建築密集地區"},{"english":"install pillars and tracks","chinese":"安裝支柱和路軌"},{"english":"a wide central avenue","chinese":"寬闊的市中心大道"},{"english":"digging beneath","chinese":"在……下面挖掘"},{"english":"historic buildings","chinese":"歷史建築"},{"english":"buried utility lines","chinese":"地底公用設施管線"},{"english":"clear disadvantages","chinese":"明顯缺點"},{"english":"financial cost","chinese":"財政成本"},{"english":"less expensive than","chinese":"比……便宜"},{"english":"subways","chinese":"地下鐵路"},{"english":"require substantial investment in","chinese":"需要在……方面作大量投資"},{"english":"substantial investment","chinese":"大量投資"},{"english":"land acquisition","chinese":"收地"},{"english":"engineering","chinese":"工程"},{"english":"long-term maintenance","chinese":"長期維修保養"},{"english":"transport budget","chinese":"交通預算"},{"english":"postpone improvements to","chinese":"推遲對……的改善"},{"english":"suburban roads","chinese":"市郊道路"},{"english":"badly needed","chinese":"非常需要"},{"english":"a second drawback","chinese":"第二個缺點"},{"english":"impact on","chinese":"對……的影響"},{"english":"the urban environment","chinese":"城市環境"},{"english":"overhead structures","chinese":"架空結構"},{"english":"block sunlight","chinese":"阻擋陽光"},{"english":"reduce privacy","chinese":"降低私隱"},{"english":"nearby residents","chinese":"附近居民"},{"english":"apartment blocks","chinese":"住宅大廈"},{"english":"beside an elevated track","chinese":"在高架路軌旁邊"},{"english":"passing their windows","chinese":"經過窗外"},{"english":"from early morning until late at night","chinese":"從清晨到深夜"},{"english":"less pleasant to live in","chinese":"居住起來較不舒適"},{"english":"in summary","chinese":"總括而言"},{"english":"offer clear benefits","chinese":"帶來明顯好處"},{"english":"bypass road congestion","chinese":"繞過道路交通擠塞"},{"english":"expand public transport capacity","chinese":"擴大公共交通運載能力"},{"english":"public transport capacity","chinese":"公共交通運載能力"},{"english":"efficiently","chinese":"有效率地"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"potential impact on","chinese":"對……的潛在影響"},{"english":"surrounding neighbourhoods","chinese":"周邊社區"},{"english":"a perfect solution to","chinese":"……的完美解決方案"},{"english":"urban traffic problems","chinese":"城市交通問題"}]},"model-essay-26-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-26-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:26","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-26-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Because nuclear families have fewer members than extended households, they can relocate with less practical difficulty. In my view, children do benefit from moving, and the advantages clearly outweigh the disadvantages because relocation builds adaptability and may open the door to better opportunities.","chinese":"因為核心家庭的成員比大家庭少，所以它們在搬遷時面對的實際困難較少。 在我看來，孩子確實能從搬遷中受益，而且優點明顯大於缺點，因為搬遷能培養適應能力，並可能為他們打開通往更好機會的大門。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main benefit is that moving teaches children how to adjust to unfamiliar environments. When a child enters a new school or city, they must learn new routines, make friends, and read unfamiliar social expectations. This may be uncomfortable at first, but it trains them to observe, communicate, and cope with change rather than fear it. For example, a child who moves from a quiet town to a large city may initially feel lost; after joining classes and sports teams, however, they often become more confident around strangers. In this sense, relocation is not just a change of address; it is a practical lesson in resilience.","chinese":"主要好處是，搬遷能教會孩子如何適應陌生環境。 當一個孩子進入一所新學校或一個新城市時，他們必須學習新的日常規律、結交朋友，並理解陌生的社交期待。 這一開始可能會令人不舒服，但它訓練孩子去觀察、溝通，並應對變化，而不是害怕變化 例如，一個從安靜小鎮搬到大城市的孩子，起初可能會感到迷失；然而，在參加課堂和運動隊之後，他們往往會在陌生人面前變得更加自信。 從這個意義上說，搬遷不只是地址的改變；它是一堂關於韌性的實際課程。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Moving can also improve a child’s long-term prospects. Parents often relocate for better jobs, safer neighbourhoods, stronger schools, or more reliable services. If a family moves to an area where education is stable and extracurricular activities are accessible, the child receives richer academic and social support. These conditions can shape future confidence, ambition, and career options.","chinese":"搬遷也能改善孩子的長遠前景。 父母往往會為了更好的工作、更安全的社區、更優質的學校，或更可靠的服務而搬遷。 如果一個家庭搬到教育穩定、課外活動容易接觸到的地區，孩子便能獲得更豐富的學業和社交支持。 這些條件能夠塑造孩子未來的自信、抱負和職業選擇。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 3","english":"Admittedly, moving can create emotional difficulties. Children may feel uprooted when they leave close friends, familiar teachers, and a place that feels like home. In some cases, this disruption may affect their mood or school performance for a while. However, these disadvantages are usually temporary if parents provide steady support, maintain routines, and help children stay connected with old friends while building new relationships. The discomfort of transition is real, but it is not greater than the lasting gains.","chinese":"誠然，搬遷可能會造成情感上的困難。 當孩子離開親密的朋友、熟悉的老師，以及一個讓他們感覺像家的地方時，他們可能會感到自己被連根拔起。 在某些情況下，這種干擾可能會在一段時間內影響他們的情緒或學校表現。 然而，如果父母能提供穩定的支持、維持日常規律，並幫助孩子在建立新關係的同時與舊朋友保持聯繫，這些缺點通常只是暫時的。 過渡期的不適是真實存在的，但它並不大於那些長遠的收穫。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, children can benefit significantly from moving. Although relocation may cause short-term stress, its advantages outweigh its disadvantages because it strengthens adaptability and may give children access to a better future.","chinese":"總結來說，孩子能夠從搬遷中獲得顯著好處。 儘管搬遷可能造成短期壓力，但它的優點大於缺點，因為它能加強適應能力，並可能讓孩子接觸到更好的未來。"}],"vocabulary":[]},"model-essay-26-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-26-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:26","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-26-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q26","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many cities, the future of historic architecture has become a matter of debate. While some argue that old buildings should be preserved, others believe that demolishing them and constructing modern replacements is more practical. In my view, old buildings should be protected because they carry cultural value that cannot be rebuilt once it is lost.","chinese":"在許多城市，歷史建築的未來已成為一個備受爭議的問題。 雖然有些人認為舊建築應該被保留，但另一些人則相信，拆除它們並建造現代化的新建築會更加實際。 在我看來，舊建築應該受到保護，因為它們承載著一旦失去便無法重建的文化價值。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Those who support replacing old buildings often have reasonable practical concern. Many ageing structures are expensive to maintain, especially when their foundations, wiring, or drainage systems no longer meet modern safety standards. If a city is short of housing or commercial space, keeping a large, outdated building may seem like a poor use of valuable land. For example, replacing a damaged warehouse with a modern apartment block could provide homes for hundreds of residents and reduce pressure on crowded neighbourhoods. From this perspective, newer buildings can make cities safer, more efficient, and better suited to present-day needs.","chinese":"支持取代舊建築的人，通常有一個合理的實際考量。 許多老化的建築維護成本高昂，尤其是當它們的地基、電線或排水系統已不再符合現代安全標準時。 如果一座城市缺乏住宅或商業空間，保留一座大型而過時的建築，可能看起來像是在不善用寶貴土地。 例如，用一座現代公寓大樓取代一個受損倉庫，可以為數百名居民提供住所，並減輕擁擠社區的壓力。 從這個角度來看，較新的建築可以使城市更安全、更有效率，也更能符合現代需求。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, I believe preservation is ultimately more important because old buildings give a city its identity. They are not merely piles of bricks; they are visible records of how previous generations lived, worked, and understood beauty. When such buildings are destroyed, a city may gain floor space, but it loses part of its memory. Historic streets, traditional shop houses, and old public buildings can also attract tourism and support local businesses, which means preservation can bring economic value as well as cultural value. More importantly, protected buildings can often be adapted rather than abandoned. An old theatre, for instance, can become a community arts centre, allowing the past to remain useful in the present.","chinese":"然而，我認為保育最終更重要，因為舊建築賦予一座城市身份。 它們不只是磚塊堆砌而成的東西；它們是前人如何生活、工作和理解美感的可見記錄。 當這些建築被摧毀時，一座城市也許會獲得更多樓面空間，但它會失去部分記憶。 歷史街道、傳統店屋和舊公共建築也可以吸引旅遊業並支持本地商業，這意味著保育不僅能帶來文化價值，也能帶來經濟價值。 更重要的是，受保護的建築往往可以被改造使用，而不是被廢棄。 例如，一座舊劇院可以變成社區藝術中心，讓過去在現在仍然保持有用。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, although replacing old buildings can sometimes solve practical problems, I strongly believe that they should be protected instead of being replaced. Cities need development, but development should not come at the cost of erasing their history.","chinese":"總結來說，雖然取代舊建築有時能解決實際問題，但我堅定地認為，它們應該被保護，而不是被取代。 城市需要發展，但發展不應以抹去其歷史為代價。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"historic architecture","chinese":"歷史建築"},{"english":"a matter of debate","chinese":"具爭議的問題"},{"english":"old buildings","chinese":"舊建築"},{"english":"be preserved","chinese":"被保育；被保留"},{"english":"demolishing them","chinese":"拆卸它們"},{"english":"constructing modern replacements","chinese":"興建現代化替代建築"},{"english":"more practical","chinese":"更實際"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"be protected","chinese":"被保護"},{"english":"carry cultural value","chinese":"承載文化價值"},{"english":"cannot be rebuilt","chinese":"不能被重建"},{"english":"once it is lost","chinese":"一旦失去"},{"english":"support replacing","chinese":"支持取代"},{"english":"reasonable practical concern","chinese":"合理的實際考慮"},{"english":"ageing structures","chinese":"老化建築"},{"english":"expensive to maintain","chinese":"維修成本高"},{"english":"foundations, wiring, or drainage systems","chinese":"地基、電線或排水系統"},{"english":"no longer meet","chinese":"不再符合"},{"english":"modern safety standards","chinese":"現代安全標準"},{"english":"be short of","chinese":"缺乏"},{"english":"housing or commercial space","chinese":"住房或商業空間"},{"english":"outdated building","chinese":"過時建築"},{"english":"a poor use of","chinese":"對……的低效使用"},{"english":"valuable land","chinese":"寶貴土地"},{"english":"a damaged warehouse","chinese":"受損倉庫"},{"english":"a modern apartment block","chinese":"現代化住宅大廈"},{"english":"provide homes for","chinese":"為……提供住所"},{"english":"hundreds of residents","chinese":"數百名居民"},{"english":"reduce pressure on","chinese":"減輕……的壓力"},{"english":"crowded neighbourhoods","chinese":"擠迫社區"},{"english":"from this perspective","chinese":"從這個角度來看"},{"english":"newer buildings","chinese":"較新的建築物"},{"english":"better suited to","chinese":"更適合"},{"english":"present-day needs","chinese":"現今需要"},{"english":"preservation","chinese":"保育"},{"english":"ultimately more important","chinese":"最終更重要"},{"english":"give a city its identity","chinese":"賦予城市身份"},{"english":"not merely piles of bricks","chinese":"不只是一堆磚頭"},{"english":"visible records of","chinese":"……的可見記錄"},{"english":"previous generations","chinese":"前幾代人"},{"english":"understood beauty","chinese":"理解美"},{"english":"be destroyed","chinese":"被摧毀"},{"english":"gain floor space","chinese":"增加樓面空間"},{"english":"lose part of its memory","chinese":"失去部分記憶"},{"english":"historic streets","chinese":"歷史街道"},{"english":"traditional shop houses","chinese":"傳統店屋"},{"english":"old public buildings","chinese":"舊公共建築"},{"english":"attract tourism","chinese":"吸引旅遊"},{"english":"support local businesses","chinese":"支持本地商戶"},{"english":"economic value as well as cultural value","chinese":"經濟價值以及文化價值"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"protected buildings","chinese":"受保護建築"},{"english":"be adapted rather than abandoned","chinese":"被改造再用，而不是被棄置"},{"english":"an old theatre","chinese":"舊劇院"},{"english":"a community arts centre","chinese":"社區藝術中心"},{"english":"allow the past to remain useful","chinese":"讓過去在當下繼續有用"},{"english":"in the present","chinese":"在當下"},{"english":"solve practical problems","chinese":"解決實際問題"},{"english":"instead of being replaced","chinese":"而不是被取代"},{"english":"cities need development","chinese":"城市需要發展"},{"english":"come at the cost of","chinese":"以犧牲……為代價"},{"english":"erasing their history","chinese":"抹去其歷史"}]},"model-essay-26-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-26-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:26","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-26-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q26","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Discussions about gender and violence often rest on long-standing assumptions about personality. While women are sometimes described as more caring and less confrontational than men, I completely disagree that they are naturally more peaceful. In my view, peacefulness is shaped far more by upbringing, social expectations and power than by biological sex.","chinese":"關於性別與暴力的討論，往往建立在一些長久以來對性格的假設之上。 雖然女性有時被描述為比男性更關懷他人，也較少具對抗性， 但我完全不同意女性天生更加和平的說法。在我看來，和平的性格遠比生理性別更大程度上受到成長環境、社會期望和權力關係所塑造。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"First, the idea that women are born more peace-loving oversimplifies how character is formed. From childhood, boys and girls are often taught to behave in different ways: girls may be encouraged to be patient, polite and emotionally aware, whereas boys may be praised for toughness, competitiveness and dominance. Over time, these expectations can become a mask that people mistake for nature. For example, a girl who is repeatedly told to avoid conflict may learn to express disagreement quietly, while a boy who is rewarded for winning arguments may become more forceful. This does not prove that one sex is naturally peaceful and the other naturally aggressive; it shows that society trains people to perform different versions of acceptable behaviour.","chinese":"首先，女性天生更愛好和平這種想法，過度簡化了性格形成的過程。 從童年開始，男孩和女孩常常被教導以不同方式行事：女孩可能被鼓勵要有耐性、有禮貌並具備情緒覺察能力，而男孩則可能因堅強、好勝和具支配性而受到稱讚。 久而久之，這些期望可能變成一副面具，而人們卻誤以為那是天性。 例如，一個反覆被教導要避免衝突的女孩，可能會學會以安靜的方式表達不同意見；而一個因在爭論中取勝而受到獎勵的男孩，則可能變得更加強勢。 這並不能證明某一性別天生和平，而另一性別天生具攻擊性；它只是顯示社會訓練人們表現出不同版本的可接受行為。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Moreover, describing women as naturally nurturing can be harmful because it places unfair moral expectations on them and excuses aggression in men. If women are assumed to be gentle by nature, those who are ambitious, angry or politically assertive may be judged as abnormal. At the same time, men who show violence may be treated as if they are simply following their instincts, which lowers the standard of responsibility expected of them. In reality, both men and women can be compassionate, cruel, diplomatic or confrontational depending on their values, circumstances and choices. A female leader can make ruthless decisions, just as a male teacher or father can create a calm and caring environment.","chinese":"此外，把女性描述為天生具養育特質可能是有害的，因為這會把不公平的道德期望加在女性身上，同時為男性的攻擊性開脫。 如果女性被假定為天性溫柔，那些有野心、會憤怒或在政治上立場堅定的女性，便可能被視為不正常。 與此同時，表現出暴力的男性可能會被看待成只是順從本能，這便降低了社會對他們責任感的要求標準。 事實上，男性和女性都可以是富有同情心的、殘酷的、圓融的或具對抗性的，這取決於他們的價值觀、處境和選擇。 一位女性領袖可以作出冷酷的決定，正如一位男性教師或父親也可以創造一個平靜而充滿關懷的環境。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I entirely reject the claim that women are generally more peaceful because they are naturally more nurturing. Peace is not written into one gender like a birthmark; it is cultivated through education, culture and personal responsibility.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全反對女性通常更和平是因為她們天生更具養育特質這一說法。 和平並不像胎記一樣寫在某一個性別身上；它是透過教育、文化和個人責任培養出來的"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"gender and violence","chinese":"性別與暴力"},{"english":"rest on","chinese":"建基於；依賴"},{"english":"long-standing assumptions","chinese":"長久以來的假設"},{"english":"personality","chinese":"性格"},{"english":"be described as","chinese":"被描述為"},{"english":"caring","chinese":"關懷他人的"},{"english":"less confrontational","chinese":"較少對抗性的"},{"english":"naturally more peaceful","chinese":"天生較和平；天生較平和"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"peacefulness","chinese":"平和性格；和平傾向"},{"english":"be shaped by","chinese":"受……塑造"},{"english":"upbringing","chinese":"成長教養"},{"english":"social expectations","chinese":"社會期望"},{"english":"biological sex","chinese":"生理性別"},{"english":"be born more peace-loving","chinese":"天生較愛好和平"},{"english":"oversimplifies","chinese":"過分簡化"},{"english":"how character is formed","chinese":"性格如何形成"},{"english":"from childhood","chinese":"從童年開始"},{"english":"behave in different ways","chinese":"以不同方式行為"},{"english":"be encouraged to","chinese":"被鼓勵去……"},{"english":"emotionally aware","chinese":"對情緒有覺察力"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；然而"},{"english":"be praised for","chinese":"因……而受到讚賞"},{"english":"toughness","chinese":"強硬；堅韌"},{"english":"competitiveness","chinese":"競爭性"},{"english":"dominance","chinese":"支配性"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨着時間過去"},{"english":"become a mask","chinese":"變成一個面具"},{"english":"mistake for nature","chinese":"誤以為是天性"},{"english":"avoid conflict","chinese":"避免衝突"},{"english":"express disagreement quietly","chinese":"安靜地表達不同意"},{"english":"be rewarded for","chinese":"因……而得到獎勵"},{"english":"winning arguments","chinese":"贏得爭論"},{"english":"forceful","chinese":"強勢的；有壓迫感的"},{"english":"naturally aggressive","chinese":"天生具攻擊性"},{"english":"trains people to","chinese":"訓練人們去……"},{"english":"perform different versions of","chinese":"表現出不同版本的……"},{"english":"acceptable behaviour","chinese":"可接受行為"},{"english":"describing women as","chinese":"將女性描述為……"},{"english":"naturally nurturing","chinese":"天生具照顧特質"},{"english":"places unfair moral expectations on","chinese":"對……施加不公平的道德期望"},{"english":"moral expectations","chinese":"道德期望"},{"english":"excuses aggression in","chinese":"為……的攻擊性開脫"},{"english":"assumed to be","chinese":"被假定為"},{"english":"gentle by nature","chinese":"天性溫和"},{"english":"politically assertive","chinese":"政治上敢於表達立場的"},{"english":"be judged as abnormal","chinese":"被評為不正常"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"show violence","chinese":"表現出暴力"},{"english":"following their instincts","chinese":"遵循自己的本能"},{"english":"lowers the standard of responsibility","chinese":"降低對責任的要求"},{"english":"in reality","chinese":"實際上"},{"english":"compassionate","chinese":"有同情心的"},{"english":"cruel","chinese":"殘酷的"},{"english":"diplomatic","chinese":"善於協調的；圓融的"},{"english":"depending on","chinese":"取決於"},{"english":"values, circumstances and choices","chinese":"價值觀、處境和選擇"},{"english":"female leader","chinese":"女性領袖"},{"english":"ruthless decisions","chinese":"無情的決定"},{"english":"just as","chinese":"正如"},{"english":"calm and caring environment","chinese":"平靜而關愛的環境"},{"english":"entirely reject the claim","chinese":"完全否定這種說法"},{"english":"generally more peaceful","chinese":"一般較和平"},{"english":"written into one gender","chinese":"寫進某一性別之中"},{"english":"birthmark","chinese":"胎記"},{"english":"be cultivated through","chinese":"透過……培養"},{"english":"personal responsibility","chinese":"個人責任"}]},"model-essay-27-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-27-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:27","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-27-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q27","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many workplaces, especially those that rely heavily on digital communication, employers now expect staff to remain reachable even during annual leave. Although this arrangement may seem commercially sensible, I do not believe it has more advantages than disadvantages. Any gain in responsiveness is outweighed by the harm it causes to employees’ recovery, morale and long-term effectiveness.","chinese":"在許多職場中，尤其是那些高度依賴數碼溝通的工作環境裡，僱主如今要求員工即使在年假期間也要保持聯絡。 儘管這種安排在商業上看似合理， 我並不認為這種發展的優點大於缺點，因為它在回應速度上的任何好處，都被其對員工休息恢復、士氣以及長遠工作效率所造成的損害所超過。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Admittedly, there is one clear benefit to this practice. If a serious problem arises unexpectedly, immediate contact with the relevant employee can prevent a minor disruption from developing into a major one. A delayed shipment, a software failure or an urgent client request can often be resolved quickly when a staff member is available to clarify information or make a decision. For example, if a hotel manager can reach the technician who understands the booking system during a holiday, dozens of reservations may be saved and customer complaints reduced. In genuinely urgent situations, therefore, constant availability can protect a company’s operations.","chinese":"誠然，這種做法的一項優點是它能讓緊急問題更快得到處理。 如果突發嚴重問題，立即聯絡相關員工可以防止小型干擾演變成重大事故。 由於該員工本身已具備所需知識或決策權，問題往往可以立即釐清，決策也能更快作出，而正常運作亦可在最少延誤下恢復。 例如，如果一位酒店經理能在假期期間聯絡到熟悉訂房系統的技術人員，便可能挽救數十個預約，並減少顧客投訴。 這種持續可聯絡的狀態，也可能令僱主和客戶更放心，認為機構能夠隨時應對突發情況。 這種印象可以增強商業信心，維護公司的聲譽，並在突發事件發生時減低財務損失的風險。 例如，一位在公眾假期期間仍能獲得緊急回覆的客戶，往往更有可能信任該公司，並維持雙方的合作關係。 因此，在真正緊急的情況下，假期期間仍可聯絡員工，的確能帶來某些運作上的好處。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Nevertheless, the disadvantages are far more significant. First, employees who know they may be contacted at any moment are unable to disconnect mentally from work, even when they are officially resting. Because their attention remains partly fixed on possible messages or calls, holidays no longer serve their essential purpose of restoring energy and relieving stress. As a result, workers often return feeling drained rather than refreshed. Second, this culture gradually damages commitment to the employer. When private time is repeatedly interrupted, people feel that their personal boundaries are not respected, which breeds resentment and reduces loyalty. A nurse, teacher or office worker who is contacted during family trips or public holidays may cooperate at first, but repeated intrusion can eventually lead to burnout or resignation. Businesses then face higher recruitment costs, weaker team stability and lower productivity.","chinese":"然而，這種發展的缺點明顯更為嚴重，因為它不但妨礙員工得到真正休息，還會逐漸削弱他們對工作的投入感。 首先，當員工知道自己隨時可能被聯絡時，即使名義上正在休假，也無法在心理上真正脫離工作。 結果是，他們始終對來電或訊息保持某種警覺，壓力水平持續偏高，而假期亦無法如其應有的功能般幫助他們恢復精力。 例如，一名在家庭旅行期間不斷查看電郵的上班族，回到工作崗位時往往會感到精神疲憊，而非重新充電。 第二，私人時間一再被工作侵入，會使員工感到自己的個人界線沒有受到尊重。 這會滋生怨氣，削弱士氣，長遠而言更可能導致職業倦怠、忠誠度下降，甚至離職，而最終受害的其實也是機構本身。 一名護士、教師或文職員工如果年復一年在假期中被打擾，起初或許仍會配合，但最終很可能選擇辭職，轉到一份界線更健康的工作。 基於以上原因，長遠來看，假期期間持續聯絡員工帶來的傷害多於好處。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, while the ability to contact staff on holidays may occasionally help employers deal with emergencies, it is a negative development overall. The limited operational advantage is decisively outweighed by the damage done to workers’ wellbeing and to the sustainable performance of the organisation itself.","chinese":"總結而言，雖然在假期期間仍能聯絡員工有時的確能幫助僱主處理緊急情況，但整體來說，這是一種負面的發展。 在回應速度方面那種有限的優勢，顯然被它對員工福祉以及機構本身可持續表現所造成的損害所超過。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"rely heavily on","chinese":"非常依賴"},{"english":"digital communication","chinese":"數碼通訊"},{"english":"expect staff to remain reachable","chinese":"期望員工保持可聯絡"},{"english":"remain reachable","chinese":"保持可聯絡"},{"english":"annual leave","chinese":"年假"},{"english":"this arrangement","chinese":"這種安排"},{"english":"commercially sensible","chinese":"在商業上合理"},{"english":"has more advantages than disadvantages","chinese":"利多於弊"},{"english":"gain in responsiveness","chinese":"反應速度上的收益"},{"english":"be outweighed by","chinese":"被……超過；不及……重要"},{"english":"employees' recovery","chinese":"員工恢復狀態"},{"english":"morale","chinese":"士氣"},{"english":"long-term effectiveness","chinese":"長遠成效"},{"english":"admittedly","chinese":"誠然"},{"english":"one clear benefit to","chinese":"……的一個明顯好處"},{"english":"a serious problem arises unexpectedly","chinese":"嚴重問題突然出現"},{"english":"immediate contact with","chinese":"與……即時聯絡"},{"english":"the relevant employee","chinese":"相關員工"},{"english":"prevent a minor disruption from","chinese":"防止小阻礙……"},{"english":"developing into a major one","chinese":"發展成重大問題"},{"english":"a delayed shipment","chinese":"延誤的貨運"},{"english":"a software failure","chinese":"軟件故障"},{"english":"an urgent client request","chinese":"緊急客戶要求"},{"english":"be resolved quickly","chinese":"被迅速解決"},{"english":"clarify information","chinese":"澄清資料"},{"english":"make a decision","chinese":"作出決定"},{"english":"reach the technician","chinese":"聯絡到技術員"},{"english":"booking system","chinese":"預訂系統"},{"english":"during a holiday","chinese":"在假期期間"},{"english":"dozens of reservations","chinese":"幾十個預訂"},{"english":"customer complaints","chinese":"顧客投訴"},{"english":"genuinely urgent situations","chinese":"真正緊急的情況"},{"english":"constant availability","chinese":"長期可聯絡狀態"},{"english":"protect a company's operations","chinese":"保障公司營運"},{"english":"far more significant","chinese":"重要得多"},{"english":"at any moment","chinese":"在任何時候"},{"english":"disconnect mentally from work","chinese":"在心理上脫離工作"},{"english":"officially resting","chinese":"正式休息中"},{"english":"attention remains partly fixed on","chinese":"注意力仍部分集中在……"},{"english":"possible messages or calls","chinese":"可能出現的訊息或電話"},{"english":"serve their essential purpose","chinese":"發揮其基本作用"},{"english":"restoring energy","chinese":"恢復精力"},{"english":"relieving stress","chinese":"紓緩壓力"},{"english":"return feeling drained rather than refreshed","chinese":"回來時感到疲憊而不是精神恢復"},{"english":"this culture","chinese":"這種文化"},{"english":"damages commitment to","chinese":"損害對……的投入感"},{"english":"private time","chinese":"私人時間"},{"english":"repeatedly interrupted","chinese":"被反覆打斷"},{"english":"personal boundaries","chinese":"個人界線"},{"english":"not respected","chinese":"不被尊重"},{"english":"breeds resentment","chinese":"滋生怨氣"},{"english":"reduces loyalty","chinese":"降低忠誠度"},{"english":"cooperate at first","chinese":"起初配合"},{"english":"repeated intrusion","chinese":"反覆侵擾"},{"english":"eventually lead to","chinese":"最終導致"},{"english":"burnout","chinese":"職業倦怠"},{"english":"resignation","chinese":"辭職"},{"english":"higher recruitment costs","chinese":"更高招聘成本"},{"english":"weaker team stability","chinese":"較弱的團隊穩定性"},{"english":"lower productivity","chinese":"較低生產力"},{"english":"deal with emergencies","chinese":"處理緊急情況"},{"english":"a negative development overall","chinese":"整體而言是負面發展"},{"english":"limited operational advantage","chinese":"有限的營運好處"},{"english":"decisively outweighed by","chinese":"明顯被……超過"},{"english":"damage done to","chinese":"對……造成的傷害"},{"english":"workers' wellbeing","chinese":"員工身心健康"},{"english":"sustainable performance","chinese":"可持續表現"},{"english":"the organisation itself","chinese":"機構本身"}]},"model-essay-27-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-27-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:27","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-27-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q27","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"As life expectancy rises, care for people in their nineties is becoming a pressing social issue. Although family affection is valuable, I believe the responsibility for elderly care should rest with the government rather than with individual families, because old age now requires organised medical, financial, and social support that private households often cannot provide.","chinese":"隨著預期壽命上升，照顧九十多歲的人正成為一個迫切的社會問題。 儘管家庭親情很有價值，我認為照顧長者的責任應該落在政府身上，而不是個別家庭身上，因為如今的老年階段需要有組織的醫療、財政和社會支援，而私人家庭往往無法提供這些支援。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that modern elderly care is far too complex to be left to relatives. A person in their nineties may need daily nursing, medicine management, home modifications, physiotherapy, and transport to hospitals. Most adult children are already juggling jobs, mortgages, and their own children, so expecting them to deliver professional care can damage both the older person’s health and the carer’s livelihood. For instance, if an elderly woman develops dementia, goodwill from her family cannot replace trained carers, safe facilities, and regular medical supervision. Government-funded services, by contrast, can provide a reliable safety net through hospitals, community nurses, subsidised residential homes, and pensions.","chinese":"第一個原因是，現代長者照護太複雜，不能只交給親屬負責。 一位九十多歲的長者可能需要日常護理、藥物管理、家居改裝、物理治療，以及往返醫院的交通安排。 大多數成年子女已經要同時應付工作、按揭和自己的孩子，因此期望他們提供專業照護，可能同時損害長者的健康和照顧者的生計。 例如，如果一位年長女性患上認知障礙症，家人的善意並不能取代受過訓練的照顧者、安全的設施和定期的醫療監督。 相比之下，由政府資助的服務可以透過醫院、社區護士、受資助的安老院舍和退休金，提供一張可靠的安全網。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is fairness. If care depends mainly on family, elderly people with no children, distant relatives, or poor households are punished for circumstances beyond their control, while those from wealthier families are more likely to age with dignity. A government system can set minimum standards, inspect care homes, offer home-care subsidies, and protect older people from neglect or financial exploitation. For example, a widower whose children live overseas should still be able to receive basic support, safe accommodation, and medical attention. In this sense, elderly care is not merely a private family matter; it is part of the social contract. People who have contributed to society throughout their working lives should not be abandoned when frailty arrives.","chinese":"另一個原因是公平。 如果照護主要依賴家庭，那麼沒有子女、親屬疏遠或家境貧困的長者，便會因一些他們無法控制的情況而受到懲罰；相反，來自較富裕家庭的人則更有可能有尊嚴地老去。 政府制度可以設立最低標準、巡查安老院舍、提供家居照護津貼，並保護長者免受忽視或財務剝削。 例如，一位子女住在海外的鰥夫，仍然應該能夠獲得基本支援、安全住所和醫療照顧。 從這個意義上說，長者照護不僅僅是私人家庭事務；它是社會契約的一部分。 那些在整個工作生涯中為社會作出貢獻的人，不應該在身體變得虛弱時被遺棄。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, families should remain emotionally involved, but the responsibility for caring for elderly citizens should belong to the government. Family love can provide warmth, but only public systems can provide consistent, regulated, and equitable care.","chinese":"總結來說，家庭應該繼續在情感上參與其中，但照顧年長公民的責任應該屬於政府。 家庭的愛可以提供溫暖，但只有公共制度才能提供持續、受監管且公平的照護。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"life expectancy rises","chinese":"預期壽命上升"},{"english":"people in their nineties","chinese":"九十多歲人士"},{"english":"a pressing social issue","chinese":"迫切的社會議題"},{"english":"family affection","chinese":"家庭感情"},{"english":"the responsibility for elderly care","chinese":"照顧長者的責任"},{"english":"should rest with","chinese":"應由……承擔"},{"english":"rather than with","chinese":"而不是由……"},{"english":"individual families","chinese":"個別家庭"},{"english":"old age","chinese":"老年階段"},{"english":"organised medical, financial, and social support","chinese":"有組織的醫療、財務和社會支援"},{"english":"private households","chinese":"私人家庭"},{"english":"the first reason","chinese":"第一個原因"},{"english":"modern elderly care","chinese":"現代長者照顧"},{"english":"far too complex to","chinese":"太複雜以致不能"},{"english":"be left to relatives","chinese":"留給親屬負責"},{"english":"daily nursing","chinese":"日常護理"},{"english":"medicine management","chinese":"藥物管理"},{"english":"home modifications","chinese":"家居改裝"},{"english":"physiotherapy","chinese":"物理治療"},{"english":"transport to hospitals","chinese":"前往醫院的交通安排"},{"english":"adult children","chinese":"成年子女"},{"english":"juggling jobs, mortgages, and their own children","chinese":"同時兼顧工作、按揭和自己的子女"},{"english":"expecting them to","chinese":"期望他們去"},{"english":"deliver professional care","chinese":"提供專業照顧"},{"english":"damage both...and...","chinese":"同時損害……和……"},{"english":"the older person's health","chinese":"長者的健康"},{"english":"the carer's livelihood","chinese":"照顧者的生計"},{"english":"develops dementia","chinese":"患上認知障礙症"},{"english":"goodwill from her family","chinese":"家人的善意"},{"english":"cannot replace","chinese":"不能取代"},{"english":"trained carers","chinese":"受過訓練的照顧者"},{"english":"safe facilities","chinese":"安全設施"},{"english":"regular medical supervision","chinese":"定期醫療監察"},{"english":"government-funded services","chinese":"政府資助服務"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"a reliable safety net","chinese":"可靠的安全網"},{"english":"community nurses","chinese":"社區護士"},{"english":"subsidised residential homes","chinese":"資助安老院舍"},{"english":"pensions","chinese":"退休金；養老金"},{"english":"another reason is fairness","chinese":"另一個原因是公平"},{"english":"depends mainly on","chinese":"主要取決於"},{"english":"distant relatives","chinese":"關係疏遠的親屬"},{"english":"poor households","chinese":"貧困家庭"},{"english":"be punished for","chinese":"因……而受懲罰"},{"english":"circumstances beyond their control","chinese":"他們無法控制的情況"},{"english":"wealthier families","chinese":"較富裕的家庭"},{"english":"more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"age with dignity","chinese":"有尊嚴地老去"},{"english":"government system","chinese":"政府制度"},{"english":"set minimum standards","chinese":"訂立最低標準"},{"english":"inspect care homes","chinese":"巡查護老院"},{"english":"home-care subsidies","chinese":"家居照顧津貼"},{"english":"protect older people from","chinese":"保護長者免受……影響"},{"english":"neglect","chinese":"忽視；疏忽照顧"},{"english":"financial exploitation","chinese":"財務剝削"},{"english":"a widower","chinese":"鰥夫"},{"english":"live overseas","chinese":"居於海外"},{"english":"basic support","chinese":"基本支援"},{"english":"safe accommodation","chinese":"安全住所"},{"english":"medical attention","chinese":"醫療照顧"},{"english":"In this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"not merely a private family matter","chinese":"不只是私人家庭事務"},{"english":"the social contract","chinese":"社會契約"},{"english":"contributed to society","chinese":"為社會作出貢獻"},{"english":"throughout their working lives","chinese":"在整個工作生涯中"},{"english":"should not be abandoned","chinese":"不應被遺棄"},{"english":"frailty arrives","chinese":"身體衰弱來臨"},{"english":"remain emotionally involved","chinese":"保持情感上的參與"},{"english":"caring for elderly citizens","chinese":"照顧長者市民"},{"english":"should belong to","chinese":"應屬於"},{"english":"family love","chinese":"家庭關愛"},{"english":"provide warmth","chinese":"提供溫暖"},{"english":"public systems","chinese":"公共制度"},{"english":"consistent, regulated, and equitable care","chinese":"持續、受規管而公平的照顧"}]},"model-essay-27-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-27-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:27","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-27-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q27","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Corporate sponsorship has become a familiar part of modern sport, from logos on team shirts to branded stadiums and televised tournaments. While some people worry that this turns sport into a marketing tool, I firmly believe that company sponsorship is a positive development because it gives athletes and sporting organisations the financial support they need.","chinese":"企業贊助已成為現代體育中常見的一部分，從球隊球衣上的標誌，到冠名體育場和電視轉播賽事皆是如此。 雖然有些人擔心這會把體育變成一種行銷工具， 我堅定認為，公司贊助是一種正面的發展，因為它為運動員和體育組織提供了他們所需要的財政支持。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"There are clear reasons why many people welcome this practice. Sport is expensive to run, especially when clubs have to pay for coaching, equipment, travel, medical support and safe facilities. Without commercial backing, many smaller teams and young athletes would struggle to train properly, let alone compete at a high level. For example, a local basketball club that receives money from a company may be able to buy better equipment, reduce membership fees and send its players to regional competitions. In this way, sponsorship does not merely advertise a brand; it can open the door to wider participation and better performance.","chinese":"人們歡迎這種做法有明顯的原因。 體育運作成本高昂，尤其是當俱樂部需要支付教練、設備、交通、醫療支援和安全設施的費用時。 如果沒有商業支持，許多較小型的隊伍和年輕運動員將難以進行適當訓練，更不用說在高水平比賽中競爭。 例如，一間獲得公司資助的本地籃球俱樂部，可能便能購買更好的設備、降低會員費，並派球員參加地區比賽。 這樣一來，贊助並不只是為品牌做廣告；它還能為更廣泛的參與和更好的表現打開大門"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, the disadvantages should not be ignored. When sponsorship becomes too dominant, sport can lose some of its original spirit. A team’s identity may be buried under logos, and young fans may start to associate athletic success with products that are not always healthy or appropriate. This is particularly concerning when fast food, sugary drinks or gambling companies use popular athletes as a shortcut into the minds of children. In addition, clubs may feel pressure to please sponsors instead of making decisions based purely on sporting values. Even so, these problems are best solved through sensible rules rather than by rejecting sponsorship altogether.","chinese":"然而，這種做法的缺點也不應被忽視。 當贊助變得過於主導時，體育可能會失去一部分原本的精神。 一支隊伍的身份可能會被各種標誌掩蓋，而年輕球迷也可能開始把運動成就與一些並不總是健康或合適的產品聯繫起來。 當快餐、含糖飲品或博彩公司利用受歡迎的運動員作為進入兒童心智的捷徑時，這一點尤其令人擔憂。 此外，俱樂部可能會感到壓力，要取悅贊助商，而不是純粹根據體育價值作出決定。 即便如此，這些問題最好透過合理規則來解決，而不是完全拒絕贊助。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, although corporate sponsorship can commercialise sport and create ethical concerns, I believe its advantages are far greater. If advertising is regulated carefully, sponsorship can act as vital fuel for sport, helping athletes, clubs and communities grow.","chinese":"總結來說，儘管企業贊助可能使體育商業化，並帶來道德方面的疑慮，我認為它的優點遠遠更大。 如果廣告受到仔細規管，贊助便可以成為體育的重要燃料，幫助運動員、俱樂部和社區成長。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"corporate sponsorship","chinese":"企業贊助"},{"english":"a familiar part of","chinese":"……中常見的一部分"},{"english":"modern sport","chinese":"現代體育"},{"english":"logos on team shirts","chinese":"球衣上的標誌"},{"english":"branded stadiums","chinese":"品牌冠名球場"},{"english":"televised tournaments","chinese":"電視轉播賽事"},{"english":"turn sport into","chinese":"將體育變成"},{"english":"a marketing tool","chinese":"市場推廣工具"},{"english":"firmly believe that","chinese":"堅信"},{"english":"company sponsorship","chinese":"公司贊助"},{"english":"a positive development","chinese":"正面發展"},{"english":"sporting organisations","chinese":"體育組織"},{"english":"financial support","chinese":"財政支持"},{"english":"there are clear reasons why","chinese":"有明確原因解釋為何"},{"english":"welcome this practice","chinese":"歡迎這種做法"},{"english":"expensive to run","chinese":"營運成本高"},{"english":"have to pay for","chinese":"需要支付"},{"english":"medical support","chinese":"醫療支援"},{"english":"safe facilities","chinese":"安全設施"},{"english":"commercial backing","chinese":"商業支持"},{"english":"smaller teams","chinese":"較小型的隊伍"},{"english":"young athletes","chinese":"年輕運動員"},{"english":"struggle to train properly","chinese":"難以接受適當訓練"},{"english":"let alone","chinese":"更不用說"},{"english":"compete at a high level","chinese":"參與高水平比賽"},{"english":"a local basketball club","chinese":"本地籃球會"},{"english":"receive money from","chinese":"從……獲得資金"},{"english":"buy better equipment","chinese":"購買更好的裝備"},{"english":"reduce membership fees","chinese":"降低會員費"},{"english":"send its players to","chinese":"派其球員參加"},{"english":"regional competitions","chinese":"區域賽事"},{"english":"in this way","chinese":"這樣一來"},{"english":"does not merely advertise","chinese":"不只是宣傳"},{"english":"advertise a brand","chinese":"宣傳品牌"},{"english":"open the door to","chinese":"為……打開大門"},{"english":"wider participation","chinese":"更廣泛參與"},{"english":"better performance","chinese":"更佳表現"},{"english":"the disadvantages should not be ignored","chinese":"不應忽視缺點"},{"english":"become too dominant","chinese":"變得過於主導"},{"english":"lose some of its original spirit","chinese":"失去部分原本精神"},{"english":"a team's identity","chinese":"隊伍身份"},{"english":"be buried under","chinese":"被……掩蓋"},{"english":"young fans","chinese":"年輕粉絲"},{"english":"associate athletic success with","chinese":"將運動成功與……聯繫起來"},{"english":"athletic success","chinese":"運動成就"},{"english":"not always healthy or appropriate","chinese":"不一定健康或合適"},{"english":"particularly concerning","chinese":"尤其令人擔心"},{"english":"fast food","chinese":"快餐"},{"english":"sugary drinks","chinese":"高糖飲品"},{"english":"gambling companies","chinese":"博彩公司"},{"english":"popular athletes","chinese":"受歡迎的運動員"},{"english":"as a shortcut into","chinese":"作為進入……的捷徑"},{"english":"the minds of children","chinese":"兒童的思想"},{"english":"in addition","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"feel pressure to","chinese":"感到有壓力去"},{"english":"please sponsors","chinese":"取悅贊助商"},{"english":"instead of making decisions based purely on","chinese":"而不是純粹基於……作決定"},{"english":"sporting values","chinese":"體育價值"},{"english":"even so","chinese":"即使如此"},{"english":"be best solved through","chinese":"最好透過……解決"},{"english":"sensible rules","chinese":"合理規則"},{"english":"rather than by rejecting","chinese":"而不是透過拒絕"},{"english":"rejecting sponsorship altogether","chinese":"完全拒絕贊助"},{"english":"commercialise sport","chinese":"令體育商業化"},{"english":"create ethical concerns","chinese":"引起道德憂慮"},{"english":"advantages are far greater","chinese":"優點大得多"},{"english":"be regulated carefully","chinese":"被審慎監管"},{"english":"act as vital fuel for","chinese":"作為……的重要燃料"},{"english":"helping athletes, clubs and communities grow","chinese":"幫助運動員、球會和社區成長"}]},"model-essay-27-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-27-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:27","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-27-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q27","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Crime prevention and criminal investigation have been transformed by modern technology. I strongly agree that crime rates are generally lower than in the past because today’s digital tools make offences harder to commit and much easier to solve.","chinese":"犯罪預防和刑事調查已被現代科技徹底改變。 我強烈同意，犯罪率整體上比過去更低，因為現今的數位工具令犯罪更難實施，也令破案容易得多。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that technology can stop many crimes before they happen. In the past, criminals often acted with little fear of being identified, especially in quiet streets, shops, car parks, or residential areas. Today, however, surveillance cameras, alarm systems, biometric locks, and mobile security apps have changed that completely. A thief who sees cameras outside a building or knows that an alarm will immediately alert the owner is far less likely to take the risk. For example, many modern shops now use CCTV and electronic tags, so stealing goods is no longer as simple as walking out unnoticed. This constant possibility of being recorded creates a powerful deterrent, which reduces everyday crimes such as theft, vandalism, and burglary.","chinese":"第一個原因是，科技可以在許多罪案發生之前便加以阻止。 在過去，罪犯行事時往往不太害怕被識別出來，尤其是在安靜的街道、商店、停車場或住宅區。 然而，今天監控攝影機、警報系統、生物識別門鎖和手機保安應用程式已完全改變了這種情況。 一個小偷如果看到建築物外有攝影機，或者知道警報會立即通知業主，就遠不太可能冒這個風險。 例如，許多現代商店現在都使用閉路電視和電子標籤，因此偷取貨物已不再像在無人察覺下走出去那麼簡單。 這種隨時可能被錄下來的可能性形成了強大的阻嚇作用，從而減少盜竊、破壞公物和入屋爆竊等日常罪案。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Technology also helps the police solve crimes more quickly and accurately. Modern investigations no longer depend only on eyewitnesses, who may forget details or give unreliable accounts. Instead, officers can use DNA testing, fingerprint databases, phone records, GPS tracking, and digital footprints to identify suspects. For instance, if someone steals a car, the vehicle may be tracked through a GPS system, while nearby cameras can show where the thief went. Similarly, online fraudsters often leave behind bank records, IP addresses, or message histories. When criminals know that their actions can leave a trail, they are less willing to offend in the first place. This means technology not only catches offenders after a crime, but also discourages others from copying them.","chinese":"科技也幫助警方更快速、更準確地偵破罪案。 現代調查不再只依賴目擊者，因為他們可能會忘記細節，或者提供不可靠的陳述。 相反，執法人員可以使用DNA測試、指紋資料庫、電話紀錄、GPS追蹤和數位足跡來識別疑犯。 例如，如果有人偷車，該車輛可能可以透過GPS系統被追蹤，而附近的攝影機也可以顯示小偷去了哪裡。 同樣地，網上騙徒往往會留下銀行紀錄、IP地址或訊息紀錄。 當罪犯知道自己的行為可能會留下痕跡時，他們一開始便會較不願意犯罪。 這意味著科技不但能在罪案發生後捉拿犯罪者，也能阻止其他人模仿他們。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully agree that advanced technology has helped reduce crime. By preventing offences and giving the police stronger evidence, it has made crime a much riskier and less attractive choice.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意先進科技已經幫助減少犯罪 透過預防罪案並為警方提供更有力的證據，科技已使犯罪成為一個風險更高、吸引力更低的選擇"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"crime prevention","chinese":"犯罪預防"},{"english":"criminal investigation","chinese":"刑事調查"},{"english":"be transformed by","chinese":"被……徹底改變"},{"english":"modern technology","chinese":"現代科技"},{"english":"crime rates","chinese":"罪案率"},{"english":"generally lower than","chinese":"一般比……低"},{"english":"in the past","chinese":"在過去"},{"english":"digital tools","chinese":"數碼工具"},{"english":"offences","chinese":"罪行"},{"english":"harder to commit","chinese":"更難犯下"},{"english":"easier to solve","chinese":"更容易偵破"},{"english":"stop many crimes before they happen","chinese":"在罪案發生前阻止它們"},{"english":"acted with little fear of","chinese":"幾乎不害怕……地行事"},{"english":"being identified","chinese":"被識別身份"},{"english":"quiet streets","chinese":"僻靜街道"},{"english":"car parks","chinese":"停車場"},{"english":"residential areas","chinese":"住宅區"},{"english":"surveillance cameras","chinese":"監控攝影機"},{"english":"alarm systems","chinese":"警報系統"},{"english":"biometric locks","chinese":"生物識別鎖"},{"english":"mobile security apps","chinese":"手機保安應用程式"},{"english":"alert the owner","chinese":"通知物主"},{"english":"far less likely to","chinese":"可能性低得多"},{"english":"take the risk","chinese":"冒險"},{"english":"CCTV","chinese":"閉路電視"},{"english":"electronic tags","chinese":"電子防盜標籤"},{"english":"stealing goods","chinese":"偷取貨物"},{"english":"walking out unnoticed","chinese":"未被察覺地走出去"},{"english":"constant possibility of","chinese":"……的持續可能性"},{"english":"being recorded","chinese":"被錄影"},{"english":"powerful deterrent","chinese":"強大的阻嚇因素"},{"english":"everyday crimes","chinese":"日常罪案"},{"english":"theft","chinese":"盜竊"},{"english":"vandalism","chinese":"破壞公物"},{"english":"burglary","chinese":"入屋爆竊"},{"english":"solve crimes more quickly and accurately","chinese":"更快速和準確地偵破罪案"},{"english":"modern investigations","chinese":"現代調查"},{"english":"no longer depend only on","chinese":"不再只依賴……"},{"english":"eyewitnesses","chinese":"目擊者"},{"english":"forget details","chinese":"忘記細節"},{"english":"unreliable accounts","chinese":"不可靠的說法"},{"english":"DNA testing","chinese":"DNA 測試"},{"english":"fingerprint databases","chinese":"指紋數據庫"},{"english":"phone records","chinese":"電話紀錄"},{"english":"GPS tracking","chinese":"GPS 追蹤"},{"english":"digital footprints","chinese":"數碼足跡"},{"english":"identify suspects","chinese":"識別疑犯"},{"english":"steals a car","chinese":"偷車"},{"english":"be tracked through","chinese":"透過……被追蹤"},{"english":"GPS system","chinese":"GPS 系統"},{"english":"nearby cameras","chinese":"附近的攝影機"},{"english":"where the thief went","chinese":"小偷去了哪裏"},{"english":"online fraudsters","chinese":"網上騙徒"},{"english":"leave behind","chinese":"留下"},{"english":"bank records","chinese":"銀行紀錄"},{"english":"IP addresses","chinese":"IP 地址"},{"english":"message histories","chinese":"訊息紀錄"},{"english":"leave a trail","chinese":"留下痕跡"},{"english":"less willing to offend","chinese":"較不願意犯罪"},{"english":"in the first place","chinese":"一開始；首先"},{"english":"catches offenders","chinese":"捉拿犯事者"},{"english":"discourages others from","chinese":"阻止其他人去……"},{"english":"copying them","chinese":"模仿他們"},{"english":"advanced technology","chinese":"先進科技"},{"english":"helped reduce crime","chinese":"幫助減少犯罪"},{"english":"preventing offences","chinese":"預防罪行"},{"english":"stronger evidence","chinese":"更有力證據"},{"english":"riskier and less attractive choice","chinese":"風險更高且吸引力較低的選擇"}]},"model-essay-28-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-28-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:28","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-28-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q28","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"As populations age and working lives lengthen, many firms are rethinking the composition of their workforce. Recruiting more older employees can certainly create challenges for a business, particularly in relation to labour costs and retraining. Nevertheless, the advantages are clearly greater, because older workers often enhance both the quality of decisions and the stability of the organisation.","chinese":"隨著人口老化，以及人們的工作年期不斷延長，許多公司都開始重新思考其勞動力的組成。 聘用更多年長員工，的確可能為企業帶來一些挑戰，尤其是在勞工成本和再培訓方面。 然而，這樣做的優點顯然更大，因為年長員工往往能提升決策的質素，以及整個組織的穩定性。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first major benefit is the depth of judgement that experienced staff can bring to a company. Having dealt with clients, deadlines and workplace problems for many years, older employees are often better at recognising risks before they become costly mistakes. A seasoned purchasing manager, for example, may detect signs that a supplier is unreliable and change vendors early, thereby preventing delays in production. Older recruits can also raise the performance of others, because their professional discipline and communication skills make them effective mentors. A veteran sales executive who coaches new hires in negotiation and client handling can shorten the adjustment period for an entire team. Consequently, the firm gains not only one capable employee, but also a more competent and resilient workforce.","chinese":"第一個主要優點，是有經驗的員工能為公司帶來更成熟、更有深度的判斷力。 由於多年來一直處理客戶、期限以及各種職場問題，年長員工往往更善於在風險演變成代價高昂的錯誤之前，及早察覺問題。 這代表他們能更早發現警號、及時採取預防措施，從而避免公司承受不必要的損失或運作上的混亂。 例如，一位資深採購經理可能會及早察覺某供應商不可靠的跡象，並提早更換供應商，從而防止生產延誤。 年長的新聘員工也能提升其他同事的表現，因為他們的專業紀律與溝通能力，使他們成為有效的指導者。 當較年輕的員工得到資深同事的指導時，他們通常能更快適應工作、避免常見錯誤，並在更短時間內達到工作成效。 例如，一位資深銷售主管若指導新員工如何談判及處理客戶關係，便能縮短整個團隊的適應期。 因此，公司得到的不只是單一一位能幹的員工，而是一支更有能力、也更有韌性的團隊。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"There are, however, some disadvantages. One is that older recruits may command higher salaries and better benefits, which can place pressure on payroll budgets, especially in smaller firms. If a start-up hires several highly experienced managers at once, its wage bill may rise faster than its revenue. Another drawback is that, in companies undergoing rapid digital change, some older employees may initially require more support when adapting to newly introduced platforms. For instance, a business that replaces paper-based systems with cloud software may need to provide extra training before output returns to normal. Even so, these are managerial challenges rather than compelling reasons to avoid older applicants.","chinese":"然而，這樣做也確實存在一些缺點。 其中一個缺點是，年長員工往往要求較高薪酬和較佳福利，這可能會對薪酬預算造成壓力，尤其是對小型企業而言。 如果人力成本上升得太快，公司便可能較難把資金投放於擴張、科技或其他營運需要之上。 例如，一間初創公司若一下子聘請多位高經驗的經理，其薪資開支的增長速度便可能快於收入增長。 另一個缺點是，在正經歷快速數碼轉型的公司中，一些年長員工在適應新引入的平台時，初期可能需要更多支援。 這可能會暫時拖慢工作流程、增加培訓需求，並使管理層需要投入更多時間，之後生產力才可恢復至原有水平。 例如，一間把紙本系統改為雲端軟件的公司，可能需要提供額外培訓，之後工作產出才會回復正常。 即使如此，這些仍只是管理上的挑戰，而不是足以令公司避免聘請年長求職者的有力理由。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, employing more older people can increase expenditure and create short-term training demands, but the benefits for companies are clearly greater. Their experience, reliability and positive influence on younger staff usually generate greater long-term value, particularly in roles that depend on judgement, trust and continuity. For this reason, more companies should be willing to recruit them.","chinese":"總括而言，聘用更多年長人士的確可能增加開支，並帶來短期培訓需求，但對公司來說，其優點顯然更大。 他們的經驗、可靠性，以及對年輕員工的正面影響，通常能帶來更高的長遠價值，尤其是在那些依賴判斷力、信任和持續性的職位中。 基於這一點，更多公司都應該更願意聘用年長員工。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"populations age","chinese":"人口老化"},{"english":"working lives lengthen","chinese":"工作年期延長"},{"english":"many firms","chinese":"許多公司"},{"english":"rethinking the composition of","chinese":"重新思考……的組成"},{"english":"workforce","chinese":"勞動力；員工隊伍"},{"english":"recruiting more older employees","chinese":"招聘更多年長員工"},{"english":"create challenges for","chinese":"為……帶來挑戰"},{"english":"particularly in relation to","chinese":"尤其與……有關"},{"english":"labour costs","chinese":"勞工成本"},{"english":"retraining","chinese":"再培訓"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"clearly greater","chinese":"明顯更大"},{"english":"enhance both...and...","chinese":"同時提升……和……"},{"english":"the quality of decisions","chinese":"決策質素"},{"english":"the stability of the organisation","chinese":"組織的穩定性"},{"english":"the first major benefit","chinese":"第一個主要好處"},{"english":"the depth of judgement","chinese":"深厚的判斷力"},{"english":"experienced staff","chinese":"經驗豐富的員工"},{"english":"bring to a company","chinese":"為公司帶來"},{"english":"having dealt with","chinese":"曾經處理過"},{"english":"deadlines","chinese":"截止期限"},{"english":"workplace problems","chinese":"工作場所問題"},{"english":"be better at recognising risks","chinese":"更善於識別風險"},{"english":"costly mistakes","chinese":"代價高昂的錯誤"},{"english":"a seasoned purchasing manager","chinese":"經驗老到的採購經理"},{"english":"detect signs that","chinese":"察覺……的跡象"},{"english":"a supplier is unreliable","chinese":"供應商不可靠"},{"english":"change vendors early","chinese":"及早更換供應商"},{"english":"thereby preventing","chinese":"從而防止"},{"english":"delays in production","chinese":"生產延誤"},{"english":"older recruits","chinese":"年長新聘員工"},{"english":"raise the performance of","chinese":"提升……的表現"},{"english":"professional discipline","chinese":"專業紀律"},{"english":"communication skills","chinese":"溝通技巧"},{"english":"effective mentors","chinese":"有效的導師"},{"english":"a veteran sales executive","chinese":"資深銷售主管"},{"english":"coaches new hires in","chinese":"指導新員工……"},{"english":"new hires","chinese":"新入職員工"},{"english":"negotiation","chinese":"談判"},{"english":"client handling","chinese":"客戶處理"},{"english":"shorten the adjustment period","chinese":"縮短適應期"},{"english":"an entire team","chinese":"整個團隊"},{"english":"consequently","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"capable employee","chinese":"有能力的員工"},{"english":"a more competent and resilient workforce","chinese":"更有能力和抗逆力的員工隊伍"},{"english":"there are, however, some disadvantages","chinese":"然而，也有一些缺點"},{"english":"command higher salaries","chinese":"要求較高薪酬"},{"english":"better benefits","chinese":"更好的福利"},{"english":"place pressure on","chinese":"對……造成壓力"},{"english":"payroll budgets","chinese":"薪酬預算"},{"english":"smaller firms","chinese":"較小型公司"},{"english":"at once","chinese":"一次過；同時；立即"},{"english":"wage bill","chinese":"工資開支"},{"english":"rise faster than","chinese":"增長得比……快"},{"english":"undergoing rapid digital change","chinese":"正經歷快速數碼轉型"},{"english":"initially require more support","chinese":"起初需要更多支援"},{"english":"adapting to","chinese":"適應"},{"english":"newly introduced platforms","chinese":"新引入的平台"},{"english":"paper-based systems","chinese":"紙本系統"},{"english":"cloud software","chinese":"雲端軟件"},{"english":"provide extra training","chinese":"提供額外培訓"},{"english":"output returns to normal","chinese":"產出回復正常"},{"english":"even so","chinese":"即使如此"},{"english":"managerial challenges","chinese":"管理上的挑戰"},{"english":"compelling reasons to avoid","chinese":"避免……的有力理由"},{"english":"older applicants","chinese":"年長申請者"},{"english":"employing more older people","chinese":"聘用更多年長人士"},{"english":"increase expenditure","chinese":"增加開支"},{"english":"short-term training demands","chinese":"短期培訓需求"},{"english":"reliability","chinese":"可靠性"},{"english":"positive influence on","chinese":"對……的正面影響"},{"english":"generate greater long-term value","chinese":"創造更大的長遠價值"},{"english":"roles that depend on","chinese":"依賴……的職位"},{"english":"judgement, trust and continuity","chinese":"判斷力、信任和延續性"},{"english":"be willing to recruit","chinese":"願意招聘"}]},"model-essay-28-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-28-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:28","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-28-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q28","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In modern societies, governments often try to influence how citizens eat, travel, work and spend their leisure time. While public authorities have a legitimate duty to provide information and protect citizens from direct harm, lifestyle choices should ultimately be made by individuals themselves. This essay will argue that personal autonomy and practical effectiveness make individual decision-making the better approach.","chinese":"在現代社會中，政府經常試圖影響公民如何飲食、出行、工作，以及度過休閒時間。 雖然公共當局有正當責任提供資訊，並保護公民免受直接傷害，但生活方式的選擇最終應由個人自己作出。 本文將論證，個人自主和實際有效性使個人自行決策成為更好的做法。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason is that lifestyle is closely tied to personal freedom, identity and dignity. People differ widely in their values, health conditions, incomes, family duties and cultural habits, so a single government standard is unlikely to suit everyone. If the state decides how citizens should live, ordinary preferences can quickly be treated as social problems, and adults may be reduced to passive subjects rather than responsible human beings. For example, a diet that is sensible for a young athlete may be unsuitable for an elderly diabetic, while a work routine that suits one family may damage another. When lifestyle decisions are made by individuals, people can adapt general advice to their own circumstances instead of being trapped in a one-size-fits-all system.","chinese":"最有力的原因是，生活方式與個人自由、身份認同和尊嚴密切相關。 人們在價值觀、健康狀況、收入、家庭責任和文化習慣方面差異很大，因此單一的政府標準不太可能適合所有人。 如果國家決定公民應該如何生活，普通的個人偏好很快就可能被視為社會問題，而成年人也可能被降低為被動服從的對象，而不是有責任感的人。 例如，對年輕運動員來說合理的飲食，可能並不適合一位年長的糖尿病患者；而適合某個家庭的工作安排，也可能傷害另一個家庭。 當生活方式的決定由個人作出時，人們便能根據自己的情況調整一般性的建議，而不是被困在一套一體適用的制度之中。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important point is that personal choice is usually more effective than official control. Healthy behaviour rarely lasts when it is imposed from above; it becomes sustainable when people understand the reason for it and choose it for themselves. A government may ban certain habits or dictate certain routines, but such pressure can create resentment, superficial compliance and even resistance. By contrast, policies such as clear food labels, public health education, safe parks and affordable sports facilities help people make wiser choices without taking ownership away from them. In this sense, the state should light the path, not drag citizens along it.","chinese":"另一個重要觀點是，個人選擇通常比官方控制更有效。 當健康行為是由上而下強加時，它很少能夠持久；當人們理解其原因並自行選擇時，它才會變得可持續。 政府也許可以禁止某些習慣，或規定某些日常安排，但這種壓力可能會引起怨氣、表面服從，甚至反抗。 相比之下，清晰的食品標籤、公共健康教育、安全的公園和價格合理的運動設施等政策，能幫助人們作出更明智的選擇，而不會剝奪他們對自己生活的主導權。 從這個意義上說，國家應該照亮道路，而不是拖著公民沿路前行。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, people should make their own lifestyle decisions. Governments should inform, warn and support, but the final choice about how to live must remain with the individual.","chinese":"總結來說，人們應該自行作出自己的生活方式決定。 政府應該提供資訊、作出提醒並給予支援，但關於如何生活的最終選擇，必須留在個人手中。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"modern societies","chinese":"現代社會"},{"english":"try to influence","chinese":"嘗試影響"},{"english":"how citizens eat, travel, work and spend their leisure time","chinese":"市民如何飲食、出行、工作和消閒"},{"english":"public authorities","chinese":"公共機關"},{"english":"a legitimate duty to","chinese":"合法而正當的責任去"},{"english":"provide information","chinese":"提供資料"},{"english":"protect citizens from","chinese":"保護市民免受……影響"},{"english":"direct harm","chinese":"直接傷害"},{"english":"lifestyle choices","chinese":"生活方式選擇"},{"english":"ultimately","chinese":"最終"},{"english":"be made by individuals themselves","chinese":"由個人自己作出"},{"english":"personal autonomy","chinese":"個人自主"},{"english":"practical effectiveness","chinese":"實際成效"},{"english":"individual decision-making","chinese":"個人決策"},{"english":"the better approach","chinese":"更好的方法"},{"english":"the strongest reason","chinese":"最有力的原因"},{"english":"closely tied to","chinese":"與……密切相關"},{"english":"personal freedom","chinese":"個人自由"},{"english":"identity and dignity","chinese":"身份認同和尊嚴"},{"english":"differ widely in","chinese":"在……方面有很大差異"},{"english":"values","chinese":"價值觀"},{"english":"health conditions","chinese":"健康狀況"},{"english":"family duties","chinese":"家庭責任"},{"english":"cultural habits","chinese":"文化習慣"},{"english":"a single government standard","chinese":"單一政府標準"},{"english":"unlikely to suit everyone","chinese":"不太可能適合所有人"},{"english":"the state decides","chinese":"國家決定"},{"english":"ordinary preferences","chinese":"普通個人偏好"},{"english":"be treated as social problems","chinese":"被視為社會問題"},{"english":"be reduced to","chinese":"被貶低為"},{"english":"passive subjects","chinese":"被動的受管對象"},{"english":"responsible human beings","chinese":"負責任的人"},{"english":"a diet that is sensible for","chinese":"對……合理的飲食"},{"english":"young athlete","chinese":"年輕運動員"},{"english":"unsuitable for","chinese":"不適合"},{"english":"elderly diabetic","chinese":"患糖尿病的長者"},{"english":"work routine","chinese":"工作規律"},{"english":"suits one family","chinese":"適合一個家庭"},{"english":"damage another","chinese":"損害另一個"},{"english":"adapt general advice to","chinese":"按照……調整一般建議"},{"english":"own circumstances","chinese":"自身情況"},{"english":"instead of being trapped in","chinese":"而不是被困在"},{"english":"a one-size-fits-all system","chinese":"一刀切制度"},{"english":"personal choice","chinese":"個人選擇"},{"english":"more effective than","chinese":"比……更有效"},{"english":"official control","chinese":"官方控制"},{"english":"healthy behaviour","chinese":"健康行為"},{"english":"rarely lasts","chinese":"很少能持久"},{"english":"be imposed from above","chinese":"由上而下強加"},{"english":"becomes sustainable","chinese":"變得可持續"},{"english":"understand the reason for","chinese":"明白……的原因"},{"english":"choose it for themselves","chinese":"自己選擇它"},{"english":"ban certain habits","chinese":"禁止某些習慣"},{"english":"dictate certain routines","chinese":"規定某些日常安排"},{"english":"such pressure","chinese":"這種壓力"},{"english":"create resentment","chinese":"造成怨氣"},{"english":"superficial compliance","chinese":"表面服從"},{"english":"resistance","chinese":"抗拒"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"clear food labels","chinese":"清晰食物標籤"},{"english":"public health education","chinese":"公共健康教育"},{"english":"safe parks","chinese":"安全公園"},{"english":"affordable sports facilities","chinese":"負擔得起的運動設施"},{"english":"make wiser choices","chinese":"作出更明智的選擇"},{"english":"without taking ownership away from","chinese":"不奪走……的自主權"},{"english":"taking ownership","chinese":"承擔自主責任"},{"english":"light the path","chinese":"照亮道路"},{"english":"drag citizens along it","chinese":"拖着市民沿路走"},{"english":"make their own lifestyle decisions","chinese":"作出自己的生活方式決定"},{"english":"inform, warn and support","chinese":"提供資訊、警告和支援"},{"english":"the final choice about","chinese":"關於……的最終選擇"},{"english":"remain with the individual","chinese":"留給個人"}]},"model-essay-28-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-28-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:28","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-28-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q28","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Photographs have become a powerful part of modern journalism, with newspapers and television channels using images to make stories more immediate and persuasive. While some people believe that photographs cannot always be trusted, others argue that they provide undeniable evidence of what has happened. I will discuss both views, but I firmly believe that photographs should be treated as supporting evidence rather than irrefutable proof.","chinese":"照片已經成為現代新聞業中一個強而有力的部分，報紙和電視頻道都會使用圖像，使新聞故事更即時、更具說服力。 雖然有些人認為照片並不總是值得信任，但另一些人則認為照片提供了事情已經發生的不可否認的證據。 我將討論雙方觀點，但我堅定地認為，照片應被視為輔助證據，而不是無可反駁的證明"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Those who distrust photographs have strong reasons for doing so. A picture may appear objective, but it can easily mislead the public if it is edited, cropped, staged, or presented without context. For example, a photograph of an angry protester might suggest violence, even if the wider scene was mostly peaceful. In this way, the camera does not always tell the whole story; it only captures one frozen moment. Moreover, with modern digital tools, images can be altered so convincingly that ordinary readers may struggle to separate fact from manipulation. As a result, relying on photographs alone can cause people to form quick but inaccurate judgments.","chinese":"那些不信任照片的人有充分理由這樣做。 一張照片可能看起來客觀，但如果它被編輯、裁剪、擺拍，或在沒有背景資料的情況下呈現，它便很容易誤導公眾。 例如，一張憤怒示威者的照片可能暗示暴力，即使更廣闊的現場其實大部分是和平的。 如此一來，相機並不總是講述完整的故事；它只是捕捉了一個凝固的瞬間。 此外，隨著現代數位工具的發展，圖像可以被修改得非常逼真，以至於普通讀者可能難以分辨事實與操控。 結果是，單靠照片可能會使人們迅速形成判斷，但這些判斷卻可能並不準確。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"On the other hand, many people regard photographs as extremely convincing because they show events in a direct and visible way. Unlike a written report, which depends heavily on the journalist’s wording and interpretation, an image can bring readers face to face with reality. Pictures of natural disasters, wars, or humanitarian crises can reveal suffering more powerfully than paragraphs of description. For instance, a photograph of destroyed homes after an earthquake may immediately communicate the scale of the damage. This is why photographs often act as a wake-up call, making distant events feel real and urgent.","chinese":"另一方面，許多人認為照片極具說服力，因為它們以直接而可見的方式呈現事件。 與書面報道不同，書面報道在很大程度上依賴記者的用詞和詮釋，而圖像則可以讓讀者直接面對現實。 自然災害、戰爭或人道危機的照片，比一段段文字描述更有力地揭示痛苦。 例如，一張地震後房屋被摧毀的照片，可以立即傳達破壞的規模。 這就是為什麼照片經常像一記警鐘，使遙遠的事件變得真實而迫切。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In my view, however, this emotional power is exactly why photographs must be handled carefully. They are valuable, but they are not self-explanatory. Without background information, verification, and responsible reporting, even a genuine image can create a false impression. Therefore, photographs are an important tool in journalism, but they should never be regarded as unquestionable evidence.","chinese":"然而，在我看來，這種情感力量正正是照片必須被謹慎處理的原因。 它們是有價值的，但它們本身並不能自動說明一切。 如果沒有背景資料、核實和負責任的報道，即使是真實的圖像也可能造成錯誤印象。 因此，照片是新聞業中的重要工具，但它們絕不應被視為不容質疑的證據。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"a powerful part of","chinese":"……的重要部分"},{"english":"modern journalism","chinese":"現代新聞業"},{"english":"newspapers and television channels","chinese":"報章和電視頻道"},{"english":"use images to","chinese":"使用圖片去"},{"english":"make stories more immediate and persuasive","chinese":"令新聞故事更即時、更有說服力"},{"english":"cannot always be trusted","chinese":"不一定可信"},{"english":"provide undeniable evidence of","chinese":"提供……的無可否認證據"},{"english":"what has happened","chinese":"發生過的事"},{"english":"discuss both views","chinese":"討論雙方觀點"},{"english":"be treated as","chinese":"被視為；被當作"},{"english":"supporting evidence","chinese":"輔助證據"},{"english":"rather than irrefutable proof","chinese":"而不是無可推翻的證明"},{"english":"irrefutable proof","chinese":"無可推翻的證明"},{"english":"distrust photographs","chinese":"不信任相片"},{"english":"have strong reasons for doing so","chinese":"這樣做有充分理由"},{"english":"appear objective","chinese":"看似客觀"},{"english":"mislead the public","chinese":"誤導公眾"},{"english":"be edited, cropped, staged, or presented without context","chinese":"被修改、裁剪、擺拍或脫離背景呈現"},{"english":"without context","chinese":"沒有背景脈絡"},{"english":"an angry protester","chinese":"憤怒的示威者"},{"english":"suggest violence","chinese":"暗示有暴力"},{"english":"the wider scene","chinese":"更廣闊的場面"},{"english":"mostly peaceful","chinese":"大致和平"},{"english":"in this way","chinese":"以這種方式"},{"english":"tell the whole story","chinese":"說出完整真相"},{"english":"capture one frozen moment","chinese":"捕捉一個凝固的瞬間"},{"english":"modern digital tools","chinese":"現代數碼工具"},{"english":"be altered so convincingly","chinese":"被改動得如此逼真"},{"english":"ordinary readers","chinese":"普通讀者"},{"english":"struggle to separate","chinese":"難以分辨"},{"english":"fact from manipulation","chinese":"事實和操控"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"relying on photographs alone","chinese":"單靠相片"},{"english":"form quick but inaccurate judgments","chinese":"形成快速但不準確的判斷"},{"english":"on the other hand","chinese":"另一方面"},{"english":"regard photographs as","chinese":"將相片視為"},{"english":"extremely convincing","chinese":"極具說服力"},{"english":"in a direct and visible way","chinese":"以直接而可見的方式"},{"english":"unlike a written report","chinese":"不像文字報道"},{"english":"depend heavily on","chinese":"非常依賴"},{"english":"the journalist's wording and interpretation","chinese":"記者的用字和詮釋"},{"english":"bring readers face to face with reality","chinese":"令讀者直接面對現實"},{"english":"natural disasters","chinese":"自然災害"},{"english":"humanitarian crises","chinese":"人道危機"},{"english":"reveal suffering","chinese":"揭示苦難"},{"english":"more powerfully than","chinese":"比……更有力"},{"english":"paragraphs of description","chinese":"大段文字描述"},{"english":"destroyed homes","chinese":"被摧毀的家園"},{"english":"after an earthquake","chinese":"地震之後"},{"english":"immediately communicate","chinese":"立即傳達"},{"english":"the scale of the damage","chinese":"損害的規模"},{"english":"act as a wake-up call","chinese":"發揮警醒作用"},{"english":"distant events","chinese":"遙遠事件"},{"english":"feel real and urgent","chinese":"感覺真實而迫切"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"emotional power","chinese":"情感力量"},{"english":"be handled carefully","chinese":"被謹慎處理"},{"english":"valuable, but not self-explanatory","chinese":"有價值，但不能自行說明一切"},{"english":"background information","chinese":"背景資料"},{"english":"verification","chinese":"核實"},{"english":"responsible reporting","chinese":"負責任的報道"},{"english":"a genuine image","chinese":"真實圖片"},{"english":"create a false impression","chinese":"製造錯誤印象"},{"english":"an important tool in journalism","chinese":"新聞業中的重要工具"},{"english":"never be regarded as","chinese":"絕不應被視為"},{"english":"unquestionable evidence","chinese":"不容置疑的證據"}]},"model-essay-28-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-28-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:28","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-28-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q28","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Crime committed by young people is a serious concern in many communities, especially when the offences are violent or deeply harmful. However, I completely disagree that teenagers who commit major crimes should automatically receive the same punishment as adults, regardless of their age. A just legal system should punish serious wrongdoing firmly, but it should not ignore the offender’s stage of development.","chinese":"年輕人犯罪在許多社區中都是一個嚴重問題，尤其是當這些罪行涉及暴力或造成深遠傷害時。 然而，我完全不同意犯下重大罪行的青少年應該自動接受與成年人相同的懲罰，而不考慮他們的年齡。 公正的法律制度應該堅定地懲罰嚴重的不當行為，但不應忽視犯罪者所處的發展階段"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason is that teenagers are not fully mature in the way adults are. They are generally more impulsive, more vulnerable to peer pressure, and less able to judge long-term consequences. If the law treats a fourteen-year-old and a forty-year-old as identical simply because the offence is serious, punishment becomes a blunt weapon rather than a fair response. For example, a teenager who joins a violent attack because of gang influence may still deserve secure detention, strict supervision, and compensation to the victim. Yet placing that teenager in the adult system ignores the fact that his character is still being formed. Justice should hold him accountable, but it should also leave room for reform.","chinese":"最有力的理由是，青少年並不像成年人那樣完全成熟。 他們通常更衝動、更容易受到朋輩壓力影響，也較不擅長判斷長遠後果。 如果法律僅僅因為罪行嚴重，就把一名十四歲少年和一名四十歲成年人視為完全相同，那麼懲罰就會變成一件鈍器，而不是一種公平的回應。 例如，一名因受幫派影響而參與暴力襲擊的青少年，仍然可能應該接受安全拘留、嚴格監管，並向受害者作出賠償。 然而，把那名青少年放入成人司法系統，便忽視了他的性格仍在形成之中的事實。 司法應該要求他承擔責任，但也應該為改過自新留下空間。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Adult punishment may also make society less safe in the long run. Teenagers sent to adult prisons are likely to lose access to education, family support, and positive role models, while being surrounded by experienced criminals. Instead of correcting their behaviour, the prison environment may teach them how to become more dangerous. When they are released, they may carry a criminal label, have few job prospects, and feel that ordinary society has closed its doors to them. By contrast, a strong youth justice system can combine secure custody with counselling, education, vocational training, and long-term monitoring. That approach protects the public while giving young offenders a realistic path back.","chinese":"從長遠來看，成人懲罰也可能令社會變得更不安全。 被送入成人監獄的青少年，很可能會失去接受教育、獲得家庭支持和接觸正面榜樣的機會，同時被有經驗的罪犯包圍。 監獄環境不但未必能糾正他們的行為，反而可能教會他們如何變得更加危險。 當他們獲釋後，他們可能背負罪犯標籤、缺乏就業前景，並感到正常社會已經向他們關上大門。 相比之下，一個完善的青少年司法制度可以把安全拘留與輔導、教育、職業培訓和長期監察結合起來。 這種做法既能保護公眾，也能給予年輕罪犯一條實際可行的回歸道路。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely disagree with giving teenagers adult punishment regardless of age. Major crimes require serious consequences, but teenage offenders should be dealt with through a separate youth justice system that balances accountability, rehabilitation, and public safety.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全不同意不論年齡都給予青少年成人懲罰。 重大罪行需要嚴重後果，但青少年罪犯應該透過一個獨立的青少年司法制度處理，而這個制度應在問責、改造和公共安全之間取得平衡。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"crime committed by","chinese":"由……犯下的罪行"},{"english":"young people","chinese":"年輕人"},{"english":"serious concern","chinese":"嚴重憂慮"},{"english":"many communities","chinese":"許多社區"},{"english":"offences","chinese":"罪行"},{"english":"violent or deeply harmful","chinese":"暴力或造成深遠傷害"},{"english":"teenagers","chinese":"青少年"},{"english":"commit major crimes","chinese":"犯下嚴重罪行"},{"english":"automatically receive","chinese":"自動受到"},{"english":"same punishment as adults","chinese":"與成年人相同的刑罰"},{"english":"regardless of their age","chinese":"不論他們的年齡"},{"english":"just legal system","chinese":"公正的法律制度"},{"english":"punish serious wrongdoing firmly","chinese":"堅定地懲罰嚴重錯誤行為"},{"english":"serious wrongdoing","chinese":"嚴重錯誤行為"},{"english":"ignore the offender's stage of development","chinese":"忽視犯事者的發展階段"},{"english":"stage of development","chinese":"發展階段"},{"english":"fully mature","chinese":"完全成熟"},{"english":"impulsive","chinese":"衝動"},{"english":"vulnerable to peer pressure","chinese":"容易受同輩壓力影響"},{"english":"peer pressure","chinese":"同輩壓力"},{"english":"less able to judge","chinese":"較不能判斷"},{"english":"long-term consequences","chinese":"長遠後果"},{"english":"treats a fourteen-year-old and a forty-year-old as identical","chinese":"將十四歲和四十歲的人視為一樣"},{"english":"simply because","chinese":"只是因為"},{"english":"blunt weapon","chinese":"粗糙的武器"},{"english":"fair response","chinese":"公平回應"},{"english":"violent attack","chinese":"暴力襲擊"},{"english":"gang influence","chinese":"幫派影響"},{"english":"deserve secure detention","chinese":"應受到安全拘留"},{"english":"secure detention","chinese":"安全拘留"},{"english":"strict supervision","chinese":"嚴格監管"},{"english":"compensation to the victim","chinese":"向受害者作出賠償"},{"english":"adult system","chinese":"成人司法制度"},{"english":"his character is still being formed","chinese":"他的性格仍在形成中"},{"english":"hold him accountable","chinese":"追究他的責任"},{"english":"leave room for reform","chinese":"留有改過空間"},{"english":"make society less safe","chinese":"令社會長遠而言更不安全"},{"english":"in the long run","chinese":"長遠而言"},{"english":"adult prisons","chinese":"成人監獄"},{"english":"be likely to","chinese":"很可能"},{"english":"lose access to","chinese":"失去取得……的機會"},{"english":"positive role models","chinese":"正面榜樣"},{"english":"be surrounded by","chinese":"被……包圍"},{"english":"experienced criminals","chinese":"老練罪犯"},{"english":"correcting their behaviour","chinese":"糾正他們的行為"},{"english":"prison environment","chinese":"監獄環境"},{"english":"criminal label","chinese":"犯罪標籤"},{"english":"job prospects","chinese":"就業前景"},{"english":"ordinary society","chinese":"正常社會"},{"english":"closed its doors to them","chinese":"對他們關上大門"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"youth justice system","chinese":"青少年司法制度"},{"english":"combine secure custody with","chinese":"將安全羈押與……結合"},{"english":"secure custody","chinese":"安全羈押"},{"english":"counselling","chinese":"輔導"},{"english":"vocational training","chinese":"職業培訓"},{"english":"long-term monitoring","chinese":"長期監察"},{"english":"protects the public while","chinese":"在……的同時保護公眾"},{"english":"young offenders","chinese":"青少年犯事者"},{"english":"realistic path back","chinese":"現實可行的回歸途徑"},{"english":"adult punishment","chinese":"成人刑罰"},{"english":"major crimes require serious consequences","chinese":"嚴重罪行需要嚴重後果"},{"english":"serious consequences","chinese":"嚴重後果"},{"english":"teenage offenders","chinese":"青少年犯事者"},{"english":"be dealt with through","chinese":"透過……處理"},{"english":"separate youth justice system","chinese":"獨立的青少年司法制度"},{"english":"balances accountability, rehabilitation, and public safety","chinese":"平衡問責、更生和公共安全"},{"english":"accountability","chinese":"問責"},{"english":"rehabilitation","chinese":"更生"},{"english":"public safety","chinese":"公共安全"}]},"model-essay-29-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-29-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:29","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-29-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q29","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Many families encourage school-age children to take part-time jobs during weekends or school holidays. Such work can offer valuable lessons beyond the classroom. At the same time, it may expose young people to pressures that they are not yet mature enough to manage well.","chinese":"很多家庭會鼓勵學齡兒童在週末或學校假期做兼職工作。 這類工作可以帶來課堂以外的寶貴經驗，但同時也可能讓年輕人面對一些他們尚未成熟到足以妥善處理的壓力。 本文將探討孩子在空閒時間從事兼職工作的優點與缺點。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One important advantage is that paid work can foster responsibility and financial awareness. When children are expected to arrive on time, follow instructions and earn their own wages, they begin to understand that money is linked to effort rather than simply provided on demand. For example, a teenager who spends a few hours each week working in a café may become far more careful about unnecessary spending. Another benefit is that part-time employment can build practical skills that schools do not always teach directly. By serving customers, cooperating with co-workers and solving small problems under pressure, young people can develop confidence, communication skills and better time management, all of which are likely to be useful in adult life.","chinese":"兼職工作的一個重要優點是，它能培養責任感和金錢觀念。 當孩子被要求準時上班、遵從指示並靠自己賺取薪水時，他們便會開始明白，金錢是與付出和努力連在一起的，而不是理所當然地隨時可得。 這有助於他們變得更有紀律、更理性地看待花費，也更懂得珍惜工作的價值。 例如，一名每週在咖啡店工作幾小時的青少年，一旦親自辛苦賺過那些錢，便可能會對購買不必要的東西變得謹慎得多。 另一個優點是，兼職工作能培養一些學校未必會直接教授的實用技能。 透過服務顧客、與同事合作，以及在壓力下處理小問題，年輕人可以培養自信、溝通能力和更好的時間管理能力。 例如，一個在小店幫忙的孩子，可能會學會如何有禮貌地與陌生人交談、在繁忙時段保持冷靜，以及在工作與學業責任之間取得平衡。 因此，兼職工作可以幫助孩子成長為更有責任感、更有能力、也更獨立的人。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, there are also clear disadvantages. The most obvious is that work can eat into time that should be reserved for study, sleep or family life. A child who works several evening shifts in a supermarket, for instance, may return home too tired to complete homework properly, and this can gradually weaken academic performance. In addition, early exposure to workplace stress may be harmful if the environment is demanding or poorly supervised. Some young workers may have to deal with rude customers, long hours or unrealistic expectations before they are emotionally ready, which can turn a potentially valuable experience into a heavy burden.","chinese":"然而，兼職工作也有明顯的缺點，尤其當它開始干擾孩子的學業或身心健康時。 最明顯的缺點是，工作可能會佔去本應留給學習、休息或家庭生活的時間。 如果孩子花太多時間工作，他們可能會變得疲累、難以好好完成作業，並且逐漸在學校表現變差。 例如，一個在超市上好幾個晚班的孩子，回到家後可能已經累得無法專心溫習，而這會慢慢損害其學業表現。 另一個缺點是，如果工作環境要求過高或缺乏妥善監管，過早接觸職場壓力可能會對孩子造成傷害。 年輕打工者可能在情感上尚未準備好之前，就要面對無禮的顧客、過長的工時或不切實際的期望，這會使原本有價值的經驗變成沉重的負擔。 例如，一名在繁忙餐廳工作的青少年，可能會因持續不斷的壓力與批評而感到不堪負荷，而不是從這段經驗中建立自信。 因此，雖然兼職工作可以帶來好處，但它也可能為孩子帶來學業和情緒上的壓力。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"Overall, part-time work can help children become more mature, capable and independent, yet it can also create academic and emotional strain. Its impact therefore depends largely on the amount of work involved and whether clear limits are kept in place.","chinese":"整體而言，兼職工作可以幫助孩子變得更成熟、更有能力和更獨立，但同時也可能帶來學業與情緒上的壓力。 它所帶來的影響，很大程度上取決於工作量是否適中，以及是否有合理的限制被清楚地設立。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"encourage school-age children to","chinese":"鼓勵學齡兒童去"},{"english":"school-age children","chinese":"學齡兒童"},{"english":"take part-time jobs","chinese":"做兼職工作"},{"english":"during weekends or school holidays","chinese":"在週末或學校假期期間"},{"english":"offer valuable lessons beyond the classroom","chinese":"提供課堂以外的寶貴經驗"},{"english":"beyond the classroom","chinese":"課堂以外"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"expose young people to pressures","chinese":"令年輕人面對壓力"},{"english":"not yet mature enough to manage well","chinese":"尚未成熟到能妥善處理"},{"english":"paid work","chinese":"有薪工作"},{"english":"foster responsibility","chinese":"培養責任感"},{"english":"financial awareness","chinese":"理財意識"},{"english":"be expected to","chinese":"被期望要"},{"english":"arrive on time","chinese":"準時到達"},{"english":"follow instructions","chinese":"遵從指示"},{"english":"earn their own wages","chinese":"賺取自己的工資"},{"english":"be linked to effort","chinese":"與努力掛鈎"},{"english":"simply provided on demand","chinese":"不是有求必應地提供"},{"english":"spends a few hours each week working in","chinese":"每星期花數小時在……工作"},{"english":"become far more careful about","chinese":"對……變得謹慎得多"},{"english":"unnecessary spending","chinese":"不必要的開支"},{"english":"part-time employment","chinese":"兼職工作"},{"english":"practical skills","chinese":"實用技能"},{"english":"teach directly","chinese":"直接教授"},{"english":"serving customers","chinese":"服務顧客"},{"english":"cooperating with co-workers","chinese":"與同事合作"},{"english":"solving small problems under pressure","chinese":"在壓力下解決小問題"},{"english":"develop confidence","chinese":"建立自信"},{"english":"communication skills","chinese":"溝通技巧"},{"english":"better time management","chinese":"更好的時間管理"},{"english":"be useful in adult life","chinese":"在成年生活中有用"},{"english":"clear disadvantages","chinese":"明顯缺點"},{"english":"eat into time","chinese":"侵佔時間"},{"english":"be reserved for","chinese":"留作……之用"},{"english":"family life","chinese":"家庭生活"},{"english":"evening shifts","chinese":"晚班"},{"english":"return home too tired to","chinese":"回家時太疲倦而不能"},{"english":"complete homework properly","chinese":"妥善完成家課"},{"english":"gradually weaken academic performance","chinese":"逐漸削弱學業表現"},{"english":"academic performance","chinese":"學業表現"},{"english":"early exposure to workplace stress","chinese":"過早接觸職場壓力"},{"english":"workplace stress","chinese":"職場壓力"},{"english":"be harmful if","chinese":"如果……便可能有害"},{"english":"demanding","chinese":"要求高的"},{"english":"poorly supervised","chinese":"監督不足的"},{"english":"deal with rude customers","chinese":"應付粗魯顧客"},{"english":"long hours","chinese":"長時間工作"},{"english":"unrealistic expectations","chinese":"不切實際的期望"},{"english":"emotionally ready","chinese":"情緒上準備好"},{"english":"turn a potentially valuable experience into","chinese":"將本來可能有價值的經驗變成"},{"english":"a heavy burden","chinese":"沉重負擔"},{"english":"overall","chinese":"總括而言"},{"english":"mature, capable and independent","chinese":"成熟、有能力和獨立"},{"english":"academic and emotional strain","chinese":"學業及情緒壓力"},{"english":"its impact depends largely on","chinese":"其影響很大程度上取決於"},{"english":"the amount of work involved","chinese":"涉及的工作量"},{"english":"clear limits are kept in place","chinese":"清晰限制是否得以維持"}]},"model-essay-29-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-29-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:29","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-29-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q29","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Childhood obesity has become a serious concern in many education systems, and some people argue that schools should devote more time to sport and exercise to address it. Although physical activity is certainly valuable, I do not believe that increasing PE lessons is the best way to solve this problem. A more effective approach is to improve children’s diets and reshape their daily habits both inside and outside school.","chinese":"兒童肥胖已成為許多教育制度中的嚴重問題，而一些人認為學校應該投放更多時間在體育和運動上，以處理這個問題。 儘管體能活動當然有價值，但我並不認為增加體育課是解決這個問題的最佳方法。 更有效的方法是改善兒童的飲食，並重塑他們在校內和校外的日常習慣。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Extra exercise at school can help overweight children, but its impact is limited. Sport allows pupils to burn energy, build strength and develop a healthier attitude towards their bodies. It can also reduce the time they spend sitting in classrooms or staring at screens. However, a few additional hours of exercise each week can easily be cancelled out if children continue to eat sugary snacks, drink soft drinks and consume oversized portions every day. In other words, exercise may strengthen the engine, but poor diet keeps pouring the wrong fuel into it. For this reason, schools should not treat more sports as the main cure for childhood obesity.","chinese":"在學校增加運動確實可以幫助超重兒童，但其影響是有限的。 運動能讓學生消耗能量、增強體力，並對自己的身體建立更健康的態度。 它也可以減少他們坐在課室裡，或盯著螢幕的時間。 然而，如果兒童每天仍然吃含糖零食、喝汽水，並攝取過大的食物份量，那麼每週額外幾小時的運動很容易被抵消。 換句話說，運動或許能強化引擎，但不良飲食卻一直把錯誤的燃料倒進去。 因此，學校不應把增加運動視為治療兒童肥胖的主要方法。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The most important solution is to change what children eat. Schools should provide healthier meals, restrict the sale of junk food on campus and teach pupils how everyday choices affect their weight. For example, a child who learns to replace sweet drinks with water and processed snacks with fruit is likely to make progress even without dramatic changes to their timetable. Parents must also be involved, because children’s eating patterns are usually formed at home. If families regularly cook balanced meals, limit screen time and encourage walking or outdoor play, healthy behaviour becomes a normal part of life rather than a punishment.","chinese":"最重要的解決方法是改變兒童的飲食內容。 學校應該提供更健康的膳食、限制校園內垃圾食品的銷售，並教導學生日常選擇如何影響他們的體重。 例如，一個學會用水取代甜飲、用水果取代加工零食的孩子，即使時間表沒有巨大改變，也很可能會有所進步。 父母也必須參與其中，因為兒童的飲食模式通常是在家中形成的。 如果家庭經常烹調均衡膳食、限制螢幕時間，並鼓勵步行或戶外玩耍，健康行為就會成為生活中的正常部分，而不是一種懲罰。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, increasing time for sport and exercise is a useful measure, but it is not the best solution to the problem of overweight children. The stronger answer is a combination of healthier school food, practical nutrition education and consistent support from families.","chinese":"總結來說，增加體育和運動時間是一項有用的措施，但它並不是解決兒童超重問題的最佳方法。 更有力的答案，是結合更健康的學校食物、實用的營養教育，以及來自家庭的持續支持"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"childhood obesity","chinese":"兒童肥胖"},{"english":"a serious concern","chinese":"嚴重關注的問題"},{"english":"education systems","chinese":"教育制度"},{"english":"devote more time to","chinese":"投放更多時間於"},{"english":"sport and exercise","chinese":"運動和鍛煉"},{"english":"address it","chinese":"處理它；應對它"},{"english":"physical activity","chinese":"體能活動"},{"english":"increasing PE lessons","chinese":"增加體育課"},{"english":"the best way to solve","chinese":"解決……的最佳方法"},{"english":"a more effective approach","chinese":"更有效的方法"},{"english":"improve children's diets","chinese":"改善孩子的飲食"},{"english":"reshape their daily habits","chinese":"重塑他們的日常習慣"},{"english":"inside and outside school","chinese":"校內和校外"},{"english":"extra exercise","chinese":"額外運動"},{"english":"overweight children","chinese":"超重兒童"},{"english":"its impact is limited","chinese":"它的影響有限"},{"english":"burn energy","chinese":"消耗能量"},{"english":"build strength","chinese":"增強體力"},{"english":"develop a healthier attitude towards","chinese":"對……培養更健康的態度"},{"english":"their bodies","chinese":"他們的身體"},{"english":"reduce the time they spend","chinese":"減少他們花在……上的時間"},{"english":"sitting in classrooms","chinese":"坐在課室裏"},{"english":"staring at screens","chinese":"盯着屏幕"},{"english":"a few additional hours of","chinese":"額外幾小時的……"},{"english":"each week","chinese":"每星期"},{"english":"be cancelled out","chinese":"被抵消"},{"english":"continue to eat","chinese":"繼續吃"},{"english":"sugary snacks","chinese":"高糖零食"},{"english":"soft drinks","chinese":"汽水；含糖飲品"},{"english":"oversized portions","chinese":"過大的食物分量"},{"english":"In other words","chinese":"換句話說"},{"english":"strengthen the engine","chinese":"強化引擎"},{"english":"poor diet","chinese":"不良飲食"},{"english":"keeps pouring","chinese":"不斷倒入"},{"english":"the wrong fuel","chinese":"錯誤燃料"},{"english":"For this reason","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"treat more sports as","chinese":"把更多運動視為"},{"english":"the main cure for","chinese":"……的主要解決方法"},{"english":"the most important solution","chinese":"最重要的解決方法"},{"english":"change what children eat","chinese":"改變孩子吃甚麼"},{"english":"provide healthier meals","chinese":"提供更健康的膳食"},{"english":"restrict the sale of","chinese":"限制……的售賣"},{"english":"junk food","chinese":"垃圾食物"},{"english":"on campus","chinese":"在校園內"},{"english":"everyday choices","chinese":"日常選擇"},{"english":"affect their weight","chinese":"影響他們的體重"},{"english":"learns to replace","chinese":"學會用……取代"},{"english":"sweet drinks","chinese":"甜飲品"},{"english":"processed snacks","chinese":"加工零食"},{"english":"be likely to","chinese":"有可能"},{"english":"make progress","chinese":"取得進步"},{"english":"even without","chinese":"即使沒有"},{"english":"dramatic changes to","chinese":"對……作出重大改變"},{"english":"timetable","chinese":"時間表"},{"english":"parents must also be involved","chinese":"父母也必須參與"},{"english":"eating patterns","chinese":"飲食模式"},{"english":"be formed at home","chinese":"在家中形成"},{"english":"regularly cook balanced meals","chinese":"定期煮均衡膳食"},{"english":"balanced meals","chinese":"均衡膳食"},{"english":"limit screen time","chinese":"限制使用屏幕的時間"},{"english":"encourage walking","chinese":"鼓勵步行"},{"english":"outdoor play","chinese":"戶外玩耍"},{"english":"healthy behaviour","chinese":"健康行為"},{"english":"a normal part of life","chinese":"生活中的正常一部分"},{"english":"rather than a punishment","chinese":"而不是懲罰"},{"english":"a useful measure","chinese":"有用措施"},{"english":"the stronger answer","chinese":"更有力的答案"},{"english":"a combination of","chinese":"……的結合"},{"english":"healthier school food","chinese":"更健康的學校食物"},{"english":"practical nutrition education","chinese":"實用營養教育"},{"english":"consistent support from families","chinese":"來自家庭的持續支持"}]},"model-essay-29-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-29-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:29","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-29-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q29","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Television has long been seen as a powerful influence on children, but people disagree about whether this influence comes mainly from the type of programmes they watch or from the number of hours they spend in front of the screen. In my view, the content children are exposed to has a stronger effect on their behaviour than viewing time alone.","chinese":"電視長期以來都被視為對兒童具有強大影響力，但人們對於這種影響主要來自他們所觀看的節目類型，還是來自他們花在螢幕前的時間長短，存在不同看法。 在我看來，兒童所接觸的內容，比單純的觀看時間對他們的行為有更強的影響。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Those who focus on screen time argue that excessive television watching can damage children’s habits and character. When young people spend several hours a day watching television, they may become passive, less physically active, and less willing to engage with family members or classmates. This can gradually affect their discipline, social confidence, and attention span. For example, a child who spends most evenings watching television may have less time for homework, outdoor play, or face-to-face conversation. Over time, this routine can make them more impatient and less able to concentrate. From this perspective, the problem is not one particular programme, but the way television fills up a child’s daily life.","chinese":"那些重視觀看時間的人認為，過度看電視會損害兒童的習慣和性格。 當年輕人每天花數小時看電視時，他們可能會變得被動、較少進行體能活動，也較不願意與家人或同學互動。 這可能會逐漸影響他們的自律能力、社交信心和專注力。 例如，一個大部分晚上都在看電視的孩子，可能會有較少時間做功課、到戶外玩耍，或進行面對面的交流。 長遠而言，這種日常習慣可能會令他們變得更急躁，也更難集中注意力。 從這個角度來看，問題並不在某一個特定節目，而在於電視佔據了孩子日常生活的方式"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, I believe that what children watch matters more because content directly shapes their ideas, emotions, and patterns of behaviour. Children often learn by imitation, especially when they repeatedly see certain actions being rewarded or normalised. If a programme presents violence, rudeness, or selfishness as entertaining, young viewers may slowly absorb the message that such behaviour is acceptable. By contrast, educational programmes or stories with positive role models can encourage curiosity, kindness, and responsible choices. In this sense, television is like a mirror and a teacher at the same time: it reflects certain values, but it can also quietly plant them in a child’s mind.","chinese":"然而，我認為兒童觀看的內容更加重要，因為內容會直接塑造他們的想法、情緒和行為模式。 兒童往往透過模仿來學習，尤其是當他們反覆看到某些行為受到獎勵或被視為正常時。 如果一個節目把暴力、無禮或自私呈現成有趣的事情，年幼觀眾可能會慢慢吸收一種訊息：這類行為是可以接受的。 相比之下，教育性節目或具正面榜樣的故事，則可以鼓勵好奇心、善良和負責任的選擇 從這個意義上說，電視就像一面鏡子，同時也是一位老師：它反映某些價值觀，但也能悄悄地把這些價值觀種在孩子心中。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, the amount of time children spend watching television can certainly affect their routines and self-control. Nevertheless, I firmly believe that programme content has the greater influence, because it directly teaches children what to admire, copy, and accept as normal.","chinese":"總結來說，兒童花在看電視上的時間，確實會影響他們的日常習慣和自我控制能力。 然而，我堅定地認為，節目內容具有更大的影響力，因為它會直接教導兒童應該欣賞甚麼、模仿甚麼，以及把甚麼視為正常。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"has long been seen as","chinese":"長久以來被視為"},{"english":"a powerful influence on","chinese":"對……有強大影響"},{"english":"disagree about whether","chinese":"對於是否……有分歧"},{"english":"comes mainly from","chinese":"主要來自"},{"english":"the type of programmes","chinese":"節目的類型"},{"english":"spend in front of the screen","chinese":"花在螢幕前"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"be exposed to","chinese":"接觸到"},{"english":"have a stronger effect on","chinese":"對……有更強影響"},{"english":"viewing time alone","chinese":"單是觀看時間"},{"english":"focus on screen time","chinese":"着眼於螢幕時間"},{"english":"screen time","chinese":"螢幕時間"},{"english":"excessive television watching","chinese":"過度看電視"},{"english":"damage children's habits and character","chinese":"損害兒童的習慣和品格"},{"english":"spend several hours a day","chinese":"每日花數小時"},{"english":"become passive","chinese":"變得被動"},{"english":"less physically active","chinese":"較少活動身體"},{"english":"less willing to engage with","chinese":"較不願意與……互動"},{"english":"family members or classmates","chinese":"家人或同學"},{"english":"gradually affect","chinese":"逐漸影響"},{"english":"discipline","chinese":"自律"},{"english":"social confidence","chinese":"社交信心"},{"english":"attention span","chinese":"專注力持續時間"},{"english":"spend most evenings","chinese":"大多數晚上都花時間"},{"english":"outdoor play","chinese":"戶外玩耍"},{"english":"face-to-face conversation","chinese":"面對面交談"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨時間"},{"english":"this routine","chinese":"這種日常習慣"},{"english":"more impatient","chinese":"更加沒有耐性"},{"english":"less able to concentrate","chinese":"較難集中精神"},{"english":"from this perspective","chinese":"從這個角度來看"},{"english":"one particular programme","chinese":"某一個特定節目"},{"english":"fill up a child's daily life","chinese":"佔據兒童的日常生活"},{"english":"what children watch matters more","chinese":"兒童看甚麼更加重要"},{"english":"directly shape","chinese":"直接塑造"},{"english":"ideas, emotions, and patterns of behaviour","chinese":"想法、情緒和行為模式"},{"english":"learn by imitation","chinese":"透過模仿學習"},{"english":"repeatedly see","chinese":"反覆看見"},{"english":"certain actions being rewarded","chinese":"某些行為得到獎勵"},{"english":"be normalised","chinese":"被正常化"},{"english":"presents violence, rudeness, or selfishness as entertaining","chinese":"將暴力、粗魯或自私呈現為娛樂"},{"english":"young viewers","chinese":"年幼觀眾"},{"english":"slowly absorb the message that","chinese":"慢慢吸收……的訊息"},{"english":"such behaviour is acceptable","chinese":"這種行為是可以接受的"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相反"},{"english":"educational programmes","chinese":"教育節目"},{"english":"positive role models","chinese":"正面榜樣"},{"english":"encourage curiosity","chinese":"鼓勵好奇心"},{"english":"responsible choices","chinese":"負責任的選擇"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"reflect certain values","chinese":"反映某些價值觀"},{"english":"quietly plant them in","chinese":"悄悄植入……之中"},{"english":"a child's mind","chinese":"兒童的思想"},{"english":"the amount of time","chinese":"……的時間長短"},{"english":"self-control","chinese":"自制能力"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"programme content","chinese":"節目內容"},{"english":"the greater influence","chinese":"更大的影響"},{"english":"teach children what to admire","chinese":"教導兒童欣賞甚麼"},{"english":"copy and accept as normal","chinese":"模仿並視為正常"}]},"model-essay-29-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-29-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:29","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-29-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q29","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Crime is a serious social problem because it weakens public safety and people's trust in everyday life. In response to rising crime rates, some people argue that putting more police officers on the streets is the only effective solution. I completely disagree with this view, because crime can be reduced more permanently through prevention and rehabilitation.","chinese":"犯罪是一個嚴重的社會問題，因為它削弱公共安全以及人們對日常生活的信任。 面對犯罪率上升，一些人認為在街上部署更多警察是唯一有效的解決方法。 我完全不同意這個觀點，因為犯罪可以透過預防和改造更長久地減少。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that many offences are rooted in social conditions, not merely in a lack of police presence. When young people grow up in poor neighbourhoods, leave school with few useful skills, or see little hope of stable work, crime can appear to be the quickest escape from hardship. More patrols may stop some offences in public places, but they do not remove the pressure that pushes people towards illegal behaviour. By contrast, better education, youth centres, job training and mental-health support can tackle crime at its source. For example, a teenager who has after-school supervision and a realistic path into employment is far less likely to join a gang or steal to survive. Prevention is therefore not a soft option; it is a practical way to stop crime before it takes root.","chinese":"第一個原因是，許多犯罪都根源於社會條件，而不只是因為警力不足。 當年輕人在貧困社區長大、離開學校時缺乏實用技能，或者看不到穩定工作的希望時，犯罪可能看起來像是逃離困境最快的方法。 更多巡邏或許能阻止公共場所中的犯罪，但它們並不能消除把人推向違法行為的壓力 相比之下，更好的教育、青少年中心、職業培訓和心理健康支援，能夠從源頭處理犯罪問題。 例如，一個有課後監督，並且有實際就業途徑的青少年，加入幫派或為了生存而偷竊的可能性會低得多。 因此，預防並不是一種軟弱的選擇；它是在犯罪生根之前阻止犯罪的實際方法。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"A second reason is that many crimes are committed by people who have already passed through the justice system. If prisons only punish offenders and release them without skills, support or employment prospects, society may simply be locking people away temporarily while leaving the underlying problem untouched. Rehabilitation programmes, counselling and supervised work opportunities can break this cycle of reoffending. A former prisoner who learns a trade and receives guidance after release has a stronger reason to live responsibly than one who returns to poverty and isolation. This makes rehabilitation a necessary partner to law enforcement, not a luxury.","chinese":"第二個原因是，許多犯罪都是由已經經歷過司法系統的人所犯下的。 如果監獄只是懲罰罪犯，然後在他們沒有技能、支援或就業前景的情況下釋放他們，社會可能只是暫時把人關起來，卻沒有處理根本問題。 改造計劃、輔導和受監督的工作機會，能夠打破這種再次犯罪的循環。 一個學會一門技能並在釋放後得到指導的前囚犯，比一個重新回到貧困和孤立中的人，更有理由負責任地生活。 這使得改造罪犯成為執法不可或缺的夥伴，而不是一種奢侈的選項。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely disagree that street policing is the only way to reduce crime. Visible officers may discourage some offences, but lasting public safety depends on prevention, education, employment and rehabilitation.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全不同意街頭警力是減少犯罪的唯一方法。 可見的警察或許能阻嚇一些犯罪，但長久的公共安全取決於預防、教育、就業和改造。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"crime","chinese":"犯罪"},{"english":"serious social problem","chinese":"嚴重社會問題"},{"english":"public safety","chinese":"公共安全"},{"english":"trust in everyday life","chinese":"對日常生活的信任"},{"english":"in response to","chinese":"為了回應……"},{"english":"rising crime rates","chinese":"上升的罪案率"},{"english":"putting more police officers on the streets","chinese":"在街上增派警員"},{"english":"the only effective solution","chinese":"唯一有效的解決方法"},{"english":"crime can be reduced","chinese":"犯罪可以被減少"},{"english":"more permanently","chinese":"更持久地"},{"english":"prevention and rehabilitation","chinese":"預防和更生"},{"english":"many offences","chinese":"許多罪行"},{"english":"be rooted in","chinese":"根源在於……"},{"english":"social conditions","chinese":"社會環境"},{"english":"not merely in","chinese":"不只是源於……"},{"english":"lack of police presence","chinese":"缺乏警力出現"},{"english":"grow up in","chinese":"在……中成長"},{"english":"poor neighbourhoods","chinese":"貧困社區"},{"english":"leave school with","chinese":"帶着……離開學校"},{"english":"useful skills","chinese":"有用技能"},{"english":"little hope of","chinese":"對……幾乎沒有希望"},{"english":"stable work","chinese":"穩定工作"},{"english":"the quickest escape from hardship","chinese":"逃離困境最快的方法"},{"english":"hardship","chinese":"困境；艱難生活"},{"english":"more patrols","chinese":"更多巡邏"},{"english":"public places","chinese":"公共地方"},{"english":"remove the pressure","chinese":"消除壓力"},{"english":"pushes people towards","chinese":"將人推向……"},{"english":"illegal behaviour","chinese":"違法行為"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"youth centres","chinese":"青少年中心"},{"english":"job training","chinese":"職業培訓"},{"english":"mental-health support","chinese":"精神健康支援"},{"english":"tackle crime at its source","chinese":"從源頭處理犯罪"},{"english":"after-school supervision","chinese":"課後監督"},{"english":"realistic path into employment","chinese":"進入就業的現實途徑"},{"english":"far less likely to","chinese":"可能性低得多"},{"english":"join a gang","chinese":"加入幫派"},{"english":"steal to survive","chinese":"為了生存而偷竊"},{"english":"soft option","chinese":"軟弱的選擇；寬鬆做法"},{"english":"practical way to","chinese":"……的實際方法"},{"english":"before it takes root","chinese":"在它扎根之前"},{"english":"be committed by","chinese":"由……犯下"},{"english":"have already passed through","chinese":"已經經歷過……"},{"english":"justice system","chinese":"司法制度"},{"english":"punish offenders","chinese":"懲罰犯事者"},{"english":"release them without","chinese":"在沒有……的情況下釋放他們"},{"english":"employment prospects","chinese":"就業前景"},{"english":"lock people away temporarily","chinese":"暫時將人關起來"},{"english":"underlying problem","chinese":"根本問題"},{"english":"untouched","chinese":"未被處理"},{"english":"rehabilitation programmes","chinese":"更生計劃"},{"english":"counselling","chinese":"輔導"},{"english":"supervised work opportunities","chinese":"受監管的工作機會"},{"english":"break this cycle of reoffending","chinese":"打破重犯循環"},{"english":"former prisoner","chinese":"前囚犯"},{"english":"learns a trade","chinese":"學一門手藝"},{"english":"receives guidance after release","chinese":"獲釋後得到指導"},{"english":"stronger reason to","chinese":"更有理由去……"},{"english":"live responsibly","chinese":"負責任地生活"},{"english":"returns to poverty and isolation","chinese":"回到貧窮和孤立之中"},{"english":"necessary partner to","chinese":"……的必要配合"},{"english":"law enforcement","chinese":"執法"},{"english":"not a luxury","chinese":"不是奢侈品"},{"english":"street policing","chinese":"街頭警務；街上巡邏"},{"english":"visible officers","chinese":"可見的警員"},{"english":"discourage some offences","chinese":"阻止部分罪行"},{"english":"lasting public safety","chinese":"持久公共安全"},{"english":"employment and rehabilitation","chinese":"就業和更生"}]},"model-essay-30-ielts-advantage-disadvantage":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-30-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","essayKey":"advantage-disadvantage:30","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-30-ielts-advantage-disadvantage","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/advantage-and-disadvantage/EdmundBd9AdDisAd-Q30","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many countries, online home-based work has become a normal form of employment. Although this shift can weaken workplace relationships and blur personal boundaries, I believe it is overall beneficial because it improves employees’ daily lives and makes the labour market more inclusive.","chinese":"在許多國家，在家線上工作已逐漸成為一種愈來愈普遍的就業模式。 儘管這種趨勢可能削弱職場人際關係，並模糊工作與私人生活之間的界線， 我認為整體而言這是一項正面的發展，因為它改善了員工的生活質素，並讓更廣泛的人群更容易獲得工作機會。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One clear advantage is better work-life balance. Without long commutes, workers recover time for sleep, exercise, childcare, and a calmer start to the day. Less time pressure usually means less stress and better concentration, so productivity may also rise. For example, someone who no longer spends two hours commuting can prepare meals at home and begin work in a far better frame of mind. Another benefit is broader access to jobs. Because location matters less, firms can hire talent from rural areas, while parents and people with limited mobility can apply for roles once beyond their reach. For instance, a city-based company can employ a skilled programmer who lives hundreds of kilometres away.","chinese":"在家線上工作的主要優點是，它讓人們對自己的時間和日常安排有更大的掌控。 由於不需要每天通勤，員工可以節省原本要花在交通上的時間和精力。 這些額外時間可以用於睡眠、運動、照顧孩子，或只是以更從容的狀態開始一天，從而減輕壓力、提升專注力，並且往往帶來更好的工作表現。 例如，一名不再每天花兩小時通勤的員工，可能可以在家準備餐食，並以好得多的精神狀態開始工作。 另一個重要好處是，遙距工作擴大了就業機會的可及性。 由於地點不再那麼重要，公司可以聘用來自偏遠地區的人才，而家長及行動不便的人也能申請以往難以從事的工作。 例如，一間位於城市的公司，仍然可以聘用住在數百公里外的優秀軟件工程師。 因此，在家線上工作既能提升個人生活質素，也能增加人們獲得就業機會的可能。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, this trend also has disadvantages. The first is social and professional isolation. When communication happens mainly through screens, spontaneous conversations, informal mentoring, and team cohesion all decline. This is particularly damaging for younger staff, who often learn by observing experienced colleagues solve problems in real time. For example, a new employee may receive formal instructions online yet still miss the quick advice that would naturally be available in a shared office. A second drawback is that home working can erase the boundary between work and private life. Because the laptop is always nearby, some people keep checking messages late into the evening. A manager who replies to emails after dinner every night, for example, may gradually slip into fatigue and burnout instead of enjoying genuine flexibility.","chinese":"然而，這種趨勢也有明顯缺點，尤其是在社交連結和個人界線方面。 第一個問題是職場中的孤立感。 當大部分互動都透過螢幕進行時，自發性的交流、非正式指導以及團隊凝聚力往往都會下降，這會使員工對同事產生疏離感，並在工作中感到較少支援。 例如，一名新員工雖然可以在線上收到正式指示，但仍然會錯過在共享辦公室中本來能自然獲得的即時建議與支持。 第二個缺點是，在家工作會模糊工作與私人生活之間的界線。 由於電腦和手機總在身邊，有些員工會感到壓力，深夜仍要回覆訊息，結果彈性工作逐漸演變成隨時待命，最終導致疲勞甚至職業倦怠。 例如，一位每天晚飯後仍持續回覆電郵的經理，可能會發現自己根本無法真正放鬆。 因此，儘管遙距工作帶來了自由，它同時也可能削弱職場歸屬感，並助長過度工作。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, working online from home brings real drawbacks, but it remains a positive development overall. While it can reduce face-to-face interaction and encourage overwork, its benefits for well-being and access to employment are more significant.","chinese":"總括而言，在家線上工作的增加確實帶來一些缺點，但整體上仍屬正面發展。 雖然它可能削弱職場中的面對面互動，並模糊私人生活的界線，但它對日常生活質素及就業機會可及性的好處更為重要。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"online home-based work","chinese":"網上在家工作"},{"english":"a normal form of employment","chinese":"一種正常的就業形式"},{"english":"this shift","chinese":"這種轉變"},{"english":"weaken workplace relationships","chinese":"削弱職場關係"},{"english":"workplace relationships","chinese":"職場關係"},{"english":"blur personal boundaries","chinese":"模糊個人界線"},{"english":"personal boundaries","chinese":"個人界線"},{"english":"overall beneficial","chinese":"整體上有益"},{"english":"daily lives","chinese":"日常生活"},{"english":"the labour market","chinese":"勞動市場"},{"english":"more inclusive","chinese":"更具包容性"},{"english":"one clear advantage","chinese":"一個明顯好處"},{"english":"work-life balance","chinese":"工作與生活平衡"},{"english":"long commutes","chinese":"長時間通勤"},{"english":"recover time for","chinese":"騰回時間給"},{"english":"childcare","chinese":"照顧子女"},{"english":"a calmer start to the day","chinese":"一天較平靜的開始"},{"english":"time pressure","chinese":"時間壓力"},{"english":"better concentration","chinese":"更佳專注力"},{"english":"productivity may also rise","chinese":"生產力也可能上升"},{"english":"spend two hours commuting","chinese":"花兩小時通勤"},{"english":"prepare meals at home","chinese":"在家準備膳食"},{"english":"in a far better frame of mind","chinese":"以好得多的心情"},{"english":"broader access to jobs","chinese":"更廣泛的就業機會"},{"english":"location matters less","chinese":"地點變得不那麼重要"},{"english":"hire talent from rural areas","chinese":"聘請來自鄉郊地區的人才"},{"english":"limited mobility","chinese":"行動能力有限"},{"english":"apply for roles","chinese":"申請職位"},{"english":"beyond their reach","chinese":"以往難以接觸到"},{"english":"a city-based company","chinese":"以城市為基地的公司"},{"english":"employ a skilled programmer","chinese":"聘用熟練的程式員"},{"english":"hundreds of kilometres away","chinese":"數百公里之外"},{"english":"this trend","chinese":"這個趨勢"},{"english":"social and professional isolation","chinese":"社交和專業上的孤立"},{"english":"communication happens mainly through screens","chinese":"溝通主要透過屏幕進行"},{"english":"spontaneous conversations","chinese":"自然發生的交談"},{"english":"informal mentoring","chinese":"非正式指導"},{"english":"team cohesion","chinese":"團隊凝聚力"},{"english":"particularly damaging for","chinese":"對……尤其有害"},{"english":"younger staff","chinese":"年輕職員"},{"english":"learn by observing","chinese":"透過觀察學習"},{"english":"experienced colleagues","chinese":"有經驗的同事"},{"english":"solve problems in real time","chinese":"即時解決問題"},{"english":"formal instructions","chinese":"正式指示"},{"english":"quick advice","chinese":"即時的小建議"},{"english":"naturally be available","chinese":"自然會有"},{"english":"a shared office","chinese":"共用辦公室"},{"english":"a second drawback","chinese":"第二個缺點"},{"english":"erase the boundary between","chinese":"抹走……之間的界線"},{"english":"private life","chinese":"私人生活"},{"english":"always nearby","chinese":"總是在身邊"},{"english":"keep checking messages","chinese":"不停查看訊息"},{"english":"late into the evening","chinese":"直到深夜"},{"english":"reply to emails after dinner","chinese":"晚飯後回覆電郵"},{"english":"gradually slip into","chinese":"逐漸陷入"},{"english":"fatigue and burnout","chinese":"疲勞和職業倦怠"},{"english":"genuine flexibility","chinese":"真正的彈性"},{"english":"working online from home","chinese":"網上在家工作"},{"english":"real drawbacks","chinese":"真正的缺點"},{"english":"a positive development overall","chinese":"整體而言是正面的發展"},{"english":"face-to-face interaction","chinese":"面對面互動"},{"english":"encourage overwork","chinese":"鼓勵過度工作"},{"english":"well-being","chinese":"身心健康"},{"english":"access to employment","chinese":"就業機會"},{"english":"more significant","chinese":"更重要"}]},"model-essay-30-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-30-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:30","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-30-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q30","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"With populations rising, governments must decide whether to expand current urban areas or create entirely new settlements in rural regions. In my view, new housing should be concentrated in existing cities, because this uses public infrastructure more efficiently and protects the countryside from unnecessary damage.","chinese":"隨著人口上升，各國政府必須決定是擴展現有城市地區，還是在鄉郊地區建立全新的聚居地。 在我看來，新住房應該集中建於現有城市之中，因為這能更有效地使用公共基礎設施，並保護鄉郊免受不必要的破壞。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest argument for building in cities is that the basic framework for daily life is already there. Roads, railways, hospitals, schools, water systems and emergency services have usually been established over many decades, so additional homes can be connected to them more quickly and cheaply than homes in a new town. If a government builds a rural settlement from scratch, it must first lay down a whole skeleton of services before families can live there properly. That money could instead be spent on higher-density apartments, upgraded transport links and better public facilities in places where people already work and study. For example, replacing low-rise, underused urban land with well-designed apartment blocks can house thousands of residents without forcing them to commute from distant areas.","chinese":"支持在城市建房最有力的理由是，日常生活所需的基本框架已經存在。 道路、鐵路、醫院、學校、供水系統和緊急服務通常已經經過數十年建立起來，因此新增房屋能比新城鎮中的房屋更快速、更低成本地接駁到這些設施。 如果政府從零開始建設一個鄉郊聚居地，在家庭能夠真正適當地生活之前，它必須先建立一整套服務骨架。 這筆資金反而可以用於在人們已經工作和學習的地方興建更高密度的公寓、改善交通連接，以及提供更好的公共設施。 例如，以設計良好的公寓大樓取代低層且未被充分利用的城市土地，可以容納數以千計的居民，而不必迫使他們從遙遠地區通勤。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that expanding into the countryside often creates long-term social and environmental costs. Rural land is not simply empty space; it may be farmland, woodland, wildlife habitat or part of a local community’s identity. Once it is covered with concrete, it is extremely difficult to restore. New countryside towns can also produce car-dependent lifestyles, because jobs and major services normally remain in the city centre. As a result, residents may spend more time on the road, traffic may increase, and the supposed solution to the housing shortage may create another burden: a larger, more scattered urban footprint.","chinese":"另一個原因是，向鄉郊擴張往往會造成長遠的社會和環境成本。 鄉郊土地並不只是空地；它可能是農田、林地、野生動物棲息地，或者是本地社區身份的一部分。 一旦它被混凝土覆蓋，就極難恢復原狀。 新的鄉郊城鎮也可能造成依賴汽車的生活方式，因為工作機會和主要服務通常仍然留在市中心。 結果，居民可能會花更多時間在路上，交通流量可能會增加，而這個本應解決住房短缺的方案，可能會製造另一種負擔：更大、更分散的城市足跡。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, new homes should be constructed in existing cities rather than in newly built countryside towns. City-based housing makes better use of infrastructure, keeps people close to work and services, and prevents the countryside from being swallowed by poorly planned development.","chinese":"總結來說，新住房應該建於現有城市之中，而不是建於新建的鄉郊城鎮。 以城市為基礎的住房能更好地利用基礎設施，使人們靠近工作和服務，並防止鄉郊被規劃不善的發展所吞噬。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"populations rising","chinese":"人口上升"},{"english":"expand current urban areas","chinese":"擴展現有城市地區"},{"english":"create entirely new settlements","chinese":"建立全新的聚居地"},{"english":"rural regions","chinese":"農村地區；鄉郊地區"},{"english":"new housing","chinese":"新住房"},{"english":"be concentrated in","chinese":"集中於"},{"english":"existing cities","chinese":"現有城市"},{"english":"public infrastructure","chinese":"公共基礎設施"},{"english":"more efficiently","chinese":"更有效率地"},{"english":"protects the countryside from","chinese":"保護郊區免受……影響"},{"english":"unnecessary damage","chinese":"不必要的破壞"},{"english":"the strongest argument for","chinese":"支持……的最有力論點"},{"english":"building in cities","chinese":"在城市興建"},{"english":"the basic framework for","chinese":"……的基本框架"},{"english":"daily life","chinese":"日常生活"},{"english":"emergency services","chinese":"緊急服務"},{"english":"have been established over","chinese":"已經過……建立"},{"english":"over many decades","chinese":"經過數十年"},{"english":"additional homes","chinese":"額外住房"},{"english":"be connected to","chinese":"連接到"},{"english":"more quickly and cheaply","chinese":"更快、更便宜地"},{"english":"a rural settlement","chinese":"農村聚居地"},{"english":"from scratch","chinese":"從零開始"},{"english":"lay down","chinese":"鋪設；建立"},{"english":"a whole skeleton of services","chinese":"一整套基本服務框架"},{"english":"live there properly","chinese":"正常地生活在那裏"},{"english":"instead be spent on","chinese":"反而用於"},{"english":"higher-density apartments","chinese":"高密度住宅"},{"english":"upgraded transport links","chinese":"升級了的交通連接"},{"english":"public facilities","chinese":"公共設施"},{"english":"where people already work and study","chinese":"在人們已經工作和學習的地方"},{"english":"low-rise urban land","chinese":"低矮城市用地"},{"english":"underused urban land","chinese":"使用率低的城市土地"},{"english":"well-designed apartment blocks","chinese":"設計良好的住宅大廈"},{"english":"house thousands of residents","chinese":"容納數千名居民"},{"english":"without forcing them to","chinese":"不用迫使他們"},{"english":"commute from distant areas","chinese":"從遙遠地區通勤"},{"english":"another reason","chinese":"另一個原因"},{"english":"expanding into the countryside","chinese":"向郊區擴展"},{"english":"long-term social and environmental costs","chinese":"長遠社會和環境成本"},{"english":"not simply empty space","chinese":"不只是空地"},{"english":"farmland","chinese":"農地"},{"english":"woodland","chinese":"林地"},{"english":"wildlife habitat","chinese":"野生動物棲息地"},{"english":"local community's identity","chinese":"本地社區身份認同"},{"english":"covered with concrete","chinese":"被混凝土覆蓋"},{"english":"extremely difficult to restore","chinese":"極難恢復"},{"english":"countryside towns","chinese":"郊區新市鎮"},{"english":"car-dependent lifestyles","chinese":"依賴汽車的生活方式"},{"english":"major services","chinese":"主要服務"},{"english":"remain in the city centre","chinese":"留在市中心"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"結果"},{"english":"spend more time on the road","chinese":"花更多時間在路上"},{"english":"traffic may increase","chinese":"交通流量可能增加"},{"english":"the supposed solution to","chinese":"對……所謂的解決方法"},{"english":"housing shortage","chinese":"住房短缺"},{"english":"create another burden","chinese":"造成另一個負擔"},{"english":"a larger, more scattered urban footprint","chinese":"更大、更分散的城市足跡"},{"english":"be constructed in","chinese":"在……興建"},{"english":"newly built countryside towns","chinese":"新建的郊區城鎮"},{"english":"city-based housing","chinese":"以城市為本的住房"},{"english":"makes better use of","chinese":"更善用"},{"english":"keeps people close to","chinese":"讓人們靠近"},{"english":"work and services","chinese":"工作地點和服務"},{"english":"prevents the countryside from being swallowed by","chinese":"防止郊區被……吞噬"},{"english":"poorly planned development","chinese":"規劃不善的發展"}]},"model-essay-30-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-30-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:30","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-30-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q30","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The rapid growth of digital reading has led some people to argue that e-books will eventually replace printed books, while others believe that traditional books will remain part of human life. This essay will discuss both views, but I strongly believe that paper books will not disappear.","chinese":"數位閱讀的迅速發展，使一些人認為電子書最終會取代印刷書籍，而另一些人則相信傳統書籍仍會是人類生活的一部分。 本文將討論雙方觀點，但我強烈認為紙本書不會消失。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Those who predict the end of printed books usually focus on convenience. E-books allow readers to store hundreds of titles on one device, download new material instantly, and read almost anywhere without carrying heavy volumes. This is especially useful for students, commuters, and frequent travellers, who may need quick access to several texts at once. Digital books can also be cheaper to produce and distribute because publishers do not need paper, printing machines, warehouses, or physical delivery networks. In this sense, e-books seem like a more efficient tool for a fast-moving society, and it is understandable why some people see them as the natural successor to paper books.","chinese":"那些預測印刷書籍將會終結的人，通常著眼於便利性。 電子書讓讀者能夠在一部裝置中儲存數百本書、即時下載新材料，並且幾乎可以在任何地方閱讀，而不需要攜帶沉重的書本。 這對學生、通勤人士和常旅行的人尤其有用，因為他們可能需要同時快速查閱多份文本 數位書籍在製作和分發方面也可以更便宜，因為出版商不需要紙張、印刷機器、倉庫或實體配送網絡。 從這個角度來看，電子書似乎是一種更適合快速運轉社會的高效工具，因此有些人把它們視為紙本書的自然繼承者，也是可以理解的。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, I believe paper books will survive because they offer qualities that digital formats cannot fully replace. A printed book is not merely a container for words; it is also a physical object that many readers value for its texture, weight, appearance, and sense of permanence. Reading from paper can feel calmer and more focused than reading from a screen, particularly for people who already spend long hours using phones and computers. For example, many parents still prefer physical storybooks for children because turning pages together creates a warmer and more memorable experience. Libraries, collectors, bookshops, and schools also help keep printed books alive, as they give books cultural and emotional value beyond simple information.","chinese":"然而，我認為紙本書會繼續存在，因為它們具有數位形式無法完全取代的特質。 一本印刷書不僅僅是文字的載體；它同時也是一件實體物品，許多讀者重視它的質感、重量、外觀和持久感。 與螢幕閱讀相比，紙本閱讀可以讓人感覺更平靜、更專注，尤其是對那些已經長時間使用手機和電腦的人來說。 例如，許多父母仍然更喜歡為孩子選擇實體故事書，因為一起翻頁能創造更溫暖、更難忘的體驗。 圖書館、收藏者、書店和學校也有助於讓印刷書籍繼續存在，因為它們賦予書本超越單純資訊的文化和情感價值。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, e-books will continue to grow because they are practical, affordable, and highly accessible. Nevertheless, paper books will not vanish. Their physical presence, reading comfort, and cultural meaning will continue to protect their place in society.","chinese":"總結來說，電子書會繼續發展，因為它們實用、價格較低，而且非常容易取得。 然而，紙本書不會消失。 它們的實體存在、閱讀舒適感和文化意義，將會繼續保護它們在社會中的位置。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"rapid growth","chinese":"快速增長"},{"english":"digital reading","chinese":"數碼閱讀"},{"english":"has led some people to argue that","chinese":"令一些人認為……"},{"english":"e-books","chinese":"電子書"},{"english":"eventually replace","chinese":"最終取代"},{"english":"printed books","chinese":"紙本書"},{"english":"traditional books","chinese":"傳統書籍"},{"english":"remain part of human life","chinese":"仍然是人類生活的一部分"},{"english":"discuss both views","chinese":"討論雙方觀點"},{"english":"strongly believe that","chinese":"強烈相信……"},{"english":"paper books will not disappear","chinese":"紙本書不會消失"},{"english":"predict the end of","chinese":"預測……的終結"},{"english":"focus on convenience","chinese":"集中於方便性"},{"english":"allow readers to","chinese":"讓讀者可以……"},{"english":"store hundreds of titles","chinese":"儲存數百本書"},{"english":"on one device","chinese":"在一部裝置上"},{"english":"download new material instantly","chinese":"即時下載新內容"},{"english":"read almost anywhere","chinese":"幾乎在任何地方閱讀"},{"english":"carrying heavy volumes","chinese":"攜帶厚重書冊"},{"english":"especially useful for","chinese":"對……尤其有用"},{"english":"quick access to","chinese":"快速取得……"},{"english":"several texts at once","chinese":"同時幾份文本"},{"english":"cheaper to produce and distribute","chinese":"製作和分發成本較低"},{"english":"physical delivery networks","chinese":"實體配送網絡"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"a more efficient tool","chinese":"更有效率的工具"},{"english":"fast-moving society","chinese":"快速變動的社會"},{"english":"understandable why","chinese":"可以理解為甚麼"},{"english":"natural successor to","chinese":"自然繼承者；自然取代者"},{"english":"fully replace","chinese":"完全取代"},{"english":"not merely a container for words","chinese":"不只是文字容器"},{"english":"physical object","chinese":"實體物件"},{"english":"sense of permanence","chinese":"持久感；長存感"},{"english":"feel calmer and more focused","chinese":"感覺更平靜和更專注"},{"english":"spend long hours using","chinese":"長時間使用……"},{"english":"physical storybooks","chinese":"實體故事書"},{"english":"turning pages together","chinese":"一起翻頁"},{"english":"warmer and more memorable experience","chinese":"更溫暖和更難忘的經驗"},{"english":"keep printed books alive","chinese":"令紙本書繼續存在；保持紙本書生命力"},{"english":"cultural and emotional value","chinese":"文化和情感價值"},{"english":"beyond simple information","chinese":"超越簡單資訊"},{"english":"continue to grow","chinese":"繼續增長"},{"english":"practical, affordable, and highly accessible","chinese":"實用、可負擔且高度容易取得"},{"english":"will not vanish","chinese":"不會消失"},{"english":"physical presence","chinese":"實體存在"},{"english":"reading comfort","chinese":"閱讀舒適感"},{"english":"cultural meaning","chinese":"文化意義"},{"english":"protect their place in society","chinese":"保護它們在社會中的位置"}]},"model-essay-30-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-30-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:30","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-30-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q30","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Public safety depends heavily on the quality of a country’s police force. Some people argue that women should be excluded from this profession, perhaps because policing is often seen as physically demanding. I strongly disagree with this view, as police work should be based on ability rather than gender, and female officers can make law enforcement more effective.","chinese":"公共安全在很大程度上取決於一個國家警隊的質素。 有些人認為女性應該被排除在這個職業之外，或許是因為警務工作經常被視為對體能要求很高。 我強烈不同意這種看法，因為警務工作應該以能力而不是性別為基礎，而且女性警員可以使執法工作更加有效。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that policing requires far more than physical strength. Although officers may sometimes need to arrest suspects or respond to dangerous situations, much of their daily work involves communication, judgment, patience, and emotional control. These qualities are not limited to men. If a woman can pass the same physical, psychological, and professional training as a man, there is no fair reason to prevent her from wearing the uniform. For example, many police duties involve interviewing witnesses, calming angry members of the public, investigating crimes, or writing accurate reports. In these situations, a clear mind and a steady voice may matter more than brute force. Excluding women simply because of their gender would therefore waste valuable talent and weaken the police force.","chinese":"第一個原因是，警務工作所需要的遠遠不只是體力。 儘管警員有時可能需要拘捕疑犯或應對危險情況，但他們大部分日常工作都涉及溝通、判斷、耐性和情緒控制。 這些特質並不限於男性。 如果一名女性能夠通過與男性相同的體能、心理和專業訓練，那麼便沒有公平的理由阻止她穿上制服。 例如，許多警務職責包括訪問證人、安撫憤怒的市民、調查罪案，或撰寫準確的報告。 在這些情況下，清晰的頭腦和沉穩的聲音可能比蠻力更加重要。 因此，單純因為性別而排除女性，會浪費寶貴的人才，並削弱警隊的力量。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important point is that female officers can improve public trust, especially when dealing with vulnerable people. Victims of domestic violence, sexual assault, or child abuse may feel safer speaking to a female officer, particularly if they are frightened, embarrassed, or traumatised. In such cases, the presence of women in the police force is not symbolic; it can directly affect whether victims are willing to report crimes and cooperate with investigations. A police force that includes both men and women is also more likely to reflect the community it serves, which makes it appear fairer, more approachable, and more human.","chinese":"另一個重要觀點是，女性警員能夠提升公眾信任，尤其是在處理弱勢人士的案件時。 家庭暴力、性侵犯或虐待兒童的受害者，在與女性警員交談時可能會感到更安全，尤其是當他們感到害怕、尷尬或受到創傷時。 在這些情況下，女性在警隊中的存在並不只是象徵性的；它可以直接影響受害者是否願意報案並配合調查。 一支同時包含男性和女性的警隊，也更有可能反映它所服務的社區，這會令它看起來更公平、更容易接近，也更有人性。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely disagree that women should be barred from police work. The badge should belong to those who are trained, capable, and committed, not only to those who fit an outdated stereotype. A stronger police force is one that welcomes ability wherever it is found.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全不同意女性應該被禁止從事警務工作。 警徽應該屬於那些受過訓練、有能力並且有承擔的人，而不應只屬於那些符合過時刻板印象的人。 一支更強大的警隊，是一支無論能力來自何處都願意接納的警隊。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"public safety","chinese":"公共安全"},{"english":"depends heavily on","chinese":"很大程度上取決於"},{"english":"police force","chinese":"警隊"},{"english":"be excluded from","chinese":"被排除於……之外"},{"english":"this profession","chinese":"這個職業"},{"english":"policing","chinese":"警務工作"},{"english":"be seen as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"physically demanding","chinese":"體力要求高的"},{"english":"strongly disagree with","chinese":"強烈不同意……"},{"english":"police work","chinese":"警務工作"},{"english":"be based on","chinese":"建基於"},{"english":"ability rather than gender","chinese":"能力而不是性別"},{"english":"female officers","chinese":"女性警務人員"},{"english":"law enforcement","chinese":"執法"},{"english":"more effective","chinese":"更有效"},{"english":"far more than","chinese":"遠不止"},{"english":"physical strength","chinese":"體力"},{"english":"arrest suspects","chinese":"拘捕疑犯"},{"english":"respond to dangerous situations","chinese":"應對危險情況"},{"english":"daily work","chinese":"日常工作"},{"english":"involves communication","chinese":"涉及溝通"},{"english":"judgment","chinese":"判斷力"},{"english":"emotional control","chinese":"情緒控制"},{"english":"be limited to","chinese":"局限於"},{"english":"pass the same training","chinese":"通過相同訓練"},{"english":"physical, psychological, and professional training","chinese":"體能、心理和專業訓練"},{"english":"fair reason to","chinese":"合理理由去……"},{"english":"prevent her from","chinese":"阻止她……"},{"english":"wearing the uniform","chinese":"穿上制服"},{"english":"police duties","chinese":"警務職責"},{"english":"interviewing witnesses","chinese":"訪問證人"},{"english":"calming angry members of the public","chinese":"安撫憤怒的公眾人士"},{"english":"investigating crimes","chinese":"調查罪案"},{"english":"accurate reports","chinese":"準確報告"},{"english":"in these situations","chinese":"在這些情況下"},{"english":"clear mind","chinese":"清晰頭腦"},{"english":"steady voice","chinese":"沉穩的聲音"},{"english":"matter more than","chinese":"比……更重要"},{"english":"brute force","chinese":"蠻力"},{"english":"simply because of","chinese":"只是因為"},{"english":"gender","chinese":"性別"},{"english":"waste valuable talent","chinese":"浪費寶貴人才"},{"english":"weaken the police force","chinese":"削弱警隊"},{"english":"public trust","chinese":"公眾信任"},{"english":"especially when dealing with","chinese":"尤其在處理……時"},{"english":"vulnerable people","chinese":"弱勢人士"},{"english":"victims of domestic violence","chinese":"家庭暴力受害者"},{"english":"sexual assault","chinese":"性侵犯"},{"english":"child abuse","chinese":"虐兒"},{"english":"feel safer speaking to","chinese":"與……交談時感到更安全"},{"english":"particularly if","chinese":"特別是如果"},{"english":"frightened, embarrassed, or traumatised","chinese":"受驚、尷尬或受創"},{"english":"in such cases","chinese":"在這些情況下"},{"english":"presence of women","chinese":"女性的存在"},{"english":"not symbolic","chinese":"不是象徵性的"},{"english":"directly affect whether","chinese":"直接影響是否……"},{"english":"be willing to","chinese":"願意去……"},{"english":"report crimes","chinese":"報案"},{"english":"cooperate with investigations","chinese":"配合調查"},{"english":"includes both men and women","chinese":"包括男性和女性"},{"english":"reflect the community it serves","chinese":"反映它所服務的社區"},{"english":"appear fairer","chinese":"顯得更公平"},{"english":"more approachable","chinese":"更親民；更容易接近"},{"english":"more human","chinese":"更有人情味"},{"english":"be barred from","chinese":"被禁止從事……"},{"english":"the badge","chinese":"警徽"},{"english":"trained, capable, and committed","chinese":"受過訓練、有能力和有承擔"},{"english":"fit an outdated stereotype","chinese":"符合過時的刻板印象"},{"english":"outdated stereotype","chinese":"過時的刻板印象"},{"english":"welcomes ability","chinese":"歡迎有能力的人才"},{"english":"wherever it is found","chinese":"無論能力出現在哪裏"}]},"model-essay-31-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-31-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:31","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-31-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q31","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"It is increasingly common for workplaces and educational buildings to be designed around large shared areas rather than separate rooms. This trend is mainly driven by the need for greater flexibility and closer interaction. I regard it as a positive development because, when planned properly, open spaces can make institutions more cooperative, adaptable and efficient.","chinese":"工作場所和教育建築越來越常以大型共享空間為核心來設計，而不是採用一間間獨立房間的形式。 這種趨勢主要是由於人們需要更高的靈活性和更緊密的互動。 我認為這是一種正面的發展，因為如果規劃得當，開放式空間可以使機構更具合作性、適應性和效率。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason behind this design choice is practical. Modern offices and schools rarely use rooms for one fixed purpose throughout the day. An open area can be rearranged quickly for group projects, staff meetings, presentations or independent work, whereas a building divided into many small rooms is much harder to adapt. In a school, for example, one large learning space can allow several classes to work on a science project together, with teachers moving freely between groups. In an office, the same logic applies: teams can form, separate and reform as projects change. This saves space and prevents buildings from becoming a maze of underused rooms.","chinese":"這種設計選擇背後的第一個原因是實用性。 現代辦公室和學校很少會整天只把房間用於一個固定用途。 開放式區域可以迅速重新安排，用於小組項目、員工會議、簡報或獨立工作；相反，一座被分割成許多小房間的建築則更難適應不同需要。 例如，在學校裡，一個大型學習空間可以讓幾個班級一起進行科學項目，而老師也能在不同小組之間自由走動。 在辦公室裡，同樣的道理也適用：團隊可以隨著項目變化而組成、分開，再重新組合。 這樣可以節省空間，並防止建築變成一個由大量使用不足房間組成的迷宮。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"I also see this as positive because open-plan buildings encourage communication. In many traditional offices, employees can become isolated behind closed doors, which slows down problem-solving and weakens team spirit. Similarly, in schools, students who learn only in sealed classrooms may have fewer chances to collaborate with classmates from other groups. Open spaces create more natural contact: people can ask quick questions, observe how others work and share ideas without turning every conversation into a formal meeting. This does not simply make a building look modern; it changes the rhythm of daily work and study.","chinese":"我也認為這是正面的，因為開放式建築能促進溝通。 在許多傳統辦公室裡，員工可能會被封閉的門隔離起來，這會減慢解決問題的速度，並削弱團隊精神。 同樣地，在學校裡，如果學生只在封閉課室中學習，他們與其他小組同學合作的機會可能會更少。 開放式空間能創造更自然的接觸：人們可以快速提問、觀察別人的工作方式，並分享想法，而不必把每一次交流都變成正式會議。 這不只是讓建築看起來現代化；它改變了日常工作和學習的節奏。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"Some noise and distraction are possible, but these can be reduced through quiet zones, movable partitions and sensible rules. The core idea remains sound. Overall, open-plan design is popular because it makes buildings more flexible, and I believe it is a positive development because it encourages collaboration and makes better use of space.","chinese":"一些噪音和干擾確實可能出現，但這些問題可以透過安靜區域、可移動隔板和合理規則來減少。 其核心理念仍然是合理的。 整體而言，開放式設計之所以受歡迎，是因為它使建築更具靈活性；而我認為這是一種正面的發展，因為它鼓勵合作，並能更有效地利用空間。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"increasingly common","chinese":"越來越普遍"},{"english":"workplaces and educational buildings","chinese":"工作場所和教育建築物"},{"english":"be designed around","chinese":"圍繞……設計"},{"english":"large shared areas","chinese":"大型共用空間"},{"english":"rather than separate rooms","chinese":"而不是獨立房間"},{"english":"mainly driven by","chinese":"主要由……推動"},{"english":"greater flexibility","chinese":"更大的靈活性"},{"english":"closer interaction","chinese":"更緊密的互動"},{"english":"regard it as","chinese":"把它視為"},{"english":"a positive development","chinese":"正面發展"},{"english":"when planned properly","chinese":"在妥善規劃下"},{"english":"more cooperative, adaptable and efficient","chinese":"更合作、更靈活、更高效"},{"english":"the first reason behind","chinese":"……背後的第一個原因"},{"english":"design choice","chinese":"設計選擇"},{"english":"for one fixed purpose","chinese":"作單一固定用途"},{"english":"throughout the day","chinese":"一整天"},{"english":"be rearranged quickly","chinese":"可快速重新安排"},{"english":"group projects","chinese":"小組項目"},{"english":"staff meetings","chinese":"員工會議"},{"english":"presentations","chinese":"匯報；簡報"},{"english":"independent work","chinese":"獨立工作"},{"english":"divided into","chinese":"被分成"},{"english":"much harder to adapt","chinese":"更難適應改變"},{"english":"learning space","chinese":"學習空間"},{"english":"allow several classes to","chinese":"讓幾個班級可以"},{"english":"work on a science project","chinese":"進行科學項目"},{"english":"moving freely between","chinese":"在……之間自由走動"},{"english":"the same logic applies","chinese":"同樣道理適用"},{"english":"teams can form, separate and reform","chinese":"團隊可以組成、分開再重組"},{"english":"as projects change","chinese":"隨着項目改變"},{"english":"saves space","chinese":"節省空間"},{"english":"prevents buildings from becoming","chinese":"防止建築物變成"},{"english":"a maze of","chinese":"一個由……組成的迷宮"},{"english":"underused rooms","chinese":"使用率低的房間"},{"english":"open-plan buildings","chinese":"開放式建築"},{"english":"encourage communication","chinese":"促進溝通"},{"english":"traditional offices","chinese":"傳統辦公室"},{"english":"become isolated behind closed doors","chinese":"在關上的門後變得孤立"},{"english":"slows down problem-solving","chinese":"拖慢解難"},{"english":"weakens team spirit","chinese":"削弱團隊精神"},{"english":"similarly","chinese":"同樣地"},{"english":"sealed classrooms","chinese":"封閉課室"},{"english":"have fewer chances to","chinese":"有較少機會去"},{"english":"collaborate with","chinese":"與……合作"},{"english":"classmates from other groups","chinese":"其他組別的同學"},{"english":"create more natural contact","chinese":"創造更自然的接觸"},{"english":"ask quick questions","chinese":"快速提問"},{"english":"observe how others work","chinese":"觀察其他人如何工作"},{"english":"share ideas","chinese":"分享想法"},{"english":"without turning every conversation into","chinese":"不用把每次對話都變成"},{"english":"a formal meeting","chinese":"正式會議"},{"english":"does not simply make","chinese":"不只是令……"},{"english":"look modern","chinese":"看起來現代化"},{"english":"changes the rhythm of","chinese":"改變……的節奏"},{"english":"daily work and study","chinese":"日常工作和學習"},{"english":"noise and distraction","chinese":"噪音和分心"},{"english":"be reduced through","chinese":"可透過……減少"},{"english":"quiet zones","chinese":"安靜區"},{"english":"movable partitions","chinese":"可移動間隔板"},{"english":"sensible rules","chinese":"合理規則"},{"english":"the core idea remains sound","chinese":"核心理念仍然合理"},{"english":"overall","chinese":"整體而言"},{"english":"makes buildings more flexible","chinese":"令建築物更靈活"},{"english":"encourages collaboration","chinese":"鼓勵協作"},{"english":"makes better use of space","chinese":"更善用空間"}]},"model-essay-31-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-31-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:31","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-31-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q31","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"International organisations often support poorer nations as they try to improve infrastructure, education and public services. While some believe that money is the most useful form of assistance, others argue that practical support and expert guidance matter more. This essay will discuss both views and argue that practical aid and advice are more valuable because they help countries use resources effectively and become less dependent on donors.","chinese":"國際組織經常在較貧困國家嘗試改善基礎建設、教育和公共服務時提供支持。 雖然有些人認為金錢是最有用的援助形式，但另一些人則主張實際支援和專家指導更為重要。 本文將討論雙方觀點，並主張實際援助和建議更有價值，因為它們能幫助國家有效使用資源，並減少對捐助者的依賴。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"On the one hand, financial aid can be essential, especially when a country lacks the basic capital needed to start development projects. Without immediate funding, governments may be unable to build roads, supply clean water, buy medical equipment or keep schools open. For example, after a natural disaster or during a food shortage, direct financial assistance can help authorities respond quickly and prevent a temporary crisis from becoming a national catastrophe. Money also gives local leaders some flexibility because they can allocate it according to urgent domestic needs. Therefore, it is understandable why many people see financial aid as the foundation of development.","chinese":"一方面，財政援助可能是必不可少的，尤其當一個國家缺乏啟動發展項目所需的基本資金時。 如果沒有即時資金，政府可能無法修建道路、供應清潔食水、購買醫療設備，或維持學校運作。 例如，在自然災害之後，或糧食短缺期間，直接的財政援助可以幫助當局迅速應對，並防止一場暫時性的危機演變成全國性的災難。 金錢也能給予本地領導者一定的靈活性，因為他們可以根據國內的緊急需要分配資金。 因此，很多人把財政援助視為發展的基礎，是可以理解的。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"On the other hand, practical aid and professional advice are often more important in the long term. The main problem with money alone is that it can be wasted, mismanaged or spent on short-term solutions if a country does not have the skills and systems to use it well. By contrast, training doctors, advising farmers, improving public administration and helping engineers design reliable infrastructure can create capacity that remains after foreign donors leave. For instance, teaching local agricultural workers how to improve irrigation may raise food production year after year, whereas a cash donation may disappear within months. In this sense, practical support acts like a bridge towards self-reliance rather than a lifeline that must be constantly replaced.","chinese":"另一方面，從長遠來看，實際援助和專業建議往往更加重要。 單靠金錢的主要問題在於，如果一個國家沒有善用資金所需的技能和制度，金錢可能會被浪費、管理不善，或被花在短期解決方案上。 相比之下，培訓醫生、指導農民、改善公共行政，以及幫助工程師設計可靠的基礎建設，都能建立一種即使外國捐助者離開後仍然存在的能力。 例如，教導本地農業工作者如何改善灌溉，可能會年復一年地提高糧食產量，而一筆現金捐款則可能在數月內便消耗殆盡。 從這個意義上說，實際支援就像一座通往自力更生的橋，而不是一條必須不斷更換的救生索。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, financial aid is certainly useful for urgent needs and basic investment. However, I believe practical aid and advice are more important because they build knowledge, strengthen institutions and help developing countries stand on their own feet.","chinese":"總結來說，財政援助對於緊急需要和基本投資當然是有用的。 然而，我認為實際援助和建議更加重要，因為它們能建立知識、強化制度，並幫助發展中國家靠自己的力量站穩腳步。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"international organisations","chinese":"國際組織"},{"english":"support poorer nations","chinese":"支援較貧窮國家"},{"english":"improve infrastructure","chinese":"改善基建"},{"english":"public services","chinese":"公共服務"},{"english":"the most useful form of assistance","chinese":"最有用的援助形式"},{"english":"practical support","chinese":"實際支援"},{"english":"expert guidance","chinese":"專家指導"},{"english":"matter more","chinese":"更重要"},{"english":"discuss both views","chinese":"討論雙方觀點"},{"english":"practical aid and advice","chinese":"實際援助和建議"},{"english":"use resources effectively","chinese":"有效運用資源"},{"english":"become less dependent on","chinese":"減少對……的依賴"},{"english":"donors","chinese":"捐助者"},{"english":"on the one hand","chinese":"一方面"},{"english":"financial aid","chinese":"財政援助"},{"english":"be essential","chinese":"是必要的"},{"english":"especially when","chinese":"尤其當"},{"english":"lack the basic capital needed to","chinese":"缺乏……所需的基本資金"},{"english":"start development projects","chinese":"開展發展項目"},{"english":"immediate funding","chinese":"即時資金"},{"english":"be unable to","chinese":"無法"},{"english":"supply clean water","chinese":"供應清潔食水"},{"english":"buy medical equipment","chinese":"購買醫療設備"},{"english":"keep schools open","chinese":"維持學校運作"},{"english":"a natural disaster","chinese":"自然災害"},{"english":"food shortage","chinese":"糧食短缺"},{"english":"direct financial assistance","chinese":"直接財政援助"},{"english":"authorities","chinese":"當局"},{"english":"respond quickly","chinese":"快速應對"},{"english":"prevent a temporary crisis from becoming","chinese":"防止暫時危機變成"},{"english":"a national catastrophe","chinese":"全國性災難"},{"english":"local leaders","chinese":"本地領袖"},{"english":"give ... some flexibility","chinese":"給予……一定靈活性"},{"english":"allocate it according to","chinese":"按照……分配"},{"english":"urgent domestic needs","chinese":"迫切的國內需要"},{"english":"financial aid as the foundation of development","chinese":"將財政援助視為發展基礎"},{"english":"the foundation of development","chinese":"發展的基礎"},{"english":"on the other hand","chinese":"另一方面"},{"english":"professional advice","chinese":"專業建議"},{"english":"in the long term","chinese":"長遠而言"},{"english":"the main problem with","chinese":"……的主要問題"},{"english":"money alone","chinese":"單靠金錢"},{"english":"be wasted","chinese":"被浪費"},{"english":"mismanaged","chinese":"管理不善"},{"english":"be spent on short-term solutions","chinese":"被花在短期解決方法上"},{"english":"short-term solutions","chinese":"短期解決方法"},{"english":"skills and systems","chinese":"技能和制度"},{"english":"use it well","chinese":"妥善運用它"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相反"},{"english":"training doctors","chinese":"培訓醫生"},{"english":"advising farmers","chinese":"指導農民"},{"english":"improving public administration","chinese":"改善公共行政"},{"english":"public administration","chinese":"公共行政"},{"english":"design reliable infrastructure","chinese":"設計可靠基建"},{"english":"create capacity","chinese":"建立能力"},{"english":"remains after foreign donors leave","chinese":"在外國捐助者離開後仍然保留"},{"english":"foreign donors","chinese":"外國捐助者"},{"english":"local agricultural workers","chinese":"本地農業工人"},{"english":"improve irrigation","chinese":"改善灌溉"},{"english":"raise food production","chinese":"提高糧食產量"},{"english":"year after year","chinese":"年復一年"},{"english":"a cash donation","chinese":"現金捐款"},{"english":"disappear within months","chinese":"在數月內用完"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"act like a bridge towards","chinese":"像通往……的橋樑"},{"english":"self-reliance","chinese":"自力更生"},{"english":"rather than a lifeline","chinese":"而不是救命索"},{"english":"be constantly replaced","chinese":"需要不斷被取代"},{"english":"urgent needs","chinese":"迫切需要"},{"english":"basic investment","chinese":"基本投資"},{"english":"build knowledge","chinese":"建立知識"},{"english":"strengthen institutions","chinese":"加強制度；強化機構"},{"english":"developing countries","chinese":"發展中國家"},{"english":"stand on their own feet","chinese":"自立；靠自己站穩"}]},"model-essay-31-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-31-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:31","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-31-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q31","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The criminal justice system should protect society, but it should also punish offenders in a way that is proportionate and useful. I completely agree that some convicted offenders, particularly those who have committed non-violent or low-level crimes, should be required to do unpaid community work rather than be sent to prison.","chinese":"刑事司法制度應該保護社會，但它也應該以合乎比例並且有實際作用的方式懲罰違法者。 我完全同意，有些被定罪的罪犯，尤其是那些犯下非暴力或低層次罪行的人，應該被要求從事無薪社區工作，而不是被送進監獄。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest argument for this approach is that community service turns punishment into direct repayment. When an offender cleans public parks, repairs community facilities, or supports local charities, the penalty is not merely symbolic; it visibly gives something back to the society that was harmed. This can be more meaningful than locking a minor offender in a cell, where the public receives little benefit and the offender may simply become isolated and resentful. Community work also forces offenders to confront the practical consequences of wrongdoing. Instead of disappearing behind prison walls, they are made to spend time and effort repairing, at least in a modest way, the damage caused by antisocial behaviour. This makes the punishment both corrective and constructive.","chinese":"支持這種做法最有力的論點是，社區服務能把懲罰轉化為直接的補償。 當一名罪犯清潔公共公園、維修社區設施，或支援本地慈善機構時，這種懲罰就不只是象徵性的；它明顯地把一些東西回饋給受害的社會。 這可能比把一名輕微罪犯關進牢房更有意義，因為在監獄中，公眾幾乎得不到實際好處，而罪犯也可能只是變得孤立和怨恨。 社區工作也迫使罪犯面對違法行為所帶來的實際後果。 他們不是消失在監獄高牆之後，而是被要求花時間和精力，以至少較有限但實際的方式，修補反社會行為造成的損害。 這使懲罰既具有糾正作用，也具有建設性。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that prison can be a blunt tool for people who are not genuinely dangerous. Minor offenders who enter prison may lose their jobs, damage family relationships, and mix with more serious criminals. As a result, a short sentence can become a trapdoor rather than a turning point. By contrast, unpaid work allows suitable offenders to remain under supervision while still keeping some connection with normal life. For example, someone convicted of minor theft could be ordered to complete months of supervised work in public spaces. That sentence would still be unpleasant and demanding, but it would be less likely to destroy the person’s chance of rehabilitation.","chinese":"另一個原因是，對於那些並非真正危險的人而言，監獄可能是一種過於粗糙的工具。 進入監獄的輕微罪犯可能會失去工作、破壞家庭關係，並與更嚴重的罪犯混在一起。 結果是，一段短期刑期可能會變成一個陷阱，而不是人生的轉捩點。 相比之下，無薪工作讓合適的罪犯仍然受到監管，同時保持與正常生活的一定連繫。 例如，一名因輕微盜竊而被定罪的人，可以被命令在公共空間完成數個月受監督的工作 這種刑罰仍然會令人不快，而且要求甚高，但它較不可能摧毀這個人改過自新的機會。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully agree that certain prisoners should do unpaid community work instead of being put behind bars. For non-dangerous offenders, it is a fairer, more useful, and more socially productive form of punishment.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意，某些囚犯應該從事無薪社區工作，而不是被關進監獄。 對於非危險罪犯而言，這是一種更公平、更有用，也更能為社會帶來成效的懲罰方式。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"criminal justice system","chinese":"刑事司法制度"},{"english":"protect society","chinese":"保護社會"},{"english":"punish offenders","chinese":"懲罰犯事者"},{"english":"proportionate and useful","chinese":"合乎比例而有用"},{"english":"convicted offenders","chinese":"被定罪的犯事者"},{"english":"non-violent crimes","chinese":"非暴力罪行"},{"english":"low-level crimes","chinese":"輕微罪行"},{"english":"be required to","chinese":"被要求去……"},{"english":"unpaid community work","chinese":"無薪社區工作"},{"english":"rather than be sent to prison","chinese":"而不是被送入監獄"},{"english":"the strongest argument for","chinese":"支持……的最有力論點"},{"english":"community service","chinese":"社區服務"},{"english":"turn punishment into","chinese":"將懲罰變成……"},{"english":"direct repayment","chinese":"直接補償"},{"english":"cleans public parks","chinese":"清潔公共公園"},{"english":"repairs community facilities","chinese":"維修社區設施"},{"english":"supports local charities","chinese":"支援本地慈善機構"},{"english":"the penalty","chinese":"懲罰；刑罰"},{"english":"merely symbolic","chinese":"只是象徵性的"},{"english":"visibly gives something back to","chinese":"明顯地回饋……"},{"english":"the society that was harmed","chinese":"受到傷害的社會"},{"english":"meaningful","chinese":"有意義的"},{"english":"locking a minor offender in a cell","chinese":"將輕微犯事者關進囚室"},{"english":"minor offender","chinese":"輕微犯事者"},{"english":"little benefit","chinese":"很少好處"},{"english":"isolated and resentful","chinese":"孤立和怨恨"},{"english":"confront the practical consequences of","chinese":"面對……的實際後果"},{"english":"wrongdoing","chinese":"不當行為"},{"english":"disappearing behind prison walls","chinese":"消失在監獄高牆後"},{"english":"be made to spend","chinese":"被安排花時間去……"},{"english":"time and effort","chinese":"時間和精力"},{"english":"at least in a modest way","chinese":"至少以有限但實際的方式"},{"english":"damage caused by","chinese":"由……造成的傷害"},{"english":"antisocial behaviour","chinese":"反社會行為"},{"english":"corrective and constructive","chinese":"具糾正作用和建設性"},{"english":"blunt tool","chinese":"粗糙的工具"},{"english":"genuinely dangerous","chinese":"真正危險"},{"english":"enter prison","chinese":"入獄"},{"english":"lose their jobs","chinese":"失去工作"},{"english":"damage family relationships","chinese":"損害家庭關係"},{"english":"mix with","chinese":"與……混在一起"},{"english":"more serious criminals","chinese":"更嚴重的罪犯"},{"english":"short sentence","chinese":"短期刑期"},{"english":"trapdoor rather than a turning point","chinese":"陷阱，而不是轉折點"},{"english":"suitable offenders","chinese":"合適的犯事者"},{"english":"remain under supervision","chinese":"繼續受到監管"},{"english":"keeping some connection with","chinese":"保持與……的一些聯繫"},{"english":"normal life","chinese":"正常生活"},{"english":"convicted of minor theft","chinese":"因輕微盜竊被定罪"},{"english":"be ordered to complete","chinese":"被命令完成"},{"english":"supervised work","chinese":"受監管工作"},{"english":"public spaces","chinese":"公共空間"},{"english":"unpleasant and demanding","chinese":"令人不快而要求高"},{"english":"be less likely to","chinese":"較不可能"},{"english":"destroy the person's chance of","chinese":"破壞某人……的機會"},{"english":"rehabilitation","chinese":"更生"},{"english":"certain prisoners","chinese":"某些囚犯"},{"english":"put behind bars","chinese":"被關進監獄"},{"english":"non-dangerous offenders","chinese":"非危險犯事者"},{"english":"fairer and more useful","chinese":"更公平和更有用"},{"english":"socially productive","chinese":"對社會更有建設性"},{"english":"form of punishment","chinese":"懲罰形式"}]},"model-essay-32-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-32-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:32","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-32-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q32","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In a world where people receive information from newspapers, websites and social media, objectivity in news reporting is often regarded as essential. I do not think all news is true, even when it is produced by established media organisations. In my view, the main function of a newspaper is to give citizens reliable information and help them understand matters of public importance.","chinese":"在一個人們從報紙、網站和社交媒體接收資訊的世界裡，新聞報導中的客觀性通常被視為至關重要。 我並不認為所有新聞都是真實的，即使它們是由成熟的媒體機構製作的。 在我看來，報紙的主要功能是向公民提供可靠資訊，並幫助他們理解具有公共重要性的議題。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Not all news can be considered true because journalism is produced by human beings, and human judgment is never completely neutral. A report may be based on real events, but the choice of headline, sources and images can still shape readers’ interpretation. For example, two newspapers may cover the same protest: one may describe it as a public demand for justice, while another may portray it as a threat to social order. Neither report may be entirely fabricated, but both can guide the reader towards a particular emotional response. In addition, commercial pressure can tempt newspapers to exaggerate stories, simplify complex issues or publish unverified claims in order to attract attention.","chinese":"並非所有新聞都可以被視為真實，因為新聞是由人製作的，而人的判斷從來不可能完全中立。 一篇報導可能以真實事件為基礎，但標題、資料來源和圖片的選擇仍然可以塑造讀者的解讀。 例如，兩份報紙可能報導同一場抗議：其中一份可能把它描述為公眾對公義的訴求，而另一份則可能把它描繪成對社會秩序的威脅。 兩篇報導可能都不是完全捏造的，但它們都可以引導讀者產生某種特定的情緒反應。 此外，商業壓力可能會誘使報紙為了吸引注意力而誇大故事、簡化複雜議題，或刊登未經核實的說法。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The function of a newspaper, therefore, should be more serious than merely entertaining readers or filling pages. Its first responsibility is to inform the public about events that affect their lives, such as government decisions, economic problems, health warnings and social conflicts. More importantly, a newspaper should act as a public watchdog. By investigating corruption, questioning powerful institutions and presenting evidence clearly, it allows ordinary people to judge whether leaders and organisations are acting responsibly. This is especially important because most citizens cannot personally attend court cases, inspect public spending or interview officials. A responsible newspaper becomes their eyes and ears.","chinese":"因此，報紙的功能應該比單純娛樂讀者或填滿版面更加嚴肅。 它的首要責任是讓公眾了解會影響他們生活的事件，例如政府決策、經濟問題、健康警告和社會衝突。 更重要的是，報紙應該扮演公共監察者的角色。 透過調查貪污、質疑有權勢的機構，以及清楚呈現證據，報紙使普通人能夠判斷領袖和組織是否負責任地行事。 這一點尤其重要，因為大多數公民無法親自出席法庭案件、檢查公共開支或訪問官員。 一份負責任的報紙便成為他們的眼睛和耳朵。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I do not believe all news is true, since facts can be selected, framed or distorted. However, this is exactly why newspapers matter. Their proper role is to verify information, explain important issues and protect the public from ignorance, manipulation and blind trust.","chinese":"總結來說，我不相信所有新聞都是真實的，因為事實可以被選擇、被框定，甚至被扭曲。 然而，這正正是報紙重要的原因。 它們真正的角色是核實資訊、解釋重要議題，並保護公眾免於無知、操控和盲目信任。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"receive information from","chinese":"從……接收資訊"},{"english":"newspapers, websites and social media","chinese":"報章、網站和社交媒體"},{"english":"objectivity in news reporting","chinese":"新聞報道中的客觀性"},{"english":"be regarded as essential","chinese":"被視為必不可少"},{"english":"all news is true","chinese":"所有新聞都是真實的"},{"english":"established media organisations","chinese":"具規模的媒體機構"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"the main function of","chinese":"……的主要功能"},{"english":"give citizens reliable information","chinese":"向市民提供可靠資訊"},{"english":"matters of public importance","chinese":"具有公共重要性的事情"},{"english":"can be considered true","chinese":"可被視為真實"},{"english":"produced by human beings","chinese":"由人類製作"},{"english":"human judgment","chinese":"人的判斷"},{"english":"completely neutral","chinese":"完全中立"},{"english":"be based on real events","chinese":"建基於真實事件"},{"english":"the choice of headline","chinese":"標題的選擇"},{"english":"sources and images","chinese":"消息來源和圖片"},{"english":"shape readers' interpretation","chinese":"影響讀者的解讀"},{"english":"cover the same protest","chinese":"報道同一場抗議"},{"english":"a public demand for justice","chinese":"公眾對公義的訴求"},{"english":"portray it as","chinese":"將它描繪成"},{"english":"a threat to social order","chinese":"對社會秩序的威脅"},{"english":"entirely fabricated","chinese":"完全捏造"},{"english":"guide the reader towards","chinese":"引導讀者走向"},{"english":"a particular emotional response","chinese":"某種特定情緒反應"},{"english":"in addition","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"commercial pressure","chinese":"商業壓力"},{"english":"tempt newspapers to","chinese":"誘使報章去"},{"english":"exaggerate stories","chinese":"誇大新聞故事"},{"english":"simplify complex issues","chinese":"簡化複雜議題"},{"english":"publish unverified claims","chinese":"發布未經核實的說法"},{"english":"in order to attract attention","chinese":"為了吸引注意"},{"english":"the function of","chinese":"……的功能"},{"english":"more serious than merely","chinese":"比單純……更嚴肅"},{"english":"entertaining readers","chinese":"娛樂讀者"},{"english":"filling pages","chinese":"填滿版面"},{"english":"first responsibility","chinese":"首要責任"},{"english":"inform the public about","chinese":"向公眾告知有關……"},{"english":"affect their lives","chinese":"影響他們的生活"},{"english":"government decisions","chinese":"政府決定"},{"english":"economic problems","chinese":"經濟問題"},{"english":"health warnings","chinese":"健康警告"},{"english":"social conflicts","chinese":"社會衝突"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"act as a public watchdog","chinese":"擔當公共監察者"},{"english":"investigating corruption","chinese":"調查貪污"},{"english":"questioning powerful institutions","chinese":"質疑有權勢的機構"},{"english":"presenting evidence clearly","chinese":"清楚呈現證據"},{"english":"ordinary people","chinese":"普通人"},{"english":"judge whether","chinese":"判斷是否"},{"english":"leaders and organisations","chinese":"領袖和機構"},{"english":"acting responsibly","chinese":"負責任地行事"},{"english":"especially important","chinese":"特別重要"},{"english":"attend court cases","chinese":"出席法庭案件"},{"english":"inspect public spending","chinese":"審查公共開支"},{"english":"interview officials","chinese":"訪問官員"},{"english":"becomes their eyes and ears","chinese":"成為他們的眼睛和耳朵"},{"english":"since facts can be selected","chinese":"因為事實可以被選取"},{"english":"framed or distorted","chinese":"被框定或扭曲"},{"english":"this is exactly why","chinese":"這正正是為甚麼"},{"english":"newspapers matter","chinese":"報章很重要"},{"english":"proper role","chinese":"應有角色"},{"english":"verify information","chinese":"核實資料"},{"english":"explain important issues","chinese":"解釋重要議題"},{"english":"protect the public from","chinese":"保護公眾免受……影響"},{"english":"ignorance","chinese":"無知"},{"english":"manipulation","chinese":"操控"},{"english":"blind trust","chinese":"盲目信任"}]},"model-essay-32-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-32-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:32","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-32-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q32","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Modern life is increasingly shaped by change, whether in work, technology, relationships, or personal goals. Some people regard this as a positive force because it keeps life dynamic and meaningful, while others argue that constant adjustment can place too much pressure on individuals. In my view, change is ultimately beneficial because it pushes people to grow, even though it can be uncomfortable in the short term.","chinese":"現代生活越來越受到變化塑造，無論是在工作、科技、人際關係，還是個人目標方面。 有些人把這視為一種積極力量，因為它令生活保持動感和意義，而另一些人則認為，持續調整會給個人帶來太大壓力。 在我看來，變化最終是有益的，因為它推動人們成長，即使它在短期內可能令人不舒服"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Those who support change often argue that it prevents people from becoming mentally stagnant. When individuals remain in the same routine for too long, they may become overly comfortable and lose the motivation to develop new skills or explore better opportunities. By contrast, change forces people to adapt, think differently, and become more resilient. For example, a worker who moves into a new industry may initially feel uncertain, but the process can broaden their knowledge, improve their confidence, and open doors that would otherwise remain closed. In this sense, change is not merely a disruption; it is a powerful engine of personal growth.","chinese":"支持變化的人常常認為，它能防止人們在思想上停滯不前。 當個人長時間停留在同一種日常模式中時，他們可能會變得過於安逸，並失去發展新技能或探索更好機會的動力。 相比之下，變化迫使人們適應、以不同方式思考，並變得更有韌性。 例如，一名轉到新行業的員工一開始可能會感到不確定，但這個過程能擴闊他的知識、提升他的信心，並打開原本可能一直關閉的機會之門。 從這個意義上說，變化不僅僅是一種干擾；它是個人成長的強大引擎。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"On the other hand, it is understandable why some people see constant change as demanding. Frequent changes in jobs, living conditions, or social expectations can make people feel unstable and emotionally exhausted. A person who has to keep learning new systems at work, moving to new places, or adjusting to new rules may struggle to build a sense of security. However, this argument mainly shows that change needs to be managed carefully, not that it should be avoided. A life with no change may feel safe, but it can also become narrow, repetitive, and limiting.","chinese":"另一方面，有些人認為持續變化令人吃力，這是可以理解的。 工作、生活條件或社會期望的頻繁變化，會使人感到不穩定，並在情緒上筋疲力盡。 一個必須不斷在工作中學習新系統、搬到新地方，或適應新規則的人，可能會難以建立安全感。 然而，這個論點主要說明的是變化需要被謹慎管理，而不是它應該被避免。 沒有變化的生活可能感覺安全，但它也可能變得狹窄、重複和受限制。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, while constant change can certainly be tiring, I believe that change is generally good for people because it encourages adaptability, courage, and long-term development. Comfort may protect people from stress, but change helps them become stronger.","chinese":"總結來說，雖然持續變化確實可能令人疲倦，但我相信變化對人們整體而言是好的，因為它鼓勵適應力、勇氣和長遠發展。 安逸或許能保護人們免受壓力，但變化能幫助他們變得更強大。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"modern life","chinese":"現代生活"},{"english":"be increasingly shaped by","chinese":"越來越受……塑造"},{"english":"whether in","chinese":"不論是在"},{"english":"personal goals","chinese":"個人目標"},{"english":"regard this as","chinese":"將這視為"},{"english":"a positive force","chinese":"正面的力量"},{"english":"keep life dynamic and meaningful","chinese":"令生活保持有活力和有意義"},{"english":"while others argue that","chinese":"而其他人則認為"},{"english":"constant adjustment","chinese":"持續適應"},{"english":"place too much pressure on","chinese":"對……造成太大壓力"},{"english":"individuals","chinese":"個人"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"ultimately beneficial","chinese":"最終是有益的"},{"english":"push people to grow","chinese":"推動人成長"},{"english":"uncomfortable in the short term","chinese":"短期內令人不適"},{"english":"those who support","chinese":"支持……的人"},{"english":"becoming mentally stagnant","chinese":"思想變得停滯"},{"english":"remain in the same routine","chinese":"留在同一套例行生活中"},{"english":"for too long","chinese":"太久"},{"english":"become overly comfortable","chinese":"變得過於安逸"},{"english":"lose the motivation to","chinese":"失去……的動力"},{"english":"develop new skills","chinese":"培養新技能"},{"english":"explore better opportunities","chinese":"探索更好的機會"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相反"},{"english":"force people to adapt","chinese":"迫使人適應"},{"english":"think differently","chinese":"以不同方式思考"},{"english":"become more resilient","chinese":"變得更有抗逆力"},{"english":"move into a new industry","chinese":"轉到新行業"},{"english":"initially feel uncertain","chinese":"起初感到不確定"},{"english":"the process","chinese":"這個過程"},{"english":"broaden their knowledge","chinese":"擴闊知識"},{"english":"improve their confidence","chinese":"提升信心"},{"english":"open doors","chinese":"帶來機會"},{"english":"would otherwise remain closed","chinese":"否則仍會關閉"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"not merely a disruption","chinese":"不只是干擾"},{"english":"a powerful engine of","chinese":"……的強大推動力"},{"english":"personal growth","chinese":"個人成長"},{"english":"on the other hand","chinese":"另一方面"},{"english":"it is understandable why","chinese":"可以理解為何"},{"english":"see constant change as demanding","chinese":"認為持續改變很吃力"},{"english":"frequent changes","chinese":"頻繁變化"},{"english":"living conditions","chinese":"生活條件"},{"english":"social expectations","chinese":"社會期望"},{"english":"make people feel unstable","chinese":"令人感到不穩定"},{"english":"emotionally exhausted","chinese":"情緒上筋疲力盡"},{"english":"keep learning new systems","chinese":"不斷學習新系統"},{"english":"move to new places","chinese":"搬到新地方"},{"english":"adjust to new rules","chinese":"適應新規則"},{"english":"struggle to build","chinese":"難以建立"},{"english":"a sense of security","chinese":"安全感"},{"english":"mainly shows that","chinese":"主要顯示"},{"english":"be managed carefully","chinese":"被審慎管理"},{"english":"should be avoided","chinese":"應被避免"},{"english":"a life with no change","chinese":"沒有改變的生活"},{"english":"become narrow, repetitive, and limiting","chinese":"變得狹窄、重複而受限制"},{"english":"can certainly be tiring","chinese":"確實可以令人疲累"},{"english":"generally good for","chinese":"一般對……有益"},{"english":"encourage adaptability","chinese":"培養適應能力"},{"english":"courage","chinese":"勇氣"},{"english":"long-term development","chinese":"長遠發展"},{"english":"protect people from stress","chinese":"保護人們免受壓力"},{"english":"become stronger","chinese":"變得更強大"}]},"model-essay-32-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-32-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:32","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-32-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q32","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Crime control is one of the central responsibilities of a justice system, especially when violent offences are involved. Some argue that capital punishment is the most effective response to serious crime. I completely disagree with this view, because the death penalty is a weak deterrent in practice and can distract governments from measures that prevent crime more reliably.","chinese":"控制犯罪是司法制度其中一項核心責任，尤其是在涉及暴力罪行時更是如此。 有些人認為，死刑是應對嚴重犯罪最有效的方式。 我完全不同意這種觀點，因為死刑在實際上嚇阻力薄弱，而且可能使政府忽略那些更可靠地預防犯罪的措施。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first problem is that the death penalty assumes criminals make calm, rational calculations before offending. Many serious crimes, however, are committed in moments of rage, under the influence of drugs, or by people who believe they will not be caught. In such situations, the severity of the possible sentence matters less than the likelihood of detection. A robber who thinks the police will never identify him is unlikely to be stopped by the thought of execution, just as he might ignore a life sentence. What reduces crime more effectively is visible policing, quick investigation, and a court system that makes punishment certain rather than merely extreme.","chinese":"第一個問題是，死刑假設犯罪者在犯罪前會作出冷靜而理性的盤算。 然而，許多嚴重犯罪都是在憤怒失控、受毒品影響，或者由那些相信自己不會被抓到的人所犯下的。 在這種情況下，潛在刑罰的嚴重程度，並不如被偵破的可能性重要。 一名認為警方永遠不會認出他的劫匪，不太可能因為想到會被處決而停止犯罪，就正如他也可能會無視終身監禁一樣。 更有效減少犯罪的，是可見度高的警務、迅速的調查，以及一套能令懲罰變得確定，而不只是極端嚴厲的法庭制度。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The death penalty also creates a serious moral and practical risk. If a person is wrongly convicted, an execution cannot be undone; a justice system that makes even rare mistakes should not use a punishment that leaves no room for correction. Moreover, capital punishment does little to address why serious crime occurs in the first place. Governments would protect the public better by investing in rehabilitation for offenders, support for vulnerable young people, and strong intelligence-led policing against organised crime. Life imprisonment can remove dangerous criminals from society without closing the door on appeals, review, or rehabilitation. This approach is less dramatic, but it is far more defensible and more useful for long-term public safety.","chinese":"死刑也會造成嚴重的道德和實務風險。 如果一個人被錯誤定罪，處決便無法挽回；即使一個司法制度只是偶爾犯錯，它也不應使用一種完全沒有修正空間的刑罰。 此外，死刑幾乎無法處理嚴重犯罪最初發生的原因。 政府若投資於罪犯更生、支援弱勢年輕人，以及針對有組織犯罪的強力情報主導警務，會更能保護公眾。 終身監禁可以把危險罪犯與社會隔離，同時不會關上上訴、覆核或更生的大門。 這種做法沒有那麼戲劇化，但它更站得住腳，也更有助於長遠的公共安全。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, the death penalty is not the best way to reduce serious crime. A safer society is built not by the harshest punishment, but by reliable policing, fair trials, prevention, and penalties that protect the public without risking irreversible injustice.","chinese":"總結來說，死刑並不是減少嚴重犯罪的最佳方法。 一個更安全的社會不是由最嚴厲的刑罰建立起來的，而是由可靠的警務、公平的審訊、犯罪預防，以及能保護公眾而不會冒上不可逆轉不公義風險的刑罰建立起來的。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"Crime control","chinese":"犯罪管控"},{"english":"central responsibilities","chinese":"核心責任"},{"english":"justice system","chinese":"司法制度"},{"english":"violent offences","chinese":"暴力罪行"},{"english":"be involved","chinese":"涉及其中"},{"english":"capital punishment","chinese":"死刑"},{"english":"the most effective response to","chinese":"對……最有效的回應"},{"english":"serious crime","chinese":"嚴重罪行"},{"english":"the death penalty","chinese":"死刑"},{"english":"weak deterrent","chinese":"阻嚇力弱的措施"},{"english":"in practice","chinese":"實際上"},{"english":"distract governments from","chinese":"令政府分心，忽略……"},{"english":"prevent crime more reliably","chinese":"更可靠地預防犯罪"},{"english":"assumes criminals make","chinese":"假設罪犯會作出……"},{"english":"calm, rational calculations","chinese":"冷靜而理性的計算"},{"english":"before offending","chinese":"犯案之前"},{"english":"be committed in moments of rage","chinese":"在憤怒一刻犯下"},{"english":"under the influence of drugs","chinese":"受毒品影響"},{"english":"believe they will not be caught","chinese":"相信自己不會被捕"},{"english":"in such situations","chinese":"在這些情況下"},{"english":"severity of the possible sentence","chinese":"可能刑罰的嚴重程度"},{"english":"matters less than","chinese":"不及……重要"},{"english":"likelihood of detection","chinese":"被偵破的可能性"},{"english":"robber","chinese":"劫匪"},{"english":"identify him","chinese":"辨認出他"},{"english":"be unlikely to be stopped by","chinese":"不大可能因……而被阻止"},{"english":"the thought of execution","chinese":"被處決的想法"},{"english":"life sentence","chinese":"終身監禁"},{"english":"visible policing","chinese":"可見的警力巡邏"},{"english":"quick investigation","chinese":"迅速調查"},{"english":"court system","chinese":"法庭制度"},{"english":"punishment certain","chinese":"刑罰確定"},{"english":"rather than merely extreme","chinese":"而不是只是極端嚴厲"},{"english":"moral and practical risk","chinese":"道德和實際風險"},{"english":"wrongly convicted","chinese":"被錯誤定罪"},{"english":"cannot be undone","chinese":"無法撤銷"},{"english":"rare mistakes","chinese":"罕見錯誤"},{"english":"leaves no room for correction","chinese":"沒有改正空間"},{"english":"address why","chinese":"處理為甚麼……"},{"english":"in the first place","chinese":"最初；根本上"},{"english":"protect the public","chinese":"保護公眾"},{"english":"investing in","chinese":"投資於……"},{"english":"rehabilitation for offenders","chinese":"犯事者更生"},{"english":"vulnerable young people","chinese":"弱勢年輕人"},{"english":"intelligence-led policing","chinese":"情報主導的警務工作"},{"english":"organised crime","chinese":"有組織犯罪"},{"english":"life imprisonment","chinese":"終身監禁"},{"english":"remove dangerous criminals from society","chinese":"將危險罪犯與社會隔離"},{"english":"without closing the door on","chinese":"而不關上……的大門"},{"english":"appeals","chinese":"上訴"},{"english":"review","chinese":"覆核"},{"english":"less dramatic","chinese":"較不戲劇化"},{"english":"far more defensible","chinese":"合理得多；更站得住腳"},{"english":"long-term public safety","chinese":"長遠公共安全"},{"english":"reduce serious crime","chinese":"減少嚴重罪行"},{"english":"safer society","chinese":"更安全的社會"},{"english":"harshest punishment","chinese":"最嚴厲的懲罰"},{"english":"reliable policing","chinese":"可靠的警務工作"},{"english":"fair trials","chinese":"公平審訊"},{"english":"prevention","chinese":"預防"},{"english":"penalties","chinese":"刑罰"},{"english":"irreversible injustice","chinese":"無法逆轉的不公義"}]},"model-essay-33-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-33-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:33","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-33-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q33","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Modern news coverage often gives the impression that the world is dominated by conflict, disaster and crime. This is not because positive events are rare, but because negative events are usually more urgent, dramatic and commercially powerful. In my view, news organisations should present a healthier balance of both good and bad news.","chinese":"現代新聞報道往往給人一種印象，彷彿這個世界是由衝突、災難和犯罪所主導的。 這並不是因為正面的事情很少發生，而是因為負面事件通常更緊急、更具戲劇性，也更具商業吸引力。 在我看來，新聞機構應該呈現一種更健康的平衡，同時報道好消息和壞消息。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"There are two main reasons why bad news receives so much attention. Firstly, serious events such as wars, famines and accidents have immediate consequences for public safety, so journalists naturally treat them as priorities. If a disease spreads, a violent crime occurs, or a natural disaster destroys homes, people need to know quickly. Secondly, negative stories tend to attract stronger emotional reactions. Fear, shock and anger make people click, watch and share, which means media companies can gain larger audiences by focusing on crises rather than ordinary progress. In this sense, bad news often works like a loud alarm bell: it is hard to ignore, even when people are tired of hearing it.","chinese":"壞消息受到如此多關注，主要有兩個原因。 首先，戰爭、饑荒和意外事故等嚴重事件會對公共安全造成即時影響，因此記者自然會把它們視為優先報道的內容。 如果一種疾病正在傳播、一宗暴力犯罪發生，或一場自然災害摧毀了家園，人們就需要盡快知道。 其次，負面新聞往往更容易引發強烈的情緒反應。 恐懼、震驚和憤怒會促使人們點擊、觀看和分享，這意味著媒體公司透過聚焦危機，而不是普通的進步，可以獲得更大的受眾。 從這個角度來看，壞消息往往像一個響亮的警鐘：即使人們已經厭倦聽到它，也很難忽視它。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, I believe the news should include more positive stories as well. A constant stream of tragedy can make people feel helpless and cynical, as if society is only moving backwards. This is a distorted picture of reality. For example, stories about medical breakthroughs, successful community projects or declining crime in some areas can remind the public that problems are not always permanent. Good news does not mean shallow entertainment; it can show solutions, inspire responsible behaviour and give people a more complete understanding of the world. If journalism only shows the wound and never the healing, it fails to tell the whole story.","chinese":"然而，我認為新聞也應該包含更多正面的故事。 源源不絕的悲劇新聞可能會令人感到無助和憤世嫉俗，彷彿社會只是在不斷倒退。 這是一幅被扭曲的現實圖像。 例如，關於醫學突破、成功的社區項目，或某些地區犯罪率下降的新聞，可以提醒公眾：問題並不總是永久存在的。 好消息並不等於膚淺的娛樂；它可以展示解決方案、激發負責任的行為，並讓人們對世界有更完整的理解。 如果新聞只展示傷口，卻從不展示癒合的過程，它就沒有把整個故事說完整。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, bad news dominates because it is urgent, emotionally powerful and commercially attractive. Nevertheless, news outlets should report both negative and positive developments, since a balanced news diet would keep people informed without making them unnecessarily pessimistic.","chinese":"總結來說，壞消息佔主導地位，是因為它緊急、情緒力量強，也具有商業吸引力。 然而，新聞機構應該同時報道負面和正面的發展，因為平衡的新聞內容能讓人們保持知情，而不會使他們不必要地變得悲觀。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"modern news coverage","chinese":"現代新聞報道"},{"english":"gives the impression that","chinese":"給人……的印象"},{"english":"be dominated by","chinese":"被……主導"},{"english":"conflict, disaster and crime","chinese":"衝突、災難和罪案"},{"english":"positive events","chinese":"正面事件"},{"english":"not because...but because...","chinese":"不是因為……而是因為……"},{"english":"negative events","chinese":"負面事件"},{"english":"more urgent, dramatic and commercially powerful","chinese":"更緊急、更戲劇化、更具商業力量"},{"english":"news organisations","chinese":"新聞機構"},{"english":"present a healthier balance of","chinese":"呈現更健康的平衡"},{"english":"good and bad news","chinese":"好消息和壞消息"},{"english":"two main reasons why","chinese":"兩個主要原因解釋為何"},{"english":"receives so much attention","chinese":"受到如此多關注"},{"english":"serious events","chinese":"嚴重事件"},{"english":"wars, famines and accidents","chinese":"戰爭、饑荒和意外"},{"english":"immediate consequences for","chinese":"對……有即時後果"},{"english":"public safety","chinese":"公眾安全"},{"english":"treat them as priorities","chinese":"把它們視為優先事項"},{"english":"a disease spreads","chinese":"疾病傳播"},{"english":"a violent crime occurs","chinese":"暴力罪案發生"},{"english":"a natural disaster destroys homes","chinese":"天災摧毀家園"},{"english":"need to know quickly","chinese":"需要迅速知道"},{"english":"negative stories","chinese":"負面新聞故事"},{"english":"tend to attract","chinese":"往往吸引"},{"english":"stronger emotional reactions","chinese":"更強烈的情緒反應"},{"english":"fear, shock and anger","chinese":"恐懼、震驚和憤怒"},{"english":"click, watch and share","chinese":"點擊、觀看和分享"},{"english":"media companies","chinese":"媒體公司"},{"english":"gain larger audiences","chinese":"獲得更大觀眾群"},{"english":"focusing on crises","chinese":"聚焦危機"},{"english":"ordinary progress","chinese":"平常的進步"},{"english":"In this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"works like a loud alarm bell","chinese":"像響亮的警鐘一樣發揮作用"},{"english":"hard to ignore","chinese":"難以忽視"},{"english":"tired of hearing it","chinese":"厭倦聽到它"},{"english":"include more positive stories","chinese":"包含更多正面故事"},{"english":"a constant stream of","chinese":"源源不絕的……"},{"english":"tragedy","chinese":"悲劇"},{"english":"feel helpless and cynical","chinese":"感到無助和憤世嫉俗"},{"english":"as if","chinese":"彷彿"},{"english":"moving backwards","chinese":"倒退"},{"english":"a distorted picture of reality","chinese":"扭曲的現實圖像"},{"english":"medical breakthroughs","chinese":"醫學突破"},{"english":"successful community projects","chinese":"成功的社區項目"},{"english":"declining crime","chinese":"罪案下降"},{"english":"remind the public that","chinese":"提醒公眾"},{"english":"not always permanent","chinese":"並不總是永久的"},{"english":"shallow entertainment","chinese":"膚淺娛樂"},{"english":"show solutions","chinese":"展示解決方法"},{"english":"inspire responsible behaviour","chinese":"鼓勵負責任的行為"},{"english":"a more complete understanding of","chinese":"對……更完整的理解"},{"english":"journalism","chinese":"新聞工作；新聞業"},{"english":"shows the wound and never the healing","chinese":"只展示傷口而從不展示痊癒"},{"english":"fails to tell","chinese":"未能講述"},{"english":"the whole story","chinese":"完整故事"},{"english":"bad news dominates","chinese":"壞消息佔主導"},{"english":"emotionally powerful","chinese":"情緒感染力強"},{"english":"commercially attractive","chinese":"具有商業吸引力"},{"english":"news outlets","chinese":"新聞媒體"},{"english":"negative and positive developments","chinese":"負面和正面發展"},{"english":"a balanced news diet","chinese":"均衡的新聞資訊"},{"english":"keep people informed","chinese":"讓人們掌握資訊"},{"english":"without making them unnecessarily pessimistic","chinese":"不會令他們不必要地悲觀"}]},"model-essay-33-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-33-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:33","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-33-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q33","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Some people regard the search for extraterrestrial intelligence as one of humanity’s most exciting scientific ambitions. While a number of scientists believe that we should actively send messages to possible life forms beyond Earth, others argue that such contact could expose humanity to unnecessary danger. I strongly agree with the latter view, because the possible risks are far greater than the likely benefits.","chinese":"有些人認為，尋找外星智慧生命是人類最令人振奮的科學抱負之一。 雖然一些科學家認為我們應該主動向地球以外可能存在的生命形式發送訊息，但另一些人則認為，這種接觸可能會使人類暴露於不必要的危險之中。 我強烈同意後一種觀點，因為潛在風險遠遠大於可能帶來的好處。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Those who support sending signals argue that contact with intelligent aliens could transform human knowledge. If another civilisation were advanced enough to receive and understand our messages, it might also possess scientific insights far beyond our own. Communication with such beings could, in theory, help humans understand space, technology and even the origins of life more deeply. Moreover, the attempt itself may encourage international cooperation, since sending a message into space would require scientists, governments and institutions to work towards a shared goal rather than compete with one another.","chinese":"支持發送訊號的人認為，與有智慧的外星生命接觸可能會徹底改變人類的知識。 如果另一個文明先進到能夠接收並理解我們的訊息，它也可能擁有遠遠超越我們的科學見解。 從理論上說，與這些生命溝通可以幫助人類更深入地理解太空、科技，甚至生命的起源。 此外，這種嘗試本身也可能促進國際合作，因為向太空發送訊息需要科學家、政府和機構朝著共同目標努力，而不是彼此競爭。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, I believe this optimism rests on a dangerous assumption: that any intelligent life we contact would be peaceful or helpful. Once a message is sent, it cannot be recalled, and humanity would have no control over who receives it or how they respond. A civilisation capable of travelling across vast distances might be far more technologically powerful than we are, and revealing our location could be like opening a door without knowing who is standing outside. Even if the chance of harm is small, the scale of the possible damage is so great that caution is the only responsible position.","chinese":"然而，我認為這種樂觀建立在一個危險的假設之上：那就是我們接觸到的任何智慧生命都會是和平或有幫助的。 一旦訊息被發出，它就無法被收回，而人類也無法控制誰接收到它，或對方如何回應 一個能夠跨越遙遠距離旅行的文明，可能在科技上遠比我們強大，而暴露我們的位置就像在不知道門外站著誰的情況下打開大門。 即使造成傷害的機會很小，潛在破壞的規模也如此巨大，以至於謹慎才是唯一負責任的立場。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, although sending messages to other planets could satisfy human curiosity and may lead to extraordinary discoveries, it is an unacceptable risk. Humanity should continue studying space and listening for signals, but deliberately announcing our presence to unknown civilisations is a gamble we should not take.","chinese":"總結來說，雖然向其他星球發送訊息可以滿足人類的好奇心，並可能帶來非凡的發現，但這是一個不可接受的風險。 人類應該繼續研究太空並聆聽訊號，但刻意向未知文明宣告我們的存在，是一場我們不應承擔的賭博。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"regard ... as","chinese":"將……視為"},{"english":"the search for extraterrestrial intelligence","chinese":"尋找外星智慧生命"},{"english":"one of humanity's most exciting scientific ambitions","chinese":"人類最令人興奮的科學抱負之一"},{"english":"a number of scientists","chinese":"一些科學家"},{"english":"actively send messages to","chinese":"主動向……發送訊息"},{"english":"possible life forms beyond Earth","chinese":"地球以外可能存在的生命體"},{"english":"such contact","chinese":"這種接觸"},{"english":"expose humanity to unnecessary danger","chinese":"使人類暴露於不必要的危險"},{"english":"the latter view","chinese":"後者觀點"},{"english":"possible risks","chinese":"可能風險"},{"english":"far greater than","chinese":"遠大於"},{"english":"the likely benefits","chinese":"可能帶來的好處"},{"english":"support sending signals","chinese":"支持發送信號"},{"english":"contact with intelligent aliens","chinese":"與智慧外星生命接觸"},{"english":"transform human knowledge","chinese":"改變人類知識"},{"english":"advanced enough to","chinese":"先進到足以"},{"english":"receive and understand our messages","chinese":"接收並理解我們的訊息"},{"english":"possess scientific insights","chinese":"擁有科學見解"},{"english":"far beyond our own","chinese":"遠超我們自己的"},{"english":"communication with","chinese":"與……溝通"},{"english":"such beings","chinese":"這類生命體"},{"english":"in theory","chinese":"理論上"},{"english":"the origins of life","chinese":"生命的起源"},{"english":"more deeply","chinese":"更深入地"},{"english":"the attempt itself","chinese":"嘗試本身"},{"english":"encourage international cooperation","chinese":"促進國際合作"},{"english":"sending a message into space","chinese":"向太空發送訊息"},{"english":"require scientists, governments and institutions to","chinese":"需要科學家、政府和機構去"},{"english":"work towards a shared goal","chinese":"為共同目標努力"},{"english":"rather than compete with one another","chinese":"而不是互相競爭"},{"english":"this optimism","chinese":"這種樂觀想法"},{"english":"rest on","chinese":"建基於"},{"english":"a dangerous assumption","chinese":"危險假設"},{"english":"intelligent life","chinese":"智慧生命"},{"english":"peaceful or helpful","chinese":"和平或有幫助"},{"english":"once a message is sent","chinese":"訊息一旦發出"},{"english":"cannot be recalled","chinese":"不能被收回"},{"english":"have no control over","chinese":"無法控制"},{"english":"how they respond","chinese":"他們如何回應"},{"english":"capable of travelling across vast distances","chinese":"有能力跨越遙遠距離"},{"english":"technologically powerful","chinese":"科技強大"},{"english":"revealing our location","chinese":"暴露我們的位置"},{"english":"be like opening a door","chinese":"就像打開一扇門"},{"english":"without knowing who is standing outside","chinese":"不知道門外站着誰"},{"english":"even if the chance of harm is small","chinese":"即使造成傷害的機會很小"},{"english":"the scale of the possible damage","chinese":"可能損害的規模"},{"english":"caution","chinese":"謹慎"},{"english":"the only responsible position","chinese":"唯一負責任的立場"},{"english":"sending messages to other planets","chinese":"向其他星球發送訊息"},{"english":"satisfy human curiosity","chinese":"滿足人類好奇心"},{"english":"lead to extraordinary discoveries","chinese":"帶來非凡發現"},{"english":"an unacceptable risk","chinese":"不能接受的風險"},{"english":"continue studying space","chinese":"繼續研究太空"},{"english":"listening for signals","chinese":"聆聽信號"},{"english":"deliberately announcing our presence","chinese":"故意宣告我們的存在"},{"english":"unknown civilisations","chinese":"未知文明"},{"english":"a gamble we should not take","chinese":"我們不應冒的賭注"}]},"model-essay-33-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-33-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:33","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-33-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q33","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Crime is a serious social problem, and many people believe that offenders should simply be sent to prison. While imprisonment may appear to be the most direct response to criminal behaviour, I firmly believe that it is not the best general solution. In most cases, rehabilitation and carefully supervised community-based punishments are more effective because they address the causes of crime rather than merely hiding criminals from society.","chinese":"犯罪是一個嚴重的社會問題，而許多人認為罪犯應該直接被送入監獄。 雖然監禁看起來可能是對犯罪行為最直接的回應， 我堅定地認為，這並不是一般情況下最好的解決方法。在大多數情況下，改造和受到仔細監管的社區式懲罰更加有效，因為它們處理的是犯罪的根源，而不是僅僅把罪犯從社會中隱藏起來。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Supporters of prison often argue that it protects the public and sends a clear warning to potential offenders. This view is understandable because dangerous criminals can cause real harm if they remain free. However, prison often treats the symptom rather than the disease. Many offenders commit crimes because of addiction, poor education, unemployment, or unstable family backgrounds. If these problems are ignored, prison can become a revolving door: criminals enter, serve their sentence, and return to society with the same weaknesses, or sometimes even worse ones. For example, a young person who commits a minor theft may leave prison with fewer job prospects and stronger links to hardened criminals. In this sense, prison can punish crime without actually reducing it.","chinese":"支持監禁的人經常認為，監獄能保護公眾，並向潛在犯罪者發出清晰警告。 這種看法是可以理解的，因為危險的罪犯如果仍然自由，確實可能造成真正的傷害。 然而，監獄往往處理的是症狀，而不是疾病本身。 許多犯罪者犯罪，是因為成癮、教育不足、失業，或不穩定的家庭背景。 如果這些問題被忽視，監獄就可能變成一扇旋轉門：罪犯進去、服刑，然後帶著同樣的弱點，甚至有時帶著更嚴重的問題回到社會。 例如，一個犯下輕微盜竊的年輕人，出獄後可能會有更少的就業機會，並與慣犯建立更深的聯繫。 從這個意義上說，監獄可以懲罰犯罪，卻未必真正減少犯罪。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"A better approach is to combine punishment with rehabilitation. Offenders should still face consequences, but those consequences should help them rebuild their lives and repay society. Drug treatment, psychological counselling, vocational training, community service, and victim compensation can all make punishment more constructive. For instance, someone who has committed a non-violent offence could be required to work in the community while attending training courses and meeting strict supervision conditions. This approach does not excuse the crime; rather, it turns punishment into a ladder instead of a cage. It gives offenders a realistic path back into society, which ultimately makes communities safer.","chinese":"更好的方法是把懲罰與改造結合起來。 犯罪者仍然應該承擔後果，但這些後果應該幫助他們重建生活，並回饋社會。 戒毒治療、心理輔導、職業培訓、社區服務，以及對受害者的賠償，都可以讓懲罰變得更具建設性。 例如，一個犯下非暴力罪行的人，可以被要求在社區工作，同時參加培訓課程，並遵守嚴格的監管條件。 這種方法並不是在為犯罪開脫；相反，它把懲罰變成一把梯子，而不是一個牢籠。 它給犯罪者一條實際可行的回歸社會之路，而這最終會令社區更加安全。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, prison may look like a strong solution, but it is often a blunt instrument. I believe that rehabilitation and structured alternatives are better ways to deal with most criminals because they reduce reoffending, repair damage, and help society break the cycle of crime.","chinese":"總結來說，監獄可能看起來是一種有力的解決方法，但它往往是一種粗糙不精準的工具 我認為，改造和有結構的替代方案是處理大多數罪犯更好的方法，因為它們能減少再犯、修補傷害，並幫助社會打破犯罪循環。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"crime","chinese":"犯罪"},{"english":"serious social problem","chinese":"嚴重社會問題"},{"english":"offenders","chinese":"犯事者"},{"english":"be sent to prison","chinese":"被送入監獄"},{"english":"imprisonment","chinese":"監禁"},{"english":"appear to be","chinese":"看似是"},{"english":"direct response to","chinese":"對……的直接回應"},{"english":"criminal behaviour","chinese":"犯罪行為"},{"english":"general solution","chinese":"一般解決方法"},{"english":"rehabilitation","chinese":"更生；改造"},{"english":"carefully supervised","chinese":"受到小心監管"},{"english":"community-based punishments","chinese":"社區為本的懲罰"},{"english":"more effective","chinese":"更有效"},{"english":"address the causes of crime","chinese":"處理犯罪成因"},{"english":"rather than merely","chinese":"而不是只是"},{"english":"hiding criminals from society","chinese":"將罪犯從社會中藏起來"},{"english":"supporters of prison","chinese":"支持監禁的人"},{"english":"protect the public","chinese":"保護公眾"},{"english":"send a clear warning to","chinese":"向……發出清晰警告"},{"english":"potential offenders","chinese":"潛在犯事者"},{"english":"understandable","chinese":"可以理解的"},{"english":"dangerous criminals","chinese":"危險罪犯"},{"english":"cause real harm","chinese":"造成真正傷害"},{"english":"remain free","chinese":"仍然自由"},{"english":"treat the symptom rather than the disease","chinese":"治標不治本"},{"english":"commit crimes","chinese":"犯罪"},{"english":"addiction","chinese":"成癮"},{"english":"poor education","chinese":"教育不足"},{"english":"unemployment","chinese":"失業"},{"english":"unstable family backgrounds","chinese":"不穩定的家庭背景"},{"english":"be ignored","chinese":"被忽視"},{"english":"revolving door","chinese":"循環不息的情況"},{"english":"serve their sentence","chinese":"服刑"},{"english":"return to society","chinese":"重返社會"},{"english":"with the same weaknesses","chinese":"帶着同樣弱點"},{"english":"minor theft","chinese":"輕微盜竊"},{"english":"job prospects","chinese":"就業前景"},{"english":"stronger links to","chinese":"與……有更強聯繫"},{"english":"hardened criminals","chinese":"老練罪犯；慣犯"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"punish crime","chinese":"懲罰犯罪"},{"english":"actually reducing it","chinese":"真正減少它"},{"english":"a better approach","chinese":"更好的方法"},{"english":"combine punishment with rehabilitation","chinese":"將懲罰與更生結合"},{"english":"face consequences","chinese":"承擔後果"},{"english":"rebuild their lives","chinese":"重建生活"},{"english":"repay society","chinese":"回報社會；彌補社會"},{"english":"drug treatment","chinese":"戒毒治療"},{"english":"psychological counselling","chinese":"心理輔導"},{"english":"vocational training","chinese":"職業培訓"},{"english":"community service","chinese":"社區服務"},{"english":"victim compensation","chinese":"對受害者的賠償"},{"english":"constructive","chinese":"有建設性的"},{"english":"non-violent offence","chinese":"非暴力罪行"},{"english":"be required to","chinese":"被要求去……"},{"english":"work in the community","chinese":"在社區工作"},{"english":"training courses","chinese":"培訓課程"},{"english":"strict supervision conditions","chinese":"嚴格監管條件"},{"english":"excuse the crime","chinese":"為罪行開脫"},{"english":"turn punishment into","chinese":"將懲罰變成……"},{"english":"a ladder instead of a cage","chinese":"階梯而不是牢籠"},{"english":"realistic path back into society","chinese":"重返社會的現實途徑"},{"english":"ultimately","chinese":"最終"},{"english":"makes communities safer","chinese":"令社區更安全"},{"english":"strong solution","chinese":"強硬的解決方法"},{"english":"blunt instrument","chinese":"粗糙的工具"},{"english":"structured alternatives","chinese":"有系統的替代方案"},{"english":"deal with","chinese":"處理"},{"english":"reduce reoffending","chinese":"減少重犯"},{"english":"repair damage","chinese":"修補傷害"},{"english":"break the cycle of crime","chinese":"打破犯罪循環"}]},"model-essay-34-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-34-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:34","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-34-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q34","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Films are now consumed in a highly globalised media environment, where audiences can access productions from almost anywhere. Many viewers therefore choose international films over domestic ones because they often seem more polished, more varied, and better advertised. In my view, governments should increase support for the local film industry because it protects cultural identity and develops creative talent.","chinese":"如今，電影是在高度全球化的媒體環境中被觀看的，觀眾幾乎可以接觸到來自世界任何地方的作品。 因此，許多觀眾會選擇國際電影而不是本地電影，因為這些電影往往看起來製作更精良、種類更多元，而且宣傳也更到位。 在我看來，政府應該增加對本地電影業的支持，因為這能保護文化身份，並培養創意人才。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main reason foreign films attract large audiences is that they usually benefit from stronger commercial backing. Major studios can spend heavily on famous actors, visual effects, sound design, and worldwide promotion, so their films often feel exciting before the audience has even entered the cinema. They also tend to offer a wide range of genres, from superhero stories to historical dramas, which allows viewers to find something that matches their taste. By contrast, local films, especially in smaller markets, may have weaker marketing and fewer technical resources. Even when the storytelling is strong, the film can struggle to reach the public. In this sense, foreign cinema sometimes wins not because it is always better, but because it arrives with a louder voice and a brighter spotlight.","chinese":"外國電影吸引大量觀眾的主要原因，是它們通常受惠於更強大的商業支持。 大型電影公司可以在知名演員、視覺特效、音效設計和全球宣傳上投入大量資金，因此它們的電影往往在觀眾真正走進戲院之前，已經讓人覺得令人期待。 它們也往往提供種類廣泛的電影類型，從超級英雄故事到歷史劇都有，這讓觀眾能找到符合自己口味的作品。 相比之下，本地電影，尤其是在較小市場中的本地電影，可能行銷能力較弱，技術資源也較少。 即使故事本身很出色，這部電影也可能難以接觸到大眾。 從這個角度來看，外國電影有時勝出，並不是因為它總是更好，而是因為它帶著更響亮的聲音和更明亮的聚光燈登場。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"For this reason, I believe public funding for local cinema is necessary. Films are not only commercial products; they are also a way for a society to remember its language, values, humour, landscapes, and everyday problems. Without support, many local directors and writers may be forced to copy foreign formulas or leave the industry altogether. Government grants, training schemes, and subsidies for cinemas that show domestic films can give new talent room to breathe. For example, a young filmmaker who receives funding may tell a story about local families, workplaces, or traditions that international studios would never produce. This strengthens a whole creative ecosystem.","chinese":"基於這個原因，我認為公共資金支持本地電影是必要的。 電影不只是商業產品；它們也是一個社會記住自身語言、價值觀、幽默、風景和日常問題的一種方式。 如果沒有支持，許多本地導演和編劇可能會被迫模仿外國公式，或者乾脆完全離開這個行業。 政府補助、培訓計劃，以及對放映本地電影的戲院提供資助，都可以給新人才喘息和發展的空間。 例如，一位獲得資助的年輕電影製作人，可能會講述關於本地家庭、工作場所或傳統的故事，而這些故事是國際電影公司永遠不會製作的。 這能強化整個創意生態系統。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, people often prefer foreign films because they are better funded, promoted, and distributed. Nevertheless, governments should spend more money on local film industries, since national cinema preserves culture and gives local talent a genuine chance to grow.","chinese":"總結來說，人們經常較喜歡外國電影，是因為它們有更充足的資金、更強的宣傳，以及更完善的發行渠道。 然而，政府應該在本地電影業上投入更多資金，因為國家電影能保存文化，並給予本地人才真正成長的機會。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"be consumed in","chinese":"在……中被觀看；被消費"},{"english":"a highly globalised media environment","chinese":"高度全球化的媒體環境"},{"english":"audiences can access","chinese":"觀眾可以接觸到"},{"english":"productions from almost anywhere","chinese":"來自幾乎任何地方的作品"},{"english":"choose international films over","chinese":"選擇國際電影而不是"},{"english":"domestic ones","chinese":"本地電影"},{"english":"more polished","chinese":"更精緻"},{"english":"more varied","chinese":"更多元化"},{"english":"better advertised","chinese":"宣傳得更好"},{"english":"increase support for","chinese":"加強對……的支持"},{"english":"the local film industry","chinese":"本地電影業"},{"english":"protects cultural identity","chinese":"保護文化身份認同"},{"english":"develops creative talent","chinese":"培養創作人才"},{"english":"the main reason","chinese":"主要原因"},{"english":"attract large audiences","chinese":"吸引大量觀眾"},{"english":"benefit from","chinese":"受惠於"},{"english":"stronger commercial backing","chinese":"更強的商業支持"},{"english":"major studios","chinese":"大型電影公司"},{"english":"spend heavily on","chinese":"大量花費於"},{"english":"famous actors","chinese":"著名演員"},{"english":"visual effects","chinese":"視覺特效"},{"english":"sound design","chinese":"音效設計"},{"english":"worldwide promotion","chinese":"全球宣傳"},{"english":"feel exciting before","chinese":"在……之前已令人期待"},{"english":"entered the cinema","chinese":"進入戲院"},{"english":"tend to offer","chinese":"往往提供"},{"english":"a wide range of genres","chinese":"廣泛的電影類型"},{"english":"superhero stories","chinese":"超級英雄故事"},{"english":"historical dramas","chinese":"歷史劇"},{"english":"allows viewers to","chinese":"讓觀眾可以"},{"english":"matches their taste","chinese":"符合他們的口味"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"local films","chinese":"本地電影"},{"english":"smaller markets","chinese":"較小的市場"},{"english":"weaker marketing","chinese":"較弱的市場推廣"},{"english":"fewer technical resources","chinese":"較少技術資源"},{"english":"the storytelling is strong","chinese":"故事性強"},{"english":"struggle to reach the public","chinese":"難以接觸大眾"},{"english":"In this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"foreign cinema","chinese":"外國電影"},{"english":"not because it is always better","chinese":"並不是因為它總是更好"},{"english":"arrives with a louder voice","chinese":"以更響亮的聲音登場"},{"english":"a brighter spotlight","chinese":"更耀眼的聚光燈"},{"english":"public funding","chinese":"公共資金；政府資助"},{"english":"local cinema","chinese":"本地電影"},{"english":"commercial products","chinese":"商業產品"},{"english":"a way for a society to","chinese":"社會用來……的一種方式"},{"english":"remember its language","chinese":"記住自身語言"},{"english":"everyday problems","chinese":"日常問題"},{"english":"without support","chinese":"沒有支持"},{"english":"local directors and writers","chinese":"本地導演和編劇"},{"english":"be forced to","chinese":"被迫"},{"english":"copy foreign formulas","chinese":"模仿外國公式"},{"english":"leave the industry altogether","chinese":"完全離開這個行業"},{"english":"government grants","chinese":"政府撥款"},{"english":"training schemes","chinese":"培訓計劃"},{"english":"subsidies for cinemas","chinese":"給戲院的津貼"},{"english":"domestic films","chinese":"本地電影"},{"english":"give new talent room to breathe","chinese":"給新人才發展空間"},{"english":"receives funding","chinese":"獲得資助"},{"english":"local families","chinese":"本地家庭"},{"english":"workplaces","chinese":"工作場所"},{"english":"traditions","chinese":"傳統"},{"english":"international studios","chinese":"國際電影公司"},{"english":"strengthens a whole creative ecosystem","chinese":"加強整個創意生態系統"},{"english":"better funded","chinese":"資金更充足"},{"english":"promoted and distributed","chinese":"宣傳和發行得更好"},{"english":"spend more money on","chinese":"在……上花更多錢"},{"english":"local film industries","chinese":"本地電影業"},{"english":"national cinema","chinese":"國家電影；本土電影"},{"english":"preserves culture","chinese":"保存文化"},{"english":"a genuine chance to","chinese":"真正的機會去"},{"english":"grow","chinese":"成長；發展"}]},"model-essay-34-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-34-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:34","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-34-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q34","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Human curiosity has always pushed society beyond familiar borders, and space is now the greatest frontier left to explore. While some argue that missions beyond Earth consume money and talent that could be used more practically, I firmly believe that space exploration is essential because it produces long-term scientific, technological, and survival benefits for humanity.","chinese":"人類的好奇心一直推動社會越過熟悉的邊界，而太空如今是仍有待探索的最大前沿。 雖然有些人認為，地球以外的探索任務會消耗本可更實際地使用的金錢和人才， 我堅定地認為，太空探索是不可或缺的，因為它能為人類帶來長遠的科學、科技和生存利益。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"On the one hand, the argument against space exploration is understandable. Launching rockets, maintaining space stations, and training astronauts require enormous financial and human resources. When hospitals are overcrowded, schools are underfunded, and many communities still lack clean water or basic infrastructure, spending billions on distant planets can appear morally questionable. For example, a taxpayer may reasonably wonder why public money is being used to examine rocks on Mars when children in poor areas cannot receive proper education. From this perspective, space exploration looks like an expensive luxury, especially because its benefits are not always immediate or visible.","chinese":"一方面，反對太空探索的論點是可以理解的。 發射火箭、維持太空站運作，以及訓練太空人都需要龐大的財政和人力資源。 當醫院人滿為患、學校資金不足，而許多社區仍然缺乏清潔食水或基本基礎設施時，把數十億資金花在遙遠星球上，便可能顯得在道德上值得質疑。 例如，一位納稅人可能會合理地質疑，為甚麼公共資金會被用來研究火星上的岩石，而貧困地區的兒童卻無法接受適當教育。 從這個角度來看，太空探索看起來像是一種昂貴的奢侈品，尤其是因為它的好處並不總是即時或明顯可見的。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"On the other hand, dismissing space exploration as a waste of resources is too narrow a view. Research beyond Earth often creates practical technologies and scientific knowledge that improve life on Earth. Satellites, for instance, support weather forecasting, global communication, navigation systems, and disaster monitoring, all of which are now woven into ordinary life. More importantly, exploring space prepares humanity for threats that cannot be solved by local policies alone, such as asteroid impacts, severe resource shortages, or the long-term possibility that Earth may become less habitable. If mankind never looks beyond its own planet, it risks becoming a species with no backup plan.","chinese":"另一方面，把太空探索視為資源浪費，是一種過於狹窄的看法。 地球以外的研究往往能創造實用科技和科學知識，從而改善地球上的生活。 例如，衛星支援天氣預報、全球通訊、導航系統和災害監測，而這些如今都已融入日常生活之中。 更重要的是，探索太空能讓人類為一些無法單靠本地政策解決的威脅作準備，例如小行星撞擊、嚴重資源短缺，或地球長遠而言可能變得較不宜居的可能性。 如果人類從不把目光投向自身星球之外，就有可能成為一個沒有後備計劃的物種。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, although critics are right to say that human needs on Earth must not be ignored, I do not believe space exploration is a wasteful activity. It is a long-term investment in knowledge, safety, and human survival. Governments and private companies should therefore continue exploring the universe, while ensuring that urgent problems on Earth are also responsibly addressed.","chinese":"總結來說，儘管批評者認為地球上的人類需求不應被忽視是正確的，但我並不認為太空探索是一項浪費資源的活動。 它是對知識、安全和人類生存的一項長遠投資。 因此，政府和私人企業應該繼續探索宇宙，同時確保地球上的緊急問題也得到負責任的處理。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"human curiosity","chinese":"人類好奇心"},{"english":"push society beyond","chinese":"推動社會超越"},{"english":"familiar borders","chinese":"熟悉的界限"},{"english":"the greatest frontier left to explore","chinese":"尚待探索的最大前沿"},{"english":"missions beyond Earth","chinese":"地球以外的任務"},{"english":"consume money and talent","chinese":"消耗金錢和人才"},{"english":"be used more practically","chinese":"被更實際地運用"},{"english":"firmly believe that","chinese":"堅信"},{"english":"space exploration","chinese":"太空探索"},{"english":"be essential","chinese":"是必要的"},{"english":"produce long-term benefits","chinese":"產生長遠好處"},{"english":"scientific, technological, and survival benefits","chinese":"科學、科技和生存方面的好處"},{"english":"for humanity","chinese":"對人類而言"},{"english":"the argument against","chinese":"反對……的論點"},{"english":"be understandable","chinese":"可以理解"},{"english":"launching rockets","chinese":"發射火箭"},{"english":"maintaining space stations","chinese":"維持太空站運作"},{"english":"training astronauts","chinese":"訓練太空人"},{"english":"require enormous financial and human resources","chinese":"需要龐大的財政和人力資源"},{"english":"overcrowded","chinese":"過度擠迫"},{"english":"underfunded","chinese":"資金不足"},{"english":"lack clean water","chinese":"缺乏清潔食水"},{"english":"basic infrastructure","chinese":"基本基建"},{"english":"spending billions on","chinese":"花費數十億於"},{"english":"distant planets","chinese":"遙遠星球"},{"english":"appear morally questionable","chinese":"看似在道德上有問題"},{"english":"a taxpayer","chinese":"納稅人"},{"english":"public money","chinese":"公帑"},{"english":"be used to","chinese":"被用來"},{"english":"examine rocks on Mars","chinese":"研究火星上的岩石"},{"english":"in poor areas","chinese":"在貧困地區"},{"english":"receive proper education","chinese":"接受適當教育"},{"english":"from this perspective","chinese":"從這個角度來看"},{"english":"look like an expensive luxury","chinese":"看似昂貴奢侈品"},{"english":"immediate or visible","chinese":"即時或明顯"},{"english":"dismiss space exploration as","chinese":"將太空探索視為"},{"english":"a waste of resources","chinese":"資源浪費"},{"english":"too narrow a view","chinese":"過於狹隘的看法"},{"english":"research beyond Earth","chinese":"地球以外的研究"},{"english":"practical technologies","chinese":"實用科技"},{"english":"scientific knowledge","chinese":"科學知識"},{"english":"improve life on Earth","chinese":"改善地球上的生活"},{"english":"weather forecasting","chinese":"天氣預報"},{"english":"global communication","chinese":"全球通訊"},{"english":"navigation systems","chinese":"導航系統"},{"english":"disaster monitoring","chinese":"災害監測"},{"english":"be woven into ordinary life","chinese":"融入日常生活"},{"english":"prepare humanity for","chinese":"令人類為……作準備"},{"english":"threats that cannot be solved by","chinese":"不能單靠……解決的威脅"},{"english":"local policies alone","chinese":"單靠本地政策"},{"english":"asteroid impacts","chinese":"小行星撞擊"},{"english":"severe resource shortages","chinese":"嚴重資源短缺"},{"english":"the long-term possibility that","chinese":"……的長遠可能性"},{"english":"become less habitable","chinese":"變得較不適合居住"},{"english":"look beyond its own planet","chinese":"放眼自身星球以外"},{"english":"risk becoming","chinese":"冒着變成……的風險"},{"english":"a species with no backup plan","chinese":"沒有後備方案的物種"},{"english":"critics are right to say that","chinese":"批評者說……是對的"},{"english":"human needs on Earth","chinese":"地球上的人類需要"},{"english":"must not be ignored","chinese":"不應被忽視"},{"english":"a wasteful activity","chinese":"浪費的活動"},{"english":"a long-term investment in","chinese":"對……的長遠投資"},{"english":"knowledge, safety, and human survival","chinese":"知識、安全和人類生存"},{"english":"private companies","chinese":"私營公司"},{"english":"continue exploring the universe","chinese":"繼續探索宇宙"},{"english":"while ensuring that","chinese":"同時確保"},{"english":"urgent problems on Earth","chinese":"地球上的迫切問題"},{"english":"be responsibly addressed","chinese":"得到負責任地處理"}]},"model-essay-34-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-34-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:34","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-34-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q34","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Some people argue that poverty is the main cause of most criminal behaviour. I disagree with this view because crime is usually produced by a wider mixture of motives, choices and social conditions, rather than by financial hardship alone.","chinese":"有些人認為，貧窮是大多數犯罪行為的主要原因。 我不同意這個觀點，因為犯罪通常是由更廣泛的動機、個人選擇和社會條件共同造成的，而不是單單由經濟困難所導致。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Poverty may place people under pressure, but it does not automatically push them into crime. Many people who live with limited income still obey the law, support their families honestly and take pride in doing the right thing. If poverty were the central explanation for most crimes, almost every poor community would be dominated by criminals, which is clearly not the case. In reality, crime often begins when individuals lack self-control, moral guidance or respect for the law. For example, a young person from a poor background may face real hardship, but whether he steals from a shop depends not only on his empty pocket, but also on his values, his family influence and his fear of consequences. Poverty may be the stage, but it is not always the actor.","chinese":"貧窮可能會使人承受壓力，但它並不會自動把人推向犯罪。 許多收入有限的人仍然遵守法律、誠實地養活家人，並為自己做正確的事而感到自豪。 如果貧窮真的是大多數犯罪的核心解釋，那麼幾乎每一個貧困社區都會被罪犯主導，而這顯然並非事實。 事實上，犯罪往往始於個人缺乏自制力、道德指引或對法律的尊重。 例如，一個出身貧困的年輕人可能確實面對困苦，但他是否會從商店偷竊，不只取決於他口袋空空，也取決於他的價值觀、家庭影響，以及他是否害怕後果。 貧窮或許是犯罪發生的舞台，但它並不總是那個真正行動的主角。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Moreover, many serious crimes are committed by people who are not poor at all. Fraud, corruption, tax evasion and cybercrime are often driven by greed, ambition or a desire for power. A wealthy businessperson who cheats investors is not acting out of hunger; he is choosing profit over honesty. Similarly, some violent crimes are linked to anger, revenge, addiction or social breakdown rather than simple economic need. This shows that crime is not merely a question of income, but a question of character, opportunity and the strength of social institutions.","chinese":"此外，許多嚴重罪行其實是由根本不貧窮的人所犯下的。 詐騙、貪污、逃稅和網絡犯罪往往是由貪婪、野心或對權力的渴望所驅動。 一個欺騙投資者的富裕商人並不是因為飢餓而行事；他是在誠實與利益之間選擇了利益。 同樣地，一些暴力犯罪與憤怒、報復、成癮或社會關係崩壞有關，不是單純的經濟需要 這說明犯罪並不只是收入問題，而是涉及品格、機會，以及社會制度強弱的問題。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I disagree that poverty is the reason behind most crimes. Although financial hardship can increase pressure on individuals, crime has deeper roots, including greed, weak moral education, poor law enforcement and personal choice. Poverty may open the door to temptation, but it does not hold the key to most criminal behaviour.","chinese":"總結來說，我不同意貧窮是大多數犯罪背後原因的說法。 雖然經濟困難可以增加個人的壓力，但犯罪有更深層的根源，包括貪婪、薄弱的道德教育、執法不足以及個人選擇。 貧窮或許會為誘惑打開一扇門，但它並不掌握大多數犯罪行為的關鍵。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"poverty","chinese":"貧窮"},{"english":"main cause of","chinese":"……的主要原因"},{"english":"criminal behaviour","chinese":"犯罪行為"},{"english":"disagree with","chinese":"不同意……"},{"english":"be produced by","chinese":"由……產生"},{"english":"wider mixture of","chinese":"更廣泛的混合因素"},{"english":"motives, choices and social conditions","chinese":"動機、選擇和社會環境"},{"english":"rather than by","chinese":"而不是由……"},{"english":"financial hardship alone","chinese":"單靠經濟困難"},{"english":"place people under pressure","chinese":"令人民承受壓力"},{"english":"automatically push them into","chinese":"自動將他們推向……"},{"english":"limited income","chinese":"有限收入"},{"english":"obey the law","chinese":"遵守法律"},{"english":"support their families honestly","chinese":"誠實地養活家人"},{"english":"take pride in","chinese":"以……為榮"},{"english":"doing the right thing","chinese":"做正確的事"},{"english":"central explanation for","chinese":"……的核心解釋"},{"english":"poor community","chinese":"貧困社區"},{"english":"be dominated by","chinese":"被……主導"},{"english":"which is clearly not the case","chinese":"但事實明顯並非如此"},{"english":"in reality","chinese":"實際上"},{"english":"lack self-control","chinese":"缺乏自制力"},{"english":"moral guidance","chinese":"道德指引"},{"english":"respect for the law","chinese":"對法律的尊重"},{"english":"poor background","chinese":"貧困背景"},{"english":"face real hardship","chinese":"面對真正困難"},{"english":"steal from a shop","chinese":"從商店偷東西"},{"english":"depends not only on","chinese":"不只取決於……"},{"english":"empty pocket","chinese":"空空的口袋；缺錢"},{"english":"family influence","chinese":"家庭影響"},{"english":"fear of consequences","chinese":"對後果的恐懼"},{"english":"poverty may be the stage","chinese":"貧窮可能是舞台"},{"english":"not always the actor","chinese":"不一定是主角"},{"english":"serious crimes","chinese":"嚴重罪行"},{"english":"be committed by","chinese":"由……犯下"},{"english":"not poor at all","chinese":"一點也不貧窮"},{"english":"fraud","chinese":"欺詐"},{"english":"corruption","chinese":"貪污；腐敗"},{"english":"tax evasion","chinese":"逃稅"},{"english":"cybercrime","chinese":"網絡犯罪"},{"english":"be driven by","chinese":"由……驅使"},{"english":"greed, ambition or a desire for power","chinese":"貪婪、野心或對權力的渴望"},{"english":"wealthy businessperson","chinese":"富有商人"},{"english":"cheats investors","chinese":"欺騙投資者"},{"english":"act out of hunger","chinese":"出於飢餓而行事"},{"english":"choosing profit over honesty","chinese":"選擇利潤而非誠實"},{"english":"violent crimes","chinese":"暴力罪行"},{"english":"be linked to","chinese":"與……有關"},{"english":"anger, revenge, addiction or social breakdown","chinese":"憤怒、報復、成癮或社會崩壞"},{"english":"simple economic need","chinese":"單純經濟需要"},{"english":"not merely a question of","chinese":"不只是……的問題"},{"english":"a question of character","chinese":"品格問題"},{"english":"opportunity","chinese":"機會"},{"english":"strength of social institutions","chinese":"社會制度的強度"},{"english":"the reason behind","chinese":"……背後的原因"},{"english":"increase pressure on","chinese":"增加對……的壓力"},{"english":"deeper roots","chinese":"更深層根源"},{"english":"weak moral education","chinese":"薄弱的道德教育"},{"english":"poor law enforcement","chinese":"執法不力"},{"english":"personal choice","chinese":"個人選擇"},{"english":"open the door to temptation","chinese":"打開誘惑之門"},{"english":"hold the key to","chinese":"掌握……的關鍵"}]},"model-essay-35-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-35-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:35","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-35-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q35","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In modern consumer societies, shopping is no longer limited to meeting basic needs. Many people now purchase items they could easily live without and replace perfectly functional products long before necessary. This essay will argue that this behaviour is mainly driven by advertising and social pressure, and that it is clearly a negative development.","chinese":"在現代消費型社會中，購物已不再只是為了滿足基本需要。如今，許多人會購買一些即使沒有也完全可以生活的物品，並且在完全沒有必要之前，就更換仍然功能正常的產品。 本文將主張，這種行為主要是由廣告和社會壓力所推動，而且它明顯是一種負面的發展"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One major reason people buy unnecessary goods is that companies have become highly skilled at creating desire. Advertisements rarely present products as ordinary objects; instead, they connect them with beauty, success, confidence, or social belonging. As a result, consumers may start to feel that owning the newest phone, outfit, or household device will improve their identity rather than simply serve a practical function. This pressure is even stronger on social media, where people are constantly exposed to influencers and friends displaying new purchases. When consumption becomes a way to gain approval, people are more likely to buy things they do not genuinely need.","chinese":"人們購買不必要商品的一個主要原因是，企業已經非常擅長製造欲望。 廣告很少把產品呈現為普通物品；相反，它們會把產品與美貌、成功、自信或社會歸屬感聯繫起來。 結果，消費者可能會開始覺得，擁有最新的手機、服裝或家用設備能提升他們的身份形象，而不只是滿足實際功能。 這種壓力在社交媒體上更加強烈，因為人們不斷看到網紅和朋友展示新的購買品。 當消費變成一種獲得認同的方式時，人們便更有可能購買自己並不真正需要的東西。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that many products are designed to feel outdated very quickly. Technology companies, for instance, release new models every year, even when the improvements are relatively minor. A person whose phone still works well may still feel tempted to replace it because the newer version looks more fashionable or slightly faster. In this way, shopping becomes less about solving real problems and more about chasing novelty. This habit can easily turn into a cycle: people buy something, enjoy it briefly, and then soon begin looking for the next upgrade.","chinese":"另一個原因是，許多產品被設計成很快就讓人覺得過時。 例如，科技公司每年都會推出新型號，即使改進其實相對有限。 一個人的手機即使仍然運作良好，也可能因為新版本看起來更時尚或速度稍快，而想要更換它。 這樣一來，購物便不再主要是為了解決真正的問題，而更像是在追逐新鮮感。 這種習慣很容易變成一個循環：人們買下某樣東西，短暫享受它，然後很快又開始尋找下一次升級。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 3","english":"I do not think this is a good thing. On a personal level, unnecessary consumption can lead to wasted money and poor financial habits, especially among people who buy on credit. More seriously, it creates environmental damage because discarded goods often end up as electronic waste, plastic waste, or landfill. Producing constant replacements also consumes energy and natural resources that could be used more responsibly.","chinese":"我不認為這是一件好事。 在個人層面上，不必要的消費可能導致金錢浪費和不良的理財習慣，尤其是在那些使用信貸購物的人身上。 更嚴重的是，它會造成環境破壞，因為被丟棄的商品往往最終變成電子垃圾、塑膠垃圾或堆填區廢物。 持續生產替代品也會消耗能源和自然資源，而這些資源本可以被更負責任地使用。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, people often buy needless products because advertising, social comparison, and rapid product cycles make unnecessary purchases seem attractive. However, this behaviour is harmful because it encourages financial waste and places avoidable pressure on the environment.","chinese":"總結來說，人們經常購買不必要的產品，是因為廣告、社會比較和快速的產品週期，令不必要的購買看起來具有吸引力。 然而，這種行為是有害的，因為它鼓勵金錢浪費，並對環境造成本可避免的壓力。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"modern consumer societies","chinese":"現代消費社會"},{"english":"be no longer limited to","chinese":"不再局限於"},{"english":"meeting basic needs","chinese":"滿足基本需要"},{"english":"purchase items","chinese":"購買物品"},{"english":"could easily live without","chinese":"沒有也可以輕易生活"},{"english":"perfectly functional products","chinese":"功能完全正常的產品"},{"english":"long before necessary","chinese":"遠早於有需要之前"},{"english":"this behaviour","chinese":"這種行為"},{"english":"mainly driven by","chinese":"主要由……推動"},{"english":"advertising and social pressure","chinese":"廣告和社會壓力"},{"english":"a negative development","chinese":"負面發展"},{"english":"one major reason","chinese":"一個主要原因"},{"english":"unnecessary goods","chinese":"不必要的商品"},{"english":"highly skilled at","chinese":"非常擅長"},{"english":"creating desire","chinese":"製造慾望"},{"english":"ordinary objects","chinese":"普通物件"},{"english":"instead","chinese":"相反；而是"},{"english":"connect them with","chinese":"將它們與……連繫起來"},{"english":"social belonging","chinese":"社會歸屬感"},{"english":"As a result","chinese":"結果"},{"english":"start to feel that","chinese":"開始覺得"},{"english":"owning the newest phone","chinese":"擁有最新手機"},{"english":"household device","chinese":"家用裝置"},{"english":"improve their identity","chinese":"提升自己的身份形象"},{"english":"rather than simply serve","chinese":"而不只是發揮"},{"english":"a practical function","chinese":"實際功能"},{"english":"even stronger on social media","chinese":"在社交媒體上更強"},{"english":"constantly exposed to","chinese":"不斷接觸到"},{"english":"influencers","chinese":"網紅"},{"english":"displaying new purchases","chinese":"展示新購買的物品"},{"english":"consumption becomes a way to","chinese":"消費成為一種……的方式"},{"english":"gain approval","chinese":"獲得認同"},{"english":"more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"genuinely need","chinese":"真正需要"},{"english":"another reason","chinese":"另一個原因"},{"english":"be designed to","chinese":"被設計成"},{"english":"feel outdated","chinese":"感覺過時"},{"english":"very quickly","chinese":"很快"},{"english":"technology companies","chinese":"科技公司"},{"english":"release new models","chinese":"推出新型號"},{"english":"every year","chinese":"每年"},{"english":"relatively minor","chinese":"相對輕微"},{"english":"still works well","chinese":"仍然運作良好"},{"english":"feel tempted to","chinese":"忍不住想"},{"english":"replace it","chinese":"替換它"},{"english":"the newer version","chinese":"較新的版本"},{"english":"more fashionable","chinese":"更時尚"},{"english":"slightly faster","chinese":"稍快一點"},{"english":"In this way","chinese":"以這種方式"},{"english":"becomes less about...and more about...","chinese":"較少是關於……而更多是關於……"},{"english":"solving real problems","chinese":"解決實際問題"},{"english":"chasing novelty","chinese":"追求新鮮感"},{"english":"turn into a cycle","chinese":"變成一個循環"},{"english":"enjoy it briefly","chinese":"短暫享受它"},{"english":"begin looking for","chinese":"開始尋找"},{"english":"the next upgrade","chinese":"下一次升級"},{"english":"on a personal level","chinese":"在個人層面上"},{"english":"unnecessary consumption","chinese":"不必要消費"},{"english":"lead to","chinese":"導致"},{"english":"wasted money","chinese":"浪費金錢"},{"english":"poor financial habits","chinese":"不良財務習慣"},{"english":"buy on credit","chinese":"賒購；用信貸購買"},{"english":"more seriously","chinese":"更嚴重的是"},{"english":"environmental damage","chinese":"環境破壞"},{"english":"discarded goods","chinese":"被丟棄的商品"},{"english":"end up as","chinese":"最終成為"},{"english":"electronic waste","chinese":"電子廢物"},{"english":"plastic waste","chinese":"塑膠廢物"},{"english":"landfill","chinese":"堆填區"},{"english":"constant replacements","chinese":"不斷替換的產品"},{"english":"consumes energy","chinese":"消耗能源"},{"english":"natural resources","chinese":"天然資源"},{"english":"used more responsibly","chinese":"更負責任地使用"},{"english":"needless products","chinese":"不必要產品"},{"english":"social comparison","chinese":"社會比較"},{"english":"rapid product cycles","chinese":"快速產品週期"},{"english":"unnecessary purchases","chinese":"不必要購買"},{"english":"harmful","chinese":"有害的"},{"english":"encourages financial waste","chinese":"鼓勵金錢浪費"},{"english":"places avoidable pressure on","chinese":"對……造成可避免的壓力"},{"english":"the environment","chinese":"環境"}]},"model-essay-35-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-35-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:35","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-35-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q35","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Risk has always been part of sport, yet the question is whether the state should remove that risk by banning dangerous activities altogether. While supporters of prohibition believe this would protect people from serious harm, I firmly believe that adults should remain free to choose such sports, provided that proper safety rules are enforced.","chinese":"風險一直都是運動的一部分，然而問題在於，政府是否應該透過全面禁止危險活動來消除這種風險。 雖然支持禁止的人認為這樣可以保護人們免受嚴重傷害， 我堅定地認為，只要適當的安全規則得到執行，成年人仍然應該有自由選擇這類運動"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Those who favour banning dangerous sports have a reasonable concern: some activities can lead to severe injury or death even when participants are experienced. Sports such as rock climbing, boxing, motor racing, and skydiving do not merely involve mild discomfort; one mistake can cause permanent damage. If an amateur climber ignores bad weather, for instance, rescue teams may have to risk their own lives to save him. In this sense, dangerous sports can create costs not only for the individual but also for families, medical services, and the wider community. From this perspective, a ban may seem like a simple way to prevent avoidable tragedy.","chinese":"支持禁止危險運動的人有一個合理的擔憂：有些活動即使參與者經驗豐富，也可能導致嚴重受傷或死亡。 攀岩、拳擊、賽車和跳傘等運動並不只是帶來輕微不適；一個錯誤便可造成永久性傷害 例如，如果一名業餘攀岩者忽視惡劣天氣，救援隊可能不得不冒著自己的生命危險去拯救他。 從這個意義上說，危險運動不但可能令個人付出代價，也可能令家庭、醫療服務和更廣泛的社區承受負擔。 從這個角度來看，禁令似乎是一種防止可避免悲劇的簡單方法。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, I believe this argument goes too far because personal freedom should not be sacrificed simply because an activity contains risk. Many meaningful human experiences, from travelling alone to starting a business, involve danger or uncertainty, but society does not ban them for that reason. A better response is strict regulation. For example, skydiving centres can require professional instructors, medical checks, age limits, high-quality equipment, and emergency procedures. These measures reduce unnecessary danger while still allowing people to test their courage, discipline, and physical limits. If a sport is driven underground by a ban, it may become even less safe because participants will no longer operate under official supervision.","chinese":"然而，我認為這種論點走得太遠，因為個人自由不應該僅僅因為某項活動包含風險就被犧牲。 許多有意義的人類經歷，從獨自旅行到創業，都包含危險或不確定性，但社會並不會因此禁止它們。 更好的應對方法是嚴格監管。 例如，跳傘中心可以要求專業教練、身體檢查、年齡限制、高質素裝備和緊急程序。 這些措施可以減少不必要的危險，同時仍然允許人們考驗自己的勇氣、紀律和身體極限 如果一項運動因禁令而轉入地下，它可能會變得更加不安全，因為參與者將不再受到官方監管。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, although dangerous sports can produce serious consequences, banning them is not the right solution. People should be allowed to take part in these activities because freedom, responsibility, and well-designed safety standards are a stronger answer than outright prohibition.","chinese":"總結來說，雖然危險運動可能帶來嚴重後果，但禁止它們並不是正確的解決方法。 人們應該被允許參與這些活動，因為自由、責任和設計良好的安全標準，比全面禁止更能有效回應這個問題。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"be part of","chinese":"是……的一部分"},{"english":"the question is whether","chinese":"問題在於是否"},{"english":"the state","chinese":"國家；政府"},{"english":"remove that risk","chinese":"消除那種風險"},{"english":"banning dangerous activities altogether","chinese":"完全禁止危險活動"},{"english":"supporters of prohibition","chinese":"禁令支持者"},{"english":"protect people from serious harm","chinese":"保護人們免受嚴重傷害"},{"english":"firmly believe that","chinese":"堅信"},{"english":"remain free to choose","chinese":"仍然有自由選擇"},{"english":"provided that","chinese":"只要；前提是"},{"english":"proper safety rules","chinese":"適當安全規則"},{"english":"be enforced","chinese":"被執行"},{"english":"favour banning","chinese":"支持禁止"},{"english":"dangerous sports","chinese":"危險運動"},{"english":"a reasonable concern","chinese":"合理擔憂"},{"english":"lead to severe injury or death","chinese":"導致嚴重受傷或死亡"},{"english":"even when","chinese":"即使在……時"},{"english":"participants are experienced","chinese":"參加者有經驗"},{"english":"sports such as","chinese":"例如……的運動"},{"english":"rock climbing","chinese":"攀石"},{"english":"motor racing","chinese":"賽車"},{"english":"skydiving","chinese":"跳傘"},{"english":"do not merely involve","chinese":"不只是涉及"},{"english":"mild discomfort","chinese":"輕微不適"},{"english":"one mistake can cause","chinese":"一個錯誤可以造成"},{"english":"permanent damage","chinese":"永久傷害"},{"english":"an amateur climber","chinese":"業餘攀山者"},{"english":"ignore bad weather","chinese":"忽視惡劣天氣"},{"english":"rescue teams","chinese":"救援隊"},{"english":"risk their own lives","chinese":"冒生命危險"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"create costs not only for","chinese":"不只為……帶來代價"},{"english":"the individual","chinese":"個人"},{"english":"medical services","chinese":"醫療服務"},{"english":"the wider community","chinese":"更廣泛的社群"},{"english":"from this perspective","chinese":"從這個角度來看"},{"english":"seem like a simple way to","chinese":"看似是……的簡單方法"},{"english":"prevent avoidable tragedy","chinese":"防止可避免的悲劇"},{"english":"this argument goes too far","chinese":"這個論點走得太遠"},{"english":"personal freedom","chinese":"個人自由"},{"english":"should not be sacrificed","chinese":"不應被犧牲"},{"english":"simply because","chinese":"只因為"},{"english":"contain risk","chinese":"帶有風險"},{"english":"meaningful human experiences","chinese":"有意義的人生經歷"},{"english":"travelling alone","chinese":"獨自旅行"},{"english":"starting a business","chinese":"創業"},{"english":"involve danger or uncertainty","chinese":"涉及危險或不確定性"},{"english":"for that reason","chinese":"因為那個原因"},{"english":"a better response","chinese":"更好的回應"},{"english":"strict regulation","chinese":"嚴格監管"},{"english":"professional instructors","chinese":"專業教練"},{"english":"medical checks","chinese":"醫療檢查"},{"english":"age limits","chinese":"年齡限制"},{"english":"high-quality equipment","chinese":"高質素裝備"},{"english":"emergency procedures","chinese":"緊急程序"},{"english":"reduce unnecessary danger","chinese":"減少不必要危險"},{"english":"while still allowing","chinese":"同時仍然容許"},{"english":"test their courage","chinese":"考驗自己的勇氣"},{"english":"physical limits","chinese":"身體極限"},{"english":"be driven underground by","chinese":"因禁令而轉入地下"},{"english":"become even less safe","chinese":"變得更加不安全"},{"english":"operate under official supervision","chinese":"在官方監督下進行"},{"english":"produce serious consequences","chinese":"造成嚴重後果"},{"english":"the right solution","chinese":"正確的解決方法"},{"english":"be allowed to take part in","chinese":"被容許參與"},{"english":"freedom, responsibility, and well-designed safety standards","chinese":"自由、責任和設計完善的安全標準"},{"english":"a stronger answer than","chinese":"比……更有力的答案"},{"english":"outright prohibition","chinese":"全面禁止"}]},"model-essay-35-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-35-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:35","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-35-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q35","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In my view, parents should not be punished when their children commit crimes. Although family upbringing undeniably shapes a young person’s character, criminal punishment must be based on personal responsibility, not guilt by association.","chinese":"我認為，當孩子犯罪時，父母不應該受到懲罰。 儘管家庭教育無疑會塑造一個年輕人的性格，但刑事懲罰必須建立在個人責任之上，而不是基於連坐式的罪責。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that blaming parents for a child’s offence would make the justice system deeply unfair. Children, especially teenagers, are influenced by many forces beyond the home, including friends, online content, school pressure, and the neighbourhood in which they grow up. A mother and father may set clear rules, teach right from wrong, and still be unable to control every decision their child makes outside the house. If a teenager steals from a shop after being encouraged by a peer group, punishing the parents would not address the actual choice made by the offender. It would simply turn the family into a convenient scapegoat, which is a dangerous way to administer justice.","chinese":"第一個原因是，把孩子的罪行歸咎於父母，會使司法制度變得極不公平。 孩子，尤其是青少年，會受到家庭以外許多力量的影響，包括朋友、網上內容、學校壓力，以及他們成長的社區環境。 父母可能已經訂立清晰規矩、教導孩子分辨是非，但仍然無法控制孩子在家以外作出的每一個決定。 如果一名青少年在同輩群體的鼓動下從商店偷竊，懲罰父母並不能處理犯罪者本身作出的實際選擇。 這只會把家庭變成一個方便的代罪羔羊，而這是一種危險的司法執行方式。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important point is that punishing parents may make youth crime harder to solve. When parents fear fines, prosecution, or public disgrace, they may become defensive and less willing to work with teachers, police officers, or social workers. This would damage the very cooperation that young offenders often need in order to change. By contrast, if parents are treated as partners in rehabilitation, they can help rebuild routines, monitor behaviour, and guide their child away from harmful influences. For example, a young offender who is required to attend counselling is far more likely to improve if the family supports the process rather than feels attacked by it. In this sense, parental punishment may satisfy public anger, but it is unlikely to produce safer communities.","chinese":"另一個重要觀點是，懲罰父母可能會使青少年犯罪更難解決。 當父母害怕罰款、檢控或公開羞辱時，他們可能會變得防衛，並且較不願意與教師、警察或社工合作。 這會破壞青少年犯人改變時往往最需要的那種合作。 相比之下，如果父母被視為改過自新過程中的合作夥伴，他們便可以幫助孩子重建生活規律、監察行為，並引導孩子遠離有害影響。 例如，一名被要求接受輔導的青少年犯人，如果家庭支持這個過程，而不是覺得自己受到攻擊，他便更有可能改善。 從這個角度來看，懲罰父母或許能滿足公眾怒氣，但它不太可能創造出更安全的社區。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I disagree that parents should be punished for crimes committed by their children. Responsibility should fall on the offender, while parents should be encouraged to assist with rehabilitation rather than be treated as criminals themselves.","chinese":"總結來說，我不同意父母應該因孩子所犯的罪行而受到懲罰。 責任應該落在犯罪者身上，而父母應該被鼓勵協助改過自新，而不是被當作罪犯看待。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"be punished when","chinese":"在……時受到懲罰"},{"english":"commit crimes","chinese":"犯罪"},{"english":"family upbringing","chinese":"家庭教養"},{"english":"undeniably shapes","chinese":"無可否認地塑造"},{"english":"young person's character","chinese":"年輕人的性格"},{"english":"criminal punishment","chinese":"刑事懲罰"},{"english":"be based on","chinese":"建基於"},{"english":"personal responsibility","chinese":"個人責任"},{"english":"guilt by association","chinese":"連坐式歸罪"},{"english":"blaming parents for","chinese":"因……而責怪父母"},{"english":"child's offence","chinese":"孩子的違法行為"},{"english":"justice system","chinese":"司法制度"},{"english":"deeply unfair","chinese":"極不公平"},{"english":"be influenced by","chinese":"受……影響"},{"english":"forces beyond the home","chinese":"家庭以外的力量"},{"english":"online content","chinese":"網上內容"},{"english":"school pressure","chinese":"學校壓力"},{"english":"neighbourhood","chinese":"社區；居住環境"},{"english":"grow up","chinese":"成長"},{"english":"set clear rules","chinese":"訂立清晰規則"},{"english":"teach right from wrong","chinese":"教導分辨是非"},{"english":"be unable to control","chinese":"無法控制"},{"english":"outside the house","chinese":"在家以外"},{"english":"steals from a shop","chinese":"從商店偷東西"},{"english":"be encouraged by","chinese":"受到……鼓動"},{"english":"peer group","chinese":"同輩群體"},{"english":"address the actual choice","chinese":"處理實際選擇"},{"english":"offender","chinese":"犯事者"},{"english":"convenient scapegoat","chinese":"方便的代罪羔羊"},{"english":"administer justice","chinese":"執行司法公義"},{"english":"youth crime","chinese":"青少年犯罪"},{"english":"harder to solve","chinese":"更難解決"},{"english":"fear fines","chinese":"害怕罰款"},{"english":"prosecution","chinese":"檢控"},{"english":"public disgrace","chinese":"公開蒙羞"},{"english":"become defensive","chinese":"變得有戒心"},{"english":"less willing to work with","chinese":"較不願意與……合作"},{"english":"police officers","chinese":"警務人員"},{"english":"social workers","chinese":"社工"},{"english":"damage the very cooperation","chinese":"損害正正需要的合作"},{"english":"young offenders","chinese":"青少年犯事者"},{"english":"in order to change","chinese":"為了改變"},{"english":"partners in rehabilitation","chinese":"更生過程中的合作伙伴"},{"english":"rebuild routines","chinese":"重建日常規律"},{"english":"monitor behaviour","chinese":"監察行為"},{"english":"guide their child away from","chinese":"引導孩子遠離……"},{"english":"harmful influences","chinese":"有害影響"},{"english":"be required to attend counselling","chinese":"被要求接受輔導"},{"english":"far more likely to improve","chinese":"更加有可能改善"},{"english":"supports the process","chinese":"支持這個過程"},{"english":"rather than feels attacked by it","chinese":"而不是覺得受到攻擊"},{"english":"satisfy public anger","chinese":"滿足公眾怒氣"},{"english":"unlikely to produce","chinese":"不大可能帶來"},{"english":"safer communities","chinese":"更安全的社區"},{"english":"crimes committed by","chinese":"由……犯下的罪行"},{"english":"responsibility should fall on","chinese":"責任應落在……身上"},{"english":"be encouraged to assist with","chinese":"被鼓勵協助……"},{"english":"rather than be treated as","chinese":"而不是被視為"},{"english":"criminals themselves","chinese":"他們本人也是罪犯"}]},"model-essay-36-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-36-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:36","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-36-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q36","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"A child’s first years at school are often shaped by what has already happened before formal education begins. Early reading is especially important because it gives children access to language, instructions and ideas, all of which are central to academic learning. However, reading alone does not determine success; preschool children are also strongly influenced by their home environment, social development and emotional readiness.","chinese":"孩子在學校最初幾年的表現，往往受到正式教育開始之前已經發生的事情所影響。 早期閱讀尤其重要，因為它讓孩子接觸語言、指示和思想，而這些全都是學術學習的核心。 然而，單靠閱讀並不能決定成功；學前兒童也會受到家庭環境、社交發展和情緒準備程度的強烈影響。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Early reading skills play a crucial role in academic performance because they form the gateway to almost every subject. A child who can recognise words, follow a sentence and understand a simple story is not merely learning English; they are learning how to learn. For example, even a basic mathematics worksheet requires pupils to read questions accurately, while science depends heavily on understanding explanations. Early readers are therefore less likely to feel lost in class and more likely to build confidence as schoolwork becomes harder. This confidence can become a quiet engine of progress, pushing them to ask questions, complete tasks independently and develop stronger study habits.","chinese":"早期閱讀能力在學業表現中扮演關鍵角色，因為它們幾乎是通往每一個學科的入口。 一個能夠認字、理解句子並明白簡單故事的孩子，並不只是正在學習英文；他們是在學習如何學習。 例如，即使是一份基本的數學工作紙，也要求學生準確閱讀題目，而科學則高度依賴對解釋內容的理解。 因此，早期具備閱讀能力的孩子在課堂上較不容易感到迷失，也更有可能在課業變得更困難時建立自信。 這份自信可以成為一個安靜卻有力的進步引擎，推動他們提出問題、獨立完成任務，並培養更強的學習習慣。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"That said, several other preschool factors also shape later achievement. One of the most important is parental involvement, especially when parents talk to children regularly, answer their questions and create a calm routine at home. Such children often arrive at school with better vocabulary, stronger concentration and a clearer sense that learning matters. Social and emotional development is another key factor. Children who can share toys, wait for their turn and cope with small frustrations are usually better prepared for classroom life. In this sense, preschool success is not only built with books; it is also built through conversation, play and stable relationships.","chinese":"話雖如此，其他幾個學前因素也會塑造孩子日後的成就。 其中最重要的因素之一是父母的參與，尤其是當父母經常與孩子交談、回答他們的問題，並在家中建立平穩的日常規律時。 這樣的孩子入學時通常已經具備更好的詞彙量、更強的專注力，以及更清楚明白學習是重要的。 社交和情緒發展是另一個關鍵因素。 能夠分享玩具、等待輪到自己，以及處理小挫折的孩子，通常更能為課堂生活作好準備。 從這個意義上說，學前成功並不只是由書本建立起來的；它也透過對話、遊戲和穩定的關係建立起來。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, early reading skills are extremely important because they support understanding, confidence and independent learning across the curriculum. Nevertheless, a child’s academic future is also shaped by family support, emotional maturity and social habits developed before school.","chinese":"總結來說，早期閱讀能力極為重要，因為它們支撐孩子在整個課程中的理解力、自信心和獨立學習能力。 然而，一個孩子的學業未來也會受到入學前已經建立的家庭支持、情緒成熟度和社交習慣所塑造。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"a child's first years at school","chinese":"孩子最初幾年的學校生活"},{"english":"be shaped by","chinese":"受……塑造"},{"english":"formal education","chinese":"正規教育"},{"english":"early reading","chinese":"早期閱讀"},{"english":"gives children access to","chinese":"讓孩子接觸到"},{"english":"language, instructions and ideas","chinese":"語言、指示和概念"},{"english":"be central to","chinese":"對……至關重要"},{"english":"academic learning","chinese":"學業學習"},{"english":"reading alone","chinese":"單靠閱讀"},{"english":"determine success","chinese":"決定成功"},{"english":"preschool children","chinese":"學前兒童"},{"english":"strongly influenced by","chinese":"深受……影響"},{"english":"home environment","chinese":"家庭環境"},{"english":"social development","chinese":"社交發展"},{"english":"emotional readiness","chinese":"情緒準備程度"},{"english":"play a crucial role in","chinese":"在……中扮演關鍵角色"},{"english":"academic performance","chinese":"學業表現"},{"english":"form the gateway to","chinese":"成為通往……的門戶"},{"english":"almost every subject","chinese":"幾乎每一個科目"},{"english":"recognise words","chinese":"認字"},{"english":"follow a sentence","chinese":"理解一句句子"},{"english":"understand a simple story","chinese":"理解簡單故事"},{"english":"not merely learning","chinese":"不只是學習"},{"english":"learning how to learn","chinese":"學會如何學習"},{"english":"a basic mathematics worksheet","chinese":"基本數學工作紙"},{"english":"requires pupils to","chinese":"要求學生去"},{"english":"read questions accurately","chinese":"準確閱讀題目"},{"english":"depends heavily on","chinese":"很大程度上取決於"},{"english":"understanding explanations","chinese":"理解解釋"},{"english":"less likely to","chinese":"較不可能"},{"english":"feel lost in class","chinese":"在課堂上感到迷失"},{"english":"more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"build confidence","chinese":"建立信心"},{"english":"schoolwork becomes harder","chinese":"學校功課變得更難"},{"english":"a quiet engine of progress","chinese":"默默推動進步的力量"},{"english":"push them to","chinese":"推動他們去"},{"english":"ask questions","chinese":"提問"},{"english":"complete tasks independently","chinese":"獨立完成任務"},{"english":"develop stronger study habits","chinese":"建立更強的學習習慣"},{"english":"That said","chinese":"話雖如此"},{"english":"preschool factors","chinese":"學前因素"},{"english":"shape later achievement","chinese":"塑造日後成就"},{"english":"parental involvement","chinese":"父母參與"},{"english":"talk to children regularly","chinese":"定期與孩子交談"},{"english":"answer their questions","chinese":"回答他們的問題"},{"english":"create a calm routine at home","chinese":"在家中建立平靜規律"},{"english":"arrive at school with","chinese":"帶着……入學"},{"english":"better vocabulary","chinese":"更好的詞彙量"},{"english":"stronger concentration","chinese":"更強的專注力"},{"english":"a clearer sense that","chinese":"更清楚意識到"},{"english":"learning matters","chinese":"學習很重要"},{"english":"another key factor","chinese":"另一個關鍵因素"},{"english":"share toys","chinese":"分享玩具"},{"english":"wait for their turn","chinese":"等候輪到自己"},{"english":"cope with small frustrations","chinese":"應付小挫折"},{"english":"better prepared for","chinese":"為……作好更充分準備"},{"english":"classroom life","chinese":"課堂生活"},{"english":"In this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"built with books","chinese":"由書本建立"},{"english":"through conversation, play and stable relationships","chinese":"透過交談、遊戲和穩定關係"},{"english":"stable relationships","chinese":"穩定關係"},{"english":"support understanding","chinese":"支持理解"},{"english":"independent learning","chinese":"獨立學習"},{"english":"across the curriculum","chinese":"橫跨整個課程"},{"english":"academic future","chinese":"學業前途"},{"english":"family support","chinese":"家庭支援"},{"english":"emotional maturity","chinese":"情緒成熟"},{"english":"social habits","chinese":"社交習慣"},{"english":"developed before school","chinese":"在入學前培養"}]},"model-essay-36-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-36-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:36","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-36-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q36","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Sport plays an important role in childhood because it teaches lessons that are difficult to learn only from books. Some people argue that its main value is that it trains children to compete, whereas others believe that it primarily develops teamwork. I will discuss both views, but I strongly believe that teamwork is the more valuable lesson.","chinese":"運動在童年中扮演重要角色，因為它能教會孩子一些單靠書本難以學到的道理。 有些人認為，運動最主要的價值在於訓練孩子競爭；然而，另一些人則相信，運動主要培養的是團隊合作能力。 我將討論雙方觀點，但我強烈認為，團隊合作是更有價值的一課。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"On the one hand, sport clearly helps children understand healthy competition. When young people take part in races, matches, or tournaments, they learn that success usually comes from effort, discipline, and preparation rather than luck. This matters because children who never face competition may struggle when they later meet academic pressure, job interviews, or professional rivalry. For example, a child who loses a football match can learn to accept disappointment, analyse mistakes, and try again instead of giving up. In this sense, competition can build resilience and teach children how to win modestly and lose gracefully.","chinese":"一方面，運動顯然能幫助孩子理解健康的競爭。 當年輕人參加賽跑、比賽或錦標賽時，他們會明白成功通常來自努力、自律和準備，而不是運氣。 這一點很重要，因為從未面對過競爭的孩子，日後遇到學業壓力、工作面試或職場競爭時，可能會難以應對。 例如，一個輸掉足球比賽的孩子，可以學會接受失望、分析錯誤，並再次嘗試，而不是選擇放棄。 從這個意義上說，競爭能建立孩子的抗逆力，並教會他們如何謙遜地勝利，以及有風度地面對失敗。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"On the other hand, team sports are even more powerful because they show children that achievement often depends on cooperation. In games such as basketball or football, no player can succeed simply by showing individual talent; children must pass, communicate, trust their teammates, and sometimes put the group’s interest before personal glory. This creates a practical lesson that reaches far beyond the sports field. For instance, a child who learns to listen to teammates during a match is also more likely to contribute well in classroom projects or future workplaces. Since most real-life success depends on working with other people, teamwork is a deeper and more transferable skill than competition alone.","chinese":"另一方面，團隊運動更具影響力，因為它們讓孩子明白，成就往往取決於合作。 在籃球或足球這類運動中，沒有任何球員能單靠個人天分取得成功；孩子必須傳球、溝通、信任隊友，有時還要把團隊利益置於個人榮耀之上。 這帶來了一種實用的教育意義，而且其影響遠遠超出運動場本身。 例如，一個在比賽中學會聆聽隊友的孩子，也更有可能在課堂小組項目或未來職場中作出良好貢獻。 由於現實生活中的大多數成功都取決於與他人合作，因此團隊合作比單純的競爭更深層，也更具可轉移性。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, sport does teach children how to compete, especially by helping them deal with pressure, failure, and self-improvement. However, I believe its greatest benefit is that it teaches teamwork, because cooperation, trust, and shared responsibility are essential in school, work, and society.","chinese":"總結來說，運動確實能教會孩子如何競爭，尤其是幫助他們應對壓力、失敗和自我提升 然而，我認為運動最大的好處是它能教會孩子團隊合作，因為合作、信任和共同責任在學校、工作和社會中都是不可或缺的。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"play an important role in","chinese":"在……中扮演重要角色"},{"english":"childhood","chinese":"童年"},{"english":"teach lessons that are difficult to learn","chinese":"教授難以學會的道理"},{"english":"only from books","chinese":"只從書本中"},{"english":"its main value","chinese":"其主要價值"},{"english":"train children to compete","chinese":"訓練兒童競爭"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"primarily develops teamwork","chinese":"主要培養團隊合作"},{"english":"discuss both views","chinese":"討論雙方觀點"},{"english":"strongly believe that","chinese":"強烈相信"},{"english":"the more valuable lesson","chinese":"更有價值的一課"},{"english":"on the one hand","chinese":"一方面"},{"english":"healthy competition","chinese":"健康競爭"},{"english":"take part in","chinese":"參加"},{"english":"races, matches, or tournaments","chinese":"賽跑、比賽或錦標賽"},{"english":"success usually comes from","chinese":"成功通常來自"},{"english":"effort, discipline, and preparation","chinese":"努力、自律和準備"},{"english":"rather than luck","chinese":"而不是運氣"},{"english":"this matters because","chinese":"這一點很重要，因為"},{"english":"face competition","chinese":"面對競爭"},{"english":"may struggle when","chinese":"在……時可能會感到吃力"},{"english":"academic pressure","chinese":"學業壓力"},{"english":"job interviews","chinese":"求職面試"},{"english":"professional rivalry","chinese":"職場競爭"},{"english":"lose a football match","chinese":"輸掉一場足球比賽"},{"english":"accept disappointment","chinese":"接受失望"},{"english":"analyse mistakes","chinese":"分析錯誤"},{"english":"try again instead of giving up","chinese":"再嘗試而不是放棄"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"build resilience","chinese":"建立抗逆力"},{"english":"win modestly","chinese":"謙虛地勝出"},{"english":"lose gracefully","chinese":"有風度地落敗"},{"english":"on the other hand","chinese":"另一方面"},{"english":"team sports","chinese":"團隊運動"},{"english":"even more powerful","chinese":"更有力量；影響更大"},{"english":"achievement often depends on","chinese":"成就往往取決於"},{"english":"cooperation","chinese":"合作"},{"english":"in games such as","chinese":"在例如……的比賽中"},{"english":"no player can succeed simply by","chinese":"沒有球員可以單靠……成功"},{"english":"individual talent","chinese":"個人才華"},{"english":"trust their teammates","chinese":"信任隊友"},{"english":"put the group's interest before","chinese":"將團隊利益放在……之前"},{"english":"personal glory","chinese":"個人榮耀"},{"english":"create a practical lesson","chinese":"帶來實用的一課"},{"english":"reach far beyond","chinese":"遠遠超出"},{"english":"the sports field","chinese":"運動場"},{"english":"for instance","chinese":"例如"},{"english":"listen to teammates","chinese":"聆聽隊友"},{"english":"during a match","chinese":"在比賽期間"},{"english":"be more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"contribute well in","chinese":"在……中作出良好貢獻"},{"english":"classroom projects","chinese":"課堂項目"},{"english":"future workplaces","chinese":"未來職場"},{"english":"since most real-life success depends on","chinese":"由於大多數現實成功取決於"},{"english":"real-life success","chinese":"現實生活中的成功"},{"english":"working with other people","chinese":"與他人合作"},{"english":"a deeper and more transferable skill","chinese":"更深入且更能轉移應用的技能"},{"english":"competition alone","chinese":"單靠競爭"},{"english":"deal with pressure","chinese":"應對壓力"},{"english":"failure and self-improvement","chinese":"失敗和自我提升"},{"english":"its greatest benefit","chinese":"其最大好處"},{"english":"cooperation, trust, and shared responsibility","chinese":"合作、信任和共同責任"},{"english":"shared responsibility","chinese":"共同責任"},{"english":"be essential in","chinese":"在……中不可或缺"},{"english":"school, work, and society","chinese":"學校、工作和社會"}]},"model-essay-36-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-36-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:36","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-36-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q36","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"For centuries, literacy and numeracy have formed the core of schooling because they allow people to read information, express ideas and solve practical problems. In the digital age, however, I completely agree that computer skills should be treated as a fourth fundamental skill, since they are now essential for learning, employment and responsible participation in society.","chinese":"幾個世紀以來，讀寫能力和計算能力一直構成學校教育的核心，因為它們使人能夠閱讀資訊、表達想法並解決實際問題。 然而，在數碼時代，我完全同意電腦技能應被視為第四項基本技能，因為它們如今對學習、就業以及負責任地參與社會都至關重要。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason is that computers have become one of the main gateways to knowledge. A student who cannot use basic software, search engines or online learning platforms is no longer simply missing a technical ability; he or she is cut off from a large part of modern education. For example, research assignments often require students to find credible sources, organize files, produce presentations and submit work through digital systems. If these skills are left to chance, students from less technologically confident families may fall behind, even when they are intelligent and hardworking. Teaching computer literacy systematically would therefore make education fairer and more complete.","chinese":"最有力的原因是，電腦已經成為通往知識的主要門戶之一。 一個不會使用基本軟件、搜尋引擎或網上學習平台的學生，不再只是缺少一項技術能力；他或她其實是被切斷了與現代教育很大一部分的連接。 例如，研究作業經常要求學生尋找可信資料來源、整理檔案、製作簡報，並透過數碼系統提交功課。 如果這些技能被任由學生自行摸索，來自較缺乏科技信心家庭的學生便可能落後，即使他們本身聰明又勤奮。 因此，系統地教授電腦素養會使教育更加公平，也更加完整。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Computer skills are also indispensable beyond the classroom. In many workplaces, even ordinary jobs now involve emails, spreadsheets, databases, video meetings or digital payment systems. A person who reads well and calculates accurately may still struggle if they cannot handle these tools efficiently. More importantly, computer education can teach pupils how to use technology safely and responsibly. They need to understand privacy, online scams, passwords and the difference between reliable information and digital noise. Without this guidance, computers may become a source of confusion rather than empowerment.","chinese":"電腦技能在課室之外同樣不可或缺。 在許多工作場所中，即使是普通工作，如今也涉及電子郵件、試算表、資料庫、視像會議或數碼支付系統。 一個閱讀能力強、計算準確的人，如果不能有效地操作這些工具，仍然可能在工作上遇到困難。 更重要的是，電腦教育能教導學生如何安全並負責任地使用科技。 他們需要理解私隱、網上騙局、密碼安全，以及可靠資訊與數碼雜音之間的分別。 如果沒有這種指導，電腦可能會成為混亂的來源，而不是賦能的工具。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, reading, writing and mathematics remain irreplaceable, but they are no longer sufficient by themselves. Computer literacy should be added as a fourth core skill because it gives students access to knowledge, improves their future employability and helps them navigate the digital world with judgment rather than fear.","chinese":"總結來說，閱讀、寫作和數學仍然無可取代，但單靠它們已經不再足夠。 電腦素養應被加入為第四項核心技能，因為它讓學生能夠接觸知識、提升他們未來的就業能力，並幫助他們以判斷力而非恐懼去面對數碼世界。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"for centuries","chinese":"多個世紀以來"},{"english":"literacy and numeracy","chinese":"讀寫能力和計算能力"},{"english":"formed the core of","chinese":"構成……的核心"},{"english":"schooling","chinese":"學校教育"},{"english":"read information","chinese":"閱讀資料"},{"english":"express ideas","chinese":"表達想法"},{"english":"solve practical problems","chinese":"解決實際問題"},{"english":"in the digital age","chinese":"在數碼時代"},{"english":"computer skills","chinese":"電腦技能"},{"english":"be treated as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"fourth fundamental skill","chinese":"第四項基本技能"},{"english":"essential for","chinese":"對……必不可少"},{"english":"responsible participation in society","chinese":"負責任地參與社會"},{"english":"main gateways to knowledge","chinese":"通往知識的主要途徑"},{"english":"basic software","chinese":"基本軟件"},{"english":"search engines","chinese":"搜尋器"},{"english":"online learning platforms","chinese":"網上學習平台"},{"english":"no longer simply","chinese":"不再只是"},{"english":"missing a technical ability","chinese":"缺少一項技術能力"},{"english":"be cut off from","chinese":"與……隔絕"},{"english":"a large part of modern education","chinese":"現代教育的一大部分"},{"english":"research assignments","chinese":"研究功課"},{"english":"credible sources","chinese":"可信來源"},{"english":"organise files","chinese":"整理檔案"},{"english":"produce presentations","chinese":"製作簡報"},{"english":"submit work through","chinese":"透過……提交功課"},{"english":"digital systems","chinese":"數碼系統"},{"english":"be left to chance","chinese":"任由機會決定"},{"english":"technologically confident families","chinese":"對科技較有信心的家庭"},{"english":"fall behind","chinese":"落後"},{"english":"intelligent and hardworking","chinese":"聰明而勤奮"},{"english":"computer literacy","chinese":"電腦素養"},{"english":"systematically","chinese":"有系統地"},{"english":"make education fairer","chinese":"令教育更公平"},{"english":"more complete","chinese":"更完整"},{"english":"indispensable beyond the classroom","chinese":"在課室以外不可或缺"},{"english":"workplaces","chinese":"工作場所"},{"english":"ordinary jobs","chinese":"普通工作"},{"english":"involve emails","chinese":"涉及電郵"},{"english":"spreadsheets","chinese":"試算表"},{"english":"databases","chinese":"數據庫"},{"english":"video meetings","chinese":"視像會議"},{"english":"digital payment systems","chinese":"數碼支付系統"},{"english":"reads well","chinese":"閱讀能力好"},{"english":"calculates accurately","chinese":"計算準確"},{"english":"handle these tools efficiently","chinese":"高效地使用這些工具"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"use technology safely and responsibly","chinese":"安全而負責任地使用科技"},{"english":"understand privacy","chinese":"明白私隱"},{"english":"online scams","chinese":"網上騙案"},{"english":"passwords","chinese":"密碼"},{"english":"reliable information","chinese":"可靠資料"},{"english":"digital noise","chinese":"數碼雜音；網上雜亂資訊"},{"english":"without this guidance","chinese":"沒有這種指引"},{"english":"a source of confusion","chinese":"混亂的來源"},{"english":"rather than empowerment","chinese":"而不是賦權"},{"english":"remain irreplaceable","chinese":"仍然無可取代"},{"english":"sufficient by themselves","chinese":"單靠它們已不足夠"},{"english":"be added as","chinese":"被加入作為……"},{"english":"fourth core skill","chinese":"第四項核心技能"},{"english":"access to knowledge","chinese":"接觸知識的機會"},{"english":"future employability","chinese":"未來就業能力"},{"english":"navigate the digital world","chinese":"在數碼世界中應對自如"},{"english":"with judgment rather than fear","chinese":"憑判斷力而不是恐懼"}]},"model-essay-37-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-37-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:37","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-37-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q37","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Modernisation has brought clear benefits, but it has also pushed many traditional ways of life to the margins. In my view, preserving these traditions is important because they give people cultural identity and social continuity. This can be achieved by making traditions part of education and community life, rather than treating them as museum pieces.","chinese":"現代化帶來了明顯的好處，但它也把許多傳統生活方式推向了邊緣。 在我看來，保留這些傳統是重要的，因為它們給予人們文化身份和社會延續性。 這可以透過把傳統融入教育和社區生活來實現，而不是把它們當成博物館裡的展品。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main reason traditional lifestyles should be protected is that they connect people with their history and with one another. Customs such as local festivals, family rituals, traditional crafts and regional food are not merely old habits; they carry shared values, memories and forms of knowledge that cannot be replaced by technology or consumer culture. When these practices disappear, younger generations may still live in modern cities, but they can lose a sense of belonging to a wider story. For example, a child who learns only global popular culture may know how to use the latest devices, yet know little about the language, manners or celebrations that shaped their grandparents’ lives. In this sense, tradition acts as a bridge between generations and helps societies remain rooted while they move forward.","chinese":"傳統生活方式應該受到保護的主要原因，是它們把人們與自己的歷史以及彼此連結起來。 本地節日、家庭儀式、傳統工藝和地區食物等習俗，並不只是舊習慣；它們承載著共同的價值觀、記憶和知識形式，而這些是科技或消費文化無法取代的。 當這些做法消失時，年輕一代也許仍然生活在現代城市中，但他們可能會失去一種屬於更大歷史故事的歸屬感。 例如，一個只接觸全球流行文化的孩子，可能知道如何使用最新的電子設備，卻對塑造祖父母生活的語言、禮儀或慶祝方式所知甚少。 從這個意義上說，傳統就像世代之間的一座橋樑，幫助社會在向前發展的同時仍然保持根基。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, traditions survive only if they are kept alive in practical ways. Schools should teach local history, traditional arts and community customs through activities rather than dry memorisation, so students can experience culture instead of simply reading about it. At the same time, governments and local communities should support festivals, craft markets, oral-history projects and public spaces where older people can pass on skills to the young. Technology can also help: short videos, digital archives and online lessons can make traditional knowledge accessible to people living far from their original communities.","chinese":"然而，傳統只有在以實際方式被延續時，才能真正存活下來。 學校應該透過活動教授本地歷史、傳統藝術和社區習俗，而不是依靠枯燥的背誦，這樣學生才能親身體驗文化，而不只是閱讀有關文化的內容。 同時，政府和本地社區應該支持節日活動、手工藝市集、口述歷史項目，以及讓長者能夠把技能傳授給年輕人的公共空間。 科技也可以提供幫助：短片、數碼檔案和網上課程，可以讓那些遠離原本社區生活的人也能接觸到傳統知識。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, it is important to preserve traditional ways of life because they protect cultural identity and strengthen social bonds. The best approach is not to resist modern life, but to weave tradition into education, community activities and digital platforms, so it remains a living part of society.","chinese":"總結來說，保留傳統生活方式是重要的，因為它們保護文化身份，並加強社會連繫。 最好的方法不是抗拒現代生活，而是把傳統編織進教育、社區活動和數碼平台之中，使它仍然成為社會中一個鮮活的部分。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"modernisation","chinese":"現代化"},{"english":"brought clear benefits","chinese":"帶來明顯好處"},{"english":"traditional ways of life","chinese":"傳統生活方式"},{"english":"push...to the margins","chinese":"把……推到邊緣"},{"english":"In my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"preserving these traditions","chinese":"保留這些傳統"},{"english":"cultural identity","chinese":"文化身份認同"},{"english":"social continuity","chinese":"社會延續性"},{"english":"be achieved by","chinese":"可以透過……達成"},{"english":"part of education and community life","chinese":"教育和社區生活的一部分"},{"english":"rather than treating them as","chinese":"而不是把它們視為"},{"english":"museum pieces","chinese":"博物館展品"},{"english":"the main reason","chinese":"主要原因"},{"english":"traditional lifestyles","chinese":"傳統生活方式"},{"english":"connect people with","chinese":"將人們與……連繫起來"},{"english":"with one another","chinese":"彼此之間"},{"english":"customs such as","chinese":"例如……的習俗"},{"english":"local festivals","chinese":"本地節慶"},{"english":"family rituals","chinese":"家庭儀式"},{"english":"traditional crafts","chinese":"傳統手工藝"},{"english":"regional food","chinese":"地區特色食物"},{"english":"not merely old habits","chinese":"不只是舊習慣"},{"english":"carry shared values","chinese":"承載共同價值觀"},{"english":"forms of knowledge","chinese":"知識形式"},{"english":"be replaced by","chinese":"被……取代"},{"english":"consumer culture","chinese":"消費文化"},{"english":"these practices disappear","chinese":"這些做法消失"},{"english":"younger generations","chinese":"年輕一代"},{"english":"lose a sense of belonging","chinese":"失去歸屬感"},{"english":"a wider story","chinese":"更宏大的故事"},{"english":"global popular culture","chinese":"全球流行文化"},{"english":"the latest devices","chinese":"最新裝置"},{"english":"know little about","chinese":"對……所知甚少"},{"english":"shaped their grandparents' lives","chinese":"塑造了祖父母輩的生活"},{"english":"In this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"acts as a bridge between generations","chinese":"成為世代之間的橋樑"},{"english":"remain rooted","chinese":"保持根基"},{"english":"move forward","chinese":"向前發展"},{"english":"kept alive in practical ways","chinese":"以實際方式保持活力"},{"english":"local history","chinese":"本地歷史"},{"english":"traditional arts","chinese":"傳統藝術"},{"english":"community customs","chinese":"社區習俗"},{"english":"through activities","chinese":"透過活動"},{"english":"dry memorisation","chinese":"枯燥的死記硬背"},{"english":"experience culture","chinese":"體驗文化"},{"english":"simply reading about it","chinese":"只是閱讀相關內容"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"local communities","chinese":"本地社區"},{"english":"craft markets","chinese":"手工藝市集"},{"english":"oral-history projects","chinese":"口述歷史項目"},{"english":"public spaces","chinese":"公共空間"},{"english":"pass on skills to","chinese":"把技能傳給"},{"english":"the young","chinese":"年輕人"},{"english":"digital archives","chinese":"數碼檔案"},{"english":"online lessons","chinese":"網上課堂"},{"english":"make traditional knowledge accessible","chinese":"令傳統知識更容易接觸"},{"english":"original communities","chinese":"原來的社區"},{"english":"protect cultural identity","chinese":"保護文化身份認同"},{"english":"strengthen social bonds","chinese":"加強社會聯繫"},{"english":"the best approach","chinese":"最佳做法"},{"english":"resist modern life","chinese":"抗拒現代生活"},{"english":"weave tradition into","chinese":"把傳統融入"},{"english":"community activities","chinese":"社區活動"},{"english":"digital platforms","chinese":"數碼平台"},{"english":"a living part of society","chinese":"社會中有生命力的一部分"}]},"model-essay-37-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-37-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:37","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-37-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q37","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"International sporting events are now seen by many governments as powerful opportunities to raise their country’s profile. While some people argue that hosting these competitions creates serious financial and social problems, I believe that the long-term benefits outweigh these drawbacks.","chinese":"國際體育賽事如今被許多政府視為提升國家形象的強大機會。 雖然有些人認為，舉辦這些比賽會造成嚴重的財政和社會問題， 但我認為，其長遠利益大於這些缺點。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"On the one hand, many countries are eager to host major sports events because they can bring economic and reputational rewards. When a nation welcomes athletes, journalists, and spectators, local businesses such as hotels, restaurants, airlines, and shops often receive a significant boost. More importantly, these events can put a country on the world map. A successful Olympic Games or World Cup allows the host nation to present itself as modern, organised, and culturally attractive. This can strengthen tourism even after the final whistle has blown. In addition, large sporting events can unite citizens behind a shared national moment, creating a sense of pride that ordinary government projects rarely generate.","chinese":"一方面，許多國家渴望舉辦大型體育賽事，因為它們可以帶來經濟和聲譽上的回報。 當一個國家迎接運動員、記者和觀眾時，酒店、餐廳、航空公司和商店等本地企業通常會得到顯著的帶動。 更重要的是，這些賽事可以讓一個國家登上世界舞台。 一屆成功的奧運會或世界盃能讓主辦國展示自己現代化、有組織，並且具有文化吸引力的一面。 即使在賽事結束之後，這仍然可以加強旅遊業。 此外，大型體育賽事能讓國民因一個共同的國家時刻而團結起來，創造出普通政府項目很少能產生的自豪感。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"On the other hand, critics argue that the costs of hosting such events can be dangerously high. Governments may spend enormous sums on stadiums, transport systems, security, and temporary facilities, even when schools, hospitals, and housing need urgent investment. If the venues are rarely used afterwards, they can become expensive “white elephants” rather than valuable public assets. There may also be disruption for local residents, especially when construction projects cause traffic, noise, or even the relocation of communities. For poorer countries in particular, these risks can make hosting an international tournament look more like a burden than a blessing.","chinese":"另一方面，批評者認為，舉辦這類賽事的成本可能高得危險。 政府可能會在體育場、交通系統、保安和臨時設施上花費巨額資金，即使學校、醫院和住房都急需投資。 如果這些場館之後很少被使用，它們便可能成為昂貴的「白象工程」，而不是有價值的公共資產。 本地居民也可能受到干擾，尤其是當建設工程造成交通問題、噪音，甚至導致社區搬遷時。 尤其對較貧窮的國家而言，這些風險可能會使舉辦國際賽事看起來更像是一種負擔，而不是一種福氣。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 3","english":"In my view, however, these problems do not outweigh the advantages. The real issue is not the event itself, but poor planning. If governments build facilities that serve the public after the tournament and control spending carefully, international sports events can generate tourism, improve infrastructure, and strengthen national identity.","chinese":"然而，在我看來，這些問題並不會超過其優點。 真正的問題並不是賽事本身，而是規劃不善。 如果政府建設的設施能在賽事後繼續服務公眾，並且謹慎控制開支，國際體育賽事便能促進旅遊業、改善基礎建設，並加強國家身份認同。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, although hosting major sports events can create financial pressure and local disruption, I believe countries should still welcome them because their economic, cultural, and social benefits are greater.","chinese":"總結來說，雖然舉辦大型體育賽事可能造成財政壓力和本地干擾， 但我認為各國仍然應該歡迎這些賽事，因為它們在經濟、文化和社會方面的利益更大。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"international sporting events","chinese":"國際體育盛事"},{"english":"be seen by many governments as","chinese":"被很多政府視為"},{"english":"powerful opportunities to","chinese":"……的強大機會"},{"english":"raise their country's profile","chinese":"提升國家形象；提高國際知名度"},{"english":"hosting these competitions","chinese":"主辦這些賽事"},{"english":"financial and social problems","chinese":"財政和社會問題"},{"english":"long-term benefits","chinese":"長遠好處"},{"english":"outweigh these drawbacks","chinese":"大於這些缺點"},{"english":"on the one hand","chinese":"一方面"},{"english":"be eager to","chinese":"渴望；熱衷於"},{"english":"host major sports events","chinese":"主辦大型體育賽事"},{"english":"economic and reputational rewards","chinese":"經濟和聲譽上的回報"},{"english":"welcome athletes, journalists, and spectators","chinese":"迎接運動員、記者和觀眾"},{"english":"local businesses","chinese":"本地商戶"},{"english":"receive a significant boost","chinese":"得到顯著推動"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"put a country on the world map","chinese":"令一個國家受到國際關注"},{"english":"a successful Olympic Games or World Cup","chinese":"成功的奧運會或世界盃"},{"english":"the host nation","chinese":"主辦國"},{"english":"present itself as","chinese":"將自己展示為"},{"english":"modern, organised, and culturally attractive","chinese":"現代化、有組織和具文化吸引力"},{"english":"strengthen tourism","chinese":"促進旅遊業"},{"english":"after the final whistle has blown","chinese":"賽事結束後"},{"english":"in addition","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"unite citizens behind","chinese":"令國民團結在……之下"},{"english":"a shared national moment","chinese":"共同的國家時刻"},{"english":"a sense of pride","chinese":"自豪感"},{"english":"ordinary government projects","chinese":"一般政府項目"},{"english":"rarely generate","chinese":"很少產生"},{"english":"on the other hand","chinese":"另一方面"},{"english":"critics argue that","chinese":"批評者認為"},{"english":"the costs of hosting","chinese":"主辦成本"},{"english":"dangerously high","chinese":"高得危險；過高"},{"english":"spend enormous sums on","chinese":"花費巨額金錢於"},{"english":"transport systems","chinese":"交通系統"},{"english":"temporary facilities","chinese":"臨時設施"},{"english":"need urgent investment","chinese":"急需投資"},{"english":"venues","chinese":"場館"},{"english":"rarely used afterwards","chinese":"之後很少被使用"},{"english":"expensive white elephants","chinese":"昂貴的大白象工程"},{"english":"valuable public assets","chinese":"有價值的公共資產"},{"english":"disruption for local residents","chinese":"對本地居民的滋擾"},{"english":"construction projects","chinese":"建築工程"},{"english":"the relocation of communities","chinese":"社區搬遷"},{"english":"for poorer countries in particular","chinese":"對較貧窮國家尤其如此"},{"english":"these risks","chinese":"這些風險"},{"english":"an international tournament","chinese":"國際錦標賽"},{"english":"more like a burden than a blessing","chinese":"更像負擔而不是好事"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"do not outweigh the advantages","chinese":"不會大於優點"},{"english":"the real issue","chinese":"真正問題"},{"english":"the event itself","chinese":"事件本身"},{"english":"poor planning","chinese":"規劃不善"},{"english":"serve the public","chinese":"服務公眾"},{"english":"after the tournament","chinese":"錦標賽之後"},{"english":"control spending carefully","chinese":"審慎控制開支"},{"english":"generate tourism","chinese":"帶動旅遊業"},{"english":"improve infrastructure","chinese":"改善基建"},{"english":"strengthen national identity","chinese":"加強國民身份認同"},{"english":"financial pressure","chinese":"財政壓力"},{"english":"local disruption","chinese":"對本地造成滋擾"},{"english":"should still welcome them","chinese":"仍然應該歡迎它們"},{"english":"economic, cultural, and social benefits","chinese":"經濟、文化和社會好處"}]},"model-essay-37-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-37-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:37","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-37-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q37","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Scientific education is often seen as the engine of national development, especially in an age shaped by medicine, engineering and technology. However, I completely disagree that governments should prioritise funding for science teaching over all other subjects. A country does not progress through scientific knowledge alone; it develops through a broad, balanced education system that produces skilled, thoughtful and socially responsible citizens.","chinese":"科學教育常被視為國家發展的引擎，尤其是在一個由醫學、工程和科技所塑造的時代。 然而，我完全不同意政府應該把科學教學的資金優先置於所有其他學科之上。 一個國家並不是單靠科學知識就能進步；它是透過一個廣泛而均衡的教育制度來發展，而這個制度能培養有技能、有思想，並且具有社會責任感的公民。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that non-science subjects are essential to the practical functioning of a modern society. Languages, history, economics and the arts are not decorative extras; they shape how people communicate, govern, trade and understand one another. For example, a nation may train excellent engineers, but if it lacks capable teachers, lawyers, journalists and public administrators, its scientific achievements may never translate into stable institutions or public trust. Development is not only about building laboratories or inventing machines. It is also about building judgment, culture and cooperation, which are largely strengthened through the humanities and social sciences.","chinese":"第一個原因是，非科學學科對現代社會的實際運作是不可或缺的。 語言、歷史、經濟學和藝術並不是裝飾性的附加項目；它們塑造了人們如何溝通、治理、交易，以及互相理解。 例如，一個國家也許能培養出優秀的工程師，但如果它缺乏有能力的教師、律師、記者和公共行政人員，它的科學成就可能永遠無法轉化為穩定的制度或公眾信任。 發展不只是關於建造實驗室或發明機器。 它同時也是關於建立判斷力、文化和合作精神，而這些能力在很大程度上是透過人文學科和社會科學來強化的。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another problem with giving science a privileged share of public funding is that it may narrow students’ opportunities and weaken the wider economy. Not every young person is suited to physics, chemistry or biology, and forcing the education system to revolve around these areas could waste human potential. Some students may become outstanding designers, entrepreneurs, translators or artists if they are properly supported. These fields also contribute directly to national progress by creating jobs, attracting investment and strengthening a country’s cultural identity. In this sense, a science-heavy curriculum may look efficient on paper, but it can become a narrow road when a country actually needs many roads to move forward.","chinese":"給予科學在公共資金中更優先的份額，另一個問題是它可能會收窄學生的機會，並削弱整體經濟。 並不是每一個年輕人都適合物理、化學或生物，而強迫教育制度圍繞這些領域運作，可能會浪費人的潛能。 如果得到適當支持，有些學生可能會成為出色的設計師、企業家、翻譯員或藝術家。 這些領域也能透過創造就業、吸引投資，以及強化一個國家的文化身份，直接為國家進步作出貢獻。 從這個意義上說，一個過度偏重科學的課程表面上看起來可能很有效率，但當一個國家其實需要多條道路向前發展時，它就可能變成一條狹窄的道路。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, while science education deserves strong public investment, it should not receive greater funding at the expense of other subjects. True national progress depends on a balanced education system, because countries need not only scientists, but also communicators, leaders, thinkers and creators.","chinese":"總結來說，雖然科學教育值得得到強而有力的公共投資，但它不應該以犧牲其他學科為代價，獲得更多資金。 真正的國家進步取決於一個均衡的教育制度，因為國家不只需要科學家，也需要溝通者、領導者、思想者和創造者。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"scientific education","chinese":"科學教育"},{"english":"be seen as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"engine of national development","chinese":"國家發展的引擎"},{"english":"national development","chinese":"國家發展"},{"english":"especially in an age shaped by","chinese":"尤其在一個由……塑造的時代"},{"english":"medicine, engineering and technology","chinese":"醫學、工程和科技"},{"english":"prioritise funding for","chinese":"優先撥款給……"},{"english":"science teaching","chinese":"科學教學"},{"english":"over all other subjects","chinese":"優先於所有其他科目"},{"english":"progress through","chinese":"透過……進步"},{"english":"scientific knowledge alone","chinese":"單靠科學知識"},{"english":"broad, balanced education system","chinese":"廣泛而均衡的教育制度"},{"english":"skilled, thoughtful and socially responsible citizens","chinese":"有技能、有思想和有社會責任感的公民"},{"english":"non-science subjects","chinese":"非科學科目"},{"english":"essential to","chinese":"對……必不可少"},{"english":"practical functioning of","chinese":"……的實際運作"},{"english":"modern society","chinese":"現代社會"},{"english":"languages, history, economics and the arts","chinese":"語言、歷史、經濟和藝術"},{"english":"decorative extras","chinese":"裝飾性的附加物"},{"english":"shape how people communicate","chinese":"塑造人們如何溝通"},{"english":"govern, trade and understand one another","chinese":"管治、貿易和互相理解"},{"english":"train excellent engineers","chinese":"培訓出色工程師"},{"english":"capable teachers","chinese":"有能力的教師"},{"english":"lawyers, journalists and public administrators","chinese":"律師、記者和公共行政人員"},{"english":"scientific achievements","chinese":"科學成就"},{"english":"translate into","chinese":"轉化為"},{"english":"stable institutions","chinese":"穩定制度"},{"english":"public trust","chinese":"公眾信任"},{"english":"not only about","chinese":"不只是關於……"},{"english":"building laboratories","chinese":"建設實驗室"},{"english":"inventing machines","chinese":"發明機器"},{"english":"building judgment, culture and cooperation","chinese":"建立判斷力、文化和合作"},{"english":"largely strengthened through","chinese":"很大程度上透過……加強"},{"english":"the humanities and social sciences","chinese":"人文學科和社會科學"},{"english":"privileged share of","chinese":"優先佔有較大份額的……"},{"english":"public funding","chinese":"公共撥款"},{"english":"narrow students' opportunities","chinese":"收窄學生的機會"},{"english":"weaken the wider economy","chinese":"削弱更廣泛的經濟"},{"english":"be suited to","chinese":"適合"},{"english":"forcing the education system to","chinese":"強迫教育制度去……"},{"english":"revolve around","chinese":"圍繞……運作"},{"english":"waste human potential","chinese":"浪費人的潛能"},{"english":"outstanding designers","chinese":"出色設計師"},{"english":"entrepreneurs, translators or artists","chinese":"企業家、翻譯員或藝術家"},{"english":"properly supported","chinese":"得到適當支持"},{"english":"contribute directly to","chinese":"直接促進"},{"english":"national progress","chinese":"國家進步"},{"english":"creating jobs","chinese":"創造就業機會"},{"english":"attracting investment","chinese":"吸引投資"},{"english":"strengthening a country's cultural identity","chinese":"加強一個國家的文化身份"},{"english":"cultural identity","chinese":"文化身份"},{"english":"science-heavy curriculum","chinese":"偏重科學的課程"},{"english":"look efficient on paper","chinese":"在紙面上看似高效"},{"english":"narrow road","chinese":"狹窄的道路"},{"english":"move forward","chinese":"向前發展"},{"english":"deserves strong public investment","chinese":"值得大量公共投資"},{"english":"at the expense of","chinese":"以犧牲……為代價"},{"english":"true national progress","chinese":"真正的國家進步"},{"english":"communicators, leaders, thinkers and creators","chinese":"溝通者、領袖、思想者和創作者"}]},"model-essay-38-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-38-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:38","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-38-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q38","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"History has always been one of the main ways through which societies understand themselves. Although different cultures preserve the past in different forms, history can be passed on through education, storytelling, public memory, and cultural traditions. It remains important because it gives people identity, wisdom, and a shared sense of direction.","chinese":"歷史一直是社會理解自身的主要方式之一。 儘管不同文化以不同形式保存過去，歷史可以透過教育、故事傳承、公共記憶和文化傳統傳給下一代。 歷史之所以仍然重要，是因為它給予人們身份認同、智慧，以及共同的方向感。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"There are several ways in which history can be handed down to younger generations. The most obvious method is formal education, as schools can teach students about major events, influential figures, and the development of their own country. However, history is not only found in textbooks. It is also preserved through oral traditions, family stories, monuments, museums, documentaries, and national ceremonies. For example, grandparents may tell children about wartime hardship or migration, allowing them to feel that the past is not just a distant chapter in a book, but part of their family’s living memory. In this way, history is like a bridge between generations: it allows people who never met to remain connected.","chinese":"歷史可以透過幾種方式傳承給年輕一代。 最明顯的方法是正規教育，因為學校可以教導學生了解重大事件、重要人物，以及自己國家的發展。 然而，歷史並不只存在於課本之中。 歷史也可以透過口述傳統、家庭故事、紀念碑、博物館、紀錄片和國家儀式被保存下來。 例如，祖父母可能會向孩子講述戰爭時期的艱難或移民經歷，讓他們感受到過去並不只是書本中遙遠的一章，而是家庭鮮活記憶的一部分。 這樣一來，歷史就像世代之間的一座橋：它讓從未見過面的人仍然保持連結。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"History is also vital to society because it shapes collective identity and helps people make wiser decisions. A community that understands its past is more likely to appreciate its language, customs, values, and struggles. Without this knowledge, people may feel rootless, as if they are living in a house whose foundations they cannot see. More importantly, history teaches societies the consequences of human choices. Wars, social movements, scientific discoveries, and political mistakes all provide lessons about power, justice, conflict, and progress. If these lessons are ignored, societies may repeat old errors under new names.","chinese":"歷史對社會也至關重要，因為它塑造集體身份，並幫助人們作出更明智的決定。 一個理解自身過去的社群，更有可能珍惜自己的語言、習俗、價值觀和曾經經歷的奮鬥。 如果沒有這種知識，人們可能會感到失去根基，彷彿住在一間看不見地基的房子裡。 更重要的是，歷史教導社會明白人類選擇所帶來的後果。 戰爭、社會運動、科學發現和政治錯誤，都提供了關於權力、正義、衝突和進步的教訓。 如果這些教訓被忽視，社會便可能以新的形式重複舊有的錯誤。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, history can be passed on through schools, families, cultural institutions, media, and public traditions. Its importance lies not only in preserving old facts, but also in helping society understand where it came from, who it is, and how it should move forward.","chinese":"總結來說，歷史可以透過學校、家庭、文化機構、媒體和公共傳統傳承下去。 它的重要性不僅在於保存過去的事實，也在於幫助社會理解自己從何而來、自己是誰，以及未來應該如何前進。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"one of the main ways through which","chinese":"……的主要方式之一"},{"english":"understand themselves","chinese":"了解自身"},{"english":"preserve the past","chinese":"保存過去"},{"english":"in different forms","chinese":"以不同形式"},{"english":"be passed on through","chinese":"透過……傳承"},{"english":"storytelling","chinese":"講故事；口述故事"},{"english":"public memory","chinese":"公共記憶"},{"english":"cultural traditions","chinese":"文化傳統"},{"english":"remains important","chinese":"仍然重要"},{"english":"gives people identity","chinese":"給予人身份認同"},{"english":"a shared sense of direction","chinese":"共同方向感"},{"english":"several ways in which","chinese":"幾種……的方式"},{"english":"be handed down to","chinese":"傳給"},{"english":"younger generations","chinese":"年輕一代"},{"english":"the most obvious method","chinese":"最明顯的方法"},{"english":"formal education","chinese":"正規教育"},{"english":"major events","chinese":"重大事件"},{"english":"influential figures","chinese":"有影響力的人物"},{"english":"the development of","chinese":"……的發展"},{"english":"their own country","chinese":"自己的國家"},{"english":"not only found in textbooks","chinese":"不只存在於教科書中"},{"english":"oral traditions","chinese":"口述傳統"},{"english":"family stories","chinese":"家族故事"},{"english":"monuments","chinese":"紀念碑；歷史建築"},{"english":"museums","chinese":"博物館"},{"english":"documentaries","chinese":"紀錄片"},{"english":"national ceremonies","chinese":"國家儀式"},{"english":"wartime hardship","chinese":"戰時艱苦"},{"english":"migration","chinese":"遷移；移民經歷"},{"english":"allowing them to","chinese":"讓他們能夠"},{"english":"a distant chapter in a book","chinese":"書中遙遠的一章"},{"english":"living memory","chinese":"鮮活記憶"},{"english":"In this way","chinese":"以這種方式"},{"english":"a bridge between generations","chinese":"世代之間的橋樑"},{"english":"remain connected","chinese":"保持連繫"},{"english":"vital to society","chinese":"對社會至關重要"},{"english":"shapes collective identity","chinese":"塑造集體身份認同"},{"english":"make wiser decisions","chinese":"作出更明智的決定"},{"english":"understands its past","chinese":"了解自身過去"},{"english":"more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"appreciate its language","chinese":"珍惜自身語言"},{"english":"customs","chinese":"風俗習慣"},{"english":"values","chinese":"價值觀"},{"english":"struggles","chinese":"奮鬥歷程；艱難經歷"},{"english":"without this knowledge","chinese":"沒有這些知識"},{"english":"feel rootless","chinese":"感到沒有根"},{"english":"as if","chinese":"彷彿"},{"english":"foundations","chinese":"根基"},{"english":"cannot see","chinese":"看不見"},{"english":"More importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"the consequences of","chinese":"……的後果"},{"english":"human choices","chinese":"人類選擇"},{"english":"wars","chinese":"戰爭"},{"english":"social movements","chinese":"社會運動"},{"english":"scientific discoveries","chinese":"科學發現"},{"english":"political mistakes","chinese":"政治失誤"},{"english":"provide lessons about","chinese":"提供關於……的教訓"},{"english":"power and justice","chinese":"權力和公義"},{"english":"conflict and progress","chinese":"衝突和進步"},{"english":"be ignored","chinese":"被忽視"},{"english":"repeat old errors","chinese":"重複舊錯誤"},{"english":"under new names","chinese":"以新的名義"},{"english":"cultural institutions","chinese":"文化機構"},{"english":"media","chinese":"媒體"},{"english":"public traditions","chinese":"公共傳統"},{"english":"its importance lies not only in","chinese":"它的重要性不只在於"},{"english":"preserving old facts","chinese":"保存舊事實"},{"english":"where it came from","chinese":"它從何而來"},{"english":"who it is","chinese":"它是誰；自身身份"},{"english":"move forward","chinese":"向前發展"}]},"model-essay-38-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-38-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:38","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-38-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q38","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Modern education is often expected to equip young people for a fast-changing, technology-driven world. Because of this, some argue that schools should remove art and music from the curriculum and give more time to practical subjects such as information technology. I completely disagree with this view, as creative subjects are not decorative extras but an essential part of a balanced education.","chinese":"現代教育通常被期望裝備年輕人去面對一個快速變化、由科技推動的世界。 正因如此，有些人主張學校應該把美術和音樂從課程中刪除，並把更多時間分配給資訊科技等實用科目。 我完全不同意這個觀點，因為創意科目並不是可有可無的裝飾，而是均衡教育中不可或缺的一部分。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"First, art and music develop forms of thinking that technical subjects alone cannot easily provide. In IT lessons, students may learn how to use software, write code or analyse digital systems. However, when they paint, compose or perform, they learn how to interpret ideas, experiment with possibilities and solve open-ended problems. These habits are highly relevant to the modern workplace, where many tasks require originality rather than mechanical obedience. For example, a student designing a website needs not only programming knowledge but also a sense of layout, colour, rhythm and audience. Without creative training, technology can become a tool in the hands of someone who knows how to press buttons but not how to create meaning.","chinese":"首先，美術和音樂能培養一些單靠技術科目難以提供的思維方式。 在資訊科技課堂中，學生可能會學習如何使用軟件、編寫程式或分析數碼系統。 然而，當他們繪畫、作曲或表演時，他們會學習如何詮釋想法、嘗試不同可能性，並解決沒有固定答案的問題。 這些習慣與現代職場高度相關，因許多工作任務需要的是原創性，而不是機械式的服從 例如，一名設計網站的學生不只需要程式知識，也需要對版面、色彩、節奏和受眾有敏感度。 如果沒有創意訓練，科技可能只會變成一件工具，落在一個懂得按按鈕、卻不懂得創造意義的人手中。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Second, schools should prepare children for life, not merely for employment. Art and music give students a language for emotion, culture and identity, which is especially important in an age dominated by screens and rapid information. A child who learns music may become more patient and disciplined through regular practice, while a child who studies art may become more observant and sensitive to different perspectives. These qualities are not soft luxuries; they help young people communicate, collaborate and remain human in a highly digital world. Removing such subjects would make education narrower, colder and less complete.","chinese":"第二，學校應該讓孩子為人生作準備，而不只是為就業作準備。 美術和音樂給予學生一種表達情感、文化和身份認同的語言，而這在一個由螢幕和快速資訊主導的時代尤其重要。 一個學習音樂的孩子，可能會透過規律練習變得更有耐性和紀律；而一個學習美術的孩子，可能會變得更善於觀察，也更能敏銳地理解不同角度。 這些特質並不是柔弱而奢侈的附加品；它們能幫助年輕人在高度數碼化的世界中溝通、合作，並保持人的本質。 刪除這些科目會令教育變得更狹窄、更冰冷，也更不完整。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, IT is undeniably useful, but it should not replace art and music. A curriculum that combines technological competence with creativity is far better suited to the modern world than one that treats children as future machines.","chinese":"總結來說，資訊科技無疑是有用的，但它不應取代美術和音樂。 一個把科技能力與創造力結合起來的課程，比一個把孩子視為未來機器的課程，更適合現代世界。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"be expected to","chinese":"被期望去……"},{"english":"equip young people for","chinese":"讓年輕人為……作好準備"},{"english":"fast-changing","chinese":"快速變化的"},{"english":"technology-driven world","chinese":"由科技主導的世界"},{"english":"because of this","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"remove art and music from","chinese":"將藝術和音樂從……移除"},{"english":"curriculum","chinese":"課程"},{"english":"give more time to","chinese":"給予更多時間"},{"english":"practical subjects","chinese":"實用科目"},{"english":"information technology","chinese":"資訊科技"},{"english":"creative subjects","chinese":"創意科目"},{"english":"decorative extras","chinese":"裝飾性的附加物"},{"english":"essential part of","chinese":"……的重要部分"},{"english":"balanced education","chinese":"均衡教育"},{"english":"develop forms of thinking","chinese":"培養思維方式"},{"english":"technical subjects alone","chinese":"單靠技術科目"},{"english":"use software","chinese":"使用軟件"},{"english":"write code","chinese":"編寫程式碼"},{"english":"analyse digital systems","chinese":"分析數碼系統"},{"english":"paint, compose or perform","chinese":"繪畫、作曲或表演"},{"english":"interpret ideas","chinese":"詮釋想法"},{"english":"experiment with possibilities","chinese":"嘗試不同可能性"},{"english":"solve open-ended problems","chinese":"解決開放式問題"},{"english":"highly relevant to","chinese":"與……高度相關"},{"english":"modern workplace","chinese":"現代職場"},{"english":"tasks require originality","chinese":"任務需要原創性"},{"english":"rather than mechanical obedience","chinese":"而不是機械式服從"},{"english":"programming knowledge","chinese":"編程知識"},{"english":"a sense of layout","chinese":"對版面佈局的觸覺"},{"english":"colour, rhythm and audience","chinese":"色彩、節奏和受眾"},{"english":"creative training","chinese":"創意訓練"},{"english":"a tool in the hands of","chinese":"在……手中的工具"},{"english":"press buttons","chinese":"按按鈕"},{"english":"create meaning","chinese":"創造意義"},{"english":"prepare children for life","chinese":"讓孩子為生活作好準備"},{"english":"not merely for employment","chinese":"不只是為了就業"},{"english":"a language for emotion, culture and identity","chinese":"表達情感、文化和身份的語言"},{"english":"especially important in","chinese":"在……中特別重要"},{"english":"an age dominated by","chinese":"一個由……主導的時代"},{"english":"screens and rapid information","chinese":"螢幕和快速資訊"},{"english":"patient and disciplined","chinese":"有耐性和有紀律"},{"english":"regular practice","chinese":"定期練習"},{"english":"become more observant","chinese":"變得更善於觀察"},{"english":"sensitive to different perspectives","chinese":"對不同角度更敏感"},{"english":"soft luxuries","chinese":"可有可無的軟性奢侈品"},{"english":"communicate, collaborate and remain human","chinese":"溝通、協作並保持人性"},{"english":"highly digital world","chinese":"高度數碼化的世界"},{"english":"removing such subjects","chinese":"移除這類科目"},{"english":"narrower, colder and less complete","chinese":"更狹窄、更冷冰冰和更不完整"},{"english":"undeniably useful","chinese":"無可否認地有用"},{"english":"replace art and music","chinese":"取代藝術和音樂"},{"english":"combines technological competence with creativity","chinese":"結合科技能力和創意"},{"english":"technological competence","chinese":"科技能力"},{"english":"far better suited to","chinese":"更適合……得多"},{"english":"treats children as future machines","chinese":"將孩子視為未來的機器"}]},"model-essay-39-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-39-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:39","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-39-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q39","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Every culture expresses itself through music and art, whether through songs, paintings, dance, sculpture, or public performances. These creative forms are not merely sources of entertainment; they carry social meaning and personal value. This essay will explain how music and art strengthen social identity and enrich individual emotional life.","chinese":"每一種文化都會透過音樂和藝術表達自己，無論是透過歌曲、繪畫、舞蹈、雕塑，還是公共表演。 這些創作形式並不只是娛樂來源；它們承載著社會意義和個人價值。 本文將解釋音樂和藝術如何強化社會身份認同，並豐富個人的情感生活。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"At the societal level, music and art are important because they preserve culture and create a shared sense of belonging. A society is not defined only by its laws, economy, or political system, but also by the stories, emotions, and values that people pass from one generation to the next. Traditional songs, murals, festivals, and performances often keep historical memory alive in a way that textbooks alone cannot. For example, national songs or folk dances can remind people of their common roots, especially during public celebrations or difficult periods. In this sense, the arts act as a cultural bridge: they connect the past with the present and help people feel that they are part of something larger than themselves.","chinese":"在社會層面，音樂和藝術之所以重要，是因為它們能保存文化，並創造共同的歸屬感。 一個社會並不只由它的法律、經濟或政治制度所定義，也由人們代代相傳的故事、情感和價值觀所定義。 傳統歌曲、壁畫、節慶和表演，往往能以教科書單獨無法做到的方式，使歷史記憶保持鮮活。 例如，國歌或民間舞蹈可以提醒人們他們共同的根源，尤其是在公共慶典或艱難時期。 從這個意義上說，藝術就像一座文化橋樑：它們連接過去與現在，並幫助人們感到自己是某個比自身更大的整體的一部分。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"For individuals, music and art are equally valuable because they provide a powerful outlet for emotion, imagination, and self-understanding. Many feelings are difficult to explain directly, but a song, a painting, or a poem can express them with surprising clarity. Someone who feels stressed after work, for instance, may listen to music to calm down, while another person may draw or write in order to process sadness or confusion. These activities do not simply fill empty time; they help people make sense of their inner lives. Without such forms of expression, life would be more practical perhaps, but also colder and less human.","chinese":"對個人而言，音樂和藝術同樣有價值，因為它們為情感、想像力和自我理解提供了一個強大的出口。 許多感受很難直接解釋，但一首歌、一幅畫或一首詩，卻能以令人驚訝的清晰度把它們表達出來。 例如，一個下班後感到壓力的人，可能會聽音樂讓自己平靜下來，而另一個人則可能會透過繪畫或寫作來處理悲傷或困惑。 這些活動並不只是填補空閒時間；它們幫助人們理解自己的內心生活。 如果沒有這些表達形式，生活也許會更加實用，但也會更加冰冷、更加缺乏人性。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, music and art are important because they give societies cultural depth and give individuals emotional space. They preserve identity, build connection, and allow people to express what ordinary language often cannot.","chinese":"總結來說，音樂和藝術之所以重要，是因為它們賦予社會文化深度，也給予個人情感空間。 它們保存身份認同、建立連結，並使人們能夠表達普通語言往往無法表達的東西。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"expresses itself through","chinese":"透過……表達自身"},{"english":"music and art","chinese":"音樂和藝術"},{"english":"public performances","chinese":"公開表演"},{"english":"creative forms","chinese":"創作形式"},{"english":"not merely sources of","chinese":"不只是……的來源"},{"english":"sources of entertainment","chinese":"娛樂來源"},{"english":"carry social meaning","chinese":"承載社會意義"},{"english":"personal value","chinese":"個人價值"},{"english":"strengthen social identity","chinese":"加強社會身份認同"},{"english":"enrich individual emotional life","chinese":"豐富個人的情感生活"},{"english":"at the societal level","chinese":"在社會層面上"},{"english":"preserve culture","chinese":"保存文化"},{"english":"create a shared sense of belonging","chinese":"建立共同歸屬感"},{"english":"a shared sense of belonging","chinese":"共同歸屬感"},{"english":"be defined only by","chinese":"只由……定義"},{"english":"political system","chinese":"政治制度"},{"english":"pass from one generation to the next","chinese":"代代相傳"},{"english":"traditional songs","chinese":"傳統歌曲"},{"english":"murals","chinese":"壁畫"},{"english":"historical memory","chinese":"歷史記憶"},{"english":"keep historical memory alive","chinese":"保持歷史記憶鮮活"},{"english":"in a way that","chinese":"以一種……的方式"},{"english":"textbooks alone","chinese":"單靠教科書"},{"english":"national songs","chinese":"國歌；民族歌曲"},{"english":"folk dances","chinese":"民間舞蹈"},{"english":"remind people of","chinese":"令人民想起"},{"english":"common roots","chinese":"共同根源"},{"english":"public celebrations","chinese":"公眾慶祝活動"},{"english":"difficult periods","chinese":"困難時期"},{"english":"In this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"the arts","chinese":"藝術"},{"english":"act as a cultural bridge","chinese":"成為文化橋樑"},{"english":"connect the past with the present","chinese":"連繫過去與現在"},{"english":"part of something larger than themselves","chinese":"比自己更大的整體的一部分"},{"english":"equally valuable","chinese":"同樣有價值"},{"english":"provide a powerful outlet for","chinese":"為……提供強大的出口"},{"english":"emotion, imagination, and self-understanding","chinese":"情感、想像力和自我理解"},{"english":"difficult to explain directly","chinese":"難以直接解釋"},{"english":"express them with surprising clarity","chinese":"以令人意外的清晰度表達它們"},{"english":"surprising clarity","chinese":"令人意外的清晰"},{"english":"feels stressed after work","chinese":"下班後感到有壓力"},{"english":"calm down","chinese":"冷靜下來；放鬆下來"},{"english":"process sadness or confusion","chinese":"處理悲傷或困惑"},{"english":"do not simply fill empty time","chinese":"不只是填補空閒時間"},{"english":"empty time","chinese":"空閒時間"},{"english":"make sense of","chinese":"理解"},{"english":"inner lives","chinese":"內心世界"},{"english":"forms of expression","chinese":"表達形式"},{"english":"more practical perhaps","chinese":"也許更實際"},{"english":"colder and less human","chinese":"更冷漠、更少人情味"},{"english":"cultural depth","chinese":"文化深度"},{"english":"emotional space","chinese":"情感空間"},{"english":"preserve identity","chinese":"保留身份認同"},{"english":"build connection","chinese":"建立連繫"},{"english":"ordinary language","chinese":"普通語言"}]},"model-essay-39-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-39-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:39","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-39-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q39","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In recent years, online communication has become one of the most common ways for people to meet others and maintain social contact. While some argue that this has made human relationships stronger by removing barriers of distance, I believe that it has, on balance, made many people more socially isolated.","chinese":"近年來，網上溝通已成為人們認識他人和維持社交聯繫最常見的方式之一。 雖然有些人認為，這透過消除距離上的障礙，使人際關係變得更牢固， 但我認為，整體而言，這反而使許多人在社交上變得更加孤立。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"On the one hand, the internet can certainly bring people closer together. Social media platforms, messaging apps and online communities allow individuals to stay in touch even when they live in different cities or countries. This is especially valuable for families separated by work, study or migration, as they can share daily experiences almost instantly rather than waiting for occasional visits. The internet also helps people who feel excluded in their local environment to find others with similar interests. For example, a shy student who struggles to make friends at school may feel more confident joining an online group about music, gaming or art. In this sense, digital communication can act as a bridge between people who might otherwise never meet.","chinese":"一方面，互聯網確實可以拉近人與人之間的距離。 社交媒體平台、即時通訊應用程式和網上社群，使人們即使住在不同城市或國家，也能保持聯絡。 這對因工作、學習或移民而分隔兩地的家庭尤其有價值，因為他們可以幾乎即時分享日常經歷，而不必等待偶爾的探訪。 互聯網也幫助那些在本地環境中感到被排斥的人，找到與自己有相似興趣的人。 例如，一個在學校難以交朋友的害羞學生，可能會在加入關於音樂、遊戲或藝術的網上群組時感到更有信心。 從這個意義上說，數位溝通可以在人們之間搭建橋樑，讓一些原本可能永遠不會相遇的人產生聯繫。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, I think the stronger argument is that online socialising often creates a thinner and less satisfying form of connection. Many people now spend hours scrolling through posts, sending short messages or reacting to photos, but these interactions rarely provide the emotional depth of face-to-face conversation. When people become used to communicating through screens, they may gradually lose the habit of meeting friends in person, reading body language, or dealing with awkward but necessary real-life conversations. For instance, a group of friends may sit together in a café while each person is absorbed in their own phone. Although they are physically close, they are socially distant. Over time, this can make relationships feel more convenient but less meaningful.","chinese":"然而，我認為更有力的觀點是，網上社交往往創造出一種較薄弱、也較不令人滿足的聯繫形式。 如今，許多人花數小時瀏覽帖文、發送簡短訊息或回應照片，但這些互動很少能提供面對面交談所具有的情感深度。 當人們習慣透過螢幕溝通時，他們可能會逐漸失去親身見朋友、理解肢體語言，以及處理尷尬但必要的現實對話的習慣。 例如，一群朋友可能一起坐在咖啡店裡，但每個人都沉浸在自己的手機之中。 雖然他們在身體距離上很接近，但在社交上卻彼此疏離。 長遠而言，這可能會使人際關係感覺更方便，卻更缺乏意義。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, the internet has undoubtedly made it easier for people to contact one another and form new connections. Nevertheless, I believe it has made society more isolated overall because online interaction too often replaces, rather than strengthens, genuine human contact","chinese":"總結來說，互聯網無疑使人們更容易彼此聯絡，並建立新的關係。 然而，我認為它整體上使社會變得更加孤立，因為網上互動太常取代真正的人際接觸，而不是加強它。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"in recent years","chinese":"近年來"},{"english":"online communication","chinese":"網上溝通"},{"english":"one of the most common ways","chinese":"最常見的方法之一"},{"english":"meet others","chinese":"認識他人"},{"english":"maintain social contact","chinese":"維持社交聯繫"},{"english":"human relationships","chinese":"人際關係"},{"english":"by removing barriers of distance","chinese":"透過消除距離障礙"},{"english":"barriers of distance","chinese":"距離障礙"},{"english":"on balance","chinese":"總體而言"},{"english":"socially isolated","chinese":"社交上更加孤立"},{"english":"on the one hand","chinese":"一方面"},{"english":"bring people closer together","chinese":"拉近人與人之間的距離"},{"english":"social media platforms","chinese":"社交媒體平台"},{"english":"messaging apps","chinese":"即時通訊應用程式"},{"english":"online communities","chinese":"網上社群"},{"english":"allow individuals to","chinese":"讓個人能夠"},{"english":"stay in touch","chinese":"保持聯絡"},{"english":"live in different cities or countries","chinese":"住在不同城市或國家"},{"english":"especially valuable for","chinese":"對……尤其有價值"},{"english":"separated by work, study or migration","chinese":"因工作、學業或移民而分隔"},{"english":"share daily experiences","chinese":"分享日常經歷"},{"english":"almost instantly","chinese":"幾乎即時地"},{"english":"rather than waiting for","chinese":"而不是等待"},{"english":"occasional visits","chinese":"偶爾探訪"},{"english":"feel excluded","chinese":"感到被排斥"},{"english":"local environment","chinese":"本地環境"},{"english":"find others with similar interests","chinese":"找到有相似興趣的人"},{"english":"a shy student","chinese":"害羞的學生"},{"english":"struggle to make friends","chinese":"難以交朋友"},{"english":"feel more confident","chinese":"感到更有信心"},{"english":"joining an online group","chinese":"加入網上群組"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"digital communication","chinese":"數碼溝通"},{"english":"act as a bridge between","chinese":"作為……之間的橋樑"},{"english":"might otherwise never meet","chinese":"否則可能永遠不會見面"},{"english":"the stronger argument","chinese":"更有力的論點"},{"english":"online socialising","chinese":"網上社交"},{"english":"a thinner and less satisfying form of connection","chinese":"較薄弱而較不滿足的聯繫形式"},{"english":"spend hours scrolling through posts","chinese":"花數小時瀏覽帖文"},{"english":"sending short messages","chinese":"發送簡短訊息"},{"english":"reacting to photos","chinese":"對相片作出反應"},{"english":"rarely provide","chinese":"很少提供"},{"english":"emotional depth","chinese":"情感深度"},{"english":"face-to-face conversation","chinese":"面對面交談"},{"english":"become used to","chinese":"習慣於"},{"english":"communicating through screens","chinese":"透過螢幕溝通"},{"english":"gradually lose the habit of","chinese":"逐漸失去……的習慣"},{"english":"meeting friends in person","chinese":"親身與朋友見面"},{"english":"reading body language","chinese":"解讀身體語言"},{"english":"dealing with","chinese":"處理；應對"},{"english":"awkward but necessary real-life conversations","chinese":"尷尬但必要的現實對話"},{"english":"a group of friends","chinese":"一班朋友"},{"english":"sit together in a café","chinese":"一起坐在咖啡店裏"},{"english":"be absorbed in","chinese":"專注於；沉迷於"},{"english":"their own phone","chinese":"自己的手機"},{"english":"physically close","chinese":"身體上接近"},{"english":"socially distant","chinese":"社交上疏離"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨時間"},{"english":"feel more convenient but less meaningful","chinese":"感覺更方便但較沒有意義"},{"english":"undoubtedly","chinese":"毫無疑問"},{"english":"make it easier for people to","chinese":"令人們更容易"},{"english":"contact one another","chinese":"互相聯絡"},{"english":"form new connections","chinese":"建立新聯繫"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"more isolated overall","chinese":"整體上更加孤立"},{"english":"online interaction","chinese":"網上互動"},{"english":"too often replaces","chinese":"太經常取代"},{"english":"rather than strengthens","chinese":"而不是加強"},{"english":"genuine human contact","chinese":"真正的人與人接觸"}]},"model-essay-39-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-39-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:39","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-39-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q39","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"At a time when schools are under pressure to prepare teenagers for a competitive job market, some argue that high school students should abandon literature and focus on more practical subjects. I completely disagree. Studying poems and novels is not a decorative extra; it is a vital part of education because it strengthens students’ language, judgment and humanity.","chinese":"在學校承受壓力、需要為青少年準備競爭激烈的就業市場之際，有些人認為高中學生應該放棄文學，專注於更實用的科目。 我完全不同意。 學習詩歌和小說並不是一種裝飾性的附加內容；它是教育中至關重要的一部分，因為它能強化學生的語言能力、判斷力和人性素養。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"First, literature trains students to read and think with precision. A poem is often compact but dense; a novel follows characters, motives and conflicts over time. To understand these texts, students must infer, compare, question and support interpretations with evidence. These are not soft skills in the trivial sense. They help students write persuasively, evaluate information online and communicate clearly in adult life. For example, a student who learns to explain why a character behaves in a certain way is also learning how to build an argument rather than merely give an opinion. Literature therefore sharpens the mind instead of wasting it.","chinese":"首先，文學訓練學生精準地閱讀和思考。 詩歌通常篇幅短小但含義密集；小說則隨著時間推進人物、動機和衝突。 為了理解這些文本，學生必須推論、比較、提問，並用證據支持自己的詮釋。 這些並不是瑣碎意義上的「軟技能」。 它們幫助學生有說服力地寫作、評估網上資訊，並在成年生活中清楚溝通。 例如，一名學會解釋某個角色為何以某種方式行動的學生，同時也在學習如何建立論證，而不只是提出意見。 因此，文學是在磨練思維，而不是浪費時間。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Second, literature gives teenagers emotional and moral insight that purely technical subjects often cannot provide. High school students are still forming their identities, and novels and poems allow them to step into lives unlike their own. When they read about loss, ambition, injustice or courage, abstract values become human and memorable. This matters because education should not produce efficient workers alone; it should also produce thoughtful citizens. A class discussion about a tragic hero, for instance, can make students reflect on responsibility, prejudice and compassion far more deeply than a list of rules ever could. In this sense, literature is like a quiet rehearsal for real life: students meet difficult situations on the page before they meet them in the world.","chinese":"其次，文學給予青少年情感和道德上的洞察，而這些往往是純技術科目無法提供的。 高中學生仍在形成自己的身份，而小說和詩歌讓他們走進與自己不同的人生。 當他們讀到失去、抱負、不公或勇氣時，抽象的價值便變得有人性，也更令人難忘。 這一點很重要，因為教育不應只培養高效率的工作者；它也應培養有思想的公民。 例如，一場關於悲劇英雄的課堂討論，能讓學生比閱讀一串規則更深入地反思責任、偏見和同情心。 從這個意義上說，文學就像真實人生的一場安靜預演：學生會先在書頁上遇見困難處境，然後才在現實世界中真正面對它們。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely reject the view that literature is a waste of time for high school students. Poems and novels cultivate precise thinking, expressive language and emotional maturity. Removing them from the curriculum would make education narrower, poorer and less human.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全反對文學對高中學生來說是浪費時間的看法。 詩歌和小說培養精準思維、具表達力的語言，以及情感成熟度。 把它們從課程中移除，會使教育變得更狹窄、更貧乏，也更缺乏人性。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"at a time when","chinese":"在……的時候"},{"english":"be under pressure to","chinese":"承受壓力去……"},{"english":"prepare teenagers for","chinese":"讓青少年為……作好準備"},{"english":"competitive job market","chinese":"競爭激烈的就業市場"},{"english":"abandon literature","chinese":"放棄文學"},{"english":"focus on","chinese":"專注於"},{"english":"practical subjects","chinese":"實用科目"},{"english":"decorative extra","chinese":"裝飾性的附加物"},{"english":"vital part of","chinese":"……的重要部分"},{"english":"strengthens students' language","chinese":"加強學生的語言能力"},{"english":"judgment and humanity","chinese":"判斷力和人性"},{"english":"trains students to","chinese":"訓練學生去……"},{"english":"with precision","chinese":"精準地"},{"english":"compact but dense","chinese":"簡短但含意豐富"},{"english":"follows characters, motives and conflicts","chinese":"跟隨人物、動機和衝突"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨着時間推移"},{"english":"infer","chinese":"推斷"},{"english":"support interpretations with evidence","chinese":"用證據支持詮釋"},{"english":"soft skills","chinese":"軟技能"},{"english":"in the trivial sense","chinese":"在瑣碎的意義上"},{"english":"write persuasively","chinese":"有說服力地寫作"},{"english":"evaluate information online","chinese":"評估網上資料"},{"english":"communicate clearly","chinese":"清晰溝通"},{"english":"adult life","chinese":"成年生活"},{"english":"behaves in a certain way","chinese":"以某種方式行為"},{"english":"build an argument","chinese":"建立論點"},{"english":"rather than merely","chinese":"而不是只是"},{"english":"give an opinion","chinese":"發表意見"},{"english":"sharpens the mind","chinese":"磨練思維"},{"english":"wasting it","chinese":"浪費它"},{"english":"emotional and moral insight","chinese":"情感和道德洞察"},{"english":"purely technical subjects","chinese":"純技術科目"},{"english":"forming their identities","chinese":"形成自己的身份認同"},{"english":"step into lives unlike their own","chinese":"走進與自己不同的人生"},{"english":"loss, ambition, injustice or courage","chinese":"失去、抱負、不公或勇氣"},{"english":"abstract values","chinese":"抽象價值"},{"english":"become human and memorable","chinese":"變得有人性而令人難忘"},{"english":"produce efficient workers alone","chinese":"只培養高效率工人"},{"english":"thoughtful citizens","chinese":"有思想的公民"},{"english":"class discussion","chinese":"課堂討論"},{"english":"tragic hero","chinese":"悲劇英雄"},{"english":"reflect on","chinese":"反思"},{"english":"responsibility, prejudice and compassion","chinese":"責任、偏見和同情心"},{"english":"far more deeply than","chinese":"比……深入得多"},{"english":"a list of rules","chinese":"一張規則清單"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"quiet rehearsal for real life","chinese":"現實生活的安靜排練"},{"english":"difficult situations","chinese":"困難情況"},{"english":"on the page","chinese":"在書頁中"},{"english":"completely reject the view that","chinese":"完全否定……的看法"},{"english":"a waste of time","chinese":"浪費時間"},{"english":"cultivate precise thinking","chinese":"培養精準思維"},{"english":"expressive language","chinese":"有表達力的語言"},{"english":"emotional maturity","chinese":"情緒成熟"},{"english":"removing them from","chinese":"將它們從……移除"},{"english":"curriculum","chinese":"課程"},{"english":"narrower, poorer and less human","chinese":"更狹窄、更貧乏、更少人情味"}]},"model-essay-40-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-40-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:40","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-40-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q40","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Modern technology has become embedded in professional life. I believe it has transformed work mainly by making it faster, more flexible and less tied to physical location. However, excessive reliance on digital systems can weaken human judgement and create serious disruption when those systems fail.","chinese":"現代科技已經深深融入職業生活之中。 我認為，它主要透過令工作變得更快捷、更靈活，以及較少受實際地點限制，從而改變了我們的工作方式。 然而，過度依賴數碼系統可能會削弱人的判斷力，並在這些系統失靈時造成嚴重干擾。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"One major change is that employees can now communicate, produce and manage work with far greater efficiency. Emails, cloud platforms, video meetings and automated software allow tasks that once required paper files, travel or long meetings to be completed almost instantly. For example, a marketing team can now edit the same document, speak to overseas clients and monitor campaign results without being in the same office. This does not merely save time; it changes workplace expectations. Workers are now expected to respond quickly, learn new tools and collaborate across departments and time zones. In this sense, technology has turned many jobs from slow, location-based routines into faster and more connected forms of work.","chinese":"其中一個主要變化是，員工現在能夠以高得多的效率進行溝通、生產和管理工作。 電子郵件、雲端平台、視像會議和自動化軟件，讓過去需要紙本文件、出差或長時間會議才能完成的任務，幾乎可以即時完成。 例如，一個市場推廣團隊現在可以在不身處同一間辦公室的情況下，共同編輯同一份文件、與海外客戶交談，並監察宣傳活動的成效。 這不只是節省時間；它也改變了職場期望。 如今，員工被期望能夠快速回應、學習新工具，並跨部門、跨時區合作。 從這個意義上說，科技已經把許多工作從緩慢、依賴固定地點的日常流程，轉變成更快捷、更互相連繫的工作形式。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Nevertheless, relying too heavily on technology has clear disadvantages. The most serious problem is that people may lose important practical skills when machines make too many decisions for them. If employees always depend on software to calculate, organise or communicate, they may become less confident when they need to solve problems independently. A further risk is vulnerability: when a company’s internet, database or automated system breaks down, work can grind to a halt. For instance, a hospital, bank or logistics company that cannot access its digital records may struggle to serve customers safely and efficiently. Technology is useful, but when it becomes the only road available, one broken bridge can stop the whole journey.","chinese":"然而，過度依賴科技也有明顯的缺點。 最嚴重的問題是，當機器替人作出過多決定時，人們可能會失去重要的實用技能。 如果員工總是依賴軟件去計算、組織或溝通，當他們需要獨立解決問題時，便可能變得較缺乏信心。 另一個風險是脆弱性：當一間公司的網絡、資料庫或自動化系統故障時，工作可能會陷入停頓。 例如，一間醫院、銀行或物流公司如果無法存取其數碼記錄，便可能難以安全而有效地為客戶服務。 科技是有用的，但當它變成唯一可走的道路時，一座斷橋便可能令整段旅程停下來。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, modern technology has changed work by making it quicker, more flexible and more globally connected. Even so, I believe excessive dependence on it is dangerous because it can reduce human competence and leave organisations exposed to technical failure. The best workplaces therefore use technology as a powerful tool, not as a substitute for human judgement.","chinese":"總結來說，現代科技透過令工作變得更快捷、更靈活，以及更具全球連繫性，改變了我們的工作方式。 即使如此，我認為過度依賴科技是危險的，因為它可能削弱人的能力，並令機構容易受到技術故障的影響。 因此，最理想的工作場所會把科技視為強大的工具，而不是人的判斷力的替代品。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"modern technology","chinese":"現代科技"},{"english":"become embedded in","chinese":"深入融入……"},{"english":"professional life","chinese":"職業生活"},{"english":"transformed work","chinese":"改變工作模式"},{"english":"mainly by making it","chinese":"主要透過令它……"},{"english":"more flexible","chinese":"更靈活"},{"english":"less tied to","chinese":"較少受……限制"},{"english":"physical location","chinese":"實體地點"},{"english":"excessive reliance on","chinese":"過度依賴"},{"english":"digital systems","chinese":"數碼系統"},{"english":"weaken human judgement","chinese":"削弱人的判斷力"},{"english":"create serious disruption","chinese":"造成嚴重干擾"},{"english":"when those systems fail","chinese":"當那些系統失靈時"},{"english":"one major change","chinese":"一個主要變化"},{"english":"communicate, produce and manage work","chinese":"溝通、生產和管理工作"},{"english":"far greater efficiency","chinese":"高得多的效率"},{"english":"cloud platforms","chinese":"雲端平台"},{"english":"video meetings","chinese":"視像會議"},{"english":"automated software","chinese":"自動化軟件"},{"english":"once required","chinese":"曾經需要"},{"english":"paper files","chinese":"紙本文件"},{"english":"be completed almost instantly","chinese":"幾乎即時完成"},{"english":"a marketing team","chinese":"市場推廣團隊"},{"english":"edit the same document","chinese":"編輯同一份文件"},{"english":"overseas clients","chinese":"海外客戶"},{"english":"monitor campaign results","chinese":"監察宣傳活動成效"},{"english":"without being in","chinese":"不用身處於"},{"english":"does not merely save time","chinese":"不只是節省時間"},{"english":"workplace expectations","chinese":"職場期望"},{"english":"be expected to","chinese":"被期望"},{"english":"respond quickly","chinese":"快速回應"},{"english":"learn new tools","chinese":"學習新工具"},{"english":"collaborate across","chinese":"跨……協作"},{"english":"departments and time zones","chinese":"部門和時區"},{"english":"In this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"turned many jobs from...into...","chinese":"將許多工作由……變成……"},{"english":"slow, location-based routines","chinese":"緩慢、受地點限制的常規工作"},{"english":"more connected forms of work","chinese":"更互相連繫的工作形式"},{"english":"Nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"relying too heavily on","chinese":"過度依賴"},{"english":"clear disadvantages","chinese":"明顯缺點"},{"english":"the most serious problem","chinese":"最嚴重的問題"},{"english":"practical skills","chinese":"實用技能"},{"english":"make too many decisions for","chinese":"為……作出太多決定"},{"english":"depend on software to","chinese":"依賴軟件去"},{"english":"calculate, organise or communicate","chinese":"計算、整理或溝通"},{"english":"become less confident","chinese":"變得較缺乏信心"},{"english":"solve problems independently","chinese":"獨立解決問題"},{"english":"a further risk","chinese":"另一個風險"},{"english":"vulnerability","chinese":"脆弱性；容易受影響"},{"english":"automated system breaks down","chinese":"自動化系統故障"},{"english":"grind to a halt","chinese":"逐漸停頓；陷入停擺"},{"english":"digital records","chinese":"數碼紀錄"},{"english":"struggle to serve customers","chinese":"難以服務顧客"},{"english":"safely and efficiently","chinese":"安全而高效地"},{"english":"the only road available","chinese":"唯一可用的道路"},{"english":"one broken bridge","chinese":"一條斷橋"},{"english":"stop the whole journey","chinese":"令整段旅程停下來"},{"english":"globally connected","chinese":"更具全球連繫"},{"english":"excessive dependence on","chinese":"對……過度依賴"},{"english":"reduce human competence","chinese":"降低人的能力"},{"english":"leave organisations exposed to","chinese":"使機構容易受到……影響"},{"english":"technical failure","chinese":"技術故障"},{"english":"the best workplaces","chinese":"最好的工作場所"},{"english":"a powerful tool","chinese":"強大的工具"},{"english":"a substitute for","chinese":"……的替代品"},{"english":"human judgement","chinese":"人的判斷力"}]},"model-essay-40-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-40-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:40","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-40-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q40","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Tourism has become one of the most visible forces shaping local communities, especially in places with distinctive traditions, architecture, and ways of life. Some argue that certain areas should be closed to tourists in order to preserve their cultural identity. However, I believe that banning tourism is not a useful solution, because culture is better protected through careful management than complete isolation.","chinese":"旅遊已成為塑造本地社區最明顯的力量之一，尤其是在擁有獨特傳統、建築和生活方式的地方。 有些人認為，某些地區應該禁止遊客進入，以保護其文化身份。 然而，我認為禁止旅遊並不是一個有用的解決方法，因為文化透過細心管理比透過完全隔離更能得到保護。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Those who support bans usually argue that local culture can be damaged when too many outsiders enter a place. Tourists may treat sacred sites, traditional festivals, or historic neighbourhoods as entertainment rather than living parts of a community. As a result, residents may feel that their customs are being turned into products, and businesses may start changing local food, music, or crafts simply to satisfy visitors. For example, a quiet fishing village could gradually become filled with souvenir shops and staged performances, making its original lifestyle harder to recognise. From this perspective, limiting or even banning tourism seems like a direct way to stop culture from being diluted.","chinese":"支持禁令的人通常認為，當太多外來者進入一個地方時，本地文化可能會受到破壞。 遊客可能會把神聖場所、傳統節日或歷史街區當作娛樂，而不是視為社區中仍然存在並運作的生活部分。 結果，居民可能會覺得自己的習俗正在被變成商品，而商家也可能開始改變本地食物、音樂或手工藝，只是為了迎合遊客。 例如，一條寧靜的漁村可能會逐漸充滿紀念品商店和刻意安排的表演，使它原本的生活方式變得更難辨認。 從這個角度來看，限制甚至禁止旅遊似乎是一種直接阻止文化被稀釋的方法。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Nevertheless, I strongly believe that banning tourism would bring few real benefits. Culture has never been frozen in time; it naturally changes as people move, communicate, trade, and adapt. If tourism is banned completely, local people may lose income, young residents may leave for better opportunities, and the community may become weaker rather than more authentic. More importantly, a ban does not teach visitors to behave respectfully. A better approach would be to control visitor numbers, protect sensitive sites, involve local residents in tourism planning, and ensure that profits support cultural preservation. That way, tourism becomes a tool for protecting heritage rather than a force that washes it away.","chinese":"然而，我強烈認為禁止旅遊幾乎不會帶來真正的好處。 文化從來都不是凝固在時間之中的；隨著人們遷移、溝通、貿易和適應，它自然會發生變化。 如果旅遊被完全禁止，本地人可能會失去收入，年輕居民可能會為了更好的機會而離開，而社區也可能變得更弱，而不是更真實。 更重要的是，禁令並不會教導遊客如何以尊重的方式行事。 更好的做法是控制遊客數量、保護敏感地點、讓本地居民參與旅遊規劃，並確保收益能夠支持文化保育。 這樣一來，旅遊便會成為保護文化遺產的工具，而不是沖走它的力量。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, while banning tourism may appear to protect local culture, it is too extreme and often ineffective. In my view, well-managed tourism is the wiser solution, as it allows culture to survive, adapt, and remain meaningful to both residents and visitors.","chinese":"總結來說，雖然禁止旅遊看似可以保護本地文化，但這種做法過於極端，而且往往無效 在我看來，管理得宜的旅遊才是更明智的解決方法，因為它能讓文化得以延續、適應變化，並且對居民和遊客都保持意義。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"some researchers believe that","chinese":"一些研究人員認為……"},{"english":"in the future","chinese":"在未來"},{"english":"humanity","chinese":"人類"},{"english":"voluntarily settle on","chinese":"自願選定"},{"english":"one shared global language","chinese":"一種共同全球語言"},{"english":"a negative development","chinese":"負面發展"},{"english":"not merely a tool for communication","chinese":"不只是溝通工具"},{"english":"carries culture, identity and social memory","chinese":"承載文化、身份和社會記憶"},{"english":"cultural loss","chinese":"文化流失"},{"english":"a particular way of seeing the world","chinese":"一種看世界的特定方式"},{"english":"family relationships","chinese":"家庭關係"},{"english":"local traditions","chinese":"本地傳統"},{"english":"moral values","chinese":"道德價值觀"},{"english":"abandon their mother tongues","chinese":"放棄母語"},{"english":"mother tongues","chinese":"母語"},{"english":"in favour of","chinese":"轉而支持；取而用"},{"english":"a single global language","chinese":"單一全球語言"},{"english":"linguistic container","chinese":"語言容器"},{"english":"disappear in translation","chinese":"在翻譯中消失"},{"english":"traditional songs","chinese":"傳統歌曲"},{"english":"proverbs and stories","chinese":"諺語和故事"},{"english":"depend on","chinese":"取決於；依賴"},{"english":"wordplay","chinese":"文字遊戲；雙關語"},{"english":"historical references","chinese":"歷史典故"},{"english":"be fully recreated","chinese":"被完全重現"},{"english":"in another language","chinese":"用另一種語言"},{"english":"once a language stops being used","chinese":"一旦一種語言停止被使用"},{"english":"public life","chinese":"公共生活"},{"english":"with the doors locked","chinese":"大門上鎖的"},{"english":"may still exist","chinese":"可能仍然存在"},{"english":"ordinary people","chinese":"普通人"},{"english":"live inside them","chinese":"活在其中"},{"english":"another serious concern","chinese":"另一個嚴重憂慮"},{"english":"deepen inequality","chinese":"加深不平等"},{"english":"rather than remove it","chinese":"而不是消除它"},{"english":"the global standard","chinese":"全球標準"},{"english":"almost certainly","chinese":"幾乎肯定"},{"english":"belong to","chinese":"屬於"},{"english":"be controlled by","chinese":"被……控制"},{"english":"existing political, economic or technological power","chinese":"現有政治、經濟或科技力量"},{"english":"enjoy an immediate advantage","chinese":"享有即時優勢"},{"english":"international institutions","chinese":"國際機構"},{"english":"spend years catching up","chinese":"花多年時間追趕"},{"english":"turn communication into","chinese":"將溝通變成……"},{"english":"gatekeeping system","chinese":"把關制度；門檻制度"},{"english":"depend less on","chinese":"較少取決於……"},{"english":"early access to","chinese":"早期接觸……的機會"},{"english":"dominant language","chinese":"主導語言"},{"english":"linguistic uniformity","chinese":"語言一致化"},{"english":"on the surface","chinese":"表面上"},{"english":"quietly reward","chinese":"悄悄獎勵"},{"english":"the already privileged","chinese":"已經享有特權的人"},{"english":"would not become richer","chinese":"不會變得更豐富"},{"english":"flatter, poorer and less human","chinese":"更平面、更貧乏、更少人情味"},{"english":"for this reason","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"predicted change","chinese":"預測中的轉變"}]},"model-essay-40-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-40-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:40","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-40-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q40","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Education is one of the few public goods that can change a person’s life before poverty becomes permanent. I completely agree that schooling and university education should be free for everyone, regardless of family income, because education is both a basic social right and a long-term investment in society.","chinese":"教育是少數能在貧窮變成永久困境之前，改變一個人一生的公共資源之一。 我完全同意學校教育和大學教育都應該對每個人免費，無論其家庭收入如何，因為教育既是一項基本社會權利，也是社會的長期投資。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that fees turn education into a privilege rather than a genuine opportunity. Children do not choose the household into which they are born, so it is deeply unfair if their future is decided by their parents’ bank balance. When families have to pay for school places, books, examinations or tuition, low-income parents may be forced to choose between education and daily necessities. As a result, bright students can be pushed out of the classroom before their abilities have had a chance to grow. Free education changes this picture: it gives every child a seat at the table and allows talent, effort and character to matter more than wealth. For a poor but capable student, school can become a ladder, not a locked gate.","chinese":"第一個原因是，學費會把教育變成一種特權，而不是一個真正的機會。 孩子並不能選擇自己出生於哪一個家庭，因此如果他們的未來由父母的銀行存款決定，這是極不公平的。 當家庭必須支付學位、書本、考試或學費時，低收入父母可能會被迫在教育和日常生活必需品之間作出選擇。 結果是，聰明的學生可能在自己的能力有機會成長之前，便被迫離開課室。 免費教育能改變這個局面：它讓每個孩子都有參與的機會，並使天分、努力和品格比財富更加重要。 對於一個貧窮但有能力的學生而言，學校可以成為一把梯子，而不是一道上鎖的大門。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"This principle should also apply to tertiary education, because modern societies need highly trained citizens. Doctors, teachers, engineers and researchers are not produced by primary education alone; they require years of advanced study. If university fees are extremely high, many young people either abandon their ambitions or begin adult life under a mountain of debt. That is not only harmful to individuals, but also wasteful for society, since national talent is left unused. Some may argue that free higher education would place pressure on public budgets. However, governments already fund roads, hospitals and police services because they benefit the whole community. Education deserves the same treatment: it creates skilled workers, informed voters and more stable communities.","chinese":"這個原則也應該適用於高等教育，因為現代社會需要受過高度訓練的公民。 醫生、教師、工程師和研究人員並不是單靠小學教育就能培養出來的；他們需要多年高階學習。 如果大學學費極高，許多年輕人不是放棄自己的抱負，就是在沉重債務下開始成年生活 這不但對個人有害，也會浪費社會資源，因為國家的才華被閒置不用。 有些人可能會認為，免費高等教育會對公共財政造成壓力。 然而，政府本來就會資助道路、醫院和警察服務，因為它們有利於整個社區。 教育也值得同樣的對待：它能培養技術熟練的勞動者、有判斷力的選民，以及更穩定的社區。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully agree that education at every level should be free. A fair society should not allow money to decide who learns, who progresses, and who is left behind.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意每一個階段的教育都應該免費。 一個公平的社會不應該讓金錢決定誰能學習、誰能進步，以及誰會被拋在後面。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"one of the few public goods","chinese":"少數公共利益之一"},{"english":"public goods","chinese":"公共利益；公共產品"},{"english":"change a person's life","chinese":"改變一個人的人生"},{"english":"before poverty becomes permanent","chinese":"在貧窮變成永久之前"},{"english":"schooling and university education","chinese":"學校教育和大學教育"},{"english":"free for everyone","chinese":"對所有人免費"},{"english":"regardless of family income","chinese":"不論家庭收入"},{"english":"basic social right","chinese":"基本社會權利"},{"english":"long-term investment in society","chinese":"對社會的長期投資"},{"english":"turn education into","chinese":"將教育變成……"},{"english":"a privilege rather than","chinese":"特權而不是……"},{"english":"genuine opportunity","chinese":"真正機會"},{"english":"do not choose","chinese":"不能選擇"},{"english":"the household into which they are born","chinese":"他們出生的家庭"},{"english":"deeply unfair","chinese":"極不公平"},{"english":"be decided by","chinese":"由……決定"},{"english":"parents' bank balance","chinese":"父母的銀行存款"},{"english":"school places","chinese":"學位"},{"english":"examinations or tuition","chinese":"考試或學費"},{"english":"low-income parents","chinese":"低收入父母"},{"english":"be forced to choose between","chinese":"被迫在……之間作選擇"},{"english":"daily necessities","chinese":"生活必需品"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"bright students","chinese":"聰明學生"},{"english":"be pushed out of","chinese":"被迫離開……"},{"english":"before their abilities have had a chance to grow","chinese":"在能力有機會發展之前"},{"english":"changes this picture","chinese":"改變這種情況"},{"english":"gives every child a seat at the table","chinese":"讓每個孩子都有參與機會"},{"english":"talent, effort and character","chinese":"才能、努力和品格"},{"english":"matter more than wealth","chinese":"比財富更重要"},{"english":"poor but capable student","chinese":"貧窮但有能力的學生"},{"english":"become a ladder","chinese":"成為階梯"},{"english":"locked gate","chinese":"上鎖的大門"},{"english":"this principle should also apply to","chinese":"這個原則也應適用於……"},{"english":"tertiary education","chinese":"高等教育"},{"english":"modern societies","chinese":"現代社會"},{"english":"highly trained citizens","chinese":"受過高度訓練的公民"},{"english":"are not produced by","chinese":"並不是由……培養出來"},{"english":"primary education alone","chinese":"單靠小學教育"},{"english":"years of advanced study","chinese":"多年的高階學習"},{"english":"university fees","chinese":"大學學費"},{"english":"extremely high","chinese":"極高"},{"english":"abandon their ambitions","chinese":"放棄抱負"},{"english":"begin adult life","chinese":"開始成年生活"},{"english":"under a mountain of debt","chinese":"背負沉重債務"},{"english":"harmful to individuals","chinese":"對個人有害"},{"english":"wasteful for society","chinese":"對社會來說浪費"},{"english":"national talent","chinese":"國家人才"},{"english":"be left unused","chinese":"被閒置；未被善用"},{"english":"place pressure on","chinese":"對……造成壓力"},{"english":"public budgets","chinese":"公共預算"},{"english":"roads, hospitals and police services","chinese":"道路、醫院和警察服務"},{"english":"benefit the whole community","chinese":"令整個社區受惠"},{"english":"deserves the same treatment","chinese":"值得得到同樣待遇"},{"english":"skilled workers","chinese":"熟練工人"},{"english":"informed voters","chinese":"有知識的選民"},{"english":"stable communities","chinese":"穩定社區"},{"english":"at every level","chinese":"在每個階段"},{"english":"fair society","chinese":"公平社會"},{"english":"allow money to decide","chinese":"讓金錢決定"},{"english":"who is left behind","chinese":"誰被拋在後面"}]},"model-essay-41-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-41-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:41","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-41-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q41","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Over the last half-century, technology has changed childhood from a mostly local experience into one shaped by screens, algorithms and instant communication. While this gives children convenience and access to information, it also creates problems for both society and family life.","chinese":"在過去半個世紀裡，科技已經把童年從一種主要以本地生活為中心的經驗，轉變成一種由螢幕、演算法和即時通訊所塑造的經驗。 雖然這給孩子帶來了便利和獲取資訊的途徑，但它也為社會和家庭生活帶來了問題。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"At the social level, the main problem is that children may develop weaker interpersonal and emotional skills. In the past, many children learned patience, cooperation and compromise through outdoor games and neighbourhood activities. By contrast, a child who spends most free time on a phone may avoid the difficulties of real interaction, such as reading facial expressions or resolving disagreements. Over time, this can produce young people who are less confident in conversation and less comfortable with conflict. Technology also exposes children to adult pressures too early. Social media and online entertainment often present edited bodies, luxurious lifestyles and popularity contests as if they were normal life. A child who constantly compares himself with influencers may begin to measure his own worth through appearance, attention and likes. This can feed anxiety and low self-esteem, creating a generation that is connected to thousands online but still feels insecure and alone.","chinese":"在社會層面上，主要問題是孩子可能會形成較弱的人際交往能力和情緒能力。 在過去，許多孩子透過戶外遊戲和社區活動學會耐性、合作和妥協。 相比之下，一個把大部分空閒時間都花在手機上的孩子，可能會避開真實互動中的困難，例如理解面部表情或解決分歧。 長遠而言，這可能會造成一批在交談中較缺乏自信、也較不適應衝突的年輕人。 科技也使孩子過早接觸成人世界的壓力。 社交媒體和網上娛樂經常把修飾過的身體、奢華的生活方式和人氣競爭呈現得彷彿它們就是正常生活。 一個不斷把自己與網紅比較的孩子，可能會開始透過外貌、關注度和讚好數來衡量自己的價值。 這可能會助長焦慮和低自尊，形成一代在線上與成千上萬的人連繫，卻仍然感到不安和孤單的人。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Within the family, the clearest problem is the loss of meaningful communication. Even when parents and children are sitting in the same room, separate screens can pull them into separate worlds. Meals become quieter, conversations become shorter and parents may fail to notice changes in their children’s mood. In addition, technology makes parental authority more difficult because parents must now control screen time, online friendships and unsuitable content. These rules can easily lead to arguments and mistrust, especially when children feel that parents are invading their private digital space. As a result, the home may become less like a place of guidance and more like a battlefield of control.","chinese":"在家庭內部，最明顯的問題是有意義溝通的流失。 即使父母和孩子坐在同一個房間裡，不同的螢幕也可以把他們拉進不同的世界。 用餐變得更安靜，對話變得更短，而父母也可能無法察覺孩子情緒上的變化。 此外，科技使父母權威更難維持，因為父母現在必須管理螢幕時間、網上朋友關係和不適合的內容。 這些規則很容易導致爭吵和不信任，尤其是當孩子覺得父母正在侵犯他們的私人數位空間時。 結果，家庭可能變得不太像一個提供引導的地方，而更像一個控制權爭奪的戰場。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, modern technology can weaken society by damaging children’s social skills and emotional health. It can also harm family life by reducing real conversation and making parental guidance harder.","chinese":"總結來說，現代科技可能會透過損害孩子的社交能力和情緒健康來削弱社會。 它也可能透過減少真實對話，並使父母引導變得更困難，從而損害家庭生活。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"over the last half-century","chinese":"在過去半個世紀"},{"english":"a mostly local experience","chinese":"主要屬於本地生活圈的經驗"},{"english":"shaped by","chinese":"受……塑造"},{"english":"screens, algorithms and instant communication","chinese":"屏幕、演算法和即時通訊"},{"english":"access to information","chinese":"獲取資料"},{"english":"creates problems for","chinese":"為……造成問題"},{"english":"society and family life","chinese":"社會和家庭生活"},{"english":"at the social level","chinese":"在社會層面上"},{"english":"the main problem is that","chinese":"主要問題是"},{"english":"develop weaker interpersonal skills","chinese":"培養出較弱的人際交往能力"},{"english":"emotional skills","chinese":"情緒能力"},{"english":"in the past","chinese":"過去"},{"english":"cooperation and compromise","chinese":"合作和妥協"},{"english":"outdoor games","chinese":"戶外遊戲"},{"english":"neighbourhood activities","chinese":"社區活動"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"spends most free time on","chinese":"把大部分空閒時間花在……上"},{"english":"avoid the difficulties of","chinese":"避開……的困難"},{"english":"real interaction","chinese":"真實互動"},{"english":"reading facial expressions","chinese":"解讀面部表情"},{"english":"resolving disagreements","chinese":"解決分歧"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨時間"},{"english":"less confident in conversation","chinese":"在交談中較缺乏信心"},{"english":"less comfortable with conflict","chinese":"對衝突較不自在"},{"english":"exposes children to","chinese":"使孩子接觸到"},{"english":"adult pressures","chinese":"成人壓力"},{"english":"too early","chinese":"太早"},{"english":"social media","chinese":"社交媒體"},{"english":"online entertainment","chinese":"網上娛樂"},{"english":"edited bodies","chinese":"經修飾的身體形象"},{"english":"luxurious lifestyles","chinese":"奢華生活方式"},{"english":"popularity contests","chinese":"人氣競賽"},{"english":"as if they were normal life","chinese":"彷彿它們是正常生活"},{"english":"constantly compares himself with","chinese":"不斷把自己與……比較"},{"english":"influencers","chinese":"網紅"},{"english":"measure his own worth through","chinese":"透過……衡量自己的價值"},{"english":"appearance, attention and likes","chinese":"外貌、關注和讚好"},{"english":"feed anxiety","chinese":"加劇焦慮"},{"english":"low self-esteem","chinese":"低自尊"},{"english":"connected to thousands online","chinese":"在網上與成千上萬人連繫"},{"english":"feels insecure and alone","chinese":"感到不安和孤單"},{"english":"within the family","chinese":"在家庭內"},{"english":"the clearest problem","chinese":"最明顯的問題"},{"english":"the loss of meaningful communication","chinese":"有意義溝通的流失"},{"english":"sitting in the same room","chinese":"坐在同一個房間"},{"english":"separate screens","chinese":"各自的屏幕"},{"english":"pull them into separate worlds","chinese":"把他們拉進不同世界"},{"english":"meals become quieter","chinese":"用餐變得更安靜"},{"english":"conversations become shorter","chinese":"對話變得更短"},{"english":"fail to notice changes in","chinese":"未能察覺……的變化"},{"english":"children's mood","chinese":"孩子的情緒"},{"english":"in addition","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"parental authority","chinese":"父母權威"},{"english":"control screen time","chinese":"控制使用屏幕的時間"},{"english":"online friendships","chinese":"網上友誼"},{"english":"unsuitable content","chinese":"不合適內容"},{"english":"lead to arguments and mistrust","chinese":"導致爭執和不信任"},{"english":"invading their private digital space","chinese":"侵犯他們的私人數碼空間"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"結果"},{"english":"a place of guidance","chinese":"提供引導的地方"},{"english":"a battlefield of control","chinese":"控制權的戰場"},{"english":"weaken society","chinese":"削弱社會"},{"english":"damaging children's social skills","chinese":"損害孩子的社交能力"},{"english":"emotional health","chinese":"情緒健康"},{"english":"harm family life","chinese":"損害家庭生活"},{"english":"reducing real conversation","chinese":"減少真實對話"},{"english":"making parental guidance harder","chinese":"令父母引導更困難"}]},"model-essay-41-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-41-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:41","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-41-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q41","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Air pollution has become one of the most pressing environmental problems in many urban areas, and road transport is often seen as a major cause. While an international car-free day can raise public awareness and temporarily improve air quality, I believe that stricter, permanent transport policies are far more effective.","chinese":"空氣污染已成為許多城市地區最迫切的環境問題之一，而道路交通往往被視為主要原因 雖然國際無車日可以提高公眾意識，並暫時改善空氣質素， 我認為更嚴格、永久性的交通政策有效得多。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"On the one hand, supporters of a global car-free day argue that it can produce an immediate, visible reduction in pollution. If private vehicles are kept off the road for even a single day, fewer exhaust fumes are released, and city centres may become cleaner, quieter and more pleasant. More importantly, such an event can act as a public reminder that everyday travel choices have environmental consequences. For example, when commuters are encouraged to walk, cycle or use buses for a day, some may realise that driving is not always necessary. In this sense, a car-free day is not merely a symbolic gesture; it can plant the seed of cleaner habits.","chinese":"一方面，全球無車日的支持者認為，它能夠立即帶來可見的污染減少。 如果私人車輛即使只是一天不上路，排放的廢氣也會減少，而市中心可能會變得更清潔、更安靜，也更令人舒適。 更重要的是，這類活動可以提醒公眾，日常出行選擇會帶來環境後果。 例如，當通勤者被鼓勵在一天之內步行、騎單車或乘搭巴士時，有些人可能會意識到開車並非總是必要的。 從這個意義上說，無車日不僅僅是一種象徵性姿態；它可以種下更清潔生活習慣的種子"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, I believe this approach is too limited to deal with a problem that occurs every day. Air pollution is not caused by one day of traffic but by millions of repeated journeys, so the solution must also be continuous. Governments should improve public transport, expand cycling lanes, and make high-emission vehicles more expensive to use. These measures directly change people’s long-term behaviour because they make cleaner options easier and dirtier choices less attractive. For instance, if buses and trains are affordable, reliable and widely available, many workers will naturally leave their cars at home, not once a year but throughout the week. This is where real environmental progress is made.","chinese":"然而，我認為這種方法太有限，無法應對一個每天都在發生的問題。 空氣污染並不是由一天的交通造成的，而是由數以百萬計反覆發生的旅程造成的，因此解決方法也必須是持續性的。 政府應該改善公共交通、擴展單車徑，並提高高排放車輛的使用成本。 這些措施會直接改變人們的長期行為，因為它們令更清潔的選擇變得更容易，也令污染較大的選擇變得較不吸引。 例如，如果巴士和火車價格合理、可靠，而且覆蓋廣泛，許多上班族自然會把車留在家中，而不是一年一次，而是整個星期都這樣做。 這才是真正環境進步發生的地方。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, an international car-free day may be useful as a wake-up call, since it shows people what a cleaner city could feel like. Nevertheless, I strongly believe that lasting reductions in air pollution depend on permanent policies that reshape daily transport habits.","chinese":"總結來說，國際無車日或許可以作為一個警醒，因為它讓人們看見一個更清潔的城市可以是甚麼感覺。 【原始 PDF 未提供中文翻譯】"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"air pollution","chinese":"空氣污染"},{"english":"one of the most pressing environmental problems","chinese":"最迫切的環境問題之一"},{"english":"urban areas","chinese":"市區"},{"english":"road transport","chinese":"道路交通"},{"english":"be seen as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"a major cause","chinese":"主要原因"},{"english":"an international car-free day","chinese":"國際無車日"},{"english":"raise public awareness","chinese":"提高公眾意識"},{"english":"temporarily improve air quality","chinese":"暫時改善空氣質素"},{"english":"stricter, permanent transport policies","chinese":"更嚴格而永久的交通政策"},{"english":"far more effective","chinese":"有效得多"},{"english":"on the one hand","chinese":"一方面"},{"english":"supporters of","chinese":"……的支持者"},{"english":"a global car-free day","chinese":"全球無車日"},{"english":"produce an immediate, visible reduction in","chinese":"立即而明顯地減少"},{"english":"be kept off the road","chinese":"不准上路"},{"english":"for even a single day","chinese":"即使只是一日"},{"english":"exhaust fumes","chinese":"廢氣"},{"english":"be released","chinese":"被排放"},{"english":"city centres","chinese":"市中心"},{"english":"cleaner, quieter and more pleasant","chinese":"更清潔、更寧靜和更舒適"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"such an event","chinese":"這類活動"},{"english":"act as a public reminder","chinese":"發揮公共提醒的作用"},{"english":"everyday travel choices","chinese":"日常出行選擇"},{"english":"have environmental consequences","chinese":"帶來環境後果"},{"english":"commuters","chinese":"通勤人士"},{"english":"be encouraged to","chinese":"被鼓勵去"},{"english":"use buses","chinese":"乘搭巴士"},{"english":"realise that","chinese":"意識到"},{"english":"not always necessary","chinese":"並非總是必要"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"not merely a symbolic gesture","chinese":"不只是象徵性姿態"},{"english":"plant the seed of","chinese":"播下……的種子"},{"english":"cleaner habits","chinese":"更環保的習慣"},{"english":"this approach","chinese":"這種做法"},{"english":"too limited to deal with","chinese":"太有限，無法處理"},{"english":"occur every day","chinese":"每日都發生"},{"english":"be caused by","chinese":"由……造成"},{"english":"one day of traffic","chinese":"一日的交通"},{"english":"millions of repeated journeys","chinese":"數以百萬計重複的旅程"},{"english":"the solution must be continuous","chinese":"解決方法必須是持續的"},{"english":"improve public transport","chinese":"改善公共交通"},{"english":"expand cycling lanes","chinese":"擴展單車徑"},{"english":"high-emission vehicles","chinese":"高排放車輛"},{"english":"more expensive to use","chinese":"使用成本更高"},{"english":"directly change people's long-term behaviour","chinese":"直接改變人們的長期行為"},{"english":"long-term behaviour","chinese":"長期行為"},{"english":"cleaner options","chinese":"較環保的選擇"},{"english":"dirtier choices","chinese":"較污染的選擇"},{"english":"less attractive","chinese":"較不吸引"},{"english":"affordable, reliable and widely available","chinese":"負擔得起、可靠和覆蓋廣泛"},{"english":"leave their cars at home","chinese":"不駕車出門"},{"english":"not once a year but throughout the week","chinese":"不是一年一次，而是整個星期"},{"english":"throughout the week","chinese":"整個星期"},{"english":"real environmental progress","chinese":"真正的環境進步"},{"english":"be useful as a wake-up call","chinese":"作為警醒訊號是有用的"},{"english":"a wake-up call","chinese":"警醒訊號"},{"english":"what a cleaner city could feel like","chinese":"一個更清潔城市的感覺"},{"english":"nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"lasting reductions in","chinese":"……的持久減少"},{"english":"depend on permanent policies","chinese":"取決於永久政策"},{"english":"reshape daily transport habits","chinese":"重塑日常交通習慣"}]},"model-essay-41-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-41-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:41","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-41-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q41","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Schools are often under pressure to raise the performance of pupils who fall behind academically. Some people argue that the most effective solution is to make after-school activities compulsory, on the grounds that this will increase pupils’ involvement in school and improve their grades. I completely disagree with this view because compulsory activities do not address the real causes of underachievement and may even weaken students’ motivation.","chinese":"學校經常面對壓力，需要提升學業落後學生的表現。 有些人認為，最有效的解決方法是把課後活動變成強制性，理由是這樣能增加學生對學校的參與感，並改善他們的成績。 我完全不同意這種看法，因為強制性活動並沒有處理學業表現不佳的真正原因，甚至可能削弱學生的學習動機。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main problem with this proposal is that it mistakes attendance for learning. Underachieving pupils are not necessarily failing because they spend too little time on school premises; they may be struggling because they have weak foundations, poor study habits, low confidence, or difficulties at home. For example, a student who cannot understand basic algebra will not suddenly improve simply because he is required to stay after school for a general activity. What he needs is targeted academic support, patient explanation, and regular feedback. If schools force such pupils to attend extra sessions that do not directly solve their learning gaps, the policy may become a burden rather than a bridge to progress.","chinese":"這項建議的主要問題在於，它把出席誤以為是學習。 學業表現不佳的學生未必是因為他們在學校逗留的時間太少而失敗；他們可能是因為基礎薄弱、學習習慣差、信心不足，或家中存在困難而掙扎。 例如，一個無法理解基礎代數的學生，不會僅僅因為被要求放學後留下來參加一般活動，就突然有所進步。 他真正需要的是有針對性的學業支援、耐心的講解，以及定期的回饋。 如果學校強迫這些學生參加一些不能直接解決學習差距的額外課程，這項政策便可能成為負擔，而不是通往進步的橋樑。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Compulsory after-school activities can also damage the very engagement they are supposed to create. Many weaker pupils already associate school with stress, failure, or embarrassment. Extending the school day by force may make them feel punished for underperforming, which can lead to resentment and even poorer attitudes towards learning. A better approach would be to offer personalised tutoring, mentoring, smaller study groups, and meaningful choices in extracurricular programmes. When pupils feel that support is designed for them rather than imposed on them, they are more likely to take ownership of their progress.","chinese":"強制性課後活動也可能破壞它們原本想要建立的參與感。 許多較弱的學生本來已經把學校和壓力、失敗或尷尬聯繫在一起。 強行延長上學時間可能會令他們覺得自己因表現欠佳而受到懲罰，這可能導致怨氣，甚至令他們對學習產生更差的態度。 更好的做法是提供個人化補習、導師輔導、較小型的學習小組，以及在課外活動中提供有意義的選擇。 當學生感到支援是為他們而設，而不是強加在他們身上時，他們更有可能主動為自己的進步負責。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I strongly disagree that compulsory after-school activities are the best way to help underachieving pupils. Real improvement comes from diagnosing students’ specific problems and giving them focused, respectful support, not from forcing them to spend more time at school.","chinese":"總結來說，我強烈不同意強制性課後活動是幫助學業表現不佳學生的最佳方法。 真正的進步來自診斷學生的具體問題，並給予他們有重點且尊重他們的支援，而不是強迫他們花更多時間留在學校。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"be under pressure to","chinese":"承受壓力去……"},{"english":"raise the performance of","chinese":"提高……的表現"},{"english":"fall behind academically","chinese":"學業上落後"},{"english":"the most effective solution","chinese":"最有效的解決方法"},{"english":"after-school activities","chinese":"課後活動"},{"english":"compulsory","chinese":"強制性的；必須參加的"},{"english":"on the grounds that","chinese":"基於……理由"},{"english":"increase pupils' involvement in","chinese":"增加學生對……的參與"},{"english":"improve their grades","chinese":"提高他們的成績"},{"english":"completely disagree with","chinese":"完全不同意……"},{"english":"address the real causes of","chinese":"處理……的真正成因"},{"english":"underachievement","chinese":"學業表現不理想"},{"english":"weaken students' motivation","chinese":"削弱學生的動力"},{"english":"the main problem with","chinese":"……的主要問題"},{"english":"this proposal","chinese":"這項建議"},{"english":"mistakes attendance for learning","chinese":"將出席誤當作學習"},{"english":"underachieving pupils","chinese":"成績落後的學生"},{"english":"are not necessarily failing because","chinese":"不一定是因為……而失敗"},{"english":"school premises","chinese":"校園範圍"},{"english":"be struggling because","chinese":"因為……而感到困難"},{"english":"weak foundations","chinese":"基礎薄弱"},{"english":"poor study habits","chinese":"不良學習習慣"},{"english":"low confidence","chinese":"信心不足"},{"english":"difficulties at home","chinese":"家庭困難"},{"english":"basic algebra","chinese":"基礎代數"},{"english":"suddenly improve","chinese":"突然進步"},{"english":"be required to","chinese":"被要求去……"},{"english":"general activity","chinese":"一般活動"},{"english":"targeted academic support","chinese":"有針對性的學業支援"},{"english":"patient explanation","chinese":"耐心講解"},{"english":"regular feedback","chinese":"定期回饋"},{"english":"force such pupils to","chinese":"強迫這些學生去……"},{"english":"extra sessions","chinese":"額外課節"},{"english":"directly solve","chinese":"直接解決"},{"english":"learning gaps","chinese":"學習缺口"},{"english":"a burden rather than a bridge to progress","chinese":"成為負擔，而不是通往進步的橋樑"},{"english":"damage the very engagement","chinese":"損害正正想建立的投入感"},{"english":"be supposed to","chinese":"本應該"},{"english":"associate school with","chinese":"將學校與……聯繫起來"},{"english":"stress, failure, or embarrassment","chinese":"壓力、失敗或尷尬"},{"english":"extending the school day","chinese":"延長上課日"},{"english":"by force","chinese":"強行地"},{"english":"feel punished for","chinese":"因……而感到受罰"},{"english":"underperforming","chinese":"表現未如理想"},{"english":"lead to resentment","chinese":"導致怨氣"},{"english":"poorer attitudes towards learning","chinese":"對學習更差的態度"},{"english":"a better approach","chinese":"更好的方法"},{"english":"personalised tutoring","chinese":"個人化補習"},{"english":"mentoring","chinese":"導師指導"},{"english":"smaller study groups","chinese":"較小型學習小組"},{"english":"meaningful choices","chinese":"有意義的選擇"},{"english":"extracurricular programmes","chinese":"課外活動計劃"},{"english":"be designed for","chinese":"為……而設計"},{"english":"imposed on","chinese":"強加於……"},{"english":"be more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"take ownership of","chinese":"主動掌握；承擔"},{"english":"their progress","chinese":"他們的進步"},{"english":"the best way to","chinese":"……的最佳方法"},{"english":"real improvement","chinese":"真正進步"},{"english":"diagnosing students' specific problems","chinese":"找出學生的具體問題"},{"english":"focused, respectful support","chinese":"有針對性而尊重學生的支援"},{"english":"forcing them to spend more time at school","chinese":"強迫他們花更多時間留在學校"}]},"model-essay-42-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-42-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:42","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-42-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q42","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Tourism has become one of the most visible parts of the modern global economy, with millions of people travelling for leisure, work and cultural experience. In my view, its greatest benefits are that it broadens individuals’ understanding of the world and strengthens society by creating jobs, funding public services and protecting local culture.","chinese":"旅遊業已成為現代全球經濟中最顯眼的部分之一，數以百萬計的人為了休閒、工作和文化體驗而旅行。 在我看來，旅遊業最大的好處是它能拓寬個人對世界的理解，並透過創造就業、資助公共服務和保護本地文化來強化社會。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"On an individual level, tourism allows people to step outside the narrow routine of daily life and see how others live. When travellers encounter different languages, customs and ways of thinking, they often become more open-minded and less quick to judge unfamiliar lifestyles. A student who visits Kyoto, for example, may learn more from observing local manners, temples and food traditions than from reading a chapter in a textbook. This kind of first-hand experience is powerful because it turns culture from an abstract idea into something people can see, hear and remember. Tourism can therefore make individuals more curious, adaptable and culturally sensitive.","chinese":"在個人層面上，旅遊讓人們走出日常生活中狹窄的固定模式，並看見其他人如何生活。 當旅客接觸到不同的語言、習俗和思維方式時，他們往往會變得更加開明，也較不會急於批判陌生的生活方式。 例如，一名到訪京都的學生，可能會透過觀察當地禮儀、寺廟和飲食傳統，學到比閱讀教科書一章更多的東西。 這種第一手經驗很有力量，因為它把文化從一個抽象概念，轉化成人們能夠看見、聽見並記住的東西。 因此，旅遊能使個人變得更有好奇心、更能適應不同環境，也更具文化敏感度。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Tourism also brings clear social benefits, especially in countries whose towns and cities rely on visitors. Hotels, restaurants, transport companies, museums and small shops all need workers, so tourism can provide income for families and reduce unemployment. The money spent by tourists can also support wider public life: governments may collect more tax revenue, improve transport links and maintain historic sites that might otherwise be neglected. For instance, when an old district becomes popular with visitors, local authorities have a stronger reason to restore buildings, train guides and keep the area clean. In this way, tourism does not merely bring money into a country; it can also give communities a practical reason to preserve their identity.","chinese":"旅遊業也帶來明顯的社會好處，尤其是在那些城鎮和城市依賴旅客的國家。 酒店、餐廳、交通公司、博物館和小商店都需要員工，因此旅遊業能為家庭提供收入，並減少失業。 旅客所花費的金錢也能支持更廣泛的公共生活：政府可以徵收更多稅收、改善交通連接，並維護那些否則可能被忽視的歷史遺址。 例如，當一個舊區變得受旅客歡迎時，地方政府便有更強的理由去修復建築、培訓導遊，並保持該區清潔。 透過這種方式，旅遊業不只是為一個國家帶來金錢；它也能給予社區一個實際理由去保留自身身份。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, tourism benefits individuals by widening their horizons and benefits society by creating employment, improving local facilities and encouraging cultural preservation. Managed responsibly, it can be both an economic engine and a bridge between cultures.","chinese":"總結來說，旅遊業透過拓寬個人視野來使個人受益，也透過創造就業、改善本地設施和鼓勵文化保育來使社會受益。 如果管理得當，旅遊業既可以成為經濟引擎，也可以成為文化之間的橋樑。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"one of the most visible parts of","chinese":"……最明顯的部分之一"},{"english":"the modern global economy","chinese":"現代環球經濟"},{"english":"travel for leisure","chinese":"為消閒而旅行"},{"english":"cultural experience","chinese":"文化體驗"},{"english":"In my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"greatest benefits","chinese":"最大好處"},{"english":"broadens individuals' understanding of","chinese":"擴闊個人對……的理解"},{"english":"strengthens society","chinese":"加強社會"},{"english":"creating jobs","chinese":"創造就業"},{"english":"funding public services","chinese":"資助公共服務"},{"english":"protecting local culture","chinese":"保護本地文化"},{"english":"on an individual level","chinese":"在個人層面上"},{"english":"step outside","chinese":"走出"},{"english":"the narrow routine of daily life","chinese":"狹窄的日常生活模式"},{"english":"see how others live","chinese":"了解其他人的生活方式"},{"english":"encounter different languages","chinese":"接觸不同語言"},{"english":"customs","chinese":"風俗習慣"},{"english":"ways of thinking","chinese":"思維方式"},{"english":"become more open-minded","chinese":"變得更開明"},{"english":"less quick to judge","chinese":"不那麼快作出批判"},{"english":"unfamiliar lifestyles","chinese":"陌生的生活方式"},{"english":"observing local manners","chinese":"觀察本地禮儀"},{"english":"temples","chinese":"寺廟"},{"english":"food traditions","chinese":"飲食傳統"},{"english":"a chapter in a textbook","chinese":"教科書中的一章"},{"english":"first-hand experience","chinese":"第一手經驗"},{"english":"turns culture from...into...","chinese":"將文化由……變成……"},{"english":"an abstract idea","chinese":"抽象概念"},{"english":"something people can see, hear and remember","chinese":"人們可以看見、聽見和記住的東西"},{"english":"make individuals more curious","chinese":"令個人更加好奇"},{"english":"adaptable","chinese":"適應力強的"},{"english":"culturally sensitive","chinese":"對文化更敏感；更懂得尊重不同文化"},{"english":"brings clear social benefits","chinese":"帶來明顯社會好處"},{"english":"rely on visitors","chinese":"依賴遊客"},{"english":"need workers","chinese":"需要員工"},{"english":"provide income for","chinese":"為……提供收入"},{"english":"reduce unemployment","chinese":"減低失業率"},{"english":"money spent by tourists","chinese":"遊客花費的金錢"},{"english":"wider public life","chinese":"更廣泛的公共生活"},{"english":"collect more tax revenue","chinese":"收取更多稅收"},{"english":"improve transport links","chinese":"改善交通連接"},{"english":"maintain historic sites","chinese":"維護歷史遺址"},{"english":"otherwise be neglected","chinese":"否則可能被忽視"},{"english":"old district","chinese":"舊區"},{"english":"becomes popular with","chinese":"受到……歡迎"},{"english":"local authorities","chinese":"地方當局"},{"english":"have a stronger reason to","chinese":"有更強理由去"},{"english":"restore buildings","chinese":"修復建築物"},{"english":"train guides","chinese":"培訓導遊"},{"english":"keep the area clean","chinese":"保持該區清潔"},{"english":"In this way","chinese":"以這種方式"},{"english":"does not merely bring money into","chinese":"不只是為……帶來金錢"},{"english":"practical reason to","chinese":"實際理由去"},{"english":"preserve their identity","chinese":"保留自身身份特色"},{"english":"widening their horizons","chinese":"擴闊眼界"},{"english":"creating employment","chinese":"創造就業"},{"english":"improving local facilities","chinese":"改善本地設施"},{"english":"encouraging cultural preservation","chinese":"鼓勵文化保育"},{"english":"managed responsibly","chinese":"在負責任管理下"},{"english":"an economic engine","chinese":"經濟引擎；經濟推動力"},{"english":"a bridge between cultures","chinese":"文化之間的橋樑"}]},"model-essay-42-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-42-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:42","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-42-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q42","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Traffic congestion has become one of the most persistent problems in modern cities. While some people argue that privately owned vehicles should be prohibited from city centres, others believe that such a policy would be impractical. In my view, although banning private cars may appear attractive in theory, it is an unrealistic solution in practice.","chinese":"交通擠塞已成為現代城市中最持久的問題之一。 有些人認為私人擁有的車輛應該被禁止進入市中心，而另一些人則認為這樣的政策並不切實際。 在我看來，雖然禁止私家車在理論上可能看似吸引，但在實際操作上卻是一個不現實的解決方法。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"On the one hand, supporters of this policy argue that a ban on private vehicles would make city centres cleaner, safer, and less crowded. Private cars often carry only one or two passengers, yet they occupy a large amount of road space. If they were removed from central areas, buses, trams, cyclists, and pedestrians could move far more efficiently. This would not only reduce traffic jams but also lower air pollution, since fewer cars would mean fewer emissions. For example, a busy shopping district with fewer private vehicles would likely become more pleasant for residents, workers, and visitors alike. From this perspective, restricting car access seems to be a direct way to improve urban life.","chinese":"一方面，支持這項政策的人認為，禁止私人車輛進入市中心會令市中心更清潔、更安全，也更不擁擠。 私家車通常只載一兩名乘客，卻佔用了大量道路空間。 如果它們被移出市中心地區，巴士、電車、單車使用者和行人便能更有效率地移動。 這不但能減少交通堵塞，也能降低空氣污染，因為車輛減少就意味著排放減少。 例如，一個繁忙的購物區如果私家車較少，對居民、上班族和遊客而言都很可能會變得更加舒適。 從這個角度來看，限制汽車進入似乎是一種直接改善城市生活的方法。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"On the other hand, opponents argue that a complete ban would create serious practical problems. Many people depend on private vehicles because public transport is either unreliable, overcrowded, or unavailable in certain areas. Elderly people, disabled passengers, families with young children, and workers who carry equipment may find it especially difficult to enter city centres without their own cars. In addition, businesses could suffer if customers, suppliers, or employees were suddenly unable to travel conveniently. A policy that sounds simple on paper could therefore disrupt daily life and place an unfair burden on people whose needs cannot be met by public transport alone.","chinese":"另一方面，反對者認為，全面禁止私家車會造成嚴重的實際問題。 許多人依賴私人車輛，因為公共交通在某些地區可能不可靠、過於擁擠，或者根本無法使用。 長者、殘疾乘客、有年幼子女的家庭，以及需要攜帶工具或設備的工人，如果沒有自己的車，可能會特別難以進入市中心。 此外，如果顧客、供應商或員工突然無法方便地出行，商業活動也可能受到損害。 因此，一項在紙面上聽起來簡單的政策，實際上可能會擾亂日常生活，並對那些單靠公共交通無法滿足需要的人造成不公平的負擔。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 3","english":"I strongly believe that banning privately owned vehicles from city centres is unrealistic. A better approach would be to reduce car use through congestion charges, improved public transport, limited parking, and better cycling infrastructure. These measures would ease congestion without punishing people who genuinely need to drive.","chinese":"我強烈認為，禁止私人擁有的車輛進入市中心是不現實的。 更好的方法是透過徵收擠塞費、改善公共交通、限制泊車，以及建設更完善的單車基礎設施來減少汽車使用。 這些措施能夠紓緩交通擠塞，同時不會懲罰那些真正需要駕車的人。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, although banning private vehicles could reduce traffic and pollution, it is too rigid to work fairly in real cities. Governments should manage car use more intelligently rather than impose a complete ban.","chinese":"總結來說，雖然禁止私人車輛能夠減少交通和污染，但它過於僵硬，難以在真實城市中公平地運作。 政府應該更明智地管理汽車使用，而不是實施全面禁令。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"traffic congestion","chinese":"交通擠塞"},{"english":"one of the most persistent problems","chinese":"最持續存在的問題之一"},{"english":"modern cities","chinese":"現代城市"},{"english":"privately owned vehicles","chinese":"私家車；私人擁有的車輛"},{"english":"be prohibited from","chinese":"被禁止進入"},{"english":"city centres","chinese":"市中心"},{"english":"such a policy","chinese":"這樣的政策"},{"english":"be impractical","chinese":"不切實際"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"appear attractive in theory","chinese":"理論上看似吸引"},{"english":"an unrealistic solution in practice","chinese":"實際上不切實際的解決方法"},{"english":"on the one hand","chinese":"一方面"},{"english":"supporters of this policy","chinese":"這項政策的支持者"},{"english":"a ban on private vehicles","chinese":"對私家車的禁令"},{"english":"cleaner, safer, and less crowded","chinese":"更清潔、更安全和較不擠迫"},{"english":"carry only one or two passengers","chinese":"只載一兩名乘客"},{"english":"occupy a large amount of road space","chinese":"佔用大量道路空間"},{"english":"central areas","chinese":"中心地區"},{"english":"buses, trams, cyclists, and pedestrians","chinese":"巴士、電車、單車人士和行人"},{"english":"move far more efficiently","chinese":"流動效率高得多"},{"english":"not only reduce traffic jams but also","chinese":"不但減少塞車，而且"},{"english":"traffic jams","chinese":"塞車"},{"english":"lower air pollution","chinese":"降低空氣污染"},{"english":"fewer emissions","chinese":"較少廢氣排放"},{"english":"a busy shopping district","chinese":"繁忙購物區"},{"english":"would likely become","chinese":"很可能會變得"},{"english":"residents, workers, and visitors alike","chinese":"居民、上班族和遊客都一樣"},{"english":"from this perspective","chinese":"從這個角度來看"},{"english":"restricting car access","chinese":"限制汽車進入"},{"english":"a direct way to","chinese":"……的直接方法"},{"english":"improve urban life","chinese":"改善城市生活"},{"english":"on the other hand","chinese":"另一方面"},{"english":"opponents argue that","chinese":"反對者認為"},{"english":"a complete ban","chinese":"全面禁令"},{"english":"create serious practical problems","chinese":"造成嚴重實際問題"},{"english":"depend on private vehicles","chinese":"依賴私家車"},{"english":"public transport","chinese":"公共交通工具"},{"english":"unreliable","chinese":"不可靠"},{"english":"overcrowded","chinese":"過度擠迫"},{"english":"unavailable in certain areas","chinese":"在某些地區沒有提供"},{"english":"elderly people","chinese":"長者"},{"english":"disabled passengers","chinese":"殘疾乘客；行動不便乘客"},{"english":"families with young children","chinese":"有年幼子女的家庭"},{"english":"workers who carry equipment","chinese":"需要攜帶工具的工人"},{"english":"find it especially difficult to","chinese":"覺得特別困難去"},{"english":"enter city centres","chinese":"進入市中心"},{"english":"without their own cars","chinese":"沒有自己的車"},{"english":"in addition","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"businesses could suffer","chinese":"企業可能受影響"},{"english":"customers, suppliers, or employees","chinese":"顧客、供應商或僱員"},{"english":"be suddenly unable to","chinese":"突然無法"},{"english":"travel conveniently","chinese":"方便出行"},{"english":"sound simple on paper","chinese":"紙面上聽起來簡單"},{"english":"disrupt daily life","chinese":"擾亂日常生活"},{"english":"place an unfair burden on","chinese":"對……造成不公平負擔"},{"english":"whose needs cannot be met by","chinese":"其需要不能由……滿足"},{"english":"public transport alone","chinese":"單靠公共交通工具"},{"english":"a better approach","chinese":"更好的做法"},{"english":"reduce car use","chinese":"減少汽車使用"},{"english":"congestion charges","chinese":"擠塞收費"},{"english":"improved public transport","chinese":"改善公共交通"},{"english":"limited parking","chinese":"限制泊車"},{"english":"cycling infrastructure","chinese":"單車基建"},{"english":"these measures","chinese":"這些措施"},{"english":"ease congestion","chinese":"紓緩交通擠塞"},{"english":"without punishing","chinese":"而不會懲罰"},{"english":"genuinely need to drive","chinese":"真正需要駕車"},{"english":"reduce traffic and pollution","chinese":"減少交通和污染"},{"english":"too rigid to work fairly","chinese":"過於僵化，難以公平實行"},{"english":"in real cities","chinese":"在真實城市中"},{"english":"manage car use more intelligently","chinese":"更明智地管理汽車使用"},{"english":"rather than impose","chinese":"而不是實施"},{"english":"impose a complete ban","chinese":"實施全面禁令"}]},"model-essay-42-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-42-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:42","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-42-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q42","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"It is sometimes argued that governments waste excessive public money on wildlife conservation when more urgent social problems exist. I strongly disagree with this view because protecting wildlife is not a luxury; it is a necessary part of protecting human life, environmental stability, and long-term economic security.","chinese":"有人認為，當社會上存在更迫切的問題時，政府把過多公共資金浪費在野生動物保育上。 我強烈不同意這種看法，因為保護野生動物並不是一種奢侈行為；它是保障人類生活、環境穩定和長遠經濟安全的必要部分。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that wildlife protection is closely connected to the health of the natural systems on which people depend. Animals and plants are not decorative extras in the background of human life; they form part of complex ecosystems that regulate climate, maintain soil quality, support food production, and keep natural habitats balanced. If governments allow forests, oceans, and animal populations to collapse, the damage will eventually return to human society in the form of food shortages, floods, disease, and higher living costs. For example, if bee populations decline because their habitats are destroyed, crop production can suffer, which may make basic food more expensive for ordinary families. In this sense, spending money on wildlife is not money thrown into the wilderness. It is an investment in the invisible machinery that keeps human life running.","chinese":"第一個原因是，野生動物保護與人類所依賴的自然系統健康密切相關。 動物和植物並不是人類生活背景中的裝飾性附屬品；它們是複雜生態系統的一部分，而這些系統能調節氣候、維持土壤質素、支持糧食生產，並保持自然棲息地的平衡。 如果政府任由森林、海洋和動物種群崩潰，這種破壞最終會以糧食短缺、洪水、疾病和更高生活成本的形式回到人類社會。 例如，如果蜜蜂種群因棲息地被破壞而減少，農作物產量便可能受影響，這可能使普通家庭的基本食物變得更昂貴。 從這個意義上說，花錢保護野生動物並不是把錢丟進荒野之中。這是對維持人類生活運作的無形機器作出投資。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important point is that conservation and social welfare should not be treated as enemies competing for the same piece of bread. Responsible governments must fund hospitals, schools, housing, and public safety, but this does not mean that wildlife protection should be pushed aside. In fact, many conservation projects also benefit local communities directly. National parks, marine reserves, and forest-protection schemes can create jobs, attract tourism, preserve clean water, and protect rural livelihoods. When these projects are managed well, they do not drain public resources; they create long-term value. Ignoring wildlife may seem cheaper in the short term, but it can become far more expensive when environmental damage has to be repaired later.","chinese":"另一個重要觀點是，保育和社會福利不應被視為爭奪同一塊麵包的敵人。 負責任的政府必須資助醫院、學校、住房和公共安全，但這並不代表野生動物保護應該被擱置一旁。 事實上，許多保育項目也能直接惠及本地社區。 國家公園、海洋保護區和森林保護計劃可以創造就業、吸引旅遊、保護潔淨水源，並保障農村生計。 當這些項目管理得宜時，它們不會耗盡公共資源；相反，它們會創造長遠價值。 忽視野生動物在短期內可能看似較便宜，但當日後必須修復環境破壞時，代價可能會高得多。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I do not agree that governments spend too much on protecting wildlife. Although many social problems deserve serious attention, wildlife conservation is one of the foundations of a safe, healthy, and sustainable society.","chinese":"總結來說，我不同意政府在保護野生動物方面花費過多這一說法。 雖然許多社會問題都值得認真關注，但野生動物保育是建立安全、健康和可持續社會的基礎之一。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"waste excessive public money on","chinese":"在……上浪費過多公帑"},{"english":"wildlife conservation","chinese":"野生動物保育"},{"english":"urgent social problems","chinese":"迫切社會問題"},{"english":"strongly disagree with","chinese":"強烈不同意……"},{"english":"not a luxury","chinese":"不是奢侈品"},{"english":"a necessary part of","chinese":"……的必要部分"},{"english":"environmental stability","chinese":"環境穩定"},{"english":"long-term economic security","chinese":"長遠經濟保障"},{"english":"be closely connected to","chinese":"與……密切相關"},{"english":"natural systems","chinese":"自然系統"},{"english":"depend on","chinese":"依賴"},{"english":"decorative extras","chinese":"裝飾性的附加物"},{"english":"in the background of","chinese":"在……的背景中"},{"english":"complex ecosystems","chinese":"複雜生態系統"},{"english":"regulate climate","chinese":"調節氣候"},{"english":"maintain soil quality","chinese":"維持土壤質素"},{"english":"support food production","chinese":"支持糧食生產"},{"english":"keep natural habitats balanced","chinese":"維持自然棲息地平衡"},{"english":"allow forests, oceans, and animal populations to collapse","chinese":"讓森林、海洋和動物種群崩潰"},{"english":"animal populations","chinese":"動物種群"},{"english":"eventually return to","chinese":"最終回到；反過來影響"},{"english":"in the form of","chinese":"以……的形式"},{"english":"food shortages","chinese":"糧食短缺"},{"english":"higher living costs","chinese":"更高生活成本"},{"english":"bee populations","chinese":"蜜蜂種群"},{"english":"decline","chinese":"下降；減少"},{"english":"habitats are destroyed","chinese":"棲息地被破壞"},{"english":"crop production","chinese":"農作物生產"},{"english":"can suffer","chinese":"可能受損"},{"english":"basic food","chinese":"基本食物"},{"english":"ordinary families","chinese":"普通家庭"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"money thrown into the wilderness","chinese":"投進荒野而白白浪費的錢"},{"english":"investment in","chinese":"對……的投資"},{"english":"invisible machinery","chinese":"隱形機器"},{"english":"keeps human life running","chinese":"令人的生活得以運作"},{"english":"conservation","chinese":"保育"},{"english":"social welfare","chinese":"社會福利"},{"english":"be treated as enemies","chinese":"被視為敵對"},{"english":"competing for","chinese":"爭奪……"},{"english":"the same piece of bread","chinese":"同一塊麵包；同一份資源"},{"english":"responsible governments","chinese":"負責任的政府"},{"english":"public safety","chinese":"公共安全"},{"english":"be pushed aside","chinese":"被擱置一旁"},{"english":"conservation projects","chinese":"保育項目"},{"english":"local communities","chinese":"本地社區"},{"english":"national parks","chinese":"國家公園"},{"english":"marine reserves","chinese":"海洋保護區"},{"english":"forest-protection schemes","chinese":"森林保護計劃"},{"english":"create jobs","chinese":"創造就業機會"},{"english":"attract tourism","chinese":"吸引旅遊業"},{"english":"preserve clean water","chinese":"保存潔淨水源"},{"english":"protect rural livelihoods","chinese":"保護鄉郊生計"},{"english":"managed well","chinese":"管理得宜"},{"english":"drain public resources","chinese":"耗盡公共資源"},{"english":"create long-term value","chinese":"創造長遠價值"},{"english":"ignoring wildlife","chinese":"忽視野生動物"},{"english":"in the short term","chinese":"短期內"},{"english":"become far more expensive","chinese":"變得昂貴得多"},{"english":"be repaired later","chinese":"日後被修復"},{"english":"spend too much on","chinese":"在……上花費太多"},{"english":"deserve serious attention","chinese":"值得認真關注"},{"english":"one of the foundations of","chinese":"……的基礎之一"},{"english":"safe, healthy, and sustainable society","chinese":"安全、健康和可持續的社會"}]},"model-essay-43-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-43-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:43","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-43-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q43","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Tourism has made many historic places more accessible than ever, but it has also placed some of the world’s most fragile buildings and sites under severe pressure. Once ancient walls, temples, or monuments are permanently damaged, they cannot simply be rebuilt with the same cultural value. To prevent this, governments and heritage authorities should focus on both controlling visitor behaviour and creating a stable system for conservation.","chinese":"旅遊業使許多歷史場所比以往任何時候都更容易被人接觸，但它也令世界上一些最脆弱的建築和遺址承受沉重壓力。 一旦古老的城牆、寺廟或紀念建築受到永久性破壞，它們便不能簡單地以相同的文化價值被重建。 為了防止這種情況，政府和文物保育機構應同時著重控制遊客行為，以及建立一個穩定的保育制度。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first and most immediate measure is to limit the physical pressure placed on vulnerable sites. Many historic attractions are damaged not by one careless visitor, but by thousands of people walking, touching, climbing, and crowding the same spaces every day. For this reason, authorities should introduce timed tickets, daily visitor limits, protected walking routes, and restricted zones around especially delicate structures. For example, if tourists are allowed to view an ancient temple from a controlled path instead of walking freely through it, the risk of erosion, accidental damage, and overcrowding is greatly reduced. This would not stop people from enjoying cultural heritage; rather, it would allow them to experience it without slowly destroying it.","chinese":"第一個也是最直接的措施，是限制脆弱遺址所承受的實際壓力。 許多歷史景點並不是被某一個粗心的遊客破壞，而是被每天成千上萬的人在同一空間中行走、觸摸、攀爬和擁擠所損害。 正因如此，當局應引入限時門票、每日遊客人數上限、受保護的步行路線，以及在特別脆弱的建築周圍設立限制區域。 例如，如果遊客只能從受管制的路徑觀賞一座古老寺廟，而不是在其中自由行走，侵蝕、意外損壞和過度擁擠的風險便會大大降低。 這並不會阻止人們欣賞文化遺產；相反，這能讓他們在不慢慢破壞它的情況下體驗它。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important solution is to make tourism directly fund preservation. Entrance fees, tourism taxes, or conservation charges should be used specifically to repair buildings, employ trained staff, install protective equipment, and monitor damage over time. At the same time, tour operators should be required to educate visitors before they enter sensitive sites, while strict fines should be imposed on those who ignore rules, remove objects, or vandalise property. Clear signs alone are often not enough; rules need both explanation and enforcement. When tourists understand that they are entering a piece of shared history rather than just another photo opportunity, they are more likely to behave responsibly.","chinese":"另一個重要的解決方法，是讓旅遊業直接資助保育工作。 入場費、旅遊稅或保育費應專門用於修復建築、聘請受過訓練的員工、安裝保護設備，以及長期監察損壞情況。 與此同時，旅行社和導遊機構應被要求在遊客進入敏感遺址前教育他們，而對於無視規則、取走物件或破壞財物的人，則應施加嚴厲罰款。 單靠清晰的標示往往並不足夠；規則既需要解釋，也需要執行。 當遊客明白自己進入的是一段共同歷史，而不只是另一個拍照機會時，他們便更有可能負責任地行事。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, historic sites can be protected by reducing excessive visitor pressure and by using tourism revenue to support long-term conservation. Tourism should open a window onto the past, not close it forever.","chinese":"總結來說，歷史遺址可以透過減少過度的遊客壓力，以及利用旅遊收入支持長期保育來得到保護。 旅遊業應該為人們打開一扇通往過去的窗，而不是永遠把它關上。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"historic places","chinese":"歷史名勝；歷史地方"},{"english":"more accessible than ever","chinese":"比以往更容易到達"},{"english":"fragile buildings and sites","chinese":"脆弱的建築物和遺址"},{"english":"under severe pressure","chinese":"承受嚴重壓力"},{"english":"ancient walls","chinese":"古老城牆"},{"english":"temples","chinese":"寺廟"},{"english":"monuments","chinese":"紀念碑；古蹟"},{"english":"permanently damaged","chinese":"永久受損"},{"english":"cannot simply be rebuilt","chinese":"不能簡單地重建"},{"english":"the same cultural value","chinese":"相同的文化價值"},{"english":"prevent this","chinese":"防止這種情況"},{"english":"heritage authorities","chinese":"文物保育機構"},{"english":"focus on","chinese":"專注於"},{"english":"controlling visitor behaviour","chinese":"管控遊客行為"},{"english":"a stable system for conservation","chinese":"穩定的保育制度"},{"english":"the first and most immediate measure","chinese":"第一項也是最即時的措施"},{"english":"physical pressure","chinese":"實際壓力"},{"english":"vulnerable sites","chinese":"脆弱的遺址"},{"english":"historic attractions","chinese":"歷史景點"},{"english":"careless visitor","chinese":"粗心大意的遊客"},{"english":"walking, touching, climbing, and crowding","chinese":"行走、觸摸、攀爬和擠滿"},{"english":"the same spaces","chinese":"同一片空間"},{"english":"for this reason","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"introduce timed tickets","chinese":"推出分時段門票"},{"english":"daily visitor limits","chinese":"每日遊客人數限制"},{"english":"protected walking routes","chinese":"受保護的步行路線"},{"english":"restricted zones","chinese":"限制進入區域"},{"english":"especially delicate structures","chinese":"特別脆弱的結構"},{"english":"be allowed to","chinese":"被允許"},{"english":"view an ancient temple","chinese":"參觀古老寺廟"},{"english":"a controlled path","chinese":"受管制的路徑"},{"english":"instead of walking freely through","chinese":"而不是自由穿行於"},{"english":"the risk of erosion","chinese":"侵蝕風險"},{"english":"accidental damage","chinese":"意外損壞"},{"english":"overcrowding","chinese":"過度擠迫"},{"english":"greatly reduced","chinese":"大大減少"},{"english":"cultural heritage","chinese":"文化遺產"},{"english":"rather","chinese":"反而；而是"},{"english":"experience it without","chinese":"在不……的情況下體驗"},{"english":"slowly destroying it","chinese":"慢慢破壞它"},{"english":"directly fund preservation","chinese":"直接資助保育"},{"english":"entrance fees","chinese":"入場費"},{"english":"tourism taxes","chinese":"旅遊稅"},{"english":"conservation charges","chinese":"保育費"},{"english":"be used specifically to","chinese":"專門用於"},{"english":"repair buildings","chinese":"修復建築物"},{"english":"employ trained staff","chinese":"聘請受過訓練的職員"},{"english":"install protective equipment","chinese":"安裝保護設備"},{"english":"monitor damage over time","chinese":"長期監察損壞情況"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"tour operators","chinese":"旅行社；旅遊營辦商"},{"english":"be required to","chinese":"被要求"},{"english":"educate visitors","chinese":"教育遊客"},{"english":"sensitive sites","chinese":"敏感遺址；需特別保護的地方"},{"english":"strict fines","chinese":"嚴厲罰款"},{"english":"be imposed on","chinese":"施加於"},{"english":"ignore rules","chinese":"無視規則"},{"english":"remove objects","chinese":"拿走物件"},{"english":"vandalise property","chinese":"破壞財物"},{"english":"clear signs alone","chinese":"單靠清晰標誌"},{"english":"explanation and enforcement","chinese":"解釋和執法"},{"english":"shared history","chinese":"共同歷史"},{"english":"photo opportunity","chinese":"拍照機會"},{"english":"behave responsibly","chinese":"負責任地行事"},{"english":"excessive visitor pressure","chinese":"過度遊客壓力"},{"english":"tourism revenue","chinese":"旅遊收入"},{"english":"long-term conservation","chinese":"長遠保育"},{"english":"open a window onto the past","chinese":"打開通往過去的一扇窗"},{"english":"close it forever","chinese":"永遠關上它"}]},"model-essay-43-ielts-discuss-both-views":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-43-ielts-discuss-both-views","essayKey":"discuss-both-views:43","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-43-ielts-discuss-both-views","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/discuss-both-views-your-opinion/EdmundBd9ExpBth-Q43","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Completing a university degree is often seen as a direct route to secure and well-paid employment. Others, however, argue that practical experience and soft skills are more valuable in the modern workplace. Although university education can provide an important foundation, I strongly believe that experience and interpersonal abilities are more important for long-term career success.","chinese":"完成大學學位常被視為獲得穩定且高薪工作的直接途徑。 然而，其他人則認為，在現代職場中，實際經驗和軟技能更有價值。 儘管大學教育能提供重要基礎，但我堅信，經驗和人際能力對長遠職業成功更加重要。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"On the one hand, a university qualification can be essential because it gives people specialised knowledge and formal credibility. In fields such as medicine, engineering, law, and finance, employers cannot simply rely on a candidate’s personality or enthusiasm; they need evidence that the person has mastered complex theories, technical procedures, and professional standards. A degree also signals discipline, commitment, and the ability to complete demanding tasks over several years. For example, a hospital would naturally prefer a doctor who has completed medical school, because patients’ lives depend on accurate knowledge and careful training. In this sense, university education acts as a gatekeeper for many respected professions.","chinese":"一方面，大學學歷可能是必要的，因為它能給予人們專門知識和正式可信度。 在醫學、工程、法律和金融等領域，僱主不能單純依靠求職者的性格或熱情；他們需要證據證明這個人已經掌握複雜理論、技術程序和專業標準。 學位也代表著自律、承諾，以及在數年時間內完成高要求任務的能力。 例如，醫院自然會更傾向聘請一位完成醫學院訓練的醫生，因為病人的生命取決於準確的知識和嚴謹的訓練。 從這個意義上說，大學教育對許多受人尊重的專業而言，起著把關人的作用。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"On the other hand, experience and soft skills are often what allow people to perform well after they are hired. Many graduates understand theory but struggle to communicate clearly, solve real problems, manage pressure, or work with difficult colleagues. By contrast, someone who has spent years in a workplace may know how to handle customers, adapt to sudden changes, and make practical decisions under pressure. These abilities are not easily taught in lecture halls; they are developed through real situations, mistakes, feedback, and responsibility. For instance, a manager with strong communication skills can motivate a team and resolve conflict, whereas a highly educated but inflexible employee may damage morale and slow down progress.","chinese":"另一方面，經驗和軟技能往往才是讓人們在受聘後表現出色的因素。 許多畢業生懂得理論，卻難以清晰溝通、解決實際問題、應對壓力，或與難相處的同事合作。 相比之下，一個在職場工作多年的人，可能知道如何應對客戶、適應突發變化，並在壓力下作出實際決定。 這些能力並不容易在演講廳中教授；它們是透過真實情境、錯誤、反饋和責任逐步培養出來的。 例如，一位具備強大溝通能力的經理可以激勵團隊並解決衝突，而一位受過高等教育但缺乏彈性的員工，則可能損害士氣並拖慢進度。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, university education is valuable, especially in professions that require technical expertise. However, I believe experience and soft skills are more important overall, because they determine whether a person can actually succeed in the complex, human reality of the workplace.","chinese":"總結來說，大學教育是有價值的，尤其是在需要專業技術知識的職業中。 然而，我認為整體而言，經驗和軟技能更加重要，因為它們決定了一個人能否真正地在複雜而充滿人際因素的職場現實中取得成功。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"completing a university degree","chinese":"完成大學學位"},{"english":"be seen as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"a direct route to","chinese":"通往……的直接途徑"},{"english":"secure and well-paid employment","chinese":"穩定而高薪的工作"},{"english":"practical experience","chinese":"實際經驗"},{"english":"soft skills","chinese":"軟技能"},{"english":"more valuable in","chinese":"在……中更有價值"},{"english":"the modern workplace","chinese":"現代職場"},{"english":"university education","chinese":"大學教育"},{"english":"provide an important foundation","chinese":"提供重要基礎"},{"english":"strongly believe that","chinese":"強烈相信"},{"english":"interpersonal abilities","chinese":"人際能力"},{"english":"long-term career success","chinese":"長遠事業成功"},{"english":"on the one hand","chinese":"一方面"},{"english":"university qualification","chinese":"大學資歷"},{"english":"be essential","chinese":"是必要的"},{"english":"specialised knowledge","chinese":"專門知識"},{"english":"formal credibility","chinese":"正式可信度；正式認可"},{"english":"in fields such as","chinese":"在例如……的領域"},{"english":"cannot simply rely on","chinese":"不能單純依賴"},{"english":"a candidate's personality or enthusiasm","chinese":"求職者的性格或熱情"},{"english":"need evidence that","chinese":"需要證據證明"},{"english":"master complex theories","chinese":"掌握複雜理論"},{"english":"technical procedures","chinese":"技術程序"},{"english":"professional standards","chinese":"專業標準"},{"english":"signal discipline and commitment","chinese":"顯示自律和投入"},{"english":"complete demanding tasks","chinese":"完成要求高的任務"},{"english":"over several years","chinese":"長達數年"},{"english":"naturally prefer","chinese":"自然會較喜歡"},{"english":"complete medical school","chinese":"完成醫學院課程"},{"english":"patients' lives depend on","chinese":"病人的生命取決於"},{"english":"accurate knowledge","chinese":"準確知識"},{"english":"careful training","chinese":"嚴謹訓練"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"act as a gatekeeper for","chinese":"作為……的入門門檻"},{"english":"respected professions","chinese":"受尊重的專業"},{"english":"on the other hand","chinese":"另一方面"},{"english":"perform well after they are hired","chinese":"受聘後表現良好"},{"english":"understand theory","chinese":"理解理論"},{"english":"struggle to communicate clearly","chinese":"難以清楚溝通"},{"english":"solve real problems","chinese":"解決實際問題"},{"english":"manage pressure","chinese":"應對壓力"},{"english":"work with difficult colleagues","chinese":"與難相處的同事合作"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相反"},{"english":"spend years in a workplace","chinese":"在職場工作多年"},{"english":"handle customers","chinese":"應對顧客"},{"english":"adapt to sudden changes","chinese":"適應突如其來的變化"},{"english":"make practical decisions under pressure","chinese":"在壓力下作出實際決定"},{"english":"be not easily taught","chinese":"不容易被教授"},{"english":"lecture halls","chinese":"演講廳；大學課堂"},{"english":"be developed through","chinese":"透過……培養"},{"english":"real situations","chinese":"真實情境"},{"english":"mistakes, feedback, and responsibility","chinese":"錯誤、回饋和責任"},{"english":"for instance","chinese":"例如"},{"english":"strong communication skills","chinese":"強大的溝通技巧"},{"english":"motivate a team","chinese":"激勵團隊"},{"english":"resolve conflict","chinese":"解決衝突"},{"english":"highly educated but inflexible","chinese":"學歷高但不懂變通的"},{"english":"damage morale","chinese":"損害士氣"},{"english":"slow down progress","chinese":"拖慢進度"},{"english":"technical expertise","chinese":"專業技術知識"},{"english":"more important overall","chinese":"整體而言更重要"},{"english":"determine whether","chinese":"決定是否"},{"english":"actually succeed","chinese":"真正成功"},{"english":"the complex, human reality of","chinese":"……中複雜而涉及人際的現實"},{"english":"the workplace","chinese":"職場"}]},"model-essay-43-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-43-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:43","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-43-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q43","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Environmental damage is one of the most serious challenges facing the modern world, and fuel consumption is often seen as an obvious target. However, I completely disagree that making fuel more expensive is the best way to deal with global environmental problems. This approach is too blunt, too unfair, and far less effective than long-term investment and regulation.","chinese":"環境破壞是現代世界面臨的最嚴重挑戰之一，而燃料消耗通常被視為一個明顯針對目標 然而，我完全不同意提高燃料價格是處理全球環境問題的最佳方法。 這種做法過於粗暴、過於不公平，而且遠不如長期投資和監管有效。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first problem is that higher fuel prices would punish many ordinary people without giving them a realistic way to change their behaviour. In many towns and rural areas, workers, parents, and small business owners depend on cars or vans because public transport is limited, unreliable, or simply unavailable. If petrol or diesel becomes much more expensive, these people may not drive less; they may just have less money for food, rent, healthcare, or education. For example, a delivery driver whose income depends on daily travel cannot suddenly stop using fuel because prices rise. In this case, the policy becomes a financial burden rather than a genuine environmental solution.","chinese":"第一個問題是，更高的燃料價格會懲罰許多普通人，卻沒有給予他們一種現實可行的方法去改變自己的行為。 在許多城鎮和鄉郊地區，工人、父母和小企業主都依賴汽車或貨車，因為公共交通有限、不可靠，或者根本不存在。 如果汽油或柴油變得昂貴得多，這些人未必會減少駕駛；他們可能只是會有更少金錢用於食物、租金、醫療或教育。 例如，一名收入依賴每日出行的送貨司機，不可能因為價格上升就突然停止使用燃料。 在這種情況下，這項政策會變成一種經濟負擔，而不是真正的環境解決方案。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"A better answer is to make cleaner choices that are practical and attractive. Governments should invest heavily in public transport, renewable energy, charging networks, and greener urban design so that people can reduce fuel use without sacrificing their basic needs. When buses are frequent, trains are affordable, and clean energy is widely available, lower-emission behaviour becomes a natural part of daily life rather than a forced sacrifice. At the same time, strict rules should be placed on industries that produce large amounts of pollution, because global environmental damage is not caused only by private drivers. Factories, airlines, shipping companies, and energy producers must also be required to modernise their systems and reduce emissions at source.","chinese":"更好的答案是讓更清潔的選擇變得實際而有吸引力。 政府應該大量投資於公共交通、可再生能源、充電網絡和更環保的城市設計，使人們能夠在不犧牲基本需要的情況下減少燃料使用。 當巴士班次頻密、火車價格可負擔，而清潔能源也廣泛可得時，低排放行為便會成為日常生活中自然的一部分，而不是一種被迫作出的犧牲。 與此同時，應該對製造大量污染的行業實施嚴格規則，因為全球環境破壞並不只是由私人駕駛者造成的。 工廠、航空公司、航運公司和能源生產商也必須被要求將其系統現代化，並從源頭減少排放。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, increasing the cost of fuel is not the best solution to global environmental problems. Real progress depends on building cleaner alternatives and holding major polluters responsible, not simply making everyday life more expensive for ordinary people.","chinese":"總結來說，提高燃料成本並不是解決全球環境問題的最佳方法。 真正的進展取決於建立更清潔的替代方案，並讓主要污染者承擔責任，而不是單純讓普通人的日常生活變得更加昂貴。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"environmental damage","chinese":"環境破壞"},{"english":"one of the most serious challenges","chinese":"最嚴重挑戰之一"},{"english":"facing the modern world","chinese":"現代世界所面對的"},{"english":"fuel consumption","chinese":"燃料消耗"},{"english":"be seen as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"obvious target","chinese":"明顯目標"},{"english":"making fuel more expensive","chinese":"令燃料更昂貴"},{"english":"deal with","chinese":"處理"},{"english":"global environmental problems","chinese":"全球環境問題"},{"english":"this approach","chinese":"這種做法"},{"english":"too blunt","chinese":"過於粗糙"},{"english":"too unfair","chinese":"過於不公平"},{"english":"far less effective than","chinese":"遠不及……有效"},{"english":"long-term investment","chinese":"長期投資"},{"english":"regulation","chinese":"規管"},{"english":"higher fuel prices","chinese":"較高燃料價格"},{"english":"punish ordinary people","chinese":"懲罰普通人"},{"english":"realistic way to","chinese":"現實可行的方法去……"},{"english":"change their behaviour","chinese":"改變他們的行為"},{"english":"rural areas","chinese":"鄉郊地區"},{"english":"small business owners","chinese":"小企業東主"},{"english":"depend on cars or vans","chinese":"依賴私家車或客貨車"},{"english":"public transport","chinese":"公共交通"},{"english":"limited, unreliable, or simply unavailable","chinese":"有限、不可靠或根本沒有"},{"english":"petrol or diesel","chinese":"汽油或柴油"},{"english":"drive less","chinese":"減少駕駛"},{"english":"have less money for","chinese":"用於……的錢較少"},{"english":"healthcare","chinese":"醫療護理"},{"english":"delivery driver","chinese":"送貨司機"},{"english":"income depends on","chinese":"收入取決於……"},{"english":"daily travel","chinese":"日常出行"},{"english":"suddenly stop using fuel","chinese":"突然停止使用燃料"},{"english":"prices rise","chinese":"價格上升"},{"english":"financial burden","chinese":"財政負擔"},{"english":"rather than a genuine environmental solution","chinese":"而不是真正的環保解決方案"},{"english":"genuine environmental solution","chinese":"真正的環保解決方案"},{"english":"a better answer","chinese":"更好的答案；更好的做法"},{"english":"cleaner choices","chinese":"較清潔的選擇"},{"english":"practical and attractive","chinese":"實際可行而具吸引力"},{"english":"invest heavily in","chinese":"大量投資於……"},{"english":"renewable energy","chinese":"可再生能源"},{"english":"charging networks","chinese":"充電網絡"},{"english":"greener urban design","chinese":"更環保的城市設計"},{"english":"reduce fuel use","chinese":"減少燃料使用"},{"english":"without sacrificing","chinese":"而不犧牲……"},{"english":"basic needs","chinese":"基本需要"},{"english":"buses are frequent","chinese":"巴士班次頻密"},{"english":"trains are affordable","chinese":"火車價格可負擔"},{"english":"clean energy is widely available","chinese":"清潔能源廣泛可用"},{"english":"lower-emission behaviour","chinese":"較低排放的行為"},{"english":"natural part of daily life","chinese":"日常生活中自然的一部分"},{"english":"forced sacrifice","chinese":"被迫作出的犧牲"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"strict rules","chinese":"嚴格規則"},{"english":"be placed on","chinese":"施加於……"},{"english":"produce large amounts of pollution","chinese":"產生大量污染"},{"english":"private drivers","chinese":"私家車司機"},{"english":"factories, airlines, shipping companies, and energy producers","chinese":"工廠、航空公司、航運公司和能源生產商"},{"english":"be required to","chinese":"被要求去……"},{"english":"modernise their systems","chinese":"現代化其系統"},{"english":"reduce emissions at source","chinese":"從源頭減少排放"},{"english":"increasing the cost of fuel","chinese":"增加燃料成本"},{"english":"real progress","chinese":"真正進步"},{"english":"cleaner alternatives","chinese":"較清潔的替代選擇"},{"english":"hold major polluters responsible","chinese":"追究主要污染者的責任"},{"english":"everyday life","chinese":"日常生活"},{"english":"more expensive for ordinary people","chinese":"對普通人而言更昂貴"}]},"model-essay-44-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-44-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:44","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-44-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q44","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Congestion has become one of the most stubborn problems in modern cities. One proposed response is to raise taxes on private vehicles. This would ease pressure on roads by changing commuters’ behaviour, but cities also need dependable alternatives to driving. This essay will explain the effect of such taxation and outline two further measures.","chinese":"交通擠塞已成為現代城市中最頑固的問題之一。 其中一個被提出的應對方法，是提高私家車的稅項。 這可以透過改變通勤者的行為來減輕道路壓力，但城市也需要提供可靠的駕車替代選擇。 本文將解釋這種稅收政策的作用，並概述另外兩項措施。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"A higher tax could reduce congestion because it makes private car ownership and use less attractive. If registration fees, annual licences or ownership charges become more expensive, many people will begin to question whether every journey needs to be made by car. For example, a worker who drives a short distance to the office mainly out of habit may switch to a train or bus once the cost of keeping a car becomes harder to justify. When thousands of similar decisions are made across a city, the number of vehicles on the road falls. In addition, the money collected from these taxes could be used to improve public transport, so the policy would not simply punish drivers; it would create a cleaner and more efficient transport system.","chinese":"較高的稅項可以減少交通擠塞，因為它會降低擁有和使用私家車的吸引力。 如果登記費、年度牌照費或車輛擁有成本變得更昂貴，許多人便會開始思考是否每一次出行都必須駕車。 例如，一位主要出於習慣而短途駕車上班的員工，一旦覺得養車成本越來越難以合理化，便可能改乘火車或巴士。 當一座城市中有成千上萬人作出類似決定時，道路上的車輛數量便會下降。 此外，從這些稅項中收取的資金可以用來改善公共交通，因此這項政策並不只是懲罰駕駛者；它會創造一個更清潔、更高效的交通系統。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Other measures are also necessary because taxation alone cannot solve urban congestion. The first is to make public transport fast, affordable and reliable. People will not leave their cars at home if buses are infrequent, trains are overcrowded or routes are poorly connected. Cities should therefore expand rail services, add dedicated bus lanes and connect residential districts more directly with workplaces and schools. A second measure is to manage road use more carefully through congestion charges, higher parking fees in crowded districts, and safer walking and cycling routes. These policies reduce unnecessary car trips while giving residents realistic alternatives.","chinese":"其他措施同樣必要，因為單靠稅收無法解決城市交通擠塞。 第一項措施是讓公共交通變得快捷、價格合理並且可靠。 如果巴士班次疏落、火車過度擠迫，或者路線銜接不佳，人們便不會把車留在家中。 因此，城市應該擴展鐵路服務、增設巴士專用線，並讓住宅區與工作地點和學校有更直接的連接。 第二項措施是透過擠塞收費、在人流密集地區提高泊車費，以及建立更安全的步行和單車路線，來更謹慎地管理道路使用。 這些政策可以減少不必要的私家車出行，同時為居民提供切實可行的替代選擇。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, increasing the tax on private vehicles can alleviate congestion by discouraging car dependency and funding better transport. However, cities will only see lasting improvement if this is combined with stronger public transport, road pricing policies and safe alternatives to driving.","chinese":"總結來說，提高私家車稅項可以透過減少人們對汽車的依賴，並為更好的交通系統提供資金，從而紓緩交通擠塞。 然而，只有當這項措施與更完善的公共交通、道路收費政策，以及安全的駕車替代選擇結合起來時，城市才會看到持久的改善。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"congestion","chinese":"交通擠塞"},{"english":"one of the most stubborn problems","chinese":"最棘手的問題之一"},{"english":"modern cities","chinese":"現代城市"},{"english":"one proposed response","chinese":"一個建議的應對方法"},{"english":"raise taxes on","chinese":"提高……的稅項"},{"english":"private vehicles","chinese":"私家車"},{"english":"ease pressure on roads","chinese":"紓緩道路壓力"},{"english":"commuters' behaviour","chinese":"通勤者的行為"},{"english":"dependable alternatives to","chinese":"可靠的……替代選擇"},{"english":"driving","chinese":"駕駛"},{"english":"such taxation","chinese":"這種徵稅"},{"english":"outline two further measures","chinese":"概述另外兩項措施"},{"english":"a higher tax","chinese":"較高稅項"},{"english":"private car ownership and use","chinese":"擁有及使用私家車"},{"english":"less attractive","chinese":"吸引力較低"},{"english":"registration fees","chinese":"登記費"},{"english":"annual licences","chinese":"年度牌照費"},{"english":"ownership charges","chinese":"車輛擁有收費"},{"english":"begin to question","chinese":"開始質疑"},{"english":"every journey","chinese":"每一程"},{"english":"be made by car","chinese":"以駕車方式完成"},{"english":"drives a short distance","chinese":"短途駕車"},{"english":"mainly out of habit","chinese":"主要出於習慣"},{"english":"switch to","chinese":"轉用"},{"english":"keeping a car","chinese":"養車"},{"english":"harder to justify","chinese":"更難說得過去"},{"english":"similar decisions","chinese":"類似決定"},{"english":"across a city","chinese":"遍及整個城市"},{"english":"the number of vehicles on the road","chinese":"路面車輛數量"},{"english":"falls","chinese":"下降"},{"english":"money collected from","chinese":"從……收取的款項"},{"english":"public transport","chinese":"公共交通"},{"english":"not simply punish drivers","chinese":"不只是懲罰司機"},{"english":"a cleaner and more efficient transport system","chinese":"更潔淨、更高效的交通系統"},{"english":"other measures","chinese":"其他措施"},{"english":"taxation alone","chinese":"單靠徵稅"},{"english":"solve urban congestion","chinese":"解決城市交通擠塞"},{"english":"fast, affordable and reliable","chinese":"快捷、負擔得起而可靠"},{"english":"leave their cars at home","chinese":"把車留在家中"},{"english":"infrequent","chinese":"班次不頻密的"},{"english":"overcrowded","chinese":"過度擠迫的"},{"english":"poorly connected","chinese":"連接不佳的"},{"english":"expand rail services","chinese":"擴展鐵路服務"},{"english":"dedicated bus lanes","chinese":"巴士專用線"},{"english":"residential districts","chinese":"住宅區"},{"english":"more directly with","chinese":"更直接地與……連接"},{"english":"workplaces and schools","chinese":"工作地點和學校"},{"english":"manage road use","chinese":"管理道路使用"},{"english":"congestion charges","chinese":"擠塞徵費"},{"english":"higher parking fees","chinese":"較高泊車費"},{"english":"crowded districts","chinese":"擠迫地區"},{"english":"safer walking and cycling routes","chinese":"更安全的步行和單車路線"},{"english":"reduce unnecessary car trips","chinese":"減少不必要的汽車旅程"},{"english":"realistic alternatives","chinese":"切實可行的替代選擇"},{"english":"increasing the tax on","chinese":"提高……的稅項"},{"english":"alleviate congestion","chinese":"紓緩交通擠塞"},{"english":"discouraging car dependency","chinese":"減少對汽車的依賴"},{"english":"funding better transport","chinese":"資助更好的交通"},{"english":"lasting improvement","chinese":"持久改善"},{"english":"be combined with","chinese":"與……結合"},{"english":"road pricing policies","chinese":"道路收費政策"},{"english":"safe alternatives to driving","chinese":"安全的駕駛替代選擇"}]},"model-essay-44-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-44-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:44","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-44-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q44","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Environmental damage is no longer a distant concern, and governments must decide carefully where limited public money should go. Some argue that local environmental issues should receive less funding so that more can be spent on global warming. I completely disagree with this view, because local problems are often immediate threats to public health and are also part of the wider climate crisis.","chinese":"環境破壞已不再是一個遙遠的問題，而政府必須謹慎決定有限的公共資金應該投放到哪裡。 有些人認為，本地環境問題應該獲得較少資金，這樣便可以把更多資源投放到全球暖化上。 我完全不同意這個觀點，因為本地問題往往是對公共健康的即時威脅，同時也是更廣泛氣候危機的一部分。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"First, local environmental problems are not minor just because they happen close to home. Polluted rivers, poor air quality, illegal dumping and unsafe drinking water can damage people’s daily lives far more directly than distant climate projections. If councils and national authorities cut spending in these areas, ordinary citizens may pay the price through respiratory illness, contaminated neighbourhoods and declining living standards. For example, a city that neglects waste collection and drainage may soon face blocked waterways, flooding and disease after heavy rain. In this sense, local environmental funding is not a luxury; it is a basic form of public protection.","chinese":"首先，本地環境問題並不會因為發生在我們身邊而變得微不足道。 受污染的河流、惡劣的空氣質素、非法傾倒垃圾以及不安全的飲用水，對人們日常生活的傷害，遠比遙遠的氣候預測更加直接。 如果地方議會和國家政府削減這些方面的開支，普通市民便可能要以呼吸系統疾病、受污染的社區和下降的生活水平作為代價。 例如，一個忽視垃圾收集和排水系統的城市，在大雨過後可能很快便會面對水道堵塞、水浸和疾病問題。 從這個意義上說，本地環境資金並不是一種奢侈，而是一種基本的公共保護。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Second, tackling global warming actually depends on strong local action. Carbon emissions are produced in real streets, homes, factories and transport systems, not in some abstract global arena. When governments invest in cleaner buses, better recycling systems, energy-efficient buildings and urban green spaces, they are addressing local problems and climate change at the same time. Reducing this funding would therefore be like removing the bricks from a house while trying to strengthen its roof. A serious climate strategy needs both a national vision and practical local delivery.","chinese":"第二，應對全球暖化其實有賴於強而有力的本地行動。 碳排放是在真實的街道、家庭、工廠和交通系統中產生的，而不是在某個抽象的全球場域中產生的。 當政府投資於更清潔的巴士、更完善的回收系統、更節能的建築和城市綠化空間時，它們其實是在同時處理本地問題和氣候變化。 因此，削減這些資金就像一邊試圖加固屋頂，一邊卻把房子的磚塊拆走。 一個認真的氣候策略既需要國家層面的願景，也需要本地層面的實際執行。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I strongly disagree that governments should divert money away from local environmental problems. Global warming is undeniably urgent, but it cannot be solved by neglecting the smaller environmental battles that protect communities and reduce emissions. The wiser approach is to strengthen local environmental programmes, because they are the foundation on which broader climate action is built.","chinese":"總結來說，我強烈不同意政府應該把資金從本地環境問題上轉移走。 全球暖化無疑是緊急問題，但它不能透過忽視那些保護社區和減少排放的較小型環境戰役來解決。 更明智的做法是加強本地環境計劃，因為它們正是更廣泛氣候行動得以建立的"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"environmental damage","chinese":"環境破壞"},{"english":"distant concern","chinese":"遙遠的憂慮"},{"english":"limited public money","chinese":"有限公帑"},{"english":"should go","chinese":"應該投放到哪裏"},{"english":"local environmental issues","chinese":"本地環境問題"},{"english":"receive less funding","chinese":"獲得較少撥款"},{"english":"be spent on","chinese":"被用於……"},{"english":"global warming","chinese":"全球暖化"},{"english":"immediate threats to","chinese":"對……的即時威脅"},{"english":"public health","chinese":"公共健康"},{"english":"part of the wider climate crisis","chinese":"更廣泛氣候危機的一部分"},{"english":"not minor just because","chinese":"不會只是因為……而變得輕微"},{"english":"happen close to home","chinese":"發生在身邊"},{"english":"polluted rivers","chinese":"受污染的河流"},{"english":"poor air quality","chinese":"惡劣空氣質素"},{"english":"illegal dumping","chinese":"非法傾倒廢物"},{"english":"unsafe drinking water","chinese":"不安全的飲用水"},{"english":"damage people's daily lives","chinese":"損害人們的日常生活"},{"english":"far more directly than","chinese":"比……直接得多"},{"english":"distant climate projections","chinese":"遙遠的氣候預測"},{"english":"councils and national authorities","chinese":"地方議會和國家機關"},{"english":"cut spending in","chinese":"削減在……上的開支"},{"english":"ordinary citizens","chinese":"普通市民"},{"english":"pay the price through","chinese":"透過……付出代價"},{"english":"respiratory illness","chinese":"呼吸系統疾病"},{"english":"contaminated neighbourhoods","chinese":"受污染的社區"},{"english":"declining living standards","chinese":"生活水平下降"},{"english":"neglects waste collection","chinese":"忽視垃圾收集"},{"english":"waste collection","chinese":"垃圾收集"},{"english":"drainage","chinese":"排水系統"},{"english":"blocked waterways","chinese":"水道堵塞"},{"english":"flooding and disease","chinese":"水浸和疾病"},{"english":"heavy rain","chinese":"大雨"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"local environmental funding","chinese":"本地環境撥款"},{"english":"not a luxury","chinese":"不是奢侈品"},{"english":"basic form of public protection","chinese":"基本公共保護形式"},{"english":"tackling global warming","chinese":"應對全球暖化"},{"english":"depends on","chinese":"取決於"},{"english":"strong local action","chinese":"強而有力的本地行動"},{"english":"carbon emissions","chinese":"碳排放"},{"english":"real streets, homes, factories and transport systems","chinese":"真實街道、住宅、工廠和交通系統"},{"english":"abstract global arena","chinese":"抽象的全球場域"},{"english":"invest in","chinese":"投資於……"},{"english":"cleaner buses","chinese":"較清潔的巴士"},{"english":"recycling systems","chinese":"回收系統"},{"english":"energy-efficient buildings","chinese":"節能建築"},{"english":"urban green spaces","chinese":"城市綠化空間"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"reducing this funding","chinese":"削減這筆撥款"},{"english":"be like removing the bricks from","chinese":"就像從……拆走磚塊"},{"english":"trying to strengthen its roof","chinese":"試圖加固屋頂"},{"english":"serious climate strategy","chinese":"認真的氣候策略"},{"english":"national vision","chinese":"國家願景"},{"english":"practical local delivery","chinese":"實際的本地執行"},{"english":"divert money away from","chinese":"將資金從……轉走"},{"english":"undeniably urgent","chinese":"無可否認地迫切"},{"english":"be solved by neglecting","chinese":"透過忽視……來解決"},{"english":"smaller environmental battles","chinese":"較小規模的環境戰役"},{"english":"protect communities","chinese":"保護社區"},{"english":"reduce emissions","chinese":"減少排放"},{"english":"wiser approach","chinese":"更明智的方法"},{"english":"strengthen local environmental programmes","chinese":"加強本地環境計劃"},{"english":"the foundation on which","chinese":"……的基礎"},{"english":"broader climate action","chinese":"更廣泛的氣候行動"}]},"model-essay-45-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-45-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:45","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-45-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q45","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many parts of the developing world, work is judged less by personal fulfilment than by the basic security it provides. This is why job satisfaction is often seen as a privilege rather than an ordinary expectation. I believe, however, that it is extremely important, because a society which ignores workers’ well-being eventually pays a price in productivity, health and human dignity.","chinese":"在許多發展中地區，人們評價工作的標準較少在於個人滿足感，而更多在於它所提供的基本保障。 這就是為甚麼工作滿足感經常被視為一種特權，而不是一種普通的期待。 然而，我認為它極其重要，因為一個忽視員工福祉的社會，最終會在生產力、健康和人的尊嚴方面付出代價。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main reason job satisfaction appears luxurious is economic pressure. In countries where wages are low, social protection is weak and unemployment is high, people often have little room to choose work that matches their interests or values. Their first concern is not whether a job is inspiring, but whether it can pay for food, rent and their children’s education. For example, a factory worker or delivery rider may accept long hours, unsafe conditions or repetitive tasks because losing the job would threaten the whole family. When survival is at stake, fulfilment naturally takes a back seat.","chinese":"工作滿足感之所以顯得像一種奢侈，主要原因是經濟壓力。 在工資低、社會保障薄弱、失業率高的國家，人們往往幾乎沒有空間去選擇符合自己興趣或價值觀的工作。 他們最先關心的並不是一份工作是否令人受到啟發，而是它是否能夠支付食物、租金和子女教育的開支。 例如，一名工廠工人或外賣配送員可能會接受長工時、不安全的工作環境或重複性的任務，因為失去這份工作會威脅到整個家庭。 當生存受到威脅時，滿足感自然會退居次位。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that many labour markets in poorer countries offer limited bargaining power. Workers may not have strong unions, clear contracts or realistic chances of promotion, so they cannot easily demand better treatment. In such circumstances, job satisfaction can feel like a luxury reserved for people with education, savings or professional skills. Those without these advantages may feel that they must take whatever work is available, even if it leaves them exhausted or undervalued.","chinese":"另一個原因是，許多較貧困國家的勞動市場給予工人的議價能力有限。 工人可能沒有強大的工會、清晰的合約，或實際可行的晉升機會，因此他們不容易要求更好的待遇。 在這種情況下，工作滿足感可能會讓人感覺像是一種只留給受過教育、有積蓄或具備專業技能人士的奢侈品。 沒有這些優勢的人可能會覺得，他們必須接受任何能找到的工作，即使那份工作令他們筋疲力盡或感到不被重視。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 3","english":"Despite this, job satisfaction should not be dismissed as unimportant. People spend much of their lives at work, so a job that causes constant stress can damage both mental and physical health. By contrast, employees who feel respected and purposeful are more likely to stay motivated, improve their skills and contribute positively to their workplace.","chinese":"儘管如此，工作滿足感不應被視為不重要而被忽略。 人們一生中有大量時間都花在工作上，因此一份會造成持續壓力的工作，可能會損害心理和身體健康。 相比之下，感到受尊重並且有目標感的員工，更有可能保持動力、提升技能，並對工作場所作出正面貢獻。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, job satisfaction is considered a luxury in many developing countries because economic insecurity limits people’s choices. Nevertheless, it is essential, not decorative, because decent work is one of the foundations of a healthier and more productive society.","chinese":"總結來說，在許多發展中國家，工作滿足感被視為一種奢侈，是因為經濟上的不安全限制了人們的選擇。 然而，它是必要的，而不是裝飾性的，因為體面的工作是建立一個更健康、更具生產力社會的基礎之一。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"in many parts of","chinese":"在……很多地區"},{"english":"the developing world","chinese":"發展中地區"},{"english":"be judged less by...than by...","chinese":"較少以……而更多以……評價"},{"english":"personal fulfilment","chinese":"個人成就感；個人滿足感"},{"english":"basic security","chinese":"基本保障"},{"english":"This is why","chinese":"這就是為甚麼"},{"english":"job satisfaction","chinese":"工作滿足感"},{"english":"be seen as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"a privilege rather than","chinese":"是一種特權而不是"},{"english":"an ordinary expectation","chinese":"普通期望"},{"english":"workers' well-being","chinese":"工人的福祉；身心健康"},{"english":"eventually pays a price in","chinese":"最終在……方面付出代價"},{"english":"productivity","chinese":"生產力"},{"english":"human dignity","chinese":"人的尊嚴"},{"english":"the main reason","chinese":"主要原因"},{"english":"appears luxurious","chinese":"顯得奢侈"},{"english":"economic pressure","chinese":"經濟壓力"},{"english":"wages are low","chinese":"工資低"},{"english":"social protection is weak","chinese":"社會保障薄弱"},{"english":"unemployment is high","chinese":"失業率高"},{"english":"have little room to","chinese":"幾乎沒有空間去"},{"english":"choose work that matches","chinese":"選擇符合……的工作"},{"english":"interests or values","chinese":"興趣或價值觀"},{"english":"first concern","chinese":"首要考慮"},{"english":"whether a job is inspiring","chinese":"一份工作是否有啟發性"},{"english":"pay for food and rent","chinese":"支付食物和租金"},{"english":"children's education","chinese":"子女教育"},{"english":"factory worker","chinese":"工廠工人"},{"english":"delivery rider","chinese":"外賣速遞員"},{"english":"accept long hours","chinese":"接受長工時"},{"english":"unsafe conditions","chinese":"不安全的工作環境"},{"english":"repetitive tasks","chinese":"重複性工作"},{"english":"threaten the whole family","chinese":"威脅整個家庭"},{"english":"survival is at stake","chinese":"生存受到威脅"},{"english":"take a back seat","chinese":"退居次位"},{"english":"labour markets","chinese":"勞動市場"},{"english":"poorer countries","chinese":"較貧窮的國家"},{"english":"limited bargaining power","chinese":"有限的議價能力"},{"english":"strong unions","chinese":"強大的工會"},{"english":"clear contracts","chinese":"清晰合約"},{"english":"realistic chances of promotion","chinese":"實際的晉升機會"},{"english":"demand better treatment","chinese":"要求更好待遇"},{"english":"in such circumstances","chinese":"在這種情況下"},{"english":"feel like a luxury","chinese":"感覺像奢侈品"},{"english":"reserved for","chinese":"留給；專屬於"},{"english":"professional skills","chinese":"專業技能"},{"english":"without these advantages","chinese":"沒有這些優勢"},{"english":"whatever work is available","chinese":"任何可得到的工作"},{"english":"leaves them exhausted","chinese":"令他們精疲力竭"},{"english":"undervalued","chinese":"不受重視"},{"english":"Despite this","chinese":"儘管如此"},{"english":"be dismissed as unimportant","chinese":"被視為不重要而不理會"},{"english":"spend much of their lives at work","chinese":"把人生很多時間花在工作上"},{"english":"constant stress","chinese":"持續壓力"},{"english":"mental and physical health","chinese":"身心健康"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"feel respected and purposeful","chinese":"感到受尊重和有目標"},{"english":"more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"stay motivated","chinese":"保持動力"},{"english":"improve their skills","chinese":"提升技能"},{"english":"contribute positively to","chinese":"對……作出正面貢獻"},{"english":"be considered a luxury","chinese":"被視為奢侈品"},{"english":"economic insecurity","chinese":"經濟不穩定"},{"english":"limits people's choices","chinese":"限制人們的選擇"},{"english":"Nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"essential, not decorative","chinese":"是必要的，不是裝飾性的"},{"english":"decent work","chinese":"體面的工作"},{"english":"one of the foundations of","chinese":"……的基礎之一"},{"english":"a healthier and more productive society","chinese":"更健康、更有生產力的社會"}]},"model-essay-45-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-45-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:45","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-45-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q45","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Public parks are often seen as pleasant but non-essential spaces, especially in cities facing pressure from population growth and economic competition. Some argue that this land would be more useful if it were converted into housing or commercial districts. I completely disagree with this view, because parks are essential to public health, social life, and the long-term sustainability of cities.","chinese":"公共公園常被視為令人愉快但並非必要的空間，尤其是在面對人口增長和經濟競爭壓力的城市中。 有些人認為，如果這些土地被改建成住宅區或商業區，會更有用途。 我完全不同意這個觀點，因為公園對公共健康、社交生活，以及城市的長遠可持續發展都是不可或缺的。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason for protecting public parks is that they provide a form of health support that buildings cannot replace. In crowded urban areas, many residents live in small apartments, work long hours, and have limited access to open space. Parks give people somewhere to walk, exercise, breathe fresh air, and recover from the pressure of city life. For example, a family living in a dense neighbourhood may not be able to afford private sports facilities, but a nearby park allows children to play safely and adults to stay active without spending money. If these spaces are replaced by apartments or offices, cities may become more crowded, more stressful, and less humane.","chinese":"保護公共公園最有力的理由是，它們提供了一種建築物無法取代的健康支持。 在擁擠的城市地區，許多居民住在狹小的公寓裡，工作時間很長，而且接觸開放空間的機會有限。 公園給人們一個可以散步、運動、呼吸新鮮空氣，並從城市生活壓力中恢復過來的地方 例如，一個住在人口密集社區的家庭，未必負擔得起私人運動設施，但附近的公園可以讓孩子安全玩耍，也讓成年人不用花錢便能保持活躍。 如果這些空間被公寓或辦公室取代，城市可能會變得更加擁擠、更令人感到壓力，也更缺乏人情味。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Public parks also strengthen communities and improve the quality of urban development. They are shared spaces where people from different ages and backgrounds can meet naturally, rather than remaining isolated in private homes or workplaces. This matters because a successful city is not simply a collection of houses and businesses; it is a living environment where people feel connected and safe. Moreover, parks can support the economy indirectly by making cities more attractive to residents, workers, and visitors. A city with only concrete, traffic, and commercial buildings may generate short-term profit, but it risks becoming a place people want to escape from rather than invest in.","chinese":"公共公園也能加強社區聯繫，並提升城市發展的質素。 它們是共享空間，讓不同年齡和背景的人可以自然地相遇，而不是一直被隔離在私人住宅或工作場所之中。 這一點很重要，因為一個成功的城市並不只是房屋和商業機構的集合；它是一個讓人們感到有聯繫和安全感的生活環境。 此外，公園也可以透過讓城市對居民、工作者和遊客更具吸引力，間接支持經濟。 一個只有混凝土、交通和商業建築的城市，或許能創造短期利潤，但它也有可能變成一個人們想逃離，而不是願意投資其中的地方。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I strongly disagree that public parks should be replaced by housing or business developments. While population growth and economic development are important, sacrificing green public spaces would damage health, weaken communities, and reduce the overall liveability of cities.","chinese":"總結來說，我強烈不同意公共公園應被住宅或商業發展取代。 雖然人口增長和經濟發展都很重要，但犧牲綠色公共空間將會損害健康、削弱社區，並降低城市整體的宜居程度。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"public parks","chinese":"公共公園"},{"english":"be seen as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"pleasant but non-essential spaces","chinese":"宜人但非必要的空間"},{"english":"especially in cities facing","chinese":"尤其在面對……的城市中"},{"english":"pressure from population growth","chinese":"來自人口增長的壓力"},{"english":"economic competition","chinese":"經濟競爭"},{"english":"be converted into","chinese":"被改建成"},{"english":"housing or commercial districts","chinese":"住宅或商業區"},{"english":"completely disagree with","chinese":"完全不同意……"},{"english":"essential to","chinese":"對……必不可少"},{"english":"public health","chinese":"公共健康"},{"english":"social life","chinese":"社交生活"},{"english":"long-term sustainability","chinese":"長遠可持續性"},{"english":"the strongest reason for","chinese":"……的最有力原因"},{"english":"protecting public parks","chinese":"保護公共公園"},{"english":"a form of health support","chinese":"一種健康支援"},{"english":"cannot replace","chinese":"不能取代"},{"english":"crowded urban areas","chinese":"擠迫的城市地區"},{"english":"small apartments","chinese":"小型住宅單位"},{"english":"work long hours","chinese":"長時間工作"},{"english":"limited access to","chinese":"接觸……的機會有限"},{"english":"open space","chinese":"開放空間"},{"english":"somewhere to","chinese":"可以……的地方"},{"english":"breathe fresh air","chinese":"呼吸新鮮空氣"},{"english":"recover from","chinese":"從……中恢復"},{"english":"pressure of city life","chinese":"城市生活的壓力"},{"english":"dense neighbourhood","chinese":"人口密集的社區"},{"english":"afford private sports facilities","chinese":"負擔私人運動設施"},{"english":"nearby park","chinese":"附近的公園"},{"english":"play safely","chinese":"安全地玩耍"},{"english":"stay active","chinese":"保持活動量"},{"english":"without spending money","chinese":"不用花錢"},{"english":"be replaced by","chinese":"被……取代"},{"english":"apartments or offices","chinese":"住宅單位或辦公室"},{"english":"more stressful","chinese":"更令人有壓力"},{"english":"less humane","chinese":"較不人性化"},{"english":"strengthen communities","chinese":"加強社區聯繫"},{"english":"improve the quality of","chinese":"改善……的質素"},{"english":"urban development","chinese":"城市發展"},{"english":"shared spaces","chinese":"共享空間"},{"english":"different ages and backgrounds","chinese":"不同年齡和背景"},{"english":"meet naturally","chinese":"自然地相遇"},{"english":"rather than remaining isolated","chinese":"而不是繼續孤立"},{"english":"private homes or workplaces","chinese":"私人住宅或工作場所"},{"english":"this matters because","chinese":"這很重要，因為……"},{"english":"successful city","chinese":"成功的城市"},{"english":"a collection of houses and businesses","chinese":"一堆住宅和商業機構"},{"english":"living environment","chinese":"生活環境"},{"english":"feel connected and safe","chinese":"感到有連繫和安全"},{"english":"support the economy indirectly","chinese":"間接支持經濟"},{"english":"make cities more attractive to","chinese":"令城市對……更有吸引力"},{"english":"residents, workers, and visitors","chinese":"居民、工人和遊客"},{"english":"commercial buildings","chinese":"商業大廈"},{"english":"generate short-term profit","chinese":"產生短期利潤"},{"english":"risk becoming","chinese":"有可能變成"},{"english":"escape from","chinese":"逃離"},{"english":"rather than invest in","chinese":"而不是投資於……"},{"english":"business developments","chinese":"商業發展項目"},{"english":"population growth","chinese":"人口增長"},{"english":"economic development","chinese":"經濟發展"},{"english":"sacrificing green public spaces","chinese":"犧牲綠色公共空間"},{"english":"damage health","chinese":"損害健康"},{"english":"weaken communities","chinese":"削弱社區"},{"english":"overall liveability","chinese":"整體宜居程度"}]},"model-essay-46-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-46-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:46","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-46-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q46","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many less economically developed nations, the movement of workers from villages to urban centres has become increasingly common. This trend is largely driven by the search for better employment and improved living standards, but it can also create serious pressure on both cities and rural communities.","chinese":"在許多經濟發展程度較低的國家，工人從鄉村遷移到城市中心的現象已變得越來越普遍。 這種趨勢主要是由尋找更好的就業機會和改善生活水平所推動，但它也可能對城市和農村社區造成嚴重壓力。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main reason people leave rural areas is that cities appear to offer a wider range of economic opportunities. In many villages, work is often limited to farming or small-scale manual labour, which may be seasonal, poorly paid, and vulnerable to weather or market changes. By contrast, cities usually have factories, service industries, construction projects, and informal businesses that seem to promise more stable incomes. For example, a young worker from a farming family may move to a capital city because even a low-paid job in a shop or factory can provide more regular cash than agricultural work. In this sense, migration is not simply a matter of ambition; for many people, it is a practical attempt to escape poverty.","chinese":"人們離開農村地區的主要原因是，城市看起來能提供更廣泛的經濟機會。 在許多村莊，工作往往局限於農業或小規模體力勞動，而這些工作可能具有季節性、薪酬低，並且容易受到天氣或市場變化的影響。 相比之下，城市通常有工廠、服務業、建築項目和非正式商業活動，而這些似乎能提供更穩定的收入。 例如，一位來自農民家庭的年輕工人可能會搬到首都城市，因為即使是在商店或工廠中一份低薪工作，也能比農業工作提供更穩定的現金收入。 從這個意義上說，遷移並不單純是野心的問題；對許多人而言，這是一種逃離貧窮的實際嘗試。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that urban areas are often associated with better public services. Cities tend to have more schools, hospitals, transport links, and training centres, so workers may believe that moving there will improve not only their own lives but also their children’s future prospects. This hope can be especially powerful when rural communities lack basic infrastructure.","chinese":"另一個原因是，城市地區通常與更好的公共服務聯繫在一起。 城市往往有更多學校、醫院、交通網絡和培訓中心，因此工人可能相信，搬到城市不但能改善自己的生活，也能改善子女未來的前景。 當農村社區缺乏基本基礎設施時，這種希望可能尤其強烈。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 3","english":"However, large-scale rural-to-urban migration can cause several problems. The most immediate one is overcrowding. When too many people arrive faster than housing, roads, and public services can expand, cities may develop slums, traffic congestion, poor sanitation, and higher living costs. At the same time, rural areas may suffer from a shortage of young and productive workers. If mostly young adults leave, villages are left with an ageing population and weaker local economies.","chinese":"然而，大規模的農村到城市遷移可能造成幾個問題。 最直接的一個問題是過度擁擠。 當太多人湧入的速度快過住房、道路和公共服務的擴展速度時，城市可能會出現貧民窟、交通擠塞、衛生條件差和生活成本上升等問題。 與此同時，農村地區可能會面臨年輕且有生產力的勞動人口短缺。 如果離開的主要是年輕成年人，村莊便會剩下老齡化人口，並且本地經濟會變得更薄弱"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, workers in developing countries often move to cities because they want better jobs and services. Nevertheless, this movement can lead to overcrowded cities and declining rural communities if it is not managed carefully.","chinese":"總結來說，發展中國家的工人經常遷移到城市，是因為他們想要更好的工作和服務。 然而，如果這種人口流動沒有得到妥善管理，它可能會導致城市過度擁擠，以及農村社區衰落。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"less economically developed nations","chinese":"經濟較不發達的國家"},{"english":"the movement of workers","chinese":"工人的流動"},{"english":"from villages to urban centres","chinese":"從鄉村到城市中心"},{"english":"has become increasingly common","chinese":"變得越來越普遍"},{"english":"this trend","chinese":"這個趨勢"},{"english":"largely driven by","chinese":"很大程度上由……推動"},{"english":"the search for","chinese":"尋找"},{"english":"better employment","chinese":"更好的就業機會"},{"english":"improved living standards","chinese":"改善了的生活水平"},{"english":"create serious pressure on","chinese":"對……造成嚴重壓力"},{"english":"rural communities","chinese":"農村社區"},{"english":"the main reason","chinese":"主要原因"},{"english":"leave rural areas","chinese":"離開農村地區"},{"english":"appear to offer","chinese":"似乎提供"},{"english":"a wider range of","chinese":"更廣泛的……"},{"english":"economic opportunities","chinese":"經濟機會"},{"english":"be limited to","chinese":"局限於"},{"english":"farming","chinese":"農業"},{"english":"small-scale manual labour","chinese":"小規模體力勞動"},{"english":"seasonal","chinese":"季節性的"},{"english":"poorly paid","chinese":"薪酬低的"},{"english":"vulnerable to","chinese":"容易受……影響"},{"english":"weather or market changes","chinese":"天氣或市場變化"},{"english":"By contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"service industries","chinese":"服務行業"},{"english":"construction projects","chinese":"建築項目"},{"english":"informal businesses","chinese":"非正式企業；非正規生意"},{"english":"seem to promise","chinese":"似乎承諾；似乎帶來"},{"english":"more stable incomes","chinese":"更穩定的收入"},{"english":"a young worker from","chinese":"來自……的年輕工人"},{"english":"farming family","chinese":"農民家庭"},{"english":"capital city","chinese":"首都城市"},{"english":"low-paid job","chinese":"低薪工作"},{"english":"provide more regular cash","chinese":"提供更穩定的現金收入"},{"english":"agricultural work","chinese":"農業工作"},{"english":"In this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"migration","chinese":"遷移；移居"},{"english":"not simply a matter of","chinese":"不只是……的問題"},{"english":"a practical attempt to","chinese":"實際嘗試去"},{"english":"escape poverty","chinese":"擺脫貧窮"},{"english":"Another reason is that","chinese":"另一個原因是"},{"english":"urban areas","chinese":"城市地區"},{"english":"be associated with","chinese":"與……有關"},{"english":"public services","chinese":"公共服務"},{"english":"tend to have","chinese":"往往有"},{"english":"transport links","chinese":"交通連接"},{"english":"training centres","chinese":"培訓中心"},{"english":"improve not only...but also...","chinese":"不但改善……，也改善……"},{"english":"future prospects","chinese":"未來前景"},{"english":"especially powerful","chinese":"特別強烈"},{"english":"lack basic infrastructure","chinese":"缺乏基本基礎設施"},{"english":"large-scale rural-to-urban migration","chinese":"大規模由農村到城市的遷移"},{"english":"cause several problems","chinese":"造成幾個問題"},{"english":"the most immediate one","chinese":"最即時的一個"},{"english":"overcrowding","chinese":"過度擠迫"},{"english":"arrive faster than","chinese":"到達速度快過"},{"english":"public services can expand","chinese":"公共服務能夠擴展"},{"english":"develop slums","chinese":"形成貧民窟"},{"english":"traffic congestion","chinese":"交通擠塞"},{"english":"poor sanitation","chinese":"惡劣衛生環境"},{"english":"higher living costs","chinese":"更高生活成本"},{"english":"At the same time","chinese":"與此同時"},{"english":"suffer from a shortage of","chinese":"面對……短缺"},{"english":"productive workers","chinese":"有生產力的工人"},{"english":"mostly young adults","chinese":"主要是年輕成年人"},{"english":"are left with","chinese":"只剩下；留下"},{"english":"an ageing population","chinese":"人口老化"},{"english":"weaker local economies","chinese":"較弱的本地經濟"},{"english":"developing countries","chinese":"發展中國家"},{"english":"move to cities","chinese":"搬到城市"},{"english":"better jobs and services","chinese":"更好的工作和服務"},{"english":"Nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"lead to","chinese":"導致"},{"english":"overcrowded cities","chinese":"過度擠迫的城市"},{"english":"declining rural communities","chinese":"衰落中的農村社區"},{"english":"if it is not managed carefully","chinese":"如果沒有妥善管理"}]},"model-essay-46-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-46-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:46","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-46-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q46","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Environmental damage is no longer a local inconvenience but a global crisis, affecting climate, biodiversity and public health. Some argue that wealthy countries should shoulder this burden because they have created much of the problem and have the resources to fix it. I understand this view, but I disagree that poorer nations should bear no responsibility at all.","chinese":"環境破壞已不再只是局部不便，而是一場影響氣候、生物多樣性和公共健康的全球危機 有人認為富裕國家應該承擔這項責任，因為它們造成了問題中的很大一部分，也擁有解決問題的資源 我理解這種觀點，但我不同意較貧困國家完全不需要承擔任何責任。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"There is a strong case for placing heavier responsibility on rich countries. Many of them built their prosperity through decades of industrial expansion, during which coal, oil and heavy manufacturing were treated as engines of growth. As a result, they enjoyed the benefits of development while leaving a large environmental footprint. Moreover, richer governments usually have the money, technology and expertise needed to invest in renewable energy, cleaner transport and climate-resilient infrastructure. For example, a wealthy country can subsidise electric buses or build flood defences without sacrificing basic services. In this sense, asking rich nations to lead is not charity; it is a fair return for the advantages they have already gained.","chinese":"把更重的責任放在富裕國家身上，是有很強道理的。 它們當中許多國家的繁榮，都是透過數十年的工業擴張建立起來的；在這段期間，煤炭、石油和重工業都被視為經濟增長的引擎。 結果是，它們享受了發展帶來的好處，同時也留下了巨大的環境足跡。 此外，較富裕的政府通常擁有投資可再生能源、更清潔交通和具氣候韌性基礎建設所需的資金、科技和專業知識。 例如，一個富裕國家可以資助電動巴士，或興建防洪設施，而不需要犧牲基本公共服務。 從這個意義上說，要求富裕國家帶頭行動並不是慈善，而是它們對已經獲得的利益作出合理回報。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"However, it does not follow that poorer countries can step aside. Environmental protection is not a spectator sport. If developing nations ignore pollution controls, destroy forests for short-term profit or allow cities to grow without proper waste systems, the damage will still be real and often irreversible. A poorer country may not be able to fund advanced technology, but it can still enforce basic rules, protect natural resources and choose development plans that do not poison its own land and water. To say that responsibility belongs only to rich nations also sends a dangerous message: that poverty gives governments permission to repeat the same mistakes that wealthier nations once made.","chinese":"然而，這並不代表較貧困國家就可以置身事外。 環境保護不是一項旁觀者運動。 如果發展中國家忽視污染管制、為短期利益而破壞森林，或容許城市在沒有完善廢物處理系統的情況下擴張，造成的破壞仍然是真實的，而且往往是不可逆轉的。 一個較貧困的國家未必有能力資助先進科技，但它仍然可以執行基本規則、保護自然資源，並選擇不會毒害自身土地和水源的發展計劃。 說責任只屬於富裕國家，也會傳遞一個危險訊息：貧窮似乎讓政府有權重複富裕國家曾經犯下的同樣錯誤。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, rich countries should lead because they have greater historical responsibility and stronger capacity. Nevertheless, I do not agree that poorer nations are free from duty. Global environmental problems require unequal contributions but shared responsibility; otherwise, the world is trying to clean one river while muddying another.","chinese":"總結來說，富裕國家應該帶頭，因為它們承擔更大的歷史責任，也擁有更強的能力。 然而，我不同意較貧困國家可以完全免除責任。 全球環境問題需要不平等的貢獻，但也需要共同承擔責任；否則，世界就像一邊清理一條河流，另一邊卻把另一條河弄髒。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"environmental damage","chinese":"環境破壞"},{"english":"no longer a local inconvenience","chinese":"不再是地方性不便"},{"english":"global crisis","chinese":"全球危機"},{"english":"affecting climate, biodiversity and public health","chinese":"影響氣候、生物多樣性和公共健康"},{"english":"wealthy countries","chinese":"富裕國家"},{"english":"shoulder this burden","chinese":"承擔這個重擔"},{"english":"created much of the problem","chinese":"造成了問題的大部分"},{"english":"have the resources to","chinese":"有資源去……"},{"english":"poorer nations","chinese":"較貧窮國家"},{"english":"bear no responsibility at all","chinese":"完全不用承擔責任"},{"english":"a strong case for","chinese":"有充分理由支持……"},{"english":"placing heavier responsibility on","chinese":"將更大責任放在……身上"},{"english":"built their prosperity through","chinese":"透過……建立繁榮"},{"english":"decades of industrial expansion","chinese":"數十年的工業擴張"},{"english":"heavy manufacturing","chinese":"重工業製造"},{"english":"engines of growth","chinese":"增長引擎"},{"english":"enjoyed the benefits of development","chinese":"享受發展帶來的好處"},{"english":"environmental footprint","chinese":"環境足跡；環境影響"},{"english":"technology and expertise","chinese":"技術和專業知識"},{"english":"renewable energy","chinese":"可再生能源"},{"english":"cleaner transport","chinese":"較清潔的交通"},{"english":"climate-resilient infrastructure","chinese":"具氣候韌性的基礎設施"},{"english":"subsidise electric buses","chinese":"資助電動巴士"},{"english":"build flood defences","chinese":"建設防洪設施"},{"english":"without sacrificing","chinese":"而不犧牲……"},{"english":"basic services","chinese":"基本服務"},{"english":"asking rich nations to lead","chinese":"要求富裕國家帶頭"},{"english":"a fair return for","chinese":"對……的公平回報"},{"english":"advantages they have already gained","chinese":"它們已經獲得的優勢"},{"english":"it does not follow that","chinese":"這並不代表……"},{"english":"step aside","chinese":"置身事外"},{"english":"environmental protection","chinese":"環境保護"},{"english":"spectator sport","chinese":"旁觀者遊戲"},{"english":"developing nations","chinese":"發展中國家"},{"english":"ignore pollution controls","chinese":"忽視污染管制"},{"english":"destroy forests for short-term profit","chinese":"為短期利益破壞森林"},{"english":"proper waste systems","chinese":"妥善的廢物處理系統"},{"english":"often irreversible","chinese":"往往不可逆轉"},{"english":"advanced technology","chinese":"先進技術"},{"english":"enforce basic rules","chinese":"執行基本規則"},{"english":"protect natural resources","chinese":"保護自然資源"},{"english":"development plans","chinese":"發展計劃"},{"english":"poison its own land and water","chinese":"污染自己的土地和水源"},{"english":"belongs only to","chinese":"只屬於……"},{"english":"sends a dangerous message","chinese":"傳達危險的信息"},{"english":"gives governments permission to","chinese":"給予政府許可去……"},{"english":"repeat the same mistakes","chinese":"重複同樣錯誤"},{"english":"historical responsibility","chinese":"歷史責任"},{"english":"stronger capacity","chinese":"更強的能力"},{"english":"free from duty","chinese":"免於責任"},{"english":"unequal contributions","chinese":"不均等的貢獻"},{"english":"shared responsibility","chinese":"共同責任"},{"english":"muddying another","chinese":"弄濁另一條河"}]},"model-essay-47-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-47-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:47","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-47-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q47","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In contemporary workplaces, promotion is often treated as a visible sign that an employee’s effort has been recognised. People are strongly motivated by it because it usually brings better pay, higher status and greater control over their professional future. However, hard work is also shaped by less tangible factors, such as purpose, security and workplace culture.","chinese":"在當代職場中，晉升通常被視為員工努力得到認可的一個明顯標誌。 人們會受到晉升的強烈激勵，因為它通常帶來更高的薪酬、更高的地位，以及對自己職業未來更大的掌控權。 然而，努力工作也受到一些較不具體的因素影響，例如目標感、安全感和職場文化。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason promotion is so powerful is that it connects effort with material and social reward. A more senior position often means a higher salary, better benefits and a stronger sense of financial stability, so employees see it as a practical route to improving their quality of life. Beyond money, promotion also carries psychological value. Being promoted suggests that a person’s judgement, discipline and competence have been noticed by managers and colleagues. This public recognition can be deeply motivating because many workers want to feel that their sacrifices have led somewhere. For example, an employee who regularly works late to complete projects may view promotion not simply as a new title, but as proof that their commitment has not disappeared into the background.","chinese":"晉升之所以如此有力量，第一個原因是它把努力與物質和社會回報連結起來。 一個更高級的職位通常意味著更高的薪金、更好的福利，以及更強的經濟穩定感，因此員工會把它視為改善生活質素的一條實際途徑。 除了金錢之外，晉升也具有心理上的價值。 獲得晉升意味著一個人的判斷力、自律能力和工作能力已經被管理層和同事看見。 這種公開的認可能夠帶來很深的激勵作用，因為許多員工都希望感覺到自己的付出並沒有白費，而是走向了某個成果。 例如，一位經常加班完成項目的員工，可能不會單純把晉升看成一個新的職銜，而會把它看作自己投入和付出沒有被埋沒的證明。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Nevertheless, promotion is not the only force that pushes people to work hard. One major factor is meaningful work. When employees believe their tasks benefit customers, students, patients or society in general, they are more likely to stay committed even without an immediate reward. Another important influence is the working environment. Supportive managers, fair rules and respectful colleagues can make people willing to raise their standards, whereas a toxic workplace can drain motivation even when promotion is possible. Personal ambition also plays a role: some people work hard because they want to master a skill, build confidence or prove to themselves that they can meet demanding goals.","chinese":"然而，晉升並不是推動人們努力工作的唯一力量。 其中一個重要因素是有意義的工作。 當員工相信自己的工作能夠令顧客、學生、病人或整個社會受益時，即使沒有即時回報，他們也更有可能保持投入。 另一個重要影響因素是工作環境。 支持員工的管理者、公平的規則和互相尊重的同事，能夠使人願意提高自己的標準；相反，即使存在晉升機會，有毒的職場環境也會耗盡人的動力。 個人抱負同樣扮演著一定角色：有些人努力工作，是因為他們想掌握一項技能、建立自信，或者向自己證明他們能夠達成具挑戰性的目標。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, promotion motivates people because it offers money, recognition and a clearer career path. Still, lasting effort also depends on purpose, fairness, personal growth and the emotional atmosphere of the workplace.","chinese":"總結來說，晉升能夠激勵人們，是因為它提供金錢、認可以及更清晰的職業道路。 不過，持久的努力也取決於目標感、公平、個人成長，以及職場中的情緒氛圍。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"contemporary workplaces","chinese":"現代職場"},{"english":"be treated as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"a visible sign that","chinese":"……的明顯標誌"},{"english":"effort has been recognised","chinese":"努力得到認可"},{"english":"strongly motivated by","chinese":"受到……強烈激勵"},{"english":"brings better pay","chinese":"帶來更高薪酬"},{"english":"higher status","chinese":"更高地位"},{"english":"greater control over","chinese":"對……有更大掌控"},{"english":"professional future","chinese":"職業前途"},{"english":"be shaped by","chinese":"受……塑造"},{"english":"less tangible factors","chinese":"較不具體的因素"},{"english":"workplace culture","chinese":"職場文化"},{"english":"the first reason","chinese":"第一個原因"},{"english":"connects effort with","chinese":"將努力與……連繫起來"},{"english":"material and social reward","chinese":"物質和社會回報"},{"english":"a more senior position","chinese":"更高級的職位"},{"english":"better benefits","chinese":"更好的福利"},{"english":"a stronger sense of","chinese":"更強的……感覺"},{"english":"financial stability","chinese":"財務穩定"},{"english":"a practical route to","chinese":"通往……的實際途徑"},{"english":"improving their quality of life","chinese":"改善生活質素"},{"english":"beyond money","chinese":"除了金錢之外"},{"english":"carries psychological value","chinese":"具有心理價值"},{"english":"being promoted","chinese":"獲得晉升"},{"english":"judgement, discipline and competence","chinese":"判斷力、紀律和能力"},{"english":"have been noticed by","chinese":"被……注意到"},{"english":"managers and colleagues","chinese":"經理和同事"},{"english":"public recognition","chinese":"公開認可"},{"english":"deeply motivating","chinese":"非常有激勵作用"},{"english":"feel that","chinese":"感覺到"},{"english":"their sacrifices have led somewhere","chinese":"他們的犧牲帶來了成果"},{"english":"regularly works late","chinese":"經常工作至很晚"},{"english":"complete projects","chinese":"完成項目"},{"english":"may view promotion as","chinese":"可能把晉升視為"},{"english":"not simply as","chinese":"不只是作為"},{"english":"a new title","chinese":"新職銜"},{"english":"proof that","chinese":"……的證明"},{"english":"commitment","chinese":"投入；承擔"},{"english":"disappear into the background","chinese":"被埋沒；消失在背景中"},{"english":"Nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"the only force that","chinese":"唯一推動……的力量"},{"english":"pushes people to","chinese":"推動人們去"},{"english":"meaningful work","chinese":"有意義的工作"},{"english":"benefit customers","chinese":"令顧客受惠"},{"english":"society in general","chinese":"整個社會"},{"english":"more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"stay committed","chinese":"保持投入"},{"english":"without an immediate reward","chinese":"即使沒有即時回報"},{"english":"another important influence","chinese":"另一個重要影響因素"},{"english":"working environment","chinese":"工作環境"},{"english":"supportive managers","chinese":"支持員工的經理"},{"english":"fair rules","chinese":"公平規則"},{"english":"respectful colleagues","chinese":"尊重別人的同事"},{"english":"raise their standards","chinese":"提高自己的標準"},{"english":"a toxic workplace","chinese":"有毒的職場；惡劣職場"},{"english":"drain motivation","chinese":"消耗動力"},{"english":"even when promotion is possible","chinese":"即使有晉升機會"},{"english":"personal ambition","chinese":"個人抱負"},{"english":"plays a role","chinese":"發揮作用"},{"english":"master a skill","chinese":"掌握一項技能"},{"english":"build confidence","chinese":"建立信心"},{"english":"prove to themselves that","chinese":"向自己證明"},{"english":"meet demanding goals","chinese":"達成高要求目標"},{"english":"a clearer career path","chinese":"更清晰的事業發展路徑"},{"english":"lasting effort","chinese":"持久努力"},{"english":"depends on","chinese":"取決於"},{"english":"personal growth","chinese":"個人成長"},{"english":"emotional atmosphere","chinese":"情緒氛圍"}]},"model-essay-47-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-47-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:47","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-47-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q47","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Environmental issues have become one of the defining challenges of the modern world. While local governments clearly have a role in protecting rivers, forests and public health, I completely agree that the most serious environmental problems must be addressed internationally because their causes and consequences do not stop at national borders.","chinese":"環境問題已成為現代世界其中一項最具代表性的挑戰。 雖然地方政府在保護河流、森林和公共健康方面明顯有其角色， 但我完全同意，最嚴重的環境問題必須在國際層面處理，因為它們的成因和後果都不會止於國界。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that many forms of environmental damage are borderless by nature. Climate change, air pollution, ocean waste and the loss of biodiversity are not problems that one country can solve behind its own walls. For example, a nation may spend heavily on clean energy, but its efforts will have limited impact if neighbouring countries continue to burn large amounts of fossil fuels. Similarly, plastic dumped into one part of the ocean can be carried by currents and damage marine life thousands of miles away. In this sense, treating global environmental problems as purely domestic matters is like trying to clean one room while smoke is still entering from the rest of the house. International cooperation is therefore essential because it allows countries to set common targets and move in the same direction.","chinese":"第一個原因是，許多形式的環境破壞本質上都是沒有國界的。 氣候變化、空氣污染、海洋垃圾和生物多樣性喪失，都不是一個國家能夠在自己的國界內單獨解決的問題。 例如，一個國家可能在清潔能源方面投入大量資金，但如果鄰近國家繼續燃燒大量化石燃料，它的努力所產生的影響仍然會十分有限。 同樣地，被傾倒到海洋某一處的塑膠垃圾，可能會被洋流帶走，並傷害數千英里以外的海洋生物。 從這個意義上說，把全球環境問題視為純粹的國內事務，就像只清潔一個房間，卻仍然讓煙霧從屋子的其他地方不斷飄進來。 因此，國際合作是必不可少的，因為它能讓各國設定共同目標，並朝著同一方向前進。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important reason is that global action can distribute responsibility more fairly. Poorer countries are often the most exposed to floods, droughts and food insecurity, even though richer industrialised nations have historically produced far more pollution. If each country is left to act alone, wealthier states may protect themselves while weaker ones are left carrying an unfair burden. International agreements, by contrast, can encourage financial support, technology sharing and joint monitoring. This makes environmental protection not only more effective, but also more just.","chinese":"另一個重要原因是，全球行動能夠更公平地分配責任。 較貧困的國家往往最容易受到洪水、乾旱和糧食不安全的影響，儘管歷史上較富裕的工業化國家製造了更多污染。 如果每個國家都被迫單獨行動，較富裕的國家可能能夠保護自己，而較弱小的國家則會被迫承擔不公平的負擔。 相比之下，國際協議能夠促進資金支援、技術分享和共同監察。 這使環境保護不但更有效，也更公平。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully agree that global environmental problems should be dealt with internationally rather than domestically. National policies are useful, but without coordinated international action, they are only small patches on a much larger wound. The planet is shared, and its protection must be shared as well.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意全球環境問題應該在國際層面處理，而不是只在國內層面處理。 國家政策是有用的，但如果沒有協調一致的國際行動，它們只是在一個更大傷口上的小小補丁。 地球是共同擁有的，因此保護地球的責任也必須共同承擔。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"environmental issues","chinese":"環境問題"},{"english":"defining challenges","chinese":"具代表性的重大挑戰"},{"english":"modern world","chinese":"現代世界"},{"english":"local governments","chinese":"地方政府"},{"english":"have a role in","chinese":"在……中有角色"},{"english":"protecting rivers, forests and public health","chinese":"保護河流、森林和公共健康"},{"english":"the most serious environmental problems","chinese":"最嚴重的環境問題"},{"english":"be addressed internationally","chinese":"在國際層面處理"},{"english":"causes and consequences","chinese":"成因和後果"},{"english":"stop at national borders","chinese":"止於國界"},{"english":"environmental damage","chinese":"環境破壞"},{"english":"borderless by nature","chinese":"本質上不受國界限制"},{"english":"climate change","chinese":"氣候變化"},{"english":"air pollution","chinese":"空氣污染"},{"english":"ocean waste","chinese":"海洋廢物"},{"english":"the loss of biodiversity","chinese":"生物多樣性喪失"},{"english":"behind its own walls","chinese":"在自己的圍牆內"},{"english":"spend heavily on","chinese":"大量投放資金於……"},{"english":"clean energy","chinese":"清潔能源"},{"english":"have limited impact","chinese":"影響有限"},{"english":"neighbouring countries","chinese":"鄰近國家"},{"english":"burn large amounts of fossil fuels","chinese":"燃燒大量化石燃料"},{"english":"similarly","chinese":"同樣地"},{"english":"be carried by currents","chinese":"被水流帶走"},{"english":"marine life","chinese":"海洋生物"},{"english":"thousands of miles away","chinese":"數千英里之外"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"purely domestic matters","chinese":"純粹國內事務"},{"english":"trying to clean one room","chinese":"嘗試只清潔一個房間"},{"english":"smoke is still entering","chinese":"煙仍然進入"},{"english":"the rest of the house","chinese":"屋內其餘部分"},{"english":"international cooperation","chinese":"國際合作"},{"english":"set common targets","chinese":"訂立共同目標"},{"english":"move in the same direction","chinese":"朝同一方向前進"},{"english":"global action","chinese":"全球行動"},{"english":"distribute responsibility more fairly","chinese":"更公平地分配責任"},{"english":"be exposed to","chinese":"面對……的風險最大；暴露於……"},{"english":"floods","chinese":"水災"},{"english":"droughts","chinese":"旱災"},{"english":"food insecurity","chinese":"糧食不安全"},{"english":"richer industrialised nations","chinese":"較富裕的工業化國家"},{"english":"historically produced","chinese":"在歷史上產生"},{"english":"far more pollution","chinese":"多得多的污染"},{"english":"be left to act alone","chinese":"被迫各自單獨行動"},{"english":"wealthier states","chinese":"較富裕國家"},{"english":"protect themselves","chinese":"保護自己"},{"english":"weaker ones","chinese":"較弱勢的國家；較弱勢者"},{"english":"be left carrying","chinese":"被留下承擔"},{"english":"unfair burden","chinese":"不公平負擔"},{"english":"international agreements","chinese":"國際協議"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"financial support","chinese":"財政支援"},{"english":"technology sharing","chinese":"技術共享"},{"english":"joint monitoring","chinese":"共同監察"},{"english":"not only more effective","chinese":"不但更有效"},{"english":"more just","chinese":"更公正"},{"english":"be dealt with internationally","chinese":"在國際層面處理"},{"english":"rather than domestically","chinese":"而不是在國內層面"},{"english":"national policies","chinese":"國家政策"},{"english":"coordinated international action","chinese":"協調一致的國際行動"},{"english":"small patches on","chinese":"……上的小補丁"},{"english":"larger wound","chinese":"更大的傷口"},{"english":"the planet is shared","chinese":"地球是共享的"},{"english":"its protection must be shared","chinese":"對它的保護也必須共同承擔"}]},"model-essay-48-ielts-direct-question":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-48-ielts-direct-question","essayKey":"direct-question:48","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-48-ielts-direct-question","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/direct-question/EdmundBd9Dir-Q48","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Choosing a career is no longer simply a matter of personal ambition; for many adults, it is directly connected to the welfare of the people who depend on them. I believe that money is undoubtedly an important factor when selecting a job, because a stable income gives a family protection and dignity. However, other considerations, especially health, suitability and long-term development, must also be taken seriously.","chinese":"選擇職業已不再只是個人抱負的問題；對許多成年人來說，這與依賴他們的人的福祉直接相關。 我認為，選擇工作時金錢無疑是一個重要因素，因為穩定的收入能給家庭帶來保障和尊嚴。 然而，其他考慮因素，尤其是健康、適合程度和長遠發展，也必須被認真看待。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Income matters because family security usually begins with basic financial stability. A person who earns enough to pay for housing, food, education and medical care is less likely to expose their household to constant anxiety. This is particularly true for parents, whose career choices can affect not only their own comfort but also their children’s opportunities. For example, a father or mother may prefer a creative but poorly paid job, but if that income cannot cover rent or school expenses, the whole family may be forced to live under unnecessary pressure. In this sense, money is not greed; it is a safety net.","chinese":"收入很重要，因為家庭安全通常始於基本的財務穩定。 一個能賺取足夠收入去支付住房、食物、教育和醫療費用的人，較不容易讓家庭長期處於焦慮之中。 這對父母來說尤其如此，因為他們的職業選擇不但會影響自己的生活舒適度，也會影響子女的機會。 例如，一位父親或母親可能較喜歡一份有創意但薪酬低的工作，但如果那份收入無法支付租金或學費，整個家庭便可能被迫承受不必要的壓力。 從這個角度來看，金錢並不是貪婪；它是一張安全網。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Nevertheless, a job should not be chosen by salary alone. One major factor is work-life balance, because a high-paying occupation can damage family life if it demands excessive hours or creates severe stress. A well-paid employee who is always exhausted, absent or emotionally unavailable may fail to provide the very security that money was supposed to create. Another important factor is whether the job suits the person’s abilities and offers room for growth. When people work in a field where they can improve their skills, gain experience and build a sustainable career, they are more likely to remain employable and confident in the long run.","chinese":"然而，一份工作不應該單憑薪金來選擇。 其中一個主要因素是工作與生活平衡，因為一份高薪工作如果要求過長工時或造成嚴重壓力，便可能損害家庭生活。 一位收入很高但總是疲憊、缺席或情感上無法投入的員工，可能反而無法提供金錢本應帶來的那種安全感。 另一個重要因素是，這份工作是否適合個人的能力，並能否提供成長空間。 當人們在一個能提升技能、累積經驗並建立可持續職業生涯的領域工作時，他們長遠而言更有可能保持就業能力和自信。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I believe money is a vital factor when choosing a job, especially for those with family responsibilities. However, the best career choice is one that provides financial stability without sacrificing health, family relationships or future development.","chinese":"總結來說，我認為金錢是選擇工作時一個至關重要的因素，尤其對有家庭責任的人而言更是如此。 然而，最好的職業選擇，是既能提供財務穩定，又不犧牲健康、家庭關係或未來發展的選擇。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"choosing a career","chinese":"選擇事業"},{"english":"no longer simply a matter of","chinese":"不再只是……的問題"},{"english":"personal ambition","chinese":"個人抱負"},{"english":"directly connected to","chinese":"與……直接相關"},{"english":"the welfare of","chinese":"……的福祉"},{"english":"depend on them","chinese":"依靠他們"},{"english":"undoubtedly","chinese":"毫無疑問"},{"english":"an important factor","chinese":"重要因素"},{"english":"selecting a job","chinese":"選擇工作"},{"english":"a stable income","chinese":"穩定收入"},{"english":"protection and dignity","chinese":"保障和尊嚴"},{"english":"other considerations","chinese":"其他考慮因素"},{"english":"long-term development","chinese":"長遠發展"},{"english":"be taken seriously","chinese":"被認真看待"},{"english":"income matters","chinese":"收入很重要"},{"english":"family security","chinese":"家庭保障"},{"english":"begins with","chinese":"始於"},{"english":"basic financial stability","chinese":"基本財務穩定"},{"english":"earns enough to","chinese":"賺取足夠金錢去"},{"english":"pay for housing","chinese":"支付住屋開支"},{"english":"medical care","chinese":"醫療護理"},{"english":"less likely to","chinese":"較不可能"},{"english":"expose their household to","chinese":"使家庭面對"},{"english":"constant anxiety","chinese":"持續焦慮"},{"english":"particularly true for","chinese":"對……尤其如此"},{"english":"career choices","chinese":"事業選擇"},{"english":"affect not only...but also...","chinese":"不但影響……，也影響……"},{"english":"own comfort","chinese":"自己的安穩"},{"english":"children's opportunities","chinese":"子女的機會"},{"english":"may prefer","chinese":"可能較喜歡"},{"english":"a creative but poorly paid job","chinese":"有創意但薪酬低的工作"},{"english":"cover rent","chinese":"支付租金"},{"english":"school expenses","chinese":"學校開支"},{"english":"be forced to","chinese":"被迫"},{"english":"live under unnecessary pressure","chinese":"在不必要的壓力下生活"},{"english":"In this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"greed","chinese":"貪婪"},{"english":"a safety net","chinese":"安全網"},{"english":"Nevertheless","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"be chosen by salary alone","chinese":"只按薪酬選擇"},{"english":"one major factor","chinese":"一個主要因素"},{"english":"work-life balance","chinese":"工作與生活平衡"},{"english":"high-paying occupation","chinese":"高薪職業"},{"english":"damage family life","chinese":"損害家庭生活"},{"english":"demands excessive hours","chinese":"要求過長工時"},{"english":"creates severe stress","chinese":"造成嚴重壓力"},{"english":"well-paid employee","chinese":"高薪員工"},{"english":"always exhausted","chinese":"經常精疲力竭"},{"english":"emotionally unavailable","chinese":"情感上無法投入的"},{"english":"fail to provide","chinese":"未能提供"},{"english":"the very security that","chinese":"正正是……的保障"},{"english":"be supposed to","chinese":"本應"},{"english":"suits the person's abilities","chinese":"適合那個人的能力"},{"english":"offers room for growth","chinese":"提供成長空間"},{"english":"work in a field where","chinese":"在一個……的領域工作"},{"english":"improve their skills","chinese":"提升技能"},{"english":"gain experience","chinese":"累積經驗"},{"english":"build a sustainable career","chinese":"建立可持續的事業"},{"english":"more likely to remain employable","chinese":"更有可能保持就業能力"},{"english":"confident in the long run","chinese":"長遠而言更有信心"},{"english":"a vital factor","chinese":"關鍵因素"},{"english":"family responsibilities","chinese":"家庭責任"},{"english":"the best career choice","chinese":"最佳事業選擇"},{"english":"provides financial stability","chinese":"提供財務穩定"},{"english":"without sacrificing","chinese":"不犧牲"},{"english":"family relationships","chinese":"家庭關係"},{"english":"future development","chinese":"未來發展"}]},"model-essay-48-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-48-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:48","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-48-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q48","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Air pollution has become a serious concern in many parts of the world, and aviation is often criticised because aircraft burn large amounts of fuel. However, I completely disagree with the view that restricting air travel is the only way to prevent this problem. Such a policy focuses too narrowly on one source of pollution, while more effective and balanced solutions are available.","chinese":"空氣污染已成為世界許多地方的嚴重問題，而航空業經常受到批評，因為飛機會燃燒大量燃料。 然而，我完全不同意限制航空旅行是防止這個問題的唯一方法這一觀點。 這樣的政策過於狹窄地集中在其中一個污染來源上，而其實還有更有效和更平衡的解決方案。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that air pollution is produced by many everyday activities, not by aviation alone. Cars, lorries, factories, power stations and construction sites can all release harmful gases or particles into the air. If governments simply limit flights while allowing old vehicles to run, industrial plants to operate with weak standards and cities to depend on dirty energy, the air will remain polluted. For example, a city with fewer international flights may still suffer from thick smog if millions of commuters drive petrol cars every day. Blaming air travel alone is like cleaning one window while leaving the rest of the house covered in dust.","chinese":"第一個原因是，空氣污染是由許多日常活動造成的，而不只是由航空業造成。 汽車、貨車、工廠、發電站和建築工地都可能向空氣中釋放有害氣體或微粒。 如果政府只是限制航班，卻容許舊車繼續行駛、工業廠房以寬鬆標準運作，以及城市繼續依賴污染性能源，空氣仍然會受到污染。 例如，一個國際航班較少的城市，如果每天仍有數百萬通勤者駕駛汽油車，仍然可能受到濃厚煙霧的困擾。 只責怪航空旅行，就像只清潔一扇窗，卻讓房子的其他部分仍然滿是灰塵。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"A better approach is to reduce pollution across the whole transport and energy system. Governments can invest in reliable public transport, encourage electric vehicles, tighten emissions standards for factories and shift electricity production towards cleaner sources. These measures would affect people’s daily habits and industrial behaviour, so their impact would be far broader than simply discouraging people from flying. At the same time, the aviation industry itself can be pushed to improve fuel efficiency and adopt cleaner technology, instead of being treated as a problem that can only be solved by restriction. This is more practical because air travel also supports business, tourism and family connections across long distances.","chinese":"更好的做法是在整個交通和能源系統中減少污染。 政府可以投資可靠的公共交通、鼓勵使用電動車、收緊工廠的排放標準，並將發電轉向更清潔的來源。 這些措施會影響人們的日常習慣和工業行為，因此它們的影響會比單純勸阻人們乘飛機更加廣泛。 同時，航空業本身也可以被推動去提高燃油效率並採用更清潔的技術，而不是被視為一個只能透過限制來解決的問題。 這樣做更實際，因為航空旅行也支撐著商業、旅遊，以及跨越長距離的家庭聯繫。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, restricting air travel may play a small role in reducing emissions, but it is certainly not the only way to tackle air pollution. I strongly believe that cleaner cities require wider reforms in transport, industry and energy, rather than a narrow focus on flights alone.","chinese":"總結來說，限制航空旅行或許在減少排放方面能發揮一小部分作用，但它絕對不是處理空氣污染的唯一方法。 我強烈認為，更清潔的城市需要在交通、工業和能源方面進行更廣泛的改革，而不是只狹隘地集中於航班本身。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"air pollution","chinese":"空氣污染"},{"english":"serious concern","chinese":"嚴重憂慮"},{"english":"in many parts of the world","chinese":"在世界很多地方"},{"english":"aviation","chinese":"航空業"},{"english":"be often criticised","chinese":"經常受到批評"},{"english":"burn large amounts of fuel","chinese":"燃燒大量燃料"},{"english":"restrict air travel","chinese":"限制航空旅遊"},{"english":"the only way to","chinese":"……的唯一方法"},{"english":"prevent this problem","chinese":"防止這個問題"},{"english":"such a policy","chinese":"這樣的政策"},{"english":"focus too narrowly on","chinese":"過於狹窄地集中於……"},{"english":"source of pollution","chinese":"污染來源"},{"english":"balanced solutions","chinese":"平衡的解決方法"},{"english":"be available","chinese":"可供使用；存在"},{"english":"be produced by","chinese":"由……產生"},{"english":"everyday activities","chinese":"日常活動"},{"english":"aviation alone","chinese":"單靠航空業"},{"english":"cars, lorries, factories, power stations and construction sites","chinese":"汽車、貨車、工廠、發電廠和建築地盤"},{"english":"release harmful gases","chinese":"釋放有害氣體"},{"english":"particles","chinese":"微粒"},{"english":"into the air","chinese":"進入空氣中"},{"english":"simply limit flights","chinese":"只是限制航班"},{"english":"allowing old vehicles to run","chinese":"允許舊車繼續行駛"},{"english":"industrial plants","chinese":"工業廠房"},{"english":"operate with weak standards","chinese":"在低標準下運作"},{"english":"depend on dirty energy","chinese":"依賴污染能源"},{"english":"remain polluted","chinese":"仍然受污染"},{"english":"fewer international flights","chinese":"較少國際航班"},{"english":"suffer from","chinese":"受……困擾"},{"english":"thick smog","chinese":"濃厚煙霧"},{"english":"millions of commuters","chinese":"數以百萬計的通勤人士"},{"english":"petrol cars","chinese":"汽油車"},{"english":"blaming air travel alone","chinese":"單單責怪航空旅遊"},{"english":"cleaning one window","chinese":"清潔一扇窗"},{"english":"the rest of the house","chinese":"屋內其餘部分"},{"english":"covered in dust","chinese":"滿佈灰塵"},{"english":"a better approach","chinese":"更好的方法"},{"english":"reduce pollution across","chinese":"在整個……中減少污染"},{"english":"whole transport and energy system","chinese":"整個交通和能源系統"},{"english":"reliable public transport","chinese":"可靠的公共交通"},{"english":"encourage electric vehicles","chinese":"鼓勵使用電動車"},{"english":"tighten emissions standards","chinese":"收緊排放標準"},{"english":"emissions standards","chinese":"排放標準"},{"english":"shift electricity production towards","chinese":"將發電轉向……"},{"english":"cleaner sources","chinese":"較清潔的來源"},{"english":"affect people's daily habits","chinese":"影響人們的日常習慣"},{"english":"industrial behaviour","chinese":"工業行為"},{"english":"their impact","chinese":"它們的影響"},{"english":"far broader than","chinese":"比……廣泛得多"},{"english":"simply discouraging people from","chinese":"只是阻止人們……"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"aviation industry","chinese":"航空業"},{"english":"be pushed to","chinese":"被推動去……"},{"english":"improve fuel efficiency","chinese":"提高燃油效率"},{"english":"adopt cleaner technology","chinese":"採用較清潔的技術"},{"english":"instead of being treated as","chinese":"而不是被視為……"},{"english":"be solved by restriction","chinese":"透過限制來解決"},{"english":"more practical","chinese":"更實際"},{"english":"supports business","chinese":"支持商業"},{"english":"tourism","chinese":"旅遊業"},{"english":"family connections","chinese":"家庭聯繫"},{"english":"across long distances","chinese":"跨越長距離"},{"english":"play a small role in","chinese":"在……中發揮小作用"},{"english":"reducing emissions","chinese":"減少排放"},{"english":"certainly not","chinese":"肯定不是"},{"english":"tackle air pollution","chinese":"處理空氣污染"},{"english":"cleaner cities","chinese":"更清潔的城市"},{"english":"wider reforms","chinese":"更廣泛的改革"},{"english":"transport, industry and energy","chinese":"交通、工業和能源"},{"english":"narrow focus on","chinese":"對……的狹窄關注"},{"english":"flights alone","chinese":"單單航班"}]},"model-essay-49-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-49-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:49","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-49-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q49","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Television has become a familiar part of many children's daily lives, and it is sometimes seen as an easy way to support learning. However, I completely disagree that children should be encouraged to watch it regularly either at home or at school. Even when a programme is well made, regular viewing is a poor substitute for active, guided education.","chinese":"電視已經成為許多孩子日常生活中熟悉的一部分，而且有時被視為一種支持學習的簡單方式。 然而，我完全不同意孩子應該被鼓勵在家中或學校定期觀看電視。 即使一個節目製作精良，定期觀看電視也不能很好地取代主動、有引導性的教育。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main problem is that television usually turns children into passive receivers rather than active learners. When a child reads, discusses, writes, experiments, or asks questions, the mind has to work: ideas are tested, mistakes are corrected, and understanding becomes deeper. Television, by contrast, often delivers information in a polished stream, leaving little room for reflection or interaction. For example, a child watching a science programme about plants may remember a few colourful images, but a child who grows a plant, records its changes, and explains the process to a teacher is far more likely to understand the concept properly. Regular television viewing therefore risks creating the illusion of learning, while real intellectual habits remain underdeveloped.","chinese":"主要問題是，電視通常會把孩子變成被動接收者，而不是主動學習者。 當孩子閱讀、討論、寫作、實驗或提問時，大腦必須運作：想法會被檢驗，錯誤會被糾正，理解也會變得更深入。 相比下，電視往往以一種經過包裝的連續形式傳遞資訊，幾乎沒有留下反思或互動空間 例如，一個觀看植物科學節目的孩子可能會記住幾個色彩鮮明的畫面，但一個親自種植植物、記錄其變化，並向老師解釋過程的孩子，更有可能真正理解這個概念。 因此，定期觀看電視有可能製造出一種正在學習的錯覺，而真正的思考習慣卻仍然未能充分發展。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that encouraging television at both home and school would weaken children’s concentration and social development. Young learners need routines that train patience, attention, and communication. If screens become a normal learning tool too often, children may find slower but more demanding tasks, such as reading a chapter, solving a problem, or listening to classmates, less appealing. At home, this could also reduce time for family conversation, outdoor play, and independent study. At school, it may turn valuable classroom time into a one-way broadcast, where students watch rather than participate. Education should not be a theatre seat; it should be a workshop.","chinese":"另一個原因是，在家庭和學校都鼓勵孩子看電視，會削弱他們的專注力和社交發展。 年幼的學習者需要一些能訓練耐性、專注力和溝通能力的日常安排。 如果螢幕過於頻繁地成為常規學習工具，孩子可能會覺得一些較慢但要求更高的任務，例如閱讀一個章節、解決一道問題，或聆聽同學發言，變得不那麼吸引。 在家中，這也可能減少孩子用於家庭對話、戶外玩耍和自主學習的時間。 在學校，它可能會把寶貴的課堂時間變成單向播放，讓學生只是觀看，而不是參與。 教育不應該是一個劇院座位；它應該是一個工作坊。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely disagree with the idea that children should be encouraged to watch television regularly. As a regular habit at home and in school, it encourages passivity, weakens attention, and takes children away from richer forms of learning.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全不同意孩子應該被鼓勵定期觀看電視這個觀點。 作為家庭和學校中的一種常規習慣，它會鼓勵被動、削弱專注力，並使孩子遠離更豐富的學習形式。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"familiar part of","chinese":"……中常見的一部分"},{"english":"children's daily lives","chinese":"兒童日常生活"},{"english":"be seen as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"support learning","chinese":"支持學習"},{"english":"be encouraged to","chinese":"被鼓勵去……"},{"english":"watch it regularly","chinese":"定期觀看它"},{"english":"either at home or at school","chinese":"無論在家中還是在學校"},{"english":"well made","chinese":"製作精良"},{"english":"regular viewing","chinese":"定期觀看"},{"english":"a poor substitute for","chinese":"……的差劣替代品"},{"english":"active, guided education","chinese":"主動而有引導的教育"},{"english":"the main problem","chinese":"主要問題"},{"english":"turn children into","chinese":"將孩子變成……"},{"english":"passive receivers","chinese":"被動接收者"},{"english":"active learners","chinese":"主動學習者"},{"english":"asks questions","chinese":"提問"},{"english":"the mind has to work","chinese":"大腦需要運作"},{"english":"ideas are tested","chinese":"想法受到檢驗"},{"english":"mistakes are corrected","chinese":"錯誤得到糾正"},{"english":"understanding becomes deeper","chinese":"理解變得更深入"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"delivers information","chinese":"傳遞資料"},{"english":"polished stream","chinese":"經修飾而流暢的資訊流"},{"english":"leave little room for","chinese":"幾乎沒有空間給……"},{"english":"reflection or interaction","chinese":"反思或互動"},{"english":"science programme","chinese":"科學節目"},{"english":"colourful images","chinese":"色彩鮮明的畫面"},{"english":"grows a plant","chinese":"種植植物"},{"english":"records its changes","chinese":"記錄它的變化"},{"english":"explains the process to","chinese":"向……解釋過程"},{"english":"far more likely to","chinese":"更加有可能"},{"english":"understand the concept properly","chinese":"正確理解概念"},{"english":"regular television viewing","chinese":"定期看電視"},{"english":"risks creating","chinese":"有可能造成"},{"english":"the illusion of learning","chinese":"學習的假象"},{"english":"intellectual habits","chinese":"思維習慣"},{"english":"remain underdeveloped","chinese":"仍未充分發展"},{"english":"another reason","chinese":"另一個原因"},{"english":"weaken children's concentration","chinese":"削弱兒童的專注力"},{"english":"social development","chinese":"社交發展"},{"english":"young learners","chinese":"年幼學習者"},{"english":"train patience","chinese":"訓練耐性"},{"english":"attention, and communication","chinese":"專注力和溝通能力"},{"english":"become a normal learning tool","chinese":"成為常規學習工具"},{"english":"too often","chinese":"過於頻密"},{"english":"slower but more demanding tasks","chinese":"較慢但要求更高的任務"},{"english":"reading a chapter","chinese":"閱讀一章"},{"english":"solving a problem","chinese":"解決問題"},{"english":"listening to classmates","chinese":"聆聽同學"},{"english":"less appealing","chinese":"較不吸引"},{"english":"reduce time for","chinese":"減少……的時間"},{"english":"family conversation","chinese":"家庭對話"},{"english":"outdoor play","chinese":"戶外玩耍"},{"english":"independent study","chinese":"自主學習"},{"english":"valuable classroom time","chinese":"寶貴課堂時間"},{"english":"one-way broadcast","chinese":"單向廣播"},{"english":"watch rather than participate","chinese":"觀看而不是參與"},{"english":"theatre seat","chinese":"劇院座位"},{"english":"workshop","chinese":"工作坊"},{"english":"regular habit","chinese":"恆常習慣"},{"english":"encourages passivity","chinese":"助長被動"},{"english":"weakens attention","chinese":"削弱注意力"},{"english":"takes children away from","chinese":"使孩子遠離……"},{"english":"richer forms of learning","chinese":"更豐富的學習形式"}]},"model-essay-50-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-50-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:50","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-50-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q50","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Children today are often given far more independence than young people in the past, whether in choosing their hobbies, expressing their opinions, or making personal decisions. I believe this is a positive development because greater freedom helps children become more confident and better prepared for adult life.","chinese":"如今的孩子往往比過去的年輕人獲得更多獨立性，無論是在選擇興趣、表達意見，還是作出個人決定方面。 我認為這是一種正面的發展，因為更大的自由能幫助孩子變得更有自信，並為成年生活作好更充分的準備。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main benefit is that freedom allows children to develop independence from an earlier age. In previous generations, many children were expected to obey adults without question, which could make them disciplined but not necessarily thoughtful. By contrast, when children are allowed to make age-appropriate choices, they learn to think, compare options, and accept the consequences of their decisions. For example, a child who is trusted to manage his own study schedule may sometimes make mistakes, but those mistakes can teach him responsibility more effectively than constant parental control. In this sense, freedom acts as a training ground for real life, where people must make decisions without always being told what to do.","chinese":"主要好處是，自由能讓孩子從較早的年齡開始培養獨立性。 在過去幾代人中，許多孩子被期望毫無疑問地服從成年人，這可能使他們變得守紀律，但未必能使他們變得有思考能力。 相比之下，當孩子被允許作出符合年齡的選擇時，他們會學會思考、比較不同選項，並承擔自己決定所帶來的後果。 例如，一個被信任能夠管理自己學習時間表的孩子，有時可能會犯錯，但這些錯誤能比父母持續控制更有效地教會他責任感。 從這個意義上說，自由就像現實生活的訓練場，因為人在現實生活中必須作出決定，而不能總是由別人告訴他們該怎麼做。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason this trend is positive is that it encourages stronger self-expression and emotional growth. Children who are allowed to speak openly are more likely to understand their own feelings, communicate their needs, and build healthier relationships with others. If young people are always silenced or overprotected, they may grow up afraid of disagreement or unable to defend themselves. For instance, when parents listen to a child’s views about school, friendships, or future goals, the child feels respected rather than controlled. This does not mean children should be allowed to do whatever they want, but reasonable freedom can help them develop confidence, judgment, and a stronger sense of identity.","chinese":"這種趨勢之所以正面，另一個原因是它能鼓勵更強的自我表達和情感成長。 被允許坦誠表達的孩子，更有可能理解自己的感受、表達自己的需要，並與他人建立更健康的關係。 如果年輕人總是被壓制或過度保護，他們長大後可能會害怕分歧，或者無法為自己辯護 例如，當父母聆聽孩子對學校、友誼或未來目標的看法時，孩子會感到自己受到尊重，而不是被控制。 這並不意味著孩子應該被允許做任何他們想做的事，但合理的自由可以幫助他們培養自信、判斷力，以及更強的身份認同感。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, giving children more freedom is a positive change. Although guidance is still necessary, independence and self-expression are essential for helping young people become responsible, confident, and emotionally mature adults.","chinese":"總結來說，給予孩子更多自由是一種正面的改變。 雖然引導仍然是必要的，但獨立性和自我表達對幫助年輕人成為負責任、有自信並且情感成熟的成年人至關重要。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"far more independence","chinese":"多得多的獨立性"},{"english":"in the past","chinese":"在過去"},{"english":"choosing their hobbies","chinese":"選擇自己的興趣"},{"english":"expressing their opinions","chinese":"表達意見"},{"english":"making personal decisions","chinese":"作出個人決定"},{"english":"a positive development","chinese":"正面發展"},{"english":"greater freedom","chinese":"更大的自由"},{"english":"become more confident","chinese":"變得更有自信"},{"english":"better prepared for","chinese":"為……作好更充分準備"},{"english":"adult life","chinese":"成年生活"},{"english":"the main benefit","chinese":"主要好處"},{"english":"develop independence","chinese":"培養獨立性"},{"english":"from an earlier age","chinese":"從較早年紀開始"},{"english":"previous generations","chinese":"以往幾代人"},{"english":"be expected to","chinese":"被期望去……"},{"english":"obey adults without question","chinese":"毫不質疑地服從成年人"},{"english":"disciplined but not necessarily thoughtful","chinese":"有紀律但不一定有思考能力"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"be allowed to","chinese":"被允許去……"},{"english":"age-appropriate choices","chinese":"適合年齡的選擇"},{"english":"compare options","chinese":"比較選項"},{"english":"accept the consequences of","chinese":"承擔……的後果"},{"english":"manage his own study schedule","chinese":"管理自己的學習時間表"},{"english":"make mistakes","chinese":"犯錯"},{"english":"teach him responsibility","chinese":"教會他責任感"},{"english":"more effectively than","chinese":"比……更有效地"},{"english":"constant parental control","chinese":"持續父母管束"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"acts as","chinese":"充當；起……作用"},{"english":"training ground","chinese":"訓練場"},{"english":"real life","chinese":"現實生活"},{"english":"make decisions","chinese":"作出決定"},{"english":"without always being told what to do","chinese":"不用總是被告知要做甚麼"},{"english":"another reason","chinese":"另一個原因"},{"english":"encourages stronger self-expression","chinese":"鼓勵更強的自我表達"},{"english":"emotional growth","chinese":"情感成長"},{"english":"speak openly","chinese":"坦誠表達"},{"english":"be more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"understand their own feelings","chinese":"理解自己的感受"},{"english":"communicate their needs","chinese":"表達自己的需要"},{"english":"build healthier relationships with","chinese":"與……建立更健康的關係"},{"english":"be always silenced","chinese":"總是被要求沉默"},{"english":"overprotected","chinese":"被過度保護"},{"english":"grow up afraid of","chinese":"長大後害怕……"},{"english":"disagreement","chinese":"意見分歧"},{"english":"unable to defend themselves","chinese":"無法為自己辯護；無法保護自己"},{"english":"listen to a child's views","chinese":"聆聽孩子的看法"},{"english":"future goals","chinese":"未來目標"},{"english":"feel respected rather than controlled","chinese":"感到被尊重，而不是被控制"},{"english":"do whatever they want","chinese":"做任何想做的事"},{"english":"reasonable freedom","chinese":"合理自由"},{"english":"develop confidence","chinese":"培養自信"},{"english":"judgment","chinese":"判斷力"},{"english":"a stronger sense of identity","chinese":"更強的身份認同"},{"english":"giving children more freedom","chinese":"給予孩子更多自由"},{"english":"positive change","chinese":"正面轉變"},{"english":"guidance is still necessary","chinese":"引導仍然必要"},{"english":"independence and self-expression","chinese":"獨立性和自我表達"},{"english":"responsible, confident, and emotionally mature adults","chinese":"負責任、有自信和情緒成熟的成年人"}]},"model-essay-51-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-51-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:51","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-51-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q51","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Family and school both shape a person’s future, but I completely agree that the values learned from parents and family have a greater influence on long-term success than academic skills or classroom knowledge. This is because family values form the inner habits that determine how people use whatever they later learn.","chinese":"家庭和學校都會塑造一個人的未來，但我完全同意，從父母和家庭中學到的價值觀，比在學校學到的任何技能或知識，對長遠成功有更大的影響。 這是因為家庭價值觀會形成一個人內在的習慣，而這些習慣會決定他們日後如何運用所學到的一切。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"First, values such as discipline, responsibility, honesty, and perseverance are the foundation on which achievement is built. Schools can teach mathematics, science, or writing, but these abilities are useful only when a person has the character to apply them consistently. A student who grows up in a family where effort is valued is more likely to revise regularly, accept corrections, and keep going after poor results. By contrast, someone who has knowledge but lacks self-control may waste opportunities, give up too quickly, or look for shortcuts. In this sense, family values are like the roots of a tree: invisible at first, but essential when the weather turns rough.","chinese":"首先，紀律、責任感、誠實和毅力等價值觀，是成就得以建立的基礎。 學校可以教授數學、科學或寫作，但只有當一個人具備能夠持續運用這些能力的品格時，這些能力才真正有用。 一個在重視努力的家庭中長大的學生，更有可能定期溫習、接受改正，並在成績不理想後繼續堅持下去。 相比之下，一個有知識但缺乏自制力的人，可能會浪費機會、太快放棄，或者尋找捷徑 從這個角度來看，家庭價值觀就像一棵樹的根：起初看不見，但風雨來臨時卻至關重要"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that success in adult life depends heavily on the way people deal with others. Qualities such as respect, empathy, patience, and reliability are often first learned at home through daily interactions with parents, siblings, and relatives. These qualities later affect friendships, teamwork, leadership, and professional trust. For example, two graduates may leave university with similar qualifications, but the one who listens carefully, treats colleagues fairly, and keeps promises is far more likely to earn respect and responsibility at work. Technical knowledge may open the door, but character often decides whether a person can stay in the room.","chinese":"另一個原因是，成年後的成功在很大程度上取決於人們如何與他人相處。 尊重、同理心、耐性和可靠性等品質，往往最初都是透過在家中與父母、兄弟姊妹和親戚的日常互動中學會的。 這些品質日後會影響友誼、團隊合作、領導能力和職場信任。 例如，兩名畢業生離開大學時可能擁有相似的資歷，但那個懂得仔細聆聽、公平對待同事並信守承諾的人，更有可能在工作中贏得尊重和責任。 專業知識也許能打開機會之門，但品格往往決定一個人能否真正留在其中。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully agree that family values have a stronger influence on future success than school-based skills or knowledge. Education is undeniably useful, but without the right values, it becomes a tool without direction. The habits and principles formed at home guide people through study, work, and relationships, making them the deeper source of lasting achievement.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意，家庭價值觀比學校所教授的技能或知識，對未來成功有更強的影響。 教育無疑是有用的，但如果沒有正確的價值觀，它就會變成一件沒有方向的工具。 在家中形成的習慣和原則，會引導人們面對學習、工作和人際關係，使它們成為持久成就更深層的來源。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"shape a person's future","chinese":"塑造一個人的未來"},{"english":"values learned from","chinese":"從……學到的價值觀"},{"english":"have a greater influence on","chinese":"對……有更大影響"},{"english":"long-term success","chinese":"長遠成功"},{"english":"academic skills","chinese":"學術技能"},{"english":"classroom knowledge","chinese":"課堂知識"},{"english":"form the inner habits","chinese":"形成內在習慣"},{"english":"determine how","chinese":"決定如何……"},{"english":"whatever they later learn","chinese":"他們日後學到的一切"},{"english":"discipline, responsibility, honesty, and perseverance","chinese":"紀律、責任感、誠實和毅力"},{"english":"the foundation on which","chinese":"……的基礎"},{"english":"achievement is built","chinese":"成就得以建立"},{"english":"useful only when","chinese":"只有在……時才有用"},{"english":"apply them consistently","chinese":"持續運用它們"},{"english":"grows up in","chinese":"在……中成長"},{"english":"effort is valued","chinese":"努力受到重視"},{"english":"be more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"revise regularly","chinese":"定期溫習"},{"english":"accept corrections","chinese":"接受糾正"},{"english":"keep going after","chinese":"在……之後繼續努力"},{"english":"poor results","chinese":"差的成績"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"lacks self-control","chinese":"缺乏自制力"},{"english":"waste opportunities","chinese":"浪費機會"},{"english":"give up too quickly","chinese":"太快放棄"},{"english":"look for shortcuts","chinese":"尋找捷徑"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"roots of a tree","chinese":"樹根"},{"english":"invisible at first","chinese":"起初看不見"},{"english":"when the weather turns rough","chinese":"當環境變得艱難時"},{"english":"adult life","chinese":"成年生活"},{"english":"depends heavily on","chinese":"很大程度上取決於"},{"english":"deal with others","chinese":"與他人相處"},{"english":"respect, empathy, patience, and reliability","chinese":"尊重、同理心、耐性和可靠"},{"english":"first learned at home","chinese":"首先在家中學到"},{"english":"daily interactions","chinese":"日常互動"},{"english":"siblings and relatives","chinese":"兄弟姊妹和親戚"},{"english":"later affect","chinese":"日後影響"},{"english":"friendships, teamwork, leadership, and professional trust","chinese":"友誼、團隊合作、領導力和專業信任"},{"english":"similar qualifications","chinese":"相似資歷"},{"english":"listens carefully","chinese":"細心聆聽"},{"english":"treats colleagues fairly","chinese":"公平對待同事"},{"english":"keeps promises","chinese":"遵守承諾"},{"english":"far more likely to","chinese":"更加有可能"},{"english":"earn respect and responsibility","chinese":"贏得尊重和責任"},{"english":"technical knowledge","chinese":"技術知識"},{"english":"open the door","chinese":"打開機會之門"},{"english":"character often decides whether","chinese":"品格往往決定是否……"},{"english":"stay in the room","chinese":"留在那個位置；持續站穩"},{"english":"stronger influence on","chinese":"對……有更強影響"},{"english":"school-based skills","chinese":"學校所教的技能"},{"english":"undeniably useful","chinese":"無可否認地有用"},{"english":"a tool without direction","chinese":"沒有方向的工具"},{"english":"habits and principles","chinese":"習慣和原則"},{"english":"formed at home","chinese":"在家中形成"},{"english":"guide people through","chinese":"引導人們經歷……"},{"english":"study, work, and relationships","chinese":"學習、工作和人際關係"},{"english":"deeper source of","chinese":"……更深層的來源"},{"english":"lasting achievement","chinese":"持久成就"}]},"model-essay-52-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-52-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:52","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-52-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q52","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In every country, protecting citizens is one of the state’s core duties. Some argue that this duty requires higher defence budgets and lower spending on welfare programmes. I completely disagree with this view, because safety is not created by weapons alone; it also depends on the health, stability and dignity of ordinary people.","chinese":"在每一個國家，保護公民都是國家的核心職責之一。 有些人認為，這項責任需要政府增加國防預算，並減少在社會福利計劃上的開支。 我完全不同意這個觀點，因為安全並不是單靠武器創造出來的；它也取決於普通人的健康、穩定和尊嚴。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"First, reducing social benefits can make society less safe, not more. Welfare spending funds healthcare, unemployment support, pensions and housing assistance. These are not luxuries; they keep vulnerable citizens from falling into desperation. When families cannot afford medicine, rent or basic food, problems that begin as private hardship can spill over into public disorder, crime and social division. For example, a worker who loses his job but receives temporary support has time to retrain and find employment. Without that safety net, the same person may face debt, eviction and deep resentment. In this sense, social benefits are not soft spending, but a form of domestic security.","chinese":"首先，削減社會福利可能會令社會變得更不安全，而不是更安全。 福利開支資助醫療、失業援助、退休金和住房援助。 這些並不是奢侈品；它們能防止弱勢公民陷入絕望。 當家庭無法負擔藥物、租金或基本食物時，原本屬於私人困境的問題，可能會蔓延成公共秩序混亂、犯罪和社會分裂。 例如，一名失業工人如果能獲得臨時支援，就有時間重新接受培訓並尋找工作。 如果沒有這張安全網，同一個人可能會面對債務、被迫搬離住所，以及深層的怨恨。 從這個意義上說，社會福利並不是軟性開支，而是一種國內安全保障。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Second, excessive military spending can become a poor use of limited public money when it crowds out services that citizens rely on every day. A larger army or newer equipment may protect borders, but it cannot educate children, treat chronic illnesses or support elderly citizens living alone. These services strengthen a country from within by producing healthier workers, more capable young people and communities that trust the state. A government that neglects these foundations risks building a strong shield around a weak society. For instance, if hospitals are underfunded while defence projects expand, citizens may feel abandoned by their own leaders even in peacetime.","chinese":"其次，當過度的軍事開支擠壓了公民日常依賴的服務時，它就可能變成對有限公共資金的不良使用。 更龐大的軍隊或更新式的裝備或許能保護邊境，但它不能教育兒童、治療慢性疾病，或支援獨居長者。 這些服務能從內部強化一個國家，因為它們能培養更健康的勞動人口、更有能力的年輕人，以及更信任政府的社區。 一個忽視這些基礎的政府，可能會冒著在一個脆弱社會外圍建立強大盾牌的風險。 例如，如果醫院資金不足，而國防項目卻不斷擴張，公民即使在和平時期也可能會覺得被自己的領袖拋棄。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I do not agree that governments should finance higher defence spending by cutting social benefits. True public safety is broader than military protection. It comes not only from secure borders, but also from citizens who are healthy, educated and protected from extreme hardship.","chinese":"總結來說，我不同意政府應該透過削減社會福利來資助更高的國防開支。 真正的公共安全比軍事保護更加廣泛。 它不僅來自安全的邊境，也來自健康、受教育，並受到保護而免於極端困境的公民。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"protecting citizens","chinese":"保護公民"},{"english":"core duties","chinese":"核心職責"},{"english":"the state","chinese":"國家；政府"},{"english":"higher defence budgets","chinese":"更高國防預算"},{"english":"lower spending on","chinese":"減少在……上的開支"},{"english":"welfare programmes","chinese":"福利計劃"},{"english":"completely disagree with","chinese":"完全不同意……"},{"english":"weapons alone","chinese":"單靠武器"},{"english":"depends on","chinese":"取決於"},{"english":"health, stability and dignity","chinese":"健康、穩定和尊嚴"},{"english":"ordinary people","chinese":"普通人"},{"english":"reducing social benefits","chinese":"削減社會福利"},{"english":"social benefits","chinese":"社會福利"},{"english":"make society less safe","chinese":"令社會更不安全"},{"english":"welfare spending","chinese":"福利開支"},{"english":"unemployment support","chinese":"失業支援"},{"english":"pensions","chinese":"退休金"},{"english":"housing assistance","chinese":"住屋援助"},{"english":"not luxuries","chinese":"不是奢侈品"},{"english":"vulnerable citizens","chinese":"弱勢公民"},{"english":"falling into desperation","chinese":"陷入絕望"},{"english":"afford medicine","chinese":"負擔藥物"},{"english":"basic food","chinese":"基本食物"},{"english":"private hardship","chinese":"個人困境"},{"english":"spill over into","chinese":"擴散成……"},{"english":"public disorder","chinese":"公共秩序混亂"},{"english":"social division","chinese":"社會分化"},{"english":"loses his job","chinese":"失去工作"},{"english":"temporary support","chinese":"臨時支援"},{"english":"retrain","chinese":"再培訓"},{"english":"find employment","chinese":"找到工作"},{"english":"safety net","chinese":"安全網"},{"english":"face debt","chinese":"面對債務"},{"english":"eviction","chinese":"被迫遷"},{"english":"deep resentment","chinese":"深層怨氣"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"soft spending","chinese":"軟性開支；非必要開支"},{"english":"domestic security","chinese":"國內安全"},{"english":"excessive military spending","chinese":"過度軍事開支"},{"english":"poor use of","chinese":"對……的不善使用"},{"english":"limited public money","chinese":"有限公帑"},{"english":"crowds out","chinese":"排擠"},{"english":"rely on every day","chinese":"每天依賴"},{"english":"larger army","chinese":"更龐大的軍隊"},{"english":"newer equipment","chinese":"較新的裝備"},{"english":"protect borders","chinese":"保護邊境"},{"english":"treat chronic illnesses","chinese":"治療慢性疾病"},{"english":"chronic illnesses","chinese":"慢性疾病"},{"english":"elderly citizens living alone","chinese":"獨居長者"},{"english":"strengthen a country from within","chinese":"從內部強化一個國家"},{"english":"healthier workers","chinese":"更健康的工人"},{"english":"more capable young people","chinese":"更有能力的年輕人"},{"english":"trust the state","chinese":"信任國家；信任政府"},{"english":"neglects these foundations","chinese":"忽視這些基礎"},{"english":"risks building","chinese":"有可能建立……"},{"english":"strong shield","chinese":"強大的盾牌"},{"english":"weak society","chinese":"脆弱的社會"},{"english":"underfunded","chinese":"資金不足"},{"english":"defence projects","chinese":"國防項目"},{"english":"feel abandoned by","chinese":"感到被……拋棄"},{"english":"own leaders","chinese":"自己的領袖"},{"english":"in peacetime","chinese":"在和平時期"},{"english":"finance higher defence spending","chinese":"資助更高國防開支"},{"english":"cutting social benefits","chinese":"削減社會福利"},{"english":"true public safety","chinese":"真正的公共安全"},{"english":"broader than","chinese":"比……更廣泛"},{"english":"military protection","chinese":"軍事保護"},{"english":"secure borders","chinese":"安全邊境"},{"english":"protected from extreme hardship","chinese":"受到保護免於極端困苦"},{"english":"extreme hardship","chinese":"極端困苦"}]},"model-essay-53-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-53-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:53","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-53-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q53","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Creative work is often treated as a private passion, yet it also shapes how a society remembers, feels and understands itself. I completely agree that governments should provide financial support to artists, musicians and other creative people, because their work creates public value that the market alone rarely protects.","chinese":"創意工作經常被視為一種個人的熱情，但也塑造了一個社會如何記憶、感受和理解自身 我完全同意政府應該向藝術家、音樂家和其他創意人士提供財政支持，因為他們的作品創造了公共價值，而單靠市場往往難以保護這種價值。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that the arts preserve and enrich a nation’s culture. Paintings, songs, films and performances are not merely forms of entertainment; they are part of a country’s collective memory. If talented people are forced to abandon their work simply because they cannot earn a stable income, valuable stories, traditions and local voices may quietly disappear. Public grants can give them the time, materials and venues they need to produce work that later becomes part of a community’s identity. For example, a composer who receives funding to write music based on local folk traditions may create performances that schools, festivals and museums can use for many years. In this sense, supporting creative people is not charity; it is cultural investment.","chinese":"第一個原因是，藝術能夠保存並豐富一個國家的文化。 繪畫、歌曲、電影和表演並不只是娛樂形式；它們是一個國家集體記憶的一部分。 如果有才華的人只是因為無法獲得穩定收入而被迫放棄創作，那麼珍貴的故事、傳統和本土聲音可能會悄然消失。 公共資助可以給予他們所需的時間、材料和場地，讓他們創作出日後成為社區身份一部分的作品。 例如，一位作曲家如果獲得資助，根據本地民間傳統創作音樂，便可能創造出學校、節日活動和博物館多年都能使用的表演作品。 從這個角度來看，支持創意人士並不是慈善；這是一種文化投資。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important reason is that creative work can benefit the wider public, even when it is not immediately profitable. Commercial markets tend to reward what sells quickly, not necessarily what is meaningful, experimental or socially useful. With government support, artists and musicians can offer free concerts in public spaces, run workshops for children, decorate neglected neighbourhoods or create work that helps people think about social issues. These projects may not make anyone rich, but they can make a city feel more alive, humane and connected. Without such funding, creativity risks becoming a luxury available only to those who can already afford to pursue it.","chinese":"另一個重要原因是，創意作品即使不能立即帶來盈利，也能惠及更廣泛的公眾。 商業市場往往獎勵那些能快速售出的東西，而不一定獎勵有意義、具實驗性或對社會有用的作品。 在政府支持下，藝術家和音樂家可以在公共空間舉辦免費音樂會、為兒童舉辦工作坊、裝飾被忽視的社區，或創作能幫助人們思考社會議題的作品。 這些項目未必會令任何人致富，但它們能讓一座城市感覺更有活力、更有人情味，也更有連結感。 如果沒有這類資助，創意便有可能變成一種奢侈品，只屬於那些本來就有能力追求它的人。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully agree that governments should give money to creative people. Art and music strengthen culture, widen public access to beauty and imagination, and give society something deeper than material comfort. A country that supports its artists is not wasting money; it is keeping its cultural heartbeat alive.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意政府應該給予創意人士金錢支持。 藝術和音樂能強化文化，擴大公眾接觸美感與想像力的機會，並給予社會一些比物質舒適更深層的東西。 一個支持藝術家的國家並不是在浪費金錢；它是在讓自己的文化心跳繼續跳動。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"creative work","chinese":"創作工作"},{"english":"be treated as","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"private passion","chinese":"個人熱情"},{"english":"shapes how a society remembers","chinese":"塑造社會如何記憶"},{"english":"understands itself","chinese":"理解自身"},{"english":"provide financial support to","chinese":"向……提供財政支援"},{"english":"artists, musicians and other creative people","chinese":"藝術家、音樂家和其他創意工作者"},{"english":"creates public value","chinese":"創造公共價值"},{"english":"the market alone","chinese":"單靠市場"},{"english":"rarely protects","chinese":"很少保護"},{"english":"preserve and enrich","chinese":"保存並豐富"},{"english":"a nation's culture","chinese":"一個國家的文化"},{"english":"paintings, songs, films and performances","chinese":"繪畫、歌曲、電影和表演"},{"english":"not merely forms of entertainment","chinese":"不只是娛樂形式"},{"english":"collective memory","chinese":"集體記憶"},{"english":"be forced to abandon","chinese":"被迫放棄"},{"english":"abandon their work","chinese":"放棄他們的工作"},{"english":"stable income","chinese":"穩定收入"},{"english":"valuable stories","chinese":"有價值的故事"},{"english":"traditions and local voices","chinese":"傳統和本地聲音"},{"english":"quietly disappear","chinese":"悄悄消失"},{"english":"public grants","chinese":"公共資助；政府撥款"},{"english":"the time, materials and venues","chinese":"時間、材料和場地"},{"english":"produce work","chinese":"創作作品"},{"english":"community's identity","chinese":"社區身份認同"},{"english":"composer","chinese":"作曲家"},{"english":"receives funding to","chinese":"獲得資助去……"},{"english":"local folk traditions","chinese":"本地民間傳統"},{"english":"schools, festivals and museums","chinese":"學校、節日活動和博物館"},{"english":"supporting creative people","chinese":"支持創意工作者"},{"english":"not charity","chinese":"不是慈善"},{"english":"cultural investment","chinese":"文化投資"},{"english":"wider public","chinese":"更廣泛的公眾"},{"english":"immediately profitable","chinese":"即時有利可圖"},{"english":"commercial markets","chinese":"商業市場"},{"english":"tend to reward","chinese":"往往獎勵"},{"english":"what sells quickly","chinese":"快速賣得出的東西"},{"english":"not necessarily","chinese":"不一定"},{"english":"meaningful, experimental or socially useful","chinese":"有意義、具實驗性或對社會有用"},{"english":"with government support","chinese":"在政府支持下"},{"english":"public spaces","chinese":"公共空間"},{"english":"run workshops for children","chinese":"為兒童舉辦工作坊"},{"english":"decorate neglected neighbourhoods","chinese":"裝飾被忽略的社區"},{"english":"neglected neighbourhoods","chinese":"被忽略的社區"},{"english":"think about social issues","chinese":"思考社會議題"},{"english":"make anyone rich","chinese":"令任何人致富"},{"english":"feel more alive","chinese":"感覺更有活力"},{"english":"humane and connected","chinese":"人性化和有連繫"},{"english":"without such funding","chinese":"沒有這類資助"},{"english":"risks becoming","chinese":"有可能變成"},{"english":"a luxury available only to","chinese":"只有……才可享有的奢侈品"},{"english":"afford to pursue it","chinese":"負擔得起去追求它"},{"english":"give money to creative people","chinese":"向創意工作者提供資金"},{"english":"strengthen culture","chinese":"加強文化"},{"english":"widen public access to","chinese":"擴大公眾接觸……的機會"},{"english":"beauty and imagination","chinese":"美感和想像力"},{"english":"material comfort","chinese":"物質舒適"},{"english":"a country that supports its artists","chinese":"支持藝術家的國家"},{"english":"wasting money","chinese":"浪費金錢"},{"english":"cultural heartbeat","chinese":"文化心跳"},{"english":"keeping its cultural heartbeat alive","chinese":"令文化生命力延續"}]},"model-essay-54-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-54-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:54","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-54-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q54","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Public money is always limited, so governments must decide carefully which areas deserve priority. Some people argue that funding for the arts should be reduced so that more money can be spent on education. I completely disagree with this view because the arts are an essential part of education and also bring wider cultural and economic benefits.","chinese":"公共資金始終是有限的，因此政府必須謹慎決定哪些範疇應該獲得優先考慮。 有些人認為，藝術方面的資助應該被削減，從而使更多金錢可以用於教育。 我完全不同意這種看法，因為藝術是教育不可或缺的一部分，而且也能帶來更廣泛的文化和經濟利益。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that cutting arts funding would actually weaken education rather than improve it. Education is not only about textbooks, examinations, and academic subjects; it should also develop creativity, confidence, emotional intelligence, and critical thinking. Subjects such as music, drama, design, and visual arts allow students to express ideas, solve problems in original ways, and understand human experience more deeply. For example, a student who takes part in school theatre may become more confident in public speaking, while a student who studies painting may learn patience, observation, and interpretation. If the government reduces support for the arts, schools may treat these subjects as luxuries, and students will receive a narrower and poorer form of education.","chinese":"第一個原因是，削減藝術資助實際上會削弱教育，而不是改善教育。 教育不僅僅關乎課本、考試和學術科目；它也應該培養創造力、自信、情緒智力和批判性思維。 音樂、戲劇、設計和視覺藝術等科目，能讓學生表達想法、以原創方式解決問題，並更深入地理解人的經驗。 例如，一個參與學校戲劇的學生，可能會在公開演說方面變得更有自信；而一個學習繪畫的學生，則可能學會耐性、觀察力和詮釋能力。 如果政府減少對藝術的支持，學校可能會把這些科目視為奢侈品，而學生將會接受一種更狹窄、也更貧乏的教育。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important point is that the arts create value beyond the classroom. Museums, galleries, concerts, public performances, and cultural festivals help preserve national identity and bring communities together. They also support jobs in tourism, media, entertainment, design, and the creative industries. In many cities, cultural attractions are not decorative extras; they are part of the local economy and public life. If arts organisations lose funding, talented people may leave the sector, cultural venues may close, and society may become richer in test scores but poorer in imagination. Education needs more investment, but that money should come from wasteful spending or inefficient policies, not from a field that gives society both memory and meaning.","chinese":"另一個重要觀點是，藝術能在課室之外創造價值。 博物館、畫廊、音樂會、公眾表演和文化節，有助保存國家身份，並把社區凝聚在一起 它們也支撐著旅遊、媒體、娛樂、設計和創意產業中的工作機會。 在許多城市，文化景點並不是裝飾性的附加品；它們是本地經濟和公共生活的一部分。 如果藝術機構失去資助，有才華的人可能會離開這個行業，文化場地可能會關閉，而社會也可能在考試分數上變得更富有，卻在想像力上變得更貧乏。 教育需要更多投資，但這些金錢應該來自浪費性的開支或低效率的政策，而不是來自一個同時給予社會記憶與意義的範疇。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I strongly disagree that governments should lower the arts budget to fund education. A wiser policy is to invest in both, because strong education needs creativity, and a healthy society needs culture.","chinese":"總結來說，我強烈不同意政府應該削減藝術預算來資助教育。 更明智的政策是同時投資於兩者，因為強大的教育需要創造力，而健康的社會需要文化"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"public money","chinese":"公帑；公共資金"},{"english":"deserve priority","chinese":"值得優先處理"},{"english":"funding for the arts","chinese":"藝術撥款"},{"english":"be reduced","chinese":"被削減"},{"english":"be spent on education","chinese":"被用於教育"},{"english":"completely disagree with","chinese":"完全不同意……"},{"english":"an essential part of","chinese":"……的重要部分"},{"english":"wider cultural and economic benefits","chinese":"更廣泛的文化和經濟好處"},{"english":"cutting arts funding","chinese":"削減藝術撥款"},{"english":"weaken education","chinese":"削弱教育"},{"english":"rather than improve it","chinese":"而不是改善它"},{"english":"not only about","chinese":"不只是關於……"},{"english":"textbooks, examinations, and academic subjects","chinese":"教科書、考試和學術科目"},{"english":"develop creativity","chinese":"培養創意"},{"english":"emotional intelligence","chinese":"情緒智能"},{"english":"critical thinking","chinese":"批判思維"},{"english":"subjects such as","chinese":"例如……的科目"},{"english":"visual arts","chinese":"視覺藝術"},{"english":"allow students to","chinese":"讓學生可以……"},{"english":"express ideas","chinese":"表達想法"},{"english":"solve problems in original ways","chinese":"以創新的方式解決問題"},{"english":"understand human experience","chinese":"理解人類經驗"},{"english":"more deeply","chinese":"更深入地"},{"english":"take part in","chinese":"參與"},{"english":"school theatre","chinese":"學校戲劇"},{"english":"public speaking","chinese":"公開演說"},{"english":"studies painting","chinese":"學習繪畫"},{"english":"patience, observation, and interpretation","chinese":"耐性、觀察力和詮釋能力"},{"english":"reduce support for","chinese":"減少對……的支持"},{"english":"treat these subjects as luxuries","chinese":"將這些科目視為奢侈品"},{"english":"narrower and poorer form of education","chinese":"更狹窄和更貧乏的教育形式"},{"english":"create value beyond","chinese":"在……以外創造價值"},{"english":"beyond the classroom","chinese":"課室以外"},{"english":"museums, galleries, concerts, public performances, and cultural festivals","chinese":"博物館、畫廊、音樂會、公開表演和文化節"},{"english":"preserve national identity","chinese":"保存國家身份認同"},{"english":"bring communities together","chinese":"凝聚社區"},{"english":"support jobs in","chinese":"支持……中的就業"},{"english":"creative industries","chinese":"創意產業"},{"english":"cultural attractions","chinese":"文化景點"},{"english":"decorative extras","chinese":"裝飾性的附加物"},{"english":"local economy","chinese":"本地經濟"},{"english":"public life","chinese":"公共生活"},{"english":"arts organisations","chinese":"藝術機構"},{"english":"lose funding","chinese":"失去撥款"},{"english":"talented people","chinese":"有才能的人"},{"english":"leave the sector","chinese":"離開該行業"},{"english":"cultural venues","chinese":"文化場地"},{"english":"richer in test scores but poorer in imagination","chinese":"考試分數更高，但想像力更貧乏"},{"english":"more investment","chinese":"更多投資"},{"english":"wasteful spending","chinese":"浪費性的開支"},{"english":"inefficient policies","chinese":"低效政策"},{"english":"a field that gives society both memory and meaning","chinese":"給予社會記憶和意義的領域"},{"english":"lower the arts budget","chinese":"削減藝術預算"},{"english":"fund education","chinese":"資助教育"},{"english":"wiser policy","chinese":"更明智的政策"},{"english":"invest in both","chinese":"同時投資於兩者"},{"english":"healthy society","chinese":"健康的社會"},{"english":"needs culture","chinese":"需要文化"}]},"model-essay-55-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-55-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:55","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-55-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Societies are shaped by many forces, but public debate often focuses on where real power lies. Some argue that meaningful social change can only come from the government because it controls laws, budgets and public institutions. I strongly disagree with this view. In my opinion, individuals can have a major influence on society because their everyday choices shape social norms and their collective voices can push institutions to change.","chinese":"社會是由許多力量塑造的，但公共討論往往集中於真正的力量究竟在哪裡。 有些人認為，有意義的社會變革只能來自政府，因為政府掌握法律、預算和公共機構。 我強烈不同意這種觀點。 在我看來，個人能夠對社會產生重大影響，因為他們的日常選擇會塑造社會規範，而他們集體的聲音也能推動機構作出改變。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that social change often begins with ordinary behaviour, not official instructions. When individuals alter the way they live, speak or spend money, they gradually change what society accepts as normal. For example, if many people choose to reduce waste, avoid unnecessary plastic and support environmentally responsible businesses, companies are pressured to improve their practices. Over time, these small actions can spread through families, workplaces and communities until they become part of public expectation. A law may draw a line on paper, but people’s habits decide whether that line matters in real life.","chinese":"第一個原因是，社會變革往往始於普通人的行為，而不是官方指示。 當個人改變自己的生活方式、說話方式或消費方式時，他們會逐漸改變社會所接受的「正常」標準。 例如，如果許多人選擇減少浪費、避免不必要的塑膠，並支持對環境負責的企業，公司便會受到壓力去改善自身的做法。 隨著時間推移，這些小行動可以在家庭、工作場所和社區之間擴散，直到它們成為公眾期望的一部分。 法律或能在紙面上劃出界線，但人們的習慣才決定那條界線在現實生活中是否真正重要"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that individuals can influence society by challenging unfair systems and giving others the courage to do the same. A single person who speaks out against discrimination, corruption or poor working conditions may seem powerless at first, but their voice can become the first spark in a much larger movement. For instance, a student who reports bullying, a worker who exposes unsafe practices, or a parent who campaigns for better school support may inspire others to act. Once enough people join that pressure, governments and organisations often have no choice but to respond.","chinese":"另一個原因是，個人可以透過挑戰不公平的制度，並給予他人同樣行動的勇氣，從而影響社會。 一個人站出來反對歧視、貪污或惡劣的工作條件，起初可能看似無力，但他的聲音可以成為更大運動中的第一點火花。 例如，一名舉報欺凌的學生、一位揭露不安全工作做法的工人，或一位爭取更好學校支援的家長，都可能激勵其他人採取行動。 一旦有足夠多的人加入這股壓力，政府和組織往往別無選擇，只能作出回應。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, although governments have formal authority, they are not the only force capable of changing society. Real progress often starts with individuals, whose choices, voices and courage can move public opinion and eventually reshape institutions.","chinese":"總結來說，儘管政府擁有正式權力，但它們並不是唯一能夠改變社會的力量。 真正的進步往往始於個人，因為他們的選擇、聲音和勇氣能夠推動公眾意見，並最終重塑制度。"}],"vocabulary":[]},"model-essay-56-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-56-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:56","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-56-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q56","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Good health policy should not begin at the hospital door. I completely agree that preventing illness is more important than treating it after it has already developed, and public funding should therefore give prevention the strongest priority.","chinese":"好的健康政策不應該從醫院門口才開始。 我完全同意，預防疾病比在疾病已經形成後才進行治療更加重要，因此公共資金應該把預防放在最優先的位置。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that prevention saves both money and human suffering. When governments invest in health education, vaccination programmes, early screening, safe parks, and better nutrition in schools, many serious conditions can be stopped before they become expensive medical crises. A health system that only responds after people are already sick is always fighting fires: hospitals become crowded, doctors are overstretched, and taxpayers must pay for long-term treatment that might have been avoided. For example, if children are taught healthy eating habits and are given places to exercise, they are less likely to develop obesity-related illnesses later in life. This means fewer patients needing complex surgery, lifelong medication, or repeated hospital visits. Prevention, therefore, does not merely reduce costs; it protects people from pain that no medicine can fully erase.","chinese":"第一個原因是，預防既能節省金錢，也能減少人類痛苦。 當政府投資於健康教育、疫苗接種計劃、早期篩查、安全的公園，以及學校中更好的營養安排時，許多嚴重疾病都可以在變成昂貴的醫療危機之前被阻止。 一個只在人們已經生病後才作出回應的醫療系統，永遠都像是在到處救火：醫院變得擁擠，醫生負擔過重，而納稅人也必須為原本可能避免的長期治療付費。 例如，如果孩子從小被教導健康飲食習慣，並且有地方可以運動，他們日後患上與肥胖相關疾病的可能性便會較低。 這意味著，需要複雜手術、終身服藥或反覆到醫院求診的病人會減少。 因此，預防不只是降低成本；它也保護人們免受那些任何藥物都無法完全抹去的痛苦。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that preventive spending creates a fairer society. Treatment often reaches people only after damage has been done, whereas prevention can protect whole communities before illness takes root. This is especially important for poorer families, who may lack access to nutritious food, safe housing, mental-health support, or regular medical checks. If public money is used to improve air quality, provide free health screenings, support school meals, and promote active lifestyles, the benefits are shared widely rather than reserved for those who can afford private care. In this sense, prevention is not just a medical strategy; it is a social investment that helps citizens remain healthy, productive, and independent.","chinese":"另一個原因是，預防性開支能創造一個更公平的社會。 治療往往只是在傷害已經造成後才接觸到人們，然而預防卻能在疾病扎根之前保護整個社區。 這對較貧困的家庭尤其重要，因為他們可能缺乏獲得營養食物、安全住所、心理健康支援或定期身體檢查的渠道。 如果公共資金被用來改善空氣質素、提供免費健康篩查、支援學校膳食，並推廣積極健康的生活方式，這些好處便能被廣泛分享，而不是只留給那些負擔得起私人醫療的人。 從這個意義上說，預防不只是一種醫療策略；它是一項社會投資，能幫助市民保持健康、有生產力，並維持獨立。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, governments should clearly prioritise the prevention of disease because it reduces avoidable suffering, lowers pressure on healthcare systems, and protects society more equally. Treating illness matters, but preventing it is the wiser use of public money.","chinese":"總結來說，政府應該明確優先考慮疾病預防，因為它能減少可避免的痛苦、降低醫療系統的壓力，並以更公平的方式保護社會。 治療疾病固然重要，但預防疾病才是更明智地使用公共資金的方式。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"health policy","chinese":"健康政策"},{"english":"begin at the hospital door","chinese":"從醫院門口才開始"},{"english":"preventing illness","chinese":"預防疾病"},{"english":"treating it after it has already developed","chinese":"在疾病已經形成後才治療"},{"english":"public funding","chinese":"公共資金；公帑"},{"english":"give prevention the strongest priority","chinese":"將預防放在最優先位置"},{"english":"saves both money and human suffering","chinese":"同時節省金錢和減少人類痛苦"},{"english":"invest in","chinese":"投資於……"},{"english":"health education","chinese":"健康教育"},{"english":"vaccination programmes","chinese":"疫苗接種計劃"},{"english":"early screening","chinese":"早期篩查"},{"english":"safe parks","chinese":"安全的公園"},{"english":"better nutrition","chinese":"更好的營養"},{"english":"serious conditions","chinese":"嚴重病症"},{"english":"be stopped before","chinese":"在……之前被阻止"},{"english":"expensive medical crises","chinese":"昂貴的醫療危機"},{"english":"respond after","chinese":"在……之後才回應"},{"english":"fighting fires","chinese":"疲於救火"},{"english":"hospitals become crowded","chinese":"醫院變得擠迫"},{"english":"doctors are overstretched","chinese":"醫生不勝負荷"},{"english":"taxpayers","chinese":"納稅人"},{"english":"long-term treatment","chinese":"長期治療"},{"english":"might have been avoided","chinese":"本來可以避免"},{"english":"healthy eating habits","chinese":"健康飲食習慣"},{"english":"places to exercise","chinese":"運動的地方"},{"english":"be less likely to develop","chinese":"較不可能患上……"},{"english":"obesity-related illnesses","chinese":"與肥胖有關的疾病"},{"english":"later in life","chinese":"日後；人生較後階段"},{"english":"complex surgery","chinese":"複雜手術"},{"english":"lifelong medication","chinese":"終身服藥"},{"english":"repeated hospital visits","chinese":"反覆到醫院求診"},{"english":"does not merely reduce costs","chinese":"不只是降低成本"},{"english":"protect people from pain","chinese":"保護人們免受痛苦"},{"english":"no medicine can fully erase","chinese":"沒有藥物能完全消除"},{"english":"preventive spending","chinese":"預防性開支"},{"english":"creates a fairer society","chinese":"建立更公平的社會"},{"english":"damage has been done","chinese":"傷害已經造成"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；然而"},{"english":"protect whole communities","chinese":"保護整個社區"},{"english":"takes root","chinese":"扎根；形成"},{"english":"poorer families","chinese":"較貧困家庭"},{"english":"lack access to","chinese":"缺乏取得……的機會"},{"english":"nutritious food","chinese":"有營養的食物"},{"english":"safe housing","chinese":"安全住所"},{"english":"mental-health support","chinese":"精神健康支援"},{"english":"regular medical checks","chinese":"定期身體檢查"},{"english":"improve air quality","chinese":"改善空氣質素"},{"english":"provide free health screenings","chinese":"提供免費健康篩查"},{"english":"support school meals","chinese":"支持學校膳食"},{"english":"promote active lifestyles","chinese":"推廣活躍生活方式"},{"english":"be shared widely","chinese":"被廣泛共享"},{"english":"rather than reserved for","chinese":"而不是只留給……"},{"english":"private care","chinese":"私營醫療服務"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"medical strategy","chinese":"醫療策略"},{"english":"social investment","chinese":"社會投資"},{"english":"remain healthy, productive, and independent","chinese":"保持健康、有生產力和獨立"},{"english":"prioritise the prevention of disease","chinese":"優先考慮疾病預防"},{"english":"avoidable suffering","chinese":"可避免的痛苦"},{"english":"lowers pressure on","chinese":"降低……的壓力"},{"english":"healthcare systems","chinese":"醫療系統"},{"english":"protects society more equally","chinese":"更公平地保護社會"},{"english":"treating illness matters","chinese":"治療疾病很重要"},{"english":"wiser use of public money","chinese":"更明智地使用公帑"}]},"model-essay-57-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-57-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:57","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-57-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q57","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many developed societies, ill health is increasingly linked not to infections, but to the way people live: long working hours, poor diets, chronic stress and physical inactivity. I completely disagree that this should lead us back towards traditional medicine. The more sensible response is to prevent these conditions through healthier routines and to keep treatment firmly based on modern evidence.","chinese":"在許多發達社會中，健康問題越來越不是與感染有關，而是與人們的生活方式有關：長時間工作、不良飲食、長期壓力以及缺乏運動。 我完全不同意這應該使我們重新回到傳統醫學。 更合理的回應，是透過更健康的日常習慣來預防這些問題，並讓治療牢牢建立在現代證據之上。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"Most modern lifestyle illnesses are rooted in habits and environments rather than in the absence of ancient remedies. A person who spends ten hours at a desk, eats takeaway meals and sleeps badly is not ill because society has forgotten herbal treatments; he is ill because his body is being pushed beyond healthy limits. In such a case, pills may reduce blood pressure or sugar levels, but no medicine, traditional or modern, can substitute for exercise, rest and better food. Therefore, governments, schools and employers should focus on prevention by promoting active transport, balanced diets, reasonable working hours and better mental-health support.","chinese":"大多數現代生活方式疾病的根源，在於習慣和環境，而不是因為缺乏古老療法。 一個每天在辦公桌前坐十小時、吃外賣、睡眠質素差的人，並不是因為社會忘記了草藥療法而生病；他生病是因為他的身體被推到了健康極限之外。 在這種情況下，藥物也許可以降低血壓或血糖水平，但無論是傳統醫學還是現代醫學，都不能取代運動、休息和更好的飲食。 因此，政府、學校和僱主應該把重點放在預防上，例如推廣主動出行、均衡飲食、合理工作時間，以及更好的心理健康支援。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Encouraging a return to traditional medicine could also give people a false sense of security. Traditional practices are often based on cultural memory rather than rigorous testing, so their effects, side effects and safe doses may be unclear. If patients rely on them for serious conditions linked to stress, obesity or heart disease, they may delay proper diagnosis until the problem becomes harder to treat. Modern healthcare is not perfect, but it offers check-ups, counselling, nutritional advice and medicines that can be tested, monitored and improved. Replacing this evidence-based system with traditional remedies would be like exchanging a map for a comforting story.","chinese":"鼓勵人們回歸傳統醫學，也可能給人一種錯誤的安全感。 傳統療法往往是基於文化記憶，而不是嚴謹測試，因此它們的效果、副作用和安全劑量可能並不清楚。 如果病人依賴它們來處理與壓力、肥胖或心臟病有關的嚴重問題，他們可能會延誤正確診斷，直到問題變得更難治療。 現代醫療並不完美，但它提供身體檢查、輔導、營養建議，以及可以被測試、監察和改良的藥物。 用傳統療法取代這種以證據為基礎的系統，就像用一張地圖換取一個令人安心的故事。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely disagree that society should encourage a return to traditional medicine. Lifestyle-related illnesses should be tackled through prevention and evidence-based healthcare, not through treatments whose reliability is often uncertain.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全不同意社會應該鼓勵人們回歸傳統醫學。 與生活方式有關的疾病，應該透過預防和以證據為基礎的醫療來處理，而不是依靠可靠性往往不確定的療法。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"developed societies","chinese":"發達社會"},{"english":"ill health","chinese":"健康欠佳"},{"english":"be increasingly linked to","chinese":"越來越與……有關"},{"english":"infections","chinese":"感染"},{"english":"the way people live","chinese":"人們的生活方式"},{"english":"long working hours","chinese":"長時間工作"},{"english":"poor diets","chinese":"不良飲食"},{"english":"chronic stress","chinese":"長期壓力"},{"english":"physical inactivity","chinese":"缺乏體能活動"},{"english":"lead us back towards","chinese":"帶領我們回到……"},{"english":"traditional medicine","chinese":"傳統醫學"},{"english":"sensible response","chinese":"明智得多的回應"},{"english":"prevent these conditions","chinese":"預防這些病症"},{"english":"healthier routines","chinese":"更健康的日常習慣"},{"english":"firmly based on","chinese":"牢牢建基於……"},{"english":"modern evidence","chinese":"現代證據"},{"english":"lifestyle illnesses","chinese":"生活方式疾病"},{"english":"be rooted in","chinese":"根源在於……"},{"english":"habits and environments","chinese":"習慣和環境"},{"english":"rather than in","chinese":"而不是在於……"},{"english":"the absence of","chinese":"缺乏……"},{"english":"ancient remedies","chinese":"古老療法"},{"english":"spend ten hours at a desk","chinese":"在書桌前坐十小時"},{"english":"takeaway meals","chinese":"外賣餐"},{"english":"sleep badly","chinese":"睡得不好"},{"english":"herbal treatments","chinese":"草藥療法"},{"english":"be pushed beyond healthy limits","chinese":"被推到超出健康界限"},{"english":"in such a case","chinese":"在這種情況下"},{"english":"blood pressure","chinese":"血壓"},{"english":"sugar levels","chinese":"血糖水平"},{"english":"substitute for","chinese":"取代"},{"english":"exercise, rest and better food","chinese":"運動、休息和更好的飲食"},{"english":"focus on prevention","chinese":"專注於預防"},{"english":"active transport","chinese":"主動出行"},{"english":"balanced diets","chinese":"均衡飲食"},{"english":"reasonable working hours","chinese":"合理工作時間"},{"english":"mental-health support","chinese":"精神健康支援"},{"english":"encouraging a return to","chinese":"鼓勵回歸……"},{"english":"false sense of security","chinese":"錯誤的安全感"},{"english":"traditional practices","chinese":"傳統做法"},{"english":"be based on","chinese":"建基於……"},{"english":"cultural memory","chinese":"文化記憶"},{"english":"rigorous testing","chinese":"嚴謹測試"},{"english":"effects, side effects and safe doses","chinese":"效果、副作用和安全劑量"},{"english":"be unclear","chinese":"不清楚"},{"english":"rely on","chinese":"依賴"},{"english":"serious conditions linked to","chinese":"與……有關的嚴重病症"},{"english":"obesity","chinese":"肥胖"},{"english":"heart disease","chinese":"心臟病"},{"english":"delay proper diagnosis","chinese":"延誤正確診斷"},{"english":"harder to treat","chinese":"較難治療"},{"english":"modern healthcare","chinese":"現代醫療"},{"english":"check-ups","chinese":"身體檢查"},{"english":"counselling","chinese":"輔導"},{"english":"nutritional advice","chinese":"營養建議"},{"english":"be tested, monitored and improved","chinese":"被測試、監察和改良"},{"english":"evidence-based system","chinese":"以證據為本的制度"},{"english":"traditional remedies","chinese":"傳統療法"},{"english":"exchanging a map for","chinese":"以……換取……"},{"english":"comforting story","chinese":"令人安心的故事"},{"english":"society should encourage","chinese":"社會應該鼓勵"},{"english":"lifestyle-related illnesses","chinese":"與生活方式有關的疾病"},{"english":"be tackled through","chinese":"透過……處理"},{"english":"prevention","chinese":"預防"},{"english":"evidence-based healthcare","chinese":"以證據為本的醫療"},{"english":"reliability is often uncertain","chinese":"可靠性往往不確定"}]},"model-essay-58-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-58-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:58","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-58-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q58","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Healthcare is one of the most essential public services in any society, and debates about who should pay for it are understandably sensitive. Some people argue that medical treatment should never be free because individuals are responsible for their own health. I completely disagree with this view, as illness is not always caused by personal choices, and free healthcare protects both individuals and society as a whole.","chinese":"醫療保健是任何社會中最基本的公共服務之一，而關於應由誰支付醫療費用的討論，自然是相當敏感的。 有些人認為，醫療服務不應該是免費的，因為個人應該對自己的健康負責。 我完全不同意這個觀點，因為疾病並不總是由個人選擇造成，而免費醫療能夠保護個人，也能保護整個社會。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that many health problems are beyond a person’s control. Although lifestyle choices such as diet, exercise, and smoking can affect health, it is far too simplistic to suggest that every patient is personally to blame for their condition. Children may be born with genetic disorders, workers may develop illnesses because of unsafe environments, and elderly people often require treatment simply because their bodies become weaker with age. For example, a low-income worker who develops cancer should not be denied medical care merely because they cannot afford expensive treatment. If healthcare depends entirely on personal wealth, disease becomes not only a medical problem but also a financial punishment for the vulnerable.","chinese":"第一個原因是，許多健康問題並不是個人能夠控制的。 雖然飲食、運動和吸煙等生活方式選擇會影響健康，但認為每位病人都應為自己的病情負上個人責任，這種說法實在過於簡化。 孩子可能天生患有遺傳疾病，工人可能因不安全的工作環境而患病，而長者往往只是因為身體隨年齡變弱而需要治療。 例如，一位低收入工人若患上癌症，不應該僅因為負擔不起昂貴治療而被剝奪醫療照顧 如果醫療完全取決於個人財富，疾病就不再只是醫學問題，也會變成對弱勢人士的一種經濟懲罰"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important point is that free healthcare benefits society, not just individual patients. When people can access treatment early, illnesses are more likely to be diagnosed before they become severe. This reduces pressure on hospitals in the long term and prevents contagious diseases from spreading widely. For instance, if poor families avoid seeing a doctor because of high fees, minor infections may worsen or spread to others in schools, workplaces, and communities. In this sense, free healthcare is not simply an act of kindness; it is a practical investment in public safety and social stability.","chinese":"另一個重要觀點是，免費醫療受益的不只是個別病人，而是整個社會。 當人們能夠及早接受治療時，疾病便更有可能在惡化之前被診斷出來。 從長遠來看，這能減輕醫院的壓力，並防止傳染病大範圍擴散。 例如，如果貧困家庭因為高昂費用而避免看醫生，輕微感染可能會惡化，或在學校、工作場所和社區中傳染給其他人。 從這個意義上說，免費醫療並不只是善意的表現；它更是對公共安全和社會穩定的一項實際投資。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I strongly disagree that healthcare should never be free. While individuals should certainly be encouraged to make healthy choices, society should not abandon people when they fall ill. A fair healthcare system recognises that health is partly personal, but never entirely personal.","chinese":"總結來說，我強烈不同意醫療永遠不應免費這個觀點。 雖然社會當然應該鼓勵個人作出健康的選擇，但當人們生病時，社會不應該拋棄他們。 一個公平的醫療制度會承認健康在某程度上屬於個人責任，但它絕不全只是個人的責任"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"healthcare","chinese":"醫療服務"},{"english":"essential public services","chinese":"必要公共服務"},{"english":"in any society","chinese":"在任何社會中"},{"english":"debates about","chinese":"關於……的爭論"},{"english":"understandably sensitive","chinese":"可以理解地敏感"},{"english":"medical treatment","chinese":"醫療治療"},{"english":"should never be free","chinese":"絕不應該免費"},{"english":"be responsible for","chinese":"對……負責"},{"english":"personal choices","chinese":"個人選擇"},{"english":"free healthcare","chinese":"免費醫療服務"},{"english":"society as a whole","chinese":"整個社會"},{"english":"health problems","chinese":"健康問題"},{"english":"beyond a person's control","chinese":"超出個人控制範圍"},{"english":"lifestyle choices","chinese":"生活方式選擇"},{"english":"affect health","chinese":"影響健康"},{"english":"far too simplistic to suggest","chinese":"認為……實在過於簡化"},{"english":"personally to blame for","chinese":"對……負有個人責任"},{"english":"their condition","chinese":"他們的病情"},{"english":"be born with","chinese":"天生患有"},{"english":"genetic disorders","chinese":"遺傳疾病"},{"english":"develop illnesses","chinese":"患上疾病"},{"english":"unsafe environments","chinese":"不安全的環境"},{"english":"elderly people","chinese":"長者"},{"english":"require treatment","chinese":"需要治療"},{"english":"become weaker with age","chinese":"隨着年齡增長而變弱"},{"english":"low-income worker","chinese":"低收入工人"},{"english":"develop cancer","chinese":"患上癌症"},{"english":"be denied medical care","chinese":"被拒絕醫療護理"},{"english":"merely because","chinese":"只是因為"},{"english":"afford expensive treatment","chinese":"負擔昂貴治療"},{"english":"depends entirely on","chinese":"完全取決於……"},{"english":"personal wealth","chinese":"個人財富"},{"english":"financial punishment","chinese":"經濟懲罰"}]},"model-essay-59-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-59-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:59","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-59-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q59","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Health has become a major concern in modern society, especially as many people now spend long hours sitting, working under pressure, and eating poorly. Some argue that exercising every day is the most effective way to become healthier. I completely agree with this view because daily exercise improves both physical condition and mental well-being in a way that few other habits can match.","chinese":"健康已成為現代社會中的一個主要關注，尤其是因為許多人如今長時間坐著、在壓力下工作，並且飲食不良。 有些人認為，每天運動是變得更健康的最有效方法。 我完全同意這個觀點，因為每天運動能改善身體狀況和心理健康，而很少有其他習慣能達到同樣的效果。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason is that regular physical activity directly strengthens the body. When people move every day, their heart, lungs, muscles, and joints are all forced to work, adapt, and become more resilient. This makes the body better able to control weight, maintain energy, and reduce the risk of common lifestyle problems. For example, an office worker who walks briskly for thirty minutes after work each day is likely to feel less tired, sleep more easily, and gradually become fitter. By contrast, a person who remains inactive may find that small physical tasks, such as climbing stairs or carrying shopping bags, become unnecessarily difficult. Therefore, daily exercise is not just a hobby; it is a practical foundation for better physical health.","chinese":"最有力的原因是，規律的身體活動能直接強化身體。 當人們每天活動時，他們的心臟、肺部、肌肉和關節都會被迫運作、適應，並變得更有韌性。 這使身體更能控制體重、維持精力，並降低常見生活方式問題的風險。 例如，一位上班族如果每天放工後快步走三十分鐘，很可能會感到較不疲倦、更容易入睡，並逐漸變得更健康。 相比之下，一個長期缺乏活動的人可能會發現，一些細小的體力任務，例如爬樓梯或提購物袋，都變得不必要地困難。 因此，每天運動不只是一種興趣；它是改善身體健康的實際基礎。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important point is that exercise also improves mental health, which is an essential part of overall well-being. Many people today suffer from stress because of study, work, and financial pressure. Daily exercise gives them a healthy outlet, allowing the mind to release tension rather than store it. For instance, a student who feels overwhelmed by examinations may feel calmer and more focused after jogging, swimming, or playing basketball. This kind of routine can also build discipline, confidence, and a stronger sense of control over life. As a result, exercise improves health not only from the outside, but also from the inside.","chinese":"另一個重要觀點是，運動也能改善心理健康，而是整體福祉中不可或缺的一部分 如今許多人因為學習、工作和經濟壓力而承受壓力。 每天運動能給他們一個健康的出口，讓心靈釋放壓力，而不是把壓力積存在內心。 例如，一個因考試而感到不堪重負的學生，在跑步、游泳或打籃球之後，可能會感到更平靜，也更能集中精神。 這種習慣也能培養自律、自信，以及對生活更強的掌控感。 結果是，運動不但從外在改善健康，也從內在改善健康。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully agree that exercising daily is the best way to improve health. It strengthens the body, clears the mind, and creates a stable routine that supports long-term well-being.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意每天運動是改善健康的最佳方法。 它能強化身體、清理思緒，並建立一種支持長遠福祉的穩定習慣。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"a major concern","chinese":"主要關注"},{"english":"modern society","chinese":"現代社會"},{"english":"especially as","chinese":"尤其因為"},{"english":"spend long hours sitting","chinese":"長時間坐着"},{"english":"work under pressure","chinese":"在壓力下工作"},{"english":"eat poorly","chinese":"飲食不良"},{"english":"some argue that","chinese":"有些人認為"},{"english":"exercising every day","chinese":"每日做運動"},{"english":"the most effective way to","chinese":"……的最有效方法"},{"english":"become healthier","chinese":"變得更健康"},{"english":"completely agree with this view","chinese":"完全同意這個看法"},{"english":"daily exercise","chinese":"每日運動"},{"english":"improve both","chinese":"同時改善"},{"english":"physical condition","chinese":"身體狀況"},{"english":"mental well-being","chinese":"精神健康；心理健康"},{"english":"few other habits can match","chinese":"很少其他習慣能媲美"},{"english":"the strongest reason","chinese":"最有力的原因"},{"english":"regular physical activity","chinese":"規律體能活動"},{"english":"directly strengthens the body","chinese":"直接強化身體"},{"english":"move every day","chinese":"每日活動身體"},{"english":"heart, lungs, muscles, and joints","chinese":"心臟、肺部、肌肉和關節"},{"english":"be forced to","chinese":"被迫去"},{"english":"work, adapt, and become more resilient","chinese":"運作、適應並變得更有韌性"},{"english":"become more resilient","chinese":"變得更有韌性"},{"english":"better able to","chinese":"更能夠"},{"english":"control weight","chinese":"控制體重"},{"english":"maintain energy","chinese":"保持精力"},{"english":"reduce the risk of","chinese":"減低……的風險"},{"english":"common lifestyle problems","chinese":"常見生活方式問題"},{"english":"an office worker","chinese":"辦公室職員"},{"english":"walk briskly","chinese":"快步行走"},{"english":"for thirty minutes","chinese":"三十分鐘"},{"english":"after work","chinese":"下班後"},{"english":"be likely to","chinese":"很可能會"},{"english":"feel less tired","chinese":"感到較不疲倦"},{"english":"sleep more easily","chinese":"更容易入睡"},{"english":"gradually become fitter","chinese":"逐漸變得更健壯"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相反"},{"english":"remain inactive","chinese":"保持不活動；缺乏活動"},{"english":"small physical tasks","chinese":"細小體力任務"},{"english":"climbing stairs","chinese":"行樓梯"},{"english":"carrying shopping bags","chinese":"提購物袋"},{"english":"become unnecessarily difficult","chinese":"變得不必要地困難"}]},"model-essay-60-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-60-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:60","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-60-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q60","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"It is often argued that doctors ought to take responsibility for teaching patients how to protect and improve their health. I completely agree with this view, because medical advice is most effective when it is practical, personal, and given by someone whom patients already trust.","chinese":"人們經常主張，醫生應該承擔責任，教導病人如何保護並改善自己的健康。 我完全同意這個觀點，因為當醫療建議具備實用性、個人化，並由病人本已信任的人提出時，它最能發揮效果。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that doctors are in the best position to turn general health knowledge into specific guidance. Many people already know that they should eat well, exercise regularly, and avoid harmful habits, but such advice can feel vague and easy to ignore. A doctor, however, can connect these habits directly to a patient’s condition. For example, a patient with high blood pressure may not understand the danger of a salty diet until a doctor explains how it affects the heart and blood vessels. In that moment, education is not just information; it becomes a wake-up call. When advice is linked to a real medical risk, patients are more likely to take it seriously and change their behaviour.","chinese":"第一個原因是，醫生最有能力把一般性的健康知識轉化為具體指導。 很多人其實已經知道自己應該健康飲食、定期運動，並避免有害習慣，但這類建議可能會顯得模糊，也很容易被忽視。 然而，醫生可以把這些習慣直接與病人的身體狀況聯繫起來。 例如，一名患有高血壓的病人，可能直到醫生解釋高鹽飲食如何影響心臟和血管時，才真正明白其危險性。 在那一刻，教育不只是資訊；它變成了一次警醒。 當建議與真實的健康風險聯繫起來時，病人便更可能認真對待，並改變自己的行為。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important reason is that patient education can prevent future illness and reduce pressure on the healthcare system. If doctors only treat diseases after they appear, medicine becomes a cycle of repair rather than prevention. By explaining early warning signs, healthy routines, and the consequences of neglecting minor symptoms, doctors can help patients avoid serious problems later. For instance, a person who is taught how to manage weight, sleep, and stress may be less likely to develop long-term conditions such as diabetes or heart disease. This not only improves individual well-being, but also allows hospitals and clinics to focus more resources on patients who urgently need treatment.","chinese":"另一個重要原因是，病人教育能夠預防未來疾病，並減輕醫療系統的壓力。 如果醫生只是在疾病出現後才加以治療，醫療就會變成一個修補的循環，而不是預防。 透過解釋早期警號、健康日常習慣，以及忽視輕微症狀的後果，醫生能夠幫助病人避免日後出現嚴重問題。 例如，一個學會如何管理體重、睡眠和壓力的人，日後患上糖尿病或心臟病等長期疾病的可能性可能會較低。 這不但能改善個人的健康福祉，也能讓醫院和診所有更多資源集中照顧迫切需要治療的病人"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully agree that doctors should educate patients about improving their health. Their guidance is trusted, personalised, and potentially life-changing, so health education should be seen as a core part of medical care rather than an optional extra.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意醫生應該教育病人如何改善健康。 他們的指導值得信任、具個人化，而且可能改變人生，因此健康教育應被視為醫療照護的核心部分，而不是可有可無的附加項目。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"it is often argued that","chinese":"人們經常認為……"},{"english":"ought to take responsibility for","chinese":"應該承擔……的責任"},{"english":"teaching patients how to","chinese":"教導病人如何……"},{"english":"protect and improve their health","chinese":"保護和改善健康"},{"english":"completely agree with","chinese":"完全同意……"},{"english":"medical advice","chinese":"醫療建議"},{"english":"most effective when","chinese":"在……時最有效"},{"english":"practical, personal, and given by","chinese":"實用、個人化，並由……給出"},{"english":"already trust","chinese":"已經信任"},{"english":"in the best position to","chinese":"最適合去……"},{"english":"general health knowledge","chinese":"一般健康知識"},{"english":"specific guidance","chinese":"具體指引"},{"english":"eat well","chinese":"飲食健康"},{"english":"exercise regularly","chinese":"定期運動"},{"english":"avoid harmful habits","chinese":"避免有害習慣"},{"english":"feel vague","chinese":"感覺含糊"},{"english":"easy to ignore","chinese":"容易忽視"},{"english":"connect these habits directly to","chinese":"將這些習慣直接聯繫到……"},{"english":"patient's condition","chinese":"病人的病情"},{"english":"high blood pressure","chinese":"高血壓"},{"english":"the danger of","chinese":"……的危險"},{"english":"salty diet","chinese":"高鹽飲食"},{"english":"affects the heart and blood vessels","chinese":"影響心臟和血管"},{"english":"in that moment","chinese":"在那一刻"},{"english":"not just information","chinese":"不只是資料"},{"english":"wake-up call","chinese":"警醒；警號"},{"english":"be linked to","chinese":"與……聯繫起來"},{"english":"real medical risk","chinese":"真正的醫療風險"},{"english":"be more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"take it seriously","chinese":"認真看待它"},{"english":"change their behaviour","chinese":"改變行為"},{"english":"patient education","chinese":"病人教育"},{"english":"prevent future illness","chinese":"預防日後疾病"},{"english":"reduce pressure on","chinese":"減輕……的壓力"},{"english":"healthcare system","chinese":"醫療系統"},{"english":"treat diseases","chinese":"治療疾病"},{"english":"after they appear","chinese":"在它們出現之後"},{"english":"a cycle of repair","chinese":"修補循環"},{"english":"rather than prevention","chinese":"而不是預防"},{"english":"early warning signs","chinese":"早期警號"},{"english":"healthy routines","chinese":"健康生活習慣"},{"english":"the consequences of","chinese":"……的後果"},{"english":"neglecting minor symptoms","chinese":"忽視輕微症狀"},{"english":"avoid serious problems later","chinese":"避免日後出現嚴重問題"},{"english":"manage weight, sleep, and stress","chinese":"管理體重、睡眠和壓力"},{"english":"be less likely to develop","chinese":"較不可能患上……"},{"english":"long-term conditions","chinese":"長期病患"},{"english":"diabetes","chinese":"糖尿病"},{"english":"heart disease","chinese":"心臟病"},{"english":"individual well-being","chinese":"個人身心健康"},{"english":"allows hospitals and clinics to","chinese":"讓醫院和診所可以……"},{"english":"focus more resources on","chinese":"將更多資源集中於……"},{"english":"urgently need treatment","chinese":"急需治療"},{"english":"educate patients about","chinese":"教育病人有關……"},{"english":"trusted, personalised, and potentially life-changing","chinese":"可信、個人化，而且有可能改變人生"},{"english":"potentially life-changing","chinese":"有可能改變人生"},{"english":"health education","chinese":"健康教育"},{"english":"core part of","chinese":"……的核心部分"},{"english":"medical care","chinese":"醫療護理"},{"english":"optional extra","chinese":"可有可無的附加項目"}]},"model-essay-61-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-61-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:61","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-61-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q61","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Urban land is becoming scarce, so decisions about empty plots in cities and towns require careful judgement. Although many people believe these spaces should be used for residential buildings, I completely agree that they should be reserved for trees and green areas, because this would make urban life healthier and more sustainable.","chinese":"城市土地正變得越來越稀缺，因此關於城市和城鎮中空置土地的決定需要審慎判斷。 儘管許多人認為這些空間應該用來興建住宅樓宇， 我完全同意它們應該被保留作種植樹木和綠化空間之用，因為這會令城市生活更健康、更可持續。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The most immediate reason is that trees make densely populated areas far more liveable. In many towns, residents already spend their daily lives surrounded by roads, concrete walls, and traffic, so the few remaining open spaces should not simply be swallowed by more construction. Trees provide shade, reduce dust, soften noise, and give people somewhere calm to walk or rest. A city without greenery can feel like a concrete oven, especially during hot seasons. For example, a small tree-filled space near apartment blocks can become a place where children play safely, elderly people exercise, and office workers clear their minds after work. This does not merely improve the appearance of a neighbourhood; it supports public health and everyday well-being.","chinese":"最直接的原因是，樹木能使人口密集的地區更加宜居。 在許多城鎮中，居民的日常生活已經被道路、混凝土牆和交通包圍，因此僅餘的少數空地不應該只是被更多建築吞噬。 樹木能提供陰涼、減少塵埃、緩和噪音，並給人們一個安靜散步或休息的地方。 一個沒有綠化的城市可能會感覺像一個混凝土焗爐，尤其是在炎熱季節。 例如，公寓大樓附近一片種滿樹木的小空間，可以成為孩子安全玩耍、長者運動，以及上班族下班後放鬆頭腦的地方。 這並不只是改善社區的外觀；它也支持公共健康和日常福祉。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that building housing on every vacant plot is a short-sighted solution to urban problems. Housing shortages are serious, but they should be addressed through better planning, redevelopment of abandoned buildings, and more efficient use of existing residential land. If every empty area is turned into apartments, cities may gain a few more homes but lose the natural spaces that help them breathe. More buildings can also increase traffic, put pressure on drainage systems, and make crowded districts even more stressful. By contrast, trees act as quiet public infrastructure: they cool the air, absorb pollution, and reduce the impact of heavy rain. Once these green spaces are destroyed, they are extremely difficult to restore.","chinese":"另一個原因是，在每一塊空置土地上興建住房，是一種短視的城市問題解決方法。 住房短缺確實嚴重，但它們應該透過更好的規劃、重建廢棄建築，以及更有效地利用現有住宅用地來處理。 如果每一片空地都被改建成公寓，城市或許會多獲得一些住房，但卻會失去幫助它們呼吸的自然空間。 更多建築也可能增加交通流量、加重排水系統的壓力，並令擁擠地區變得更加壓抑。 相比之下，樹木就像安靜的公共基礎設施：它們能降低氣溫、吸收污染，並減輕暴雨帶來的影響。 一旦這些綠色空間被破壞，它們就極難恢復。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I strongly agree that vacant urban areas should be used for planting trees rather than constructing more housing. Homes are necessary, but cities also need green lungs if they are to remain healthy, humane, and sustainable.","chinese":"總結來說，我強烈同意城市中的空置地區應該用來種植樹木，而不是建造更多住房。 住房是必要的，但如果城市要保持健康、人性化和可持續，它們也需要綠色的肺。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"urban land","chinese":"城市土地"},{"english":"becoming scarce","chinese":"變得短缺"},{"english":"empty plots","chinese":"空置地皮"},{"english":"cities and towns","chinese":"城市和市鎮"},{"english":"require careful judgement","chinese":"需要謹慎判斷"},{"english":"residential buildings","chinese":"住宅樓宇"},{"english":"be reserved for","chinese":"被保留作……用途"},{"english":"trees and green areas","chinese":"樹木和綠化地區"},{"english":"urban life","chinese":"城市生活"},{"english":"more sustainable","chinese":"更可持續"},{"english":"the most immediate reason","chinese":"最直接的原因"},{"english":"densely populated areas","chinese":"人口稠密地區"},{"english":"far more liveable","chinese":"宜居得多"},{"english":"daily lives","chinese":"日常生活"},{"english":"be surrounded by","chinese":"被……包圍"},{"english":"concrete walls","chinese":"石屎牆"},{"english":"traffic","chinese":"交通；車流"},{"english":"remaining open spaces","chinese":"剩餘的開放空間"},{"english":"be swallowed by","chinese":"被……吞噬"},{"english":"construction","chinese":"建築工程"},{"english":"provide shade","chinese":"提供遮蔭"},{"english":"reduce dust","chinese":"減少塵埃"},{"english":"soften noise","chinese":"減低噪音"},{"english":"somewhere calm to","chinese":"可以安靜地……的地方"},{"english":"walk or rest","chinese":"散步或休息"},{"english":"without greenery","chinese":"沒有綠化"},{"english":"concrete oven","chinese":"石屎焗爐"},{"english":"especially during","chinese":"尤其是在……期間"},{"english":"hot seasons","chinese":"炎熱季節"},{"english":"tree-filled space","chinese":"種滿樹木的空間"},{"english":"apartment blocks","chinese":"住宅大廈"},{"english":"play safely","chinese":"安全地玩耍"},{"english":"elderly people","chinese":"長者"},{"english":"office workers","chinese":"辦公室員工"},{"english":"clear their minds","chinese":"清理思緒"},{"english":"after work","chinese":"下班後"},{"english":"does not merely improve","chinese":"不只是改善"},{"english":"appearance of a neighbourhood","chinese":"社區外觀"},{"english":"supports public health","chinese":"支持公共健康"},{"english":"everyday well-being","chinese":"日常身心健康"},{"english":"vacant plot","chinese":"空置地皮"},{"english":"short-sighted solution","chinese":"短視的解決方法"},{"english":"urban problems","chinese":"城市問題"},{"english":"housing shortages","chinese":"房屋短缺"},{"english":"be addressed through","chinese":"透過……處理"},{"english":"better planning","chinese":"更好的規劃"},{"english":"redevelopment of abandoned buildings","chinese":"重建廢棄建築物"},{"english":"more efficient use of","chinese":"更有效使用……"},{"english":"existing residential land","chinese":"現有住宅土地"},{"english":"be turned into apartments","chinese":"被改建成住宅單位"},{"english":"gain a few more homes","chinese":"增加少量住宅"},{"english":"natural spaces","chinese":"自然空間"},{"english":"help them breathe","chinese":"幫助城市呼吸"},{"english":"increase traffic","chinese":"增加交通流量"},{"english":"put pressure on","chinese":"對……造成壓力"},{"english":"drainage systems","chinese":"排水系統"},{"english":"crowded districts","chinese":"擠迫地區"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"quiet public infrastructure","chinese":"安靜的公共基礎設施"},{"english":"cool the air","chinese":"令空氣降溫"},{"english":"absorb pollution","chinese":"吸收污染"},{"english":"reduce the impact of","chinese":"減低……的影響"},{"english":"heavy rain","chinese":"大雨"},{"english":"be destroyed","chinese":"被破壞"},{"english":"extremely difficult to restore","chinese":"極難恢復"},{"english":"vacant urban areas","chinese":"城市空置地"},{"english":"planting trees","chinese":"種樹"},{"english":"rather than constructing","chinese":"而不是建造……"},{"english":"green lungs","chinese":"綠肺"},{"english":"remain healthy, humane, and sustainable","chinese":"保持健康、人性化和可持續"}]},"model-essay-62-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-62-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:62","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-62-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q62","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In my view, cities should definitely be designed to appeal to both residents and international visitors. A successful city is not merely a place where people live or pass through; it is a public home whose streets, buildings, and open spaces should make daily life richer while also presenting the city confidently to the wider world.","chinese":"在我看來，城市確實應該被設計得能夠吸引本地居民和國際旅客。 一個成功的城市不僅僅是一個讓人居住或經過的地方；它是一個公共的家園，而它的街道、建築和開放空間應該讓日常生活更加豐富，同時也自信地向更廣闊的世界展現這座城市。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason is that attractive urban design improves the lives of local people. When a city contains green parks, safe pavements, efficient public transport, and welcoming community spaces, residents are more likely to walk, meet, relax, and feel attached to their surroundings. This matters because people do not experience a city only through major landmarks; they experience it through their daily routines, from commuting to work to taking their children to playgrounds. For example, a well-designed square with shade, seating, trees, and nearby shops can become a small social heart of a neighbourhood. It gives people somewhere to pause, talk, and breathe. In this sense, beauty is not a luxury; it is part of public well-being.","chinese":"最有力的原因是，具吸引力的城市設計能改善本地人的生活。 當一座城市擁有綠色公園、安全的人行道、高效的公共交通，以及令人感到親切的社區空間時，居民便更有可能步行、見面、放鬆，並對周圍環境產生歸屬感。 這一點很重要，因為人們並不是只透過主要地標去體驗一座城市；他們是透過日常生活去體驗城市，從上班通勤到帶孩子去遊樂場都是如此。 例如，一個設計良好的廣場，如果有遮蔭、座位、樹木和附近的商店，就可以成為一個社區小小的社交核心。 它給人們一個可以停下來、交談和喘息的地方。 從這個意義上說，美感並不是一種奢侈品；它是公共福祉的一部分。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"At the same time, designing cities to attract foreign tourists is equally important because tourism can strengthen both the economy and cultural identity of a place. Visitors are drawn to cities that are clean, accessible, distinctive, and easy to explore. If historic streets, museums, waterfronts, and public markets are carefully maintained, tourists will spend money in local businesses while also learning about the character of the city. More importantly, this kind of design does not have to serve outsiders at the expense of residents. A preserved old district, a lively pedestrian street, or a clear transport system benefits everyone. Good urban design can therefore turn local culture into something shared rather than something hidden.","chinese":"同時，把城市設計得能吸引外國遊客也同樣重要，因為旅遊業可以同時加強一個地方的經濟和文化身份。 遊客會被那些乾淨、交通便利、具獨特性，而且容易探索的城市所吸引。 如果歷史街道、博物館、海濱和公共市場得到細心維護，遊客便會在本地商店消費，同時也會了解這座城市的特色。 更重要的是，這種設計不必以犧牲居民利益為代價去服務外來者。 一個被保留下來的舊區、一條充滿活力的行人街，或者一個清晰易用的交通系統，都能惠及所有人。 因此，良好的城市設計可以把本地文化變成一種被共同分享的東西，而不是被隱藏起來的東西。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully agree that cities should be made attractive for both local people and foreign tourists. When this is done well, a city becomes liveable for its residents and memorable for its visitors.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意城市應該被打造得對本地人和外國遊客都具有吸引力。 當這一點做得好時，一座城市便會成為居民宜居的地方，也會成為遊客難忘的地方。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"be designed to","chinese":"被設計成……"},{"english":"appeal to","chinese":"吸引；迎合"},{"english":"residents and international visitors","chinese":"居民和國際遊客"},{"english":"successful city","chinese":"成功的城市"},{"english":"not merely","chinese":"不只是"},{"english":"pass through","chinese":"經過"},{"english":"public home","chinese":"公共家園"},{"english":"open spaces","chinese":"開放空間"},{"english":"make daily life richer","chinese":"令日常生活更豐富"},{"english":"present the city confidently to","chinese":"自信地向……展示城市"},{"english":"the wider world","chinese":"更廣闊的世界"},{"english":"attractive urban design","chinese":"吸引人的城市設計"},{"english":"improve the lives of","chinese":"改善……的生活"},{"english":"local people","chinese":"本地人"},{"english":"green parks","chinese":"綠化公園"},{"english":"safe pavements","chinese":"安全的行人路"},{"english":"efficient public transport","chinese":"高效公共交通"},{"english":"welcoming community spaces","chinese":"友善宜人的社區空間"},{"english":"be more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"feel attached to","chinese":"對……有歸屬感"},{"english":"their surroundings","chinese":"他們周圍的環境"},{"english":"this matters because","chinese":"這很重要，因為……"},{"english":"experience a city through","chinese":"透過……體驗一座城市"},{"english":"major landmarks","chinese":"主要地標"},{"english":"daily routines","chinese":"日常習慣"},{"english":"commuting to work","chinese":"上班通勤"},{"english":"taking their children to playgrounds","chinese":"帶孩子去遊樂場"},{"english":"well-designed square","chinese":"設計良好的廣場"},{"english":"shade","chinese":"遮蔭"},{"english":"seating","chinese":"座位"},{"english":"nearby shops","chinese":"附近商店"},{"english":"social heart of","chinese":"……的社交核心"},{"english":"neighbourhood","chinese":"社區"},{"english":"somewhere to pause","chinese":"可以停下來的地方"},{"english":"talk, and breathe","chinese":"交談和放鬆"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"not a luxury","chinese":"不是奢侈品"},{"english":"public well-being","chinese":"公共福祉"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"attract foreign tourists","chinese":"吸引外國遊客"},{"english":"equally important","chinese":"同樣重要"},{"english":"tourism","chinese":"旅遊業"},{"english":"strengthen both","chinese":"同時加強兩者"},{"english":"cultural identity","chinese":"文化身份"},{"english":"be drawn to","chinese":"被……吸引"},{"english":"clean, accessible, distinctive, and easy to explore","chinese":"清潔、容易到達、有特色和易於探索"},{"english":"easy to explore","chinese":"易於探索"},{"english":"historic streets","chinese":"歷史街道"},{"english":"museums","chinese":"博物館"},{"english":"waterfronts","chinese":"海濱地區"},{"english":"public markets","chinese":"公共市場"},{"english":"carefully maintained","chinese":"細心保養"},{"english":"spend money in","chinese":"在……消費"},{"english":"local businesses","chinese":"本地商戶"},{"english":"learn about","chinese":"了解"},{"english":"the character of the city","chinese":"城市特色"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"serve outsiders","chinese":"服務外來人士"},{"english":"at the expense of","chinese":"以犧牲……為代價"},{"english":"preserved old district","chinese":"保留下來的舊區"},{"english":"lively pedestrian street","chinese":"熱鬧的行人專用街道"},{"english":"clear transport system","chinese":"清晰的交通系統"},{"english":"benefits everyone","chinese":"令所有人受惠"},{"english":"good urban design","chinese":"良好的城市設計"},{"english":"turn local culture into","chinese":"將本地文化變成……"},{"english":"something shared rather than something hidden","chinese":"共享的東西，而不是隱藏的東西"},{"english":"be made attractive for","chinese":"被打造得對……有吸引力"},{"english":"local people and foreign tourists","chinese":"本地人和外國遊客"},{"english":"when this is done well","chinese":"當這件事做得好時"},{"english":"liveable for","chinese":"對……宜居"},{"english":"memorable for","chinese":"對……來說難忘"}]},"model-essay-63-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-63-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:63","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-63-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q63","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Some people argue that key services, including shops, schools and commercial centres, should be moved away from central urban areas. I completely disagree, because this would reduce access to essential facilities and weaken the social and economic life of cities.","chinese":"有些人認為，主要服務設施，包括商店、學校和商業中心，應該搬離城市中心地區。 我完全不同意，因為這樣做會降低人們使用基本設施的便利性，並削弱城市的社會與經濟活力。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason for keeping these services in city centres is accessibility. Central districts are usually where transport networks meet, so people from different neighbourhoods can reach schools, shops and workplaces without travelling far. If these services were pushed to the outskirts, many residents would have to rely on cars or longer public-transport journeys. This would be especially harmful for families with young children, elderly people and low-income workers, who may not have the money or flexibility to travel long distances every day. For example, a parent who can now take a child to a nearby school and then walk to work might be forced into a costly commute. Relocation, therefore, would not make cities better organised; it would simply make daily life less convenient and less fair.","chinese":"把這些服務保留在市中心的最有力理由，是可及性。 中心地區通常是交通網絡匯聚的地方，因此來自不同社區的人可以不必長途跋涉，便到達學校、商店和工作場所。 如果這些服務被推到城市外圍，許多居民就不得不依賴汽車，或者花更長時間乘坐公共交通。 這對有年幼子女的家庭、長者和低收入工人尤其不利，因為他們未必有金錢或時間彈性每天長距離通勤。 例如，一位家長現在可以把孩子帶到附近的學校，然後步行上班；但如果服務搬離市中心，他可能會被迫承擔昂貴的通勤。 因此，搬遷這些服務並不會令城市規劃得更好；它只會讓日常生活變得更不方便，也更不公平。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important point is that these services keep city centres alive. Shops, schools and commercial centres create foot traffic, employment and regular human interaction. Without them, central areas could become empty spaces that people pass through rather than places where communities actually function. Moving businesses to the edge of the city could also encourage car-dependent development, increasing congestion and pollution instead of reducing them. A healthy city centre should not be a silent monument of offices and roads; it should be a mixed, active environment where people can learn, work, buy goods and meet others in the same area.","chinese":"另一個重要觀點是，這些服務能讓市中心保持活力。 商店、學校和商業中心能帶來人流、就業機會，以及持續的人際互動。 如果沒有這些服務，中心地區可能會變成人們只是經過的空洞空間，而不再是真正有社區功能的地方。 把商業設施搬到城市邊緣，也可能鼓勵依賴汽車的發展模式，從而增加交通擠塞和污染，而不是減少它們。 一個健康的市中心不應該只是由辦公室和道路組成的沉默紀念碑；它應該是一個混合而活躍的環境，讓人們可以在同一區域學習、工作、購物和與他人相遇。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely disagree that major services should be relocated out of city centres. Keeping them there protects accessibility, supports urban life and makes cities more practical for the people who use them every day.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全不同意主要服務應該搬離市中心。 把它們保留在市中心能保障可及性、支持城市生活，並讓城市對每天使用它的人來說更加實用。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"key services","chinese":"主要服務"},{"english":"including shops, schools and commercial centres","chinese":"包括商店、學校和商業中心"},{"english":"be moved away from","chinese":"從……遷走"},{"english":"central urban areas","chinese":"城市中心地區"},{"english":"reduce access to","chinese":"減少接觸……的機會"},{"english":"essential facilities","chinese":"必要設施"},{"english":"weaken the social and economic life of","chinese":"削弱……的社會和經濟生活"},{"english":"city centres","chinese":"市中心"},{"english":"the strongest reason for","chinese":"……的最有力原因"},{"english":"keeping these services","chinese":"保留這些服務"},{"english":"accessibility","chinese":"可達性；方便到達"},{"english":"central districts","chinese":"中心區"},{"english":"transport networks meet","chinese":"交通網絡交匯"},{"english":"different neighbourhoods","chinese":"不同社區"},{"english":"reach schools, shops and workplaces","chinese":"到達學校、商店和工作地點"},{"english":"without travelling far","chinese":"不用走很遠"},{"english":"be pushed to the outskirts","chinese":"被推到市郊"},{"english":"the outskirts","chinese":"市郊；外圍地區"},{"english":"rely on cars","chinese":"依賴汽車"},{"english":"public-transport journeys","chinese":"公共交通旅程"},{"english":"especially harmful for","chinese":"對……特別有害"},{"english":"families with young children","chinese":"有年幼子女的家庭"},{"english":"elderly people","chinese":"長者"},{"english":"low-income workers","chinese":"低收入工人"},{"english":"the money or flexibility to","chinese":"金錢或靈活性去……"},{"english":"travel long distances","chinese":"長途出行"},{"english":"nearby school","chinese":"附近的學校"},{"english":"walk to work","chinese":"步行上班"},{"english":"be forced into","chinese":"被迫陷入……"},{"english":"costly commute","chinese":"昂貴的通勤"},{"english":"relocation","chinese":"遷移；搬遷"},{"english":"better organised","chinese":"組織得更好"},{"english":"less convenient and less fair","chinese":"較不方便和較不公平"},{"english":"another important point","chinese":"另一個重要觀點"},{"english":"keep city centres alive","chinese":"令市中心保持活力"},{"english":"create foot traffic","chinese":"帶來人流"},{"english":"employment","chinese":"就業機會"},{"english":"regular human interaction","chinese":"恆常的人際互動"},{"english":"empty spaces","chinese":"空蕩的地方"},{"english":"pass through rather than","chinese":"只是經過而不是……"},{"english":"places where communities actually function","chinese":"社區真正運作的地方"},{"english":"move businesses to","chinese":"將商業遷到……"},{"english":"the edge of the city","chinese":"城市邊緣"},{"english":"car-dependent development","chinese":"依賴汽車的發展"},{"english":"increasing congestion and pollution","chinese":"增加交通擠塞和污染"},{"english":"instead of reducing them","chinese":"而不是減少它們"},{"english":"healthy city centre","chinese":"健康的市中心"},{"english":"silent monument","chinese":"沉默的紀念碑"},{"english":"offices and roads","chinese":"辦公室和道路"},{"english":"mixed, active environment","chinese":"多元而活躍的環境"},{"english":"buy goods","chinese":"購買商品"},{"english":"in the same area","chinese":"在同一區域"},{"english":"major services","chinese":"主要服務"},{"english":"be relocated out of","chinese":"從……遷出"},{"english":"protect accessibility","chinese":"保障可達性"},{"english":"support urban life","chinese":"支持城市生活"},{"english":"make cities more practical for","chinese":"令城市對……更實用"},{"english":"use them every day","chinese":"每天使用它們"}]},"model-essay-64-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-64-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:64","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-64-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q64","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Urban planners often face difficult choices over how limited land should be used. Some people argue that public green spaces should take priority over new residential projects. I strongly disagree with this view, because affordable housing is a more basic urban need, and parks can still be protected through intelligent design.","chinese":"城市規劃者經常面對艱難的選擇，要決定有限的土地應該如何被使用。 有些人認為，公共綠化空間應該比新的住宅發展項目獲得更高優先次序。 我強烈不同意這個觀點，因為可負擔住房是更基本的城市需要，而公園仍然可以透過明智的設計得到保護。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main reason is that housing directly affects people's security, health and dignity. When cities fail to build enough homes, rents rise, families are forced into overcrowded flats, and young adults may be unable to live independently. These problems do not stay private; they spill into society through homelessness, long commutes and weaker community ties. For example, a teacher who cannot afford to live near school may spend hours travelling every day, arriving tired before the working day even begins. A pleasant park may improve that person's weekend, but a stable home shapes every day of their life. Therefore, where land is limited, residential development should come first.","chinese":"主要原因是，住房直接影響人們的安全感、健康和尊嚴。 當城市未能興建足夠住房時，租金會上升，家庭會被迫住進過度擠迫的單位，而年輕成年人也可能無法獨立生活。 這些問題不會只停留在私人層面；它們會透過無家可歸、漫長通勤和較弱的社區聯繫擴散到整個社會。 例如，一位負擔不起住在學校附近的教師，可能每天要花數小時通勤，甚至在工作日正式開始前已經感到疲憊。 一個舒適的公園也許能改善那個人的週末，但一個穩定的住所卻會塑造他們生活中的每一天。 因此，在土地有限的地方，住宅發展應該優先。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that prioritising housing does not mean sacrificing nature. The real issue is not whether cities should have homes or green spaces, but whether they can combine the two wisely. Modern housing projects can include small gardens, tree-lined streets, rooftop greenery and shared courtyards, giving residents access to nature without leaving badly needed homes unbuilt. By contrast, placing large parks above housing developments may create attractive scenery while ordinary workers are priced out of the city. A city that looks green but cannot house its people is like a beautifully painted door that no one can enter. Parks should therefore support housing policy, not outrank it.","chinese":"另一個原因是，優先考慮住房並不代表要犧牲自然。 真正的問題並不是城市應該擁有住房還是綠化空間，是它們能否明智地把兩者結合起來 現代住宅項目可以包括小花園、綠樹成蔭的街道、天台綠化和共享庭院，讓居民能夠接觸自然，同時又不會讓急需的住房無法興建。 相比之下，把大型公園置於住宅發展之上，可能會創造吸引人的景觀，卻同時令普通工人被高昂成本排擠出城市。 一座看起來綠意盎然卻無法安置居民的城市，就像一扇畫得很漂亮、但沒有人能夠進入的門 因此，公園應該配合住房政策，而不是凌駕於住房政策之上。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I strongly disagree that cities should prioritise parks rather than housing developments. Green spaces are valuable, but housing is the foundation of a liveable city.","chinese":"總結來說，我強烈不同意城市應該優先考慮公園而不是住宅發展。 綠化空間固然有價值，但住房才是一座宜居城市的基礎。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"urban planners","chinese":"城市規劃師"},{"english":"face difficult choices over","chinese":"面對關於……的艱難選擇"},{"english":"limited land","chinese":"有限土地"},{"english":"be used","chinese":"被使用"},{"english":"public green spaces","chinese":"公共綠化空間"},{"english":"take priority over","chinese":"優先於……"},{"english":"residential projects","chinese":"住宅項目"},{"english":"strongly disagree with","chinese":"強烈不同意……"},{"english":"affordable housing","chinese":"可負擔住屋"},{"english":"basic urban need","chinese":"基本城市需要"},{"english":"be protected through","chinese":"透過……得到保護"},{"english":"intelligent design","chinese":"智慧設計"},{"english":"the main reason","chinese":"主要原因"},{"english":"directly affects","chinese":"直接影響"},{"english":"security, health and dignity","chinese":"安全感、健康和尊嚴"},{"english":"fail to build enough homes","chinese":"未能興建足夠住宅"},{"english":"rents rise","chinese":"租金上升"},{"english":"be forced into","chinese":"被迫住進；被迫進入"},{"english":"overcrowded flats","chinese":"擠迫單位"},{"english":"young adults","chinese":"年輕成年人"},{"english":"live independently","chinese":"獨立生活"},{"english":"spill into society","chinese":"擴散到社會層面"},{"english":"homelessness","chinese":"無家者問題；露宿問題"},{"english":"long commutes","chinese":"漫長通勤"},{"english":"weaker community ties","chinese":"較薄弱的社區聯繫"},{"english":"cannot afford to","chinese":"負擔不起去……"},{"english":"live near school","chinese":"住在學校附近"},{"english":"spend hours travelling","chinese":"花數小時通勤；花數小時出行"},{"english":"arriving tired","chinese":"疲倦地到達"},{"english":"working day","chinese":"工作日"},{"english":"pleasant park","chinese":"宜人的公園"},{"english":"shape every day of","chinese":"塑造……的每一天"},{"english":"stable home","chinese":"穩定住所"},{"english":"residential development","chinese":"住宅發展"},{"english":"come first","chinese":"放在首位"},{"english":"prioritising housing","chinese":"優先考慮住屋"},{"english":"sacrificing nature","chinese":"犧牲自然環境"},{"english":"the real issue","chinese":"真正問題"},{"english":"combine the two wisely","chinese":"明智地結合兩者"},{"english":"modern housing projects","chinese":"現代住宅項目"},{"english":"include small gardens","chinese":"包括小花園"},{"english":"tree-lined streets","chinese":"綠樹成蔭的街道"},{"english":"rooftop greenery","chinese":"天台綠化"},{"english":"shared courtyards","chinese":"共享庭院"},{"english":"give residents access to","chinese":"讓居民接觸到……"},{"english":"access to nature","chinese":"接觸自然的機會"},{"english":"badly needed homes","chinese":"急需的住宅"},{"english":"leaving homes unbuilt","chinese":"讓住宅沒有被興建"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"place large parks above","chinese":"將大型公園置於……之上"},{"english":"housing developments","chinese":"住宅發展項目"},{"english":"attractive scenery","chinese":"吸引人的景色"},{"english":"ordinary workers","chinese":"普通工人"},{"english":"be priced out of the city","chinese":"因負擔不起而被迫離開城市"},{"english":"a beautifully painted door","chinese":"漆得漂亮的門"},{"english":"no one can enter","chinese":"沒有人能進入"},{"english":"support housing policy","chinese":"支持住屋政策"},{"english":"outrank it","chinese":"凌駕於其上"},{"english":"prioritise parks rather than","chinese":"優先考慮公園而不是……"},{"english":"green spaces are valuable","chinese":"綠化空間有價值"},{"english":"the foundation of","chinese":"……的基礎"},{"english":"liveable city","chinese":"宜居城市"}]},"model-essay-65-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-65-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:65","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-65-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q65","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Translation software has become an ordinary part of daily life, and it can now convert many texts within seconds. However, I completely disagree that this makes foreign-language learning pointless, because a language is not only a tool for decoding words; it is also a way of thinking, building relationships and participating in another culture.","chinese":"翻譯軟件已經成為日常生活中普通的一部分，而且它現在能夠在數秒之內轉換許多文本 然而，我完全不同意這使外語學習變得毫無意義， 因為語言不只是解讀文字的工具；它也是一種思考方式、一種建立關係的方式，以及一種參與另一種文化的方式。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that computer translation, however convenient, cannot replace genuine human understanding. Many expressions carry tone, humour, politeness and cultural assumptions that are hidden behind the literal meaning of words. A device may translate a sentence accurately on the surface, but it may still miss whether the speaker is being warm, sarcastic, formal or rude. For example, a tourist who relies entirely on a translation app may understand a restaurant menu, but they may still fail to notice local etiquette or the emotional weight of certain phrases. In this sense, translation is like a map: useful for direction, but unable to recreate the full landscape. Learning the language allows people to engage with others more naturally and respectfully.","chinese":"第一個原因是，電腦翻譯無論多麼方便，都無法取代真正的人類理解。 許多表達都帶有語氣、幽默、禮貌和文化假設，而這些往往隱藏在文字的字面意思背後。 一部裝置也許能在表面上準確翻譯一句話，但它仍然可能錯過說話者究竟是親切、諷刺、正式還是無禮。 例如，一位完全依賴翻譯應用程式的遊客，也許能看懂餐廳菜單，但他們仍然可能無法察覺當地禮儀，或者某些短語背後的情感分量。 從這個意義上說，翻譯就像一張地圖：它對指引方向很有用，但無法重現完整的風景。 學習一種語言能讓人們更自然、更有尊重地與他人交流。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that studying a foreign language brings lasting educational and professional benefits. It trains people to think more flexibly, listen more carefully and express ideas with greater precision. These skills are valuable far beyond the language classroom. In the workplace, for instance, an employee who can speak directly to overseas clients is often more trusted than someone who must pause after every sentence to use a machine. Direct communication creates confidence, speed and a stronger human connection, especially in negotiations, interviews or teamwork. Even if technology improves, people who know another language will still have an advantage because they can communicate without a digital wall standing between them and others.","chinese":"另一個原因是，學習外語能帶來長遠的教育和職業好處。 它訓練人們更靈活地思考、更仔細地聆聽，並更精準地表達想法。 這些能力的價值遠遠超出了語言課堂本身。 例如，在職場中，一位能夠直接與海外客戶交談的員工，往往比一個每說完一句話都必須停下來使用機器的人更容易獲得信任。 直接溝通能建立信心、提升速度，並形成更強的人際連結，尤其是在談判、面試或團隊合作之中。 即使科技進步，懂得另一種語言的人仍然會有優勢，因為他們能夠溝通，而不需要一道數碼牆隔在自己和他人之間。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely disagree that learning foreign languages is a waste of time. Computers can support communication, but they cannot replace the cultural understanding, personal confidence and human connection that language learning provides.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全不同意學習外語是浪費時間。 電腦可以支援溝通，但它們無法取代語言學習所帶來的文化理解、個人信心和人際連結"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"translation software","chinese":"翻譯軟件"},{"english":"an ordinary part of daily life","chinese":"日常生活中普通的一部分"},{"english":"convert many texts within seconds","chinese":"在數秒內轉換大量文字"},{"english":"completely disagree that","chinese":"完全不同意……"},{"english":"makes foreign-language learning pointless","chinese":"令外語學習變得毫無意義"},{"english":"not only a tool for","chinese":"不只是用來……的工具"},{"english":"decoding words","chinese":"解讀文字"},{"english":"a way of thinking","chinese":"思維方式"},{"english":"building relationships","chinese":"建立關係"},{"english":"participating in another culture","chinese":"參與另一種文化"},{"english":"computer translation","chinese":"電腦翻譯"},{"english":"however convenient","chinese":"無論多方便"},{"english":"genuine human understanding","chinese":"真正的人類理解"},{"english":"carry tone, humour, politeness and cultural assumptions","chinese":"承載語氣、幽默、禮貌和文化假設"},{"english":"cultural assumptions","chinese":"文化假設"},{"english":"hidden behind","chinese":"隱藏在……背後"},{"english":"literal meaning","chinese":"字面意思"},{"english":"translate a sentence accurately","chinese":"準確翻譯一句句子"},{"english":"on the surface","chinese":"表面上"},{"english":"miss whether","chinese":"錯過判斷是否……"},{"english":"warm, sarcastic, formal or rude","chinese":"親切、諷刺、正式或無禮"},{"english":"relies entirely on","chinese":"完全依賴"},{"english":"translation app","chinese":"翻譯應用程式"},{"english":"restaurant menu","chinese":"餐廳餐牌"},{"english":"fail to notice","chinese":"未能察覺"},{"english":"local etiquette","chinese":"當地禮儀"},{"english":"emotional weight","chinese":"情感分量"},{"english":"certain phrases","chinese":"某些短語"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"useful for direction","chinese":"對指引方向有用"},{"english":"unable to recreate","chinese":"無法重現"},{"english":"the full landscape","chinese":"完整景象"},{"english":"engage with others","chinese":"與他人交流互動"},{"english":"more naturally and respectfully","chinese":"更自然和更有禮地"},{"english":"studying a foreign language","chinese":"學習外語"},{"english":"lasting educational and professional benefits","chinese":"長遠的教育和專業好處"},{"english":"trains people to","chinese":"訓練人們去……"},{"english":"think more flexibly","chinese":"更靈活地思考"},{"english":"listen more carefully","chinese":"更細心聆聽"},{"english":"express ideas with greater precision","chinese":"更精準地表達想法"},{"english":"valuable far beyond","chinese":"價值遠超……"},{"english":"language classroom","chinese":"語言課堂"},{"english":"in the workplace","chinese":"在職場中"},{"english":"speak directly to","chinese":"直接與……交談"},{"english":"overseas clients","chinese":"海外客戶"},{"english":"more trusted than","chinese":"比……更受信任"},{"english":"pause after every sentence","chinese":"每句之後停頓"},{"english":"direct communication","chinese":"直接溝通"},{"english":"stronger human connection","chinese":"更強的人際連繫"},{"english":"especially in","chinese":"尤其在……"},{"english":"negotiations","chinese":"談判"},{"english":"even if technology improves","chinese":"即使科技進步"},{"english":"know another language","chinese":"懂另一種語言"},{"english":"have an advantage","chinese":"有優勢"},{"english":"without a digital wall","chinese":"沒有一道數碼牆"},{"english":"standing between them and others","chinese":"站在他們和別人之間"},{"english":"a waste of time","chinese":"浪費時間"},{"english":"support communication","chinese":"支援溝通"},{"english":"cultural understanding","chinese":"文化理解"},{"english":"personal confidence","chinese":"個人信心"},{"english":"human connection","chinese":"人際連繫"}]},"model-essay-66-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-66-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:66","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-66-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q66","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Some researchers believe that, in the future, humanity may voluntarily settle on one shared global language. I believe this would be a negative development because language is not merely a tool for communication; it also carries culture, identity and social memory.","chinese":"一些研究人員認為，在未來，人類可能會自願地選擇使用一種共同的全球語言。 我認為這會是一種負面的發展，因為語言不僅僅是溝通工具；它也承載著文化、身份認同和社會記憶。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first problem is cultural loss. Every language contains a particular way of seeing the world, from family relationships and humour to local traditions and moral values. If people gradually abandon their mother tongues in favour of a single global language, these meanings would not simply move into a new linguistic container; many would disappear in translation. For example, traditional songs, proverbs and stories often depend on sounds, wordplay and historical references that cannot be fully recreated in another language. Once a language stops being used in homes, schools and public life, it becomes like an old library with the doors locked: the books may still exist, but ordinary people can no longer enter and live inside them.","chinese":"第一個問題是文化流失。 每一種語言都包含一種獨特的世界觀，從家庭關係和幽默感，到本地傳統和道德價值，皆包含其中。 如果人們逐漸放棄自己的母語，轉而使用一種單一的全球語言，這些意義並不會只是被轉移到一個新的語言容器中；許多意義會在翻譯中消失。 例如，傳統歌曲、諺語和故事往往依賴聲音、文字遊戲和歷史典故，而這些都無法在另一種語言中被完整重現。 一旦一種語言停止在家庭、學校和公共生活中被使用，它就會變得像一座門被鎖上的舊圖書館：書本也許仍然存在，但普通人已經無法再進入其中，並活在那些文字所承載的世界裡。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another serious concern is that a single global language would deepen inequality rather than remove it. The language chosen as the global standard would almost certainly belong to, or be controlled by, a group with existing political, economic or technological power. Those who already speak it would enjoy an immediate advantage in education, business and international institutions, while others would have to spend years catching up. This would turn communication into a gatekeeping system, where opportunities depend less on talent and more on early access to the dominant language. In this sense, linguistic uniformity would look fair on the surface but would quietly reward the already privileged.","chinese":"另一個嚴重的問題是，單一的全球語言會加深不平等，而不是消除不平等。 被選為全球標準的語言，幾乎肯定會屬於某個已經擁有政治、經濟或科技權力的群體，或者受到這個群體控制。 那些本來已經會說這種語言的人，會立即在教育、商業和國際機構中享有優勢，而其他人則需要花多年時間追趕。 這會把溝通變成一種把關制度，在這種制度下，機會較少取決於才能，而更多取決於一個人是否早早接觸到主導語言。 從這個角度來看，語言上的一致性表面上看似公平，但實際上會悄悄地獎賞那些本來已經處於優勢地位的人。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, the world would not become richer if everyone spoke only one global language. It would become flatter, poorer and less human. For this reason, I see this predicted change as a negative development.","chinese":"總結來說，如果每個人只說一種全球語言，世界並不會變得更豐富。 它會變得更單薄、更貧乏，也更缺少人性的厚度。 基於這個原因，我認為這種被預測的改變是一種負面的發展。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"some researchers believe that","chinese":"一些研究人員認為……"},{"english":"in the future","chinese":"在未來"},{"english":"humanity","chinese":"人類"},{"english":"voluntarily settle on","chinese":"自願選定"},{"english":"one shared global language","chinese":"一種共同全球語言"},{"english":"a negative development","chinese":"負面發展"},{"english":"not merely a tool for communication","chinese":"不只是溝通工具"},{"english":"carries culture, identity and social memory","chinese":"承載文化、身份和社會記憶"},{"english":"cultural loss","chinese":"文化流失"},{"english":"a particular way of seeing the world","chinese":"一種看世界的特定方式"},{"english":"family relationships","chinese":"家庭關係"},{"english":"local traditions","chinese":"本地傳統"},{"english":"moral values","chinese":"道德價值觀"},{"english":"abandon their mother tongues","chinese":"放棄母語"},{"english":"mother tongues","chinese":"母語"},{"english":"in favour of","chinese":"轉而支持；取而用"},{"english":"a single global language","chinese":"單一全球語言"},{"english":"linguistic container","chinese":"語言容器"},{"english":"disappear in translation","chinese":"在翻譯中消失"},{"english":"traditional songs","chinese":"傳統歌曲"},{"english":"proverbs and stories","chinese":"諺語和故事"},{"english":"depend on","chinese":"取決於；依賴"},{"english":"wordplay","chinese":"文字遊戲；雙關語"},{"english":"historical references","chinese":"歷史典故"},{"english":"be fully recreated","chinese":"被完全重現"},{"english":"in another language","chinese":"用另一種語言"},{"english":"once a language stops being used","chinese":"一旦一種語言停止被使用"},{"english":"public life","chinese":"公共生活"},{"english":"with the doors locked","chinese":"大門上鎖的"},{"english":"may still exist","chinese":"可能仍然存在"},{"english":"ordinary people","chinese":"普通人"},{"english":"live inside them","chinese":"活在其中"},{"english":"another serious concern","chinese":"另一個嚴重憂慮"},{"english":"deepen inequality","chinese":"加深不平等"},{"english":"rather than remove it","chinese":"而不是消除它"},{"english":"the global standard","chinese":"全球標準"},{"english":"almost certainly","chinese":"幾乎肯定"},{"english":"belong to","chinese":"屬於"},{"english":"be controlled by","chinese":"被……控制"},{"english":"existing political, economic or technological power","chinese":"現有政治、經濟或科技力量"},{"english":"enjoy an immediate advantage","chinese":"享有即時優勢"},{"english":"international institutions","chinese":"國際機構"},{"english":"spend years catching up","chinese":"花多年時間追趕"},{"english":"turn communication into","chinese":"將溝通變成……"},{"english":"gatekeeping system","chinese":"把關制度；門檻制度"},{"english":"depend less on","chinese":"較少取決於……"},{"english":"early access to","chinese":"早期接觸……的機會"},{"english":"dominant language","chinese":"主導語言"},{"english":"linguistic uniformity","chinese":"語言一致化"},{"english":"on the surface","chinese":"表面上"},{"english":"quietly reward","chinese":"悄悄獎勵"},{"english":"the already privileged","chinese":"已經享有特權的人"},{"english":"would not become richer","chinese":"不會變得更豐富"},{"english":"flatter, poorer and less human","chinese":"更平面、更貧乏、更少人情味"},{"english":"for this reason","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"predicted change","chinese":"預測中的轉變"}]},"model-essay-67-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-67-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:67","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-67-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q67","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"As digital devices become an established part of school life, some schools have begun to reduce, or even remove, handwriting lessons. I strongly believe that children should still be taught how to write with a pen, because handwriting supports early learning and remains a basic practical skill.","chinese":"隨著數位裝置成為學校生活中既定的一部分，一些學校已開始減少，甚至取消手寫課程 我堅信兒童仍然應該被教導如何用筆書寫，因為手寫能支持早期學習，並且仍然是一項基本的實用技能。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that handwriting helps children build a stronger foundation for literacy. When young learners form letters by hand, they do not simply copy shapes; they connect sound, movement, spelling and meaning at the same time. This slower physical process can make words feel more memorable than pressing keys on a screen. For example, a child who repeatedly writes difficult words such as “beautiful” or “necessary” is more likely to notice their letter patterns than a child who only types them and relies on autocorrect. In this sense, handwriting acts like a small workshop for the mind: it trains attention, patience and accuracy while children are still developing basic language skills.","chinese":"第一個原因是，手寫能幫助兒童為讀寫能力建立更堅實的基礎。 當年幼的學習者用手寫出字母時，他們不只是複製形狀；他們同時把聲音、動作、拼寫和意思連結起來。 這種較慢的身體動作過程，能使單字比在螢幕上按鍵更容易被記住。 例如，一個反覆書寫“beautiful”或“necessary”這類困難單字的孩子，比起只打字並依賴自動更正的孩子，更有可能注意到這些單字的字母模式。 從這個意義上說，手寫就像一個給大腦使用的小工作坊：當孩子仍在發展基本語言能力時，它訓練了專注力、耐心和準確性。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important reason is that handwriting gives children independence in situations where technology is unavailable or inappropriate. Schools should prepare pupils not only for ideal digital environments, but also for ordinary real-life moments. A student may need to complete a paper exam, write a quick note, label a diagram, fill in a form or communicate when a device has run out of battery. If handwriting is abandoned completely, children may become unnecessarily dependent on screens for even the simplest written tasks. This would be a narrow form of progress, because a useful old skill would be lost without a good reason.","chinese":"另一個重要原因是，在科技不可用或不適合使用的情況下，手寫能給予兒童獨立能力。 學校不應只讓學生為理想的數位環境作準備，也應讓他們為普通的真實生活場景作準備 一名學生可能需要完成紙本考試、快速寫一張便條、為圖表加上標籤、填寫表格，或在裝置沒電時進行溝通。 如果手寫被完全放棄，兒童甚至在最簡單的書寫任務上，也可能變得不必要地依賴螢幕 這將會是一種狹隘的進步，因為一項有用的舊技能會在沒有充分理由的情況下被失去。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, children should definitely learn handwriting skills. Typing is essential in the modern world, but it should add to children’s abilities rather than replace handwriting altogether. A pen may look old-fashioned beside a tablet, but it still teaches control, concentration and self-reliance.","chinese":"總結來說，兒童絕對應該學習手寫技能。 打字在現代世界中是必要的，但它應該增加兒童的能力，而不是完全取代手寫。 一支筆在平板電腦旁邊也許看起來很老派，但它仍能教會人控制力、專注力和自立能力"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"digital devices","chinese":"數碼裝置"},{"english":"an established part of","chinese":"……中固定的一部分"},{"english":"school life","chinese":"學校生活"},{"english":"have begun to","chinese":"已開始去……"},{"english":"reduce, or even remove","chinese":"減少，甚至取消"},{"english":"handwriting lessons","chinese":"手寫課"},{"english":"strongly believe that","chinese":"強烈相信……"},{"english":"be taught how to","chinese":"被教導如何……"},{"english":"write with a pen","chinese":"用筆書寫"},{"english":"supports early learning","chinese":"支持早期學習"},{"english":"basic practical skill","chinese":"基本實用技能"},{"english":"build a stronger foundation for","chinese":"為……建立更穩固的基礎"},{"english":"literacy","chinese":"讀寫能力"},{"english":"young learners","chinese":"年幼學習者"},{"english":"form letters by hand","chinese":"用手寫出字母"},{"english":"do not simply","chinese":"不只是"},{"english":"copy shapes","chinese":"複製形狀"},{"english":"connect sound, movement, spelling and meaning","chinese":"連繫聲音、動作、串法和意思"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"slower physical process","chinese":"較慢的身體動作過程"},{"english":"make words feel more memorable","chinese":"令文字感覺更容易記住"},{"english":"pressing keys on a screen","chinese":"在螢幕上按鍵"},{"english":"repeatedly writes","chinese":"反覆書寫"},{"english":"difficult words","chinese":"困難的字詞"},{"english":"be more likely to notice","chinese":"更有可能留意到"},{"english":"letter patterns","chinese":"字母組合規律"},{"english":"relies on autocorrect","chinese":"依賴自動更正"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"acts like","chinese":"像……一樣發揮作用"},{"english":"a small workshop for the mind","chinese":"大腦的小型工作室"},{"english":"trains attention, patience and accuracy","chinese":"訓練專注、耐性和準確度"},{"english":"basic language skills","chinese":"基本語言技能"},{"english":"gives children independence","chinese":"給予孩子獨立能力"},{"english":"unavailable or inappropriate","chinese":"無法使用或不適合使用"},{"english":"prepare pupils not only for","chinese":"讓學生不只是為……作好準備"},{"english":"ideal digital environments","chinese":"理想的數碼環境"},{"english":"ordinary real-life moments","chinese":"普通的現實生活時刻"},{"english":"complete a paper exam","chinese":"完成紙本考試"},{"english":"write a quick note","chinese":"寫一張簡短便條"},{"english":"label a diagram","chinese":"標註圖表"},{"english":"fill in a form","chinese":"填寫表格"},{"english":"run out of battery","chinese":"電量耗盡"},{"english":"be abandoned completely","chinese":"被完全放棄"},{"english":"become unnecessarily dependent on","chinese":"變得不必要地依賴……"},{"english":"the simplest written tasks","chinese":"最簡單的書寫任務"},{"english":"a narrow form of progress","chinese":"狹隘形式的進步"},{"english":"useful old skill","chinese":"有用的舊技能"},{"english":"be lost without a good reason","chinese":"無充分理由地失去"},{"english":"definitely learn","chinese":"絕對應該學習"},{"english":"handwriting skills","chinese":"手寫技能"},{"english":"essential in the modern world","chinese":"在現代世界中必不可少"},{"english":"add to children's abilities","chinese":"增加孩子的能力"},{"english":"rather than replace handwriting altogether","chinese":"而不是完全取代手寫"},{"english":"old-fashioned beside","chinese":"在……旁邊顯得過時"},{"english":"teaches control, concentration and self-reliance","chinese":"教導控制力、專注力和自立能力"}]},"model-essay-68-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-68-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:68","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-68-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q68","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Culture is not simply a collection of food, festivals, and traditional clothing; it is also a way of thinking that is stored in language. I completely agree that a person cannot truly understand a country’s culture unless they speak its language, because language carries shared values and allows meaningful contact with local people.","chinese":"文化並不只是一系列食物、節日和傳統服飾；它也是一種儲存在語言之中的思維方式。 我完全同意，一個人若不會說一個國家的語言，就不能真正理解該國文化，因為語言承載著共同價值，也讓人能夠與當地人建立有意義的接觸。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that language contains meanings which are often invisible to outsiders. Words do not only describe objects; they express politeness, humour, hierarchy, emotion, and social expectations. If a visitor relies only on translation, these deeper meanings can easily disappear. For example, in many Asian cultures, indirect expressions are often used to show respect or avoid embarrassment. A foreigner may understand the literal meaning of a sentence, but without knowing the language, they may miss why something is said gently, indirectly, or even left unsaid. In this sense, language is like a cultural map: without it, people may see the landscape, but they cannot read the signs.","chinese":"第一個原因是，語言包含一些對外來者而言往往看不見的意義。 詞語不只是描述事物；它們也表達禮貌、幽默、階級、情感和社會期望。 如果一位訪客只依賴翻譯，這些更深層的意義便很容易消失。 例如，在許多亞洲文化中，間接的表達方式常被用來表示尊重或避免尷尬。 外國人或許能理解一句話的字面意思，但如果不懂該語言，他們便可能錯過為甚麼某些話要說得委婉、間接，甚至選擇不說出口。 從這個意義上說，語言就像一張文化地圖：沒有它，人們或許能看見風景，卻讀不懂其中的指示牌。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that real cultural understanding comes from interaction, not passive observation. A person can watch local ceremonies, eat local food, and visit famous buildings, but these experiences remain fairly shallow if they cannot communicate with residents in their own language. Speaking the language allows people to ask questions, understand jokes, join ordinary conversations, and notice how people behave in daily life. For instance, someone who speaks Spanish while living in Mexico is far more likely to understand family values, humour, and social warmth than someone who only observes these things from a distance. Language opens doors that sightseeing alone cannot open.","chinese":"另一個原因是，真正的文化理解來自互動，而不是被動觀察。 一個人可以觀看當地儀式、品嚐當地食物、參觀著名建築，但如果不能用當地人的語言與居民溝通，這些經歷仍然相當表面。 會說該語言讓人能夠提出問題、理解笑話、參與日常對話，並留意人們在日常生活中的行為方式 例如，一個住在墨西哥並會說西班牙語的人，比一個只是從遠處觀察這些事情的人，更有可能理解當地的家庭價值、幽默感和社交上的溫暖。 語言能打開一些單靠觀光無法打開的門。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully agree that language is essential for understanding culture. Without it, people may gain impressions of a country, but those impressions remain incomplete. To understand a culture deeply, one must understand the language through which that culture breathes.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意語言對理解文化是不可或缺的。 沒有語言，人們也許能對一個國家形成一些印象，但這些印象仍然是不完整的。 要深入理解一種文化，一個人必須理解那種文化賴以呼吸的語言。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"not simply","chinese":"不只是"},{"english":"a collection of","chinese":"一系列；一組"},{"english":"traditional clothing","chinese":"傳統服飾"},{"english":"a way of thinking","chinese":"思維方式"},{"english":"be stored in","chinese":"儲存在……中"},{"english":"truly understand","chinese":"真正理解"},{"english":"a country's culture","chinese":"一個國家的文化"},{"english":"unless they speak","chinese":"除非他們會說……"},{"english":"carries shared values","chinese":"承載共同價值觀"},{"english":"meaningful contact with","chinese":"與……有意義的接觸"},{"english":"local people","chinese":"當地人"},{"english":"contains meanings","chinese":"包含意思"},{"english":"invisible to outsiders","chinese":"外人看不見的；外人難以察覺的"},{"english":"describe objects","chinese":"描述物件"},{"english":"express politeness","chinese":"表達禮貌"},{"english":"hierarchy","chinese":"等級關係"},{"english":"social expectations","chinese":"社會期望"},{"english":"rely only on","chinese":"只依賴……"},{"english":"translation","chinese":"翻譯"},{"english":"deeper meanings","chinese":"更深層的意思"},{"english":"can easily disappear","chinese":"很容易消失"},{"english":"Asian cultures","chinese":"亞洲文化"},{"english":"indirect expressions","chinese":"間接表達"},{"english":"be used to","chinese":"被用來……"},{"english":"show respect","chinese":"表示尊重"},{"english":"avoid embarrassment","chinese":"避免尷尬"},{"english":"literal meaning","chinese":"字面意思"},{"english":"miss why","chinese":"錯過理解為甚麼"},{"english":"be said gently","chinese":"被溫和地說出"},{"english":"left unsaid","chinese":"沒有說出口"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"cultural map","chinese":"文化地圖"},{"english":"see the landscape","chinese":"看見風景"},{"english":"read the signs","chinese":"看懂標記；理解暗示"},{"english":"real cultural understanding","chinese":"真正的文化理解"},{"english":"passive observation","chinese":"被動觀察"},{"english":"watch local ceremonies","chinese":"觀看當地儀式"},{"english":"visit famous buildings","chinese":"參觀著名建築"},{"english":"remain fairly shallow","chinese":"仍然相當膚淺"},{"english":"communicate with residents","chinese":"與居民溝通"},{"english":"in their own language","chinese":"用他們自己的語言"},{"english":"allows people to","chinese":"讓人們可以……"},{"english":"ask questions","chinese":"提問"},{"english":"understand jokes","chinese":"明白笑話"},{"english":"join ordinary conversations","chinese":"參與日常對話"},{"english":"notice how people behave","chinese":"留意人們如何行為"},{"english":"daily life","chinese":"日常生活"},{"english":"far more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"family values","chinese":"家庭價值觀"},{"english":"social warmth","chinese":"社交上的親切感"},{"english":"from a distance","chinese":"從遠處"},{"english":"opens doors","chinese":"打開機會之門"},{"english":"sightseeing alone","chinese":"單靠觀光"},{"english":"essential for","chinese":"對……必不可少"},{"english":"gain impressions of","chinese":"對……獲得印象"},{"english":"remain incomplete","chinese":"仍然不完整"},{"english":"understand a culture deeply","chinese":"深入理解一種文化"},{"english":"through which","chinese":"透過……"},{"english":"culture breathes","chinese":"文化得以呼吸；文化活起來"}]},"model-essay-69-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-69-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:69","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-69-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q69","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Language learning has changed greatly in recent years, especially because learners can now communicate, study, and practise across borders. Some argue that true fluency is impossible unless a person has lived or worked in the country where that language is spoken. I completely disagree, because fluency depends far more on purposeful practice than on physical location.","chinese":"近年來，語言學習已經發生了很大變化，尤其是因為學習者如今可以跨越地域進行溝通、學習和練習。 有些人認為，除非一個人曾經在使用該語言的國家生活或工作，否則真正的流利是不可能達到的。 我完全不同意，因為流利程度更多取決於有目的的練習，而不是身處哪個地方。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason is that modern learners can build real communicative ability without moving abroad. Fluency is not produced by scenery; it is produced by repeated use, correction, and confidence under pressure. A learner who speaks the language every day, receives feedback from teachers, and engages with native-level materials can gradually train the mind to respond naturally rather than translate word by word. For example, a student in Hong Kong who joins an English debate club, takes online lessons with native speakers, reads English news, and watches interviews without subtitles is constantly exposed to natural rhythm, vocabulary, and pronunciation. Over time, this kind of deliberate routine can turn the language from a school subject into a living tool. Therefore, a well-designed learning environment at home can still lead to genuine fluency.","chinese":"最有力的原因是，現代學習者即使不移居海外，也能建立真正的溝通能力。 流利並不是由周圍環境本身產生的；它是由反覆使用、糾正，以及在壓力下建立起來的信心所產生的。 一個每天說該語言、從老師那裡獲得反饋，並接觸母語水平材料的學習者，可以逐漸訓練大腦自然回應，而不是逐字翻譯。 例如，一名香港學生如果參加英語辯論社、與母語人士上網課、閱讀英文新聞，並觀看沒有字幕的訪談，就會不斷接觸自然的語言節奏、詞彙和發音。 久而久之，這種有意識的日常練習可以把一門語言從學校科目轉化成一種真正生活中的工具。 因此，一個設計良好的本地學習環境，仍然可以帶來真正的流利程度。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that living in a country does not automatically create fluency. A person may spend years abroad but remain linguistically isolated if they mainly socialise with people from their own background, rely on translation apps, or avoid difficult conversations. In that case, the language is around them, but it never truly enters their daily thinking. By contrast, someone who has never left home but actively speaks, writes, listens, and reflects every day may progress much faster. Fluency grows when learners step into the language and use it actively; passive exposure alone is only background noise.","chinese":"另一個原因是，生活在某個國家並不會自動帶來語言流利。 一個人可能在海外生活多年，但如果他們主要與相同背景的人社交、依賴翻譯應用程式，或者避免有難度的對話，他們在語言上仍然可能是孤立的。 在這種情況下，語言雖然存在於他們周圍，卻從未真正進入他們的日常思維之中。 相比之下，一個從未離開本地、但每天主動說、寫、聽和反思的人，可能進步得更快。 當學習者真正走進語言並主動使用它時，流利程度才會增長；單靠被動接觸只不過是背景噪音。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely disagree that living or working in a country is necessary for language fluency. The decisive factor is not where learners are, but how consistently and meaningfully they use the language.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全不同意在一個國家生活或工作是達到語言流利的必要條件。 決定性因素不是學習者身處哪裡，而是他們能否持續並有意義地使用該語言。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"language learning","chinese":"語言學習"},{"english":"changed greatly","chinese":"有很大改變"},{"english":"in recent years","chinese":"近年來"},{"english":"especially because","chinese":"尤其是因為"},{"english":"communicate, study, and practise","chinese":"溝通、學習和練習"},{"english":"across borders","chinese":"跨越國界"},{"english":"true fluency","chinese":"真正流利"},{"english":"is impossible unless","chinese":"除非……否則不可能"},{"english":"where that language is spoken","chinese":"使用該語言的地方"},{"english":"completely disagree","chinese":"完全不同意"},{"english":"depend far more on","chinese":"更大程度上取決於……"},{"english":"purposeful practice","chinese":"有目的的練習"},{"english":"physical location","chinese":"實際身處的地方"},{"english":"the strongest reason","chinese":"最有力的原因"},{"english":"build real communicative ability","chinese":"建立真正的溝通能力"},{"english":"without moving abroad","chinese":"不用移居外國"},{"english":"be produced by","chinese":"由……產生"},{"english":"repeated use","chinese":"重複使用"},{"english":"correction","chinese":"糾正"},{"english":"confidence under pressure","chinese":"在壓力下的信心"},{"english":"receive feedback from","chinese":"從……獲得回饋"},{"english":"engage with","chinese":"接觸並投入使用……"},{"english":"native-level materials","chinese":"母語者水平的材料"},{"english":"gradually train the mind to","chinese":"逐漸訓練大腦去……"},{"english":"respond naturally","chinese":"自然回應"},{"english":"rather than translate word by word","chinese":"而不是逐字翻譯"},{"english":"debate club","chinese":"辯論學會"},{"english":"online lessons","chinese":"網上課堂"},{"english":"native speakers","chinese":"母語者"},{"english":"without subtitles","chinese":"不看字幕"},{"english":"be constantly exposed to","chinese":"不斷接觸到……"},{"english":"natural rhythm","chinese":"自然節奏"},{"english":"vocabulary and pronunciation","chinese":"詞彙和發音"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨着時間過去"},{"english":"deliberate routine","chinese":"有意識安排的習慣"},{"english":"turn the language from","chinese":"將語言由……轉化為……"},{"english":"school subject","chinese":"學科"},{"english":"living tool","chinese":"活生生的工具"},{"english":"well-designed learning environment","chinese":"設計良好的學習環境"},{"english":"lead to","chinese":"帶來；通往"},{"english":"genuine fluency","chinese":"真正流利"},{"english":"living in a country","chinese":"住在一個國家"},{"english":"does not automatically create","chinese":"不會自動帶來"},{"english":"remain linguistically isolated","chinese":"在語言上仍然孤立"},{"english":"socialise with","chinese":"與……交往"},{"english":"people from their own background","chinese":"與自己背景相同的人"},{"english":"rely on translation apps","chinese":"依賴翻譯應用程式"},{"english":"avoid difficult conversations","chinese":"避免艱難的對話"},{"english":"in that case","chinese":"在那種情況下"},{"english":"around them","chinese":"在他們身邊"},{"english":"truly enters their daily thinking","chinese":"真正進入他們的日常思維"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"actively speaks, writes, listens, and reflects","chinese":"主動說、寫、聽和反思"},{"english":"progress much faster","chinese":"進步快得多"},{"english":"step into the language","chinese":"走進那種語言"},{"english":"use it actively","chinese":"主動使用它"},{"english":"passive exposure alone","chinese":"單靠被動接觸"},{"english":"background noise","chinese":"背景噪音"},{"english":"living or working in","chinese":"在……生活或工作"},{"english":"necessary for","chinese":"對……必要"},{"english":"language fluency","chinese":"語言流利程度"},{"english":"decisive factor","chinese":"決定性因素"},{"english":"not where learners are, but how","chinese":"不是學習者身處何地，而是如何……"},{"english":"consistently and meaningfully","chinese":"持續而有意義地"}]},"model-essay-70-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-70-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:70","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-70-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q70","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Violence has become a familiar feature of modern entertainment, from films and online videos to games and social media clips. I completely agree that such content encourages violence in society because it can normalise aggressive behaviour and give vulnerable audiences models to copy.","chinese":"暴力已成現代娛樂中常見的一部分，從電影、網上影片到遊戲和社交媒體短片皆是如此 我完全同意這類內容會助長社會中的暴力，因為它可能使攻擊性行為變得正常化，並為容易受影響的觀眾提供可模仿的模式。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that repeated exposure to violent scenes can make aggression seem ordinary rather than shocking. When viewers constantly see characters solving problems through threats, revenge, or physical force, violence may gradually lose its moral weight. This is especially harmful for young people, whose judgement and self-control are still developing. For example, a child who repeatedly watches heroes being rewarded for brutal behaviour may begin to see intimidation as a sign of strength rather than a serious social harm. Over time, this does not create violence in every individual, but it can lower society’s emotional resistance to it, like slowly turning down the volume on a warning alarm.","chinese":"第一個原因是，反覆接觸暴力場面會使攻擊行為看起來普通，而不再令人震驚。 當觀眾不斷看到角色透過威脅、報復或武力解決問題時，暴力可能會逐漸失去其道德上的嚴重性。 這對年輕人尤其有害，因為他們的判斷力和自我控制能力仍在發展之中。 例如，一個反覆觀看英雄因殘暴行為而受到獎賞的孩子，可能會開始把恐嚇視為力量的象徵，而不是嚴重的社會傷害。 長遠而言，這並不會使每個人都變得暴力，但它可能降低社會對暴力的情感抵抗力，就像慢慢把警報器的音量調低一樣。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another problem is that media violence often provides a script for real-life behaviour. Some people who already feel angry, isolated, or powerless may imitate what they have seen because the media offers them ready-made images of how to act. Online platforms make this risk even greater, as violent clips can spread quickly and be watched again and again without much context or adult guidance. For instance, teenagers involved in conflicts may copy aggressive language, fighting styles, or even the desire to record violent acts for attention. In this way, the media does not merely reflect violence; it can amplify it and make it more visible, dramatic, and tempting.","chinese":"另一個問題是，媒體暴力往往為現實生活中的行為提供了一套劇本。 一些本來已經感到憤怒、孤立或無力的人，可能會模仿他們所看到的內容，因為媒體為他們提供了現成的行為畫面。 網上平台使這種風險變得更大，因為暴力短片可以迅速傳播，並在缺乏充分背景或成人指導的情況下被反覆觀看。 例如，捲入衝突的青少年可能會模仿攻擊性的語言、打鬥方式，甚至模仿為了吸引注意而錄下暴力行為的想法。 這樣一來，媒體並不只是反映暴力；它還可能放大暴力，使其變得更加顯眼、更具戲劇性，也更具誘惑力。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully agree that violence in the media promotes violence in society. While not every viewer becomes aggressive, repeated exposure can normalise harmful conduct and provide clear patterns for imitation, particularly among those who are young or emotionally unstable.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意媒體中的暴力會助長社會中的暴力。 雖然不是每一位觀眾都會變得具攻擊性，但反覆接觸這類內容可能會使有害行為正常化，並提供清晰的模仿模式，尤其是在年輕或情緒不穩定的人群之中。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"a familiar feature of","chinese":"……的常見特徵"},{"english":"modern entertainment","chinese":"現代娛樂"},{"english":"online videos","chinese":"網上影片"},{"english":"social media clips","chinese":"社交媒體短片"},{"english":"such content","chinese":"這類內容"},{"english":"encourage violence in society","chinese":"鼓勵社會中的暴力"},{"english":"normalise aggressive behaviour","chinese":"令攻擊性行為變得正常化"},{"english":"vulnerable audiences","chinese":"脆弱觀眾；易受影響的觀眾"},{"english":"models to copy","chinese":"可模仿的模式"},{"english":"repeated exposure to","chinese":"反覆接觸……"},{"english":"violent scenes","chinese":"暴力場面"},{"english":"make aggression seem ordinary","chinese":"令攻擊性看起來平常"},{"english":"rather than shocking","chinese":"而不是令人震驚"},{"english":"constantly see","chinese":"不斷看見"},{"english":"solving problems through","chinese":"透過……解決問題"},{"english":"threats, revenge, or physical force","chinese":"威脅、報復或武力"},{"english":"gradually lose its moral weight","chinese":"逐漸失去其道德重量"},{"english":"especially harmful for","chinese":"對……特別有害"},{"english":"judgement and self-control","chinese":"判斷力和自制力"},{"english":"still developing","chinese":"仍在發展中"},{"english":"be rewarded for","chinese":"因……而得到獎賞"},{"english":"brutal behaviour","chinese":"殘暴行為"},{"english":"begin to see","chinese":"開始視……為"},{"english":"intimidation","chinese":"恐嚇"},{"english":"a sign of strength","chinese":"強大的表現"},{"english":"serious social harm","chinese":"嚴重社會傷害"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨着時間過去"},{"english":"in every individual","chinese":"在每個人身上"},{"english":"lower society's emotional resistance to","chinese":"降低社會對……的情感抵抗"},{"english":"turn down the volume on","chinese":"調低……的音量"},{"english":"warning alarm","chinese":"警報"},{"english":"media violence","chinese":"媒體暴力"},{"english":"provide a script for","chinese":"為……提供劇本"},{"english":"real-life behaviour","chinese":"現實生活中的行為"},{"english":"feel angry, isolated, or powerless","chinese":"感到憤怒、孤立或無力"},{"english":"imitate what they have seen","chinese":"模仿他們所見過的事"},{"english":"ready-made images","chinese":"現成的畫面"},{"english":"how to act","chinese":"如何行動"},{"english":"online platforms","chinese":"網上平台"},{"english":"make this risk even greater","chinese":"令這種風險更大"},{"english":"spread quickly","chinese":"快速傳播"},{"english":"again and again","chinese":"一次又一次"},{"english":"without much context","chinese":"缺乏足夠背景脈絡"},{"english":"adult guidance","chinese":"成人指導"},{"english":"teenagers involved in conflicts","chinese":"捲入衝突的青少年"},{"english":"copy aggressive language","chinese":"模仿攻擊性語言"},{"english":"fighting styles","chinese":"打鬥方式"},{"english":"violent acts","chinese":"暴力行為"},{"english":"for attention","chinese":"為了博取注意"},{"english":"in this way","chinese":"以這種方式"},{"english":"merely reflect","chinese":"只是反映"},{"english":"amplify it","chinese":"將它放大"},{"english":"make it more visible","chinese":"令它更顯眼"},{"english":"dramatic and tempting","chinese":"戲劇化而具誘惑力"},{"english":"promotes violence in society","chinese":"助長社會中的暴力"},{"english":"not every viewer becomes aggressive","chinese":"不是每個觀眾都會變得具攻擊性"},{"english":"harmful conduct","chinese":"有害行為"},{"english":"clear patterns for imitation","chinese":"清晰的模仿模式"},{"english":"particularly among","chinese":"尤其是在……之中"},{"english":"emotionally unstable","chinese":"情緒不穩定的"}]},"model-essay-71-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-71-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:71","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-71-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q71","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The private lives of famous people have become an increasingly profitable target for newspapers, television programmes, and online platforms. Some argue that celebrities and media personalities should accept this as the price of fame and lose any claim to privacy. I completely disagree with this view, because public recognition does not remove a person’s basic human rights, and intrusive reporting often creates harm without serving any genuine public interest.","chinese":"名人的私人生活已經成為報紙、電視節目和網上平台越來越有利可圖的目標。 有些人認為，名人和媒體人物應該把這視為成名的代價，並失去任何主張私隱的權利。 我完全不同意這種觀點，因為公眾知名度並不會剝奪一個人的基本人權，而侵擾性的報道往往會造成傷害，卻沒有服務任何真正的公共利益。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason is that famous people are still human beings, not public property. Although they may choose careers that place them in the spotlight, this does not mean every part of their life should be exposed. Constant surveillance can damage their mental health, relationships, and sense of safety. For example, a singer may be willing to discuss a new album in an interview, but that does not justify photographers following their children to school or publishing private medical details. When the press crosses that line, journalism stops being information and becomes harassment. A society that allows this is not protecting free speech; it is feeding public curiosity at another person’s expense.","chinese":"最有力的理由是，名人仍然是人，而不是公共財產。 儘管他們可能選擇了使自己處於聚光燈下的職業，但這並不意味著他們生活中的每一部分都應該被公開。 持續的監視可能會損害他們的心理健康、人際關係和安全感。 例如，一位歌手可能願意在訪問中談論新專輯，但這並不能合理化攝影師跟蹤他們的孩子上學，或公開他們的私人醫療資料。 當新聞媒體越過這條界線時，新聞便不再是資訊，而變成騷擾。 一個容許這種情況的社會，並不是在保護言論自由；它只是在以犧牲他人為代價來滿足公眾的好奇心。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Moreover, removing privacy from famous people can encourage a shallow and irresponsible media culture. Instead of reporting on work, talent, public behaviour, or serious wrongdoing, media outlets may focus on rumours, private arguments, or embarrassing photographs simply because they attract attention. This lowers the quality of public discussion and teaches audiences to confuse gossip with news. Of course, the press should be allowed to investigate celebrities when their actions affect the public, such as criminal behaviour, fraud, or hypocrisy in public campaigns. However, that is very different from claiming that famous people deserve no privacy at all.","chinese":"此外，剝奪名人的私隱可能會助長一種膚淺而不負責任的媒體文化。 媒體機構可能不再報道工作、才華、公眾行為或嚴重不當行為，而是只因為謠言、私人爭執或尷尬照片能吸引注意，便把焦點放在這些內容上。 這會降低公共討論的質素，並使觀眾把八卦和新聞混為一談。 當然，當名人的行為影響公眾時，例如涉及犯罪行為、欺詐，或在公共宣傳中表裡不一，新聞媒體應該被允許調查他們。 然而，這與聲稱名人完全不應享有私隱是非常不同的。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely disagree that famous people in the media should have no right to privacy. Fame may bring public attention, but it should never turn a person’s private life into an open hunting ground for the press. A fair society must protect both responsible journalism and basic human dignity.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全不同意媒體中的名人不應享有私隱權這種說法。 名氣可能會帶來公眾關注，但它絕不應該把一個人的私人生活變成新聞媒體可以公開狩獵的場地。 一個公平的社會必須同時保護負責任的新聞工作和基本的人性尊嚴。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"private lives of famous people","chinese":"名人私生活"},{"english":"increasingly profitable target","chinese":"越來越有利可圖的目標"},{"english":"newspapers, television programmes, and online platforms","chinese":"報章、電視節目和網上平台"},{"english":"media personalities","chinese":"媒體名人"},{"english":"the price of fame","chinese":"成名的代價"},{"english":"lose any claim to privacy","chinese":"失去任何私隱權主張"},{"english":"completely disagree with","chinese":"完全不同意……"},{"english":"public recognition","chinese":"公眾知名度"},{"english":"remove a person's basic human rights","chinese":"取消一個人的基本人權"},{"english":"intrusive reporting","chinese":"侵擾式報道"},{"english":"creates harm","chinese":"造成傷害"},{"english":"genuine public interest","chinese":"真正的公眾利益"},{"english":"the strongest reason","chinese":"最有力的原因"},{"english":"human beings","chinese":"人；有血有肉的人"},{"english":"public property","chinese":"公共財產"},{"english":"choose careers that","chinese":"選擇……的職業"},{"english":"place them in the spotlight","chinese":"令他們成為焦點"},{"english":"every part of their life","chinese":"他們生活的每一部分"},{"english":"be exposed","chinese":"被公開"},{"english":"constant surveillance","chinese":"持續監視"},{"english":"mental health","chinese":"精神健康"},{"english":"sense of safety","chinese":"安全感"},{"english":"be willing to","chinese":"願意去……"},{"english":"discuss a new album","chinese":"談論新專輯"},{"english":"in an interview","chinese":"在訪問中"},{"english":"justify photographers following","chinese":"使攝影師跟蹤……變得合理"},{"english":"publishing private medical details","chinese":"公開私人醫療資料"},{"english":"private medical details","chinese":"私人醫療資料"},{"english":"cross that line","chinese":"越過那條界線"},{"english":"journalism","chinese":"新聞工作"},{"english":"stops being information","chinese":"不再是提供資訊"},{"english":"becomes harassment","chinese":"變成騷擾"},{"english":"free speech","chinese":"言論自由"},{"english":"feed public curiosity","chinese":"滿足公眾好奇心"},{"english":"at another person's expense","chinese":"以犧牲別人為代價"},{"english":"removing privacy from","chinese":"剝奪……的私隱"},{"english":"shallow and irresponsible media culture","chinese":"膚淺而不負責任的媒體文化"},{"english":"instead of reporting on","chinese":"而不是報道……"},{"english":"media outlets","chinese":"傳媒機構"},{"english":"public behaviour","chinese":"公開行為"},{"english":"serious wrongdoing","chinese":"嚴重不當行為"},{"english":"focus on rumours","chinese":"專注於謠言"},{"english":"private arguments","chinese":"私人爭吵"},{"english":"embarrassing photographs","chinese":"令人尷尬的相片"},{"english":"simply because","chinese":"只是因為"},{"english":"attract attention","chinese":"吸引注意"},{"english":"lower the quality of","chinese":"降低……的質素"},{"english":"public discussion","chinese":"公共討論"},{"english":"confuse gossip with news","chinese":"將八卦與新聞混淆"},{"english":"of course","chinese":"當然"},{"english":"be allowed to investigate","chinese":"被允許調查"},{"english":"actions affect the public","chinese":"行為影響公眾"},{"english":"criminal behaviour","chinese":"犯罪行為"},{"english":"fraud","chinese":"欺詐"},{"english":"hypocrisy in public campaigns","chinese":"公開宣傳活動中的虛偽"},{"english":"very different from","chinese":"與……很不同"},{"english":"deserve no privacy at all","chinese":"完全不應有私隱"},{"english":"have no right to privacy","chinese":"沒有私隱權"},{"english":"bring public attention","chinese":"帶來公眾關注"},{"english":"should never turn","chinese":"絕不應將……變成"},{"english":"private life","chinese":"私生活"},{"english":"open hunting ground for the press","chinese":"供傳媒任意追逐的場所"},{"english":"responsible journalism","chinese":"負責任的新聞工作"},{"english":"basic human dignity","chinese":"基本人性尊嚴"}]},"model-essay-72-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-72-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:72","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-72-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q72","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The rapid growth of digital platforms has changed how people follow news, music, and entertainment. Some therefore argue that radio is approaching the end of its life. I completely disagree with this view, because radio still serves practical needs that online media cannot fully replace and it can adapt successfully to the digital age.","chinese":"數位平台的快速發展已經改變了人們獲取新聞、音樂和娛樂內容的方式。 因此，有些人認為收音機正逐漸走向生命的盡頭。 我完全不同意這個觀點，因為收音機仍然滿足一些網上媒體無法完全取代的實際需要，而且它能夠成功適應數位時代。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"First, radio remains valuable because it allows people to receive information without giving their full visual attention. Online media is powerful, but much of it depends on screens, scrolling, and constant interaction. Radio, by contrast, can be used while people are driving, cooking, exercising, or working. A driver travelling through heavy traffic, for instance, can listen to a traffic bulletin immediately, whereas checking a website or watching a news clip would be unsafe and impractical. This everyday convenience gives radio a lasting role. It is not merely an old device from the past, but a simple and reliable companion in situations where screens become a burden.","chinese":"首先，收音機仍然有價值，因為它讓人們能夠在不需要全神貫注觀看螢幕的情況下接收資訊。 網上媒體固然強大，但其中很多內容都依賴螢幕、滑動操作和持續互動。 相比之下，人們在駕車、煮食、運動或工作時仍然可以使用收音機。 例如，一位正在繁忙交通中駕駛的人可以即時收聽交通消息；相反，查看網站或觀看新聞短片則既不安全，也不實際。 這種日常便利性賦予了收音機一個持久的角色。 它不僅僅是一件來自過去的舊設備，而是在螢幕變成負擔的情況下，一個簡單而可靠的陪伴"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Second, the development of online media can actually strengthen radio rather than destroy it. Modern radio is no longer confined to a physical receiver in the corner of a room. Stations can stream live programmes, upload interviews, share short audio clips, and reach listeners through mobile phones. More importantly, radio often provides a local and human voice that large online platforms struggle to offer. During community events, bad weather, or public emergencies, people may still value a familiar presenter who speaks directly to their area and explains what is happening in plain language. This sense of immediacy and trust is difficult to replace.","chinese":"第二，網上媒體的發展其實可以強化收音機，而不是摧毀它。 現代收音機不再局限於房間角落裡的一部實體接收器。 電台可以直播節目、上載訪問、分享短音訊片段，並透過手機接觸聽眾。 更重要的是，收音機往往能提供一種本地而具有人情味的聲音，而這正是大型網上平台難以提供的。 在社區活動、惡劣天氣或公共緊急情況期間，人們仍然可能重視一位熟悉的主持人，因為他能直接向他們所在的地區說話，並用簡明的語言解釋正在發生的事情。 這種即時感和信任感是很難被取代的。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely disagree that radio has no future. Although online media has changed people’s habits, radio remains useful because it is convenient, accessible, adaptable, and locally relevant. Its form may continue to evolve, but its core purpose will survive.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全不同意收音機沒有未來這種說法。 儘管網上媒體已經改變了人們的習慣，收音機仍然有用，因為它方便、容易接觸、具適應力，並且與本地生活息息相關。 它的形式可能會繼續演變，但它的核心功能將會繼續存在。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"rapid growth of","chinese":"……的快速增長"},{"english":"digital platforms","chinese":"數碼平台"},{"english":"changed how people","chinese":"改變了人們如何……"},{"english":"follow news","chinese":"追蹤新聞"},{"english":"entertainment","chinese":"娛樂"},{"english":"therefore argue that","chinese":"因此認為……"},{"english":"approaching the end of its life","chinese":"快將走到盡頭"},{"english":"completely disagree with","chinese":"完全不同意……"},{"english":"serves practical needs","chinese":"滿足實際需要"},{"english":"online media","chinese":"網上媒體"},{"english":"fully replace","chinese":"完全取代"},{"english":"adapt successfully to","chinese":"成功適應……"},{"english":"the digital age","chinese":"數碼時代"},{"english":"remains valuable","chinese":"仍然有價值"},{"english":"receive information","chinese":"接收資料"},{"english":"without giving their full visual attention","chinese":"不用完全投入視覺注意力"},{"english":"visual attention","chinese":"視覺注意力"},{"english":"powerful","chinese":"強大；有影響力"},{"english":"depends on","chinese":"依賴"},{"english":"screens, scrolling, and constant interaction","chinese":"螢幕、滑動瀏覽和持續互動"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"while people are driving","chinese":"當人們駕車時"},{"english":"exercising","chinese":"做運動"},{"english":"heavy traffic","chinese":"交通非常擠塞"},{"english":"traffic bulletin","chinese":"交通消息"},{"english":"immediately","chinese":"即時"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；然而"},{"english":"checking a website","chinese":"查看網站"},{"english":"news clip","chinese":"新聞短片"},{"english":"unsafe and impractical","chinese":"不安全且不實際"},{"english":"everyday convenience","chinese":"日常便利"},{"english":"lasting role","chinese":"持久的角色"},{"english":"merely an old device","chinese":"只是舊時代的裝置"},{"english":"from the past","chinese":"來自過去"},{"english":"simple and reliable companion","chinese":"簡單而可靠的陪伴"},{"english":"in situations where","chinese":"在……的情況下"},{"english":"become a burden","chinese":"成為負擔"},{"english":"the development of","chinese":"……的發展"},{"english":"actually strengthen","chinese":"其實加強"},{"english":"rather than destroy it","chinese":"而不是摧毀它"},{"english":"modern radio","chinese":"現代電台廣播"},{"english":"no longer confined to","chinese":"不再局限於……"},{"english":"physical receiver","chinese":"實體收音機"},{"english":"in the corner of a room","chinese":"在房間角落"},{"english":"stream live programmes","chinese":"串流直播節目"},{"english":"upload interviews","chinese":"上載訪問"},{"english":"share short audio clips","chinese":"分享音頻短片"},{"english":"reach listeners through","chinese":"透過……接觸聽眾"},{"english":"mobile phones","chinese":"手提電話"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"local and human voice","chinese":"本地而有人情味的聲音"},{"english":"large online platforms","chinese":"大型網上平台"},{"english":"struggle to offer","chinese":"難以提供"},{"english":"community events","chinese":"社區活動"},{"english":"bad weather","chinese":"惡劣天氣"},{"english":"public emergencies","chinese":"公共緊急情況"},{"english":"familiar presenter","chinese":"熟悉的主持人"},{"english":"speaks directly to","chinese":"直接向……說話"},{"english":"their area","chinese":"他們所屬地區"},{"english":"in plain language","chinese":"用淺白語言"},{"english":"sense of immediacy","chinese":"即時感"},{"english":"trust","chinese":"信任"},{"english":"difficult to replace","chinese":"難以取代"},{"english":"has no future","chinese":"沒有未來"},{"english":"changed people's habits","chinese":"改變了人們的習慣"},{"english":"convenient, accessible, adaptable, and locally relevant","chinese":"方便、容易接觸、適應力強，並切合本地需要"},{"english":"locally relevant","chinese":"切合本地需要"},{"english":"continue to evolve","chinese":"繼續演變"},{"english":"core purpose","chinese":"核心目的"},{"english":"will survive","chinese":"會繼續存在"}]},"model-essay-73-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-73-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:73","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-73-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q73","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In recent years, online streaming platforms have changed the way people watch films and series. Because viewers can now enjoy a huge range of content at home, some argue that cinemas will eventually disappear. I completely disagree with this view because cinemas offer a social and sensory experience that streaming cannot fully replace, and they remain commercially important for the film industry.","chinese":"近年來，網上串流平台改變了人們觀看電影和劇集的方式。 由於觀眾現在可以在家中欣賞大量不同類型的內容，有些人認為電影院最終會消失。 我完全不同意這個觀點，因為電影院提供的是一種社交和感官體驗，而串流平台無法完全取代，而且電影院對電影產業來說在商業上仍然十分重要。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason cinemas will survive is that watching a film on a large screen is fundamentally different from watching it on a phone, laptop or television. A cinema is not just a place where people consume a story; it is a place where sound, scale and atmosphere work together. When the lights go down and the audience becomes silent, even an ordinary film can feel more memorable. By contrast, home viewing is often interrupted by messages, household noise or the temptation to pause. For example, action films, fantasy films and horror films are usually far more powerful in a theatre, where the visual effects and sound design can be experienced as intended. This unique atmosphere gives cinemas a role that online platforms cannot simply copy.","chinese":"電影院會繼續存在的最有力原因是，在大銀幕上看電影，和在手機、手提電腦或電視上看電影，本質上是完全不同的體驗。 電影院不只是一個讓人觀看故事的地方；它是一個讓聲音、畫面規模和氣氛共同發揮作用的空間。 當燈光暗下來，而觀眾安靜下來時，即使是一部普通的電影也可以變得更加令人難忘。 相比之下，在家中觀影經常會被訊息、家中的噪音，或想要暫停影片的誘惑所打斷。 例如，動作片、奇幻片和恐怖片通常在戲院中更具震撼力，因為觀眾能按照創作者原本設計的方式體驗視覺效果和聲音設計。 這種獨特的氣氛賦予了電影院一種網上平台無法輕易複製的角色。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that cinemas remain valuable to both filmmakers and audiences as public cultural spaces. Major studios still use theatrical releases to create excitement, media attention and a sense of occasion. A film that becomes successful in cinemas often gains prestige before it moves to streaming services. Moreover, many people treat going to the cinema as a shared activity, not merely a way to pass time. Families, couples and friends often go there to mark birthdays, weekends or special releases. If cinemas disappeared, society would lose one of the few entertainment spaces where strangers can enjoy the same story together.","chinese":"另一個原因是，作為公共文化空間，電影院對電影製作人和觀眾來說仍然具有價值。 大型電影公司仍然利用院線上映來製造期待感、媒體關注和一種盛事感。 一部在電影院取得成功的電影，往往會在轉到串流平台之前先獲得聲望。 此外，許多人把去電影院看電影視為一種共同參與的活動，而不僅僅是消磨時間的方法。 家庭、情侶和朋友經常會去電影院慶祝生日、度過週末，或觀看特別上映的電影。 如果電影院消失，社會將會失去少數能讓陌生人一起欣賞同一個故事的娛樂空間之一。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, although streaming services have made home entertainment more convenient, they will not cause cinemas to close completely. Cinemas will continue to exist because they provide immersion, community and cultural value that private screens cannot match.","chinese":"總結來說，雖然串流服務讓家庭娛樂變得更加方便，但它們不會導致電影院完全關閉。 電影院將會繼續存在，因為它們提供了私人螢幕無法相比的沉浸感、群體感和文化價值"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"in recent years","chinese":"近年來"},{"english":"online streaming platforms","chinese":"網上串流平台"},{"english":"changed the way","chinese":"改變了……的方式"},{"english":"films and series","chinese":"電影和劇集"},{"english":"huge range of content","chinese":"大量不同類型的內容"},{"english":"at home","chinese":"在家中"},{"english":"eventually disappear","chinese":"最終消失"},{"english":"completely disagree with","chinese":"完全不同意……"},{"english":"social and sensory experience","chinese":"社交和感官體驗"},{"english":"fully replace","chinese":"完全取代"},{"english":"remain commercially important","chinese":"在商業上仍然重要"},{"english":"film industry","chinese":"電影業"},{"english":"the strongest reason","chinese":"最有力的原因"},{"english":"will survive","chinese":"會繼續存在"},{"english":"large screen","chinese":"大銀幕"},{"english":"fundamentally different from","chinese":"與……有根本不同"},{"english":"consume a story","chinese":"消費一個故事"},{"english":"sound, scale and atmosphere","chinese":"聲音、規模感和氣氛"},{"english":"work together","chinese":"共同發揮作用"},{"english":"the lights go down","chinese":"燈光暗下來"},{"english":"the audience becomes silent","chinese":"觀眾安靜下來"},{"english":"ordinary film","chinese":"普通電影"},{"english":"feel more memorable","chinese":"感覺更難忘"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"home viewing","chinese":"在家觀看"},{"english":"be interrupted by","chinese":"被……打斷"},{"english":"household noise","chinese":"家中噪音"},{"english":"the temptation to pause","chinese":"想暫停的誘惑"},{"english":"action films","chinese":"動作片"},{"english":"fantasy films","chinese":"奇幻電影"},{"english":"horror films","chinese":"恐怖片"},{"english":"far more powerful","chinese":"有震撼力得多"},{"english":"in a theatre","chinese":"在戲院裏"},{"english":"visual effects","chinese":"視覺效果"},{"english":"sound design","chinese":"聲音設計"},{"english":"be experienced as intended","chinese":"按原意被體驗"},{"english":"unique atmosphere","chinese":"獨特氣氛"},{"english":"cannot simply copy","chinese":"不能簡單複製"},{"english":"remain valuable to","chinese":"對……仍然有價值"},{"english":"filmmakers and audiences","chinese":"電影製作人和觀眾"},{"english":"public cultural spaces","chinese":"公共文化空間"},{"english":"major studios","chinese":"大型電影公司"},{"english":"theatrical releases","chinese":"戲院上映"},{"english":"create excitement","chinese":"製造興奮感"},{"english":"media attention","chinese":"媒體關注"},{"english":"a sense of occasion","chinese":"一種特別時刻的感覺"},{"english":"become successful in cinemas","chinese":"在戲院取得成功"},{"english":"gain prestige","chinese":"獲得聲望"},{"english":"move to streaming services","chinese":"轉到串流服務"},{"english":"moreover","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"going to the cinema","chinese":"去戲院看電影"},{"english":"shared activity","chinese":"共同活動"},{"english":"merely a way to pass time","chinese":"只是打發時間的方式"},{"english":"mark birthdays","chinese":"慶祝生日"},{"english":"special releases","chinese":"特別上映的電影"},{"english":"society would lose","chinese":"社會會失去"},{"english":"one of the few","chinese":"少數……之一"},{"english":"entertainment spaces","chinese":"娛樂空間"},{"english":"strangers","chinese":"陌生人"},{"english":"enjoy the same story together","chinese":"一起欣賞同一個故事"},{"english":"home entertainment","chinese":"家庭娛樂"},{"english":"more convenient","chinese":"更方便"},{"english":"close completely","chinese":"完全結業"},{"english":"continue to exist","chinese":"繼續存在"},{"english":"provide immersion","chinese":"提供沉浸感"},{"english":"community and cultural value","chinese":"社群和文化價值"},{"english":"private screens","chinese":"私人螢幕"},{"english":"cannot match","chinese":"不能媲美"}]},"model-essay-74-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-74-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:74","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-74-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q74","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Television remains a powerful commercial medium, especially in the hours after school, when many children are tired, hungry, and looking for entertainment. I firmly believe that advertisements deliberately aimed at young viewers should be prohibited, because children are not mature enough to recognise persuasive techniques and because such marketing places unnecessary pressure on families.","chinese":"電視仍然是一種強大的商業媒介，尤其是在放學後的時段，當許多孩子感到疲倦、飢餓，並正在尋找娛樂時。 我堅定地認為，刻意針對年輕觀眾的廣告應該被禁止，因為兒童尚未成熟到足以識別說服技巧，而且這類行銷會給家庭帶來不必要的壓力。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason for banning these advertisements is that children are especially easy to influence. Unlike adults, they often cannot separate information from persuasion, so a colourful commercial can feel less like a sales pitch and more like a promise of happiness. Advertisers know this, and they frequently use cartoon characters, catchy songs, exaggerated excitement, and bright images to turn ordinary products into objects of desire. For example, a child who sees an advert for a sugary cereal or a new toy may not think about nutrition, cost, or whether the product is necessary; they simply feel that they must have it. This is not fair competition. It is the deliberate use of adult marketing skills against people whose judgement is still developing.","chinese":"禁止這些廣告最有力的理由是，兒童特別容易受到影響。 與成年人不同，他們往往無法區分資訊與說服，因此一個色彩繽紛的廣告可能不像是在推銷商品，而更像是在承諾幸福。 廣告商深知這一點，因此他們經常使用卡通人物、朗朗上口的歌曲、誇張的興奮感和鮮明的畫面，把普通產品變成令人渴望的物品。 例如，一個看到含糖早餐穀物或新玩具廣告的孩子，可能不會思考營養、成本，或這件產品是否必要；他們只是覺得自己一定要擁有它。 這並不是公平競爭。這是刻意把成年人的行銷技巧用在判斷力仍在發展中的人身上。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important concern is the pressure these advertisements create inside the home. When children are repeatedly encouraged to want particular snacks, toys, or fast-food meals, parents are often forced into an unnecessary battle. They either give in and spend money on things the family may not need, or they refuse and face arguments, disappointment, and guilt. This problem is even sharper for low-income families, where every small purchase matters. In addition, many child-focused advertisements promote short-term pleasure rather than healthy habits, which can quietly normalise overconsumption. Childhood should not become a marketplace in which family routines are constantly interrupted by commercial demands.","chinese":"另一個重要的擔憂，是這些廣告在家庭內部製造的壓力。 當兒童被反覆鼓勵去想要某些零食、玩具或快餐時，父母往往會被迫陷入一場不必要的爭戰。 他們要麼讓步，花錢購買家庭可能並不需要的東西；要麼拒絕，然後面對爭吵、失望和內疚。 對低收入家庭來說，這個問題更加尖銳，因為每一筆小額開支都很重要。 此外，許多以兒童為對象的廣告推廣的是短暫的快樂，而不是健康的習慣，這可能會悄悄地使過度消費變得正常化。 童年不應該變成一個市場，讓家庭日常不斷被商業需求打斷。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, advertisements aimed at children should not be allowed. Young viewers deserve protection from manipulation, and parents should not have to compete with carefully designed marketing campaigns in their own living rooms.","chinese":"總結來說，針對兒童的廣告不應該被允許。 年輕觀眾應該受到保護，免受操控，而父母也不應該在自己的客廳裡與精心設計的行銷活動競爭。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"remains a powerful commercial medium","chinese":"仍然是強大的商業媒介"},{"english":"commercial medium","chinese":"商業媒介"},{"english":"especially in the hours after school","chinese":"尤其是在放學後的時段"},{"english":"looking for entertainment","chinese":"尋找娛樂"},{"english":"firmly believe that","chinese":"堅信……"},{"english":"advertisements deliberately aimed at","chinese":"蓄意針對……的廣告"},{"english":"young viewers","chinese":"年輕觀眾"},{"english":"should be prohibited","chinese":"應被禁止"},{"english":"mature enough to","chinese":"成熟到足以……"},{"english":"recognise persuasive techniques","chinese":"識別說服技巧"},{"english":"persuasive techniques","chinese":"說服技巧"},{"english":"such marketing","chinese":"這類營銷"},{"english":"place unnecessary pressure on","chinese":"對……造成不必要壓力"},{"english":"the strongest reason for","chinese":"……的最有力原因"},{"english":"banning these advertisements","chinese":"禁止這些廣告"},{"english":"especially easy to influence","chinese":"特別容易受影響"},{"english":"unlike adults","chinese":"不像成年人"},{"english":"separate information from persuasion","chinese":"分辨資料和說服"},{"english":"colourful commercial","chinese":"色彩鮮艷的廣告"},{"english":"sales pitch","chinese":"推銷說辭"},{"english":"a promise of happiness","chinese":"幸福的承諾"},{"english":"advertisers","chinese":"廣告商"},{"english":"frequently use","chinese":"經常使用"},{"english":"cartoon characters","chinese":"卡通人物"},{"english":"catchy songs","chinese":"易記的歌曲"},{"english":"exaggerated excitement","chinese":"誇張的興奮感"},{"english":"bright images","chinese":"鮮明圖像"},{"english":"turn ordinary products into","chinese":"將普通產品變成……"},{"english":"objects of desire","chinese":"渴望得到的東西"},{"english":"sugary cereal","chinese":"高糖早餐穀物"},{"english":"a new toy","chinese":"新玩具"},{"english":"think about nutrition","chinese":"考慮營養"},{"english":"whether the product is necessary","chinese":"產品是否必要"},{"english":"must have it","chinese":"必須擁有它"},{"english":"fair competition","chinese":"公平競爭"},{"english":"deliberate use of","chinese":"蓄意使用……"},{"english":"adult marketing skills","chinese":"成人營銷技巧"},{"english":"against people whose judgement is still developing","chinese":"對判斷力仍在發展的人"},{"english":"judgement is still developing","chinese":"判斷力仍在發展"},{"english":"another important concern","chinese":"另一個重要憂慮"},{"english":"inside the home","chinese":"在家庭內"},{"english":"be repeatedly encouraged to","chinese":"反覆被鼓勵去……"},{"english":"particular snacks","chinese":"特定零食"},{"english":"fast-food meals","chinese":"快餐餐點"},{"english":"be forced into","chinese":"被迫陷入……"},{"english":"unnecessary battle","chinese":"不必要的爭執"},{"english":"give in","chinese":"讓步"},{"english":"spend money on","chinese":"花錢在……上"},{"english":"refuse","chinese":"拒絕"},{"english":"face arguments, disappointment, and guilt","chinese":"面對爭吵、失望和內疚"},{"english":"low-income families","chinese":"低收入家庭"},{"english":"every small purchase matters","chinese":"每一筆小開支都重要"},{"english":"in addition","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"child-focused advertisements","chinese":"針對兒童的廣告"},{"english":"short-term pleasure","chinese":"短暫快樂"},{"english":"rather than healthy habits","chinese":"而不是健康習慣"},{"english":"normalise overconsumption","chinese":"令過度消費變得正常化"},{"english":"overconsumption","chinese":"過度消費"},{"english":"childhood","chinese":"童年"},{"english":"become a marketplace","chinese":"變成市場"},{"english":"family routines","chinese":"家庭日常"},{"english":"be constantly interrupted by","chinese":"不斷被……打斷"},{"english":"commercial demands","chinese":"商業要求"},{"english":"be allowed","chinese":"被允許"},{"english":"deserve protection from","chinese":"值得受到保護，免受……"},{"english":"manipulation","chinese":"操控"},{"english":"compete with","chinese":"與……競爭"},{"english":"carefully designed marketing campaigns","chinese":"精心設計的營銷活動"},{"english":"in their own living rooms","chinese":"在自己的客廳裏"}]},"model-essay-75-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-75-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:75","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-75-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q75","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Foreign films are now watched widely in many parts of the world, and some people fear that they weaken local traditions. I completely disagree with this view. Rather than damaging local culture, foreign films can broaden people’s understanding of the world and even encourage local artists to value their own cultural identity more deeply.","chinese":"外國電影如今在世界許多地方被廣泛觀看，而有些人擔心它們會削弱本地傳統。 我完全不同意這個觀點。 外國電影並不會破壞本地文化，反而能拓闊人們對世界的理解，甚至鼓勵本地藝術工作者更深入地重視自身的文化身份。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that exposure to foreign films does not automatically make people abandon their own customs. Culture is not a fragile glass ornament that breaks the moment it touches something new; it is a living system that can absorb outside influences while still keeping its own character. When people watch films from other countries, they may learn about different languages, family values, social problems, and ways of life. This comparison can actually make them more aware of what is special about their own society. For example, a young person who watches Japanese or Korean films may notice differences in manners, humour, or family relationships, but this does not mean they will stop valuing local festivals, food, or traditions. In many cases, contrast makes cultural identity clearer, not weaker.","chinese":"第一個原因是，接觸外國電影並不會自動使人們放棄自己的習俗。 文化並不是一件脆弱的玻璃裝飾品，一接觸新事物就會破碎；它是一個有生命力的系統，能夠吸收外來影響，同時仍然保留自身特色。 當人們觀看來自其他國家的電影時，他們可能會了解不同的語言、家庭價值觀、社會問題和生活方式。 這種比較其實可以使他們更加意識到自己社會的獨特之處。 例如，一個觀看日本或韓國電影的年輕人，可能會注意到禮儀、幽默感或家庭關係方面的差異，但這並不意味著他們會停止重視本地節日、食物或傳統。 在許多情況下，對比會使文化身份更加清晰，而不是更加薄弱。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important point is that foreign films can push local film industries to improve. If audiences are exposed only to domestic productions, local filmmakers may become comfortable and repetitive. However, when they compete with international films, they are often forced to tell better stories, improve production quality, and present local culture in a more attractive way. For instance, a director may choose to use local dialects, historical settings, or traditional music more carefully in order to give the film a distinct voice. In this sense, foreign films can act as a spark rather than a threat.","chinese":"另一個重要觀點是，外國電影可以推動本地電影業進步。 如果觀眾只接觸本地作品，本地電影製作人可能會變得安於現狀並不斷重複。 然而，當他們與國際電影競爭時，他們往往會被迫講述更好的故事、提升製作品質，並以更具吸引力的方式呈現本地文化。 例如，一位導演可能會選擇更仔細地使用本地方言、歷史背景或傳統音樂，以賦予電影一種鮮明的聲音。 從這個意義上說，外國電影可以是一種火花，而不是一種威脅。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely disagree that foreign films have a negative impact on local culture. They widen people’s perspectives and can motivate local creators to protect and present their culture more powerfully.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全不同意外國電影會對本地文化產生負面影響這一說法。 它們能拓闊人們的視野，並能激勵本地創作者更有力地保護和呈現自己的文化。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"foreign films","chinese":"外國電影"},{"english":"be watched widely","chinese":"被廣泛觀看"},{"english":"local traditions","chinese":"本地傳統"},{"english":"weaken local traditions","chinese":"削弱本地傳統"},{"english":"completely disagree with","chinese":"完全不同意……"},{"english":"rather than damaging","chinese":"而不是損害……"},{"english":"local culture","chinese":"本地文化"},{"english":"broaden people's understanding of","chinese":"擴闊人們對……的理解"},{"english":"encourage local artists to","chinese":"鼓勵本地藝術家去……"},{"english":"cultural identity","chinese":"文化身份"},{"english":"more deeply","chinese":"更深入地"},{"english":"exposure to","chinese":"接觸……"},{"english":"does not automatically","chinese":"不會自動；不一定會"},{"english":"abandon their own customs","chinese":"放棄自己的習俗"},{"english":"fragile glass ornament","chinese":"脆弱的玻璃擺設"},{"english":"the moment","chinese":"一……就……"},{"english":"something new","chinese":"新事物"},{"english":"living system","chinese":"活的系統"},{"english":"absorb outside influences","chinese":"吸收外來影響"},{"english":"keep its own character","chinese":"保持自身特色"},{"english":"films from other countries","chinese":"來自其他國家的電影"},{"english":"family values","chinese":"家庭價值觀"},{"english":"social problems","chinese":"社會問題"},{"english":"ways of life","chinese":"生活方式"},{"english":"this comparison","chinese":"這種比較"},{"english":"make them more aware of","chinese":"令他們更意識到……"},{"english":"what is special about","chinese":"……有何特別之處"},{"english":"own society","chinese":"自己的社會"},{"english":"Japanese or Korean films","chinese":"日本或韓國電影"},{"english":"notice differences in","chinese":"注意到……上的差異"},{"english":"manners","chinese":"禮貌；行為禮儀"},{"english":"humour","chinese":"幽默"},{"english":"family relationships","chinese":"家庭關係"},{"english":"stop valuing","chinese":"停止重視"},{"english":"local festivals","chinese":"本地節日"},{"english":"in many cases","chinese":"在很多情況下"},{"english":"contrast","chinese":"對比"},{"english":"clearer, not weaker","chinese":"更清晰，而不是更薄弱"},{"english":"push local film industries to improve","chinese":"推動本地電影業進步"},{"english":"local film industries","chinese":"本地電影業"},{"english":"be exposed only to","chinese":"只接觸到……"},{"english":"domestic productions","chinese":"本地製作"},{"english":"local filmmakers","chinese":"本地電影製作人"},{"english":"become comfortable and repetitive","chinese":"變得安於現狀和重複"},{"english":"compete with","chinese":"與……競爭"},{"english":"international films","chinese":"國際電影"},{"english":"be forced to","chinese":"被迫去……"},{"english":"tell better stories","chinese":"講出更好的故事"},{"english":"improve production quality","chinese":"提高製作質素"},{"english":"present local culture","chinese":"呈現本地文化"},{"english":"in a more attractive way","chinese":"以更吸引人的方式"},{"english":"local dialects","chinese":"本地方言"},{"english":"historical settings","chinese":"歷史背景"},{"english":"traditional music","chinese":"傳統音樂"},{"english":"give the film a distinct voice","chinese":"令電影有獨特聲音"},{"english":"act as a spark","chinese":"起激發作用"},{"english":"rather than a threat","chinese":"而不是威脅"},{"english":"have a negative impact on","chinese":"對……有負面影響"},{"english":"widen people's perspectives","chinese":"擴闊人們的視野"},{"english":"motivate local creators to","chinese":"推動本地創作者去……"},{"english":"protect and present their culture","chinese":"保護並呈現他們的文化"},{"english":"more powerfully","chinese":"更有力地"}]},"model-essay-76-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-76-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:76","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-76-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Historical dramas occupy an interesting place between education and entertainment. Some people argue that any film drawn from real events must reproduce the past with total precision. I disagree with this view because absolute accuracy is unrealistic in cinema and would often weaken the historical understanding that such films can create.","chinese":"歷史劇情片處於教育與娛樂之間一個相當有趣的位置。 有些人認為，任何取材自真實事件的電影，都必須以完全精確的方式重現過去。 我不同意這種看法，因為在電影中做到絕對準確並不現實，而且往往會削弱這類電影所能創造的歷史理解。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"First, complete accuracy is almost impossible once history is turned into a two-hour narrative. Historical events usually involve missing records, conflicting accounts, and countless minor details that no screenwriter can verify or include. If a director had to show every conversation, journey and background figure exactly as it happened, the film would become painfully slow and almost impossible to follow. For example, a film about a revolution may need to combine several minor politicians into one character or compress months of negotiation into a few scenes. These changes do not betray history when they help viewers grasp its main forces without getting lost in its dust.","chinese":"首先，一旦歷史被轉化成一個兩小時的敘事，完全準確便幾乎是不可能的。 歷史事件通常涉及缺失的記錄、互相矛盾的說法，以及無數編劇既無法核實也無法全部包含的細微細節。 如果導演必須把每一段對話、每一段旅程和每一位背景人物都完全按照真實情況呈現出來，電影就會變得極其沉悶，並且幾乎難以理解。 例如，一部關於革命的電影，可能需要把幾位次要政治人物合併成一個角色，或者把數月的談判濃縮成幾個場景。 當這些改動能幫助觀眾掌握歷史的主要力量，而不是迷失在瑣碎細節之中時，它們並不算是背叛歷史。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Second, films are valuable because they make the past emotionally accessible. Many people first become interested in history through a gripping story, not through an archive or a textbook. Dramatic dialogue, selective scenes and carefully shaped characters can make distant events feel human, especially for younger audiences who might otherwise see history as a dry list of dates. A film that captures fear, courage and moral conflict may leave a stronger educational impression than one that merely records every factual detail. Therefore, the standard should be historical responsibility rather than perfect reproduction: filmmakers should not reverse causes, whitewash crimes or invent outcomes, but they should be free to simplify the path by which the story is told.","chinese":"第二，電影之所以有價值，是因為它們能讓過去在情感上變得更容易接近。 許多人最初對歷史產生興趣，是透過一個扣人心弦的故事，而不是透過檔案或教科書。 富有戲劇性的對話、經過選取的場景，以及被精心塑造的人物，可以讓遙遠的事件顯得更有人情味，尤其是對年輕觀眾而言；否則，他們可能只會把歷史看成一串枯燥的日期。 一部能捕捉恐懼、勇氣和道德衝突的電影，可能比一部只是記錄每一個事實細節的電影留下更深刻的教育印象。 因此，標準應該是歷史責任，而不是完美重現：電影製作者不應顛倒因果、美化罪行或虛構結果，但他們應該有自由去簡化故事被講述的方式。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I do not agree that historical films ought to be completely accurate. Total accuracy is neither achievable nor desirable in a cinematic form. What matters more is that such films preserve the essential truth of events while using the language of cinema to make history vivid and meaningful.","chinese":"總結來說，我不同意歷史電影應該完全準確。 在電影形式中，完全準確既無法實現，也未必值得追求。 更重要的是，這類電影應該保留事件的核心真實，同時運用電影語言使歷史變得生動而有意義。"}],"vocabulary":[]},"model-essay-77-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-77-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:77","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-77-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q77","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Advertising is one of the most powerful tools in modern business, and fast food brands use it especially well. While some people argue that every company should be free to promote its products, I believe that fast food companies should not be allowed to advertise because their products can damage public health and their marketing often targets vulnerable consumers.","chinese":"廣告是現代商業中最強大的工具之一，而快餐品牌尤其善於運用它。 雖然有些人認為每間公司都應該有自由推廣自己的產品， 但我認為快餐公司不應該被允許賣廣告，因為它們的產品可能損害公共健康，而且它們的營銷往往針對容易受影響的消費者。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason for banning fast food advertising is that it encourages unhealthy eating habits on a large scale. Fast food is usually high in salt, sugar, and fat, so repeated exposure to attractive advertisements can make people see it as a normal part of daily life rather than an occasional choice. This is particularly harmful because advertising does not simply provide information; it creates desire. For example, a busy worker who constantly sees posters and online promotions for fried food is more likely to buy a quick meal instead of preparing something healthier. Over time, this can contribute to obesity, heart disease, and other diet-related problems. Therefore, restricting these advertisements would be a reasonable way to protect public health.","chinese":"禁止快餐廣告最有力的原因是，它會大規模地鼓勵不健康的飲食習慣。 快餐通常含有高鹽、高糖和高脂肪，因此反覆接觸吸引人的廣告，可能會使人們把它視為日常生活中的正常部分，而不是偶爾的選擇。 這尤其有害，因為廣告並不只是提供資訊；它會製造慾望。 例如，一位忙碌的上班族如果經常看到炸物的海報和網上促銷，就更有可能買一份快捷餐，而不是準備一些更健康的食物。 長遠而言，這可能導致肥胖、心臟病以及其他與飲食相關的健康問題。 因此，限制這些廣告會是保護公共健康的一種合理方式。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important point is that fast food marketing often influences children and teenagers, who may not have the maturity to judge advertising critically. Bright colours, cartoon characters, celebrity endorsements, and catchy slogans can make unhealthy food seem exciting and harmless. Although companies may claim that they are only exercising their commercial freedom, this freedom should not come at the expense of young people’s well-being. Society already limits the advertising of some harmful products, such as cigarettes, because profit should not be placed above health. Fast food may not be as dangerous as tobacco, but the same basic principle applies: when a product creates serious social costs, advertising it should be controlled.","chinese":"另一個重要觀點是，快餐營銷經常影響兒童和青少年，而他們未必有足夠成熟度去批判性地判斷廣告。 鮮艷的顏色、卡通人物、名人代言和朗朗上口的標語，可能會令不健康的食物看起來令人興奮而且無害。 儘管公司可能聲稱自己只是在行使商業自由，但這種自由不應以年輕人的福祉作為代價 社會已經限制一些有害產品的廣告，例如香煙，因為利潤不應被置於健康之上。 快餐或許不像煙草那樣危險，但同樣的基本原則仍然適用：當一種產品造成嚴重的社會成本時，它的廣告就應該受到控制。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I strongly believe that fast food companies should not have the right to advertise freely. Business freedom is important, but public health is more important, especially when children and long-term eating habits are involved.","chinese":"總結來說，我強烈認為快餐公司不應該擁有自由賣廣告的權利。 商業自由很重要，但公共健康更為重要，尤其是當涉及兒童和長期飲食習慣時。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"advertising","chinese":"廣告"},{"english":"one of the most powerful tools","chinese":"最強大的工具之一"},{"english":"modern business","chinese":"現代商業"},{"english":"fast food brands","chinese":"快餐品牌"},{"english":"be free to","chinese":"可自由去……"},{"english":"promote its products","chinese":"推廣其產品"},{"english":"not be allowed to","chinese":"不應被允許去……"},{"english":"damage public health","chinese":"損害公共健康"},{"english":"vulnerable consumers","chinese":"弱勢消費者"},{"english":"the strongest reason for","chinese":"……的最有力原因"},{"english":"banning fast food advertising","chinese":"禁止快餐廣告"},{"english":"unhealthy eating habits","chinese":"不健康的飲食習慣"},{"english":"on a large scale","chinese":"大規模地"},{"english":"high in salt, sugar, and fat","chinese":"鹽、糖和脂肪含量高"},{"english":"repeated exposure to","chinese":"反覆接觸……"},{"english":"attractive advertisements","chinese":"吸引人的廣告"},{"english":"a normal part of daily life","chinese":"日常生活中正常的一部分"},{"english":"rather than an occasional choice","chinese":"而不是偶爾的選擇"},{"english":"particularly harmful","chinese":"特別有害"},{"english":"provide information","chinese":"提供資料"},{"english":"create desire","chinese":"製造慾望"},{"english":"busy worker","chinese":"忙碌的上班族"},{"english":"constantly sees","chinese":"不斷看見"},{"english":"online promotions","chinese":"網上推廣"},{"english":"fried food","chinese":"油炸食物"},{"english":"be more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"buy a quick meal","chinese":"買一頓快捷餐"},{"english":"instead of preparing","chinese":"而不是準備……"},{"english":"something healthier","chinese":"較健康的東西"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨着時間過去"},{"english":"contribute to","chinese":"導致；促成"},{"english":"obesity","chinese":"肥胖"},{"english":"heart disease","chinese":"心臟病"},{"english":"diet-related problems","chinese":"與飲食有關的問題"},{"english":"restricting these advertisements","chinese":"限制這些廣告"},{"english":"a reasonable way to","chinese":"……的合理方法"},{"english":"protect public health","chinese":"保障公共健康"},{"english":"another important point","chinese":"另一個重要觀點"},{"english":"fast food marketing","chinese":"快餐推廣"},{"english":"influence children and teenagers","chinese":"影響兒童和青少年"},{"english":"have the maturity to","chinese":"有成熟程度去……"},{"english":"judge advertising critically","chinese":"批判地判斷廣告"},{"english":"bright colours","chinese":"鮮艷顏色"},{"english":"cartoon characters","chinese":"卡通人物"},{"english":"celebrity endorsements","chinese":"名人代言"},{"english":"catchy slogans","chinese":"易記的口號"},{"english":"make unhealthy food seem","chinese":"令不健康食物看起來……"},{"english":"exciting and harmless","chinese":"令人興奮而無害"},{"english":"claim that","chinese":"聲稱"},{"english":"exercising their commercial freedom","chinese":"行使其商業自由"},{"english":"commercial freedom","chinese":"商業自由"},{"english":"come at the expense of","chinese":"以犧牲……為代價"},{"english":"young people's well-being","chinese":"年輕人的身心健康"},{"english":"society already limits","chinese":"社會已經限制"},{"english":"harmful products","chinese":"有害產品"},{"english":"such as cigarettes","chinese":"例如香煙"},{"english":"profit","chinese":"利潤"},{"english":"be placed above","chinese":"被置於……之上"},{"english":"as dangerous as tobacco","chinese":"像煙草一樣危險"},{"english":"the same basic principle applies","chinese":"同一基本原則適用"},{"english":"create serious social costs","chinese":"造成嚴重社會成本"},{"english":"be controlled","chinese":"受到管制"},{"english":"strongly believe that","chinese":"強烈相信……"},{"english":"the right to advertise freely","chinese":"自由賣廣告的權利"},{"english":"business freedom","chinese":"商業自由"},{"english":"long-term eating habits","chinese":"長遠飲食習慣"},{"english":"be involved","chinese":"涉及其中"}]},"model-essay-78-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-78-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:78","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-78-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q78","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"With the rise of smartphones, streaming platforms and short online articles, some argue that books are becoming less central to how people learn and relax. I completely disagree with this view. Although the form of reading has changed, books, whether printed or digital, remain one of the most valuable sources of both reliable knowledge and meaningful enjoyment.","chinese":"隨著智能手機、串流平台和短篇網上文章的興起，有些人認為書本在人們學習和放鬆的方式中正變得不那麼重要。 我完全不同意這種看法。 儘管閱讀的形式已經改變，但無論是紙本書還是電子書，書本仍然是可靠知識和有意義娛樂中最有價值的來源之一。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"First, books still play an essential role in providing deep and structured information. Unlike many online posts, which are often brief, fragmented and written for speed, books usually develop an argument carefully and place facts in context. This matters because real understanding rarely comes from isolated pieces of information; it grows when readers can follow a subject from its foundations to its wider implications. For example, a person who wants to understand personal finance, history or health may find short videos useful for quick tips, but a well-written book can explain the principles behind those tips. In this sense, books do not merely give answers; they build judgement.","chinese":"首先，書本在提供深入而有系統的資訊方面，仍然扮演著不可或缺的角色。 不同於許多網上帖文通常簡短、零散，並且為了快速閱讀而寫，書本通常會仔細地發展一個論點，並把事實放在適當的背景之中。 這一點很重要，因為真正的理解很少來自零散孤立的資訊；當讀者能夠從一個主題的基礎一路理解到它更廣泛的影響時，理解才會逐漸形成。 例如，一個想了解個人理財、歷史或健康的人，可能會覺得短片對獲取快速提示很有用，但一本寫得好的書能夠解釋這些提示背後的原則。 從這個意義上說，書本不只是給出答案；它們還能培養判斷力"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Books are also far from obsolete as a form of entertainment. In fact, their slower pace is precisely what makes them valuable. A novel allows readers to enter a world gradually, imagine characters in their own way and experience emotions without the constant noise of advertisements, notifications and algorithms. This kind of entertainment is quieter than a film or a game, but it can be just as powerful. For instance, many commuters still read crime stories, romances or autobiographies on trains, not because they lack digital alternatives, but because reading gives them a private mental space. Books therefore offer an experience that modern media often struggles to replace.","chinese":"作為一種娛樂形式，書本也遠遠未被淘汰。 事實上，書本較慢的節奏正正是它們有價值的地方。 一本小說能讓讀者慢慢進入一個世界，以自己的方式想像人物，並在沒有廣告、通知和演算法不斷干擾的情況下體驗情感。 這種娛樂比電影或遊戲更安靜，但它同樣可以很有力量。 例如，許多通勤者仍然會在火車上閱讀犯罪故事、愛情小說或自傳，並不是因為他們缺乏數碼娛樂選擇，而是因為閱讀能給他們一個私人的精神空間。 因此，書本提供了一種現代媒體往往難以取代的體驗。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I do not agree that books are losing importance. Technology has changed the way people access information and entertainment, but it has not reduced the fundamental value of books. They remain important because they encourage depth, concentration and imagination, qualities that are becoming more necessary, not less.","chinese":"總結來說，我不同意書本正在失去重要性這一看法。 科技已經改變了人們獲取資訊和娛樂的方式，但它並沒有削弱書本的根本價值。 書本仍然重要，因為它們鼓勵深度、專注力和想像力，而這些素質正變得更加必要，而不是更不必要。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"with the rise of","chinese":"隨着……的興起"},{"english":"streaming platforms","chinese":"串流平台"},{"english":"short online articles","chinese":"網上短文"},{"english":"become less central to","chinese":"對……變得較不核心"},{"english":"learn and relax","chinese":"學習和放鬆"},{"english":"although the form of reading has changed","chinese":"雖然閱讀形式已經改變"},{"english":"whether printed or digital","chinese":"不論是印刷版還是數碼版"},{"english":"one of the most valuable sources of","chinese":"……最有價值的來源之一"},{"english":"reliable knowledge","chinese":"可靠知識"},{"english":"meaningful enjoyment","chinese":"有意義的享受"},{"english":"play an essential role in","chinese":"在……中發揮重要作用"},{"english":"deep and structured information","chinese":"深入而有系統的資料"},{"english":"unlike many online posts","chinese":"不像許多網上帖文"},{"english":"brief, fragmented and written for speed","chinese":"簡短、零碎，並為速度而寫"},{"english":"develop an argument carefully","chinese":"仔細展開論點"},{"english":"place facts in context","chinese":"將事實放在背景脈絡中"},{"english":"real understanding","chinese":"真正理解"},{"english":"isolated pieces of information","chinese":"零散資料"},{"english":"follow a subject from","chinese":"從……追溯一個主題"},{"english":"its foundations","chinese":"它的基礎"},{"english":"wider implications","chinese":"更廣泛的影響"},{"english":"personal finance","chinese":"個人理財"},{"english":"quick tips","chinese":"快速貼士"},{"english":"well-written book","chinese":"寫得好的書"},{"english":"the principles behind","chinese":"……背後的原則"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"not merely give answers","chinese":"不只是提供答案"},{"english":"build judgement","chinese":"培養判斷力"},{"english":"far from obsolete","chinese":"遠未過時"},{"english":"form of entertainment","chinese":"娛樂形式"},{"english":"slower pace","chinese":"較慢的節奏"},{"english":"precisely what makes them valuable","chinese":"正正是令它們有價值的地方"},{"english":"enter a world gradually","chinese":"逐漸進入一個世界"},{"english":"imagine characters in their own way","chinese":"以自己的方式想像角色"},{"english":"constant noise of","chinese":"持續的……滋擾"},{"english":"advertisements, notifications and algorithms","chinese":"廣告、通知和演算法"},{"english":"just as powerful","chinese":"同樣有力量"},{"english":"commuters","chinese":"通勤人士"},{"english":"crime stories","chinese":"犯罪小說"},{"english":"romances","chinese":"愛情小說"},{"english":"autobiographies","chinese":"自傳"},{"english":"lack digital alternatives","chinese":"缺乏數碼替代選擇"},{"english":"private mental space","chinese":"私人的精神空間"},{"english":"offer an experience","chinese":"提供一種體驗"},{"english":"modern media","chinese":"現代媒體"},{"english":"struggle to replace","chinese":"難以取代"},{"english":"losing importance","chinese":"重要性下降"},{"english":"access information and entertainment","chinese":"接觸資料和娛樂"},{"english":"fundamental value","chinese":"根本價值"},{"english":"encourage depth","chinese":"鼓勵深入思考"},{"english":"concentration and imagination","chinese":"專注力和想像力"},{"english":"becoming more necessary, not less","chinese":"變得更加必要，而不是更不必要"}]},"model-essay-79-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-79-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:79","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-79-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q79","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many families, activities are often judged by how quickly they produce visible results. For that reason, some people believe that children who spend many hours reading story books are wasting time that could be used for more practical pursuits. I completely disagree with this view, because story reading develops language, thinking, and emotional intelligence in ways that few childhood activities can match.","chinese":"在許多家庭中，活動往往會根據它們能多快產生可見成果來被評價。 因此，有些人認為，花很多時間閱讀故事書的兒童是在浪費時間，而這些時間本可以用於更實用的活動。 我完全不同意這種觀點，因為閱讀故事能培養語言、思考能力和情緒智力，而這些是很少其他兒童活動能夠相比的。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that story books build the foundation for almost every form of learning. When children read, they are not merely passing time; they are absorbing vocabulary, sentence patterns, ideas, and ways of organising events. A child who follows a plot must remember earlier details, predict what may happen next, and understand why characters make certain choices. This is mental training, not idleness. For example, a child who regularly reads adventure stories may gradually become better at explaining causes, describing situations, and writing coherent paragraphs at school. Other activities may teach useful habits, but story books give children a language-rich environment, and language is the bridge to almost every academic subject.","chinese":"第一個原因是，故事書為幾乎所有形式的學習建立基礎。 當兒童閱讀時，他們並不只是在消磨時間；他們是在吸收詞彙、句式、想法，以及組織事件的方式。 一個跟隨情節發展的孩子，必須記住之前的細節、預測接下來可能發生的事情，並理解角色為何作出某些選擇。 這是思維訓練，而不是無所事事。 例如，一個經常閱讀冒險故事的孩子，可能會逐漸更擅長在學校解釋原因、描述情境，以及寫出連貫的段落。 其他活動也許能教導有用的習慣，但故事書能給孩子一個語言豐富的環境，而語言正是通往幾乎所有學科的橋樑。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Reading story books is also valuable because it develops imagination and empathy. Unlike many forms of entertainment, a book does not hand every image to the child ready-made; it asks the child to picture places, voices, dangers, and emotions internally. This quiet act of imagination strengthens concentration and gives children space to think deeply. More importantly, stories allow them to step into other people’s shoes. A child who reads about a lonely character, a frightened animal, or a brave friend can begin to understand feelings beyond his or her own small world. That kind of emotional growth is not a decorative extra; it helps children become kinder classmates, better listeners, and more thoughtful adults.","chinese":"閱讀故事書同樣有價值，因為它能培養想像力和同理心。 不同於許多娛樂形式，書本不會把每一個畫面都現成地交給孩子；它要求孩子在內心想像地方、聲音、危險和情感。 這種安靜的想像行為能加強專注力，並給孩子深入思考的空間。 更重要的是，故事讓他們能夠代入他人的處境。 一個讀到孤單角色、受驚動物或勇敢朋友的孩子，能開始理解超出自己小小世界之外的情感。 那種情感上的成長並不是可有可無的裝飾；它能幫助孩子成為更友善的同學、更好的聆聽者，以及更體貼的成年人。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely reject the idea that reading children’s story books is a waste of time. Far from being useless, it is one of the richest ways for children to build language, imagination, and character.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全反對「閱讀兒童故事書是浪費時間」這個想法。 它絕非毫無用處，反而是兒童建立語言能力、想像力和品格最豐富的方式之一。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"Visiible results","chinese":"可見成果"},{"english":"practical pursuits","chinese":"實用活動"},{"english":"spend many hours reading","chinese":"花很多時間閱讀"},{"english":"wasting time","chinese":"浪費時間"},{"english":"completely disagree with","chinese":"完全不同意……"},{"english":"develop language, thinking, and emotional intelligence","chinese":"培養語言、思維和情緒智能"},{"english":"few childhood activities can match","chinese":"很少童年活動能媲美"},{"english":"build the foundation for","chinese":"為……打好基礎"},{"english":"almost every form of learning","chinese":"幾乎每一種學習形式"},{"english":"not merely passing time","chinese":"不只是打發時間"},{"english":"absorb vocabulary","chinese":"吸收詞彙"},{"english":"sentence patterns","chinese":"句式"},{"english":"ways of organising events","chinese":"組織事件的方式"},{"english":"follow a plot","chinese":"跟隨情節發展"},{"english":"remember earlier details","chinese":"記住較早前的細節"},{"english":"predict what may happen next","chinese":"預測接下來可能發生甚麼"},{"english":"make certain choices","chinese":"作出某些選擇"},{"english":"mental training","chinese":"思維訓練"},{"english":"idleness","chinese":"無所事事"},{"english":"adventure stories","chinese":"冒險故事"},{"english":"gradually become better at","chinese":"逐漸更擅長……"},{"english":"explaining causes","chinese":"解釋原因"},{"english":"describing situations","chinese":"描述情況"},{"english":"coherent paragraphs","chinese":"連貫的段落"},{"english":"useful habits","chinese":"有用的習慣"},{"english":"language-rich environment","chinese":"語言豐富的環境"},{"english":"the bridge to","chinese":"通往……的橋樑"},{"english":"academic subject","chinese":"學科"},{"english":"imagination and empathy","chinese":"想像力和同理心"},{"english":"unlike many forms of entertainment","chinese":"不像許多娛樂形式"},{"english":"hand every image to","chinese":"將每個畫面直接交給……"},{"english":"ready-made","chinese":"現成的"},{"english":"picture places, voices, dangers, and emotions","chinese":"想像地方、聲音、危險和情緒"},{"english":"internally","chinese":"在內心；在腦海中"},{"english":"quiet act of imagination","chinese":"安靜的想像行為"},{"english":"strengthen concentration","chinese":"加強專注力"},{"english":"give children space to","chinese":"給孩子空間去……"},{"english":"think deeply","chinese":"深入思考"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"step into other people's shoes","chinese":"代入別人的處境"},{"english":"lonely character","chinese":"孤獨的角色"},{"english":"frightened animal","chinese":"受驚的動物"},{"english":"brave friend","chinese":"勇敢的朋友"},{"english":"feelings beyond","chinese":"超出……以外的感受"},{"english":"own small world","chinese":"自己狹小的世界"},{"english":"emotional growth","chinese":"情感成長"},{"english":"decorative extra","chinese":"可有可無的附加物"},{"english":"kinder classmates","chinese":"更友善的同學"},{"english":"better listeners","chinese":"更好的聆聽者"},{"english":"thoughtful adults","chinese":"更有思想的成年人"},{"english":"completely reject the idea that","chinese":"完全否定……的想法"},{"english":"a waste of time","chinese":"浪費時間"},{"english":"far from being useless","chinese":"絕非無用"},{"english":"one of the richest ways to","chinese":"……最豐富的方式之一"},{"english":"build language, imagination, and character","chinese":"培養語言、想像力和品格"}]},"model-essay-80-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-80-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:80","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-80-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q80","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Libraries have traditionally been associated with long shelves of printed books, but their purpose has changed in an age where information is increasingly digital. I fully agree that libraries should prioritise technological resources rather than simply expanding their paper-book collections, because technology makes knowledge more accessible and helps users develop skills that are essential in modern life.","chinese":"圖書館傳統上一直與一排排擺滿紙本書籍的書架聯繫在一起，但在資訊日益數碼化的時代，它們的功能已經發生變化。 我完全同意圖書館應該優先發展科技資源，而不是單純擴大紙本書籍館藏，因為科技能讓知識更容易取得，並幫助使用者培養現代生活中不可或缺的技能。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason is that digital resources allow libraries to serve far more people than printed books can. A physical book can usually be borrowed by only one reader at a time, and it must be collected, returned and stored. By contrast, e-books, online journals, academic databases and digital archives can often be accessed by many users at the same time, even from home. This is especially useful for students, shift workers and elderly people who may not be able to visit a library regularly. For example, a student preparing for an assignment can search electronic journals within minutes, whereas relying only on printed volumes may involve several visits and a great deal of wasted time. In this sense, technology allows libraries to reach beyond their own walls.","chinese":"最有力的原因是，數碼資源能讓圖書館服務的人數遠遠多於紙本書籍所能服務的人數。 一本實體書通常一次只能由一位讀者借閱，而且它必須被領取、歸還和存放。 相比之下，電子書、網上期刊、學術資料庫和數碼檔案往往可以由許多使用者同時存取，甚至可以在家中使用。 這對學生、輪班工作者和長者尤其有用，因為他們未必能夠定期親身前往圖書館。 例如，一位正在準備作業的學生可以在幾分鐘內搜尋電子期刊，而如果只依賴紙本書籍，可能需要多次到訪圖書館，並浪費大量時間。 從這個意義上說，科技使圖書館能夠突破自身建築空間的限制，接觸到更廣泛的人群。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important point is that modern libraries should help people build practical digital skills. Education, employment and public services increasingly depend on the ability to search for, evaluate and use online information responsibly. If libraries invest in computers, media rooms, online catalogues and trained staff, they become active learning centres rather than quiet storage spaces. Children can learn how to research safely, job seekers can prepare applications, and adults can access government services that have moved online. A larger paper collection alone cannot meet these needs. It may look impressive, but it is like adding more candles in an age that requires electric light.","chinese":"另一個重要觀點是，現代圖書館應該幫助人們建立實用的數碼技能。 教育、就業和公共服務越來越依賴人們負責任地搜尋、評估和使用網上資訊的能力。 如果圖書館投資於電腦、媒體室、網上目錄和受過培訓的職員，它們就會成為活躍的學習中心，而不只是安靜的儲存空間。 兒童可以學習如何安全地進行資料搜集，求職者可以準備求職申請，而成年人則可以使用已轉移到網上的政府服務。 單靠更大的紙本館藏無法滿足這些需求。 它也許看起來令人印象深刻，但這就像在一個需要電燈的時代裡增加更多蠟燭一樣。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely agree that libraries should focus on improving their technological resources instead of building ever-larger collections of paper books. This approach gives libraries wider reach, greater efficiency and a more relevant role in contemporary society.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意圖書館應該專注於改善科技資源，而不是建立越來越龐大的紙本書籍館藏。 這種做法能讓圖書館擁有更廣泛的覆蓋範圍、更高的效率，以及在當代社會中更貼切的角色。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"have traditionally been associated with","chinese":"傳統上與……有關"},{"english":"long shelves of printed books","chinese":"一排排印刷書籍"},{"english":"their purpose has changed","chinese":"它們的用途已經改變"},{"english":"in an age where","chinese":"在一個……的時代"},{"english":"increasingly digital","chinese":"越來越數碼化"},{"english":"fully agree that","chinese":"完全同意……"},{"english":"prioritise technological resources","chinese":"優先發展科技資源"},{"english":"rather than simply","chinese":"而不是單純……"},{"english":"expanding their paper-book collections","chinese":"擴充紙本藏書"},{"english":"make knowledge more accessible","chinese":"令知識更容易取得"},{"english":"develop skills","chinese":"培養技能"},{"english":"be essential in modern life","chinese":"在現代生活中必不可少"},{"english":"digital resources","chinese":"數碼資源"},{"english":"serve far more people than","chinese":"服務比……多得多的人"},{"english":"printed books","chinese":"印刷書籍"},{"english":"physical book","chinese":"實體書"},{"english":"be borrowed by","chinese":"被……借閱"},{"english":"one reader at a time","chinese":"每次一位讀者"},{"english":"be collected, returned and stored","chinese":"被取走、歸還和存放"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"e-books","chinese":"電子書"},{"english":"online journals","chinese":"網上期刊"},{"english":"academic databases","chinese":"學術數據庫"},{"english":"digital archives","chinese":"數碼檔案庫"},{"english":"be accessed by","chinese":"被……取用"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"even from home","chinese":"甚至在家中"},{"english":"especially useful for","chinese":"對……特別有用"},{"english":"shift workers","chinese":"輪班工作者"},{"english":"elderly people","chinese":"長者"},{"english":"visit a library regularly","chinese":"定期到訪圖書館"},{"english":"preparing for an assignment","chinese":"準備功課"},{"english":"search electronic journals","chinese":"搜尋電子期刊"},{"english":"within minutes","chinese":"幾分鐘內"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；然而"},{"english":"relying only on","chinese":"只依賴……"},{"english":"printed volumes","chinese":"紙本書冊"},{"english":"involve several visits","chinese":"涉及多次到訪"},{"english":"a great deal of wasted time","chinese":"大量浪費的時間"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"reach beyond their own walls","chinese":"超越自身建築範圍"},{"english":"practical digital skills","chinese":"實用數碼技能"},{"english":"public services","chinese":"公共服務"},{"english":"increasingly depend on","chinese":"越來越依賴"},{"english":"the ability to search for","chinese":"搜尋……的能力"},{"english":"evaluate and use online information responsibly","chinese":"負責任地評估和使用網上資料"},{"english":"invest in","chinese":"投資於……"},{"english":"media rooms","chinese":"媒體室"},{"english":"online catalogues","chinese":"網上目錄"},{"english":"trained staff","chinese":"受過訓練的職員"},{"english":"active learning centres","chinese":"主動學習中心"},{"english":"rather than quiet storage spaces","chinese":"而不是安靜的儲物空間"},{"english":"research safely","chinese":"安全地做資料搜集"},{"english":"job seekers","chinese":"求職者"},{"english":"prepare applications","chinese":"準備申請"},{"english":"access government services","chinese":"使用政府服務"},{"english":"have moved online","chinese":"已轉到網上"},{"english":"paper collection alone","chinese":"單靠紙本藏書"},{"english":"meet these needs","chinese":"滿足這些需要"},{"english":"look impressive","chinese":"看起來令人印象深刻"},{"english":"adding more candles","chinese":"增加更多蠟燭"},{"english":"requires electric light","chinese":"需要電燈"},{"english":"focus on improving","chinese":"專注於改善……"},{"english":"instead of building","chinese":"而不是建立……"},{"english":"ever-larger collections of","chinese":"越來越龐大的……藏量"},{"english":"this approach","chinese":"這種做法"},{"english":"wider reach","chinese":"更廣的覆蓋範圍"},{"english":"greater efficiency","chinese":"更高效率"},{"english":"a more relevant role","chinese":"更切合需要的角色"},{"english":"contemporary society","chinese":"當代社會"}]},"model-essay-81-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-81-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:81","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-81-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q81","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Marriage has long been associated not only with love and family life, but also with economic protection. In many societies, however, women now have far greater access to education and paid work. I completely agree that this financial independence is the main reason why many women no longer regard marriage as a necessity.","chinese":"婚姻長久以來不只與愛情和家庭生活有關，也與經濟保障聯繫在一起。 然而，在許多社會中，女性如今有更多機會接受教育和從事有薪工作。 我完全同意，這種經濟獨立是許多女性不再把婚姻視為必要選擇的主要原因。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason is that earning an income allows women to meet their basic needs without depending on a husband. In the past, a woman who could not easily own property, enter well-paid employment or support children alone often had little choice but to see marriage as a safety net. By contrast, a woman with a stable salary can rent a home, pay bills, save for the future and make major life decisions on her own terms. For example, a professional woman in a large city may postpone or reject marriage because her career already gives her the security that marriage once promised. In this sense, money does not simply buy comfort; it buys freedom.","chinese":"最有力的原因是，賺取收入使女性能夠滿足自己的基本需要，而不必依賴丈夫。 在過去，一個不容易擁有財產、進入高薪工作或獨自撫養孩子的女性，往往別無選擇，只能把婚姻視為一張安全網。 相比之下，一個擁有穩定薪水的女性可以租住房屋、支付賬單、為將來儲蓄，並按照自己的條件作出重大人生決定。 例如，一位在大城市工作的專業女性可能會推遲甚至拒絕婚姻，因為她的事業已經給予她婚姻過去所承諾的安全感。 從這個意義上說，金錢買到的不只是舒適；它買到的是自由。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Financial independence also changes how women judge relationships. When marriage is no longer required for survival, it has to offer emotional respect, equality and genuine companionship. A woman who can support herself is less likely to tolerate a controlling or unhappy marriage merely because leaving would be financially impossible. This shift raises the standard of marriage itself: it becomes a choice rather than a cage. For instance, many working women would rather remain single than enter a relationship where domestic responsibilities, career sacrifice and emotional labour fall mainly on them.","chinese":"經濟獨立也改變了女性判斷關係的方式。 當婚姻不再是生存所必需的條件時，它就必須提供情感上的尊重、平等和真正的陪伴。 一個能夠養活自己的女性，較不可能僅僅因為離開在經濟上不可行，就忍受一段控制慾強或不快樂的婚姻。 這種轉變提高了婚姻本身的標準：它變成了一種選擇，而不是一個牢籠。 例如，許多職業女性寧願保持單身，也不願進入一段家務責任、事業犧牲和情感勞動主要都落在自己身上的關係。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully agree that women’s ability to earn their own income is the key reason why marriage feels less necessary in many countries. As financial dependence fades, marriage loses its old function as economic protection and must stand on the firmer ground of love, respect and equality.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意，女性能夠賺取自己的收入，是婚姻在許多國家變得較不必要的關鍵原因。 隨著經濟依賴逐漸消退，婚姻失去了其作為經濟保障的舊有功能，並必須建立在愛、尊重和平等這些更穩固的基礎之上。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"has long been associated with","chinese":"長久以來與……有關"},{"english":"not only with","chinese":"不只是與……"},{"english":"but also with","chinese":"而且與……"},{"english":"economic protection","chinese":"經濟保障"},{"english":"far greater access to","chinese":"更大得多的機會接觸……"},{"english":"paid work","chinese":"受薪工作"},{"english":"financial independence","chinese":"經濟獨立"},{"english":"the main reason why","chinese":"……的主要原因"},{"english":"no longer regard","chinese":"不再視為"},{"english":"as a necessity","chinese":"作為必需品"},{"english":"earning an income","chinese":"賺取收入"},{"english":"meet their basic needs","chinese":"滿足基本需要"},{"english":"depend on","chinese":"依賴"},{"english":"in the past","chinese":"在過去"},{"english":"own property","chinese":"擁有物業"},{"english":"well-paid employment","chinese":"高薪工作"},{"english":"support children alone","chinese":"獨自撫養孩子"},{"english":"have little choice but to","chinese":"別無選擇，只能……"},{"english":"a safety net","chinese":"安全網"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"stable salary","chinese":"穩定薪金"},{"english":"rent a home","chinese":"租屋"},{"english":"pay bills","chinese":"支付帳單"},{"english":"save for the future","chinese":"為將來儲蓄"},{"english":"make major life decisions","chinese":"作出重大人生決定"},{"english":"on her own terms","chinese":"按自己的條件"},{"english":"professional woman","chinese":"職業女性"},{"english":"postpone marriage","chinese":"延遲結婚"},{"english":"reject marriage","chinese":"拒絕結婚"},{"english":"gives her the security","chinese":"給予她安全感"},{"english":"once promised","chinese":"曾經承諾"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"buy comfort","chinese":"買來舒適"},{"english":"buy freedom","chinese":"買來自由"},{"english":"judge relationships","chinese":"評價關係"},{"english":"be no longer required for","chinese":"不再是……所必需"},{"english":"offer emotional respect","chinese":"提供情感上的尊重"},{"english":"genuine companionship","chinese":"真正的陪伴"},{"english":"support herself","chinese":"養活自己"},{"english":"be less likely to","chinese":"較不可能"},{"english":"tolerate","chinese":"容忍"},{"english":"controlling marriage","chinese":"控制慾強的婚姻"},{"english":"unhappy marriage","chinese":"不快樂的婚姻"},{"english":"merely because","chinese":"只是因為"},{"english":"financially impossible","chinese":"經濟上不可行"},{"english":"this shift","chinese":"這種轉變"},{"english":"raises the standard of","chinese":"提高……的標準"},{"english":"a choice rather than a cage","chinese":"一個選擇，而不是牢籠"},{"english":"remain single","chinese":"保持單身"},{"english":"enter a relationship","chinese":"進入一段關係"},{"english":"domestic responsibilities","chinese":"家務責任"},{"english":"career sacrifice","chinese":"事業上的犧牲"},{"english":"emotional labour","chinese":"情緒勞動"},{"english":"fall mainly on","chinese":"主要落在……身上"},{"english":"ability to earn","chinese":"賺取……的能力"},{"english":"own income","chinese":"自己的收入"},{"english":"the key reason why","chinese":"……的關鍵原因"},{"english":"feels less necessary","chinese":"感覺較不必要"},{"english":"financial dependence fades","chinese":"經濟依賴逐漸消退"},{"english":"loses its old function as","chinese":"失去其作為……的舊功能"},{"english":"stand on the firmer ground of","chinese":"建基於更穩固的……基礎上"},{"english":"love, respect and equality","chinese":"愛、尊重和平等"}]},"model-essay-82-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-82-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:82","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-82-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q82","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Homelessness is one of the clearest signs that a society is failing some of its most vulnerable members, and it is natural to feel that handing over money is a kind response. However, I completely disagree that this is the best way to help homeless people. Direct cash can ease immediate discomfort, but lasting help must address the causes of homelessness.","chinese":"無家可歸是最清楚顯示一個社會未能照顧部分最弱勢成員的跡象之一，而人們自然會覺得直接給錢是一種善意的回應。 然而，我完全不同意這是幫助無家可歸者的最佳方法。 直接給予金錢可以緩解眼前的不適，但長遠的幫助必須處理無家可歸的根本原因。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that money treats the problem as if it were only financial. A person living on the street may need a meal, but they may also lack a stable address, official documents, medical care, family support or the confidence to return to work. In such cases, a donation can be swallowed by daily survival without changing the person’s life. For example, someone might use the money to buy food and stay safe for one more night, yet wake up the next morning facing the same barriers. This is a kind action, but it is not a real solution.","chinese":"第一個原因是，金錢把這個問題處理得好像它只是經濟問題。 一個露宿街頭的人可能需要一餐飯，但他們也可能缺乏穩定地址、官方文件、醫療照顧、家庭支持，或者重新工作的信心。 在這些情況下，一筆捐款可能只會被日常求生所消耗，而不能真正改變這個人的生活。 例如，有人可能會用這筆錢買食物，並安全地度過多一個晚上，但第二天早上醒來時仍然要面對同樣的障礙。 這是一種善意的行動，但它並不是真正的解決方法。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"A more effective response is to provide organised support that helps people rebuild their lives step by step. Shelters, counselling, addiction treatment, affordable housing and job-training schemes deal with the roots of homelessness rather than merely softening its surface. Trained workers can also guide homeless individuals through systems that are difficult to manage alone. For instance, helping someone get an identity card, attend medical appointments and move into temporary accommodation can become a bridge back into ordinary life. In this sense, money is useful only when it is turned into structure, safety and direction.","chinese":"一個更有效的回應，是提供有組織的支援，幫助人們一步一步重建生活。 庇護所、輔導、戒癮治療、可負擔房屋和職業培訓計劃，處理的是無家可歸的根源，而不只是減輕其表面問題。 受過訓練的工作人員也可以引導無家可歸者處理一些獨自難以應付的制度。 例如，幫助一個人取得身份證、出席醫療預約，並搬進臨時住所，可以成為他回到正常生活的一座橋樑。 從這個意義上說，金錢只有在被轉化為制度、保障和方向時，才真正有用。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I strongly disagree that giving money is the best response to homelessness. Although the impulse is compassionate, it is too limited for such a deep social problem. The best help is sustained support that gives people a genuine route off the street.","chinese":"總結來說，我強烈不同意給錢是應對無家可歸問題的最佳方法。 雖然這種衝動是出於同情，但對於這樣一個深層的社會問題而言，它太有限了。 最好的幫助，是持續性的支援，為人們提供一條真正離開街頭的道路。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"homelessness","chinese":"無家者問題；露宿問題"},{"english":"official documents","chinese":"官方文件"},{"english":"medical care","chinese":"醫療照顧"},{"english":"family support","chinese":"家庭支援"},{"english":"the confidence to return to work","chinese":"重返工作的信心"},{"english":"in such cases","chinese":"在這些情況下"},{"english":"be swallowed by","chinese":"被……耗盡"},{"english":"daily survival","chinese":"每日求生"},{"english":"without changing","chinese":"而沒有改變……"},{"english":"stay safe","chinese":"保持安全"},{"english":"one more night","chinese":"多一晚"},{"english":"wake up the next morning","chinese":"第二天早上醒來"},{"english":"face the same barriers","chinese":"面對同樣障礙"},{"english":"a real solution","chinese":"真正的解決方法"},{"english":"a more effective response","chinese":"更有效的回應"},{"english":"organised support","chinese":"有組織的支援"},{"english":"rebuild their lives","chinese":"重建生活"},{"english":"step by step","chinese":"一步一步地"},{"english":"shelters","chinese":"收容所；臨時宿舍"},{"english":"counselling","chinese":"輔導"},{"english":"addiction treatment","chinese":"戒癮治療"},{"english":"affordable housing","chinese":"可負擔房屋"},{"english":"job-training schemes","chinese":"職業培訓計劃"},{"english":"deal with the roots of","chinese":"處理……的根源"},{"english":"rather than merely","chinese":"而不是只是……"},{"english":"soften its surface","chinese":"只紓緩表面問題"},{"english":"trained workers","chinese":"受過訓練的工作人員"},{"english":"guide homeless individuals through","chinese":"引導無家者通過……"},{"english":"difficult to manage alone","chinese":"難以獨自處理"},{"english":"identity card","chinese":"身份證"},{"english":"attend medical appointments","chinese":"出席醫療預約"},{"english":"temporary accommodation","chinese":"臨時住宿"},{"english":"a bridge back into","chinese":"回到……的橋樑"},{"english":"ordinary life","chinese":"正常生活"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"be turned into","chinese":"被轉化為"},{"english":"structure, safety and direction","chinese":"結構、安全和方向"},{"english":"strongly disagree that","chinese":"強烈不同意……"},{"english":"the impulse is compassionate","chinese":"這種衝動是出於同情心"},{"english":"too limited for","chinese":"對……來說太有限"},{"english":"deep social problem","chinese":"深層社會問題"},{"english":"sustained support","chinese":"持續支援"},{"english":"genuine route off the street","chinese":"真正脫離街頭生活的途徑"}]},"model-essay-83-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-83-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:83","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-83-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q83","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"It is often argued that international travel makes people more tolerant and more capable of understanding those who live differently. I completely agree with this view because travelling replaces distant assumptions with real human contact, and it also teaches people the humility that comes from being a stranger in another society.","chinese":"人們常常認為，國際旅行會使人更加寬容，也更有能力理解那些生活方式與自己不同的人。 我完全同意這個觀點，因為旅行會用真實的人際接觸取代遙遠的假設，而且它也教會人們一種謙卑：那就是身處另一個社會、成為陌生人時所產生的謙卑。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that travelling weakens stereotypes. When people judge foreign cultures from a distance, their opinions are often shaped by headlines, films, or second-hand stories, which can reduce whole communities to a few simple labels. However, once travellers eat local food, use public transport, speak to residents, and observe daily routines, unfamiliar customs begin to make sense. For example, a visitor who initially sees quiet public behaviour in another country as cold or unfriendly may later realise that it reflects respect for shared spaces. In this way, travel turns differences from something suspicious into something understandable.","chinese":"第一個原因是，旅行會削弱刻板印象。 當人們從遠處評價外國文化時，他們的看法往往受到新聞標題、電影或二手故事所影響，而這可能會把整個群體簡化成幾個簡單的標籤。 然而，一旦旅客品嚐當地食物、使用公共交通、與居民交談，並觀察日常生活習慣，那些原本陌生的風俗便開始變得可以理解。 例如，一位旅客起初可能會把另一個國家安靜的公共行為視為冷淡或不友善，但後來可能會意識到，這其實反映了對公共空間的尊重。 透過這種方式，旅行把差異從一種令人懷疑的東西，轉化成一種可以理解的東西。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important reason is that travel forces people to experience vulnerability. In a foreign country, even simple tasks such as ordering a meal, asking for directions, or reading a sign can become unexpectedly difficult. This experience can be uncomfortable, but it is also valuable because it reminds travellers how it feels to be confused, dependent, or misunderstood. A person who has once struggled with a foreign language is less likely to look down on immigrants or tourists who face the same problem at home. Travel therefore acts like a mirror: it shows people not only how others live, but also how easily their own confidence depends on familiar surroundings.","chinese":"另一個重要原因是，旅行會迫使人們體驗脆弱感。 在外國，即使是點餐、問路或閱讀標示這些簡單任務，也可能變得出乎意料地困難。 這種經歷可能令人不舒服，但它同時也很有價值，因為它提醒旅客，被困惑、依賴他人或被誤解是一種怎樣的感覺。 一個曾經因外語而掙扎的人，較容易看不起那些在自己國家面對同樣問題的移民或遊客 因此，旅行就像一面鏡子：它不但讓人看見別人如何生活，也讓人看見自己的自信其實多麼容易依賴熟悉的環境。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully agree that travelling abroad can make people more tolerant and understanding. By challenging stereotypes and placing individuals in unfamiliar situations, it broadens their judgement and softens their attitude towards others.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意，到海外旅行能使人更加寬容，也更能理解他人。 透過挑戰刻板印象，並把個人置於陌生情境之中，旅行能拓寬人的判斷力，也能使他們對他人的態度變得更柔和。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"it is often argued that","chinese":"人們經常認為……"},{"english":"international travel","chinese":"國際旅遊"},{"english":"more tolerant","chinese":"更包容"},{"english":"be capable of","chinese":"有能力去……"},{"english":"live differently","chinese":"以不同方式生活"},{"english":"completely agree with","chinese":"完全同意……"},{"english":"replace distant assumptions with","chinese":"以……取代遠距離的假設"},{"english":"distant assumptions","chinese":"遠距離的假設"},{"english":"real human contact","chinese":"真實的人與人接觸"},{"english":"teach people the humility","chinese":"教會人謙卑"},{"english":"comes from","chinese":"來自……"},{"english":"being a stranger","chinese":"成為陌生人"},{"english":"another society","chinese":"另一個社會"},{"english":"weaken stereotypes","chinese":"削弱刻板印象"},{"english":"judge foreign cultures from a distance","chinese":"從遠處評價外國文化"},{"english":"be shaped by","chinese":"受……塑造"},{"english":"headlines","chinese":"新聞標題"},{"english":"second-hand stories","chinese":"二手故事；間接聽來的故事"},{"english":"reduce whole communities to","chinese":"將整個群體簡化為……"},{"english":"whole communities","chinese":"整個群體"},{"english":"a few simple labels","chinese":"幾個簡單標籤"},{"english":"however","chinese":"然而"},{"english":"once travellers","chinese":"一旦旅客……"},{"english":"eat local food","chinese":"吃當地食物"},{"english":"use public transport","chinese":"使用公共交通"},{"english":"speak to residents","chinese":"與居民交談"},{"english":"observe daily routines","chinese":"觀察日常習慣"},{"english":"unfamiliar customs","chinese":"陌生習俗"},{"english":"begin to make sense","chinese":"開始變得合理；開始明白"},{"english":"initially sees","chinese":"起初視為"},{"english":"quiet public behaviour","chinese":"公共場合安靜的行為"},{"english":"cold or unfriendly","chinese":"冷漠或不友善"},{"english":"may later realise that","chinese":"後來可能意識到……"},{"english":"reflect respect for","chinese":"反映對……的尊重"},{"english":"shared spaces","chinese":"共享空間"},{"english":"in this way","chinese":"以這種方式"},{"english":"turn differences from","chinese":"將差異由……轉化為……"},{"english":"something suspicious","chinese":"可疑的東西"},{"english":"something understandable","chinese":"可以理解的東西"},{"english":"force people to","chinese":"迫使人們去……"},{"english":"experience vulnerability","chinese":"經歷脆弱感"},{"english":"even simple tasks","chinese":"即使是簡單任務"},{"english":"ordering a meal","chinese":"點餐"},{"english":"asking for directions","chinese":"問路"},{"english":"reading a sign","chinese":"閱讀告示"},{"english":"unexpectedly difficult","chinese":"出乎意料地困難"},{"english":"uncomfortable","chinese":"令人不自在"},{"english":"reminds travellers how it feels to","chinese":"提醒旅客……是甚麼感受"},{"english":"be confused, dependent, or misunderstood","chinese":"感到困惑、依賴他人或被誤解"},{"english":"struggle with","chinese":"為……而感到困難"},{"english":"foreign language","chinese":"外語"},{"english":"be less likely to","chinese":"較不可能"},{"english":"look down on","chinese":"看不起"},{"english":"immigrants","chinese":"移民"},{"english":"face the same problem","chinese":"面對同樣問題"},{"english":"at home","chinese":"在本地；在自己國家"},{"english":"acts like a mirror","chinese":"像一面鏡子"},{"english":"not only how","chinese":"不只是如何……"},{"english":"how others live","chinese":"別人如何生活"},{"english":"how easily","chinese":"多麼容易"},{"english":"confidence depends on","chinese":"自信取決於……"},{"english":"familiar surroundings","chinese":"熟悉的環境"},{"english":"travelling abroad","chinese":"到外國旅遊"},{"english":"tolerant and understanding","chinese":"包容和體諒"},{"english":"challenging stereotypes","chinese":"挑戰刻板印象"},{"english":"placing individuals in","chinese":"將個人置於……"},{"english":"unfamiliar situations","chinese":"陌生情況"},{"english":"broaden their judgement","chinese":"擴闊判斷"},{"english":"soften their attitude towards","chinese":"軟化對……的態度"},{"english":"towards others","chinese":"對他人"}]},"model-essay-84-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-84-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:84","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-84-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q84","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Many governments devote substantial public funds to programmes that search for life beyond Earth. I completely agree that this is an unjustifiable use of taxpayers’ money, because governments have an immediate duty to solve human problems and because this research can be pursued by private organisations rather than the state.","chinese":"許多政府把大量公共資金投放於尋找地球以外生命的計劃。 我完全同意，這是對納稅人金錢的不合理使用，因為政府有即時責任去解決人類面對的問題，而且這類研究可以由私人機構而不是國家來進行。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason is that public money is limited, so it should first protect citizens whose basic needs are still unmet. In many countries, hospitals are overcrowded, schools lack resources, and low-income families struggle with housing and food. When a government spends huge sums trying to detect alien life, it is choosing a distant possibility over visible suffering. This choice is hard to defend because public services are not luxuries; they are the foundation of a stable society. For example, money directed towards medical equipment, mental-health support, or rural schools can improve lives within years, whereas the search for extraterrestrial life may produce no practical benefit for generations. Government budgets should not chase stars while ordinary citizens are left in the dark.","chinese":"最有力的理由是，公共資金是有限的，因此它應該首先保障那些基本需求仍未被滿足的市民。 在許多國家，醫院過度擠迫，學校缺乏資源，而低收入家庭則在住房和食物方面苦苦掙扎。 當政府花費巨額資金試圖探測外星生命時，它就是在把一個遙遠的可能性置於眼前可見的痛苦之上。 這種選擇很難被合理辯護，因為公共服務並不是奢侈品；它們是一個穩定社會的基礎。 例如，投放在醫療設備、心理健康支援或鄉村學校上的金錢，可以在數年內改善人們的生活；然而，尋找地球以外生命的工作，可能幾代人都不會產生實際利益。 政府預算不應該在普通市民仍被留在黑暗中時，卻去追逐星辰。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that discovering life on other planets is a scientific curiosity rather than a core governmental responsibility. Granted, space science can inspire innovation, but the specific goal of finding alien life does not deserve priority over poverty, disease, and unemployment. If wealthy technology companies, universities, or international research bodies wish to explore this question, they are better placed to do so because they can accept long-term uncertainty without neglecting public duties. Governments, by contrast, are elected to provide security, opportunity, and basic welfare. Every dollar spent on speculative missions is a dollar not spent on making healthcare more accessible, education more equal, or cities safer.","chinese":"另一個理由是，發現其他星球上的生命是一種科學上的好奇心，而不是政府的核心責任 誠然，太空科學可以激發創新；然而，尋找外星生命這一具體目標，並不應比貧窮、疾病和失業更優先。 如果富有的科技公司、大學或國際研究機構希望探索這個問題，它們更適合去做，因為它們可以承受長期的不確定性，而不會忽略公共責任。 相比之下，政府是被選出來提供安全、機會和基本福利的。 每一元花在投機性的任務上，就等於少了一元用來讓醫療更容易取得、教育更平等，或城市更安全。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully agree that governments should reduce spending on the search for life on other planets and redirect those funds to public problems. Curiosity is valuable, but public responsibility must come first; a government should repair the ground beneath its people’s feet before looking for life in the sky.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意政府應該減少在尋找其他星球生命方面的開支，並把這些資金重新投放到公共問題上。 好奇心是有價值的，但公共責任必須優先；政府應該先修補人民腳下的土地，才去仰望天空尋找生命。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"devote substantial public funds to","chinese":"投入大量公帑於……"},{"english":"search for life beyond Earth","chinese":"尋找地球以外的生命"},{"english":"unjustifiable use of","chinese":"對……不合理的使用"},{"english":"taxpayers' money","chinese":"納稅人的錢"},{"english":"immediate duty to","chinese":"有即時責任去……"},{"english":"human problems","chinese":"人類問題"},{"english":"be pursued by","chinese":"由……進行"},{"english":"private organisations","chinese":"私營機構"},{"english":"rather than the state","chinese":"而不是由國家"},{"english":"public money is limited","chinese":"公帑有限"},{"english":"protect citizens","chinese":"保護公民"},{"english":"basic needs are still unmet","chinese":"基本需要仍未得到滿足"},{"english":"hospitals are overcrowded","chinese":"醫院過度擠迫"},{"english":"schools lack resources","chinese":"學校缺乏資源"},{"english":"low-income families","chinese":"低收入家庭"},{"english":"struggle with","chinese":"為……而掙扎"},{"english":"housing and food","chinese":"住屋和食物"},{"english":"spend huge sums","chinese":"花費巨額金錢"},{"english":"detect alien life","chinese":"探測外星生命"},{"english":"a distant possibility","chinese":"遙遠的可能性"},{"english":"visible suffering","chinese":"眼前可見的苦難"},{"english":"hard to defend","chinese":"難以辯護"},{"english":"public services","chinese":"公共服務"},{"english":"not luxuries","chinese":"不是奢侈品"},{"english":"the foundation of","chinese":"……的基礎"},{"english":"stable society","chinese":"穩定社會"},{"english":"money directed towards","chinese":"投放於……的金錢"},{"english":"medical equipment","chinese":"醫療設備"},{"english":"mental-health support","chinese":"精神健康支援"},{"english":"rural schools","chinese":"鄉郊學校"},{"english":"improve lives within years","chinese":"在數年內改善生活"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；然而"},{"english":"extraterrestrial life","chinese":"地球以外的生命"},{"english":"practical benefit","chinese":"實際好處"},{"english":"for generations","chinese":"好幾代人"},{"english":"government budgets","chinese":"政府預算"},{"english":"chase stars","chinese":"追逐星辰；追求遙遠目標"},{"english":"ordinary citizens","chinese":"普通公民"},{"english":"be left in the dark","chinese":"被留在黑暗中；得不到幫助"},{"english":"scientific curiosity","chinese":"科學上的好奇"},{"english":"core governmental responsibility","chinese":"政府核心責任"},{"english":"granted","chinese":"誠然"},{"english":"inspire innovation","chinese":"啟發創新"},{"english":"the specific goal of","chinese":"……這個具體目標"},{"english":"deserve priority over","chinese":"比……更值得優先處理"},{"english":"poverty, disease, and unemployment","chinese":"貧窮、疾病和失業"},{"english":"wealthy technology companies","chinese":"富有的科技公司"},{"english":"universities","chinese":"大學"},{"english":"international research bodies","chinese":"國際研究機構"},{"english":"explore this question","chinese":"探索這個問題"},{"english":"be better placed to","chinese":"更適合去……"},{"english":"accept long-term uncertainty","chinese":"接受長期不確定性"},{"english":"without neglecting","chinese":"而不忽視……"},{"english":"public duties","chinese":"公共責任"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"be elected to","chinese":"被選出去……"},{"english":"provide security","chinese":"提供安全保障"},{"english":"opportunity","chinese":"機會"},{"english":"basic welfare","chinese":"基本福利"},{"english":"speculative missions","chinese":"投機性任務；不確定性高的任務"},{"english":"make healthcare more accessible","chinese":"令醫療更容易取得"},{"english":"education more equal","chinese":"令教育更平等"},{"english":"cities safer","chinese":"令城市更安全"},{"english":"reduce spending on","chinese":"減少在……上的開支"},{"english":"redirect those funds to","chinese":"將那些資金重新投放到……"},{"english":"public problems","chinese":"公共問題"},{"english":"public responsibility","chinese":"公共責任"},{"english":"come first","chinese":"放在首位"},{"english":"repair the ground beneath","chinese":"修補人民腳下的土地"},{"english":"before looking for life in the sky","chinese":"在尋找天上生命之前"}]},"model-essay-85-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-85-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:85","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-85-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q85","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Teamwork is an essential social skill, and many parents believe that children can learn it best through team sports. However, I completely disagree with the view that introducing children to sports such as football, basketball, or volleyball is the best way to teach this quality. A more reliable method is to involve children in structured group tasks where cooperation is directly taught, monitored, and reflected upon.","chinese":"團隊合作是一項重要的社交技能，而許多父母相信，孩子最能透過團隊運動學會這能力 然而，我完全不同意讓孩子接觸足球、籃球或排球等運動是教授這種品質的最佳方式這一觀點。 一種更可靠的方法，是讓孩子參與有結構的團體任務，在這些任務中，合作會被直接教授、監察並反思。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main weakness of team sports is that they often reward performance more than cooperation. In a competitive game, children may become focused on winning, scoring, or avoiding blame, rather than listening carefully to others or sharing responsibility fairly. Stronger players can easily dominate the activity, while less confident children may be pushed to the side and learn silence rather than teamwork. For example, in a school football match, the fastest child may receive most of the passes because classmates believe this gives them the best chance of winning. In that situation, the group may appear united, but the weaker players are not genuinely learning how to contribute, negotiate, or solve problems together.","chinese":"團隊運動的主要弱點在於，它們往往更重視表現，而不是合作。 在競爭性的比賽中，孩子可能會專注於取勝、得分或避免被責怪，而不是仔細聆聽他人，或公平地分擔責任。 能力較強的孩子很容易主導整個活動，而較缺乏自信的孩子則可能被推到一旁，學到的不是團隊合作，而是沉默。 例如，在一場校內足球比賽中，跑得最快的孩子可能會接到大多數傳球，因為同學們相信這樣最有機會獲勝。 在這種情況下，整個團體看起來可能很團結，但較弱的孩子並沒有真正學會如何貢獻、協商或共同解決問題。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"By contrast, carefully designed group activities teach teamwork more directly and inclusively. When children complete a class project, prepare a group presentation, or organise a small charity event, they must divide responsibilities, exchange ideas, manage disagreements, and depend on one another’s effort. These activities also allow adults to guide the process explicitly. A teacher can ask children why one member was ignored, how tasks should be shared more fairly, and what the group should do when someone falls behind. This kind of reflection turns cooperation from a vague experience into a conscious skill. It also prepares children for real-life teamwork, where success usually depends less on physical ability and more on communication, patience, and shared accountability.","chinese":"相比之下，經過精心設計的團體活動能夠更直接、更具包容性地教授團隊合作。 當孩子完成班級專題、準備小組匯報，或組織一場小型慈善活動時，他們必須分配責任、交換想法、處理分歧，並依靠彼此的努力。 這些活動也讓成人能夠明確地引導整個合作過程。 老師可以問孩子，為甚麼某位成員被忽略、任務應如何更公平地分配，以及當有人落後時，小組應該怎樣處理。 這種反思能把合作從一種模糊的經驗，轉化為一項有意識的技能。 它也能讓孩子為現實生活中的團隊合作做好準備，因為在真實世界中，成功通常較少取決於體能，而更多取決於溝通、耐性和共同責任感。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely disagree that team sports are the best way to teach children teamwork. Structured collaborative tasks are more effective because they give every child a meaningful role and teach the actual habits that teamwork requires.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全不同意團隊運動是教導孩子團隊合作的最佳方式。 有結構的合作任務更有效，因為它們能讓每個孩子都擁有有意義的角色，並教會他們團隊合作真正需要的習慣。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"teamwork","chinese":"團隊合作"},{"english":"essential social skill","chinese":"重要社交技能"},{"english":"learn it best through","chinese":"最能透過……學到"},{"english":"team sports","chinese":"團隊運動"},{"english":"introducing children to","chinese":"讓孩子接觸……"},{"english":"football, basketball, or volleyball","chinese":"足球、籃球或排球"},{"english":"the best way to teach","chinese":"教授……的最佳方法"},{"english":"this quality","chinese":"這種品質"},{"english":"a more reliable method","chinese":"更可靠的方法"},{"english":"involve children in","chinese":"讓孩子參與……"},{"english":"structured group tasks","chinese":"結構化小組任務"},{"english":"directly taught","chinese":"被直接教授"},{"english":"monitored","chinese":"被監察"},{"english":"reflected upon","chinese":"被反思"},{"english":"the main weakness of","chinese":"……的主要弱點"},{"english":"reward performance more than cooperation","chinese":"獎勵表現多於合作"},{"english":"competitive game","chinese":"競爭性比賽"},{"english":"become focused on","chinese":"變得專注於……"},{"english":"avoiding blame","chinese":"避免受責備"},{"english":"rather than listening carefully to","chinese":"而不是細心聆聽……"},{"english":"sharing responsibility fairly","chinese":"公平分擔責任"},{"english":"stronger players","chinese":"較強的隊員"},{"english":"dominate the activity","chinese":"主導活動"},{"english":"less confident children","chinese":"較缺乏自信的孩子"},{"english":"be pushed to the side","chinese":"被推到一旁"},{"english":"learn silence rather than teamwork","chinese":"學會沉默而不是團隊合作"},{"english":"school football match","chinese":"學校足球比賽"},{"english":"receive most of the passes","chinese":"接到大部分傳球"},{"english":"the best chance of winning","chinese":"最大勝算"},{"english":"appear united","chinese":"看似團結"},{"english":"genuinely learning how to","chinese":"真正學會如何……"},{"english":"contribute","chinese":"作出貢獻"},{"english":"negotiate","chinese":"協商"},{"english":"solve problems together","chinese":"一起解決問題"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"carefully designed group activities","chinese":"精心設計的小組活動"},{"english":"more directly and inclusively","chinese":"更直接和更具包容性地"},{"english":"complete a class project","chinese":"完成課堂專題"},{"english":"prepare a group presentation","chinese":"準備小組匯報"},{"english":"organise a small charity event","chinese":"組織小型慈善活動"},{"english":"divide responsibilities","chinese":"分配責任"},{"english":"exchange ideas","chinese":"交流想法"},{"english":"manage disagreements","chinese":"處理分歧"},{"english":"depend on one another's effort","chinese":"依靠彼此的努力"},{"english":"allow adults to","chinese":"讓成年人可以……"},{"english":"guide the process explicitly","chinese":"明確地引導過程"},{"english":"one member was ignored","chinese":"某個成員被忽視"},{"english":"be shared more fairly","chinese":"被更公平地分配"},{"english":"falls behind","chinese":"落後；跟不上"},{"english":"this kind of reflection","chinese":"這種反思"},{"english":"vague experience","chinese":"模糊的經驗"},{"english":"conscious skill","chinese":"有意識的技能"},{"english":"real-life teamwork","chinese":"現實生活中的團隊合作"},{"english":"depend less on","chinese":"較少取決於……"},{"english":"physical ability","chinese":"體能"},{"english":"communication, patience, and shared accountability","chinese":"溝通、耐性和共同問責"},{"english":"structured collaborative tasks","chinese":"結構化協作任務"},{"english":"meaningful role","chinese":"有意義的角色"},{"english":"actual habits","chinese":"實際習慣"},{"english":"teamwork requires","chinese":"團隊合作所需要的"}]},"model-essay-86-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-86-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:86","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-86-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q86","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Regular physical activity is essential to children’s health, yet I completely disagree that it should be treated only as a parental duty or removed from the school timetable. Schools should continue to provide sports lessons because they ensure equal access to exercise and support children’s wider development.","chinese":"定期進行體能活動對兒童健康至關重要，然而我完全不同意它應該只被視為父母的責任，或應該從學校時間表中移除。 學校應該繼續提供體育課，因為它們能確保所有孩子都有平等的運動機會，並支持兒童更全面的發展。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that leaving physical exercise entirely to parents would create serious inequalities. Some parents have the time, money and knowledge to take their children to parks, sports clubs or swimming lessons, but many do not. Others may work long hours, live in unsafe neighbourhoods or simply underestimate how much movement children need. If schools abandon physical education, the children who already have fewer opportunities outside school will be the first to lose out. By contrast, compulsory sports lessons give every child a regular chance to move, regardless of family background. For example, a child from a low-income household may never join a private football academy, but school PE can still introduce that child to running, teamwork and basic fitness. In this sense, schools act as a safety net, not a substitute for parents.","chinese":"第一個原因是，將體能活動完全交由父母負責，會造成嚴重的不平等。 有些父母有時間、金錢和知識，可以帶孩子去公園、體育俱樂部或游泳課，但許多父母並沒有這些條件。 另一些父母可能長時間工作、住在不安全的社區，或者只是低估了孩子需要多少活動量 如果學校放棄體育教育，那些在校外本來已經較少機會運動的孩子，將會是最先受損的一群 相比之下，必修體育課能給每一個孩子定期活動的機會，不論他們的家庭背景如何。 例如，一個來自低收入家庭的孩子可能永遠不會參加私人足球學院，但學校體育課仍然可以讓這個孩子接觸跑步、團隊合作和基本體能訓練。 從這個意義上說，學校扮演的是安全網的角色，而不是父母的替代品。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Moreover, sports lessons are not a waste of valuable school time; they make academic time more effective. Children are not machines that can sit at desks all day and absorb information without rest. Physical activity improves concentration, reduces stress and teaches discipline, cooperation and resilience. These qualities matter just as much as exam results because education should prepare young people for life, not only for tests. For instance, a basketball lesson can teach pupils how to follow rules, handle defeat and work with others towards a shared goal. These are practical lessons that cannot be learned as easily from textbooks.","chinese":"此外，體育課並不是浪費寶貴的學校時間；它們反而令學術學習時間更有效。 孩子並不是機器，不能整天坐在書桌前，毫無休息地吸收資訊。 體能活動能提升專注力、減輕壓力，並教會孩子紀律、合作和抗逆力。 這些素質和考試成績一樣重要，因為教育應該讓年輕人為人生作好準備，而不只是為考試作準備。 例如，一堂籃球課可以教學生如何遵守規則、面對失敗，並與他人一起朝著共同目標努力。 這些都是實用的人生課，而它們並不能輕易地從課本中學到。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely disagree with the view that schools should remove sports from the curriculum. Parents certainly influence children’s habits, but schools have a vital responsibility to guarantee regular exercise for all pupils and to educate the whole child.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全不同意學校應該將體育從課程中移除這一觀點。 父母固然會影響孩子的習慣，但學校也有重要責任，去確保所有學生都能定期運動，並讓孩子獲得全面教育。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"regular physical activity","chinese":"定期體能活動"},{"english":"be essential to","chinese":"對……必不可少"},{"english":"children's health","chinese":"兒童健康"},{"english":"be treated only as","chinese":"只被視為……"},{"english":"parental duty","chinese":"父母責任"},{"english":"be removed from","chinese":"從……移除"},{"english":"school timetable","chinese":"學校時間表"},{"english":"continue to provide","chinese":"繼續提供"},{"english":"sports lessons","chinese":"體育課"},{"english":"ensure equal access to","chinese":"確保平等接觸……的機會"},{"english":"exercise","chinese":"運動"},{"english":"wider development","chinese":"更全面的發展"},{"english":"leaving physical exercise entirely to","chinese":"將體能活動完全交給……"},{"english":"create serious inequalities","chinese":"造成嚴重不平等"},{"english":"have the time, money and knowledge to","chinese":"有時間、金錢和知識去……"},{"english":"sports clubs","chinese":"體育會；運動俱樂部"},{"english":"swimming lessons","chinese":"游泳課"},{"english":"work long hours","chinese":"長時間工作"},{"english":"unsafe neighbourhoods","chinese":"不安全的社區"},{"english":"underestimate how much","chinese":"低估……有多少"},{"english":"movement","chinese":"活動量"},{"english":"abandon physical education","chinese":"放棄體育教育"},{"english":"physical education","chinese":"體育教育；體育課"},{"english":"fewer opportunities","chinese":"較少機會"},{"english":"outside school","chinese":"在校外"},{"english":"be the first to lose out","chinese":"最先吃虧"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"compulsory sports lessons","chinese":"必修體育課"},{"english":"a regular chance to move","chinese":"定期活動身體的機會"},{"english":"regardless of family background","chinese":"不論家庭背景"},{"english":"low-income household","chinese":"低收入家庭"},{"english":"private football academy","chinese":"私人足球學院"},{"english":"school PE","chinese":"學校體育課"},{"english":"introduce that child to","chinese":"讓那個孩子接觸到……"},{"english":"teamwork","chinese":"團隊合作"},{"english":"basic fitness","chinese":"基本體能"},{"english":"act as a safety net","chinese":"充當安全網"},{"english":"substitute for","chinese":"……的替代品"},{"english":"moreover","chinese":"此外"},{"english":"a waste of valuable school time","chinese":"浪費寶貴上課時間"},{"english":"academic time","chinese":"學習時間"},{"english":"more effective","chinese":"更有效"},{"english":"sit at desks all day","chinese":"整天坐在書桌前"},{"english":"absorb information","chinese":"吸收資料"},{"english":"without rest","chinese":"沒有休息"},{"english":"improve concentration","chinese":"提高專注力"},{"english":"reduce stress","chinese":"減輕壓力"},{"english":"teach discipline","chinese":"教導紀律"},{"english":"cooperation and resilience","chinese":"合作和韌性"},{"english":"matter just as much as","chinese":"與……同樣重要"},{"english":"exam results","chinese":"考試成績"},{"english":"prepare young people for life","chinese":"讓年輕人為生活作好準備"},{"english":"not only for tests","chinese":"不只是為考試"},{"english":"basketball lesson","chinese":"籃球課"},{"english":"follow rules","chinese":"遵守規則"},{"english":"handle defeat","chinese":"面對失敗"},{"english":"work with others towards","chinese":"與他人一起為……努力"},{"english":"shared goal","chinese":"共同目標"},{"english":"practical lessons","chinese":"實用課堂；實際教訓"},{"english":"cannot be learned as easily from","chinese":"不能那麼容易從……學到"},{"english":"remove sports from the curriculum","chinese":"將體育從課程中移除"},{"english":"curriculum","chinese":"課程"},{"english":"influence children's habits","chinese":"影響孩子的習慣"},{"english":"a vital responsibility","chinese":"重要責任"},{"english":"guarantee regular exercise","chinese":"保障定期運動"},{"english":"educate the whole child","chinese":"培育孩子的全面發展"}]},"model-essay-87-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-87-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:87","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-87-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q87","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In modern workplaces, employees are often expected to remain seated for long hours while meeting demanding deadlines. I strongly believe that companies should set aside time for physical exercise during the working day, because this would improve both employee health and workplace performance.","chinese":"在現代職場中，員工經常被期望長時間坐著，同時應付要求很高的截止期限。 我堅定認為，公司應該在工作日中預留時間讓員工進行體育鍛煉，因為這既能改善員工健康，也能提升工作表現。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The most important reason is that regular movement helps protect workers from the physical and mental damage caused by sedentary jobs. Many office employees spend most of the day in front of a screen, which can lead to back pain, tiredness and stress. If companies allow staff to take a short period for exercise, such as stretching, walking or using a gym, workers are more likely to return to their desks feeling refreshed rather than drained. For example, an accountant who takes a twenty-minute walk after several hours of concentrated work may be able to clear his mind and avoid the sense of exhaustion that often builds up in the afternoon. In this sense, exercise time is not a luxury; it is a practical way to prevent the workplace from slowly damaging people’s well-being.","chinese":"最重要的原因是，定期活動有助於保護員工免受久坐工作所造成的身體和心理損害。 許多辦公室員工一天大部分時間都在螢幕前度過，這可能導致背痛、疲倦和壓力。 如果公司允許員工用一小段時間做運動，例如伸展、步行或使用健身室，員工回到辦公桌時便更可能感到精神恢復，而不是筋疲力盡。 例如，一位會計師在數小時專注工作後散步二十分鐘，可能能夠清理思緒，並避免下午經常累積起來的疲憊感。 從這個意義上說，運動時間並不是奢侈品；它是一種實際的方法，可以防止職場慢慢損害人們的身心健康。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"It is also likely to benefit employers themselves. A healthy workforce tends to be more energetic, focused and loyal, so the time spent on exercise can be recovered through better productivity. Some managers may worry that exercise breaks reduce working hours, but this view is rather short-sighted. Employees who are tired, inactive and under pressure rarely produce their best work simply because they sit at their desks for longer. By contrast, when a company encourages exercise, it sends a clear message that staff are valued as human beings, not just as machines for producing output. This can strengthen morale and reduce unnecessary absence.","chinese":"這也很可能會讓僱主本身受益。 健康的員工隊伍往往更有活力、更專注，也更忠誠，因此花在運動上的時間可以透過更高的生產力補回來。 有些管理者可能會擔心運動休息會減少工作時間，但這種看法相當短視。 疲倦、缺乏活動並承受壓力的員工，很少會僅僅因為坐在辦公桌前更久，就能交出最佳工作表現。 相比之下，當一家公司鼓勵運動時，它傳達出一個清晰的訊息：員工是作為人被重視，而不只是被視為產出工作的機器。 這可以增強士氣，並減少不必要的缺勤。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I firmly support the idea that companies should provide exercise time during the day. Done sensibly, it protects employees’ health and helps businesses build a more productive, humane workplace.","chinese":"總結來說，我堅定支持公司應該在一天中提供運動時間這個想法。 如果做得合理，它能保護員工健康，並幫助企業建立一個更具生產力、也更有人性的工作場所。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"modern workplaces","chinese":"現代工作場所"},{"english":"be expected to","chinese":"被期望去……"},{"english":"remain seated","chinese":"保持坐着"},{"english":"for long hours","chinese":"長時間"},{"english":"demanding deadlines","chinese":"要求高的限期"},{"english":"strongly believe that","chinese":"強烈相信……"},{"english":"set aside time for","chinese":"預留時間給……"},{"english":"physical exercise","chinese":"體能運動"},{"english":"during the working day","chinese":"在工作日內"},{"english":"employee health","chinese":"員工健康"},{"english":"workplace performance","chinese":"工作場所表現"},{"english":"the most important reason","chinese":"最重要的原因"},{"english":"regular movement","chinese":"定期活動身體"},{"english":"protect workers from","chinese":"保護員工免受……"},{"english":"physical and mental damage","chinese":"身體和精神上的損害"},{"english":"caused by","chinese":"由……造成"},{"english":"sedentary jobs","chinese":"久坐的工作"},{"english":"office employees","chinese":"辦公室員工"},{"english":"spend most of the day","chinese":"花大半天"},{"english":"in front of a screen","chinese":"在螢幕前"},{"english":"lead to","chinese":"導致"},{"english":"back pain","chinese":"背痛"},{"english":"tiredness and stress","chinese":"疲倦和壓力"},{"english":"allow staff to","chinese":"允許員工去……"},{"english":"take a short period for","chinese":"抽一小段時間去……"},{"english":"stretching","chinese":"伸展運動"},{"english":"using a gym","chinese":"使用健身室"},{"english":"be more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"return to their desks","chinese":"回到辦公桌"},{"english":"feeling refreshed","chinese":"感到精神恢復"},{"english":"rather than drained","chinese":"而不是筋疲力盡"},{"english":"accountant","chinese":"會計師"},{"english":"twenty-minute walk","chinese":"二十分鐘步行"},{"english":"concentrated work","chinese":"高度集中的工作"},{"english":"clear his mind","chinese":"清理思緒"},{"english":"avoid the sense of exhaustion","chinese":"避免疲憊感"},{"english":"build up","chinese":"逐漸累積"},{"english":"in the afternoon","chinese":"在下午"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"not a luxury","chinese":"不是奢侈品"},{"english":"practical way to","chinese":"……的實際方法"},{"english":"prevent the workplace from","chinese":"防止工作場所……"},{"english":"slowly damaging","chinese":"慢慢損害"},{"english":"well-being","chinese":"身心健康"},{"english":"be likely to benefit","chinese":"很可能令……受惠"},{"english":"employers themselves","chinese":"僱主本身"},{"english":"healthy workforce","chinese":"健康的員工隊伍"},{"english":"tend to be","chinese":"往往會"},{"english":"energetic, focused and loyal","chinese":"精力充沛、專注和忠誠"},{"english":"time spent on","chinese":"花在……上的時間"},{"english":"be recovered through","chinese":"透過……補回"},{"english":"better productivity","chinese":"更高生產力"},{"english":"exercise breaks","chinese":"運動休息時間"},{"english":"reduce working hours","chinese":"減少工作時間"},{"english":"short-sighted","chinese":"短視的"},{"english":"inactive","chinese":"缺乏活動的"},{"english":"under pressure","chinese":"承受壓力"},{"english":"produce their best work","chinese":"發揮最佳工作表現"},{"english":"sit at their desks for longer","chinese":"在辦公桌前坐更久"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"encourages exercise","chinese":"鼓勵運動"},{"english":"send a clear message","chinese":"傳達清晰信息"},{"english":"be valued as human beings","chinese":"作為人而受到重視"},{"english":"producing output","chinese":"製造產出"},{"english":"strengthen morale","chinese":"提升士氣"},{"english":"reduce unnecessary absence","chinese":"減少不必要的缺勤"},{"english":"firmly support","chinese":"堅定支持"},{"english":"provide exercise time","chinese":"提供運動時間"},{"english":"done sensibly","chinese":"如果安排得宜"},{"english":"productive, humane workplace","chinese":"高效而人性化的工作場所"}]},"model-essay-88-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-88-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:88","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-88-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q88","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"An unhealthy rise in body weight has led some people to argue that every university student should be required to study sport, regardless of their degree. I completely disagree with this proposal. Making sport compulsory across all courses would distort the purpose of higher education and offer a blunt response to a complex health problem.","chinese":"體重不健康地上升，使一些人認為每一位大學生都應該被要求修讀體育，不論他們攻讀的是甚麼學位。 我完全不同意這項建議。 把體育變成所有課程的必修科，會扭曲高等教育的目的，並且以一種粗糙的方式回應一個複雜的健康問題。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that university programmes should be built around academic and professional priorities, not a one-size-fits-all activity requirement. A medical student, an engineering student and a literature student already face demanding lectures, projects, placements and deadlines. Adding an assessed sport module would take time away from the specialist training that their degrees are meant to provide. Universities are not health camps; their central role is to cultivate knowledge, judgement and employable expertise. If every course is forced to carry the same sports requirement, curricula become less flexible, and students may see exercise not as a healthy habit but as another box to tick.","chinese":"第一個原因是，大學課程應該圍繞學術和專業優先事項來設計，而不是圍繞一項一刀切的活動要求。 醫科,工程學生和文學學生本身已經要面對要求很高的講座、項目、實習和截止日期 加入一個需要評核的體育單元，會佔用他們本應用於專業訓練的時間，而這正是他們的學位應該提供的核心內容。 大學不是健康訓練營；它們的核心角色是培養知識、判斷力和具就業價值的專業能力。 如果每個課程都被迫加入相同的體育要求，課程設計就會變得較不靈活，而學生也可能不再把運動視為一種健康習慣，而只是另一項需要完成的任務。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"A second problem is that compulsory sport is unlikely to tackle the real causes of weight gain. Many students become overweight because of poor diet, stress, lack of sleep, long screen time and habits formed long before they enter university. Forcing them to play sport for a few hours a week may change their timetable, but it will not necessarily change their lifestyle. In fact, compulsion can backfire: students who dislike sport may participate reluctantly, do the bare minimum, or associate exercise with embarrassment and punishment. Universities would be wiser to provide accessible gyms, affordable healthy food, counselling, active travel schemes and optional fitness classes. These measures encourage students to build routines they can sustain.","chinese":"第二個問題是，強制體育不太可能處理體重增加的真正原因。 許多學生變得超重，是因為飲食不良、壓力、睡眠不足、長時間使用螢幕，以及早在進入大學之前已經形成的習慣。 強迫他們每週做幾小時運動，或許能改變他們的時間表，但未必能真正改變他們的生活方式。 事實上，強制措施可能適得其反：不喜歡運動的學生可能只是勉強參與、做最低限度的要求，甚至把運動和尷尬、懲罰聯繫起來。 大學更明智的做法，是提供容易使用的健身設施、價格可負擔的健康食物、輔導服務、鼓勵步行或騎車的出行計劃，以及自願參加的健身課程。 這些措施能鼓勵學生建立他們可以長期維持的日常習慣"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I do not agree that sport should be made a compulsory module on every degree course. Universities should support healthier living, but they should not sacrifice academic purpose or pretend that obesity can be solved by forcing all students into the same sporting mold.","chinese":"總結來說，我不同意體育應該被列為每一個學位課程的必修單元。 大學應該支持更健康的生活方式，但它們不應犧牲學術目的，也不應假裝只要把所有學生強行套入同一種運動模式，就可以解決肥胖問題。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"unhealthy rise in body weight","chinese":"體重不健康地上升"},{"english":"has led some people to argue that","chinese":"令一些人主張……"},{"english":"be required to","chinese":"被要求去……"},{"english":"regardless of","chinese":"不論；不管"},{"english":"this proposal","chinese":"這項建議"},{"english":"making sport compulsory","chinese":"將體育列為必修"},{"english":"across all courses","chinese":"在所有課程中"},{"english":"distort the purpose of","chinese":"扭曲……的目的"},{"english":"higher education","chinese":"高等教育"},{"english":"a blunt response to","chinese":"對……的粗糙回應"},{"english":"complex health problem","chinese":"複雜的健康問題"},{"english":"university programmes","chinese":"大學課程"},{"english":"be built around","chinese":"圍繞……而設計"},{"english":"academic and professional priorities","chinese":"學術和專業上的優先事項"},{"english":"one-size-fits-all activity requirement","chinese":"一刀切的活動要求"},{"english":"medical student","chinese":"醫科學生"},{"english":"engineering student","chinese":"工程學生"},{"english":"literature student","chinese":"文學學生"},{"english":"demanding lectures","chinese":"要求高的講課"},{"english":"placements and deadlines","chinese":"實習安排和限期"},{"english":"assessed sport module","chinese":"受評核的體育單元"},{"english":"take time away from","chinese":"佔用……的時間"},{"english":"specialist training","chinese":"專門訓練"},{"english":"be meant to provide","chinese":"旨在提供"},{"english":"health camps","chinese":"健康訓練營"},{"english":"central role","chinese":"核心角色"},{"english":"cultivate knowledge","chinese":"培養知識"},{"english":"judgement","chinese":"判斷力"},{"english":"employable expertise","chinese":"有助就業的專業知識"},{"english":"be forced to carry","chinese":"被迫加入"},{"english":"sports requirement","chinese":"體育要求"},{"english":"curricula become less flexible","chinese":"課程變得較不靈活"},{"english":"healthy habit","chinese":"健康習慣"},{"english":"another box to tick","chinese":"另一項要完成的指定任務"},{"english":"compulsory sport","chinese":"強制體育"},{"english":"be unlikely to","chinese":"不大可能"},{"english":"tackle the real causes of","chinese":"處理……的真正成因"},{"english":"weight gain","chinese":"體重增加"},{"english":"become overweight","chinese":"變得超重"},{"english":"poor diet","chinese":"不良飲食"},{"english":"lack of sleep","chinese":"睡眠不足"},{"english":"long screen time","chinese":"長時間使用螢幕"},{"english":"habits formed long before","chinese":"早已形成的習慣"},{"english":"enter university","chinese":"入讀大學"},{"english":"forcing them to","chinese":"強迫他們去……"},{"english":"for a few hours a week","chinese":"每星期幾小時"},{"english":"change their timetable","chinese":"改變他們的時間表"},{"english":"not necessarily","chinese":"不一定"},{"english":"in fact","chinese":"事實上"},{"english":"compulsion","chinese":"強制"},{"english":"backfire","chinese":"產生反效果"},{"english":"participate reluctantly","chinese":"勉強參與"},{"english":"do the bare minimum","chinese":"只做最低限度"},{"english":"associate exercise with","chinese":"將運動與……聯繫起來"},{"english":"embarrassment and punishment","chinese":"尷尬和懲罰"},{"english":"be wiser to provide","chinese":"更明智的是提供……"},{"english":"accessible gyms","chinese":"容易使用的健身室"},{"english":"affordable healthy food","chinese":"可負擔的健康食物"},{"english":"counselling","chinese":"輔導服務"},{"english":"active travel schemes","chinese":"主動出行計劃"},{"english":"optional fitness classes","chinese":"自選健身課程"},{"english":"encourage students to","chinese":"鼓勵學生去……"},{"english":"build routines","chinese":"建立日常習慣"},{"english":"sustain","chinese":"維持"},{"english":"be made a compulsory module","chinese":"被列為必修單元"},{"english":"degree course","chinese":"學位課程"},{"english":"support healthier living","chinese":"支持更健康的生活"},{"english":"sacrifice academic purpose","chinese":"犧牲學術目的"},{"english":"pretend that","chinese":"假裝……"},{"english":"obesity","chinese":"肥胖問題"},{"english":"be solved by","chinese":"透過……解決"},{"english":"force all students into","chinese":"強迫所有學生進入……"},{"english":"the same sporting mold","chinese":"同一套體育模式"}]},"model-essay-89-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-89-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:89","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-89-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q89","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Professional athletes occupy a powerful place in modern society. Because many children admire them not only for their skill but also for their image, I completely agree that they have a responsibility to behave as good role models at all times.","chinese":"職業運動員在現代社會中佔有非常有影響力的位置。 由於許多孩子崇拜他們，不只是因為他們的技術，也因為他們的形象，所以我完全同意他們有責任在任何時候都表現得像良好的榜樣。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that children often copy what famous sports figures do before they fully understand why they are doing it. A young fan may watch a footballer arguing with a referee, insulting an opponent, or boasting online, and see that behaviour as a sign of confidence rather than immaturity. Over time, this can normalise arrogance, aggression, and poor discipline. By contrast, when athletes show respect after defeat, train consistently, and accept responsibility for mistakes, they turn success into something children can actually learn from. Their behaviour becomes a silent lesson, and for impressionable minds that lesson can be louder than any classroom speech.","chinese":"第一個原因是，孩子往往會模仿著名體育人物的行為，甚至在他們還未完全明白為甚麼那樣做之前便已經開始模仿。 一位年輕球迷可能會看到一名足球員與裁判爭吵、侮辱對手，或在網上自誇，並把這些行為視為自信的表現，而不是不成熟。 長遠而言，這可能會使傲慢、攻擊性和缺乏紀律的行為變得正常化。 相比之下，當運動員在失敗後表現出尊重、持續訓練，並為錯誤承擔責任時，他們便能把成功轉化成孩子真正可以學習的東西。 他們的行為會成為一堂無聲的課，而對容易受影響的孩子來說，這堂課可能比任何課堂演講都更有力量。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important point is that professional sportspeople benefit directly from public admiration. Their fame, sponsorships, and high salaries are built partly on the loyalty of ordinary fans, including young supporters who buy shirts, watch matches, and follow them online. Since they enjoy these privileges, they should also accept the social duty that comes with them. This does not mean they must live like saints or pretend to be perfect. It simply means that, whether they are on the field, in interviews, online, or away from competition, they should show basic decency, restraint, and integrity. For example, an athlete who avoids drugs, treats teammates respectfully, and apologises sincerely after a mistake sends a far healthier message than one who hides behind talent as an excuse for bad conduct.","chinese":"另一個重要觀點是，職業運動員直接受益於公眾的仰慕。 他們的名氣、贊助和高薪，在一定程度上建立於普通球迷的忠誠之上，包括那些購買球衣、觀看比賽，並在網上追蹤他們的年輕支持者。 既然他們享有這些特權，他們也應該接受隨之而來的社會責任。 這並不代表他們必須像聖人一樣生活，或者假裝自己完美無缺。 這只是意味著，無論他們是在球場上、接受訪問時、在網上，還是離開比賽場合，他們都應該表現出基本的得體、克制和誠信。 例如，一位遠離毒品、尊重隊友，並在犯錯後真誠道歉的運動員，所傳達的信息遠比一位用天賦作為不良行為藉口的運動員健康得多。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I strongly agree that professional sportspeople should be good role models at all times. Their influence on children is too great to be treated casually, and their privileged position makes responsible behaviour not a burden, but part of the job.","chinese":"總結來說，我強烈同意職業運動員應該在任何時候都成為良好的榜樣。 他們對孩子的影響太大，不能被隨便看待，而他們所處的優越位置，也使負責任的行為不是一種負擔，而是這份工作的一部分。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"professional athletes","chinese":"職業運動員"},{"english":"occupy a powerful place","chinese":"佔有重要而有影響力的位置"},{"english":"modern society","chinese":"現代社會"},{"english":"admire them not only for","chinese":"欣賞他們不只是因為……"},{"english":"their skill","chinese":"他們的技術"},{"english":"their image","chinese":"他們的形象"},{"english":"have a responsibility to","chinese":"有責任去……"},{"english":"behave as","chinese":"表現得像……"},{"english":"good role models","chinese":"好榜樣"},{"english":"at all times","chinese":"在任何時候"},{"english":"famous sports figures","chinese":"著名體育人物"},{"english":"fully understand why","chinese":"完全明白為甚麼"},{"english":"a young fan","chinese":"年輕粉絲"},{"english":"arguing with a referee","chinese":"與裁判爭論"},{"english":"insulting an opponent","chinese":"侮辱對手"},{"english":"boasting online","chinese":"在網上吹噓"},{"english":"see that behaviour as","chinese":"將那種行為視為……"},{"english":"a sign of confidence","chinese":"自信的表現"},{"english":"rather than immaturity","chinese":"而不是不成熟"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨着時間過去"},{"english":"normalise arrogance","chinese":"令傲慢變得正常化"},{"english":"aggression","chinese":"攻擊性"},{"english":"poor discipline","chinese":"缺乏紀律"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"show respect after defeat","chinese":"失敗後表現尊重"},{"english":"train consistently","chinese":"持續訓練"},{"english":"accept responsibility for","chinese":"為……承擔責任"},{"english":"turn success into","chinese":"將成功轉化成……"},{"english":"learn from","chinese":"從……中學習"},{"english":"a silent lesson","chinese":"無聲的教訓"},{"english":"impressionable minds","chinese":"容易受影響的心智"},{"english":"louder than any classroom speech","chinese":"比任何課堂演講更有力"},{"english":"professional sportspeople","chinese":"職業運動員"},{"english":"benefit directly from","chinese":"直接受惠於……"},{"english":"public admiration","chinese":"公眾仰慕"},{"english":"fame","chinese":"名氣"},{"english":"sponsorships","chinese":"贊助"},{"english":"high salaries","chinese":"高薪"},{"english":"be built partly on","chinese":"部分建基於……"},{"english":"the loyalty of ordinary fans","chinese":"普通球迷的支持和忠誠"},{"english":"young supporters","chinese":"年輕支持者"},{"english":"watch matches","chinese":"觀看比賽"},{"english":"follow them online","chinese":"在網上追蹤他們"},{"english":"enjoy these privileges","chinese":"享有這些特權"},{"english":"accept the social duty","chinese":"承擔社會責任"},{"english":"comes with them","chinese":"隨之而來"},{"english":"live like saints","chinese":"像聖人般生活"},{"english":"pretend to be perfect","chinese":"假裝完美"},{"english":"on the field","chinese":"在球場上"},{"english":"in interviews","chinese":"在訪問中"},{"english":"away from competition","chinese":"離開比賽場合時"},{"english":"basic decency","chinese":"基本得體和正派"},{"english":"restraint","chinese":"克制"},{"english":"integrity","chinese":"誠信；正直"},{"english":"avoid drugs","chinese":"避免毒品"},{"english":"treat teammates respectfully","chinese":"尊重地對待隊友"},{"english":"apologise sincerely after","chinese":"在……之後真誠道歉"},{"english":"send a far healthier message","chinese":"傳達健康得多的信息"},{"english":"hide behind talent","chinese":"躲在天賦背後"},{"english":"as an excuse for","chinese":"作為……的藉口"},{"english":"bad conduct","chinese":"不良行為"},{"english":"strongly agree that","chinese":"強烈同意……"},{"english":"influence on children","chinese":"對兒童的影響"},{"english":"too great to be treated casually","chinese":"太大而不能隨便看待"},{"english":"privileged position","chinese":"優越地位"},{"english":"responsible behaviour","chinese":"負責任的行為"},{"english":"not a burden, but part of the job","chinese":"不是負擔，而是工作的一部分"}]},"model-essay-90-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-90-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:90","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-90-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q90","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Some people believe that combat sports such as boxing and martial arts should be removed from television and international sporting events because they involve physical aggression. I completely disagree with this view. Although these sports must be regulated carefully, banning them would be an excessive response that misunderstands both their nature and social value.","chinese":"有些人認為，拳擊和武術等搏擊運動應該從電視和國際體育賽事中移除，因為它們涉及身體上的攻擊性。 我完全不同意這個觀點。 雖然這些運動必須受到謹慎規管，但禁止它們會是一種過度反應，而且誤解了它們的本質和社會價值。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that organised combat sports are not the same as uncontrolled violence. In a street fight, there are no rules, medical checks, or clear limits. By contrast, professional boxing, judo, karate, and taekwondo are built around agreed rules, trained referees, protective procedures, and fair contests. This structure turns physical force into disciplined competition. When audiences watch a properly supervised match, they are not simply seeing people hurt one another; they are seeing athletes control fear, respect boundaries, and accept victory or defeat with restraint. For example, a young viewer who sees a referee stop a fight when one competitor is at risk can learn that strength must be governed by rules. Removing these sports from television would not remove aggression from society; it may simply push interest towards less regulated entertainment.","chinese":"第一個原因是，有組織的搏擊運動並不等同於失控的暴力。 在街頭打鬥中，沒有規則、醫療檢查，也沒有清晰的限制。 相比之下，職業拳擊、柔道、空手道和跆拳道都是建立在共同認可的規則、受訓裁判、保護程序和公平競賽之上的。 這種結構把身體力量轉化為有紀律的競技。 當觀眾觀看一場受到妥善監督的比賽時，他們看到的並不只是人們互相傷害；他們看到的是運動員控制恐懼、尊重界線，並以克制的態度接受勝利或失敗。 例如，一位年輕觀眾看到裁判在其中一名選手有危險時中止比賽，便可以學到力量必須受到規則約束。 把這些運動從電視上移除並不會消除社會中的攻擊性；這可能只是把人們的興趣推向較少受到規管的娛樂形式。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"A ban on international competition would also be unfair to athletes and damaging to sport as a whole. Many combat sports require years of sacrifice, technical training, and mental discipline. For competitors from less privileged backgrounds, these events can provide income, national pride, and personal dignity. Moreover, martial arts are often tied to cultural traditions in which respect, patience, and self-control are central values. If they were excluded from global tournaments, society would be treating committed athletes as if they were criminals rather than skilled professionals. A better solution is to improve safety standards, age guidance, and responsible broadcasting, not to erase the sports altogether.","chinese":"禁止它們出現在國際比賽中，也會對運動員不公平，並對整個體育界造成損害。 許多搏擊運動都需要多年犧牲、技術訓練和心理紀律。 對於來自較不優越背景的參賽者而言，這些賽事可以帶來收入、民族自豪感和個人尊嚴 此外，武術往往與文化傳統相連，而在這些傳統中，尊重、耐性和自我控制都是核心價值。 如果它們被排除在全球性賽事之外，社會便會把投入訓練的運動員視為罪犯，而不是技術純熟的專業人士。 更好的解決方法是改善安全標準、年齡指引和負責任的播放安排，而不是完全抹去這些運動。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I strongly disagree that combat sports should be banned from television or international competitions. With proper regulation, they can promote discipline, opportunity, and cultural respect far more effectively than a blanket ban ever could.","chinese":"總結來說，我強烈不同意搏擊運動應該被禁止出現在電視或國際比賽中。 在適當規管之下，它們能夠促進紀律、機會和文化尊重，而這遠比一刀切的禁令更有效"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"combat sports","chinese":"格鬥運動"},{"english":"boxing and martial arts","chinese":"拳擊和武術"},{"english":"be removed from","chinese":"從……移除"},{"english":"international sporting events","chinese":"國際體育賽事"},{"english":"involve physical aggression","chinese":"涉及肢體攻擊性"},{"english":"completely disagree with","chinese":"完全不同意……"},{"english":"be regulated carefully","chinese":"受到小心規管"},{"english":"banning them","chinese":"禁止它們"},{"english":"an excessive response","chinese":"過度反應"},{"english":"misunderstand both their nature and social value","chinese":"誤解它們的本質和社會價值"},{"english":"organised combat sports","chinese":"有組織的格鬥運動"},{"english":"uncontrolled violence","chinese":"不受控制的暴力"},{"english":"street fight","chinese":"街頭打鬥"},{"english":"medical checks","chinese":"醫療檢查"},{"english":"clear limits","chinese":"清晰界限"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"agreed rules","chinese":"約定好的規則"},{"english":"trained referees","chinese":"受過訓練的裁判"},{"english":"protective procedures","chinese":"保護程序"},{"english":"fair contests","chinese":"公平競賽"},{"english":"physical force","chinese":"身體力量"},{"english":"disciplined competition","chinese":"有紀律的競賽"},{"english":"properly supervised match","chinese":"受到適當監督的比賽"},{"english":"hurt one another","chinese":"互相傷害"},{"english":"control fear","chinese":"控制恐懼"},{"english":"respect boundaries","chinese":"尊重界限"},{"english":"accept victory or defeat with restraint","chinese":"克制地接受勝利或失敗"},{"english":"young viewer","chinese":"年輕觀眾"},{"english":"referee stop a fight","chinese":"裁判叫停比賽"},{"english":"at risk","chinese":"處於危險中"},{"english":"be governed by rules","chinese":"受規則約束"},{"english":"remove aggression from society","chinese":"消除社會中的攻擊性"},{"english":"push interest towards","chinese":"將興趣推向……"},{"english":"less regulated entertainment","chinese":"較少受規管的娛樂"},{"english":"a ban on international competition","chinese":"禁止國際比賽"},{"english":"damaging to sport as a whole","chinese":"對整個體育界有害"},{"english":"years of sacrifice","chinese":"多年的犧牲"},{"english":"technical training","chinese":"技術訓練"},{"english":"mental discipline","chinese":"心理紀律"},{"english":"competitors from less privileged backgrounds","chinese":"來自較弱勢背景的參賽者"},{"english":"provide income","chinese":"提供收入"},{"english":"national pride","chinese":"國家自豪感"},{"english":"personal dignity","chinese":"個人尊嚴"},{"english":"be tied to","chinese":"與……有關聯"},{"english":"cultural traditions","chinese":"文化傳統"},{"english":"central values","chinese":"核心價值"},{"english":"be excluded from","chinese":"被排除於……之外"},{"english":"global tournaments","chinese":"全球錦標賽"},{"english":"committed athletes","chinese":"投入的運動員"},{"english":"as if they were criminals","chinese":"好像他們是罪犯一樣"},{"english":"rather than skilled professionals","chinese":"而不是熟練的專業人士"},{"english":"improve safety standards","chinese":"改善安全標準"},{"english":"age guidance","chinese":"年齡指引"},{"english":"responsible broadcasting","chinese":"負責任的播放安排"},{"english":"erase the sports altogether","chinese":"完全抹走這些運動"},{"english":"proper regulation","chinese":"適當規管"},{"english":"promote discipline","chinese":"促進紀律"},{"english":"cultural respect","chinese":"文化尊重"},{"english":"blanket ban","chinese":"一刀切禁令"}]},"model-essay-91-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-91-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:91","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-91-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q91","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Technology has changed not only how people communicate, but also how much effort they put into real social contact. I agree that inventions such as mobile phones are making people less socially interactive, because they often weaken face-to-face communication and replace meaningful conversations with quick, shallow exchanges.","chinese":"科技不但改變了人們溝通的方式，也改變了人們願意投入多少努力進行真正的社交接觸 我同意手機等發明正在使人們變得較少進行社交互動，因為它們往往削弱面對面溝通，並以快速而膚淺的交流取代有意義的對話。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that mobile phones constantly compete for people's attention in social settings. A person may be physically present at a dinner table, in a classroom or at a workplace, but mentally pulled away by messages, notifications and online content. When this happens, conversation becomes fragmented: people listen with half an ear, respond mechanically, and miss the small expressions that make communication warm and personal. For example, it is now common to see friends sitting together in a café while each person silently scrolls through their phone. They are sharing the same space, but not really sharing the same moment. Over time, this habit can make direct interaction feel less natural and less valued.","chinese":"第一個原因是，手機在社交場合中不斷爭奪人們的注意力。 一個人可能身體上在飯桌旁、課室裡或工作場所中，但精神上卻被訊息、通知和網上內容拉走。 當這種情況發生時，對話便會變得零碎：人們只用半邊耳朵聆聽、機械式地回應，並錯過那些使溝通變得溫暖而個人的細微表情。 例如，現在很常見到朋友們一起坐在咖啡店裡，但每個人卻都靜靜地滑著自己的手機。 他們共享著同一個空間，但其實並沒有真正共享同一個時刻。 長遠而言，這種習慣會使直接互動變得較不自然，也較不被重視。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another important issue is that mobile phones encourage people to choose convenience over genuine engagement. Sending a short message or reacting with an emoji is easier than meeting someone, having a difficult discussion, or building a relationship through regular conversation. This is especially harmful for younger people, who need practice in reading body language, handling disagreement and speaking confidently with others. If most of their communication takes place behind a screen, they may become less comfortable with spontaneous face-to-face contact. In other words, the phone can become a social shortcut, but one that slowly removes the skills needed for deeper human connection.","chinese":"另一個重要問題是，手機鼓勵人們選擇方便，而不是真正投入地交流。 傳送一則短訊或用一個表情符號作出反應，比起與某人見面、進行困難的討論，或透過定期交談建立關係，都要容易得多。 這對年輕人尤其有害，因為他們需要練習理解肢體語言、處理分歧，以及自信地與他人交談。 如果他們大部分溝通都是在螢幕背後進行，他們便可能變得較不習慣自然即興的面對面接觸。 換言之，手機可以變成一種社交捷徑，但這種捷徑會慢慢削弱建立更深層人際連結所需要的能力。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I agree that modern technologies, particularly mobile phones, are reducing social interaction. They distract people from those around them and make low-effort digital contact feel like a substitute for real conversation. While they connect us quickly, they can also quietly make us less present, less attentive and less socially confident.","chinese":"總結來說，我同意現代科技，尤其是手機，正在減少人們的社交互動。 它們使人們分心，不再專注於身邊的人，並令低成本的數位接觸感覺像是真實對話的替代品。 雖然它們能讓我們快速連繫彼此，但它們也可能悄悄地使我們變得較不投入、較不專注，也較缺乏社交自信。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"not only how","chinese":"不只是如何……"},{"english":"how much effort","chinese":"多少努力"},{"english":"put into","chinese":"投入於……"},{"english":"real social contact","chinese":"真實社交接觸"},{"english":"inventions such as","chinese":"例如……的發明"},{"english":"mobile phones","chinese":"手提電話"},{"english":"less socially interactive","chinese":"較少社交互動"},{"english":"weaken face-to-face communication","chinese":"削弱面對面溝通"},{"english":"replace meaningful conversations with","chinese":"以……取代有意義的對話"},{"english":"meaningful conversations","chinese":"有意義的對話"},{"english":"quick, shallow exchanges","chinese":"快速而膚淺的交流"},{"english":"constantly compete for","chinese":"不斷爭奪……"},{"english":"people's attention","chinese":"人們的注意力"},{"english":"social settings","chinese":"社交場合"},{"english":"physically present","chinese":"身體在場"},{"english":"mentally pulled away","chinese":"心思被拉走"},{"english":"messages, notifications and online content","chinese":"訊息、通知和網上內容"},{"english":"conversation becomes fragmented","chinese":"對話變得零碎"},{"english":"listen with half an ear","chinese":"心不在焉地聽"},{"english":"respond mechanically","chinese":"機械式地回應"},{"english":"small expressions","chinese":"細微表情"},{"english":"warm and personal","chinese":"溫暖而有人情味"},{"english":"it is now common to","chinese":"現在很常見"},{"english":"sitting together","chinese":"坐在一起"},{"english":"silently scrolls through","chinese":"默默地滑動瀏覽"},{"english":"share the same space","chinese":"共享同一空間"},{"english":"share the same moment","chinese":"共享同一時刻"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨着時間過去"},{"english":"direct interaction","chinese":"直接互動"},{"english":"less natural and less valued","chinese":"較不自然，也較不被重視"},{"english":"another important issue","chinese":"另一個重要問題"},{"english":"choose convenience over","chinese":"選擇方便而非……"},{"english":"genuine engagement","chinese":"真誠投入；真正互動"},{"english":"sending a short message","chinese":"發一個短訊"},{"english":"reacting with an emoji","chinese":"用表情符號回應"},{"english":"having a difficult discussion","chinese":"進行艱難的討論"},{"english":"building a relationship through","chinese":"透過……建立關係"},{"english":"regular conversation","chinese":"恆常對話"},{"english":"especially harmful for","chinese":"對……特別有害"},{"english":"need practice in","chinese":"需要練習……"},{"english":"reading body language","chinese":"解讀肢體語言"},{"english":"handling disagreement","chinese":"處理分歧"},{"english":"speaking confidently with","chinese":"自信地與……交談"},{"english":"take place behind a screen","chinese":"在螢幕背後進行"},{"english":"less comfortable with","chinese":"對……較不自在"},{"english":"spontaneous face-to-face contact","chinese":"自然即興的面對面接觸"},{"english":"in other words","chinese":"換句話說"},{"english":"social shortcut","chinese":"社交捷徑"},{"english":"slowly removes","chinese":"慢慢奪走"},{"english":"skills needed for","chinese":"……所需的技能"},{"english":"deeper human connection","chinese":"更深入的人際連繫"},{"english":"modern technologies","chinese":"現代科技"},{"english":"particularly mobile phones","chinese":"尤其是手提電話"},{"english":"reduce social interaction","chinese":"減少社交互動"},{"english":"distract people from","chinese":"令某人分心，忽略……"},{"english":"those around them","chinese":"身邊的人"},{"english":"low-effort digital contact","chinese":"低投入的數碼接觸"},{"english":"feel like a substitute for","chinese":"感覺像是……的替代品"},{"english":"real conversation","chinese":"真實對話"},{"english":"connect us quickly","chinese":"令我們快速連繫"},{"english":"quietly make us less present","chinese":"悄悄令我們較不投入當下"},{"english":"less attentive","chinese":"較不專注"},{"english":"less socially confident","chinese":"社交上較不自信"}]},"model-essay-92-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-92-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:92","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-92-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q92","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Television and video games have become a normal part of childhood, and many children now spend hours each day in front of a screen. I completely agree that this pattern is harmful to their mental health because it weakens emotional control and replaces healthier forms of social and imaginative play.","chinese":"電視和電子遊戲已經成為童年的正常一部分，而許多孩子現在每天都會花數小時坐在螢幕前。 我完全同意這種模式對他們的心理健康有害，因為它會削弱情緒控制能力，並取代更健康的社交和想像性遊戲形式。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first major problem is that excessive screen entertainment can overstimulate the developing mind. Many programmes and games are built around fast movement, instant rewards, loud sounds, and constant visual change. When children are exposed to this for long periods, their minds become used to a high level of stimulation. As a result, ordinary activities such as reading, homework, or conversation may start to feel slow and unrewarding. For example, a child who spends every evening playing action games may become angry when asked to stop, not because he has a bad character, but because his brain has grown used to a quick cycle of challenge, reward, and excitement. Over time, this can erode patience, concentration, and emotional stability.","chinese":"第一個主要問題是，過度的螢幕娛樂可能會過度刺激正在發展中的大腦。 許多節目和遊戲都是圍繞快速動作、即時獎勵、響亮聲音和不斷變化的畫面而設計的。 當孩子長時間接觸這些內容時，他們的大腦便會習慣高強度的刺激。 結果是，閱讀、做功課或交談等普通活動可能開始顯得緩慢而缺乏回報感。 例如，一個每晚都玩動作遊戲的孩子，在被要求停止時可能會變得憤怒，這並不是因為他性格不好，而是因為他的大腦已經習慣了挑戰、獎勵和興奮快速循環的模式。 久而久之，這可能會侵蝕耐性、專注力和情緒穩定性。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that heavy screen use pushes aside the experiences that protect children’s mental health. Children need exercise, sleep, face-to-face friendships, and unstructured play in order to process feelings and build confidence. If television and gaming fill most of their free time, these protective routines are squeezed out. Instead of learning how to negotiate, share, lose gracefully, and solve conflict in the real world, children become spectators or players in an artificial one. A lonely child who goes straight home to video games every day may feel entertained, but not genuinely connected. This can deepen isolation and make social situations feel more difficult later.","chinese":"另一個原因是，大量使用螢幕會擠走那些能保護兒童心理健康的經歷。 兒童需要運動、睡眠、面對面的友誼，以及非結構化的遊戲，才能處理情緒並建立自信。 如果電視和遊戲佔據了大部分的空閒時間，這些具有保護作用的日常活動便會被擠走 孩子不是在真實世界中學習如何協商、分享、體面地面對失敗和解決衝突，而是變成了一個人工世界中的旁觀者或玩家。 一個孤獨的孩子如果每天放學後直接回家打電子遊戲，他可能會感到被娛樂了，但並沒有真正與他人建立聯繫。 這可能會加深孤立感，並使日後的社交場合變得更加困難。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely agree that excessive television viewing and video gaming are damaging to children’s mental health. They may look like harmless entertainment, but when they dominate a child’s daily life, they can weaken emotional control, reduce real-world interaction, and turn childhood into a much narrower experience.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意過度觀看電視和玩電子遊戲會損害兒童的心理健康。 它們看起來可能像是無害的娛樂，但當它們主導孩子的日常生活時，便可能削弱情緒控制能力、減少真實世界中的互動，並把童年變成一種狹窄得多的經歷"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"television and video games","chinese":"電視和電子遊戲"},{"english":"a normal part of childhood","chinese":"童年生活中正常的一部分"},{"english":"spend hours each day","chinese":"每天花數小時"},{"english":"in front of a screen","chinese":"在螢幕前"},{"english":"completely agree that","chinese":"完全同意……"},{"english":"this pattern","chinese":"這種模式"},{"english":"be harmful to","chinese":"對……有害"},{"english":"mental health","chinese":"精神健康"},{"english":"weaken emotional control","chinese":"削弱情緒控制"},{"english":"replace healthier forms of","chinese":"取代較健康形式的……"},{"english":"social and imaginative play","chinese":"社交和想像遊戲"},{"english":"the first major problem","chinese":"第一個主要問題"},{"english":"excessive screen entertainment","chinese":"過度的螢幕娛樂"},{"english":"overstimulate","chinese":"過度刺激"},{"english":"the developing mind","chinese":"發展中的心智"},{"english":"be built around","chinese":"圍繞……而設計"},{"english":"fast movement","chinese":"快速動作"},{"english":"instant rewards","chinese":"即時獎勵"},{"english":"loud sounds","chinese":"嘈雜聲音"},{"english":"constant visual change","chinese":"持續的視覺變化"},{"english":"be exposed to","chinese":"接觸到……"},{"english":"for long periods","chinese":"長時間"},{"english":"become used to","chinese":"習慣於……"},{"english":"a high level of stimulation","chinese":"高度刺激"},{"english":"as a result","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"ordinary activities","chinese":"日常活動"},{"english":"start to feel","chinese":"開始覺得"},{"english":"slow and unrewarding","chinese":"緩慢而沒有回報感"},{"english":"playing action games","chinese":"玩動作遊戲"},{"english":"be asked to stop","chinese":"被要求停止"},{"english":"not because","chinese":"並不是因為"},{"english":"bad character","chinese":"性格差"},{"english":"grow used to","chinese":"逐漸習慣"},{"english":"a quick cycle of","chinese":"……的快速循環"},{"english":"challenge, reward, and excitement","chinese":"挑戰、獎勵和興奮感"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨着時間過去"},{"english":"erode patience","chinese":"侵蝕耐性"},{"english":"concentration","chinese":"專注力"},{"english":"emotional stability","chinese":"情緒穩定"},{"english":"heavy screen use","chinese":"大量使用螢幕"},{"english":"push aside","chinese":"排擠；擠走"},{"english":"protect children's mental health","chinese":"保護兒童精神健康"},{"english":"face-to-face friendships","chinese":"面對面的友誼"},{"english":"unstructured play","chinese":"非結構化遊戲"},{"english":"in order to","chinese":"為了"},{"english":"process feelings","chinese":"處理情緒"},{"english":"build confidence","chinese":"建立自信"},{"english":"fill most of their free time","chinese":"佔據大部分空餘時間"},{"english":"protective routines","chinese":"具保護作用的日常習慣"},{"english":"be squeezed out","chinese":"被擠走"},{"english":"instead of learning how to","chinese":"而不是學習如何……"},{"english":"negotiate","chinese":"協商"},{"english":"lose gracefully","chinese":"有風度地接受失敗"},{"english":"solve conflict","chinese":"解決衝突"},{"english":"in the real world","chinese":"在現實世界中"},{"english":"spectators or players","chinese":"旁觀者或玩家"},{"english":"an artificial one","chinese":"人造的世界"},{"english":"go straight home to","chinese":"直接回家做……"},{"english":"feel entertained","chinese":"感到被娛樂"},{"english":"genuinely connected","chinese":"真正與人連繫"},{"english":"deepen isolation","chinese":"加深孤立感"},{"english":"social situations","chinese":"社交場合"},{"english":"excessive television viewing","chinese":"過度看電視"},{"english":"video gaming","chinese":"打機；玩電子遊戲"},{"english":"damaging to","chinese":"對……有損害"},{"english":"harmless entertainment","chinese":"無害的娛樂"},{"english":"dominate a child's daily life","chinese":"主導孩子的日常生活"},{"english":"real-world interaction","chinese":"現實世界中的互動"},{"english":"turn childhood into","chinese":"將童年變成……"},{"english":"a much narrower experience","chinese":"狹窄得多的經歷"}]},"model-essay-93-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-93-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:93","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-93-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q93","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Modern households are increasingly filled with smartphones, tablets and laptops, and it is no longer unusual for parents and children to retreat into separate digital worlds. I fully agree that this trend damages family relationships and weakens communication, because it reduces shared time and changes the way relatives respond to one another.","chinese":"現代家庭中越來越充滿智能手機、平板電腦和手提電腦，而父母和子女各自退回自己的數碼世界，已經不再罕見。 我完全同意這種趨勢會損害家庭關係並削弱溝通，因為它減少了家人共同相處的時間，也改變了親人之間回應彼此的方式。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that personal technology quietly replaces the ordinary moments through which family bonds are built. Family relationships do not usually grow through dramatic conversations; they are strengthened by repeated small interactions, such as eating together, chatting after school, or helping one another with daily tasks. When every family member has a screen in front of them, these simple moments are easily lost. For example, a child may watch videos during dinner while the parents answer work messages, so the meal becomes a silent routine rather than a chance to reconnect. Over time, this habit creates emotional distance, because people may live under the same roof but no longer share the same space in any meaningful sense.","chinese":"第一個原因是，個人科技會悄悄取代那些建立家庭關係的日常時刻。 家庭關係通常不是透過戲劇性的對話而成長；它們是透過反覆出現的小互動而被加強，例如一起吃飯、放學後聊天，或在日常事情上互相幫助。 當每個家庭成員面前都有一個螢幕時，這些簡單的時刻便很容易消失。 例如，一個孩子可能在晚餐時觀看影片，而父母則回覆工作訊息，因此這頓飯便變成一個沉默的例行程序，而不是重新建立聯繫的機會。 久而久之，這種習慣會造成情感距離，因為人們可能住在同一屋簷下，卻不再以任何真正有意義的方式共享同一個空間。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another serious problem is that modern devices encourage shallow and fragmented communication. Face-to-face conversation requires attention, eye contact and patience, whereas digital entertainment trains people to expect constant stimulation and quick replies. If a teenager is always wearing headphones or checking social media, parents may find it harder to understand their child’s worries, friendships or behaviour. Similarly, children may begin to see their parents as distant figures who are physically present but mentally elsewhere. This weakens trust, and without trust, small misunderstandings can easily grow into family tension.","chinese":"另一個嚴重問題是，現代設備會助長膚淺而零碎的溝通。 面對面的交談需要專注、眼神接觸和耐性，而數碼娛樂則訓練人們期待持續刺激和快速回覆。 如果一個青少年總是戴著耳機或查看社交媒體，父母可能會更難理解孩子的煩惱、友誼或行為。 同樣地，孩子也可能開始把父母看成是遙遠的人物：身體上在場，但精神上卻在別處。 這會削弱信任，而沒有信任，小小的誤解也很容易發展成家庭緊張。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely agree that individual ownership of modern technology can lead to a breakdown in family relationships and communication. By stealing everyday interaction and replacing deep conversation with distraction, personal devices can turn the family home from a shared living space into a collection of isolated private worlds.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意個人擁有現代科技產品可能導致家庭關係和溝通破裂。 透過偷走日常互動，並以分心取代深入交談，個人設備可以把家庭住所從一個共享的生活空間，變成一個個孤立私人世界的集合。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"modern households","chinese":"現代家庭"},{"english":"be increasingly filled with","chinese":"越來越充滿……"},{"english":"smartphones, tablets and laptops","chinese":"智能電話、平板電腦和手提電腦"},{"english":"it is no longer unusual for","chinese":"……已不再罕見"},{"english":"retreat into","chinese":"退到；躲進"},{"english":"separate digital worlds","chinese":"各自分離的數碼世界"},{"english":"fully agree that","chinese":"完全同意……"},{"english":"damage family relationships","chinese":"損害家庭關係"},{"english":"weaken communication","chinese":"削弱溝通"},{"english":"shared time","chinese":"共同相處的時間"},{"english":"respond to one another","chinese":"互相回應"},{"english":"personal technology","chinese":"個人科技"},{"english":"quietly replaces","chinese":"悄悄取代"},{"english":"ordinary moments","chinese":"平凡時刻"},{"english":"family bonds","chinese":"家庭感情；家庭聯繫"},{"english":"be built through","chinese":"透過……建立"},{"english":"dramatic conversations","chinese":"戲劇性的對話"},{"english":"be strengthened by","chinese":"透過……加強"},{"english":"repeated small interactions","chinese":"重複的小互動"},{"english":"eating together","chinese":"一起吃飯"},{"english":"chatting after school","chinese":"放學後聊天"},{"english":"daily tasks","chinese":"日常事務"},{"english":"a screen in front of them","chinese":"面前有一個螢幕"},{"english":"simple moments","chinese":"簡單時刻"},{"english":"be easily lost","chinese":"很容易失去"},{"english":"watch videos during dinner","chinese":"晚飯時看影片"},{"english":"answer work messages","chinese":"回覆工作訊息"},{"english":"silent routine","chinese":"沉默的例行公事"},{"english":"rather than a chance to reconnect","chinese":"而不是重新聯繫的機會"},{"english":"reconnect","chinese":"重新聯繫"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨着時間過去"},{"english":"emotional distance","chinese":"情感距離"},{"english":"live under the same roof","chinese":"住在同一屋簷下"},{"english":"share the same space","chinese":"共享同一空間"},{"english":"in any meaningful sense","chinese":"在任何有意義的層面上"},{"english":"another serious problem","chinese":"另一個嚴重問題"},{"english":"modern devices","chinese":"現代電子裝置"},{"english":"shallow and fragmented communication","chinese":"膚淺而零碎的溝通"},{"english":"face-to-face conversation","chinese":"面對面交談"},{"english":"eye contact","chinese":"眼神接觸"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；然而"},{"english":"digital entertainment","chinese":"數碼娛樂"},{"english":"constant stimulation","chinese":"持續刺激"},{"english":"quick replies","chinese":"快速回覆"},{"english":"check social media","chinese":"查看社交媒體"},{"english":"find it harder to","chinese":"發覺更難去……"},{"english":"friendships or behaviour","chinese":"友誼或行為"},{"english":"distant figures","chinese":"疏離的人物"},{"english":"physically present","chinese":"身體在場"},{"english":"mentally elsewhere","chinese":"心不在焉"},{"english":"weaken trust","chinese":"削弱信任"},{"english":"small misunderstandings","chinese":"小誤會"},{"english":"family tension","chinese":"家庭緊張關係"},{"english":"individual ownership of","chinese":"個人擁有……"},{"english":"lead to","chinese":"導致"},{"english":"a breakdown in","chinese":"……的破裂"},{"english":"stealing everyday interaction","chinese":"奪走日常互動"},{"english":"deep conversation","chinese":"深入交談"},{"english":"replace deep conversation with distraction","chinese":"以分心取代深入交談"},{"english":"personal devices","chinese":"個人電子裝置"},{"english":"shared living space","chinese":"共享生活空間"},{"english":"a collection of isolated private worlds","chinese":"一堆孤立的私人世界"}]},"model-essay-94-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-94-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:94","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-94-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q94","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Travel content has become an established part of modern entertainment, from television documentaries to short videos posted by influencers. Some argue that because people can now see foreign cities, landscapes and cultures on a screen, they will be less prepared to spend money on overseas trips. I completely disagree with this view, as digital travel content usually stimulates curiosity rather than replacing real travel, and the experience of being abroad cannot be reproduced through media.","chinese":"旅遊內容已成為現代娛樂中既定的一部分，從電視紀錄片到網紅發布的短影片皆是如此 有些人認為，由於人們現在可以透過螢幕看到外國城市、風景和文化，他們便會較不願意花錢到海外旅行。 我完全不同意這個觀點，因為數位旅遊內容通常會激發好奇心，而不是取代真正的旅行；而身處外國的體驗也無法透過媒體被複製。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that travel programmes and online videos often act as a gateway to tourism. When viewers see clear blue water in Greece, street food in Thailand or ancient streets in Italy, they are not simply ticking these places off a list; they are being invited to imagine themselves there. Social media, in particular, turns destinations into living postcards, making people feel that a place is reachable, desirable and worth saving for. For example, a person who watches several videos about Japan may become more interested in visiting temples, trying local food and experiencing the atmosphere in person. In this sense, online travel content is more likely to spark curiosity than extinguish it.","chinese":"第一個原因是，旅遊節目和網上影片往往會成為人們走向旅遊的入口。 當觀眾看到希臘清澈湛藍的海水、泰國的街頭美食，或意大利古老的街道時，他們並不只是把這些地方從清單上劃掉；他們其實是在被邀請去想像自己身處其中。 尤其是社交媒體，會把旅遊目的地變成生動的明信片，讓人們覺得一個地方是可到達的、令人嚮往的，也是值得為其儲錢的。 例如，一個看過幾段關於日本影片的人，可能會變得更想親身參觀寺廟、品嘗當地食物，並感受那裡的氣氛。 從這個角度來看，網上旅遊內容更有可能點燃好奇心，而不是熄滅它。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"More importantly, watching a destination is fundamentally different from living it. A screen can show the colour of a market or the shape of a mountain, but it cannot reproduce the smell of local food, the pressure of a crowded train, or the small conversations that make travel memorable. People do not pay for foreign trips merely to collect information; they pay for freedom, discovery and a break from their normal routines. Even a beautifully filmed documentary remains second-hand experience, whereas travelling abroad gives people direct contact with places and people that may change how they see the world.","chinese":"更重要的是，觀看一個目的地和親身經歷它，在本質上是完全不同的。 螢幕可以呈現市場的色彩或山脈的形狀，但它無法重現當地食物的氣味、擁擠列車中的壓迫感，或那些令旅行變得難忘的小小對話。 人們花錢到外國旅行，並不只是為了收集資訊；他們付錢是為了自由、探索，以及暫時脫離日常生活的規律。 即使是一部拍攝精美的紀錄片，也始終只是二手經驗；相比之下，出國旅行能讓人們直接接觸地方和人，而這些接觸可能會改變他們看待世界的方式。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I disagree that travel media will reduce people’s willingness to pay for international travel. It may entertain audiences at home, but it more often fuels their desire to go abroad and experience the world first-hand.","chinese":"總結來說，我不同意旅遊媒體會降低人們願意為國際旅行付費的意願。 它或許能娛樂留在家中的觀眾，但更多時候，它會激發他們出國並親身體驗世界的渴望"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"travel content","chinese":"旅遊內容"},{"english":"an established part of","chinese":"……中固定的一部分"},{"english":"modern entertainment","chinese":"現代娛樂"},{"english":"television documentaries","chinese":"電視紀錄片"},{"english":"short videos posted by influencers","chinese":"由網紅發布的短片"},{"english":"foreign cities, landscapes and cultures","chinese":"外國城市、風景和文化"},{"english":"on a screen","chinese":"在螢幕上"},{"english":"be less prepared to","chinese":"較不願意去……"},{"english":"spend money on","chinese":"花錢在……上"},{"english":"overseas trips","chinese":"海外旅行"},{"english":"completely disagree with","chinese":"完全不同意……"},{"english":"digital travel content","chinese":"數碼旅遊內容"},{"english":"stimulate curiosity","chinese":"激發好奇心"},{"english":"rather than replacing","chinese":"而不是取代……"},{"english":"real travel","chinese":"真實旅遊"},{"english":"the experience of being abroad","chinese":"身處外地的體驗"},{"english":"cannot be reproduced through","chinese":"無法透過……重現"},{"english":"through media","chinese":"透過媒體"},{"english":"travel programmes","chinese":"旅遊節目"},{"english":"online videos","chinese":"網上影片"},{"english":"act as a gateway to","chinese":"成為通往……的入口"},{"english":"tourism","chinese":"旅遊業；旅遊活動"},{"english":"clear blue water","chinese":"清澈蔚藍的海水"},{"english":"street food","chinese":"街頭小食"},{"english":"ancient streets","chinese":"古老街道"},{"english":"tick these places off a list","chinese":"將這些地方從清單上剔走"},{"english":"be invited to imagine","chinese":"被引導去想像"},{"english":"imagine themselves there","chinese":"想像自己身處當地"},{"english":"social media","chinese":"社交媒體"},{"english":"in particular","chinese":"尤其是"},{"english":"turn destinations into","chinese":"將目的地變成……"},{"english":"living postcards","chinese":"活生生的明信片"},{"english":"reachable, desirable and worth saving for","chinese":"可到達、令人嚮往，而且值得儲錢去"},{"english":"worth saving for","chinese":"值得為……儲錢"},{"english":"become more interested in","chinese":"對……變得更感興趣"},{"english":"visit temples","chinese":"參觀寺廟"},{"english":"try local food","chinese":"嘗試當地食物"},{"english":"experience the atmosphere in person","chinese":"親身感受氣氛"},{"english":"more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"spark curiosity","chinese":"激發好奇心"},{"english":"extinguish it","chinese":"將它熄滅；消除它"},{"english":"more importantly","chinese":"更重要的是"},{"english":"fundamentally different from","chinese":"與……有根本不同"},{"english":"living it","chinese":"親身體驗它"},{"english":"reproduce the smell of","chinese":"重現……的氣味"},{"english":"local food","chinese":"當地食物"},{"english":"the pressure of a crowded train","chinese":"擠迫火車帶來的壓迫感"},{"english":"small conversations","chinese":"小小的交談"},{"english":"make travel memorable","chinese":"令旅遊難忘"},{"english":"merely to collect information","chinese":"只是為了收集資料"},{"english":"a break from","chinese":"從……中暫時抽離"},{"english":"normal routines","chinese":"日常慣例"},{"english":"beautifully filmed documentary","chinese":"拍攝精美的紀錄片"},{"english":"second-hand experience","chinese":"間接體驗"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；然而"},{"english":"travelling abroad","chinese":"到外國旅行"},{"english":"direct contact with","chinese":"與……直接接觸"},{"english":"change how they see the world","chinese":"改變他們看世界的方式"},{"english":"travel media","chinese":"旅遊媒體"},{"english":"reduce people's willingness to","chinese":"降低人們去……的意願"},{"english":"pay for international travel","chinese":"為國際旅遊付費"},{"english":"entertain audiences at home","chinese":"娛樂在家中的觀眾"},{"english":"fuel their desire to","chinese":"加強他們想……的慾望"},{"english":"experience the world first-hand","chinese":"親身體驗世界"}]},"model-essay-95-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-95-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:95","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-95-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q95","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"International travel brings people into contact with customs that may be unfamiliar, uncomfortable, or even puzzling at first. Some people therefore argue that visitors should adjust to the local way of life rather than expect the host culture to accommodate them. I completely agree with this view, because adaptation is both a basic form of respect and the best route to genuine cultural understanding.","chinese":"國際旅行使人們接觸到一些起初可能陌生、令人不自在，甚至令人困惑的風俗習慣。 因此，有些人認為，旅客應該適應當地的生活方式，而不是期望東道主文化去遷就他們 我完全同意這觀點，因為適應既是一種基本的尊重，也是通往真正文化理解的最佳途徑。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that local customs often act as unwritten rules for peaceful social life. They are not merely decorative traditions; they show what a community regards as polite, modest, sacred, or offensive. If a tourist speaks loudly in a temple, ignores dress expectations at a religious site, or walks into a home with shoes on, the action may be innocent in intention but insulting in effect. By contrast, when visitors observe local etiquette, they show that residents are not just part of the scenery but people whose values deserve recognition. This reduces unnecessary tension and allows both sides to meet on more respectful ground.","chinese":"第一個原因是，當地習俗往往充當著和平社會生活中的不成文規則。 它們不只是裝飾性的傳統；它們顯示了一個社群認為甚麼是禮貌、謙遜、神聖，或冒犯的行為。 如果一名遊客在寺廟裡大聲說話、忽視宗教場所的衣著要求，或穿著鞋走進別人家中，這個行為在意圖上可能是無心的，但實際效果卻可能帶有冒犯性。 相比之下，當旅客遵守當地禮儀時，他們便表明當地居民並不只是風景的一部分，而是其價值觀值得被承認的人。 這能減少不必要的緊張，並讓雙方在更尊重彼此的基礎上交流。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Adapting to local practices also makes travel more meaningful. A person who carries their own habits everywhere may see another culture only through a glass wall: close enough to photograph, but not close enough to understand. Simple acts, such as learning local greetings, following dining customs, or joining community routines, can open doors to real conversation. Residents are more likely to explain traditions, share stories, and treat visitors as sincere guests rather than passing consumers. In this sense, adaptation does not narrow a traveller’s freedom; it expands the experience by turning observation into participation.","chinese":"適應當地習俗也會使旅行變得更有意義。 一個無論到哪裡都帶著自己習慣的人，可能只會隔著一道玻璃牆去看另一種文化：距離近得足以拍照，卻不足以真正理解。 一些簡單的行為，例如學習當地問候語、遵守用餐習俗，或參與社區日常活動，都能為真正的交流打開大門。 當地居民便更有可能解釋傳統、分享故事，並把旅客視為真誠的客人，而不是匆匆而過的消費者。 從這個意義上說，適應並不會限制旅客的自由；它反而透過把旁觀轉化為參與，擴展了旅行體驗。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully agree that people should adapt to local practices and customs when travelling in a different culture. Such adaptation protects social harmony and transforms travel from shallow sightseeing into respectful cultural exchange.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意人們在前往不同文化旅行時，應該適應當地的習俗和做法。 這種適應能維護社會和諧，並把旅行從表面的觀光轉化為尊重彼此的文化交流。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"international travel","chinese":"國際旅遊"},{"english":"bring people into contact with","chinese":"令人民接觸到……"},{"english":"customs","chinese":"習俗"},{"english":"unfamiliar, uncomfortable, or even puzzling","chinese":"陌生、不自在，甚至令人困惑"},{"english":"at first","chinese":"起初"},{"english":"adjust to","chinese":"適應……"},{"english":"the local way of life","chinese":"當地生活方式"},{"english":"rather than expect","chinese":"而不是期望……"},{"english":"host culture","chinese":"東道主文化；當地文化"},{"english":"accommodate them","chinese":"遷就他們"},{"english":"completely agree with","chinese":"完全同意……"},{"english":"adaptation","chinese":"適應"},{"english":"a basic form of respect","chinese":"基本的尊重形式"},{"english":"the best route to","chinese":"通往……的最佳途徑"},{"english":"genuine cultural understanding","chinese":"真正的文化理解"},{"english":"local customs","chinese":"當地習俗"},{"english":"act as","chinese":"充當；起……作用"},{"english":"unwritten rules","chinese":"不成文規則"},{"english":"peaceful social life","chinese":"和諧的社會生活"},{"english":"merely decorative traditions","chinese":"只是裝飾性的傳統"},{"english":"regard as","chinese":"視為……"},{"english":"polite, modest, sacred, or offensive","chinese":"有禮、端莊、神聖或冒犯"},{"english":"religious site","chinese":"宗教場所"},{"english":"innocent in intention","chinese":"動機上無惡意"},{"english":"insulting in effect","chinese":"效果上令人感到冒犯"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"observe local etiquette","chinese":"遵守當地禮儀"},{"english":"part of the scenery","chinese":"景色的一部分"},{"english":"deserve recognition","chinese":"值得被認可"},{"english":"reduce unnecessary tension","chinese":"減少不必要的緊張"},{"english":"both sides","chinese":"雙方"},{"english":"on more respectful ground","chinese":"在更互相尊重的基礎上"},{"english":"local practices","chinese":"當地做法；當地習慣"},{"english":"meaningful","chinese":"有意義的"},{"english":"carry their own habits everywhere","chinese":"到處都帶着自己的習慣"},{"english":"through a glass wall","chinese":"隔着玻璃牆"},{"english":"close enough to","chinese":"足夠接近去……"},{"english":"local greetings","chinese":"當地問候語"},{"english":"dining customs","chinese":"用餐習俗"},{"english":"community routines","chinese":"社區日常習慣"},{"english":"open doors to","chinese":"為……打開機會"},{"english":"real conversation","chinese":"真正的交流"},{"english":"be more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"explain traditions","chinese":"解釋傳統"},{"english":"share stories","chinese":"分享故事"},{"english":"sincere guests","chinese":"真誠的客人"},{"english":"rather than passing consumers","chinese":"而不是短暫停留的消費者"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"narrow a traveller's freedom","chinese":"限制旅客的自由"},{"english":"expand the experience","chinese":"擴闊體驗"},{"english":"turn observation into participation","chinese":"將旁觀變成參與"},{"english":"adapt to local practices and customs","chinese":"適應當地做法和習俗"},{"english":"travelling in a different culture","chinese":"在不同文化中旅遊"},{"english":"protect social harmony","chinese":"維護社會和諧"},{"english":"transform travel from","chinese":"將旅遊由……轉化為……"},{"english":"shallow sightseeing","chinese":"膚淺的觀光"},{"english":"respectful cultural exchange","chinese":"互相尊重的文化交流"}]},"model-essay-96-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-96-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:96","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-96-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q96","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Air pollution caused by aviation is a serious environmental concern, and some people believe that international flights should simply be made more expensive. I completely disagree. Raising ticket prices is a blunt and unfair measure, whereas reducing pollution at its source would be far more effective.","chinese":"航空所造成的空氣污染是一個嚴重的環境問題，而有些人認為國際航班應該直接變得更昂貴。 我完全不同意。 提高機票價格是一種粗暴而不公平的措施，而從源頭減少污染會有效得多。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first problem is that higher airfares would mainly restrict ordinary passengers rather than solve the environmental problem itself. Families visiting relatives abroad, students studying overseas, and migrant workers returning home would be hit hard, while wealthy travellers and large companies could still afford to fly as often as before. In other words, the policy would place the heaviest burden on those with thinner wallets, but it would not necessarily change the behaviour of the biggest users of air travel. A business executive might still take regular long-haul flights, while a family might have to give up one important trip after years of saving. This reduces access, not pollution, in a fair or reliable way.","chinese":"第一個問題是，更高的機票價格主要會限制普通乘客，而不是解決環境問題本身。 探望海外親人的家庭、在外國讀書的學生，以及回鄉的外籍勞工會受到嚴重打擊，而富裕旅客和大型公司仍然能夠像以前一樣經常乘搭飛機。 換句話說，這項政策會把最沉重的負擔加在經濟能力較弱的人身上，但它未必能改變最大航空使用者的行為。 一位企業高層可能仍然會定期乘搭長途航班，而一個家庭則可能在多年儲蓄後，仍不得不放棄一次重要的旅程。 這只是限制了人們的出行機會，而不是以公平或可靠的方式減少污染。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"A better approach is to make each flight cleaner and to replace unnecessary flights with practical alternatives. Governments should require airlines to use cleaner fuels, newer aircraft, stricter emission standards, and more efficient routes. If planes burn less fuel, avoid wasteful delays, and operate with modern technology, pollution falls on every journey, not only on the journeys that poorer people can no longer afford. At the same time, rail links where practical and wider acceptance of online business meetings can reduce avoidable flights without treating travel as a luxury for the rich. This kind of policy attacks the engine of the problem rather than merely raising the gate price.","chinese":"更好的方法是讓每一班航班變得更清潔，並用實際可行的替代方式取代不必要的飛行。 政府應該要求航空公司使用更清潔的燃料、更新型的飛機、更嚴格的排放標準，以及更高效率的航線。 如果飛機燃燒更少燃料、避免浪費性的延誤，並使用現代科技運作，那麼每一次旅程的污染都會下降，而不只是減少那些較貧窮人士再也負擔不起的旅程。 同時，在可行的地方發展鐵路連接，以及更廣泛地接受線上商務會議，都可以減少可避免的航班，而不會把旅行變成富人的奢侈品。 這類政策針對的是問題的核心，而不是僅僅提高進門的價格。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I do not agree that increasing the cost of international flights is the best way to reduce air pollution. It may discourage some travel, but it is socially unfair and environmentally incomplete. Cleaner aviation and better alternatives would produce a deeper and more balanced solution.","chinese":"總結來說，我不同意提高國際航班成本是減少空氣污染的最佳方法。 它也許會阻止部分出行，但在社會層面上並不公平，在環境層面上也並不完整。 更清潔的航空技術和更好的替代方案，才會帶來更深入、更平衡的解決方法。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"air pollution caused by","chinese":"由……造成的空氣污染"},{"english":"aviation","chinese":"航空業"},{"english":"environmental concern","chinese":"環境憂慮"},{"english":"international flights","chinese":"國際航班"},{"english":"be made more expensive","chinese":"被變得更昂貴"},{"english":"raising ticket prices","chinese":"提高票價"},{"english":"a blunt and unfair measure","chinese":"粗糙而不公平的措施"},{"english":"whereas","chinese":"而；然而"},{"english":"reduce pollution at its source","chinese":"從源頭減少污染"},{"english":"far more effective","chinese":"有效得多"},{"english":"higher airfares","chinese":"較高機票價格"},{"english":"restrict ordinary passengers","chinese":"限制普通乘客"},{"english":"rather than solve","chinese":"而不是解決"},{"english":"the environmental problem itself","chinese":"環境問題本身"},{"english":"visiting relatives abroad","chinese":"探望海外親人"},{"english":"studying overseas","chinese":"海外升學"},{"english":"migrant workers returning home","chinese":"回鄉的外來工人"},{"english":"be hit hard","chinese":"受到沉重打擊"},{"english":"wealthy travellers","chinese":"富裕旅客"},{"english":"large companies","chinese":"大公司"},{"english":"afford to fly","chinese":"負擔得起乘飛機"},{"english":"as often as before","chinese":"像以前一樣頻密"},{"english":"in other words","chinese":"換句話說"},{"english":"place the heaviest burden on","chinese":"將最沉重負擔加於……"},{"english":"those with thinner wallets","chinese":"經濟能力較弱的人"},{"english":"not necessarily","chinese":"不一定"},{"english":"change the behaviour of","chinese":"改變……的行為"},{"english":"the biggest users of ……","chinese":"的最大使用者"},{"english":"business executive","chinese":"商業行政人員"},{"english":"regular long-haul flights","chinese":"定期長途航班"},{"english":"give up","chinese":"放棄"},{"english":"years of saving","chinese":"多年儲蓄"},{"english":"reduce access","chinese":"減少使用機會"},{"english":"in a fair or reliable way","chinese":"以公平或可靠的方式"},{"english":"a better approach","chinese":"更好的方法"},{"english":"replace unnecessary flights with","chinese":"以……取代不必要的航班"},{"english":"practical alternatives","chinese":"實際可行的替代選擇"},{"english":"require airlines to","chinese":"要求航空公司去……"},{"english":"cleaner fuels","chinese":"較清潔的燃料"},{"english":"newer aircraft","chinese":"較新的飛機"},{"english":"stricter emission standards","chinese":"更嚴格的排放標準"},{"english":"more efficient routes","chinese":"更高效的航線"},{"english":"burn less fuel","chinese":"燃燒較少燃料"},{"english":"avoid wasteful delays","chinese":"避免浪費性的延誤"},{"english":"operate with modern technology","chinese":"以現代技術運作"},{"english":"pollution falls","chinese":"污染下降"},{"english":"on every journey","chinese":"在每次旅程中"},{"english":"can no longer afford","chinese":"不再負擔得起"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"rail links","chinese":"鐵路連接"},{"english":"where practical","chinese":"在可行的地方"},{"english":"wider acceptance of","chinese":"對……更廣泛接受"},{"english":"online business meetings","chinese":"網上商務會議"},{"english":"avoidable flights","chinese":"可避免的航班"},{"english":"treat travel as a luxury for the rich","chinese":"將旅遊視為富人的奢侈品"},{"english":"attack the engine of the problem","chinese":"針對問題的核心"},{"english":"merely raising","chinese":"只是提高……"},{"english":"the gate price","chinese":"入場門檻價格"},{"english":"increasing the cost of","chinese":"增加……的成本"},{"english":"discourage some travel","chinese":"阻止部分出行"},{"english":"socially unfair","chinese":"社會上不公平"},{"english":"environmentally incomplete","chinese":"環保上不完整"},{"english":"cleaner aviation","chinese":"更清潔的航空業"},{"english":"better alternatives","chinese":"更好的替代選擇"},{"english":"a deeper and more balanced solution","chinese":"更深入而更平衡的解決方案"}]},"model-essay-97-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-97-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:97","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-97-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q97","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Traffic congestion is a serious problem in modern life. Some argue that people should be encouraged to live in cities rather than in suburbs or rural areas to solve transport problems. I completely agree, because compact urban living makes public transport more efficient and reduces long daily journeys.","chinese":"交通擠塞是現代生活中的一個嚴重問題。 有人認為，為了解決交通問題，應該鼓勵人們居住在城市，而不是住在郊區或鄉村地區 我完全同意，因為緊湊的城市生活能使公共交通更有效率，並減少漫長的日常出行。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason is that cities can support public transport in a way that low-density areas usually cannot. When many people live close together, governments can justify investing in underground railways, buses, tram lines, and cycle lanes, since these services will be used by large numbers of passengers each day. By contrast, when homes are spread across distant suburbs or villages, public transport becomes expensive to run and inconvenient to use. Residents then often have no realistic choice but to drive. For example, an office worker who lives near a metro station can travel to work without adding another car to the road, whereas someone in a remote suburb may need to drive even for basic errands. Urban concentration therefore turns transport from a private burden into a shared public service.","chinese":"最有力的原因是，城市能夠支撐公共交通，而低密度地區通常做不到這一點。 當很多人住得很接近時，政府便有理由投資地下鐵路、巴士、電車路線和單車徑，因為這些服務每天都會被大量乘客使用。 相比之下，當住宅分散在遙遠的郊區或村莊時，公共交通的營運成本會變得很高，而且使用起來也不方便。 居民於是往往沒有實際選擇，只能開車。 例如，一位住在地鐵站附近的上班族可以不增加路面車輛便前往工作地點；然而，住在偏遠郊區的人即使只是處理基本雜務，也可能需要開車。 因此，城市集中化能把交通從個人的負擔，轉化為共享的公共服務。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that city life shortens the distance between people and the places they need to reach. In well-planned cities, workplaces, schools, hospitals, shops, and entertainment venues are often within walking, cycling, or short-transit distance. This matters because traffic problems are not caused simply by vehicles; they are caused by unnecessary vehicle journeys. If people can walk to a supermarket, cycle to a park, or take a short bus ride to a clinic, fewer cars will be needed. Over time, this reduces congestion, fuel use, parking pressure, and pollution. Rural living may offer space and quiet, but it often turns every small task into a car trip.","chinese":"另一個原因是，城市生活縮短了人們與他們需要前往的地方之間的距離。 在規劃良好的城市中，工作場所、學校、醫院、商店和娛樂場所通常都在步行、騎單車或短途公共交通可達的範圍內。 這一點很重要，因為交通問題並不只是由車輛造成的；它們是由不必要的車程造成的。 如果人們可以步行去超市、騎單車去公園，或乘搭短途巴士去診所，需要使用的汽車便會減少。 長遠而言，這會減少交通擠塞、燃料使用、泊車壓力和污染。 鄉村生活或許能提供空間與寧靜，但它往往會把每一件小事都變成一次汽車出行。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully agree that people should be encouraged to live in cities in order to ease transport problems. Dense urban living makes public transport viable and daily travel shorter, which directly tackles the roots of congestion.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意人們應該被鼓勵居住在城市，以緩解交通問題。 高密度的城市生活使公共交通變得可行，並縮短日常出行，而這正正直接處理了交通擠塞的根源。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"traffic congestion","chinese":"交通擠塞"},{"english":"a serious problem","chinese":"嚴重問題"},{"english":"modern life","chinese":"現代生活"},{"english":"be encouraged to","chinese":"被鼓勵去……"},{"english":"rather than in","chinese":"而不是在……"},{"english":"suburbs or rural areas","chinese":"郊區或鄉郊地區"},{"english":"solve transport problems","chinese":"解決交通問題"},{"english":"compact urban living","chinese":"緊湊的城市生活"},{"english":"public transport","chinese":"公共交通"},{"english":"reduce long daily journeys","chinese":"減少漫長的日常通勤"},{"english":"the strongest reason","chinese":"最有力的原因"},{"english":"support public transport","chinese":"支持公共交通發展"},{"english":"in a way that","chinese":"以……的方式"},{"english":"low-density areas","chinese":"低密度地區"},{"english":"live close together","chinese":"住得很近"},{"english":"justify investing in","chinese":"有理由投資於……"},{"english":"underground railways","chinese":"地下鐵路"},{"english":"tram lines","chinese":"電車路線"},{"english":"cycle lanes","chinese":"單車徑"},{"english":"large numbers of passengers","chinese":"大量乘客"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"be spread across","chinese":"分散在……"},{"english":"distant suburbs","chinese":"遙遠的郊區"},{"english":"expensive to run","chinese":"營運成本高"},{"english":"inconvenient to use","chinese":"使用不方便"},{"english":"have no realistic choice but to","chinese":"除了……之外沒有現實選擇"},{"english":"office worker","chinese":"上班族"},{"english":"metro station","chinese":"地鐵站"},{"english":"travel to work","chinese":"上班；通勤"},{"english":"add another car to the road","chinese":"增加路面車輛"},{"english":"remote suburb","chinese":"偏遠郊區"},{"english":"basic errands","chinese":"基本日常雜務"},{"english":"urban concentration","chinese":"城市集中發展"},{"english":"turn transport from","chinese":"將交通由……轉變為……"},{"english":"private burden","chinese":"個人負擔"},{"english":"shared public service","chinese":"共享公共服務"},{"english":"city life","chinese":"城市生活"},{"english":"shorten the distance between","chinese":"縮短……之間的距離"},{"english":"well-planned cities","chinese":"規劃良好的城市"},{"english":"entertainment venues","chinese":"娛樂場所"},{"english":"within walking distance","chinese":"在步行距離內"},{"english":"cycling distance","chinese":"在踩單車可到的距離內"},{"english":"short-transit distance","chinese":"短途公共交通可到的距離內"},{"english":"matters because","chinese":"這很重要，因為……"},{"english":"unnecessary vehicle journeys","chinese":"不必要的車程"},{"english":"take a short bus ride to","chinese":"乘短途巴士去……"},{"english":"fewer cars will be needed","chinese":"所需車輛會較少"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨着時間過去"},{"english":"fuel use","chinese":"燃油使用"},{"english":"parking pressure","chinese":"泊車壓力"},{"english":"rural living","chinese":"鄉郊生活"},{"english":"offer space and quiet","chinese":"提供空間和寧靜"},{"english":"turn every small task into","chinese":"將每件小事變成……"},{"english":"car trip","chinese":"駕車出行"},{"english":"in order to ease","chinese":"為了紓緩"},{"english":"dense urban living","chinese":"高密度城市生活"},{"english":"public transport viable","chinese":"令公共交通具可行性"},{"english":"daily travel","chinese":"日常出行"},{"english":"directly tackles","chinese":"直接處理"},{"english":"the roots of congestion","chinese":"交通擠塞的根源"}]},"model-essay-98-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-98-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:98","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-98-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q98","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Air travel has become one of the most visible symbols of modern convenience, but its environmental cost is increasingly difficult to ignore. Some argue that governments should raise taxes on flights in order to reduce the number of passengers. I disagree that this would solve the problem, because it would affect travellers unevenly while doing too little to change the aviation system itself.","chinese":"航空旅行已成為現代便利生活中最明顯的象徵之一，但它所帶來的環境代價也越來越難以被忽視。 有些人認為，政府應該提高航班稅，以減少乘客數量。 我不同意這能解決問題，因為它會不公平地影響不同旅客，同時對航空系統本身的改變太少。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"To begin with, a higher flight tax would be a blunt and unfair tool. Many people do not fly for pleasure; they travel for work, education, medical treatment or family responsibilities. If tickets became more expensive, these passengers would simply pay more rather than stop flying, especially when there is no realistic alternative. At the same time, wealthier tourists would barely feel the increase, so the policy would punish ordinary travellers more than frequent luxury passengers. A measure that mainly changes who can afford to fly, rather than how aviation operates, cannot be considered a genuine environmental solution.","chinese":"首先，更高的航班稅會是一種粗糙而不公平的工具。 許多人乘搭飛機並不是為了享樂；他們是為了工作、教育、醫療治療或家庭責任而出行 如果機票變得更昂貴，這些乘客只會支付更多費用，而不是停止飛行，尤其是在沒有現實可行替代方案的情況下。 與此同時，較富裕的遊客幾乎不會感受到加價，因此這項政策對普通旅客的懲罰會比對經常乘搭豪華航班的乘客更大。 一項主要改變誰負擔得起飛行，而不是改變航空業如何運作的措施，不能被視為真正的環境解決方案。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"The deeper problem is that aircraft still rely heavily on polluting fuel, and taxation alone does not automatically fix that. Airlines may pass the cost to customers without improving their fleets, while governments may spend the extra revenue on unrelated areas. A more effective approach would be to invest directly in cleaner aircraft technology, sustainable fuels and high-speed rail routes for shorter journeys. For example, if people could take an affordable train between major cities, many would choose it without feeling that they had been forced off planes. This would reduce emissions in a practical and lasting way.","chinese":"更深層的問題是，飛機仍然嚴重依賴污染性燃料，而單靠徵稅並不會自動解決這一點。 航空公司可能會把成本轉嫁給顧客，而不改善機隊；同時，政府也可能把額外收入花在不相關的領域。 更有效的方法會是直接投資於更清潔的飛機技術、可持續燃料，以及適合短途旅程的高速鐵路路線。 例如，如果人們可以在主要城市之間乘搭價格合理的火車，許多人會選擇這種方式，而不會覺得自己是被迫放棄飛機。 這將以實際而持久的方式減少排放。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, increasing tax on flights would not solve the environmental damage caused by aviation. Instead of using price as a gatekeeper, governments should focus on cleaner transport systems and realistic alternatives that reduce the need to fly.","chinese":"總結來說，提高航班稅並不能解決航空業所造成的環境破壞。 政府不應把價格作為限制人們出行的門檻，而應該專注於更清潔的交通系統，以及能減少飛行需求的現實替代方案。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"air travel","chinese":"航空旅遊；乘搭飛機"},{"english":"one of the most visible symbols of ……","chinese":"最明顯的象徵之一"},{"english":"modern convenience","chinese":"現代便利"},{"english":"environmental cost","chinese":"環境代價"},{"english":"increasingly difficult to ignore","chinese":"越來越難以忽視"},{"english":"raise taxes on flights","chinese":"提高航班稅"},{"english":"in order to reduce","chinese":"為了減少"},{"english":"the number of passengers","chinese":"乘客數量"},{"english":"solve the problem","chinese":"解決問題"},{"english":"affect travellers unevenly","chinese":"對旅客造成不均等影響"},{"english":"do too little to","chinese":"對……作用太小"},{"english":"the aviation system itself","chinese":"航空系統本身"},{"english":"to begin with","chinese":"首先"},{"english":"flight tax","chinese":"航班稅"},{"english":"a blunt and unfair tool","chinese":"粗糙而不公平的工具"},{"english":"fly for pleasure","chinese":"為了娛樂而乘飛機"},{"english":"medical treatment","chinese":"醫療治療"},{"english":"family responsibilities","chinese":"家庭責任"},{"english":"simply pay more rather than","chinese":"只是支付更多，而不是……"},{"english":"no realistic alternative","chinese":"沒有現實可行的替代選擇"},{"english":"at the same time","chinese":"同時"},{"english":"wealthier tourists","chinese":"較富裕的遊客"},{"english":"barely feel the increase","chinese":"幾乎感受不到加幅"},{"english":"punish ordinary travellers","chinese":"懲罰普通旅客"},{"english":"frequent luxury passengers","chinese":"經常奢華旅遊的乘客"},{"english":"a measure that","chinese":"一項……的措施"},{"english":"afford to fly","chinese":"負擔得起乘飛機"},{"english":"rather than how","chinese":"而不是如何……"},{"english":"aviation operates","chinese":"航空業運作"},{"english":"be considered","chinese":"被視為"},{"english":"genuine environmental solution","chinese":"真正的環保解決方案"},{"english":"the deeper problem","chinese":"更深層的問題"},{"english":"rely heavily on","chinese":"嚴重依賴"},{"english":"polluting fuel","chinese":"造成污染的燃料"},{"english":"taxation alone","chinese":"單靠徵稅"},{"english":"automatically fix","chinese":"自動解決"},{"english":"pass the cost to customers","chinese":"將成本轉嫁給顧客"},{"english":"improve their fleets","chinese":"改善機隊"},{"english":"extra revenue","chinese":"額外收入"},{"english":"unrelated areas","chinese":"無關範疇"},{"english":"a more effective approach","chinese":"更有效的方法"},{"english":"invest directly in","chinese":"直接投資於……"},{"english":"cleaner aircraft technology","chinese":"更清潔的飛機技術"},{"english":"sustainable fuels","chinese":"可持續燃料"},{"english":"high-speed rail routes","chinese":"高速鐵路路線"},{"english":"shorter journeys","chinese":"較短途旅程"},{"english":"take an affordable train","chinese":"乘搭可負擔的火車"},{"english":"major cities","chinese":"主要城市"},{"english":"without feeling that","chinese":"而不覺得……"},{"english":"be forced off planes","chinese":"被迫不乘飛機"},{"english":"reduce emissions","chinese":"減少排放"},{"english":"in a practical and lasting way","chinese":"以實際而持久的方式"},{"english":"increasing tax on flights","chinese":"增加航班稅"},{"english":"environmental damage caused by","chinese":"由……造成的環境破壞"},{"english":"instead of using","chinese":"而不是使用……"},{"english":"price as a gatekeeper","chinese":"以價格作為門檻"},{"english":"cleaner transport systems","chinese":"更清潔的交通系統"},{"english":"realistic alternatives","chinese":"現實可行的替代選擇"},{"english":"reduce the need to fly","chinese":"減少乘飛機的需要"}]},"model-essay-99-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-99-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:99","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-99-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q99","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"Poor infrastructure is often one of the clearest signs that a country is struggling to develop. Some argue that foreign aid should therefore deal with this issue before anything else. I completely agree, because strong infrastructure is the foundation on which education, healthcare, trade, and government services can properly function.","chinese":"貧乏的基礎建設往往是一個國家正努力發展時最明顯的跡象之一。 因此，有些人認為外國援助應該先處理這個問題，再處理其他事情。 我完全同意，因為完善的基礎建設是教育、醫療、貿易和政府服務能夠正常運作的根基。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that infrastructure directly affects almost every part of national development. Without reliable roads, electricity, clean water, and communication networks, even well-intentioned aid projects may fail to reach the people who need them most. For example, a rural school may receive books and trained teachers, but if there are no safe roads or stable electricity, students may be unable to attend regularly and lessons may remain extremely limited. Similarly, hospitals cannot operate effectively if medicines cannot be transported, equipment cannot be powered, and patients cannot reach treatment in time. In this sense, infrastructure is not merely one development problem among many; it is the bridge that allows other forms of aid to work.","chinese":"第一個原因是，基礎建設會直接影響國家發展的幾乎每一個部分。 如果沒有可靠的道路、電力、清潔食水和通訊網絡，即使是出於善意的援助項目，也可能無法到達最需要幫助的人手中。 例如，一所鄉村學校可能收到書本，也可能有受過訓練的教師，但如果沒有安全的道路或穩定的電力，學生可能無法定期上學，課堂也可能仍然受到極大限制。 同樣地，如果藥物無法運送、設備無法供電，而病人又不能及時獲得治療，醫院便無法有效運作。 從這個意義上說，基礎建設並不只是眾多發展問題中的其中一個；它是一座橋樑，讓其他形式的援助能夠發揮作用。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that better infrastructure helps under-developed countries become less dependent on foreign support in the long run. When roads, ports, power systems, and digital networks improve, local businesses can grow, farmers can bring goods to wider markets, and workers can access more employment opportunities. This creates a stronger domestic economy, which is far more sustainable than repeated short-term donations. For instance, building a dependable transport system may allow small producers to sell their products nationally rather than only within isolated villages. As income rises, the government can collect more tax revenue and reinvest it in public services. Foreign aid, therefore, should first strengthen the physical backbone of the country so that future progress can stand on its own feet.","chinese":"另一個原因是，從長遠來看，更好的基礎建設能幫助欠發達國家減少對外國支援的依賴。 當道路、港口、電力系統和數碼網絡得到改善時，本地企業便能成長，農民能把商品帶到更廣闊的市場，工人也能獲得更多就業機會。 這會創造一個更強大的國內經濟，而這比反覆接受短期捐助要可持續得多。 例如，建立一個可靠的交通系統，可能讓小型生產者把產品銷售到全國，而不是只能在偏遠村落內出售。 隨著收入上升，政府可以徵收更多稅收，並將其重新投資於公共服務。 因此，外國援助應該首先強化一個國家的實體骨幹，使未來的進步能夠靠自身力量站穩腳步。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I fully agree that poor infrastructure should be the first issue addressed by foreign aid. Without it, other development efforts are likely to be slow, fragile, and inefficient; with it, a country gains the basic platform it needs to modernise independently.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意，貧乏的基礎建設應該是外國援助首先處理的問題。 沒有它，其他發展努力很可能會緩慢、脆弱而低效；有了它，一個國家便能獲得獨立現代化所需要的基本平台。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"poor infrastructure","chinese":"落後的基礎設施"},{"english":"one of the clearest signs","chinese":"最明顯跡象之一"},{"english":"struggle to develop","chinese":"難以發展"},{"english":"foreign aid","chinese":"外國援助"},{"english":"deal with this issue","chinese":"處理這個問題"},{"english":"before anything else","chinese":"優先於其他事情"},{"english":"the foundation on which ……","chinese":"的基礎"},{"english":"properly function","chinese":"正常運作"},{"english":"national development","chinese":"國家發展"},{"english":"reliable roads","chinese":"可靠的道路"},{"english":"clean water","chinese":"潔淨食水"},{"english":"communication networks","chinese":"通訊網絡"},{"english":"well-intentioned aid projects","chinese":"出於好意的援助項目"},{"english":"fail to reach","chinese":"未能到達；未能幫助"},{"english":"need them most","chinese":"最需要它們"},{"english":"rural school","chinese":"鄉村學校"},{"english":"trained teachers","chinese":"受過培訓的教師"},{"english":"safe roads","chinese":"安全道路"},{"english":"stable electricity","chinese":"穩定電力"},{"english":"attend regularly","chinese":"定期上課；經常出席"},{"english":"remain extremely limited","chinese":"仍然極為有限"},{"english":"operate effectively","chinese":"有效運作"},{"english":"be transported","chinese":"被運送"},{"english":"be powered","chinese":"獲得供電"},{"english":"reach treatment in time","chinese":"及時接受治療"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"merely one development problem among many","chinese":"眾多發展問題中的其中一個"},{"english":"other forms of aid","chinese":"其他形式的援助"},{"english":"under-developed countries","chinese":"欠發達國家"},{"english":"become less dependent on","chinese":"變得較少依賴……"},{"english":"foreign support","chinese":"外國支援"},{"english":"in the long run","chinese":"長遠而言"},{"english":"power systems","chinese":"電力系統"},{"english":"digital networks","chinese":"數碼網絡"},{"english":"local businesses","chinese":"本地企業"},{"english":"bring goods to wider markets","chinese":"將貨物帶到更廣闊的市場"},{"english":"employment opportunities","chinese":"就業機會"},{"english":"domestic economy","chinese":"本地經濟"},{"english":"far more sustainable than","chinese":"比……可持續得多"},{"english":"short-term donations","chinese":"短期捐助"},{"english":"dependable transport system","chinese":"可靠的運輸系統"},{"english":"small producers","chinese":"小型生產者"},{"english":"sell their products nationally","chinese":"在全國銷售產品"},{"english":"rather than only within","chinese":"而不只是局限於……"},{"english":"isolated villages","chinese":"偏遠村落"},{"english":"as income rises","chinese":"隨着收入上升"},{"english":"collect more tax revenue","chinese":"收取更多稅收"},{"english":"reinvest it in","chinese":"將其重新投資於……"},{"english":"public services","chinese":"公共服務"},{"english":"strengthen the physical backbone","chinese":"加強國家的實體支柱"},{"english":"future progress","chinese":"未來進步"},{"english":"stand on its own feet","chinese":"自力更生"},{"english":"fully agree that","chinese":"完全同意……"},{"english":"be the first issue addressed by","chinese":"成為……首先處理的問題"},{"english":"development efforts","chinese":"發展工作"},{"english":"be likely to","chinese":"很可能會"},{"english":"slow, fragile, and inefficient","chinese":"緩慢、脆弱而低效"},{"english":"basic platform","chinese":"基本平台"},{"english":"modernise independently","chinese":"獨立地現代化"}]},"model-essay-100-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-100-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:100","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-100-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q100","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In today’s competitive labour market, many applicants possess similar degrees, training, and technical skills, so employers often rely on interviews to decide who is truly suitable. I completely agree that performing well in an interview is the key to securing a good job because it allows candidates to create trust and demonstrate qualities that a written application cannot fully show.","chinese":"在當今競爭激烈的勞動市場中，許多求職者都擁有相似的學位、培訓和技術能力，因此僱主往往依靠面試來判斷誰才是真正合適的人選。 我完全同意，在面試中表現出色是獲得一份好工作的關鍵，因為它能讓求職者建立信任，並展現書面申請無法完全呈現的特質。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The most important reason is that interviews turn a candidate from a set of documents into a real person. A strong first impression can make employers feel that an applicant is confident, prepared, and reliable, which is crucial when they are choosing someone to represent their company. If a candidate answers clearly, listens carefully, and speaks with genuine interest, the interviewer is more likely to imagine that person working well with colleagues and clients. For example, two graduates may have almost identical academic results, but the one who explains ideas calmly and shows enthusiasm will usually appear more employable. In this sense, the interview is not a minor formality; it is the moment when paper qualifications become professional credibility.","chinese":"最重要的原因是，面試能把一位求職者從一堆文件轉化成一個真實的人。 良好的第一印象能讓僱主覺得申請者自信、有準備，而且可靠；當他們要選擇一個能代表公司的人時，這一點至關重要。 如果求職者回答清晰、細心聆聽，並且帶著真誠的興趣說話，面試官就更有可能想像這個人能與同事和客戶良好合作。 例如，兩位畢業生的學業成績可能幾乎完全相同，但能夠冷靜解釋想法並展現熱誠的那一位，通常會顯得更具就業能力。 從這個意義上說，面試並不是一個次要的形式程序；它是紙面資歷轉化為專業可信度的時刻。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that many valuable workplace qualities can only be tested through direct interaction. A good job rarely depends on technical knowledge alone. Employers also need people who can communicate under pressure, solve problems sensibly, and adapt to unexpected questions. Interviews reveal these abilities because candidates must think on their feet rather than hide behind polished documents. For instance, when an applicant is asked how they would handle a difficult customer or a tight deadline, their response can show maturity, judgement, and emotional control. These qualities are difficult to measure through a résumé, yet they strongly influence whether someone will succeed in a demanding role.","chinese":"另一個原因是，許多寶貴的職場特質只能透過直接互動來測試。 一份好工作很少只取決於技術知識本身。 僱主也需要能夠在壓力下溝通、理性解決問題，並適應意想不到問題的人。 面試能揭示這些能力，因為求職者必須即場思考，而不是躲在精心修飾的文件背後。 例如，當一位申請者被問到他們會如何處理一位難應付的客戶或一個緊迫的截止期限時，他們的回答可以展現成熟度、判斷力和情緒控制能力。 這些特質很難透過履歷來衡量，但它們會強烈影響一個人能否在要求高的職位中取得成功"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely agree that doing well in interviews is central to getting a good job. Qualifications may help a candidate enter the race, but the interview is usually where the race is won.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全同意，在面試中表現出色是獲得一份好工作的核心。 資歷也許能幫助求職者進入這場競賽，但面試通常才是這場競賽勝出的地方。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"competitive labour market","chinese":"競爭激烈的勞動市場"},{"english":"possess similar degrees","chinese":"擁有相似學位"},{"english":"technical skills","chinese":"技術技能"},{"english":"rely on interviews to","chinese":"依靠面試去……"},{"english":"truly suitable","chinese":"真正適合"},{"english":"performing well in an interview","chinese":"在面試中表現良好"},{"english":"the key to securing","chinese":"獲得……的關鍵"},{"english":"create trust","chinese":"建立信任"},{"english":"demonstrate qualities","chinese":"展示特質"},{"english":"written application","chinese":"書面申請"},{"english":"fully show","chinese":"充分展示"},{"english":"a set of documents","chinese":"一組文件"},{"english":"a real person","chinese":"真實的人"},{"english":"strong first impression","chinese":"良好的第一印象"},{"english":"make employers feel that","chinese":"令僱主覺得……"},{"english":"confident, prepared, and reliable","chinese":"自信、有準備和可靠"},{"english":"be crucial when","chinese":"在……時十分關鍵"},{"english":"represent their company","chinese":"代表公司"},{"english":"answer clearly","chinese":"清楚回答"},{"english":"listens carefully","chinese":"細心聆聽"},{"english":"speaks with genuine interest","chinese":"帶着真誠興趣說話"},{"english":"be more likely to imagine","chinese":"更有可能想像"},{"english":"working well with","chinese":"與……合作良好"},{"english":"colleagues and clients","chinese":"同事和客戶"},{"english":"almost identical academic results","chinese":"幾乎相同的學業成績"},{"english":"explains ideas calmly","chinese":"冷靜地解釋想法"},{"english":"shows enthusiasm","chinese":"表現出熱誠"},{"english":"appear more employable","chinese":"顯得更適合受聘"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"a minor formality","chinese":"小小的形式程序"},{"english":"paper qualifications","chinese":"紙面資歷"},{"english":"professional credibility","chinese":"專業可信度"},{"english":"valuable workplace qualities","chinese":"有價值的職場特質"},{"english":"direct interaction","chinese":"直接互動"},{"english":"technical knowledge alone","chinese":"單靠技術知識"},{"english":"communicate under pressure","chinese":"在壓力下溝通"},{"english":"solve problems sensibly","chinese":"理智地解決問題"},{"english":"adapt to unexpected questions","chinese":"適應突如其來的問題"},{"english":"reveal these abilities","chinese":"顯示這些能力"},{"english":"think on their feet","chinese":"即場反應；臨場思考"},{"english":"hide behind","chinese":"躲在……背後"},{"english":"polished documents","chinese":"經修飾的文件"},{"english":"handle a difficult customer","chinese":"處理難纏顧客"},{"english":"a tight deadline","chinese":"緊迫的限期"},{"english":"maturity, judgement, and emotional control","chinese":"成熟、判斷力和情緒控制"},{"english":"be difficult to measure through","chinese":"難以透過……衡量"},{"english":"a résumé","chinese":"履歷；履歷表"},{"english":"strongly influence whether","chinese":"強烈影響是否……"},{"english":"succeed in","chinese":"在……中成功"},{"english":"demanding role","chinese":"要求高的職位"},{"english":"doing well in interviews","chinese":"在面試中表現好"},{"english":"be central to","chinese":"對……十分重要"},{"english":"enter the race","chinese":"進入競爭"},{"english":"where the race is won","chinese":"決勝之處"}]},"model-essay-101-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-101-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:101","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-101-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q101","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many countries, the largest salaries are often earned by actors, singers and professional athletes rather than by those who protect public health or educate the next generation. I completely agree that doctors, nurses and teachers should be paid more than entertainment and sports celebrities, because their work is both more socially essential and more deserving of public investment.","chinese":"在許多國家，最高的薪酬往往由演員、歌手和職業運動員賺取，而不是由那些保護公共健康或教育下一代的人獲得。 我完全同意醫生、護士和教師應該比娛樂和體育明星獲得更高薪酬，因為他們的工作在社會上更為重要，也更值得公共投資。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason is that these professionals form the backbone of a functioning society. Doctors and nurses do not merely perform a job; they preserve life, relieve suffering and keep families from falling apart when illness strikes. Their decisions can mean the difference between recovery and tragedy. Teachers play a similarly fundamental role, although their contribution is less dramatic on the surface. A good teacher can turn a confused child into a confident learner, and that learner may later become a skilled worker, responsible parent or thoughtful citizen. Celebrities may entertain millions, but entertainment is a luxury; healthcare and education are the oxygen of social progress. For this reason, it is morally difficult to justify paying a footballer more than a nurse who saves lives every week.","chinese":"最有力的理由是，這些專業人士構成了一個正常運作社會的支柱。 醫生和護士不只是執行一份工作；他們守護生命、減輕痛苦，並在疾病來襲時防止家庭崩潰。 他們的決定可能意味著康復與悲劇之間的差別。 教師也扮演著同樣根本的角色，儘管他們的貢獻在表面上沒有那麼戲劇性。 一位好老師可以把一個迷惘的孩子變成一個有自信的學習者，而這位學習者日後可能成為一名有技能的工人、負責任的父母，或有思想的公民。 名人或許能娛樂數以百萬計的人，但娛樂是一種奢侈；醫療和教育才是社會進步的氧氣 因此，從道德角度看，很難合理化一名足球員比一位每週拯救生命的護士獲得更高薪酬"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Higher pay for these professions is also necessary because it would attract and retain capable people in demanding public-service roles. Becoming a doctor, nurse or teacher requires years of training, emotional resilience and daily responsibility, yet many of these workers face stress, long hours and limited recognition. If their salaries remain modest, talented young people may avoid these careers or leave them early, which weakens hospitals and schools. By contrast, celebrity income is often inflated by advertising, ticket sales and global media attention, not by deeper social importance. A society that rewards fame more than service sends the wrong message about what it values.","chinese":"提高這些職業的薪酬也是必要的，因為這能吸引並留住有能力的人才，讓他們繼續從事要求很高的公共服務崗位。 成為醫生、護士或教師需要多年的訓練、情緒韌性和日常責任感，然而這些工作者中的許多人卻面對壓力、長工時和有限的認可。 如果他們的薪酬仍然偏低，有才華的年輕人可能會避開這些職業，或很早便離開，這會削弱醫院和學校的力量。 相比之下，名人的收入往往是由廣告、門票銷售和全球媒體關注所推高，而不是由更深層的社會重要性所決定。 一個獎勵名氣多於服務的社會，會向人們傳遞錯誤的價值訊息。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I firmly agree that doctors, nurses and teachers should be paid more than entertainment and sports celebrities. While celebrities can enrich people’s leisure time, essential workers protect lives, shape minds and hold society together.","chinese":"總結來說，我堅定同意醫生、護士和教師應該比娛樂和體育明星獲得更高薪酬。 雖然名人可豐富人們的休閒時間，但必要工作者保護生命、塑造思想，並維繫整個社會"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the largest salaries","chinese":"最高薪酬"},{"english":"be earned by","chinese":"由……賺取"},{"english":"professional athletes","chinese":"職業運動員"},{"english":"rather than by","chinese":"而不是由……"},{"english":"protect public health","chinese":"保障公共健康"},{"english":"educate the next generation","chinese":"教育下一代"},{"english":"completely agree that","chinese":"完全同意……"},{"english":"be paid more than","chinese":"薪酬高於……"},{"english":"entertainment and sports celebrities","chinese":"娛樂和體育名人"},{"english":"socially essential","chinese":"對社會更必要"},{"english":"deserving of public investment","chinese":"更值得公共投資"},{"english":"the strongest reason","chinese":"最有力的原因"},{"english":"form the backbone of","chinese":"構成……的支柱"},{"english":"functioning society","chinese":"正常運作的社會"},{"english":"merely perform a job","chinese":"只是做一份工作"},{"english":"preserve life","chinese":"維持生命；保護生命"},{"english":"relieve suffering","chinese":"減輕痛苦"},{"english":"keep families from falling apart","chinese":"防止家庭崩潰"},{"english":"when illness strikes","chinese":"當疾病來襲時"},{"english":"mean the difference between","chinese":"可能決定是……還是……"},{"english":"recovery and tragedy","chinese":"康復和悲劇"},{"english":"play a similarly fundamental role","chinese":"發揮同樣根本的作用"},{"english":"contribution","chinese":"貢獻"},{"english":"less dramatic on the surface","chinese":"表面上較不戲劇化"},{"english":"on the surface","chinese":"表面上"},{"english":"turn a confused child into","chinese":"將一個困惑的孩子變成……"},{"english":"confident learner","chinese":"有自信的學習者"},{"english":"skilled worker","chinese":"熟練工人"},{"english":"responsible parent","chinese":"負責任的父母"},{"english":"thoughtful citizen","chinese":"有思想的公民"},{"english":"entertain millions","chinese":"娛樂數以百萬計的人"},{"english":"a luxury","chinese":"奢侈品；非必需品"},{"english":"the oxygen of social progress","chinese":"社會進步的氧氣"},{"english":"morally difficult to justify","chinese":"道德上難以合理化"},{"english":"saves lives","chinese":"拯救生命"},{"english":"higher pay","chinese":"較高薪酬"},{"english":"attract and retain","chinese":"吸引並留住"},{"english":"capable people","chinese":"有能力的人才"},{"english":"demanding public-service roles","chinese":"要求高的公共服務職位"},{"english":"require years of training","chinese":"需要多年培訓"},{"english":"emotional resilience","chinese":"情緒韌性"},{"english":"daily responsibility","chinese":"日常責任"},{"english":"face stress","chinese":"面對壓力"},{"english":"long hours","chinese":"長時間工作"},{"english":"limited recognition","chinese":"有限認可"},{"english":"salaries remain modest","chinese":"薪酬維持不高"},{"english":"talented young people","chinese":"有才能的年輕人"},{"english":"avoid these careers","chinese":"避免選擇這些職業"},{"english":"leave them early","chinese":"早早離開這些職業"},{"english":"weakens hospitals and schools","chinese":"削弱醫院和學校"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"celebrity income","chinese":"名人收入"},{"english":"be inflated by","chinese":"因……而被推高"},{"english":"advertising","chinese":"廣告"},{"english":"ticket sales","chinese":"門票銷售"},{"english":"global media attention","chinese":"全球媒體關注"},{"english":"deeper social importance","chinese":"更深層的社會重要性"},{"english":"reward fame more than service","chinese":"獎勵名氣多於服務"},{"english":"send the wrong message","chinese":"傳達錯誤信息"},{"english":"what it values","chinese":"它重視甚麼"},{"english":"firmly agree that","chinese":"堅定同意……"},{"english":"enrich people's leisure time","chinese":"豐富人們的閒暇時間"},{"english":"essential workers","chinese":"必要工作者"},{"english":"shape minds","chinese":"塑造思想"},{"english":"hold society together","chinese":"維繫社會"}]},"model-essay-103-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-103-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:103","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-103-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q103","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In any organisation, pay is more than a monthly transfer; it is a signal of responsibility, contribution, and trust. For this reason, I completely disagree that giving all workers the same salary would create genuine harmony or mutual respect. Although the idea may sound fair at first glance, it would quickly become unfair in practice.","chinese":"在任何機構中，薪酬不僅僅是每月的一筆轉帳；它也是責任、貢獻和信任的象徵。 因此，我完全不同意給所有員工相同薪金會創造真正的和諧或相互尊重。 儘管這個想法乍看之下可能很公平，但在實際操作中，它很快便會變得不公平。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The main problem is that equal pay ignores real differences in workload, skill, and responsibility. A senior engineer who designs complex systems, a manager who is accountable for a whole department, and a junior employee who is still being trained do not carry the same burden. If they all receive identical salaries, the company is not treating them equally; it is refusing to recognise meaningful differences. This can easily breed resentment rather than unity, because employees whose roles are more demanding may feel that their effort has been quietly erased. For example, a team leader who works late to solve client problems is unlikely to feel respected if a colleague with far fewer duties receives exactly the same reward.","chinese":"主要問題是，劃一薪酬忽視了工作量、技能和責任上的真實差異。 一位設計複雜系統的資深工程師、一位需要對整個部門負責的經理，以及一位仍在接受培訓的初級員工，並不承擔相同的負擔。 如果他們都獲得完全相同的薪金，公司並不是在平等對待他們；而是在拒絕承認有意義的差異。 這很容易滋生怨氣，而不是團結，因為那些職責更繁重的員工可能會覺得自己的努力被悄悄抹去。 例如，一位為了解決客戶問題而工作至很晚的團隊主管，如果看到一位職責少得多的同事獲得完全相同的報酬，便很難感到自己受到尊重。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that a flat salary system would weaken motivation and damage performance. In a healthy workplace, pay should not be the only incentive, but it is still one important way to reward progress, reliability, and excellence. If extra effort brings no extra recognition, ambitious workers may eventually slow down or leave for companies that value their contribution more accurately. At the same time, weaker employees may have little reason to improve, since the system protects them from the consequences of poor performance. Over time, this would not create a peaceful workplace; it would create a quiet frustration under the surface.","chinese":"另一個原因是，劃一薪酬制度會削弱動力並損害工作表現。 在一個健康的工作場所中，薪酬不應該是唯一的激勵因素，但它仍然是獎勵進步、可靠性和卓越表現的重要方式之一。 如果額外努力得不到額外認可，有抱負的員工最終可能會放慢步伐，或者離開並加入那些能更準確重視他們貢獻的公司。 與此同時，表現較弱的員工可能沒有太多改善的理由，因為這個制度會保護他們免受低效表現所帶來的後果。 長遠而言，這並不會創造一個平和的工作場所；它只在表面之下製造一種沉默的挫敗感"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, paying everyone the same may appear to remove jealousy, but it would actually undermine fairness, motivation, and respect. True workplace harmony comes from fair treatment, not identical treatment.","chinese":"總結來說，給每個人相同薪金看似可以消除嫉妒，但實際上卻會削弱公平、動力和尊重 真正的職場和諧來自公平對待，而不是完全相同的對待。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"in any organisation","chinese":"在任何機構中"},{"english":"pay is more than","chinese":"薪酬不只是……"},{"english":"a monthly transfer","chinese":"每月轉賬"},{"english":"a signal of ……","chinese":"的信號；……的象徵"},{"english":"responsibility, contribution, and trust","chinese":"責任、貢獻和信任"},{"english":"for this reason","chinese":"因此"},{"english":"completely disagree that","chinese":"完全不同意……"},{"english":"giving all workers the same salary","chinese":"給所有員工相同薪金"},{"english":"genuine harmony","chinese":"真正的和諧"},{"english":"mutual respect","chinese":"互相尊重"},{"english":"sound fair at first glance","chinese":"乍看之下似乎公平"},{"english":"unfair in practice","chinese":"實際上變得不公平"},{"english":"equal pay","chinese":"相同薪酬"},{"english":"ignore real differences in","chinese":"忽視……的實際差異"},{"english":"workload, skill, and responsibility","chinese":"工作量、技能和責任"},{"english":"senior engineer","chinese":"高級工程師"},{"english":"design complex systems","chinese":"設計複雜系統"},{"english":"be accountable for","chinese":"對……負責"},{"english":"a whole department","chinese":"整個部門"},{"english":"junior employee","chinese":"初級員工"},{"english":"be still being trained","chinese":"仍在接受培訓"},{"english":"carry the same burden","chinese":"承擔相同負擔"},{"english":"receive identical salaries","chinese":"收取完全相同的薪金"},{"english":"treat them equally","chinese":"平等對待他們"},{"english":"refuse to recognise","chinese":"拒絕承認"},{"english":"meaningful differences","chinese":"有意義的差異"},{"english":"breed resentment rather than unity","chinese":"滋生怨氣而不是團結"},{"english":"roles are more demanding","chinese":"職位要求更高"},{"english":"effort has been quietly erased","chinese":"努力被默默抹去"},{"english":"team leader","chinese":"團隊主管"},{"english":"work late","chinese":"工作至很晚"},{"english":"solve client problems","chinese":"解決客戶問題"},{"english":"far fewer duties","chinese":"少得多的職責"},{"english":"exactly the same reward","chinese":"完全相同的回報"},{"english":"flat salary system","chinese":"劃一薪酬制度"},{"english":"weaken motivation","chinese":"削弱動力"},{"english":"damage performance","chinese":"損害表現"},{"english":"healthy workplace","chinese":"健康的工作場所"},{"english":"the only incentive","chinese":"唯一誘因"},{"english":"one important way to ……","chinese":"的一個重要方式"},{"english":"reward progress","chinese":"獎勵進步"},{"english":"reliability and excellence","chinese":"可靠性和卓越表現"},{"english":"extra effort","chinese":"額外努力"},{"english":"extra recognition","chinese":"額外認可"},{"english":"ambitious workers","chinese":"有抱負的員工"},{"english":"eventually slow down","chinese":"最終放慢步伐"},{"english":"value their contribution","chinese":"重視他們的貢獻"},{"english":"more accurately","chinese":"更準確地"},{"english":"weaker employees","chinese":"表現較弱的員工"},{"english":"have little reason to","chinese":"沒有太大理由去……"},{"english":"protect them from","chinese":"保護他們免受……"},{"english":"the consequences of ……","chinese":"的後果"},{"english":"poor performance","chinese":"表現欠佳"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨着時間過去"},{"english":"peaceful workplace","chinese":"和諧安穩的工作場所"},{"english":"quiet frustration under the surface","chinese":"表面下暗藏的不滿"},{"english":"appear to remove jealousy","chinese":"看似消除妒忌"},{"english":"undermine fairness","chinese":"損害公平"},{"english":"true workplace harmony","chinese":"真正的職場和諧"},{"english":"fair treatment","chinese":"公平對待"},{"english":"identical treatment","chinese":"一模一樣的待遇"}]},"model-essay-104-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-104-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:104","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-104-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q104","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"The movement of workers across national borders has become an important part of many modern economies. Some argue that foreign workers should no longer be recruited for jobs that local people refuse to do because their presence may create pressure within the community. I completely disagree with this view, as stopping this practice would damage essential services and ignore the real causes of local tension.","chinese":"勞工跨越國界流動，已經成為許多現代經濟體的重要一部分。 有些人認為，不應再招聘外籍工人去從事本地人拒絕做的工作，因為他們的存在可能會為本地社區帶來壓力。 我完全不同意這個觀點，因為停止這種做法會損害基本服務，並忽視本地緊張關係的真正原因。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first reason is that many communities rely heavily on migrant workers to keep basic sectors functioning. Jobs in agriculture, elderly care, cleaning, construction, and food production are often physically demanding, low-status, or poorly paid, which explains why many local workers avoid them. If employers were suddenly prevented from hiring foreign staff, these roles would not magically become attractive to domestic workers. Instead, farms could lose crops, care homes could become understaffed, and building projects could slow down. For example, a city that depends on migrant carers for its ageing population would face a serious welfare problem if those workers were removed. In this sense, banning foreign labour would not protect the community; it would weaken the very services that residents depend on.","chinese":"第一個原因是，許多社區都高度依賴外來勞工來維持基本行業的運作。 農業、長者照顧、清潔、建築和食品生產方面的工作，往往體力要求高、社會地位較低，或者薪酬欠佳，這解釋了為甚麼許多本地工人會避開這些工作。 如果僱主突然被禁止聘請外籍員工，這些職位並不會神奇地變得吸引本地工人。 相反，農場可能會失去收成，護老院可能會人手不足，而建築項目也可能會放慢。 例如，一個依賴外來護理員照顧老齡人口的城市，如果這些工人被移走，便會面對嚴重的福利問題。 從這個角度來看，禁止外籍勞工並不會保護社區；它反而會削弱居民所依賴的基本服務。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Another reason is that the problems linked to foreign workers are usually caused by poor management rather than immigration itself. Local resentment may arise when wages are unfair, housing is overcrowded, or newcomers are left socially isolated. However, these issues can be addressed through stronger labour laws, fair recruitment, language support, and proper housing standards. Blaming foreign workers is therefore a convenient but shallow solution. It treats them as the problem, when in reality they are often filling gaps that the local labour market has failed to solve. A well-regulated system can protect domestic workers, prevent exploitation, and help migrants integrate into the community more smoothly.","chinese":"另一個原因是，與外籍工人有關的問題通常是由管理不善造成，而不是由移民本身造成 當工資不公平、住房過度擁擠，或者新來者在社交上被孤立時，本地人的不滿情緒便可能出現 然而，這些問題可以透過更強而有力的勞工法例、公平招聘、語言支援和適當的住房標準來處理。 因此，責怪外籍工人是一個方便但膚淺的解決方法。 這種做法把他們視為問題，但事實上，他們往往是在填補本地勞動市場未能解決的空缺 一個受到良好規管的制度可以保障本地工人、防止剝削，並幫助移民更順利地融入社區。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I completely disagree that foreign workers should be stopped from taking jobs local workers are unwilling to do. Such a ban would create labour shortages, harm public services, and fail to address the underlying causes of social conflict. The better solution is not exclusion, but fair regulation and thoughtful integration.","chinese":"總結來說，我完全不同意應該阻止外籍工人從事本地工人不願意做的工作。 這樣的禁令會造成勞工短缺、損害公共服務，並且無法處理社會衝突背後的根本原因。 更好的解決方法不是排斥，而是公平規管和周全融合。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"the movement of workers","chinese":"工人的流動"},{"english":"across national borders","chinese":"跨越國界"},{"english":"modern economies","chinese":"現代經濟體"},{"english":"foreign workers","chinese":"外勞；外籍工人"},{"english":"no longer be recruited","chinese":"不再被招聘"},{"english":"local people refuse to do","chinese":"本地人拒絕做的"},{"english":"their presence","chinese":"他們的存在"},{"english":"create pressure within","chinese":"在……內造成壓力"},{"english":"completely disagree with","chinese":"完全不同意"},{"english":"stopping this practice","chinese":"停止這種做法"},{"english":"essential services","chinese":"基本服務"},{"english":"local tension","chinese":"本地緊張關係"},{"english":"rely heavily on","chinese":"非常依賴"},{"english":"migrant workers","chinese":"外來工人；移民工人"},{"english":"keep basic sectors functioning","chinese":"維持基本行業運作"},{"english":"agriculture","chinese":"農業"},{"english":"elderly care","chinese":"長者照顧"},{"english":"food production","chinese":"食品生產"},{"english":"physically demanding","chinese":"體力要求高的"},{"english":"low-status","chinese":"社會地位較低的"},{"english":"poorly paid","chinese":"薪酬低的"},{"english":"explains why","chinese":"解釋了為甚麼"},{"english":"local workers","chinese":"本地工人"},{"english":"be prevented from","chinese":"被阻止去……"},{"english":"hiring foreign staff","chinese":"聘請外籍員工"},{"english":"magically become attractive to","chinese":"神奇地變得對……有吸引力"},{"english":"domestic workers","chinese":"本地工人"},{"english":"lose crops","chinese":"失去農作物收成"},{"english":"care homes","chinese":"護老院"},{"english":"become understaffed","chinese":"人手不足"},{"english":"building projects","chinese":"建築項目"},{"english":"slow down","chinese":"放慢；拖慢"},{"english":"depend on migrant carers","chinese":"依賴外來護理員"},{"english":"ageing population","chinese":"老齡化人口"},{"english":"face a serious welfare problem","chinese":"面對嚴重的福利問題"},{"english":"be removed","chinese":"被移走；被撤走"},{"english":"banning foreign labour","chinese":"禁止外勞"},{"english":"protect the community","chinese":"保護社區"},{"english":"weaken the very services","chinese":"削弱正正是……的服務"},{"english":"residents depend on","chinese":"居民依賴"},{"english":"problems linked to","chinese":"與……有關的問題"},{"english":"poor management","chinese":"管理不善"},{"english":"rather than immigration itself","chinese":"而不是移民本身"},{"english":"local resentment","chinese":"本地人的不滿"},{"english":"may arise when","chinese":"可能在……時出現"},{"english":"wages are unfair","chinese":"工資不公平"},{"english":"housing is overcrowded","chinese":"住屋過度擠迫"},{"english":"newcomers","chinese":"新來者"},{"english":"be left socially isolated","chinese":"被社會孤立"},{"english":"be addressed through","chinese":"透過……處理"},{"english":"stronger labour laws","chinese":"更強而有力的勞工法例"},{"english":"fair recruitment","chinese":"公平招聘"},{"english":"language support","chinese":"語言支援"},{"english":"proper housing standards","chinese":"適當的住屋標準"},{"english":"blaming foreign workers","chinese":"責怪外勞"},{"english":"a convenient but shallow solution","chinese":"方便但膚淺的解決方法"},{"english":"in reality","chinese":"實際上"},{"english":"filling gaps","chinese":"填補缺口"},{"english":"local labour market","chinese":"本地勞動市場"},{"english":"well-regulated system","chinese":"監管良好的制度"},{"english":"prevent exploitation","chinese":"防止剝削"},{"english":"integrate into the community","chinese":"融入社區"},{"english":"more smoothly","chinese":"更順利地"},{"english":"be stopped from","chinese":"被阻止做……"},{"english":"unwilling to do","chinese":"不願意做"},{"english":"such a ban","chinese":"這樣的禁令"},{"english":"labour shortages","chinese":"勞工短缺"},{"english":"harm public services","chinese":"損害公共服務"},{"english":"underlying causes","chinese":"根本原因"},{"english":"social conflict","chinese":"社會衝突"},{"english":"exclusion","chinese":"排斥"},{"english":"fair regulation","chinese":"公平監管"},{"english":"thoughtful integration","chinese":"周全的融合措施"}]},"model-essay-105-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-105-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:105","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-105-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q105","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In any organisation, employers have to decide whether their main duty is to improve the human atmosphere of the workplace or to invest in better physical resources. In my view, creating a respectful and supportive environment should be the clear priority, because people cannot perform well for long if they feel ignored, unsafe, or unfairly treated.","chinese":"在任何機構中，僱主都必須決定，他們的主要責任是改善工作場所中的人際氛圍，還是投資於更好的實體資源。 在我看來，創造一個尊重和支持員工的環境應該是明確的優先事項，因為如果人們感到被忽視、不安全或受到不公平對待，他們便無法長期有良好表現。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The strongest reason is that a healthy workplace culture directly affects motivation and loyalty. When employees are respected equally, they are more willing to share ideas, admit mistakes, and cooperate with colleagues. This kind of trust is not a soft luxury; it is the foundation on which serious work is built. For example, a junior employee who is listened to during meetings is more likely to point out a problem early, whereas someone who is constantly dismissed may stay silent until the problem becomes costly. In this sense, respect can prevent small issues from growing into major failures.","chinese":"最有力的原因是，健康的職場文化會直接影響員工的動力和忠誠度。 當員工受到平等尊重時，他們會更願意分享想法、承認錯誤，並與同事合作。 這種信任並不是一種可有可無的溫和奢侈品；它是嚴肅工作得以建立的基礎。 例如，一位在會議中受到聆聽的初級員工，更有可能及早指出問題；相反，一個經常被否定的人，可能會保持沉默，直到問題變得代價高昂。 從這個角度來看，尊重可以防止小問題演變成重大失誤。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"Better facilities and equipment are certainly useful, but they cannot compensate for a toxic or unequal environment. A modern computer, a comfortable office, or an attractive staff room may make daily tasks easier, yet these things have limited value if workers feel humiliated by managers or excluded by their team. In fact, employees in such conditions may use the best tools with little enthusiasm, simply doing the minimum because they no longer feel emotionally invested in the organisation. By contrast, people in a fair and encouraging workplace often remain productive even when resources are not perfect, because they feel that their effort matters.","chinese":"更好的設施和設備當然有用，但它們無法彌補一個有毒或不平等的工作環境。 一部現代化的電腦、一間舒適的辦公室，或一個吸引人的員工休息室，可能會令日常工作更容易完成；然而，如果員工感到被管理層羞辱，或被團隊排斥，這些東西的價值便十分有限。 事實上，在這種情況下的員工，即使使用最好的工具，也可能缺乏熱情，只是完成最低限度的工作，因為他們在情感上已不再投入這個機構。 相比之下，在一個公平而鼓勵人的工作場所中，即使資源並不完美，人們往往仍能保持生產力，因為他們覺得自己的努力是有意義的。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, although equipment and facilities can improve efficiency, they should not be the employer’s central focus. A workplace where people are respected, valued, and supported is far more important, because it builds the trust and commitment that no machine or office design can replace.","chinese":"總結來說，儘管設備和設施可以提升效率，它們不應該成為僱主的核心關注點。 一個讓人受到尊重、重視和支持的工作場所遠為重要，因為它能建立信任和投入感，而這是任何機器或辦公室設計都無法取代的。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"in any organisation","chinese":"在任何機構中"},{"english":"main duty","chinese":"主要責任"},{"english":"improve the human atmosphere","chinese":"改善人際氣氛"},{"english":"the workplace","chinese":"工作場所"},{"english":"invest in","chinese":"投資於……"},{"english":"physical resources","chinese":"實體資源"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"respectful and supportive environment","chinese":"互相尊重和支持的環境"},{"english":"the clear priority","chinese":"明確的優先事項"},{"english":"perform well for long","chinese":"長期有良好表現"},{"english":"feel ignored","chinese":"感到被忽視"},{"english":"unfairly treated","chinese":"受到不公平對待"},{"english":"the strongest reason","chinese":"最有力的原因"},{"english":"healthy workplace culture","chinese":"健康的工作場所文化"},{"english":"directly affects","chinese":"直接影響"},{"english":"motivation and loyalty","chinese":"動力和忠誠度"},{"english":"be respected equally","chinese":"受到平等尊重"},{"english":"be more willing to","chinese":"更願意去……"},{"english":"share ideas","chinese":"分享想法"},{"english":"admit mistakes","chinese":"承認錯誤"},{"english":"cooperate with colleagues","chinese":"與同事合作"},{"english":"this kind of trust","chinese":"這種信任"},{"english":"a soft luxury","chinese":"可有可無的奢侈品"},{"english":"the foundation on which ……","chinese":"的基礎"},{"english":"serious work","chinese":"認真而重要的工作"},{"english":"a junior employee","chinese":"初級員工"},{"english":"be listened to","chinese":"被聆聽"},{"english":"during meetings","chinese":"在會議期間"},{"english":"be more likely to","chinese":"更有可能"},{"english":"point out a problem","chinese":"指出問題"},{"english":"constantly dismissed","chinese":"經常被否定"},{"english":"stay silent","chinese":"保持沉默"},{"english":"become costly","chinese":"變得代價高昂"},{"english":"in this sense","chinese":"從這個意義上說"},{"english":"prevent small issues from","chinese":"防止小問題……"},{"english":"major failures","chinese":"重大失誤"},{"english":"better facilities and equipment","chinese":"更好的設施和設備"},{"english":"compensate for","chinese":"彌補"},{"english":"toxic environment","chinese":"有害的工作環境"},{"english":"unequal environment","chinese":"不平等的環境"},{"english":"comfortable office","chinese":"舒適的辦公室"},{"english":"attractive staff room","chinese":"吸引人的員工休息室"},{"english":"daily tasks","chinese":"日常工作"},{"english":"have limited value","chinese":"價值有限"},{"english":"feel humiliated by","chinese":"因……而感到受辱"},{"english":"be excluded by","chinese":"被……排斥"},{"english":"in such conditions","chinese":"在這種情況下"},{"english":"use the best tools","chinese":"使用最好的工具"},{"english":"with little enthusiasm","chinese":"沒有甚麼熱誠"},{"english":"do the minimum","chinese":"只做最低限度的工作"},{"english":"emotionally invested in","chinese":"在情感上投入於……"},{"english":"by contrast","chinese":"相比之下"},{"english":"fair and encouraging workplace","chinese":"公平而鼓勵人的工作場所"},{"english":"remain productive","chinese":"保持生產力"},{"english":"resources are not perfect","chinese":"資源並不完善"},{"english":"their effort matters","chinese":"他們的努力有價值"},{"english":"improve efficiency","chinese":"提高效率"},{"english":"central focus","chinese":"核心焦點"},{"english":"be respected, valued, and supported","chinese":"受到尊重、重視和支持"},{"english":"far more important","chinese":"重要得多"},{"english":"build the trust and commitment","chinese":"建立信任和承諾"},{"english":"no machine or office design can replace","chinese":"沒有機器或辦公室設計可以取代"}]},"model-essay-106-ielts-opinion":{"exerciseId":"model-essay-106-ielts-opinion","essayKey":"opinion:106","writingHref":"writing-practice.html?exercise=model-essay-106-ielts-opinion","flashDeckId":"ielts/writing/task-2/opinions/EdmundBd9OP-Q106","paragraphs":[{"label":"Introduction","english":"In many parts of the world, family-run companies are a familiar part of commercial life, from small shops to large enterprises. Although such businesses may appear stable because relatives know one another well, I do not believe that family ownership is the best way to run a company. In my view, it often creates more serious problems than advantages because it can weaken professional decision-making and turn private tensions into business risks.","chinese":"在世界許多地方，家族企業都是商業生活中常見的一部分，從小型店舖到大型企業皆是如此。 儘管這類企業可能看起來很穩定，因為親屬之間彼此熟悉， 我並不認為家族擁有權是經營公司的最佳方式。 在我看來，它往往會帶來比好處更嚴重的問題，因為它可能削弱專業決策，並把私人緊張關係轉化為商業風險。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 1","english":"The first problem is that family businesses can easily place loyalty above competence. When important positions are given mainly to relatives, promotion no longer depends on ability, experience, or performance. For example, a founder may appoint a son or daughter to manage sales even though an experienced employee is clearly better suited to the role. This does not only damage efficiency; it also sends a quiet but powerful message to other workers that hard work may never be rewarded fairly. Over time, talented staff may leave, standards may fall, and the company can become a closed room rather than a growing organisation.","chinese":"第一個問題是，家族企業很容易把忠誠放在能力之上。 當重要職位主要交給親屬時，晉升便不再取決於能力、經驗或表現。 例如，一位創辦人可能會任命自己的兒子或女兒管理銷售部門，即使一位有經驗的員工明顯更適合這個職位。 這不但會損害效率，也會向其他員工傳遞一個安靜卻有力的訊息：努力工作可能永遠不會得到公平回報。 長遠而言，有才能的員工可能會離開，標準可能會下降，而公司也可能變成一個封閉的房間，而不是一個正在成長的組織。"},{"label":"Body Paragraph 2","english":"A second issue is that family relationships can make business decisions emotionally complicated. In a professionally managed company, disagreements can be handled through clear rules, contracts, and performance targets. In a family firm, however, a dispute about money, succession, or control may carry years of personal history behind it. For instance, two siblings may argue over whether profits should be reinvested or shared among family members, and this private conflict can quickly slow down decisions that affect employees, customers, and suppliers. When the dining table and the boardroom start to overlap, the business becomes vulnerable to emotions that have little to do with commercial judgment.","chinese":"第二個問題是，家庭關係可能會使商業決策在情感上變得複雜。 在一間由專業方式管理的公司中，分歧可以透過清晰的規則、合約和績效目標來處理。 然而，在家族企業中，一場關於金錢、繼承或控制權的爭議，背後可能承載著多年的私人恩怨與家庭歷史。 例如，兩名兄弟姊妹可能會爭論利潤應該重新投資，還是分配給家庭成員，而這種私人衝突很快就可能拖慢影響員工、顧客和供應商的決策。 當飯桌和董事會議室開始重疊時，企業便會容易受到情緒影響，而這些情緒與商業判斷幾乎沒有關係。"},{"label":"Conclusion","english":"In conclusion, I firmly believe that family ownership is not the best way to run a business. While trust between relatives may seem useful, a company needs merit-based leadership, clear boundaries, and professional accountability more than family loyalty.","chinese":"總結來說，我堅定地認為，家族擁有權並不是經營企業的最佳方式。 雖然親屬之間的信任看似有用，但一間公司更需要以能力為本的領導、清晰的界線，以及專業的問責，而不是家族忠誠。"}],"vocabulary":[{"english":"family-run companies","chinese":"家族經營的公司"},{"english":"a familiar part of ……","chinese":"中常見的一部分"},{"english":"commercial life","chinese":"商業生活；商業活動"},{"english":"small shops to large enterprises","chinese":"從小店到大型企業"},{"english":"appear stable","chinese":"看似穩定"},{"english":"know one another well","chinese":"彼此十分熟悉"},{"english":"family ownership","chinese":"家族擁有權"},{"english":"run a company","chinese":"經營一間公司"},{"english":"in my view","chinese":"在我看來"},{"english":"create more serious problems than advantages","chinese":"帶來的嚴重問題多於好處"},{"english":"weaken professional decision-making","chinese":"削弱專業決策"},{"english":"private tensions","chinese":"私人矛盾"},{"english":"business risks","chinese":"商業風險"},{"english":"place loyalty above competence","chinese":"將忠誠置於能力之上"},{"english":"important positions","chinese":"重要職位"},{"english":"depend on","chinese":"取決於"},{"english":"ability, experience, or performance","chinese":"能力、經驗或表現"},{"english":"appoint a son or daughter to","chinese":"任命兒子或女兒去……"},{"english":"manage sales","chinese":"管理銷售"},{"english":"experienced employee","chinese":"有經驗的員工"},{"english":"be clearly better suited to","chinese":"明顯更適合……"},{"english":"damage efficiency","chinese":"損害效率"},{"english":"send a quiet but powerful message","chinese":"傳達一個不明顯但有力的信息"},{"english":"be rewarded fairly","chinese":"得到公平回報"},{"english":"over time","chinese":"隨着時間過去"},{"english":"talented staff","chinese":"有才能的員工"},{"english":"standards may fall","chinese":"水準可能下降"},{"english":"a growing organisation","chinese":"不斷發展的組織"},{"english":"family relationships","chinese":"家庭關係"},{"english":"emotionally complicated","chinese":"情緒上複雜"},{"english":"professionally managed company","chinese":"專業管理的公司"},{"english":"disagreements","chinese":"分歧；意見不合"},{"english":"be handled through","chinese":"透過……處理"},{"english":"clear rules","chinese":"清晰規則"},{"english":"performance targets","chinese":"表現目標"},{"english":"family firm","chinese":"家族企業"},{"english":"a dispute about","chinese":"關於……的爭議"},{"english":"succession","chinese":"繼承權；接班安排"},{"english":"carry years of personal history behind it","chinese":"背後帶有多年的私人恩怨"},{"english":"argue over whether","chinese":"就是否……而爭論"},{"english":"be reinvested","chinese":"被重新投資"},{"english":"be shared among","chinese":"在……之間分配"},{"english":"family members","chinese":"家庭成員"},{"english":"private conflict","chinese":"私人衝突"},{"english":"slow down decisions","chinese":"拖慢決策"},{"english":"affect employees, customers, and suppliers","chinese":"影響員工、顧客和供應商"},{"english":"the dining table and the boardroom","chinese":"飯桌和董事會會議室"},{"english":"start to overlap","chinese":"開始重疊"},{"english":"become vulnerable to","chinese":"容易受到……影響"},{"english":"have little to do with","chinese":"與……幾乎無關"},{"english":"commercial judgment","chinese":"商業判斷"},{"english":"firmly believe that","chinese":"堅信"},{"english":"not the best way to","chinese":"不是……的最佳方法"},{"english":"trust between relatives","chinese":"親屬之間的信任"},{"english":"merit-based leadership","chinese":"以能力為本的領導"},{"english":"clear boundaries","chinese":"清晰界線"},{"english":"professional accountability","chinese":"專業問責"},{"english":"more than family loyalty","chinese":"多於家族忠誠"}]}};
